var data={"en":{"blocks":{"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Add\n\nAdds any two values together and reports the sum.\n\n![add](static/help/iq/blocks/en/add/add.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Add** can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe length of **add** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\nAdd two numbers.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/en/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nAdd with values from variables.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/en/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nAdd with values from sensors or devices.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/en/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# And\n\nReports if two Boolean conditions are both true. \n\n![and](static/help/iq/blocks/en/and/and.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **and** block reports **true** when both conditions are **true**. \n\nThe **and** block reports **false** when one (or both) of the conditions are **false**.\n\nThe **and** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![and_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/en/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will check if two VEX IQ Controller buttons are being pressed at the same time.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/en/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nThe **and** block will return **true** when both the **Controller E Up button** and the **Controller L Down button** are being pressed.\n\nThe **and** block will return **false** when one (or both) of the controller buttons are not pressed.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/en/and/and_truth.png)"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Battery level\n\nReports the charge level of the VEX IQ Brain's battery.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Battery level** reports a range from **0% to 100%**.\n\nThe reporter block **battery level** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will play an alarm sound if the VEX IQ's Brain **battery level** is lower than 50%.\n\n![battery_capacity_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/battery_level/battery_capacity_example_revised.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Boolean variable\n\nReports the value of a Boolean variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Boolean variable** blocks are used to report a **true** or **false** value stored inside of the variable. Use the **set boolean variable** block to set or update the value of a boolean variable.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/iq/blocks/en/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nThe **boolean variable** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nBoolean variables are created using the **Make a Boolean** button.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"boolean_variable_virtual":{"name":"boolean_variable_virtual","markdown":"# Boolean variable\n\nReports the value of a Boolean variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Boolean variable** blocks are used to report a **true** or **false** value stored inside of the variable. Use the **set boolean variable** block to set or update the value of a boolean variable.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/iq/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nThe **boolean variable** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nBoolean variables are created using the **Make a Boolean** button.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_button.png)  \n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of a **boolean** block, select the checkbox next to its reporter block.\n\n![boolean_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the **boolean** reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![boolean_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_monitor.png)"},"brain_button_pressed":{"name":"brain_button_pressed","markdown":"# Brain button pressed\n\nReports if a button on the VEX IQ Brain is pressed.\n\n![button_pressed_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Brain button pressed** reports **true** if the selected Brain button is pressed.\n\n**Brain button pressed** reports **false** if the selected Brain button is not pressed.\n\n\nChoose which Brain button to use on the VEX IQ (1st generation) Brain.\n\n![button_pressed_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_options.png)\n\nOr choose which Brain button to use on the VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain.\n\n![brain_pressed_options2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brain_button_pressed/brain_pressed_options2.png)\n\nThe **brain button pressed** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the robot drive forward and turn right after the Brain **Up** button is pressed.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_example_revised.png)\n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Break\n\nExits a repeating loop immediately.\n\n![break](static/help/iq/blocks/en/break/break.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen added to repeating 'C' block, the **break** block will exit the loop it is currently in. \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will move the Drivetrain forward and check if the VEX IQ (1st generation) Brain’s **up** button is pressed. \n\nIf the **up** button is **pressed**, the **break** block will exit the repeat forever loop and stop the Drivetrain.\n\n![break_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Brightness of\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Brightness of** reports a range from **0% to 100%**.\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to use.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nThe reporter block **brightness of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"brightness_of_virtual":{"name":"brightness_of_virtual","markdown":"# Brightness of\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brightness_of_virtual/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Brightness of** reports a range from **0% to 100%**.\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to use.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brightness_of_virtual/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Brightness of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brightness_of_virtual/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Brightness of** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![brightness_of_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brightness_of_virtual/brightness_of_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![brightness_of_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/brightness_of_virtual/brightness_of_monitor.png)"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Broadcast\n\nBroadcasts a message to activate any stacks that begin with a **when I receive** block listening for the broadcasted message.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/en/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe stack that sends the **broadcast** will continue to run blocks at the same time as other stacks that receive the broadcasted message.\n\nChoose which message to **broadcast**. A new message can also be created.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will display red on the VEX IQ Touch LED and then wait two seconds before broadcasting \"message1\". \n\nOnce the messaged is received, the **when I receive** stack will cause the Drivetrain will move forward while the ClawMotor will move upwards at the same time. \n\nThe two stacks will continue to run at the same time as indicated by the red arrows.\n\n![broadcast_example_arrows](static/help/iq/blocks/en/broadcast/broadcast_example_arrows.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Broadcast and wait\n\nBroadcasts a message to activate any stacks that begin with a **when I receive** block listening for the broadcasted message while also pausing the rest of the stack.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe stack that sends the **broadcast and wait** will pause until the other stacks that receive the broadcasted message have completed.\n\nChoose which message to **broadcast**. A new message can also be created.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/iq/blocks/en/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will display red on the VEX IQ Touch LED and then wait two seconds before broadcasting \"message1\". \n\nOnce the messaged is received, the **when I receive** stack will cause the Drivetrain will move forward and play a sound effect.\n\nThe broadcasting stack will wait until the receiving stack is completed before continuing to run blocks as indicated by the red arrows.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows_3](static/help/iq/blocks/en/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows3.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Calibrate gyro\n\nCalibrating the VEX IQ Gyro Sensor is used to reduce the amount drift generated by Gyro Sensor.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nDrifting occurs when the Gyro Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Gyro Sensor must remain still during the calibration process.\n\nChoose which Gyro Sensor to use.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/en/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nChoose how long to calibrate. The longer the Gyro Sensor calibrates, the less drifting will occur.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_seconds](static/help/iq/blocks/en/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_seconds.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Change variable\n\nChanges a variable by the given value.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which variable to use - the selected variable can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nThe **Change variable** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/iq/blocks/en/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will increase the variable that sets the drive velocity by 10 each time the **repeat loop** loops.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows_new":{"name":"clear_all_rows_new","markdown":"# Clear all rows\n\nClears the entire VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_all_rows_new/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Clear all rows** will not reset the Brain's screen cursor. Use the **set cursor** block to reset the Brain's screen cursor back the desired position.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Hello\" for one second and then clear the entire screen before printing \"Goodbye\".\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_all_rows_new/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"clear_all_rows_new_console":{"name":"clear_all_rows_new_console","markdown":"# Clear all rows\n\nClears the entire Print Console or VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_all_rows_new_console/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Clear all rows** will not reset the Brain's screen cursor. Use the **set cursor** block to reset the Brain's screen cursor back the desired position.\n\nHowever, using the **clear all rows** block with the Console option selected will reset the cursor to the top of the Print Console window.\n\nChoose whether to clear the Brain's screen or the Print Console.\n\n![clear_all_rows_dropdown](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_all_rows_new_console/clear_all_rows_dropdown.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Hello\" for one second and then clear the entire screen before printing \"Goodbye\".\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_all_rows_new_console/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"clear_all_rows_virtual":{"name":"clear_all_rows_virtual","markdown":"# Clear all rows\n\nClears all the rows in the Print Console.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_all_rows_virtual/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nUse the **clear all rows** block to remove all of the lines in the Print Console.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Hello\" for one second and then clear the entire display before printing \"Goodbye\".\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_all_rows_virtual/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"clear_row_new":{"name":"clear_row_new","markdown":"# Clear row\n\nClears a single row on the VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_row_new/clear_row.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe **Clear row** block can accept integers or numeric blocks between **1 - 5** to set which row to clear.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_row_new/row_column_index.png)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\nThe **Clear row** block can accept integers or numeric blocks between **1 to 9** to set which row to clear, depending on what font is currently selected.\n\n![row_column_index2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_row_new/iq2_row_column_brain2.jpg) \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"VEXcode\" at row 2 column 1 for three seconds before clearing row 2.\n\n![clear_row_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/clear_row_new/clear_row_example.png)"},"color_detects_color":{"name":"color_detects_color","markdown":"# Color detects\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Color Sensor detects a specific color.\n\n![color_detects](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color/color_detects.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Color detects** reports **true** when the Color Sensor detects the selected color.\n\n**Color detects** reports **false** when the Color Sensor detects a different color than the one selected.\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to use.\n\n![color_detects_chosen](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color/color_detects_chosen.png)\n\nChoose which color to detect.\n\n![color_detects_selected](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color/color_detects_selected.png)\n\nThe **color detects** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![color_detects_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color/color_detects_shape.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Color Red\" or \"Other Color\" depending on whether or not the Color Sensor detects the color \"red\".\n\n![color_detects_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color/color_detects_example.png)\n\n"},"color_detects_color_virtual":{"name":"color_detects_color_virtual","markdown":"# Color detects\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Color Sensor detects a specific color.\n\n![color_detects](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color_virtual/color_detects.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Color detects** reports **true** when the Color Sensor detects the selected color.\n\n**Color detects** reports **false** when the Color Sensor detects a different color than the one selected.\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to use.\n\n![color_detects_chosen](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color_virtual/color_detects_chosen.png)\n\nChoose which color to detect.\n\n![color_detects_selected](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color_virtual/color_detects_selected.png)\n\nThe **Color detects** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![color_detects_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color_virtual/color_detects_shape.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Color Red\" or \"Other Color\" depending on whether or not the Color Sensor detects the color \"red\".\n\n![color_detects_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color_virtual/color_detects_example.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Color detects** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![color_detects_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color_virtual/color_detects_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![color_detects_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_detects_color_virtual/color_detects_monitor.png)"},"color_of":{"name":"color_of","markdown":"# Color of\n\nReports the name of the color detected by the VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_of/color_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Color of** reports one the following colors: **red, red-violet, violet, blue-violet, blue, blue-green, green, yellow-green, yellow, yellow-orange, orange, or red-orange.**\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to use.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_of/color_of_color.png)\n\nThe reporter block **color of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![color_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_of/color_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"color_of_virtual":{"name":"color_of_virtual","markdown":"# Color of\n\nReports the name of the color detected by the VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_of_virtual/color_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Color of** reports one the following colors: **red, red-violet, violet, blue-violet, blue, blue-green, green, yellow-green, yellow, yellow-orange, orange, or red-orange.**\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to use.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_of_virtual/color_of_color.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Color of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![color_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_of_virtual/color_of_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Color of** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![color_of_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_of_virtual/color_of_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![color_of_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/color_of_virtual/color_of_monitor.png)\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Comment\n\nAllows programmers to write information to help describe their program. \n\n![comment_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nProfessional programmers use comments throughout their programs to help others understand their code. Comments can also help with troubleshooting and collaboration. \n\nAdd text into the **Comment** block by first selecting the transparent square and delete any existing text. Then, type in the new text.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/en/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Example\n\nComments do not change the program or blocks surrounding it.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Controller enable/disable\n\nEnables or disables Controller configured actions from the Devices menu.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose to either enable or disable the configured Controller actions by selecting the desired state from the dropdown. By default, the Controller is Enabled in every project.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThe configured action in this example is using the robot's Drivetrain behavior set by the Controller's configuration in the Devices window.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/blocks/en/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nThis example will have the configured Controller disabled when the program starts. \n\nThen, the robot will drive forward for 6 inches.\n\nFinally, the **controller enabled** block will enable the Controller to restore Controller driving behaviors.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Current of motor\n\nReports the amount of power a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently using in amperes (amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Current of motor** reports a range from **0.0 to 1.2 amps**. \n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nThe reporter block **current of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Cursor column\n\nReports the column number of the VEX IQ Brain screen cursor's location.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n**Cursor column** reports a range from **1 to 21**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/en/cursor_column/row_column_index.png)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\n**Cursor column** reports a range from **1 to 28**, depending on the font that is currently being used.\n\n![row_column_index2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/cursor_column/iq2_row_column_brain2.jpg)    \n\nThe **set cursor** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.  \n\nThe reporter block **cursor column** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will check if the **cursor column** position is greater than 15. If the position is greater than 15, the project will set the cursor to row 1, column 1, and then print ‘Hello’.\n\n![cursor_column_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/en/cursor_column/cursor_column_example_simple.png)\n\n"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Cursor row\n\nReports the row number of the VEX IQ Brain screen cursor's location.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n**Cursor row** reports a range from **1 to 5**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/en/cursor_row/row_column_index.png)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\n**Cursor row** reports a range from **1 to 9**, depending on the font that is currently being used.\n\n![iq2_row_column_brain2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/cursor_row/iq2_row_column_brain2.jpg)\n\nThe reporter block **cursor row** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will check if the **cursor row** position is greater than 4. If the position is greater than 4, the project will set the cursor to row 1, column 1, and then print ‘Hello’.\n\n![cursor_row_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/en/cursor_row/cursor_row_example_simple.png)"},"distance_found_object":{"name":"distance_found_object","markdown":"# Distance object found\n\nReports if the Distance sensor sees an object within its field of view.\n\n![distance_found_object_block1](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block1.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Distance object found** reports true when the Distance sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n**Distance object found** reports false when the Distance sensor does not detect an object or surface.\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_found_object_block2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block2.png)\n\n\nThe **distance object found** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![distance_found_object_block3](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block3.png)\n"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Distance from\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the VEX IQ Distance Sensor.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Distance from** reports a range from **24mm to 1000mm** or **1 inch to 40 inches**.\n\nChoose which Distance Sensor to use.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nChoose whether **distance from** is reported in inches or millimeters. \n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **distance from** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"distance_from_virtual":{"name":"distance_from_virtual","markdown":"# Distance from\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the VEX IQ Distance Sensor.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_from_virtual/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Distance from** reports a range from **24mm to 1000mm** or **1 inch to 40 inches**.\n\nChoose which Distance Sensor to use.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_from_virtual/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nChoose whether **Distance from** is reported in inches or millimeters. \n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_from_virtual/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Distance from** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_from_virtual/distance_from_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Distance from** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![distance_from_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_from_virtual/distance_from_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![distance_from_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_from_virtual/distance_from_monitor.png)"},"distance_object_distance":{"name":"distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Object distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the Distance sensor.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object distance** reports a range from **20mm to 2000mm**.\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether **object distance** is reported in inches or millimeters. \n\n![distance_object_distance_block3](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block **object distance** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block4](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block4.png)\n"},"distance_object_size":{"name":"distance_object_size","markdown":"# Object size is\n\nReports if the Distance Sensor detects the specified object size.  \n\n![distance_object_size_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe sensor determines the size of the object detected (small, medium, large) based on the amount of light reflected and returned to the sensor.\n\nChoose a Distance Sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_size_block1](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block1.png)\n\nChoose which size of the object you want the sensor to check for.\n\n![distance_object_size_block2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block2.png)\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **true** when the Distance Sensor detects the specified size.\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **false** if it doesn't detect the specified size.\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![distance_object_size_block3](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block3.png)\n"},"distance_object_velocity":{"name":"distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Object velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of an object in m/s.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object velocity** reports the current velocity of an object in m/s (meters per second).\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block2.png)\n\n\nThe reporter block **object velocity** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block3](static/help/iq/blocks/en/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block3.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Divide\n\nDivides the first value by the second value and reports the dividend.\n\n![divide](static/help/iq/blocks/en/divide/divide.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Divide** can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe length of the **divide** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\nEnter numbers to be divided.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/en/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nDivide with values of variables.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/en/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nDivide with values from sensors or devices.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/en/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"draw_circle":{"name":"draw_circle","markdown":"# Draw circle\n\nDraws a circle on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n![draw_circle](static/help/iq/blocks/en/draw_circle/draw_circle.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **draw circle** block requires 3 values:\n\n* Value 1: Center Point X\n* Value 2: Center Point Y\n* Value 3: Radius of Circle (in pixels)\n\nThe outside line color of the circle is determined by the **set pen color** block. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the circle is determined by the **set fill color** block. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/blocks/en/draw_circle/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"draw_line":{"name":"draw_line","markdown":"# Draw line\n\nDraws a line on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n![draw_line](static/help/iq/blocks/en/draw_line/draw_line.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **draw line** block requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Beginning X coordinate\n* Value 2: Beginning Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Ending X coordinate\n* Value 4: Ending Y coordinate\n\nThe line color is determined by the **set pen color** block. The default line color is white.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/blocks/en/draw_line/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_pixel":{"name":"draw_pixel","markdown":"# Draw pixel\n\nDraws a pixel on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n![draw_pixel](static/help/iq/blocks/en/draw_pixel/draw_pixel.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **draw pixel** block requires 2 values:\n\n* Value 1: X Coordinate\n* Value 2: Y Coordinate\n\nThe pixel color is determined by the **set pen color** block. The default pixel color is white.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/blocks/en/draw_pixel/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_rectangle":{"name":"draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Draw rectangle\n\nDraws a rectangle on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n![draw_rectangle](static/help/iq/blocks/en/draw_rectangle/draw_rectangle.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **draw rectangle** block requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Top Left Corner X coordinate\n* Value 2: Top Left Corner Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Width of the rectangle\n* Value 4: Height of the rectangle\n\nThe outside line color of the rectangle is determined by the **set pen color** block. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the rectangle is determined by the **set fill color** block. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/blocks/en/draw_rectangle/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Drive\n\nMoves the Drivetrain forever.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **drive** block will run the Drivetrain forever until a new Drivetrain block is used or the program is stopped.\n\nChoose the direction the Drivetrain will move.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Drive current\n\nReports the amount of current the Drivetrain is currently using.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive current** reports a range from **0.0 to 1.2 amps**. \n\nThe reporter block **drive current** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Drive for\n\nMoves the Drivetrain for a given distance.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which direction the Drivetrain will move.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\nThe **Drive for** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nSet how far the Drivetrain will move by entering a value and choosing the unit of measurement (inches or millimeters).\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Drivetrain is done moving.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Drivetrain moves.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Drive heading\n\nReports the heading that the Drivetrain is facing.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive heading** reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**.\n\n### VEX IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe **drive heading** block reports a counter-clockwise heading as shown in the image below.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_heading/TopDownBot01.png)\n\n### VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe **drive heading** block reports a counter-clockwise or clockwise heading depending on whether the intergrated brain inertial or a gyro sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the integrated inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\n![drive_heading_clockwise](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_heading/drive_heading_clockwise.png)\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\n![drive_heading_counterclockwise](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_heading/drive_heading_counterclockwise.png)\n\nThe reporter block **drive heading** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_heading_virtual":{"name":"drive_heading_virtual","markdown":"# Drive heading\n\nReports the direction that the Drivetrain is facing.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_heading_virtual/drive_heading.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive heading** reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**.\n\nThe **Drive heading** reports a counter-clockwise heading as shown in the image below.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_heading_virtual/TopDownBot01.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Drive heading** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_heading_virtual/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Drive heading** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![drive_heading_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_heading_virtual/drive_heading_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![drive_heading_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_heading_virtual/drive_heading_monitor.png)"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Drive is done\n\nReports if the Drivetrain has completed its movement.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive is done** reports **true** when the Drivetrain's motors have completed their movement.\n\n**Drive is done** reports **false** when the Drivetrain's motors are still moving.\n\nThe **drive is done** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done_virtual":{"name":"drive_is_done_virtual","markdown":"# Drive is done\n\nReports if the Drivetrain has completed its movement.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_done_virtual/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive is done** reports **true** when the Drivetrain's motors have completed their movement.\n\n**Drive is done** reports **false** when the Drivetrain's motors are still moving.\n\nThe **Drive is done** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_done_virtual/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Drive is done** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![drive_is_done_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_done_virtual/drive_is_done_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![drive_is_done_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_done_virtual/drive_is_done_monitor.png)"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Drive is moving\n\nReports if the Drivetrain is currently moving.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive is moving** reports **true** when the Drivetrain's motors are moving.\n\n**Drive is moving** reports **false** when the Drivetrain's motors are stopped.\n\nThe **drive is moving** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving_virtual":{"name":"drive_is_moving_virtual","markdown":"# Drive is moving\n\nReports if the Drivetrain is currently moving.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_moving_virtual/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive is moving** reports **true** when the Drivetrain's motors are moving.\n\n**Drive is moving** reports **false** when the Drivetrain's motors are stopped.\n\nThe **Drive is moving** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_moving_virtual/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Drive is moving** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![drive_is_moving_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_moving_virtual/drive_is_moving_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![drive_is_moving_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_is_moving_virtual/drive_is_moving_monitor.png)"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Drive rotation\n\nReports the Drivetrain's angle of rotation in degrees when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro or Brain Inertial Sensor.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### VEX IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\n**Drive rotation** reports a **positive** value when the Drivetrain turns in a **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n**Drive rotation** reports a **negative** value when the Drivetrain turns in a **clockwise** direction.\n\n### VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe **drive rotation** block can report a counter-clockwise or clockwise rotation depending on whether the intergrated brain inertial or a gyro sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the integrated inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\nThe reporter block **drive rotation** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_rotation_virtual":{"name":"drive_rotation_virtual","markdown":"# Drive rotation\n\nReports the Drivetrain's angle of rotation in degrees when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_rotation_virtual/iq_drive_rotation_reporter.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive rotation** reports a **positive** value when the Drivetrain turns in a **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n**Drive rotation** reports a **negative** value when the Drivetrain turns in a **clockwise** direction.\n\nThe reporter block **Drive rotation** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_rotation_virtual/iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Drive rotation** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![drive_rotation_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_rotation_virtual/drive_rotation_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![drive_rotation_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_rotation_virtual/drive_rotation_monitor.png)"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Drive velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\n**Drive velocity** reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-127rpm to 127rpm**\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in % or in revolutions per minute (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **drive velocity** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"drive_velocity_virtual":{"name":"drive_velocity_virtual","markdown":"# Drive velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_velocity_virtual/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\n**Drive velocity** reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-127rpm to 127rpm**\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in % or in revolutions per minute (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_velocity_virtual/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Drive velocity** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_velocity_virtual/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Drive velocity** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![drive_velocity_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_velocity_virtual/drive_velocity_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![drive_velocity_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/drive_velocity_virtual/drive_velocity_monitor.png)"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Equal to\n\nReports if the first value is the same as (equal) to the second value. \n\n![equal_to](static/help/iq/blocks/en/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Equal to** reports **true** when the two values are exactly the same.\n\n**Equal to** reports **false** when the two values are not the same.\n\nThe **equal to** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe **equal to** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Drivetrain Stalled\" on the VEX IQ Brain's screen if the Drivetrain's current is equal to 100%.\n\n![equal_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/equal_to/equal_to_example.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Forever\n\nA 'C' block that repeats any blocks contained inside forever.\n\n![forever](static/help/iq/blocks/en/forever/forever.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nPlace blocks in **forever** 'C' block to have those actions repeat **forever**.\n\nYou can exit a **forever** loop by placing a **break** block inside.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\n'C' blocks can also be put inside of each other. This concept is called nesting which can help save time when programming different behaviors.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will play the same sound effect every 5 seconds forever.\n\n![forever_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/forever/forever_example.png)"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Function\n\nPerforms a selected math function.\n\n![function](static/help/iq/blocks/en/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - absolute value\n* **floor** - rounds down to the nearest integer\n* **ceiling** - rounds up to the nearest integer\n* **sqrt** - square root\n* **sin** - sine\n* **cos** - cosine\n* **tan** - tangent\n* **asin** - arcsine or the inverse of sine\n* **acos** - arccosine or the inverse of cosine\n* **atan** - arctan or the inverse of tangent\n* **ln** - the natural logarithm base e\n* **log** - logarithm base 10\n* **e ^** - powers of e\n* **10 ^** - powers of 10\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **function** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose the math **function** from a list of options.\n\n![function_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/function/function_select.png)\n\nThe length of the **function** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\n![function_fit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Greater than\n\nReports if the first value is larger (greater) than the second value.  \n\n![greater_than](static/help/iq/blocks/en/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Greater than** reports **true** when the first value is larger than the second value. \n\n**Greater than** reports **false** when the first value is smaller than or equal to the second value.\n\nThe **greater than** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe **greater than** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Battery Charged!\" on the VEX IQ Brain's screen if the battery level is greater than 50%.\n\n![greater_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/greater_than/greater_than_example.png)\n\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Angle of heading\n\nReports the VEX IQ Gyro Sensor or IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/en/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Gyro heading** reports a range between **0.00 to 359.99**.\n\n### Gyro Sensor\n\nThe **Gyro heading** block reports a counter-clockwise-positive heading as shown in the image below.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/en/heading_of_gyro/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\n### VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor\n\nThe **Gyro heading** block reports a clockwise-positive heading when used with the Brain Inertial option.\n\n![BrainInertial](static/help/iq/blocks/en/heading_of_gyro/brain_inertial.png)\n\nChoose which Gyro Sensor to check or to check the VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/en/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nThe **Gyro heading** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"hue_of":{"name":"hue_of","markdown":"# Hue of\n\nReports the hue of the color detected by the VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/hue_of/hue_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Hue of** reports a range from **0 to 360**.\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to check.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/hue_of/hue_of_color.png)\n\nThe reporter block **hue of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![hue_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/hue_of/hue_of_inserted.png)\n"},"hue_of_virtual":{"name":"hue_of_virtual","markdown":"# Hue of\n\nReports the hue of the color detected by the VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/hue_of_virtual/hue_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Hue of** reports a range from **0 to 360**.\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to check.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/en/hue_of_virtual/hue_of_color.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Hue of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![hue_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/hue_of_virtual/hue_of_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Hue of** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![hue_of_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/hue_of_virtual/hue_of_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![hue_of_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/hue_of_virtual/hue_of_monitor.png)"},"if_elseif_else":{"name":"if_elseif_else","markdown":"# If then else if then else\n\nA 'C' Block that runs the blocks inside the first set of internal blocks in the **if then else if then else** block where the condition returns true.\n\n![if_elseif_else](static/help/iq/blocks/en/if_elseif_else/if_elseif_else.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **if then else if then else** 'C' Block will only check the Boolean condition once. \n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **true** on the **if** line, the blocks inside of **if** section will be run.\n\nIf the Boolean condition is **false**, the **if then else if then else** block will check the first of the **else if** lines. For each **else if** line, the block will check if the Boolean condition is reported as **true**. If it is **true**, the internal blocks directly under that line will run before continuing on to the next block under the **if then else if then else** block.\n\nIf all the Boolean conditions for the **else if** lines are **false**, the blocks inside of **else** section will be run.\n\nThe **if then else if then else** 'C' block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks for its conditions.\n\n![if_elseif_else_2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/if_elseif_else/if_elseif_else_2.png)\n\n## How to Add and Remove Conditions\n\nThe **if then else if then else** block is unique amongst the conditional blocks in that you can add additional conditional statements. The block allows for 6 **else if** conditions.\n\n![if_elseif_else_expanded](static/help/iq/blocks/en/if_elseif_else/if_elseif_else_expanded.png)\n\nTo add another **else if** condition, click on the \"+\" on the **else** line. This will add a new **else if** condition to the bottom of the current list.\n\nTo remove an **else if** condition, click on the \"-\" on the **else** line. This will remove the last **else if** condition line, but will not delete the blocks in the condition.\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# If then\n\nA 'C' Block that runs the blocks inside if the Boolean condition is reported to be **true**.  \n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/en/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **if then** 'C' block will only check the Boolean condition once. \n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **true**, the blocks inside of **if then** will run.\n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **false**, the blocks inside of **if then** will be skipped.\n\nThe **if then** 'C' block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks as its condition.\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/en/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will play a sound effect every time the VEX IQ Bumper Switch is pressed.\n\nThe **if then** 'C' block can be “nested” or placed inside the forever block to ensure that the sound effect plays every time instead of just once. \n\n![if_then_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/if_then/if_then_example.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# If then else\n\nA 'C' Block that runs the blocks inside the first or second parts of the **if then else** based on the Boolean value reported.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/en/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **if then else** 'C' Block will only check the Boolean condition once. \n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **true**, the blocks inside of **if** section will be run.\n\nIf the Boolean condition is **false**, the blocks inside of **else** section will be run.\n\nThe **if then else** 'C' block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks as its condition.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/en/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will be green if the VEX IQ Touch LED is pressed and will be red when the Touch LED is not pressed.\n\nThe **If then else** 'C' block can be “nested” or placed inside the forever block to ensure that the Touch LED will turn red and green more than once. \n\n![if_then_else_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/if_then_else/if_then_else_example.png)"},"inertial_acceleration":{"name":"inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Acceleration of\n\nReports the acceleration value from one of the axes (x, y, or z) of the VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n**Acceleration of** reports a range from **-4.0 to 4.0** Gs.\n\nChoose which axis to use:\n\n* The **X-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **forward to backward**\n* The **Y-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **side to side**\n* The **Z-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **up to down**\n\n![inertial_acceleration_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_axis.png)\n\nThe sensing block **acceleration of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_calibrate":{"name":"inertial_calibrate","markdown":"# Calibrate\n\nCalibrate is used to reduce the amount of incorrectly reported movement generated by the IQ (2nd generation) Brain’s built-in Inertial Sensor.\n\n![inertial_calibrate_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_calibrate/inertial_calibrate_block.png)\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor can incorrectly detect movement when the Brain is not moving.\n\n## How To Use\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor should be calibrated before using drivetrain turning blocks to allow for more accurate turns.\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor must remain still during the calibration process. The calibration process will take approximately 2 seconds to complete.\n\n![inertial_calibrate_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_calibrate/inertial_calibrate_example.png)"},"inertial_gyrorate":{"name":"inertial_gyrorate","markdown":"# Gyro rate\n\nGets the rate of rotation from one of the axes (x, y, or z) of the VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n![gyro_rate_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_gyrorate/gyro_rate_block.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\n**Gyro rate** reports a range from **-1000.0 to 1000.0** in dps (degrees per second).\n\nChoose which axis to use.\n\n* The **X-axis** reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the X-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* The **Y-axis** reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Y-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* The **Z-axis** reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Z-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n![gyroRate_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_axis.png)\n\nThe sensing block **gyro rate** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_orientation":{"name":"inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Orientation of\n\nGets an orientation angle of the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor. Reports the unit value specified by the parameter of the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n![orientation_inertial_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/orientation_inertial_block.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\nThe orientation reported is determined by the selected axis (x, y, or z).\n\n* The **X-axis** represents **pitch**, which reports a value between -90 to +90 degrees.\n* The **Y-axis** represents **roll**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n* The **Z-axis** represents **yaw**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n\n---\n\n**Pitch** is the angle of the robot tilted forwards and backwards.\n\n![IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Pitch](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Pitch.png)\n\n**Roll** is the angle of the robot tilted left and right.\n\n![IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Roll](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Roll.png)\n\n**Yaw** is angular rotation of the robot.\n\n![IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Yaw](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Yaw.png)\n\n---\n\nChoose which axis to use.\n\n![orientation_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/orientation_axis.png)\n\nThe sensing block **orientation of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![orientation_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/orientation_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n\n"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Item of 2D list\n\nReports the value of an item in a 2D list. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which 2D list to use. The 2D list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nEnter the item's row (first number) and column (second number) position within the list to be reported. Here, the item in position row 2, column 3 in the 2D list is being reported.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nThe **item of 2D list** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_2d_array_virtual":{"name":"item_of_2d_array_virtual","markdown":"# Item of 2D list\n\nReports the value of an item in a 2D list. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which 2D list to use. The 2D list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nEnter the item's row (first number) and column (second number) position within the list to be reported. Here, the item in position row 2, column 3 in the 2D list is being reported.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nThe **item of 2D list** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of a 2D list, open the Monitor Console and click the 'Add Lists' button on the bottom right corner.\n\n![array_monitor_add](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/array_monitor_add.png)\n\nThen, select the checkbox for the 2D list that should be added. Multiple checkboxes can be selected if more than one 2D list is defined. Click 'Save' to add the list(s) to the Monitor Console.\n\n![array_monitor_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/array_monitor_select.png)\n\n Return to the Monitor Console to view the 2D list(s) selected for monitoring.\n\n![array_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/array_monitor.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Item of\n\nReports the value of an item in a list. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nEnter the number of the item's position within the list. Here, the second item in list (item 2) is being reported. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nThe **item of** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the Drivetrain velocity to the value stored in item 3. The Drivetrain will now move forward at a 90% velocity.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"item_of_array_virtual":{"name":"item_of_array_virtual","markdown":"# Item of\n\nReports the value of an item in a list. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/item_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/item_of_options.png)\n\nEnter the number of the item's position within the list. Here, the second item in list (item 2) is being reported. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nThe **item of** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the Drivetrain velocity to the value stored in item 3. The Drivetrain will now move forward at a 90% velocity.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/item_of_example2.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of a list, open the Monitor Console and click the 'Add Lists' button on the bottom right corner.\n\n![array_monitor_add](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/array_monitor_add.png)\n\nThen, select the checkbox for the list that should be added. Multiple checkboxes can be selected if more than one list is defined. Click 'Save' to add the list(s) to the Monitor Console.\n\n![array_monitor_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/array_monitor_select.png)\n\nReturn to the Monitor Console to view the list(s) selected for monitoring.\n\n![array_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/array_monitor.png)"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Length of 2D list\n\nReports the number of rows or columns in a 2D list.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/en/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\nChoose which 2D list to use. The 2D list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nChoose which value to report. The 2D list can report either **rows** or **columns**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nThe **length of 2D list** reporter block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Less than\n\nReports if the first value is less (smaller) than the second value. \n\n![less_than](static/help/iq/blocks/en/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Less than** reports **true** when the first value is smaller than the second value. \n\n**Less than** reports **false** when the first value is greater than or equal to the second value.\n\nThe **less than** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\nThe **less than** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Low Battery!\" on the VEX IQ Brain's screen if the battery level is less than 25%.\n\n![less_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/less_than/less_than_example.png)\n\n"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor is done\n\nReports if the selected VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Motor is done** reports **true** when the selected Motor/Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n**Motor is done** reports **false** when the selected Motor/Motor Group is still moving.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nThe **motor is done** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\nThe block for reporting if the motor is done is used inside blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces for other blocks. \n"},"motor_is_done_virtual":{"name":"motor_is_done_virtual","markdown":"# Motor is done\n\nReports if the selected VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_done_virtual/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Motor is done** reports **true** when the selected Motor/Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n**Motor is done** reports **false** when the selected Motor/Motor Group is still moving.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_done_virtual/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nThe **Motor is done** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_done_virtual/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\nThe block for reporting if the motor is done is used inside blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces for other blocks. \n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Motor is done** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![motor_is_done_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_done_virtual/motor_is_done_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![motor_is_done_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_done_virtual/motor_is_done_monitor.png)"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor is spinning\n\nReports if the selected VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently spinning.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Motor is spinning** reports **true** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is spinning.\n\n**Motor is spinning** reports **false** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is stopped.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nThe **motor is spinning** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"motor_is_spinning_virtual":{"name":"motor_is_spinning_virtual","markdown":"# Motor is spinning\n\nReports if the selected VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently spinning.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning_virtual/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Motor is spinning** reports **true** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is spinning.\n\n**Motor is spinning** reports **false** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is stopped.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning_virtual/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nThe **Motor is spinning** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning_virtual/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Motor is spinning** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning_virtual/motor_is_spinning_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning_virtual/motor_is_spinning_monitor.png)"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Multiply\n\nMultiplies any two values together and reports the product.\n\n![multiply](static/help/iq/blocks/en/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Multiply** can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe length of the **multiply** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\nMultiply two numbers.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/en/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nMultiply with values of variables.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/en/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nMultiply with values from sensors or devices.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/en/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row_new":{"name":"next_row_new","markdown":"# Next row\n\nSets the print output on the Brain's screen to the next available row.\n\n![next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new/next_row.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1. The **next row** block will move the cursor down by a single row on the Brain's screen. \n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new/row_column_index.png)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\n![row_column_index2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new/iq2_row_column_brain2.jpg)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"First Message\" and then will set the cursor to the next available row before printing \"Second Message\".\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new/set_cursor_welcome.png)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\n![set_cursor_welcome2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new/set_cursor_welcome2.png)\n"},"next_row_new_console":{"name":"next_row_new_console","markdown":"# Next row\n\nSets the print output on the Print Console or VEX IQ Brain's screen to the next available row.\n\n![next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new_console/next_row.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1 and row 1 on the Print Console. The **next row** block will move the cursor down by a single row on the Brain's screen or Print Console.\n\nChoose whether to set the cursor to the next row on the IQ Brain's screen or the Print Console.\n\n![next_row_dropdown_with_console](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new_console/next_row_dropdown_with_console.png)\n\n---\n\nThe VEX IQ Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\n![row_column_index2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new_console/iq2_row_column_brain2.jpg)\n\n---\n\nPrinting to the Print Console requires using a **next row** block after a **print** block to output the contents of the Print Console buffer into the Print Console window.\n\n![look_print_set_cursor_console](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new_console/look_print_set_cursor_console.png)\n\nAlternatively, the **and set cursor to next row** mutator on a **print** block can also be used to output the contents of the Print Console buffer into the Print Console window.\n\n![print_expanded](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new_console/print_expanded.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"First Message\" and then will set the cursor to the next available row before printing \"Second Message\".\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new_console/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_welcome2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_new_console/set_cursor_welcome2.png)\n"},"next_row_virtual":{"name":"next_row_virtual","markdown":"# Set cursor to next row\n\nSets the cursor to a new line in the Print Console when using the **print** blocks. \n\n![set_cursor_next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_virtual/set_cursor_next_row.png)\n\n\n## How To Use\n\nUse the **set cursor to next row** block to set the cursor to a new line in the display.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Hello\" and on the next line in the display it will print \"World!\"\n\n![set_cursor_next_row_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/next_row_virtual/set_cursor_next_row_code_example.png)"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# Not\n\nReports the opposite (inverse) of the Boolean result.\n\n![not](static/help/iq/blocks/en/not/not.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **not** block reports **true** when the Boolean block inside reports **false**.\n\nThe **not** block reports **false** when the Boolean block inside reports **true**.\n\nThe **not** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will report **true** when the VEX IQ Brain's \"check\" button is not pressed. \n\n![not_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/en/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/en/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Object count\n\nReports how many objects the Vision Sensor detects. \n\nAn object will need to be configured before the  **object count** block can detect it.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Vision Sensor to use.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nThe **snapshot of** block will need to be used before the **object count** block reports a number of objects.\n\nThe **object count** block will only detect the number of objects from the last snapshot signature.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Object exists\n\nReports if the Vision Sensor detects a configured object. \n\nAn object will need to be configured before the **object exists** block can detect it.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Vision Sensor to use.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n**Object exists** reports **true** when the Vision Sensor detects a configured object.\n\n**Object exists** reports **false** when the Vision Sensor does not detect a configured object.\n\nThe **object exists** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nThe **snapshot of** block will need to be used before the **object exists** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Object found\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Distance Sensor sees an object within its field of view. \n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object found** reports **true** when the Distance Sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n**Object found** reports **false** when the Distance Sensor does not detect an object or surface.\n\nChoose which Distance Sensor to use.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nThe **object found** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"object_in_front_virtual":{"name":"object_in_front_virtual","markdown":"# Object found\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Distance Sensor sees an object within its field of view. \n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_in_front_virtual/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object found** reports **true** when the Distance Sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n**Object found** reports **false** when the Distance Sensor does not detect an object or surface.\n\nChoose which Distance Sensor to use.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_in_front_virtual/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nThe **Object found** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_in_front_virtual/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n \n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Object found** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![object_in_front_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_in_front_virtual/object_in_front_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![object_in_front_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_in_front_virtual/object_in_front_monitor.png)"},"object_is_near":{"name":"object_is_near","markdown":"# Found an object\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Color Sensor detects an object.\n\n![object_is_near](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_is_near/object_is_near_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Found an object** reports **true** when the Color Sensor detects an object or surface close to the front of the sensor.\n\n**Found an object** reports **false** when the Color Sensor does not detect an object or surface close to the front of the sensor.\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to use.\n\n![object_is_near_color](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_is_near/object_is_near_color.png)\n\nThe **found an object** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![object_is_near_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_is_near/object_is_near_inserted.png)\n\n\n "},"object_is_near_virtual":{"name":"object_is_near_virtual","markdown":"# Object is near\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Color Sensor detects an object nearby.\n\n![object_is_near](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_is_near_virtual/object_is_near_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object is near** reports **true** when the Color Sensor detects an object or surface close to the front of the sensor.\n\n**Object is near** reports **false** when the Color Sensor detects empty space in front of the sensor.\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to use.\n\n![object_is_near_color](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_is_near_virtual/object_is_near_color.png)\n\nThe **Object is near** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![object_is_near_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_is_near_virtual/object_is_near_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Object is near** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![object_is_near_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_is_near_virtual/object_is_near_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![object_is_near_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/object_is_near_virtual/object_is_near_monitor.png)\n "},"optical_brightness":{"name":"optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_brightness](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_brightness/optical_brightness.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_brightness_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical brightness** block reports a number value from **0%** to **100%**.\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.\n\nThe **Optical brightness** block reports number values and is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_brightness_use](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_use.png)\n"},"optical_color":{"name":"optical_color","markdown":"# Color name\n\nReports the name of the color detected by the VEX IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_color_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_color/optical_color_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Color name** reports one the following colors: **red, green, blue, yellow, orange, purple, or cyan.**\n\nChoose which Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_color_block_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_color/optical_color_block_options.png)\n\nThe reporter block **color name** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_color_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_color/optical_color_block_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"optical_detect":{"name":"optical_detect","markdown":"# Optical detects color\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects the specified color.\n\n![optical_detect](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect/optical_detect.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_detect_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect/optical_detect_device.png)\n\nChoose which color you want the sensor to check for.\n\n![optical_detect_colors](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect/optical_detect_colors.png)\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **true** when the Optical Sensor detects the specified color.\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **false** if it doesn't detect the specified color.\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![optical_detect_use](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect/optical_detect_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect_gesture":{"name":"optical_detect_gesture","markdown":"# When Optical detects a gesture \n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the Optical sensor detects a gesture.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBefore using the **When Optical detects a gesture** event, the **Optical set mode** block must be used to set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures.\n\n![optical_set_mode_gesture_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect_gesture/optical_set_mode_gesture_block.png)\n\nThe **When Optical detects a gesture** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on gestures that the Optical Sensor detects.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_detects_gesture_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detects_gesture_device.png)\n\nChoose which gesture triggers the **When Optical detects a gesture** event.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block2.png)"},"optical_detect_object":{"name":"optical_detect_object","markdown":"# When Optical detects/loses \n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the Optical sensor detects or loses an object.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **When Optical detects/loses** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on whether the Optical Sensor **detects** an object in range of the sensor or **loses** an object that was in range of the sensor.\n\nChoose an optical sensor.\n\n![optical_detect_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_device.png)\n\nChoose whether the **When Optical detects/loses** event is triggered when the sensor **detects** an object, or **loses** an object.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block2.png)"},"optical_found_object":{"name":"optical_found_object","markdown":"# Optical found object\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\n\n![optical_found_object](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_found_object/optical_found_object.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_found_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **true** when the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **false** if an object is not within range.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block should be used to check if an object is close to the Optical Sensor so that the color readings from the **Optical detects color** block are accurate.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![optical_found_object_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_condition.png)"},"optical_gesture_detected":{"name":"optical_gesture_detected","markdown":"# Optical gesture detected\n\nReports whether an Optical Sensor has detected the specified gesture.\n\n![optical_gesture_detected_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_gesture_detected/optical_gesture_detected_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Optical gesture detected** block reports whether a gesture has been detected.\n\nBefore using the **Optical gesture detected** block, the Optical Sensor needs to be set to detect gestures with the **Optical set mode** block.\n\n![optical_set_mode_gesture_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_gesture_detected/optical_set_mode_gesture_block.png)\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_gesture_detected_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_gesture_detected/optical_gesture_detected_device.png)\n\nChoose which gesture to check for.\n\n![optical_gesture_detected_gestures](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_gesture_detected/optical_gesture_detected_gestures.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below waits until the Optical Sensor detects an **up** gesture before driving the robot forward.\n\n![optical_gesture_detected_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_gesture_detected/optical_gesture_detected_example.png)"},"optical_hue":{"name":"optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical hue\n\nReports the hue of the color of an object.\n\n![optical_hue](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_hue/optical_hue.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose an optical sensor.\n\n![optical_hue_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_hue/optical_hue_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical hue** block reports a number value that is the hue of the color of an object. It returns a number between **0** and **359**, which can be thought of as the location of the color on a color wheel.\n\nThe **Optical hue** block reports number values and is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_hue_use](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_hue/optical_hue_use.png)"},"optical_set_light":{"name":"optical_set_light","markdown":"# Set Optical light\n\nSets the light on the Optical Sensor to on or off.\n\n![optical_set_light](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_light/optical_set_light.png)\n\n## How To Use\nThe **Set optical light** block allows you to turn the Optical Sensor's light **on** or **off**. The light lets the sensor see objects if it is looking at an object in a dark area.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_set_light_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_device.png)\n\nChoose whether you want to set the light on the Optical Sensor to **on** or **off**.\n\n![optical_set_light_state](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_state.png)\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the **Set optical light** block is used to turn the light on. Then, if the Optical Sensor detects an object, the hue is printed to the Brain.\n\n\n![optical_set_light_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_example.png)"},"optical_set_light_power":{"name":"optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Set optical light power \n\nSet the light power of the Optical sensor\n\n![optical_set_light_power_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_light_power_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Set optical light power** block accepts a range of **0%** to **100%**. This will change the brightness of the light on the Optical Sensor. If the light is off, this block will turn the light on.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_set_power_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_device.png)\n\nThe set optical light power block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![optical_set_power_num](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_num.png)\n\n## Example\nIn this example the **Set optical light power** block is used to set the power of the light to **50%**, then  the **Set optical light** block is used to turn the light on. Then, if the Optical Sensor detects an object, the hue is printed to the Brain.\n\n![optical_set_power_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_example.png)\n"},"optical_set_mode":{"name":"optical_set_mode","markdown":"# Set Optical mode\n\nSets an Optical Sensor to either detect colors or gestures.\n\n![optical_set_mode_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_mode/optical_set_mode_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Set optical mode** block allows you to set an Optical Sensor to either detect colors or gestures.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_set_mode_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_mode/optical_set_mode_device.png)\n\nChoose whether you want to set the mode of the Optical Sensor to either detect colors or gestures.\n\n![optical_set_mode_mode](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_mode/optical_set_mode_mode.png)\n\nBy default, an Optical Sensor is set to always detect colors. Before using any Optical Sensor gesture blocks, the Optical Sensor must be set to detect gestures.\n\n![optical_set_mode_gesture_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/optical_set_mode/optical_set_mode_gesture_block.png)"},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# Or\n\nReports if one of two Boolean conditions are true.\n\n![or](static/help/iq/blocks/en/or/or.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **or** block reports **true** when one (or both) of the conditions are **true**. \n\nThe **or** block reports **false** when both of the conditions are **false**.\n\nThe **or** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\nThe **or** block reports **true** when either (or both) the VEX IQ Bumper and VEX IQ Touch LED are pressed and reports **false** only when both the Bumper and Touch LED are not pressed.\n\n![or_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/en/or/or_truth.png)"},"play_note":{"name":"play_note","markdown":"# Play note\n\nPlays the selected musical note.\n\n![play_note](static/help/iq/blocks/en/play_note/play_note.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose a musical note.\n\n![play_note_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/play_note/play_note_select.png)\n\nSelect how long (duration) the note will play.\n\n![play_note_duration](static/help/iq/blocks/en/play_note/play_note_duration.png)\n\n* A **whole** note plays for 1 second (1000 milliseconds)\n* A **half** note plays for 0.5 seconds (500 milliseconds)\n* A **quarter** note plays for 0.25 seconds (250 milliseconds)\n\nOnce a musical note starts playing, the next block will begin immediately."},"play_sound":{"name":"play_sound","markdown":"# Play sound\n\nPlays the sound effect that is selected.\n\n![play_sound](static/help/iq/blocks/en/play_sound/play_sound.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose the sound effect from a list of options. \n\n![play_sound_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/play_sound/play_sound_select.png)\n\nOnce a sound effect starts playing, the next block will begin immediately."},"pneumatics_compressor":{"name":"pneumatics_compressor","markdown":"# Set pneumatic pump\n\nSets the pneumatic solenoid to turn the pneumatic pump on or off.\n\n![set_pump](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pneumatics_compressor/set_pump.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set pneumatic pump** block will control the power to the pump connected to the pneumatic solenoid. Turning the pump on will begin to refill the attached air tank.\n\nChoose which pneumatic solenoid to control.\n\n![set_controller](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pneumatics_compressor/set_controller.png)\n\nChoose to turn the pump on or off.\n\n![set_pump_option](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pneumatics_compressor/set_pump_option.png) "},"pneumatics_cylinder":{"name":"pneumatics_cylinder","markdown":"# Set pneumatic cylinder\n\nSets the pneumatic solenoid to extend or retract the selected cylinder.\n\n![set_cylinder](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pneumatics_cylinder/set_cylinder.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set pneumatic cylinder** block will control the solenoid to set the airflow within the pneumatic system to extend or retract the selected cylinder's piston.\n\nChoose which pneumatic solenoid to control.\n\n![select_controller](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pneumatics_cylinder/select_controller.png)\n\nChoose which cylinder connected to the pneumatic to control.\n\n![select_cylinder](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pneumatics_cylinder/select_cylinder.png)\n\nChoose how to control the cylinder - to either extend or retract the piston.\n\n![select_extend](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pneumatics_cylinder/select_extend.png)\n"},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Position of controller\n\nReports the position of a joystick on the controller along an axis.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of controller** reports a range between **-100 to 100**.\n\n**Position of controller** will report zero (0) when a joystick axis is centered.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nChoose the joystick's axis to check its position.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nThe **position of controller** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will repeatedly check the controller's D joystick axis to control the velocity of the arm motor.\n\n![position_of_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Position of motor\n\nReports the distance a VEX IQ Smart Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group has traveled.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of motor** reports the position of a Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group in integer numbers for degrees and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nChoose whether the value is reported in degrees rotated or in turns. \n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **position of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"position_of_motor_virtual":{"name":"position_of_motor_virtual","markdown":"# Position of motor\n\nReports the distance a VEX IQ Smart Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group has traveled.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of motor** reports the position of a Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group in integer numbers for degrees and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nChoose whether the value is reported in degrees rotated or in turns. \n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Position of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Position of motor** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![position_of_motor_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![position_of_motor_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_monitor.png)"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Pressing bumper\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Bumper Switch is pressed.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Pressing bumper** reports **true** if the Bumper Switch is being pressed.\n\n**Pressing bumper** reports **false** if the Bumper Switch is not pressed.\n\nChoose which Bumper Switch to use.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nThe **pressing bumper** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_bumper_virtual":{"name":"pressing_bumper_virtual","markdown":"# Pressing bumper\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Bumper Switch is pressed.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_bumper_virtual/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Pressing bumper** reports **true** if the Bumper Switch is being pressed.\n\n**Pressing bumper** reports **false** if the Bumper Switch is not pressed.\n\nChoose which Bumper Switch to use.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_bumper_virtual/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nThe **Pressing bumper** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_bumper_virtual/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Pressing bumper** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![pressing_bumper_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_bumper_virtual/pressing_bumper_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![pressing_bumper_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_bumper_virtual/pressing_bumper_monitor.png)"},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Pressing controller\n\nReports if a button on the VEX IQ Controller is pressed.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Pressing controller** reports **true** if the selected Controller button is being pressed.\n\n**Pressing controller** reports **false** if the selected Controller button is not pressed.\n\nChoose which Controller button to use.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nThe **pressing controller** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will checks if the E Up button is pressed and spins the claw motor forward if it is. \n\n![pressing_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_example_revised.png)"},"pressing_touchled":{"name":"pressing_touchled","markdown":"# Pressing Touch LED\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Touch LED is pressed.\n\n![pressing_touch_led](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Pressing Touch LED** reports **true** if the selected Touch LED is being pressed.\n\n**Pressing Touch LED** reports **false** if the selected Touch LED is not pressed.\n\nChoose which Touch LED to use.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_led](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_led.png)\n\nThe **pressing Touch LED** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_inserted.png)\n\n"},"print_new":{"name":"print_new","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text on the VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new/look_print.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **print** block will print data at the cursor location on the Brain's screen.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1, column 1.\n\nAll reporter blocks will be printed as integer (whole) numbers by default. Use the **set print precision** block to adjust the number of decimal places printed.\n\nBy default, the cursor will remain on the same row after printing for any subsequent print commands.\n\nTo set the cursor on the device to the next row after printing, you can select the arrow to expand **and set cursor to next row** - this will move the cursor to the next row after printing the statement.\n\n![print_expanded](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new/print_expanded.png)\n\nPrint words and numbers.\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new/print_words.png)\n\nPrint the reported value from a variable.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new/print_variable1.png)  \n\nPrint the reported calculation of an operator.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new/print_addition.png)  \n\nPrint the reported value from a sensor or device.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"print_new_console":{"name":"print_new_console","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text on the Print Console or VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new_console/look_print.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **print** block will print data at the cursor location on the Brain's screen or on the Print Console.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1, and at row 1 on the Print Console.\n\nAll reporter blocks will be printed as integer (whole) numbers by default. Use the **set print precision** block to adjust the number of decimal places printed.\n\nChoose whether to print to the Brain or the Print Console.\n\n![looks_print_dropdown_with_console](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new_console/looks_print_dropdown_with_console.png)\n\nFor adding values to the Print Console buffer, only the **print** block is needed.\n\n![look_print_dropdown_console](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new_console/look_print_dropdown_console.png)\n\nHowever, to output the values from the Print Console buffer onto the Print Console, a **set cursor to next row** block is needed. The blocks below will print \"VEXcode\" to the Print Console and set the cursor to the next row.\n\n![look_print_set_cursor_console](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new_console/look_print_set_cursor_console.png)\n\nBy default, the cursor will remain on the same row after printing for any subsequent print commands.\n\nTo set the cursor on the device to the next row after printing, you can select the arrow to expand **and set cursor to next row** - this will move the cursor to the next row after printing the statement.\n\n![print_expanded](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new_console/print_expanded.png)\n\n---\n\nPrint words and numbers.\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new_console/print_words.png)\n\nPrint the reported value from a variable.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new_console/print_variable1.png)  \n\nPrint the reported calculation of an operator.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new_console/print_addition.png)  \n\nPrint the reported value from a sensor or device.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_new_console/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"print_virtual":{"name":"print_virtual","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text in the Print Console.\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_virtual/look_print.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **print** block will print data within the Monitor Window tab\n\n![monitor_tab_icon](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_virtual/monitor_tab_icon.png)\n\nAll reporter blocks will be printed as integer (whole) numbers by default. Use the **set print precision** block to adjust the number of decimal places printed.\n\nPrint words and numbers.\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_virtual/print_words.png)\n\nPrint the reported value from a variable.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_virtual/print_variable1.png)  \n\nPrint the reported calculation of an operator.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_virtual/print_addition.png)  \n\nPrint the reported value from a sensor or device.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/print_virtual/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# My block\n\nMy Blocks are used to create custom blocks.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**My blocks** are used to create a sequence of blocks that can be used multiple times throughout a project. \n\n**My blocks** are made using the **Make a Block** button.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**My blocks** can have multiple parameters - text labels, numberic variables, and boolean variables - to add more functionality to your custom block.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nTo use a **my block**, attach the calling **my block** to a hat block. When the **my block** is reached in your prject, the stack inside of the **my block** will run using the parameter values specified.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nAttach a stack of blocks to the **my blocks** \"define\" hat block to set the action that occur when a **my block** is used.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Note: Creating multiple My Blocks with the same labels and variables may cause errors when downloading your project.***\n\n## Example 1\n\nIn this example, the robot will use **my blocks** to:\n\n* Play the siren sound 3 times.\n* Drive forward for 12 inches.\n* Play the siren sound 3 times.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_call/sound_example.png)\n\n## Example 2\n\nIn this example, the robot will use **my blocks** to:\n\n* Drive forward for 15 inches\n* Prints the battery capacity and also move the cursor to a new line on the Brain's screen\n* Turns the robot 180 degrees to the right\n* Prints the battery capacity and also move the cursor to a new line on the Brain's screen\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# My block\n\nMy Blocks are used to create custom blocks.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**My blocks** are used to create a sequence of blocks that can be used multiple times throughout a project. \n\n**My blocks** are made using the **Make a Block** button.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**My blocks** can have multiple parameters - text labels, numberic variables, and boolean variables - to add more functionality to your custom block.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nTo use a **my block**, attach the calling **my block** to a hat block. When the **my block** is reached in your prject, the stack inside of the **my block** will run using the parameter values specified.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nAttach a stack of blocks to the **my blocks** \"define\" hat block to set the action that occur when a **my block** is used.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Note: Creating multiple My Blocks with the same labels and variables may cause errors when downloading your project.***\n\n## Example 1\n\nIn this example, the robot will use **my blocks** to:\n\n* Play the siren sound 3 times.\n* Drive forward for 12 inches.\n* Play the siren sound 3 times.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_definition/sound_example.png)\n\n## Example 2\n\nIn this example, the robot will use **my blocks** to:\n\n* Drive forward for 15 inches\n* Prints the battery capacity and also move the cursor to a new line on the Brain's screen\n* Turns the robot 180 degrees to the right\n* Prints the battery capacity and also move the cursor to a new line on the Brain's screen\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/en/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Random\n![random](static/help/iq/blocks/en/random/random.png)\n\nReports a random value between the lowest and highest values in the block.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe length of the **random** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\nThe **random** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThis example uses a **random** block to randomize the drivetrain's velocity.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/iq/blocks/en/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nThis example uses a **random** block to randomize the length of a wait block.\n\n![random_control](static/help/iq/blocks/en/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"rate_of_gyro":{"name":"rate_of_gyro","markdown":"# Rate of gyro\n\nReports the VEX IQ Gyro Sensor's rate of angular velocity.\n\n![rate_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/en/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Rate of gyro** reports a range between **0 to 249.99 dps**.\n\n**Rate of gyro** reports values in degrees per second (dps).\n\nChoose which Gyro Sensor to use.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/en/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nThe **rate of gyro** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_inserted.png)"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Remainder\n\nDivides the first value by the second value and reports the remainder.\n\n![remainder](static/help/iq/blocks/en/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **remainder** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nNumbers that divide evenly will report a remainder of zero.\n\nThe length of the **remainder** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will divide 7 and 2 and report the remainder to print \"1\" on the VEX IQ Brain screen.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/en/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Repeat\n\nA 'C' block that repeats the blocks contained inside for a set number of times.\n\n![repeat](static/help/iq/blocks/en/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nFirst enter a value to indicate how many times the stack will **repeat** the blocks contained inside.\n \nThe **repeat** 'C' block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n'C' blocks can also be put inside of each other. This concept is called nesting which can help save time when programming different behaviors.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/repeat/repeat_select.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will repeat playing a sound effect every 3 seconds for 5 times.\n\n![repeat_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/repeat/repeat_example.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Repeat until\n\nA 'C' block that repeats the blocks inside until the Boolean condition is reported to be **true**.  \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/en/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **repeat until** block will only check the Boolean condition at the beginning of each loop. \n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **false**, the blocks inside of **repeat until** will run.\n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **true**, the blocks inside of **repeat until** will be skipped.\n\nThe **repeat until** 'C' block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks as its condition.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/en/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print the value of the timer to the VEX IQ Brain screen and move the Drivetrain forward until the **check** button is pressed on the VEX IQ Brain. Once the **check** button is pressed, the Drivetrain will stop.\n\n![repeat_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/repeat_until/repeat_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Reset timer\n\nResets the VEX IQ Brain's timer.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/iq/blocks/en/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Brain's timer begins at the beginning of each project. The **reset timer** block is used to reset the timer back to 0 seconds.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the timer will be reset before moving the Drivetrain forward for 3 seconds. After 3 seconds has elapsed, the Drivetrain will stop.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Angle of rotation\n\nReports the VEX IQ Gyro Sensor or IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation.png](static/help/iq/blocks/en/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### Gyro Sensor\n\n**Gyro rotation** reports an increasingly **positive** value when a Gyro Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n**Gyro rotation** reports an increasingly **negative** value when a Gyro Sensor turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\n### Brain Inertial Sensor - IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nHowever, when used with the Brain Inertial option, the **Gyro rotation** block reports an increasingly **positive** value when the Brain Inertial turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\nThe Brain Inertial Sensor follows a clockwise-positive rotation while a Gyro Sensor follows a counter-clockwise-positive rotation.\n\nChoose which Gyro Sensor to check or to check the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/en/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_devices.png)\n\nThe **Gyro rotation** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png](static/help/iq/blocks/en/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Round\n\nRounds the inputed value to the nearest integer.\n\n![round](static/help/iq/blocks/en/round/round.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nDecimals that are 0.5 or greater **round** up and decimals less than 0.5 **round** down.\n\nThe length of the **round** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\nThe **round** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/en/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will round 2.7 and will print \"3\".\n\n![round_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/en/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Set 2D list to\n\nSets every item in the 2D list to the entered values.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen creating a 2D list, you can set the number of **columns** of the list between 1 to 10 items and the number of **rows** of the list between 1 to 10 items.\n\nChoose which 2D list to use. The 2D list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nThe **set 2D list to** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Set list to\n\nSets every value in a list to the entered values.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe length of the list (1 to 10 items) is set when the list is created.\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nThe **set list to** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\nThis example will set the list to initial values and then report item #3 (90) from the list to set the position of the Arm. \n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Set boolean variable\n\nSets a boolean variable to a given value.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which boolean variable to use. Boolean variables can also be renamed or deleted. \n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nChoose a Boolean value.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nThe **set boolean variable** block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks.\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_color_sensor_brightness":{"name":"set_color_sensor_brightness","markdown":"# Set color sensor light\n\nSets the brightness of the VEX IQ Color Sensor's light. \n\n![set_color_sensor_light](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_light.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Color Sensor has a light source that can be adjusted to help detect the color of an object or the brightness of a surface.\n\n**Set color sensor light** accepts a range of **0% to 100%**. The higher the light % is set, the brighter the Color Sensor's light source will shine.\n\nChoose which Color Sensor to use.\n\n![set_color_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor.png)\n\nThe **set color sensor light** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n![set_color_sensor_2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_2.png)\n\n\n"},"set_cursor_new":{"name":"set_cursor_new","markdown":"# Set cursor\n\nSets the cursor location for **print** blocks.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_cursor_new/set_cursor.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet the cursor's row and column position to have all **print** commands display at a specific location on the VEX IQ Brain screen.\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n**Set cursor** accepts a range for **row** of **1 to 5** for the IQ (1st generation) Brain.\n\n**Set cursor** accepts a range for **column** of **1 to 21** for the IQ (1st generation) Brain.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_cursor_new/row_column_index.png)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\n![row_column_index2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_cursor_new/iq2_row_column_brain2.jpg)    \n\nThe **set cursor** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example 1\n\nThis example will set the cursor to location row 3 column 7 before printing the text \"VEXcode!\" to the IQ (1st generation) Brain's screen.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_cursor_new/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_cursor_new/set_cursor_hello.png)\n\n## Example 2\n\nThis example will set the cursor to location row 3 column 5 before printing the text \"VEXcode!\" to the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_cursor_new/set_cursor_code2.png)\n\n![set_cursor_hello2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_cursor_new/set_cursor_hello2.png)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Set drive heading\n\nSets the Drivetrain's Gyro heading value.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### VEX IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe **set drive heading** block can be used to set the Drivetrain's position to any given counter-clockwise heading as shown in the image below.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n### VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nDrivetrain heading references can differ depending on whether a gyro or the integrated inertial sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\n![set_drive_heading_clockwise](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_heading/set_drive_heading_clockwise.png)\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\n![set_drive_heading_counterclockwise](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_heading/set_drive_heading_counterclockwise.png)\n\n**Set drive heading** accepts a range of **0 to 359.99** degrees.\n\nThe **set drive heading** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will rotate the robot a total of 135 degrees:\n\n![setDriveHeading_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_example_revised.png)\n\n(The descriptions below are based on an IQ (1st generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration, or an IQ (2nd generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration with a gyro sensor)\n\n- Turn left to heading 45 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current position as heading of 0 degrees.\n- Turn left an additional 90 degrees based on the set heading value from the previous block.\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Set drive rotation\n\nSets the Drivetrain's angle of rotation when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro or Brain Inertial Sensor.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe **set drive rotation** block can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive or negative value.\n\nThe **set drive rotation** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nDrivetrain rotation references can differ depending on whether a gyro or the integrated inertial sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the integrated inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\nThe **set drive rotation** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will turn the robot a total of 210 degrees:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n(The descriptions below are based on an IQ (1st generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration, or an IQ (2nd generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration with a gyro sensor)\n\n- Turn left (counter-clockwise) to rotation 120 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current position as rotation of -45 degrees.\n- Turn left (counter-clockwise) an additional 90 degrees (-45 degrees to +45 degrees) based on the set rotation value from the previous block."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Set drive stopping\n\nSets the behavior of the Drivetrain once it stops moving.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n* **Brake** will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop.\n* **Coast** lets the Drivetrain spin gradually to a stop.\n* **Hold** will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop and returns it to its stopped position if moved.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the Drivetrain move forward for 3 seconds and then hold its position once stopped.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Set drive timeout\n\nSets a time limit for Drivetrain movement commands.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Drivetrain's time limit is used to prevent drive blocks that do not reach their position from preventing other blocks in the stack from running.\n\nAn example of a Drivetrain not reaching its position is when a robot is driven against a wall and cannot completed its movement.\n\nThe **set drive timeout** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will end the **drive** command after 2 second if the Drivetrain has not reached the target of 24 inches. Once the time limit or distance is reached, the Drivetrain will move on to the **turn** command.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Set drive velocity\n\nSets the speed of the Drivetrain.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set drive velocity** will only set the speed of the Drivetrain but will not cause the Drivetrain to move. A **drive** block is still required.\n\n**Set drive velocity** accepts a range of **-100% to 100%** or **-127rpm to 127rpm**.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to move in reverse.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's velocity to 0 will cause the Drivetrain to stop.\n\nThe **set drive velocity** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the Drivetrain drive at 50% velocity for 12 inches.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_fill_color":{"name":"set_fill_color","markdown":"# Set fill color\n\nSets the color that fills in shapes drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n![set_fill_color_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set fill color** block is used to set the color of the inside of circles and rectangles drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen. \n\nChoose a fill color. \n\n![set_fill_color_color](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_color.png)  \n\nThe fill color will be used for any future objects drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen."},"set_font":{"name":"set_font","markdown":"# Set font\n\nSets the style and size of font used on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen when printing numbers or text.\n\n![set_font_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_font/set_font_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThere are two different types of fonts available on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - each character takes up the same width.\n* Proportional (Prop) - each character takes up different size widths based on the character.\n\nChoose which font type and size to use.\n\n![set_font_block_font](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_font/set_font_block_font.png)  \n\nThe new font size will be used for any future text written to the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen."},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Set gyro heading\n\nSets the Gyro Sensor or IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor's current heading position to the specified value.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### Gyro Sensor\n\nThe **set gyro heading** block can be used to set a Gyro Sensor's heading to any given counter-clockwise-positive heading as shown in the image below.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_gyro_heading/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\n### Brain Inertial Sensor\n\nAlternatively, the **set gyro heading** block can also be used to set a IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor's heading to a given clockwise-positive heading as illustrated below.\n\n![BrainInertial](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_gyro_heading/brain_inertial.png)\n\n**Set gyro heading** accepts a range of **0 to 359.99** degrees.\n\nThe **set gyro heading** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose which Gyro Sensor to use or choose the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Set gyro rotation\n\nSets the VEX IQ Gyro Sensor or IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor's current rotation position to the specified value.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### Gyro Sensor\n\nThe **set gyro rotation** block can be used to set a Gyro Sensor's rotation to any given positive (counter-clockwise) or negative (clockwise) value.\n\n### Brain Inertial\n\nHowever, when used with the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor option, the **set gyro rotation** block can be used to set the rotation to a given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value. Note that this is opposite of that of a Gyro Sensor as the Brain Inertial Sensor follows a clockwise-positive rotation.\n\n**Set gyro rotation** accepts a range of any positive or negative decimal or integer number.\n\nThe **set gyro rotation** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose which Gyro Sensor to use or choose the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation_devices.png)\n\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Replace item of 2D list\n\nUpdates an item in the 2D list to a new value.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nEnter the item's row (first number) and column (second number) position within the list to be replaced.\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nThe **replace item** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Replace item\n\nUpdates an item in the list to a new value.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nThe **replace item** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n\nThis example will update item #2 in my list to a value of 15 and print item #2 of my list to the VEX IQ Brain Screen.\n\n![replace_item_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_item_of_array/replace_item_example.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Set motor position\n\nSets a VEX IQ Motor or Motor Group's encoder position(s) to the entered value.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **motor position** block can be used to set a Motor or Motor Group's position to any given value.\n\nUsually, the **motor position** block is used to set the position to 0 to reset a Motor or Motor Group's encoder position(s).\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nChoose the unit of measurement in degrees or turns.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Set motor stopping\n\nSets the behavior of the VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group once it stops moving.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n* **Brake** will cause the Motor/Motor Group to come to an immediate stop.\n* **Coast** lets the Motor/Motor Group spin gradually to a stop.\n* **Hold** will cause the Motor/Motor Group to come to an immediate stop and returns it to its stopped position if moved.\n\nThe **set motor stopping** will take effect for all future motion commands for the rest of the program until otherwise changed.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nChoose the Motor/Motor Group's stopping behavior.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the ArmMotor move forward for 90 degrees and then will resist outside forces (like gravity) to hold its position.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Set motor timeout\n\nSets a time limit for VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group movement commands.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nA Motor or Motor Group's timeout is used to prevent movement blocks that do not reach their position from preventing other blocks in the stack from running. An example of a Motor not reaching its position is an arm or claw that reaches its mechanical limit and cannot complete its movement.\n\nThe **set motor timeout** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will end the **set motor** command after 2 second if the ClawMotor has not reached the position of 270 degrees. Once the time limit or target is reached, the ClawMotor will move to position 0 degrees.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Set motor torque\n\nSets the strength of the VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set motor torque** accepts a range of **0% to 100%**.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nThe **set motor torque** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the Claw Motor to the 40 degree position with only 20% maximum torque. This allows the claw to grab an object without damaging it with too much force.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Set motor velocity\n\nSets the speed of a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set motor velocity** accepts a range of **-100% to 100%** or **-127rpm to 127rpm**.\n\nSetting a Motor or Motor Group's velocity to a negative value will cause the Motor or Motor Group to spin in reverse.\n\nSetting a Motor or Motor Group's velocity to 0 will cause the Motor or Motor Group to stop.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nChoose if the speed is set in % or in revolutions per minute (rpm).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the Arm Motor is set to slowly spin at 25% speed to the 90 degree position.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_pen_color":{"name":"set_pen_color","markdown":"# Set pen color\n\nSets the color of lines drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen or the values printed to the Print Console.\n\n![set_pen_color_block_with_console](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_block_with_console.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set pen color** block is used to set the color of lines, pixels, and text drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen or the values printed to the Print Console. \n\n**Set pen color** will also be used to set the color the outline of circles and rectangles drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\nChoose a pen color. \n\n![set_pen_color_dropdown_with_console](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_dropdown_with_console.png)  \n\nThe pen color will be used for any future objects drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\nThe text color of the Print Console is reset to black at the start of every program."},"set_print_precision_new":{"name":"set_print_precision_new","markdown":"# Set print precision\n\nSets the number of digits that appear after the decimal point when printing reporter blocks on the VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_print_precision_new/print_precision.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose the level of precision that inserted reporter blocks will be printed to the screen.\n\n* Ones (1) (Default)\n* Tenths (0.1)\n* Hundredths (0.01)\n* Thousandths (0.001)\n* All Digits (0.000001)\n\nReporter blocks printed to the screen will round to the nearest level of precision. For example, 1.67 will be printed as 2 at ones precision and 1.7 at tenths precision.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_print_precision_new/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_print_precision_new_console":{"name":"set_print_precision_new_console","markdown":"# Set print precision\n\nSets the number of digits that appear after the decimal point when printing reporter blocks on the Print Console or VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_print_precision_new_console/print_precision.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose the level of precision that inserted reporter blocks will be printed to the screen.\n\n* Ones (1) (Default)\n* Tenths (0.1)\n* Hundredths (0.01)\n* Thousandths (0.001)\n* All Digits (0.000001)\n\nReporter blocks printed to the Print Console or screen will round to the nearest level of precision. For example, 1.67 will be printed as 2 at ones precision and 1.7 at tenths precision.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_print_precision_new_console/print_precision_choice.png)\n\nChoose whether to set the print precision of values printed to the Print Console or the Brain's screen.\n\n![print_precision_dropdown_with_console](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_print_precision_new_console/print_precision_dropdown_with_console.png)"},"set_print_precision_virtual":{"name":"set_print_precision_virtual","markdown":"# Set print precision\n\nSets the number of digits that appear after the decimal point when using print blocks to print variables and values to the Print Console.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_print_precision_virtual/set_print_precision.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose the level of precision that inserted reporter blocks will be printed to the screen.\n\n* Ones (1)\n* Tenths (0.1) (Default)\n* Hundredths (0.01)\n* Thousandths (0.001)\n* All Digits (0.000001)\n\nReporter blocks printed to the display will round to the nearest level of precision. For example, 1.67 will be printed as 2 at ones precision and 1.7 at tenths precision.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_print_precision_virtual/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_touchled_brightness":{"name":"set_touchled_brightness","markdown":"# Set Touch LED brightness\n\nSets the brightness level of the VEX IQ Touch LED.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set Touch LED brightness** accepts a range of **0% to 100%**.\n\nChoose which Touch LED to use.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor3](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_sensor3.png)\n\nThe **Set Touch LED brightness** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness2.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will illuminate the Touch LED green at 25% brightness.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_touchled_color":{"name":"set_touchled_color","markdown":"# Set Touch LED color\n\nSets the color of the VEX IQ Touch LED. \n\n![set_touchLED_color](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which **Touch LED** to use.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_sensor.png)\n\nChoose the color that will be displayed.  \n\n![set_touchLED_color2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color2.png)\n\nTo turn the **Touch LED** off, set the color to none.\n\nYou can also set the color of the **Touch LED** to the color being detected by a Color Sensor.\n\n![set_touchLED_color3](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color3.png)\n\nAlternatively, the **Touch LED** can also be set to the color being detected by an Optical Sensor.\n\n![set_touchLED_optical](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_optical.png)"},"set_touchled_fade":{"name":"set_touchled_fade","markdown":"# Set Touch LED fade\n\nSets how fast the color of the VEX IQ Touch LED fades between colors.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Touch LED to use.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_sensor2.png)\n\nChoose how fast the Touch LED will fade.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_speed](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_speed.png)\n\n* Slow - The Touch LED will slowly fade to a new color.\n* Fast - The Touch LED will quickly fade to a new color. colors.\n* Off - The Touch LED will change colors instantly.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will slowly fade the Touch LED to blue.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Set turn velocity\n\nSets the angular velocity to control the rate of speed of turns.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set turn velocity** will only set the speed the Drivetrain will rotate but will not cause the Drivetrain to move. A **turn** block is still required.\n\n**Set turn velocity** accepts a range of **-100% to 100%** or **-127rpm to 127rpm**.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to turn in the opposite direction.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to 0 will cause the Drivetrain to stop.\n\nThe **set turn velocity** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the Drivetrain turn to the left slowly at 25% velocity.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Set variable\n\nSets a variable to a given value.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which variable to use. Variables can also be renamed or deleted. \n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nThe **set variable** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will report the VEX IQ Distance Sensor into the \"my variable\" variable and use the \"my variable\" to set the speed of the Drivetrain.\n\n![set_variable_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_variable/set_variable_example.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Set vision object item\n\nSets the object item (of the object you want to learn more information about) out of the number of objects detected.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **object count** block can be used before the **set vision object item** block to determine the number of objects detected.\n\nChoose which Vision Sensor to use.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nThe **set vision object item** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n\n\n"},"set_width":{"name":"set_width","markdown":"# Set pen width\n\nSets the width of the outline for shapes drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n![set_width_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_width/set_width_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set width** block is used to set the width of the line on the outside of circles and rectangles drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen. \n\nThe **set width** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/iq/blocks/en/set_width/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Length of list\n\nReports the number of items in a list.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/en/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nThe **length of list** reporter block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/iq/blocks/en/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# Snapshot\n\nTakes a snapshot from the Vision Sensor.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **snapshot** block will capture the current image from the Vision Sensor to be processed and analyzed for color signatures and codes. \n\nTypically, a **snapshot** is required first before using any other Vision Sensor blocks.\n\nSelect which Vision Sensor to use.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nSelect which vision signature to use. Vision signatures are configured from the Devices window.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/iq/blocks/en/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Spin\n\nSpins a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group until stopped.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **spin** block will run a Motor or Motor Group forever until a new motion block is used or the program is stopped.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nChoose which direction to spin. Direction names can be changed in the Devices window. \n\n![spin_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Spin for\n\nSpins a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group for a given distance.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Spin for** will tell a Motor or Motor Group to travel in a given direction for a given distance from where it is currently located.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nChoose which direction to spin. Direction names can be changed in the Devices window. \n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nThe **spin for** for block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoosing the unit of measurement in degrees or turns.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Motor or Motor Group is done moving.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Motor or Motor Group moves.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Spin to position\n\nSpins a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group to a set position.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Spin to position** will tell a Motor or Motor Group to travel to a specific position. Based on the current position of the Motor or Motor Group, **spin to position** will determine the direction to rotate.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nThe **spin to position** for block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose the unit of measurement in degrees or turns.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Motor or Motor Group is done moving.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Motor or Motor Group moves.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/en/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Stop driving\n\nStops the Drivetrain.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will stop the Drivetrain after 3 seconds.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Stop motor\n\nStops a Motor or Motor Group.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to stop.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the Claw Motor open for 3 seconds before stopping.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_project":{"name":"stop_project","markdown":"# Stop project\n\nStops a running project.\n\n![stop_project](static/help/iq/blocks/en/stop_project/stop_project.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **stop project** block will cause a running project to stop. \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will drive the IQ Robot forward 200mm and turn right for 90 degrees before stopping the project.\n\n![stop_project2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/stop_project/stop_project2.png)"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Subtract\n\nSubtracts one value from another and reports the difference.\n\n![subtract](static/help/iq/blocks/en/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Subtract** can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe length of **subtract** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\nSubtract two numbers.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/iq/blocks/en/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nSubtract with values from variables.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nSubtract with values from sensors or devices.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/en/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Timer value\n\nReports the value of the VEX IQ Brain timer in seconds.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe timer starts at 0 seconds when the program starts and reports decimal values.\n\nThe reporter block **timer value** is used inside of blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will move the Drivetrain forward and play a sound effect for 4.5 seconds before making a 90-degree turn.\n\n![timerValue_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/timer_value/timerValue_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"timer_value_virtual":{"name":"timer_value_virtual","markdown":"# Timer value\n\nReports the value of the VEX IQ Brain timer in seconds.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/timer_value_virtual/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe timer starts at 0 seconds when the program starts and reports decimal values.\n\nThe reporter block **Timer value** is used inside of blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/timer_value_virtual/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will move the Drivetrain forward and play a sound effect for 4.5 seconds before making a 90-degree turn.\n\n![timerValue_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/en/timer_value_virtual/timerValue_example_revised.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Timer value** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![timerValue_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/timer_value_virtual/timerValue_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![timerValue_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/timer_value_virtual/timerValue_monitor.png)"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Turn\n\nRotates the Drivetrain forever.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **turn** block will rotate the Drivetrain forever until a new Drivetrain block is used or the program is stopped.\n\nChoose the direction the Drivetrain will move.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Turn for\n\nRotates the Drivetrain for a given distance.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which direction the Drivetrain will turn.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\nThe **Drive for** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nSet how far the Drivetrain will move by entering a number of degrees.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Drivetrain is done turning.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Drivetrain turns.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Turn to heading\n\nTurns a Drivetrain to a specific heading when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro or VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain Brain Inertial Sensor.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### VEX IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe **turn to heading** block can be used to turn the Drivetrain to any given counter-clockwise heading as shown in the image below.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n### VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe **turn to heading** block can be used to turn the Drivetrain either in a counter-clockwise or clockwise heading depending on whether the integrated inertial or a gyro sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\n![turn_to_heading_clockwise](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_clockwise.png)\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\n![turn_to_heading_counterclockwise](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_counterclockwise.png)\n\nBased on the current heading of the Gyro, **turn to heading** will determine which direction to turn.\n\n**Turn to heading** accepts a range of **0.00 to 359.99** degrees.\n\nThe **turn to heading** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns: \n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 45 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 90 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 270 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to 180 degrees\n\n(The clockwise/counter-clockwise motions described above are based on an IQ (1st generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration, or an IQ (2nd generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration with a gyro sensor)\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Drivetrain is done turning.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Drivetrain turns.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Turn to rotation\n\nTurns a Drivetrain to a specific angle of rotation when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro or VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n### VEX IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe **turn to rotation** block can be used to turn the Drivetrain to a given positive (counter-clockwise) or negative (clockwise) value.\n\n### VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe **turn to rotation** block can be used to turn the Drivetrain either in a counter-clockwise or clockwise rotation depending on whether the integrated inertial or a gyro sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\nBased on the current **rotation** value of the Drivetrain, **turn to rotation** will determine which direction to turn.\n\nThe **turn to rotation** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns: \n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 90 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 180 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to -45 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 0 degrees\n\n(The clockwise/counter-clockwise motions described above are based on an IQ (1st generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration, or an IQ (2nd generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration with a gyro sensor)\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Drivetrain is done turning.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Drivetrain turns.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/en/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Variable\n\nReports the value assigned to the variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/variable/variable.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Variable** blocks are used to report a values stored inside of the variable. Use the **set variable** block to set or update the value of a variable.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nThe **variable** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nVariables are created using the **Make a Variable** button.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"variable_virtual":{"name":"variable_virtual","markdown":"# Variable\n\nReports the value assigned to the variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/variable_virtual/variable.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Variable** blocks are used to report a values stored inside of the variable. Use the **set variable** block to set or update the value of a variable.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/variable_virtual/variable_cursor.png)\n\nThe **variable** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/variable_virtual/variable_inserted.png)\n\nVariables are created using the **Make a Variable** button.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/en/variable_virtual/make_variable.png)  \n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of a **variable** block, select the checkbox next to its reporter block.\n\n![variable_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/variable_virtual/variable_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the **variable** reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![variable_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/variable_virtual/variable_monitor.png)"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Velocity of motor\n\nReports the current velocity of a VEX IQ Smart Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To use\n\n**Velocity of motor** reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-127rpm to 127rpm**.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in % or in revolutions per minute (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **velocity of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"velocity_of_motor_virtual":{"name":"velocity_of_motor_virtual","markdown":"# Velocity of motor\n\nReports the current velocity of a VEX IQ Smart Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To use\n\n**Velocity of motor** reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-127rpm to 127rpm**.\n\nChoose which Motor/Motor Group to use.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in % or in revolutions per minute (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Velocity of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Velocity of motor** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_checkbox](static/help/iq/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_monitor](static/help/iq/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_monitor.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Vision object\n\nReports information about a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/en/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use the **Vision object** block, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Devices window.\n2. Use **snapshot** to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use **object exists** to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code.\n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision blocks to learn more about the object detected.\n\n* Use **set vision object item** to set which detected object you want to learn more information about. By default, the largest object detected is used.\n* Use **object count** to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use **vision object** to determine which information to report from the detected object.\n\nSelect which Vision Sensor to use.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/iq/blocks/en/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nSelect which value to report from the Vision Sensor:\n\n* Width - How wide the object is in pixels. Returns a value of **2 - 316 px**.\n* Height - How tall the object is in pixels. Returns a value of **2 - 212 px**. \n* CenterX - Reports the X coordinate of the center of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 315 px**.\n* CenterY - Reports the Y coordinate of the center of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 211 px**.\n* Angle - Reports the angle of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 180 degrees**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/en/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nThe reporter block **vision object** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Wait\n\nWaits for a specific amount of time before moving to the next block.\n\n![wait](static/help/iq/blocks/en/wait/wait.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose an amount of time to **wait**.\n\nThe **wait** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will change the VEX IQ Touch LED from red to green after **waiting** 3.25 seconds.\n\n![wait_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/wait/wait_example.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Wait until\n\nWaits for a Boolean block to report **true** before moving to the next block.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/iq/blocks/en/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Wait until** will repeatedly check a Boolean reporter block and will not move to the next block until the Boolean report block reports **true**.\n\nThe **wait until** Boolean block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks.\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will turn the Touch LED to Yellow and wait until the Touch LED is pressed. Once pressed, the Brain will print \"Done!\" to the LCD.\n\n![wait_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/wait_until/wait_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"when_brain_button":{"name":"when_brain_button","markdown":"# When Brain button\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected VEX IQ Brain button is pressed or released.\n\n![when_brain_button](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_brain_button/when_brain_button.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which IQ (1st generation) Brain button to use.\n\n![when_brain_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select.png)\n\nOr choose which IQ (2nd generation) Brain button to use.\n\n![when_brain_button_select_iq2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select_iq2.png)\n\nSelect which action will trigger the event - **pressed** or **released** \n\n![when_brain_button_select_2](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select_2.png)  \n"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# When I receive\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected message is received from a **broadcasted** message.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which message to listen for. A new message can also be created.\n\nThe **when I receive** block will only from a **broadcast** or **broadcast and wait** block in a different stack.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will display red on the VEX IQ Touch LED and then wait two seconds before broadcasting \"message1\". \n\nOnce the messaged is received, the **when I receive** stack will cause the Drivetrain will move forward while the Arm Motor will move upwards at the same time. \n\nThe two stacks will continue to run at the same time as indicated by the red arrows.\n\n\n![when_broadcast_example](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_example.png)\n\n"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# When bumper\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected VEX IQ Bumper is pressed or released.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Bumper Switch to use.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nSelect which action will trigger the event - **pressed** or **released** \n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# When controller axis\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected VEX IQ Controller joystick axis is moved.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller joystick axis to use.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# When controller button\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected VEX IQ Controller button is pressed or released.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller button to use.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_controller_button/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_controller_button/controller_button_back.png)\n\nSelect which action will trigger the event - **pressed** or **released** \n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# When started\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the project is started.\n\n![when_started](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**When started** event will be run when the program is started from the VEX IQ Brain's menu or from the **run** button in VEXcode IQ Blocks.\n\nAll new programs will automatically include a **when started** block.\n\nProjects for the IQ (1st generation) Brain can support up to 3 **when started** blocks.\n\nProjects for the IQ (2nd generation) Brain can support up to 8 **when started** blocks.\n"},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# When timer\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the VEX IQ Brain timer is greater than the given value.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Brain's timer begins at the beginning of each project.\n\nChoose an amount of time. The **when timer** event will run once the Brain's timer is **greater than** the entered amount.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nThe **when timer** block can accept decimals or integer values.\n\nThe **when timer** block cannot accept other reporter blocks."},"when_touchled":{"name":"when_touchled","markdown":"# When Touch LED\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected VEX IQ Touch LED is pressed or released.\n\n![when_touchLED](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_touchled/when_touchled.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Touch LED to use.\n\n![when_touchLED_select](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_touchled/when_touchled_select.png)\n\nSelect which action will trigger the event - **pressed** or **released** \n\n![when_touchLED_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/en/when_touchled/when_touchled_condition.png)"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# While\n\nA 'C' block that repeats the blocks inside while the Boolean condition is reported to be **true**.  \n\n![while](static/help/iq/blocks/en/while/while.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **while** block will only check the Boolean condition at the beginning of each loop. \n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **true**, the blocks inside of **while** will run.\n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **false**, the blocks inside of **while** will be skipped.\n\nThe **while** 'C' block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks as its condition.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/en/while/while_inserted.png)"}},"python":{"control_break":{"name":"control_break","markdown":"# Break\n\nExits a repeating loop immediately.\n\n```python\nbreak\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen added inside of a loop, the `break` command will exit the loop it is currently running inside of. \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will drive the robot and check if its `bumper` has been pressed.\n\nIf the bumper is **pressed**, the `break` command will exit the `while` loop. The robot will then stop driving forward.\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n    if bumper.pressing():\n        break\n\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"break"},"control_elseif_statement":{"name":"control_elseif_statement","markdown":"# Elif\n\nA control flow statement that executes one block of commands if a condition evaluates to true. \n\n```python\nif condition:\n    pass\nelif condition2:\n    pass\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `elif` statement is a conditional that will check if its condition evaluates to **True** or **False**. It is possible to combine many conditions with the use of logical operators such as `and`, `or`, and `not`. \n\nIf the totality of the condition is **True** and all previous `if` and `elif` conditions are **False**, then the code block indented below the `elif condition:` will run.\n\nCode blocks below the `elif` should be indented four spaces.\n\nAn `elif` statement should not contain empty blocks of code. If necessary, add  `pass` statements to a previously empty `elif` statement. \n\n## Example\n\nThis code will drive the robot FORWARD if the variable equals 1. If the variable equals -1, it will drive the robot REVERSE. If the variable is anything else it will stop the robot.\n\n```python\nmy_variable = 1\n\nif my_variable == 1:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nelif my_variable == -1:\n    drivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\nelse:\n    drivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"if condition:\\n\\tpass\\nelif condition:\\n\\tpass\\nelse:\\n\\tpass"},"control_for_loop":{"name":"control_for_loop","markdown":"# For\n\nA type of loop that repeats the code contained in its body for a set number of iterations.\n\n```python\nfor repeat_count in range(10):\n    pass\n```\n\n# How To Use\n\nFirst, replace `repeat_count` with a variable that will iterate through the `range()` function.\n\nSecond, replace `10` with a value to specify the end of the iteration.\n\nAdd a four-spaced indentation using the spacebar to include statements as part of the `for` control statement.\n\nA `for` statement should not contain an empty block of code. If necessary, add a `pass` statement to a previously empty for statement.\n\nNote that for loops start at the index 0 instead of 1.\n\n`For` loops can also be nested inside each other.\n\nAdd a brief delay after each loop iteration for optimal loop performance (see example below).\n\n# Example\n\nThe following for loop will print numbers 0 to 2:\n\n```python\nfor i in range(3):\n   brain.screen.print(i)\n   brain.screen.next_row()\n   wait(0.1, SECONDS)\n```\n   \nThis will print:\n\n```\n0\n1\n2\n```","signature":"for value in range (10"},"control_if_else_statement":{"name":"control_if_else_statement","markdown":"# If/else\n\nA control flow statement that executes one block of commands if a condition evaluates to true, or another block of commands if a condition evaluates to false. \n\n```python\nif condition:\n    pass\nelse:\n    pass\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `if` statement is a conditional that will check if its condition evaluates to **True** or **False**. It is possible to combine many conditions with the use of logical operators such as `and`, `or`, and `not`. \n\nIf the totality of the condition is **True**, then the code block indented below the `if condition:` will run. If the totality of the condition is **False**, the code block indented below the `else:` statement will run instead.\n\nCode blocks below the `if` and `else` should be indented four spaces.\n\nAn `if/else` statement should not contain empty blocks of code. If necessary, add  `pass` statements to a previously empty `if/else` statement. \n\n## Example\n\nThis `if/else` code will drive the robot FORWARD if the variable equals 1. If it does not, it will drive the robot REVERSE. \n\n```python\nmy_variable = 1\n\nif my_variable == 1:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nelse:\n    drivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"if conditio"},"control_if_statement":{"name":"control_if_statement","markdown":"# If\n\nA control statement used to decide whether a block of code will be executed based on the provided `condition`.\n\n```python\nif condition:\n    pass \n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReplace the word `condition` with an expression that can either evaluate to `True` or `False`. An evaluation to `True` will allow the statement(s) indented below the `if` statement to execute.\n\nAdd a four-spaced indentation using the **spacebar** to include statements as part of the `if` control statement. \n\nAn `if` statement should not contain an empty block of code. If necessary, add a `pass` statement to a previously empty `if` statement. \n\n## Example\n\nThis `if` statement will run if `my_variable` equals 1, causing the robot to drive forward.\n\n```python\nmy_variable = 1\n\nif my_variable == 1:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"if condition:\\n\\tpass"},"control_wait":{"name":"control_wait","markdown":"# Wait\n\nWaits for a specific amount of time before moving to the next command.\n\n```python\nwait(TIME, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet an amount of time in **SECONDS** or **MSEC** on the **UNITS** parameter to have your program **wait** before executing subsequent commands.\n\n```python\nwait(10, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"wait(TIME, UNITS)"},"control_wait_until":{"name":"control_wait_until","markdown":"# While Not\nA control statement that continues looping until the expression turns **True**.\n\n```python\nwhile not condition:\n    pass\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `while not` statement will repeatedly check the condition, and will not move to the next command until the condition reports **True**.\n\nIf the condition evaluates to **False**, the code inside of `while not` will run.\n\nIf the condition evaluates to **True**, the code inside of `while not` will be skipped, and the next command after the `while not` statement will be executed.\n\nThe `while not` statement accepts any expression that evaluates to `True` or `False` as its condition. You can place Booleans as well as expressions using comparison and logical operators. \n\nYou can also use numerical values; **0** evaluates to `False`, and any **non-zero numbers** evaluates to `True`. \n\nAdd a four-spaced indentation using the **spacebar** to include statements as part of the `while not` control statement. \n\nA `while not` statement should not contain an empty block of code. If necessary, add a `pass` statement to a previously empty `while not` statement. \n\nAdd a brief delay after each loop iteration for optimal loop performance (see example below).\n\n## Example\n\nThis `while not` loop will print \"Hello\" on separate lines until the value of my_variable is equal to 5.\n\n```python\nmy_variable = 0\n\nwhile not my_variable == 5:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\n    brain.screen.new_line()\n    my_variable += 1\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"while not expressio"},"control_while_loop":{"name":"control_while_loop","markdown":"# While\nA loop that repeats the code in its body as long as the condition expression evaluates to **True**.   \n\n```python\nwhile condition:\n    pass\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `while` loop will only check the condition inside the parenthesis at the beginning of each loop. \n\nIf the condition evaluates to **True**, the code inside of `while` will run.\n\nIf the condition evaluates to **False**, the code inside of `while` will be skipped.\n\nThe `while` loop accepts anything that evaluates to `True` or `False` as its condition. You can place Booleans as well as expressions using comparison and logical operators. \n\nYou can also use numerical values; **0** evaluates to `False`, and any **non-zero numbers** evaluates to `True`. \n\nAdd a four-spaced indentation using the **spacebar** to include statements as part of the `while` control statement. \n\nA `while` statement should not contain an empty block of code. If necessary, add a `pass` statement to a previously empty `while` statement. \n\nAdd a brief delay after each loop iteration for optimal loop performance (see example below).\n\n## Example\n\nThis `while` loop will continue to print the word \"Hello\" on separate lines when the timer value is less than 10 seconds.\n\n```python\nwhile brain.timer.time(SECONDS) < 10:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"while expressio"},"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain":{"name":"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain","markdown":"# Drivetrain Calibrate\n\nCalibrates the Drivetrain's Inertial or Gyro Sensor based on which is currently configured with the Drivetrain.\n\n```python\n# Inertial Sensor\nbrain_inertial.calibrate()\n\n# Gyro Sensor\ndrivetrain_gyro.calibrate()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain Calibrate` command will calibrate the Drivetrain's Inertial or Gyro Sensor. The Drivetrain must remain stationary during the calibration process.\n\nA `wait` should be added after the `Drivetrain Calibrate` command is used to allow for the calibration process to finish correctly.\n\n```python\nbrain_inertial.calibrate()\nwait(3, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.calibrate()"},"drivetrain_drive":{"name":"drivetrain_drive","markdown":"# Drive\n\nMoves the Drivetrain forever in the direction specified inside the parentheses. \n\nAll Drivetrain motors run forward or in reverse at the velocity set using the Drivetrain's `Set Drive Velocity` command. The default velocity is 50%.\n\nNegative values will cause the Drivetrain to drive forward with a REVERSE input and in reverse with a FORWARD input.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drive` command will run the Drivetrain forever, until a new drivetrain command is used, or the program is stopped.\n\n## Examples\n\nUse the `FORWARD` argument in all-capital letters to move the Drivetrain forward.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nUse the `REVERSE` argument in all-capital letters to move the Drivetrain in reverse.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.drive(FOWARD)"},"drivetrain_drive_for":{"name":"drivetrain_drive_for","markdown":"# Drive For\n\nMoves the Drivetrain for a given distance. All Drivetrain motors run forward or in reverse at the velocity set by the Drivetrain's `Set Drive Velocity` command. After the Drivetrain has moved the specified distance the Drivetrain will stop.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive_for(DIRECTION, DISTANCE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet how far the Drivetrain will move by entering at least three valid arguments inside of the parentheses, separated by commas. \n\nThe first argument specifies the direction. Valid inputs are either `FORWARD` or `REVERSE` in all capital letters.  \n\nThe second argument specifies the distance that the IQ Robot should drive.\n\nThe third argument specifies the unit of measurement that should be used. Valid inputs are either `INCHES` or `MM` (millimeters) in all-capital letters.\n\nThe `DISTANCE` parameter accepts numeric values. Negative values will cause the IQ Robot to drive in the opposite of the input `DIRECTION`.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive_for(REVERSE, 5.0, INCHES)\n```\n\nThe `Drive For` command is by default a blocking command. It will prevent subsequent commands from executing until the Drivetrain movement has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameter\n\nYou can set a fourth parameter to `wait=False` to allow proceeding commands to run even before the Drivetrain is done moving.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM, wait=False)\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows the `Drive For` command being used with a variable as a distance.\n\nThe IQ Robot will drive 200 MM forward.\n\n```python\ndistance_variable = 200\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, distance_variable, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 2, MM, wait=True)"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Set Drive Velocity\n\nSets the velocity of the Drivetrain for `Drive` and `Drive For` commands.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Set Drive Velocity` will set the Drivetrain's velocity when used with a `Drive` or `Drive For` command. It will not cause the Drivetrain to move when used by itself.\n\n`Set Drive Velocity` accepts a range of values depending on what units are passed as the second parameter.\n\nIf `PERCENT` is used as the second parameter, **VELOCITY** accepts a range from **-100 to 100**.\n\n`Set Drive Velocity` can also use `RPM` as a valid **UNITS** parameter, accepting a range from **-127 to 127**.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to drive opposite of the `DIRECTION` passed into a `Drive` or `Drive For` command.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to 0 will prevent the Drivetrain from moving even if a `Drive` or `Drive For` command is used.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows that the Drivetrain will go in reverse due to a negative value.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nThis example will prevent the Drivetrain from moving.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(0, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_drive_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)"},"drivetrain_set_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_set_heading","markdown":"# Set Heading\n\nSets the Drivetrain's Inertial or Gyro Sensor to the specified heading.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Drivetrain's `Set Heading` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's heading to a specified value. This command can be used to reset the orientation of the Drivetrain's Inertial or Gyro Sensor when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`Set Heading` accepts a number value between **0 and 360** as it's first argument, and `DEGREES` written in all-capital letters as it's second argument.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example sets the Drivetrain heading to 90 degrees. \n\nSince the heading of the IQ Robot is set to 90 degrees, the subsequent Drivetrain's `Turn to Heading` command will not cause the robot to turn as its current heading is already 90 degrees.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_heading(90, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_set_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_rotation","markdown":"# Set Rotation\n\nSets the Drivetrain's Inertial or Gyro Sensor to a specified rotation.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Drivetrain's `Set Rotation` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive or negative value.\n\nThe `ROTATION` parameter can accept numeric values.\n\nThe `ROTATION` parameter **does not** have a limit of 0-359 degrees.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will turn the robot a total of 210 degrees if the Drivetrain is configured with the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(120, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(45, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Turn right (clockwise) to rotation 120 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current position as rotation of -45 degrees.\n- Turn right (clockwise) an additional 90 degrees (-45 degrees to +45 degrees) based on the set rotation value from the previous command.","signature":"drivetrain.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_set_stopping":{"name":"drivetrain_set_stopping","markdown":"# Set Stopping\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_stopping(MODE)\n```\n\n## How to Use\n\nReplace the `MODE` parameter with one of the following options:\n\n* BRAKE: will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop.\n* COAST: lets the Drivetrain slow gradually to a stop.\n* HOLD: will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved. \n\nThe brake mode applied by the `Set Stopping` command will be applied to subsequent Drivetrain `Stop` commands in the program unless otherwise changed.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows the robot driving forward for 2 seconds before coasting to a stop.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_stopping(COAST)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nwait(2, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_stopping(MODE)"},"drivetrain_set_timeout":{"name":"drivetrain_set_timeout","markdown":"# Set Timeout\n\nSets a time limit for the Drivetrain's definite movement commands.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)\n```\n\n## How to Use\n\nThe command is used to prevent definite movement commands that do not reach their position from preventing other proceeding commands from running.\n\nSpecify the amount of time in `SECONDS`.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below sets the timeout of the Drivetrain to 3 seconds. If the Drivetrain does not complete its 2000 MM movement after 3 seconds has elapsed, it will stop driving.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_timeout(3, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 2000, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Set Turn Velocity\n\nSets the Drivetrain's turn velocity.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Set Turn Velocity` will set the velocity of the Drivetrain when turning, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move when used without a `Turn` or `Turn For` command.\n\n`Set Turn Velocity` accepts a range of values depending on what units are passed as the second parameter.\n\nIf `PERCENT` is used as the second parameter, **VELOCITY** accepts a range from **-100 to 100**.\n\nAlternatively, `Set Turn Velocity` can also use `RPM` as a valid **UNITS** parameter, accepting a range from **-127 to 127** as the **VELOCITY** parameter.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to turn in the opposite of the direction passed into any following `drivtrain.turn` commands.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to 0 will prevent the Drivetrain from turning.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the Drivetrain will turn in the opposite direction (LEFT) due to a negative turn velocity.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_turn_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)"},"drivetrain_stop":{"name":"drivetrain_stop","markdown":"# Stop\n\nStops the Drivetrain.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Stop` command stops the Drivetrain. It does not take any arguments in its parentheses.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will stop the Drivetrain after the IQ Robot has driven forward for 3 seconds.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"drivetrain.stop()"},"drivetrain_turn":{"name":"drivetrain_turn","markdown":"# Turn\n\nTurns the Drivetrain to the right or left indefinitely.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Turn` command will rotate the Drivetrain in the given direction forever until a new Drivetrain command is used, or until the program is stopped.\n\nUse the `LEFT` argument in all-capital letters to turn the Drivetrain to the left.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn(LEFT)\n```\n\nUse the `RIGHT` argument in all-capital letters to turn the Drivetrain to the right.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the robot will drive forward 200 MM before turning right indefinitely.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn(RIGHT)"},"drivetrain_turn_for":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_for","markdown":"# Turn For\n\nTurns the Drivetrain in the specified direction for a set number of degrees.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn_for(DIRECTION, ANGLE, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe first argument specifies the turn direction: `LEFT` or `RIGHT`, written in all-capital letters. \n\nThe second argument specifies the turn angle as a numeric value; this can be any number or numeric variable. \n\nThe third argument is the turn units. This should be set as `DEGREES` in all-capital letters. \n\nThe `Turn For` command is by default a blocking command. It prevents any proceeding code from executing until the Drivetrain has completed its turn.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nIf the fourth argument is set to `wait=False`, proceeding commands will be allowed to execute even before the Drivetrain has completed its turn.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn_for(LEFT, 90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will turn the IQ Robot 270 degrees to the right.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 270, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 90, DEGREES, wait=True)"},"drivetrain_turn_to_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Turn To Heading\n\nTurns a Drivetrain to a specific heading, when using a Gyro or Inertial Sensor.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Turn to Heading` command can be used to turn the Drivetrain to any given clockwise or counter-clockwise positive heading, depending on whether a Gyro or Inertial Sensor is configured with the Drivetrain.\n\nBased on the current heading, `Turn to Heading` will determine the shortest direction to turn.\n\nThe `HEADING` parameter accepts numeric values in the range of **0.00 to 359.99** .\n\nThe second parameter should be set to `DEGREES`.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns:\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(45.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(270.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(180.0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Right to 45 degrees\n- Right to 90 degrees\n- Right to 270 degrees\n- Left to 180 degrees\n\n(The direction descriptions below are based on a clockwise positive heading, with the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor configured with the Drivetrain)\n\nThe `Turn to Heading` command will by default block proceeding commands until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `wait=False` as a third parameter to prevent the `Turn to Heading` command from blocking proceeding commands from executing until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(180.0, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Turn To Rotation\n\nTurns the Drivetrain to a specific angle of rotation when used with a Gyro or Inertial Sensor.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Turn to Rotation` command can be used to turn the Drivetrain to an absolute rotation value.\n\nDepending on whether the Drivetrain is configured with a Gyro or Inertial Sensor, rotation values can either be counter-clockwise positive (Gyro), or clockwise positive (Inertial).\n\nBased on the current rotation of the Drivetrain, `Turn to Rotation` will determine which direction to turn.\n\nThe `ROTATION` parameter can accept numeric values.\n\nNumeric values are **not** limited to the range of **0 - 359.99** degrees. Turns will be absolute and may cause the robot to rotate more than once if necessary.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns:\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(180, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Right (clockwise) to 90 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to 180 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to -45 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to 0 degrees\n\n(The direction descriptions above are aligned with an IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor being configured with the Drivetrain)\n\nThe `Turn to Rotation`command will by default block proceeding commands until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameter\n\nYou can set a third parameter to  `wait=False` to prevent the `Turn to Rotation` command from blocking proceeding commands until the Drivetrain turn is completed.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(180.0, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90, DEGREES, wait=True)"},"events_brain_button_pressed":{"name":"events_brain_button_pressed","markdown":"# Brain Button Pressed\n\nRuns the callback function when one of the VEX IQ Brain's buttons is pressed.\n\n```python\nbrain.button.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a Brain Button is pressed.\n\n```python\ndef button_pressed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Button pressed\")\n```\n\nThe `Brain Button Pressed` function can be used with the different buttons on the VEX IQ Brain.\n\nSupported Brain buttons are as follows:\n\n- `buttonUp` / `buttonLeft`\n- `buttonDown` / `buttonRight`\n- `buttonCheck`\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```python\ndef callback_function():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Pressed\")\n\nbrain.buttonCheck.pressed(callback_function)\n```","signature":"brain.button.pressed(callback)"},"events_brain_button_released":{"name":"events_brain_button_released","markdown":"# Brain Button Released\n\nRuns the callback function when one of the VEX IQ Brain's buttons is released.\n\n```python\nbrain.button.released(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a Brain Button is released.\n\n```python\ndef button_released():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Button released\")\n```\n\nThe `Brain Button Released` function can be used with the different buttons on the VEX IQ Brain.\n\nSupported Brain buttons are as follows:\n\n- `buttonUp` / `buttonLeft`\n- `buttonDown` / `buttonRight`\n- `buttonCheck`\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```python\ndef callback_function():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Released\")\n\nbrain.buttonCheck.released(callback_function)\n```","signature":"brain.button.released(callback)"},"events_brain_timer":{"name":"events_brain_timer","markdown":"# Timer Event\n\nRuns the specified callback function when the IQ Brain's timer is greater than the specified time value.\n\n```python\nbrain.timer.event(callback, time)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe IQ Brain's timer begins at the start of each program.\n\nThe `Timer Event` function takes 2 parameters.\n\nThe first is the **callback function** parameter. A function will need to be created to pass to the `Timer Event` function.\n\nThe second parameter is the time at which the function will run. The **callback function** will run once the IQ Brain's timer is greater than the passed value. The amount of **time** should be in **milliseconds**.\n\n```python\n# Call the callback function after 1000 milliseconds\nbrain.timer.event(callback, 1000)\n```\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs.\n\nIn the snippet below, \"Callback Function Called\" will be printed to the VEX IQ's Brain Screen after 10 seconds.\n\n```python\ndef callback_function():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Timer Elapsed\")\n\nbrain.timer.event(callback_function, 10000)\n```","signature":"brain.timer.event(callback, time)"},"events_bumper_pressed":{"name":"events_bumper_pressed","markdown":"# Bumper Pressed\n\nRuns the specified **callback function** when a bumper is pressed.\n\n```python\nbumper.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Bumper Sensor is pressed. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```python\ndef bumper_pressed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Bumper Pressed\")\n```\n\nThen, the function is passed as the parameter of the `Bumper Pressed` function call.\n\n```python\nbumper.pressed(bumper_pressed)\n```\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```python\ndef callback_function():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Pressed\")\n\nbumper.pressed(callback_function)\n```","signature":"bumper.pressed(callback)"},"events_bumper_released":{"name":"events_bumper_released","markdown":"# Bumper Released\n\nRuns the specified function when a bumper is released.\n\n```python\nbumper.released(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCreate a function to call when the Bumper is released. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```python\ndef bumper_released():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Bumper released\")\n```\n\nThen, the function is passed as the parameter of the `Bumper Released` function call.\n\n```python\nbumper.released(bumper_released)\n```\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```python\ndef callback_function():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Released\")\n\nbumper.released(callback_function)\n```","signature":"bumper.released(callback)"},"events_controller_axis_changed":{"name":"events_controller_axis_changed","markdown":"# Controller Axis Changed\n\nRuns the provided callback funtion when the selected VEX IQ Controller's joystick axis is moved.\n\n```python\ncontroller.axis.changed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a callback function to call when a joystick axis on the Controller is moved.\n\nChoose which Controller joystick axis to use and pass the callback function:\n\n- `axisA`\n- `axisB`\n- `axisC`\n- `axisD`\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/python/en/events_controller_axis_changed/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```python\ndef callback_function():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Changed\")\n\ncontroller.axisA.changed(callbackFunction)\n```","signature":"`controller.axis.changed(callback)"},"events_controller_button_pressed":{"name":"events_controller_button_pressed","markdown":"# Controller Button Pressed\n\nRuns the **callback function** when the VEX IQ Controller button is pressed.\n\n```python\ncontroller.button.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a **callback function** that will be called when a Controller button is pressed.\n\nChoose which Controller button to call the `Controller Button Pressed` function with:\n\n* `buttonEUp`\n* `buttonEDown`\n* `buttonFUp`\n* `buttonFDown`\n* `buttonLUp`\n* `buttonLDown`\n* `buttonRUp`\n* `buttonRDown`\n* `buttonL3`\n* `buttonR3`\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints to the IQ Brain's screen when the Controller's L3 button is pressed.\n\n```python\ndef button_pressed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Button pressed\")\n    \ncontroller.buttonL3.pressed(button_pressed)\n```","signature":"controller.button.pressed(callback)"},"events_controller_button_released":{"name":"events_controller_button_released","markdown":"# Controller Button Released\n\nRuns the **callback function** when the VEX IQ Controller button is released.\n\n```python\ncontroller.button.released(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a **callback function** that will be called when a Controller button is released.\n\nChoose which Controller button to call the `Controller Button Released` function with:\n\n* `buttonEUp`\n* `buttonEDown`\n* `buttonFUp`\n* `buttonFDown`\n* `buttonLUp`\n* `buttonLDown`\n* `buttonRUp`\n* `buttonRDown`\n* `buttonL3`\n* `buttonR3`\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints to the IQ Brain's screen when the Controller's L3 button is released.\n\n```python\ndef button_released():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Button released\")\n    \ncontroller.buttonL3.released(button_released)\n```","signature":"controller.button.released(callback)"},"events_event":{"name":"events_event","markdown":"# Event Register Callback\n\nRegister a callback function to run when an event is triggered.\n\n```python\nevent(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nRegister a callback to a user-defined event.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"my_event\")\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n    brain.screen.print(\"broadcasted\")\n  \n# Create a new event.\nmy_event = Event()\n\n# Register a callback function to the my_event event\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the event\nmy_event.broadcast()\n```","signature":"EVENT(callback);"},"events_event_broadcast":{"name":"events_event_broadcast","markdown":"# Event Broadcast\n\nBroadcast event message to run listener functions.\n\n```python\nevent.broadcast()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe code will continue to run the commands after the `event.broadcast()` command so that it will run at the same time as the event listener functions.\n\nBefore using this command, a user defined event must be created and register at least one callback.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast1():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast1\")\n\ndef run_on_broadcast2():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(2, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast2\")\n  \n# Create a new event.\nmy_event = Event()\n\n# Register callback functions to event.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast1)\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast2)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the event.\nmy_event.broadcast()\n\n```","signature":"my_event.broadcast()"},"events_event_broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Event Broadcast and Wait\n\nBroadcast event message to run listener functions and wait for all listeners to finish before continuing.\n\n```python\nevent.broadcast_and_wait()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `event.broadcast_and_wait()` command will wait for all listeners to complete before returning. This will pause the code execution in the current function, until all the broadcast listeners have finished.\n\nBefore using this command, a user defined event must be created and register at least one callback.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast1():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast1\")\n\ndef run_on_broadcast2():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(2, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast2\")\n\n# Create a new event.\nmy_event = Event()\n\n# Register callback functions to event.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast1)\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast2)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the event and wait for completion.\nmy_event.broadcast_and_wait()\n\nbrain.screen.set_cursor(3, 1)\nbrain.screen.print(\"Complete\")\n```","signature":"my_event.broadcast_and_wait()"},"events_event_new_event":{"name":"events_event_new_event","markdown":"# New Event\n\nCreate a new event.\n\n```python\nmy_event = Event()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nUsing the above syntax, a new user-defined event can be created before registering callback functions.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast1():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast1\")\n\ndef run_on_broadcast2():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(2, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast2\")\n\n# Create new events.\nmy_event1 = Event()\nmy_event2 = Event()\n\n# Register callback functions to the events.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event1(run_on_broadcast1)\nmy_event2(run_on_broadcast2)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the events.\nmy_event1.broadcast()\nmy_event2.broadcast()\n```","signature":"my_event = Event()"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_down":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_down","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_down(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `optical.gesture_enable()` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gesture_up`\n- `gesture_down`\n- `gesture_left`\n- `gesture_right`\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_gesture_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Down detected!\")\n\n# Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\noptical.gesture_enable()\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.gesture_down(run_on_gesture_detected)\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_down(callback)"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_left":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_left","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_left(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `optical.gesture_enable()` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gesture_up`\n- `gesture_down`\n- `gesture_left`\n- `gesture_right`\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_gesture_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Left detected!\")\n\n# Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\noptical.gesture_enable()\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.gesture_left(run_on_gesture_detected)\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_left(callback)"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_right":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_right","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_right(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `optical.gesture_enable()` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gesture_up`\n- `gesture_down`\n- `gesture_left`\n- `gesture_right`\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_gesture_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Right detected!\")\n\n# Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\noptical.gesture_enable()\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.gesture_right(run_on_gesture_detected)\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_right(callback)"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_up":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_up","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_up(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `optical.gesture_enable()` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gesture_up`\n- `gesture_down`\n- `gesture_left`\n- `gesture_right`\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_gesture_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Up detected!\")\n\n# Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\noptical.gesture_enable()\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.gesture_up(run_on_gesture_detected)\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_up(callback)"},"events_optical_object_detected":{"name":"events_optical_object_detected","markdown":"# Optical Object Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when an object is detected by an Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.object_detected(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Object Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when an object is detected by an Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when an object is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_event():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Object detected!\")\n\n# Register event with a callback function\noptical.object_detected(run_on_event)\n```","signature":"optical.object_detected(callback)"},"events_optical_object_lost":{"name":"events_optical_object_lost","markdown":"# Optical Object Lost\n\nRuns the callback function when a detected object is no longer being detected by an Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.object_lost(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Object Lost` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when an Optical Sensor no longer detects a previously-detected object.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the object is no longer being detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_event():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Object lost!\")\n\n# Register event with a callback function\noptical.object_lost(run_on_event)\n```","signature":"optical.object_lost(callback)"},"events_touch_led_pressed":{"name":"events_touch_led_pressed","markdown":"# TouchLED Pressed\n\nRuns the specified **callback function** when an IQ TouchLED is pressed.\n\n```python\ntouchled.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the TouchLED is pressed. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```python\ndef touchled_pressed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Touch LED pressed\")\n```\n\nThen, the function is passed as the parameter of the `TouchLED Pressed` function call.\n\n```python\ntouchled.pressed(touchled_pressed)\n```\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```python\ndef callback_function():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Pressed\")\n\ntouchled.pressed(callback_function)\n```","signature":"touchled.pressed(callback)"},"events_touch_led_released":{"name":"events_touch_led_released","markdown":"# TouchLED Released\n\nRuns the specified **callback function** when an IQ TouchLED is released.\n\n```python\ntouchled.released(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the TouchLED is released. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```python\ndef touchled_released():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Touch LED released\")\n```\n\nThen, the function is passed as the parameter of the `TouchLED Released` function call.\n\n```python\ntouchled.released(touchled_released)\n```\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```python\ndef callback_function():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Released\")\n\ntouchled.released(callback_function)\n```","signature":"touchled.released(callback)"},"function_name":{"name":"function_name","markdown":"# Functions\n\nFunctions are blocks of code used to perform an action.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a function, create a meaningful function name. This means that the function name should accurately describe what it does.\n\nUse the **keyword** `def` before your function name to define the function.\n\nInclude parentheses `()` enclosing optional parameters after the function name, followed by a colon`:`. Multiple parameters should be separated by commas `(parameter1, parameter2)`.\n\nThe body of the function should be indented four spaces. If there isn't any code for the function to execute, a `pass` should be included in the function definition.\n\n```python\ndef my_function():\n    pass\n```\n\n## Example 1\n\nThis function has no parameters and will print \"VEXcode\" to the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Screen.\n\n```python\ndef print_hello_world():\n    brain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")\n```\n## Example 2\n\nThis function takes one parameter, `name` and will print the value of `name` to the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Screen.\n\n```python\ndef print_name(name):\n    brain.screen.print(name)\n```","signature":"def function_name(parameters):\\n\\tpass"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Clear Line\n\nClears the current row on the VEX IQ Brain's Screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.clear_row()\n```\n\nClears a specified row on the VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.clear_row(ROW)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou can call the `Clear Line` command without any arguments to clear the current row.\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\n`Clear Line` accepts a range of values from **1 to 9** for the row to clear, depending on what font is currently selected.\n\n![row_column_index2](static/help/iq/python/en/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/iq2_row_column_brain2.jpg) \n\n## Example \n\nThis example will print \"Hello\" on row 2, column 1, wait for three seconds, then clear row 2.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.set_cursor(2, 1)\nbrain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\nwait(3, SECONDS)\nbrain.screen.clear_row(2)\n```","signature":"brain.screen.clear_row(ROW)"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Clear Screen\n\nClears the entire VEX IQ Brain's Screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Clear Screen` will not reset the Brain's screen cursor. \n\nUse the `Set Cursor` command to set the Brain's cursor to the desired position.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Hello\", wait one second, and then clear the entire screen before printing \"Goodbye\".\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\nwait(1, SECONDS)\nbrain.screen.clear_screen()\nbrain.screen.print(\"Goodbye\")\n```","signature":"brain.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen_virtual":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen_virtual","markdown":"# Clear All Rows\n \nClears the entire Print Console and resets the cursor to the first row.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n```python\n# Print \"VEXcode IQ\" on the first line, wait 2 seconds, then clear the Print Console\nbrain.screen.print(\"VEXcode IQ\")\nwait(2, SECONDS)\nbrain.screen.clear_screen()\n```","signature":"brain.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Circle\n\nDraws a circle on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.draw_circle(X, Y, RADIUS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain Screen Draw Circle` command requires 3 values:\n\n* **X**: X coordinate of the circle's center\n* **Y**: Y coordinate of the circle's center\n* **RADIUS**: Radius of circle (in pixels)\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/python/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_circle/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\nThe outside line color of the circle is determined by the Brain's `Set Pen Color` command. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the circle is determined by the Brain's `Set Fill Color` command. The default fill color is black.","signature":"brain.screen.draw_circle(X, Y, RADIUS)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_line","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Line\n\nDraws a line on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.draw_line(START_X, START_Y, END_X, END_Y)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain Screen Draw Line` command requires 4 values:\n\n* **START_X**: Beginning X coordinate\n* **START_Y**: Beginning Y coordinate\n* **END_X**: Ending X coordinate\n* **END_Y**: Ending Y coordinate\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/python/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_line/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\nThe line color is determined by the Brain's `Set Pen Color` command. The default line color is white.","signature":"brain.screen.draw_line(START_X, START_Y, END_X, END_Y)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Pixel\n\nDraws a pixel on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.draw_pixel(X, Y)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain Screen Draw Pixel` command requires 2 values:\n\n* **X**: X coordinate\n* **Y**: Y coordinate\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/python/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\nThe pixel color is determined by the Brain's `Set Pen Color` command. The default pixel color is white.","signature":"brain.screen.draw_pixel(X, Y)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Rectangle\n\nDraws a rectangle on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.draw_rectangle(X, Y, WIDTH, HEIGHT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain Screen Draw Rectangle` command requires 4 values:\n\n* **X**: Top Left Corner X coordinate\n* **Y**: Top Left Corner Y coordinate\n* **WIDTH**: Width of the rectangle\n* **HEIGHT**: Height of the rectangle\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/python/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\nThe outside line color of the rectangle is determined by the Brain's `Set Pen Color` command. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the rectangle is determined by the Brain's `Set Fill Color` command. The default fill color is black.","signature":"brain.screen.draw_rectangle(X, Y, WIDTH, HEIGHT)"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line","markdown":"# New Line\n\nSets the print output cursor on the IQ Brain's screen to the next available row.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.next_row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1. The `New Line` command will move the cursor down by a single row on the screen.\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\n![row_column_index2](static/help/iq/python/en/looks_brain_screen_new_line/iq2_row_column_brain2.jpg) \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"First Message\" and then will set the cursor to the next available row before printing \"Second Message\".\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"First Message\")\nbrain.screen.next_row()\nbrain.screen.print(\"Second Message\")\n```\n\n![set_cursor_welcome2](static/help/iq/python/en/looks_brain_screen_new_line/set_cursor_welcome2.png)","signature":"brain.screen.next_row()"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line_virtual":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line_virtual","markdown":"# Next Row\n\nSets the print output cursor of the Print Console to the next line.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.next_row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the print cursor at row 1. The `brain.screen.next_row()` command will move the cursor down by a single line on the Print Console.\n\n---\n\n```python\n# Print \"VEXcode\" on the first line, then \"IQ\" on the next line\nbrain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")\nbrain.screen.next_row()\nbrain.screen.print(\"IQ\")\n```","signature":"brain.screen.new_line()"},"looks_brain_screen_print":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text on the IQ Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Print` command will print data at a cursor location on the screen.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1.\n\n* Print words and numbers: \n`brain.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n\n* Print the reported value from a variable: \n`brain.screen.print(my_variable)`\n\n* Print the reported value from a sensor or device:  \n`brain.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`\n\n## Formatting Values\n\nYou can use either the `%` operator or the `format` function to adjust the precision of a printed value.\n\nWhen displaying values, you can specify how many decimal places to print. For example, if your value is `3.14159265`, but you only want to display `3.14`, you can use either approach below to format it.\n\n### Using the `%` Operator\n\nThe `%` operator can be used with any of the format specifiers listed below to format a floating point value.\n\nA number before the decimal in the format specifier denotes the total number of characters to be printed.\nIf the value being printed is shorter than the total number of characters to be printed, the printed value is padded with blank spaces.\n\n* `%d` - Prints a decimal integer\n* `%f` - Prints a floating point number\n* `%.2f` - Prints a floating point number to two decimal places\n* `%6.2f` - Prints a floating point number with a minimum of six characters and two decimal places\n\nHence, to print `3.14` from `3.14159265`:\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"%.2f\" % 3.14159265)\n```\n\n### Using the `format` Function\n\nThe string `format` function can also be used to format a floating point value.\n\nSimilar to how the `%` operator is used, a format specifier denotes how a value will be formatted. However, the format string does not include the `%` operator, but utilizes `{}` to wrap a format specifier and calls the `format` function with a value to be formatted instead.\n\n* `.d` - Prints a decimal integer\n* `.f` - Prints a floating point number\n* `.2f` - Prints a floating point number to two decimal places\n* `6.2f` - Prints a floating point number with a minimum of six characters and two decimal places\n\nHence, to print `3.14` from `3.14159265`:\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"{0:.2f}\".format(3.14159265))\n```\n\nThe `format` function can also be used to format and print more than one value. The value before the `:` (colon) in the format specifier is used to index a parameter from the `format` function call.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"{0:.2f}, {1:.2f}\".format(1.234, 5.678))\n```\n\nIn the above snippet, the `0` before the `:` in the first format specifier points to the first (zero-index) parameter in the `format` function call - `1.234`.\n\nThe `1` before the `:` in the second format specifier points to the second parameter in the `format` function call - `5.678`.\n\nThis will get printed to the IQ Brain:\n\n```python\n1.23, 5.68\n```","signature":"brain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")"},"looks_brain_screen_print_virtual":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print_virtual","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text to the Print Console.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.print()` command will print data to the Print Console.\n\n* Print words and numbers: \n`brain.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n\n* Print numbers with decimal points:\n```brain.screen.print(\"Timer Value:\", brain.timer.time(SECONDS), precision=2)```\n\n* Print the reported value from a variable: \n`brain.screen.print(my_variable)`\n\n* Print the reported value from a sensor or device:  \n`brain.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`","signature":"brain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")"},"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Set Cursor\n\nSets the cursor location for Brain's `Print` commands.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.set_cursor(ROW, COL)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Set Cursor` command requires 2 parameters:\n\n* **ROW**: Screen row position \n* **COL**: Screen column position\n\nSet the cursor's row and column position to have a `Print` command print at a specific location on the screen.\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\nAccepts a range for **ROW** of **1 to 9**.\n\nAccepts a range for **COL** of **1 to 28**.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the cursor to location row 3 column 5 before printing the text \"VEXcode!\" to the Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.set_cursor(3, 5)\nbrain.screen.print(\"VEXcode!\")\n```\n\n![set_cursor_hello2](static/help/iq/python/en/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/set_cursor_hello2.png)","signature":"brain.screen.set_cursor(ROW, COL)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Fill Color\n\nSets the color that fills in shapes drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.set_fill_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain Screen Set Fill Color` command is used to set the color of the inside of circles and rectangles drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen. \n\nYou can replace the **COLOR** parameter with one of the following options:\n\n* `Color.BLACK`\n* `Color.BLUE`\n* `Color.BLUE_GREEN`\n* `Color.BLUE_VIOLET`\n* `Color.GREEN`\n* `Color.ORANGE`\n* `Color.PURPLE`\n* `Color.RED`\n* `Color.RED_ORANGE`\n* `Color.RED_VIOLET`\n* `Color.VIOLET`\n* `Color.WHITE`\n* `Color.YELLOW`\n* `Color.YELLOW_GREEN`\n* `Color.YELLOW_ORANGE`\n\nThe fill color will be used for any next objects drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.","signature":"brain.screen.set_fill_color(COLOR)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_font":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_font","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Font\n\nSets the style and size of font used on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen when printing numbers or text.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.set_font(FONT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThere are two different types of fonts available on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - each character takes up the same width.\n* Proportional (Prop) - each character takes up different size widths based on the character.\n\nChoose which font type and size to use. You can replace the **FONT** parameter with one of the following font options:\n\n* `FontType.MONO12`\n* `FontType.MONO15`\n* `FontType.MONO20`\n* `FontType.MONO30`\n* `FontType.MONO40`\n* `FontType.MONO60`\n* `FontType.PROP20`\n* `FontType.PROP30`\n* `FontType.PROP40`\n* `FontType.PROP60`\n\nThe new font size will be used for any future text written to the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.","signature":"brain.screen.set_font(FONT)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Pen Color\n\nSets the color of lines drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.set_pen_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain Screen Set Pen Color` command is used to set the color of lines, pixels, and text drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen. \n\nIt can also be used to set the color the outline of circles and rectangles drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\nYou can replace the **COLOR** parameter with one of the following options:\n\n* `Color.BLACK`\n* `Color.BLUE`\n* `Color.BLUE_GREEN`\n* `Color.BLUE_VIOLET`\n* `Color.GREEN`\n* `Color.ORANGE`\n* `Color.PURPLE`\n* `Color.RED`\n* `Color.RED_ORANGE`\n* `Color.RED_VIOLET`\n* `Color.VIOLET`\n* `Color.WHITE`\n* `Color.YELLOW`\n* `Color.YELLOW_GREEN`\n* `Color.YELLOW_ORANGE`\n\nThe pen color will be used for any next objects drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.","signature":"brain.screen.set_pen_color(COLOR)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Pen Width\n\nSets the width of the outline for shapes drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.set_pen_width(WIDTH)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain Screen Set Pen Width` command is used to set the width of the line on the outside of circles and rectangles drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen. \n\nIt accepts integer values for the **WIDTH** parameter, with a larger value equating to a larger width.\n\n![iq2_row_column_brain](static/help/iq/python/en/looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.set_pen_width(WIDTH)"},"looks_color_set_light":{"name":"looks_color_set_light","markdown":"# Set Color Sensor Light\n\nSets the brightness of the VEX IQ Color Sensor's light. \n\n```python\ncolor.set_light(BRIGHTNESS, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Color Sensor has a light source that can be adjusted to help detect the color of an object or a surface.\n\n`Set Color Sensor Light` accepts a range of **0 to 100** for the `BRIGHTNESS` parameter.\n\nThe higher the value is set, the brighter the Color Sensor's light source will shine.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will set the brightness of the Color Sensor to 75%.\n\n```python\ncolor.set_light(75, PERCENT)\n```","signature":"color.set_light(BRIGHTNESS, PERCENT)"},"looks_console_clear_console":{"name":"looks_console_clear_console","markdown":"# Console Clear\n\nClears the Print Console.\n\n```python\nprint(\"\\033[2J\")\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `print` command used with the `\\033[2J` command sequence will clear the Print Console.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will print \"VEXcode\" and then clear the Print Console after 3 seconds.\n\n```python\nprint(\"\\033[31mVEXcode\")\nwait(3, SECONDS)\nprint(\"\\033[2J\")\n```","signature":"print(\"\\033[2J\")"},"looks_console_print":{"name":"looks_console_print","markdown":"# Console Print\n\nPrints values or text to the Print Console.\n\n```python\nprint(\"VEXcode\")\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `print` command will print data at the cursor location on the Print Console.\n\nAll new projects begin with the cursor at row 1.\n\n## Printing Lines\n\nBy default, Python will always add a new line after each `print` command.\n\nTo print multiple values to a single line, you can utilize the `end` parameter.\n\n```python\nprint(\"This text will be \", end=\"\")\nprint(\"printed on the same line\")\n```\n\n## Printing Values\n\nYou can use the Python `format` method to format the values being printed in the print statements.\n\nTo use the `format` method, you must first provide a template string with replacement fields enclosed by a set of curly braces - `{}`.\n\nThen, call the `format` method on the template string. Any parameter(s) passed into the `format` method will be inserted into the replacement fields in sequence (if there are multiple replacement fields).\n\nYou can also provide formatting options into the template string to set the number of decimal places to be printed. Any formatting options must begin with a semicolon - `:`.\n\nIn the example below, the value of the Brain Timer will be inserted into the single replacement field in the template string and printed to two decimal places.\n\n```python\nprint(\"{:.2f}\".format(brain.timer.time(SECONDS)))\n```\n\nSimilarly, the example below will print the row/column position of the Brain Cursor. The number of replacement fields (enclosed by `{}`) must match the number of parameters passed into the `format` method.\n\n```python\n# The value of brain.screen.row() will be passed into the first replacement field\n# The value of brain.screen.column() will be passed into the second replacement field\nprint(\"Row: {:d}, Column: {:d}\".format(brain.screen.row(), brain.screen.column()))\n```\n\nHere is a list of commonly-used format specifiers. Remember that to use a format specifier inside a replacement field (enclosed by `{}`), it must follow a semicolon - `:`.\n\n* `d` - Decimal Integer\n* `f` - Floating Point Number\n* `o` - Octal Integer\n* `s` - String\n\nUsing the Floating Point Number format specifier, `f`, you can also specify how many decimal places to format a number.\n\n* `.2f` - Formats a floating point number with 2 decimal places\n* `.4f` - Formats a floating point number with 4 decimal places\n\n## Printing Colors\n\nYou can use any of the color codes below with a `print` command to set the color of the text being printed.\n\nThe example below will show two ways in which a color sequence command can be used when printing. All color codes will need to be attached to an escape sequence - `\\033`.\n\n* `[31m` - Red\n* `[32m` - Green\n* `[34m` - Blue\n* `[30m` - Black\n* `[37m` - White\n* `[33m` - Yellow\n* `[91m` - Orange\n* `[35m` - Purple\n* `[38;5;207m` - Red Violet\n* `[38;5;213m` - Violet\n* `[38;5;063m` - Blue Violet\n* `[38;5;081m` - Blue Green\n* `[38;5;118m` - Yellow Green\n* `[38;5;190m` - Yellow Orange\n* `[38;5;214m` - Red Orange\n\n```python\n# Using color codes in-line\n# This will print \"VEXcode\" in Red to the Print Console\nprint(\"\\033[31mVEXcode\")\n\n# Using color codes in separate commands\n# Sets the print color for any subsequent prints\nprint(\"\\033[31m\")\nprint(\"VEXcode\")\n```","signature":"print(\"VEXcode\")"},"looks_monitor_sensor":{"name":"looks_monitor_sensor","markdown":"# Monitor Sensor\n\nThe `monitor_sensor()` command is used to add sensors to the monitor console so that the sensor values can monitored. \n\n```don\nmonitor_sensor(\"sensor_name\", \"another_sensor_name\", ...)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo monitor sensor values in the monitor console, use the `monitor_sensor()` function by adding the identifiers of the sensors as string parameters. This function should be called at the start of the program.\n\nBelow is the list of supported sensor identifiers:\n\n- `brain.timer.time`\n- `drivetrain.is_done`\n- `drivetrain.is_moving`\n- `drivetrain.heading`\n- `drivetrain.rotation`\n- `drivetrain.velocity_rpm`\n- `drivetrain.velocity_percent`\n- `arm_motor.is_done`\n- `arm_motor.is_spinning`\n- `arm_motor.position_degrees`\n- `arm_motor.position_turns`\n- `arm_motor.velocity_rpm`\n- `arm_motor.velocity_percent`\n- `intake_motor.is_done`\n- `intake_motor.is_spinning`\n- `intake_motor.position_degrees`\n- `intake_motor.position_turns`\n- `intake_motor.velocity_rpm`\n- `intake_motor.velocity_percent`\n- `intake_bumper.pressing`\n- `front_distance.is_object_detected`\n- `front_distance.object_distance_mm`\n- `front_distance.object_distance_inches`\n- `front_optical.is_near_object`\n- `front_optical.color`\n- `front_optical.brightness`\n- `front_optical.hue`\n\nWhen adding sensor identifiers to the monitor_sensor() command, they have to be added as strings - therefore enclosed with quotation marks:\n\n```don\nmonitor_sensor(\"intake_bumper.pressing\")\n```\nMultiple sensor identifiers, separated by commas, can be added to the monitor_sensor() command:\n\n```don\nmonitor_sensor(front_distance.object_distance_mm”, “drivetrain.rotation”, “brain.timer.time”)\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis code will have the robot spin around and monitor the drivetrain heading and the drivetrain velocity.\n\n```don\ndef main():\n    monitor_sensor(\"drivetrain.heading\", \"drivetrain.velocity_percent\")\n    drivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 10, TURNS)\n```","signature":"monitor_sensor()"},"looks_monitor_variable":{"name":"looks_monitor_variable","markdown":"# Monitor Variable\n\nThe `monitor_variable()` command is used to add variables to the monitor console so that the value of the variables can be monitored.\n\n```don\nmonitor_variable(\"my_variable\", \"my_boolean\", ...)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo add variables to the monitor console, use the `monitor_variable()` command. Add the name of the variable(s) as strings in the command. Only global variables can be monitored with the `monitor_variable()` command.\n\n## Examples\n\nThis example will monitor a variable that increments every 0.5 seconds. It will also print the value to the console.\n\n```don\ncounter = 0\n\ndef main():\n    global counter\n    monitor_variable(\"counter\")\n    while True:\n        counter = counter + 1\n        brain.screen.print(counter)\n        brain.screen.next_row()\n        wait(0.5, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"monitor_variable()"},"looks_touch_led_set_brightness":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_brightness","markdown":"# Set TouchLED Brightness\n\nSets the brightness of an IQ TouchLED.\n\n```python\ntouchled.set_brightness(BRIGHTNESS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Set TouchLED Brightness` accepts a range of **0 to 100** for the `BRIGHTNESS` parameter.\n \n```python\ntouchled.set_brightness(50)\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will illuminate the TouchLED green at 25% brightness.\n\n```python\ntouchled.set_brightness(25)\ntouchled.set_color(Color.GREEN)\n```","signature":"touchled.set_brightness(BRIGHTNESS)"},"looks_touch_led_set_color":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_color","markdown":"# Set TouchLED Color\n\nSets the color of an IQ TouchLED.\n\n```python\ntouchled.set_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReplace the **COLOR** parameter with one of the following options:\n\n- `Color.RED`\n- `Color.GREEN`\n- `Color.BLUE`\n- `Color.WHITE`\n- `Color.YELLOW`\n- `Color.ORANGE`\n- `Color.PURPLE`\n- `Color.RED_VIOLET`\n- `Color.VIOLET`\n- `Color.BLUE_VIOLET`\n- `Color.BLUE_GREEN`\n- `Color.YELLOW_GREEN`\n- `Color.YELLOW_ORANGE`\n- `Color.RED_ORANGE`\n\nTo turn the TouchLED off, set the color to `Color.BLACK`.\n\n```python\ntouchled.set_color(Color.BLACK)\n```","signature":"touchled.set_color(COLOR)"},"looks_touch_led_set_fade":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_fade","markdown":"# Set TouchLED Fade\n\nSets how fast the color of an IQ TouchLED fades between colors.\n\n```python\ntouchled.set_fade(TYPE)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose how fast the TouchLED will fade between colors. Replace **TYPE** with one of the following options:\n\n* **FadeType.SLOW** - The TouchLED will slowly fade to a new color.\n* **FadeType.FAST** - The TouchLED will quickly fade to a new color.\n* **FadeType.OFF** - The TouchLED will change colors instantly.\n\n```python\ntouchled.set_fade(FadeType.SLOW)\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will slowly fade the TouchLED from red to blue.\n\n```python\ntouchled.set_color(Color.RED)\ntouchled.set_fade(FadeType.SLOW)\ntouchled.set_color(Color.BLUE)\n```","signature":"touchled.set_fade(TYPE)"},"motion_motor_set_max_torque":{"name":"motion_motor_set_max_torque","markdown":"# Set Motor Torque\n\nSets the strength of an IQ Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.set_max_torque(AMOUNT, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command accepts a range of **0 to 100** for the **AMOUNT** parameter.\n\nThe `Set Max Torque` command can accept decimals, integers, or numeric values.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the Claw Motor to the 40 degree position with only 20% maximum torque. This allows the claw to grab an object without damaging it with too much force.\n\n```python\nclaw_motor.set_max_torque(20, PERCENT)\nclaw_motor.spin_to_position(40, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_max_torque(50, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor_set_position":{"name":"motion_motor_set_position","markdown":"# Set Motor Position\n\nSets an IQ Motor's or Motor Group's encoder(s) position to the given position value.\n\n```python\nmotor.set_position(VALUE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command can be used to set a Motor or Motor Group's position to a given positional value.\n\nUsually, the `Set Motor Position` command is used to set the position to 0 to reset a Motor or Motor Group's encoder position(s).\n\nThe `Set Motor Position` command accepts **DEGREES** or **TURNS** as valid **UNITS**.","signature":"motor.set_position(0, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_set_stopping":{"name":"motion_motor_set_stopping","markdown":"# Set Motor Stopping\n\nSets the behavior of an IQ Motor or Motor Group once it stops moving.\n\n```python\nmotor.set_stopping(MODE)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `MODE` parameter can be replaced with any of the following options:\n\n* BRAKE: will cause the Motor/Motor Group to come to an immediate stop.\n* COAST: lets the Motor/Motor Group spin gradually to a stop.\n* HOLD: will cause the Motor/Motor Group to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved.\n\nThe stopping behavior set by this command will apply to subsequent Motor/Motor Group `Stop` commands for the entirety of the project, unless otherwise changed.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the Arm Motor spin forward for 2 seconds (to raise the arm) and then will hold its position.\n\n```python\narm_motor.set_stopping(HOLD)\narm_motor.spin(FORWARD)\nwait(2, SECONDS)\narm_motor.stop()\n```","signature":"motor.set_stopping(MODE)"},"motion_motor_set_timeout":{"name":"motion_motor_set_timeout","markdown":"# Set Motor Timeout\n\nSets a time limit for an IQ Motor or Motor Group movement commands.\n\n```python \nmotor.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA Motor or Motor Group's `Set Motor Timeout` command is used to prevent motion commands that do not reach their intended position from preventing subsequent commands from running. \n\nAn example of a Motor not reaching its position is an Arm or Claw that reaches its mechanical limit and cannot complete its movement.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the timeout of the `Spin To Position` command to 2 seconds.\n\nIf the Claw Motor has not reached the position of 270 degrees after 2 seconds, the Claw Motor will stop spinning.\n\n```python\nclaw_motor.set_timeout(2, SECONDS)\nclaw_motor.spin_to_position(270, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)"},"motion_motor_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity","markdown":"# Set Motor Velocity\n\nSets the speed of an IQ Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```python \nmotor.set_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command accepts a range from **-100 to 100** when used with the `PERCENT` parameter or **-127 to 127** when used with `RPM`.\n\nSetting an IQ Motor or Motor Group's velocity to a negative value will cause the Motor/Motor Group to spin in reverse.\n\nSetting the velocity to 0 will prevent the Motor/Motor Group from spinning.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the Arm Motor to spin at 25% speed to the 90 degree position.\n\n```python\narm_motor.set_velocity(25, PERCENT)\narm_motor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_spin":{"name":"motion_motor_spin","markdown":"# Spin \n\nSpins an IQ Motor or Motor Group indefinitely.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which **DIRECTION** the Motor or Motor Group will spin to with either **FORWARD** or **REVERSE** as the parameter.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"motor.spin(DIRECTION)"},"motion_motor_spin_for":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_for","markdown":"# Spin For\n \nThis command spins an IQ Motor or Motor Group for a given amount of degrees or turns.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin_for(DIRECTION, AMOUNT, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which `DIRECTION` the Motor or Motor Group will spin to: **FORWARD** or **REVERSE**.\n\nChoose the `UNIT` of measurement to be either **DEGREES** or **TURNS**.\n\nChoose whether or not this command should be waited on by proceeding commands by setting an optional fourth parameter to either **wait=True** or **wait=False**. \n\n```python\nmotor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\nBy default, this command is a blocking command unless **wait=False** is passed as the fourth parameter.","signature":"motor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_spin_to_position":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_to_position","markdown":"# Spin To Position\n\nSpins an IQ Motor or Motor Group to a given position.\n\n```python \nmotor.spin_to_position(POSITION, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command will tell a Motor or Motor Group to travel to a specific position. Based on the current position of the Motor or Motor Group, `Spin To Position` will determine the direction to rotate the Motor or Motor Group.\n\nChoose the unit of measurement to be either **DEGREES** or **TURNS**.\n\nChoose whether or not this command should be waited on by other commands by changing the optional third parameter to either **wait=True** or **wait=False**.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\nSetting **wait=True** means that proceeding commands will not execute until the motor spin is completed. Conversely, **wait=False** will not wait for it to be completed.  \n\nBy default, this command will have the wait to be set to **True**.","signature":"motor.spin_to_position(POSITION, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_stop":{"name":"motion_motor_stop","markdown":"# Stop Motor\n\nStops an IQ Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.stop()\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows a motor spinning for 3 seconds before stopping.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\nmotor.stop()\n```","signature":"motor.stop()"},"motion_pneumatics_cylinder_extend":{"name":"motion_pneumatics_cylinder_extend","markdown":"# Extend pneumatic cylinder\n\nSets the pneumatic solenoid to extend a specific cylinder.\n\n```cpp\npneumatic_1.extend(CYLINDER1)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `extend pneumatic cylinder` command will control the solenoid to set the airflow within the pneumatic system to extend the specified cylinder's piston.\n\n```cpp\npneumatic_1.extend(CYLINDER1)\n```","signature":"pneumatic_1.extend(CYLINDER1)"},"motion_pneumatics_cylinder_retract":{"name":"motion_pneumatics_cylinder_retract","markdown":"# Retract pneumatic cylinder\n\nSets the pneumatic solenoid to retract a specific cylinder.\n\n```cpp\npneumatic_1.retract(CYLINDER1)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `retract pneumatic cylinder` command will control the solenoid to set the airflow within the pneumatic system to retract the specified cylinder's piston.\n\n```cpp\npneumatic_1.retract(CYLINDER1)\n```","signature":"pneumatic_1.retract(CYLINDER1)"},"motion_pneumatics_pump_off":{"name":"motion_pneumatics_pump_off","markdown":"# Pneumatic Pump Off\n\nSets the pneumatic solenoid to turn the pneumatic pump off.\n\n```cpp\npneumatic_1.pump_off()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **pneumatic pump off** command will control the power to the pump connected to the pneumatic solenoid. Turning the pump off will stop refilling the attached air tank.\n\n```cpp\npneumatic_1.pump_off()\n```","signature":"pneumatic_1.pump_off()"},"motion_pneumatics_pump_on":{"name":"motion_pneumatics_pump_on","markdown":"# Pneumatic Pump On\n\nSets the pneumatic solenoid to turn the pneumatic pump on.\n\n```cpp\npneumatic_1.pump_on()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **pneumatic pump on** command will control the power to the pump connected to the pneumatic solenoid. Turning the pump on will start refilling the attached air tank.\n\n```cpp\npneumatic_1.pump_on()\n```","signature":"pneumatic_1.pump_on()"},"sensing_brain_battery_capacity":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_capacity","markdown":"# Battery Capacity\n\nReports the charge level of the IQ Brain's battery.\n\n```python\nbrain.battery.capacity()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBattery capacity reports a range from **0 to 100** percent.","signature":"brain.battery.capacity()"},"sensing_brain_button_pressing":{"name":"sensing_brain_button_pressing","markdown":"# Brain Button Pressing\n\nReports if the specified button on the VEX IQ Brain is being pressed.\n\n```python\nbrain.button.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReports **True** if the specified Brain button is pressed. Reports **False** if the specified Brain button is not pressed.\n\nAfter `brain.` enter a Brain button to receive the pressed status on.\n\nSupported Brain buttons are as follows:\n\n- `buttonUp` / `buttonLeft`\n- `buttonDown` / `buttonRight`\n- `buttonCheck`\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the VEX IQ robot drive forward.\n\nThen, it will check for a press on the Brain's **buttonUp** and then turn the robot right indefinitely.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n\nwhile True:\n    if brain.buttonUp.pressing():\n        drivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n        break\n```","signature":"brain.button.pressing()"},"sensing_brain_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_column","markdown":"# Screen Cursor Column\n\nReports the column number of the VEX IQ Brain's screen cursor location.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.column()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\nA value ranging from **1 to 28** is reported, depending on what font is currently selected.\n\nThe value of `Screen Cursor Column` increases from left-to-right on the VEX IQ Brain's screen.","signature":"brain.screen.column()"},"sensing_brain_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_row","markdown":"# Screen Cursor Row\n\nReports the row number of the VEX IQ Brain's screen cursor location.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\nThe `Screen Cursor Row` command reports an integer which ranges from **1 to 9** when used with an IQ (2nd generation) Brain, depending on what font is currently selected.\n\nThe value reported by `Screen Cursor Row` increases from top-to-bottom on the VEX IQ Brain's screen cursor location.","signature":"brain.screen.row()"},"sensing_brain_timer_clear":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_clear","markdown":"# Reset Timer\n\nResets the IQ Brain's timer.\n\n```python \nbrain.timer.clear()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Brain's timer begins at the beginning of each project. The `Reset Timer` command can be used to reset the timer value back to 0 seconds.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the timer will be reset before moving the Drivetrain forward for 3 seconds. After 3 seconds has elapsed, the Drivetrain will stop.\n\n```python\nbrain.timer.clear()\nwhile brain.timer.time(SECONDS) <= 3:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"brain.timer.clear()"},"sensing_brain_timer_time":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_time","markdown":"# Timer Value\n\nReports the value of the IQ Brain's timer.\n\n```python\nbrain.timer.time(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe timer starts at 0 seconds when the program starts, and reports the timer's value as a decimal value.\n\nThe **UNITS** parameter accepts either **SECONDS** or **MSEC** (milliseconds) as a valid argument.\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Timer:\", brain.timer.time(SECONDS))\n\n    # A brief wait to print values without distortion or tearing\n    wait(20, MSEC)\n```","signature":"brain.timer.time(UNITS)"},"sensing_bumper_pressing":{"name":"sensing_bumper_pressing","markdown":"# Pressing Bumper\n \nReports if a VEX IQ Bumper is currently being pressed.\n\n```python\nbumper.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Pressing Bumper` reports **True** if the Bumper is being pressed.\n\n`Pressing Bumper` reports **False** if the Bumper is not being pressed.","signature":"bumper.pressing()"},"sensing_color_brightness":{"name":"sensing_color_brightness","markdown":"# Color Brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by a VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n```python\ncolor.brightness()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Color Brightness` reports a range of values from **0 to 100** percent.\n\nA larger amount of light will report a higher value, while a smaller amount of light will report a lower value.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the amount of light detected by a Color Sensor.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"Brightness:\", color.brightness())\n```","signature":"color.brightness()"},"sensing_color_colorname":{"name":"sensing_color_colorname","markdown":"# Color\n\nReports the color currently being detected by a VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n```python\ncolor.color()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCompare the value returned by `Color` to one of the following colors to check if a specific color is being detected:\n \n- `Color.RED`\n- `Color.RED_VIOLET`\n- `Color.VIOLET`\n- `Color.BLUE_VIOLET`\n- `Color.BLUE`\n- `Color.BLUE_GREEN`\n- `Color.GREEN`\n- `Color.YELLOW_GREEN`\n- `Color.YELLOW`\n- `Color.YELLOW_ORANGE`\n- `Color.ORANGE`\n- `Color.RED_ORANGE`\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints \"Red\" to the IQ Brain's screen if a red object is currently being detected by a Color Sensor.\n\n```python\nif color.color() == Color.RED:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Red\")\n```","signature":"color.color()"},"sensing_color_hue":{"name":"sensing_color_hue","markdown":"# Color Hue\n\nReports the hue of the color detected by a VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n```python\ncolor.hue()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Color Hue` reports a range of values from **0 to 360** degrees, which represents the position of the color on the color wheel.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example prints the hue of the color detected by the Color Sensor.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"Hue:\", color.hue())\n```","signature":"color.hue()"},"sensing_color_is_near_object":{"name":"sensing_color_is_near_object","markdown":"# Color Is Near Object\n\nReports if a VEX IQ Color Sensor detects an object or surface.\n\n```python\ncolor.is_near_object()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReports **True** when a Color Sensor detects an object or surface close to the front of the sensor. \n\nReports **False** when a Color Sensor does not detect an object or surface close to the front of the sensor.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints whether an object or surface is being detected by a Color Sensor.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"True\" if color.is_near_object() else \"False\")\n```","signature":"color.is_near_object()"},"sensing_controller_axis_position":{"name":"sensing_controller_axis_position","markdown":"# Controller Axis Position\n\nReports the position of a joystick on the VEX IQ Controller along the specified axis.\n\n```python\ncontroller.axis.position()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Controller Axis Position` reports a range between **-100 to 100**.\n\n`Controller Axis Position` will report **0** when a joystick axis is centered.\n\nChoose which Controller axis to report.\n\n* `axisA` - left joystick (up and down)\n* `axisB` - left joystick (left and right)\n* `axisC` - right joystick (left and right)\n* `axisD` - right joystick (up and down)\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will print the position of the Controller's A axis to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"AxisA:\", controller.axisA.position())\n\n    # Brief wait to prevent print distortion or tearing\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"controller.axis.position()"},"sensing_controller_button_pressing":{"name":"sensing_controller_button_pressing","markdown":"# Controller Button Pressing\n\nReports if the specified button on the VEX IQ's Controller is being pressed.\n\n```python\ncontroller.button.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller button to detect a press on:\n\n- `buttonEUp`\n- `buttonEDown`\n- `buttonFUp`\n- `buttonFDown`\n- `buttonLUp`\n- `buttonLDown`\n- `buttonRUp`\n- `buttonRDown`\n- `buttonL3`\n- `buttonR3`\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/python/en/sensing_controller_button_pressing/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n`Controller Button Pressing` reports **True** if the specified Controller button is being pressed.\n\n`Controller Button Pressing` reports **False** if the specified Controller button is not being pressed.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below drives the VEX IQ robot forward. If the Controller's E Up button is pressed, the robot will then stop driving.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n\nwhile True:\n    if controller.buttonEUp.pressing():\n        drivetrain.stop()\n        break\n```","signature":"controller.button.pressing()"},"sensing_distance_distance":{"name":"sensing_distance_distance","markdown":"# Distance From\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from a VEX IQ Distance Sensor (1st generation).\n\n```python\ndistance.distance(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance From` reports a range of values between **24 to 1000** mm (millimeters) or **1 to 40** in (inches).\n\nSpecify whether the value returned by `Distance From` is reported in **inches** or **mm** (millimeters) by replacing the **UNITS** parameter with either **INCHES** or **MM**, respectively.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints to an IQ Brain's screen if an object or surface is detected within 100 mm.\n\n```python\nif distance.distance(MM) < 100:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Detected\")\n```","signature":"distance.distance(UNITS)"},"sensing_distance_found_object":{"name":"sensing_distance_found_object","markdown":"# Distance Found Object\n\nReports if a VEX IQ Distance Sensor (1st generation) detects an object within its field of view. \n\n```python\ndistance.is_object_detected()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReports **True** when a Distance Sensor detects an object or surface within its field of view.\n\nReports **False** when a Distance Sensor does not detect an object or surface.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints whether the Distance Sensor detects an object or surface in its range.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"True\" if distance.is_object_detected() else \"False\")\n```","signature":"distance.found_object()"},"sensing_distance_is_object_detected":{"name":"sensing_distance_is_object_detected","markdown":"# Distance Object Detected\n\nReports if a VEX IQ Distance Sensor (2nd generation) detects an object or surface in its range.\n\n```python\ndistance.is_object_detected()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance Object Detected` returns **True** if an object or surface is detected in its range, and **False** if not.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints \"True\" to a VEX IQ Brain's screen if an object or surface is detected by a Distance Sensor.\n\n```python\nif dstance.is_object_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"True\")\n```","signature":"distance.is_object_detected()"},"sensing_distance_object_distance":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Distance Object Distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object or surface from a VEX IQ Distance Sensor (2nd generation).\n\n```python\ndistance.object_distance(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance Object Distance` accepts **MM** or **INCHES** as the **UNITS** parameter and reports a range from **20 to 2000** mm (millimeters) or approximately **0.8 to 79.0** inches.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints to a VEX IQ Brain's screen if an object or surface is detected within 100 mm.\n\n```python\nif distance.object_distance(MM) < 100:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Detected\")\n```","signature":"distance.object_distance(UNITS)"},"sensing_distance_object_size":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_size","markdown":"# Distance Object Size\n\nReports an estimation of the detected object's size.\n\n```python\ndistance.object_size()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance Object Size` can be used to approximately determine if a detected object is of a certain size.\n\nThere are three defined sizes that can be used for comparison:\n\n- ObjectSizeType.SMALL\n- ObjectSizeType.MEDIUM\n- ObjectSizeType.LARGE\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints \"Large!\" to a VEX IQ Brain's screen if a large object is detected by an IQ Distance Sensor (2nd generation).\n\n```python\nif distance.object_size() == ObjectSizeType.LARGE:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Large!\")\n```","signature":"distance.object_size()"},"sensing_distance_object_velocity":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Distance Object Velocity\n\nReports the velocity of a detected object in m/s.\n\n```python\ndistance.object_velocity()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance Object Velocity` reports the current velocity of an object in m/s (meters per second).\n\nThe velocity of a detected object will change when the object is moving while in the range of an IQ Distance Sensor (2nd generation).\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"Velocity:\", distance.object_velocity())\n```","signature":"distance.object_velocity()"},"sensing_drivetrain_current":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_current","markdown":"# Drive Current\n\nReports the amount of current that the Drivetrain is currently using.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.current(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drive Current` reports a range from **0.0 to 2.5** when **CurrentUnits.AMP** is passed as the **UNITS** parameter.","signature":"drivetrain.current(UNITS)"},"sensing_drivetrain_heading":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_heading","markdown":"# Drive Heading\n \nReports the direction that the Drivetrain is facing by using the Gyro or Inertial Sensor's current angular position.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDrive heading reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**.\n\nWhen the Drivetrain is configured with a Gyro Sensor, the `Drive Heading` command reports an increase in heading when rotating counter-clockwise.\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor, the `Drive Heading` command reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.","signature":"drivetrain.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_done":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_done","markdown":"# Drive Is Done\n\nReports if the Drivetrain has completed its movement.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.is_done()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drive Is Done` reports **True** when the robot's Drivetrain has completed its movement.\n\n`Drive Is Done` reports **False** when the robot's Drivetrain is still moving.","signature":"drivetrain.is_done()"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving","markdown":"# Drive Is Moving\n \nReports if the Drivetrain is currently moving.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.is_moving()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drive Is Moving` reports **True** when the Drivetrain's motors are moving.\n\n`Drive Is Moving` reports **False** when the Drivetrain's motors are stopped.\n\n**Note:** This command will always return **false** if the Drivetrain is moving because of a `drivetrain.drive` or `drivetrain.turn` command (which do *not* specify a set distance to drive).","signature":"drivetrain.is_moving()"},"sensing_drivetrain_rotation":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_rotation","markdown":"# Drive Rotation\n \nReports the Drivetrain's angle of rotation when configured with a Gyro or Inertial Sensor.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen configured with a Gyro Sensor, the Drivetrain's `Drive Rotation` command reports an increasingly **positive** value when the Drivetrain turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\nConversely, when configured with an Inertial Sensor, `Drive Rotation` reports an increasingly **positive** value when the Drivetrain turns in the **clockwise** direction.","signature":"drivetrain.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_drivetrain_velocity":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_velocity","markdown":"# Drive Velocity\n \nReports the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.velocity(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drive Velocity` returns a decimal value representing the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\nAcceptable `UNITS` are **PERCENT** and **RPM**.\n\nIf the provided `UNITS` parameter is **PERCENT**, the reported values ranges between **-100 to 100**.\n\nAlternatively, if the provided `UNITS` is **RPM**, the reported values range between **-127 to 127**.","signature":"drivetrain.velocity(UNITS)"},"sensing_gps_heading_virtual":{"name":"sensing_gps_heading_virtual","markdown":"# GPS Heading\n\nReports the heading that a robot is currently facing based on a GPS Sensor's readings from the VEX GPS Field Code.\n\n```python\ngps.heading()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.heading()` command reports a range of heading values from **0.00** to **359.99** degrees, increasing in value when a GPS Sensor is rotated clockwise.\n\nBy default, a GPS Sensor should be mounted facing behind a robot. Then, for example, if the GPS Sensor is facing the South wall as defined by the VEX GPS Field Code, the reported heading will be **0.00** degrees, which is the heading that the front of the robot is facing.\n\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below uses the `gps.heading()` command to stop the Drivetrain's turn when the reported GPS Sensor heading is more than or equal to 180 degrees.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(25, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n\nwhile gps.heading() < 180:\n    wait(5, MSEC)\n\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"gps.heading()"},"sensing_gps_xposition_virtual":{"name":"sensing_gps_xposition_virtual","markdown":"# GPS X Position\n\nReports the X positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\n```python\ngps.x_position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.x_position()` command reports the current X positional offset of the V5 robot's turning reference (midpoint between the two front wheels) relative to the center of a field.\n\nValues can be reported in mm or inches, depending on whether **MM** or **INCHES** is passed in the `UNITS` parameter.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Print the current X position\nbrain.screen.print(\"GPS X Position (MM): \", gps.x_position(MM))\n```","signature":"gps.x_position(MM)"},"sensing_gps_yposition_virtual":{"name":"sensing_gps_yposition_virtual","markdown":"# GPS Y Position\n\nReports the Y positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\n```python\ngps.y_position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.y_position()` command reports the current Y positional offset of the V5 robot's turning reference (midpoint between the two front wheels) relative to the center of a field.\n\nValues can be reported in mm or inches, depending on whether **MM** or **INCHES** is passed in the `UNITS` parameter.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Print the current Y position\nbrain.screen.print(\"GPS Y Position (MM): \", gps.y_position(MM))\n```","signature":"gps.y_position(MM)"},"sensing_gyro_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_calibrate","markdown":"# Gyro Calibrate\n\nCalibrates a VEX IQ Gyro Sensor to reduce the amount of drift generated by the Gyro Sensor.\n\n```python\ngyro.calibrate(TYPE)\n```\n\nDrifting occurs when the Gyro Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Gyro Sensor must remain still during the calibration process.\n\nThe **TYPE** parameter can be replaced with any of the following options to set the calibration duration of the Gyro Sensor:\n\n- **GyroCalibrationType.NORMAL** will calibrate the Gyro Sensor for 2 seconds\n- **GyroCalibrationType.SLOW** will calibrate the Gyro Sensor for 4 seconds\n- **GyroCalibrationType.EXTENDED** will calibrate the Gyro Sensor for 8 seconds","signature":"gyro.calibrate(TYPE)"},"sensing_gyro_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Gyro Heading\n\nReports a VEX IQ Gyro Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```python\ngyro.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Gyro Heading` reports a range of values from **0.00 to 359.99**.\n\nThe `Gyro Heading` command reports an increase in heading when rotating **counter-clockwise**.\n\nThe `Gyro Heading` command reports a decrease in heading when rotating **clockwise**.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the heading of the Gyro Sensor to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn(LEFT)\n\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Heading:\", gyro.heading(DEGREES))\n\n    # Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"gyro.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Gyro Rate\n\nReports a VEX IQ Gyro Sensor's rate of angular velocity.\n\n```python\ngyro.rate()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Gyro Rate` reports a range of values between **0 to 249.99** in degrees per second (DPS).","signature":"gyro.rate()"},"sensing_gyro_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Gyro Rotation\n\nReports a VEX IQ Gyro Sensor's current rotation in degrees.\n\n```python\ngyro.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Gyro Rotation` reports an increasing value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n`Gyro Rotation` reports a decreasing value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the rotation of the Gyro Sensor to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn(LEFT)\n\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Rotation:\", gyro.rotation(DEGREES))\n\n    # Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"gyro.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_heading","markdown":"# Gyro Set Heading\n\nSets a VEX IQ Gyro Sensor's current heading to the specified heading.\n\n```python\ngyro.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Gyro Set Heading` can be used to set the gyro's position to a heading in the range of **0 to 359.99** degrees. \n\nThis command is typically used to reset the orientation of the gyro when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`Gyro Set Heading` can accept decimal or integer inputs.\n\n## Example\n\nThe below snippet sets the Gyro Sensor's current heading to 0 degrees.\n\n```python\ngyro.set_heading(0, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"gyro.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_rotation","markdown":"# Gyro Set Rotation\n\nSets a VEX IQ Gyro Sensor's current angle of rotation to the specified rotation. \n\n```python\ngyro.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Gyro Set Rotation` command can be used to set a Gyro Sensor's angle of rotation to any given positive (counter-clockwise increasing) or negative (clockwise decreasing) value.\n\n`Gyro Set Rotation` accepts a range of any positive or negative decimal or integer as the specified **ROTATION**.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below sets the rotation of the Gyro Sensor to -45 degrees.\n\n```python\ngyro.set_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"gyro.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Inertial Acceleration\n\nReports the acceleration value from one of the axes (x, y, or z) on the VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.  \n\n```python\nbrain_inertial.acceleration(AXIS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReplace the **AXIS** parameter with one of the following options to get the acceleration values along the selected axis:\n\n* **AxisType.XAXIS**: reports acceleration of an Inertial Sensor's **forward to backward** movements\n* **AxisType.YAXIS**: reports acceleration of an Inertial Sensor's **side to side** movements\n* **AxisType.ZAXIS**: reports acceleration of an Inertial Sensor's **up to down** movements\n\n`Inertial Acceleration` returns a decimal value that ranges from **-4.0 to 4.0** Gs.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints an Inertial Sensor's acceleration values to the VEX IQ Brain in a loop.\n\n```python\n# Set a smaller font to ensure lines fit when printed\nbrain.screen.set_font(FontType.MONO12)\n\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    \n    # X Axis\n    brain.screen.print(\"X:\", brain_inertial.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS))\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n    \n    # Y Axis\n    brain.screen.print(\"Y:\", brain_inertial.acceleration(AxisType.YAXIS))\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n    \n    # Z Axis\n    brain.screen.print(\"Z:\", brain_inertial.acceleration(AxisType.ZAXIS))\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n\n    # Brief wait to prevent tearing when printing values\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"inertial.acceleration(AXIS)"},"sensing_inertial_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_calibrate","markdown":"# Inertial Calibrate\n\nCalibrates a VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor to reduce the amount of drift generated.\n\n```python\nbrain_inertial.calibrate()\n```\n\nDrifting occurs when the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not physically moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor must remain still during the calibration process. The calibration process will take approximately 2 seconds to complete.","signature":"inertial.calibrate()"},"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Inertial Gyro Rate\n\nGets the rate of rotation for the specified axis (x, y, or z) on a VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n```python\nbrain_inertial.gyro_rate(AXIS, VelocityUnits.DPS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReplace the **AXIS** parameter with one of the following options to get the gyro rate along an axis on the Inertial Sensor:\n\n* **AxisType.XAXIS**: reports rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the X-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* **AxisType.YAXIS**: reports rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Y-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* **AxisType.ZAXIS**: reports rotations when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Z-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n`Inertial Gyro Rate` is used to return a range from **-1000.0 to 1000.0** in dps (degrees per second).","signature":"inertial.gyro_rate(AXIS, VelocityUnits.DPS)"},"sensing_inertial_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_heading","markdown":"# Inertial Heading\n\nReports a VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```python\nbrain_inertial.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Inertial Heading` command reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n`Inertial Heading` reports a range of values from **0.00 to 359.99** degrees.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below turns a Drivetrain until the Inertial Sensor's heading value is more than 180 degrees before stopping.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\nwhile not brain_inertial.heading(DEGREES) > 180:\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"inertial.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_orientation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Inertial Orientation\n\nGets an orientation angle of the VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n```python\nbrain_inertial.orientation(TYPE, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe orientation reported is determined by the selected axis (x, y, or z). Replace the **TYPE** parameter with one of the following options:\n\n* **OrientationType.PITCH**: represents **pitch**, which reports a value between -90 to +90 degrees.\n* **OrientationType.ROLL**: represents **roll**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n* **OrientationType.YAW**: represents **yaw**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n\n---\n\nPitch is the rotation around the side to side axis.\n\n![IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Pitch](static/help/iq/python/en/sensing_inertial_orientation/IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Pitch.png)\n\nRoll is the rotation around the front to back axis.\n\n![IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Roll](static/help/iq/python/en/sensing_inertial_orientation/IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Roll.png)\n\nYaw is rotation around the vertical axis.\n\n![IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Yaw](static/help/iq/python/en/sensing_inertial_orientation/IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Yaw.png)","signature":"inertial.orientation(TYPE, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_rotation","markdown":"# Inertial Rotation\n\nReports a VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n```python\nbrain_inertial.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Inertial Rotation` command reports an increasingly **positive** value when the Inertial Sensor turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\n`Inertial Rotation` reports an increasingly **negative** value when the Inertial Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below turns a Drivetrain until the Inertial Sensor's rotation value is more than 180 degrees before stopping.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\nwhile not brain_inertial.rotation(DEGREES) > 180:\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"inertial.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_heading","markdown":"# Inertial Set Heading\n\nSets a VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor's current heading position to a specified heading.\n\n```python\nbrain_inertial.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Inertial Set Heading` can be used to set the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor's position to any clockwise-positive heading. This command is typically used to reset the orientation of the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`Inertial Set Heading` accepts a range of **0.0 to 359.99** for the **HEADING** parameter.","signature":"inertial.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_rotation","markdown":"# Inertial Set Rotation\n\nSets a VEX IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor's angle of rotation to a specified rotation.\n\n```python\nbrain_inertial.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Inertial Set Rotation` command can be used to set the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor's angle of rotation to any given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.","signature":"inertial_set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)"},"sensing_motor_current":{"name":"sensing_motor_current","markdown":"# Motor Current\n\nReports the amount of current an IQ Motor or Motor Group is using.\n\n```python\nmotor.current(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor Current` reports a range from **0.0 to 2.5** when **CurrentUnits.AMP** is passed as the **UNITS** parameter.","signature":"motor.current(UNITS)"},"sensing_motor_is_done":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor Is Done \n\nReports if an IQ Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n```python\nmotor.is_done()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor Is Done` reports **True** when the selected Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n`Motor Is Done` reports **False** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is still moving.","signature":"motor.is_done()"},"sensing_motor_is_spinning":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor Is Spinning\n\nReports if an IQ Motor or Motor Group is currently spinning.\n\n```python\nmotor.is_spinning()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor Is Spinning` reports **True** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is still moving.\n\n`Motor Is Spinning` reports **False** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is stopped.\n\n**Note:** This command will always return **false** if the Motor/Motor Group is spinning as a result of a previous `motor.spin` command (which does *not* specify a set distance to spin).\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will print whether the ArmMotor is still spinning to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```python\narm_motor.spin_for(FORWARD, 270, DEGREES, wait=False)\n\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"ArmMotor is Spinning:\", \"TRUE\" if arm_motor.is_spinning() else \"FALSE\")\n\n    # Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n    wait(20, MSEC);\n```","signature":"motor.is_spinning()"},"sensing_motor_position":{"name":"sensing_motor_position","markdown":"# Motor Position\n\nReports the current rotational position of the selected IQ Motor or the first motor of the selected Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor Position` reports the position of an IQ Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group.\n\nAcceptable values for `UNITS` are: **DEGREES** or **TURNS**.","signature":"motor.position(UNITS)"},"sensing_motor_velocity":{"name":"sensing_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Motor Velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of an IQ Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.velocity(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMotor velocity reports a range from **-100 to 100** when **PERCENT** is passed as the **UNITS** parameter, or **-127 to 127** if **RPM** is passed.","signature":"motor.velocity(UNITS)"},"sensing_optical_brightness":{"name":"sensing_optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical Brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by a VEX IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.brightness()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical Brightness` reports a range of values from **0 to 100** percent.\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"Brightness:\", optical.brightness())\n```","signature":"optical.brightness()"},"sensing_optical_color":{"name":"sensing_optical_color","markdown":"# Optical Color\n\nReturns the color detected by a VEX IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.color()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Color` command returns the closest color match base on the hue of a detected object.\n\nThe following colors can be used as a comparison to the color detected by an IQ Optical Sensor:\n\n- `Color.RED`\n- `Color.GREEN`\n- `Color.BLUE`\n- `Color.YELLOW`\n- `Color.ORANGE`\n- `Color.PURPLE`\n- `Color.CYAN`\n\n## Example\n\nThe example prints to a VEX IQ Brain's screen if a red object is detected by an Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\nif optical.color() == Color.RED:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Red!\")\n```","signature":"optical.color()"},"sensing_optical_gesture_detected":{"name":"sensing_optical_gesture_detected","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nReports detected gesture data from an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.get_gesture()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command returns an object with gesture information. To check the type of the detected gesture, access the `type` property on the returned object.\n\n```python\noptical.get_gesture().type\n```\n\nBefore using any IQ Optical Sensor gesture commands, an IQ Optical Sensor must be correctly set to detect gestures with the `optical.gesture_enable()` command.\n\nBelow are the gestures that an IQ Optical Sensor can detect:\n\n- `GestureType.UP`\n- `GestureType.DOWN`\n- `GestureType.LEFT`\n- `GestureType.RIGHT`\n\n## Example\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set an IQ Optical Sensor to detect gestures before checking for gestures.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_enable()\nwhile optical.get_gesture().type != GestureType.UP:\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\nbrain.screen.print(\"Up!\")\n```","signature":"optical.get_gesture()"},"sensing_optical_hue":{"name":"sensing_optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical Hue\n\nReports the hue of the object detected by a VEX IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.hue()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical Hue` reports a range of values from **0 to 359**, which represents the location of the detected color on a color wheel.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.print(\"Hue: \", optical.hue())\n```","signature":"optical.hue()"},"sensing_optical_is_near_object":{"name":"sensing_optical_is_near_object","markdown":"# Optical Is Near Object\n\nReports if a VEX IQ Optical Sensor detects an object in its range.\n\n```python\noptical.is_near_object()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical Is Near Object` returns **True** if an object is detected, and returns **False** otherwise.\n\nIt should be used to check if an object is close to the IQ Optical Sensor so that the color readings from the Optical Sensor's `Color` command is accurate.\n\n```python\nif optical.is_near_object() and optical.color() == Color.Red:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Red object!\")\n```","signature":"optical.is_near_object()"},"sensing_optical_set_light":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light","markdown":"# Set Optical Light\n\nSets the light on a VEX IQ Optical Sensor to **on** or **off**.\n\n```python\noptical.set_light(STATE)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Set Optical Light` allows you to turn the Optical Sensor's light **on** or **off**. The light lets the sensor see objects if it is looking at an object in a dark area.\n\nTo turn the light **on** you pass `LedStateType.ON` as the **STATE** parameter.\n\n```\noptical.set_light(LedStateType.ON)\n```\n\nTo turn the light **off** you pass `LedStateType.OFF` as the **STATE** parameter.\n\n```\noptical.set_light(LedStateType.OFF)\n```","signature":"optical.set_light(STATE)"},"sensing_optical_set_light_power":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Set Optical Light Power\n\nSets the light power of a VEX IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.set_light_power(POWER, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Set Optical Light Power` will change the brightness of the light on an Optical Sensor. \n\nThe command accepts a range of **0 to 100** percent for the **POWER** parameter, and **PERCENT** as the unit. If the light is off, this command will turn the light on.","signature":"optical.set_light_power(POWER, PERCENT)"},"sensing_optical_set_mode_disable":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_mode_disable","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Disable\n\nSets an IQ Optical Sensor to detect colors.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_disable()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Disable` command allows you to set an IQ Optical Sensor to detect colors.\n\nBy default, an IQ Optical Sensor will be set to detect colors.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set an IQ Optical Sensor to detect colors after checking for gestures.\n\n```python\n# Detect gestures\noptical.gesture_enable()\nwhile optical.get_gesture().type != GestureType.UP:\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\nbrain.screen.print(\"Up!\")\n\nwait(1, SECONDS)\n\n# Detect colors\noptical.gesture_disable()\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    if optical.color() == Color.RED:\n        brain.screen.print(\"Red Object!\")\n    else:\n        brain.screen.print(\"Not Red Object!\")\n    wait(0.02, SECONDS)\n\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_disable()"},"sensing_optical_set_mode_enable":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_mode_enable","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Enable\n\nSets an IQ Optical Sensor to detect gestures.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_enable()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Enable` command allows you to set an IQ Optical Sensor to detect gestures.\n \nBy default, an IQ Optical Sensor will be set to detect colors.\n\nBefore using any IQ Optical Sensor gesture commands, an IQ Optical Sensor must be correctly set to detect gestures.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set an IQ Optical Sensor to detect gestures before checking for gestures.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_enable()\nwhile optical.get_gesture().type != GestureType.UP:\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\nbrain.screen.print(\"Up!\")\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_enable()"},"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled":{"name":"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled","markdown":"# Controller Enable/Disable\n\nEnables Controller-configured actions from the Devices menu.\n\n```python\nremote_control_code_enabled = True\n```\n\nDisables Controller-configured actions from the Devices menu.\n\n```python\nremote_control_code_enabled = False\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose to either enable or disable the configured Controller actions. \n\nBy default, the Controller is enabled in every project.","signature":"remote_control_code_enabled"},"sensing_touchled_pressing":{"name":"sensing_touchled_pressing","markdown":"# TouchLED Pressing\n\nReports if a VEX IQ TouchLED is currently being pressed.\n\n```python\ntouchled.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReports **True** if the selected TouchLED is being pressed. Reports **False** if the selected TouchLED is not being pressed.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below sets the TouchLED to red. When the TouchLED is pressed, its color is set to green.\n\n```python\ntouchled.set_color(Color.RED)\n\nwhile not touchled.pressing():\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS);\n\ntouchled.set_color(Color.GREEN)\n```","signature":"touchled.pressing()"},"sensing_vision_largest_object":{"name":"sensing_vision_largest_object","markdown":"# Largest Object\n\nReports information about the largest detected object from a VEX Vision Sensor.\n\n```python\nvision.largest_object()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nConfigure the Vision Sensor by adding signatures / codes.\n\nA call to the Vision Sensor's `Take Snapshot` command is then required to capture an image in the Vision Sensor prior to using the `Largest Object` command.\n\nThe example below will print some information about a detected object onto an IQ Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n\n    # Take a snapshot with the Vision Sensor with the specified signature and \n    # store the object data into a variable\n    vision_object = vision.take_snapshot(signature)\n\n    # Check the variable to see if a valid object was detected when the snapshot\n    # was captured. If yes, print the data\n    if vision_object is not None:\n        brain.screen.print(\"Center X:\", vision.largest_object().centerX)\n        brain.screen.next_row()\n\n        brain.screen.print(\"Center Y:\", vision.largest_object().centerY)\n        brain.screen.next_row()\n\n        # Take a new snapshot every 0.2 seconds\n        wait(0.2, SECONDS)\n    else:\n        brain.screen.print(\"No Object Found\")\n```\n\nThe following is a list of properties that can be accessed on the object returned by the `Largest Object` command:\n\n- `id` - A unique ID assigned to each object by the Vision Sensor\n- `originX` - The top left X position of the object\n- `originY` - The top left Y position of the object\n- `centerX` - The center X position of the object\n- `centerY` - The center Y position of the object\n- `width` - The width of the object\n- `height` - The height of the object\n- `angle` - The angle of the object\n- `exists` - If the Vision Sensor detects the object or not","signature":"vision.largest_object()"},"sensing_vision_take_snapshot":{"name":"sensing_vision_take_snapshot","markdown":"# Snapshot\n\nTakes a snapshot from a VEX Vision Sensor.\n\n```python\nvision.take_snapshot(SIGNATURE)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe snapshot command will capture the current image from a Vision Sensor to be processed and analyzed for color signatures and codes.\n\nTypically, a snapshot is required first before using any other Vision Sensor commands.","signature":"vision.take_snapshot(SIGNATURE)"},"sound_play_note":{"name":"sound_play_note","markdown":"# Play Note\n\nPlays the selected musical note.\n\n```python\nbrain.play_note(OCTAVE, NOTE, DURATION)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose an octave to replace the **OCTAVE** parameter. The lowest is 1 and the highest is 7.\n\n*Note: Octave is currently unsupported on IQ (2nd Generation) Brains*\n\nChoose a note to replace the **NOTE** parameter:\n\n- 0 (C)\n- 1 (D)\n- 2 (E)\n- 3 (F)\n- 4 (G)\n- 5 (A)\n- 6 (B)\n\nChoose a duration for the note to play in milliseconds. You can use of the established options below for the **DURATION** parameter:\n\n- 1000 (whole note plays for 1 second)\n- 500 (half note plays for 0.5 seconds)\n- 250 (quarter note plays for 0.25 seconds)\n\nAlternatively, you can also use a custom duration in the range of **0 to 1000** milliseconds.\n\nOnce a musical note starts playing, the proceeding command will begin executing immediately.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will play a Middle C note for 1 second.\n\n```python\nbrain.play_note(4, 0, 1000)\n```","signature":"brain.play_note(OCTAVE, NOTE, DURATION)"},"sound_play_sound":{"name":"sound_play_sound","markdown":"# Play Sound\n\nPlays the specified sound effect.\n\n```python\nbrain.play_sound(SOUND)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReplace the **SOUND** parameter with one of the following sounds to play:\n- `SoundType.SIREN`\n- `SoundType.WRONG_WAY`\n- `SoundType.WRONG_WAY_SLOW`\n- `SoundType.FILLUP`\n- `SoundType.HEADLIGHTS_ON`\n- `SoundType.HEADLIGHTS_OFF`\n- `SoundType.TOLLBOOTH`\n- `SoundType.ALARM`\n- `SoundType.TADA`\n- `SoundType.DOOR_CLOSE`\n- `SoundType.RATCHET`\n- `SoundType.WRENCH`\n- `SoundType.SIREN2`\n- `SoundType.RATCHET2`\n- `SoundType.ALARM2`\n- `SoundType.POWER_DOWN`\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below plays the siren sound.\n\n```python\nbrain.play_sound(SoundType.SIREN)\n```\n\nOnce a sound effect starts playing, the proceeding command will begin executing immediately.","signature":"brain.play_sound(SOUND)"},"variables_my_2d_list":{"name":"variables_my_2d_list","markdown":"# 2D List Variable\n\n2D list variables are used to store lists with multiple rows and columns.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a 2D list variable, create a unique and meaningful variable name. This means that the variable name should accurately describe the nature of its values.\n\nFor example, a 2D list variable name `coordinates`  can be used to store multiple sets of coordinate values.\n\nDeclare this list using a single equal symbol `=` after your list name followed by square brackets `[ ]`.\n\nInside these square brackets, insert multiple sets of square brackets, separated by a comma, like so: `[[ ], [ ]]`. More than two sets of square brackets can be nested within the outer-most set of square brackets.\n\nInclude values that are separated with a comma or `,` in their respective brackets. If the variable is storing strings, place the comma outside of the enclosing `\" \"`.\n\nEach inner set of brackets represents a row of list items. The index of the item within the row represents a column of the 2D list.\n\nTo access the value of within a 2D list, use the name of the list, immediately followed by two indexes enclosed in square brackets. The first index references the row, while the second index references the column in the 2D list. Keep in mind that array indexes begin at 0, not 1.\n\nFor example, given a 2D list `coordinates = [[X1, Y1], [X2, Y2]]`, the expression `coordinates[0][0]` will return `X1`. \n\n## Example 1\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_list being assigned two separate lists of colors.\n\n```python\nmy_list = [[\"Green\", \"Red\", \"Blue\"], [\"Black\", \"Yellow\", \"Orange\"]]\n```\n\n## Example 2\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_list being assigned two separate lists of numbers.\n\n```python\nmy_list = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]\n```","signature":"my_2d_list = [\\n\\t[0,0,0],\\n\\t[0,0,0],\\n\\t[0,0,0]\\n]"},"variables_my_boolean":{"name":"variables_my_boolean","markdown":"# Boolean Variable\n\nBoolean variables can hold either **True** or **False** values.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a boolean variable, create a unique and meaningful variable name. This means that the name of the variable should accurately describe the value that it is storing.\n\nFor example, a variable `pressed` should be used to store the value of whether a button is pressed.\n\nDeclare this variable with a equal symbol `=` following the Boolean name. Its value can either be `True` or `False`.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example assigns a value `True` to a `my_boolean` variable.\n\n```python\nmy_variable = True\n```","signature":"my_boolean = True"},"variables_my_list":{"name":"variables_my_list","markdown":"# List Variable\n\nList variables are used to store multiple values.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a list variable, create a meaningful variable name. This means that the variable name should accurately describe the nature of its values.\n\nFor example, a list variable `colors` can be used to store multiple color values.\n\nTo assign a list of values to a list variable, use the `=` operator, followed by comma-separated values enclosed in a set of square brackets, `[ ]`.\n\nIf the values are numbers, the separating commas should come right after each value.\n\n`my_number_list = [1, 2, 3]`\n\nIf the values are strings, the commas should go outside of the `\" \"`.\n\n`my_string_list = [\"Hello\", \"World\"]`\n\nTo access a specific value in the list variable, enter the name of the list variable, immediately followed by an index enclosed by a set of square brackets. Keep in mind that the index of an array starts at 0, not 1.\n\nFor example, `my_string_list[0]` will return the value `\"Hello\"`.\n\n## Example 1\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_list being assigned the string values of several colors.\n\n```python\nmy_list = [\"Green\", \"Red\", \"Blue\"]\n```\n\n## Example 2\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_list being assigned several numbers.\n\n```python\nmy_list = [1, 2, 3]\n```","signature":"my_list = [0, 0, 0]"},"variables_my_number":{"name":"variables_my_number","markdown":"# Numeric Variable\n\nNumeric variables are used to store numerical values.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a numeric variable, create a meaningful variable name. This means that the variable name should accurately describe the value that it is storing. \n\nFor example, a variable `counter` should be used to store the value of a counter.\n\nTo assign a value to the variable, use the `=` operator. \n\n## Example 1\n\nThis example keeps the default variable name `my_number` and assigns it a value of 10.\n\n```python\nmy_number = 10\n```\n## Example 2\n\nThis example gives the variable the name `three_plus_two` and stores the result of the 3 added to 2. \n\n```python\nthree_plus_two = 3 + 2\n```","signature":"my_number = 1"},"variables_my_string":{"name":"variables_my_string","markdown":"# String Variable\n\nString variables are used to store strings.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a string variable, create a meaningful variable name. This means that the variable name should accurately describe its value. \n\nFor example, a variable `name` should be used to store the value of a name.\n\nTo assign a string to a string variable, use the `=` operator. It's string value can be enclosed in either `\" \"` or `' '`.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_string being assigned the string value `\"Hello\"`.\n\n```python\nmy_string = \"Hello\"\n```","signature":"my_string = \\\"Hello World\\\""},"vr_thread":{"name":"vr_thread","markdown":"# VR Thread\n\nThe VR Thread function must be used to call functions at the global level of the program. It can be used to start threads to run simultaneously.\n\n```python\nvr_thread(function_name)\n```\nNotice that the function name is passed as a reference to the `vr_thread()` call rather than calling the function inside a VR Thread such as `vr_thread(function_name())`.\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou can take any function you have in the program and pass its reference to `vr_thread()` on the global scope. Using VR Threads are necessary in order for multiple functions to run in parallel. \n\nThe functions will, in general, execute in the order that they are passed into `vr_thread()` calls. If a function is waiting for a command to complete, it will pass program execution to another function, and resume its execution when the other function finishes running, or is also waiting for a command to complete.\n\nThe functions that causes threads to switch program execution:\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM, wait=True)\ndrivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 90, DEGREES, wait=True)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES, wait=TRUE)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90, DEGREES, wait=TRUE)\ndrivetrain.set_heading(0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)\nwait(1, SECONDS)\n\nAny user-created function\n```\n\n## Example 1\n\nWe make a single function that is executed in the global scope with `vr_thread()`. The `move_drivetrain()` function will make the robot move 200 mm and then print when it is done.\n\n```python\ndef move_drivetrain():\n    drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Done moving\")\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n\nvr_thread(move_drivetrain)\n```\n\n## Example 2\n\nNow we added the `lower_fork()` function. This will move the fork down and print a message when the fork is fully lowered.\n\nWe make the call `vr_thread(lower_fork)` **after** the `vr_thread(move_drivetrain)` call. However, because `drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 500, MM)` makes the thread wait, it will switch program execution over to the `lower_fork` function, which will start lowering the fork before the drivetrain completes its movements.\n\n```python\ndef move_drivetrain():\n    drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 500, MM)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Done moving\")\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n\ndef lower_fork():\n    fork_motor_group.spin_for(FORWARD, 1700, DEGREES)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Fork lowered\")\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n\nvr_thread(move_drivetrain)\nvr_thread(lower_fork)\n```","signature":"vr_thread(function_name)"}},"cpp":{"control_break":{"name":"control_break","markdown":"# Break\n\nExits a repeating loop immediately.\n\n```cpp\nbreak;\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen added inside of a loop, the `break` command will exit the loop it is currently in. \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will move the Drivetrain forward and repeatedly check if the VEX IQ Brain’s up button is pressed.\n\nIf the up button is pressed, the `break` command will exit the `while` loop and stop the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n  if (Brain.buttonUp.pressing()) {\n    break;\n  }\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"control_break"},"control_elseif":{"name":"control_elseif","markdown":"# Else If\n\nA control statement that runs the code inside the set of curly brackets based on the Boolean value of the conditional.\n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n  // Some code to run if the condition returns true\n} else if (condition2) {\n  // Some code to run if the first condition returns false and the second condition returns true\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe else if statement will only check the Boolean condition once.\n\nIf the Boolean `(condition)` is **false** and the Boolean `(condition2)` is reported as **true**, the code inside of `else if's` curly brackets will run.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the VEX IQ TouchLED will glow green if it is pressed and will glow red when it is not pressed.\n\nAn if/else conditional can be “nested” or placed inside a while loop to ensure that the Touch LED can turn red and green more than once.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  if (TouchLED.pressing()) {\n    TouchLED.setColor(green);\n  } else if (!TouchLED.pressing()) {\n    TouchLED.setColor(red);\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"control_elseif"},"control_for":{"name":"control_for","markdown":"# For\n\nRepeats the code inside the curly braces for a set number of times.\n\n```cpp\nfor (initialization; condition; increment/decrement) {\n  // some code to repeat\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nEnter a value to indicate how many times the code will **repeat** using 3 expressions:\n\n* initialization\n* condition\n* increment/decrement\n\n**Initialization** declares the starting value of the iterating variable.\n\n**Condition** specifies how long the for loop will run. The loop will stop repeating when the condition becomes **false**.\n\n**Increment/decrement** changes the iterating variable at the end of each loop.\n\n## Example 1\n\nThis example will print the numbers 0 to 9 to the VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nfor (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"%d\", i);\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```\n## Example 2\n\nThis example will drive the VEX IQ robot forward ten inches then turn the robot 60 degrees three times to the right. \n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 10.0, inches);\n\nfor (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n  Drivetrain.turnFor(right, 60, degrees);\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"control_for"},"control_if":{"name":"control_if","markdown":"# If\n\nRuns the code inside if-statement's curly brackets, if the condition returns true. \n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n  // code to run if condition is true \n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **if-statement** will only check its condition inside the parentheses once.\n\nIf the condition returns **true**, the code inside the curly brackets will run.\n\nIf the condition returns **false**, the code inside the curly brackets will be skipped.\n\n```cpp\n// Stop Motor1 if BumperA is pressed\nif (BumperA.pressing()) {\n  Motor1.stop();\n}\n```","signature":"control_if"},"control_if_else":{"name":"control_if_else","markdown":"# If/else\n\nA control statement that runs the code inside the first or second set of curly brackets based on the Boolean value of the conditional.\n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n  // Some code to run if the condition returns true\n} else {\n  // Some code to run if the condition returns false\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe if/else statement will only check the Boolean condition once.\n\nIf the Boolean `(condition)` is reported as **true**, the code inside of `if's` curly brackets will run.\n\nIf the Boolean `(condition)` is **false**, the code inside of `else's` curly brackets will run.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the VEX IQ TouchLED will glow green if it is pressed and will glow red when it is not pressed.\n\nAn if/else conditional can be “nested” or placed inside a while loop to ensure that the Touch LED can turn red and green more than once.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  if (TouchLED.pressing()) {\n    TouchLED.setColor(green);\n  } else {\n    TouchLED.setColor(red);\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"control_if_else"},"control_repeat":{"name":"control_repeat","markdown":"# Repeat\n\nRepeats the commands inside curly brackets for the number set inside the parentheses.\n`repeat (number of times to repeat){code to repeat}`\n\n```\nrepeat (10) {\n\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **repeat-statement** will loop through the code contained in the brackets until it reaches the number of iterations set in the condition.\n\nFirst, set the number of times the code will loop by changing the condition to any positive integer. The condition can also be a variable or sensor data.\n\nThe snippet below will print \"iteration\" to the Brain's Screen four times. Each time, it will create a new line before printing the next iteration.\n\n```\nrepeat (4) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"iteration\");\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  wait(5, msec);\n}\n```\n\nNote that the **repeat-statement** cannot be nested inside of another repeat statement.","signature":"repeat(10) { }"},"control_wait":{"name":"control_wait","markdown":"# Wait\n\nWaits for a specific amount of time before moving to the next command.\n\n```cpp\nwait(time, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet an amount of time in **seconds** or **msec** (milliseconds) to have your program `wait` before executing additional commands.\n\n```cpp\nwait(10, seconds);\nwait(100, msec);\n```","signature":"wait(time, units);"},"control_waitUntil":{"name":"control_waitUntil","markdown":"# Wait Until\n\nRepeats a segment of code until the provided **condition** returns **true**.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (!condition) { \n  // Code to repeat until condition returns true\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis control statement will repeatedly check its condition, and will **not** execute any proceeding code until the condition returns **true**. At the same time, it will repeat any code provided between its curly braces.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (!TouchLED.pressing()) {\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```\n\n## Example \n\nThis example will turn the TouchLED to Yellow and wait until the TouchLED is pressed. Once pressed, the TouchLED will then change to green.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(yellow);\n\nwhile (!TouchLED.pressing()) {\n  wait(1, seconds);\n}\n\nTouchLED.setColor(green);\n```","signature":"control_waitUntil"},"control_while":{"name":"control_while","markdown":"# While\n\nA loop that repeats the code inside its curly brackets while the **condition** provided evaluates to **true**.   \n\n```cpp\nwhile (condition) {\n  // Code to repeat while the condition returns true\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `while` loop will only check the condition inside the rounded parenthesis at the beginning of each loop. \n\nIf the condition evaluates as **true**, the code inside of `while` will run.\n\nIf the condition evaluates as **false**, the code inside of `while` will be skipped.\n\nThe `while` loop accepts anything that evaluates to **true** or **false** as its condition. Conditions can be Booleans or expressions using comparison or logical operators.  \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will drive the VEX IQ robot forward while the timer value is less than 60 seconds.\n\nAfter 60 seconds, the VEX IQ robot will stop.\n\n```cpp\nwhile(Brain.Timer.value() < 60) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"control_while"},"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain":{"name":"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain","markdown":"# Calibrate Drivetrain\n\nCalibrates the Drivetrain when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n```cpp\ncalibrateDrivetrain();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCall the `calibrateDrivetrain` command at the start of the program to calibrate the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nint main() {\n  // Calibrate the Drivetrain at the top of the main function\n  calibrateDrivetrain();\n\n  // Add other program code here\n  Drivetrain.driveFor(forward, 500, mm);\n  Drivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n}\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will calibrate the VEX IQ Drivetrain before driving 200 mm forward and turning to heading 45 degrees.\n\n```cpp\ncalibrateDrivetrain();\n\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45, degrees);\n```","signature":"calibrateDrivetrain();"},"drivetrain_drive":{"name":"drivetrain_drive","markdown":"# Drive\n\nMoves the Drivetrain forever.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(direction);\n```\n\nAll drivetrain motors are run forwards or backwards at the speed that was set using `Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity`. The default speed is 50 rpm.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.drive` command will run the Drivetrain forever, until a new Drivetrain command is used, or the program is stopped.\n\nUse the **forward** parameter to drive the Drivetrain in the forward direction.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n```\n\nUse the **reverse** parameter to drive the Drivetrain in the reverse direction.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(reverse);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.drive(forward);"},"drivetrain_drive_for":{"name":"drivetrain_drive_for","markdown":"# Drive For\n\nMoves the Drivetrain for a given distance. \n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(direction, distance, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which `direction` the Drivetrain will move - either **forward** or **reverse**. \n\nSet how far the Drivetrain will move by entering a numeric value for `distance`. \n\nThen, specify the `units` of measurement as either **inches** or **mm**.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(reverse, 5, inches);\n```\n\nThe `Drivetrain.driveFor` command will by default block other commands until the Drivetrain movement has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to prevent the `Drivetrain.driveFor` command from blocking the program until the movement has completed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.driveFor(forward, 1, inches);"},"drivetrain_set_drive_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Set Rotation\n\nSets the Drivetrain's angle of rotation when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setRotation(value, rotationUnits);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setRotation()` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive or negative value.\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setRotation()` command can accept integers or numeric commands.\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setRoation()` command **does not** have a limit of 0-359 degrees.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will turn the robot a total of 210 degrees:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(120, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n```\n\n- Turn left (counter-clockwise) to rotation 120 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current position as rotation of -45 degrees.\n- Turn left (counter-clockwise) an additional 90 degrees (-45 degrees to +45 degrees) based on the set rotation value from the previous block.","signature":"Drivetrain.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Set Drive Velocity\n\nSets the velocity of the Drivetrain that will be used for `Drivetrain.drive` and `Drivetrain.driveFor` commands. \n\nIf this command is used when the Drivetrain is moving, the Drivetrain movement will be updated with the new speed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity` will set the speed of the Drivetrain, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move by itself.\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity` accepts a range from **-100 to 100** when using **percent** units.\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity` accepts a range from **-127 to 127** when using **rpm** units.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to drive in the opposite direction.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to 0 will prevent the Drivetrain from moving.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the Drivetrain drive forward at 50% speed for 12 inches.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(50, percent);\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 12.0, inches);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity(50, percent);"},"drivetrain_set_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_set_heading","markdown":"# Set Heading\n\nSets the Drivetrain's Gyro heading value.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setHeading(heading, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setHeading` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's heading to any given counter-clockwise-positive heading as shown in the image below.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/cpp/en/drivetrain_set_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nDrivetrain heading references can differ depending on whether a gyro or the integrated inertial sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the integrated inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\n![set_drive_heading_clockwise](static/help/iq/cpp/en/drivetrain_set_heading/set_drive_heading_clockwise.png)\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\n![set_drive_heading_counterclockwise](static/help/iq/cpp/en/drivetrain_set_heading/set_drive_heading_counterclockwise.png)\n\n`Drivetrain.setHeading` accepts a range of **0 to 359.99** for the `heading` parameter.\n\n## Example \n\nThis example will rotate the robot a total of 135 degrees:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setHeading(0.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees);\n```\n\n(The descriptions below are based on an IQ (1st generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration, or an IQ (2nd generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration with a gyro sensor)\n\n- Turn left to heading 45 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current heading as heading of 0 degrees.\n- Turn left an additional 90 degrees.","signature":"Drivetrain.setHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_rotation","markdown":"# Set Rotation\n\nSets the Drivetrain's angle of rotation when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro or Brain Inertial Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setRotation` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive or negative value.\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\n`Drivetrain.setRotation` can also be used to set the Drivetrain's rotation to any given positive or negative value. However, drivetrain rotation references can differ depending on whether a gyro or the integrated inertial sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the integrated inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will turn the robot a total of 210 degrees:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(120, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n```\n\n(The descriptions below are based on an IQ (1st generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration, or an IQ (2nd generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration with a gyro sensor)\n\n- Turn left (counter-clockwise) to rotation 120 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current position as rotation of -45 degrees.\n- Turn left (counter-clockwise) an additional 90 degrees (-45 degrees to +45 degrees).","signature":"Drivetrain.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_stopping":{"name":"drivetrain_set_stopping","markdown":"# Set Stopping\n\nSets the brake mode of the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setStopping(brakeType);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nHere are the valid inputs for the `brakeType` parameter that you can specify: \n\n* **brake** will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop, and will not correct for outside forces.\n* **coast** lets the Drivetrain slow gradually to a stop.\n* **hold** will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved by an outside force.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the Drivetrain move forward for 3 seconds and then hold its position once stopped.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setStopping(hold);\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setStopping(brake);"},"drivetrain_set_timeout":{"name":"drivetrain_set_timeout","markdown":"# Set Timeout\n\nSets the timeout for the Drivetrain to stop moving if a blocking Drivetrain command cannot reach its target.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setTimeout` command is used to prevent drive commands that do not complete from preventing other commands in the program from running.\n\nAn example of a Drivetrain not reaching its position is when a robot is driven against a wall and cannot complete its movement.\n\nSet the timeout by specifying the amount of time in `seconds`.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(2.0, seconds);\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will end the `Drivetrain.driveFor` command after 2 seconds if the Drivetrain has not reached the target distance of 24 inches. \n\nOnce the time limit or distance is reached (whichever is earlier), the Drivetrain will then turn 90 degrees to the right.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(2.0, seconds);\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 24.0, inches);\nDrivetrain.turnFor(right, 90.0, degrees);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setTimeout(1, seconds);"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Set Turn Velocity\n\nSets the velocity of the Drivetrain when turning. \n\nIf this is used when the drivetrain is turning, the drivetrain will be updated with the new speed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTurnVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity` will set the speed of the Drivetrain when turning, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move when used by itself. \n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity` accepts a range from **-100 to 100** when using **percent** units.\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity` accepts a range from **-127 to 127** when using **rpm** units.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to turn in the opposite direction.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to 0 will prevent the Drivetrain from turning.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the Drivetrain turn to the left at 25% speed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTurnVelocity(25, percent);\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity(50, percent);"},"drivetrain_stop":{"name":"drivetrain_stop","markdown":"# Stop\n\nStops the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.stop` command will cause the Drivetrain to come to a stop.\n\nThe stopping behavior can be set with the `Drivetrain.setStopping` command.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will move the VEX IQ robot forward for 3 seconds then come to a stop.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.stop();"},"drivetrain_turn":{"name":"drivetrain_turn","markdown":"# Turn\n\nTurns the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(direction);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turn` command will turn the Drivetrain forever, until a new Drivetrain command is used, or the program is stopped.\n\nUse the **left** argument to turn the Drivetrain to the left.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n```\n\nUse the **right** argument to turn the Drivetrain to the right.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(right);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turn(right);"},"drivetrain_turn_for":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_for","markdown":"# Turn For\n\nTurns the Drivetrain for the specified angle and direction.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(direction, angle, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet the `direction` and amount the Drivetrain will turn by entering a direction - **left** or **right**, and a number of degrees.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(right, 270, degrees);\n```\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turnFor` command will by default block other commands until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to prevent the `Drivetrain.turnFor` command from blocking the program until the movement has completed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(left, 90, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnFor(right, 90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_turn_to_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Turn To Heading\n\nTurns a Drivetrain to a specific heading when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro or Brain Inertial Sensor.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading(heading, degrees);`\n\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` command can be used to turn the Drivetrain to any given counter-clockwise heading as shown in the image below.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/cpp/en/drivetrain_turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` command can be used to turn the Drivetrain either in a counter-clockwise or clockwise heading depending on whether the integrated inertial or a gyro sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the integrated inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\n![turn_to_heading_clockwise](static/help/iq/cpp/en/drivetrain_turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_clockwise.png)\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\n![turn_to_heading_counterclockwise](static/help/iq/cpp/en/drivetrain_turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_counterclockwise.png)\n\nBased on the current heading of the Gyro, `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` will determine which direction to turn.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading` accepts a range of **0.00 to 359.99** for the `heading` parameter.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns: \n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(270.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(180.0, degrees);\n```\n\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 45 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 90 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 270 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to 180 degrees\n\n(The clockwise/counter-clockwise motions described above are based on an IQ (1st generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration, or an IQ (2nd generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration with a gyro sensor)\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` command will by default block other commands until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to prevent the `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` command from blocking the program until the turn has completed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnToHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Turn To Rotation\n\nTurns a Drivetrain to a specific angle of rotation when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro or Brain Inertial Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turnToRotation` command can be used to turn the Drivetrain to a given positive (counter-clockwise) or negative (clockwise) value.\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turnToRotation` command can be used to turn the Drivetrain either in a counter-clockwise or clockwise rotation depending on whether the integrated inertial or a gyro sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the integrated inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\nBased on the current rotation of the Drivetrain, `Drivetrain.turnToRotation` will determine which direction to turn.\n\nThe `rotation` parameter is **not** limited to **0 to 359.99 degrees**. Turns will be absolute and may cause the robot to rotate more than once if necessary.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(90.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(180, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(0, degrees);\n```\n\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 90 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 180 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to -45 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to 0 degrees\n\n(The clockwise/counter-clockwise motions described above are based on an IQ (1st generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration, or an IQ (2nd generation) Brain + Drivetrain configuration with a gyro sensor)\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turnToRotation`command will by default block other commands until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to prevent the `Drivetrain.turnToRotation` command from blocking the program until the turn has completed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(180.0, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnToRotation(90, degrees);"},"events_brain_button_pressed":{"name":"events_brain_button_pressed","markdown":"#  Brain Button Pressed\n\nRuns the callback function when the VEX IQ Brain button is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Button.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a Brain Button is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button pressed.\");\n}\n```\n\nThe `Brain.Button.pressed` function can be used with the different buttons on the VEX IQ Brain.\n\nAn IQ (1st generation) Brain and IQ (2nd generation) Brain has slightly different button options, but they can be interchangeably used on either Brain generation.\n\nSupported Brain buttons are as follows:\n- `buttonUp` / `buttonLeft`\n- `buttonDown` / `buttonRight`\n- `buttonCheck`\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Brain.Button.pressed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.buttonUp.pressed(callback);"},"events_brain_button_released":{"name":"events_brain_button_released","markdown":"# Brain Button Released\n\nRuns the callback function when the specified VEX IQ Brain button is released.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Button.released(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a Brain Button is released.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button released.\");\n}\n```\n\nThe `Brain.Button.released` function can be used with the different buttons on the VEX IQ Brain.\n\nAn IQ (1st generation) Brain and IQ (2nd generation) Brain has slightly different button options, but they can be interchangeably used on either Brain generation.\n\nSupported Brain buttons are as follows:\n- `buttonUp` / `buttonLeft`\n- `buttonDown` / `buttonRight`\n- `buttonCheck`\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Brain.Button.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.button.released();"},"events_brain_timer":{"name":"events_brain_timer","markdown":"# Timer Event\n\nSets a callback that will be called after the specified amount of time.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.event(callback, time);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe IQ Brain's timer begins at the start of each program.\n\nThe `Brain.Timer.event` function takes 2 parameters.\n\nThe first is the **callback function** parameter. A function will need to be created to pass to the `Brain.Timer.event` function.\n\nThe second parameter is the time at which the function will run. The **callback function** will run once the **Brain Timer** is greater than the entered amount. The amount of `time` should be in **milliseconds**.\n\n```cpp\n// Call the callback function after 1000 milliseconds\nBrain.Timer.event(callback, 1000);\n```\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs.\n\nIn the snippet below, \"Callback Function Called\" will be printed to the VEX IQ's Brain Screen after 10 seconds.\n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Brain.Timer.event(callbackFunction, 10000);\n}\n```","signature":"events_brain_timer"},"events_bumper_pressed":{"name":"events_bumper_pressed","markdown":"# Bumper Pressed\n\nRuns the specified **callback function** when the bumper is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Bumper Sensor is pressed. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\nvoid bumperPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Bumper pressed.\");\n}\n```\nThen, the function is passed as the parameter of the `Bumper.pressed` function call.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressed(bumperPressed);\n```\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Bumper.pressed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"BUMPER.pressed(callback);"},"events_bumper_released":{"name":"events_bumper_released","markdown":"# Bumper Released\n\nRuns the specified function when the bumper is released.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.released(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCreate a function to call when the Bumper is released. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\nvoid bumperReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Bumper released.\");\n}\n```\nThen, the function is passed as the parameter of the `Bumper.released` function call.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.released(bumperReleased);\n```\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Bumper.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Bumper.released(callback);"},"events_controller_axis":{"name":"events_controller_axis","markdown":"# Controller Axis Changed\n\nRuns the provided callback funtion when the selected VEX IQ Controller's joystick axis is moved.\n\n```cpp\nController.Axis.changed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a callback function to call when an Axis on the controller is moved.\n\n```cpp\nvoid axisMoved() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Axis moved.\");\n}\n```\n\nChoose which Controller joystick axis to use and pass the callback function\n\n- `Controller.AxisA.changed(axisMoved);`\n- `Controller.AxisB.changed(axisMoved);`\n- `Controller.AxisC.changed(axisMoved);`\n- `Controller.AxisD.changed(axisMoved);`\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/en/events_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Controller.AxisA.changed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"`Controller.AxisA.changed(callback)`"},"events_controller_button_pressed":{"name":"events_controller_button_pressed","markdown":"# Controller Button Pressed\n\nRuns the **callback function** when the VEX IQ Controller button is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a **callback function** that will be called when a Controller Button is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button pressed.\");\n}\n```\n\nChoose which Controller button to call the `pressed()` function with.\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/cpp/en/events_controller_button_pressed/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonEUp.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonEDown.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonFUp.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonFDown.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/en/events_controller_button_pressed/controller_button_back.png)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonLUp.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonLDown.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonRUp.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonRDown.pressed(buttonPressed);`","signature":"Controller.Button.pressed();"},"events_controller_button_released":{"name":"events_controller_button_released","markdown":"# Controller Button Released\n\nRuns the **callback function** when the VEX IQ Controller Button is released.\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.released(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a **callback function** that will be called when a Controller Button is released.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button released.\");\n}\n```\n\nChoose which Controller button to call the `released()` function with.\n\n- `Controller.ButtonEUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonEDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonFUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonFDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonLUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonLDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonRUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonRDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/cpp/en/events_controller_button_released/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/en/events_controller_button_released/controller_button_back.png)\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Controller.ButtonRDown.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Controller.Button.released();"},"events_event":{"name":"events_event","markdown":"# Event\n\nCreates a new event to trigger user defined functions.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n```\n\n## How To Use\nThe **event** object can be used to trigger a user defined function. To use it, an **event** object needs to be created. This can be done in two ways.\n\nA **callback function** can be used as an argument to the creation function.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n```\nA **callback function** does not need to be passed to the creation function.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event();\n```\nMultiple **callback functions** can be added to an event. All of the functions will be called and ran at the same time when the event occurs.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event();\nmyEvent(callbackFunction1);\nmyEvent(callbackFunction1);\n```\nOnly **2 event callback functions** should run at the same time. Additional **events callback functions** may reduce the performance of the VEX IQ robot.\n\nThe callback functions will execute when either the `myEvent.broadcast` or `myEvent.broadcastAndWait` functions are called.\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create a new event called myEvent in the main function and pass callbackFunction\n  event myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n\n  // Broadcast myEvent, triggering \"Function Called.\" to be printed to the Brain's Screen\n  myEvent.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"event myEvent = event(myEventCallback);"},"events_event_broadcast":{"name":"events_event_broadcast","markdown":"# Broadcast\n\nBroadcasts a message to activate any functions that are passed to the **Event**.\n\n```cpp\nmyEvent.broadcast();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe code will continue to run the commands after the `myEvent.broadcast` command so that it will run at the same time as the event listener functions.\n\nBefore using this command, a user-defined event must be created and register at least one callback.\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast1() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\");\n}\n\nvoid runOnBroadcast2() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create an event in the main function\n  event myEvent = event();\n\n  // Register callback functions to event\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast1);\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast2);\n\n  // Broadcast the event\n  myEvent.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"EVENT.broadcast();"},"events_event_broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Broadcast and Wait\n\nBroadcasts a message to activate any functions that are passed to the **Event** while also pausing the rest of the current program.\n\n```cpp\nmyEvent.broadcastAndWait();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `myEvent.broadcastAndWait` command will wait for all listeners to complete before returning. This will pause the code execution in the current function until all the broadcast listeners have finished execution.\n\nBefore using this command, an event must be created and have at least one callback registered.\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Function Called.\");\n\n  wait(5, seconds);\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register a new event in the main function and pass the callbackFunction\n  event myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n\n  // Broadcast the event and wait for it to finish executing\n  myEvent.broadcastAndWait();\n\n  // This will not run until the callbackFunction has completed execution\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Done!\");\n}\n```","signature":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_down":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_down","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when the gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureDown(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `Optical.gestureEnable();` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gestureUp`\n- `gestureDown`\n- `gestureLeft`\n- `gestureRight`\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Down detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\n  Optical.gestureEnable();\n\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.gestureDown(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureDown(callback);"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_left":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_left","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when the gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureLeft(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `Optical.gestureEnable();` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gestureUp`\n- `gestureDown`\n- `gestureLeft`\n- `gestureRight`\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Left detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\n  Optical.gestureEnable();\n\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.gestureLeft(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureLeft(callback);"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_right":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_right","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when the gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureRight(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `Optical.gestureEnable();` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gestureUp`\n- `gestureDown`\n- `gestureLeft`\n- `gestureRight`\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Right detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\n  Optical.gestureEnable();\n\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.gestureRight(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureRight(callback);"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_up":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_up","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when the gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureUp(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `Optical.gestureEnable();` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gestureUp`\n- `gestureDown`\n- `gestureLeft`\n- `gestureRight`\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Up detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\n  Optical.gestureEnable();\n\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.gestureUp(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureUp(callback);"},"events_optical_object_detected":{"name":"events_optical_object_detected","markdown":"# Optical Object Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when an object is detected by an Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.objectDetected(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical.objectDetected();` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when an object is detected by an Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when an object is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Object detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.objectDetected(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.objectDetected(callback);"},"events_optical_object_lost":{"name":"events_optical_object_lost","markdown":"# Optical Object Lost\n\nRuns the callback function when a detected object is no longer being detected by an Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.objectLost(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical.objectLost();` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when an Optical Sensor no longer detects a previously-detected object.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the object is no longer being detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Object lost!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.objectLost(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.objectLost(callback);"},"events_touch_led_pressed":{"name":"events_touch_led_pressed","markdown":"# TouchLED Pressed\n\nRuns the specified **callback function** when the TouchLED is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the TouchLED is pressed. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\nvoid touchLEDPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Touch LED pressed.\");\n}\n```\nThen, the function is passed as the parameter of the `TouchLED.pressed` function call.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.pressed(touchLEDPressed);\n```\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  TouchLED.pressed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"TouchLED.pressed(callback);"},"events_touch_led_released":{"name":"events_touch_led_released","markdown":"# TouchLED Released\n\nRuns the specified **callback function** when the TouchLED is released.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.released(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the TouchLED is released. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\nvoid touchLEDReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Touch LED released.\");\n}\n```\nThen, the function is passed as the parameter of the `TouchLED.released` function call.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.released(touchLEDReleased);\n```\n\n## Callback Functions\n\nA callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. The code inside the **callback function** will run whenever the **event** occurs. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  TouchLED.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"TouchLED.released(callback);"},"function_name":{"name":"function_name","markdown":"# Functions\n\nFunctions are segments of code used to perform a set of actions.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myFunction() {\n  // function code\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo define a function, declare the type of data that the function will return.\n\n- `int`, `float`, `double`, and `string` are commonly returned data types. If the function will not return a value declare the return type as `void`. \n\nThen, use a meaningful function name that describes what the function does.\n\n```cpp\nint returnZero() {\n  return 0;\n}\n```\n\nInclude parentheses `()` with optional *parameters* after the function name. Multiple parameters should be separated by commas (parameter1, parameter2).\n\nThe body of the function should be enclosed in curly brackets `{ }`.\n    \n## Example\n\nThis function has no parameters and returns no value and so its return type is declared as `void`. This function prints \"The battery is low!\" to the VEX IQ Brain Screen if the battery capacity is below 25%.\n\n```cpp\nvoid lowOnBattery() {\n  if (Brain.Battery.capacity(percent) < 25.0) {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"The battery is low!\");\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"function_name"},"function_thread":{"name":"function_thread","markdown":"# Thread\n\nAllows you to execute multiple threads at the same time.\n\n```cpp\nthread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA function needs to be defined that will be passed as a callback to the thread.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myThreadCallback() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"In a different thread!\");\n}\n```\nOnce you have the function written, you can use it to make a new thread. This function is referred to as the **callback function**.\n\n```cpp\nthread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n```\nThe **thread** will start executing once it is created. It will then run at the same time as the main thread.\n\nOnly **2 threads** should be running at a given time. Additional threads may reduce the performance of the VEX IQ robot.\n    \n## Example\n\nThis example will print two counters to the VEX IQ's Brain at the same time. One will be printed by the `myThread` thread. The other will be printed by the main thread at the same time.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myThreadCallback() {\n  int count = 0;\n  while(true) {\n    Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"thread1: %d\", count);\n    count++;\n    // Wait to allow the main thread to execute\n    wait(25, msec);\n  }\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Once a thread is created it begins executing\n  thread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n  \n  int count = 0;\n  while(true) {\n    Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"main: %d\", count);\n    count++;\n    // Wait to allow myThread to execute\n    wait(25, msec);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"function_thread"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Clear Line\n\nClears the current row on the VEX IQ Brain's Screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine();\n```\n\nClears a specified row on the Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine(1);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou can call the `Brain.Screen.clearLine` command without any arguments to clear the current row.\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.clearLine` command can accept integer values between **1 to 5**, to set which row to clear. \n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/row_column_index.png)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\n`Brain.Screen.clearLine` accepts a range of values from **1 to 9** for the row to clear, depending on what font is currently selected.\n\n![row_column_index2](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/iq2_row_column_brain2.jpg) \n\n## Example \nThis example will print \"Hello\" on row 2, column 1, wait for three seconds, then clear row 2.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");\nwait(3.0, seconds);\nBrain.Screen.clearLine(2);\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.clearLine();"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Clear Screen\n\nClears the entire VEX IQ Brain's Screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearScreen();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Brain.Screen.clearScreen` will not reset the Brain's screen cursor. \n\nUse the `Brain.Screen.setCursor` command to set the Brain's cursor to the desired position.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Hello\", wait one second, and then clear the entire screen before printing \"Goodbye\".\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");\nwait(1.0, seconds);\nBrain.Screen.clearScreen();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Goodbye\");\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.clearScreen();"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Circle\nDraws a circle on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawCircle(1, 1, 10);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.drawCircle();` command requires 3 values:\n\n* Value 1: Center Point X\n* Value 2: Center Point Y\n* Value 3: Radius of Circle (in pixels)\n\nThe outside line color of the circle is determined by the `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the circle is determined by the `Brain.Screen.setFillColor();` command. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_circle/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawCircle(1, 1, 10);"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_line","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Line\nDraws a line on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawLine(1, 1, 10, 10);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.drawLine();` command requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Beginning X coordinate\n* Value 2: Beginning Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Ending X coordinate\n* Value 4: Ending Y coordinate\n\nThe line color is determined by the `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command. The default line color is white.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_line/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawLine(1, 1, 10, 10);"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Pixel\nDraws a pixel on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawPixel(1, 1);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.drawPixel();` command requires 2 values:\n\n* Value 1: X Coordinate\n* Value 2: Y Coordinate\n\nThe pixel color is determined by the `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command. The default pixel color is white.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawPixel(1, 1);"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Rectangle\nDraws a rectangle on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawRectangle(1, 1, 10, 10);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.drawRectangle();` command requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Top Left Corner X coordinate\n* Value 2: Top Left Corner Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Width of the rectangle\n* Value 4: Height of the rectangle\n\nThe outside line color of the rectangle is determined by the `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the rectangle is determined by the `Brain.Screen.setFillColor();` command. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawRectangle(1, 1, 10, 10);"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line","markdown":"# New Line\n\nSets the print output on the Brain's screen to the next available row.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1. The `Brain.Screen.newLine` command will move the cursor down by a single row on the screen.\n\n---\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_new_line/row_column_index.png)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\n![row_column_index2](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_new_line/iq2_row_column_brain2.jpg) \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"First Message\" and then will set the cursor to the next available row before printing \"Second Message\".\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"First Message\");\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Second Message\");\n```\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_new_line/set_cursor_welcome.png)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\n![set_cursor_welcome2](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_new_line/set_cursor_welcome2.png)","signature":"Brain.Screen.newLine();"},"looks_brain_screen_print":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text on the VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.print` command will print data at a cursor location on the screen.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1.\n\nPrint string values:\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"String: 123 + Words\");\n```\n\nPrint integer or decimal values:\n\n```cpp\n// When printing integer values, the \"%d\" format specifier is\n// required as the first parameter\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Integer: %d\", 5 + 10);\n\n// When printing decimal values, the \"%f\" format specifier is\n// required as the first parameter\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Decimal: %f\", 5.0 + 10.0);\n```\n\nPrint the reported value from a sensing command:\n\n```cpp\n// If the reported value is a decimal or integer,\n// use \"%f\" or \"%d\" respectively as the format specifier\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%d\", Brain.Timer.time());\n\n// If the reported value is a boolean,\n// use \"%s\" as the format specifier\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%s\", Motor.isDone() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");"},"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Set Cursor\n\nSets the cursor location for `Brain.Screen.print` commands.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(row, col);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setCursor` command requires 2 parameters:\n\n* Parameter 1: Screen row position \n* Parameter 2: Screen column position\n\nSet the cursor's row and column position to have a `Brain.Screen.print` command print at a specific location on the screen.\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\nAccepts a range for `row` of **1 to 5** .\n\nAccepts a range for `col` of **1 to 21**.\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\nAccepts a range for `row` of **1 to 9**.\n\nAccepts a range for `col` of **1 to 28**.\n\n## Example 1\n\nThis example will set the cursor to location row 3 column 7 before printing the text \"VEXcode!\" to the Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(3, 7);\nBrain.Screen.print(\"VEXcode!\");\n```\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/set_cursor_hello.png)\n\n## Example 2\n\nThis example will set the cursor to location row 3 column 5 before printing the text \"VEXcode!\" to the Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(3, 5);\nBrain.Screen.print(\"VEXcode!\");\n```\n\n![set_cursor_hello2](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/set_cursor_hello2.png)","signature":"Brain.screen.setCursor(1, 1);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Fill Color\n\nSets the color that fills in shapes drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setFillColor(red);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setFillColor();` command is used to set the color of the inside of circles and rectangles drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen. \n\nYou can select from the following colors\n\n* black\n* white\n* red\n* green\n* blue\n* yellow\n* orange\n* purple\n* cyan\n* transparent\n\nThe fill color will be used for any next objects drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.","signature":"Brain.Screen.setFillColor(red);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_font":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_font","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Font\n\nSets the style and size of font used on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen when printing numbers or text.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setFont(monoM);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThere are two different types of fonts available on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - each character takes up the same width.\n* Proportional (Prop) - each character takes up different size widths based on the character.\n\nChoose which font type and size to use. You can select from the following font options.\n\n* `mono12`\n* `mono15`\n* `mono20`\n* `mono30`\n* `mono40`\n* `mono60`\n* `prop20`\n* `prop30`\n* `prop40`\n* `prop60`\n\nThe new font size will be used for any future text written to the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.","signature":"Brain.Screen.setFont(monoM);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Pen Color\n\nSets the color of lines drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setPenColor(black);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command is used to set the color of lines, pixels, and text drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen. \n\n`Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` will also be used to set the color the outline of circles and rectangles drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\nYou can select from the following colors\n\n* `black`\n* `white`\n* `red`\n* `green`\n* `blue`\n* `yellow`\n* `orange`\n* `purple`\n* `cyan`\n\nThe pen color will be used for any next objects drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.","signature":"Brain.Screen.setPenColor(red);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Pen Width\n\nSets the width of the outline for shapes drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setPenWidth(5);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setPenWidth();` command is used to set the width of the line on the outside of circles and rectangles drawn on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's screen. \n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setPenWidth();` command can accept integer values, with a larger value equating to a larger width.\n\n![iq2_row_column_brain](static/help/iq/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width/iq2_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.setPenWidth(10);"},"looks_color_set_light":{"name":"looks_color_set_light","markdown":"# Set Color Sensor Light\n\nSets the brightness of the VEX IQ Color Sensor's light. \n\n```cpp\nColor.setLight(brightness, percent);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Color Sensor has a light source that can be adjusted to help detect the color of an object or a surface.\n\n`Color.setLight` accepts a range of **0 to 100** for the `brightness` parameter.\n\nThe higher the value is set, the brighter the Color Sensor's light source will shine.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will set the brightness of the Color Sensor to 75%.\n\n```cpp\nColor.setLight(75, percent);\n```","signature":"Color.setLight(50, percent);"},"looks_console_clear_console":{"name":"looks_console_clear_console","markdown":"# Console Clear\n\nClears the Print Console and resets the cursor.\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"\\033[2J\\n\");\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nUsing the `printf` command with the special `\\033[2J` escape sequence and code will clear the Print Console.\n\nThe newline character, `\\n` is needed in a `printf` command to output the contents of the Print Console buffer into the Print Console. In this instance, the Print Console will be immediately updated/cleared when this command is executed.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will print `VEXcode` to the Print Console, wait 2 seconds, and then clear the Console.\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"VEXcode\\n\");\nwait(2, seconds);\nprintf(\"\\033[2J\\n\");\n```","signature":"printf(\"\\033[2J\\n\");"},"looks_console_print":{"name":"looks_console_print","markdown":"# Console Print\n\nPrints values or text to the Print Console\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"VEXcode\");\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `printf` command will print data at the cursor location on the Print Console.\n\nAll new projects begin with the cursor at row 1.\n\nThe newline character, `\\n` is needed in a `printf` command to output the contents of the Print Console buffer into the Print Console.\n\n## Printing Values\n\nYou can use format specifiers to show values inside of your print statements:\n\n* `%d` - Signed decimal integer\n* `%f` - Decimal floating point number\n* `%o` - Signed octal\n* `%s` - String of characters\n* `%x` - Unsigned hexadecimal integer\n* `%c` - Character\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"Time Elapsed %f\\n\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```\n\nWhen displaying values, you can specify how many decimals places to print. For example, if your value is `3.14159265`, but you only want to display `3.14`, your format specifier would be `%.2f`.\n\nThe number before the decimal in the format specifier denotes the total number of characters to be printed. If the value being printed is shorter than the total number of characters to be printed, the printed value is padded with blank spaces.\n\nThe format specifier can also contain flags, width, precision and modifiers sub-specifiers:\n\n* `%d`\t- Prints a decimal integer\n* `%6d`\t- Prints a decimal integer, with a minimum of 6 characters wide\n* `%f`\t- Prints a floating point number\n* `%6f`\t- Prints a floating point number, with a minimum of 6 characters wide\n* `%.2f`  - Prints a floating point number, with 2 decimal characters places\n* `%6.2f` - Prints a floating point number, with a minimum of 6 characters wide and 2 decimal places\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"Screen Pressed? %s\\n\", Brain.Screen.pressing());\n```\n\n## Printing Colors\n\nYou can use any of the color codes below with a `printf` command to set the color of the text being printed. The example below will show two ways in which a color sequence command can be used when printing. All color codes will need to be attached to an escape sequence - `\\033`.\n\n* `[31m` - Red\n* `[32m` - Green\n* `[34m` - Blue\n* `[30m` - Black\n* `[37m` - White\n* `[33m` - Yellow\n* `[91m` - Orange\n* `[35m` - Purple\n* `[38;5;207m` - Red Violet\n* `[38;5;213m` - Violet\n* `[38;5;063m` - Blue Violet\n* `[38;5;081m` - Blue Green\n* `[38;5;118m` - Yellow Green\n* `[38;5;190m` - Yellow Orange\n* `[38;5;214m` - Red Orange\n\n```cpp\n// Using color codes in-line\n// This will print \"VEXcode\" in Red to the Print Console\nprintf(\"\\033[31m VEXcode\\n\");\n\n// Using color codes in separate commands\nprintf(\"\\033[31m\");\nprintf(\"VEXcode\\n\");\n```","signature":"printf(\"VEXcode\");"},"looks_touch_led_set_brightness":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_brightness","markdown":"# Set TouchLED Brightness\n\nSets the brightness level of the VEX IQ TouchLED.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setBrightness(brightness);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`TouchLED.setBrightness` accepts a range of **0 to 100** for the `brightness` parameter.\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance. \n\n```cpp\nTouchLED1.setBrightness(100);\nTouchLED2.setBrightness(50);\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will illuminate the TouchLED green at 25% brightness.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setBrightness(25);\nTouchLED.setColor(green);\n```","signature":"TouchLED.brightness();"},"looks_touch_led_set_color":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_color","markdown":"# Set TouchLED Color\n\nSets the color of the VEX IQ TouchLED.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(color);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED1.setColor(red);\nTouchLED2.setColor(green);\n```\nChoose the color that will be displayed.  \n\nColor Options:\n\n- `red`\n- `green`\n- `blue`\n- `white`\n- `yellow`\n- `orange`\n- `purple`\n- `red_violet`\n- `violet`\n- `blue_violet`\n- `blue_green`\n- `yellow_green`\n- `yellow_orange`\n- `red_orange`\n\nTo turn the TouchLED off, set the color to **colorType::none**.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(colorType::none);\n```","signature":"touchLED.color();"},"looks_touch_led_set_fade":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_fade","markdown":"# Set TouchLED Fade\n\nSets how fast the color of the VEX IQ TouchLED fades between colors.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setFade(fade);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED1.setFade(fast);\nTouchLED2.setFade(slow);\n```\nChoose how fast the TouchLED will fade between colors. Replace `fade` with one of the following options:\n\n* **slow** - The TouchLED will slowly fade to a new color.\n* **fast** - The TouchLED will quickly fade to a new color.\n* **off** - The TouchLED will change colors instantly.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will slowly fade the TouchLED from red to blue.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(red);\nTouchLED.setFade(slow);\nTouchLED.setColor(blue);\n```","signature":"TouchLED.setFade(fade);"},"motion_motor_set_max_torque":{"name":"motion_motor_set_max_torque","markdown":"# Motor Set Max Torque\n\nSets a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group's maximum torque output.  \n\n```cpp\nMotor.setMaxTorque(value, percent);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.setMaxTorque` accepts a range of **0% to 100%**.\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setMaxTorque(25, percent);\nArmMotor.setMaxTorque(75, percent);\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the ClawMotor to the 40-degree position with only 20% maximum torque. This allows the Claw to grab an object without too much force.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setMaxTorque(20, percent);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(40, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setMaxTorque(50, percent);"},"motion_motor_set_position":{"name":"motion_motor_set_position","markdown":"# Motor Set Position\n\nSets the VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group's encoder position(s) to the specified positional value.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setPosition(position, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Motor.setPosition` command can be used to set a Motor or Motor Group's position to any given positional value.\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setPosition(0, degrees);\nArmMotor.setPosition(90, degrees);\n```\n\nUsually, the `Motor.setPosition` command is used to set the position to 0 to reset a Motor or Motor Group's encoder position(s).\n\nProvide the `units` as either **degrees** or **turns**.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the ClawMotor's position to 50 degrees.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setPosition(50, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setPosition(0, degrees);"},"motion_motor_set_stopping":{"name":"motion_motor_set_stopping","markdown":"# Motor Set Stopping\n\nSets the behavior of the VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group once it stops moving.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setStopping(brakeType);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setStopping(brake);\nArmMotor.setStopping(hold);\n```\n\nSpecify the Motor/Motor Group's stopping behavior:\n\n- **brake** will cause the Motor/Motor Group to come to an immediate stop.\n- **coast** will spin the Motor/Motor Group gradually to a stop.\n- **hold** will cause the Motor/Motor Group to come to an immediate stop and returns it to its initial stopped position if moved.\n\nThe `Motor.setStopping` command will affect the behavior of subsequent `Motor.stop` commands until otherwise changed.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the ArmMotor forward for 90 degrees and then will resist outside forces (like gravity) to hold its position.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.setStopping(hold);\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 90, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setStopping(brake);"},"motion_motor_set_timeout":{"name":"motion_motor_set_timeout","markdown":"# Motor Set Timeout\n\nSets a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group's timeout to stop if a blocking command never reaches its target.  \n\n```cpp\nMotor.setTimeout(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Motor.setTimeout` command is used to prevent Motor movements that do not reach their intended position from preventing other commands in the program from running. \n\nAn example of a Motor not reaching its position is an Arm or Claw that reaches its mechanical limit and cannot complete its movement.\n\nSet the timeout by specifying the amount of time in **seconds**.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will end the `Motor.spinToPosition` command after 2 seconds if the ClawMotor has not reached the intended position of 270 degrees. \n\nOnce the timeout or target is reached, the ArmMotor will spin to 90 degrees.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setTimeout(2, seconds);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(270, degrees);\nArmMotor.spinToPosition(90, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setTimeout(1, seconds);"},"motion_motor_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity","markdown":"# Set Motor Velocity\n\nSets the speed of a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.setVelocity` accepts a range of **-100% to 100%** or **-127rpm to 127rpm**.\n\nSetting a Motor or Motor Group's velocity to a negative value will cause the Motor/Motor Group to spin in reverse.\n\nSetting a Motor or Motor Group's velocity to 0 will cause the Motor/Motor Group to stop.\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setVelocity(25, percent);\nArmMotor.setVelocity(75, percent);\n```\n\nSpecify if the velocity `units` is set to either **percent** or **rpm** (revolutions per minute).\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the ClawMotor to spin at 25% speed to the 90-degree position.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setVelocity(25, percent);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(90, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setVelocity(50, percent);"},"motion_motor_spin":{"name":"motion_motor_spin","markdown":"# Spin Motor\n\nSpins a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group in a direction until stopped.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(direction);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Motor.spin` command will spin a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group forever until a new motion command is used or the program is stopped.\n\n- **forward** spins the Motor forward.\n- **reverse** spins the Motor in reverse.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(forward);\nMotor.spin(reverse);\n```","signature":"Motor.spin(forward);"},"motion_motor_spin_for":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_for","markdown":"# Spin Motor For\n\nSpins a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group for a given distance.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinFor(direction, rotation, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.spinFor` will spin a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group in the given direction for a given distance.\n\nPossible arguments:\n\n- `direction` accepts either **forward** or **reverse**\n- `rotation` accepts numeric values\n- `units` accepts either **degrees** or **turns**\n\nThe `Motor.spinFor` command will block other commands until the motor movement has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to tell the `Motor.spinFor` command to not block the program until the movement has completed.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinFor(reverse, 360, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Motor.spinFor(forward, 90, degrees);"},"motion_motor_spin_to_position":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_to_position","markdown":"# Spin Motor To Position\n\nSpins a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group to a set position.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinToPosition(rotation, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.spinToPosition` will tell a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group to spin to a specific position.\n\nBased on the current position of the Motor/Motor Group, `Motor.spinToPosition` will determine the direction to spin.\n\nThe `Motor.spinToPosition` command accepts numeric values for `rotation`.\n\nYou can specify the `units` of the rotation in either **degrees** or **turns**. \n\nThe `Motor.spinToPosition` command will block other commands until the motor movement has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to tell the `Motor.spinToPosition` command to not block the program until the movement has completed.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinToPosition(360, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Motor.spinToPosition(90, degrees);"},"motion_motor_stop":{"name":"motion_motor_stop","markdown":"# Stop Motor\n\nStops a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.stop();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.stop();\nArmMotor.stop();\n``` \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the ClawMotor open for 3 seconds before stopping.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.spin(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nClawMotor.stop();\n```","signature":"Motor.stop();"},"motion_pneumatics_cylinder_extend":{"name":"motion_pneumatics_cylinder_extend","markdown":"# Extend pneumatic cylinder\n\nSets the pneumatic solenoid to extend a specific cylinder.\n\n```cpp\nPneumatic1.extend(cylinder1);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `extend pneumatic cylinder` command will control the solenoid to set the airflow within the pneumatic system to extend the specified cylinder's piston.\n\n```cpp\nPneumatic1.extend(cylinder1);\n```","signature":"Pneumatic.extend(cylinder1);"},"motion_pneumatics_cylinder_retract":{"name":"motion_pneumatics_cylinder_retract","markdown":"# Retract pneumatic cylinder\n\nSets the pneumatic solenoid to retract a specific cylinder.\n\n```cpp\nPneumatic1.retract(cylinder1);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `retract pneumatic cylinder` command will control the solenoid to set the airflow within the pneumatic system to retract the specified cylinder's piston.\n\n```cpp\nPneumatic1.retract(cylinder1);\n```","signature":"Pneumatic.retract(cylinder1);"},"motion_pneumatics_pump_off":{"name":"motion_pneumatics_pump_off","markdown":"# Pneumatic Pump Off\n\nSets the pneumatic solenoid to turn the pneumatic pump off.\n\n```cpp\nPneumatic1.pumpOff();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **pneumatic pump off** command will control the power to the pump connected to the pneumatic solenoid. Turning the pump off will stop refilling the attached air tank.\n\n```cpp\nPneumatic1.pumpOff();\n```","signature":"Pneumatic.pumpOff();"},"motion_pneumatics_pump_on":{"name":"motion_pneumatics_pump_on","markdown":"# Pneumatic Pump On\n\nSets the pneumatic solenoid to turn the pneumatic pump on.\n\n```cpp\nPneumatic1.pumpOn();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **pneumatic pump on** command will control the power to the pump connected to the pneumatic solenoid. Turning the pump on will start refilling the attached air tank.\n\n```cpp\nPneumatic1.pumpOn();\n```","signature":"Pneumatic.pumpOn();"},"sensing_brain_battery_capacity":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_capacity","markdown":"# Battery Capacity\n\nReports the current capacity of the VEX IQ robot's battery.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Battery.capacity(percent)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Brain.Battery.capacity` returns an **integer** that represents the VEX IQ robot's battery capacity in the default unit of `percent`, and will return a value in the range of **0 to 100**.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will play an alarm sound if the VEX IQ robot's battery level is lower than 25%.\n\n```cpp\nif (Brain.Battery.capacity(percent) < 25){\n  Brain.playSound(alarm);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Battery.capacity(percent)"},"sensing_brain_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_column","markdown":"# Screen Cursor Column\n\nReports the column number of the VEX IQ Brain's screen cursor location.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.column()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\n`Brain.Screen.column` reports an integer which ranges from **1 to 21** if used with an IQ (1st generation) Brain.\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\nA value ranging from **1 to 28** is reported if used with an IQ (2nd generation) Brain, depending on what font is currently selected.\n\nThe value of `Brain.Screen.column` increases from left-to-right on the VEX IQ Brain's screen.","signature":"Brain.Screen.column()"},"sensing_brain_screen_pressing":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_pressing","markdown":"# Brain Button Pressing\n\nReports if the specified button on the VEX IQ Brain is being pressed.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Button.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReports **true** if the specified Brain button is pressed. Reports **false** if the specified Brain button is not pressed.\n\nAfter `Brain.` enter a Brain button to receive the pressed status on.\n\nAn IQ (1st generation) Brain and IQ (2nd generation) Brain has slightly different button options, but they can be interchangeably used on either Brain generation.\n\nSupported Brain buttons are as follows:\n- `buttonUp` / `buttonLeft`\n- `buttonDown` / `buttonRight`\n- `buttonCheck`\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the VEX IQ robot drive forward.\n\nThen, it will check for a press on the Brain's **buttonUp** and then turn the robot right indefinitely.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  if (Brain.buttonUp.pressing()) {\n    Drivetrain.turn(right);\n    break;\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Button.pressing()"},"sensing_brain_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_row","markdown":"# Screen Cursor Row\n\nReports the row number of the VEX IQ Brain's screen cursor location.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\n`Brain.Screen.row` reports an integer which ranges from **1 to 5** when used with an IQ (1st generation) Brain.\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the Brain's screen.\n\n| Font |  | Rows |  | Columns |\n| :--- | --- | :--- | --- | :--- |\n| Mono Extra Small (mono12) |  | 9 |  | 26 |\n| Mono Small (mono15) |  | 7 |  | 20 |\n| Mono Medium (mono20) (Default) |  | 5 |  | 16 |\n| Mono Large (mono30) |  | 3 |  | 10 |\n| Mono Extra Large (mono40) |  | 3 |  | 8 |\n| Mono Super Large (mono60) |  | 1 |  | 5 |\n| Prop Medium (prop20) |  | 5 |  | 28 |\n| Prop Large (prop30) |  | 3 |  | 21 |\n| Prop Extra Large (prop40) |  | 2 |  | 15 |\n| Prop Super Large (prop60) |  | 1 |  | 9 |\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.row` command reports an integer which ranges from **1 to 9** when used with an IQ (2nd generation) Brain, depending on what font is currently selected.\n\nThe value reported by `Brain.Screen.row` increases from top-to-bottom on the VEX IQ Brain's screen cursor location.","signature":"sensing_brain_screen_row"},"sensing_brain_timer_reset":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_reset","markdown":"# Reset Timer\n\nResets the VEX IQ Brain's timer.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.reset();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Brain's timer begins at the start of running a program. `Brain.Timer.reset` is used to reset the timer back to 0 seconds.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the timer will be reset before moving the Drivetrain forward for 3 seconds. After 3 seconds has elapsed, the Drivetrain will stop.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.reset();\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  if (Brain.Timer.value() > 3) {\n    break;\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"sensing_brain_timer_reset"},"sensing_brain_timer_value":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_value","markdown":"# Timer Value\n\nReports the value of the VEX IQ Brain's timer in seconds.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.value()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Brain's timer starts at 0 seconds when the program starts, and returns the timer's value as a decimal value (as a *double*).\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the value of the Brain's timer.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Timer: %.2f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n  \n  // Brief delay to prevent distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"sensing_brain_timer_value"},"sensing_bumper_pressing":{"name":"sensing_bumper_pressing","markdown":"# Bumper Pressing\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Bumper is being pressed.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Bumper.pressing` reports **true** if the Bumper is being pressed.\n\n`Bumper.pressing` reports **false** if the Bumper is not being pressed.\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nBumper2.pressing()\nBumper4.pressing()\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints whether a Bumper is being pressed to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Bumper Pressed: %s\", Bumper2.pressing() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Bumper.pressing()"},"sensing_color_brightness":{"name":"sensing_color_brightness","markdown":"# Color Brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nColor.brightness()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Color.brightness` reports a range of values from **0% to 100%**.\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nColor2.brightness()\nColor4.brightness()\n```\n\nA larger amount of light will report a higher value, while a smaller amount of light will report a lower value.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the amount of light detected by the Color Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Brightness: %d\", Color.brightness());\n```","signature":"Color.brightness()"},"sensing_color_colorname":{"name":"sensing_color_colorname","markdown":"# Color Of\n\nReports the name of the color detected by the VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nColor.colorname()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Color.colorname` reports one the following colors: \n- `red`\n- `red_violet`\n- `violet`\n- `blue_violet`\n- `blue`\n- `blue_green`\n- `green`\n- `yellow_green`\n- `yellow`\n- `yellow_orange`\n- `orange`\n- `red_orange`\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance. \n\n```cpp\nColor4.colorname()\nColor5.colorname()\n```","signature":"Color9.colorname()"},"sensing_color_detect":{"name":"sensing_color_detect","markdown":"# Color Detects\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Color Sensor detects the specified color.\n\n```cpp\nColor.detects(color)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReports **true** when the Color Sensor detects the specified color. Reports **false** when the Color Sensor detects a different color than the one specified.\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nColor1.detects(red)\nColor2.detects(blue)\n```\n\nChoose which color to detect.\n\n- `red`\n- `orange`\n- `yellow`\n- `green`\n- `blue`\n- `purple`\n- `violet`\n- `red_violet`\n- `blue_violet`\n- `blue_green`\n- `yellow_green`\n- `yellow_orange`\n- `red_orange`\n- `white`\n\nYou can also pass **colorType::none** as the specified `color` to check if the Color Sensor does **not** detect an object.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Color Red\" or \"Other Color\" depending on whether or not the Color Sensor detects the color \"red\".\n\n```cpp\nif (Color.detects(red)) { \n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Color Red\");\n} else {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Other Color\");\n}\n```","signature":"Color.detects(color)"},"sensing_color_hue":{"name":"sensing_color_hue","markdown":"# Color Hue\n\nReports the hue of the color detected by the VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nColor.hue()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Color.hue` reports a range of values from **0** to **360** degrees, which represents the position of the color on the color wheel.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example prints the hue of the color detected by the Color Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hue: %.0f\", Color.hue());\n```","signature":"Color.hue()"},"sensing_color_isNearObject":{"name":"sensing_color_isNearObject","markdown":"# Color Is Near Object\n\nReports if the Color Sensor detects an object or surface. \n\n```cpp\nColor.isNearObject()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nColor5.isNearObject()\nColor7.isNearObject()\n```\n\nReports **true** when the Color Sensor detects an object or surface close to the front of the sensor. \n\nReports **false** when the Color Sensor does not detect an object or surface close to the front of the sensor.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints whether an object or surface is being detected by the Color Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Is Near Object: %s\", Color.isNearObject() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"Color.isNearObject()"},"sensing_controller_axis_position":{"name":"sensing_controller_axis_position","markdown":"# Controller Axis Position\n\nReports the position of a joystick on the VEX IQ's Controller along the specified axis.\n\n```cpp\nController.Axis.position()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Controller.Axis.position` reports a range between **-100 to 100**.\n\n`Controller.Axis.position` will report **0** when a joystick axis is centered.\n\nChoose which Controller axis to report.\n\n* `AxisA` - left joystick (up and down)\n* `AxisB` - left joystick (left and right)\n* `AxisC` - right joystick (left and right)\n* `AxisD` - right joystick (up and down)\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will print the position of the Controller's AxisA axis to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"AxisA Position: %.0f\", Controller.AxisA.position());\n\n  // Brief wait to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\n```","signature":"Controller.Axis.position()"},"sensing_controller_button_pressing":{"name":"sensing_controller_button_pressing","markdown":"# Controller Button Pressing\n\nReports if the specified button on the VEX IQ's Controller is being pressed.\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller button to detect a press on.\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/cpp/en/sensing_controller_button_pressing/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonEUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonEDown.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonFUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonFDown.pressing()`\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/en/sensing_controller_button_pressing/controller_button_back.png)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonLUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonLDown.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonRUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonRDown.pressing()`\n\n`Controller.Button.pressing()` reports **true** if the specified Controller button is being pressed.\n\n`Controller.Button.pressing()` reports **false** if the specified Controller button is not being pressed.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below drives the VEX IQ robot forward. If the Controller's ButtonEUp button is pressed, the robot will then stop driving.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  if (Controller.ButtonEUp.pressing()) {\n    Drivetrain.stop();\n    break;\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\n```","signature":"Controller.Button.pressing()"},"sensing_distance_distance":{"name":"sensing_distance_distance","markdown":"# Distance From\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the VEX IQ Distance Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.distance(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance.distance` reports a range from **24mm to 1000mm** or **1 inch to 40 inches**.\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nDistance6.distance(mm)\nDistance8.distance(inches)\n```\n\nSpecify whether the value returned by `Distance.distance` is reported in **inches** or **mm** (millimeters). \n\n```cpp\nDistance6.distance(mm)\nDistance8.distance(inches)\n```","signature":"Distance.distance(units)"},"sensing_distance_found_object":{"name":"sensing_distance_found_object","markdown":"# Distance Found Object\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Distance Sensor detects an object within its field of view. \n\n```cpp\nDistance.foundObject()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReports **true** when the Distance Sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view. Reports **false** when the Distance Sensor does not detect an object or surface.\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance.\n\n```cpp\nDistance3.foundObject()\nDistance4.foundObject()\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints whether the Distance Sensor detects an object or surface in its range.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Found Object: %s\", Distance.foundObject() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"Distance.foundObject()"},"sensing_distance_is_object_detected":{"name":"sensing_distance_is_object_detected","markdown":"# Distance Object Detected\n\nReports if an IQ Distance Sensor detects an object or surface in its range.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.isObjectDetected()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance.isObjectDetected()` returns **true** if an object or surface is detected in its range, and **false** if not.\n\nThe snippet below will print **TRUE** or **FALSE** depending on whether an object or surface is detected.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%s\", Distance.isObjectDetected() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.isObjectDetected()"},"sensing_distance_object_distance":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Distance Object Distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object or surface from an IQ Distance Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.objectDistance(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance.objectDistance()` accepts **mm** or **inches** as units and reports a range from **20 mm to 2000 mm** (~0.8 inches to 79.0 inches ) as a decimal value.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Distance.objectDistance(inches));\n```\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Distance.objectDistance(mm));\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.objectDistance(inches)"},"sensing_distance_object_size":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_size","markdown":"# Distance Object Size\n\nReports an estimation of the detected object's size.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.objectSize()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance.objectSize()` can be used to determine if a detected object is of a certain size.\n\nThere are three defined sizes that can be used for comparison:\n\n* sizeType::large\n* sizeType::medium\n* sizeType::small\n\n```cpp\nif (Distance.objectSize() == sizeType::large) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Large object detected!\");\n}\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.objectSize()"},"sensing_distance_object_velocity":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Distance Object Velocity\n\nReports the velocity of a detected object in m/s.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.objectVelocity()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance.objectVelocity()` reports the current velocity of an object in m/s (meters per second).\n\nThe velocity of a detected object will change when the object is moving while in the range of an IQ Distance Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Distance.objectVelocity());\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.objectVelocity()"},"sensing_drivetrain_current":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_current","markdown":"# Drivetrain Current\n\nReports the amount of current that the Drivetrain is currently using.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.current(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drivetrain.current` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the amount of current the Drivetrain is currently using.\n\nThe `Drivetrain.current` command accepts **amp** (Amperes) as a valid `units` parameter.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the current (in Amperes) of the VEX IQ robot's Drivetrain to the Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.current(amp));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.current(units)"},"sensing_drivetrain_heading":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_heading","markdown":"# Drive Heading\n\nReports the heading that the Drivetrain is facing.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.heading(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drivetrain.heading` reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**.\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\nThe `Drivetrain.heading` command reports a counter-clockwise-positive heading as shown in the image below.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/cpp/en/sensing_drivetrain_heading/TopDownBot01.png)\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe `Drivetrain.heading` command can report a counter-clockwise or clockwise heading depending on whether intergrated brain inertial or a gyro sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the integrated inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\n![drivetrain_heading_clockwise](static/help/iq/cpp/en/sensing_drivetrain_heading/drivetrain_heading_clockwise.png)\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive heading, meaning that heading will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\n![drivetrain_heading_counterclockwise](static/help/iq/cpp/en/sensing_drivetrain_heading/drivetrain_heading_counterclockwise.png)\n\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the heading of the Drivetrain to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain Heading: %.2f\", Drivetrain.heading(degrees));\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.heading(degrees)"},"sensing_drivetrain_isDone":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_isDone","markdown":"# Drive Is Done\n\nReports if the Drivetrain has completed its movement.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.isDone()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drivetrain.isDone` reports **true** when the Drivetrain's motors have completed their movement.\n\n`Drivetrain.isDone` reports **false** when the Drivetrain's motors are still moving.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints whether the Drivetrain has completed its movements to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 1000, mm, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain is Done: %s\", Drivetrain.isDone() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.isDone()"},"sensing_drivetrain_isMoving":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_isMoving","markdown":"# Drive Is Moving\n\nReports if the Drivetrain is currently moving.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.isMoving()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command returns **true** if the Drivetrain is moving because of a `Drivetrain.driveFor` or `Drivetrain.turnFor` command that specifies a set distance.\n\nThis command returns **false** if the Drivetrain movement has completed.\n\n**Note:** This command will always return **false** if the Drivetrain is moving because of a `Drivetrain.drive` or `Drivetrain.turn` command (which do *not* specify a set distance to drive).\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints whether the Drivetrain is moving to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 1000, mm, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain is Moving: %s\", Drivetrain.isMoving() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.isMoving()"},"sensing_drivetrain_rotation":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_rotation","markdown":"# Drive Rotation\n\nReports the Drivetrain's angle of rotation in degrees when configured with a VEX IQ Gyro or Brain Inertial Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.rotation(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\n`Drivetrain.rotation` reports an increasing value when the Drivetrain turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n`Drivetrain.rotation` reports a decreasing value when the Drivetrain turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\nThe `Drivetrain.rotation` command can report a counter-clockwise or clockwise rotation depending on whether the intergrated brain inertial or a gyro sensor is configured in the Drivetrain configuration.\n\nIf the Drivetrain is configured with the integrated inertial sensor, the Drivetrain will have a clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns right.\n\nAlternatively, if the Drivetrain is configured with a gyro sensor, the Drivetrain will have a counter-clockwise-positive rotation, meaning that rotation will increase as the Drivetrain turns left.\n\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the rotation of the Drivetrain to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain Rotation: %.2f\", Drivetrain.rotation(degrees));\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.rotation(degrees)"},"sensing_drivetrain_velocity":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_velocity","markdown":"# Drivetrain Velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## How to Use\n`Drivetrain.velocity` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the current velocity of the Drivetrain. \n\n`Drivetrain.velocity` returns a value from **-100% to 100%** if the provided `units` is **percent**.\n\n`Drivetrain.velocity` can also take **rpm** (revolutions per minute) as the provided `units` parameter.\n\nIf a negative value is returned, it means that the Drivetrain is currently moving in reverse.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the Drivetrain's velocity (in percent) to the VEX IQ's Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.velocity(percent));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.velocity(units)"},"sensing_gyro_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_calibrate","markdown":"# Gyro Calibrate\n\nCalibrate the Gyro Sensor to reduce the amount of drift generated by the Gyro Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.calibrate(calibrationType);\n```\n\nDrifting occurs when the Gyro Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Gyro Sensor must remain still during the calibration process.\n\nThe `calibrationType` parameter can be replaced with any of the following options to set the calibration duration of the Gyro Sensor:\n- **calNormal** will calibrate the Gyro Sensor for 2 seconds\n- **calSlow** will calibrate the Gyro Sensor for 4 seconds\n- **calExtended** will calibrate the Gyro Sensor for 8 seconds","signature":"Gyro.calibrate(calibrationType);"},"sensing_gyro_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Gyro Heading\n\nReports a Gyro Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.heading()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Gyro.heading` reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99**.\n\nThe `Gyro.heading` command reports an increase in heading when rotating **counter-clockwise**.\n\nThe `Gyro.heading` command reports a decrease in heading when rotating **clockwise**.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the heading of the Gyro Sensor to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Gyro Heading: %.2f\", Gyro.heading());\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Gyro.heading()"},"sensing_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Gyro Rate\n\nReports the VEX IQ Gyro Sensor's rate of angular velocity.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.rate()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Gyro.rate` reports a range between **0 to 249.99** as degrees per second (DPS).","signature":"Gyro.rate()"},"sensing_gyro_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Gyro Rotation\n\nReports a VEX IQ Gyro Sensor's current rotation in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.rotation()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Gyro.rotation` reports an increasing value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n`Gyro.rotation` reports a decreasing value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the rotation of the Gyro Sensor to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Gyro Rotation: %.2f\", Gyro.rotation());\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Gyro.rotation()"},"sensing_gyro_setHeading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_setHeading","markdown":"# Gyro Set Heading\n\nSets the Gyro Sensor's current heading to the specified heading. \n\n```cpp\nGyro.setHeading(heading, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Gyro.setHeading` can be used to set the gyro's position to a heading in the range of **0** to **359.99**. \n\nThis command is typically used to reset the orientation of the gyro when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`Gyro.setHeading` can accept decimals or integer inputs.\n\n## Example\n\nThe below snippet sets the Gyro Sensor's current heading to 0 degrees.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"Gyro.setHeading(heading, degrees);"},"sensing_gyro_setRotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_setRotation","markdown":"# Gyro Set Rotation\n\nSets the VEX IQ Gyro Sensor's angle of rotation to the specified rotation. \n\n```cpp\nGyro.setRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Gyro.setRotation` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive (counter-clockwise) or negative (clockwise) value.\n\n`Gyro.setRotation` accepts a range of any positive or negative decimal or integer as the specified `rotation`.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below sets the rotation of the Gyro Sensor to -45 degrees.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setRotation(-45, degrees);\n```","signature":"Gyro.setRotation(rotation, degrees);"},"sensing_inertial_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Inertial Acceleration\n\nReports the acceleration value from one of the axes (x, y, or z) on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.  \n\n* The **X-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **forward to backward**\n* The **Y-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **side to side**\n* The **Z-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **up to down**\n\n```cpp\nBrainInertial.acceleration(xaxis)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`BrainInertial.acceleration()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) that ranges from **-4.0 to 4.0 Gs**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", BrainInertial.acceleration(xaxis));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", BrainInertial.acceleration(yaxis));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", BrainInertial.acceleration(zaxis));\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.acceleration(xaxis);"},"sensing_inertial_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_calibrate","markdown":"# Inertial Calibrate\n\nCalibrating the Inertial Sensor is used to reduce the amount of drift generated by the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nBrainInertial.calibrate();\n```\n\nDrifting occurs when the IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not physically moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe IQ (2nd generation) Brain's Inertial Sensor must remain still during the calibration process. The calibration process will take approximately 2 seconds to complete.","signature":"INERTIAL.calibrate();"},"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Inertial Gyro Rate\n\nGets the rate of rotation for the specified axis (x, y, or z) on the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor.\n\n* The **X-axis** reports rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the X-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* The **Y-axis** reports rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Y-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* The **Z-axis** reports rotations when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Z-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n```cpp\nBrainInertial.gyroRate(axis, dps)\n```\n\n## How To Use \n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon\n\n`BrainInertial.gyroRate()` is used to return a range from **-1000.0 to 1000.0** in dps (degrees per second). \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", BrainInertial.gyroRate(xaxis, dps));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", BrainInertial.gyroRate(yaxis, dps));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", BrainInertial.gyroRate(zaxis, dps));\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.gyroRate(xaxis, dps)"},"sensing_inertial_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_heading","markdown":"# Inertial Heading\n\nReports the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nBrainInertial.heading(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon\n\nThe `BrainInertial.heading(degrees)` command reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n`BrainInertial.heading(degrees)` reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(right);\nwaitUntil(BrainInertial.heading(degrees) > 180);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.heading(degrees)"},"sensing_inertial_orientation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Inertial Orientation\n\nGets an orientation angle of the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor. Reports the unit value specified by the parameter of the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor.\n\nThe orientation reported is determined by the selected axis (x, y, or z).\n\n* The **X-axis** represents **pitch**, which reports a value between -90 to +90 degrees.\n* The **Y-axis** represents **roll**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n* The **Z-axis** represents **yaw**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n\n---\n\nPitch is the rotation around the side to side axis.\n\n![IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Pitch](static/help/iq/cpp/en/sensing_inertial_orientation/IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Pitch.png)\n\nRoll is the rotation around the front to back axis.\n\n![IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Roll](static/help/iq/cpp/en/sensing_inertial_orientation/IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Roll.png)\n\nYaw is rotation around the vertical axis.\n\n![IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Yaw](static/help/iq/cpp/en/sensing_inertial_orientation/IQ_Gen2_Basebot_Yaw.png)\n\n---\n\n```cpp\nBrainInertial.orientation(axis, units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon\n\n```cpp\nwhile(!(BrainInertial.orientation(yaw, degrees) > 60));\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.orientation(pitch, degrees);"},"sensing_inertial_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_rotation","markdown":"# Inertial Rotation\n\nReports the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nBrainInertial.rotation(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe `BrainInertial.rotation(degrees)` command reports an increasingly **positive** value when the Inertial Sensor turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\n`BrainInertial.rotation(degrees)` reports an increasingly **negative** value when the Inertial Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(right);\nwaitUntil(BrainInertial.rotation(degrees) > 180);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.rotation(degrees)"},"sensing_inertial_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_heading","markdown":"# Inertial Set Heading\n\nSets the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial sensor's current heading position to a specified value.\n\n```cpp\nBrainInertial.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`BrainInertial.setHeading()` can be used to set the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial sensor's position to any clockwise-positive heading. This command is typically used to reset the orientation of the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial sensor when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`BrainInertial.setHeading()` accepts a range of **0.0 to 359.99** degrees.\n\n`BrainInertial.setHeading()` can accept decimals, integers, or other commands that return a numeric value.","signature":"INERTIAL.setHeading(0, degrees);"},"sensing_inertial_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_rotation","markdown":"# Inertial Set Rotation\n\nSets the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor's angle of rotation to the value provided.\n\n```cpp\nBrainInertial.setRotation(0, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Inertial.setRotation()` command can be used to set the IQ (2nd generation) Brain Inertial Sensor's angle of rotation to any given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\n`BrainInertial.setRotation()` accepts any positive or negative decimal or integer number.","signature":"INERTIAL.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"sensing_motor_current":{"name":"sensing_motor_current","markdown":"# Motor Current\n\nReports the amount of current a VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently using.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.current(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.current` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the amount of current a Motor or Motor Group is using.\n\nThe `Motor.current` command accepts **amp** (Amperes) as a valid `units` parameter.\n\nPrints the Motor/Motor Group's current in Amperes:\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.current(amp));\n```","signature":"Motor.current(units)"},"sensing_motor_isDone":{"name":"sensing_motor_isDone","markdown":"# Motor Is Done\n\nReports if the VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.isDone()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.isDone` reports **true** when the specified Motor/Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n`Motor.isDone` reports **false** when the specified Motor/Motor Group has not completed its movement.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints whether the ArmMotor has completed its movements to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 270, degrees, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"ArmMotor is Done: %s\", ArmMotor.isDone() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Motor.isDone()"},"sensing_motor_isSpinning":{"name":"sensing_motor_isSpinning","markdown":"# Motor Is Spinning\n\nReports if the selected VEX IQ Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently spinning.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.isSpinning()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command returns **true** if the specified Motor/Motor Group is currently spinning.\n\nThis command returns **false** if the specified Motor/Motor Group is not currently spinning.\n\n**Note:** This command will always return **false** if the Motor/Motor Group is spinning as a result of a previous `Motor.spin` command (which does *not* specify a set distance to spin).\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will print whether the ArmMotor is still spinning to the VEX IQ brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 270, degrees, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"ArmMotor is Spinning: %s\", ArmMotor.isSpinning() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Motor.isSpinning()"},"sensing_motor_position":{"name":"sensing_motor_position","markdown":"# Motor Position\n\nReports the current position of the encoder in the specified VEX IQ Smart Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.position(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.position` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the position of the encoder in a Motor or in the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\nReplace the `units` parameter with either **degrees** or **turns**.\n\nValues can be returned in **degrees**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Motor Position (Degrees): %.2f\", Motor.position(degrees));\n```\n\nValues can be returned in **turns**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Motor Position (Turns): %.2f\", Motor.position(turns));\n```","signature":"Motor.position(units)"},"sensing_motor_velocity":{"name":"sensing_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Motor Velocity\n\nReports the velocity of the specified VEX IQ Smart Motor or of the first motor in a Motor Group.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## How to Use\n\n`Motor.velocity` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the current velocity of a Motor or of the first motor in a Motor Group. \n\nSpecify the `units` when using this command.\n\n**percent** - will return a value from **-100% to 100%**.\n \n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.velocity(percent));\n```\n  \n`Motor.velocity` can also return values in **rpm** (revolutions per minute).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.velocity(rpm));\n```","signature":"Motor.velocity(units)"},"sensing_optical_brightness":{"name":"sensing_optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical Brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.brightness()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.brightness()` reports a range of values from **0% to 100%**.\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Optical.brightness());\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.brightness()"},"sensing_optical_color":{"name":"sensing_optical_color","markdown":"# Optical Color\n\nReturns the color detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\n// IQ (1st generation)\nOptical.colorname()\n\n// IQ (2nd generation)\nOptical.color()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Color` command returns the closest color match base on the hue of a detected object.\n\nThe following colors can be used as a comparison to the color detected by an IQ Optical Sensor:\n- red\n- green\n- blue\n- yellow\n- orange\n- purple\n- cyan\n\n### IQ (1st generation) Brain\n\n```cpp\nif (Optical.colorname() == red) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Red object detected!\");\n}\n```\n\n### IQ (2nd generation) Brain\n\n```cpp\nif (Optical.color() == red) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Red object detected!\");\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.color()"},"sensing_optical_gesture_detected":{"name":"sensing_optical_gesture_detected","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nReports detected gesture data from an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.getGesture()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command returns an object with gesture information. To check the type of the detected gesture, access the `type` property on the returned object.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.getGesture().type\n```\n\nBefore using any IQ Optical Sensor gesture commands, an IQ Optical Sensor must be correctly set to detect gestures with the `Optical.gestureEnable();` command.\n\nBelow are the gestures that an IQ Optical Sensor can detect:\n\n- `gestureType::up`\n- `gestureType::down`\n- `gestureType::left`\n- `gestureType::right`\n\n## Example\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set an IQ Optical Sensor to detect gestures before checking for gestures.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureEnable();\nwhile (Optical.getGesture().type != gestureType::up) {\n  wait(0.1, seconds);\n}\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Up!\");\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.getGesture()"},"sensing_optical_hue":{"name":"sensing_optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical Hue\n\nReports the hue of the object detected by an IQ Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.hue()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.hue()` reports a range of values from **0 to 359**, which represents the location of the detected color on a color wheel.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Optical.hue());\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.hue()"},"sensing_optical_is_near_object":{"name":"sensing_optical_is_near_object","markdown":"# Optical Is Near Object\n\nReports if an IQ Optical Sensor detects an object in its range.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.isNearObject()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.isNearObject()` returns **true** if an object is detected, and returns **false** otherwise.\n\nIt should be used to check if an object is close to the IQ Optical Sensor so that the color readings from the `Optical.color()` command is accurate.\n\n```cpp\nif (Optical.isNearObject() && Optical.color() == red) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Red object detected!\");\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.isNearObject()"},"sensing_optical_set_light":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light","markdown":"# Optical Set Light\n\nSets the state of the IQ Optical Sensor's LED.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLight(ledState);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.setLight()` can be used to set the state of the LED on the IQ Optical Sensor.\n\nIt accepts either **ledState::on** or **ledState::off** as a parameter.\n\n**ledState::on** will turn the LED on.\n\n**ledState::off** will turn the LED off.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLight(ledState::on);\nwait(2, seconds);\nOptical.setLight(ledState::off);\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.setLight(ledState::on);"},"sensing_optical_set_light_power":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Optical Set Light Power\n\nSets the intensity of an IQ Optical Sensor's LED.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLightPower(power, percent);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.setLightPower()` can be used to set the intensity of the LED on the IQ Optical Sensor.\n\nIt accepts a range of values from **0 to 100** as the first parameter.\n\nThe second parameter is **percent**.\n\nA higher value will increase the intensity of the LED, while a lower value will decrease the intensity.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLightPower(100, percent);\nOptical.setLight(ledState::on);\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.setLightPower(100, percent);"},"sensing_optical_set_mode_disable":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_mode_disable","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Disable\n\nSets an IQ Optical Sensor to detect colors.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureDisable();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Disable` command allows you to set an IQ Optical Sensor to detect colors.\n\nBy default, an IQ Optical Sensor will be set to detect colors.\n\n## Examples\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set an IQ Optical Sensor to detect colors after checking for gestures.\n\n```cpp\n// Detect gestures\nOptical.gestureEnable();\nwhile (Optical.getGesture().type != gestureType::up) {\n  wait(0.1, seconds);\n}\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Up!\");\n\nwait(1, seconds);\n\n// Detect colors\nOptical.gestureDisable();\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  if (Optical.color() == red) {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"Red Object!\");\n  } else {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"Not Red Object!\");\n  }\n  wait(0.02, seconds);\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureDisable();"},"sensing_optical_set_mode_enable":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_mode_enable","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Enable\n\nSets an IQ Optical Sensor to detect gestures.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureEnable();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Enable` command allows you to set an IQ Optical Sensor to detect gestures.\n\nBy default, an IQ Optical Sensor will be set to detect colors.\n\nBefore using any IQ Optical Sensor gesture commands, an IQ Optical Sensor must be correctly set to detect gestures.\n\n## Examples\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set an IQ Optical Sensor to detect gestures before checking for gestures.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureEnable();\nwhile (Optical.getGesture().type != gestureType::up) {\n  wait(0.1, seconds);\n}\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Up!\");\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureEnable();"},"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled":{"name":"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled","markdown":"# Controller Enable/Disable\n\n```cpp\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = false;\n```\n\nEnables or disables Controller-configured actions from the Devices menu.\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose to either enable or disable the configured Controller actions by declaring it as either `true` or `false`. By default, the Controller is Enabled in every project.\n\n## Example\n\nThe configured action in this example is using the robot's Drivetrain behavior set by the Controller's configuration in the Devices window.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/cpp/en/sensing_remote_control_code_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nThis example will have the configured Controller disabled when the program starts. \n\nThen, the robot will drive forward for 6 inches.\n\nFinally, the **controller enabled** command will enable the Controller to restore Controller driving behaviors.\n\n```cpp\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = false;\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 6.0, inches);\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = true;\n```","signature":"RemoteControlCodeEnabled = true;"},"sensing_touchled_pressing":{"name":"sensing_touchled_pressing","markdown":"# TouchLED Pressing\n\nReports if the VEX IQ TouchLED is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReports **true** if the selected TouchLED is being pressed. Reports **false** if the selected TouchLED is not being pressed.\n\nThe first part of the command is the device instance. \n\n```cpp\nTouchLED2.pressing()\nTouchLED4.pressing()\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below sets the TouchLED to **red**. When the TouchLED is pressed, its color is set to **green**.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(red);\n\nwhile (!TouchLED.pressing()) {\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nTouchLED.setColor(green);\n```","signature":"TouchLED.pressing()"},"sensing_vision_largestObject":{"name":"sensing_vision_largestObject","markdown":"# Vision Largest Object\n\nReturns the largest object that the Vision Sensor sees.\n\n```cpp\nVision.largestObject\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA call to `Vision.takeSnapshot` will need to be made before using the `Vision.largestObject` command.\n\nThe `Vision.largestObject` command will return an object of type `vision::object`.\n\n```cpp\n// Take a snapshot with the COLOR_SIG signature\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"X: %d\", Vision.largestObject.centerX);\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Y: %d\", Vision.largestObject.centerY);\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\nThe `Vision.largestObject` is of the type `vision::object` which has these properties which can be accessed.\n\n- `id` - A unique ID assigned to each object by the Vision Sensor, is an `int`\n- `originX` - The top left X position of the object, is an `int`\n- `originY` - The top left Y position of the object, is an `int`\n- `centerX` - The center X position of the object, is an `int`\n- `centerY` - The center Y position of the object, is an `int`\n- `width` - The width of the object, is an `int`\n- `height` - The height of the object, is an `int`\n- `angle` - The angle of the object, is a `double`\n- `exists` - If the vision sensor detects the object or not, is a `bool`","signature":"Vision.largestObject"},"sensing_vision_objectCount":{"name":"sensing_vision_objectCount","markdown":"# Vision Object Count\n\nReports how many objects the Vision Sensor detects. \n\n```cpp\nVision.objectCount\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMake sure you specify the Vision Sensor when using this command. \n\nA signature will need to be configured before the `Vision.objectCount` command can detect it.\n\nBefore the `Vision.objectCount` can report the number of objects detected, `Vision.takeSnapshot` will need to be called to capture a snapshot with the specified signature.\n\n`Vision.objectCount` will return the number of objects detected from the last snapshot.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below prints the number of objects detected by the Vision Sensor with the specified signature to the VEX IQ Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n\n  // Take a snapshot with the specified signature\n  Vision.takeSnapshot(SIGNATURE);\n\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Number of Objects Detected: %d\", Vision.objectCount);\n\n  // Take a new snapshot every 20 milliseconds\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Vision.objectCount"},"sensing_vision_objects":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects","markdown":"# Vision Objects\n\nReturns an array of all of the objects that the Vision Sensor detects.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA call to `Vision.takeSnapshot` will need to be made before accessing the `Vision.objects` array.\n\n`Vision.objects` is an array that contains all of the objects that the Vision Sensor detects in the captured snapshot.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\nvision::object firstObject = Vision.objects[0];\n```\nThis can be used like any other array. You can access the objects in it with the index of each element.\n\n```cpp\nvision::object visionObject = Vision.objects[0];\n```\n\nYou can also use it in control structures like **for loops**. The `Vision.objectCount` command can be used as a loop condition.\n\nThe snippet below prints the `centerX` and `centerY` values of each detected object to the VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\n\nfor(int i = 0; i < Vision.objectCount; i++) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"X: %d\", Vision.objects[i].centerX);\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Y: %d\", Vision.objects[i].centerY);\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n}\n```\n\nThe objects in the `Vision.objects` are of the type `vision::object` which has these accessible properties.\n\n- `id` - A unique ID assigned to each object by the Vision Sensor, is an `int`\n- `originX` - The top left X position of the object, is an `int`\n- `originY` - The top left Y position of the object, is an `int`\n- `centerX` - The center X position of the object, is an `int`\n- `centerY` - The center Y position of the object, is an `int`\n- `width` - The width of the object, is an `int`\n- `height` - The height of the object, is an `int`\n- `angle` - The angle of the object, is a `double`\n- `exists` - If the vision sensor detects the object or not, is a `bool`","signature":"Vision.objects"},"sensing_vision_objects_angle":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_angle","markdown":"# Objects angle\n\nReports the angle of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].angle\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision commands to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].angle` reports the angle of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 180 degrees**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.screen.print(MyVision.objects[0].angle);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].angle"},"sensing_vision_objects_centerx":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_centerx","markdown":"# Objects center X\n\nReports the X coordinate of the center of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].centerX\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision commands to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].centerX` reports the X coordinate of the center of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 315 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[1].centerX);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].centerX"},"sensing_vision_objects_centery":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_centery","markdown":"# Objects center Y\n\nReports the Y coordinate of the center of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].centerY\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision commands to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].centerY` reports the Y coordinate of the center of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 211 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[2].centerY);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].centerY"},"sensing_vision_objects_exists":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_exists","markdown":"# Objects exists\n\nReports if the Vision Sensor detects a configured object. \n\nAn object will need to be configured before the `Vision.objects[index].exists` command can detect it.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].exists\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMake sure you specify the Vision Sensor when using this command. \n\n\n`Vision.objects[index].exists` reports **true** when the Vision Sensor detects a configured object.\n\n`Vision.objects[index].exists` reports **false** when the Vision Sensor does not detect a configured object.\n\nBefore the `Vision.objects[index].exists` can report reports a **true** or **false** value, `Vision.takeSnapshot()` will need to be used.\n\n\n```cpp\nif(Vision.objects[0].exists){\n\n}\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].exists;"},"sensing_vision_objects_height":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_height","markdown":"# Objects height\n\nReports the height of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].height\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision commands to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].height` reports how tall the object is in pixels. It returns a value of **2 - 212 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[3].height);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].height;"},"sensing_vision_objects_width":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_width","markdown":"# Objects width\n\nReports the width of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].width\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision blocks to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].width` reports how wide the object is in pixels. It returns a value of **2 - 316 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[1].width);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].width;"},"sensing_vision_takeSnapshot":{"name":"sensing_vision_takeSnapshot","markdown":"# Vision Take Snapshot\n\nTakes a snapshot from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(signature);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Vision.takeSnapshot` will capture a signature from the Vision Sensor to be processed and analyzed for color signatures and codes.\n\nTo use the `Vision.takeSnapshot` command, the Vision Sensor will need to be configured with at least one signature before this command is called. The signature name will be automatically generated.\n\nFor example, if the instance of the Vision Sensor has the name `Vision1` and the signature is configured with the name `REDBOX`, the name of the signature will be `Vision1__REDBOX` and to take the snapshot with that signature you would then call:\n\n```cpp\nVision1.takeSnapshot(Vision1__REDBOX);\n```\n\nTypically, the `Vision.takeSnapshot` will need to be called first before using any other Vision Sensor commands.\n\nMake sure you specify the Vision Sensor and the vision signature when using this command. Vision signatures are configured from the Robot Configuration window.","signature":"Vision.takeSnapshot(signature);"},"sound_play_note":{"name":"sound_play_note","markdown":"# Play Note\n\nPlays the selected musical note.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playNote(octave, note, duration);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose an octave. The lowest is 1 and the highest is 7.\n\n*Note: Octave is currently unsupported on IQ (2nd Generation) Brains*\n\nChoose a note to play within that octave:\n- `C = 0`\n- `D = 1`\n- `E = 2`\n- `F = 3`\n- `G = 4`\n- `A = 5`\n- `B = 6`\n\nChoose a duration for the note to play in **milliseconds**:\n\n- A whole note plays for 1 second (1000 milliseconds)\n- A half note plays for 0.5 seconds (500 milliseconds)\n- A quarter note plays for 0.25 seconds (250 milliseconds)\n\nOnce a musical note starts playing, the proceeding command will begin executing immediately.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will play a Middle C note for 1 second.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playNote(4, 0, 1000);\n```","signature":"Brain.playNote(octave, note, duration);"},"sound_play_sound":{"name":"sound_play_sound","markdown":"# Play Sound\n\nPlays the specified sound effect through the VEX IQ's Brain's Speakers.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playSound(sound);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReplace `sound` with one of the following sounds to play.\n\n- `siren`\n- `wrongWay`\n- `wrongWaySlow`\n- `fillup`\n- `headlightsOn`\n- `headlightsOff`\n- `tollBooth`\n- `alarm`\n- `tada`\n- `doorClose`\n- `ratchet`\n- `wrench`\n- `siren2`\n- `ratchet2`\n- `alarm2`\n- `powerDown`\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below plays the **siren** sound.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playSound(siren);   \n```\n\nOnce a sound effect starts playing, the proceeding command will begin executing immediately.","signature":"Brain.playSound(sound);"},"variables_2d_arrays":{"name":"variables_2d_arrays","markdown":"# 2D Array Variables\n\nDeclares the type, name, length of a 2D array. \n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 },\n};\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDeclare what type of data will be stored in your 2D array. \n\n- `int`\n- `double`\n- `bool`\n\nName the array something descriptive and unique. Set the array dimensions inside 2 pairs of square brackets `[]` just after the array name. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new 2D array with 3 rows and 3 columns\n\nint my2DArray[3][3];\n```\n\nThe values in the array can be assigned when creating the array using curly brackets.\n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 }\n};\n```\n\nThe values can also be declared individually by index. The index always starts at zero. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new turnAngles array with 3 rows and 3 columns\nint turnAngles[3][3];\n\n// Assign values by index\nint turnAngles[0][0] = 45;\nint turnAngles[0][1] = 90;\nint turnAngles[0][2] = 180;\nint turnAngles[1][0] = 270;\n```\n\nTo read values from an array, provide the index of the specific element in the square brackets.\n\n```cpp\n// The angle variable will be assigned the value of 270\n\nint angle = turnAngles[1][0];\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows a **double** 2D array called `myAngles` that will be a 2D array of angles.\n\n```cpp\ndouble myAngles[2][3] = {\n  {45.5, 90.0, 88.2},\n  {25.0, 75.5, 45.0}\n};\n```","signature":"variables_2d_array"},"variables_arrays":{"name":"variables_arrays","markdown":"# Array Variables\n\nDeclares the type, name, and length of an array. \n\n```cpp\nint myArray[3] = { 1, 2, 3 };\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDeclare what type of data will be stored in your array. \n\n- `int`\n- `double`\n- `bool`\n\nName the array something descriptive and unique. Set the length of the array inside a pair of square brackets `[]` just after the array name. \n\n```cpp\nint turnAngles[3];\n```\n\nThe values in the array can be declared when creating the array using curly brackets.\n\n```cpp\nbool boolArray[2] = { false, true };\n```\n\nThe values can also be declared individually by index. The index always starts at zero. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new array of length 3\ndouble doubleArray[3];\n\n// Assign values to the array by index\ndouble doubleArray[0] = 1.5;\ndouble doubleArray[1] = 3.14;\ndouble doubleArray[2] = 2.18;\n```\n\nTo read values from an array, provide the index of a specific element in the square brackets.\n\n```cpp\n// Read the value at index 2 in integerArray\n\nint value = integerArray[2];\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the array to initial values and then report item #3 (index number 2) from the list to spin a Motor. \n\n```cpp\nint degreesArray[3] = { 30, 60, 90 };\nMotor.spinFor(forward, degreesArray[2], degrees);\n```","signature":"variables_arrays"},"variables_boolean":{"name":"variables_boolean","markdown":"# Boolean Variable\n\nStores a **true** or **false** value.\n\n`bool myBoolean = true;`\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Boolean variables** store a **true** or **false** value. Declare with the keyword `bool` in front of a unique and descriptive variable name and set it to equal either `true` or `false`. \n\n`bool goFast = true;`\n\nBooleans can be used inside of control statement conditionals. \n\n```cpp\nif (goFast) {\n  Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity(100, percent);\n}\n```","signature":"variables_boolean"},"variables_double":{"name":"variables_double","markdown":"# Double Variable\n\nSets a variable to a `double` type.\n\n`double myDouble = 1.5;`\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `double` variable type is a number that has a decimal point.\n\n`double pi = 3.14;`\n\nCreate a unique and descriptive variable name. Then, assign a value to your variable.\n\n`double turnAngle = 40.5;`","signature":"variables_double"},"variables_intergers":{"name":"variables_intergers","markdown":"# Integer Variable\n\nSets an integer variable with a declared name and value.\n\n`int myNumber = 10;`\n\n## How To Use\n\nCreate a unique and descriptive variable name.\n\n`int driveTime = 60;`\n\nAssign a value to your variable. A variable can equal the returned value of a sensing command or the result of an equation, as long as it is declared using the correct **type**.\n\n```cpp\nint lowBatteryLifeWarning = Brain.Battery.capacity(percent);\n```\n\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will assign the distance (in inches) detected by the VEX IQ Distance Sensor to the \"myVariable\" variable and use the value of \"myVariable\" to set the speed of the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nint myVariable = Distance7.distance(inches);\n\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(myVariable, percent);\n```","signature":"variables_intergers"},"variables_my_string":{"name":"variables_my_string","markdown":"# String Variable\n\nSets a variable to a **string** type.\n\n`char myString[] = \"my string\";`\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **string** variable type can be assigned any combination of numbers and letters, while it is enclosed in quotation marks `\" \"`.\n\nCreate a unique and descriptive variable name. Then, assign a value to your **string** variable. On IQ the **string** variable type can be assigned like this.\n\n`char driveMessage[] = \"Time to Drive!\";`","signature":"variables_my_string"}}},"es":{"blocks":{"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Añadir\n\nAgrega dos valores juntos e informa la suma.\n\n![add](static/help/iq/blocks/es/add/add.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Añadir** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLa longitud de **add** bloque encaja en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nAñadir dos números.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/es/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nAñadir con valores de variables.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/es/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nAñadir con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/es/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# Y\n\nInforma si dos condiciones booleanas son ambas verdaderas. \n\n![and](static/help/iq/blocks/es/and/and.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nEl bloque **y** reporta **true** cuando los dos condiciones son **true**. \n\nEl **y** bloque reporta **false** cuado uno (o los dos) condicione(s) son **false**.\n\nEl **y** bloque booleano reporta un **true** o **false** valor y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonal (de seis lados).\n\n![and_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/es/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo comprobará si dos botones en el VEX IQ Controller se están presionando al mismo tiempo.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/es/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nEl **y** bloque volverá **true** cuando los dos **Controller E Up button** y el **Controller L Down button** están siendo presionados.\n\nEl **y** bloque volverá **false** cuando uno (o los dos) de los botones del control no se presionan.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/es/and/and_truth.png)"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Nivel de la Batería\n\nInforma del nivel de carga de la batería del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Nivel de la Batería** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nEl bloque de reportero **nivel de la batería** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo reproducirá un sonido de alarma si el **nivel de la batería** del VEX IQ's Brain inferior al 50%\n\n![battery_capacity_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es/battery_level/battery_capacity_example_revised.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Variable Booleana \n\nReporta valor de una variable booleana.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nBloques de **Variable Booleana** se utilizan para reportar de un valor de **true** o **false** almacendo dentro de la variable. Utilice el **establecer variable booleana** bloque para establecer o actualizar el valor de una variable booleana.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/iq/blocks/es/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nEl bloque **Variable Booleana** reporta **true** o **false** valor y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nLas variables booleanas se crean utilizando el **Hacer un Booleano** botón.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"brain_button_pressed":{"name":"brain_button_pressed","markdown":"# Botón del Brain Presionado\n\nReporta si fue presionado un botón en el VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![button_pressed_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Botón del Brain Presionado** reporta **true** si se presiona el botón del Brain seleccionado.\n\n**Botón del Brain Presionado** reporta **false** si no esta se presiona el botón del Brain seleccionado.\n\nElige qué botón para usar del Brain.\n\n![button_pressed_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_options.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **Botón del Brain Presionado** reporta un **true** o **false** valor y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![brainButtonPressed_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_inserted.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el robot conduzca hacia adelante y dar vuelta a la derecha después de the que el botón **Up** se presiona.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_example_revised.png)\n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Romper\n\nSale de un bucle de repetición inmediatamente.\n\n![break](static/help/iq/blocks/es/break/break.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nCuando se añade a la repetición de bloque 'C', el bloque **romper** saldrá del bucle que se encuentra actualmente en. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo moverá el chasis hacia adelante y comprobará si el botón del VEX IQ Brain **up** esta presionado. \n\nSi el botón **up** esta **presionado**, el bloque **romper** saldrá del bucle de repetición para siempre y detendrá el chasis.\n\n![break_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Brillo de\n\nReporta de la cantidad de luz detectada por el VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Brillo de** reporta de un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija cuál Color Sensor utilizar.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **brillo de** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Emitir\n\nTransmite un mensaje para activar cualquier pila que comience con un bloque **cuando recibo** escuchando el mensaje transmitido.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/es/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa pila que envía la **emisión** seguirá ejecutando bloques al mismo tiempo que otras pilas que reciben el mensaje transmitido.\n\nElija el mensaje para **emitir**. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo mostrará rojo en el VEX IQ Touch LED y luego esperará dos segundos antes de emitir \"message1\" \n\nCuando se recibe el mensaje, la pila **cuando recibo** hará que el chasis se moverá hacia adelante, mientras que el ClawMotor se moverá hacia arriba al mismo tiempo. \n\nLas dos pilas continuarán ejecutándose al mismo tiempo que se indica en las flechas rojas.\n\n![broadcast_example_arrows](static/help/iq/blocks/es/broadcast/broadcast_example_arrows.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Emitir y Espera\n\nEmita un mensaje para activar las pilas que comienzan con un bloque **cuando recibo** escuchando el mensaje transmitido mientras que también pausa el resto de la pila.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa pila que transmite **emitir y espera** se detendrá hasta que se hayan completado las otras pilas que reciben el mensaje transmitido.\n\nElija el mensaje para **emitir**. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/iq/blocks/es/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo mostrará rojo en el VEX IQ Touch LED y luego esperará dos segundos antes de transmitir \"message1\". \n\nUna vez que el mensaje es recibido, la pila **cuando recibo** causará que el chasis se mueva hacia adelante y reproduzca un efecto de sonido.\n\nLa pila emitiendo esperará hasta que se complete la pila de recepción antes de continuar ejecutando bloques cómo se indica en las flechas rojas.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows_3](static/help/iq/blocks/es/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows3.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Calibrar Gyro\n\nCalibración del sensor VEX IQ Gyro se utiliza para reducir la cantidad de deriva generada por Gyro Sensor.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nLa deriva se produce cuando el sensor Gyro detecta incorrectamente el movimiento aunque el sensor no se esté moviendo.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl sensor Gyro debe permanecer inmóvil durante el proceso de calibración.\n\nElija qué Gyro Sensor utilizar.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nElija el tiempo que desea calibrar. Cuanto más tiempo calibra el Gyro Sensor, menos deriva ocurrirá.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_seconds](static/help/iq/blocks/es/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_seconds.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Cambiar Variable\n\nCambia una variable por el valor dado.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la variable que desea utilizar - la variable seleccionada también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **Cambiar Variable** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/iq/blocks/es/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\nEste ejemplo aumentará la variable que establece la velocidad del chasis por 10 cada vez **bucle de repetición** se repite.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows_new":{"name":"clear_all_rows_new","markdown":"# Borrar Todas las Filas\n\nBorra toda la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/es/clear_all_rows_new/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Borrar todas las filas** no restablecerá el cursor de la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain. Utilice el bloque **ajuste el cursor**  para restablecer el cursor de la pantalla de nuevo la posición deseada.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Hola\" durante un segundo y luego borrará toda la pantalla antes de imprimir \"Adiós\".\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/clear_all_rows_new/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"clear_row_new":{"name":"clear_row_new","markdown":"# Borrar Fila\n\nBorra una sola fila en el la plantilla del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/iq/blocks/es/clear_row_new/clear_row.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Borrar fila** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos entre **1 - 5** para establecer qué fila se va a borrar.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/es/clear_row_new/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Hola\" en la fila 2 columna 1 durante tres segundos antes de borrar la fila 2.\n\n![clear_row_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/clear_row_new/clear_row_example.png)"},"color_detects_color":{"name":"color_detects_color","markdown":"# Detecta color\n\nReporta si el VEX IQ Color Sensor detecta un color específico.\n\n![color_detects](static/help/iq/blocks/es/color_detects_color/color_detects.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Detecta color** reporta **true** cuando el sensor de color detecta el color seleccionado.\n\n**Detecta color** reporta **false** cuando el sensor de color detecta un color diferente al seleccionado.\n\nElija qué Sensor de Color utilizar.\n\n![color_detects_chosen](static/help/iq/blocks/es/color_detects_color/color_detects_chosen.png)\n\nElija el color que desea detectar.\n\n![color_detects_selected](static/help/iq/blocks/es/color_detects_color/color_detects_selected.png)\n\nEl Bloque booleano **Detecta color** reporta **true** o **false** valor y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![color_detects_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/es/color_detects_color/color_detects_shape.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Color Red\" u \"Otro Color\" dependiendo de si el Sensor de Color detecta o no el color \"rojo\".\n\n![color_detects_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/color_detects_color/color_detects_example.png)\n\n"},"color_of":{"name":"color_of","markdown":"# Color de\n\nReporta del nombre del color detectado por el VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es/color_of/color_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Color de** reporta uno de los siguientes colores: **rojo, rojo-violeta, violeta, azul-violeta, azul, azul-verde, verde, amarillo-verde, amarillo, amarillo-naranja, naranja o rojo-naranja.**\n\nElija cuál Sensor de Color utilizar.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es/color_of/color_of_color.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **color de** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![color_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/color_of/color_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Comentario\n\nPermite a los programadores escribir información para ayudar a describir su programa.\n\n![comment_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLos programadores profesionales utilizan comentarios a través de sus programas para ayudar a otros a entender su código. Los comentarios también pueden ayudar con la solución de problemas y la colaboración. \n\nAgregue texto en bloque **comentario** seleccionando primero el cuadrado transparente y eliminando cualquier texto existente. A continuación, escriba el nuevo texto.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/es/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nLos comentarios no cambian el programa o los bloques que lo rodean.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Control Activado/Desactivado\n\nActiva o desactiva las acciones configuradas del Control desde el menú dispositivos.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nSeleccione activar o desactivar las acciones del Control configuradas seleccionando el estado deseado en el menú desplegable. Por defecto, el Controlador está Activado en cada proyecto.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nLa acción configurada en este ejemplo es utilizar el comportamiento de Chasis del robot establecido por la configuración del Control en la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/blocks/es/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nEste ejemplo tendrá el controlador configurado Desactivado cuando se inicie el programa. \n\nLuego, el robot conducirá hacia adelante durante 6 pulgadas.\n\nPor último, el bloque **control Activado** permitirá al control restaurar los comportamientos de conducción del controlador.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Corriente del Motor\n\nInforma de la cantidad de energía que un VEX IQ Motor está utilizando actualmente en porcentaje (%) o amperios (amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Corriente del Motor** reporta de un rango de **0% to 100%** or **0.0 to 1.2 amps**. \n\nElija el Motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nElija si la corriente del Motor se reporta en % o en amperios.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **corriente del motor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Columna del Cursor\n\nReporta del número de columna de la ubicación del cursor del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Columna del Cursor** reporta de un rango de **1 a 21**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/es/cursor_column/row_column_index.png)  \n\nEl bloque de reportero **columna del cursor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo comprobará si la posición de la **columna del cursor** es mayor que 15. Si la posición es mayor que 15, el proyecto establecerá el cursor en la fila 1, columna 1, y luego imprimirá el valor de \"Hello\".\n\n![cursor_column_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/es/cursor_column/cursor_column_example_simple.png)\n\n"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Fila del cursor\n\nInforma del número de fila de la ubicación del cursor del VEX IQ Brain Screen.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## cómo utilizar\n\n**Fila del cursor** reporta de un rango de **1 a 5**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/es/cursor_row/row_column_index.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **fila del cursor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo comprobará si la **posición** de la fila del cursor es mayor que 4. Si la posición es mayor que 4, el proyecto establecerá el cursor en la fila 1, columna 1 y, a continuación, imprimirá en \"Hola\"\n\n![cursor_row_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/es/cursor_row/cursor_row_example_simple.png)"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Distancia de\n\nReporta la distancia del objeto más cercano desde al VEX IQ Distance Sensor.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Distancia de** reporta de un rango de **24mm a 1000mm** o **1 inch a 40 inches**.\n\nElija qué Sensor de Distancia utilizar.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/iq/blocks/es/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nElija si **distancia de** se reporta en pulgadas o milímetros. \n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **distancia de** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Dividir\n\nDivide el primer valor por el segundo valor e informa del dividendo.\n\n![divide](static/help/iq/blocks/es/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Dividir** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **dividir** se adapta a bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nIntroduzca los números que se van a dividir.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/es/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nDividir con valores de variables.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/es/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nDividir con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/es/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Conducir\n\nMueve el Tren Mortiz por siempre.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **conducir** ejecutará el Tren Mortiz para siempre hasta que se utilice un nuevo bloque Tren Mortiz o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija la dirección en la que se moverá el Tren Mortiz.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Corriente del Tren Mortiz\n\nReporta la cantidad de corriente (potencia) que el tren mortiz está utilizando actualmente.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Corriente del Tren Mortiz** reporta de un rango de **0% a 100%** o **0.0 to 1.2 amps**. \n\nElija si la **corriente del tren mortiz** se indica en % o amperios (amps).\n\n![drive_current_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_current/drive_current_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **corriente del tren mortiz** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Conducir por\n\nMueve el chasis para una distancia determinada.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija en qué dirección se moverá el chasis.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\nEl bloque **conducir por** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEstablezca hasta dónde se moverá el chasis introduciendo un valor y eligiendo la unidad de medida (pulgadas o milímetros).\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nAutomáticamente, otros bloques **esperarán** hasta que el chasis termine de moverse.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandirla **y no espere** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen ejecutándose mientras el chasis se mueve.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Dirección del Chasis\n\nReporta la dirección que enfrenta el chasis.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Dirección del Chasis** reporta de un rango de **0.00 a 359.99 grados**.\n\nEl **dirección del chasis** informa de un encabezado en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj como se muestra en la imagen de abajo.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_heading/TopDownBot01.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **dirección del chasis** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Conducir ya termino\n\nInforma si el chasis ha completado su movimiento.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Conducir ya termino** reporta **true** cuando los motores del chasis han completado su movimiento.\n\n**Conducir ya termino** reporta **false** cuando los motores del chasis todavía están en movimiento.\n\nEl bloque booleano **drive is done** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis caras).\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Tren Mortiz esta Moviendo\n\nReporta si el chasis se está moviendo actualmente.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Tren Mortiz esta Moviendo** reporta **true** cuando los motores del tren mortiz se está moviendo.\n\n**Tren Mortiz esta Moviendo** reporta **false** cuando los motores del tren mortiz de mando se detienen.\n\nEl bloque booleano **tren mortiz esta moviendo** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Rotación del Chasis\n\nInforma del ángulo de rotación del Chasis en grados cuando se configura con un VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Rotación del chasis** informa de un valor **positivo** cuando el Chasis gira en una dirección **en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj**.\n\n**Rotación del Chasis** informa de un valor **negativo** cuando el Chasis gira en una dirección **en el sentido de las agujas del reloj**..\n\nEl bloque de reportero **rotación del Chasis** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad del Chasis\n\nReporta la velocidad actual del chasis.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Velocidad del Chasis** reporta de un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-127rpm a 127rpm**\n\nElija si la velocidad se notifica en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **velocidad del chasis** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Igual a\n\nReporta si el primer valor es el mismo que (igual) al segundo valor. \n\n![equal_to](static/help/iq/blocks/es/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Igual a** reporta **true** cuando los dos valores son exactamente los mismos.\n\n**Igual a** reporta **false** cuando los dos valores no son los mismos.\n\nEl bloque **igual a** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque booleano **igual a** reporta un valor **true** or **false** y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Drivetrain Stalled\" en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain si la corriente del chasis es igual al 100%.\n\n![equal_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/equal_to/equal_to_example.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Por Siempre\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite cualquier bloque contenido en su interior para siempre.\n\n![forever](static/help/iq/blocks/es/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nColoque bloques en el bloque **por siempre** 'C' para que esas acciones se repitan **por siempre**.\n\nPuedes salir de un circuito de **por siempre** colocando un bloque de **romper** adentro.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nLos bloques 'C' también pueden colocarse entre sí. Este concepto se denomina anidamiento, que puede ayudar a ahorrar tiempo al programar diferentes comportamientos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo reproducirá el mismo efecto de sonido cada 5 segundos por siempre.\n\n![forever_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/forever/forever_example.png)"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Función\n\nRealiza una función matemática seleccionada.sinestesia\n\n![function](static/help/iq/blocks/es/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - valor absoluto\n* **floor** - redondea hacia abajo al entero más cercano\n* **ceiling** - redondea hasta el entero más cercano\n* **sqrt** - raíz cuadrada\n* **sin** - seno\n* **cos** - coseno\n* **tan** - tangente\n* **asin** - arcoseno o el inverso del seno\n* **acos** - arcocoseno o el inverso del coseno\n* **atan** - arco o el inverso de tangente\n* **ln** - el logaritmo natural base e\n* **log** - base del logaritmo 10\n* **e ^** - poderes de e\n* **10 ^** - poderes de 10\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **función** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija la **función** matemática de una lista de opciones.\n\n![function_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/function/function_select.png)\n\nLa longitud del bloque **función** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\n![function_fit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Más que\n\nReporta si el primer valor es más grande (mayor) que el segundo valor.  \n\n![greater_than](static/help/iq/blocks/es/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Más que** reporta **true** cuando el primer valor es mayor que el segundo valor. \n\n**Más que** reporta **false** cuando el primer valor es menor o igual que el segundo valor.\n\nEl bloque **más que** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque booleano **más que** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis caras).\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Nivel de batería bueno\" en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain si el nivel de batería es superior al 75%.\n\n![greater_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/greater_than/greater_than_example.png)\n\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Dirección de Gyro\n\nReporta la dirección actual del encabezamiento del VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Dirección de Gyro** informa de un rango entre **0.00 a 359.99**.\n\nEl bloque **dirección de Gyro** reporta un rumbo en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj como se muestra en la imagen siguiente.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/es/heading_of_gyro/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\nElija qué Gyro Sensor comprobar.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **heading of Gyro** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"hue_of":{"name":"hue_of","markdown":"# Matiz de\n\nInforma del matiz del color detectado por el VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es/hue_of/hue_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Matiz de** reporta de un rango de **0 a 360**.\n\nElija qué sensor de color desea comprobar.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es/hue_of/hue_of_color.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **matiz de** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![hue_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/hue_of/hue_of_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Si entonces\n\nUn bloque 'C' que ejecuta los bloques en el interior si se notifica que la condición booleana es **true**.  \n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/es/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nEl bloque 'C' **si entonces** solo comprobará la condición booleana una vez. \n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta **true**, los bloques dentro de **si entonces** se ejecutarán.\n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta **false**, los bloques dentro de **si entonces** se omitirán.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **if then** puede aceptar bloques hexagonales (seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/es/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo reproducirá un efecto de sonido cada vez que se pulse el VEX IQ Bumper Switch.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **si entonces** puede ser anidado o colocado dentro del bloque \"por siempre\" para asegurar que el efecto de sonido se reproduce cada vez en lugar de una sola vez. \n\n![if_then_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/if_then/if_then_example.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Si entonces si no\n\nUn bloque 'C' que ejecuta los bloques dentro de la primera o segunda parte de la **si entonces si no** dependiendo del valor booleano reportado.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/es/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque 'C' **si entonces si no**  sólo comprobará la condición booleana una vez. \n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **true**, los bloques dentro de la section **si** se ejecutará.\n\nSi la condición booleana es **false**, los bloques dentro de la section **else** se ejecutará.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **si entonces si no** puede aceptar bloques hexagonales (de seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/es/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo será verde si se pulsa el VEX IQ Touch LED y estará en rojo cuando no se pulse el Touch LED.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **si entonces si no**  puede estar ubicado â o colocado dentro del bloque \"por siempre\" para asegurar que el Touch LED se vuelva rojo y verde más de una vez. \n\n![if_then_else_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/if_then_else/if_then_else_example.png)"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Elemento de la lista 2D\n\nReporta el valor de un elemento en una lista 2D. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la lista 2D que desea utilizar. La lista 2D también se puede cambiar de nombre o eliminar.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nIntroduzca la fila del elemento (primer número) y la posición de columna (segundo número) dentro de la lista que se reportara. Aquí, el elemento en la fila de posición 2, columna 3 de la lista 2D se está reportando.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nEl bloque **Elemento de la lista 2D** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Elemento de\n\nReporta el valor de un elemento de una lista. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la lista que desea utilizar. La lista también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nIntroduzca el número de la posición del elemento dentro de la lista. Aquí, el segundo elemento de la lista (punto 2) se está reportando. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nEl bloque **elemento de** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá la velocidad del chasis al valor almacenado en el elemento 3. El chasis ahora avanzará a una velocidad del 90%.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Longitud de la lista 2D\n\nReporta el número de filas o columnas de una lista 2D.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/es/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija qué lista 2D utilizar. La lista 2D también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nElija el valor que desea reportar. La lista 2D puede reportar **filas** o **columnas**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **longitud de la lista 2D** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Menos que\n\nReporta si el primer valor es menos (más pequeño) que el segundo valor. \n\n![less_than](static/help/iq/blocks/es/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Menos que** reporta **true** cuando el primer valor es menos que el segundo valor. \n\n**Menos que** reporta **false** cuando el primer valor es mayor o igual que el segundo valor.\n\nEl bloque booleano **menos que** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\nEl bloque **menos que** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Low Battery!\" en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain si el nivel de batería es inferior al 25%.\n\n![less_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/less_than/less_than_example.png)\n\n"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor ha terminado\n\nReporta si el motor seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Motor ha terminado** reporta **true** cuando el motor seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\n**Motor ha terminado** reporta **true** cuando el motor seleccionado todavía se está moviendo.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **motor is done** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\nEl bloque para reportar si el motor ha terminado se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados) para otros bloques. \n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor esta girando\n\nReporta si el motor seleccionado está girando actualmente.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/iq/blocks/es/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Motor esta girando** reporta **true** cuando el motor seleccionado está girando.\n\n**Motor esta girando** reporta **false** cuando el motor seleccionado está parado.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **motor is spinning** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Multiplicar\n\nMultiplica los dos valores juntos e informa del producto.\n\n![multiply](static/help/iq/blocks/es/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Multiplicar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **multiply** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nMultiplicar dos números.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/es/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nMultiplicar con valores de variables.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/es/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nMultiplique con los valores de los sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/es/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row_new":{"name":"next_row_new","markdown":"# Siguiente fila\n\nEstablece la salida de impresión en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain en la siguiente fila disponible.\n\n![next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/es/next_row_new/next_row.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nDe forma predeterminada, todos los proyectos comienzan con el cursor de pantalla en la fila 1 columna 1. El bloque **siguiente fila** moverá el cursor hacia abajo por una sola fila en la pantalla del IQ Brain. \n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/es/next_row_new/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"primer mensaje\" y luego pondrá el cursor en la siguiente fila disponible antes de imprimir \"segundo mensaje\".\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/next_row_new/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/blocks/es/next_row_new/set_cursor_welcome.png)\n"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# No\n\nReporta de lo contrario (inverso) del resultado booleano\n\n![not](static/help/iq/blocks/es/not/not.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **no** reporta **true** cuando el bloque booleano adentro reporta **false**.\n\nEl bloque **no** reporta **false** cuando el bloque booleano adentro reporta **true**.\n\nEl bloque booleano **no** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\nEste ejemplo reportara **true** cuando el botón de \"comprobar\" del VEX IQ Brain no se presiona. \n\n![not_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/es/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/es/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Recuento de objetos\n\nReporta de cuántos objetos detecta el Vision Sensor. \n\nUn objeto tendrá que configurarse antes de que el bloque **recuento de objetos** pueda detectarlo.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija qué Vision Sensor utilizar.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **instantánea de** tendrá que utilizarse antes del bloque **recuento de objetos** reporta un número de objetos.\n\nEl bloque **recuento de objetos** sólo detectará el número de objetos de la última firma de instantánea.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Objeto existe\n\nReporta si el Vision Sensor detecta un objeto configurado. \n\nUn objeto tendrá que configurarse antes de que el bloque **object exista** puede detectarlo.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija qué Vision Sensor utilizar.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n**Objeto exista** reporta **true** cuando el Vision Sensor detecta un objeto configurado.\n\n**Objeto exista** reporta **false** cuando el Vision Sensor no detecta un objeto configurado.\n\nEl bloque booleano **objeto exista** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nEl bloque **instantánea de** tendrá que utilizarse antes de que el bloque booleano **objeto exista** reporta un valor **true** o **false**."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Objeto encontrado\n\nReporta si el VEX IQ Distance sensor ve un objeto dentro de su campo de visión. \n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Objeto encontrado** reporta **true** cuando el Distance Sensor ve un objeto o una superficie dentro de su campo de visión.\n\n**Objeto encontrado** reporta **false** cuando el Distance Sensor no detecta ningún objeto o superficie.\n\nElija qué Distance Sensor utilizar.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **objeto encontrado** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"object_is_near":{"name":"object_is_near","markdown":"# Objeto Cercano\n\nInforma si el VEX IQ Color Sensor detecta un objeto cercano.\n\n![object_is_near](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_is_near/object_is_near_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Objeto Cercano** reporta **true** cuando el sensor de color detecta un objeto o superficie cerca de la parte frontal del sensor.\n\n**Objeto Cercano** reporta **false** cuando el sensor de color detecta el espacio  vacío delante del sensor.\n\nElija cuál sensor de color utilizar.\n\n![object_is_near_color](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_is_near/object_is_near_color.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **objeto cercano** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![object_is_near_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/object_is_near/object_is_near_inserted.png)\n\n\n "},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# O\n\nReporta si una de las dos condiciones booleanas son verdaderas.\n\n![or](static/help/iq/blocks/es/or/or.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **true** cuando una (o ambas) de las condiciones son **true**. \n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **false** cuando ambas condiciones son **false**.\n\nEl bloque booleano **o** reporta **true** o **false** valor y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **true** cuando (o ambos) se presionan el VEX IQ Bumper y el VEX IQ Touch LED y reporta **false** sólo cuando el parachoques y el LED táctil no se presionan.\n\n![or_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/es/or/or_truth.png)"},"play_note":{"name":"play_note","markdown":"# Tocar nota\n\nToca la nota musical seleccionada.\n\n![play_note](static/help/iq/blocks/es/play_note/play_note.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nElija una nota musical.\n\n![play_note_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/play_note/play_note_select.png)\n\nSeleccione cuánto tiempo (duración) se tocara la nota.\n\n![play_note_duration](static/help/iq/blocks/es/play_note/play_note_duration.png)\n\n* Una nota **entera** se reproduce durante 1 segundo (1000 milisegundos)\n* Una nota de **media** se reproduce durante 0.5 segundos (500 milisegundos)\n* Una nota de **cuarto** se reproduce durante 0.25 segundos (250 milisegundos)\n\nUna vez que una nota musical comienza a reproducirse, el siguiente bloque comenzaróก inmediatamente.\n"},"play_sound":{"name":"play_sound","markdown":"# Tocar Sonido\n\nReproduce el efecto de sonido seleccionado.\n\n![play_sound](static/help/iq/blocks/es/play_sound/play_sound.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el efecto de sonido de una lista de opciones. \n\n![play_sound_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/play_sound/play_sound_select.png)\n\nUna vez que un efecto de sonido comienza a tocar, el siguiente bloque comenzará inmediatamente."},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Posición del Controller\n\nReporta la posición de un joystick en el controller a lo largo de un eje.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Posición del Controller** informa de un rango entre **-100 a 100**.\n\n**Posición del Controller** reportara (0) cuando un eje joystick está centrado.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nElija el eje del joystick para comprobar su posición.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nEl bolque reportero **posición del controller** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo comprobará repetidamente el eje D del joystick de mando del controlador para controlar la velocidad del motor del brazo.\n\n![position_of_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Posición del motor\n\nReporta la distancia que ha recorrido el motor.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Posición del motor** reporta la posición del motor en números enteros para grados y números decimales para giros.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nElija si el valor se reporta en grados rotados o en giros del motor. \n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **posición del motor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Presionando el parachoques\n\nReporta si el VEX IQ Bumper Switch esta presionado .\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/es/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Presionando el parachoques** reporta **true** si se está presionando el interruptor del parachoques.\n\n**Presionando el parachoques** reporta **false** si no se está presionando el interruptor del parachoques.\n\nElija el interruptor del parachoques que desea utilizar.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/es/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **presionando el parachoques** reporta un **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Presionando controller\n\nReporta si está presionado un botón en el VEX IQ Controller.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Presionando controller** reporta **true** si se está presionando el botón del controller seleccionado.\n\n**Presionando controller** reporta **false** si no se está presionando el botón del controller seleccionado.\n\nElija el botón Controller que desea utilizar.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **presionando controller** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo comprobará si se pulsa el botón E Up y hará girar el motor de garras hacia delante si lo está. \n\n![pressing_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_example_revised.png)"},"pressing_touchled":{"name":"pressing_touchled","markdown":"# Presionando Touch LED\n\nReporta si el VEX IQ Touch LED se está presionando.\n\n![pressing_touch_led](static/help/iq/blocks/es/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Presionando Touch LED** reporta **true** si el Touch LED seleccionado se está presionando.\n\n**Presionando Touch LED** reporta **false** si el Touch LED seleccionado no se está presionando.\n\nElija el LED táctil que desea utilizar.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_led](static/help/iq/blocks/es/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_led.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **presionando Touch LED** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![pressing_touch_led_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_inserted.png)\n\n"},"print_new":{"name":"print_new","markdown":"# Imprimir\n\nImprime valores o texto en la pantalla de VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/es/print_new/look_print.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **imprimir** imprimirá los datos en la ubicación del cursor en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain.\n\nTodos los nuevos proyectos comienzan con el cursor de pantalla en la fila 1, columna 1.\n\nTodos los bloques de informador se imprimirán como números enteros de forma predeterminada. Utilice el bloque **establecer precisión de impresión** para ajustar el número de decimales impresos.\n\nImprima palabras y números.\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/es/print_new/print_words.png)\n\nImprima el valor reportado a partir de una variable.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/es/print_new/print_variable1.png)  \n\nImprima el cálculo reportado de un operador.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/es/print_new/print_addition.png)  \n\nImprima el valor reportado desde un sensor o dispositivo.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/print_new/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Mi bloque\n\nMis bloques se utilizan para crear bloques personalizados.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Mis bloques** se utilizan para crear una secuencia de bloques que se pueden utilizar varias veces a lo largo de un proyecto. \n\n**Mis bloques** se realizan utilizando el botón **Crear un Bloque**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Mis bloques** puede tener múltiples parámetros - etiquetas de texto, variables numéricas y variables booleanas - para agregar más funcionalidad a su bloque personalizado.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nPara usar un **mi bloque**, adjunte la llamada **mi bloque** a un bloque con tapa. Cuando se alcanza el **mi bloque** en su proyecto, la pila dentro del **mi bloque** se ejecutará utilizando los valores de parámetro especificados.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nAdjunte una pila de bloques al bloque con tapa \"definir\" **mis bloques** para establecer la acción que se produce cuando se utiliza un **mi bloque**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Nota: La creación de varios Mis bloques con las mismas etiquetas y variables puede provocar errores al descargar el proyecto.***\n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **mis bloques** para:\n\n* Reproducir el sonido de la sirena 3 veces.\n* Conducir hacia adelante durante 12 pulgadas.\n* Reproducir el sonido de la sirena 3 veces.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_call/sound_example.png)\n\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **mis bloques** para:\n\n* Conducir hacia adelante durante 15 pulgadas\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del Brain\n* Gira el robot 180 grados a la derecha\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del Brain\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Mi Bloque\n\nMis bloques se utilizan para crear bloques personalizados.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Mis bloques** se utilizan para crear una secuencia de bloques que se pueden utilizar varias veces a lo largo de un proyecto. \n\n**Mis bloques** se hacen usando el botón **Crear un Bloque**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Mis bloques** puede tener múltiples parámetros - etiquetas de texto, variables numéricas y variables booleanas - para agregar más funcionalidad a su bloque personalizado.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nPara usar un **mi bloque**, adjunte la llamada **mi bloque** a un bloque con tapa. Cuando se alcanza el **mi bloque** en su proyecto, la pila dentro del **mi bloque** se ejecutará utilizando los valores de parámetro especificados.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nAdjunte una pila de bloques al bloque con tapa \"definir\" **mis bloques** para establecer la acción que se produce cuando se utiliza un **mi bloque**..\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Nota: La creación de varios Mis bloques con las mismas etiquetas y variables puede provocar errores al descargar el proyecto.***\n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **mis bloques** para:\n\n* Reproducir el sonido de la sirena 3 veces.\n* Conducir hacia adelante durante 12 pulgadas.\n* Reproducir el sonido de la sirena 3 veces.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_definition/sound_example.png)\n\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **mis bloques** para:\n\n* Conducir hacia adelante durante 15 pulgadas\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del Brain\n* Gira el robot 180 grados a la derecha\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del Brain\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/es/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Al azar\n![random](static/help/iq/blocks/es/random/random.png)\n\nInforma de un valor aleatorio entre los valores más bajos y más altos del bloque.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa longitud del bloque **al azar** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nEl bloque **al azar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEste ejemplo utiliza un bloque **al azar** para aleatorizar la velocidad del chasis.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/iq/blocks/es/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nEste ejemplo utiliza un bloque **al azar** para aleatorizar la longitud de un bloque de espera.\n\n![random_control](static/help/iq/blocks/es/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"rate_of_gyro":{"name":"rate_of_gyro","markdown":"# Tasa de giroscopio\n\nInforma de la velocidad angular del sensor VEX IQ Gyro.\n\n![rate_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Tasa de giroscopio** reporta de un rango de **0 a 249.99 dps** (grados por segundo).\n\n**Tasa de giroscopio** reporta valores en grados por segundo (dps).\n\nElija que sensor de giroscopio utilizar.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **tasa de giroscopio** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_inserted.png)"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# El resto\n\nDivide el primer valor por el segundo valor y reporta el resto.\n\n![remainder](static/help/iq/blocks/es/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **el resto** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLos números que se dividen uniformemente reportarán un resto de cero.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **el resto** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\nEste ejemplo dividirá 7 y 2 e informará el resto para imprimir \"1\" en la pantalla de VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/es/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Repetir\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques contenidos en el interior durante un número determinado de veces.\n\n![repeat](static/help/iq/blocks/es/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPrimero introduzca un valor para indicar cuántas veces se va a utilizar la pila **repetir** los bloques contenidos en el interior.\n \nEl bloque 'C' **repetir** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLos bloques 'C' también se pueden poner dentro unos de otros. Este concepto es llamado anidando que puede ayudar a ahorrar el tiempo programando comportamientos diferentes.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/repeat/repeat_select.png)\n\nEste ejemplo repetirá la reproducción de un efecto de sonido cada 3 segundos durante 5 veces.\n\n![repeat_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/repeat/repeat_example.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Repita hasta que\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques dentro hasta que se notifica que la condición booleana es **true**.  \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/es/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Repita hasta que** sólo comprobará la condición booleana al principio de cada bucle. \n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **false**, los bloques dentro de **repita hasta que** se ejecutará.\n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **true**, los bloques dentro de **repita hasta que** se omitirá.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **repita hasta que** puede aceptar bloques hexagonales (de seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/es/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá el valor del temporizador en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain y moverá el Chasis hacia adelante hasta que se presione el botón **check** en el VEX IQ Brain. Una vez que el botón **check** se pulsa, el chasis se detendra.\n\n![repeat_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/repeat_until/repeat_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Restablecer temporizador\n\nRestablece el temporizador del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/iq/blocks/es/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl temporizador del VEX IQ Brain comienza al principio de cada proyecto. El bloque **restablecer temporizador** se utiliza para restablecer el temporizador a 0 segundos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el temporizador se restablecerá antes de mover el chasis hacia delante durante 3 segundos. Después de 3 segundos, el chasis se detendrá.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/iq/blocks/es/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Ángulo de Rotación\n\nInforma del ángulo de rotación actual del VEX IQ Gyro Sensor en grados.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation.png](static/help/iq/blocks/es/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Rotación del Gyro** informa de un valor **positivo** cuando el sensor Gyro gira en la dirección en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj.\n\n**Rotación del Gyro** informa de un valor **negativo** cuando el sensor Gyro gira en la dirección **en el sentido de las agujas del reloj**.\n\nElija qué sensor Gyro para comprobar.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/es/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_devices.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **Rotación del Gyro** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png](static/help/iq/blocks/es/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Redondear\n\nRedondea el valor introducido al entero más cercano.\n\n![round](static/help/iq/blocks/es/round/round.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nDecimales que son 0.5 o mayores **redondean** hacia arriba y decimales menores de 0.5 **redondean** hacia abajo.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **redondear** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nEl bloque **redondear** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/es/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo redondeará 2.7 e imprimirá \"3\".\n\n![round_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/es/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Establezca la lista 2D a\n\nEstablece cada elemento de la lista 2D en los valores introducidos.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nAl crear una lista 2D, puede establecer el número de las **columnas** de la lista entre 1 y 10 elementos y el número de las **filas** de la lista entre 1 y 10 elementos.\n\nElija la lista 2D que desea utilizar. La lista 2D también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **establezca la lista 2D a** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Establecer lista a\n\nEstablece cada valor de una lista en los valores introducidos.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa longitud de la lista (1 a 10 elementos) se establece cuando se crea la lista.\n\nElija la lista que desea utilizar. La lista también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer lista a** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\nEn este ejemplo, se establecerá la lista en valores iniciales y, a continuación, se informará del elemento #3 (90) de la lista para establecer la posición del brazo. \n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Establecer variable booleana\n\nEstablece una variable booleana en un valor dado.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la variable booleana que desea utilizar. Las variables booleanas también se pueden cambiar de nombre o eliminar. \n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nElija un valor booleano.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **set boolean variable** puede aceptar bloques hexagonal (de seis lados).\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_color_sensor_brightness":{"name":"set_color_sensor_brightness","markdown":"# Ajuste la luz del sensor de color\n\nEstablece el brillo de la luz del VEX IQ Color Sensor. \n\n![set_color_sensor_light](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_light.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl sensor de color tiene una fuente de luz que se puede ajustar para ayudar a detectar el color de un objeto o el brillo de una superficie.\n\n**Ajuste la luz del sensor de color** acepta un intervalo de **0% a 100%**. Cuanto más alto esté establecido el % de luz, cuanto más brillante brille la fuente de luz del sensor de color.\n\nElija qué sensor de color desea utilizar.\n\n![set_color_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor.png)\n\nEl bloque **ajuste la luz del sensor de color** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_color_sensor_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_2.png)\n\n\n"},"set_cursor_new":{"name":"set_cursor_new","markdown":"# Establecer cursor\n\nEstablece la ubicación del cursor para los bloques **imprimir**.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_cursor_new/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEstablezca la posición de fila y columna del cursor para que todos los comandos **imprimir** se muestren en una ubicación específica en la pantalla VEX IQ Brain.\n\n**Establecer cursor** acepta de un rango de **1 a 5** para la **fila**.\n\n**Establecer cursor** acepta de un rango de **1 a 21** para la **columna**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_cursor_new/row_column_index.png)  \n\nEl bloque **establecer cursor** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá el cursor en la fila de ubicación 3 columna 8 antes de imprimir el texto \"Hello!\" a la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_cursor_new/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_cursor_new/set_cursor_hello.png)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Establecer dirección del chasis\n\nEstablece el valor de rumbo del giroscopio de la transmisión.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer dirección del chasis** se puede utilizar para ajustar la posición del chasis a cualquier rumbo en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj, como se muestra en la imagen de abajo.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n**Establecer dirección del chasis** acepta de un rango de **0 a 360** grados.\n\nEl bloque **establecer dirección del chasis** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el robot un total de 135 grados:\n\n![setDriveHeading_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_example_revised.png)\n\n- Dar vuelta a la izquierda hasta la dirección 45 grados.\n- Ajuste la posición actual del robot como rumbo de 0 grados.\n- Dar vuelta a la izquierda 90 grados adicionales según el nuevo valor de rumbo.\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer la Rotación del Chasis\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del Chasis cuando se configura con un VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del Chasis a cualquier valor positivo o negativo dado.\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el robot un total de 210 grados:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Gire a la izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) hasta rotación 120 grados.\n- Establece la posición actual del robot como rotación de -45 grados.\n- Gire a la izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) 90 grados adicionales (-45 grados a 45 grados) en función del valor de rotación establecido del bloque anterior."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Establecer parada de conducción\n\nEstablece el comportamiento del chasis una vez que deja de moverse.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n* **Frenar** hará que el chasis llegue a una parada inmediata.\n* **Deslizarse** deja que el Drivetrain gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* **Detener** hará que el Drivetrain se detenga inmediatamente y lo devuelva a su posición de parada si se mueve.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que él chasis avance durante 3 segundos y luego mantendrá su posición una vez detenido.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer tiempo de espera para conducir\n\nEstablece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del chasis.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl límite de tiempo del chasis se utiliza para evitar que los bloques de accionamiento que no alcanzan su posición impidan que otros bloques de la pila funcionen.\n\nUn ejemplo de un chasis que no alcanza su posición es cuando un robot es conducido contra una pared y no puede completar su movimiento.\n\nEl bloque **Establecer tiempo de espera para conducir** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo terminará el comando **conducir** después de 2 segundos si la transmisión no ha alcanzado el objetivo de 24 pulgadas. Una vez alcanzado el límite de tiempo o la distancia, el chasis pasará al comando **dar vuelta**.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer velocidad de Conducción\n\nEstablece la velocidad de Conducción.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Establecer velocidad de Conducción** sólo establecerá la velocidad del chasis, pero no hará que se mueva. Un bloque **conducir** todavía se requiere.\n\n**Establecer velocidad de Conducción** aceptando un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-127rpm a 127rpm**.\n\nSi se establece la velocidad de conducir en un valor negativo, el chasis se moverá en retroceso.\n\nSi se establece la velocidad de conducir en 0, el chasis se detendrá.\n\nEl bloque **establecer velocidad de Conducción** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis conduzca a una velocidad del 50% para 12 pulgadas.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Establecer la dirección del giroscopio\n\nEstablece la posición actual del sensor Gyro en el valor dentro del bloque de comandos. \n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## cómo utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer la dirección del giroscopio** se puede utilizar para ajustar la posición del chasis a cualquier rumbo en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj, como se muestra en la imagen de abajo.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_gyro_heading/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\n**Establecer la dirección del giroscopio** acepta de un rango de **0 a 360** grados.\n\nEl bloque **establecer la dirección del giroscopio** bloque puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija qué sensor Gyro utilizar.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer Rotación del Gyro\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del sensor de VEX IQ Gyro en el valor establecido dentro del bloque de comandos. \n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer rotación del gyro** puede usarse para ajustar el ángulo de rotación del Chasis a cualquier positivo dado (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) o valor negativo (en sentido horario).\n\n**Establecer Rotación del Gyro** acepta un rango de cualquier número decimal o entero positivo o negativo.\n\nEl bloque **establecer rotación del gyro** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija qué sensor Gyro utilizar.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation_devices.png)\n\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Reemplazar elemento de la lista 2D\n\nActualiza un elemento de la lista 2D a un nuevo valor.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nIntroduzca la fila del elemento (primer número) y la posición de la columna (segundo número) dentro de la lista que se va a reemplazar.\n\nElija la lista que desea utilizar. La lista también se puede cambiar de nombre o eliminar.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **reemplazar elemento** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Reemplazar elemento\n\nActualiza un elemento de la lista a un nuevo valor.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la lista que desea utilizar. La lista también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **reemplazar elemento** bloque puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n\nEste ejemplo actualizará el elemento #2 de mi lista a un valor de 15 e imprimirá el #2 de mi lista a la pantalla VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![replace_item_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_item_of_array/replace_item_example.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Establecer la posición del motor \n\nEstablece la posición del codificador del VEX IQ Motor en el valor introducido.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **posición del motor** se puede utilizar para ajustar la posición del motor a cualquier valor dado.\n\nNormalmente, el bloque **posición del motor** se utiliza para ajustar la posición a 0 para restablecer la posición del codificador del motor.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nElija la unidad de medida en grados o vueltas.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Establecer la parada del motor\n\nEstablece el comportamiento del VEX IQ Smart Motor una vez que deja de moverse.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n* **Frenar** hará que el Motor se detenga de inmediato.\n* **Deslizarse** permite que el motor gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* **Detener** hará que el Motor se detenga inmediatamente y lo devuelva a su posición parada si se mueve.\n\nEl **establecer la parada del motor** tendrá efecto para todos los comandos de motor futuros para el resto del proyecto.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nElija el ajuste del motor después de que se detenga.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el ArmMotor avance durante 90 grados y luego resistirá a las fuerzas externas (como la gravedad) para mantener su posición.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer el tiempo de espera del motor\n\nEstablece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del VEX IQ Smart Motor.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl límite de tiempo del motor se utiliza para evitar que los bloques de movimiento que no alcanzan su posición impidan que otros bloques de la pila funcionen. Un ejemplo de un motor que no alcanza su posición es un brazo o garra que alcanza su límite mecánico y no puede completar su movimiento.\n\nEl bloque **establecer el tiempo de espera del motor** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo finalizará el comando **establecer motor** después de 2 segundos si el Claw Motor no ha alcanzado la posición de 270 grados. Una vez alcanzado el límite de tiempo o el objetivo, el Claw Motor se moverá a la posición 0 grados.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Establecer par de torsión del motor\n\nEstablece la fuerza del VEX IQ Smart Motor.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Establecer par de torsión del motor** acepta de un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer par de torsión del motor** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo girará el motor de garra a la posición de 40 grados con sólo un 20% de par máximo. Esto permite que la garra agarre un objeto sin dañarlo con demasiada fuerza.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer la velocidad del motor\n\nEstablece la velocidad de un VEX IQ Smart Motor.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Establecer la velocidad del motor** acepta de un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-127rpm a 127rpm**.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de un motor en un valor negativo hará que el motor gire en reversa.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de un motor en 0 hará que el motor se detenga.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad está establecida en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm)\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá que el motor del brazo gire lentamente a una velocidad del 25% a la posición de 90 grados.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_print_precision_new":{"name":"set_print_precision_new","markdown":"# Establecer la precisión de impresión\n\nEstablece el número de dígitos que aparecen después del punto decimal al imprimir bloques de reportero en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_print_precision_new/print_precision.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el nivel de precisión que los bloques de reportero insertados se imprimirán en la pantalla.\n\n* Unos (1) (Predeterminado)\n* Décima (0.1)\n* Centésima (0.01)\n* Milésima (0.001)\n* Todos los dígitos (0.000001)\n\nLos bloques de informadores impresos en la pantalla se redondearán al nivel de precisión más cercano. Por ejemplo, 1.67 se imprimirá como 2 con precisión y 1.7 con precisión de décimas.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_print_precision_new/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_touchled_brightness":{"name":"set_touchled_brightness","markdown":"# Establecer el brillo del Touch LED\n\nEstablece el nivel de brillo del VEX IQ Touch LED.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Establecer el brillo del Touch LED** acepta de un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija el Touch LED que desea utilizar.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor3](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_sensor3.png)\n\nEl bloque **Establecer el brillo del Touch LED** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo iluminará el Touch LED verde con un brillo del 25%.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_touchled_color":{"name":"set_touchled_color","markdown":"# Establecer el color del Touch LED\n\nEstablece el color del VEX IQ Touch LED.\n\n![set_touchLED_color](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElegir el **Touch LED** que desea utilizar.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_sensor.png)\n\nElija el color que se mostrará.  \n\n![set_touchLED_color2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color2.png)\n\nPara apagar el **Touch LED**, ajusta el color a ninguno."},"set_touchled_fade":{"name":"set_touchled_fade","markdown":"# Establecer desvaneció de color del VEX IQ Touch LED\n\nEstablece la velocidad con la que el color del VEX IQ Touch LED se desvanece entre los colores.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el Touch LED que desea utilizar.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_sensor2.png)\n\nElige la intensidad con la que se desvanecerá el LED táctil\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_speed](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_speed.png)\n\n* Lento - El Touch LED se desvanecerá lentamente a un nuevo color.\n* Rápido - El Touch LED se desvanecerá rápidamente a un nuevo color.\n* Apagado - El Touch LED cambiará de color al instante.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo se desvanecerá lentamente el Touch LED a azul.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer la velocidad de dar vuelta\n\nEstablece la velocidad de las vueltas del chasis.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Establecer la velocidad de dar vuelta** sólo establecerá la velocidad del chasis, pero no hará que el chasis se mueva. Un bloque **vuelta** todavía se requiere.\n\n**Establecer la velocidad de dar vuelta** acepta de un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-127rpm a 127rpm**.\n\nEstableciendo la velocidad de giro del chasis a un valor negativo hará que el chasis de vuelta en la dirección opuesta.\n\nEstableciendo la velocidad de giro de una transmisión en 0 hará que la transmisión se detenga.\n\nEl bloque **Establecer la velocidad de dar vuelta** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis gire a la izquierda lentamente a una velocidad del 25%.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Establecer variable\n\nEstablece una variable en un valor determinado.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la variable que desea utilizar. Las variables también se pueden cambiar de nombre o eliminar. \n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer variable** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo reportera el VEX IQ Distance Sensor en la variable \"my variable\" y utilizará la \"mi variable\" para establecer la velocidad del chasis.\n\n![set_variable_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_variable/set_variable_example.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Establecer elemento de objeto de visión\n\nEstablece el elemento de objeto (del objeto sobre el que desea obtener más información) fuera del número de objetos detectados.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **recuento de objetos** puede ser utilizado antes del **establecer elemento de objeto de visión** para determinar el número de objetos detectados.\n\nElija qué sensor de visión utilizar.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/es/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer elemento de objeto de visión** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n\n\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Longitud de la lista\n\nReporta el número de elementos de una lista.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/es/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\nElija la lista que desea utilizar. La lista también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **Longitud de la lista** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/iq/blocks/es/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# Instantánea\n\nToma una instantánea del sensor de visión.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **instantánea** capturará la imagen actual del sensor de visión para ser procesada y analizada en busca de firmas de color y códigos. \n\nTípicamente, primero se necesita una **instantánea** antes de usar cualquier otro bloque de sensores de visión.\n\nSeleccione el sensor de visión que desea utilizar.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/iq/blocks/es/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nSeleccione el sensor de visión que desea utilizar. Las firmas de visión se configuran desde la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/iq/blocks/es/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Gira\n\nGira un VEX IQ Smart Motor hasta que se detiene.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **gira** ejecutará un motor por siempre hasta que se utilice un nuevo bloque de motor o el programa se detenga.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nElija la dirección para girar. Los nombres de dirección se pueden cambiar en la ventana Dispositivos. \n\n![spin_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Gira por\n\nGira un VEX IQ Snart Motor para una distancia determinada.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Gira por** le dirá a un Motor que viaje en una dirección dada para una distancia dada desde donde se encuentra actualmente.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nElija la dirección para girar. Los nombres de dirección se pueden cambiar en la ventana Dispositivos. \n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nEl bloque **gira por** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElegir la unidad de medida en grados o vueltas.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques van a **esperar** hasta que el motor termine de moverse.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no espere** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el motor se mueve.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Gira a la posición\n\nHace girar un VEX IQ Smart Motor a una posición establecida.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Gira a la posición** le dirá a un Motor que viaje a una posición específica. Basado en la posición actual del Motor, **gira a la posición** determinará la dirección de rotación.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque **gira a la posición** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija la unidad de medida en grados o giros.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques van a **esperar** hasta que el motor termine de moverse.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no espera** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el motor se mueve.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/es/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Dejar de conducir\n\nDetiene el chasis.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dejar de conducir** hará que el Drivetrain se detenga por completo\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo detendrá el chasis después de 3 segundos.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Pare el motor\n\nDetiene un motor.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija qué motor detener.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo girará el motor de la garra abierto durante 3 segundos antes de detenerse.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Restar\n\nResta un valor de otro y reporta la diferencia.\n\n![subtract](static/help/iq/blocks/es/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Restar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **restar** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nRestar dos números.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/iq/blocks/es/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nRestar con valores de variables.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nReste con los valores de los sensores o dispositivos\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/es/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Valor del temporizador\n\nReporta el valor del temporizador VEX IQ Brain en segundos.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl temporizador comienza a 0 segundos cuando el programa se inicia e informa de valores decimales.\n\nEl bloque de reportero **valor del temporizador** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo moverá el Drivetrain hacia adelante y reproducirá un efecto de sonido durante 4.5 segundos antes de realizar una vuelta de 90 grados.\n\n![timerValue_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es/timer_value/timerValue_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Dar vuelta\n\nGira el chasis por siempre.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta** girará el Drivetrain para siempre hasta que se utilice un nuevo bloque Drivetrain o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija la dirección en la que se moverá el chasis.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Dar vuelta por\n\nGira el chasis durante una distancia determinada.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la dirección en la que girará el chasis.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEstablezca la distancia que se moverá el tren de mando introduciendo un número de grados.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques van a **esperar** hasta que el chasis termine de girar.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no espera** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el chasis gira.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Dar vuelta a dirección de\n\nGira un Drivetrain a un dirección específico con el VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a dirección de** se puede utilizar para girar el chasis a cualquier encabezado en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj como se muestra en la imagen de abajo.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nBasado en el rumbo actual del Gyro, **dar vuelta a dirección de** determinará la dirección a girar.\n\n**Dar vuelta a dirección de** acepta de un rango **0.00 a 359.99** grados.\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a dirección de** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis haga cuatro vueltas: \n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Izquierda a 45 grados\n- Izquierda a 90 grados\n- Izquierda a 270 grados\n- Derecha a 180 grados\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques van a **esperar** hasta que el chasis termine de girar.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no espera** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el chasis gira.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Dar Vuelta a la Rotación\n\nGira un Chasis a un ángulo de rotación específico cuando configurado con un VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a la rotación** se puede utilizar para girar el chasis a un valor positivo (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) o negativo (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj).\n\nBasado en el valor actual de **rotación** del Chasis, **dar vuelta a la rotación** determinará la dirección a girar.\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a la rotación** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el Chasis haga cuatro vueltas: \n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) a 90 grados\n- Izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) a 180 grados\n- Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) a -45 grados\n- Izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) a 0 grados\n\nDe forma predeterminada, otros bloques *esperarán* hasta que el Chasis haya terminado de girar.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir ** y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen ejecutándose mientras el Chasis gira.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/es/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Variable\n\nReporta del valor asignado a la variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nBloques **variable** se utilizan para informar de un valor almacenado dentro de la variable. Utilice el bloque **definir variable** para definir o actualizar el valor de una variable.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **variable** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nLas variables se crean con el botón **hacer una variable**.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Velocidad del motor\n\nInforma de la velocidad actual de un VEX IQ Smart Motor.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Velocidad del motor** reporta de un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-127rpm a 127rpm**.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad se notifica en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **velocidad del motor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Objeto de visión\n\nInforma sobre un objeto detectado desde el Vision Sensor.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara utilizar el bloque **objeto de visión**, siga estos pasos:\n\n1. Configure su sensor de visión mediante la ventana Dispositivos.\n2. Utiliza **instantánea** para capturar una imagen del Vision Sensor y buscar una firma / código de color.\n3. Utiliza **object exists** para comprobar si el Vision Sensor detectó la firma / código de color solicitado.\n\nUna vez que el Vision Sensor detecta un objeto, puede utilizar otros bloques de visión para obtener más información sobre el objeto detectado.\n\n* Utiliza **establecer elemento de objeto de visión** para establecer qué objeto detectado desea obtener más información sobre. Por defecto, se utiliza el objeto más grande detectado.\n* Utiliza **object count** para determinar cuántos objetos se detectaron de esa firma solicitada / código de color.\n* Utiliza **vision object** para determinar qué información informar desde el objeto detectado.\n\nSeleccione el Vision Sensor que desea utilizar.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/iq/blocks/es/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nSeleccione el valor que desea informar desde el Vision Sensor:\n\n* El ancho - Qué tan ancho es el objeto en píxeles. Devuelve un valor de **2 - 316 px**.\n* Altura - La altura del objeto en píxeles. Devuelve un valor de **2 - 212 px**. \n* CentroX - Reporta la coordenada X del centro del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 315 px**.\n* CentroY - Reporta la coordenada Y del centro del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 211 px**.\n* Ángulo - Reporta del ángulo del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 180 degrees**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/es/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **objeto de visión** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Espera\n\nEspera una cantidad específica de tiempo antes de pasar al siguiente bloque.\n\n![wait](static/help/iq/blocks/es/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nElija una cantidad de tiempo para **espera**.\n\nEl bloque **espera** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/wait/wait_select.png)\n\nEste ejemplo cambiará el VEX IQ Touch LED de rojo a verde después de **esperar** 3.25 segundos.\n\n![wait_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/wait/wait_example.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Espera hasta que\n\nEspera a que un bloque booleano reporta **true** antes de pasar al siguiente bloque.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/iq/blocks/es/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Espera hasta que** comprobará repetidamente un bloque de reportero booleano y no se moverá al siguiente bloque hasta que el bloque de informe booleano informe informe **true**.\n\nEl bloque booleano **espera hasta que** puede aceptar bloques con forma hexagonal (seis lados).\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo convertirá el Touch LED a amarillo y esperará hasta que se presione el Touch LED. Una vez presionado, el cerebro imprimirá \"Terminado!\" en la pantalla LCD.\n\n![wait_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/wait_until/wait_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"when_brain_button":{"name":"when_brain_button","markdown":"# Cuando botón del Brain\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques adjunta cuando se pulsa o suelta el botón del VEX IQ Brain seleccionado.\n\n![when_brain_button](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_brain_button/when_brain_button.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElige qué botón del Brain usar.\n\n![when_brain_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select.png)\n\nSeleccione la acción que activará el evento - **presionado** or **suelto** \n\n![when_brain_button_select_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select_2.png)  \n"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Cuando recibo\n\nEjecuta la pila adjunta de bloques cuando se recibe el mensaje seleccionado de un mensaje **emitido**.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el mensaje que desea escuchar. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\nEl bloque **cuando recibo** solo lo hará un bloque **transmitir** o **transmitir y espera** en una pila diferente.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo se mostrará en rojo en el VEX IQ Touch LED y, a continuación, espera dos segundos antes de transmitir el \"mensaje1\". \n\nUna vez recibido el mensaje, la pila **cuando recibo** hará que el chasis se moverá hacia adelante, mientras que el motor de brazo se moverá hacia arriba al mismo tiempo. \n\nLas dos pilas continuarán ejecutándose al mismo tiempo que se indica en las flechas rojas.\n\n\n![when_broadcast_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_example.png)\n\n"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Cuando parachoques\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta el VEX IQ Bumper seleccionado.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el interruptor del parachoques que desea utilizar.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nSeleccione qué acción desencadenará el evento - **presionado** o **suelto** \n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Cuando eje del controller\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques adjunta cuando se mueve el eje de joystick del VEX IQ Controller seleccionado.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el eje del joystick del Controller que desea utilizar.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Cuando botón del controller\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta el botón del VEX IQ Controller seleccionado.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el botón del Controller que desea utilizar.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_controller_button/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_controller_button/controller_button_back.png)\n\nSeleccione la acción que activará el evento - **presionado** o **suelto** \n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Cuando empieza\n\nEjecuta la pila adjunta de bloques cuando se inicia el proyecto.\n\n![when_started](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl evento **cuando empieza** Se ejecutará cuando el programa se inicie desde el menú de VEX IQ Brain o desde el botón **correr** en bloques de VEXcode IQ.\n\nTodos los nuevos programas incluirán automáticamente un bloque **cuando empieza**. Los proyectos pueden soportar hasta 3 bloques **cuando empieza**."},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Cuando temporizador\n\nEjecuta la pila adjunta de bloques cuando el temporizador del VEX IQ Brain es mayor que el valor dado.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nEl temporizador del Brain comienza al principio de cada proyecto.\n\nElija una cantidad de tiempo. El evento **cuando temporizador** se ejecutará una vez que el temporizador del cerebro es **más que** la cantidad introducida.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nEl bloque **cuando temporizador** puede aceptar decimales o valores enteros.\n\nEl bloque **cuando temporizador** no puede aceptar otros bloques de reporteros."},"when_touchled":{"name":"when_touchled","markdown":"# Cuando Touch LED\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques conectada cuando se presiona o suelta el VEX IQ Touch LED seleccionado.\n\n![when_touchLED](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_touchled/when_touchled.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nElija el LED táctil que desea utilizar.\n\n![when_touchLED_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_touchled/when_touchled_select.png)\n\nSeleccione la acción que activará el evento - **presionado** o **suelto** \n\n![when_touchLED_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/es/when_touchled/when_touchled_condition.png)"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Mientras\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques dentro mientras que la condición booleana se notifica que es **true**.\n\n![while](static/help/iq/blocks/es/while/while.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **mientras** sólo comprobará la condición booleana al principio de cada bucle. \n\nSi la condición booleana se notifica como **true**, los bloques dentro de **while** se ejecutará.\n\nSi la condición booleana se notifica como **false**, los bloques dentro de **while** se omitirá.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **mientras** puede aceptar bloques hexagonales (de seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es/while/while_inserted.png)"}}},"es-419":{"blocks":{"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Añadir\n\nAgrega dos valores juntos e informa la suma.\n\n![add](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/add/add.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Añadir** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLa longitud de **add** bloque encaja en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nAñadir dos números.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nAñadir con valores de variables.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nAñadir con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# Y\n\nInforma si dos condiciones booleanas son ambas verdaderas. \n\n![and](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/and/and.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nEl bloque **y** reporta **true** cuando los dos condiciones son **true**. \n\nEl **y** bloque reporta **false** cuado uno (o los dos) condicione(s) son **false**.\n\nEl **y** bloque booleano reporta un **true** o **false** valor y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonal (de seis lados).\n\n![and_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo comprobará si dos botones en el VEX IQ Controller se están presionando al mismo tiempo.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nEl **y** bloque volverá **true** cuando los dos **Controller E Up button** y el **Controller L Down button** están siendo presionados.\n\nEl **y** bloque volverá **false** cuando uno (o los dos) de los botones del control no se presionan.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/and/and_truth.png)"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Nivel de la Batería\n\nInforma del nivel de carga de la batería del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Nivel de la Batería** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nEl bloque de reportero **nivel de la batería** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo reproducirá un sonido de alarma si el **nivel de la batería** del VEX IQ's Brain inferior al 50%\n\n![battery_capacity_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/battery_level/battery_capacity_example_revised.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Variable Booleana \n\nReporta valor de una variable booleana.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nBloques de **Variable Booleana** se utilizan para reportar de un valor de **true** o **false** almacendo dentro de la variable. Utilice el **establecer variable booleana** bloque para establecer o actualizar el valor de una variable booleana.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nEl bloque **Variable Booleana** reporta **true** o **false** valor y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nLas variables booleanas se crean utilizando el **Hacer un Booleano** botón.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"brain_button_pressed":{"name":"brain_button_pressed","markdown":"# Botón del Brain Presionado\n\nReporta si fue presionado un botón en el VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![button_pressed_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Botón del Brain Presionado** reporta **true** si se presiona el botón del Brain seleccionado.\n\n**Botón del Brain Presionado** reporta **false** si no esta se presiona el botón del Brain seleccionado.\n\nElige qué botón para usar del Brain.\n\n![button_pressed_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_options.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **Botón del Brain Presionado** reporta un **true** o **false** valor y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![brainButtonPressed_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_inserted.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el robot conduzca hacia adelante y dar vuelta a la derecha después de the que el botón **Up** se presiona.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_example_revised.png)\n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Romper\n\nSale de un bucle de repetición inmediatamente.\n\n![break](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/break/break.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nCuando se añade a la repetición de bloque 'C', el bloque **romper** saldrá del bucle que se encuentra actualmente en. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo moverá el chasis hacia adelante y comprobará si el botón del VEX IQ Brain **up** esta presionado. \n\nSi el botón **up** esta **presionado**, el bloque **romper** saldrá del bucle de repetición para siempre y detendrá el chasis.\n\n![break_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Brillo de\n\nReporta de la cantidad de luz detectada por el VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Brillo de** reporta de un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija cuál Color Sensor utilizar.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **brillo de** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Emitir\n\nTransmite un mensaje para activar cualquier pila que comience con un bloque **cuando recibo** escuchando el mensaje transmitido.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa pila que envía la **emisión** seguirá ejecutando bloques al mismo tiempo que otras pilas que reciben el mensaje transmitido.\n\nElija el mensaje para **emitir**. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo mostrará rojo en el VEX IQ Touch LED y luego esperará dos segundos antes de emitir \"message1\" \n\nCuando se recibe el mensaje, la pila **cuando recibo** hará que el chasis se moverá hacia adelante, mientras que el ClawMotor se moverá hacia arriba al mismo tiempo. \n\nLas dos pilas continuarán ejecutándose al mismo tiempo que se indica en las flechas rojas.\n\n![broadcast_example_arrows](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/broadcast/broadcast_example_arrows.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Emitir y Espera\n\nEmita un mensaje para activar las pilas que comienzan con un bloque **cuando recibo** escuchando el mensaje transmitido mientras que también pausa el resto de la pila.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa pila que transmite **emitir y espera** se detendrá hasta que se hayan completado las otras pilas que reciben el mensaje transmitido.\n\nElija el mensaje para **emitir**. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo mostrará rojo en el VEX IQ Touch LED y luego esperará dos segundos antes de transmitir \"message1\". \n\nUna vez que el mensaje es recibido, la pila **cuando recibo** causará que el chasis se mueva hacia adelante y reproduzca un efecto de sonido.\n\nLa pila emitiendo esperará hasta que se complete la pila de recepción antes de continuar ejecutando bloques cómo se indica en las flechas rojas.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows_3](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows3.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Calibrar Gyro\n\nCalibración del sensor VEX IQ Gyro se utiliza para reducir la cantidad de deriva generada por Gyro Sensor.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nLa deriva se produce cuando el sensor Gyro detecta incorrectamente el movimiento aunque el sensor no se esté moviendo.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl sensor Gyro debe permanecer inmóvil durante el proceso de calibración.\n\nElija qué Gyro Sensor utilizar.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nElija el tiempo que desea calibrar. Cuanto más tiempo calibra el Gyro Sensor, menos deriva ocurrirá.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_seconds](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_seconds.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Cambiar Variable\n\nCambia una variable por el valor dado.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la variable que desea utilizar - la variable seleccionada también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **Cambiar Variable** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\nEste ejemplo aumentará la variable que establece la velocidad del chasis por 10 cada vez **bucle de repetición** se repite.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows_new":{"name":"clear_all_rows_new","markdown":"# Borrar Todas las Filas\n\nBorra toda la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/clear_all_rows_new/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Borrar todas las filas** no restablecerá el cursor de la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain. Utilice el bloque **ajuste el cursor**  para restablecer el cursor de la pantalla de nuevo la posición deseada.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Hola\" durante un segundo y luego borrará toda la pantalla antes de imprimir \"Adiós\".\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/clear_all_rows_new/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"clear_row_new":{"name":"clear_row_new","markdown":"# Borrar Fila\n\nBorra una sola fila en el la plantilla del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/clear_row_new/clear_row.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Borrar fila** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos entre **1 - 5** para establecer qué fila se va a borrar.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/clear_row_new/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Hola\" en la fila 2 columna 1 durante tres segundos antes de borrar la fila 2.\n\n![clear_row_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/clear_row_new/clear_row_example.png)"},"color_detects_color":{"name":"color_detects_color","markdown":"# Detecta color\n\nReporta si el VEX IQ Color Sensor detecta un color específico.\n\n![color_detects](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/color_detects_color/color_detects.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Detecta color** reporta **true** cuando el sensor de color detecta el color seleccionado.\n\n**Detecta color** reporta **false** cuando el sensor de color detecta un color diferente al seleccionado.\n\nElija qué Sensor de Color utilizar.\n\n![color_detects_chosen](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/color_detects_color/color_detects_chosen.png)\n\nElija el color que desea detectar.\n\n![color_detects_selected](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/color_detects_color/color_detects_selected.png)\n\nEl Bloque booleano **Detecta color** reporta **true** o **false** valor y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![color_detects_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/color_detects_color/color_detects_shape.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Color Red\" u \"Otro Color\" dependiendo de si el Sensor de Color detecta o no el color \"rojo\".\n\n![color_detects_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/color_detects_color/color_detects_example.png)\n\n"},"color_of":{"name":"color_of","markdown":"# Color de\n\nReporta del nombre del color detectado por el VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/color_of/color_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Color de** reporta uno de los siguientes colores: **rojo, rojo-violeta, violeta, azul-violeta, azul, azul-verde, verde, amarillo-verde, amarillo, amarillo-naranja, naranja o rojo-naranja.**\n\nElija cuál Sensor de Color utilizar.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/color_of/color_of_color.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **color de** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![color_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/color_of/color_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Comentario\n\nPermite a los programadores escribir información para ayudar a describir su programa.\n\n![comment_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLos programadores profesionales utilizan comentarios a través de sus programas para ayudar a otros a entender su código. Los comentarios también pueden ayudar con la solución de problemas y la colaboración. \n\nAgregue texto en bloque **comentario** seleccionando primero el cuadrado transparente y eliminando cualquier texto existente. A continuación, escriba el nuevo texto.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nLos comentarios no cambian el programa o los bloques que lo rodean.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Control Activado/Desactivado\n\nActiva o desactiva las acciones configuradas del Control desde el menú dispositivos.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nSeleccione activar o desactivar las acciones del Control configuradas seleccionando el estado deseado en el menú desplegable. Por defecto, el Controlador está Activado en cada proyecto.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nLa acción configurada en este ejemplo es utilizar el comportamiento de Chasis del robot establecido por la configuración del Control en la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nEste ejemplo tendrá el controlador configurado Desactivado cuando se inicie el programa. \n\nLuego, el robot conducirá hacia adelante durante 6 pulgadas.\n\nPor último, el bloque **control Activado** permitirá al control restaurar los comportamientos de conducción del controlador.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Corriente del Motor\n\nInforma de la cantidad de energía que un VEX IQ Motor está utilizando actualmente en porcentaje (%) o amperios (amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Corriente del Motor** reporta de un rango de **0% to 100%** or **0.0 to 1.2 amps**. \n\nElija el Motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nElija si la corriente del Motor se reporta en % o en amperios.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **corriente del motor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Columna del Cursor\n\nReporta del número de columna de la ubicación del cursor del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Columna del Cursor** reporta de un rango de **1 a 21**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/cursor_column/row_column_index.png)  \n\nEl bloque de reportero **columna del cursor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo comprobará si la posición de la **columna del cursor** es mayor que 15. Si la posición es mayor que 15, el proyecto establecerá el cursor en la fila 1, columna 1, y luego imprimirá el valor de \"Hello\".\n\n![cursor_column_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/cursor_column/cursor_column_example_simple.png)\n\n"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Fila del cursor\n\nInforma del número de fila de la ubicación del cursor del VEX IQ Brain Screen.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## cómo utilizar\n\n**Fila del cursor** reporta de un rango de **1 a 5**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/cursor_row/row_column_index.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **fila del cursor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo comprobará si la **posición** de la fila del cursor es mayor que 4. Si la posición es mayor que 4, el proyecto establecerá el cursor en la fila 1, columna 1 y, a continuación, imprimirá en \"Hola\"\n\n![cursor_row_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/cursor_row/cursor_row_example_simple.png)"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Distancia de\n\nReporta la distancia del objeto más cercano desde al VEX IQ Distance Sensor.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Distancia de** reporta de un rango de **24mm a 1000mm** o **1 inch a 40 inches**.\n\nElija qué Sensor de Distancia utilizar.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nElija si **distancia de** se reporta en pulgadas o milímetros. \n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **distancia de** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Dividir\n\nDivide el primer valor por el segundo valor e informa del dividendo.\n\n![divide](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Dividir** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **dividir** se adapta a bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nIntroduzca los números que se van a dividir.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nDividir con valores de variables.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nDividir con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Conducir\n\nMueve el Tren Mortiz por siempre.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **conducir** ejecutará el Tren Mortiz para siempre hasta que se utilice un nuevo bloque Tren Mortiz o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija la dirección en la que se moverá el Tren Mortiz.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Corriente del Tren Mortiz\n\nReporta la cantidad de corriente (potencia) que el tren mortiz está utilizando actualmente.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Corriente del Tren Mortiz** reporta de un rango de **0% a 100%** o **0.0 to 1.2 amps**. \n\nElija si la **corriente del tren mortiz** se indica en % o amperios (amps).\n\n![drive_current_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_current/drive_current_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **corriente del tren mortiz** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Conducir por\n\nMueve el chasis para una distancia determinada.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija en qué dirección se moverá el chasis.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\nEl bloque **conducir por** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEstablezca hasta dónde se moverá el chasis introduciendo un valor y eligiendo la unidad de medida (pulgadas o milímetros).\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nAutomáticamente, otros bloques **esperarán** hasta que el chasis termine de moverse.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandirla **y no espere** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen ejecutándose mientras el chasis se mueve.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Dirección del Chasis\n\nReporta la dirección que enfrenta el chasis.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Dirección del Chasis** reporta de un rango de **0.00 a 359.99 grados**.\n\nEl **dirección del chasis** informa de un encabezado en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj como se muestra en la imagen de abajo.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_heading/TopDownBot01.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **dirección del chasis** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Conducir ya termino\n\nInforma si el chasis ha completado su movimiento.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Conducir ya termino** reporta **true** cuando los motores del chasis han completado su movimiento.\n\n**Conducir ya termino** reporta **false** cuando los motores del chasis todavía están en movimiento.\n\nEl bloque booleano **drive is done** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis caras).\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Tren Mortiz esta Moviendo\n\nReporta si el chasis se está moviendo actualmente.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Tren Mortiz esta Moviendo** reporta **true** cuando los motores del tren mortiz se está moviendo.\n\n**Tren Mortiz esta Moviendo** reporta **false** cuando los motores del tren mortiz de mando se detienen.\n\nEl bloque booleano **tren mortiz esta moviendo** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Rotación del Chasis\n\nInforma del ángulo de rotación del Chasis en grados cuando se configura con un VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Rotación del chasis** informa de un valor **positivo** cuando el Chasis gira en una dirección **en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj**.\n\n**Rotación del Chasis** informa de un valor **negativo** cuando el Chasis gira en una dirección **en el sentido de las agujas del reloj**..\n\nEl bloque de reportero **rotación del Chasis** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad del Chasis\n\nReporta la velocidad actual del chasis.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Velocidad del Chasis** reporta de un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-127rpm a 127rpm**\n\nElija si la velocidad se notifica en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **velocidad del chasis** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Igual a\n\nReporta si el primer valor es el mismo que (igual) al segundo valor. \n\n![equal_to](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Igual a** reporta **true** cuando los dos valores son exactamente los mismos.\n\n**Igual a** reporta **false** cuando los dos valores no son los mismos.\n\nEl bloque **igual a** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque booleano **igual a** reporta un valor **true** or **false** y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Drivetrain Stalled\" en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain si la corriente del chasis es igual al 100%.\n\n![equal_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/equal_to/equal_to_example.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Por Siempre\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite cualquier bloque contenido en su interior para siempre.\n\n![forever](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nColoque bloques en el bloque **por siempre** 'C' para que esas acciones se repitan **por siempre**.\n\nPuedes salir de un circuito de **por siempre** colocando un bloque de **romper** adentro.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nLos bloques 'C' también pueden colocarse entre sí. Este concepto se denomina anidamiento, que puede ayudar a ahorrar tiempo al programar diferentes comportamientos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo reproducirá el mismo efecto de sonido cada 5 segundos por siempre.\n\n![forever_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/forever/forever_example.png)"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Función\n\nRealiza una función matemática seleccionada.sinestesia\n\n![function](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - valor absoluto\n* **floor** - redondea hacia abajo al entero más cercano\n* **ceiling** - redondea hasta el entero más cercano\n* **sqrt** - raíz cuadrada\n* **sin** - seno\n* **cos** - coseno\n* **tan** - tangente\n* **asin** - arcoseno o el inverso del seno\n* **acos** - arcocoseno o el inverso del coseno\n* **atan** - arco o el inverso de tangente\n* **ln** - el logaritmo natural base e\n* **log** - base del logaritmo 10\n* **e ^** - poderes de e\n* **10 ^** - poderes de 10\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **función** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija la **función** matemática de una lista de opciones.\n\n![function_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/function/function_select.png)\n\nLa longitud del bloque **función** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\n![function_fit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Más que\n\nReporta si el primer valor es más grande (mayor) que el segundo valor.  \n\n![greater_than](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Más que** reporta **true** cuando el primer valor es mayor que el segundo valor. \n\n**Más que** reporta **false** cuando el primer valor es menor o igual que el segundo valor.\n\nEl bloque **más que** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque booleano **más que** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis caras).\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Nivel de batería bueno\" en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain si el nivel de batería es superior al 75%.\n\n![greater_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/greater_than/greater_than_example.png)\n\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Dirección de Gyro\n\nReporta la dirección actual del encabezamiento del VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Dirección de Gyro** informa de un rango entre **0.00 a 359.99**.\n\nEl bloque **dirección de Gyro** reporta un rumbo en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj como se muestra en la imagen siguiente.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/heading_of_gyro/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\nElija qué Gyro Sensor comprobar.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **heading of Gyro** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"hue_of":{"name":"hue_of","markdown":"# Matiz de\n\nInforma del matiz del color detectado por el VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/hue_of/hue_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Matiz de** reporta de un rango de **0 a 360**.\n\nElija qué sensor de color desea comprobar.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/hue_of/hue_of_color.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **matiz de** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![hue_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/hue_of/hue_of_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Si entonces\n\nUn bloque 'C' que ejecuta los bloques en el interior si se notifica que la condición booleana es **true**.  \n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nEl bloque 'C' **si entonces** solo comprobará la condición booleana una vez. \n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta **true**, los bloques dentro de **si entonces** se ejecutarán.\n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta **false**, los bloques dentro de **si entonces** se omitirán.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **if then** puede aceptar bloques hexagonales (seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo reproducirá un efecto de sonido cada vez que se pulse el VEX IQ Bumper Switch.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **si entonces** puede ser anidado o colocado dentro del bloque \"por siempre\" para asegurar que el efecto de sonido se reproduce cada vez en lugar de una sola vez. \n\n![if_then_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/if_then/if_then_example.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Si entonces si no\n\nUn bloque 'C' que ejecuta los bloques dentro de la primera o segunda parte de la **si entonces si no** dependiendo del valor booleano reportado.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque 'C' **si entonces si no**  sólo comprobará la condición booleana una vez. \n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **true**, los bloques dentro de la section **si** se ejecutará.\n\nSi la condición booleana es **false**, los bloques dentro de la section **else** se ejecutará.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **si entonces si no** puede aceptar bloques hexagonales (de seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo será verde si se pulsa el VEX IQ Touch LED y estará en rojo cuando no se pulse el Touch LED.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **si entonces si no**  puede estar ubicado â o colocado dentro del bloque \"por siempre\" para asegurar que el Touch LED se vuelva rojo y verde más de una vez. \n\n![if_then_else_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/if_then_else/if_then_else_example.png)"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Elemento de la lista 2D\n\nReporta el valor de un elemento en una lista 2D. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la lista 2D que desea utilizar. La lista 2D también se puede cambiar de nombre o eliminar.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nIntroduzca la fila del elemento (primer número) y la posición de columna (segundo número) dentro de la lista que se reportara. Aquí, el elemento en la fila de posición 2, columna 3 de la lista 2D se está reportando.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nEl bloque **Elemento de la lista 2D** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Elemento de\n\nReporta el valor de un elemento de una lista. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la lista que desea utilizar. La lista también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nIntroduzca el número de la posición del elemento dentro de la lista. Aquí, el segundo elemento de la lista (punto 2) se está reportando. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nEl bloque **elemento de** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá la velocidad del chasis al valor almacenado en el elemento 3. El chasis ahora avanzará a una velocidad del 90%.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Longitud de la lista 2D\n\nReporta el número de filas o columnas de una lista 2D.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija qué lista 2D utilizar. La lista 2D también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nElija el valor que desea reportar. La lista 2D puede reportar **filas** o **columnas**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **longitud de la lista 2D** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Menos que\n\nReporta si el primer valor es menos (más pequeño) que el segundo valor. \n\n![less_than](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Menos que** reporta **true** cuando el primer valor es menos que el segundo valor. \n\n**Menos que** reporta **false** cuando el primer valor es mayor o igual que el segundo valor.\n\nEl bloque booleano **menos que** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\nEl bloque **menos que** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"Low Battery!\" en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain si el nivel de batería es inferior al 25%.\n\n![less_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/less_than/less_than_example.png)\n\n"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor ha terminado\n\nReporta si el motor seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Motor ha terminado** reporta **true** cuando el motor seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\n**Motor ha terminado** reporta **true** cuando el motor seleccionado todavía se está moviendo.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **motor is done** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\nEl bloque para reportar si el motor ha terminado se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados) para otros bloques. \n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor esta girando\n\nReporta si el motor seleccionado está girando actualmente.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Motor esta girando** reporta **true** cuando el motor seleccionado está girando.\n\n**Motor esta girando** reporta **false** cuando el motor seleccionado está parado.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **motor is spinning** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Multiplicar\n\nMultiplica los dos valores juntos e informa del producto.\n\n![multiply](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Multiplicar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **multiply** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nMultiplicar dos números.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nMultiplicar con valores de variables.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nMultiplique con los valores de los sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row_new":{"name":"next_row_new","markdown":"# Siguiente fila\n\nEstablece la salida de impresión en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain en la siguiente fila disponible.\n\n![next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/next_row_new/next_row.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nDe forma predeterminada, todos los proyectos comienzan con el cursor de pantalla en la fila 1 columna 1. El bloque **siguiente fila** moverá el cursor hacia abajo por una sola fila en la pantalla del IQ Brain. \n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/next_row_new/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá \"primer mensaje\" y luego pondrá el cursor en la siguiente fila disponible antes de imprimir \"segundo mensaje\".\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/next_row_new/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/next_row_new/set_cursor_welcome.png)\n"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# No\n\nReporta de lo contrario (inverso) del resultado booleano\n\n![not](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/not/not.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **no** reporta **true** cuando el bloque booleano adentro reporta **false**.\n\nEl bloque **no** reporta **false** cuando el bloque booleano adentro reporta **true**.\n\nEl bloque booleano **no** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\nEste ejemplo reportara **true** cuando el botón de \"comprobar\" del VEX IQ Brain no se presiona. \n\n![not_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Recuento de objetos\n\nReporta de cuántos objetos detecta el Vision Sensor. \n\nUn objeto tendrá que configurarse antes de que el bloque **recuento de objetos** pueda detectarlo.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija qué Vision Sensor utilizar.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **instantánea de** tendrá que utilizarse antes del bloque **recuento de objetos** reporta un número de objetos.\n\nEl bloque **recuento de objetos** sólo detectará el número de objetos de la última firma de instantánea.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Objeto existe\n\nReporta si el Vision Sensor detecta un objeto configurado. \n\nUn objeto tendrá que configurarse antes de que el bloque **object exista** puede detectarlo.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija qué Vision Sensor utilizar.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n**Objeto exista** reporta **true** cuando el Vision Sensor detecta un objeto configurado.\n\n**Objeto exista** reporta **false** cuando el Vision Sensor no detecta un objeto configurado.\n\nEl bloque booleano **objeto exista** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nEl bloque **instantánea de** tendrá que utilizarse antes de que el bloque booleano **objeto exista** reporta un valor **true** o **false**."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Objeto encontrado\n\nReporta si el VEX IQ Distance sensor ve un objeto dentro de su campo de visión. \n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Objeto encontrado** reporta **true** cuando el Distance Sensor ve un objeto o una superficie dentro de su campo de visión.\n\n**Objeto encontrado** reporta **false** cuando el Distance Sensor no detecta ningún objeto o superficie.\n\nElija qué Distance Sensor utilizar.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **objeto encontrado** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"object_is_near":{"name":"object_is_near","markdown":"# Objeto Cercano\n\nInforma si el VEX IQ Color Sensor detecta un objeto cercano.\n\n![object_is_near](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_is_near/object_is_near_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Objeto Cercano** reporta **true** cuando el sensor de color detecta un objeto o superficie cerca de la parte frontal del sensor.\n\n**Objeto Cercano** reporta **false** cuando el sensor de color detecta el espacio  vacío delante del sensor.\n\nElija cuál sensor de color utilizar.\n\n![object_is_near_color](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_is_near/object_is_near_color.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **objeto cercano** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![object_is_near_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/object_is_near/object_is_near_inserted.png)\n\n\n "},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# O\n\nReporta si una de las dos condiciones booleanas son verdaderas.\n\n![or](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/or/or.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **true** cuando una (o ambas) de las condiciones son **true**. \n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **false** cuando ambas condiciones son **false**.\n\nEl bloque booleano **o** reporta **true** o **false** valor y cabe en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **true** cuando (o ambos) se presionan el VEX IQ Bumper y el VEX IQ Touch LED y reporta **false** sólo cuando el parachoques y el LED táctil no se presionan.\n\n![or_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/or/or_truth.png)"},"play_note":{"name":"play_note","markdown":"# Tocar nota\n\nToca la nota musical seleccionada.\n\n![play_note](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/play_note/play_note.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nElija una nota musical.\n\n![play_note_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/play_note/play_note_select.png)\n\nSeleccione cuánto tiempo (duración) se tocara la nota.\n\n![play_note_duration](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/play_note/play_note_duration.png)\n\n* Una nota **entera** se reproduce durante 1 segundo (1000 milisegundos)\n* Una nota de **media** se reproduce durante 0.5 segundos (500 milisegundos)\n* Una nota de **cuarto** se reproduce durante 0.25 segundos (250 milisegundos)\n\nUna vez que una nota musical comienza a reproducirse, el siguiente bloque comenzaróก inmediatamente.\n"},"play_sound":{"name":"play_sound","markdown":"# Tocar Sonido\n\nReproduce el efecto de sonido seleccionado.\n\n![play_sound](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/play_sound/play_sound.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el efecto de sonido de una lista de opciones. \n\n![play_sound_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/play_sound/play_sound_select.png)\n\nUna vez que un efecto de sonido comienza a tocar, el siguiente bloque comenzará inmediatamente."},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Posición del Controller\n\nReporta la posición de un joystick en el controller a lo largo de un eje.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Posición del Controller** informa de un rango entre **-100 a 100**.\n\n**Posición del Controller** reportara (0) cuando un eje joystick está centrado.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nElija el eje del joystick para comprobar su posición.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nEl bolque reportero **posición del controller** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo comprobará repetidamente el eje D del joystick de mando del controlador para controlar la velocidad del motor del brazo.\n\n![position_of_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Posición del motor\n\nReporta la distancia que ha recorrido el motor.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Posición del motor** reporta la posición del motor en números enteros para grados y números decimales para giros.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nElija si el valor se reporta en grados rotados o en giros del motor. \n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **posición del motor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Presionando el parachoques\n\nReporta si el VEX IQ Bumper Switch esta presionado .\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Presionando el parachoques** reporta **true** si se está presionando el interruptor del parachoques.\n\n**Presionando el parachoques** reporta **false** si no se está presionando el interruptor del parachoques.\n\nElija el interruptor del parachoques que desea utilizar.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **presionando el parachoques** reporta un **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Presionando controller\n\nReporta si está presionado un botón en el VEX IQ Controller.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Presionando controller** reporta **true** si se está presionando el botón del controller seleccionado.\n\n**Presionando controller** reporta **false** si no se está presionando el botón del controller seleccionado.\n\nElija el botón Controller que desea utilizar.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **presionando controller** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo comprobará si se pulsa el botón E Up y hará girar el motor de garras hacia delante si lo está. \n\n![pressing_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_example_revised.png)"},"pressing_touchled":{"name":"pressing_touchled","markdown":"# Presionando Touch LED\n\nReporta si el VEX IQ Touch LED se está presionando.\n\n![pressing_touch_led](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Presionando Touch LED** reporta **true** si el Touch LED seleccionado se está presionando.\n\n**Presionando Touch LED** reporta **false** si el Touch LED seleccionado no se está presionando.\n\nElija el LED táctil que desea utilizar.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_led](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_led.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **presionando Touch LED** reporta un valor **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![pressing_touch_led_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_inserted.png)\n\n"},"print_new":{"name":"print_new","markdown":"# Imprimir\n\nImprime valores o texto en la pantalla de VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/print_new/look_print.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **imprimir** imprimirá los datos en la ubicación del cursor en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain.\n\nTodos los nuevos proyectos comienzan con el cursor de pantalla en la fila 1, columna 1.\n\nTodos los bloques de informador se imprimirán como números enteros de forma predeterminada. Utilice el bloque **establecer precisión de impresión** para ajustar el número de decimales impresos.\n\nImprima palabras y números.\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/print_new/print_words.png)\n\nImprima el valor reportado a partir de una variable.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/print_new/print_variable1.png)  \n\nImprima el cálculo reportado de un operador.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/print_new/print_addition.png)  \n\nImprima el valor reportado desde un sensor o dispositivo.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/print_new/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Mi bloque\n\nMis bloques se utilizan para crear bloques personalizados.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Mis bloques** se utilizan para crear una secuencia de bloques que se pueden utilizar varias veces a lo largo de un proyecto. \n\n**Mis bloques** se realizan utilizando el botón **Crear un Bloque**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Mis bloques** puede tener múltiples parámetros - etiquetas de texto, variables numéricas y variables booleanas - para agregar más funcionalidad a su bloque personalizado.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nPara usar un **mi bloque**, adjunte la llamada **mi bloque** a un bloque con tapa. Cuando se alcanza el **mi bloque** en su proyecto, la pila dentro del **mi bloque** se ejecutará utilizando los valores de parámetro especificados.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nAdjunte una pila de bloques al bloque con tapa \"definir\" **mis bloques** para establecer la acción que se produce cuando se utiliza un **mi bloque**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Nota: La creación de varios Mis bloques con las mismas etiquetas y variables puede provocar errores al descargar el proyecto.***\n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **mis bloques** para:\n\n* Reproducir el sonido de la sirena 3 veces.\n* Conducir hacia adelante durante 12 pulgadas.\n* Reproducir el sonido de la sirena 3 veces.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/sound_example.png)\n\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **mis bloques** para:\n\n* Conducir hacia adelante durante 15 pulgadas\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del Brain\n* Gira el robot 180 grados a la derecha\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del Brain\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Mi Bloque\n\nMis bloques se utilizan para crear bloques personalizados.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Mis bloques** se utilizan para crear una secuencia de bloques que se pueden utilizar varias veces a lo largo de un proyecto. \n\n**Mis bloques** se hacen usando el botón **Crear un Bloque**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Mis bloques** puede tener múltiples parámetros - etiquetas de texto, variables numéricas y variables booleanas - para agregar más funcionalidad a su bloque personalizado.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nPara usar un **mi bloque**, adjunte la llamada **mi bloque** a un bloque con tapa. Cuando se alcanza el **mi bloque** en su proyecto, la pila dentro del **mi bloque** se ejecutará utilizando los valores de parámetro especificados.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nAdjunte una pila de bloques al bloque con tapa \"definir\" **mis bloques** para establecer la acción que se produce cuando se utiliza un **mi bloque**..\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Nota: La creación de varios Mis bloques con las mismas etiquetas y variables puede provocar errores al descargar el proyecto.***\n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **mis bloques** para:\n\n* Reproducir el sonido de la sirena 3 veces.\n* Conducir hacia adelante durante 12 pulgadas.\n* Reproducir el sonido de la sirena 3 veces.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/sound_example.png)\n\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **mis bloques** para:\n\n* Conducir hacia adelante durante 15 pulgadas\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del Brain\n* Gira el robot 180 grados a la derecha\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del Brain\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Al azar\n![random](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/random/random.png)\n\nInforma de un valor aleatorio entre los valores más bajos y más altos del bloque.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa longitud del bloque **al azar** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nEl bloque **al azar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEste ejemplo utiliza un bloque **al azar** para aleatorizar la velocidad del chasis.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nEste ejemplo utiliza un bloque **al azar** para aleatorizar la longitud de un bloque de espera.\n\n![random_control](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"rate_of_gyro":{"name":"rate_of_gyro","markdown":"# Tasa de giroscopio\n\nInforma de la velocidad angular del sensor VEX IQ Gyro.\n\n![rate_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Tasa de giroscopio** reporta de un rango de **0 a 249.99 dps** (grados por segundo).\n\n**Tasa de giroscopio** reporta valores en grados por segundo (dps).\n\nElija que sensor de giroscopio utilizar.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **tasa de giroscopio** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_inserted.png)"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# El resto\n\nDivide el primer valor por el segundo valor y reporta el resto.\n\n![remainder](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **el resto** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLos números que se dividen uniformemente reportarán un resto de cero.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **el resto** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\nEste ejemplo dividirá 7 y 2 e informará el resto para imprimir \"1\" en la pantalla de VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Repetir\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques contenidos en el interior durante un número determinado de veces.\n\n![repeat](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPrimero introduzca un valor para indicar cuántas veces se va a utilizar la pila **repetir** los bloques contenidos en el interior.\n \nEl bloque 'C' **repetir** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLos bloques 'C' también se pueden poner dentro unos de otros. Este concepto es llamado anidando que puede ayudar a ahorrar el tiempo programando comportamientos diferentes.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/repeat/repeat_select.png)\n\nEste ejemplo repetirá la reproducción de un efecto de sonido cada 3 segundos durante 5 veces.\n\n![repeat_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/repeat/repeat_example.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Repita hasta que\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques dentro hasta que se notifica que la condición booleana es **true**.  \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Repita hasta que** sólo comprobará la condición booleana al principio de cada bucle. \n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **false**, los bloques dentro de **repita hasta que** se ejecutará.\n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **true**, los bloques dentro de **repita hasta que** se omitirá.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **repita hasta que** puede aceptar bloques hexagonales (de seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo imprimirá el valor del temporizador en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain y moverá el Chasis hacia adelante hasta que se presione el botón **check** en el VEX IQ Brain. Una vez que el botón **check** se pulsa, el chasis se detendra.\n\n![repeat_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/repeat_until/repeat_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Restablecer temporizador\n\nRestablece el temporizador del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl temporizador del VEX IQ Brain comienza al principio de cada proyecto. El bloque **restablecer temporizador** se utiliza para restablecer el temporizador a 0 segundos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el temporizador se restablecerá antes de mover el chasis hacia delante durante 3 segundos. Después de 3 segundos, el chasis se detendrá.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Ángulo de Rotación\n\nInforma del ángulo de rotación actual del VEX IQ Gyro Sensor en grados.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation.png](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Rotación del Gyro** informa de un valor **positivo** cuando el sensor Gyro gira en la dirección en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj.\n\n**Rotación del Gyro** informa de un valor **negativo** cuando el sensor Gyro gira en la dirección **en el sentido de las agujas del reloj**.\n\nElija qué sensor Gyro para comprobar.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_devices.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **Rotación del Gyro** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Redondear\n\nRedondea el valor introducido al entero más cercano.\n\n![round](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/round/round.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nDecimales que son 0.5 o mayores **redondean** hacia arriba y decimales menores de 0.5 **redondean** hacia abajo.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **redondear** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nEl bloque **redondear** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo redondeará 2.7 e imprimirá \"3\".\n\n![round_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Establezca la lista 2D a\n\nEstablece cada elemento de la lista 2D en los valores introducidos.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nAl crear una lista 2D, puede establecer el número de las **columnas** de la lista entre 1 y 10 elementos y el número de las **filas** de la lista entre 1 y 10 elementos.\n\nElija la lista 2D que desea utilizar. La lista 2D también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **establezca la lista 2D a** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Establecer lista a\n\nEstablece cada valor de una lista en los valores introducidos.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa longitud de la lista (1 a 10 elementos) se establece cuando se crea la lista.\n\nElija la lista que desea utilizar. La lista también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer lista a** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\nEn este ejemplo, se establecerá la lista en valores iniciales y, a continuación, se informará del elemento #3 (90) de la lista para establecer la posición del brazo. \n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Establecer variable booleana\n\nEstablece una variable booleana en un valor dado.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la variable booleana que desea utilizar. Las variables booleanas también se pueden cambiar de nombre o eliminar. \n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nElija un valor booleano.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **set boolean variable** puede aceptar bloques hexagonal (de seis lados).\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_color_sensor_brightness":{"name":"set_color_sensor_brightness","markdown":"# Ajuste la luz del sensor de color\n\nEstablece el brillo de la luz del VEX IQ Color Sensor. \n\n![set_color_sensor_light](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_light.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl sensor de color tiene una fuente de luz que se puede ajustar para ayudar a detectar el color de un objeto o el brillo de una superficie.\n\n**Ajuste la luz del sensor de color** acepta un intervalo de **0% a 100%**. Cuanto más alto esté establecido el % de luz, cuanto más brillante brille la fuente de luz del sensor de color.\n\nElija qué sensor de color desea utilizar.\n\n![set_color_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor.png)\n\nEl bloque **ajuste la luz del sensor de color** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_color_sensor_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_2.png)\n\n\n"},"set_cursor_new":{"name":"set_cursor_new","markdown":"# Establecer cursor\n\nEstablece la ubicación del cursor para los bloques **imprimir**.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_cursor_new/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEstablezca la posición de fila y columna del cursor para que todos los comandos **imprimir** se muestren en una ubicación específica en la pantalla VEX IQ Brain.\n\n**Establecer cursor** acepta de un rango de **1 a 5** para la **fila**.\n\n**Establecer cursor** acepta de un rango de **1 a 21** para la **columna**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_cursor_new/row_column_index.png)  \n\nEl bloque **establecer cursor** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá el cursor en la fila de ubicación 3 columna 8 antes de imprimir el texto \"Hello!\" a la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_cursor_new/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_cursor_new/set_cursor_hello.png)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Establecer dirección del chasis\n\nEstablece el valor de rumbo del giroscopio de la transmisión.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer dirección del chasis** se puede utilizar para ajustar la posición del chasis a cualquier rumbo en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj, como se muestra en la imagen de abajo.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n**Establecer dirección del chasis** acepta de un rango de **0 a 360** grados.\n\nEl bloque **establecer dirección del chasis** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el robot un total de 135 grados:\n\n![setDriveHeading_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_example_revised.png)\n\n- Dar vuelta a la izquierda hasta la dirección 45 grados.\n- Ajuste la posición actual del robot como rumbo de 0 grados.\n- Dar vuelta a la izquierda 90 grados adicionales según el nuevo valor de rumbo.\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer la Rotación del Chasis\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del Chasis cuando se configura con un VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del Chasis a cualquier valor positivo o negativo dado.\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el robot un total de 210 grados:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Gire a la izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) hasta rotación 120 grados.\n- Establece la posición actual del robot como rotación de -45 grados.\n- Gire a la izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) 90 grados adicionales (-45 grados a 45 grados) en función del valor de rotación establecido del bloque anterior."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Establecer parada de conducción\n\nEstablece el comportamiento del chasis una vez que deja de moverse.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n* **Frenar** hará que el chasis llegue a una parada inmediata.\n* **Deslizarse** deja que el Drivetrain gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* **Detener** hará que el Drivetrain se detenga inmediatamente y lo devuelva a su posición de parada si se mueve.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que él chasis avance durante 3 segundos y luego mantendrá su posición una vez detenido.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer tiempo de espera para conducir\n\nEstablece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del chasis.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl límite de tiempo del chasis se utiliza para evitar que los bloques de accionamiento que no alcanzan su posición impidan que otros bloques de la pila funcionen.\n\nUn ejemplo de un chasis que no alcanza su posición es cuando un robot es conducido contra una pared y no puede completar su movimiento.\n\nEl bloque **Establecer tiempo de espera para conducir** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo terminará el comando **conducir** después de 2 segundos si la transmisión no ha alcanzado el objetivo de 24 pulgadas. Una vez alcanzado el límite de tiempo o la distancia, el chasis pasará al comando **dar vuelta**.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer velocidad de Conducción\n\nEstablece la velocidad de Conducción.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Establecer velocidad de Conducción** sólo establecerá la velocidad del chasis, pero no hará que se mueva. Un bloque **conducir** todavía se requiere.\n\n**Establecer velocidad de Conducción** aceptando un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-127rpm a 127rpm**.\n\nSi se establece la velocidad de conducir en un valor negativo, el chasis se moverá en retroceso.\n\nSi se establece la velocidad de conducir en 0, el chasis se detendrá.\n\nEl bloque **establecer velocidad de Conducción** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis conduzca a una velocidad del 50% para 12 pulgadas.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Establecer la dirección del giroscopio\n\nEstablece la posición actual del sensor Gyro en el valor dentro del bloque de comandos. \n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## cómo utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer la dirección del giroscopio** se puede utilizar para ajustar la posición del chasis a cualquier rumbo en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj, como se muestra en la imagen de abajo.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_gyro_heading/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\n**Establecer la dirección del giroscopio** acepta de un rango de **0 a 360** grados.\n\nEl bloque **establecer la dirección del giroscopio** bloque puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija qué sensor Gyro utilizar.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer Rotación del Gyro\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del sensor de VEX IQ Gyro en el valor establecido dentro del bloque de comandos. \n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer rotación del gyro** puede usarse para ajustar el ángulo de rotación del Chasis a cualquier positivo dado (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) o valor negativo (en sentido horario).\n\n**Establecer Rotación del Gyro** acepta un rango de cualquier número decimal o entero positivo o negativo.\n\nEl bloque **establecer rotación del gyro** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija qué sensor Gyro utilizar.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation_devices.png)\n\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Reemplazar elemento de la lista 2D\n\nActualiza un elemento de la lista 2D a un nuevo valor.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nIntroduzca la fila del elemento (primer número) y la posición de la columna (segundo número) dentro de la lista que se va a reemplazar.\n\nElija la lista que desea utilizar. La lista también se puede cambiar de nombre o eliminar.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **reemplazar elemento** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Reemplazar elemento\n\nActualiza un elemento de la lista a un nuevo valor.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la lista que desea utilizar. La lista también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **reemplazar elemento** bloque puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n\nEste ejemplo actualizará el elemento #2 de mi lista a un valor de 15 e imprimirá el #2 de mi lista a la pantalla VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![replace_item_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_array/replace_item_example.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Establecer la posición del motor \n\nEstablece la posición del codificador del VEX IQ Motor en el valor introducido.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **posición del motor** se puede utilizar para ajustar la posición del motor a cualquier valor dado.\n\nNormalmente, el bloque **posición del motor** se utiliza para ajustar la posición a 0 para restablecer la posición del codificador del motor.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nElija la unidad de medida en grados o vueltas.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Establecer la parada del motor\n\nEstablece el comportamiento del VEX IQ Smart Motor una vez que deja de moverse.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n* **Frenar** hará que el Motor se detenga de inmediato.\n* **Deslizarse** permite que el motor gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* **Detener** hará que el Motor se detenga inmediatamente y lo devuelva a su posición parada si se mueve.\n\nEl **establecer la parada del motor** tendrá efecto para todos los comandos de motor futuros para el resto del proyecto.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nElija el ajuste del motor después de que se detenga.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el ArmMotor avance durante 90 grados y luego resistirá a las fuerzas externas (como la gravedad) para mantener su posición.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer el tiempo de espera del motor\n\nEstablece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del VEX IQ Smart Motor.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl límite de tiempo del motor se utiliza para evitar que los bloques de movimiento que no alcanzan su posición impidan que otros bloques de la pila funcionen. Un ejemplo de un motor que no alcanza su posición es un brazo o garra que alcanza su límite mecánico y no puede completar su movimiento.\n\nEl bloque **establecer el tiempo de espera del motor** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo finalizará el comando **establecer motor** después de 2 segundos si el Claw Motor no ha alcanzado la posición de 270 grados. Una vez alcanzado el límite de tiempo o el objetivo, el Claw Motor se moverá a la posición 0 grados.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Establecer par de torsión del motor\n\nEstablece la fuerza del VEX IQ Smart Motor.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Establecer par de torsión del motor** acepta de un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer par de torsión del motor** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo girará el motor de garra a la posición de 40 grados con sólo un 20% de par máximo. Esto permite que la garra agarre un objeto sin dañarlo con demasiada fuerza.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer la velocidad del motor\n\nEstablece la velocidad de un VEX IQ Smart Motor.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Establecer la velocidad del motor** acepta de un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-127rpm a 127rpm**.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de un motor en un valor negativo hará que el motor gire en reversa.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de un motor en 0 hará que el motor se detenga.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad está establecida en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm)\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá que el motor del brazo gire lentamente a una velocidad del 25% a la posición de 90 grados.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_print_precision_new":{"name":"set_print_precision_new","markdown":"# Establecer la precisión de impresión\n\nEstablece el número de dígitos que aparecen después del punto decimal al imprimir bloques de reportero en la pantalla del VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_print_precision_new/print_precision.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el nivel de precisión que los bloques de reportero insertados se imprimirán en la pantalla.\n\n* Unos (1) (Predeterminado)\n* Décima (0.1)\n* Centésima (0.01)\n* Milésima (0.001)\n* Todos los dígitos (0.000001)\n\nLos bloques de informadores impresos en la pantalla se redondearán al nivel de precisión más cercano. Por ejemplo, 1.67 se imprimirá como 2 con precisión y 1.7 con precisión de décimas.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_print_precision_new/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_touchled_brightness":{"name":"set_touchled_brightness","markdown":"# Establecer el brillo del Touch LED\n\nEstablece el nivel de brillo del VEX IQ Touch LED.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Establecer el brillo del Touch LED** acepta de un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija el Touch LED que desea utilizar.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor3](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_sensor3.png)\n\nEl bloque **Establecer el brillo del Touch LED** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo iluminará el Touch LED verde con un brillo del 25%.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_touchled_color":{"name":"set_touchled_color","markdown":"# Establecer el color del Touch LED\n\nEstablece el color del VEX IQ Touch LED.\n\n![set_touchLED_color](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElegir el **Touch LED** que desea utilizar.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_sensor.png)\n\nElija el color que se mostrará.  \n\n![set_touchLED_color2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color2.png)\n\nPara apagar el **Touch LED**, ajusta el color a ninguno."},"set_touchled_fade":{"name":"set_touchled_fade","markdown":"# Establecer desvaneció de color del VEX IQ Touch LED\n\nEstablece la velocidad con la que el color del VEX IQ Touch LED se desvanece entre los colores.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el Touch LED que desea utilizar.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_sensor2.png)\n\nElige la intensidad con la que se desvanecerá el LED táctil\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_speed](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_speed.png)\n\n* Lento - El Touch LED se desvanecerá lentamente a un nuevo color.\n* Rápido - El Touch LED se desvanecerá rápidamente a un nuevo color.\n* Apagado - El Touch LED cambiará de color al instante.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo se desvanecerá lentamente el Touch LED a azul.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer la velocidad de dar vuelta\n\nEstablece la velocidad de las vueltas del chasis.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Establecer la velocidad de dar vuelta** sólo establecerá la velocidad del chasis, pero no hará que el chasis se mueva. Un bloque **vuelta** todavía se requiere.\n\n**Establecer la velocidad de dar vuelta** acepta de un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-127rpm a 127rpm**.\n\nEstableciendo la velocidad de giro del chasis a un valor negativo hará que el chasis de vuelta en la dirección opuesta.\n\nEstableciendo la velocidad de giro de una transmisión en 0 hará que la transmisión se detenga.\n\nEl bloque **Establecer la velocidad de dar vuelta** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis gire a la izquierda lentamente a una velocidad del 25%.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Establecer variable\n\nEstablece una variable en un valor determinado.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la variable que desea utilizar. Las variables también se pueden cambiar de nombre o eliminar. \n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer variable** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\nEste ejemplo reportera el VEX IQ Distance Sensor en la variable \"my variable\" y utilizará la \"mi variable\" para establecer la velocidad del chasis.\n\n![set_variable_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_variable/set_variable_example.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Establecer elemento de objeto de visión\n\nEstablece el elemento de objeto (del objeto sobre el que desea obtener más información) fuera del número de objetos detectados.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **recuento de objetos** puede ser utilizado antes del **establecer elemento de objeto de visión** para determinar el número de objetos detectados.\n\nElija qué sensor de visión utilizar.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer elemento de objeto de visión** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n\n\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Longitud de la lista\n\nReporta el número de elementos de una lista.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\nElija la lista que desea utilizar. La lista también puede ser renombrada o eliminada.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **Longitud de la lista** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# Instantánea\n\nToma una instantánea del sensor de visión.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **instantánea** capturará la imagen actual del sensor de visión para ser procesada y analizada en busca de firmas de color y códigos. \n\nTípicamente, primero se necesita una **instantánea** antes de usar cualquier otro bloque de sensores de visión.\n\nSeleccione el sensor de visión que desea utilizar.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nSeleccione el sensor de visión que desea utilizar. Las firmas de visión se configuran desde la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Gira\n\nGira un VEX IQ Smart Motor hasta que se detiene.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **gira** ejecutará un motor por siempre hasta que se utilice un nuevo bloque de motor o el programa se detenga.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nElija la dirección para girar. Los nombres de dirección se pueden cambiar en la ventana Dispositivos. \n\n![spin_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Gira por\n\nGira un VEX IQ Snart Motor para una distancia determinada.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Gira por** le dirá a un Motor que viaje en una dirección dada para una distancia dada desde donde se encuentra actualmente.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nElija la dirección para girar. Los nombres de dirección se pueden cambiar en la ventana Dispositivos. \n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nEl bloque **gira por** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElegir la unidad de medida en grados o vueltas.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques van a **esperar** hasta que el motor termine de moverse.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no espere** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el motor se mueve.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Gira a la posición\n\nHace girar un VEX IQ Smart Motor a una posición establecida.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Gira a la posición** le dirá a un Motor que viaje a una posición específica. Basado en la posición actual del Motor, **gira a la posición** determinará la dirección de rotación.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque **gira a la posición** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija la unidad de medida en grados o giros.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques van a **esperar** hasta que el motor termine de moverse.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no espera** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el motor se mueve.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Dejar de conducir\n\nDetiene el chasis.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dejar de conducir** hará que el Drivetrain se detenga por completo\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo detendrá el chasis después de 3 segundos.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Pare el motor\n\nDetiene un motor.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija qué motor detener.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo girará el motor de la garra abierto durante 3 segundos antes de detenerse.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Restar\n\nResta un valor de otro y reporta la diferencia.\n\n![subtract](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Restar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **restar** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\nRestar dos números.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nRestar con valores de variables.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nReste con los valores de los sensores o dispositivos\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Valor del temporizador\n\nReporta el valor del temporizador VEX IQ Brain en segundos.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl temporizador comienza a 0 segundos cuando el programa se inicia e informa de valores decimales.\n\nEl bloque de reportero **valor del temporizador** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo moverá el Drivetrain hacia adelante y reproducirá un efecto de sonido durante 4.5 segundos antes de realizar una vuelta de 90 grados.\n\n![timerValue_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/timer_value/timerValue_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Dar vuelta\n\nGira el chasis por siempre.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta** girará el Drivetrain para siempre hasta que se utilice un nuevo bloque Drivetrain o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija la dirección en la que se moverá el chasis.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Dar vuelta por\n\nGira el chasis durante una distancia determinada.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la dirección en la que girará el chasis.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEstablezca la distancia que se moverá el tren de mando introduciendo un número de grados.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques van a **esperar** hasta que el chasis termine de girar.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no espera** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el chasis gira.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Dar vuelta a dirección de\n\nGira un Drivetrain a un dirección específico con el VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a dirección de** se puede utilizar para girar el chasis a cualquier encabezado en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj como se muestra en la imagen de abajo.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nBasado en el rumbo actual del Gyro, **dar vuelta a dirección de** determinará la dirección a girar.\n\n**Dar vuelta a dirección de** acepta de un rango **0.00 a 359.99** grados.\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a dirección de** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis haga cuatro vueltas: \n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Izquierda a 45 grados\n- Izquierda a 90 grados\n- Izquierda a 270 grados\n- Derecha a 180 grados\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques van a **esperar** hasta que el chasis termine de girar.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no espera** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el chasis gira.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Dar Vuelta a la Rotación\n\nGira un Chasis a un ángulo de rotación específico cuando configurado con un VEX IQ Gyro Sensor.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a la rotación** se puede utilizar para girar el chasis a un valor positivo (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) o negativo (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj).\n\nBasado en el valor actual de **rotación** del Chasis, **dar vuelta a la rotación** determinará la dirección a girar.\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a la rotación** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el Chasis haga cuatro vueltas: \n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) a 90 grados\n- Izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) a 180 grados\n- Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) a -45 grados\n- Izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) a 0 grados\n\nDe forma predeterminada, otros bloques *esperarán* hasta que el Chasis haya terminado de girar.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir ** y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen ejecutándose mientras el Chasis gira.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Variable\n\nReporta del valor asignado a la variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nBloques **variable** se utilizan para informar de un valor almacenado dentro de la variable. Utilice el bloque **definir variable** para definir o actualizar el valor de una variable.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **variable** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nLas variables se crean con el botón **hacer una variable**.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Velocidad del motor\n\nInforma de la velocidad actual de un VEX IQ Smart Motor.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Velocidad del motor** reporta de un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-127rpm a 127rpm**.\n\nElija el motor que desea utilizar.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad se notifica en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **velocidad del motor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Objeto de visión\n\nInforma sobre un objeto detectado desde el Vision Sensor.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara utilizar el bloque **objeto de visión**, siga estos pasos:\n\n1. Configure su sensor de visión mediante la ventana Dispositivos.\n2. Utiliza **instantánea** para capturar una imagen del Vision Sensor y buscar una firma / código de color.\n3. Utiliza **object exists** para comprobar si el Vision Sensor detectó la firma / código de color solicitado.\n\nUna vez que el Vision Sensor detecta un objeto, puede utilizar otros bloques de visión para obtener más información sobre el objeto detectado.\n\n* Utiliza **establecer elemento de objeto de visión** para establecer qué objeto detectado desea obtener más información sobre. Por defecto, se utiliza el objeto más grande detectado.\n* Utiliza **object count** para determinar cuántos objetos se detectaron de esa firma solicitada / código de color.\n* Utiliza **vision object** para determinar qué información informar desde el objeto detectado.\n\nSeleccione el Vision Sensor que desea utilizar.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nSeleccione el valor que desea informar desde el Vision Sensor:\n\n* El ancho - Qué tan ancho es el objeto en píxeles. Devuelve un valor de **2 - 316 px**.\n* Altura - La altura del objeto en píxeles. Devuelve un valor de **2 - 212 px**. \n* CentroX - Reporta la coordenada X del centro del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 315 px**.\n* CentroY - Reporta la coordenada Y del centro del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 211 px**.\n* Ángulo - Reporta del ángulo del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 180 degrees**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nEl bloque de reportero **objeto de visión** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Espera\n\nEspera una cantidad específica de tiempo antes de pasar al siguiente bloque.\n\n![wait](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nElija una cantidad de tiempo para **espera**.\n\nEl bloque **espera** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/wait/wait_select.png)\n\nEste ejemplo cambiará el VEX IQ Touch LED de rojo a verde después de **esperar** 3.25 segundos.\n\n![wait_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/wait/wait_example.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Espera hasta que\n\nEspera a que un bloque booleano reporta **true** antes de pasar al siguiente bloque.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Espera hasta que** comprobará repetidamente un bloque de reportero booleano y no se moverá al siguiente bloque hasta que el bloque de informe booleano informe informe **true**.\n\nEl bloque booleano **espera hasta que** puede aceptar bloques con forma hexagonal (seis lados).\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo convertirá el Touch LED a amarillo y esperará hasta que se presione el Touch LED. Una vez presionado, el cerebro imprimirá \"Terminado!\" en la pantalla LCD.\n\n![wait_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/wait_until/wait_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"when_brain_button":{"name":"when_brain_button","markdown":"# Cuando botón del Brain\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques adjunta cuando se pulsa o suelta el botón del VEX IQ Brain seleccionado.\n\n![when_brain_button](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_brain_button/when_brain_button.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElige qué botón del Brain usar.\n\n![when_brain_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select.png)\n\nSeleccione la acción que activará el evento - **presionado** or **suelto** \n\n![when_brain_button_select_2](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select_2.png)  \n"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Cuando recibo\n\nEjecuta la pila adjunta de bloques cuando se recibe el mensaje seleccionado de un mensaje **emitido**.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el mensaje que desea escuchar. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\nEl bloque **cuando recibo** solo lo hará un bloque **transmitir** o **transmitir y espera** en una pila diferente.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo se mostrará en rojo en el VEX IQ Touch LED y, a continuación, espera dos segundos antes de transmitir el \"mensaje1\". \n\nUna vez recibido el mensaje, la pila **cuando recibo** hará que el chasis se moverá hacia adelante, mientras que el motor de brazo se moverá hacia arriba al mismo tiempo. \n\nLas dos pilas continuarán ejecutándose al mismo tiempo que se indica en las flechas rojas.\n\n\n![when_broadcast_example](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_example.png)\n\n"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Cuando parachoques\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta el VEX IQ Bumper seleccionado.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el interruptor del parachoques que desea utilizar.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nSeleccione qué acción desencadenará el evento - **presionado** o **suelto** \n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Cuando eje del controller\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques adjunta cuando se mueve el eje de joystick del VEX IQ Controller seleccionado.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el eje del joystick del Controller que desea utilizar.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Cuando botón del controller\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta el botón del VEX IQ Controller seleccionado.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el botón del Controller que desea utilizar.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_controller_button/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_controller_button/controller_button_back.png)\n\nSeleccione la acción que activará el evento - **presionado** o **suelto** \n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Cuando empieza\n\nEjecuta la pila adjunta de bloques cuando se inicia el proyecto.\n\n![when_started](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl evento **cuando empieza** Se ejecutará cuando el programa se inicie desde el menú de VEX IQ Brain o desde el botón **correr** en bloques de VEXcode IQ.\n\nTodos los nuevos programas incluirán automáticamente un bloque **cuando empieza**. Los proyectos pueden soportar hasta 3 bloques **cuando empieza**."},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Cuando temporizador\n\nEjecuta la pila adjunta de bloques cuando el temporizador del VEX IQ Brain es mayor que el valor dado.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nEl temporizador del Brain comienza al principio de cada proyecto.\n\nElija una cantidad de tiempo. El evento **cuando temporizador** se ejecutará una vez que el temporizador del cerebro es **más que** la cantidad introducida.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nEl bloque **cuando temporizador** puede aceptar decimales o valores enteros.\n\nEl bloque **cuando temporizador** no puede aceptar otros bloques de reporteros."},"when_touchled":{"name":"when_touchled","markdown":"# Cuando Touch LED\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques conectada cuando se presiona o suelta el VEX IQ Touch LED seleccionado.\n\n![when_touchLED](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_touchled/when_touchled.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nElija el LED táctil que desea utilizar.\n\n![when_touchLED_select](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_touchled/when_touchled_select.png)\n\nSeleccione la acción que activará el evento - **presionado** o **suelto** \n\n![when_touchLED_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/when_touchled/when_touchled_condition.png)"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Mientras\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques dentro mientras que la condición booleana se notifica que es **true**.\n\n![while](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/while/while.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **mientras** sólo comprobará la condición booleana al principio de cada bucle. \n\nSi la condición booleana se notifica como **true**, los bloques dentro de **while** se ejecutará.\n\nSi la condición booleana se notifica como **false**, los bloques dentro de **while** se omitirá.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **mientras** puede aceptar bloques hexagonales (de seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/es-419/while/while_inserted.png)"}}},"fi":{"blocks":{"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Lisää\n\nLisää/laske kaksi arvoa yhteen ja antaa summan.\n\n![add](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/add/add.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Lisää** blokissa voi käyttää kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n**Lisää** blokin voi laittaa muiden blokkien ympyräuotoisiin arvokenttiin. \n\nLaske yhteen kaksi lukua.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nLaske yhteen kaksi muuttujaa.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nLaske yhteen kahden sensorin antamaa arvoa.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# Ja\n\nRaoportoi onko kahden Boolean muuttujan molemmat arvot tosia. \n\n![and](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/and/and.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ja** blokki antaa arvon **tosi** kun molemmat ehdot ovat **tosia**. \n\n**Ja** blokki antaa arvon **epätosi** kun molemmat tai toinen ehdoista ovat/on **epätosia**. \n\n![and_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tutkitaan, onko kahta VEX IQ -ohjaimen nappia yhtäaikaa painettu alas.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/and/and_sensors.png)\n\n**Ja** blokki antaa arvon **tosi** kun molemmat **Ohjainnappi E ylös** ja **Ohjainnappi L Alas** on painettu alas. \n\nMuutoin **Ja** blokki antaa arvon **epätosi**.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/and/and_truth.png)"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Akun varaus %\n\nKertoo lataustason VEX IQ Aivojen akussa.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Akun varaus %** antaa luvun väliltä **0% - 100%**.\n\n**Akun varaus %** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä annetaan äänimerkk,i kun akun varaustaso **Akun varaus %** on alle 50 %.\n\n![battery_capacity_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/battery_level/battery_capacity_example_revised.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Boolean muuttuja\n\nAntaa Boolean muuttujan arvon.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n##Miten käytetään\n\n**Boolean muuttuja** saa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi**. Käytä *Aseta arvoon** blokkia, kun päivität muuttujan arvon.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\n**Boolean muuttuja** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa toisten blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nBoolean muuttujan saa tehtyä **Tee Boolean** painikkeella.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"brain_button_pressed":{"name":"brain_button_pressed","markdown":"# Aivojen nappia painettu\n\nRaportoi, jos VEX IQ aivojen nappia painettu.\n\n![button_pressed_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aivojen nappia painettu** antaa arvon **tosi** jos valittua Aivojen nappia on painettu.\n\n**Aivojen nappia painettu** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos valittua Aivojen nappia ei ole painettu.\n\nValitse mitä nappia tutkitaan.\n\n![button_pressed_options](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_options.png)\n\n**Aivojen nappia painettu** Boolean blokki saa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa muiden blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokentttiin.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä robotti ajaa eteenpäin ja kääntyy oikealla kun aivojen **Ylös** nappia on painettu.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_example_revised.png)\n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Keskeytä\n\nKeskeyttää heti toistorakenteen sisällä komentojen suorituksen.\n\n![break](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/break/break.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun komento **keskeytä** blokki on lisätty toistorakenteen sisälle, se aiheuttaa toiston komentojen päättymisen. \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin ja tarkistaa onko Aivojen  **ylös** nappia painettu. \n\nJos **ylös** nappia on **painettu**, **keskeytä** blokki aiheuttaa toistokomentojen suorituksen päättymisen ja ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n![break_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Valovoima\n\nRaportoi VEX IQ värisensorin havaitseman valon valovoiman/kirkkauden prosentteina.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Valovoima** antaa arvot välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\nValitse värisensori, jota käytetään.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\n**Valovoima** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Lähetä viesti\n\nLähettää viestin käynnistämään **Kun saan viestin** -blokin alla olevat blokit halutulla viestinimellä.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nViestin lähettäjän blokkipinon suoritus jatkuu heti viestilähetyksen jälkeen samaan aikaan kuin **Kun saan viestin** blokkia suoritetaan.\n\nValitse viestille nimi, joka läheteään **Lähetä viesti** -blokilla. Voit luoda myös uuden viestin.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä VEX IQ KosketusLED :n valo muuttuu punaiseksi ja odottaa 2 sekuntia  ennen kuin lähetään viesti nimellä \"message1\". \n\nKun viesti on vastaanotettu, **Kun saan viestin** pinon komento ajaa ajopeliä eteenpäin samaan aikaan kun kouramoottori pyörii eteenpäin. \n\nMolemmat pinot, kutsuva ja kutsuttu, suorittavat komentoja yhtäaikaa kuten punaisilla nuolilla on kuvattu.\n\n![broadcast_example_arrows](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/broadcast/broadcast_example_arrows.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Lähetä viesti ja odota\n\nLähettää viestin aktivoimalla **Kun saan viestin** hattublokin ja oodotetaan kunnes hattublokki on suorittasnut kaikki siinä nipussa olevat blokit.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKutsuja jää odotaan komennolla **Lähetä viesti ja odota** kunnes kutsun saanut hattublokki on suorittanut nipun komennot loppuun.\n\nValitse viestinimi, joka läheteään. Myös uusi viesti voidaan luoda samalla.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä VEX IQ KosketusLED:n väri on punainen ja se odottaa pari sekuntia ennen viestin \"message1\" lähetystä. \n\nKun viesti on saatu **Kun saan viestin** hattublokin alta käynnistyy nippu komentoja, joilla ajopeli liikkuu eteenpäin ja soittaa ääniefektin.\n\nKutsuja odottaa kunnens hattublokki on suorittanut komennot loppuun kuvan punaisten nuolien mukaisesti.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows_3](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows3.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Kalibroi gyro\n\nVEX IQ Gyro sensorin kalibroinnilla estetään Gyro Sensorin virhettä (drifting).\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nHeiluntaa tapahtuu, kun Gyro Sensori virheellisesti huomaa liikett vaikka sensori on paikallaan.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nGyro sensorin pitää olla levossa kun kalibrointi suoritetaan.\n\nvalitse Gyro sensori, jota käytetään.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nValitse aika kauanko kalibrointia suoritetaan. Pidempi kalinrointiaika parantaa gyron luetettavuutta.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_seconds](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_seconds.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Muuta arvolla\n\nMuuttaa muuttujan arvoa syötetyllä määrällä.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Kuinka käytetään\n\nValitse muuttuja, voit samalla myös uudelleennimetä muuttujan tai poistaa sen.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\n**Muuta arvolla** blokissa voi käyttää kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja sekä numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTämä esimerkissä lisätään ajonopeutta 10 -yksiköllä jokaisella kierroksella **toista** blokissa.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Tyhjää kaikki rivit\n\nTyhjentää VEX IQ aivojen näytön.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Tyhjää kaikki rivit** ei muuta kursorin paikkaa näytöllä. Valitse **aseta kursori** blokki, jos haluat siirtää osoitin uuteen paikkaan.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTulostetaan \"Hello\" sekunnin ajan ja tyhjennetään koko näyttö ennen kun tulostetaan \"Goodbye\".\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Tyhjää rivi\n\nTyhjää yksittäisen rivin VEX IQ aivojen näytöltä.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Tyhjää rivi** hyväksyy rivinumerot väliltä **1 - 5**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/clear_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan \"Hello\" rivin 2 sarakeeseen 1 kolmeksi sekunnin ajaksi ennen 2 rivin tyhjäämistä.\n\n![clear_row_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/clear_row/clear_row_example.png)"},"color_detects_color":{"name":"color_detects_color","markdown":"# Havaitsee värin?\n\nraportoi löytääkö VEX IQ värisensori tietyn värin.\n\n![color_detects](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/color_detects_color/color_detects.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Havaitsee värin?** antaa arvon **tosi** jos sensori havaitsee valitun värin.\n\n**Havaitsee värin?** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos sensori ei havaitse valittua väriä.\n\nValise värisensori, jota käytetään.\n\n![color_detects_chosen](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/color_detects_color/color_detects_chosen.png)\n\nValitse väri, jota etsitään.\n\n![color_detects_selected](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/color_detects_color/color_detects_selected.png)\n\n**Havaitsee värin?** Boolean blokin arvot ovat **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa muiden blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![color_detects_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/color_detects_color/color_detects_shape.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTulostetaan  \"Color Red\" tai \"Other Color\" riippuen löytääkö värisensori värin \"punainen\".\n\n![color_detects_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/color_detects_color/color_detects_example.png)\n\n"},"color_of":{"name":"color_of","markdown":"# Värin nimi\n\nRaportoi VEX IQ värisensorin havaitseman värin nimen.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/color_of/color_of_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Värin nimi** tunnistaa seuraavat värit: **punainen, purppura, punavioletti,violetti, sinivioletti, sininen, sinivihreä, vihreä, keltavihreä, keltainen, keltaoranssi, oranssi tai punaoranssi.**\n\nValitse värisensori, jota käytetään.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/color_of/color_of_color.png)\n\n**Värin nimi** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![color_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/color_of/color_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Kommentti\n\nOhjelmoija voi kommenteilla selittää ohjelman toimintaa. \n\n![comment_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAmmattikoodaajat kommentoivat ohjelmiaan koko läpi ohjelman. Kommentit helpottavat myös virheiden selvitystä ja muiden kanssa yhteistyötä. \n\nLisää/päivitä teksti **Kommentti** blokkiin valitsemalla ensiksi neliösyöttökenttä ja päivitä teksti sitten ko.kenttään.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nKommentit eivät vaikuta muuhun suoritettavaan ohjelmaan sen ympärillä.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Ohjain Ota käyttöön/Poista käytöstä\n\nOttaa käyttöön tai Poistaa käytöstä Laitteet menussa tehdyt valmiit ohjainmääritykset.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse joko Ota käyttöön tai Poista käytöstä. Oletuksena Ohjain on käytössä.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nValmiiksi määritelty ohjain toiminto tässä esimerkissä on ajopelin ajokäyttäytyminen.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nTässä esimerkissä konfiguroitu ohjain otetaan pois käytöstä kun ohjelma alkaa. \n\nRobotti ajaa sitten eteenpäin 6 tuumaa.\n\n**Ota käyttöön** bloki mahdollistaa sitten ohjaimen käytön uudelleen.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Moottorin sähkövirta\n\nAntaa moottorin sähkövirran käytön joko yksikössä prosentti (%) or ampeerisekunti (amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottorin sähkövirta** antaa arvot väliltä **0% - 100%** tai **0.0 - 1.2 amps**. \n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nValitse yksikkö joko % tai amps.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\n**Moottorin sähkövirta** arvoa voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Osoittimen sarake\n\nRaportoi VEX IQ aivojen näytöllä näkyvän osoittimen sarakearvon.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Osoittimen sarake** rvoi olla välillä **1 to 21**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/cursor_column/row_column_index.png)  \n\n**Osoittimen sarake** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä jos **Osoittimen sarake** arvo on suurempi kuin 15, kursori siirretään riville 1 sarakkaaseen 1 ja tulostetaan 'Hello'.\n\n![cursor_column_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/cursor_column/cursor_column_example_simple.png)\n\n"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Osoittimen rivi\n\nantaa VEX IQ aivojen näytön rivin, jolla kursori nyt on.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Osoittimen rivi** antaa rivinumeron väliltä **1 - 5**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/cursor_row/row_column_index.png)\n\n**Osoittimen rivi** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tutkitaan, jos **Osoittimen rivi** rivinumero on suurempi kuin 4. Jos on, kursori siirretään riville 1 ja tulostetaan teksti 'Hello'.\n\n![cursor_row_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/cursor_row/cursor_row_example_simple.png)"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Välimatka\n\nAntaa lähimmän havaitun esineen välimatkan käytössä olevastaVEX IQ etäisyysanturista.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Välimatka** antaa arvot väliltä **24 mm - 1000 mm** tai **1 tuuma - 40 tuumaa**.\n\nValitse etäisyysanturi, jota käytät.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nValitse mittayksikkö, jota **Välimatka** blokki käyttää joko tuumaa tai mm. \n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\n**Välimatka** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien pyöreissä arvokentissä.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Jakolasku\n\nlaskee ensimmäisen luvun jakamisen toisella luvulla.\n\n![divide](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Jakolasku** hyväksyy kokonais-ja desimaalilukuja sekä numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n**Jakolasku** blokin voi sijoittaa muiden blokkien pyöreisiin arvokenttiin. \n\nAnna jakolaskun tekijänumerot.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nJakolasku muuttujilla.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nJakolasku sensoreiden arvoilla.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Aja\n\nLiikuttaa ajopeliä ikuisesti.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aja** blokki liikuttaa ajopeliä ikuisesti kunnes uusi ajoblokki käynnistyy tai ohjelman suoritus loppuu.\n\nValitse ajosuunta **Eteenpäin** tai **Taaksepäin**.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Kulkupelin sähkövirta\n\nAntaa sähkövirran kulutuksen, jota ajo/kulkupeli tällä hetkellä kuluttaa.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kulkupelin sähkövirta** raportoi kulutusarvon välillä **0% - 100%** tai **0.0 - 1.2 amps**. \n\nValitse kumpaa yksikköä käytetään % tai ampeerisekuntia (amps).\n\n![drive_current_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_current/drive_current_unit.png)\n\n**Kulkupelin sähkövirta** voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Aja matkan\n\nAjopeli ajaa annetun matkan.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse suunta, johon ajopeli liikkuu.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\n**Aja matkan** blokissa voi käyttää kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\nAnna matkan lukuarvo sekä yksikkö (tuumia tai mm).\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nOletuksena seuraavat blokit odottavat kunnes ajopelin liike loppuu.\n\nVoit valita option **ja älä odota**, jolloin seuraavat blokit käynnistyvät jo ajon aikana.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Ajopelin kulkusuunta\n\nAntaa ajopelin nykyisen kulkusuunnan.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopelin kulkusuunta** antaa arvon välillä **0.00 - 359.99 astetta**.\n\n**Ajopelin kulkusuunta** antaa kellotaulun vastapäivään kulkusuunnan kuvan mukaan.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_heading/TopDownBot01.png)\n\n**Ajopelin kulkusuunta** blokkia käytetään muiden blokkien pyöreissä arvokentissä.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Ajo on suoritettu?\n\nRaportoi onko ajopelin liike loppunut.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajo on suoritettu?** antaa arvon **tosi** kun ajopelin moottoreiden liike on loppunut.\n\n**Ajo on suoritettu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** kun ajopelin moottoreiden liike jatkuu.\n\n**Ajo on suoritettu?** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Ajopeli liikkuu?\n\nAntaa vastauksen liikkuuko ajopeli tällä hetkellä.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopeli liikkuu?** antaa arvon **tosi** jos ajopelin ajomoottorit liikkuvat.\n\n**Ajopeli liikkuu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos ajopelin ajomoottorit eivät liikku.\n\n**Ajopeli liikkuu?** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa eri blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Käännös asteina\n\nAntaa ajopelin kääntymisen kulman asteina VEX IQ Gyro Sensorin avulla.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Käännös asteina** antaa **positiivisen** arvon kun ajopeli on kääntynyt **vastapäivään**.\n\n**Käännös asteina** antaa **negatiivisen** arvon kun ajopeli on kääntynyt **myötäpäivään**.\n\n**Käännös asteina** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien pyöreissä arvokentissä.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Kulkupelin nopeus\n\nRaportoi ajo/kulkupelin nykyisen nopeuden.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kulkupelin nopeus** antaa arvon väliltä **-100% - 100%** tai **-127rpm - 127rpm**\n\nValitse yksikkö, jolla nopeus raportoidaan prosentti  % tai kierrosta minuutissa (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\n**Kulkupelin nopeus** blokkia käytetään eri blokkien pyöreissä arvokentissä.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Yhtä suuri\n\nRaportoi, onko kaksi lukua yhtäsuurta. \n\n![equal_to](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Yhtä suuri** antaa arvon **tosi** jos kaksi lukua on yhtäsuurta.\n\n**Yhtä suuri** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos kaksi lukua ei ole yhtäsuurta\n\n**Yhtä suuri** blokin voi laittaa kokonais- ja desimaalilukja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n**Yhtä suuri** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan \"Drivetrain Stalled\" VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle, jos ajopelin nykyinen nopeus on 100%.\n\n![equal_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/equal_to/equal_to_example.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Toista ikuisesti\n\nToistoblokki toistaa sen sisällä olevat blokit ikuisesti.\n\n![forever](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLaita silmukan alle blokit, joiden suoritus jatkuu **Toista ikuisesti**.\n\nVoit hypätä pois **Toista ikuisesti** loopista blokilla **break** silmukan sisällä.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nSilmukoita voi laittaa toistensa sisään. Sitä kutsutaan upotukseksi ja sillä voi saada ohjelmaan erilaisia ominaisuuksia.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä sama ääni toistetaan 5 sekunnin välein ikuisesti.\n\n![forever_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/forever/forever_example.png)"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Funktio\n\nSuorittaa valitun matemaatisen funktion.\n\n![function](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/function/function.png)\n\n* **itseisarvo** - itseisarvo\n* **pyöristys alas** - lähin kokonaisluku alas pyöristys\n* **pyöristys ylös** - lähin kokonaisluku ylös pyöristys\n* **neliöjuuri** - neliöjuuri\n* **sin** - sin (vastakkaisen kateetin suhde hyponenuusaan)\n* **cos** - cos (viereisen kateetin suhde hyponenuusaan)\n* **tan** - tangentti(vastakkaisen kateetin suhde viereiseen)\n* **asin** - arc sin (sinin vastafuntio)\n* **acos** - arc cos (cosinin vastafuntio)\n* **atan** - arc tan (tangentin vastafuntio)\n* **ln** - luonnollinen logaritmi e kantaluvulla\n* **log** - 10 logaritmi\n* **e ^** - luonnollisen luvun e potenssi\n* **10 ^** - 10 potenssi\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Funktio** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaaliluvut sekä numeeriset blokit.\n\nValitse se matemaattinen **funktio** optiolistalta, jota haluat käyttää.\n\n![function_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/function/function_select.png)\n\n**funktio** blokin voi sijoittaa blokkien pyöreämuotoisiin arvokenttiin. \n\n![function_fit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Suurempi kuin\n\nRaportoi, onko tarkastelun ensimmäinen luku suurempi kuin toinen.  \n\n![greater_than](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Suurempi kuin** antaa arvon **tosi** kun ensimmäinen luku on suurempi kuin tarkastelun toinen luku. \n\n**Suurempi kuin** antaa arvon **epätosi** kun ensimmäinen luku ei ole suurempi kuin tarkastelun toinen luku. \n\n**Suurempi kuin** blokissa voi olla kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\n**Suurempi kuin** Boolean blokin arvo on **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi laittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin kenttiin.\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan \"Battery level good\" VEX IQ aivojen näytölle, jos robotin akun lataustaso on suurempi kuin 75%.\n\n![greater_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/greater_than/greater_than_example.png)\n\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Ajosuunta aste\n\nAntaa VEX IQ Gyro sensorin tän hetkisen ajosuunnan asteina.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajosuunta aste** antaa arvon välillä **0.00 to 359.99**.\n\n**Ajosuunta aste** raportoi kellotaulun vastapäivään kasvavan suuntaarvon kuten kuvassa.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/heading_of_gyro/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\nValitse Gyro anturi, jota käytetään.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\n**Ajosuunta aste** blokkia voi käyttää blokkien pyöreissä arvokenttissä.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"hue_of":{"name":"hue_of","markdown":"# Värisävy\n\nRaportoi VEX IQ Värianturin antaman värisävyn.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/hue_of/hue_of_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n*Värisävy** on värispektrin arvo väliltä **0 - 360**.\n\nValitse värisensori, jota käytetään.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/hue_of/hue_of_color.png)\n\n**Värisävy** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![hue_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/hue_of/hue_of_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Jos niin\n\nEhtoblokki suorittaa ehtohaaran komennot vain jos Boolean -ehto on **tosi**.  \n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Jos niin** -ehtoblokki tarkistaa Boolean -ehdon vain kerran. \n\nJos Boolean -ehto on **tosi**, haaran sisällä olevat blokit suoritetaan.\n\nJos Boolean -ehto on **epätosi**, hypätään haaran yli seuraavaan komentoon.\n\n**Jos niin** ehtoblokkiiin voi sijoittaa ehdoksi kuusikulmaisia blokkiarvoja.\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä soitetaan ääntä aina kun VEX IQ Painokytkintä on painettu.\n\n**Jos niin** 'ehtoblokin voi sijoittaa ikuiseen luuppiin, jotta ääniefekti toimii jatkuvasti.\n\n![if_then_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/if_then/if_then_example.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Jos niin muuten\n\nOn ehtoblokki, jossa suoritaan joko jos-haaran tai muuten -haaran komennot Boolean -ehdon perusteella.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Jos niin muuten** ehtoblokki testaa siinä olevaa Boolean -ehtoa vain kerran. \n\nJos Boolean -ehto on **tosi**, niin **jos** haaran blokit suoritetaan.\n\nJos Boolean -ehto on **epätosi**, niin **muuten** haaran blokit suoritetaan.\n\n**Jos niin muuten** ehtoblokkiin voi sijoittaa vain kuusikulmaisia blokkeja ehdoksi.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nVEX IQ painoLED valo on vihreä, jos sitä painetaan ja valo on punainen, jos ei ole painettu.\n\n**Jos niin muuten** ehtoblokin sijoittaa ikuiseen blokkiin niin ledin valo muuttuu punaisesta vihreään kun sitä on painettu. \n\n![if_then_else_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/if_then_else/if_then_else_example.png)"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 2D alkio\n\nAntaa halutun taulukon alkion arvon. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse 2D taulukko, jota käytetään. Voit myös uudelleen nimetä tai poistaa valitun taulukon.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nAnna taulukon alkion rivi (ensimmäinen luku) ja sarake (toinen luku). Tässä esimerkissä on valittu rivi 2, sarake 3.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\n**2D alkio** taulukon valitut alkionumerot voivat olla vain kokonaislukuja.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Luettelon alkio\n\nAntaa luettelon valitun alkion arvon. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse luettelo, jota käytetään. Voit myös uudeleennimetä tai poistaa valitun luettelon.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nAnna luettelon alkion järjestysnumero. Tässä näytetään luettelon toisen alkion arvo. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\n**Luettelon alkio** blokin alkiovalinnassa voi olla kokonaislukuja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä ajopelin nopeuteen laitetaan arvoksi luettelon 3. alkio. Tällöin ajopelin nopeus on 90%.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 2D taulukon pituus\n\nkeroo montako riviä tai saraketta 2d taulukossa on.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse 2d taulukko, jota käytetään. Voit samlla uudelleen nimetä tai poistaa 2d taulukon.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nValitse kumpaa tekijää raportoit **rivit** tai **sarakkeet**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\n** 2D taulukon pituus** arvon voi sijoittaa blokkien pyöreisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Pienempi kuin\n\nKertoo onko kahdesta luvusta vertailun ensimmäinen pienempi kuin toinen. \n\n![less_than](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Pienempi kuin** antaa arvon **tosi**jos vertailun ensimmäinen luku on pienenmpi kuin jälkimmäinen luku. \n\n**Pienempi kuin** antaa arvon **epätosi**jos vertailun ensimmäinen luku on ei ole pienenmpi kuin jälkimmäinen luku. \n\n**Pienempi kuin** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokin arvoja.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan teksti \"Low Battery!\" VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle jos IQ akun lataustaso on pienempi kuin 25%.\n\n![less_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/less_than/less_than_example.png)\n\n"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Moottorin liike loppu?\n\nKertoo jos valitun moottorin liike on valmis/päättynyt.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottorin liike loppu?** antaa arvon **tosi** jos valitun moottorin liike on valmis/päättynyt.\n\n**Moottorin liike loppu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos valittu moottori on edelleen liikkeessä.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\n**Moottorin liike loppu?** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\nMoottorin liike loppu? -blokki on sijoitettu Kun -toistorakenteen kuusikulmaiseseen ehtorakenteeseen. \n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Moottori pyörii?\n\nKertoo jos valittu moottori vielä pyörii?\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottori pyörii?** antaa arvon **tosi** kun kohdemoottori pyörii.\n\n**Moottori pyörii?** antaa arvon **epätosi** kun kohdemoottori on pysähtynyt.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\n**Mooottori pyörii?** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa muiden blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvoalueisiin.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Kertolasku\n\nantaa kahden luvun kertolaskun tuloksen.\n\n![multiply](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kertolasku** hyväksuu kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisisten blokkien arvoja.\n\n**Kertolasku** blokin voi laittaa blokkien pyöreisiin arvokohtiin. \n\nKahden luvun kertolasku.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nKahden muuttujan kertolasku.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nKahden sensoriarvon kertolasku.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Siirrä kursori seuraavalle riville\n\nSiirtää kursorin aivojen näytöllä seuraavalle riville.\n\n![next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOletetuksena ohjelman alussa näytöllä kursori on kohdassa rivi 1 sarake 1. **seuraavalle riville** blokki pudottaa kursorin seuraavalle riville. \n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/next_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTulostetaan viesti \"First Message\" ja siirretään kursori seuraavalle riville viestin \"Second Message\" tulostusta varten.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/next_row/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/next_row/set_cursor_welcome.png)\n"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# Ei\n\nAntaa vastakkaisen totuusarvon Boolean -muuttujalle.\n\n![not](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/not/not.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ei** blokki antaa arvon **tosi** kun Boolean blokki sen sisällä antaa arvon **epätosi**.\n\n**Ei** blokki antaa arvon **epätosi** kun Boolean blokki sen sisällä antaa arvon **tosi**.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTämä esimerkki antaa arvon **tosi** kun VEX IQ Aivojen \"check\" painiketta ei ole painettu. \n\n![not_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Kohteiden lukumäärä\n\nKertoo montako esinekohdetta Vision -kamera havaitsee. \n\nEsine pitää aina olla määritelty Laitteet-ikkunassa ennen kuin **Kohteiden lukumäärä** voi sen havaita kuvassa.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse Vision -kamera, jota käytetään.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\n**Ota kuva** blokkia pitää käyttää ennen kuin **Kohteiden lukumäärä** blokki voi laskea kohteiden määrän.\n\n**Kohteiden lukumäärä** blokki havaitsee vain merkattujen kohteiden lukumäärän viimeisestä kuvasta.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Kohde havaittu\n\nKertoo jos Vision -kamera havaitsee sille määritellyn esineen. \n\nEsine pitää olla määritelty kameralle ennen kuin **Kohde havaittu** blokki voi esineen havaita.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse kamera, jota käytetään.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n**Kohde havaittu** antaa arvon **tosi** jos Vision -kamera havaitsee sille määritellyn esineen.\n\n**Kohde havaittu**  antaa arvon **epätosi** jos Vision -kamera ei havaitse sille määriteltyä esinettä.\n\n**Kohde havaittu** Boolean blokki antaa arvon **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvoalueisiin.\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\n**Ota kuva** blokki pitää aina olla käytetty ts kuva otettu ennen kuin **Kohde havaittu** Boolean blokki voi antaa arvon **tosi** tai **epätosi** ."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Etäisyysanturi havaitsi esineen\n\nKertoo jos VEX IQ Etäisyysanturi löytää esineen näkökentässään. \n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Havaitsi esineen** anta arvon **tosi** kun Etäisyysanturi löytää esineen tai esineenpinnan näkökentässään.\n\n**Havaitsi esineen**  anta arvon **epätosi** kun Etäisyysanturi ei havaitse esinettä tai esineenpintaa näkökentässään.\n\nValitse etäisyysanturi, jota käytetään.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nThe **havaitsi esineen** Boolean blokki antaa arvo **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa toisten blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvoalueisiin.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"object_is_near":{"name":"object_is_near","markdown":"# Esine on havaittu?\n\nKertoo,jos VEX IQ Värianturi havaitsee esineen lähellä.\n\n![object_is_near](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_is_near/object_is_near_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Esine on havaittu?** antaa arvon **tosi** kun Värianturi havaitsee esineen pinnan sen edessä.\n**Esine on havaittu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** Värianturin edessä on vain tyhjää.\n\nValitse käytetty värianturi.\n\n![object_is_near_color](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_is_near/object_is_near_color.png)\n\n**Esine on havaittu?** Boolean blokki antaa arvon **tosi** tai  **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa muiden blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvoalueisiin.\n\n![object_is_near_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/object_is_near/object_is_near_inserted.png)\n\n\n "},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# Tai\n\nraportoi onko toinen kahdesta Boolean -ehdoista totta.\n\n![or](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/or/or.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Tai** Boolean blokki antaa arvoksi **tosi** kun yksi (tai molemmat) ehdoista on **tosi**. \n\n**Tai** Boolean blokki antaa arvoksi **epätosi** kun molemmat ehdoista ovat **epätosi**.\n\n**Tai** Boolean blokki antaa arvoksi **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaiseen arvokenttään.\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\n**Tai** blokki antaa arvoksi **tosi** kun joko toinen (tai molemmat) VEX IQ Painokytkin ja VEX IQ PainoLED laitteita on painettu ja antaa arvoksi **epätosi** vain jos kumpaakaan ei ole painettu.\n\n![or_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/or/or_truth.png)"},"play_note":{"name":"play_note","markdown":"# Soita nuotti\n\nSoittaa valitun nuotin.\n\n![play_note](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/play_note/play_note.png)\n\n## Miten k채ytet채채n\n\nValitse nuotti, jota soitetaan.\n\n![play_note_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/play_note/play_note_select.png)\n\nValitse kesto, kauanko nuotti soi.\n\n![play_note_duration](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/play_note/play_note_duration.png)\n\n* **koko** nuotti soittaa nuottia 1 sekuntia (1000 millisekunttia)\n* **puoli** nuotti soittaa nuottia  0.5 sekuntia (500 millisekunttia)\n* **nelj채nnes** nuotti soittaa nuottia 0.251 sekuntia (250 millisekunttia)\n\nHeti kun nuotti alkaa soimaan, seuraava komentoblokki suoritetaan."},"play_sound":{"name":"play_sound","markdown":"# Soita ääni\n\nSoittaa halutun ääniefektin.\n\n![play_sound](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/play_sound/play_sound.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse haluttu ääniefekti alasvetolistalta. \n\n![play_sound_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/play_sound/play_sound_select.png)\n\nKun ääniefekti käynnistyy niin samalla seuraava ohjelmablokki ohjelmassa käynnistyy."},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Ohjaintatin asento\n\nraportoi, missä asennossa ohjaintatti on akselilla.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ohjaintatin asento** antaa asennosta arvon välillä **-100 - 100**.\n\n**Ohjaintatin asento** antaa arvon 0, jos tatti on akselin keskellä levossa.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nValitse ohjaintatti, jota käytetään.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\n**Ohjaintatin asento** raportointiblokkia käytetään blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä tarkastellaan koko ajan ohjainen D tatin asentoa ohjaamaan käsimooottorin nopeutta.\n\n![position_of_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Moottori asento\n\nMittaa moottorin pyörimismatkaa.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottori asento** raportoi moottorin pyörimisasennon joko kokonaislukuna asteina tai desimaalilukuna kierroksina.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nValitse tarkastellaanko moottorin pyörimismatkaa asteina vai kierroksina. \n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\n*Moottori asento** arvoa voidaan käyttää pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Painokytkintä painettu?\n\nRaportoi, jos VEX IQ Painokytkintä on painettu.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Painokytkintä painettu?** antaa arvon **tosi** jos Painokytkintä on painettu.\n\n**Painokytkintä painettu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos Painokytkintä ei ole painettu.\n\nValitse se Painokytkin, jota käytetään.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\n**Painokytkintä on painettu.** Boolean blokki antaa arvon **tosi** or **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa kuusikulmaisten blokkien arvoalueisiin.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Ohjainnappia painettu?\n\nRaportoi kun VEX IQ ohjainnappia on painettu.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ohjainnappia painettu?** antaa arvon **tosi** jos painonappia on painettu.\n\n**Ohjainnappia painettu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos painonappia ei ole painettu..\n\nValitse ohjain, jota käytät.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nValitse nappi, jota käytetään.\n\n**Ohjainnappia painettu?** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sitä voi käyttää kentissä, johon tarvitaan kuusikulmainen arvokenttä.\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä tutkitaan, onko ohjaimen E Up nappia painettu, ja jos on, kouramoottori pyörii eteenpäin. \n\n![pressing_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_example_revised.png)"},"pressing_touchled":{"name":"pressing_touchled","markdown":"# KosketusLed painettu?\n\nRaportoi, onko KosketusLED iä painettu.\n\n![pressing_touch_led](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**KosketusLed painettu?** antaa arvon **tosi** jos sitä on painettu.\n\n**KosketusLed painettu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos sitä ei ole painettu.\n\nValiotse KosketusLed, jota käytetään.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_led](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_led.png)\n\n**KosketusLed painettu?** on boolean blokki, joka antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sitä voi käyttää kuusikulmaisten blokkien arvokentissä.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_inserted.png)\n\n"},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Tulosta\n\nTulostaa lukuarvoja tai tekstiä VEX IQ aivojen näytölle.\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/print/look_print.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Tulosta** blokki rivitulostaa dataa nykyiselle kursoripaikalle aivojen näytöllä.\n\nUudet ohjelmat tulostaa oletuksena riville 1 sarakkeeseen 1.\n\nKaikki raportoivat tuntoaistiblokit tulostavat oletuksena kokonaislukuina. Käytä **Aseta tulostustarkkuus** blokkia, jos haluat tulostaa desimaalimuodossa arvoja.\n\nTulosta tekstiä ja numeroita.\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/print/print_words.png)\n\nTulosta muuttujien arvoja.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nTulosta laskutoimitusten tuloksia.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nTulosta jonkun sensorin antama arvo.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Minun blokki (kutsu)\n\nMinun blokit -toimintoa käytetään, kun tehdään omia aliohjelmia tee blokki-painikkeella.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Minun blokit** käytetään, kun tehdään kutsuttavaa blokkijonoa kertaalleen niin, että sitä voi kutsua pääohjelmasta useamman kerran (kyseessä ns aliohjelma). \n\n**Minun blokki** tehdään **Tee blokki** -painikkeella.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Minun blokki** hattublokki eli aliohjelma voi sisältää useampia kutsuparametreja ja selventäviä tekstejä, numeerisia muuttujia , boolean muuttujia, joilla saa lisää toiminnallisuutta omalle aliohjelmablokille.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nJos haluat kutsua **Minun blokki** kutsualiohjelmaa, lisää kutsu pääohjelmaan ns trikkeriblokilla, joka kutsuu **Minun blokki** hattublokkia (aliohjelmaa). Kun **Minun blokki** hattublokkia kutsutaan pääohjelmassa, niin hattublokin alla olevat blokit suoritetaan kutsujan parametriarvoilla.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nLiitä tarvittavat aliohjelman suoritusblokit nippuun **Minun blokki** hattublokin alle määrittämään aliohjelman toiminnallisuus ja kutsuvaa triggeriblokkia **Minun blokki** käytetään pääohjelmassa.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Huom!: Jos teet useamman Minun blokki -aliohjelman, älä käytä samoja teksteja ja muuttujanimiä. Se aiheuttaa virheen ohjelmaa ladattessa robottiin***\n\n## Esimmerkki 1\n\nTässä esimerkissä käytetään **Minun blokki** hattublokkia:\n\n* Soita sireeniä 3 kertaa.\n* Aja eteenpäin 12 tuumaa.\n* Soita sireeniä 3 kertaa.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_call/sound_example.png)\n\n## Esimerkki 2\n\nTässä esimerkissä käytetään **Minun blokki** hattublokkia:\n\n* Aja eteenpäin 15 tuumaa.\n* Tulosta akun latausaste ja siirrä kursori seuraavalle riville aivojen näytöllä\n* Käännä robottia 180 astetta oikealle\n* Tulosta akun latausaste ja siirrä kursori seuraavalle riville aivojen näytöllä\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Minun blokki\n\nMinun blokit -toimintoa käytetään, kun tehdään omia aliohjelmaproseduureja painikkeella Tee blokki.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Miten toimii\n\n**Minun blokit** käytetään, kun tehdään kutsuttavaa blokkijonoa kertaalleen niin, että sitä voi kutsua pääohjelmasta useamman kerran (kyseessä ns aliohjelma). \n\n**Minun blokit** tehdään **Tee blokki** -painikkeella.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Minun blokki** hattublokki eli aliohjelma voi sisältää useampia kutsuparametreja ja käytöä selventäviä tekstejä, numeerisia muuttujia , boolean muuttujia, joilla saa lisää toiminnallisuutta omalle aliohjelmablokille.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nJos haluat kutsua **Minun blokki** aliohjelmaa, lisää kutsu pääohjelmaan ns trikkeriblokilla, joka kutsuu **Minun blokki** hattublokkia (aliohjelmaa). Kun **Minun blokki** hattublokkia kutsutaan pääohjelmassa, niin hattublokin alla olevat blokit suoritetaan kutsujan parametriarvoilla.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nLiitä tarvittavat aliohjelman suoritusblokit nippuun **Minun blokki** hattublokin alle määrittämään aliohjelman toiminnallisuus ja kutsuvaa triggeriblokkia **Minun blokki** käytetään pääohjelmassa.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Huom!Note: Jos teet useamman Minun blokki -aliohjelman, älä käytä samoja teksteja ja muuttujanimiä. Se aiheuttaa virheen ohjelmaa ladattessa robottiin***\n\n## Esimmerkki 1\n\nTässä esimerkissä käytetään **Minun blokki** hattublokkia:\n\n* Soita sireeniä 3 kertaa.\n* Aja eteenpäin 12 tuumaa.\n* Soita sireeniä 3 kertaa.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/sound_example.png)\n\n## Esimerkki 2\n\nTässä esimerkissä käytetään **Minun blokki** hattublokkia:\n\n* Aja eteenpäin 15 tuumaa.\n* Tulosta akun latausaste ja siirrä kursori seuraavalle riville aivojen näytöllä\n* Käännä robottia 180 astetta oikealle\n* Tulosta akun latausaste ja siirrä kursori seuraavalle riville aivojen näytöllä\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Satunnaisluku väliltä\n\n![random](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/random/random.png)\n\nRaportoi satunnaisluvun annetulta väliltä.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Satunnaisluku väliltä** blokkia voi käyttää ympyrämuotoisten blokkien arvojen paikalla. \n\n**Satunnaisluku väliltä** blokissa voi käyttää kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\nEsimerkissä **Satunnaisluku väliltä** blokkia käytetään arpomaan ajopelin nopeutta.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nTässä esimerkissä **Satunnaisluku väliltä** blokkia taas käytetään arpomaan odotusaikaa.\n\n![random_control](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"rate_of_gyro":{"name":"rate_of_gyro","markdown":"# Gyron nopeus\n\nRaportoi VEX IQ Gyron kulmanopeuden.\n\n![rate_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Gyron nopeus** raportoi arvot välillä **0 - 249.99 dps**.\n\n**Gyron nopeus** yksikkö on astetta sekunnissa (dps).\n\nValitse mitä gyroa käytetään.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\n**Gyron nopeus** blokin arvon voi sijoittaa muihin ympyrämuotoisten blokkien arvokenttään.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_inserted.png)"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Jakojäännös\n\nKun jaetaan luku toisella niin jakojöönnös kertoo sen luvun, joka ei mene tasan jaossa.\n\n![remainder](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Jakojäännös** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaaliluvut sekä numeeristen blokkien arvot.\n\nJos jako menee tasan, niin jakojäännös on 0.\n\n**Jakojäännös** blokki voidaan sijoittaa ympyrämuotoisen blokin arvon paikalla.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä luku 7 jaetaan luvulla 2 ja jakojäännös tulostetaan VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Toista kertaa\n\nToistoblokki joka toistaa sen sisällä olevat blokit syötetyn kertamäärän.\n\n![repeat](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAnna toistokertojen lukumäärä, montako kertaa **Toista kertaa** blokin sisällä olevat blokit toistetaan.\n \n**Toista kertaa** blokki hyväksyy kokonaisluvut ja numeerisen blokin arvot.\n\nToistoja voi laittaa toisensa sisään, jolloin niitä kutsutaan upotukseksi ja sillä voidaan saada suorituksen ajansäästöä ja erilaista ohjelman käyttäytymistä.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/repeat/repeat_select.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä soitetaan ääniefektiä 3 sekunnin ajan 5 kertaa peräkkäin.\n\n![repeat_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/repeat/repeat_example.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Toista kunnes\n\nToistoblokki suoritetaan niin kauan kunnes Boolean ehto saa arvon **tosi**.  \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Toista kunnes** blokki tutkii vain Boolean ehdon aina kierroksen alussa. \n\nJos Boolean ehto on **epätosi**, blokit kierroksen sisällä toistetaan niin monta kertaa kuin **Toista kunnes** pyörii.\n\nJos Boolean ehto on **tosi**, hypätään **Toista kunnes** blokin ohi suorittamaan seuraavaa blokkia ohjelmassa.\n\n**Toista kunnes** toistoblokin ehdoksi voi laittaa minkä tahansa kuusikulmaisen muodon ehdon.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan kellon aika VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle ja ajopeli liikkuu kunnes aivojen **check** painiketta on painettu. Heti kun painiketta painetaan, ajo päättyy.\n\n![repeat_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/repeat_until/repeat_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Nollaa kello\n\nNollaa VEX IQ aivojen kellon.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAivojen kello käynnistyy aina ohjelman suorituksen aloituksesta. **Nollaa kello** blokissa kello nollataan ohjelman suorituksen aikana.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä kello nollataan ennen kuin ajopeli ajaa 3 sekuntia. Sen jälkeen ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Gyro käännös asteina\n\nRaportoi VEX IQ Gyro sensorin nykyisen kääntymiskulman asteina.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation.png](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Gyro käännös asteina** raportoi **positiivinen** arvon kun Gyro Sensori on kääntynyt **vastapäivään**.\n**Gyro käännös asteina** raportoi **negatiivinen** arvon kun Gyro Sensori on kääntynyt **myötäpäivään**.\n\nValitse se gyroanturi, jota käytät\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_devices.png)\n\n**Gyro käännös asteina** blokin arvon voi sijoittaa pyöreisiin blokkikenttiin.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Pyöristys\n\npyöristää syöteluvun lähimpään kokonaislukuun.\n\n![round](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/round/round.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nDesimaalit 0.5 ja suuremmat **pyöristys** blokki pyöristää ylöspäin seuraavaan kokonaislukuun ja alle 0.5 **pyöristys** taas alaspäin.\n\n**Pyöristys** blokin arvo voidan sijoittaa pyöreämuotoisten alkioiden kenttään. \n\n**Pyöristys** blokkiin voi sijoittaa kokonais- ja desdimaalilukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä pyöristetään luku 2.7 tulostusblokin arvoksi ja se tulostuu  \"3\".\n\n![round_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Aseta 2d taulukon arvo\n\nAseta 2d taulukon alkioille arvot.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun luodaan 2d taulukko, voit määritellä **sarakkeet** määrän väliltä 1-10 alkiota ja rivien **rivit** määrän vastavasti 1-10 alkiota.\n\nValitse se taulukko, jota käsittelet. Samalla voit uudelleen nimetä tai poistaa taulukon.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\n**Aseta taulukon arvo** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Aseta luettelon arvoksi\n\nAsettaa arvot jokaiselle luettelon alkiolle.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuettelon alkioiden lukumäärä (1 - 10) määritellään, kun luettelo luodaan.\n\nValitse luettelo, jota käytätään. Samalla voi myös uudeleennimetä tai poistaa luettelon.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\n**Aseta luettelon arvoksi** blokissa voi käyttää kokonais-ja desimaalilukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\nTässä esimerkissä syötetään arvot (30,60,90,120) ja käytetään luettelon alkiota #3 (90) asettamamalla se Käsimoottorin kääntymiskulmaksi. \n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Aseta Boolean arvoon\n\nAntaa Boolean muuttujalle arvon.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse Boolean muuttujalle arvo, jota käytät. Voit myös uudelleen nimetä muuttujan tai poistaa sen. \n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nValitse Boolean muuttuja.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\n**Aseta boolean arvoon** blokki hyväksyy kuusikulmaisen muotoisia blokkeja.\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_color_sensor_brightness":{"name":"set_color_sensor_brightness","markdown":"# Aseta värisensorin valoisuus\n\nAsettaa VEX IQ Värisensorin lampun valoisuuden. \n\n![set_color_sensor_light](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_light.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nVärisensorissa on valonlähde, jonka voimakkuutta voi säätää havaitsemaan esinepintoja paremmin.\n\n**Set color sensor light** sallii arvovälin **0% - 100%**. Valovoima kasvaa prosenttilukuja kasvattamalla.\n\nValitse se värisensori, jota käytät.\n\n![set_color_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor.png)\n\n**Aseta värisensorin valoisuus** blokki sallii kokonaislukuja ja numeroblokkien arvoja.\n\n![set_color_sensor_2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_2.png)\n\n\n"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# Aseta kursori\n\nasettaa kursorin paikan näytöllä **tulosta** blokkia varten.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse rivi ja sarake **tulosta** komennolle VEX IQ Aivot näytöllä.\n\n**Aseta kursori** hyväksyy **rivi** väliltä **1 - 5**.\n\n**Aseta kursori** hyväksyy **sarake** väliltä **1 - 21**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_cursor/row_column_index.png)  \n\n**Aseta kursori** hyväksyy kokonaislukuja ja numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä näytön kursorin paikka on 3. rivi ja sarake 8, kun tulostetaan teksti \"Hello!\" aivojen näytölle.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_cursor/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_cursor/set_cursor_hello.png)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Aseta ajosuunta\n\nAsettaa ajopelin ajosuunnan arvon.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta ajosuunta** blokilla ajopelin ajosuunnaksi voidaan muuttaa mikä tahansa arvo kellotaulun mukaan kuvassa.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n**Aseta ajosuunta** hyväksyy arvoväliltä **0 - 360** astetta annetun arvon.\n\n**Aseta ajosuunta** blokki hyväksyy kokonais-ja numeerisia blokkien arvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli kääntyy yhteensä 135 astetta:\n\n![setDriveHeading_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_example_revised.png)\n\n- Käännyn ajosuunnasta arvoon 45 astetta.\n- aseta asjosuunta arvoon 0 astetta.\n- Käänny edelleen 90 astetta vasempaan edellisen ajosuunnan asetuksen 0 mukaisesti.\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Aseta kiertokulma arvoon\n\nAsettaa ajopelin kiertokulman, kun kiertyminen on määritelty VEX IQ Gyro -anturilla.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta kiertokulma arvoon** blokilla voi asettaa ajopelin kääntymiskulmalle joko positiivisen tai negatiivisen arvon.\n\n**Aseta kiertokulma arvoon** blokki hyväksyy sekä kokonais- että desimaalilukuja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä robotti kääntyy yhteensä 210 astetta:\n\n- Käänny vasemmalle (vastapäivään) 120 asetta.\n- Aseta robotin kääntymiskulma arvoon -45 astetta.\n- Käänny vasemmalle (vastapäivään) 90 astetta (nykyisestä arvosta -45 astetta arvoon +45 astetta edellisen asetuksen vuoksi).\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n"},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Aseta pysähdymistapa\n\nAsettaa ajopelin pysähtymistavan.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n* **Jarruta** pysäyttää ajopelin heti.\n* **Älä jarruta** pysäyttää ajopelin vaiheittain.\n* **Jarrut lukossa** lukitsee ajopelin jarrut ja pitää ajoneuvon paikallaan , kun sitä yrittää ulkoisesti liikuttaa.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin 3 sekuntia ja pysähtyy jarrrut lukossa.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Aseta ajoajan päättyminen\n\nAsettaa ajopelin liikkumiselle aikarajan.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAjopelin ajoajan päättyminen estää ohjelman väärän pysähtymisen tilanteissa että ajopelin ajo loppuun asti on estynyt.\n\nTällainen voi tapahtua esimerkiksi että ajopeli törmää seinään ja liikkuminen estyy.\n\n**Aseta ajoajan päättyminen** blokki voi sisältää kokonais- ja desimaaliluja sekä numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä ajo keskeytyy **aja** komennossa kun aikaa on kulunut 2 sekuntia ellei ajopeli ole siihen mennessä saavuttanut 24 tuuman ajomatkaa. Kummassakin tapauksessa ajopeli pääsee kääntymään seuraavalla **käänny** komennolla.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta ajonopeus\n\nasettaa ajopelin ajonopeuden.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta ajonopeus** asettaa ajopelin nopeuden muttei liikuta sitä. **Aja** blokki vaaditaan liikkumiseen.\n\n**Aseta ajonopeus**hyväksyy arvovälin **-100% - 100%** tai **-127rpm - 127rpm**.\n\nAsettamalla ajonopeudelle negatiivisen arvon aiheuttaa samalla ajopelin kulkusuunnan muuttumisen taaksepäin.\n\nAsettamalla ajonopeudelle arvon 0 aiheuttaa samalla ajopelin pysähtymisen.\n\n**Aseta ajonopeus** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaalilukua ja numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä ajopelille asetaan nopeus 50% matkan 12 tuuman matkalle.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Aseta ajosuunta\n\nAsettaa Gyron nykyisen ajosuunnan tilalle uuden arvon. \n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta ajosuunta** blokilla voi ajopelin ajosuunnan nykyistä arvoa muuttaa kellotaulun mukaiseen arvoon kuvan mukaan.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_gyro_heading/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\n**Aseta ajosuunta** hyväksyy arvot välillä **0 - 360** astetta.\n\n**Aseta ajosuunta** blokissa voi käyttää kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\nValitse haluttu gyro.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Aseta kiertokulma\n\nAsettaa VEX IQ Gyron kääntymiskulmalle arvon. \n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta kiertokulma** blokilla voi asettaa ajopelin kääntymiskulman haluttuun asentoon, positiivinen arvo vastapäiväarvoon tai negatiivisen kulman myötöpäiväasentoon.\n\n**Aseta kiertokulma** hyväksyy kokonaislukuja ja desimaalilukuja etumerkein.\n\nValitse gyro, jota haluat käsitellä.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation_devices.png)\n\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Vaihda alkio 2d taulukossa\n\nPäivittää 2d taulukossahalutun alkion.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAnna 2d taulukon rivi (1.arvo) ja sarake (2.arvo), jota haluat päiviittää\nValitse oikea 2d taulukko. Voit mös uudelleen nietä tai poistaa taulukon.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\n**Vaihda alkio** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja sekä numeerisia blokkiarvoja.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Vaihda luettelossa alkio\n\nKorvaa luettelon tai 2d Taulukon valitun alkion arvon uudella.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse luettelo, jota käsittelet. Voit myös uudelleen nimetä tai poistaa sen.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\n**Vaihda alkio** hyväksyy desimaali- jakokonaislukuja sekä numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n\nEsimerkissä alkio #2 luettelossa korvataan alkiolla 15 ja sitten alkion arvo tulostetaan VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle.\n\n![replace_item_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_item_of_array/replace_item_example.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Aseta moottori asentoon\n\nAsettaa VEX IQ Moottorin kierroslaskurille (encoder) uuden arvon.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta moottori asentoon** blokkia voi käyttää ja asettaa mikä tahansa arvo .\n\nTyypillisesti  **aseta moottori asentoon** blokilla nollataan kierroslaskuri kesken ohjelmaa.\n\nValitse haluamasi moottori.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nValitse yksikkö laskurille, asteet tai kierrokset.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Aseta moottorin pysähtymistapa\n\nAsettaa tavan, jolla moottori pysähtyminen määritellään.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n* **Jarruta** valinta aiheittaa moottorin pysähtymisen heti.\n* **Älä jarruta** valinta pysäyttää moottorin pikkuhiljaa.\n* **Jarrut lukossa** valinta aiheittaa moottorin pysähtymisen heti ja pitää sen tiukasti pysähtyneenä samassa asennossa muita voimia vastaan.\n\n**Aseta moottorin pysähtymistapa** on voimassa myös jatkossa, jos sitä ei muuteta myöhemmin.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytät.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nAseta moottorin pysähtymistapa.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä Käsimooottori pyörii eteenpäin 90 astetta ja pitää asennon esimerkiksi maan vetovoimaa vastaan samassa asennossa.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Aseta moottorin suoritusaika\n\nAsettaa aikarajan VEX IQ Älymoottorin liikkeelle.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMoottorin aikarajaa käytetään siihen, ettei ohjelman suoritus pääty, jos moottori ei saavuta tavoiteasentoa ja näin ollen estäisi ohjelman jatkumisen loppuun. Esimerkki, jossa moottori ei saavuta tavoiteasentoa voi olla käsi- tai kouramoottori , jotka saavuttavat mekaanisen liikerajan esteen ja astetavoite estyisi.\n\nAseta moottorin suoritusaika** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä moottorille on asetettu  **Aseta moottorin suoritusaika** komennolla 2 sekuntia saavuttaa asento 270 astetta. Joko aikaraja tai tavoite saavutetaan ja Kouramoottori liikkuu asentoon 0 astetta.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Aseta moottorin vääntövoima\n\nAsettaa VEX IQ Älymoottorin vääntökyvyn.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta moottorin vääntövoima** hyväksyy arvot välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytät.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\n**Aseta moottorin vääntövoima** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaaliluvut ja numeeriset blokkiarvot.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä Kouramoottoria pyöritetään asentoon 40 astetta vain 20 % vääntövoimalla. Valinta suojelee esinettä rikkoutumatta liian isolla voiman käytöllä.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta moottorin nopeus\n\nAsettaa VEX IQ älymoottorin nopeuden\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta moottorin nopeus** hyväksyy arvot väliltä **-100% - 100%** tai **-127rpm - 127rpm**.\n\nAsettamalla nopeuden miinusmerkkiseksi aiheuttaa moottorin pyörimisen taaksepäin.\n\nAsettamalla nopeuden arvoon 0 saa moottorin pysähtymään.\n\nValitse moottori, jota haluat käyttää.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nValitse nopeuden yksiköksi joko % tai kierrosta minuutissa (rpm).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä Käsimoottori pyörii hitaasti 25% nopeudella asentoon 90 astetta.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Aseta tulostuksen tarkkuus\n\nAseta desimaalien lukumäärä tulostuksessa VEX IQ Aivojen näytöllä.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nChoose the level of precision that inserted reporter blocks will be printed to the screen.\n\n* Kokonainen (1) (Oletus))\n* Kymmenysosat (0.1)\n* Sadasosat (0.01)\n* Tuhannesosat (0.001)\n* Kaikki desimaalit (0.000001)\n\nTulostuksessa pyöristetään aina lähimpään arvoon. Esimerkiksi 1.67 tulostetaan kokonaisena tarkkuudella arvoon 2 ja  1.7 kymmenesosa tarkkuudella.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_touchled_brightness":{"name":"set_touchled_brightness","markdown":"# Aseta KosketusLED valovoima\n\nAsettaa VEX IQ KosketusLED -laitteen valovoimakkuuden/valon kirkkauden.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta Touch LED valovoima** hyväksyy arvovälin **0% to 100%**.\n\nValitse, mitä KosketusLED -laitetta käytetään.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor3](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_sensor3.png)\n\n**Aseta Touch LED valovoima** blokki hyväksyy kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokin arvoja.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness2.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTämä esimerkki valaisee KosketusLED:ssä vihreää valoa valovoimalla/kirkkaudella 25%.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_touchled_color":{"name":"set_touchled_color","markdown":"# Aseta TouchLED väri\n\nasettaa VEX IQ KosketusLED :n värin. \n\n![set_touchLED_color](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse se **Touch LED**, jota käytetään.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_sensor.png)\n\nValitse väri,joka halutaan näkyvän ledissä.  \n\n![set_touchLED_color2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color2.png)\n\nVärit saa pois **Touch LED** laitteesta, kun valitsee väriksi **ei mitään**.\n\nVoit myös valita **Touch LED** väriksi sen värin nimen, jonka  värisensori tunnistaa.\n\n![set_touchLED_color3](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color3.png)"},"set_touchled_fade":{"name":"set_touchled_fade","markdown":"# Aseta kosketusledin värinvaihto\n\nasettaa kuinka nopeasti VEX IQ KosketusLED vaihtuu värien välillä.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse KosketusLed, jota käytät.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_sensor2.png)\n\nValitse nopeus värinvaihtoon.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_speed](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_speed.png)\n\n* Hidas - KosketusLed vaihtaa hitaasti väriä.\n* Nopea - KosketusLed vaihtaa nopeasti väriä.\n* Pois - KosketusLed vaihtaa heti väriä.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nKosketusLed vaihtaa hitaasti väriä siniseksi\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta kääntymisnopeus\n\nAsettaa ajopelin kääntymisnopeuden.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta kääntymisnopeus** asettaa vain nopeuden ajoneuvolle, muttei liituta sitä. **Käänny** blokki tarvitaan ajoneuvon liikkumiseen.\n\n**Aseta kääntymisnopeus** hyväksyy arvot väliltä **-100% - 100%** tai **-127rpm - 127rpm**.\n\nAsettamalla ajopelin kääntymisnopeuden negatiiviseksi se kääntyy vastakkaiseen suuntaan.\n\nAsettamalla kääntymisnopeudena arvoon 0 pysäyttää ajopelin.\n\n**Aseta kääntymisnopeus**blokin arvoina voi olla desimaali- ja kokonaisluvut sekä numeerisen blokin arvot.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä ajopeli kääntyy hitaasi 25 % nopeudella vasemmalle.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Aseta arvoon\n\nasettaa muuttujalle tietyn arvon.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse muuttuja, jota käytetään. Muuttujan voi myös nimetä uudelleen tai poistaa käytöstä. \n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\n**Aseta arvoon** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeerisen blokin arvon.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä VEX IQ Etäisyysanturin antama luku asetetaan \"my variable\" muuttujaan ja \"my variable\" muuttujaa käytetään ajopelin nopeuden määritykseen.\n\n![set_variable_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_variable/set_variable_example.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Merkitse Vision kohde indeksillä\n\nMerkitse Vision kohde indeksi havaitusta joukosta kohdeindeksejä.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**kohteiden lukumäärä** blokkia voi käyttää ennen **Merkitse Vision kohde indeksillä** blokkia selvittämään, montako kohdetta kamera löytää.\n\nValitse Vision -kamera, jota käytät.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\n**Merkitse Vision kohde indeksillä** blokki hyväksyy kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n\n\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Luettelon pituus\n\nkertoo luettelon alkioiden määrän.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\nValitse luettelo, jota käytät. Voit samalla uudelleennimetä tai poistaa luettelo.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\n**Luettelon pituus** raportoi alkioden lukumäärän.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# ota kuva\n\nottaa kuvan Vision -kameralla.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**ota kuva** blokki ottaa kuvan nykyhetkessä ja Vision kamera tulkitsee ja analysoi merkit/värikoodit kuvasta. \n\nAina **ota kuva** vaaditaan ensiksi ennen muiden Vision -kamera blokkien käyttöä.\n\nValitse Vision -kamera.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nValitse mitä merkkiä/värikoodia käytät. Merkit määritellään etukäteen Laite-ikkunassa.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Pyöritä\n\nVEX IQ älymoottori pyörii kunnes pyöriminen pysäytetään.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Pyöritä** blokki pyörittää moottoria ikuisesti kunnes uusi moottoriblokki käynnistyy tai pysäyttää pyörimisen.\n\nValitse haluttu moottori.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nValitse pyörimissuunta. Oletussuunta määritellään Laitteet -ikkunassa. \n\n![spin_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Pyöritä määrän\n\npyörittää moottoria tietyn määrän.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Kuinka käytetään\n\n**Pyöritä määrän** kertoo moottorille pyöriä tiettyyn suuntaan tietyn määrän alkuasennosta.\n\nValitse moottori.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nValitse moottorin pyörimissuunta. Oletussuunnat voi määritellä Laitteet -ikkunassa. \n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\n**Pyöritä määrän** voi sallia desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\nValitse yksiköksi joko asteita tai kierroksia.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nOletuksen muut blokit **odota** kunnes moottori on liikkunut loppuun.\n\nVoit vaihtaa option **ja älä odota**, jolloin seuraavat blokit suoritetaan samaan aikaan kun moottori pyörii.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Pyöritä asentoon\n\nPyörittää VEX IQ älymoottoria asentoon.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetääm\n\n**Pyöritä asentoon** määrää moottoria pyörivän tiettyyn asentoon.Asento perustuu nykyiseen moottorin pyörimisasentoon, **Pyöritä asentoon** määrää pyörimissuunnan.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\n**Pyöritä asentoon** blokki sallii desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeerisia blokkiarvoja.\n\nValitse pyörimisyksikkönä jokio asteet tai käännöslukumäärä.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nOletuksena seuraavat blokit odottavat **odota** kunnes moottori on pyörinyt asetetun määrän.\n\nVoit muuttaa oletuksen nuolesta **ja älä odota**, jolloin seuraavat blokit suoritetaan moottorin vielä pyöriessä.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Pysähdy\n\nPysäyttää ajopelin.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli pysäytetään 3 sekunnin kuluttua.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Pysäytä moottori\n\nPysäyttää moottorin.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse moottori, jonka haluat pysäyttää.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä kouramoottoria pyöritetään 3 sekuntia ennen pysäyttämistä.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Erotus\n\nVähennyslaskussa luku vähennetään toisesta ja lasketaan tekijöiden erotus.\n\n![subtract](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Erotus** hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n**erotus** blokin voi sijoittaa kaikkiin pyöreisiin arvokenttiin. \n\nKahden numeron vähennyslasku.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nKahden muuttujan vähennyslasku.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nSensoriarvon ja numeron vähennyslasku.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Kelloaika sekunteina\n\nRaportoi VEX IQ aivojen kellon sekunteina.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKello käynnistyy ohjelman alusta ajasta nolla sekuntia ja kulunut kellon aika raportoituu sekunteina.\n\n**Kelloaika sekunteina** arvoa käytetään eri blokkien pyöreissä arvokentissä.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin ja soittaa ääntä 4.5 sekuntia ennen 90 asteen käännöstä.\n\n![timerValue_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/timer_value/timerValue_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Käänny\n\nKääntää ajopeliä jatkuvasti.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Käänny** blokki kääntää ajopeliä kunnes uusi ajopeli -blokki tulee käyttöön tai ohjelman suoritus loppuu.\n\nValitse suunta, johon ajopeli kääntyy.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Käänny määrän\n\nKääntää ajopeliä tietyn määrän.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse suunta mihin ajopeli kääntyy.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\n**Käänny määrän** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeerisia blokinarvoja.\n\nAnna astemäärä, jonka ajopeli kääntyy.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nOletuksena muut blokit **odottaa** kunnes ajopeli on kääntynyt.\n\nVoit myös valita **ja älä odota**, jolloin seuraavat blokit suoritetaan samalla kun ajopeli kääntyy.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Käänny ajosuunnasta\n\nKääntää ajopelin tiettyyn suuntaan käyttäen VEX IQ Gyroa.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Käänny ajosuunnasta** blokkia voi käyttää kääntämään ajopelin kellotaulun mukaiseen asentoon (kuvassa).\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nPerustuu nykyisen gyron antamasta suunnasta , **Käänny ajosuunasta** päättelee, mihin suuntaan käännös tehdään.\n\n**Käänny ajosuunasta** hyväksyy arvoväliltä **0.00 - 359.99** asteita.\n\n**Käänny ajosuunnasta** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli tekee 4 käännöstä: \n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Vasemmalle (vastapäivään) kellotaulun kohtaan 45 astetta\n- Vasemmalle (vastapäivään) kellotaulun kohtaan 90 astetta\n- Vasemmalle (vastapäivään) kellotaulun kohtaan 270 astetta\n- Oikealle (myötäpäivään) kellotaulukohtaan 180 astetta\n\nOletuksena seuraavat blokit **odotaa** kunnes ajopeli on kääntynyt.\n\nVoit valita nuolivalinnasta **ja älä odota** , joka antaa seuraaville blokeilla ajoluvan ennen ajopelin käännöstä.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Käännä kiertokulmaa\n\nKääntää ajopeliä tiettyyn kulmaan lähtöasennosta käyttäen VEX IQ Gyroa.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Käännä kiertokulmaa** blokkia käytetään, kun halutaa kääntää ajopeliä tiettyyn asentoon lähtöasennosta joko vastapäivään positiivisilla arvoilla tai myötäpäivään negatiivisilla arvoilla.\n\nPerustuu nykyiselle **Ajosuunta asteina** ajopelin nykyisenä suuntana, **Käännä kiertokulmaa** määrittää suunnan etumerkillä.\n\n**Käännä kiertokulmaa** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokinarvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä ajopeli kääntyy 4 eri kertaa: \n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Vasemmalle(vastapäivään) kohtaan 90 astetta lähtöasennosta\n- Vasemmalle(vastapäivään) 180 astetta lähtöasennosta\n- Oikealle (myötäpäivään) -45 astetta lähtöasennosta\n- Vasemmalle (myötäpäivään) 0 asetta lähtöasennosta (alkuperäinen asento)\n\nOletuksena muut blokit noudattaa **odota** kunnes ajopeli on kääntynyt.\n\nVoit valita alasvetonuolesta **ja älä odota**, jolloin siirrytään heti seuraavaan blokkiin samaan aikaan kun ajopeli kääntyy.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Muuttuja\n\nRaportoi muuttujan arvon.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Muuttuja** blokkia käytetään tallentamaan muuttujan arvoja. Käytä **Aseta arvoon** -blokkia antamaan muuttujalle alkuarvo tai muuttamaan sen arvoa.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\n**Muuttuja** raportointiblokkia käytetään muiden blokkien pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nMuuttujat luodaan **Tee muuttuja**-painikkeella.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Moottorin nopeus\n\nAntaa VEX IQ Älymoottorin nopeuden.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottorin nopeus** antaa nopeuden arvoväliltä **-100% - 100%** tai **-127rpm - 127rpm**.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytät.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nValitse, millä yksiköllä nopeutta tarkastellaan nopeus % tai kierrosta minuutissa (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nRaportointiblokkia **Moottorin nopeus** käytetään eri blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa kentissä.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Vision kohde \n\nRaportoi tiedot Vision -kameran havaitsemasta kohteesta.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Vision kohde** blokin käytössä, suorita seuraavat vaiheet:\n\n1. Lisää ja määrittele Vision -kamera Laitteet -ikkunassa.\n2. **Ota kuva** Vision -kameralla ja tarkista kuvan merkki/värikoodi.\n3. Käytä **Vision kohde havaittu?** blokkia ja tarkista onko Vision -kamera löytänyt halutun merkin/ värikoodin.\n\nKun Vision -kamera havaitsee kohteen, voit käyttää muita Vision -blokkeja kertomaan tarkemmin kohteesta tietoja.\n\n* Käytä **merkitse vision kohde indeksillä** kohteesta, josta haluta lisätietoja. Oletuksena suurin kohde valitaan.\n* Käytä **kohteiden lukumäärä** kohteesta, jolla saat tietää, kuinka monta kysytyn merkin / värikoodin esinettä löytyy.\n* Käytä **vision kohde** kohteesta, jolla saat tiedot kohteen koosta ja sijainnista.\n\nValitse Vision -kamera,jota haluat käyttää.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nValitse mitä arvoa haluat Vision -kameran raportoivan:\n\n* Leveys - Kuinka leveä kohde on pixeleinä väliltä **2 - 316 px**.\n* Korkeus - Kuinka korkea kohde on pixeleinä väliltä **2 - 212 px**. \n* KeskipisteX - Raportoi kohteen X keskipisteen koordinaatin väliltä **0 - 315 px**.\n* KeskipisteY - Raportoi kohteen Y keskipisteen koordinaatin väliltä  **0 - 211 px**.\n* Kulma - Raportoi kohteen kulman väliltä **0 - 180 astetta**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nRaportointiblokkia **vision kohde** voi käyttää eri blokkien pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Odota\n\nOdota -komennolla voit määrätä ohjelman odottavan halutun sekuntimäärän ennenkuin siirrytään seuraavaan blokkiin.\n\n![wait](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse haluttu sekuntimäärä komentoon **Odota**.\n\n**Odota** blokiin voi kirjoittaa desimaali ja kokonaislukauja.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä ohjelmassa muutetaan VEX IQ PainoLED punaisesta väristä vihreään, kun **Odota** alusta on kulunut 3.25 sekuntia.\n\n![wait_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/wait/wait_example.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Odota kunnes\n\nOdottaa, että Boolean ehto toteutuu arvolla **tosi** ennenkuin siirrytään seuraavan blokin suoritukseen.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Odota kunnes** toistaa ja tarkistaa ehdon joka kierroksella Boolean -tarkistajalta ja siirtyy seuraavaan blokkiin vasta kun ehto on **tosi**.\n\n**Odota kunnes** Boolean ehto hyväksyy kuusikulmaisia blokkimuotoja.\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkkiohjelmassa PainoLED: n väriksi asetetaan keltainen ja kun PainoLED:ä painetaan *Painettu**, aivojen näytölle tulostuu \"Done!\".\n\n![wait_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/wait_until/wait_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"when_brain_button":{"name":"when_brain_button","markdown":"# Kun aivojen nappia on\n\nSuorittaa pinon komentoja, kun VEX IQ Aivojen tiettyä nappia on painettu tai vapautettu.\n\n![when_brain_button](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_brain_button/when_brain_button.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse aivojen nappi, jota käytät.\n\n![when_brain_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select.png)\n\nValitse toiminnot, jotka suoritetaan kun nappia **painettu** tai **vapautettu** \n\n![when_brain_button_select_2](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select_2.png)  \n"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Kun saan viestin\n\nSuorittaa ehtoblokin alla nipussa olevat blokit, kun valittu viesti **viesti1** on lähetetty.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse, mitä viestiä käytetään. Voit luoda myös uuden viestin.\n\n**Kun saan viestin** reagoi vain **lähetä viesti** or **lähetä viesti ja odota** blokkeihin eri komentonipuissa.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTämä esimerkki näyttää punaista VEX IQ PainoLED:ssä ja odottaa 2 sekuntia ennen kun lähettää viestin \"message1\". \n\nKun viesti on saatu, **Kun saan viestin** pino suorittaa toimenpiteet, joissa ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin ja Käsimoottori pyörii ylöspäin samanaikaisesti.\n\nKumpikin pino, kutsuva ja kutsuttu jatkavat samanaikaisesti suoritusta punaisten nuolien mukaisesti.\n\n\n![when_broadcast_example](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_example.png)\n\n"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Kun painokytkintä painettu\n\nSuorittaa halutun nipun blokkeja ehtoblokin alta, kun VEX IQ Painokytkintä on painettu tai vapautettu.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse Painokytkin, jota käytät.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nValitse ne toiminnot, jotka suoritetaan tapahtumista - **painettu** tai **vapautettu** \n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Kun ohjaintatin\n\nSuorittaa ehtoblokin alle niputetut blokit, kun VEX IQ Ohjaimen ao tattia on liikuteltu.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse Ohjaimen tatti, jota käytetään.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Kun ohjainnappia\n\nSuoriteen blokin alla nipussa olevat komennot kun valittua VEX IQ Ohjaimen nappia on painettu tai vapautettu.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse nappi, jota haluat käyttää.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_controller_button/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_controller_button/controller_button_back.png)\n\nValitse toiminnot, jotka napin painallus käynnistää tapahtumissa - **painettu** tai **vapautettu** \n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Kun käynnissä\n\nSuorittaa sen alla nipussa olevat blokit kun ohjelma käynnistyy.\n\n![when_started](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kun käynnissä** tapahtuma käynnistyy, kun VEX IQ Aivojen valikosta ko ohjelma valittu tai  **suorita ohjelma** painiketta on painettu VEXcode IQ Blocks -ohjelmassa.\n\nKaikkien uusien ohjemmien pitää automaattisesti sisältää **Kun käynnissä** blokki. Ohjelma voi sisältää korkeintaan kolme **Kun käynnissä** blokkeja."},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Kun kello > \n\nSuorittaa käynnistysehdolla olevat blokit, kun VEX IQ Aivojen kellonaika on suurempi kuin annettu aika sekunteina.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAivojen kello käynnistyy joka ohjelman alussa.\n\nValitse haluttu sekuntimäärä ehdon käynnistykseen.**Kun kello >** blokin alla olevat komennot suoritetaan, kun Aivojen kellon sekuntimäärä on suurempi kuin **Kun kello>** tapahtumaan annettu sekunttimäärä.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\n**Kun kello >** ehto hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaisluvut.\n\n**Kun kello >** ei hyväksy muita ehtoja."},"when_touchled":{"name":"when_touchled","markdown":"# Kun KosketusLED painettu\n\nSuoritetaan painalluksen ehtoon sidotut blokit, jos VEX IQ PainoLED -painiketta on painettu tai vapautettu.\n\n![when_touchLED](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_touchled/when_touchled.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse se PainoLED,jota haluat käyttää ehdossa.\n\n![when_touchLED_select](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_touchled/when_touchled_select.png)\n\nValitse se toiminto, joka suorittaa komennot ehdoista  **painettu** tai **vapautettu** \n\n![when_touchLED_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/when_touchled/when_touchled_condition.png)"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Kun\n\nEhtoblokki, joka toistaa sen sisällä olevat blokit, kun sen Boolean ehto on **tosi**.  \n\n![while](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/while/while.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kun** blokki tarkistaa Boolean ehdon joka toiston alussa. \n\nJos Boolean ehto on **tosi**,niin **Kun** silmukan sisällä olevat blokit suoritetaan.\n\nJos Boolean ehto on **epätosi**,niin hypätään **Kun** silmukan ohi seuraavaan komentoon.\n\n**Kun** toistoblokki hyväksyy ehdoksi kaikki kuusikulmaisen muotoiset ehtoblokit.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/fi/while/while_inserted.png)"}},"cpp":{"control_break":{"name":"control_break","markdown":"# Keskeytä\n\nHyvätään toistorakmneteen sisältä.\n\n```cpp\nbreak;\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun asetaa luupin sisälle `break` komennon, niin loopista tehdään hyppy pois exit heti. \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nesimerkissäe ajopeli liikkuu eteenpäin ja tutkitaan onko  VEX IQ aivojen Ylös-painiketta on painettu.\n\nHeti jos Ylös-painiketta on painettu poistutaan 'while' luupista ja ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n  if (Brain.buttonUp.pressing()) {\n    break;\n  }\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"control_break"},"control_for":{"name":"control_for","markdown":"# Toista\n\nToistetaan aaltosulkujen sisällä oleva koodi halutun kertamäärän.\n\n```cpp\nfor (initialization; condition; increment/decrement) {\n  // koodi, jota toistetaan\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAnna lukumäärä, joka toistetaan ehdossa **repeat** käyttäen kolmea parametria:\n\n* initialization (alkuarvo)\n* condition (ehto)\n* increment/decrement (askel)\n\n**Initialization** asetaa alkuarvon toistomuuttujalle.\n\n**Condition** asettaa ehdon, kuinka kauan koodia toistetaan. Toistetaan kunnes toistoehto toteutuu eli se saa arvon tosi **false**.\n\n**Increment/decrement** vaihtaa iterointimuuttujan askelarvoa loopin lopussa laskukaavalla.\n\n## Esimerkki 1\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan luvut välillä  0 arvoon 9 VEX IQ aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nfor (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"%d\", i);\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```\n## Esimerkki 2\n\nesimerkissä ajopeli ajaa ensin eteenpäin 10 tuumaa ja sitten kääntyy 60 astetta oikealle kolme kertaa peräkkäin. \n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 10.0, inches);\n\nfor (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n  Drivetrain.turnFor(right, 60, degrees);\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"control_for"},"control_if":{"name":"control_if","markdown":"# Jos\n\nIf -Koodin aaltosulkulauseen sisällä olevat komennot suoritetaan jos ehto on tosi. \n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n  // koodi suoritetaan jos ehto on tosi \n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**if-statement** tutkii ehtoa vain kerran.\n\nJos ehto on tosi **true**, aaltosulkujen sisällä oleva koodi suoritetaan.\n\nJos ehto on epätosi **false**, aaltosulkujen sisällä olevan koodin yli hypätään.\n\n```cpp\n// Stop Motor1 if BumperA is pressed\nif (BumperA.pressing()) {\n  Motor1.stop();\n}\n```","signature":"control_if"},"control_if_else":{"name":"control_if_else","markdown":"# Jos niin muuten\n\nOhjaislauseen ensimmäisen tai toisen aaltosulun sisällä olevat komennot suoritetaan riippuen ehdon Boolean arvosta.\n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n  // Koodi joka suoritettan tosi tilanteessa\n} else {\n  // Kood, joka suoritetaan epätosi tilanteessa\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nJos niin muuten -komento tutkii vain Boolean ehtoa kerran.\n\nJos Boolean `(condition)` ehto on tosi **true**, suoritetaan Jos -haara.\n\nJos Boolean `(condition)` ehto on epätosi **false**, suoritetaan Muuten -haara.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä VEX IQ KosketusLED loistaa vihreää, kun sitä on painettu, muuten se loistaa punaista kun sitä ei ole painettu.\n\nJos muuten -ehdon voi laittaa jatkuvaan toistorakenteeseen upotettuna nestedâ, jolloin ledilampun valoa voidaan muuttaa useamman kerran.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  if (TouchLED.pressing()) {\n    TouchLED.setColor(green);\n  } else {\n    TouchLED.setColor(red);\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"control_if_else"},"control_repeat":{"name":"control_repeat","markdown":"# Toista kertaa\n\nToistetaan ehdon sisällä aaltosuloussa olevat komennot suluissa oleva kertamäärä\n\n`repeat (number of times to repeat){code to repeat}`\n\n```\nrepeat (10) {\n\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**repeat-statement** toistaa aaltosuluissa olevat komenno normaalisuluissa olevan kertamäärän.\n\nEnsiksi aseta kertamäärä toistolle , se voi olla myös kokonaislukumuuttuja tai vastaava sensoriarvo.\n\nKoodipätkä alhaalla tulsotaa sanan \"iteration\" Aivojen näytölle 4 kertaa ja vaihtaa samalla riviä ennen seuraavaa kierrosta.\n\n```\nrepeat (4) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"iteration\");\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  wait(5, msec);\n}\n```\n\nHuomioi että **repeat-statement** sisällä olevasta koodista ei voi siirtyä toiseen toisto komentoon.","signature":"repeat(10) { }"},"control_wait":{"name":"control_wait","markdown":"# odota\n\nOdottaa asetetun ajan ennen kuin siirrytään seuraavaan komentoon.\n\n```cpp\nwait(time, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAsettaa ajan joko **seconds** (sekuntia) tai **msec** (millisekunttia), jonka ohjelman suoritus odottaa ennen seuraavan komennon suoritusta ohjelmassa.\n\n```cpp\nwait(10, seconds);\nwait(100, msec);\n```","signature":"wait(time, units);"},"control_waitUntil":{"name":"control_waitUntil","markdown":"# Odota kunnes\n\nToistaa koodisegmentin kunnes ehto **condition** antaa arvon tosi **true**.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (!condition) { \n  // Koodi toistetaan kunnes ehto toteutuu\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKontrollimkomentoa tutkitaaan jatkuvasti ja ei -ehto  **not** suorittaa koodia kunnes ehto tosi **true** pysäyttää aaltosulkujen sisällä olevankoodin suorituksen.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (!TouchLED.pressing()) {\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```\n\n## Esimerkki \n\nEsimerkissä asetetaan  KosketusLED väriksi keltainen ja odotetaan kunnes KosketusLediä kosketetaan ja sen jälkeen Ledin valo muutetaan vihreäksi.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(yellow);\n\nwhile (!TouchLED.pressing()) {\n  wait(1, seconds);\n}\n\nTouchLED.setColor(green);\n```","signature":"control_waitUntil"},"control_while":{"name":"control_while","markdown":"# Kun\n\nToistorakenne toistaa sen sisältämän koodin kun ehto **condition** on voimassa **true**.   \n\n```cpp\nwhile (condition) {\n  // Koodi suoritetaan toistuvasti kun ehto on voimassa\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n'Kun` toisto tutkii sen sisältämää ehtoa aina kierroksen alussa. \n\nJos ehto on totta **true**, silmukan sisällä oleva koodi suoritetaan.\n\nJo ehto on epätosi **false**, silmuikan yli hypätään suorittemaan seuraaavaa komentoa.\n\n`while` hyväksyy kaikki Boolean arvoiset esitykset, jotka antavat totuusarvot **true** tai **false** ehdossaan. Ehdot voivat olla myös vertailuoperaatioita tai mitä tahansa loogisia ehtolauseita.  \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin kun kello on käynyt alle 60 sekuntia.\n\nSen jälkeen ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n```cpp\nwhile(Brain.Timer.value() < 60) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"control_while"},"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain":{"name":"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain","markdown":"# kalibroi ajopelin gyro -sensori\n\nkalibroi ajopelin VEX IQ Gyro -sensorin.\n\n```cpp\ncalibrateDrivetrain();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKäytä `calibrateDrivetrain` komentoa ajon alussa kalibroimaan siihen liitetty Gyro -sensori.\n\n```cpp\nint main() {\n  // kalibroi Gyro -sensori ohjelman alussa\n  calibrateDrivetrain();\n\n  // Sitten vasta ajokomennot\n  Drivetrain.driveFor(forward, 500, mm);\n  Drivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n}\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä VEX IQ -ajopelin Gyro kalibroidaan ennen 200 mm eteenpäin ajoa ja kääntymistä ajosuuntaan 45 astetta.\n\n```cpp\ncalibrateDrivetrain();\n\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45, degrees);\n```","signature":"calibrateDrivetrain();"},"drivetrain_drive":{"name":"drivetrain_drive","markdown":"# Aja\n\nAjopeli liikkuu jatkuvasti (ikuisesti).\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(direction);\n```\n\nKaikki ajopelin ajomoottorit pyörivät eteen- tai taaksepäin nopeuden `Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity`-kommennon mukaisesti. Oletuksena on ilman asetusta 50 kierrosta minuutissa.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.drive` komennolla ajopeli liikkuu ikuisesti kunnes uusi ajopelikomento on asetettu tai ohjelma päättyy.\n\nValitse **forward** (eteenpäin) parametri ,jos haluat ajopelin ajavan eteenpäin.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n```\n\nValitse **reverse** (taaksepäin) parametri ,jos haluat ajopelin ajavan (peruuttavan) taaksepäin .\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(reverse);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.drive(forward);"},"drivetrain_drive_for":{"name":"drivetrain_drive_for","markdown":"# Aja matka\n\nLiikuttaa ajopeliä tietyn matkan. \n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(direction, distance, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse `direction` (suunta), johon ajopeli liikkuu - joko **forward** (eteenpäin) tai **reverse** (taaksepäin). \n\nAseta matka, jonka ajopeli liikkuu numeerisen arvona parametrissa `distance` (matka). \n\nValise 'units' yksiköksi joko **inches** (tuumaa) tai **mm**.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(reverse, 5, inches);\n```\n\n`Drivetrain.driveFor` oletuksena blokkaa seuraavien komentojen suorituksen matkan ajaksi.\n\n## Lisäparametrit\n\nVoit asetaa viimeiseksi parametriksi `false` (epätosi), jolloin `Drivetrain.driveFor` komento ei blokkaa seuraavien komentojen suoritusta matkan ajaksi.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.driveFor(forward, 1, inches);"},"drivetrain_set_drive_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Aseta kiertokulma\n\nAsettaa ajopelin Gyro -sensorin käännöskulman arvon.\n\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setRotation(value, rotationUnits);\n```\n\n## Mitennkäytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.setRotation()` komennolla ajopelin käännöskulmaksi voidaan asettaa mikä tahansa postivinen tai negatiivinen lukuarvo.\n\n`Drivetrain.setRotation()` komento hyväksyy kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia komentoja.\n\n`Drivetrain.setRoation()` komennolla **ei ole** rajoitusta välille 0-359 astetta.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä robotti kääntyy yhteensä 210 astetta:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(120, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n```\n\n- Käänny vasempaan (vastapäivään) 120 astetta.\n- Aseta nykyiseksi käännöskulmaksi -45 astetta.\n- Käänny vasempaan (vastapäivään) 90 astetta (-45 asteesta arvoon +45 astetta) edellisen komennon perusteella.","signature":"Drivetrain.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta ajopelin nopeus\n\nAsettaa ajopelin nopeuden, jota käytetään `Drivetrain.drive` ja `Drivetrain.driveFor` komennoissa. \n\nJos komentoa käytetään ajopelin ajon aikana, niin nopeus päivittyy uudeksi nopeudeksi kesken ajon.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity` asettaa ajopelin nopeuden, mutta ei liikuta sitä.\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity` hyväksyy arvot väliltä **-100 - 100**, kun käytetään yksikköä **percent** (prosenttia).\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity` hyväksyy arvot väliltä **-127 - 127**, kun käytetään yksikköä **rpm** (kierrosta minuutissa).\n\nJos ajopelin nopeudeksi asetetaan negatiivinen luku, ajopeli liikkuu taaksepäin oletuksesta.\n\nJos ajopelin nopeudeksi asetetaan nolla, ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n## Example\n\nEsimerkissä ajopelin nopeudeksi asetetaan 50 % ja ajetaan sillä matka 12 tuumaa.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(50, percent);\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 12.0, inches);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity(50, percent);"},"drivetrain_set_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_set_heading","markdown":"# Aseta ajosuunta\n\nAsettaa ajopelin Gyrolle ajosuunnan arvon.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setHeading(heading, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.setHeading` komennolla voidaan muuttaa ajopelin nykyinen ajosuunnan arvo. \n\n`Drivetrain.setHeading` hyväksyy arvot väliltä **0 - 359.99** `heading` (ajosuunta) parametrille.\n\n## Esimerkki \n\nEsimerkissä robotti kääntyy 135 astetta:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setHeading(0.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees);\n```\n- Käänny vasempaan ajosuuntaan 45 astetta\n- Aseta ajosuunnan arvoksi 0 astetta\n- Käänny vasemmalle lisää 90 astetta","signature":"Drivetrain.setHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_rotation","markdown":"# Aseta ajopelin kääntymiskulma\n\nAsettaa ajopelin kääntymiskulmalle uuden arvon VEX IQ Gyro Sensorissa.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.setRotation` komennolla voi ajopelin kääntymiskulmaa asettaa mihin postiiviseen tai negatiiviseen kääntymiskulmaan haluaa.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä robotti kääntyy 210 astetta:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(120, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n```\n\n- Käänny vasemmalle (vastapäivään) suuntaan 120 astetta.\n- Aseta robotin nykyinen kääntymiskulma arvoon -45 asetta.\n- Käänny vasemmalle (vastapäivään) lisää suuntaan 45 astetta (-45 degrees to +45 degrees).","signature":"Drivetrain.setHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_stopping":{"name":"drivetrain_set_stopping","markdown":"# Aseta pysähtymistapa\n\nAsettaa ajopelin pysähtymistavan.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setStopping(brakeType);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTässä pysähtymistavat `brakeType`parametrit, joita voi käyttää: \n\n* **brake** (jarruta) ajopeli pysähtyy heti , jos ulkopuolisia voimia ei esiinny\n* **coast** (hitaasti) antaa ajopelin pysähtyä vaiheittain\n* **hold** (lukitse) aiheuttaa ajopelin pysähtymisen ja asennon palautumisen pysähtymisasentoon , jos siihen vaikuttaa ulkoisia voimia\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin 3 sekuntia ja pysähtyy jarrujen lukituksella.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setStopping(hold);\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setStopping(brake);"},"drivetrain_set_timeout":{"name":"drivetrain_set_timeout","markdown":"# Aseta ajoajan päättyminen\n\nAsettaa ajopelin ajoajalle ylärajan, jos ajopeli ei saavuta muuten tavoite ajomatkaa.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.setTimeout` komentoa käytetään estämään tilanne, että ohjelma päättyy kesken suorituksen ajopelin liikkumisen esteen vuoksi.\n\nHyvä esimerkki ajopelin liikkumisen estymisestä on, että se törmää sivuseinään eikä pysty jatkamaan asetettua tavoitematkaa.\n\nAseta ajoajan päättyminen ajaksi voi asettaa yksiköksi `seconds` (sekuntia).\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(2.0, seconds);\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä `Drivetrain.driveFor` komento katkaisee liikkeen aika-arvoon 2 sekuntia ellei ajopeli ole ajanut tavoitematkaa 24 tuumaa. \n\nKun joko aikaraja tai matka 24 tuumaa on saavutettu, ajopeli kääntyy 90 astetta oikealla.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(2.0, seconds);\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 24.0, inches);\nDrivetrain.turnFor(right, 90.0, degrees);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setTimeout(1, seconds);"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta kääntymisnopeus\n\nAsettaa ajopelin kääntymisnopeuden. \n\nJos asetus tehdään kesken kääntymisen nopeus päivitetään ajon aikana.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTurnVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity` asettaa vain kääntyminopeuden ts se ei liiikuta ajopeliä. \n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity` hyväksyy arvot välillä **-100 - 100** kun yksikkönä on **percent** (prosenttia).\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity` hyväksyy arvot välillä **-127 - 127** kun yksikkönä on **rpm** (kierrosta minuutissa).\n\nAsettanmalla ajopelin kääntymisnopeudeksi negatiivisen arvon, ajopeli kääntyy vastakkaiseen suuntaan.\n\nJos kääntymiselle asettaa arvon 0 , se estää kääntymisen.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli kääntyy vasemmalle nopeudella 25% prosenttia.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTurnVelocity(25, percent);\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity(50, percent);"},"drivetrain_stop":{"name":"drivetrain_stop","markdown":"# Pysähdy\n\nPysäyttää ajopelin.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.stop` komento pysäyttää ajopelin.\n\nPysähtymistavan voi asettaa `Drivetrain.setStopping` komennolla.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä VEX IQ robotti liikkuu eteenpäin 3 sekuntia ja sen jälkeen pysähtyy.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.stop();"},"drivetrain_turn":{"name":"drivetrain_turn","markdown":"# Käänny\n\nKääntää ajopeliä.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(direction);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.turn` komento kääntää ajopeliä ikuisuuden kunnes uusi ajopelikomento suoritetaan tai ohjelma loppuu.\n\nKäytä **left** (vasemmalle) argumenttia, kun ajopeli kääntyy vasemmalle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n```\n\nKäytä **right** (oikealle) argument to turn the Drivetrain to the right.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(right);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turn(right);"},"drivetrain_turn_for":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_for","markdown":"# Käänny määrän\n\nKääntää ajopelin tietyn kulman haluttuun suuntaan.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(direction, angle, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAseta `direction` (suunta) ja määrä, jonka ajopeli kääntyy. Suuntavalinnat ovat **left** (vasempaan) tai **right** (oikeaan) ja määrä annetaan asteina.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(right, 270, degrees);\n```\n\n`Drivetrain.turnFor` komento blokkaa oletuksena muiden komentojen suorituksen käännöksen ajaksi.\n\n## Lisäparametrit\n\nVoit asettaa lisäparametriksi `false`, jos et halua että komento blokkaa oletuksena muiden komentojen suorituksen käännöksen aikana.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(left, 90, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnFor(right, 90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_turn_to_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Käänny ajosuuntaan\n\nKääntää ajopeliä tiettyyn ajosuuntaan VEX IQ Gyron avulla.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading(heading, degrees);`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading` komentoa voi käyttää, kun kääntää ajopeliä tiettyyn vastapäiväiseen ajosuuntaan kuten kuvassa.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/drivetrain_turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nPerustuu nykyiseen ajosuuntaan, komento `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` määrää mihin suuntaan käännytään.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading` hyväksyy arvot väliltä **0.00 - 359.99** ajosuunta parametriksi.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli tekee 4 kääntymistä: \n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(270.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(180.0, degrees);\n```\n\n- Vasemmalle (vastapäivään) arvoon 45 astetta\n- Vasemmalle (vastapäivään) arvoon 90 astetta\n- Vasemmalle (vastapäivään) arvoon 270 astetta\n- Oikealle (myötäpäivään) arvoon 180 astetta\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading` komento estää seuraavien komentojen suorituksen kunnes oma kääntyminen on tehty loppuun.\n\n## Lisäparametrit\n\nVoit asettaa lisäparametrin `false`, jolloin se estää `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` komennon seuraavien komentojen blokkaamisen kesken käännöksen.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnToHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Käännä kiertokulmaa\n\nKääntää ajopelin kiertokulmaa VEX IQ Gyro Sensorin avulla.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToRotation` komentoa voi käyttää kääntämään ajopeliä tiettyyn asentoon , positiiviseen (vastapäivään) tai negatiiviseen (myötäpäivään) arvoon.\n\nPerustuu ajopelin nykyiselle kääntymiskulmalle, `Drivetrain.turnToRotation` määrittää mihin suuntaan käännytään.\n\n`Kääntymis` parametri **ei** ole rajattu arvoihin välillä **0 - 359.99 astetta**. Käännös on absoluuttinen ja kääntää robottia useammin kuin kerran jos tarvis.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli tekee 4 käännöstä:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(90.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(180, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(0, degrees);\n```\n\n- Vasempaan (vastapäivään) kiertokulmaa 90 astetta\n- Vasempaan (vastapäivään) kiertokulmaa 180 astetta\n- Oikealle (myötäpäivään) kiertokulmaa -45 astetta\n- vasemmalle (vastapäivään) kiertokulmaa 0 astetta\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToRotation`komento blokkaa seuraavat komennot kunnes käännös on suoritettu.\n\n## Lisäparametrit\n\nVoi asettaa lisäparametrin arvon `false`, jolloin `Drivetrain.turnToRotation();` seuraava komento ei odota liikkeen loppumista.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(180.0, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnToRotation(90, degrees);"},"events_brain_button_pressed":{"name":"events_brain_button_pressed","markdown":"#  Aivojen painiketta painettu\n\nSuorittaa ns callback funktion kun VEX IQ Aivojen nappia on painettu.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Button.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nPitää luoda funktio , jota kutsutaan, kun Aivojen nappia on painettu.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button pressed.\");\n}\n```\n\n`Brain.Button.pressed` funktion voi kohdistaa VEX IQ Aivojen nappeihin.\n\n- `Brain.buttonUp.pressed(buttonPressed);` Ylös-nappi\n- `Brain.buttonDown.pressed(buttonPressed);`Alas -nappi\n- `Brain.buttonCheck.pressed(buttonPressed);`Check-nappi\n\n## Callback funktiot\n\nCallback -funktio on funktio, joka välitetään toiselle funktiolle argumenttina. **Callback funktion** koodi suoritetaan kun ko tapahtuma **event** sattuu. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Brain.Button.pressed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.buttonUp.pressed(callback);"},"events_brain_button_released":{"name":"events_brain_button_released","markdown":"# Aivojen painike vapautettu\n\nSuorittaa ns callback funktion, kun tiettyä VEX IQ Aivojen painike on vapautettu.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Button.released(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nPitää luoda funktio, joka kutsutaan, kun tietty Aivojen painike vapautettavan.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button released.\");\n}\n```\n\n`Brain.Button.released` funktiota voi käyttää eri VEX IQ Aivojen painikkeisiin.\n\n- `Brain.buttonUp.released(buttonReleased);` Ylös\n- `Brain.buttonDown.released(buttonReleased);` Alas\n- `Brain.buttonCheck.released(buttonReleased);`Check\n\n## Callback Funktiot\n\nCallback funktio on funktio, joka asetataan toisen funktion argumentiksi. **Callback funktion** koodi suoritetaan kun tapahtuma **event** sattuu. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Brain.Button.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.button.released();"},"events_brain_timer":{"name":"events_brain_timer","markdown":"# Kello tapahtuma\n\nTehdään callback joka suoritetaan tietyna jan kuluttua.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.event(callback, time);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nIQ Aivojen kello käynnistuu ohjelman alussa.\n\n`Brain.Timer.event` funktioon annetaan 2 parametria.\n\nEnsimmäinen on ns **callback funktio** parametri. Funtio pitää luoda/nimetä, jotta se voidan välittää `Brain.Timer.event` funktion parametrina.\n\nToinen parametri on aika. jolloin funktio suoritus alkaa. **Callback funkktion** koodi alkaa pyörimään heti kun **Brain Timer** aikamäärä on suurempi kuin parametrin arvo `time` yksikössä **millisekuntia**.\n\n```cpp\n// Call the callback function after 1000 milliseconds\nBrain.Timer.event(callback, 1000);\n```\n\n## Callback Funktiot\n\nCallback funktion on käyttäjän määrittämä funktio, joka välitetään argumenttina tosielle funktiolle. **Callback funktion** koodi suoritetaan kun ko tapahtuma **event** sattuu.\n\nEsimerkissä \"Callback Function Called\" teksti tulostetaan  VEX IQ's Aivojen näytölle 10 sekunnin kuluttua ohjelma alusta.\n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Brain.Timer.event(callbackFunction, 10000);\n}\n```","signature":"events_brain_timer"},"events_bumper_pressed":{"name":"events_bumper_pressed","markdown":"# Painokytkin painettu\n\nSuorittaa tietyn **callback funktion** (taustafunktion) kun painokytkintä on painettu.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuodaan funktio, jota kutsutaan, kun Painokytkintä on painettu. Anna funktiolle nimi, joka suoritetaan kun tapahtuma sattuu `callback` parametrissa.\n\n```cpp\nvoid bumperPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Bumper pressed.\");\n}\n```\nFunktion nimi välitetään `Bumper.pressed` funktiokutsun parametrina.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressed(bumperPressed);\n```\n\n## Callback Functions (Taustafunktiot)\n\nCallback funktio on funktio, joka välitetään toiselle funktiolle argumenttina. **Callback funktion** koodi suoritetaan kun tapahtuma **event** sattuu. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Bumper.pressed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"BUMPER.pressed(callback);"},"events_bumper_released":{"name":"events_bumper_released","markdown":"# Painokytkin vapautettu\n\nSuorittaa tietyn funktion kunn painaokytkin on vapautettu.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.released(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuiodaan funktio, jota kutsutaan kun Painokytkin on vapautettu. Anna funktiolle nimi joka annetaan `callback` (kutsu) parametrina.\n\n```cpp\nvoid bumperReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Bumper released.\");\n}\n```\nNimetty funktio välitetään `Bumper.released` funktion kutsussa parametrina.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.released(bumperReleased);\n```\n\n## Callback Funktiot\n\ncallback funktion on funktio, joka välitetään toiselle funktiolle parametrina . **callback function** suoritetaan kun ko tapahtuma **event** tapahtuu. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Bumper.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Bumper.released(callback);"},"events_controller_axis":{"name":"events_controller_axis","markdown":"# Ohjaimen tattia käännetty\n\nSuorittaa tietyn callback funktion, kun VEX IQ ohjaimen joystick tattia on liikutettu.\n\n```cpp\nController.Axis.changed(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuodaan oma ns callback funktio, jota kutsutaan kun ohjaintattia on liikutettu.\n\n```cpp\nvoid axisMoved() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Axis moved.\");\n}\n```\n\nvalise mätä ohjaintattia käytetään funktiossa\n\n- `Controller.AxisA.changed(axisMoved);` A-tappi\n- `Controller.AxisB.changed(axisMoved);` B-tatti\n- `Controller.AxisC.changed(axisMoved);` C-tatti\n- `Controller.AxisD.changed(axisMoved);` D-tappi\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/events_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n## Callback funktiot\n\nCallback funktio on funktionimi, joka välitetään toiselle funktiolle argumenttina. **Callback funktion** koodi suoritetaan kun ko tapahtuma **event** sattuu. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Controller.AxisA.changed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"`Controller.AxisA.changed(callback)`"},"events_controller_button_pressed":{"name":"events_controller_button_pressed","markdown":"# Ohjaimen nappia painettu\n\nSuorittaa ns **callback funktion**, kun VEX IQ Ohjaimen tiettyä nappia on painettu.\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuodaan oma **Callback funktio**, jota kutsutaan nimettynä parametrina tapahtumassa, kun Ohjaimen tiettyä painonappia on painettu.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button pressed.\");\n}\n```\n\nValitse mitä nappia käytetään painettu `pressed()` funktiossa.\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/events_controller_button_pressed/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonEUp.pressed(buttonPressed);` EYlä\n- `Controller.ButtonEDown.pressed(buttonPressed);` EAla\n- `Controller.ButtonFUp.pressed(buttonPressed);` FYlä\n- `Controller.ButtonFDown.pressed(buttonPressed);` FAla\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/events_controller_button_pressed/controller_button_back.png)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonLUp.pressed(buttonPressed);` LYlä\n- `Controller.ButtonLDown.pressed(buttonPressed);` LAla\n- `Controller.ButtonRUp.pressed(buttonPressed);` RYlä\n- `Controller.ButtonRDown.pressed(buttonPressed);` RAla","signature":"Controller.Button.pressed();"},"events_controller_button_released":{"name":"events_controller_button_released","markdown":"# Ohjaimen nappi vapautettu\n\nSuorittaa **callback funktion** kun VEX IQ Ohjainen nappi on vapautettu.\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.released(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nPitää luoda ns **callback funktio** ,jota kutsutaan kun Ohjaimen tietty nappi on vapautettu.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button released.\");\n}\n```\n\nValise minkä napin otat käyttöön, kun kutsut `released()` funktiota.\n\n- `Controller.ButtonEUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonEDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonFUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonFDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonLUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonLDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonRUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonRDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/events_controller_button_released/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/events_controller_button_released/controller_button_back.png)\n\n## Callback Funktiot\n\nCallback -funktio on funktio joka viedään toisen funktion argumentiksi. **Callback funktio** suoritetaan kun tapahtuma eli **event** sattuu. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Controller.ButtonRDown.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Controller.Button.released();"},"events_event":{"name":"events_event","markdown":"# Oma tapahtuma\n\nLuo uuden oman tapahtuman triggeröimään käyttäjän määrittämä oma funktio.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Event** tapahtumaobjektia käytetään kännistämään käyttäjän määrittelemä funktio. Jotta sitä voi käyttää, pitää, **event** tapahtumaobjekti luoda omalla nimellä. \n\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n```\nAina ei **Callback funktiota** tarvitse välittää luotuun tapahtumaan.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event();\n```\nUseita **callback functioita** voi liittää samaan tapahtumaan. Kaikki kutsutut funktiot suoritetaan yhtäaikaaa kun tapahtuma sattuu ja niitä kutsutaan.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event();\nmyEvent(callbackFunction1);\nmyEvent(callbackFunction1);\n```\nMutta vain **2 event callback funktiota** voidaan suorittaa samanaikaisesti. Isompi määrä **events callback funktioita** voivat vaikuttaa VEX IQ robotin toimintakykyyn.\n\nCallback funktio suoritetaan kun joko `myEvent.broadcast` tai `myEvent.broadcastAndWait` funktio suoritetaan.\n\n## Callback Funktiot\n\nCallback funktio on funktio, joka on välitetty toiselle funktiolle argumenttina. **Callback funktion** koodi suoritetaan kun haluttu **event** tapahtuma sattuu. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Luo uusi tapahtuma nimeltään myEvent pääfunktiossa ja välitä callbackFunction tapahtumana myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n\n  // Lähetä myEvent, trggeroimaan \"Function Called.\" jotta se tulostaa aivojen näytölle\n  myEvent.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"event myEvent = event(myEventCallback);"},"events_event_broadcast":{"name":"events_event_broadcast","markdown":"# Lähetä viesti\n\nLähettää viestin aktivoimaan tapahtumalla  **Event** toisen funktion.\n\n```cpp\nmyEvent.broadcast();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nPääohjelman koodi jatkuu heti kun komento `myEvent.broadcast` on lähetetty ts molemmat osat suoritetaan samaan aikaan.\n\nEnnenkuin komentoa voi käyttää, käyttäjämääritelty tapahtuma pitää luoda ja rekisteröidä ainakin yhteen callback-funktioon.\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast1() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\");\n}\n\nvoid runOnBroadcast2() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create an event in the main function\n  event myEvent = event();\n\n  // Register callback functions to event\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast1);\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast2);\n\n  // Broadcast the event\n  myEvent.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"EVENT.broadcast();"},"events_event_broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Lähetä viesti ja odota\n\nLähettää viestin aktivoimaan toivotun tapahtumafunktion tapahtuman **Event** , jolloin pääohjelma keskeytyy suorituksen ajaksi.\n\n```cpp\nmyEvent.broadcastAndWait();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`myEvent.broadcastAndWait` komento odottaa kaikkia viestejä, jotka kuuntelevat pyyntöä ennen jatkoa. Ja odota aiheuttaa pääohjelman seisahtumisen kunnes kutsutut funktiot on suoritettu loppuun.\n\nEnnen komennon käyttöä pitää tapahtuma luoda ja ainakin yksi callback-funktio rekisteröidä.\n\n## Callback funktiot\n\nCallback funktio on funktio, joka välitetään argumenttina toiseen funktioon. **Callback function** sisällä oleva koodi suoritetaan kun haluttu **event** tapahtuma sattuu. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Function Called.\");\n\n  wait(5, seconds);\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register a new event in the main function and pass the callbackFunction\n  event myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n\n  // Broadcast the event and wait for it to finish executing\n  myEvent.broadcastAndWait();\n\n  // This will not run until the callbackFunction has completed execution\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Done!\");\n}\n```","signature":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait"},"events_touch_led_pressed":{"name":"events_touch_led_pressed","markdown":"# KosketusLED painettu\n\nSuorittaa määrätyn **callback funktion** kun KosketusLED painiketta on painettu.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuodaan funktio, jota kutsutaan, kun KosketusLED painettu. Nimeä funktio, joka suoritetaan, kun haluttu tapahtuma 'event' sattuu ja anna se  `callback` parametrina.\n\n```cpp\nvoid touchLEDPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Touch LED pressed.\");\n}\n```\nThen, the function is passed as the parameter of the `TouchLED.pressed` function call.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.pressed(touchLEDPressed);\n```\n\n## Callback Funktiot\n\nCallback funktio on funktio, joka välitetään toiseen funktioon argumenttina. **Callback function** komennot suoritetaan kun **event** eli tapahtuma sattuu. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  TouchLED.pressed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"TouchLED.pressed(callback);"},"events_touch_led_released":{"name":"events_touch_led_released","markdown":"# KosketusLED vapautettu\n\nSuorittaa määrätyn **callback funktion**, kun KosketusLED on vapautettu.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.released(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nSinun pitää luoda nimetty kutsufunktio esim touchLEDReleased, joka suoritetaan kun ko tapahtuma sattuu\n\n```cpp\nvoid touchLEDReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Touch LED released.\");\n}\n```\nFunktion nimi välitetään parametrina valmiin `TouchLED.released` funktion kutsuparametrissa.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.released(touchLEDReleased);\n```\n\n## Callback Funktiot\n\ncallback funktio on funktio, jonka nimi välitetään argumenttina  **callback funktion** sisällä, kun tapahtuma **event** sattuu. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  TouchLED.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"TouchLED.released(callback);"},"function_name":{"name":"function_name","markdown":"# Funktiot\n\nFunktioiksi kutsutaan joukkoa komentoja , jotka voi suorittaan useampaan kertaan kutsuttaessa.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myFunction() {\n  // function code\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMäärittele funktio ja määritä datatyyppi, jonka funtio palauttaa.\n\n- `int` (kokonaisluku), `float` (liukuluku), `double` (desimaaliluku), ja `string` (merkkijoino) ovat datatyypit normaalisti. Jos funtio ei palauta mitään arvoa, määrittele se tyypiksi `void`. \n\nKannataa määritellä funktion nimi kuvaavaksi, mitä se tekee.\n\n```cpp\nint returnZero() {\n  return 0;\n}\n```\n\nKutsuparametrit *parameters* laitetaan sulkuihin `()`funtionimen jälkeen. Useampi parametri erotellaan pilkuilla (parameter1, parameter2).\n\nFunktion komennot laietaan aaltosulkuihin `{ }`.\n    \n## Esimerkki\n\nTämä fuktio ei palauta arvoa ts se on tyyppiä `void`. Se tulostaa \"The battery is low!\" VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle, kun akun varaustaso on alle 25%.\n\n```cpp\nvoid lowOnBattery() {\n  if (Brain.Battery.capacity(percent) < 25.0) {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"The battery is low!\");\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"function_name"},"function_thread":{"name":"function_thread","markdown":"# Ohjelmasäie\n\nAntaa suorittaa useamman komentosäikeen samaan aikaan rinnakkain.\n\n```cpp\nthread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nPitää määritellä funktio, jota suoritetaan ohjelmasäikeenä.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myThreadCallback() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"In a different thread!\");\n}\n```\nKun funtio on määritelty, voit käyttää sitä toisena rinnakkaisena säikeenä. Funktiota kutsutaan ns **callback function** eli kutsufuntioksi.\n\n```cpp\nthread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n```\n**thread** säie suoritetaan heti alussa samaan aikaan kuin pääohjelma (säie).\n\nVain **2 threads** säiettä kerrallaan vahva suositus. Lisäsäikeet voivat heikentää VEX IQ robotin suorituskykyä.\n    \n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä VEX IQ's aivoissa käytetään kahta kelloa yhtäaikaa eri säikeissä. Toisen tulostuksen hoitaa `myThread` säie. Toisen taas tulostaa pääohjelma main() säie yhtäaikaa.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myThreadCallback() {\n  int count = 0;\n  while(true) {\n    Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"thread1: %d\", count);\n    count++;\n    // Odota että pääsäie suoritetaan\n    wait(25, msec);\n  }\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Kun säie on luotu aloita suoritus\n  thread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n  \n  int count = 0;\n  while(true) {\n    Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"main: %d\", count);\n    count++;\n    // Odota että myThread suoritetaan\n    wait(25, msec);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"function_thread"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Tyhjennä rivi\n\nTyhjentää halutun rivin VEX IQ aivojen näytöltä.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine();\n```\n\nTyhjentää rivin 1  näytöllä.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine(1);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.clearLine` tarvitsee kokonaisluvun rivinumeroksi väliltä **1 - 5**, mikä rivi tyhjätään. \n\nJos rivinumeroa ei anneta, tyhjätään nykyinen rivi.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Esimerkki \nEsimerkissä tulostetaan \"Hello\" rivin 2 sarakkeeseen 1, odotetaan 3 sekuntia ja tyhjätään rivi 2.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");\nwait(3.0, seconds);\nBrain.Screen.clearLine(2);\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.clearLine();"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Tyhjää näyttö\n\nTyhjää koko VEX IQ Aivojen näytön.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearScreen();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.clearScreen` ei muuta kurssorin paikkaa näytöllä tyhjennyksen jälkeen. \n\nKäytä komentoa `Brain.Screen.setCursor` , jos haluat muuttuu kursorin paikkaa.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan \"Hello\", odotetaan sekunti ja putsataan koko näyttö ennen kuin tulostetaan \"Goodbye\".\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");\nwait(1.0, seconds);\nBrain.Screen.clearScreen();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Goodbye\");\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.clearScreen();"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Uusi rivi\n\nAsettaa tulostuksen kursorin rivin näytöllä seuraavalle riville.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOletuksena ohjelman alussa näytön kursori on rivillä 1 sarakkeessa 1. `Brain.Screen.newLine` komento siirtää kursoria näytön seuraavalle riville alaspäin.\n\n---\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_new_line/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan \"First Message\" ja siirretään kursori seuraavalle riville ja tulostetaan  \"Second Message\".\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"First Message\");\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Second Message\");\n```\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_new_line/set_cursor_welcome.png)","signature":"Brain.Screen.newLine();"},"looks_brain_screen_print":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print","markdown":"# Tulosta \n\nTulostaa numeroarvoja tai tekstiä Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.print` komento tulostaa dataa näytön kursorin kohdalle näytöllä.\n\nKaikki uudet ohjelmat tulostaa kohtaan rivi 1 sarake 1.\n\nTulosta tekstiä:\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"String: 123 + Words\");\n```\n\nTulosta kokonaisluku tai deimaalilukuja:\n```cpp\n// Kun tulostaa kokonaislukuja, käytetään \"%d\" formaattia\n// ensimmäisenä parametrina\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Integer: %d\", 5 + 10);\n\n// Kun tulostaa desimaalilukuja, käytetään \"%f\" formaattia\n// ensimmäisenä parametrina\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Decimal: %f\", 5.0 + 10.0);\n```\n\nTulosta sensoriarvo:\n```cpp\n// Kumpaa muotoa käytetään\n// Kokonaisluvulle käytä\"%f\" tai desimaaaliluvulle käytä \"%d\" formaattia\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%d\", Brain.Timer.time());\n\n// Boolean muuttujalle\n// käytä \"%s\" formaattia\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%s\", Motor.isDone() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");"},"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Aseta kursorin paikka\n\nAsettaa kursorin paikan `Brain.Screen.print` komennossa.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(row, col);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.setCursor` komento tarvitsee 2 parametria:\n\n* Parametri 1: Näytön rivinumero \n* Parametri 2: Näytön sarakenumero\n\nAseta rivi- ja sarakearvot `Brain.Screen.print` komennossa, kun haluat tulostaa tiettyy pisteeseen näytöllä.\n\nRivn arvot välillä **1 - 5**.\n\nSarakearvot välillä **1 - 21**.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä kursori(näytön osoitin) asetataan arvoon rivi 3 sarake 8 ennenkuin tulostetaan teksti \"Hello!\" Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(3, 8);\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hello!\");\n```\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/set_cursor_hello.png)","signature":"Brain.screen.setCursor(1, 1);"},"looks_color_set_light":{"name":"looks_color_set_light","markdown":"# Aseta Värisensorin valon voimakkuus.\n\nAsettaa VEX IQ Värisensorin valkoisen valon voimakkuuden. \n\n```cpp\nColor.setLight(brightness, percent);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nVäriSensoria voi käyttää taskulampun tavoin valolähteenä, kun se valaisee esineitä tai pintoja paremmin.\n\n`Color.setLight` hyväksyy parametrin arvovälin **0 - 100** valon voimakkuudelle.\n\nMitä isompi arvo, sitä kirkkaampi valo.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä Värisensorin valon voimakkuuss asetetaan arvoon 75 %.\n\n```cpp\nColor.setLight(75, percent);\n```","signature":"Color.setLight(50, percent);"},"looks_touch_led_set_brightness":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_brightness","markdown":"# Aseta KosketusLED valovoima\n\nAsttaa VEX IQ KosketusLED :n valovoiman (valon kirkkauden).\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setBrightness(brightness);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`TouchLED.setBrightness` hyväksyy arvot välillä **0 - 100** 'brightness` parametrille.\n\nKomennon ensimmäinen osa on laitteen nimiesiintymä. \n\n```cpp\nTouchLED1.setBrightness(100);\nTouchLED2.setBrightness(50);\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä KosketusLED :n vihreävalo loistaa kirkkausarvolla 25 %.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setBrightness(25);\nTouchLED.setColor(green);\n```","signature":"TouchLED.brightness();"},"looks_touch_led_set_color":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_color","markdown":"# Aseta KosketusLED väri\n\nAsettaa KosketusLED:n värin\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(color);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomennon ensimmäinen osa on laitteen nimi.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED1.setColor(red);\nTouchLED2.setColor(green);\n```\nValitse väri, jonka haluat LED :ssä näyttää.  \n\nVäri optiot:\n\n- `red` (punainen)\n- `green` (vihreä)\n- `blue` (sininen)\n- `white` (valkoinen)\n- `yellow` (keltainen)\n- `orange` (oranssi)\n- `purple` (purppura)\n- `red_violet` (punavioletti)\n- `violet` (violetti)\n- `blue_violet` (sinivioletti)\n- `blue_green` (sinivihreä)\n- `yellow_green` (keltavihreä)\n- `yellow_orange` (keltaoranssi)\n- `red_orange` (punaoranssi)\n\nJos haluat kääntää KosketusLED :n valon pois päältä, aseta väri arvoon **colorType::none**.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(colorType::none);\n```","signature":"touchLED.color();"},"looks_touch_led_set_fade":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_fade","markdown":"# Aseta KosketusLED värinvaihto\n\nAsettaa värinvaihdon nopeuden, kun VEX IQ KosketusLED vaihtaa väriä.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setFade(fade);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomennon ensimäinen osa on laitenimen valinta.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED1.setFade(fast);\nTouchLED2.setFade(slow);\n```\nValitse värinvaihdon nopeus:\n\n* **slow** - KosketusLED hitaasti vaihtaa toiseen väriin\n* **fast** - KosketusLED nopeasti vaihtaa toiseen väriin\n* **off** - KosketusLED heti vaihtaa toiseen väriin\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä vaihdetaan LED:n väriä hitaasti punaisesta siniseen.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(red);\nTouchLED.setFade(slow);\nTouchLED.setColor(blue);\n```","signature":"TouchLED.setFade(fade);"},"motion_motor_set_max_torque":{"name":"motion_motor_set_max_torque","markdown":"# Moottori Max vääntövoima\n\nAsettaa moottorin maksimi vääntövoiman.  \n\n```cpp\nMotor.setMaxTorque(value, percent);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.setMaxTorque` hyväksyy arvot välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\nKomennon ensimmäinen osa on moottorin nimi.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setMaxTorque(25, percent);\nArmMotor.setMaxTorque(75, percent);\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä kouramoottori ClawMotor pyörii asentoon 40 astetta vain 20% maksimi väännöllä. Tällöin säästytään turhalta voimankäytöltä ja puristukseltaa, kun esine otetaan kiinni kouraan.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setMaxTorque(20, percent);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(40, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setMaxTorque(50, percent);"},"motion_motor_set_position":{"name":"motion_motor_set_position","markdown":"# Moottori Aseta asentoon\n\nAsettaa VEX IQ Moottorin pyörimismitan encoder-arvon uudelleen haluttuun arvoon.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setPosition(position, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.setPosition` komennolla pyörimismitta/asento voidaan laittaa mihin haluttuun asentoarvoon tahansa kesken ohjelman.\n\nKomennon ensimmäinen osa on valittu moottori.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setPosition(0, degrees);\nArmMotor.setPosition(90, degrees);\n```\n\nTavallisesti `Motor.setPosition` komennossa nollataan pyörimisen asentomuisti.\n\nKomennossa voi käyttää `yksikkönä` joko **degrees** (asteita) tai **turns** (kierroksia).\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä kouramoottorin ClawMotor asennoksi (encoder) asetetaan 50 astetta.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setPosition(50, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setPosition(0, degrees);"},"motion_motor_set_stopping":{"name":"motion_motor_set_stopping","markdown":"# Moottori Aseta pysähtymistapa\n\nAsettaa tarkemmin miten VEX IQ Älymoottori pysähtyy.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setStopping(brakeType);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomennon ensimmäinen osa on nimetyn moottorin nimi.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setStopping(brake);\nArmMotor.setStopping(hold);\n```\n\nMäärittele moottorin pysähdystapa:\n\n- **brake** pysähtyy heti\n- **coast** pysähtyy hitaasti rullaten\n- **hold** pysähtyy heti (jarrut lukossa) ja jää asentoon, vaikka sitä yritetään ulkoisesti liikuttaa.\n\n`Motor.setStopping` vaikuttaa ohjelman jatkossa jokaisessa `Motor.stop` komennossa ellei sitä myöhemmin muuteta.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nKäsimoottori ArmMotor pyörii eteenpäin 90 astetta ja vastustaa lukkojarrutuksella muita voimia (maan vetovoima) ja pysyy lukitttuna loppuasennossa.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.setStopping(hold);\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 90, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setStopping(brake);"},"motion_motor_set_timeout":{"name":"motion_motor_set_timeout","markdown":"# Moottori Aseta suoritusaika\n\nAsettaaa moottorille suoritusajan katon, kuinka kauan se pyörii , jos se ei saavuta haluttua pyörimismäärää sitä ennen.  \n\n```cpp\nMotor.setTimeout(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.setTimeout` komentoa käytetään tilanteissa, että halutaan varmistua että ohjelma jatkuu seuraavalla komennolla vaikka pyörimiselle asetettua tavoitetta ei saavuteta. \n\nTällainen moottori on esimerkiksi koura- tai nostomoottori, jonka liikkeen voi pysäyttää robotin mekaniikan rakenne tai kouraan otettava esine.\n\nAikaraja annetaan yksikössä **seconds** (sekuntia).\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä `Motor.spinToPosition` komento rajaa pyörimisajan arvoon 2 sekuntia ellei kouramoottori nimeltään ClawMotor saavuta asentoa 270 astetta. \n\nSen jälkeen käsimoottori ArmMotor pyörii asentoon 90 astetta.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setTimeout(2, seconds);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(270, degrees);\nArmMotor.spinToPosition(90, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setTimeout(1, seconds);"},"motion_motor_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta Moottorin Nopeus\n\nAsettaa VEX IQ Älymoottorin nopeuden.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.setVelocity` hyväksyy arvot **-100% - 100%** tai **-127rpm - 127rpm**.\n\nJos antaa nopeudelle negatiivisen arvon, moottori pyörii oletetusta taaksepäin.\n\nJos asetaa nopeudella arvon 0 , moottori pysähtyy.\n\nKomennon ensimmäinen osa on halutun moottorin nimi.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setVelocity(25, percent);\nArmMotor.setVelocity(75, percent);\n```\n\nNopeuden yksikkö on joko **percent** (prosentti) tai **rpm** (kierrosta minuutissa).\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nKouramoottori ClawMotor pyörii asetettua nopeutta 25% asentoon 90 asetta.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setVelocity(25, percent);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(90, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setVelocity(50, percent);"},"motion_motor_spin":{"name":"motion_motor_spin","markdown":"# Pyöritä Moottoria\n\nPyörittää VEX IQ Älämoottoria haluttuun suuntaan (kunnes se pysäytetään).\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(direction);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.spin` komento pyörittää VEX IQ Älymoottora ikuisesti kunnes uusi moottorikomento on annettu tai ohjelman suoritus loppuu.\n\n- **forward** pyörittää moottoria eteenpäin\n- **reverse** pyörittää moottoria taaksepäin\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(forward);\nMotor.spin(reverse);\n```","signature":"Motor.spin(forward);"},"motion_motor_spin_for":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_for","markdown":"# Pyöritä moottoria määrän\n\nPyörittää VEX IQ Älymoottoria tietyn asetetun määrän yksiköitä.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinFor(direction, rotation, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.spinFor` pyörittää VEX IQ Älymoottoria asetettuun suuntaan asetetun määrän yksiköitä .\n\nMahdolliset argumentit:\n\n- `direction` (suunta) hyväksyy joko arvon **forward** (eteenpäin) tai arvon **reverse** (taaksepäin)\n- `rotation` (kierroksia) hyväksyy numeeerisen arvon\n- `units` (yksikkö) hyväksyy joko **degrees** (asteita) tai **turns** (kierroksia)\n\n`Motor.spinFor` estää muiden komentojen suorituksen kunnes sen liike on päättynyt.\n\n## Lisäparametrit\n\nVoit asettaa lisäparametrin `false` (epätosi) viimeiseksi parametriksi, jos haluet ettei `Motor.spinFor` komennon suoritus estä seuraavien komentojen suoritusta .\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinFor(reverse, 360, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Motor.spinFor(forward, 90, degrees);"},"motion_motor_spin_to_position":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_to_position","markdown":"# Pyöritä Moottori Asentoon\n\nPyörittää moottorin tiettyyn asentoon.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinToPosition(rotation, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.spinToPosition` pyörittää VEX IQ Älymoottorin tiettyy haluttuun asentoon nykyisestä asennosta, `Motor.spinToPosition` päättää mihin suuntaan pitää pyöriä.\n\n`Motor.spinToPosition` hyväksyy numeerisia arvoja pyörimiselle `rotation`.\n\nVoit valita pyörimisen yksiköksi jokoa **asteita** tai **kierroksia**. \n\n`Motor.spinToPosition` komento blokkaa muut komennot kunnes se on saavuttanut halutun asennon.\n\n## Parametrit\n\nVoit valita parametriarvon `epätosi` viimeiseksi arvoksi, jolloin 'Motor.spinToPosition` ei estä seuraavaa komentoa ennen kuin sen pyörimisliike on valmis.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinToPosition(360, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Motor.spinToPosition(90, degrees);"},"motion_motor_stop":{"name":"motion_motor_stop","markdown":"# Pysäytä Moottori\n\nPysäyttää moottorin.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.stop();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAlkuosa komentoa kertoo, mikä moottori on valittu.\n```cpp\nClawMotor.stop();\nArmMotor.stop();\n``` \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä Kouramoottori ClawMotor pysäytetään kun 3 sekuntia on kulunut eteenpäin pyörimisestä.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.spin(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nClawMotor.stop();\n```","signature":"Motor.stop();"},"sensing_brain_battery_capacity":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_capacity","markdown":"# Akun lataustaso\n\nRaportoi tämänhetkisen VEX IQ robotin akun lataustason.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Battery.capacity(percent)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Battery.capacity` palauttaa **kokonaisluku** arvona VEX IQ robotin akun lataustason yksikkönä `%` väliltä **0 - 100**.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä aivojen näytölle tulostetaan VEX IQ roobotin akun lataustaso, jos se on alle 25%.\n\n```cpp\nif (Brain.Battery.capacity(percent) < 25){\n  Brain.playSound(alarm);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Battery.capacity(percent)"},"sensing_brain_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_column","markdown":"# Aivojen Näytön sarake\n\nRaportoi näytön sarakenumeron, jolla kursori/osoitin on tällä hetkellä.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.column()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.column` raportoi sarakkeen arvoilla **1 - 21**.\n\n`Brain.Screen.column` arvo kasvaa näytöllä vasemmalta oikealle.","signature":"Brain.Screen.column()"},"sensing_brain_screen_pressing":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_pressing","markdown":"# Aivojen painiketta painettu\n\nRaportoi jos tiettyä VEX IQ aivojen painiketta on painettu.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Button.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nRaportoi arvon **tosi** jos tiettyä Aivojen painiketta on painettu ja arvon **epätosi** jos painiketta ei ole painettu.\n\n`Brain.` jälkeen pitää antaa painike, jota tarkastelaan. \n\nTuetut painikkeet ovat:\n- `Ylös`\n- `Alas`\n- `Tarkista`\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä VEX IQ robotti ajaa eteenpäin.\n\nKun aivojen **Alas** painiketta painetaan se kääntyy heti oikealle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  if (Brain.buttonUp.pressing()) {\n    Drivetrain.turn(right);\n    break;\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Button.pressing()"},"sensing_brain_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_row","markdown":"# Näytön Kursorin rivi\n\nRaportoi millä aivojen näytön rivillä kursori/osoitin tällä hetkellä on.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.row()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.row` raportoi kokonaislukuna väliltä  **1 - 5** kursorin rivin.\n\n`Brain.Screen.row` arvo kasvaa näytön ylhäältä alkaen.","signature":"sensing_brain_screen_row"},"sensing_brain_timer_reset":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_reset","markdown":"# Nollaa kello\n\nNollaa aivojen kellon.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.reset();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAivojen kello käynnistyy kun ohjelma alkaa.`Brain.Timer.reset` käytetään nollaamaan kello.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä kello nollataan ennen kuin ajopeli ajaa 3 sekuntia eteenpäin, jonka jälkeen ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.reset();\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  if (Brain.Timer.value() > 3) {\n    break;\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"sensing_brain_timer_reset"},"sensing_brain_timer_value":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_value","markdown":"# Kello\n\nRaportoi VEX IQ Aivojen kellon ajankulun sekunteina.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.value()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAivojen kello lähtee liikkeelle arvosta 0, kun ohjelma käynnistyy ja palauttaa arvon desimaalilukuna (*double*).\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostaan aivojen kellon aika.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Timer: %.2f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n  \n  // Pieni odotus estää päällekkäisen tulostuksen sotkun\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"sensing_brain_timer_value"},"sensing_bumper_pressing":{"name":"sensing_bumper_pressing","markdown":"# Painokytkintä Painettu\n\nRaportoi, onko painokytkintä painettu.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Bumper.pressing` raportoi arvon **tosi**, kun painokytkintä on painettu.\n\n`Bumper.pressing` raportoi arvon **epätosi**, kun painokytkintä ei ole painettu.\n\nKomennon ensimmäinen osa on nimetty painokytkin.\n\n```cpp\nBumper2.pressing()\nBumper4.pressing()\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä aivojen näytölle tulostetaan, onko painokytkintä painettu ai ei.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Bumper Pressed: %s\", Bumper2.pressing() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Pieno odotus, ettei tulostu sotkua\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Bumper.pressing()"},"sensing_color_brightness":{"name":"sensing_color_brightness","markdown":"# Värin valovoima %\n\nRaportoi värisensorin havaitseman värin valovoiman/kirkkauden.\n\n```cpp\nColor.brightness()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Color.brightness` raportoi arvot väliltä **0% - 100%**.\n\nKomennon ensimmäinen osa on nimetty värisensori.\n\n```cpp\nColor2.brightness()\nColor4.brightness()\n```\n\nMitä enemmän valoa sitä suurempi arvo, mitä himmeämpi valo sitä pienempi arvo.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan värisensorin havaitseman valon kirkkaus/valovoima.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Brightness: %d\", Color.brightness());\n```","signature":"Color.brightness()"},"sensing_color_colorname":{"name":"sensing_color_colorname","markdown":"# Värin nimi\n\nraportoi värin nimen jonka VEX IQ Värisensori havaitsee.\n\n```cpp\nColor.colorname()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Color.colorname` raportoi yhden seuraavista väreistä: \n\n- `red` (punainen)\n- `green` (vihreä)\n- `blue` (sininen)\n- `white` (valkoinen)\n- `yellow` (keltainen)\n- `orange` (oranssi)\n- `purple` (purppura)\n- `red_violet` (punavioletti)\n- `violet` (violetti)\n- `blue_violet` (sinivioletti)\n- `blue_green` (sinivihreä)\n- `yellow_green` (keltavihreä)\n- `yellow_orange` (keltaoranssi)\n- `red_orange` (punaoranssi)\n\nKomennon ensimmäinen osa on nimetty värisensori. \n\n```cpp\nColor4.colorname()\nColor5.colorname()\n```","signature":"Color9.colorname()"},"sensing_color_detect":{"name":"sensing_color_detect","markdown":"# Värisensori havaitsee tietyn värin?\n\nRaportoi värin nimen, jonka värisensori havaitsee.\n\n```cpp\nColor.detects(color)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nRaportoi arvon **tosi** kun värisensori havaitsee tietyn värin ja  **epätosi** kun ao väriä ei havaita.\n\nKomennon alku on nimetty värisensori.\n\n```cpp\nColor1.detects(red)\nColor2.detects(blue)\n```\n\nValitse väri, jonka värisensori havaitsee.\n\n- `punainen`\n- `oranssi`\n- `keltainen`\n- `vihreä`\n- `sininen`\n- `punavioletti`\n- `violetti`\n- `puna-violetti`\n- `sini_violetti`\n- `sini-vihreä`\n- `kelta-vihreä`\n- `kelta-oranssi`\n- `puna-oranssi`\n- `valkoinen`\n\nVoit myös valita **colorType::none** jos värisensori **ei** havaitse esinettä.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTTässä esimerkissä tulostetaan joko \"Color Red\" , jos värisensori havaitsee punaisen esineen tai \"Other Color\" jos punaista ei havaita.\n\n```cpp\nif (Color.detects(red)) { \n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Color Red\");\n} else {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Other Color\");\n}\n```","signature":"Color.detects(color)"},"sensing_color_hue":{"name":"sensing_color_hue","markdown":"# Värisävy\n\nRaportoi VEX IQ värisensorin havaitseman esineen värisävyn.\n\n```cpp\nColor.hue()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Color.hue` raportoi värisävyn arvon välillä **0** - **360** astetta VEX värispetrillä.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä Aivojen näytölle tulostetaan havaittu värisävyn numeroarvo.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hue: %.0f\", Color.hue());\n```","signature":"Color.hue()"},"sensing_color_isNearObject":{"name":"sensing_color_isNearObject","markdown":"# Värisensori Havaitsee värin?\n\nRaportoi näkeekö Värisensori esineen tai pinnan värin. \n\n```cpp\nColor.isNearObject()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nEnsimmäinen osa komentoa on nimetty värisensori.\n\n```cpp\nColor5.isNearObject()\nColor7.isNearObject()\n```\n\nAntaa arvon **tosi**, jos värisensori havaitsee esineen tai pinnan värin edessään. \n\nAntaa arvon **epätosi**, jos värisensori ei havaitse esineen tai pinnan väriä edessään. \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTulostetaan Aivojen näytölle, näkeekö nimetty värisensori väriesineen edessään.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Is Near Object: %s\", Color.isNearObject() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"Color.isNearObject()"},"sensing_controller_axis_position":{"name":"sensing_controller_axis_position","markdown":"# Ohjain Tatin Asento\n\nRaportoi valitun ohjaimen tatin asennon akselillaan.\n\n```cpp\nController.Axis.position()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Controller.Axis.position` antaa arvot välillä **-100 - 100**.\n\n`Controller.Axis.position` antaa arvon **0**, kun tatin asento on keskellä.\n\nValitse tatti, jota seurataan.\n\n* `AxisA` - vasen tatti (ylös ja alas)\n* `AxisB` - vasen tatti vasempaan ja oikeaan)\n* `AxisC` - oikea tatti vasempaan ja oikeaan)\n* `AxisD` - oikea tatti (ylös ja alas)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan Aivojen näytölle ohjaimen tatin A (AxisA) arvo.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"AxisA Position: %.0f\", Controller.AxisA.position());\n\n  // Pieni odotus,ette näytölle tulostu sotkua\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\n```","signature":"Controller.Axis.position()"},"sensing_controller_button_pressing":{"name":"sensing_controller_button_pressing","markdown":"# Ohjain Nappia painettu\n\nRaportoi, onko tiettyä ohjainnappia painettu.\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValise ohjaimen nimetty nappi, jota seurataan.\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/sensing_controller_button_pressing/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonEUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonEDown.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonFUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonFDown.pressing()`\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/sensing_controller_button_pressing/controller_button_back.png)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonLUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonLDown.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonRUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonRDown.pressing()`\n\n`Controller.Button.pressing()` raportoi arvon **tosi** jos nimettyä ohjainnappia on painettu.\n\nController.Button.pressing()` raportoi arvon **epätosi** jos nimettyä ohjainnappia ei ole painettu.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli liikkuu eteenpäin. Jos ohjaimen nappia E Ylös on painettu , robotti pysähtyy.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  if (Controller.ButtonEUp.pressing()) {\n    Drivetrain.stop();\n    break;\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\n```","signature":"Controller.Button.pressing()"},"sensing_distance_distance":{"name":"sensing_distance_distance","markdown":"# Etäisyysanturi etäisyys esineestä\n\nRaportoi lähimmän esineen ja etäisyysanturin välisen välimatkan.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.distance(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Distance.distance` raportoi välimatkat väliltä **24mm - 1000mm** tai **1 tuumaa - 40 tuumaa**.\n\nEnsimmäinen osa komentoa on nimetty etäisyysanturi.\n\n```cpp\nDistance6.distance(mm)\nDistance8.distance(inches)\n```\n\nValitse yksikkö, jolla välimatka `Distance.distance` mitataan:  **tuuma** tai **mm**. \n\n```cpp\nDistance6.distance(mm)\nDistance8.distance(inches)\n```","signature":"Distance.distance(units)"},"sensing_distance_found_object":{"name":"sensing_distance_found_object","markdown":"# Etäisyysanturi havaitsi esineen\n\nRaportoi tiedon, havaitseeko VEX IQ Etäisyysanturi esineen näkökentässään. \n\n```cpp\nDistance.foundObject()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAntaa arvon **tosi**, jos se havaitsee esineen tai esinepinnan näkökentässään. \n\nAntaa arvon **epätosi**, jos se ei havaitse esinettä tai esinepintaa näkökentässään.\n\nEnsinmmäisessä osassa annetaan nimetty etäisyysanturi, jota käytetään.\n\n```cpp\nDistance3.foundObject()\nDistance4.foundObject()\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan tieto aivojen näytölle, havaitseeko anturi esineen  tulostusarvoilla Ei tai Kyllä.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Found Object: %s\", Distance.foundObject() ? \"Ei\" : \"Kyllä\");\n```","signature":"Distance.foundObject()"},"sensing_drivetrain_current":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_current","markdown":"# Ajopelin sähkövirta\n\nRaportoi ajopelin virrankulutuksen tällä hetkellä.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.current(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.current` palauttaa desimaalilukuarvon (*double*) , kun raportoidaan ajopelin tämänhetkistä virrankulutusta.\n\n`Drivetrain.current` palauttaa valitun `yksikkö` mukaisen arvon.\n\nValittavaissa on yksiköt **amp** (ampeerit) or **prosentti**.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan ajopelin asähkövirta yksikössä amp (ampeeri) VEX IQ robotin aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.current(amp));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.current(units)"},"sensing_drivetrain_heading":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_heading","markdown":"# Ajopelin kulkusuunta\n\nRaportoi ajopelin kulkusuunnan.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.heading(degrees)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.heading` raportoi kulkusuunnan arvon välillä **0.00 - 359.99 astetta**.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan ajopelin kulkusuunta VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain Heading: %.2f\", Drivetrain.heading(degrees));\n\n  // Pieni odotus, ettei tulostu sotkua\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.heading(degrees)"},"sensing_drivetrain_isDone":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_isDone","markdown":"# Ajo on suoritettu?\n\nRaportoi onko ajopeli suorittanut liikkeen loppuun.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.isDone()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.isDone` raportoi arvon **tosi** kun ajopelin moottorit on suorittaneet ajon loppuun.\n\n`Drivetrain.isDone` raportoi arvon **epätosi** kun ajopelin moottorit eivät liiku.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan tieto, liikkuuko ajopelivielä vai ei, VEX IQ aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 1000, mm, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain is Done: %s\", Drivetrain.isDone() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.isDone()"},"sensing_drivetrain_isMoving":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_isMoving","markdown":"# Ajopeli liikkuu?\n\nRaportoi jos ajopeli liikkuu tällä hetkellä.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.isMoving()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento palauttaa arvon **tosi** jos ajopeli liikkuu vielä komentojen `Drivetrain.driveFor` tai `Drivetrain.turnFor` mukaan, joissa on annettu tietty matka tai astemäärä.\n\nKomento palauttaa arvon **epätosi** jos ajopelin liike on loppunut.\n\n**Huomio:** Komento antaa aina **epätosi** jos käytetään jatkuvia komentoja `Drivetrain.drive` tai `Drivetrain.turn` (ne *ei* määrittele ajolle tarkkaa matkaa tai kulmaa).\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan tieto, liikkuuko ajopeli, VEX IQ aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 1000, mm, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain is Moving: %s\", Drivetrain.isMoving() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.isMoving()"},"sensing_drivetrain_rotation":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_rotation","markdown":"# Ajopelin Käännös asteina\n\nRaportoi ajopelin kääntymiskulman asteina\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.rotation(degrees)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.rotation` raportoi kasvavan kulman arvon, jos ajopeli kääntyy **vastapäivään**.\n\n`Drivetrain.rotation` raportoi pienenevän kulman arvon, jos ajopeli kääntyy **myötäpäivään**.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan ajopelin kääntymiskulma VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain Rotation: %.2f\", Drivetrain.rotation(degrees));\n\n  // Pieni odotus ettei tulostu sotkua\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.rotation(degrees)"},"sensing_drivetrain_velocity":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_velocity","markdown":"# Ajopelin Nopeus\n\nRaportoi ajopelin nykyisen nopeuden.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n`Drivetrain.velocity` palauttaa desimaaliluvun (*double*), kun se raportoi ajopelin nykyisen nopeuden. \n\n`Drivetrain.velocity` palauttaa arvon väliltä **-100% - 100%**, jos yksikkönä käytetään prosenttia **percent**.\n\n`Drivetrain.velocity` yksikkönä voi olla myös **rpm** (kierrosta per minuutti).\n\nNegatiiviset lukuarvot tarkoittavat, että ajopeli liikkuu taaksepäin.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan ajopelin nopeus (prosentteina) VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.velocity(percent));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.velocity(units)"},"sensing_gyro_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_calibrate","markdown":"# Gyro Kalibrointi\n\nKaliprointi vähentää Gyro Sensorin virheheiluntaa.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.calibrate(calibrationType);\n```\n\nHeiluntaa tapahtuu, kun Gyro Sensori virheellisesti havaitsee liikkumista vaikka sensori on levossa.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nGyro Sensorin pitää olla levossa kalibroinnin aikana.\n\n`calibrationType` parametrit voivat mitä tahansa seuraavista:\n- **calNormal** 2 sekunnin kalibrointi\n- **calSlow** 4 sekunnin kalibrointi\n- **calExtended** 8 sekunnin kalibrointi","signature":"Gyro.calibrate(calibrationType);"},"sensing_gyro_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Gyro Ajosuunta\n\nRaportoi Gyro Sensorin nykyisen ajosuunnan asteina.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.heading()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Gyro.heading` komento antaa kasvavia arvoja kun käännytään **vastapäivään**.\n\n`Gyro.heading` antaa arvoja välillä **0.00 to 359.99**.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan Gyro Sensorin ajosuunta VEX IQ aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Gyro Heading: %.2f\", Gyro.heading());\n\n  // Brief delay to prevent print distortion or tearing\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Gyro.heading()"},"sensing_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Gyro Nopeus\n\nRaportoi VEX IQ Gyro sensorin kulmanopeuden.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.rate()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetääm\n\n`Gyro.rate` antaa arvon väliltä **0 to 249.99** yksikkönä astetta per sekunti (DPS).","signature":"Gyro.rate()"},"sensing_gyro_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Gyron kiertokulma asteina\n\nAntaa VEX IQ Gyro Sensorin mnykyisen asennon asteina.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.rotation()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Gyro.rotation` raportoi kasvavia arvoja kun Gyro Sensori kääntyy **counter-clockwise** vastapäivään.\n\n`Gyro.rotation` raportoi pieneneviä arvoja kun Gyro Sensori kääntyy **clockwise** myötäpäivään.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan Gyro Sensorin arvo VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Gyro Rotation: %.2f\", Gyro.rotation());\n\n  // Odotus ettei tule päällekkäistulostusta tai sotkua\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Gyro.rotation()"},"sensing_gyro_setHeading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_setHeading","markdown":"# Gyro Aseta Ajosuunta\n\nAsettaa Gyro Sensorin nykyisenajosuunnan tiettyyn arvoon. \n\n```cpp\nGyro.setHeading(heading, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Gyro.setHeading` komentoa voi käyttää asettamaan nykyisen ajosuunnan arvoon välillä **0** - **359.99**. \n\nYleensä tätä käytetään asettamaan ajosuunta ohjelman keskellä arvoon 0.\n\n`Gyro.setHeading` hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nAlla esimerkissä laitetaan Gyro Sensorin uusi ajosuunta arvoon 0 astetta.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"Gyro.setHeading(heading, degrees);"},"sensing_gyro_setRotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_setRotation","markdown":"# Gyro Aseta kiertokulma\n\nAsettaa VEX IQ Gyro sensorin kiertokulmalle tietyn arvon. \n\n```cpp\nGyro.setRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Gyro.setRotation` komentoa voi käyttää, kun haluaa asettaa ajopelin kääntymiskulman tiettyyn positiiviseen (vastapäivään kierto) tai negatiiviseen (myötäpäivään kierto) arvoon.\n\n`Gyro.setRotation` hyväksyy positiiviset ja negatiiviset desimaali- ja kokonaisluvut.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä Gyron kiertokulma asetetaan arvoon -45 astetta.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setRotation(-45, degrees);\n```","signature":"Gyro.setRotation(rotation, degrees);"},"sensing_motor_current":{"name":"sensing_motor_current","markdown":"# Moottorin sähkövirta\n\nraportoi määrän, jota VEX IQ älymoottori kuluttaa sähköä tällä hetkellä.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.current(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.current` palauttaa desimaaliluvun (muoto *double*) ja antaa sähkövirran kulutustiedon, jota moottori tällä hetkellä kuluttaa.\n\n`Motor.current` komento hyväkyy sekä **amp** (Ampeeria) or **percent** as a valid `units` parameter.\n\nTulostetaan sähkövirta prosentteina:\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\" , Motor.current(percent));\n```\n\nTulostetaan sähkövirta ampeereina:\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.current(amp));\n```","signature":"Motor.current(units)"},"sensing_motor_isDone":{"name":"sensing_motor_isDone","markdown":"# Mooottori on pysähtynyt?\n\nraportoi onko moottori suorittanut loppuun liikkeensä.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.isDone()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.isDone` antaa arvon **tosi**, kun tietty moottori on pysähtynyt.\n\n`Motor.isDone` antaa arvon **epätosi**, kun tietty moottori ei ole suorittanut liikettä loppuun.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetan aivojen näytölle tiedot, onko käsimoottori suorittanut pyörimisen loppuun.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 270, degrees, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"ArmMotor is Done: %s\", ArmMotor.isDone() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Pieni odotus, ettei tulostus aiheuta sotkua\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Motor.isDone()"},"sensing_motor_isSpinning":{"name":"sensing_motor_isSpinning","markdown":"# Moottori Pyörii\n\nRaportoi, pyöriikö valittu moottori.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.isSpinning()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento antaa arvon **tosi**, jos valittu moottori pyörii tällä hetkellä.\n\nKomento antaa arvon **epätosi**, jos valittu moottori ei pyöri tällä hetkellä.\n\n**Huomio:** Komento antaa aina arvon 'epätosi', jos moottorin pyörimiseen on annettu pelkkä `Motor.spin` -komento ilman matkaa tai astemäärää.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan vastaus VEX IQ aivojen näytölle, pyöriikö Käsimoottori.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 270, degrees, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"ArmMotor is Spinning: %s\", ArmMotor.isSpinning() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Pieni odotus ettei tulostus aiheuta sotkua\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Motor.isSpinning()"},"sensing_motor_position":{"name":"sensing_motor_position","markdown":"# Moottorin asento \n\nAntaa tämän hetkisen VEX IQ älymoottorin kierroslaskimen/encoderin pyörimisarvon.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.position(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.position` palauttaa moottorin tämänhetkisen pyörimismäärän desimaalilukuna (*double*).\n\nValitse 'yksikkö` parametriarvoksi joko **asteita** tai **kierroksia**.\n\nArvot voivat olla **asteita**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Motor Position (Degrees): %.2f\", Motor.position(degrees));\n```\n\nArvot voivat olla kierroksia **turns**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Motor Position (Turns): %.2f\", Motor.position(turns));\n```","signature":"Motor.position(units)"},"sensing_motor_velocity":{"name":"sensing_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Moottorin Nopeus\n\nRaportoi valitun VEX IQ älymoottorin nopeuden.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.velocity` palauttaa desimaalilukuna (muodossa *desimaali*) tämänhetkisen moottorin nopeuden. \n\nMäärittele `yksikkö`, kun komentoa käytetään.\n\n**%** - palauttaa nopeuden arvon välillä **-100% - 100%**.\n \n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.velocity(percent));\n```\n  \n`Motor.velocity` voi palauttaa myös arvon **rpm** (kierrosta minuutissa).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.velocity(rpm));\n```","signature":"Motor.velocity(units)"},"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled":{"name":"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled","markdown":"# Ohjain Käytössä/Poissa käytöstä\n\n```cpp\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = false;\n```\n\nOttaa käyttöön tai poistaa Laitteet -ikkunassa Ohjain-määritellyt painikkeet.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse joko käytössä tai pois käytöstä Ohjain-määritellyt painonapit ja tatit. Arvo onjoko `tosi` tai `epätosi`. Oletuksena Ohjain on aina käytössä.  \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä on Laitteeet -ikkunassa ajopelin ohjaukseen tehdyt Ohjain-määritykset.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/cpp/fi/sensing_remote_control_code_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nOhjelmassa tehdyt Ohjain-määritykset otetaan pois kun ohjelma alkaa. \n\nSen jälkeen robotti ajaa 6 tuumaa eteenpäin.\n\nLopussa ohjain on taas **Ohjain käytössä** -komento määritelty ja tulee voimaan ja ajopeliä voi ohjata ohjaimella.\n\n```cpp\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = false;\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 6.0, inches);\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = true;\n```","signature":"RemoteControlCodeEnabled = true;"},"sensing_touchled_pressing":{"name":"sensing_touchled_pressing","markdown":"# KosketusLED Painettu\n\nRaportoi, jos VEX IQ KosketusLED nappia on painettu.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAntaa arvon **tosi**, jos valittua KosketusLED on painettu ja arvon **epätosi**, jos lediä ei ole painettu.\n\nEnsimmäinen osa komentoa on valittu laite-esiintymä. \n\n```cpp\nTouchLED2.pressing()\nTouchLED4.pressing()\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä KosketusLED valo muutetaan arvoon **punainen**. Heti kun KosketusLediä painetaan, väri muutetaan arvoon **vihreä**.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(red);\n\nwhile (!TouchLED.pressing()) {\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nTouchLED.setColor(green);\n```","signature":"TouchLED.pressing()"},"sensing_vision_largestObject":{"name":"sensing_vision_largestObject","markdown":"# Vision Suurin Kohde\n\nPalauttaa Kameran kuvasta havaituista kohteista suurimman kohteen tiedot.\n\n```cpp\nVision.largestObject\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOta kuva `Vision.takeSnapshot` ennenkuin voit käyttää suurimman kohteen tietoja `Vision.largestObject` komennolla.\n\n`Vision.largestObject` suurimman kohteen komento on luokkatyyppiä `vision::object`.\n\n```cpp\n// Ota kuva merkillä COLOR_SIG \nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"X: %d\", Vision.largestObject.centerX);\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Y: %d\", Vision.largestObject.centerY);\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\n`Vision.largestObject` on luokkatyyppiä `vision::object` , jolla on seuraavat ominaisuudet.\n\n- `id`      - Kohteen yksikäsitteinen ID numero , on tyyppiä `int`\n- `originX` - Kohten vasen yläkulma X -akselilla, on tyyppiä `int`\n- `originY` - kohteen vasen yläkulma Y -akselilla, on tyyppiä `int`\n- `centerX` - Kohteen Keskipiste X-akselilla on tyyppiä `int`\n- `centerY` - Kohteen keskipiste Y -akselilla on tyyppiä `int`\n- `width`   - Kohteen leveys on tyyyppiä `int`\n- `height`  - Kohteen korkeus on tyyppiä `int`\n- `angle`   - Kohteen muodostama kulma kameraan on tyyppiä `double`\n- `exists`  - Jos kohde löytyy on tyyppiä `bool`","signature":"Vision.largestObject"},"sensing_vision_objectCount":{"name":"sensing_vision_objectCount","markdown":"# Vision Kohteiden lukumäärä\n\nraportoi monta haettua kohdetta Vision -kamera havaitsee kuvassa. \n\n```cpp\nVision.objectCount\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMäärittele Vision -kamera käyttöön Laitteet-ikkunassa\n\nMäärittele merkit/värikoodit Kameran määritysikkunassa. \n\nOta kuva `Vision.takeSnapshot` halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla .\n\n`Vision.objectCount` antaa viimeisimmästä kuvasta havaittujen kohteiden lukumäärän.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan aivojen näytölle viimeisimmän kuvan havaittujen kohteiden lukumäärä.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n\n  // Ota kuva merkillä SIGNATURE\n  Vision.takeSnapshot(SIGNATURE);\n\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Number of Objects Detected: %d\", Vision.objectCount);\n\n  // Ota kuva joka 20 millisekuntia\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Vision.objectCount"},"sensing_vision_objects":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects","markdown":"# Vision Kohteet\n\nAntaa taulukon kaikista Vision -kameran havaitsemista haetuista kohteisa.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAina ensimmäisenä pitää ottaa kuva `Vision.takeSnapshot` ennen komentoa `Vision.objects` taulukkoa.\n\n`Vision.objects` on taulukko, jossa on kuvasta kaikkien havaittujen kohteiden tiedot.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\nvision::object firstObject = Vision.objects[0];\n```\nKuvataulukkoa voi käyttää normaalin taulukon tavoin hyödyntämällä taulukon indeksejä.\n\n```cpp\nvision::object visionObject = Vision.objects[0];\n```\n\nVoit sijoittaa sen alkioita myös toistorakenteisiin esimerkiksi **Toista** komennossa `Vision.objectCount` arvoa voi käyttäää ehdoissa.\n\nEsimerkkiohjelmasssa alla ominaisuudet `keskipisteX` and `keskipisteY` arvot tulostetaan Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\n\nfor(int i = 0; i < Vision.objectCount; i++) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"X: %d\", Vision.objects[i].centerX);\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Y: %d\", Vision.objects[i].centerY);\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n}\n```\n\n`Vision.objects` kohteet on luokkatyyppiä `vision::object` ja sillä on nämä ominaisuudet.\n\n- `id`      - Kohteen yksikäsitteinen ID numero , on tyyppiä `int`\n- `originX` - Kohten vasen yläkulma X -akselilla, on tyyppiä `int`\n- `originY` - kohteen vasen yläkulma Y -akselilla, on tyyppiä `int`\n- `centerX` - Kohteen Keskipiste X-akselilla on tyyppiä `int`\n- `centerY` - Kohteen keskipiste Y -akselilla on tyyppiä `int`\n- `width`   - Kohteen leveys on tyyyppiä `int`\n- `height`  - Kohteen korkeus on tyyppiä `int`\n- `angle`   - Kohteen muodostama kulma kameraan on tyyppiä `double`\n- `exists`  - Jos kohde löytyy on tyyppiä `bool`","signature":"Vision.objects"},"sensing_vision_objects_angle":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_angle","markdown":"# Kohteen kulma\n\nRaportoi Vision -kameran havaitseman kohteen muodostaman kulman.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].angle\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTee järjestyksessä seuraavat toimenpideaskeleet, kun käytät `Vision.objects[index]` komentoa:\n\n1. Määrittele Vision -kamerasi Laitteet - ja Kameran määritysikkunassa.\n2. Käytä `Vision.takeSnapshot()` ottamaan kuvan ja etsimään siitä nimettyä merkkiä/värikoodia.\n3. Käytä `Vision.objects[index].exists` tarkistamaan että halutun kohteen merkki/värikoodi löytyy kuvassa. \n\nKun kohde löytyy, niin voit käyttää muita Vision -komentoja selvittämään tarkempia tietoja kohteeta. \n\n* Käytä **indeksi** muuttujaa kiinnittämään kohde, josta haluat tarkempaa tietoa. Suurinesinekohde on aina edessä, jolloin se on  `Vision.objects[0]`.\n* Käytä `Vision.objectCount` määrittämään motako samanlaista kohdetta löytyy halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla.\n* Sitten voit käyttää muita ominaisuuksia: `kulma`, `keskipisteX`, `keskipisteY`, `korkeus`, `leveys` ja `on olemassa`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].angle` raportoi esineen kamerakulman arvolla **0 - 180 degrees**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.screen.print(MyVision.objects[0].angle);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].angle"},"sensing_vision_objects_centerx":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_centerx","markdown":"# Kohteen keskipisteX\n\nAntaa Vision -kameran kuvan löytämän kohteen x -akselin keskipisteen.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].centerX\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTee järjestyksessä seuraavat toimenpideaskeleet, kun käytät `Vision.objects[index]` komentoa:\n\n1. Määrittele Vision -kamerasi Laitteet - ja Kameran määritysikkunassa.\n2. Käytä `Vision.takeSnapshot()` ottamaan kuvan ja etsimään siitä nimettyä merkkiä/värikoodia.\n3. Käytä `Vision.objects[index].exists` tarkistamaan että halutun kohteen merkki/värikoodi löytyy kuvassa. \n\nKun kohde öytyy, niin voit käyttää muita Vision -komentoja selvittämään tarkempia tietoja kohteeta. \n\n* Käytä **indeksi** muuttujaa kiinnittämään kohde, josta haluat tarkempaa tietoa. Suurinesinekohde on aina edessä, jolloin se on  `Vision.objects[0]`.\n* Käytä `Vision.objectCount` määrittämään motako samanlaista kohdetta löytyy halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla.\n* Sitten voit käyttää muita ominaisuuksia: `kulma`, `keskipisteX`, `keskipisteY`, `korkeus`, `leveys` ja `on olemassa`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].centerX` raportoi löydetyn kohteen keskipisteen X koordinaatin arvolla **0 - 315 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[1].centerX);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].centerX"},"sensing_vision_objects_centery":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_centery","markdown":"# Kohteen KeskipisteY\n\nAntaaa y-akselilla Vision -kameran havaitseman kohteen keskipisteen.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].centerY\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTee järjestyksessä seuraavat toimenpideaskeleet, kun käytät `Vision.objects[index]` komentoa:\n\n1. Määrittele Vision -kamerasi Laitteet - ja Kameran määritysikkunassa.\n2. Käytä `Vision.takeSnapshot()` ottamaan kuvan ja etsimään siitä nimettyä merkkiä/värikoodia.\n3. Käytä `Vision.objects[index].exists` tarkistamaan että halutun kohteen merkki/värikoodi löytyy kuvassa. \n\nKun kohde öytyy, niin voit käyttää muita Vision -komentoja selvittämään tarkempia tietoja kohteeta. \n\n* Käytä **indeksi** muuttujaa kiinnittämään kohde, josta haluat tarkempaa tietoa. Suurinesinekohde on aina edessä, jolloin se on  `Vision.objects[0]`.\n* Käytä `Vision.objectCount` määrittämään motako samanlaista kohdetta löytyy halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla.\n* Sitten voit käyttää muita ominaisuuksia: `kulma`, `keskipisteX`, `keskipisteY`, `korkeus`, `leveys` ja `on olemassa`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].centerY` raportoi Y -akselin kohteen keskipisteen arvolla **0 - 211 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[2].centerY);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].centerY"},"sensing_vision_objects_exists":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_exists","markdown":"# Kohde löytyy\n\nRaportoi jos Vision -kamera näkee kuvassa sille määritellyn kohteeen. \n\nKohde pitää aina määritellä ennen kuin `Vision.objects[index].exists` komentoa voi käyttää etsimään kohdetta.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].exists\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTee tarkemmat kohteen määrityksen enne kuin voit käyttää tätä komentoa. \n\n\n`Vision.objects[index].exists` antaa arvon **tosi** kun Vision -kamera havaitsee kohteen merkin/värikoodin.\n\n`Vision.objects[index].exists` antaa arvon **epätosi** kun Vision -kamera ei havaitse kohteen merkiä/värikoodia.\n\nAina enne analysointia pitää ottaa kuva ts suorittaa `Vision.takeSnapshot()` -komento.\n\n\n```cpp\nif(Vision.objects[0].exists){\n\n}\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].exists;"},"sensing_vision_objects_height":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_height","markdown":"# Kohde korkeus\n\nAataa Vision -kameran havaitun kohteen korkeuden.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].height\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTee järjestyksessä seuraavat toimenpideaskeleet, kun käytät `Vision.objects[index]` komentoa:\n\n1. Määrittele Vision -kamerasi Laitteet - ja Kameran määritysikkunassa.\n2. Käytä `Vision.takeSnapshot()` ottamaan kuvan ja etsimään siitä nimettyä merkkiä/värikoodia.\n3. Käytä `Vision.objects[index].exists` tarkistamaan että halutun kohteen merkki/värikoodi löytyy kuvassa. \n\nKun kohde öytyy, niin voit käyttää muita Vision -komentoja selvittämään tarkempia tietoja kohteeta. \n\n* Käytä **indeksi** muuttujaa kiinnittämään kohde, josta haluat tarkempaa tietoa. Suurinesinekohde on aina edessä, jolloin se on  `Vision.objects[0]`.\n* Käytä `Vision.objectCount` määrittämään motako samanlaista kohdetta löytyy halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla.\n* Sitten voit käyttää muita ominaisuuksia: `kulma`, `keskipisteX`, `keskipisteY`, `korkeus`, `leveys` ja `on olemassa`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].height` antaa kohteen korkeuden pikseleinä arvovälillä **2 - 212 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[3].height);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].height;"},"sensing_vision_objects_width":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_width","markdown":"# Kohteen leveys\n\nAntaa Vision -kamerassa havaitun kohteen leveyden.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].width\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTee järjestyksessä seuraavat toimenpideaskeleet, kun käytät `Vision.objects[index]` komentoa:\n\n1. Määrittele Vision -kamerasi Laitteet - ja Kameran määritysikkunassa.\n2. Käytä `Vision.takeSnapshot()` ottamaan kuvan ja etsimään siitä nimettyä merkkiä/värikoodia.\n3. Käytä `Vision.objects[index].exists` tarkistamaan että halutun kohteen merkki/värikoodi löytyy kuvassa. \n\nKun kohde öytyy, niin voit käyttää muita Vision -komentoja selvittämään tarkempia tietoja kohteeta. \n\n* Käytä **indeksi** muuttujaa kiinnittämään kohde, josta haluat tarkempaa tietoa. Suurinesinekohde on aina edessä, jolloin se on  `Vision.objects[0]`.\n* Käytä `Vision.objectCount` määrittämään motako samanlaista kohdetta löytyy halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla.\n* Sitten voit käyttää muita ominaisuuksia: `kulma`, `keskipisteX`, `keskipisteY`, `korkeus`, `leveys` ja `on olemassa`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].width` antaa esineen kuvaleveyden pikseleinä  **2 - 316 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[1].width);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].width;"},"sensing_vision_takeSnapshot":{"name":"sensing_vision_takeSnapshot","markdown":"# Vision Ota kameran kuva\n\nOttaa Vision -kameralla kuvan.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(signature);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Vision.takeSnapshot` ottaa kuvan ja prosessoi/analysoi sen annetun Vision -kameran haetun värimerkin tiedot.\n\nJotta voit ottaa `Vision.takeSnapshot` komennon, Vision -kameralle pitää olla määritelty ainakin yksi esine/värimerkki. Värimerkin oletusnimi on automaattisesti määritelty.\n\nEsimerkissä Vision -kameran nimi on `Vision1` ja värimerkin `REDBOX`, valittu kokonimi on `Vision1__REDBOX` ja jos haluat ottaa kuvan ko. värimerkillä valitse komento:\n\n```cpp\nVision1.takeSnapshot(Vision1__REDBOX);\n```\n\nTyypillisesti aina ensimmäinen Vision -komento on `Vision.takeSnapshot` ennen muita Vision -kamerakomentoja.\n\nMuista tarkentaa Vision -merkki (esine jota haet).Merkit määritellään ensin Kameran määritys-ikkunassa.","signature":"Vision.takeSnapshot(signature);"},"sound_play_note":{"name":"sound_play_note","markdown":"# Soita Nuotti\n\nSoittaa valitun musiikkinuotin.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playNote(octave, note, duration);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse oktaavi, alhaisin on 1 ja korkein on 7. \n\nValitse seuraavaksi oktaavin nuotti, joka soitetaan:\n- `C = 0`\n- `D = 1`\n- `E = 2`\n- `F = 3`\n- `G = 4`\n- `A = 5`\n- `B = 6`\n\nValise kesto nuotille **millisekunteina**:\n\n- Koko nuotti 1 s (1000 ms)\n- Puoli nuotti 0.5 s (500 ms)\n- Neljännes nuotti 0.25 s (250 ms)\n\nHeti kun nuotin soitto alkaa, suoritetaan myös seuraava komento ohjelmassa.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTämä soittaa keskipktaavin C kokonuotin 1 s ajan.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playNote(4, 0, 1000);\n```","signature":"Brain.playNote(octave, note, duration);"},"sound_play_sound":{"name":"sound_play_sound","markdown":"# Soita ääni\n\nSoittaa valitun ääniefektin VEX IQ's Aivojen kaiuttimesta.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playSound(sound);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse ääniefekti listalta, jonka haluat soittaa.\n\n- `siren`\n- `wrongWay`\n- `wrongWaySlow`\n- `fillup`\n- `headlightsOn`\n- `headlightsOff`\n- `tollBooth`\n- `alarm`\n- `tada`\n- `doorClose`\n- `ratchet`\n- `wrench`\n- `siren2`\n- `ratchet2`\n- `alarm2`\n- `powerDown`\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä soitetaan **siren** ääniefekti.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playSound(siren);   \n```\n\nHeti kun ääniefekti alkaa siirrytään seuraavan komennon suoritukseen ohjelmassa.","signature":"Brain.playSound(sound);"},"variables_2d_arrays":{"name":"variables_2d_arrays","markdown":"# 2D Taulukko Muuttuja\n\nMäärittelee tyypin,nomen ja 2d taulukon koon ja antaa alkuarvot. \n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 },\n};\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMäärittele mitä tyyppiä 2d taulukkko on. \n\n- `int`\n- `double`\n- `bool`\n\nAnna yksikäsitteinen nimi, joka kuvaa taulukkon käyttöä ja koko 2 parilla hakasulkuja `[]` heti nimen jälkeen. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new 2D array with 3 rows and 3 columns\n\nint my2DArray[3][3];\n```\n\nOletusarvot taulukon alkiohin voi antaa aaltosuluissa yhtäläisyysmerkin jälkeen.\n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 }\n};\n```\n\nArvoja voi myös antaa indeksi kerrallaan, ensimmäinen indeksi on aina nolla. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new turnAngles array with 3 rows and 3 columns\nint turnAngles[3][3];\n\n// Assign values by index\nint turnAngles[0][0] = 45;\nint turnAngles[0][1] = 90;\nint turnAngles[0][2] = 180;\nint turnAngles[1][0] = 270;\n```\n\nKun arvoja käyttää, pitää haluttu alkio tarkentaa hakasuluilla.\n\n```cpp\n// The angle variable will be assigned the value of 270\n\nint angle = turnAngles[1][0];\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä **desimaali** 2d taulukko`myAngles` sisältää kulma-asteita.\n\n```cpp\ndouble myAngles[2][3] = {\n  {45.5, 90.0, 88.2},\n  {25.0, 75.5, 45.0}\n};\n```","signature":"variables_2d_array"},"variables_arrays":{"name":"variables_arrays","markdown":"# Taulukko/Luettelo Muuttuja\n\nMäärittele tyyppi, nimi ja taulukon (luettelon) nimi. \n\n```cpp\nint myArray[3] = { 1, 2, 3 };\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMäärittele minkä tyyppistä dataa taulukko sisältää. \n\n- `int`\n- `double`\n- `bool`\n\nTaulukon nimi pitää olla yksikäsitteinen ja kuvaava. Aseta taulkukona lkioidern lukumäärä hakasuluissa `[]` heti nimen jälkeen. \n\n```cpp\nint turnAngles[3];\n```\n\nAlkuarvot voi antaa heti taulukon luonnissa aaltosuluissa.\n\n```cpp\nbool boolArray[2] = { false, true };\n```\n\nArvot voi myös antaa yksitellen indeksi kerrallaan indeksiarvosta 0 lähtien. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new array of length 3\ndouble doubleArray[3];\n\n// Assign values to the array by index\ndouble doubleArray[0] = 1.5;\ndouble doubleArray[1] = 3.14;\ndouble doubleArray[2] = 2.18;\n```\n\nKun sijoitat taulukon arvoja johonkin, niin valitse indeksiarvo hakasuluissa.\n\n```cpp\n// Read the value at index 2 in integerArray\n\nint value = integerArray[2];\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä numerotaulukolle annetaan alkuarvot ja alkio #3 (indeksi arvo 2) sijoitetaan Moottorin kääntymiskulmaksi asteina. \n\n```cpp\nint degreesArray[3] = { 30, 60, 90 };\nMotor.spinFor(forward, degreesArray[2], degrees);\n```","signature":"variables_arrays"},"variables_boolean":{"name":"variables_boolean","markdown":"# Boolean Muuttuja\n\nMuuttaja saa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi**.\n\n`bool myBoolean = true;`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Boolean Muuttuja** arvo voi olla **tosi** tai **epätosi**. Määrittele muuttujanimen alkuun `bool` ja anna sille alkuarvo `tosi` tai `epätosi`. \n\n`bool goFast = true;`\n\nBoolean muuttujia voi käyttää ohjauskomentojen ehdoissa. \n\n```cpp\nif (goFast) {\n  Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity(100, percent);\n}\n```","signature":"variables_boolean"},"variables_double":{"name":"variables_double","markdown":"# Desimaali Muuttuja\n\nMäärittelee muuttujan `desimaali` tyyppiseksi.\n\n`double myDouble = 1.5;`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`desimaali` muuttujatyypin muuttuja on luku, jossa on desimaalipiste.\n\n`double pi = 3.14;`\n\nAnna muuttujalle yksikäsitteinen ja kuvaava nimi ja anna sille alkuarvo.\n\n`double turnAngle = 40.5;`","signature":"variables_double"},"variables_intergers":{"name":"variables_intergers","markdown":"# Kokonaisluku muuttuja\n\nMäärittelee kokonaislukumuuttujan ja antaa sille nimen ja alkuarvon.\n\n`int myNumber = 10;`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAnna yksikäsitteinen ja kuvaava nimi muuttujalle.\n\n`int driveTime = 60;`\n\nAnna muuttujalle alkuarvo. Muuttujan arvo voi olla jonkun sensorin antama arvo tai laskutoimituksen tulos edellyttäen, että tulos on oikeaa **tyyppiä**.\n\n```cpp\nint lowBatteryLifeWarning = Brain.Battery.capacity(percent);\n```\n\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä VEX IQ etäisyysanturin mittaama etäisyysarvo sijoitetaan \"myVariable\" muuttujaan ja sen jälkeen \"myVariable\" sijoitetaan ajopelin nopeudeksi.\n\n```cpp\nint myVariable = Distance7.distance(inches);\n\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(myVariable, percent);\n```","signature":"variables_intergers"},"variables_my_string":{"name":"variables_my_string","markdown":"# Merkkijono muuttuja\n\nMäärittele muuttujan **Merkkijono** tyyppiseksi ja antaa sille nimen ja alkusisällön.\n\n`char myString[] = \"my string\";`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Merkkijono** muuttujatyyppiseen muuttujaan voi sijoittaa sekä numeroita että kirjaimia, kun ne on merkkien `\" \"`välissä.\n\nLuo yksikäsitteinen ja kuvaava nimi muuttujalle. Anna sisältö **Merkkijono** muuttujalle. IQ Vexcodessa  **Merkkijono** muuttujatyyppin sisältö voidaan antaa näin.\n\n`char driveMessage[] = \"Time to Drive!\";`","signature":"variables_my_string"}}},"hu-HU":{"blocks":{"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Összeadás\n\nBármely két értéket összead, és jelenti az összeget.\n\n![add](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/add/add.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **Összeadás** tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogad el.\n\nAz **összeadás** blokk hossza olyan blokkokba illeszkedik, amelyek kör alakú helyeket fogadnak be.\n\nAdjon össze két számot.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nAdjon össze értékeket a változókból.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nAdjon össze értékeket az érzékelőkből vagy eszközökből.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# És\n\nJelzi, ha mindkét logikai feltétel igaz.\n\n![and](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/and/and.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **és** blokk azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha mindkét feltétel **igaz**. \n\nAz **és** blokk azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha az egyik feltétel (vagy mindkettő) **hamis**.\n\nAz **és** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkokba illeszkedik.\n\n![and_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa azt ellenőrzi, hogy egyszerre két VEX IQ Kontroller gombot nyomnak-e meg.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nAz **és** blokk **igaz** értékre tér vissza, ha mind a **Kontroller E Fel gomb** és a **Kontroller L Le gomb** meg lettek nyomva.\n\nAz **és** blokk **hamis** értékre tér vissza, ha az egyik Kontroller gombot nem (vagy egyiket sem) nyomják meg.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/and/and_truth.png)"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Akkumulátor szint\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ Agy akkumulátorának töltöttségi szintjét.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **akkumulátor szint** **0% és 100%** közötti tartományt jelent.\n\nAz **akkumulátor szint** jelentő blokkot kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkok belsejében használják.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa riasztó hangot ad ki, ha a VEX IQ Agy **akkumulátor szint** töltöttsége alacsonyabb, mint 50%.\n\n![battery_capacity_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/battery_level/battery_capacity_example_revised.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Logikai változó\n\nJelzi egy logikai változó értékét.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **logikai változó** blokkok a változó belsejében tárolt **igaz** vagy **hamis** értékek jelentésére szolgálnak. Használja a **logikai változó beállítása** blokkot a logikai változó értékének beállításához vagy frissítéséhez.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nA **logikai változó** **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nA logikai változókat a **Logikai változó készítése** gombbal lehet létrehozni.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"brain_button_pressed":{"name":"brain_button_pressed","markdown":"# Agy gomb megnyomva\n\nJelzi, ha megnyomnak egy gombot a VEX IQ Agyon.\n\n![button_pressed_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\n**Agy gomb megnyomva** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz** ha a kiválasztott Agy gombot megnyomják.\n\n**Agy gomb megnyomva** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis** ha a kiválasztott Agy gombot nem nyomják meg.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt Agy gombot.\n\n![button_pressed_options](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_options.png)\n\nAz **agy gomb megnyomva** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) hellyel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEbben a példában a robot előre fog menni, majd jobbra fordul, miután az Agy **Fel** gombját megnyomták.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_example_revised.png)\n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Törés\n\nAzonnal kilép egy ismétlődésből.\n\n![break](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/break/break.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nHa egy ismétlő 'C' blokkhoz hozzáadunk egy **törés** blokkot, akkor a blokk kilép az aktuális csoportból.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa előre viszi a hajtást és ellenőrzi, hogy a VEX IQ Agy **fel** gombja meg van-e nyomva.\n\nHa a **fel** gomb meg van **nyomva**, a **törés** blokk kilép az örök ismétlés csoportból és megállítja a hajtást.\n\n![break_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Fényerő\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ szín érzékelő által észlelt fény mennyiségét.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **Fényerő** **0% és 100%** közötti tartományt jelez.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt Színérzékelőt.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nA **fényerő** nevű jelentő blokkot kör alakú hellyel ellátott blokkokon belül használjuk.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Adás\n\nÜzenetet közvetít minden olyan csoport aktiválásához, amely **amikor kapok** blokkal kezdődik, amely meghallgatja az üzenetet. \n\n![broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA csoport, ami küldi az **adás**-t továbbra is blokkokat fog futtatni a többi csoporttal együtt, amelyek a sugárzott üzenetet fogadják.\n\nVálassza ki melyik üzenetet közvetítse az **adás**. Új üzenet is létrehozható.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa piros színnel fog megjelenni a VEX IQ Érintő LED-en, majd várjon két másodpercet, mielőtt az \"üzenet1\" üzenetet sugározná.\n\nAmint megkapta az üzenetet, az **amikor kapok** csoport hatására a hajtás előre fog haladni, míg a Karom Motor egyidejűleg felfelé fog haladni.\n\nA két csoport ugyanabban az időben fog futni piros nyilak által jelezve.\n\n![broadcast_example_arrows](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/broadcast/broadcast_example_arrows.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Közvetítés és várakozás\n\nÜzenetet közvetít minden olyan csoport aktiválásához, amelyek **amikor kapok** blokkal kezdődnek, amely meghallgatja az üzenetet, \nmiközben szünetelteti is a csoport többi részét.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **közvetítés és várakozás** blokkot küldő csoport szünetel, amíg a többi csoport, amely fogadja a sugárzott üzenetet, elkészül.\n\nVálassza ki, melyik üzenetet szeretné közvetíteni az **adás**. Új üzenet is létrehozható.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa piros színnel fog megjelenni a VEX IQ Érintő LED-en, majd várjon két másodpercet, mielőtt az \"üzenet1\" üzenetet sugározná.\n\nAmint megkapta az üzenetet, az **amikor kapok** csoport hatására a hajtás előre fog haladni és lejátszik egy hangeffektust.\n\nA sugárzó csoport megvárja, amíg a vevő csoport befejeződik, mielőtt folytatná a blokkok futtatását, amit a piros nyilak jeleznek.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows_3](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows3.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Giroszkóp beállítása\n\nA VEX IQ Giroszkóp kalibrálásával csökkenthető a Giroszkóp által generált sodródás.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nSodródás akkor következik be, amikor a giroszkóp helytelenül mozgást érzékel annak ellenére, hogy az érzékelő nem mozog.\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA giroszkópnak mozdulatlanul kell maradnia a kalibrálási folyamat alatt.\n\nVálassza ki, melyik giroszkópot fogja használni.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nVálassza ki, hogy meddig szeretné kalibrálni. Minél több ideig állítjuk a giroszkópot, annál kevesebb sodródás történik.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_seconds](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_seconds.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Változó módosítása\n\nVáltozót módosít a megadott értékkel.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt változót - a kiválasztott változó átnevezhető vagy törölhető is.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nA **változó módosítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat képes elfogadni.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa 10-zel növeli a hajtás sebességét beállító változót minden alkalommal, amikor a **csoport megismétlése** történik. \n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Összes sor törlése\n\nTörli a VEX IQ Agy teljes képernyőjét.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **Összes sor törlése** nem állítja vissza az Agy képernyő kurzorát. A **kurzor beállítása** blokk segítségével állítsa vissza az Agy képernyő kurzorát a kívánt pozícióba.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa egy másodpercig kiírja a \"Hello\" szót, majd a \"Goodbye\" kiírása előtt törli az egész képernyőt.\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Sor törlése\n\nEgyetlen sort töröl a VEX IQ Agy képernyőn.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **sor törlése** \nblokk egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el **1 - 5** között annak beállításához, hogy melyik sort törölje.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/clear_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa három másodpercig kiírja a \"Hello\" szót a 2. sor 1. oszlopában, mielőtt törölné a 2. sort.\n\n![clear_row_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/clear_row/clear_row_example.png)"},"color_detects_color":{"name":"color_detects_color","markdown":"# Szín észlelés\n\nJelzi, ha a VEX IQ színérzékelő egy adott színt érzékel.\n\n![color_detects](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/color_detects_color/color_detects.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **szín észlelés** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a színérzékelő észleli a kiválasztott színt.\n\nA **szín észlelés** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha a színérzékelő a kiválasztottól eltérő színt észlel.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt színérzékelőt.\n\n![color_detects_chosen](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/color_detects_color/color_detects_chosen.png)\n\nVálassza ki az észlelni kívánt színt.\n\n![color_detects_selected](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/color_detects_color/color_detects_selected.png)\n\nA **szín észlelés** logikai változó **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![color_detects_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/color_detects_color/color_detects_shape.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa ki fogja írni a \"Piros\" vagy \"Egyéb szín\" feliratot, attól függően, hogy a színérzékelő érzékeli-e a \"piros\" színt.\n\n![color_detects_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/color_detects_color/color_detects_example.png)\n\n"},"color_of":{"name":"color_of","markdown":"# Szín\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ színérzékelő által észlelt szín nevét.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/color_of/color_of_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **szín** a következő színek egyikét jelzi: **piros, bordó, lila, kékes lila, blue, kékeszöld, zöld, sárgás +zöld, sárga, sárgás narancssárga, narancssárga, vagy pirosas narancssárga.**\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt színérzékelőt.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/color_of/color_of_color.png)\n\nA **szín** jelentő blokkot kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkok belsejében használják.\n\n![color_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/color_of/color_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Komment\n\nLehetővé teszi a programozók számára, hogy információkat írjanak a programjukról a megértés érdekében.\n\n![comment_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA profi programozók a programjuk során használt megjegyzésekkel segítenek másoknak megérteni kódjukat. A megjegyzések segíthetnek a hibaelhárításban és az együttműködésben is.\n\nAz átlátszó négyzet kiválasztásával lehet szöveget hozzáadni és a meglévő szöveget törölni a **Komment** blokkban. Ezután tudja beírni az új szöveget.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nA megjegyzések nem változtatják meg a programot vagy a körülötte lévő blokkot.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Kontroller engedélyezése/letiltása\n\nEngedélyezi vagy letiltja a Kontroller által konfigurált műveleteket az Eszközök menüből.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza a konfigurált kontroller műveletek engedélyezését vagy letiltását a legördülő menüből, a kívánt állapot kiválasztásával. Alapértelmezés szerint a kontroller minden projektben engedélyezve van.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEbben a példában a konfigurált művelet a robot vezérléséz használja, amelyet a kontroller konfigurációja állított be az Eszközök ablakban.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nEbben a példában a konfigurált kontroller letiltásra kerül, amikor a program elindul.\n\nEzután a robot 6 hüvelyknyire halad előre.\n\nVégül, a **kontroller engedélyezése** blokk lehetővé teszi a kontroller számára, hogy visszaállítsa a kontroller vezetési viselkedését.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Motor árama\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ motor által jelenleg használt energiamennyiséget százalékban (%) vagy amperben (amper).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **motor árama** **0% és 100%** vagy **0.0 és 1.2 amps** között jelez. \n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nVálassza ki, hogy a motor áramát %-ban vagy amperben adják-e meg.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nA **motor árama** jelentő blokkot kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkokban használják.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Kurzor oszlopa\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ Agí képernyő kurzor oszlopának számát.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **Kurzor oszlopa** **1 és 21** közötti tartományt jelent.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/cursor_column/row_column_index.png)  \n\nA **Kurzor árama** jelentő blokkot kör alakú hellyel ellátott blokkokban használják.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa azt ellenőrzi, hogy a **kurzor oszlop** pozíciója nagyobb-e, mint 15. Ha a pozíció nagyobb, mint 15, a projekt a kurzort az 1. sorra és az 1. oszlopra állítja, majd kiírja a „Hello” szót.\n\n![cursor_column_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/cursor_column/cursor_column_example_simple.png)\n\n"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Kurzor sor\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ Agy képernyő kurzorának sorszámát.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **kurzor sor** **1 és 5** közötti tartományt jelent.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/cursor_row/row_column_index.png)\n\nA **kurzor sor** jelentő blokk kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkokban kerül felhasználásra.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa azt ellenőrzi, hogy a **kurzor sor** pozíciója nagyobb-e, mint 4. Ha a pozíció nagyobb, mint 4, a projekt a kurzort az 1. sor 1. oszlopára állítja, majd kiírja \"Hello\" szót.\n\n![cursor_row_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/cursor_row/cursor_row_example_simple.png)"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Távolság\n\nJelzi a legközelebbi objektum távolságát a VEX IQ távolságérzékelőtől.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **távolság** **24mm és 1000mm** vagy **1 hüvelyk és 40 hüvelyk** között jelez.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt távolságérzékelőt.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nVálassza ki, hogy a **távolság** hüvelykben vagy milliméterben legyen megadva.\n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nA **távolság** jelentő blokk kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkok belsejében használják.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Osztás\n\nElosztja az első értéket a második értékkel, és beszámol az eredményről.\n\n![divide](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **osztás** tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat képes elfogadni.\n\nAz **osztás** blokk hossza olyan blokkokba illeszkedik, amelyekben a kör alakú helyek vannak.\n\nÍrja be az elosztandó számokat.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nOsztás a változók értékeivel.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nOsztás az érzékelők vagy eszközök értékeivel.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Mozgás\n\nÖrökké mozog a hajtáslánc.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **mozgás** blokk mindaddig futtatja a hajtásláncot, amíg egy új hajtáslánc blokkot nem kezdenek el használni, vagy a program le nem áll.\n\nVálassza ki a hajtáslánc irányát.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Hajtás árama\n\nJelzi a hajtáslánc által jelenleg használt áram (teljesítmény) mennyiségét.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **Hajtás árama** **0% és 100%** vagy **0.0 és 1.2 amper** közötti tartományt jelent. \n\nVálassza ki, hogy a **hajtás árama** %-ban vagy amperben (amps) legyen megadva.\n\n![drive_current_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_current/drive_current_unit.png)\n\nA **hajtás árama** jelentő blokkat kör alakú hellyel ellátott blokkok belsejében használják.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Vezetés\n\nEgy adott távolságra mozgatja a hajtásláncot.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a hajtáslánc irányát.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\nA **vezetés** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nAdja meg az értéket, és válassza ki a mértékegységet (hüvelykben vagy milliméterben), hogy beállítsa, hogy a hajtáslánc milyen távolságra mozogjon.\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nAlapértelmezés szerint más blokkok a **várj** parancsot követik, amíg a hajtáslánc befejezi a haladást.\n\nKiválaszthatja a nyilat az **és ne várj** parancs bővítésével - ez más blokkok folytatását eredményezi, miközben a hajtáslánc mozog.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Hajtás Menetiránya\n\nJelzi a hajtáslánc irányát.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **hajtás menetiránya** **0.00 és 359.99 fok** közötti skálát jelez.\n\nA **hajtás menetiránya** az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba mutat, az alábbi képen látható módon.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_heading/TopDownBot01.png)\n\nA **hajtás menetiránya** kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkok belsejében használják.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Mozgás vége\n\nJelzi, ha a hajtáslánc befejezte mozgását.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **mozgás vége** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a hajtáslánc motorjai befejezték mozgásukat.\n\nA **mozgás vége** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha a hajtáslánc motorjai még mindig mozognak.\n\nA **mozgás vége** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Mozog\n\nJelzi, ha a hajtáslánc éppen mozog.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **mozgás** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a hajtáslánc motorjai mozognak.\n\nA **mozgás** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha a hajtáslánc motorjai megálltak.\n\nA **mozgás** logikai változó **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Forgatás\n\nJelzi a hajtáslánc forgási szögét fokban, ha VEX IQ giroszkóppal konfigurálva van.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **Forgatás** azt jelzi, hogy **pozitív**, ha a fordulás **óramutató járásával ellentétes irányban** történik.\n\nA **Forgatás** azt jelzi, hogy **negatív**, ha a fordulás **óramutató járásával megegyező irányban** történik.\n\nA **forgatás** jelentő blokkot kör alakú hellyel ellátott blokkok belsejében használják.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Hajtás sebessége\n\nJelzi a hajtáslánc aktuális sebességét.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **hajtás sebessége** **-100% és 100%** közötti vagy **-127rpm és 127rpm** közötti értéket jelez.\n\nVálassza ki, hogy a sebességet %-ban vagy percenkénti fordulatszámban (rpm) adják meg.\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nA **hajtás sebessége** jelentő blokkot kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkok belsejében használják.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Egyenlő\n\nJelzi, ha az első érték megegyezik (egyenlő) a második értékkel.\n\n![equal_to](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **egyenlő** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a két érték teljesen megegyezik.\n\nAz **egyenlő** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha a két érték nem egyezik meg.\n\nAz **egyenlő** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nAz **egyenlő** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a \"Hajtáslánc elakadt\" feliratot írja a VEX IQ Agy képernyőjére, ha a hajtáslánc áramértéke 100%.\n\n![equal_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/equal_to/equal_to_example.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Örök\n\nEgy 'C' blokk, amely örökre megismétli a benne lévő blokkokat.\n\n![forever](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nHelyezze a blokkokat **örök** 'C' blokkba, hogy ezek a műveletek **örök** időre megismétlődjenek.\n\nEgy **örök** ciklusból kiléphet egy **törés** blokk belsejébe helyezésével.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nA 'C' blokkok egymásba is helyezhetők. Ezt a koncepciót fészkelésnek hívják, amely időt takaríthat meg a különböző viselkedések programozásakor.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa 5 másodpercenként ugyanazt a hanghatást fogja lejátszani örökké.\n\n![forever_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/forever/forever_example.png)"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Függvény\n\nKiválasztott matematikai függvényt hajt végre.\n\n![function](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - abszolút érték\n* **floor** - lefelé kerekít a legközelebbi egész számra\n* **ceiling** - felkerekekít a legközelebbi egész számra\n* **sqrt** - négyzetgyök\n* **sin** - sinus\n* **cos** - cosinus\n* **tan** - tangens\n* **asin** - arcsinus vagy sinus inverze\n* **acos** - arccosinus vagy cosinus inverze\n* **atan** - arctangens vagy tangens inverze\n* **ln** - a természetes logaritmus e alap\n* **log** - logaritmus 10 alap\n* **e ^** - e\n* **10 ^** - 10\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **függvény** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nVálassza ki a matematikai **függvény** opciót a lehetőségek listájából.\n\n![function_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/function/function_select.png)\n\nA **függvény** blokk hossza olyan blokkokba illeszkedik, amelyek befogadják a kör alakú szóközöket.\n\n![function_fit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Több, mint\n\nJelzi, ha az első érték több (nagyobb), mint a második érték.\n\n![greater_than](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **Több, mint** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz** ha az első érték nagyobb, mint a második érték. \n\nA **Több, mint** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis** ha az első érték kisebb, vagy ugyanannyi, mint a második érték.\n\nA ** több, mint ** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nA **több, mint** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) hellyel ellátott blokkokba illeszkedik.\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa az \"Akkumulátor szintje megfelelő\" feliratot fogja kiírni a VEX IQ Brain képernyőjére, ha az akkumulátor töltöttségi szintje több, mint 75%.\n\n![greater_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/greater_than/greater_than_example.png)\n\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Menetirány szöge\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ giroszkóp aktuális menetirányát fokban.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **Giroszkóp menetiránya** **0.00 és 359.99** közötti tartományt jelent.\n\nA **Giroszkóp menetiránya** az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba mutat, az alábbi képen látható módon.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/heading_of_gyro/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\nVálassza ki, hogy melyik giroszkópot szeretné ellenőrizni.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nA **Giroszkóp menetiránya** jelentő blokkot kör alakú hellyel ellátott blokkokban használják.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"hue_of":{"name":"hue_of","markdown":"# Színárnyalat\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ színérzékelő által észlelt színárnyalatot.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/hue_of/hue_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nA **színárnyalat** **0 és 360** közötti skálát jelez.\n\nVálassza ki az ellenőrizni kívánt színérzékelőt.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/hue_of/hue_of_color.png)\n\nA **színárnyalat** jelentő blokk kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkok belsejében használják.\n\n![hue_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/hue_of/hue_of_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Ha, akkor\n\nEgy 'C' blokk, amely a blokkokat futtatja belül, ha a logikai feltételt **igaz** értéknek jelentik.\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **ha, akkor** 'C' blokk csak egyszer ellenőrzi a logikai állapotot.\n\nHa a logikai feltétel **igaz**, a **ha, akkor** belsejében lévő blokk elindul.\n\nHa a logikai feltétel **hamis**, a **ha, akkor** belsejében lévő blokkot kihagyja.\n\nA **ha, akkor** 'C' blokk elfogadhatja a hatszögletű (hatoldalas) blokkokat.\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa hangeffektust játszik le, amikor a VEX IQ ütközőt megnyomják.\n\nA **ha, akkor** 'C' blokk elhelyezhető az örök blokkokban annak biztosítása érdekében, hogy a hanghatást ne csak egyszer játssza le, hanem mindig.\n\n![if_then_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/if_then/if_then_example.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Ha-akkor-különben\n\nEgy 'C' blokk, amely a **ha-akkor-különben** első vagy második részében lévő blokkokat futtatja a jelentett logikai érték alapján.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **ha-akkor-különben** 'C' blokk csak egyszer ellenőrzi a logikai állapotot. \n\nHa a logikai feltétel **igaz** értékű, akkor akkor a **ha** szakaszon belüli blokkok kerülnek futtatásra.\n\nHa a logikai feltétel **hamis**, értékű, akkor akkor a **különben** szakasz kerül futtatásra.\n\nA **ha-akkor-különben** 'C' blokkot hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa zöld lesz, ha megnyomják a VEX IQ Érintő LED-et, és piros, ha az Érintő LED nincs megnyomva.\n\nA **ha-akkor-különben** 'C' blokk elhelyezhető az örök blokkokban, hogy a LED többször megváltoztassa a színét.\n\n![if_then_else_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/if_then_else/if_then_else_example.png)"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 2D Lista Eleme\n\nJelzi a 2D listában szereplő elem értékét.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt 2D listát. A 2D lista átnevezhető vagy törölhető.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nÍrja be az elem sorának (első szám) és oszlopának (második szám) pozícióját a jelentendő listán belül. Itt a 2D lista 2. sorában 3. oszlopában szereplő elemet jelenti.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nA **2D lista eleme** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Tétel\n\nJelzi a lista egy elemének értékét.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt listát. A lista átnevezhető vagy törölhető is.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nÍrja be az elem pozíciójának a számát a listában. Itt a lista második tételét (2. tétel) fogja jelezni.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nA **tétel** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a hajtáslánc sebességét a 3. tételben tárolt értékre állítja. A hajtáslánc most 90%-os sebességgel halad előre.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 2D lista hossza\n\nJelzi a 2D-s lista sorainak vagy oszlopainak számát.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt 2D listát. A 2D lista átnevezhető vagy törölhető.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nVálassza ki a jelentendő értéket. A 2D lista **sorok** vagy **oszlopok** számát jelentheti.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nA **2D lista hossza** jelentő blokk olyan blokkokba illeszkedik, amelyek befogadják a kör alakú helyeket.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Kevesebb, mint\n\nJelzi, ha az első érték kevesebb (kisebb), mint a második érték.\n\n![less_than](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **Kevesebb, mint** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz** ha az első érték kisebb, mint a második érték. \n\nA **Kevesebb, mint** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis** ha az első érték nagyobb, vagy ugyanannyi, mint a második érték.\n\nA **kevesebb, mint** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) hellyel ellátott blokkokba illeszkedik.\n\nA **kevesebb, mint** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a \"Merül az elem!\" feliratot fogja kiírni a VEX IQ Brain képernyőjére, ha az akkumulátor töltöttségi szintje kevesebb, mint 25%.\n\n![less_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/less_than/less_than_example.png)\n\n"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor végzett\n\nJelzi, ha a kiválasztott motor befejezte a mozgását.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **motor végzett** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a kiválasztott motor befejezte a mozgását.\n\nA **motor végzett** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha a kiválasztott motor még mindig mozog.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nA **motor végzett** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\nAz a blokk, amely azt jelzi, hogy a motor végzett-e, hatszögletű (hatoldalú) hellyel rendelkező blokkok belsejében található."},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Forog a motor\n\nJelzi, ha a kiválasztott motor éppen forog.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **Forog a motor** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a kiválasztott motor forog.\n\nA **Forog a motor** azt jelti, hogy **hamis**, ha a kiválasztott motor megállt.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nA **forog a motor** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Szorzás\n\nBármely két értéket összeszorozza és beszámol az eredményről.\n\n![multiply](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **szorzás** tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat képes elfogadni.\n\nA **szorzás** blokk hossza olyan blokkokba illeszkedik, amelyek elfogadják a kör alakú helyeket.\n\nSzorozzon össze két számot.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nSzorozás a változók értékeivel.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nSzorozás az érzékelők vagy az eszközök által kapott értékekkel.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Következő sor\n\nA Brain képernyőn a következő elérhető sorra állítja a nyomtatási kimenetet.\n\n![next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAlapértelmezés szerint az összes projektben a képernyő kurzora az 1. sor 1. oszlopában kezd. A **következő sor** blokk egyetlen sorral lefelé mozgatja a kurzort az Agy képernyőn.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/next_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa kiírja az \"Első üzenet\" szót, majd a kurzort a következő elérhető sorra állítja a \"Második üzenet\" nyomtatása előtt.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/next_row/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/next_row/set_cursor_welcome.png)\n"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# Nem\n\nJelzi a logikai eredmény ellentétes (inverz) értékét.\n\n![not](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/not/not.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **nem** blokk azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a logikai blokk belül **hamis** értéket jelez.\n\nA **nem** blokk azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha a logikai blokk belül **igaz** értéket jelez.\n\nA **nem** logikai változó **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa **igaz** értéket jelez, ha a VEX IQ Agy 'pipa' gombját nem nyomják meg.\n\n![not_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Tárgyak száma\n\nJelzi, hogy a látásérzékelő hány darab objektumot érzékel.\n\nEgy objektumot konfigurálni kell, mielőtt a **tárgyak száma** blokk észlelni tudná.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt látásérzékelőt.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nA **pillanatkép** blokkot kell használni, mielőtt a **tárgyak száma** blokk jelentené a tárgyak számát.\n\nA **tárgyak száma** blokk csak az utolsó pillanatfelvételen lévő tárgyak számát érzékeli.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Tárgy létezik\n\nJelzi, ha a látás érzékelő egy konfigurált tárgyat észlel.\n\nAz objektumot konfigurálni kell, hogy a **tárgy létezik** blokk észlelni tudja.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt látásérzékelőt.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\nA **tárgy létezik** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a látásérzékelő érzékel egy konfigurált tárgyat.\n\nA **tárgy létezik** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha a látásérzékelő nem észlel konfigurált tárgyat.\n\nA **tárgy létezik** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nA blokk **pillanatképét** a **tárgy létezik** logikai változó **igaz** vagy **hamis** érték jelzése előtt kell használni."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Tárgy megtalálva\n\nJelzi, ha a VEX IQ távolságérzékelő lát egy objektumot a látómezőjében.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **Tárgy megtalálva** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz** ha a távolságérzékelő lát egy tárgyat vagy felületet a látómezőjén belül.\n\nA **Tárgy megtalálva** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis** ha a távolságérzékelő nem észlel tárgyat vagy felületet a látómezőjén belül.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt távolságérzékelőt.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nA **tárgy megtalálva** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"object_is_near":{"name":"object_is_near","markdown":"# Tárgy a közelben\n\nJelzi, ha a VEX IQ színérzékelő közelben lévő tárgyat észlel.\n\n![object_is_near](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_is_near/object_is_near_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **tárgy a közelben** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a színérzékelő az érzékelő elejéhez közel eső tárgyat vagy felületet észlel.\n\nA **tárgy a közelben** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha a színérzékelő üres helyet érzékel az érzékelő előtt.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt színérzékelőt.\n\n![object_is_near_color](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_is_near/object_is_near_color.png)\n\nA **tárgy a közelben** logikai változó **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![object_is_near_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/object_is_near/object_is_near_inserted.png)\n\n\n "},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# Vagy\n\nJelzi, ha a két logikai feltétel egyike igaz.\n\n![or](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/or/or.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **vagy** blokk azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha az egyik (vagy mindkét) feltétel **igaz**. \n\nA **vagy** blokk azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha mindkét feltétel **hamis**.\n\nA **vagy** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hatoldalú) terekkel rendelkező blokkokba illeszkedik.\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\nA **vagy** blokk azt jelzi, hogy **igaz** ha a VEX IQ ütközőt és a VEX IQ érintő LED egyikét (vagy mindkettőt) lenyomják, és csak akkor jelentenek  **hamis** értéket, ha az ütköző és az érintő LED sincs lenyomva.\n\n![or_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/or/or_truth.png)"},"play_note":{"name":"play_note","markdown":"# Kotta lejátszása\n\nLejátssza a kiválasztott kottát.\n\n![play_note](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/play_note/play_note.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálasszon kottát.\n\n![play_note_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/play_note/play_note_select.png)\n\nVálassza ki, hogy mennyi ideig (időtartamig) játssza a hangot.\n\n![play_note_duration](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/play_note/play_note_duration.png)\n\n* Egy **egész** hangjegy lejátszása 1 másodpercig (1000 milliszekundum)\n* Egy **fél** hangjegy lejátszása 0.5 másodpercig (500 milliszekundum)\n* Egy **negyed** hangjegy lejátszása 0.25 másodpercig (250 milliszekundum)\n\nAmint a kotta lejátszása kezdetét veszi, a következő blokk azonnal elkezdődik."},"play_sound":{"name":"play_sound","markdown":"# Hang lejátszása\n\nLejátsza a kiválasztott hanghatást.\n\n![play_sound](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/play_sound/play_sound.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a hanghatást a lehetőségek listájából.\n\n![play_sound_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/play_sound/play_sound_select.png)\n\nAmint elkezd lejátszani egy hanghatást, a következő blokk azonnal elkezdődik."},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Kontroller helyzete\n\nJelzi a joystick helyzetét a kontrolleren egy tengely mentén.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **kontroller helyzete** **-100 és 100** között jelez.\n\nA **kontroller helyzete** nulla (0) lesz, ha a joystick tengelye középre kerül.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nVálassza ki a joystick tengelyét a helyzetének ellenőrzéséhez.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nA **kontroller helyzete** jelentő blokk kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkokban használják.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa ismételten ellenőrzi a vezérlő D joystick tengelyét a kar motorjának sebességének szabályozásához.\n\n![position_of_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Motor helyzete\n\nJelzi a motor megtett távolságát.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **motor helyzete** jelzi a motor helyzetét a fokok miatt egész számokban és fordulatok esetén tizedes számokban.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nVálassza ki, hogy az értéket a forgatás fokában vagy a motor fordulatszámaiban adják-e meg.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nA **motor helyzete** jelentő blokkot kör alakú hellyel ellátott blokkokban használják. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Ütköző megnyomása\n\nJelzi, ha megnyomják a VEX IQ ütközőt.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **ütköző megnyomása** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha megnyomják az ütközőt.\n\nAz **ütköző megnyomása** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha nem nyomják meg az ütközőt.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt ütközőt.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nAz **ütköző megnyomása** logikai blokk **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Kontroller megnyomása\n\nJelzi, ha megnyomnak egy gombot a VEX IQ Kontrolleren.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **kontroller megnyomása** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a kiválasztott Kontroller gombot lenyomják.\n\nA **kontroller megnyomása** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha a kiválasztott Kontroller gombot nem nyomják le.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt kontroller gombot.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nA **kontroller megnyomása** logikai változó **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa ellenőrzi, hogy megnyomták-e az E Fel gombot, és előre forgatja a karom motort.\n\n![pressing_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_example_revised.png)"},"pressing_touchled":{"name":"pressing_touchled","markdown":"# Érintő LED megnyomása\n\nJelzi, ha megnyomják a VEX IQ Érintő LED-et.\n\n![pressing_touch_led](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **érintő LED megnyomása** azt jelzi, hogy **igaz**, ha a kiválasztott Érintő LED-et megnyomják.\n\nAz **érintő LED megnyomása** azt jelzi, hogy **hamis**, ha a kiválasztott Érintő LED-et nem nyomják meg.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt Érintő LED-et.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_led](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_led.png)\n\nAz **érintő LED megnyomása** logikai változó **igaz** vagy **hamis** értéket jelez és hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkoknál használják.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_inserted.png)\n\n"},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Kiír\n\nÉrtékeket vagy szöveget ír a VEX IQ Brain képernyőjére.\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/print/look_print.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **kiír** blokk adatokat ír a kurzor helyére az Agy képernyőn.\n\nMinden új projekt a képernyő kurzorának 1. sor 1. oszlopával kezdődik.\n\nAz összes jelentő blokkot alapértelmezés szerint egész számként írja ki. Használja a **írás precizitásának beállítása** blokkot a kiírt tizedesjegyek számának beállításához.\n\nSzavak és számok kiírása.\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/print/print_words.png)\n\nÍrja ki a jelentett értéket egy változóból.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nÍrja ki a kezelő által jelentett számítást.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nÍrja ki a jelentett értéket egy érzékelőről vagy eszközről.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Saját blokk\n\nA Saját blokkok egyedi blokkok létrehozására szolgálnak.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **saját blokkok** blokkok sorozatának létrehozására szolgálnak, amelyek többször is felhasználhatók a projekt során.\n\nA **saját blokkok** a **Blokk készítése** gombbal készülnek.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\nA **saját blokkok** blokknak több paramétere lehet - szöveges címkék, numerikus változók és logikai változók -, hogy további funkciókat adhasson az egyéni blokkhoz.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nA **saját blokkok** használatához, csatolja a hívó **saját blokkok** blokkot a kalap blokkhoz. Amikor a eléri a **saját blokkok** blokkot a projektben, a **saját blokkok** belsejében lévő csoport a megadott paraméterértékek alapján fog futni.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nCsatoljon egy csoport blokkot a **saját blokkok** értékhez, hogy definiálja a kalap blokkot a **saját blokkok** használatakor fellépő művelet beállításához.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Megjegyzés: Több Saját Blokk létrehozása ugyanazokkal a címkékkel és változókkal hibákat okozhat a projekt letöltésekor.***\n\n## 1. Példa\n\nEbben a példában a robot a **saját blokkokat** használja, hogy:\n\n* Játssza le a sziréna hangját háromszor.\n* Hajtson előre 12 hüvelyket.\n* Játssza le a sziréna hangját háromszor.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_call/sound_example.png)\n\n## 2. Példa\n\nEbben a példában a robot a **saját blokkokat** használja, hogy:\n\n* Hajtson előre 15 hüvelyket.\n* Írja ki az akkumulátor kapacitását, és mozgassa a kurzort egy új sorra az Agy képernyőjén.\n* Fordítsa a robotot 180 fokkal jobbra.\n* Írja ki az akkumulátor kapacitását, és mozgassa a kurzort egy új sorra az Agy képernyőjén.\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Saját blokk\n\nA Saját blokkok egyedi blokkok létrehozására szolgálnak.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **saját blokkok** blokkok sorozatának létrehozására szolgálnak, amelyek többször is felhasználhatók a projekt során. \n\nA **saját blokkok** a **Blokk Létrehozása** gombbal hozhatóak létre.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\nA **saját blokkok** blokkoknak több paraméterük lehet - szöveges címkék, numerikus változók és logikai változók -, hogy további funkciókat adhasson az egyéni blokkhoz.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nA **saját blokkok** használatához, csatolja a hívó **saját blokkok** blokkot a kalap blokkhoz. Amikor a eléri a **saját blokkok** blokkot a projektben, a **saját blokkok** belsejében lévő csoport a megadott paraméterértékek alapján fog futni.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nCsatoljon egy csoport blokkot a **saját blokkok** értékhez, hogy definiálja a kalap blokkot a **saját blokkok** használatakor fellépő művelet beállításához.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Megjegyzés: Több Saját Blokkok létrehozása ugyanazokkal a címkékkel és változókkal hibákat okozhat a projekt letöltésekor.***\n\n## 1. Példa\n\nEbben a példában a robot a **saját blokkokat** használja, hogy:\n\n* Játssza le a sziréna hangját háromszor.\n* Hajtson előre 12 hüvelyket.\n* Játssza le a sziréna hangját háromszor.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_definition/sound_example.png)\n\n## 2. Példa\n\nEbben a példában a robot a **saját blokkokat** használja, hogy:\n\n* Hajtson előre 15 hüvelyket.\n* Írja ki az akkumulátor kapacitását, és mozgassa a kurzort egy új sorra az Agy képernyőjén.\n* Fordítsa a robotot 180 fokkal jobbra.\n* Írja ki az akkumulátor kapacitását, és mozgassa a kurzort egy új sorra az Agy képernyőjén.\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Véletlenszerű\n![random](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/random/random.png)\n\nVéletlenszerű értéket jelent a blokk legalacsonyabb és legmagasabb értéke között.\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **véletlenszerű** blokk hossza olyan blokkokba illeszkedik, amelyek befogadják a kör alakot.\n\nA **véletlenszerű** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nEz a példa **véletlenszerű** blokkot használ a hajtáslánc sebességének véletlenszerűsítésére.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nEz a példa **véletlenszerű** blokkot használ a várj blokk hosszának véletlenszerűsítésére.\n\n![random_control](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"rate_of_gyro":{"name":"rate_of_gyro","markdown":"# Giroszkóp mértéke\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ Giroszkóp szögsebességének mértékét.\n\n![rate_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **giroszkóp mértéke** **0 és 249.99 dps** közötti tartományt jelez.\n\nA **giroszkóp mértéke** fok per másodpercben (dps) van megadva.\n\nVálassza ki, hogy melyik giroszkópot használja.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nA **giroszkóp mértéke** jelentő blokkot reporter kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkokban használják.\n\n\n![rate_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_inserted.png)"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Maradék\n\nElosztja az első értéket a második értékkel, és jelent a maradékról.\n\n![remainder](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **maradék**blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nAz egyformán elosztott számok maradéka nullát jelez.\n\nA **maradék** blokk hossza olyan blokkokba illeszkedik, amelyek befogadják a kör alakú helyeket.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa elosztja a 7-et a 2-vel, és a fennmaradó részt \"1\"-ként írja ki a VEX IQ Agy képernyőjére.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Ismétlés\n\nEgy 'C' blokk, amely meghatározott számú alkalommal megismétli a benne lévő blokkokat.\n\n![repeat](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nElőször adjon meg egy értéket annak jelzésére, hogy a csoport hányszor vigye véghez az **ismétlés** blokkot a benne lévő blokkokkal.\n\nAz **ismétlés** 'C' blokk egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nA 'C' blokkok egymásba is helyezhetők. Ezt a koncepciót fészkelésnek hívják, amely időt takaríthat meg a különböző viselkedések programozásakor.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/repeat/repeat_select.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa megismétli a hanghatás lejátszását 3 másodpercenként 5 alkalommal.\n\n![repeat_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/repeat/repeat_example.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Ismételd, amíg\n\nEgy 'C' blokk, amely addig ismételgeti a belső blokkokat, amíg a logikai feltétel **igaz** értéknek nem lesz jelentve.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **ismételd, amíg** blokk csak a ciklus elején ellenőrzi a logikai feltételt.\n\nHa a logikai feltétel **hamis** értéknek lett jelentve, az **ismételd, amíg** blokkon belüli blokkok futni fognak.\n\nHa a logikai feltétel **igaz** értéknek lett jelentve, az **ismételd, amíg** blokkon belüli blokkok kimaradnak.\n\nAz **ismételd, amíg** A „C” blokk elfogadhatja a hatszögletű (hatoldalas) alakú blokkokat.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa kiírja az időzítő értékét a VEX IQ Agy képernyőre, és előre mozgatja a hajtásláncot, amíg a **pipa** gomb meg nem lesz nyomva a VEX IQ Agyon. A **pipa** gomb megnyomása után a hajtáslánc leáll.\n\n![repeat_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/repeat_until/repeat_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Időzítő visszaállítása\n\nVisszaállítja a VEX IQ Agy időzítőjét.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz Agy időzítője minden projekt elején elindul. Az **időzítő visszaállítása** blokkal az időzítő visszaállítható 0 másodpercre.\n\n## Példa\n\nEbben a példában az időzítő visszaáll 0-ra, mielőtt a hajtásláncot 3 másodpercig előre mozgatná. 3 másodperc elteltével a hajtáslánc leáll.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Forgásszög\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ giroszkóp aktuális forgási szögét fokban.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation.png](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **giroszkóp forgása** **pozitív** értéket jelez, amikor a giroszkóp az **óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba** fordul.\n\nA **giroszkóp forgása** **negatív** értéket jelez, amikor a giroszkóp érzékelő az **óramutató járásával megegyező irányba** fordul.\n\nVálassza ki, hogy melyik giroszkópot kell ellenőrizni.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_devices.png)\n\nA **giroszkóp forgása** jelentő blokkot kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkokban használják.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Kerekítés\n\nA bevitt értéket a legközelebbi egész számra kerekíti.\n\n![round](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/round/round.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAhol a tizedesjegyek legalább 0,5 értékűek vagy nagyobbak, a **kerekítés** felfelé történik, ahol kisebbek, mint 0,5, a **kerekítés** lefelé történik. \n\nA **kerekítés** blokk hossza olyan blokkokba illeszkedik, amelyek befogadják a kör alakú helyeket.\n\nA **kerekítés** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa kerekíteni fogja a 2.7-et, és \"3\"-t fog kiírni.\n\n![round_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# 2D lista beállítása\n\nA 2D lista minden elemét a megadott értékekre állítja.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\n2D lista létrehozásakor beállíthatja a lista **oszlopok** számát 1–10 elemre és a **sorok** számát is 1–10 elemre.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt 2D listát. A 2D lista átnevezhető vagy törölhető.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nA **2D lista beállítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Lista beállítása\n\nA lista minden értékét a megadott értékekre állítja.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA lista hosszát (1-10 elem) a lista létrehozásakor kell beállítani.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt listát. A lista átnevezhető vagy törölhető is.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nA **lista beállítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\nEz a példa a listát kezdeti értékekre állítja, majd a lista 3. elemét (90) jelenti a kar helyzetének beállításához.\n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Logikai változó beállítása\n\nLogikai változót állít be egy adott értékre.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt logikai változót. A logikai változókat át lehet nevezni vagy törölni is lehet.\n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nVálasszon logikai értéket.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nA **logikai változó beállítása** blokk hatszögletű (hatoldalú) alakú blokkokat képes elfogadni.\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_color_sensor_brightness":{"name":"set_color_sensor_brightness","markdown":"# Színérzékelő fényerejének beállítása\n\nBeállítja a VEX IQ színérzékelő fényének fényerejét.\n\n![set_color_sensor_light](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_light.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA színérzékelőnek van egy fényforrása, amely beállítható a tárgy színének vagy a felület fényerejének észleléséhez.\n\nA **színérzékelő fényerejének beállítása** **0% és 100%** közötti értéket fogad el. Minél magasabbra állítja a fény %-át, annál erősebben ragyog a színérzékelő fényforrása.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt színérzékelőt.\n\n![set_color_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor.png)\n\nA **színérzékelő fényerejének beállítása** blokk elfogadhat egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat.\n\n![set_color_sensor_2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_2.png)\n\n\n"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# Kurzor beállítása\n\nBeállítja a kurzor helyét a **kiír** blokkokban.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nÁllítsa be a kurzor sor- és oszloppozícióját úgy, hogy az összes **kiír** parancs egy adott helyen jelenjen meg a VEX IQ Agy képernyőn.\n\nA **kurzor beállítása** **1 és 5** közötti **sor** számot fogad el.\n\nA **kurzor beállítása** **1 és 21** közötti **oszlop** számot fogad el.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_cursor/row_column_index.png)  \n\nA **kurzor beállítása** blokk elfogadhat egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a kurzort a 3. sor 8. oszlopába állítja, mielőtt kiírná a \"Hello!\" szöveget az Agy képernyőjére.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_cursor/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_cursor/set_cursor_hello.png)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Menetirány beállítása\n\nBeállítja a hajtáslánc giroszkópjának irányértékét.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **menetirány beállítása** blokk segítségével beállíthatja a hajtáslánc helyzetét bármely adott óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba, ahogy az az alábbi képen látható.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nA **menetirány beállítása** **0 és 360** fok közötti tartományt fogad el.\n\nA **menetirány beállítása**blokk elfogadhat egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a robotot összesen 135 fokkal forgatja el:\n\n![setDriveHeading_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_example_revised.png)\n\n- Forduljon balra a 45 fokos irányba.\n- Állítsa be a robot jelenlegi helyzetét 0 fokos menetirányra.\n- Forduljon balra további 90 fokkal az előző mondat beállított irányértéke alapján.\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Forgatás beállítása\n\nBeállítja a hajtáslánc forgási szögét, ha VEX IQ giroszkóppal konfigurálják.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **forgatás beállítása** blokk segítségével beállítható a hajtáslánc forgási szöge bármely adott pozitív vagy negatív értékre.\n\nA **forgatás beállítása** blokk elfogadhat egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a robotot összesen 210 fokkal fogja elforgatni:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Forduljon balra (az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba) 120 fokos elforgatásig.\n- Állítsa be a robot aktuális helyzetét -45 fokos forgatásként.\n- Forduljon balra (az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba) további 90 fokkal (-45 fok és +45 fok) az előző mondatban beállított forgási érték alapján."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Hajtás leállításának beállítása\n\nBeállítja a hajtáslánc viselkedését, amint leáll.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\n* A **Fék** a motor azonnali leállítását eredményezi.\n* A **Forgás** hagyja, hogy a motor fokozatosan forogjon megállásig.\n* A **Tartás** hatására a motor azonnal leáll, és mozgatásakor visszaáll a leállított helyzetbe.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa arra készteti a hajtásláncot, hogy 3 másodpercig előre menjen, majd megállás után megtartsa a helyzetét.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Mozgás időkorlátjának beállítása\n\nIdőkorlátot határoz meg a hajtáslánc mozgásparancsainak.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA hajtáslánc időkorlátja arra szolgál, hogy megelőzze, hogy a helyzetüket el nem érő hajtóblokkok megakadályozzák a csoport többi blokkjának futását.\n\nPéldául a hajtáslánc nem éri el a helyzetét, amikor a robotot a falnak vezetik, és nem tudja befejezni a mozgását.\n\nA **mozgás időkorlátjának beállítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa 2 másodperc múlva fejezi be a **mozgás** parancsot, ha a hajtáslánc nem érte el a 24 hüvelykes célt. Az időkorlát vagy a távolság elérése után a hajtáslánc továbbhalad a **fordulj** parancsra.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Hajtás sebességének beállítása\n\nBeállítja a hajtáslánc sebességét.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **hajtás sebességének beállítása** csak a hajtáslánc sebességét állítja be, de a hajtásláncot nem fogja mozgatni. A **mozgás** blokk továbbra is szükséges.\n\nA **hajtás sebességének beállítása** **-100% és 100%** vagy **-127rpm és 127rpm** közötti skálát fogad el.\n\nHa a hajtáslánc sebességét negatív értékre állítja, a hajtáslánc hátramenetben fog mozogni.\n\nHa a hajtáslánc sebességét 0-ra állítja, a hajtáslánc leáll.\n\nA **hajtás sebességének beállítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEzzel a példával a hajtáslánc 50%-os sebességgel mozog 12 hüvelykre.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Giroszkóp irányának beállítása\n\nA giroszkóp aktuális irányát a parancsblokkban lévő értékre állítja.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **giroszkóp irányának beállítása** blokk segítségével beállíthatja a hajtáslánc helyzetét bármely adott óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba, ahogy az az alábbi képen látható.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_gyro_heading/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\nA **giroszkóp irányának beállítása** **0 és 360** fok közötti értéket fogad el.\n\nA **giroszkóp irányának beállítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nVálassza ki, hogy melyik giroszkópot használja.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Giroszkóp forgásának beállítása\n\nA VEX IQ giroszkóp forgásszögét a parancs mondatban beállított értékre állítja.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **giroszkóp forgásának beállítása** blokk segítségével beállítható a hajtáslánc forgási szöge bármely adott pozitív (óramutató járásával ellentétes irányú) vagy negatív (óramutató járásával megegyező irányú) értékre.\n\nA **giroszkóp forgásának beállítása** elfogad minden pozitív vagy negatív tizedes- vagy egész számtartományt.\n\nA **giroszkóp forgásának beállítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nVálassza ki, hogy melyik giroszkópot használja.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation_devices.png)\n\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 2D lista elemének cseréje\n\nÚj elemre frissíti a 2D lista elemét.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nÍrja be az elem sorának (első szám) és oszlopának (második szám) pozícióját a cserélendő listán.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt listát. A lista átnevezhető vagy törölhető is.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nAz **elem cseréje** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Elem cseréje\n\nFrissíti a lista egy elemét egy új értékre.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt listát. A lista átnevezhető vagy törölhető is.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nAz **elem cseréje** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n\nEz a példa frissíti a lista 2-es tételét 15-ös értékre, és a lista 2-es tételét kiírja a VEX IQ Agy képernyőre.\n\n![replace_item_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_item_of_array/replace_item_example.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Motor helyzetének beállítása\n\nBeállítja a VEX IQ Motor kódolójának helyzetét a megadott értékre.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **motor helyzete** blokk segítségével beállíthatja a motor helyzetét bármely adott értékre.\n\nÁltalában a **motor helyzete** blokkot használják a helyzet 0-ra állításához, hogy a motor jeladóját visszaállítsák.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nVálassza ki a mértékegységet fokban vagy fordulatokban.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Motor leállításának beállítása\n\nBeállítja a VEX IQ intelligens motor viselkedését, amint leáll.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\n* A **Fék** a motor azonnali leállítását eredményezi.\n* A **Forgás** hagyja, hogy a motor fokozatosan forogjon megállásig.\n* A **Tartás** hatására a motor azonnal leáll, és mozgatásakor visszaáll a leállított helyzetbe.\n\nA **motor leállításának beállítása** a projekt hátralévő részében az összes jövőbeli motorparancsra érvényes.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nVálassza ki a motor beállítását, miután leáll.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa arra készteti a Kar Motort, hogy 90 fokkal előre mozogjon, majd ellenálljon a külső erőknek (például a gravitációnak), hogy megtartsa pozícióját.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Motor időkorlátjának beállítása\n\nIdőkorlátot határoz meg a VEX IQ Intelligens Motor mozgásparancsokhoz.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA motor időkorlátja megelőzi azt, hogy a mozgásblokkok, amelyek nem érik el a helyzetüket, megakadályozzák a csoport többi blokkjának futását.Például egy motor nem éri el a helyzetét amiatt, mert egy kar vagy karom eléri a mechanikai határát, és nem tudja befejezni a mozgását.\n\nA **motor időkorlátjának beállítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa 2 másodperc múlva befejezi a **motor beállítása** parancsot, ha a Karom Motor nem érte el a 270 fokos helyzetet. Az időkorlát vagy a cél elérése után a Karom Motor 0 fokos helyzetbe fordul.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Motor nyomatékának beállítása\n\nBeállítja a VEX IQ intelligens motor erősségét.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **motor nyomatékának beállítása** **0% és 100%** közötti értéket fogad el.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nA **motor nyomatékának beállítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a Karom motort 40 fokos helyzetbe forgatja, csak 20%-os maximális nyomatékkal. Ez lehetővé teszi a karom számára, hogy megragadjon egy tárgyat anélkül, hogy túl nagy erővel károsítaná.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Motor sebességének beállítása\n\nBeállítja a VEX IQ intelligens motor sebességét.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **motor sebességének beállítása** **-100% és 100%** vagy **-127rpm és 127rpm** közötti skálát fogad el.\n\nHa a motor sebességét negatív értékre állítja, a motor hátrafelé fog forogni.\n\nHa a motor sebességét 0-ra állítja, a motor leáll.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nVálassza ki, hogy a sebesség %-ban vagy fordulat/perc (rpm) értékben legyen beállítva.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa azt mutatja meg, hogy a kar motor lassan forogjon 25%-os sebességgel 90 fokos helyzetbe.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Írás pontosságának beállítása\n\nBeállítja a tizedes vessző után megjelenő számjegyek számát, ha jelentő blokkokat ír ki a VEX IQ Agy képernyőjére.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki azt a pontosságot, amelyet a beszúrt jelentő blokkok kiírnak a képernyőre.\n\n* Egész számok (1) (Alapértelmezett)\n* Tizedek (0.1)\n* Századok (0.01)\n* Ezredek (0.001)\n* Minden számjegy (0.000001)\n\nA képernyőre írt jelentő blokkok a legközelebbi pontosságra kerekítenek. Például, az 1,67-et 2-nek írjuk Egész számok pontossággal, és 1,7-nek tizedes pontossággal.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_touchled_brightness":{"name":"set_touchled_brightness","markdown":"# Érintő LED fényerejének beállítása\n\nBeállítja a VEX IQ Érintő LED fényerejét.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **érintő LED fényerejének beállítása** **0% és 100%** közötti értéket fogad el.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt Touch LED-et.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor3](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_sensor3.png)\n\nAz **érintő LED fényerejének beállítása** blokk elfogadhat egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness2.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa zölden világítja meg az Érintő LED-et 25%-os fényerővel.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_touchled_color":{"name":"set_touchled_color","markdown":"# Érintő LED színének beállítása\n\nBeállítja a VEX IQ Érintő LED színét.\n\n![set_touchLED_color](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki, melyik **Érintő LED**-et szeretné használni.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_sensor.png)\n\nVálassza ki a megjeleníteni kívánt színt.\n\n![set_touchLED_color2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color2.png)\n\nAz **Érintő LED** kikapcsolásához állítsa a színt semmire.\n\nAz **Érintő LED** színét beállíthatja a színérzékelő által észlelt színre is.\n\n![set_touchLED_color3](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color3.png)"},"set_touchled_fade":{"name":"set_touchled_fade","markdown":"# Érintő LED elhalványulásának beállítása\n\nBeállítja, hogy a VEX IQ Érintő LED színe milyen gyorsan halványuljon a színek között.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt Érintő LED-et.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_sensor2.png)\n\nVálassza ki, hogy az Érintő LED mennyire halványuljon el.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_speed](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_speed.png)\n\n* Lassú - Az Érintő LED lassan új színűvé válik.\n* Gyors - Az Érintő LED gyorsan új színűvé válik.\n* Ki - Az Érintő LED azonnal színt vált.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa lassan kékre váltja az Érintő LED-et.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Fordulás sebességének beállítása\n\nBeállítja a hajtáslánc fordulatainak sebességét.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **fordulás sebességének beállítása** csak a hajtáslánc sebességét állítja be, de a hajtásláncot nem fogja mozgatni. A **fordulj** blokk továbbra is szükséges.\n\nA **fordulás sebességének beállítása** **-100% és 100%** vagy **-127rpm és 127rpm** közötti értéket fogad el.\n\nHa a hajtáslánc fordulás sebességét negatív értékre állítjuk, a hajtáslánc ellenkező irányba fordul.\n\nHa a hajtáslánc fordulás sebességét 0-ra állítjuk, a hajtáslánc leáll.\n\nA **fordulás sebességének beállítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a hajtásláncot lassan balra fordítja 25%-os sebességgel.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Változó beállítása\n\nEgy változót beállít egy adott értékre.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt változót. A változókat átnevezhetjük vagy törölhetjük is.\n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nA **változó beállítása** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa jelenti a VEX IQ távolságérzékelőt a \"változóm\" változóba, és a \"változóm\" segítségével állítja be a hajtáslánc sebességét.\n\n![set_variable_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_variable/set_variable_example.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Észlelt tárgy beállítása\n\nBeállítja az objektumot (az az objektum, amelyről további információkat szeretne megtudni) az észlelt objektumok számából.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **tárgyak száma**blokk használható az **észlelt tárgyak beállítása** blokk előtt az észlelt objektumok számának meghatározásához.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt látásérzékelőt.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nAz **észlelt tárgy beállítása** blokk elfogadhat egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat.\n\n\n\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Lista hossza\n\nJelzi a listában szereplő elemek számát.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt listát. A lista átnevezhető vagy törölhető is.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nA **lista hossza** jelentő blokk olyan blokkokba illeszkedik, amelyek befogadják a kör alakot.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# Pillanatkép\n\nPillanatképet készít a látásérzékelővel.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **pillanatkép** blokk rögzíti az aktuális képet a látásérzékelővel, hogy feldolgozza és elemezze a szín aláírásokat és kódokat.\n\nÁltalában egy **pillanatkép** szükséges, mielőtt bármilyen más látásérzékelő blokkot használna.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt látásérzékelőt.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt látás aláírását. A látás aláírásokait az Eszközök ablakban konfigurálhatjuk.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Pörgés\n\nPörgeti a VEX IQ intelligens motort, amíg le nem áll.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **pörgés** blokk örökké működtet egy motort, amíg új motorblokkot nem használnak, vagy a program le nem áll.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nVálassza ki a pörgetés irányát. Az iránynevek az Eszközök ablakban módosíthatók.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Forogj\n\nForgat egy VEX IQ intelligens motort egy adott távolságra.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **forogj** megmondja a motornak, hogy adott irányban haladjon egy adott távolságra attól a helytől, ahol éppen tartózkodik.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nVálassza ki a forgatás irányát. Az iránynevek az Eszközök ablakban módosíthatók.\n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nA **forogj** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nVálassza ki a mértékegységet fokban vagy fordulatokban.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nAlapértelmezés szerint más blokkok a **várj** parancsot teljesítik, amíg a motor meg nem áll.\n\nKiválaszthatja a nyilat, hogy kibővítse az **és ne várj** parancssal - You can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - ez más blokkok folytatását eredményezi, miközben a motor mozog.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Forogj helyzetbe\n\nA VEX IQ intelligens motort beállított helyzetbe forgatja.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **forogj helyzetbe** megmondja a motornak, hogy haladjon egy meghatározott helyzetbe. A motor pillanatnyi helyzete alapján a **forogj helyzetbe** meghatározza a forgás irányát.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nA **forogj helyzetbe** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nVálassza ki a mértékegységet fokban vagy fordulatokban.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nAlapértelmezés szerint más blokkok a **várj** parancsot teljesítik, amíg a motor abba hagyja a mozgást.\n\nKiválaszthatja a nyilat, hogy bővítse a **és ne várj** paranccsal - ez más blokkok folytatását eredményezi, miközben a motor mozog.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Állj meg\n\nLeállítja a hajtásláncot.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa 3 másodperc múlva leállítja a hajtásláncot.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Motor leállítása\n\nLeállítja a motort.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki, melyik motort állítsa le.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa 3 másodpercig nyitva forgatja a kar motorját, mielőtt leállna.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Kivonás\n\nKivon egy értéket a másikból, és jelenti a különbséget.\n\n![subtract](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **kivonás** tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat képes elfogadni.\n\nA **kivonás** blokk hossza olyan blokkokba illeszkedik, amelyek elfogadják a kör alakú helyeket.\n\nVonjon ki két számot.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nKivonás a változók értékeivel.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nKivonás érzékelők vagy eszközök értékeivel.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Időzítő értéke\n\nMásodpercek alatt beszámol a VEX IQ Agy időzítőjének értékéről.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz időzítő 0 másodpercnél indul, a program elindulásával egyidőben, és tizedesértékeket jelent.\n\nAz **időzítő értéke** jelentő blokkot kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkok belsejében használják.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa előre mozgatja a hajtásláncot, és 4,5 másodpercig hangeffektust játszik le, mielőtt 90 fokos fordulatot végezne.\n\n![timerValue_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/timer_value/timerValue_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Fordulj\n\nÖrökre forgatja a hajtásláncot.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **fordulj** blokk örökké forgatja a hajtásláncot, amíg egy új hajtáslánc blokkot nem használnak, vagy a program le nem áll.\n\nVálassza ki a hajtáslánc irányát.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Forduljon\n\nAdott távolságra forgatja a hajtásláncot.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki, hogy melyik irányba forduljon a hajtáslánc.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\nA **forduljon** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\nSzámos fok megadásával állítsa be a hajtáslánc elmozdulását.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nAlapértelmezés szerint más blokkok a **várj** parancsot teljesítik, amíg a hajtáslánc meg nem fordul.\n\nKiválaszthatja a nyilat, hogy kibővítse az **és ne várj** parancsra - ettől más blokkok tovább futnak, miközben a hajtáslánc megfordul.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Menetirányba fordulás\n\nA hajtásláncot egy meghatározott irányba fordítja, ha VEX IQ giroszkóppal van konfigurálva.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **menetirányba fordulás** blokk segítségével a hajtáslánc az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba fordulhat az alábbi képen látható módon.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nA giroszkóp jelenlegi iránya alapján a **menetirányba fordulás** határozza meg, hogy melyik irányba forduljon.\n\nA **menetirányba fordulás** **0.00 és 359.99** fok közötti skálát fogad el.\n\nA **menetirányba fordulás** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a hajtásláncot négy fordulatra készteti:\n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Balra (az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba) 45 fokra\n- Balra (az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba) 90 fokra\n- Balra (az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba) 270 fokra\n- Jobbra (az óramutató járásával megegyező irányba) 180 fokra\n\nAlapértelmezés szerint más blokkok a **várj** parancsot teljesítik, amíg a hajtáslánc meg nem fordul.\n\nKiválaszthatja a nyilat, hogy kibővítse az **és ne várj** paranccsal - ettől más blokkok tovább futnak, miközben a hajtáslánc megfordul.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Irányba fordulás\n\nA hajtásláncot egy meghatározott forgási szögbe fordítja, ha a VEX IQ giroszkóppal konfigurálják.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz **irányba fordulás** blokk segítségével a hajtáslánc egy adott pozitív (óramutató járásával ellentétes irányú) vagy negatív (óramutató járásával megegyező irányú) értékre állítható.\n\nA hajtáslánc aktuális **forgás** értéke alapján az **irányba fordulás** határozza meg, melyik irányba forduljon.\n\nAz **irányba fordulás** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a hajtásláncnak négy fordulatot ad:\n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Balra (az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba) 90 fokig\n- Balra (az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba) 180 fokig\n- Jobbra (jobbra) -45 fokig\n- Balra (az óramutató járásával ellentétes irányba) 0 fokig\n\nAlapértelmezés szerint más blokkok a **várj** parancsot teljesítik, amíg a hajtáslánc meg nem fordul.\n\nKiválaszthatja a nyilat, hogy kibővítse **és ne várj** parancsra - ez más blokkok folytatását eredményezi, miközben a hajtáslánc megfordul.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Változó\n\nJelzi a változóhoz rendelt értéket.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **változó** blokkok a változóban tárolt értékek jelentésére szolgálnak. A **változó beállítása** blokk segítségével állíthatja be vagy frissítheti egy változó értékét.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nA **változó** jelentő blokkot kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkokban használják.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nA változókat a **változó készítése** gombbal hozzák létre.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Motor sebessége\n\nJelzi a VEX IQ intelligens motor aktuális sebességét.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **motor sebessége** **-100% és 100%** vagy **-127rpm és 127rpm** közötti értéket jelez.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt motort.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nVálassza ki, hogy a sebességet %-ban vagy percenkénti fordulatszámban (rpm) adja-e meg.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nA **motor sebessége** jelentő blokkot kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkokban használják.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Tárgy észlelése\n\nJelzi az észlelt tárgyra vonatkozó információkat a látásérzékelő segítségével.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **tárgy észlelése** blokk használatához tegye a következőket:\n\n1. Konfigurálja a látásérzékelő készülékét az Eszközök ablakban.\n2. A **pillanatkép** használatával rögzítsen egy látásérzékelő képet, és keressen aláírási kódot/színkódot.\n3. Használja a **tárgy létezik** blokkot annak ellenőrzésére, hogy a látásérzékelő észlelte-e a kért aláírást/színkódot.\n\nMiután a látásérzékelő észlelt egy objektumot, más Vision blokkok segítségével többet tudhat meg az észlelt objektumról.\n\n* A **észlelt tárgy beállítása** segítségével állítsa be, melyik észlelt objektumról szeretne további információt megtudni. Alapértelmezés szerint a legnagyobb észlelt objektum kerül felhasználásra.\n* Használja a **tárgyak száma** annak meghatározásához, hogy hány objektumot észleltek a kért aláírásból/színkódból.\n* A **tárgy észlelése** segítségével határozhatja meg, mely információkat kell jelentenie az észlelt objektumból.\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt látásérzékelőt.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nVálassza ki, hogy mely értéket jelentse a látásérzékelő segítségével:\n\n* Szélesség - Az objektum szélessége pixelben. **2 - 316 px** közötti értéket ad vissza.\n* Magasság - Milyen magas az objektum pixelben. **2 - 212 px** közötti értéket ad vissza. \n* KözéppontX - Jelzi az észlelt objektum középpontjának X koordinátáját. **0 - 315 px** közötti értéket ad vissza.\n* KözéppontY - Jelzi az észlelt objektum középpontjának Y koordinátáját. **0 - 211 px** közötti értéket ad vissza.\n* Szög - Jelzi az észlelt objektum szögét. **0 - 180 degrees** közötti értéket ad vissza.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nA **tárgy észlelése** jelentő blokkot kör alakú helyekkel ellátott blokkokban használják.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Várj\n\nMeghatározott ideig vár, mielőtt áttérne a következő blokkra.\n\n![wait](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálasszon egy időtartamot a **várj** beállításához.\n\nA **várj** blokk tizedeseket, egész számokat vagy numerikus blokkokat fogadhat el.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa a **várj** 3,25 másodpercet után pirosról zöldre váltja a VEX IQ Érintő LED-et.\n\n![wait_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/wait/wait_example.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Várj, amíg\n\nVár egy logikai blokkra, hogy **igaz** értéket jelentsen, mielőtt a következő blokkra lép.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\n\nA **várj, amíg** újra ellenőrzi a logikai jelentő blokkot, és csak akkor lép át a következő blokkra, ha a logikai jelentő blokk **igaz** értéket jelez.\n\nA **várj, amíg** logikai blokk hatszögletű (hat oldalú) helyekkel ellátott blokkokat fogad el.\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa az Érintő LED-et sárgára váltja, és vár, amíg az Érintő LED megnyomódik. Miután megnyomta, az Agy kiírja, hogy \"Kész!\" az LCD-re.\n\n![wait_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/wait_until/wait_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"when_brain_button":{"name":"when_brain_button","markdown":"# Ha az Agy gomb\n\nA csatolt blokk csoportot futtatja, ha a kiválasztott VEX IQ Agy gombot megnyomják vagy elengedik.\n\n![when_brain_button](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_brain_button/when_brain_button.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt Agy gombot.\n\n![when_brain_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select.png)\n\nVálassza ki, melyik művelet váltja ki az eseményt - **megnyomva** vagy **elengedve** \n\n![when_brain_button_select_2](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select_2.png)  \n"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Amikor kapok\n\nFuttatja a csatolt blokk csoportot, ha a kiválasztott üzenet **adás** üzenetből érkezik.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki, hogy melyik üzenetet szeretné meghallgatni. Új üzenet is létrehozható.\n\nAz **amikor kapok** blokk csak **adás** vagy **közvetítés és várakozás** blokkból származik egy másik csoportban.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Példa\n\nEz a példa piros színnel jelenik meg a VEX IQ Érintő LED-en, majd vár két másodpercet, mielőtt az \"üzenet1\" üzenetet sugározná.\n\nMiután megkapta az üzenetet, az **amikor kapok** csoport előidézi a hajtáslánc előrehaladását, miközben ugyanakkor a kar motor felfelé mozog.\n\nA két csoport a piros nyilak által jelzve, ugyanabban az időben fut.\n\n![when_broadcast_example](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_example.png)\n\n"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Amikor az ütköző\n\nFuttatja a csatolt blokk csoportot, amikor a kiválasztott VEX IQ ütközőr megnyomják vagy elengedik.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt ütközőt.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nVálassza ki, melyik művelet váltja ki az eseményt - **megnyomva** vagy **elengedve** \n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Ha a Kontroller tengelye\n\nFuttatja a csatolt blokk csoportot, ha a kiválasztott VEX IQ Kontroller joystick tengelye elmozdul.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a vezérlő joystick tengelyét.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Amikor a Kontroller gomb\n\nA csatolt blokk csoportot futtatja, amikor a kiválasztott VEX IQ Kontroller gombot megnyomják vagy elengedik.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt Kontroller gombot.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_controller_button/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_controller_button/controller_button_back.png)\n\nVálassza ki, melyik művelet váltja ki az eseményt - **megnyomva** vagy **elengedve**\n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Kezdéskor\n\nFuttatja a csatolt blokk csoportot a projekt indításakor.\n\n![when_started](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **kezdéskor** esemény akkor indul, amikor a program elindul a VEX IQ Agy menüjéből, vagy a **futtatás** gombra kell nyomni a VEXcode IQ blokkokból.\n\nMinden új projekt automatikusan tartalmaz egy **kezdéskor** blokkot. A projektek akár 3 **kezdéskor** blokkot is tartalmazhatnak."},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Ha az időzítő\n\nFuttatja a csatolt blokk csoportot, ha a VEX IQ Agy időzítője nagyobb, mint a megadott érték.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nAz Agy időzítője minden projekt elején elindul.\n\nVálasszon egy időtartamot. A **ha az időzítő** esemény akkor fut, ha az Agy időzítője **több, mint** a megadott összeg.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nA **ha az időzítő** blokk képes tizedesjegyeket vagy egész számokat elfogadni.\n\nA **ha az időzítő** blokk nem képes más jelentő blokkokat elfogadni."},"when_touchled":{"name":"when_touchled","markdown":"# Amikor az Érintő LED\n\nFuttatja a csatolt blokk csoportot, amikor a kiválasztott VEX IQ Érintő LED-et megnyomják vagy elengedik.\n\n![when_touchLED](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_touchled/when_touchled.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nVálassza ki a használni kívánt Érintő LED-et.\n\n![when_touchLED_select](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_touchled/when_touchled_select.png)\n\nVálassza ki, melyik művelet váltja ki az eseményt - **megnyomva** vagy **elengedve** \n\n![when_touchLED_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/when_touchled/when_touchled_condition.png)"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Miközben\n\nEgy 'C' blokk, amely megismétli a belső blokkokat, miközben a logikai feltétel **igaz**.\n\n![while](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/while/while.png)\n\n## Hogyan kell használni\n\nA **miközben** blokk csak a ciklus elején ellenőrzi a logikai feltételt.\n\nHa a logikai feltétel **igaz** értékként van megadva, akkor a **miközben** belső blokkjai futni fognak.\n\nHa a logikai feltétel **hamis**, a **miközben** belső blokkjai átugrásra kerülnek.\n\nA **miközben** 'C' blokk képes elfogadni feltételként hatszögletű (hatoldalú) blokkokat.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/hu-HU/while/while_inserted.png)"}}},"pl":{"blocks":{"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Dodaj\n\nDodaje do siebie dwie dowolne wartości i podaje sumę.\n\n![add](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/add/add.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Dodaj** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok **dodaj** pasuje do bloków, które posiadają okrągłe wolne miejsca i mogą zawierać inne okrągłe bloki. \n\nDodawanie dwóch liczb.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nDodaj wartości ze zmiennych.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nDodaj wartości z czujników lub urządzeń.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/add/add_sensors.png)\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# I\n\nPotwierdza czy oba warunki logiczne są prawdziwe. \n\n![and](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/and/and.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **i** raportuje **prawda** kiedy oba warunki są **prawda**. \n\nBlok **i** raportuje **fałsz** kiedy jeden lub oba warunki są **fałsz**.\n\nBlok **i** raportuje **prawda** lub **fałsz** i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![and_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie sprawdzamy czy **OkoPrzednie** znajduje się bloko obiektu i ten obiekt jest czerwony.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nBlok **i** zwróci **prawda** kiedy zarówno **OkoPrzednie** jest blisko obiektu i **OkoPrzednie** wykrywa go jako czerwony.\n\nBlok **i** zwróci **fałsz** kiedy **OkoPrzednie** nie jest blisko obiektu, kiedy **OkoPrzednie** nie rozpoznaje go jako czerwonego lub oba.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/and/and_truth.png)"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Poziom baterii\n\nPodaje poziom naładowania baterii VEX IQ.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Battery level** podaje zakres od **0% do 100%**.\n\nBlok **battery level** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład odtworzy dźwięk alarmu, jeśli  **battery level** jest niższy niż 50%.\n\n![battery_capacity_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/battery_level/battery_capacity_example_revised.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Zmienna logiczna\n\nPodaje wartość zmiennej logicznej.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **zmienna logiczna** zwraca wartość **prawda** lub **fałsz** w zależności od przechowywanej wewnątrz zmiennej. Użyj bloku **set zmienna logiczna**, aby ustawić lub zaktualizować wartość zmiennej logicznej.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nBlok **zmienna logiczna** zmiennej logicznej zwraca **prawda** lub **fałsz** value i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nWartość logiczna jest tworzona po naciśnięciu przycisku **stwórz zmienną logiczną**.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png) \n"},"brain_button_pressed":{"name":"brain_button_pressed","markdown":"# Przycisk Mózgu wciśnięty\n\nZgłasza naciśnięcie przycisku na Mózgu VEX IQ.\n\n![button_pressed_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Brain button pressed** zwraca **true** kiedy wybrany przycisk Mózgu jest wciśniety.\n\n**Brain button pressed** zwraca **false** kiedy wybrany przycisk Mózgu jest nie wciśniety.\n\nWybierz przycisk mózgu, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![button_pressed_options](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_options.png)\n\nBlok **brain button pressed** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_inserted.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład sprawi, że robot pojedzie do przodu i skręci w prawo kiedy przycisk Mózgu **Up** jest naciśnięty.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_example_revised.png)\n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Przerwa\n\nPrzerywa istniejącą pętlę.\n\n![break](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/break/break.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nPo dodaniu do powtarzającego się bloku „C”, blok **przerwa** zakończy pętlę, w której się aktualnie znajduje.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład przesunie napęd do przodu i sprawdzi, czy przycisk VEX IQ Brain **up** jest naciśnięty. \n\nKiedy przycisk **up** jest **pressed**, blok **break** opuści pętlę  i zatrzyma układ napędowy.\n\n![break_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Jasność\n\nPodaje ilość światła wykrytą przez czujnik koloru VEX IQ.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Brightness of** podaje dane w zakresie **0% do 100%**.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika koloru chcesz użyć.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nBlok **brightness of** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Nadaj\n\nBlok nadaj nadaje komunikat aby odtworzyć wszystkie stosy zaczynające sie od **kiedy otrzymam**, bloki te oczekuja na nadawaną wiadomość.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nStos, który wysyła ** nadaj **, będzie nadal uruchamiał bloki w tym samym czasie, co inne stosy, które odbierają wiadomość.\n\nWybierz, która wwiadomość ma być nadana **nadaj**. Można również stworzyć nową wiadomość.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie dotykowy czujnik LED będzie czerwony, a następnie odczeka dwie sekundy przed nadaniem \"message1\". \n\nPo odebraniu wiadomości **when I receive** stos spowoduje, że układ napędowy będzie poruszał się do przodu, podczas gdy silnik kleszczy będzie poruszał się w górę w tym samym czasie.\n\nOba stosy będą nadal działać w tym samym czasie, jak wskazują czerwone strzałki.\n\n![broadcast_example_arrows](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/broadcast/broadcast_example_arrows.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Nadaj i czekaj\n\nNadaje wiadomośc, aby aktywować wszystkie stosy, które zaczynaja się od  **when I receive** blok ten czeka na otrzymanie wiadomości jednocześnie blokując resztę stosu.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nStos wysyłający zgłoszenie **broadcast and wait** zatrzyma się, aż inne stosy odbierające zgłoszoną wiadomość zostaną zakończone.\n\nWybierz wiadomość do **broadcast**. Można również utworzyć nową wiadomość.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie dotykowy czujnik LED będzie czerwony, a następnie odczeka dwie sekundy przed wysłaniem \"message1\". \n\nKiedy wiadomość jest odebrana **when I receive** stos spowoduje, że układ napędowy poruszy się do przodu i odtworzy efekt dźwiękowy.\n\nStos nadawczy będzie czekał, aż stos odbiorczy zostanie zakończony, zanim będzie kontynuował uruchamianie bloków, jak wskazują czerwone strzałki.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows_3](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows3.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Skalibruj żyroskop\n\nKalibracja czujnika żyroskopowego VEX IQ służy do zmniejszenia wartości odchylenia generowanej przez czujnik żyroskopowy.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nDryfowanie występuje, gdy czujnik żyroskopowy nieprawidłowo wykrywa ruch, mimo że czujnik się nie porusza.\n\n## Jak uźywać\n\nPodczas procesu kalibracji czujnik żyroskopowy musi pozostać nieruchomy.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika żyroskopowego chcesz użyć.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nWybierz, jak długo chcesz kalibrować. Im dłużej kalibrowany jest czujnik żyroskopowy, tym mniej dryfowania będzie występować.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_seconds](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_seconds.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Zmień zmienną\n\nZmienia zmienną o podaną wartość.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz zmienną, której chcesz użyć - wybranej zmiennej można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nBlok **zmień zmienną** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie zmieniamy zmienną, która ustawia prędkość napędu, o 10 za każdym razem gdy zotanie wykonana pętla **powtórz pętlę**.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Wyczyść wszystkie wiersze\n\nCzyści wszystkie wiersze w Konsoli.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nUżyj bloku **Wyczyść wszystkie wiersze** aby usunąć wszystkie linie w Konsoli\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie wyświetlasz \"Hello\" przez jedną sekundę a następnie czyścisz cały ekran przed wyświetlenniem \"Goodbye\".\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Wyczyść wiersz\n\nCzyści pojedynczy wiersz na ekranie VEX IQ.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **Clear row** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne z przedziału od **1 do 5**, aby ustawić wiersz do wyczyszczenia.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/clear_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie wyświetlimy \"Hello\" w wierszu 2 w kolumnie 1 przez 2 sekundy przed wyczyszczeniem wiersza.\n\n![clear_row_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/clear_row/clear_row_example.png)"},"color_detects_color":{"name":"color_detects_color","markdown":"# Wykrywanie koloru\n\nPodaje, czy czujnik koloru VEX IQ wykryje określony kolor.\n\n![color_detects](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/color_detects_color/color_detects.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Color detects** zwraca **true** kiedy czujnik koloru wykrył wybrany kolor.\n\n**Color detects** zwraca **false** kiedy czujnik koloru wykrył inny kolor niż ten wybrany.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika koloru chcesz użyć.\n\n![color_detects_chosen](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/color_detects_color/color_detects_chosen.png)\n\nWybierz kolor do wykrycia.\n\n![color_detects_selected](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/color_detects_color/color_detects_selected.png)\n\nBlok **color detects**  zwraca zmienną logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![color_detects_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/color_detects_color/color_detects_shape.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie zostanie wydrukowany „Kolor czerwony” lub „Inny kolor” w zależności od tego, czy czujnik koloru wykryje kolor „czerwony”.\n\n![color_detects_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/color_detects_color/color_detects_example.png)\n\n"},"color_of":{"name":"color_of","markdown":"# Kolor\n\nPodaje nazwę koloru wykrytego przez czujnik koloru VEX IQ.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/color_of/color_of_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Color of** zgłasza jeden z następujących kolorów: **red, red-violet, violet, blue-violet, blue, blue-green, green, yellow-green, yellow, yellow-orange, orange, or red-orange.**\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika koloru chcesz użyć.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/color_of/color_of_color.png)\n\nBlok **color of** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![color_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/color_of/color_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Komentarz\n\nUmożliwia programistom pisanie informacji pomagających opisać program.\n\n![comment_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nProfesjonalni programiści używają komentarzy w swoich programach, aby pomóc innym zrozumieć ich kod. Komentarze mogą również pomóc w rozwiązywaniu problemów i we współpracy.\n\nDodaj tekst do bloku **Comment**, najpierw wybierając przezroczysty prostokąt i usuwając istniejący tekst. Następnie wpisz nowy tekst.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nKomentarze nie zmieniają programu ani otaczających go bloków.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Kontroler jest aktywny/wyłączony\n\nWłącza lub wyłącza działania skonfigurowane przez kontroler w menu Urządzenia.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, czy chcesz włączyć, czy wyłączyć skonfigurowane akcje kontrolera, wybierając żądany stan z listy rozwijanej. Domyślnie kontroler jest włączony w każdym projekcie.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie, skonfigurowana akcja wykorzystuje zachowanie układu napędowego robota, ustawione przez konfigurację kontrolera w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nW tym przykładzie skonfigurowany kontroler będzie wyłączony podczas uruchamiania programu.\n\nNastępnie robot będzie jechał do przodu przez 6 cali.\n\nW końcu blok **controller enabled** umożliwi Kontrolerowi przywrócenie zachowania, podczas jazdy.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Natężenie prądu silnika\n\nPodaje natężenie prądu, które silnik VEX IQ aktualnie wykorzystuje w procentach (%) lub w amperach (amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Current of motor** podaje dane w zakresie **0% do 100%** lub **0.0 do 1.2 amps**. \n\nWybierz jaki silnik użyć.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nWybierz, czy natężenie prądu silnika jest podawany w % czy w amperach.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nBlok **current of motor** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Kolumna kursora\n\nPodaje numer kolumny, w której znajduje się kursor na ekranie Mózgu VEX IQ.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Cursor column** podaje zakres od **1 do 21**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/cursor_column/row_column_index.png)  \n\nBlok **cursor column** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie sprawdzimy czy pozycja **cursor column** jest większa niż 15. Jeśli pozycja jest większa niż 15, projekt ustawi kursor na wiersz 1, kolumny 1, a następnie wydrukuje napis „Hello”.\n\n![cursor_column_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/cursor_column/cursor_column_example_simple.png)\n\n"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Cursor row\n\nReports the row number of the VEX IQ Brain screen cursor's location.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Cursor row** reports a range from **1 to 5**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/cursor_row/row_column_index.png)\n\nThe reporter block **cursor row** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will check if the **cursor row** position is greater than 4. If the position is greater than 4, the project will set the cursor to row 1, column 1, and then print ‘Hello’.\n\n![cursor_row_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/cursor_row/cursor_row_example_simple.png)"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Odległość od\n\nPodaje odległość najbliższego obiektu od czujnika odległości VEX IQ.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Distance from** podaje dane w zakresie od **24mm do 1000mm** lub **1 cal do 40 cali**.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika odległości chcesz użyć.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nWybierz czy **distance from** ma być podawana w calach czy centymetrach\n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nBlok **distance from** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Podziel\n\nDzieli pierwszą wartość przez drugą wartość i podaje resztę.\n\n![divide](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Divide** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok **divide** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe wypełnienia, i mogą również zawierać okrągłe bloki.\n\nWprowadź liczby do podzielenia.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nPodziel przez wartości zmiennych.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nPodzielić przez wartość z czujników lub urządzeń.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n\n"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Jedź\n\nZaczyna poruszać napędem na zawsze.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **drive** uruchomi napęd, do momentu użycia nowego bloku na zawsze lub zatrzymania programu.\n\nWybierz kierunek, w którym będzie się poruszał układ napędowy.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Natężenie prądu w napędzie\n\nPodaje ilość prądu (mocy) aktualnie używanego przez układ napędowy.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive current** podaje dane w zakresie od **0% do 100%** lub **0.0 do 1.2 amps**. \n\nWybierz czy **drive current** ma być podawane w  % czy amperach (amps).\n\n![drive_current_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_current/drive_current_unit.png)\n\nBlok **drive current** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Jedź o\n\nPrzesuwa układ napędowy na zadaną odległość.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, w którym kierunku będzie się poruszał układ napędowy.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\nUstaw, jak daleko przesunie się układ napędowy, wprowadzając wartość i wybierając jednostkę miary (cale lub milimetry).\n\nBlok **Drive for** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nDomyślnie, inne bloki **wait** aż układ napędowy zakonczy ruch.\n\nMożna strzałka wybrać opcję **and don't wait** z listy rozwijanej - spowoduje to, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy układ napędowy będzie się poruszał.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Pozycja jazdy\n\nPodaje kierunek, w którym zwrócony jest układ napędowy\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive heading** podaje zakres od **0.00 do 359.99 degrees**.\n\nBlok **drive heading** porusza się w kierunku przeciwnym do ruchu wskazówek zegara, jak pokazano na poniższym obrazku.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_heading/TopDownBot01.png)\n\nBlok **drive heading** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Zakończona jazda\n\nZgłasza, czy układ napędowy zakończył ruch.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive is done** zwraca **true** kiedy silniki układu napędowego zakończą swój ruch.\n\n**Drive is done** zwraca **false** kiedy silniki układu napędowego dalej sie poruszają.\n\nBlok **drive is done** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Napęd się porusza\n\nInformuje czy układ napędowy jest w ruchu.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive is moving** zwraca **true** kiedy silniki  są w ruchu.\n\n**Drive is moving** zwraca **false** kiedy silniki nie ruszają się.\n\nBlok **drive is moving** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Obrót napędu w stopniach\n\nPodaje kąt obrotu układu napędowego w przypadku konfiguracji z czujnikiem żyroskopowym.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive rotation** zwraca **positive** kiedy napęd obraca się w **clockwise** .\n\n**Drive rotation** zwraca **negative** kiedy napęd obraca się w **counter-clockwise**.\n\nBlok **drive rotation** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Prędkość jazdy\n\nPodaje aktualną prędkość układu napędowego.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive velocity** podawana jest w zakresie od **-100% do 100%** lub **-127rpm do 127rpm**\n\nWybierz, czy prędkość jest podawana w %, czy w obrotach na minutę (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nBlok **drive velocity** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Równe z\n\nPodaje, czy pierwsza wartość jest taka sama lub równa drugiej wartości. \n\n![equal_to](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Equal to** zwraca **true** gdy te dwie wartości są dokładnie takie same\n\n**Equal to** zwraca **false** gdy te dwie wartości nie są takie same\n\nBlok **equal to** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok **equal to** zwraca zmienna logiczną **true** lub **false** i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscam.\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykładzie jazda zakończy się, jeśli odległość w mm wyniesie 500.\n\n![equal_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/equal_to/equal_to_example.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Bez końca\n\nBlok typu „C”, który bez końca wszystkie bloki zawarte w środku.\n\n![forever](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nUmieśc bloki w bloku **forever** aby te czynności powtarzały się **forever**.\n\nMożesz wyjść z pętli **forever**umiesszczając blok **break** wewnątrz.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nBloki typu'C' można również umieścić jeden w drugim. Pojęcie to nazywa się zagnieżdżaniem, które może pomóc zaoszczędzić czas podczas programowania różnych zachowań..\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład będzie odtwarzał ten sam efekt dźwiękowy co 5 sekund w nieskończoność.\n\n![forever_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/forever/forever_example.png)"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Funkcje\n\nWykonuje wybraną funkcję matematyczną.\n\n![function](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - wartośc absolutna\n* **floor** - zaokrągla w dół do najbliższej liczby całkowitej\n* **ceiling** - zaokrągla w górę do najbliższej liczby całkowitej\n* **sqrt** - pierwiastek kwadratowy\n* **sin** - sinus\n* **cos** - cosinus\n* **tan** - tanges\n* **asin** - arcsine lub odwrotność sinusa\n* **acos** - arccosine lub odwrotność cosinusa\n* **atan** - arctan lub odwrotność tangensa\n* **ln** - podstawa logarytmu naturalnego e\n* **log** - logarytm o podstawie 10\n* **e ^** - potęga e\n* **10 ^** - potęga 10\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **function** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWyberz mateematyczną **function** z listy opcji.\n\n![function_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/function/function_select.png)\n\nBlok **function** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe miejsca.\n\n![function_fit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Wiekse niż\n\nPodaje, czy pierwsza wartość jest większa niż druga wartość.  \n\n![greater_than](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Greater than** zwraca **true** gdy pierwsza wartość jest większa niż druga wartość.\n\n**Greater than** zwraca **false** gdy pierwsza wartość jest mniejsza lub równa drugiej wartości.\n\nBlok **greater than** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok **greater than** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false** i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie na ekranie VEX IQ Brain pojawi się napis „Poziom baterii dobry”, jeśli poziom naładowania baterii jest większy niż 75%.\n\n![greater_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/greater_than/greater_than_example.png)\n\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Kąt kursu\n\nPodaje aktualny kurs czujnika żyroskopowego VEX IQ w stopniach.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Gyro heading** podaje zakres od **0.00 do 359.99**.\n\nBlok **Gyro heading** zgłasza kurs przeciwny do ruchu wskazówek zegara, jak pokazano na poniższym obrazku.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/heading_of_gyro/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\nWybierz, który czujnik żyroskopowy chcesz sprawdzić.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nBlok **Gyro heading** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"hue_of":{"name":"hue_of","markdown":"# Odcień\n\nPodaje odcień koloru wykryty przez czujnik koloru VEX IQ.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/hue_of/hue_of_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Hue of** podawany jest w skali od **0 do 360**.\n\nWybierz czujnik koloru do sprawdzenia.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/hue_of/hue_of_color.png)\n\nBlok **hue of** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![hue_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/hue_of/hue_of_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Jeśli to \n\nBlok typu 'C' uruchamia bloki wewnątrz, jeśli warunek logiczny ma wartość **true**.  \n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **if then** 'C' sprawdzi warunek logiczny tylko raz.\n\nJeśli wartość logiczna jest **true**, blok wewnątrz **if then** zostanie wykonany.\n\nJeśli wartość logiczna jest **false**, blok wewnątrz **if then** zostanie pominięty.\n\nBlok **if then** może przyjąć sześciokątne (sześcioboczne) bloki jako warunek.\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład odtworzy efekt dźwiękowy za każdym razem, gdy zostanie naciśnięty przełącznik zderzaka VEX IQ.\n\nBlok typu 'C' **if then** może być „opanowanym” lub umieszczony w bloku zawsze, aby zapewnić, że efekt dźwiękowy będzie odtwarzany za każdym razem, a nie tylko raz.\n\n![if_then_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/if_then/if_then_example.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Jeśli to w przeciwnym razie\n\nBlok typu 'C' Block that uruchamia bloki wewnątrz pierwszej lub drugiej części ** if then else **, na podstawie zgłoszonej wartości logicznej.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **if then else** sprawdzi warunek logiczny tylko raz.\n\nJeśli wartość logiczna jest **true**, blok wewnątrz **if** zostanie wykonany.\n\nJeśli wartość logiczna jest **false**, blok wewnątrz **else** zostanie wykonany.\n\nBlok **if then else** akceptuje jako warunek sześciokątne (sześcioboczne) bloki.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie dioda dotykowa LED będzie zielona, jeśli zostanie naciśnięta i czerwona, gdy nie zostanie naciśnięta.\n\nBlok typu 'C' **If then else** można umieścić wewnatrz bloki pętli na zawsze, by sprawić, że dioda LED zmieni swój kolor więcej niz raz.\n\n![if_then_else_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/if_then_else/if_then_else_example.png)"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Element z listy 2D\n\nPodaje wartość elementu na liście 2D.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, której listy 2D chcesz użyć. Liście 2D można również zmienić nazwę lub usunąć.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nWprowadź lokalizację pozycji na liście: wiersz (pierwszy numer) i kolumna (druga liczba), która ma być raportowana. Tutaj zgłaszana jest pozycja o lokalizacji wiersz 2, kolumna 3 na liście 2D.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nBlok **item of 2D list** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Element z\n\nPodaje wartość danej pozycji na liście.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz listę, której chcesz użyć. Liście można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nWprowadź numer pozycji elementu na liście. Tutaj raportowana jest druga pozycja na liście (pozycja 2).\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nBlok **item of** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie ustawimy prędkość Napędu na wartość zapisaną w pozycji 3 mojej listy. Układ napędowy będzie teraz poruszał się do przodu z prędkością 90%.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Długośc listy 2D\n\nPodaje liczbę wierszy lub kolumn na liście 2D.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, której listy 2D chcesz użyć. Liście 2D można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nWybierz wartość do sprawdzenia. Lista 2D może raportować **rows** lub **columns**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nBlok **length of 2D list** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Mniej niż\n\nPodaje, czy pierwsza wartość jest mniejsza niż druga wartość.\n\n![less_than](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Less than** zwraca **true** gdy pierwsza wartość jest mniejsza niż druga wartość.\n\n**Less than** zwraca **false** gdy pierwsza wartość jest większa lub równa drugiej wartości.\n\nBlok **less than** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\nBlok **less than** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie zostanie wyświetlony komunikat „Słaba bateria!” na ekranie VEX IQ Brain, jeśli poziom naładowania baterii jest mniejszy niż 25%.\n\n![less_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/less_than/less_than_example.png)\n\n"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Ruch zakończony\n\nInformuje o zakończeniu ruchu wybranego silnika VR.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Jak uzywać\n\n**Motor is done** zwraca **true** kiedy wybrany silnik zakończy swój ruch.\n\n**Motor is done** zwraca **true** kiedy wybrany silnik nadal się porusza.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nBlok **motor is done** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\nBlok do zgłaszania zakończenia pracy silnika jest używany wewnątrz bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami na inne bloki.\n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Silnik sie obraca\n\nInformuje, czy wybrany silnik VR aktualnie się obraca.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Motor is spinning** zwraca **true** kiedy obraca się wybrany silnik.\n\n**Motor is spinning** zwraca **false** gdy wybrany silnik jest zatrzymany.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nBlok **motor is spinning** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Mnożenie\n\nMnoży dowolne dwie wartości i podaje iloczyn.\n\n![multiply](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Multiply** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok  **multiply** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki, i mogą również zawierać okrągłe bloki. \n\nPomnóż dwie liczby.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nPomnóż przez wartości zmiennych.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nPomnóż przez wartości z czujników lub urządzeń.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Ustaw kursor w następnym wierszu\n\nUstawia kursor, na ekranie mózgu, w następnym dostępnym wierszu.\n\n![next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nDomyślnie wszystkie projekty zaczynają się od kursora w wierszu 1, kolumnie 1. Blok **next row** przesunie kursor w dół o jeden wiersz na ekranie Mózgu.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/next_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład wydrukuje „Pierwsza wiadomość”, a następnie ustawi kursor w następnym dostępnym wierszu przed wydrukowaniem „Drugiej wiadomości”.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/next_row/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/next_row/set_cursor_welcome.png)\n"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# Nie\n\nPodaje przeciwieństwo (odwrotność) podanej wartości logicznej.\n\n![not](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/not/not.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **not** zwraca **true** kiedy wartośc logiczna wewnątrz to **false**.\n\nBlok **not** zwraca **false** kiedy wartośc logiczna wewnątrz to **true**.\n\nBlok **not** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład zwrróci **true** gdy przycisk „Check” na VEX IQ Brain nie jest wciśnięty.\n\n![not_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Liczba obiektów\n\nPodaje, ile obiektów wykrył czujnik wizyjny.\n\nObiekt będzie musiał zostać skonfigurowany przed użyciem bloku **object count**, by ten mógł go zydentyfikować.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika wizyjnego chcesz użyć.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nBlok **snapshot of** mosi zostać uzyty przed zastosowanieem bloku **object count**, by mógł opodać liczbę obiektów.\n\nBlok **object count** poda liczbę obiektów z ostatniego, zrobionego snapshota.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Objekt istnieje\n\nInformuje, czy czujnik wizyjny wykryje skonfigurowany obiekt.\n\nObiekt będzie musiał zostać skonfigurowany przed użyciem bloku **object exists**\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika wizyjnego chcesz użyć.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n**Object exists** zgłasza **true** kiedy czujnik wykryje skonfigurowany obiekt.\n\n**Object exists** zgłasza **false** kiedy czujnik nie wykryje skonfigurowanego obiektu.\n\nBlok **object exists** zgłasza zmienną logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nBlok **snapshot of** musi zostać użyty przed blokiem **object exists** który zgłasza wartość logiczną **true** lub **false**."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Wykryto obiekt\n\nInformuje, czy czujnik odległości widzi obiekt w swoim polu widzenia. \n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Jak używac\n\n**Object found** zwraca **true** gdy czujnik odległości wykryje obiekt lub powierzchnię w swoim polu widzenia.\n\n**Object found** zwraca **false** gdy czujnik odległości nie wykryje przedmiotu lub powierzchni.\n\nWybierz, który czujnik odległości ma być używany.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nBlok **object found** zwraca wartość logioczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"object_is_near":{"name":"object_is_near","markdown":"# Obiekt jest blisko\n\nInformuje, czy czujnik koloru VEX IQ wykryje obiekt w pobliżu.\n\n![object_is_near](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_is_near/object_is_near_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Object is near** zwraca **true** gdy czujnik koloru wykryje obiekt lub powierzchnię w pobliżu przedniej części czujnika.\n\n**Object is near** zwraca **false** gdy czujnik koloru wykryje pustą przestrzeń przed czujnikiem.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika koloru chcesz użyć.\n\n![object_is_near_color](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_is_near/object_is_near_color.png)\n\nBlok **object is near** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![object_is_near_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/object_is_near/object_is_near_inserted.png)\n\n\n "},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# Lub\n\nZwraca, jeśli spełniony jest jeden z dwóch warunków logicznych.\n\n![or](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/or/or.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **or** zwraca **true** gdy jeden (lub oba) z warunków są spełnione **true**. \n\nBlok **or** zwraca **false** gdy oba warunki są spełnione**false**.\n\nBlok **or** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** or **false**  i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\nBlok **or** zwraca **true** po naciśnięciu jednego (lub obu) zderzaka VEX IQ i diody LED VEX IQ i zwraca **false** tylko wtedy, gdy nie są wciśnięte ani zderzak, ani dotykowy czujnik LED.\n\n![or_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/or/or_truth.png)"},"play_note":{"name":"play_note","markdown":"# Zagraj nutę\n\nOdtwarza wybraną nutę.\n\n![play_note](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/play_note/play_note.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz nutę.\n\n![play_note_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/play_note/play_note_select.png)\n\nWybierz, jak długo (czas trwania) będzie odtwarzana nuta.\n\n![play_note_duration](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/play_note/play_note_duration.png)\n\n* **whole** nuta odtwarzana przez 1 sekundę (1000 millisekund)\n* **half** nuta odtwarzana przez 0.5 sekundy (500 millisekund)\n* **quarter** nuta odtwarzana przez 0.25 sekundy (250 millisekund)\n\nGdy nuta zacznie grać, następny blok rozpocznie się natychmiast."},"play_sound":{"name":"play_sound","markdown":"# Odtwórz dźwięk\n\nOdtwarza wybrany efekt dźwiękowy.\n\n![play_sound](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/play_sound/play_sound.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz efekt dźwiękowy z listy dostępnych opcji. \n\n![play_sound_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/play_sound/play_sound_select.png)\n\nGdy efekt zacznie być odtwarzany, następny blok rozpocznie się natychmiast."},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Pozycja kontrolera\n\nPodaje położenie joysticka na kontrolerze wzdłuż osi.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Position of controller** podajee zakres między **-100 a 100**.\n\n**Position of controller** zgłosi zero (0), gdy oś joysticka jest wycentrowana.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nWybierz oś joysticka, aby sprawdzić jego położenie.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nBlok **position of controller** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład będzie wielokrotnie sprawdzać oś joysticka kontrolera w celu sterowania prędkością silnika ramienia.\n\n![position_of_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Pozycja silnika\n\nPodaje odległość, jaką przebył silnik.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Position of motor** podaje położenie silnika VR w liczbach całkowitych dla stopni i liczbach dziesiętnych dla obrotów.\n\nWybierz silnik VR, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nWybierz, czy wartość jest podawana w stopniach czy ilościach obrotów.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nBlok **position of motor** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Naciśnięcie zderzaka\n\nInformuje o naciśnięciu włącznika zderzaka.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Pressing bumper** zwraca **true** jeśli włącznik zderzaka jest wciśnięty.\n\n**Pressing bumper** zwraca **false** jeśli włącznik zderzaka nie jest wciśnięty.\n\nWybierz, którego przełącznika zderzaka użyć.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nBlok **pressing bumper** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false**  i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Naciskanie kontrolera\n\nZgłasza naciśnięcie przycisku na kontrolerze VEX IQ.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Pressing controller** zwraca**true** czy wybrany przycisk kontrolera jest wciśnięty.\n\n**Pressing controller** zwraca **false** czy wybrany przycisk kontrolera nie jest wciśnięty.\n\nWybierz, którego przycisku kontrolera chcesz użyć.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nBlok **pressing controller** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład sprawdzi, czy przycisk E Up jest wciśnięty i czy obraca silnik kleszczy. \n\n![pressing_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_example_revised.png)"},"pressing_touchled":{"name":"pressing_touchled","markdown":"# Naciskanie czujnika dotykowego LED\n\nInformuje o naciśnięciu diody dotykowej LED VEX IQ.\n\n![pressing_touch_led](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Pressing Touch LED** zwraca **true** jeśli wybrana dioda jest naciśnięta.\n\n**Pressing Touch LED** zwraca **false** jeśli wybrana dioda nie jest naciśnięta\nWybierz, której diody dotykowejLED chcesz użyć.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_led](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_led.png)\n\nBlok **pressing Touch LED** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_inserted.png)\n\n"},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Wyświetl\n\nWyświetla wartości lub tekst na ekranie.\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/print/look_print.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **print** wydrukuje dane w miejscu kursora na ekranie Mózgu.\n\nWszystkie nowe projekty zaczynają się od kursora ekranowego w wierszu 1, kolumnie 1.\n\nWszystkie bloki reporterów będą domyślnie drukowane jako liczby całkowite (całkowite). Użyj bloku **set print precision** aby dostosować liczbę drukowanych miejsc dziesiętnych.\n\nDrukuj słowa i liczby.\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/print/print_words.png)\n\nWyświetl zgłoszoną wartość ze zmiennej.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nWyświetl wartość obliczeń.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nWyświetl wartość z czujnika lub urządzenia.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Moje bloki\n\nMoje bloki służą do tworzenia niestandardowych bloków.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**My blocks** służą do tworzenia sekwencji bloków, których można używać wielokrotnie w całym projekcie. \n\n**My blocks** tworzy się poprzez naciśnięcie przycisku **Make a Block**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**My blocks** mogą mieć wiele parametrów - etykiety tekstowe, zmienne numeryczne i zmienne logiczne - aby dodać więcej funkcji do niestandardowego bloku.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nAby użyć **my block**, dołącz **my block** do bloku \"kapeluszowego\". Kiedy blok **my block** zostaje zaczytany przez program, stok wewnątrz **my block** zostanie uruchomiony z określonymi wartościami parametrów.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nDołącz stos bloków do **my blocks** \"zdefiniuj\" blok \"kapeluszowy\", aby ustawić kacje, które maja być wykonane, gdy używany jest **my block**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Uwaga: Tworzenie wielu Moich bloków z tymi samymi etykietami i zmiennymi może powodować błędy podczas uruchamiania projektu na boisku.***\n\n## Przykład 1\n\nW tym przykładzie robot użyje bloku **my blocks** do:\n\n* Odtwórz dźwięk syreny 3 razy.\n* Jedź do przodu przez 12 cali.\n* Odtwórz dźwięk syreny 3 razy.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_call/sound_example.png)\n\n## Przykład 2\n\nW tym przykładzie robot użyje bloku **my blocks** do:\n\n* Jedź do przodu przez 15 cali\n* Drukuje pojemność baterii, a także przesuwa kursor do nowej linii na ekranie Mózgu\n* Obraca robota o 180 stopni w prawo\n* Drukuje pojemność baterii, a także przesuwa kursor do nowej linii na ekranie Mózgu\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Mój blok\n\nMoje bloki służą do tworzenia niestandardowych bloków.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**My blocks** służą do tworzenia sekwencji bloków, których można używać wielokrotnie w całym projekcie.\n\n**My blocks** można stworzyć przez przycisk **Make a Block**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**My blocks** może mieć wiele parametrów - etykiety tekstowe, zmienne numeryczne i zmienne logiczne - aby dodać więcej funkcji do niestandardowego bloku.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nAby użyć **my block**, dodaj **my block** do bloku \"kapeluszowego\". Kiedy **my block** zostanie osiągnięty w projekcie, stos wewnątrz **my block** będzie działać z określonymi wartościami parametrów.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nDołącz stos bloków do **my blocks** \"zdefinjuj\" blok \"kapeluszowy\", aby ustawić akcję, która ma miejsce, gdy **my block** jest używany.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Uwaga: utworzenie wielu Moich bloków z tymi samymi etykietami i zmiennymi może spowodować błędy podczas pobierania projektu.***\n\n## Przykład 1\n\nW tym przykładzie robot użyje **my blocks** do:\n\n* Odtwórz dźwięk syreny 3 razy.\n* Jedź do przodu przez 12 cali.\n* Odtwórz dźwięk syreny 3 razy.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/sound_example.png)\n\n## Przykład 2\n\nW tym przykładzie robot użyje **my blocks** do:\n\n* Jedź do przodu przez 15 cali\n* Wskazuje pojemność baterii, a także przesuwa kursor do nowej linii na ekranie Mózgu\n* Obraca robota o 180 stopni w prawo\n* Wskazuje pojemność baterii, a także przesuwa kursor do nowej linii na ekranie Mózgu\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Losowo\nPoodaje losową wartość między najwyższą a najwyższą warością w bloku.\n\n![random](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/random/random.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok  **losowo** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki.\n\nBlok **losowo** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nW tym przykładzie użyjemy bloku **losowo** aby losowo ustawić prędkość układu napędowego.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nW tym przykładzie użyjemy bloku **losowo** aby losowo określić długość bloku oczekiwania.\n\n![random_control](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"rate_of_gyro":{"name":"rate_of_gyro","markdown":"# Prędkość żyroskopu\n\nPodaje prędkość kątową czujnika żyroskopu VEX IQ.\n\n![rate_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Rate of gyro** przyjmuje zakres między **0 a 249.99 dps**.\n\n**Rate of gyro** podaje wartości w stopniach na sekundę (dps).\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika żyroskopowego chcesz użyć.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nBlok **rate of gyro** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami\n\n![rate_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_inserted.png)"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Reszta\n\nDzieli pierwszą wartość przez drugą wartość i podaje resztę\n\n![remainder](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **remainder** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nLiczby, które dzielą się równo, będą zgłaszać resztę zero.\n\nDługość bloku **remainder** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład podzieli 7 na 2, a resztę „1” wyświetli na ekranie Mózgu VEX IQ.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Powtórz\n\nBlok typu 'C'powtarza bloki zawarte w środku przez określoną liczbę razy.\n\n![repeat](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nNajpierw wprowadź wartość, aby określić, ile razy będzie się  stos wewnątrz **repeat**.\n \nBlok typu 'C' **repeat** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBloki typu 'C' można również umieścić jeden w drugim. Pojęcie to nazywa się zagnieżdżaniem, które może pomóc zaoszczędzić czas podczas programowania różnych zachowań.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/repeat/repeat_select.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład będzie powtarzał odtwarzanie efektu dźwiękowego co 3 sekundy 5 razy.\n\n![repeat_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/repeat/repeat_example.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Powtarzaj do\n\nBlok typu 'C, który powtarza bloki wewnątrz, aż zostanie wykonany warunek logiczny: **prawda**.  \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **repeat until** sprawdzi warunek logiczny tylko na początku każdej pętli.\n\nKiedy warunek logiczny jest zwrócony jako **fałsz**, bloki wewnątrz **repeat until** zostaną wykonane.\n\nKiedy warunek logiczny jest zwrócony jako **prawda**, bloki wewnątrz **repeat until** zostaną pominięte.\n\nBlok typu 'C' **repeat until** może przyjąć sześciokątne (sześcioboczne) bloki jako warunek.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład wydrukuje wartość timera na ekranie Mózgu VEX IQ i będzie napędał układ napędowy do przodu, aż przycisk **check** nie zostanie wciśniety. Kiedy przcisk **check** zostanie wciśnięty układ napędowy zatrzyma się\n\n![repeat_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/repeat_until/repeat_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Resetuj licznik\n\nResetuje licznik Mózgu robota.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nLicznik rozpoczyna pracę po urochumieniu projektu. Blok **reset timer** jest używany by zresetować licznik do 0s.\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie licznik czasu zostanie zresetowany przed przesunięciem układu napędowego do przodu przez 3 sekundy. Po upływie 3 sekund układ napędowy zatrzyma się.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Kąt obrotu\n\nPodaje aktualny kąt obrotu czujnika żyroskopowego w stopniach.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation.png](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Gyro rotation** zwraca wartość **positive** kiedy czujnik żyroskopowy obraca się w stronę**counter-clockwise**.\n\n**Gyro rotation** zwraca wartość **negative** kiedy czujnik żyroskopowy obraca się w stronę **clockwise**.\n\nWybierz, który czujnik żyroskopowy chcesz sprawdzić.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_devices.png)\n\nBlok **Gyro rotation** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Zaokrąglij\n\nZaokrągla wprowadzoną wartość do najbliższej liczby całkowitej.\n\n![round](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/round/round.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nLiczby dziesiętne o wartości 0,5 lub większej **round** są w górę, a mniejsze niż 0.5 **round** w dół.\n\nBlok **round** block pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki, i może również akceptować okrągłe bloki.\n\nBlok **round** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład zaokrągli 2,7 i przesunie robota VEX VR do przodu o „3” cale.\n\n![round_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Ustaw listę 2D na\n\nUstawia wszystkie pozycje na liście 2D na wprowadzone wartości.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nTworząc listę 2D, możesz ustawić liczbę **columns** między 1 a 10 a liczbę **rows** listy między 1 a 10.\n\nWybierz, której listy 2D chcesz użyć. Liście 2D można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nBlok **set 2D list to** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Ustaw listę na\n\nUstawia wszystkie pozycje na liście na wprowadzone wartości.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nPodczas tworzenia listy można ustawić długość listy od 1 do 10 elementów.\n\nWybierz listę, której chcesz użyć. Liście można również zmienić jej nazwę lub usunąć.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nBlok **set list to** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\nTen przykład ustawi listę na wartości początkowe, a następnie zgłosi pozycję nr 3 (90) z listy, aby ustawić pozycję Ramienia.\n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Ustaw zmienną logiczną\n\nUstawia zmienną logiczną na podaną wartość.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz zmienną logiczną, której chcesz użyć. Można również zmieniać nazwy lub usuwać zmienne logiczne.\n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nWybierz wartość logiczną.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nBlok **set boolean variable** akceptuje bloki o kształcie sześciokątnym (sześciobocznym).\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_color_sensor_brightness":{"name":"set_color_sensor_brightness","markdown":"# Ustaw koloru czujnika światła\n\nUstawia jasność światła czujnika koloru VEX IQ.\n\n![set_color_sensor_light](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_light.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nCzujnik koloru ma źródło światła, które można regulować, aby pomóc w wykrywaniu koloru obiektu lub jasności powierzchni.\n\n**Set color sensor light** akceptuje zakres od **0% do 100%**. Im wyższy % światła jest ustawiony, tym jaśniejsze będzie źródło światła czujnika koloru.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika koloru chcesz użyć.\n\n![set_color_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor.png)\n\nBlok **set color sensor light** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![set_color_sensor_2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_2.png)\n\n\n"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# Ustaw kursor\n\nUstawia położenie kursora dla bloku **print**.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nUstaw wiersz i kolumnę kursora na wszystkie komendy **print** (wyświetlać) w określonym miejscu na ekranie VEX IQ Brain.\n\n**Set cursor** akceptuje zakres **row** od **1 do 5**.\n\n**Set cursor** akceptuje zakres **column** od **1 do 21**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_cursor/row_column_index.png)  \n\nBlok **set cursor** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład ustawi kursor w wierszu 3, kolumnie 8 przed wydrukowaniem tekstu „Hello!” na ekranie Mózgu.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_cursor/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_cursor/set_cursor_hello.png)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Ustaw kierunek napędu\n\nUstawia wartość kursu żyroskopu.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlock **set drive heading** block można użyć do ustawienia pozycji zespołu napędowego na dowolny podany kierunek przeciwny do ruchu wskazówek zegara, jak pokazano na poniższym obrazku.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n**Set drive heading** akceptuje zakres od **0 do 360** stopni.\n\nBlok **set drive heading** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład obróci robota łącznie o 135 stopni:\n\n![setDriveHeading_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_example_revised.png)\n\n- Skręć w lewo do kierunku 45 stopni.\n- Ustaw aktualną pozycję robota jako kurs 0 stopni.\n- Skręć w lewo o dodatkowe 90 stopni w oparciu o ustawioną wartość kursu z poprzedniego bloku.\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Ustaw rotację\n\nUstawia kąt obrotu układu napędowego w przypadku konfiguracji z czujnikiem żyroskopowym VEX IQ.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **set drive rotation** można użyć do ustawienia kąta obrotu napędu na dowolną dodatnią lub ujemną wartość.\n\nBlok **set drive rotation** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład obróci robota łącznie o 210 stopni:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Obróć w prawo (zgodnie ze wskazówkami zegara) o rotację 120 stopni.\n- Ustaw aktualną pozycję robota jako obrót -45 stopni.\n- Obróć w prawo (zgodnie ze wskazówkami zegara) na dodatkowe 90 stopni (z -45 stopni do +45 stopni) na podstawie ustawionej wartości obrotu z poprzedniego bloku."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Ustaw zatrzymanie napędu\n\nUstawia zachowanie układu napędowego po zatrzymaniu się.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n* **Brake** spowoduje natychmiastowe zatrzymanie układu napędowego.\n* **Coast** pozwala układowi napędowemu obracać się stopniowo, aż do zatrzymania.\n* **Hold** spowoduje natychmiastowe zatrzymanie układu napędowego i powrót do pozycji zatrzymania, jeśli zostanie przesunięty.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje, że układ napędowy będzie poruszał się do przodu przez 3 sekundy, a następnie utrzyma tą pozycję po zatrzymaniu.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Ustaw limit czasu jazdy\n\nUstawia limit czasu dla poleceń ruchu układu napędowego.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nUstawienie limitu czasu jazdy układu napędowego, służy do zapobiegania blokom napędu, które nie osiągają swojej pozycji, uniemożliwiając pracę innych bloków w stosie.\n\nPrzykładem układu napędowego, który nie osiąga swojej pozycji, jest napotkanie ściany przez robota i niemożność zakończenia ruchu.\n\nBlok **set drive timeout** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład zakończy komendę **drive** po 2 sekundach, jeśli układ napędowy nie osiągnął celu 24 cali. Po osiągnięciu limitu czasu lub odległości układ napędowy przejdzie do **turn**.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Ustaw prędkość napędu\n\nUstawia prędkość układu napędowego.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Set drive velocity** ustawi tylko prędkość układu napędowego, ale nie spowoduje ruchu układu napędowego. Nadal wymagany jest blok **drive**.\n\n**Set drive velocity** akceptuje zakres **-100% do 100%** lub **-127rpm do 127rpm**.\n\nUstawienie prędkości układu napędowego na wartość ujemną spowoduje, że układ napędowy porusza się do tyłu.\n\nUstawienie prędkości na 0 spowoduje zatrzymanie układu napedowego.\n\nBlok **set drive velocity** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład sprawi, że układ napędowy będzie jechał z prędkością 50% przez 12 cali.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Ustaw kurs żyroskopu\n\nUstawia bieżącą pozycję kursu czujnika żyroskopowego na wartość z bloku poleceńk. \n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBloku **set gyro heading** można użyć do ustawienia pozycji zespołu napędowego na dowolny podany kierunek przeciwny do ruchu wskazówek zegara, jak pokazano na poniższym obrazku.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_gyro_heading/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\n**Set gyro heading** akceptuje zakres od **0 do 360** stopni.\n\nBlok **set gyro heading** block może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika żyroskopowego chcesz użyć.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Ustaw rotację żyroskopu\n\nUstawia kąt obrotu czujnika żyroskopowego VEX IQ na wartość ustawioną w bloku poleceń.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **set gyro rotation** może być użyty do ustawienia kąta obrotu zespołu napędowego na dowolną dodatnią (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara) lub ujemną (zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara) wartość.\n\n**Set gyro rotation** akceptuje zakres dowolnej dodatniej lub ujemnej liczby dziesiętnej lub całkowitej.\n\nBlok **set gyro rotation** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika żyroskopowego chcesz użyć.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation_devices.png)\n\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Zastąp pozycję listy 2D\n\nAktualizuje element na liście 2D do nowej wartości.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWprowadź pozycję wiersza (pierwszy numer) i kolumny (drugi numer) pozycji na liście, która ma zostać zastąpiona.\n\nWybierz listę, której chcesz użyć. Liście można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nBlok **replace item** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Zamień wartość\n\nAktualizuje pozycję na liście do nowej wartości.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nWybierz listę, której chcesz użyć. Liście można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nBlok **replace item** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n\nTen przykład zaktualizuje pozycję nr 2 na mojej liście do wartości 15 i wydrukuje pozycję nr 2 z mojej listy na ekranie mózgu VEX IQ.\n\n![replace_item_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_item_of_array/replace_item_example.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Ustaw pozycję silnika\n\nUstawia silnik robota VEX VR na wprowadzoną wartość.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **motor position** można użyć do ustawienia dowolnej pozycji silnika.\n\nZazwyczaj, blok **motor position** służy do ustawienia pozycji na 0, aby zresetować pozycję enkodera silnika.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nWybierz jednostkę miary w stopniach lub obrotach.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Ustaw zatrzymanie silnika\n\nUstawia zachowanie inteligentnego silnika VEX IQ po zatrzymaniu się.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n* **Hamulec** spowoduje natychmiastowe zatrzymanie silnika.\n* **Coast** pozwala silnikowi obracać się stopniowo, aż do zatrzymania.\n* **Zatrzymaj** spowoduje natychmiastowe zatrzymanie silnika i powrót do pozycji zatrzymania, jeśli zostanie przesunięty.\n\nBlok **set motor stopping** będzie obowiązywać dla wszystkich przyszłych poleceń silnika w pozostałej części projektu.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nWybierz ustawienie silnika po jego zatrzymaniu.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje, że silnik ramienia poruszy się do przodu o 90 stopni, a następnie oprze się siłom zewnętrznym (takim jak grawitacja), aby utrzymać swoją pozycję.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Ustaw limit czasu silnika\n\nUstawia limit czasu dla poleceń ruchu silnika robota VEX IQ.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nLimit czasu silnika służy do zapobiegania obrotom silnika, które nie osiągają swojej pozycji po określonym czasie, od zatrzymania kolejnych bloków w programie. Przykładem silnika, który nie osiąga swojej pozycji, jest ramię lub kleszcze, które osiągają swoje mechaniczne ograniczenie (maksimum zakresu ruchów) i nie mogą zakończyć ruchu.\n\nBlok **set motor timeout** może przyjmować wartości liczbowe jako dane wejściowe.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład zakończy polecenie ustalone dla silnika po 2 sekundach, jeśli silnik podnośnika nie osiągnie pozycji 270 stopni. Po osiągnięciu limitu czasu lub celu silnik podnośnika przesunie się do pozycji 0 stopni.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Ustaw moment obrotowy silnika\n\nUstawia siłę inteligentnego silnika VEX IQ.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Set motor torque** akceptuje zakres od **0% do 100%**.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nBlok **set motor torque** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie silnik kleszczy zostanie obrócony do pozycji 40 stopni z maksymalnym momentem obrotowym wynoszącym tylko 20%. Pozwala to kleszczom chwycić przedmiot bez uszkodzenia go przez użycie zbyt dużej siły.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Ustaw prędkość silnika\n\nUstawia prędkość obrotów silnika.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Set motor velocity** akceptuje zakres **-100% do 100%** lub **-127rpm do 127rpm**.\n\nUstawienie prędkości silnika na wartość ujemną spowoduje wirowanie silnika do tyłu.\n\nUstawienie prędkości silnika na 0 spowoduje, że silnik w ogóle się nie obraca.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nWybierz, czy prędkość jest ustawiona w %, czy w obrotach na minutę (obr / min).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład ustawi silnik podnośnika tak, aby powoli obracał się z prędkością 25% do pozycji 90 stopni.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Ustaw precyzję wydruku\n\nUstawia liczbę cyfr, które pojawiają się po przecinku podczas używania bloków drukowania do wyświetlania zmiennych i wartości w konsoli.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz poziom precyzji, z jakim wstawione bloki będą drukowane na ekranie.\n\n* Całości (1) (domyślnie)\n* Dziesiętne (0,1)\n* Setne (0,01)\n* Tysięczne (0,001)\n* Wszystkie cyfry (0,000001)\n\nWartości wydrukowane na wyświetlaczu zostaną zaokrąglone do najbliższego poziomu dokładności. Na przykład 1,67 zostanie wydrukowane jako 2 z dokładnością do jedności i 1,7 z dokładnością do dziesiątych.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_touchled_brightness":{"name":"set_touchled_brightness","markdown":"# Ustaw jasność diody LED\n\nUstawia poziom jasności diody dotykowej LED VEX IQ.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Set Touch LED brightness**  akceptuje zakres od **0% do 100%**.\n\nWybierz, której Touch LED chcesz użyć.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor3](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_sensor3.png)\n\nBlok **Set Touch LED brightness** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness2.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie dioda LED będzie świecić na zielono przyz jasnością 25%.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_touchled_color":{"name":"set_touchled_color","markdown":"# Ustaw kolor diody LED\n\nUstawia kolor diody dotykowej LED VEX IQ.\n\n![set_touchLED_color](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz, z której **Touch LED** chcesz korzystać.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_sensor.png)\n\nWybierz kolor, który będzie wyświetlany. \n\n![set_touchLED_color2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color2.png)\n\nAby wyłączyć **Touch LED**, ustaw kolor jako żaden.\n\nYMożesz także ustawik kolor **Touch LED** na ten wykryty przez czujnik koloru.\n\n![set_touchLED_color3](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color3.png)"},"set_touchled_fade":{"name":"set_touchled_fade","markdown":"# Ustaw zanikanie diody dotykowej LED\n\nOkreśla, jak szybko kolor diody  zanika między róznymi kolorami.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz, której diody LED chcesz użyć.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_sensor2.png)\n\nWybierz, jak szybko będzie gasnąć dioda dotykowa LED.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_speed](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_speed.png)\n\n* Wolno - Dotykowa dioda LED będzie powoli przybierać nowy kolor.\n* Szybko - dioda LED Touch szybko zgaśnie do nowego koloru.\n* Wył. - Dotykowa dioda LED natychmiast zmieni kolory.\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie dioda zmieni kolor na niebieski.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Ustaw prędkość skrętu\n\nUstawia prędkość skrętów układu napędowego.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Set turn velocity** ustawi prędkość układu napędowego, ale nie spowoduje ruchu układu napędowego. Blok **turn** jest nadal wymagany.\n\n**Set turn velocity** akceptuje zakres od **-100% do 100%** lub **-127rpm do 127rpm**.\n\nUstawienie prędkości skrętu napędu na wartość ujemną spowoduje, że napęd skręci w przeciwnym kierunku.\n\nUstawienie prędkości skrętu w napędzie na 0 spowoduje zatrzymanie napędu.\n\nBlok **set turn velocity** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje, że układ napędowy skręci powoli, z prędkością 25%, w lewo.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Ustaw zmienną\n\nUstawia zmienną na daną wartość.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz zmienną, której chcesz użyć. Zmiennym można również zmieniać nazwy lub je usuwać.\n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nBlok **set variable** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład zgłosi wartość czujnika odległości VEX IQ do zmiennej „moja zmienna” i użyje „moja zmienna” do ustawienia prędkości układu napędowego.\n\n![set_variable_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_variable/set_variable_example.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Ustal pozycję obiektu\n\nUstawia pozycję obiektu (obiektu, o którym chcesz uzyskać więcej informacji) z liczby wykrytych obiektów.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **object count** może zostać użyty przed blokiem **set vision object item** do określenia liczby wykrytych obiektów.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika wizyjnego chcesz użyć.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nBlok **set vision object item** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n\n\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Długość listy\n\nPodaje liczbę elementów na liście.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\nWybierz listę, której chcesz użyć. Liście można zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nBlok **length of list** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# Zrzut\n\nWykonuje zdjęcie - zrzut z czujnika wizyjnego.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **snapshot** przechwyci bieżący obraz z czujnika wizyjnego do przetworzenia i analizy pod kątem sygnatur i kodów kolorów.\n\nZazwyczaj blok **snapshot** jest wymagany przed użyciem jakichkolwiek innych bloków czujnika wizyjnego.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika wizyjnego chcesz użyć.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nWybierz sygnaturę wizji, której chcesz użyć. Sygnatury konfiguruje się w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Obracaj\n\nObraca silnik robota VEX VR Motor do zatrzymania.  \n\n![spin_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **spin** będzie uruchamiał silnik bez końca, dopóki nie zostanie użyty nowy blok silnika lub program nie zostanie zatrzymany.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nWybierz kierunek obrotu. Nazwy kierunków można zmienić w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Obracaj o\n\nObraca silnik robota VEX IQ o zadaną wartość.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Spin for** powie silnikowi, aby jechał w danym kierunku na określoną odległość od miejsca, w którym aktualnie się znajduje.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nChoose which direction to spin. Direction names can be changed in the Devices window. \n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nBlok **spin for** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWybierz jednostkę miary w stopniach lub obrotach.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nDomyślnie inne bloki będą **wait** do zakończenia pracy silnika.\n\nMożesz wybrać strzałkę, aby rozwinąć i uwzględnić **and don't wait** - spowoduje to, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy silnik się obraca.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Obróć do pozycji\n\nObraca silnik robota VEX VR do ustalonej pozycji.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Spin to position** powie silnikowi, aby obrócił się do określonej pozycji. Na podstawie aktualnej pozycji silnika, **spin to position** określi kierunek obrotu.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nBlok **spin to position** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWybierz jednostkę miary w stopniach lub obrotach.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nDomyślnie inne bloki będą **wait** do zakończenia akcji silnika.\n\nMożesz wybrać strzałkę, aby rozwinąć i uwzględnić **and don't wait** - spowoduje to, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy silnik się obraca.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Zatrzymaj jazdę\n\nZatrzymuje napęd.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład zatrzyma układ napędowy po 3 sekundach.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Zatrzymaj silnik\n\nZatrzymuje silnik.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz silnik do zatrzymania.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje otwarcie kleszczy na 3 sekundy przed zatrzymaniem.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Odejmowanie\n\nOdejmuje jedna wartość od drugiej i wyświetla różnicę.\n\n![subtract](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Subtract** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok **subtract** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki, i akceptuje również okrągłe bloki.\n\nOdejmij dwie liczby.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nOdejmij wartości od zmiennych.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nOdejmij wartości z czujników lub urządzeń.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Wartość licznika\n\nPodaje wartość licznika czasu w sekundach.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nLicznik czasu startuje od 0 sekund po uruchomieniu programu i podaje wartość licznika jako wartość dziesiętną.\n\nBlok **timer value** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład przesunie układ napędowy do przodu i odtworzy efekt dźwiękowy przez 4,5 sekundy przed wykonaniem skrętu o 90 stopni.\n\n![timerValue_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/timer_value/timerValue_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Skręć\n\nCały czas obraca układ napędowy.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **turn** będzie cały czas obracał napęd, do momentu użycia nowego bloku napędu lub zatrzymania programu.\n\nWybierz kierunek skrętu układu napędowego.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Obróć o\n\nObraca układ napędowy na zadaną odległość.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, w którym kierunku skręci się układ napędowy.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\nBlok **turn for** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nUstaw, jak daleko przesunie się układ napędowy, wprowadzając liczbę stopni.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nDomyślnie inne bloki będą **wait** dopóki układ napędowy nie skręci.\n\nMożesz wybrać strzałkę, aby rozwinąć opcje i wybrać **and don't wait** - spowoduje to, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy układ napędowy będzie się obracał.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Zmień pozycję do\n\nUstawia układ napędowy na określony kurs w przypadku konfiguracji z czujnikiem żyroskopowym VEX IQ.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **turn to heading** można użyć do obrócenia układu napędowego do dowolnego kierunku przeciwnego do ruchu wskazówek zegara, jak pokazano na poniższym obrazku.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nNa podstawie aktualnego kursu żyroskopu, **turn to heading** określi kierunek skrętu.\n\n**Turn to heading** akceptuje zakres **0.00 do 359.99** stopni.\n\nBlok **turn to heading** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje, że układ napędowy wykona cztery obroty:\n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- W lewo (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara) do 45 stopni\n- W lewo (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara) do 90 stopni\n- W lewo (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara) do 270 stopni\n- W prawo (zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara) do 180 stopni\n\nDomyślnie inne bloki będą **wait** dopóki układ napędowy nie skręci.\n\nMożesz wybrać strzałkę, aby rozwinąć opcje i wybrać **and don't wait** - spowoduje to, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy układ napędowy będzie się obracał.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Skręć do obrotu\n\nUstawia układ napędowy na określony kąt obrotu za pomocą wbudowanego czujnika żyroskopowego.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **turn to rotation** można użyć, aby ustawić układ napędowy na zadaną wartość dodatnią (zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara) lub ujemną (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara).\n\nNa podstawie obecnej wartości **rotation** napędu, **turn to rotation** określi kierunek skrętu.\n\nBlok **turn to rotation** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje, że układ napędowy wykona cztery obroty\n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- W lewo (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara) do 90 stopni\n- W lewo (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara) do 180 stopni\n- W prawo (zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara) do -45 stopni\n- W lewo (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara) do 0 stopni\n\nDomyślnie inne bloki będą **wait** dopóki układ napędowy nie skręci.\n\nMożesz wybrać strzałkę, aby rozwinąć opcjie i wybrać **and don't wait** - to spowoduje, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy układ napędowy będzie się obracał.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Zmienna\n\nPodaje wartość liczbową przypisaną do zmiennej.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBloki **Variable** służą do zgłaszania wartości liczbowej przechowywanej wewnątrz zmiennej. Użyj bloku **set variable** aby ustawić lub zaktualizować wartość liczbową zmiennej.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nBlok **variable** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nZmienne są tworzone przy użyciu przycisku **Make a Variable**.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Prędkość silnika\n\nPodaje aktualną prędkość inteligentnego silnika VEX IQ.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Velocity of motor** podaje zakres między **-100% a 100%** lub **-127rpm a 127rpm**.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nWybierz, czy prędkość jest podawana w %, czy w obrotach na minutę (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nBlok **velocity of motor** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Vision obiekt\n\nPodaje informacje o wykrytym obiekcie z czujnika wizyjnego.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nAby użyć bloku **Vision object**, wykonaj następujące kroki:\n\n1. Skonfiguruj czujnik wizyjny za pomocą okna Urządzenia.\n2. Użyj bloku **snapshot** aby uchwycić obraz z czujnika wizyjnego i poszukać kodu podpisu / koloru.\n3. Użyj bloku **object exists** aby sprawdzić, czy czujnik wizyjny wykrył żądany kod podpisu / koloru.\n\nGdy czujnik wizyjny wykryje obiekt, możesz użyć innych bloków wizyjnych, aby dowiedzieć się więcej o wykrytym obiekcie.\n\n* Użyj bloku **set vision object item** aby ustawić, o którym wykrytym obiekcie chcesz uzyskać więcej informacji. Domyślnie używany jest największy wykryty obiekt.\n* Użyj bloku **object count** aby określić, ile obiektów zostało wykrytych z żądanego kodu podpisu / koloru.\n* Użyj bloku **vision object** aby określić, które informacje z wykrytego obiektu zgłosić.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika wizyjnego chcesz użyć.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nWybierz, którą wartość raportować z czujnika wizyjnego:\n\n* Szerokość - szerokość obiektu w pikselach. Zwraca wartość **2 - 316 pikseli**.\n* Wysokość - wysokość obiektu w pikselach. Zwraca wartość **2 - 212 pikseli**.\n* CenterX - zgłasza współrzędną X środka wykrytego obiektu. Zwraca wartość **0 - 315 pikseli**.\n* CenterY - podaje współrzędną Y środka wykrytego obiektu. Zwraca wartość **0 - 211 pikseli**.\n* Kąt - podaje kąt wykrytego obiektu. Zwraca wartość **0 - 180 stopni**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nBlok **vision object** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Czekaj\n\nCzeka przez określony czas, zanim przejdzie do następnego bloku.\n\n![wait](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz czas **wait**.\n\nBlok **wait** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie dioda LED  zmieni kolor z czerwonego na zielony po 3,25 sekundy **waiting**.\n\n![wait_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/wait/wait_example.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Czekaj do\n\nCzeka na zwrócenie od bloku logicznego **prawda** przed przejściem do następnego bloku.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Wait until** będzie wielokrotnie sprawdzać blok wartości logicznej i nie przejdzie do następnego bloku, dopóki wartość logiczna nie zwróci **prawda**.\n\nBlok logiczny **wait until** akceptuje bloki o kształcie sześciokątnym (sześciobocznym).\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie dioda LED zmieni kolor na żółty i będzie czekać, aż zostanie naciśnięta. Po naciśnięciu Mózg wyświetli „Gotowe!” na wyświetlaczu LCD.\n\n![wait_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/wait_until/wait_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"when_brain_button":{"name":"when_brain_button","markdown":"# Kiedy przycisk Mózgu\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków po naciśnięciu lub zwolnieniu wybranego przycisku Mózgu VEX IQ.\n\n![when_brain_button](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_brain_button/when_brain_button.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz przycisk mózgu, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![when_brain_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select.png)\n\nWybierz, które działanie wywoła zdarzenie - **wciśnięcie** lub **zwolnienie**\n\n![when_brain_button_select_2](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select_2.png)  \n"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Kiedy otrzymam\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków, gdy wybrana wiadomość zostanie odebrana z bloku **broadcasted**.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz wiadomość, której chcesz słuchać. Można również utworzyć nową wiadomość.\n\nBlok **when I receive** zostanie uruchomiony tylko z bloku **broadcast** lub **broadcast and wait** w innym stosie.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład podświetli na czerwono diodę VEX IQ, a następnie odczeka dwie sekundy przed nadaniem „wiadomości1”.\n\nPo odebraniu wiadomości blok **when I receive** w stosie spowoduje, że układ napędowy przesunie się do przodu, podczas gdy silnik ramienia będzie poruszał się w górę w tym samym czasie.\n\nOba stosy będą nadal działać w tym samym czasie, jak wskazują czerwone strzałki.\n\n\n![when_broadcast_example](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_example.png)\n\n"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Kiedy zderzak\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków po naciśnięciu lub zwolnieniu wybranego czujnika zderzaka.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, którego przełącznika zderzaka użyć.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nWybierz, które działanie wywoła zdarzenie - **pressed** lub **released** \n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Kiedy oś kontrolera\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków, gdy wybrana oś joysticka kontrolera VEX IQ jest przesuwana.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz, której osi joysticka kontrolera chcesz użyć.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Gdy przycisk kontrolera\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków po naciśnięciu lub zwolnieniu wybranego przycisku kontrolera VEX IQ.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz przycisk kontrolera, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_controller_button/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_controller_button/controller_button_back.png)\n\nWybierz, które działanie wywoła zdarzenie - **wciśnięcie** lub **zwolnienie**\n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Po uruchomieniu\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków podczas uruchamiania projektu.\n\n![when_started](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nZdarzenia **When started** zostaną uruchomione, gdy program zostanie uruchomiony z menu  Mózgu VEX IQ lub przyciskiem **run** w blokach.\n\nWszystkie nowe programy będą automatycznie zawierać blok **when started**. Projekty mogą obsługiwać do 3 bloków **when started**."},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Kiedy zegar\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków, gdy licznik czasu mózgu V5 jest większy niż podana wartość.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nLicznik czasu zaczyna się na początku każdego projektu.\n\nWybierz czas. Blok wydarzenia **when timer** uruchomi się, gdy zegar Mózgu jest ustawiony **greater than** na daną wartość.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nBlok **when timer** może akceptować wartości dziesiętne lub całkowite.\n\nBlok **when timer** nie może akceptować innych bloków."},"when_touchled":{"name":"when_touchled","markdown":"# Kiedy dioda dotykowa LED\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków po naciśnięciu lub zwolnieniu wybranej diody LED.\n\n![when_touchLED](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_touchled/when_touchled.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz, której diody dotykowej LED chcesz użyć.\n\n![when_touchLED_select](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_touchled/when_touchled_select.png)\n\nWybierz, które działanie wywoła zdarzenie - **wciśnięcie** lub **zwolnienie**\n\n![when_touchLED_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/when_touchled/when_touchled_condition.png)"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Kiedy\n\nBlok typu 'C' powtarza bloki wewnątrz, podczas gdy zwrócony jest warunek logiczny **prawda**.  \n\n![while](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/while/while.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **while** sprawdzi warunek logiczny tylko na początku każdej pętli.\n\nKiedy wartość logiczna jest zwrócona jako **prawda**, bloki wewnątrz **while** zostaną uruchomione.\n\nKiedy wartość logiczna jest zwrócona jako **fałsz**, bloki wewnątrz **while** zostaną pominięte.\n\nBlok typu 'C' **while** może przyjąć sześciokątne (sześcioboczne) bloki jako warunek.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/pl/while/while_inserted.png)"}}},"ru":{"blocks":{"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Сумма\n\nСумма двух объектов.\n\n![add](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/add/add.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Сумма** производится между десятичными, целыми и числовыми блоками.\n\nБлок **суммы** может быть включён в блоки с овальными рамками для аргументов и может принимать в качестве значений такие же овальные блоки.\n\nСумма двух чисел.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nСумма числа и переменной.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nСумма числа и значений, получаемых с датчиков и устройств.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# Логическое И\n\nВыражение возвращает правду, если оба аргумента оператора И - правда.\n\n![and](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/and/and.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **и** возвращает **правду** в случае, если оба значения **правда**. \n\nБлок **и** возвращает **ложь** в случае, если хотя бы один из блоков **ложь**.\n\nЛогический блок **и** возвращает **правду** или **ложь** и может быть помещён в блоки, содержащие шестиугольные рамки.\n\n![and_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере рассматривается проверка одновременного нажатия двух кнопок на пульте управления.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nБлок **логического И** вернёт **правду** в случае, если обе кнопки на пульте управления (**Кнопка E Up пульта управления** и **Кнопка L Down пульта управления**) будут нажаты.\n\nБлок **логического И** вернёт **правду** в случае, если хотя бы одна или обе кнопки пульта управления не будут нажаты.\n\nТаблица истинности.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/and/and_truth.png)"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Уровень заряда аккумулятора\n\nВозвращает текущее значение заряда аккумулятора контроллера.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Уровень заряда аккумулятора** возвращает значение **от 0% до 100%**.\n\nБлок **уровня заряда аккумулятора** может быть использован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере будет воспроизводиться звук тревоги на контроллере в случае, если **уровень заряда аккумулятора** будет меньше 50%.\n\n![battery_capacity_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/battery_level/battery_capacity_example_revised.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Логическая переменная\n\nСоздаёт переменную логического типа.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **логической переменной** возвращает значение **правды** или **лжи**, хранящееся внутри переменной. Используйте блок **установки логической переменной** для обновления или изменения значения переменной.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nБлок **логической переменной**  - логический и возвращает **правду** или **ложь**, и может использоваться в блоках, содержащих шестиугольные вставки.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nЛогическая переменная создаётся с помощью кнопки **Создать логическую переменную**.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"brain_button_pressed":{"name":"brain_button_pressed","markdown":"# Нажатие кнопки контроллера\n\nСообщает о нажатии кнопки контроллера.\n\n![button_pressed_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Нажатие кнопки контроллера** возвращает **правду**, если будет нажата кнопка на контроллере.\n\n**Нажатие кнопки контроллера** возвращает **ложь**, если не будет нажата кнопка на контроллере.\n\nВыберите кнопку на контроллере, которую будете использовать.\nChoose which Brain button to use.\n\n![button_pressed_options](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_options.png)\n\n**Нажатие кнопки контроллера** - логический блок, который возвращает **правду** или **ложь**. Блок может быть использован в других блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_inserted.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере робот будет ехать вперёд и повернёт направо после нажатия кнопки **Вверх**.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_example_revised.png)\n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Прервать\n\nНезамедлительно заканчивает текущий цикл.\n\n![break](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/break/break.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПри добавлении в блок цикла (блок 'C') блок **прервать** незамедлительно заканчивает выполнение цикла.  \n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере тележка будет ехать вперёд, ожидая нажатие кнопки **вверх** на контроллере.\n\nВ случае нажатия кнопки **вверх** на контроллере, блок **прерывания** остановит бесконечный цикл и, соответственно, тележку. \n\n![break_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Количество яркости\n\nВозвращает количество отраженного света, полученного датчиком цвета VEX IQ.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nЗначение **количества яркости** лежит в пределах **от 0% до 100%**.\n\nВыберите датчик цвета.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nБлок **количества яркости** используется внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Передача сообщения\n\nПередача сообщения для активации действий, заложенных внутри блока **когда получил**.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **передачи сообщения** используется для параллельного выполнения действий внутри основного блока и блока приёма сообщений.\n\nВыберите сообщение для **передачи сообщения** или создайте новое сообщение.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере датчик Touch LED загорится красным цветом и будет ждать две секунды перед отправкой \"message1\".\n\nПосле отправки сообщения, действия внутри блока **когда получил** и действия в основной программе будут выполняться одновременно.\n\n![broadcast_example_arrows](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/broadcast/broadcast_example_arrows.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Передать сообщение и ждать\n\nБлок аналогичен блоку **передачи сообщений**, но при использовании данного блока действия внутри **когда получил** блока и основной программы будут выполняться последовательно, а не параллельно.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПри использовании блока **передать сообщение и ждать**, остальные блоки программы будут ожидать выполнения действий внутри блока **когда получил**.\n\nВыберите сообщение для **передачи сообщения** или создайте новое сообщение.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере датчик Touch LED загорится красным цветом и будет ждать две секунды перед отправкой \"message1\".\n\nПосле отправки сообщения, действия внутри блока **когда получил** и действия в основной программе будут выполняться в следующем порядке: сначала тележка проедет вперёд 12 дюймов и заиграет сирена, после чего начнёт свою работу схват робота.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows_3](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows3.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Калибровка гироскопа\n\nКалибрует VEX IQ гироскоп для уменьшения влияния дрифта (получения показаний датчика в состоянии покоя).\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nДрифт гироскопа - изменение показаний гироскопа в состоянии покоя.\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nГироскоп должен оставаться неподвижным в режиме калибровки.\n\nВыберите гироскоп для использования.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nВыберите длительность калибровки. Чем дольше гироскоп калибруется, тем меньше влияние дрифта на показания при работе.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_seconds](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_seconds.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Изменить переменную\n\nИзменяет значение переменной на предложенное значение.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите переменную, которую необходимо изменить. Выбранная переменная может быть переименована или удалена.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nБлок **изменения переменной** может содержать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере значение переменной, соответствующее скорости, изменяется на 10 каждый раз при прохождении **повторяющегося цикла**.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Очистка всех строк\n\nОчистка всех строк на контроллере.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **очистки всех строк** не сбрасывает текущее положении курсора. Для изменения положения курсора необходимо использовать блок **установки курсора**.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере на экране будет напечатана надпись \"Hello\", а через секунду экран будет очищен, после чего появится надпись \"Goodbye\".\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Очистить строку\n\nОчистка одной строки на экране контроллера.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **очистки строки** работает с целыми числами **от 1 до 5**, означающими номер очищаемой строки.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/clear_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере будет напечатана надпись \"Hello\" на второй строке в первой колонке и через три секунды строка будет очищена.\n\n![clear_row_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/clear_row/clear_row_example.png)"},"color_detects_color":{"name":"color_detects_color","markdown":"# Определение цвета\n\nСообщает об обнаружении датчиком цвета определённого цвета.\n\n![color_detects](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/color_detects_color/color_detects.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **определения цвета** возвращает **правду**, если датчик цвета обнаружил искомый цвет.\n\nБлок **определения цвета** возвращает **ложь**, если датчик цвета не обнаружил искомый цвет или обнаружил цвет отличный от искомого.\n\nВыберите датчик цвета для использования.\n\n![color_detects_chosen](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/color_detects_color/color_detects_chosen.png)\n\nВыберите искомый цвет.\n\n![color_detects_selected](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/color_detects_color/color_detects_selected.png)\n\nБлок **определения цвета** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![color_detects_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/color_detects_color/color_detects_shape.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере в случае обнаружения датчиком красного объекта будет напечатана фраза \"Color Red\". В случае отсуствия красного объекта будет выведена фраза \"Other Color\".\n\n![color_detects_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/color_detects_color/color_detects_example.png)\n\n"},"color_of":{"name":"color_of","markdown":"# Имя цвета\n\nВозвращает имя цвета, обнаруженного датчиком цвета.\nReports the name of the color detected by the VEX IQ Color Sensor.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/color_of/color_of_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **имён цветов** возвращает следующие цвета: **red, red-violet, violet, blue-violet, blue, blue-green, green, yellow-green, yellow, yellow-orange, orange, or red-orange.**\n\nВыберите датчик цвета для использования.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/color_of/color_of_color.png)\n\nБлок **имени цвета** может быть использован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![color_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/color_of/color_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Комментарий\n\nПозволяет разработчику оставлять пояснения для своей программы.\n\n![comment_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПрофессиональные разработчики используют комментарии на протяжении всей программы для облегчения понимания своего кода другими разработчиками. Комментарии также могут помочь в поиске ошибок.\n\nДля добавления текста в блок **комментария** необходимо удалить предыдущий текст.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nКомментарии никак не влияют на выполнение программы.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Включить/выключить пульт управления\n\nВключает или отключает связь с пультом управления контроллером.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите статус пульта управления при соединении с устройством. По умолчанию, связь с пультом управления всегда активирована.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nРабота трансмиссии в данном примере происходит без участия пульта управления.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nВ начале программы связь между пультом и контроллером отключается.\n\nРобот проезжает вперёд шесть дюймов.\n\nПосле движения робота связь с пультом управления активируется.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Ток привода\n\nВозвращает значение тока привода для текущего момента работы в процентах (%) или амперах (А).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **тока привода** возвращает значения в диапазонах **от 0% до 100%** или **от 0.0 до 1.2 А**. \n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nВыберите привод, значение тока с которого вы бы хотели получить.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nБлок **тока привода** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Столбец курсора\n\nВозвращает номер столбца на экране контроллера, в которой стоит курсор.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **столбца курсора** возвращает значения **от 1 до 21**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/cursor_column/row_column_index.png)  \n\nБлок **столбца курсора** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере проверяется положение курсора по отношению к столбцам. Если столбец курсора больше 15, то курсор будет установлен в первую строку первого столбца, после чего будет напечатана надпись \"Hello\".\n\n![cursor_column_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/cursor_column/cursor_column_example_simple.png)\n\n"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Строка курсора\n\nВозращает значение строки, в которой установлен курсор.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **строки курсора** возвращает значения **от 1 до 5**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/cursor_row/row_column_index.png)\n\nБлок **строки курсора** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере проверяется положение курсора по отношению к строкам. Если строка курсора больше 4, то курсор будет установлен в первую строку первого столбца, после чего будет напечатана надпись \"Hello\".\n\n![cursor_row_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/cursor_row/cursor_row_example_simple.png)"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Расстояние до объекта\n\nСообщает о расстоянии до ближайшего объекта от датчика расстояния.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **расстояния до объекта** считывает показания в диапазоне **от 24мм до 1000мм** или **от 1 до 40 дюймов**. \n\nВыберите датчик расстояния для использования.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nВыберите единицу измерения расстояния: миллиметры или дюймы.\n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nБлок **расстояния до объекта** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Деление\n\nОперация делит первое значение на второе для получения частного.\n\n![divide](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Деление** работает с десятичными, целыми или числовыми блоками.\n\nБлок **деления** может быть включён в блоки с овальными рамками для аргументов и может принимать в качестве значений такие же овальные блоки. \n\nВведите числа, с которыми необходимо произвести операцию деления.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nДеление между переменными.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nДеление значений, получаемых с различных устройств.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Движение\n\nЗапускает непрерывное движение трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **движения** запускает непрерывное движение трансмиссии до тех пор, пока не будет использован другой блок для трансмиссии или программа не будет остановлена.\n\nВыберите направление движения для запуска трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Ток трансмиссии\n\nВозвращает значение тока трансмиссии для текущего момента работы в процентах (%) или амперах (А).\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **тока трансмиссии** возвращает значения в диапазонах **от 0% до 100%** или **от 0.0 до 1.2 А**. \n\nВыберите единицу измерения тока: проценты (%) или амперы (А).\n\n![drive_current_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_current/drive_current_unit.png)\n\nБлок **тока трансмиссии** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Движение на расстояние\n\nРеализует проезд трансмиссии на определённое расстояние.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите направление движения трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\nУстановите числовое значение расстояния и выберите единицу измерения (миллиметры или дюймы).\n\nБлок **движения на расстояние** принимает десятичные, целые и числовые значения..\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nПо умолчанию остальные блоки **ждут** остановки трансмисии.\n\nВы можете выбрать из раскрывающегося списка **и не ждать** для того, чтобы параллельно с движением выполнялись другие блоки.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Курс движения\n\nСообщает о текущем направлении движения трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Курс движения** возвращает значения **от 0.00 до 359.99 градусов**.\n\nБлок **курс движения** сообщает об увеличении угла при вращении против часовой стрелки как показано на рисунке ниже.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_heading/TopDownBot01.png)\n\nБлок **курс движения** спользуется внутри блоков, имеющих овальные вставки.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Движение закончено\n\nСообщает об окончании движения трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **движение закончено** возвращает **правду**, когда приводы трансмиссии закончили свою работу.\n\nБлок **движение закончено** возвращает **ложь**, когда приводы трансмиссии всё ещё работают.\n\nБлок **движение закончено** - логический и возвращает **правду** или **ложь**, и может использоваться в блоках, содержащих шестиугольные вставки.\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Движение продолжается\n\nСообщает о движении трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **движение продолжается** возвращает **правду**, когда приводы трансмиссии работают.\n\nБлок **движение продолжается** возвращает **ложь**, когда приводы остановились.\n\nБлок **движение продолжается** - логический и возвращает **правду** или **ложь**, и может использоваться в блоках, содержащих шестиугольные вставки.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Вращение движения\n\nСообщает об угле вращения трансмисии в соответствии с настройками гироскопа.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **вращение движения** возвращает **положительное** значение в случае поворота трансмиссии **по часовой стрелке**.\n\nБлок **вращение движения** возвращает **отрицательное** значение в случае поворота трансмиссии **против часовой стрелке**.\n\nБлок **вращение движения** может использовать в своей структуре овальные блоки.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Скорость трансмиссии\n\nВозвращает текущее значение скорости трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **скорости трансмисии** возвращает значения в диапазонах **от -100 до 100 %** или **от -127 до 127 об/мин**.\n\nВыберите единицу измерения возвращаемого значения в процентах (%) или оборотах в минуту (об/мин).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nБлок **скорости трансмисии** может использоваться в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Сравнение\n\nСообщает равно ли первое значение второму. \n\n![equal_to](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **сравнения** возвращает **правду**, когда значения равны.\n\nБлок **сравнения** возвращает **ложь**, когда значения не равны.\n\nБлок **сравнения** десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nБлок **сравнения** - логический, возвращает **правду** или **ложь** и используется в блоках, содержащих шестигольные рамки.\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере на экране контроллера будет напечатано \"Drivetrain Stalled\", если ток трансмиссии будет равен 100%.\n\n![equal_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/equal_to/equal_to_example.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Бесконечный цикл\n\n'C' подобный блок цикла бесконечно запускает блоки внутри себя.\n\n![forever](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПоместите блоки в **бесконечный цикл** для повторения этих блоков **бесконечно**.\n\nДля выхода из **бесконечного цикла** вы можете использовать блок **прервать**.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\n'C' подобные блоки могут быть помещены друг в друга. Данная концепция называется \"вложенностью\", которая обеспечивает более разнообразное поведение роботов.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере звуки будут воспроизводиться бесконечно каждые пять секунд.\n\n![forever_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/forever/forever_example.png)"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Математические операции\n\nРаботает в соответствие с выбранной функцией.\n\n![function](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - модуль числа\n* **floor** - округляет в меньшую сторону до ближайшего целого числа\n* **ceiling** - округляет в большую сторону до ближайшего целого числа\n* **sqrt** - корень из числа\n* **sin** - синус\n* **cos** - косинус\n* **tan** - тангенс\n* **asin** - арксинус\n* **acos** - арккосинус\n* **atan** - арктангенс\n* **ln** - натуральный логарифм по основанию e (экспонента)\n* **log** - десятичный логарифм по основанию 10\n* **e ^** - возведение e (экспоненты) в степень\n* **10 ^** - возведение десяти (10) в степень\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **математических операций** принимает десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nВыберите нужную **математическую операцию** из списка.\n\n![function_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/function/function_select.png)\n\nБлок **математических операций** может быть использован в блоках с овальной вставкой.\n\n![function_fit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Больше\n\nСообщает больше ли значение слева по сравнению со значением справа.  \n\n![greater_than](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **больше** возвращает **правду**, когда первое значение больше второго. \n\nБлок **больше** возвращает **ложь**, когда первое значение меньше или равно второму. \n\nБлок **больше** принимает десятичные, целый или числовые блоки.\n\nБлок **больше** - логический и возвращает **правду** или **ложь**, и может использоваться в блоках, содержащих шестиугольные вставки.\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере на экране контроллера будет напечатано \"Battery level good\", если уровень заряда аккумулятора выше, чем 75%.\n\n![greater_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/greater_than/greater_than_example.png)\n\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Угол курса\n\nВозвращает значение курса гироскопа в градусах.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **угла курса** возвращает значение в диапазоне **от 0.00 до 359.99**.\n\nБлок **угла курса** сообщает об увеличении угла при вращении против часовой стрелки как показано на рисунке ниже.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/heading_of_gyro/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\nВыберите гироскоп для считывания показаний.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nБлок **угла курса** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"hue_of":{"name":"hue_of","markdown":"# Оттенок цвета\n\nВозвращает значение оттенка цвета.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/hue_of/hue_of_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **оттенка цвета** возвращает значения в диапазоне **от 0 до 360**.\n\nВыберите датчик цвета для использования.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/hue_of/hue_of_color.png)\n\nБлок **оттенка цвета** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![hue_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/hue_of/hue_of_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Если тогда\n\n'C' подобный блок запускает блоки внутри себя, если условие после \"если\" правдиво.\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **если тогда** в первую очередь проверяет условие. \n\nЕсли условие **правда**, то выполняются блоки внутри **если тогда**.\n\nЕсли условие **ложь**, то блоки внутри **если тогда** пропускаются и управление передаётся дальше.\n\nБлок **если тогда** может принимать шестиугольные блоки в качестве условия.\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере мелодия будет проигрываться каждый раз при нажатии датчика касания.\n\nБлок **если тогда** может быть вложен внутрь бесконечного цикла для повтора воспроизведения мелодии при нажатии бесконечное число раз вместо одного раза.\n\n![if_then_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/if_then/if_then_example.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Если тогда иначе\n\n'C' подобный блок **если тогда иначе** запускает блоки в первой или второй части в зависимости от условия.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **если тогда иначе** в первую очередь проверяет условие. \n\nЕсли условие **правда**, то выполняются блоки внутри **если тогда**.\n\nЕсли условие **ложь**, то выполняются блоки внутри **иначе**.\n\nБлок **если тогда иначе** может принимать шестиугольные блоки в качестве условия.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере датчик TouchLED загорится зелёным в случае нажатия и красным в противоположном случае.\n\nВ случае установки блока внутри бесконечного цикла, датчик TouchLED будет менять цвета в зависимости от нажатия бесконечное число раз.\n\n![if_then_else_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/if_then_else/if_then_else_example.png)"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Элемент двумерного массива\n\nВозвращает значение элемента двумерного массива.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите двумерный массив, который вы бы хотели использовать. Кроме того, двумерный массив может быть удалён или переименован.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nВведите номер строки (первое число) и номер столбца (второе число) элемента, значение которого вы бы хотели получить. В этом примере выбран элемент из второй строки и третьего столбца.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nБлок **элемента двумерного массива** принимает значения десятичных, целых или числовых блоков.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Элемент списка\n\nВозвращает значение элемента выбранного списка. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите список. Список может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nВведите номер элемента в списке. В данном примере выбран второй элемент списка. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nБлок **элементов списка** принимает десятичные, целый или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере скорость трансмиссии будет равна значению третьего элемента списка. Теперь трансмиссия движется вперёд со скоростью 90%.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Длина 2D списка\n\nВозвращает число строк или столбцов двумерного списка.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите 2D список. Двумерный список может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nВыберите значение, которое необходимо узнать. Двумерный список может сообщить число **строк** или **столбцов**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nБлок **длины 2D списка** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Меньше\n\nСообщает меньше ли значение слева по сравнению со значением справа.  \n\n![less_than](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **меньше** возвращает **правду**, когда первое значение меньше второго. \n\nБлок **меньше** возвращает **ложь**, когда первое значение больше или равно второму. \n\nБлок **меньше** принимает десятичные, целый или числовые блоки.\n\nБлок **меньше** - логический и возвращает **правду** или **ложь**, и может использоваться в блоках, содержащих шестиугольные вставки.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере на экран контроллера выводится надпись \"Low Battery!\" в случае, если уровень заряда аккумулятора меньше 25%.\n\n![less_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/less_than/less_than_example.png)\n\n"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Остановка привода\n\nСообщает о завершении движения выходного вала привода.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **остановки привода** возвращает **правду**, если привод закончил выполнение движения.\n\nБлок **остановки привода** возвращает **ложь**, если привод продолжает выполнение движения.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nБлок **остановки привода** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Вращение привода\n\nСообщает о движении выходного вала привода.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **вращения привода** возвращает **правду**, если привод продолжает выполнение движения.\n\nБлок **вращения привода** возвращает **ложь**, если привод закончил выполнение движения.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nБлок **вращения привода** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Умножение\n\nПроизводит умножение двух указанных значений.\n\n![multiply](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Умножение** принимает десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nБлок **умножения** может быть включён в блоки с овальными рамками для аргументов и может принимать в качестве значений такие же овальные блоки. \n\nУмножение двух чисел.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nУмножение переменных.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nУмножение показаний устройств.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Следующая строка\n\nУстанавливает вывод на экране контроллера на следующую строку.\n\n![next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПо умолчанию, курсор установлен в первой строке первого столбца. Блок **следующей строки** сдвигает курсор на одну строку вниз.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/next_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере будет напечатано сообщение \"First message\", после чего произойдёт переход на следующую строку для печати сообщения \"Second Message\".\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/next_row/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/next_row/set_cursor_welcome.png)\n"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# Отрицание\n\nВозвращает противоположное значение для указанного логического блока.\n\n![not](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/not/not.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **отрицания** возвращает **правду**, когда блок внутри содержит **ложь**.\n\nБлок **отрицания** возвращает **ложь**, когда блок внутри содержит **правду**.\n\nЛогический блок **отрицания** возвращает **правду** или **ложь** и может быть помещён в блоки, содержащие шестиугольные рамки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере будет возвращено значение **правды**, если галочка на контроллере не будет нажата.\n\n![not_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Число объектов\n\nВозвращает число объектов, обнаруженных камерой. \n\nОбъекты должны быть определены заранее для их обнаружения камерой с помощью блока **числа объектов**.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите камеру для использования.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nПеред использованием блока **числа объектов** необходимо воспользоваться блоком **получения снимка**.\n\nБлок **числа объектов** определяет число объектов, полученного из последнего снимка.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Существование объекта\n\nСообщает о наличии объекта перед камерой.\n\nОбъекты должны быть определены заранее для их обнаружения камерой с помощью блока **существования объекта**.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите камеру для использования.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\nБлок **существования объекта** возвращает **правду**, если камера обнаружила объект.\n\nБлок **существования объекта** возвращает **ложь**, если камера не обнаружила объект.\n\nБлок **существования объекта** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками. \n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nПеред использованием блока **существования объекта** необходимо воспользоваться блоком **получения снимка**."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Наличие объекта\n\nСообщает о наличии объекта перед датчиком расстояния.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **наличия объекта** возвращает **правду**, если в диапазоне действия датчика расстояния находится объект.\n\nБлок **наличия объекта** возвращает **ложь**, если в диапазоне действия датчика расстояния нет объекта.\n\nВыберите датчик расстояния для использования.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nБлок **наличия объекта** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"object_is_near":{"name":"object_is_near","markdown":"# Близость объекта\n\nСообщает о наличии объекта перед датчиком цвета.\n\n![object_is_near](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_is_near/object_is_near_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **близости объекта** возвращает **правду**, если на небольшом расстоянии перед дачтиком есть объект.\n\nБлок **близости объекта** возвращает **ложь**, если перед датчиком нет объекта.\n\nВыберите датчик цвета для использования.\n\n![object_is_near_color](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_is_near/object_is_near_color.png)\n\nБлок **близости объекта** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![object_is_near_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/object_is_near/object_is_near_inserted.png)\n\n\n "},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# Или\n\nВыражение возвращает правду, если хотя бы один из аргументов - правда.\n\n![or](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/or/or.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **или** возвращает **правду** в случае, если хотя бы одно значение **правда**. \n\nБлок **или** возвращает **ложь** в случае, если оба значения **ложь**.\n\nЛогический блок **или** возвращает **правду** или **ложь** и может быть помещён в блоки, содержащие шестиугольные рамки.\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nБлок **или** вернёт **правду**, если хотя бы один из датчиков касания будет нажат и **ложь**, если они оба не будут нажаты.\n\n![or_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/or/or_truth.png)"},"play_note":{"name":"play_note","markdown":"# Играть ноту\n\nПроигрывает выбранную ноту.\n\n![play_note](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/play_note/play_note.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите музыкальную ноту.\n\n![play_note_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/play_note/play_note_select.png)\n\nВыберите длительность звучания ноты.\n\n![play_note_duration](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/play_note/play_note_duration.png)\n\n* **Полностью** нота звучит 1 секунду (1000 миллисекунд)\n* **Половина** ноты звучит 0.5 секунды (500 миллисекунд)\n* **Четверть** ноты звучит 0.25 секунды (250 миллисекунд)\n\nКак только нота начнёт проигрываться, блоки после блока воспроизведения сразу начинают незамедлительно выполняться."},"play_sound":{"name":"play_sound","markdown":"# Играть мелодию\n\nПроигрывает выбранную мелодию.\n\n![play_sound](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/play_sound/play_sound.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите мелодию из списка.\n\n![play_sound_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/play_sound/play_sound_select.png)\n\nКак только мелодия начнёт проигрываться, блоки после блока воспроизведения сразу начинают незамедлительно выполняться."},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Положение джойстика\n\nСообщает о текущем положении джойстика вдоль осей.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **положения джойстика** возвращает значение из диапазона **от -100 до 100**.\n\nБлок **положения джойстика** возвращает ноль в случае установки джойстика в центре осей.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nВыберите ось джойстика.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nБлок **положения джойстика** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Примеп\n\nВ данном примере перемещение джойстика вдоль оси D пульта управления позволяет контролировать скорость руки робота.\n\n![position_of_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Положение привода\n\nВозвращает значение расстояния пройденного приводом.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **положения привода** возвращает целое значения угла поворота и целое число оборотов привода.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nВыберите единицу измерения: угол поворота или число оборотов.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nБлок **положения привода** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Нажатие датчика касания\n\nВозвращает текущее состояние датчика касания.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **нажатия датчика касания** возвращает **правду**, если датчик касания был нажат.\n\nБлок **нажатия датчика касания** возвращает **ложь**, если датчик касания не был нажат.\n\nВыберите датчик касания для использования.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nБлок **нажатия датчика касания** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Нажатие кнопок пульта управления\n\nСообщает о состоянии кнопок на пульте управления.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **нажатия кнопок на пульте управления** возвращает **правду**, если выбранная кнопка на пульте управления нажата.\n\nБлок **нажатия кнопок на пульте управления** возвращает **ложь**, если выбранная кнопка на пульте управления не нажата.\n\nВыберите пульт управления для использования.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nБлок **нажатия кнопок на пульте управления** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере при нажатии кнопки E Up активируется привод на схвате.\n\n![pressing_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_example_revised.png)"},"pressing_touchled":{"name":"pressing_touchled","markdown":"# Нажатие Touch LED\n\nСообщает о нажатии датчика Touch LED.\n\n![pressing_touch_led](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **нажатия датчика Touch LED** возвращает **правду**, если выбранный датчик Touch LED нажат.\n\nБлок **нажатия датчика Touch LED** возвращает **ложь**, если выбранный датчик Touch LED не нажат.\n\nВыберите датчик для использования.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_led](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_led.png)\n\nБлок **нажатия датчика Touch LED** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_inserted.png)\n\n"},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Печать\n\nПечатает на экране контроллера текст и/или значения.\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/print/look_print.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **печати** выводит информацию на экран в месте текущего расположения курсора.\n\nВо всех новых проектах печать начинается с первой строки первого столбца.\n\nПо умолчанию, все числа блока выводятся как целые. Используйте блок **точности печати** для указания числа знаков после точки.\n\nПечатает слова и/или числа\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/print/print_words.png)\n\nПечать значения переменной.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nПечать результата вычисления.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nПечать данных с различных устройств.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Мои блоки\n\nСоздаёт блок с функционалом, описываемым пользователем.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Мой блок** используется для создания нового блока и позволяет использовать его неограниченное число раз в данной программе. \n\n**Мой блок** создаётся нажатием кнопки **Создать блок**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\nБлок **Мои блоки** может принимать в себя разные параметры на вход: текст, числа или логические переменные. Это позволяет расширить функциональность блока.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nДля использования **вашего блока** поместите **ваш блок** в основное тело программы. Когда программа достигнет **вашего блока**, то запустятся блоки внутри **вашего блока**.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nПрикрепите необходимые блоки к **вашим блокам**, чтобы определить действия, которые будут воспроизводиться при вызове **вашего блока**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Примечание: Создание блоков с одинаковыми именами может привести к ошибке в работе программы на Игровых полях.***\n\n## Пример 1\n\nВ данном примере **ваши блоки** будут реализовывать следующие действия:\n\n* Играть звук сирены три раза.\n* Проехать вперёд 12 дюймов.\n* Играть звук сирены три раза.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_call/sound_example.png)\n\n## Пример 2\n\nВ данном примере **ваши блоки** будут реализовывать следующие действия:\n\n* Проехать вперёд 15 дюймов.\n* Вывод значения текущего значения заряда аккумулятора и перенос курсора на новую строку.\n* Поворот робота на 180 градусов направо.\n* Вывод значения текущего значения заряда аккумулятора и перенос курсора на новую строку.\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Мои блоки\n\nСоздаёт блок с функционалом, описываемым пользователем.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Мой блок** используется для создания нового блока и позволяет использовать его неограниченное число раз в данной программе. \n\n**Мой блок** создаётся нажатием кнопки **Создать блок**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\nБлок **Мои блоки** может принимать в себя разные параметры на вход: текст, числа или логические переменные. Это позволяет расширить функциональность блока.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nДля использования **вашего блока** поместите **ваш блок** в основное тело программы. Когда программа достигнет **вашего блока**, то запустятся блоки внутри **вашего блока**.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nПрикрепите необходимые блоки к **вашим блокам**, чтобы определить действия, которые будут воспроизводиться при вызове **вашего блока**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Примечание: Создание блоков с одинаковыми именами может привести к ошибке в работе программы на Игровых полях.***\n\n## Пример 1\n\nВ данном примере **ваши блоки** будут реализовывать следующие действия:\n\n* Играть звук сирены три раза.\n* Проехать вперёд 12 дюймов.\n* Играть звук сирены три раза.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/sound_example.png)\n\n## Пример 2\n\nВ данном примере **ваши блоки** будут реализовывать следующие действия:\n\n* Проехать вперёд 15 дюймов.\n* Вывод значения текущего значения заряда аккумулятора и перенос курсора на новую строку.\n* Поворот робота на 180 градусов направо.\n* Вывод значения текущего значения заряда аккумулятора и перенос курсора на новую строку.\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Случайное значение\n\n![random](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/random/random.png)\n\nВозвращает случайное значение между наименьшим и наибольшим значениями блока.\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **случайного значения** может использоваться в блоках с овальными вставками. \n\nБлок **случайного значения** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример 1\n\nВ данном примере блок **случайного значения** используется для генерации случайной скорости трансмиссии.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\n## Пример 2\n\nВ данном примере блок **случайного значения** используется для генерации случайной длительности в блоке ожидания.\n\n![random_control](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"rate_of_gyro":{"name":"rate_of_gyro","markdown":"# Скорость гироскопа\n\nВозвращает значение угловой скорости для гироскопа.\n\n![rate_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **скорости гироскопа** возвращает значения в диапазоне **от 0 до 249.99 град/с**\n\nБлок **скорости гироскопа** возвращает значения с единицей измерения градусы в секунду (град/с).\n\nВыберите гироскоп для использования.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nБлок **скорости гироскопа** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_inserted.png)"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Остаток от деления\n\nДелит первое значение на второе и возвращает остаток от деления.\n\n![remainder](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **остатка от деления** может принимать десятичные, целые и числовые блоки.\n\nБлок возвращает ноль в случае, если одно число кратно другому.\n\nБлок **остатка от деления** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере остаток деления семи на два равен \"1\", поэтому на экране будет напечатана единица.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Цикл повторения\n\n'C' подобный блок повторяет действия внутри себя заданное число раз.\n\n![repeat](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nЗначение перед действиями блока **повторения** определяет число повторений.\n \n 'C' подобный блок **повторения** принимает целые или числовые блоки.\n\n'C' подобные блоки могут быть использованы внутри похожих блоков. Данная концепция называется \"вложенностью\" и помогает программировать более сложные алгоритмы.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/repeat/repeat_select.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере звук будет воспроизведён пять раз каждые три секунды.\n\n![repeat_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/repeat/repeat_example.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Цикл повторять пока\n\n'C' подобный блок цикла работает до тех пор, пока условие **ложь**.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nЦикл **повторять пока** проверяет значение условия на каждой итерации цикла.\n\nЕсли условие **ложь**, то действия внутри цикла **повторять пока** будут запущены.\n\nЕсли условие **правда**, то действия внутри цикла **повторять пока** будут пропущены.\n\n'C' подобный блок цикла **повторять пока** может принимать в качестве условия шестиугольные блоки.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере на экране контроллера будет отображаться значения таймера и трансмиссия будет двигаться вперёд до тех пор, пока не нажата кнопка **галочка** на контроллере. После нажатия **галочки** трансмиссия остановится.\n\n![repeat_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/repeat_until/repeat_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Сбросить таймер\n\nОбнуляет таймер контроллера.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nТаймер начинает работу в начале программы. Используйте блок **сброса таймера** для обнуления текущего значения таймера.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере таймер будет обнулён перед движением трансмиссии вперёд три секунды. После трёх секунд трансмиссия закончит работу.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Угол вращения\n\nСообщает о текущем угле вращения гироскопа.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation.png](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **угла вращения** возвращает **положительное** значение в случае вращения гироскопа **против часовой стрелки**.\n\nБлок **угла вращения** возвращает **отрицательное** значение в случае вращения гироскопа **по часовой стрелке**.\n\nВыберите гироскоп для использования.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_devices.png)\n\nБлок **угла вращения** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Окргулить\n\nОкругляет заданное число до ближайшего целого значения.\n\n![round](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/round/round.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nДесятичные числа будут **округляться** меньшую сторону, если десятичная часть меньше 0.5, и в большую сторону, если десятичная часть больше или равна 0.5.\n\nБлок **округления** может быть использован в блоках с овальными вставками и сам может принимать блоки круглой формы.\n\nБлок **округления** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки. \n\n![round_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере робот проедет три дюйма вперёд после округления 2,7.\n\n![round_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Задать 2D массив\n\nУстанавливает значения двумерного массива.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПри создании двумерного массива вы можете указать число **строк** и **столбцов**, варьирующиеся в пределах от 1 до 10.\n\nВыберите двумерный массив. Массив может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nБлок **задания 2D массива** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Установить элементы списка\n\nЗадаёт значения списка.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПри создании списка вы можете задать длину списка в диапазоне от 1 до 10 элементов.\n\nВыберите список. Список может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nБлок **установки элементов списка** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере инициализируются значения списка после чего происходит обращение к элементу номер 3 (90) из списка для установки руки робота нужное положение.\n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Установить логическую переменную\n\nУстанавливает значение логической переменной.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите логическую переменную. Логические переменные могут быть переименованы или удалены.\n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nВыберите логическую переменную.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nБлок **установки логической переменной** может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_color_sensor_brightness":{"name":"set_color_sensor_brightness","markdown":"# Установка яркости датчика цвета\n\nУстанавливает яркость фонарика датчика цвета.\n\n![set_color_sensor_light](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_light.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nИсточник света на датчика цвета может помочь в определении цвета поверхности или яркости поверхности.\n\nЗначения блок **установки яркости датчика цвета** лежат в диапазоне **от 0 до 100%**. Чем больше значение, тем ярче будет светить фонарик.\n\nВыберите датчик цвета для использования.\n\n![set_color_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor.png)\n\nБлок **установки яркости датчика цвета** может принимать целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![set_color_sensor_2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_2.png)\n\n\n"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# Установка курсора\n\nУстанавливает курсор в указанную область для печати.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nУстанавливает курсор в выбранные строку и столбец на экране для **печати**.\n\nДиапазон строк: от 1 до 5.\nДиапазон столбцов: от 1 до 21.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_cursor/row_column_index.png)  \n\nБлок **установки курсора** может принимать целые и числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере курсор будет перемещён на 3 строку и 8 столбец для печати надписи \"Hello!\".\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_cursor/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_cursor/set_cursor_hello.png)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Установить курс движения\n\nУстанавливает значение курса трансмиссии.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки курса движения** может быть использован для установки углового положения трансмисии в любой точке при вращении против часовой стрелки.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nБлок **установки курса движения** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 359,99 градусов**.\n\nБлок **установки курса движения** может принимать целые и числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере робот в совокупности развернётся на 135 градусов:\n\n![setDriveHeading_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_example_revised.png)\n\n- Поворот налево на 45 градусов.\n- Установка значения курса в ноль для текущей позиции.\n- Поворот налево на дополнительные 90 градусов от текущей позиции.\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Установка вращения\n\nУстановка угла вращения трансмиссии.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки вращения** может быть использован для установки положительного или отрицательного значения угла вращения.\n\nБлок **установки вращения** может принимать целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ этом примере робот повернётся в общей сложности на 210 градусов:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Повернуть направо (по часовой стрелке) до 120 градусов.\n- Установите текущую позицию вращения в -45 градусов.\n- Поверните направо (по часовой стрелке) на 90 градусов (от -45 до 45 градусов), полагаясь на установленное значение вращения."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Установка режима торможения\n\nУстанавливает характер торможения трансмиссии.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n* **Brake** приведёт к немедленной остановке трансмиссии.\n* **Coast** привёдет к плавному торможению.\n* **Hold** приведёт к удержанию положения приводов трансмиссии после её остановки.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссии проедет вперёд три секунды после чего остановится с удержанием положени приводов.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Установка времени работы\n\nУстанавливает максимальное время работы команд движения трансмисии.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nУстановка максимального времени работы приводит к ограничению выполнения любых других действий, связанных с блоками движения трансмиссии.\n\nНапример, трансмиссия не достигнет конечного положения в случае движения по направлению к стене.\n\nБлок **установки времени работы** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере робот закончит движение по истечении двух секунд, не доехав 24 дюйма. После достижения порога времени трансмиссия начнёт поворот.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Установить скорость движения\n\nУстановка скорости движения трансмиссии.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки скорости движения** только устанавливает скорость. Для запуска трансмиссии необходим блок **движения**.\n\nДиапазоны значений для блока **установки скорости движения** равны **от -100 до 100%** или **от -127 до 127 об/мин**.\n\nУстановка отрицательного значения изменит направление движения на противоположное.\n\nУстановка скорости, равной 0, приведёт к остановке трансмиссии.\n\nБлок **установки скорости движения** может принимать десятичные, целые и числовые блоки.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссия проедет 12 дюймов со скоростью 50%.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Установить курс гироскопа\n\nУстанавливает текущее положение гироскопа в качестве курса.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nКурс гироскопа может быть назначен в любом положении при движении против часовой стрелки.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_gyro_heading/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\nБлок **установки курса гироскопа** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 359,99** градусов.\n\nБлок **установки курса гироскопа** может принимать положительные десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nВыберите гироскоп для использования.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Установка вращения гироскопа.\n\nУстанавливает текущее положение гироскопа в качестве вращения.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВ качестве значения для блока **установки вращения гироскопа** может быть использовано любое положительное (вращение против часовой стрелки) или отрицательное (вращение по часовой стрелке)значение.\n\nБлок **установки вращения гироскопа** может принимать любые положительные или отрицательные десятичные или целые значения.\n\nБлок **установки вращения гироскопа** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nВыберите гироскоп для использования.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation_devices.png)\n\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Замена элементов 2D списка\n\nУстанавливает новое значение для выбранного элемента.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВведите положение элемента (сначала номер строки, затем номер столбца) элемента, который вы бы хотели заменить.\n\nВыберите список. Список может быть удалён или переименован.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nБлок **замены элементов 2D списка** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Замена элемента списка\n\nУстанавливает новое значение для выбранного элемента списка.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите список. Список может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nБлок **замены элементов списка** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере второй элемент списка будет заменён на 15 и после этого напечатан на экране контроллера.\n\n![replace_item_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_item_of_array/replace_item_example.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Установка положения привода\n\nУстанавливает энкодер привода в выбранное положение.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки положения привода** может быть использован для установки привода в любое положение. \n\nОбычно данный блок используется для установки значения энкодера в ноль.\n\nВыберите привод энкодера.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nВыберите единицу измерения в градусах или оборотах.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Установка режима торможения\n\nУстанавливает характер торможения привода.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n* **Brake** приведёт к немедленной остановке привода.\n* **Coast** привёдет к плавному торможению привода.\n* **Hold** приведёт к удержанию положения привода после его остановки.\n\nБлок **установки режима торможения** повлияет на режим торможения на протяжении всей программы.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nВыберите настройки привода после остановки.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере привод руки изменит провернётся на 90 градусов после чего будет удерживать руку в данном положении. \n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Установка времени работы\n\nУстанавливает максимальное время работы команд движения привода.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nУстановка максимального времени работы приводит к ограничению выполнения любых других действий, связанных с блоками движения привода.\n\nИспользование блока ограничения времени работы позволяет избежать непредвиденных ситуаций, связанных, например, с достижением максимального угла работы одной из степеней свободы робота.\n\nБлок **установки времени работы** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере блок установки положения привода будет остановлен через две секунды и не достигнет положения 270 градусов. После двух секунд привод на схвате будет установлен в положение ноль.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Установка момента привода\n\nУстанавливает максимальные момент привода.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки момента привода** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 100%**.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nБлок **установки момента привода** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере привод схвата робота повернётся на 40 градусов с двадцатипроцентным (20%) моментом. Это позволит захватить объект без нанесения ущерба из-за слишком большой силы сжатия.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Установка скорости привода\n\nУстанавливает скорость привода.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки скорости привода** работает в диапазонах **от -100 до 100%** или **от -127 до 127 об/мин**.\n\nУстановка отрицательного значения изменит направление движения на противоположное.\n\nУстановка скорости, равной 0, приведёт к остановке привода.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nЕдиницы измерения скорости: проценты (%) или обороты в минуту (об/мин).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере рука поднимается до 90 градусов на скорости 25%.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Установка точности печати\n\nУстанавливает число знаков после точки при выводе на экран контроллера.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите точность для печати на экране.\n\n* Единицы (1) (по умолчанию)\n* Десятки (0.1)\n* Сотни (0.01)\n* Тысячи (0.001)\n* Все цифры (0.000001)\n\nБлок печати округляет значение при выводе до ближайшего. Например, для значения 1.67 при точности до десятков будет выведено число 1.7.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_touchled_brightness":{"name":"set_touchled_brightness","markdown":"# Установка яркости Touch LED.\n\nУстанавливает яркость светодиодной панели на Touch LED.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки яркости Touch LED** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 100%**.\n\nВыберите Touch LED для использования.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor3](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_sensor3.png)\n\nБлок **установки яркости Touch LED** может принимать целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness2.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере светодиодная панель загорится зелёным цветом с яркостью 25%.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_touchled_color":{"name":"set_touchled_color","markdown":"# Установка цвета Touch LED\n\nУстанавливает цвет на Touch LED. \n\n![set_touchLED_color](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите датчик **Touch LED** для использования.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_sensor.png)\n\nВыберите цвет для отображения.\n\n![set_touchLED_color2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color2.png)\n\nДля выключения светодиодной панели, установите цвет в никакой."},"set_touchled_fade":{"name":"set_touchled_fade","markdown":"# Установить затухание Touch LED\n\nУстанавливает время перехода между разными цветами Touch LED.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберит Touch LED для использования.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_sensor2.png)\n\nВыберите время перехода.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_speed](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_speed.png)\n\n* Медленный - медленный переход между цветами.\n* Быстрый - быстрый переход между цветами.\n* Выключен - смена цветом происходит скачкообразно.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере Touch LEd будет медленно изменять цвет на синий.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Установить скорость поворота\n\nУстанавливает скорость поворота трансмиссии.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки скорости поворота** задаёт скорость поворота трансмиссии, но не запускает движение трансмиссии. Для запуска движения требуется блок **поворота**.\n\n**Скорость поворота** может быть задана в диапазоне **от 0% до 100%** или **от -127 до 127 об/мин**.\n\nОтрицательное значение скорости поворота меняет направление движения на противоположное.\n\nУстановка скорости поворота в ноль останавливает движение трансмиссии.\n\nБлок **установки скорости поворота** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссия будет медленно поворачивать со скоростью 25%.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Установка значения переменной\n\nЗадаёт указанное значение переменной\n\n![set_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите переменную. Переменные могут быть переименованы или удалены.\n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nБлок **установки переменных** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере показания с датчика расстояния будут записаны в переменную \"my variable\" и будут использованы для установки скорости трансмиссии.\n\n![set_variable_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_variable/set_variable_example.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Установить индекс объекта\n\nНазначает индекс объекту, который в дальнейшем мы бы хотели исследовать подробнее.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **числа объектов** может быть использован перед блоком **установки индекса объекта** для определения числа объектов.\n\nВыберите камеру для использования.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nБлок **установки индекса объекта** может принимать целые или числовые блоки.\n\n\n\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Длина массива\n\nВозвращает число элементов списка. \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите список. Список может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nБлок **длины массива** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# Снимок\n\nПолучает снимок с камеры.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **снимка** получает изображение с выбранной камеры для обработки и анализа объектов.\n\nОчевидно, что блок **снимка** необходимо использовать перед вызовом других блоков для камеры.\n\nВыберите камеру для использования.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nВыберите объект для анализа. Получение объекта осуществляется в меню настройки камеры.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Вращать\n\nЗапускает привод VEX IQ.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **вращения** запускает привод до вызова блока остановки привода.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nВыберите направление вращения. Имена направлений вращения могут быть изменены в настройках устройства.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Повернуть на\n\nЗапускает привод для поворота на определённое расстояние.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **поворота на** запускает привод для движения на определённое расстояние от текущего положения.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nВыберите направление вращения. Имена направлений вращения могут быть изменены в настройках устройства.\n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nБлок Блок **поворота на** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nВыберите единицу измерения в градусах или оборотах.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nПо умолчанию, другие блоки будут ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота на**.\n\nНажатием на стрелку можно вызвать **и не ждать**. Данная команда позволяет не ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота на** для выполнения следующих.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Поворот в положение\n\nПоворачивает привод в указанное положение.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **поворота в положение** указывает приводу на поворот в необходимое положение. Основываясь на текущем положении привода, блок **поворота в положение** определит направление вращения.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nБлок **поворота в положение** может принимать деятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nВыберите единицу измерения в градусах или оборотах.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nПо умолчанию, другие блоки будут ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота в положение**.\n\nНажатием на стрелку можно вызвать **и не ждать**. Данная команда позволяет не ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота в положение** для выполнения следующих.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Остановка движения\n\nОстанавливает трансмиссию.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **остановки движения** останавливает движение трансмиссии при использовании блока.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссия остановится черз три секунды.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Остановить привод\n\nОстанавливает привод.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите привод, который необходимо остановить.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примерепривод будет работать три секунды перед остановкой.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Вычитание\n\nПолучает разность между первым и вторым значениями.\n\n![subtract](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **вычитания** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nБлок **вычитания** может быть использован в блоках с овальными вставками, и сам может использовать овальные блоки.\n\nВычитание двух чисел.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nВычитание из переменной числа.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nВычитание значений датчиков и устройств.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Значение таймера\n\nВозвращает текущее значение таймера в секундах.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nТаймер запускается в начале программы, и его значение является десятичным числом.\n\nБлок **значение таймера** используется в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере перед выполнением поворота на 90 градусов трансмиссия проедет вперёд с воспроизведением звука 4.5 секунды.\n\n![timerValue_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/timer_value/timerValue_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Поворот\n\nБесконечно поворачивает трансмиссию.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **поворота** будет поворачивать трансмиссию бесконечно, пока не будет использован другой блок для остановки.\n\nВыберите направление поворота трансмиссии.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Поворот на\n\nПоворачивает трансмиссию на определённую градусную меру.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите направление поворота трансмиссии.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\nУстановите угол поворота трансмиссии.\n\nБлок **поворот на** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nПо умолчанию, другие блоки будут ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота на**.\n\nНажатием на стрелку можно вызвать **и не ждать**. Данная команда позволяет не ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота на** для выполнения следующих.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Повернуть на курс\n\nПоворот трансмиссии на определённый курс, установленный с помощью гироскопа.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **поворота на курс** может быть использован для поворота трансмиссии по часовой стрелке к любому углу.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nНаправление поворота с помощью блока **поворота на курс** определяется текущим положением гироскопа.\n\nБлок **поворота на курс** принимает значения  в диапазоне **от 0.00 до 359.00** градусов.\n\nБлок **поворота на курс** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссия сделает четыре поворота: \n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Поворот направо до 45 градусов\n- Поворот направо до 90 градусов\n- Поворот направо до 270 градусов\n- Поворот налева до 180 градусов\n\nПо умолчанию, другие блоки будут **ждать** окончания поворота трансмисии.\n\nВы можете установить значение **и не ждать** для выполнения других действий параллельно с поворотом.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Повернуть к вращению\n\nПоворот трансмиссии на определённый угол, установленный с помощью гироскопа.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **поворота к вращению** может быть использован для поворота по часовой стрелке (положительного поворота) и против часовой стрелки (отрицательного поворота).\n\nНаправление поворота трансмиссии определяется текущим значением **вращения**.\n\nБлок **поворота к вращению** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссия сделает четыре поворота: \n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Направо (по часовой стрелке) до 90 градусов\n- Направо (по часовой стрелке) до 180 градусов\n- Налево (против часовой стрелке) до -45 градусов\n- Направо (по часовой стрелке) до 0 градусов\n\nПо умолчанию, другие блоки будут **ждать** окончания поворота трансмисии.\n\nВы можете установить значение **и не ждать** для выполнения других действий параллельно с поворотом.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Переменная\n\nЗадаёт числовое значение переменной.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлоки **переменных** используются для присваивания числового значения переменной. Используйте блок **задания переменной** для обновления значения переменной.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nБлок **переменной** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nПеременные создаются нажатием кнопки **создание переменных**.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Скорость привода\n\nВозвращает текущую скорость привода.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **скорости привода** работает в диапазоне **от -100 до 100%** или **от -127 до 127 об/мин**.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nВыберите единицу измерения скорости в % или оборотах в минуту (об/мин).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nБлок **скорости привода** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Информация об объекте\n\nСообщает параметры найденного объекта.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nДля использования блока **информации об объекте** необходимо проделать следующие шаги:\n\n1. Настройте камеру в окне настройки камеры.\n2. Используйте блок **снимка** для получения изображения с камеры.\n3. Используйте  блок **существования объекта** для определения наличия объекта/цвета.\n\nПосле обнаружения объекта, вы можете использовать блок **информации об объекте** для изучения его параметров.\n\n* Используйте блок **установки индекса объекта** для получения информации о нём. По умолчанию, определяются параметры самого крупного объекта.\n* Используйте блок **количества объектов** для определения количества объектов нужных сигнатуры/цвета перед камерой.\n* Используйте блок **информации об объекте** для плучения параметров объекта.\n\nВыберите камеру для использования.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nВыберите параметр, который необходимо получить:\n\n* Width - ширина объекта в пикселях. Возвращает значение **от 2 до 316 пикселей**.\n* Height - высота объекта в пикселях. Возвращает значение **от 2 до 212 пикселей**.\n* CenterX - сообщает координату X центра объекта. Возвращает значение **от 0 до 315 пикселей**.\n* CenterY - сообщает координату Y центра объекта. Возвращает значение **от 0 до 211 пикселей**.\n* Angle - угол наклона объекта. Возвращает значения **от 0 до 180 градусов**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nБлок **информации об объекте** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Ждать\n\nЖдёт указанное время перед переходом к следующим блокам.\n\n![wait](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите требуемое значение времени в блоке **ждать**.\n\nБлок **ждать** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере цвет датчика TouchLED изменится с красного на зелёный после 3.25 секунд ожидания.\n\n![wait_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/wait/wait_example.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Ждать пока\n\nЖдёт изменения значения логического блока внутри на **правду**.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **ждать пока** непрерывно проверяет условие внутри, пока значение внутри блока не станет **правдой**.\n\nБлок **ждать пока** может принимать шестиугольные блоки.\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере датчик Touch LED зажжётся желтым и будет ожидать нажатия. После нажатия на датчик, на экране появится надпись \"Done!\".\n\n![wait_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/wait_until/wait_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"when_brain_button":{"name":"when_brain_button","markdown":"# Нажатие кнопки контроллера\n\nВыполняет определённые действия после нажатия одной из кнопок на контроллере.\n\n![when_brain_button](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_brain_button/when_brain_button.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите кнопку для использования.\n\n![when_brain_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select.png)\n\nВыберите действие над кнопкой - **нажата** или **отжата**.\n\n![when_brain_button_select_2](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select_2.png)  \n"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Когда получил сообщение\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков после получения нужного сообщения.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите ожидаемое сообщение. Кроме того, вы можете создать новой сообщение.\n\nБлок **получения сообщения** получает сообщения только от блоков **передачи сообщения** или **передачи сообщения и ожидания**.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере Touch LED загорится красным и подождёт две секунды перед отправкой сообщения \"message1\".\n\nПосле получения сообщения блоком **когда получил сообщение**, трансмиссия будет двигаться вперёд, параллельно поднимая руку.\n\nДействия будут выполняться параллельно (обозначены красными стрелками).\n\n![when_broadcast_example](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_example.png)\n\n"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Когда датчик касания\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков в случае нажатия/отжатия датчика касания.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите датчик касания для использования.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nВыберите действие: нажат или отжат.\n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Когда ось пульта управления\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков в случае движения джойстика на пульте управления.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите ось джойстика на пульте управления.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Когда кнопка на пульте управления\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков в случае нажатия/отжатия кнопки на пульте управления.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите пульт управления.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_controller_button/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_controller_button/controller_button_back.png)\n\nВыберите действие над кнопкой: нажата или отжата.\n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Начало программы\n\nЗапускает блоки при запуске программы.\n\n![when_started](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **начала программы** начинает работу при нажатии кнопки **запуска** программы или кнопки **галочка** на контроллере.\n\nВсе новые программы автоматически содержат блок **начала программы**. Проекты могут поддерживать до трёх блоков **начала программы**."},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Когда таймер\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков в случае, если текущее значение таймера больше установленного.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nТаймер контроллера запускается автоматически в начале каждой программы.\n\nВыберите величину времени. Блок **когда таймер** начнёт работы, если текущее значение таймера больше установленного.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nБлок **когда таймер** может принимать десятичные и целые значения.\n\nБлок **когда таймер** не может принимать другие блоки."},"when_touchled":{"name":"when_touchled","markdown":"# Когда Touch LED\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков в случае нажатия/отжатия датчика Touch LED.\n\n![when_touchLED](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_touchled/when_touchled.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите датчик Touch LED для использования.\n\n![when_touchLED_select](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_touchled/when_touchled_select.png)\n\nВыберите действие: нажат или отжат.\n\n![when_touchLED_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/when_touchled/when_touchled_condition.png)"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Пока\n\n'C' подобный блок цикла работает до тех пор, пока условие **правда**.\n\n![while](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/while/while.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nЦикл **пока** проверяет значение условия на каждой итерации цикла.\n\nЕсли условие **правда**, то действия внутри цикла **пока** будут запущены.\n\nЕсли условие **ложь**, то действия внутри цикла **пока** будут пропущены.\n\n'C' подобный блок цикла **пока** может принимать в качестве условия шестиугольные блоки.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/ru/while/while_inserted.png)"}}},"set_font":{"blocks":{}},"set_width":{"blocks":{}},"uk":{"blocks":{"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Додавання\n\nДодає будь-які два значення і передає суму.\n\n![add](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/add/add.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Додавання** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\nБлок **додавання** підходить до блоків, які мають круглий проміжок.\n\nДодавайте два числа.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nДодавайте значення змінних.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nДодавайте показники датчиків або пристроїв.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# І\n\nПовідомляє, якщо обидва логічні значення істинні.\n\n![and](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/and/and.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **і** передає значення **істина**, коли обидва значення **істина**. \n\nБлок **і** передає значення **хиба**, коли одне (або обидва) значення **хиба**.\n\nЛогічний блок **і** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![and_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад перевіряє, чи затиснуті дві кнопки контролера IQ водночас.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nБлок **і** передає значення **істина**, коли **Кнопка контролера E верхня** та **Кнопка контролера L нижня** натиснуті одночасно.\n\nБлок **і** передає значення **хиба**, коли одна (або обидві) кнопка контролера не натиснута.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/and/and_truth.png)"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Ємність акумулятора\n\nПередає значення заряду акумулятора VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Ємність акумулятора** передає значення в діапазоні **від 0% до 100%**.\n\nБлок **ємність акумулятора** приєднується до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад грає звук тривоги, якщо **ємність акумулятора** VEX IQ Brain нижче 50%.\n\n![battery_capacity_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/battery_level/battery_capacity_example_revised.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Логічна змінна\n\nПередає значення логічної змінної.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **логічна змінна** призначений для зберігання значень **істина** або **хиба**. Використовуйте блок **надати логічне значення**, щоб записати або оновити значення логічної змінної.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nБлок **логічна змінна** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nЛогічну змінну можна створити після натискання на кнопку **Створити логічну змінну**.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"brain_button_pressed":{"name":"brain_button_pressed","markdown":"# Кнопка на Brain натиснута\n\nПередає значення, якщо кнопка на VEX IQ Brain натиснута.\n\n![button_pressed_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Кнопка на Brain натиснута** передає значення **істина**, якщо обрана кнопка на Brain натиснута.\n\n**Кнопка на Brain натиснута** передає значення **хиба**, якщо обрана кнопка на Brain не натиснута.\n\nВиберіть, яку кнопку на Brain використовувати.\n\n![button_pressed_options](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_options.png)\n\nЛогічний блок **кнопка на Brain натиснута** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змушує робота їхати вперед і повернути, коли буде натиснуто кнопку **Вгору** на Brain.\n\n![brainButtonPressed_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_example_revised.png)\n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Зупинити\n\nНегайно виходить із повторюваного циклу.\n\n![break](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/break/break.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЯкщо його додати до \"С\"-подібного блока повторення, блок **зупинитит** вийде з циклу в момент виконання.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад запускає трансмісію вперед і перевіряє, чи натиснута кнопка **вгору** на VEX IQ Brain. \n\nЯкщо кнопку **вгору** **натиснути**, блок **зупинити** зупинить нескінченний цикл і зупинить трансмісію.\n\n![break_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Яскравість\n\nПередає кількість світла, виміряну датчиком кольору VEX IQ.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Яскравість** передає значення в діапазоні **від 0% до 100%**.\n\nВиберіть, який датчик використати.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nБлок **яскравість** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Надіслати\n\nНадсилає повідомлення для активації стеків блоків, які починаються з блока **коли отримано**.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nСтек, який активує **надіслати**, продовжить працювати, коли інші стеки отримають повідомлення.\n\nВиберіть, яке повідомлення **надіслати**. Можна створити нове повідомлення.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад встановлює червоний колір LED датчика дотику VEX IQ і чекає дві секунди перед надсиланням \"message1\". \n\nЩойно повідомлення отримано, стек із блоком **коли отримано** запускає трансмісію вперед і ClawMotor рухається вгору водночас.\n\nДва стека продовжують працювати водночас, як показано червоними стрілками на зображенні.\n\n![broadcast_example_arrows](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/broadcast/broadcast_example_arrows.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Надіслати і чекати\n\nНадсилає повідомлення для активації стеків блоків, які починаються з блока **коли отримано**, і зупиняє наступні блоки свого стека.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nСтек, який активує **надіслати і чекати**, зупиняє роботу, поки інші стеки, які отримали повідомлення, не виконаються.\n\nВиберіть, яке повідомлення **надіслати**. Можна створити нове повідомлення.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад встановлює червоний колір LED датчика дотику VEX IQ і чекає дві секунди перед надсиланням \"message1\". \n\nЩойно повідомлення отримано, стек із блоком **коли отримано** запускає трансмісію вперед і грає звук.\n\nСтек, який надіслав повідомлення, чекає, поки не виконається стек, який отримав повідомлення, а потім продовжує виконувати свої блоки, як показано червоними стрілками на зображенні.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows_3](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows3.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Калібрувати гіроскоп\n\nКалібрування гіроскопічного датчика VEX IQ потрібне для зменшення загального зміщення, спричиненого гіроскопом.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nВ гіроскопі виникає зміщення, і гіродатчик неправильно розпізнає рухи, навіть якщо датчик не рухається.\n\n## Як це працює\n\nГіроскоп повинен бути нерухомим, поки триває калібрування.\n\nВиберіть, який гіроскоп використати.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nВиберіть тривалість калібрування. Чим довше калібрування, тим менше зміщення виникне.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_seconds](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_seconds.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Змінити змінну\n\nЗмінює (збільшує) змінну на задане значення.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, яку змінну використати - цю змінну також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nБлок **Змінити змінну** приймає десяткові, цілі числа або числові блоки.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад збільшує змінну, що встановлює швидкість мотору, на 10 щоразу, коли цикл **повторити** виконується.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Очистити всі рядки\n\nОчищує весь екран VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Очистити всі рядки** не скидає позицію курсора на екрані Brain. Використовуйте блок **встановити курсор** для встановлення потрібної позиції курсора на екрані Brain.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує \"Hello\" на 1 секунду, а потім очистить увесь екран перед написанням \"Goodbye\".\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_example.png)"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Очистити рядок\n\nОчистить один рядок на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **очистити рядок** приймає ціле число або числовий блок із результатом у діапазоні **1 - 5**, число встановлює рядок для очищення.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/clear_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує \"Hello\" із 2 рядка і 1 стовпця на три секунди, а потім очистить рядок 2.\n\n![clear_row_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/clear_row/clear_row_example.png)"},"color_detects_color":{"name":"color_detects_color","markdown":"# Побачив колір\n\nПовідомляє, якщо датчик кольору VEX IQ побачив певний колір.\n\n![color_detects](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/color_detects_color/color_detects.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Побачив колір** передає значення **істина**, якщо датчик кольору побачив обраний колір.\n\n**Побачив колір** передає значення **хиба**, якщо датчик кольору побачив колір, не схожий на обраний.\n\nВиберіть, який датчик кольору використати.\n\n![color_detects_chosen](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/color_detects_color/color_detects_chosen.png)\n\nВиберіть, який колір шукати.\n\n![color_detects_selected](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/color_detects_color/color_detects_selected.png)\n\nЛогічний блок **побачив колір** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![color_detects_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/color_detects_color/color_detects_shape.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує \"Color Red\" або \"Other Color\" залежно від того, побачив датчик кольору червоний, чи ні.\n\n![color_detects_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/color_detects_color/color_detects_example.png)\n\n"},"color_of":{"name":"color_of","markdown":"# Колір\n\nПередає назву кольору, знайденого датчиком кольору VEX IQ. \n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/color_of/color_of_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Колір** може передати назву таких кольорів: **червоний, червоно-фіолетовий, фіолетовий, синьо-фіолетовий, синій, синьо-зелений, зелений, жовто-зелений, жовтий, жовтогарячий, оранжевий або червоногарячий.**\n\nВиберіть, який колір використати.\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/color_of/color_of_color.png)\n\nБлок **колір** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![color_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/color_of/color_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Коментар\n\nДає змогу програмісту писати інформацію, яка допомагає описати програму.\n\n![comment_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПрофесійні програмісти використовують коментарі у різних частинах програми, щоб допомогти іншим зрозуміти їхній код. Коментарі також допомагають вирішувати проблеми і працювати в команді.\n\nДодайте текст у блок **коментар**. Виберіть прозоре поле і видаліть наявний текст. Потім пишіть тут новий текст.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nКоментарі не впливають на програму або навколишні блоки.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Контролер увімкнути/вимкнути\n\nУвімкнення або вимкнення налаштованих дій контролера з меню пристроїв. \n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВстановіть увімкнення або вимкнення налаштованих дій контролера, вибравши потрібний варіант у спадному меню. За замовчуванням, контролер увімкнено в кожному проєкті.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nНалаштовані дії у цьому прикладі використовуються для керуванням трансмісією і встановлюються у налаштуваннях контролера в меню пристроїв.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nУ цьому прикладі налаштовані дії контролера вимкнені на початку роботи програми.\n\nПотім, робот проїде вперед.\n\nЗрештою, блок **контролер увімкнути** вмикає контролер для відновлення керування роботом із контролера.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Струм мотора\n\nПередає кількість енергії, яку мотор VEX IQ зараз використовує у відсотках(%) або амперах(amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Струм мотора** передає значення в діапазоні **від 0% до 100%** або **від 0.0 до 1.2 ампер**. \n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nВиберіть, в яких одиницях передавати струм мотора: у % або в амперах.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nБлок **струм мотора** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Курсор у стовпчику\n\nПередає номер стовпця з екрану Brain, де розміщений курсор.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Курсор у стовпчику** передає число в діапазоні **від 1 до 21**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/cursor_column/row_column_index.png)  \n\nБлок **курсор у стовпчику** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад перевіряє, чи позиція **курсора у стовпчику** більша за 15. Якщо більша, проєкт встановить курсор у 1 рядок 1 стовпець і надрукує \"Hello\".\n\n![cursor_column_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/cursor_column/cursor_column_example_simple.png)\n\n"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Курсор у рядку\n\nПередає номер рядка з екрану Brain, де розміщений курсор.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Курсор у рядку** передає число в діапазоні **від 1 до 5**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/cursor_row/row_column_index.png)\n\nБлок **курсор у рядку** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад перевіряє, чи позиція **курсора у рядку** більша за 4. Якщо більша, проєкт встановить курсор у 1 рядок 1 стовпець і надрукує \"Hello\".\n\n![cursor_row_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/cursor_row/cursor_row_example_simple.png)"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Відстань\n\nПередає відстань до найближчого об'єкта від датчика відстані VEX IQ.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Відстань** передає значення в діапазоні **від 24 до 1000 мм** або **від 1 до 40 дюймів**.\n\nВиберіть, який датчик відстані використати.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nВиберіть, в яких одиницях передавати **відстань**: в міліметрах або дюймах.\n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nБлок **відстань** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Ділення\n\nДілить перше значення на друге і передає частку.\n\n![divide](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Ділення** працює з десятковими, цілими числами, значеннями з інших блоків.\n\nБлок **Ділення** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\nВводьте значення для ділення.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nДіліть значення змінних.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nДіліть показники датчиків або пристроїв.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Їхати\n\nПостійний рух трансмісії.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **їхати** змушує трансмісію їхати, поки новий блок трансмісії не активується, або програма не зупиниться.\n\nВиберіть напрямок руху трансмісії.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Струм привода\n\nПередає кількість струму (енергії), яку зараз використовує трансмісія.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Струм привода** передає значення в діапазоні **від 0% до 100%** або **від 0.0 до 1.2 ампер**. \n\nВиберіть, в яких одиницях передавати **струм привода**: у % або в амперах.\n\n![drive_current_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_current/drive_current_unit.png)\n\nБлок **струм привода** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Їхати відстань\n\nРух трансмісії на певну відстань.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, у якому напрямку рухається трансмісія.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\nБлок **їхати відстань** приймає десяткові, цілі числа або числові блоки.\n\nВстановіть, як далеко проїде трансмісія. Для цього введіть значення і виберіть одиниці вимірювання (дюйми або міліметри).\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nЗа замовчуванням, інші блоки **чекатимуть**, поки трансмісія не доїде.\n\nВи можете натиснути на стрілку, щоб активувати **і не чекати** - це змусить наступні блоки продовжувати роботу, поки трансмісія їде.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Курс\n\nПередає напрямок у який спрямована трансмісія.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Курс** передає значення в діапазоні **від 0.00 до 359.99 градусів**.\n\n**Курс** рахує курс у напрямку проти годинникової стрілки, як показано на зображенні.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_heading/TopDownBot01.png)\n\nБлок **курс** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Рух закінчено\n\nПовідомляє, коли трансмісія закінчила рух.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Рух закінчено** передає значення **істина**, коли мотори трансмісії закінчили свою роботу.\n\n**Рух закінчено** передає значення **хиба**, коли мотори трансмісії досі працюють.\n\nЛогічний блок **рух закінчено** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Рух триває\n\nПовідомляє, якщо трансмісія рухається.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Рух триває** передає значення **істина**, коли мотори трансмісії працюють.\n\n**Рух триває** передає значення **хиба**, коли мотори трансмісії зупинені.\n\nЛогічний блок **рух триває** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Кут повороту\n\nПередає кут повороту трансмісії у градусах, якщо налаштовано гіроскоп VEX IQ.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Кут повороту** передає **позитивне** значення, коли трансмісія повертає **проти годинникової стрілки**.\n\n**Кут повороту** передає **негативне** значення, коли трансмісія повертає **за годинниковою стрілкою**.\n\nБлок **кут повороту** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted.png)"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Швидкість руху\n\nПередає поточну швидкість трансмісії.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Швидкість руху** передає значення в діапазоні **від -100% до 100%** або **від -127rpm до 127rpm**\n\nВиберіть, в яких одиницях передавати швидкість: у % або в обертах за хвилину (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nБлок **швидкість руху** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Порівняння\n\nПовідомляє, коли перше значення таке ж, як і друге (однакові).\n\n![equal_to](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Порівняння** передає значення **істина**, коли обидва значення однакові\n\n**Порівняння** передає значення **хиба**, коли два значення різні.\n\nБлок **порівняння** працює з десятковими, цілими числами, значеннями з числових блоків.\n\nЛогічний блок **порівняння** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує \"Drivetrain Stalled\" на екрані VEX IQ Brain, якщо струм трансмісії дорівнюватиме 100%.\n\n![equal_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/equal_to/equal_to_example.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Завжди\n\n'C'-подібний блок, який нескінченно повторює всі блоки всередині.\n\n![forever](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nРозмістіть блоки у 'С'-подібному блоці **завжди**, щоб повторювати ці дії нескінченно.\n\nВи можете вийти з цикла **завжди**, розмістивши всередині блок **зупинити**.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\n'C'-подібні блоки можна ставити один в одного. Цей принцип називається гніздування і допомагає зберегти час під час програмування варіативної поведінки.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад гратиме один звук кожні 5 секунд і буде повторювати процес завжди.\n\n![forever_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/forever/forever_example.png)"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Функція\n\nВиконує вибрану математичну функцію.\n\n![function](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/function/function.png)\n\n* **модуль** - модуль значення\n* **округлити до меншого** - округлити до меншого цілого\n* **округлити до більшого** - округлити до більшого цілого\n* **корінь** - квадратний корінь\n* **sin** - синус\n* **cos** - косинус\n* **tan** - тангенс\n* **asin** - арксинус або обернений синус\n* **acos** - арккосинус або обернений косинус\n* **atan** - арктангенс або обернений тангенс\n* **ln** - натуральний логарифм із основою e\n* **log** - логарифм із основою 10\n* **e ^** - ступінь e\n* **10 ^** - ступінь 10\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **функція** працює з десятковими, цілими числами, значеннями з числових блоків.\n\nВиберіть математичну **функцію** зі списку варіантів\n\n![function_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/function/function_select.png)\n\nБлок **функція** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![function_fit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/function/function_fit.png)"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Більше\n\nПовідомляє, якщо перше значення більше за друге.\n\n![greater_than](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Більше** передає значення **істина**, коли перше значення більше за друге значення.\n\n**Більше** передає значення **хиба**, коли перше значення менше за друге значення або вони однакові.\n\nБлок **більше** працює з десятковими, цілими числами, значеннями з числових блоків.\n\nЛогічний блок **більше** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує \"Battery level good\" на екрані VEX IQ Brain, якщо рівень заряду акумулятора більше 75%.\n\n![greater_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/greater_than/greater_than_example.png)"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Курс гіродатчика\n\nПередає курс гіродатчика VEX IQ у градусах.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Курс гіродатчика** передає значення в діапазоні **від 0.00 до 359.99**.\n\n**Курс гіродатчика** рахує курс у напрямку проти годинникової стрілки, як показано на зображенні.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/heading_of_gyro/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\nВиберіть, який гіродатчик використати.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nБлок **Курс гіродатчика** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"hue_of":{"name":"hue_of","markdown":"# Відтінок\n\nПередає відтінок кольору, який побачив датчик кольору VEX IQ.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/hue_of/hue_of_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Відтінок** передає значення в діапазоні **від 0 до 360**.\n\nВиберіть, який датчик кольору використати.\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/hue_of/hue_of_color.png)\n\nБлок **відтінок** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![hue_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/hue_of/hue_of_inserted.png)"},"if_elseif_else":{"name":"if_elseif_else","markdown":"# Якщо тоді інакше якщо тоді інакше\n\n'C'-подібний блок виконує блоки всередині першої частини **якщо тоді інакше якщо тоді інакше**, якщо умова повертає значення істина.\n\n![if_elseif_else](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/if_elseif_else/if_elseif_else.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n'C'-подібний блок **якщо тоді інакше якщо тоді інакше** перевіряє значення логічної умови лише один раз.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова частини **якщо**передає значення **істина**, виконуються блоки всередині частини **якщо**.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова передає значення **хиба**, блок **якщо тоді інакше якщо тоді інакше** перевіряє перший рядок **інакше якщо**. Блок перевіряє значення умови кожного рядка **інакше якщо** по черзі, поки не отримає значення **істина**. Якщо отримано **істина**, виконуються вкладені під цим рядком блоки, потім виконується наступний блок після **якщо тоді інакше якщо тоді інакше**.\n\nЯкщо всі логічні умови рядків **інакше якщо** **хиба**, виконуються блоки всередині частини **інакше**.\n\n'C'-подібний блок **якщо тоді інакше якщо тоді інакше** приймає блоки шестикутної форми як логічну умову.\n\n\n![if_elseif_else_2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/if_elseif_else/if_elseif_else_2.png)\n\n## Як додати і видалити умову\n\nБлок **якщо тоді інакше якщо тоді інакше** унікальний тим, що ви можете додати додаткові умовні оператори. Блок дає змогу додати 6 умов **інакше якщо**.\n\n![if_elseif_else_expanded](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/if_elseif_else/if_elseif_else_expanded.png)\n\nЩоб додати умову **інакше якщо**, натисніть на \"+\" у рядку **інакше**. Це додасть новий рядок умови **інакше якщо** внизу поточного списку.\n\nЩоб видалити умову **інакше якщо**, натисніть на \"-\" у рядку **інакше**. Це прибере останній рядок умови **інакше якщо**, але не видалить блоки всередині цієї умови."},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Якщо то\n\n'C'-подібний блок виконує блоки всередині, якщо логічна умова має значення **істина**.  \n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n'C'-подібний блок **якщо то** перевіряє значення логічної умови лише один раз.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова передає значення **істина**, блоки всередині **якщо то** виконуються.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова передає значення **хиба**, блоки всередині **якщо то** ігноруються.\n\n'C'-подібний блок **якщо то** приймає блоки шестикутної форми як логічну умову.\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад грає звук щоразу, коли натискається бамперний перемикач VEX IQ.\n\n'C'-подібний блок **якщо то** можна “вкласти” або розмістити всередині блока завжди, щоб звук грав після кожного натискання, а не один раз.\n\n![if_then_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/if_then/if_then_example.png)"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Якщо то інакше\n\n'C'-подібний блок виконує блоки всередині першої або другої частини **якщо то інакше** залежно від значення логічної умови.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n'C'-подібний блок **якщо то інакше** перевіряє значення логічної умови лише один раз.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова передає значення **істина**, виконуються блоки всередині частини **якщо**.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова передає значення **хиба**, виконуються блоки всередині частини **інакше**.\n\n'C'-подібний блок **якщо то інакше** приймає блоки шестикутної форми як логічну умову.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад активує зелений колір, якщо LED датчик дотику VEX IQ натиснуто, і активує червоний колір, якщо LED датчик дотику не натиснуто.\n\n'C'-подібний блок **якщо то інакше** можна “вкласти” або розмістити всередині блока завжди, щоб LED датчик дотику перемикав колір більше, ніж один раз.\n\n![if_then_else_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/if_then_else/if_then_else_example.png)"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Елемент 2D списку\n\nПередає значення елемента 2D списку.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, який 2D список використати. 2D список також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nЩоб отримати елемент списку, введіть номер його рядка (перше число) і стовпця (друге число) в списку. У прикладі нижче буде отримано значення елемента 2D списку із позиції рядка 2 і стовпця 3.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nБлок **елемент 2D списку** приймає десяткові, цілі числа, значення з числових блоків.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Елемент списку\n\nПередає значення елемента списку.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, який список використати. Список також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nЩоб отримати елемент списку, введіть номер його позиції в списку. У прикладі нижче буде отримано значення другого елемента списку.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nБлок **елемент списку** приймає десяткові, цілі числа, значення з числових блоків.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад встановлює швидкість трансмісії у значення елемента 3 списку. Тепер трансмісія поїде вперед зі швидкістю 90%.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Довжина 2D списку\n\nПередає кількість рядків або стовпців у 2D списку.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, який 2D список використати. 2D список також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nВиберіть, яке значення передати. 2D список може передати **рядки** або **стовпців**. \n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\n**Довжина 2D списку** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Менше\n\nПовідомляє, якщо перше значення менше за друге.\n\n![less_than](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Менше** передає значення **істина**, коли перше значення менше за друге значення. \n\n**Менше** передає значення **хиба**, коли перше значення більше за друге значення або вони однакові.\n\nЛогічний блок **менше** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\nБлок **менше** працює з десятковими, цілими числами, значеннями з числових блоків.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує \"Low Battery!\" на екрані VEX IQ Brain, якщо рівень заряду акумулятора менше 25%.\n\n![less_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/less_than/less_than_example.png)\n\n"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Мотор зупинився\n\nПовідомляє, якщо вибраний мотор зупинився.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Мотор зупинився** передає значення **істина**, коли вибраний мотор  закінчив свою роботу.\n\n**Мотор зупинився** передає значення **хиба**, коли вибраний мотор досі працює.\n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nЛогічний блок **мотор зупинився** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Мотор обертається\n\nПовідомляє, якщо вибраний мотор обертається.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Мотор обертається** передає значення **істина**, коли вибраний мотор обертається.\n\n**Мотор обертається** передає значення **хиба**, коли вибраний мотор зупинено.\n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nЛогічний блок **мотор обертається** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Множення\n\nМножить будь-які два значення і передає добуток.\n\n![multiply](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Множення** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\nБлок **Множення** підходить до блоків, які мають круглий проміжок.\n\nМножте два числа.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nМножте значення змінних.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nМножте показники датчиків або пристроїв.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Наступний рядок\n\nВстановлює курсор для друку на екрані Brain в наступний доступний рядок.\n\n![next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЗа замовчуванням, усі проєкти починають із курсором в рядку 1 стовпці 1. Блок **наступний рядок** переміщує курсор на рядок нижче на екрані Brain.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/next_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує \"First Message\" і встановить курсор у наступний доступний рядок перед друком \"Second Message\".\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/next_row/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/next_row/set_cursor_welcome.png)"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# Не\n\nПередає протилежне (зворотнє) значення логічного входу.\n\n![not](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/not/not.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **не** передає значення **істина**, коли логічний блок всередині має значення **хиба**.\n\nБлок **не** передає значення **хиба**, коли логічний блок всередині має значення **істина**.\n\nЛогічний блок **не** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад передає значення **істина**, коли кнопка VEX IQ Brain \"обрати\" не натиснута. \n\n![not_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Кількість об'єктів\n\nПовідомляє, скільки об'єктів бачить датчик зору.\n\nОб'єкт треба налаштувати, щоб блок **кількість об'єктів** зміг його знайти.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть датчик зору.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nЩоб блок **кількість об'єктів** міг порахувати і передати кількість об'єктів, перед ним треба поставити блок **знімок**.\n\nБлок **кількість об'єктів** знайде кількість об'єктів лише з останнього знімку сигнатури."},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Об'єкт існує\n\nПовідомляє, чи датчик зору бачить налаштований об'єкт.\n\nОб'єкт треба налаштувати, щоб блок **об'єкт існує** міг його знайти.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть датчик зору.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n**Об'єкт існує** передає значення **істина**, коли датчик зору бачить налаштований об'єкт.\n\n**Об'єкт існує** передає значення **хиба**, коли датчик зору не бачить налаштований об'єкт.\n\nЛогічний блок **об'єкт існує** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nЩоб блок **об'єкт існує** міг передати значення **істина** або **хиба**, перед ним треба поставити блок **знімок**."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Знайшов об'єкт\n\nПовідомляє, якщо датчик відстані VEX IQ бачить об'єкт у полі зору.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Знайшов об'єкт** передає значення **істина**, коли датчик відстані бачить об'єкт або перешкоду в полі зору.\n\n**Знайшов об'єкт** передає значення **хиба**, коли датчик відстані не бачить об'єктів або перешкод.\n\nВиберіть, який датчик відстані використати.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nЛогічний блок **знайшов об'єкт** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"object_is_near":{"name":"object_is_near","markdown":"# Бачить об'єкт\n\nПовідомляє, якщо датчик кольору VEX IQ знайшов об'єкт попереду.\n\n![object_is_near](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_is_near/object_is_near_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Бачить об'єкт** передає значення **істина**, коли датчик кольору бачить перешкоду або об'єкт попереду датчика.\n\n**Бачить об'єкт** передає значення **хиба**, коли датчик кольору бачить пустий простір попереду датчика.\n\nВиберіть, який датчик кольору використати.\n\n![object_is_near_color](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_is_near/object_is_near_color.png)\n\nЛогічний блок **бачить об'єкт** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![object_is_near_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/object_is_near/object_is_near_inserted.png)\n\n\n "},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# Або\n\nПовідомляє, якщо одне або два логічні значення істинні.\n\n![or](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/or/or.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **або** передає значення **істина**, коли одне (або обидва) значення **істина**. \n\nБлок **або** передає значення **хиба**, коли обидва значення **хиба**.\n\nЛогічний блок **або** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\nБлок **або** передає значення **істина**, коли бампер VEX IQ, або LED датчик дотику VEX IQ, або обидва датчика натиснуті, і передає значення **хиба** лише коли обидва датчика не натиснуті.\n\n![or_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/or/or_truth.png)"},"play_note":{"name":"play_note","markdown":"# Грати ноту\n\nГрає вибрану музичну ноту.\n\n![play_note](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/play_note/play_note.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть музичну ноту.\n\n![play_note_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/play_note/play_note_select.png)\n\nВиберіть, як довго гратиме нота (тривалість).\n\n![play_note_duration](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/play_note/play_note_duration.png)\n\n* **Повністю** нота гратиме 1 секунду (1000 мілісекунд)\n* **Половину** нота гратиме 0,5 секунди (500 мілісекунд)\n* **Чверть** нота гратиме 0,25 секунди (250 мілісекунд)\n\nЩойно музична нота почне грати, наступний блок одразу спрацює."},"play_sound":{"name":"play_sound","markdown":"# Грати звук\n\nГрає вибраний звуковий ефект.\n\n![play_sound](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/play_sound/play_sound.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть звуковий ефект із варіантів списку. \n\n![play_sound_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/play_sound/play_sound_select.png)\n\nЩойно звуковий ефект почне грати, наступний блок одразу спрацює."},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Позиція контролера\n\nПередає позицію джойстика на контролері уздовж вісі\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Позиція контролера** передає значення в діапазоні **від -100 до 100**.\n\n**Позиція контролера** передає нуль (0), коли вісь джойстика посередині.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nВиберіть, позицію якої вісі джойстика перевіряти.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nБлок **позиція контролера** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад постійно перевіряє позицію вісі D джойстика, щоб контролювати швидкість мотора руки.\n\n![position_of_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Позиція мотора\n\nПередає відстань, яку проїхав мотор.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Позиція мотора** передає позицію мотора цілим числом у градусах або десятковим числом в обертах.\n\nВиберіть мотор, який використати.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nВиберіть, в яких одиницях передавати значення: у градусах або в обертах мотора.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nБлок **позиція мотора** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Бампер натиснуто\n\nПовідомляє, чи бамперний перемикач VEX IQ натиснуто.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Бампер натиснуто** передає значення **істина**, якщо бамперний перемикач натиснуто.\n\n**Бампер натиснуто** передає значення **хиба**, якщо бамперний перемикач не натиснуто.\n\nВиберіть, який бамперний перемикач використати.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nЛогічний блок **бампер натиснуто** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Контролер натиснуто\n\nПовідомляє, якщо кнопка на контролері VEX IQ натиснута.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Контролер натиснуто** передає значення **істина**, якщо вибрана кнопка контролера натиснута.\n\n**Контролер натиснуто** передає значення **хиба**, якщо вибрана кнопка контролера не натиснута.\n\nВиберіть, яку кнопку контролера використати.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nЛогічний блок **контролер натиснуто** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад перевіряє, чи кнопка E верхня натиснута, якщо так - обертає мотор клешні для відкривання.\n\n![pressing_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_example_revised.png)"},"pressing_touchled":{"name":"pressing_touchled","markdown":"# LED датчик дотику натиснуто\n\nПовідомляє, якщо LED датчик дотику натиснуто.\n\n![pressing_touch_led](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**LED датчик дотику натиснуто** передає значення **істина**, якщо обраний LED датчик дотику натиснуто.\n\n**LED датчик дотику натиснуто** передає значення **хиба**, якщо обраний LED датчик дотику не натиснуто.\n\nВиберіть, який LED датчик дотику використати.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_led](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_led.png)\n\nЛогічний блок **LED датчик дотику натиснуто** передає значення **істина** або **хиба** і підходить до блоків із шестикутним проміжком.\n\n![pressing_touch_led_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_inserted.png)\n\n"},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Надрукувати\n\nДрукує значення або текст на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/print/look_print.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **надрукувати** надрукує дані з позиції курсора на екрані Brain.\n\nВсі нові проєкти починають із курсором в рядку 1 стовпці 1.\n\nВсі блоки виведення друкуються цілими числами за замовчуванням. Використайте блок **встановити точність друку**, щоб налаштувати кількість надрукованих після коми знаків у десятковому числі.\n\nДрукуйте слова або числа.\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/print/print_words.png)\n\nДрукуйте значення змінних.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nДрукуйте результати розрахунків операцій.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nДрукуйте показники датчиків або пристроїв.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/print/print_sensor.png)"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Мої блоки\n\nМої блоки використовують для створення власних блоків.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Мої блоки** використовують для створення послідовності блоків, яку можна використати у проєкті декілька разів.\n\n**Мої блоки** створюють із використанням кнопки **Створити блок**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Мої блоки** можуть мати кілька параметрів для розширення функціоналу нових блоків - текстові позначки, числові та логічні входи.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nЩоб використати **мої блоки**, приєднайте створений **мій блок** до заголовного блока. Коли настане черга виконувати **мій блок**, стек усередині **мого блока** почне працювати, врахувавши введені параметри.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nПриєднайте стек блоків до заголовного блока \"визначити\" **мого блока**, щоб задати дії, які виконаються під час запуску **мого блока**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Примітка: створення кількох моїх блоків з однаковими текстовими позначками і входами для змінних може спричинити помилки під час завантаження проєкта.***\n\n## Приклад 1\n\nУ цьому прикладі робот використовує **мій блок** для:\n\n* Гри звуку сирени 3 рази.\n* Руху вперед на 300 міліметрів.\n* Гри звуку сирени 6 разів.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_call/sound_example.png)\n\n## Приклад 2\n\nУ цьому прикладі робот використовує **мій блок** для:\n\n* Руху вперед на 400 міліметрів\n* Друку заряду акумулятора і переміщення курсора на новий рядок на екрані Brain.\n* Повороту робота праворуч на 180 градусів\n* Друку заряду акумулятора і переміщення курсора на новий рядок на екрані Brain.\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Мій блок\n\nМої блоки використовують для створення власних блоків.\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Мої блоки** використовують для створення послідовності блоків, яку можна використати у проєкті декілька разів. \n\n**Мої блоки** створюють із використанням кнопки **Створити блок**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Мої блоки** можуть мати кілька параметрів для розширення функціоналу нових блоків - текстові позначки, числові та логічні входи.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nЩоб використати **мої блоки**, приєднайте створений **мій блок** до заголовного блока. Коли настане черга виконувати **мій блок**, стек усередині **мого блока** почне працювати, врахувавши введені параметри.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nПриєднайте стек блоків до заголовного блока \"визначити\" **мого блока**, щоб задати дії, які виконаються під час запуску **мого блока**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Примітка: створення кількох моїх блоків з однаковими текстовими позначками і входами для змінних може спричинити помилки під час завантаження проєкта.***\n\n## Приклад 1\n\nУ цьому прикладі робот використовує **мій блок** для:\n\n* Гри звуку сирени 3 рази.\n* Руху вперед на 300 міліметрів.\n* Гри звуку сирени 6 разів.\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_definition/sound_example.png)\n\n## Приклад 2\n\nУ цьому прикладі робот використовує **мій блок** для:\n\n* Руху вперед на 400 міліметрів\n* Друку заряду акумулятора і переміщення курсора на новий рядок на екрані Brain.\n* Повороту робота праворуч на 180 градусів\n* Друку заряду акумулятора і переміщення курсора на новий рядок на екрані Brain.\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/procedures_definition/print_number.png)"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Випадкове\n![random](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/random/random.png)\n\nПередає випадкове значення від найменшого до найбільшого значення у блоці.\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **випадкове** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\nБлок **випадкове** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\nУ цьому прикладі блок **випадкове** вибирає випадкову швидкість трансмісії.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nУ наступному прикладі блок **випадкове** передає випадкове значення часу для блока очікування.\n\n![random_control](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/random/random_control.png)"},"rate_of_gyro":{"name":"rate_of_gyro","markdown":"# Швидкість гіроскопа\n\nПередає кутову швидкість гіроскопічного датчика VEX IQ.\n\n![rate_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Швидкість гіроскопа** передає значення в діапазоні **від 0 до 249.99 dps**.\n\n**Швидкість гіроскопа** передає значення у градусах за секунду (dps).\n\nВиберіть, який гіродатчик використати.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nБлок **швидкість гіроскопа** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![rate_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_inserted.png)"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Остача\n\nДілить перше значення на друге значення і передає остачу.\n\n![remainder](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **остача** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\nЧисла, що діляться повністю, повертають нуль.\n\nБлок **остача** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад поділить 7 на 2 і поверне остачу, надрукувавши \"1\" на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Повторити\n\n'C'-подібний блок повторює блоки всередині задану кількість разів.\n\n![repeat](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВведіть число для визначення кількості повторювань, які здійснять блоки всередині **повторити**.\n \n'C'-подібний блок **повторити** працює з цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n'C'-подібні блоки можна ставити один в одного. Цей принцип називається гніздування і допомагає зберегти час під час програмування варіативної поведінки.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/repeat/repeat_select.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад повторюватиме гру звукового ефекта кожні 3 секунди 5 разів.\n\n![repeat_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/repeat/repeat_example.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Повторювати поки не\n\n'C'-подібний блок повторюватиме блоки всередині, поки логічна умова не матиме значення **істина**.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **Повторювати поки не** перевіряє логічну умову лише на початку кожного циклу.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова матиме значення **хиба**, блоки всередині **повторювати поки не** працюватимуть.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова матиме значення **істина**, блоки всередині **повторювати поки не** пропускаються.\n\n'C'-подібний блок **повторювати поки не** приймає блоки шестикутної форми.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад друкуватиме значення таймера на екрані VEX IQ Brain і змусить трансмісію їхати вперед, поки кнопка **обрати** не натиснута. Щойно кнопку **обрати** натиснути, трансмісія зупиниться.\n\n![repeat_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/repeat_until/repeat_until_example.png)"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Скинути таймер\n\nСкидає таймер VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nТаймер Brain починає відлік після старту кожного проєкта. Блок **скинути таймер** скидає таймер до 0 секунд.\n\n## Приклад\n\nУ цьому прикладі таймер буде скинуто, коли трансмісія проїде вперед упродовж 3 секунд. Коли мине 3 секунди, трансмісія зупиниться.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Кут повороту гіродатчика\n\nПередає кут повороту гіродатчика VEX IQ у градусах.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation.png](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Кут гіродатчика** передає **позитивне** значення, коли гіродатчик повертає **проти годинникової стрілки**.\n\n**Кут гіродатчика** передає **негативне** значення, коли гіродатчик повертає **за годинниковою стрілкою**.\n\nВиберіть, який гіродатчик використати.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_devices.png)\n\nБлок **кут гіродатчика** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Округлити\n\nОкругляє вхідне значення до найближчого цілого.\n\n![round](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/round/round.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЧисла з десятковою частиною 0,5 або більше **округляються** до більшого цілого, числа з десятковою частиною, меншою за 0,5, **округляються** до меншого цілого.\n\nБлок **округлити** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\nБлок **округлити** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад округлить 2,7 і надрукує \"3\".\n\n![round_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/round/round_variables.png)"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Надати 2D списку значення\n\nЗадає кожному елементу 2D списку введені значення.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПід час створення 2D списку ви можете встановити кількість **стовпців** списку в межах від 1 до 20 елементів і кількість **рядків** списку в межах від 1 до 20 елементів.\n\nВиберіть, який 2D список використати. 2D список також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nБлок **надати 2D списку значення** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Надати списку значення\n\nЗадає кожному елементу списку введені значення.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nДовжина списку (від 1 до 20 елементів) встановлюється під час створення списку.\n\nВиберіть, який список використати. Список також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nБлок **надати списку значення** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\nЦей приклад надає списку початкові значення, а потім викликає елемент №3 (90) зі списку, щоб встановити в це значення позицію руки. \n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Надати логічній змінній значення\n\nНадає логічній змінній обране значення.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, яку логічну змінну використати. Логічну змінну також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nВиберіть логічну змінну.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nБлок **надати логічній змінній значення** приймає блоки шестикутної форми.\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_color_sensor_brightness":{"name":"set_color_sensor_brightness","markdown":"# Встановити для датчика кольору яскравість\n\nВстановлює яскравість випромінюваного світла датчика кольору VEX IQ.\n\n![set_color_sensor_light](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_light.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nДатчик кольору має джерело світла, яке можна відрегулювати, щоб покращити розпізнавання кольору об'єкта або яскравості поверхні.\n\n**Встановити для датчика кольору яскравість** приймає значення в діапазоні **від 0% до 100%**. Чим більший % яскравості встановлено, тим яскравіше світитиме джерело світла датчика кольору.\n\nВиберіть, який датчик кольору використати.\n\n![set_color_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor.png)\n\nБлок **встановити для датчика кольору яскравість** працює з цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n![set_color_sensor_2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_2.png)"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# Встановити курсор\n\nВстановлює позицію курсора для блока **друкувати**.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВстановлює позицію рядка та стовпця курсора на екрані VEX IQ Brain, з якої відображатимуться команди **друкувати**.\n\n**Встановити курсор** приймає позицію **рядка** в діапазоні **від 1 до 5**.\n\n**Встановити курсор** приймає позицію **стовпця** в діапазоні **від 1 до 21**.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_cursor/row_column_index.png)  \n\nБлок **встановити курсор** працює з цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад встановлює позицію курсора в рядок 3 стовпець 8, а потім друкує текст \"Hello!\" на екрані Brain.\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_cursor/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_cursor/set_cursor_hello.png)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Встановити курс привода\n\nВстановлює значення курсу гіроскопа трансмісії.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **встановити курс привода** використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію курсу трансмісії на введене значення курсу, яке рахується в напрямку проти годинникової стрілки, як показано на зображенні.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n**Встановити курс привода** приймає позицію в діапазоні **від 0 до 360** градусів.\n\nБлок **встановити курс привода** працює з цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад поверне робота на загальний кут 135 градусів.\n\n![setDriveHeading_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_example_revised.png)\n\n- Поворот ліворуч на курс 45 градусів.\n- Встановлення поточної позиції курсу робота 0 градусів.\n- Поворот ліворуч на додаткові 90 градусів, оскільки позиція курсу в попередньому блоці була перевизначена."},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Встановити кут повороту привода\n\nВстановлює значення кута повороту трансмісії, якщо налаштовано гіроскопічний датчик VEX IQ.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **встановити кут повороту привода** використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію кута повороту трансмісії на введене позитивне або негативне значення.\n\nБлок **встановити кут повороту привода** працює з цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад поверне робота на загальний кут 210 градусів:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Поворот ліворуч (проти годинникової стрілки) на 120 градусів.\n- Встановлення поточної позиції кута повороту -45 градусів.\n- Поворот ліворуч (проти годинникової стрілки) на додаткові 90 градусів (від -45 градусів до +45 градусів) через перевизначення кута в попередньому блоці."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Встановити режим зупинки\n\nВстановлює поведінку трансмісії під час зупинки моторів.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n* **Гальмувати** змушує трансмісію миттєво зупинитися.\n* **По інерції** дає змогу трансмісії поступово зменшити оберти до зупинки.\n* **Утримувати** змушує трансмісію миттєво зупинитися і повертатиме її до позиції зупинки, якщо вона зміститься.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змушує трансмісію їхати вперед 3 секунди, а потім утримувати позицію після зупинки.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Обмежити час руху\n\nВстановлює часові обмеження на всі команди руху трансмісії.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЧасові обмеження руху трансмісії потрібні, щоб блоки руху, які не змогли досягти своєї позиції, не заважали працювати наступним блокам. Приклад трансмісії, яка не досягла своєї позиції - коли під час руху робот зіткнувся зі стіною і не може закінчити свій рух.\n\nБлок **обмежити час руху** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад зупинить команду **їхати** через дві секунди, якщо трансмісія не встигне проїхати 600 міліметрів. Щойно часові обмеження або відстань будуть подолані, трансмісія перейде до виконання команди **повернути**.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Встановити швидкість руху\n\nВстановлює швидкість руху трансмісії.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Встановити швидкість руху** задає швидкість трансмісії, але не запускає її рух. Необхідний блок **їхати**.\n\n**Встановити швидкість руху** приймає значення в діапазоні **від -100% до 100%** або **від -127rpm до 127rpm**.\n\nВстановлення швидкості трансмісії у від'ємне значення змусить її працювати у зворотному напрямку.\n\nВстановлення швидкості трансмісії в 0 спричинить зупинку трансмісії.\n\nБлок **встановити швидкість руху** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змусить трансмісію проїхати 300 міліметрів зі швидкістю 50%.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_example.png)"},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Задати курс для гіроскопа\n\nВстановлює поточну позицію курсу гіроскопічного датчика у задане значення. \n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **задати курс для гіроскопа** використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію курсу гіродатчика на введене значення курсу, яке рахується в напрямку проти годинникової стрілки, як показано на зображенні.\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_gyro_heading/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\n**Задати курс для гіроскопа** приймає позицію в діапазоні **від 0 до 360** градусів.\n\nБлок **задати курс для гіроскопа** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\nВиберіть, який гіродатчик використати.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Задати кут повороту для гіроскопа\n\nВстановлює кут повороту гіродатчика VEX IQ в задане значення.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **задати кут повороту для гіроскопа** використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію кута повороту гіродатчика на введене позитивне (проти годинникової стрілки) або негативне (за годинниковою стрілкою) значення.\n\n**Задати кут повороту для гіроскопа** приймає позицію в межах будь-якого негативного або позитивного десяткового чи цілого числа.\n\nБлок **задати кут повороту для гіроскопа** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\nВиберіть, який гіродатчик використати.\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation_devices.png)"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Замінити елемент в 2D списку\n\nЗмінює значення елемента 2D списку на нове.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВведіть рядок (перший номер) і стовпець (другий номер) позиції елемента у списку, щоб замінити його.\n\nВиберіть, який список використати. Список також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nБлок **замінити елемент** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Замінити елемент\n\nЗмінює значення елемента списку на нове.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, який список використати. Список також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nБлок **замінити елемент** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n\nЦей приклад змінює елемент №2 у моєму списку на 15 і друкує цей елемент на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![replace_item_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_item_of_array/replace_item_example.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Встановити мотор у позицію\n\nВстановлює значення позиції енкодера мотора VEX IQ на введену величину.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **встановити мотор у позицію** використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію мотора на задане значення.\n\nЗазвичай, блок **встановити мотор у позицію** використовують, щоб скинути позицію енкодера мотора в 0.\n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nВиберіть одиниці вимірювання: градуси або оберти.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Встановити для мотора режим зупинки\n\nВстановлює поведінку мотора VEX IQ під час зупинки.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n* **Гальмувати** змушує мотор миттєво зупинитися.\n* **По інерції** дає змогу мотору поступово зменшити оберти до зупинки.\n* **Утримувати** змушує мотор миттєво зупинитися і повертатиме його до позиції зупинки, якщо він зміститься.\n\nБлок **встановити для мотора режим зупинки** впливатиме на роботу всіх команд для мотора у цьому проєкті.\n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nВиберіть параметр для мотора після зупинки.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змусить мотор руки рухатися вгору 90 градусів, а потім миттєво зупинитися.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Обмежити час руху для мотора\n\nВстановлює часові обмеження на всі команди руху мотора VEX IQ.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЧасові обмеження руху мотора потрібні, щоб блоки руху, які не змогли досягти своєї позиції, не заважали працювати наступним блокам. Приклад мотору, який не досягнув своєї позиції - клешня або рука, яка зіштовхнулась із механічними обмеженнями і не може закінчити свій рух.\n\nБлок **обмежити час руху для мотора** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад зупинить команду **обертати мотор** через 2 секунди, якщо ClawMotor не встигне досягти позиції 270 градусів. Щойно часові обмеження або обертання будуть подолані, ClawMotor обертатиметься до позиції 0 градусів.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Встановити крутний момент мотора\n\nВстановлює силу обертання мотора VEX IQ.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Встановити крутний момент мотора** приймає значення в діапазоні **від 0% до 100%**.\n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nБлок **встановити крутний момент мотора** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад обертатиме ClawMotor в позицію 40 градусів із крутним моментом 20%. Це дасть змогу клешні схопити об'єкт без пошкоджень від надмірного стиснення.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Встановити для мотора швидкість\n\nВстановлює швидкість для мотора VEX IQ.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Встановити для мотора швидкість** приймає значення в діапазоні **від -100% до 100%** або **від -127rpm до 127rpm**.\n\nВстановлення швидкості мотора у від'ємне значення змусить його обертатися у зворотному напрямку.\n\nВстановлення швидкості мотора в 0 спричинить його зупинку.\n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nВиберіть, в яких одиницях встановити швидкість: у % або в обертах за хвилину (rpm).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад встановлює повільне обертання мотора руки зі швидкістю 25% на 90 градусів.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Встановити точність друку\n\nВстановлює кількість надрукованих після коми знаків десяткового числа або блока на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть рівень точності, з якою вставлений блок виведення друкуватиме на екрані.\n\n* Цілі (1) (За замовчуванням)\n* Десяті (0.1)\n* Соті (0.01)\n* Тисячні (0.001)\n* Всі знаки (0.000001)\n\nБлок виведення друкуватиме на екрані результат, округлений до найближчого рівня точності. Наприклад, 1,67 буде надруковано як 2 на рівні точності цілих і як 1,7 на рівні точності десятих.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_touchled_brightness":{"name":"set_touchled_brightness","markdown":"# Встановити для LED датчика дотику яскравість\n\nВстановлює рівень яскравості LED датчика дотику VEX IQ.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Встановити для LED датчика дотику яскравість** приймає значення в діапазоні **від 0% до 100%**.\n\nВиберіть, який LED датчик дотику використати.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor3](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_sensor3.png)\n\nБлок **встановити для LED датчика дотику яскравість** працює з цілими числами та числовими блоками.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness2.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змушує LED датчик дотику випромінювати зелене світло з яскравістю 25%.\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness_example.png)"},"set_touchled_color":{"name":"set_touchled_color","markdown":"# Встановити для LED датчика дотику колір\n\nВстановлює колір для LED датчика дотику VEX IQ. \n\n![set_touchLED_color](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, який **LED датчик дотику** використати.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_sensor.png)\n\nВиберіть колір світіння.\n\n![set_touchLED_color2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color2.png)\n\nЩоб вимкнути підсвітку **LED датчика дотику**, встановіть колір \"нічого\".\n\nВи також можете зробити, щоб колір **LED датчика дотику** змінювався на колір, який побачить датчик кольору.\n\n![set_touchLED_color3](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color3.png)"},"set_touchled_fade":{"name":"set_touchled_fade","markdown":"# Встановити швидкість зникання LED датчика дотику\n\nВизначає, як швидко відбудеться перехід між кольорами LED датчика дотику VEX IQ.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, який LED датчик дотику використати.\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_sensor2.png)\n\nВиберіть, як швидко відбудеться перехід LED датчика дотику.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_speed](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_speed.png)\n\n* Повільно - LED датчик дотику повільно змінюватиме колір.\n* Швидко - LED датчик дотику швидко змінюватиме колір.\n* Вимкнено - LED датчик дотику миттєво змінюватиме колір.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад повільно змінить колір LED датчика дотику на синій.\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Встановити швидкість повороту\n\nВстановлює швидкість поворотів трансмісії.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Встановити швидкість повороту** задає швидкість повороту трансмісії, але не запускає її рух. Необхідний блок **повернути**.\n\nБлок **Встановити швидкість повороту** приймає значення в діапазоні **від -100% до 100%** або **від -127rpm до 127rpm**.\n\nВстановлення швидкості повороту трансмісії у від'ємне значення змусить її повертати у зворотному напрямку.\n\nВстановлення швидкості повороту трансмісії в 0 спричинить зупинку трансмісії.\n\nБлок **встановити швидкість повороту** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змусить трансмісію повертати ліворуч зі швидкістю 25%.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Надати змінній значення\n\nНадає змінній введене значення.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, яку змінну використати. Змінну також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nБлок **надати змінній значення** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надає змінній \"myVariable\" показники датчика відстані VEX IQ і використовує \"myVariable\" для встановлення швидкості трансмісії.\n\n![set_variable_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_variable/set_variable_example.png)"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Встановити для об'єкта з датчика зору індекс\n\nВибирає об'єкт (про який ви хочете дізнатись більше) серед усіх виявлених об'єктів.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **кількість об'єктів** ставиться перед блоком **встановити для об'єкта з датчика зору індекс**, щоб визначити кількість виявлених об'єктів.\n\nВиберіть, який датчик зору використати.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nБлок **встановити для об'єкта з датчика зору індекс** працює з цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n\n\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Довжина списку\n\nПередає кількість елементів у списку.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\nВиберіть, який список використати. Список також можна перейменувати або видалити.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nБлок **довжина списку** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"﻿# Зробити знімок\n\nДатчик зору робить знімок.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **зробити знімок** фіксує поточне зображення з датчика зору, щоб обробити і проаналізувати його на сигнатури кольору та коди.\n\nЗазвичай, блок **зробити знімок** потрібно ставити перед усіма іншими блоками датчика зору.\n\nВиберіть, який датчик зору використати.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nВиберіть, яку сигнатуру кольору використати. Налаштувати сигнатури кольору можна з вікна пристроїв.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Обертати\n\nОбертає мотор VEX IQ.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **обертати** постійно крутитиме мотор, поки не запрацює інший блок мотору або програма не зупиниться.\n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nВиберіть напрямок обертання. Можна змінити назву напрямку у вікні пристроїв.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Повернути\n\nПовертає мотор VEX IQ на певну величину.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **повернути** повідомляє мотору, в який бік і на яку відстань прокрутитися відносно поточної позиції.\n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nВиберіть напрямок повороту. Можна змінити назву напрямку у вікні пристроїв.\n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nБлок **повернути** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\nВиберіть одиниці вимірювання: градуси або повороти.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nЗа замовчуванням, інші блоки **чекатимуть**, поки мотор не прокрутиться.\n\nВи можете натиснути на стрілку, щоб активувати **і не чекати** - це змусить наступні блоки продовжувати роботу, поки мотор обертається.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Повернути у позицію\n\nПовертає мотор VEX IQ у певну позицію.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **повернути у позицію** повідомляє мотору, в яку позицію прокрутитися. Зважаючи на поточну позицію мотора, **повернути у позицію** сам обере напрямок обертання.\n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nБлок **повернути у позицію** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\nВиберіть одиниці вимірювання: градуси або повороти.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nЗа замовчуванням, інші блоки **чекатимуть**, поки мотор не прокрутиться.\n\nВи можете натиснути на стрілку, щоб активувати **і не чекати** - це змусить наступні блоки продовжувати роботу, поки мотор обертається.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Зупинитися\n\nЗупиняє трансмісію.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад зупинить трансмісію через 3 секунди.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Зупинити мотор\n\nЗупиняє мотор.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, який мотор зупинити.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад обертатиме мотор 3 секунди до зупинки.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Віднімання\n\nВіднімає одне значення від іншого і передає різницю.\n\n![subtract](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Віднімання** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\nБлок **віднімання** підходить до блоків, які мають круглий проміжок.\n\nВіднімайте одне число від іншого.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nВіднімайте значення змінних.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nВіднімайте показники датчиків або пристроїв.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Значення таймера\n\nПовертає значення таймера з VEX IQ Brain у секундах.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nТаймер починає відлік з 0 секунд, коли програма запускається, і передає десяткові значення.\n\nБлок **значення таймера** підходить до блоків, які мають круглий проміжок.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад запускає трансмісію вперед і грає звук 4,5 секунди, а потім повертає праворуч на 90 градусів.\n\n![timerValue_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/timer_value/timerValue_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Повернути\n\nНескінченно повертає трансмісію.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **повернути** постійно повертатиме трансмісію, поки не запрацює інший блок трансмісії або програма не зупиниться.\n\nВиберіть напрямок обертання трансмісії.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Поворот на\n\nПовертає трансмісію на певний кут.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть напрямок обертання трансмісії.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\nБлок **поворот на** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\nВстановіть величину кута повороту трансмісії у градусах.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nЗа замовчуванням, інші блоки **чекатимуть**, поки трансмісія не поверне.\n\nВи можете натиснути на стрілку, щоб активувати **і не чекати** - це змусить наступні блоки продовжувати роботу, поки трансмісія повертає.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Повернути на курс\n\nПовертає трансмісію на визначений курс, якщо налаштовано гіроскопічний датчик VEX IQ.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **повернути на курс** використовують, щоб повернути трансмісію на введене значення курсу, яке рахується в напрямку проти годинникової стрілки, як показано на зображенні.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nЗважаючи на поточну позицію гіродатчика, **повернути на курс** сам обере напрямок обертання.\n\n**Повернути на курс** приймає значення в діапазоні **від 0.00 до 359.99** градусів.\n\nБлок **повернути на курс** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змусить трансмісію здійснити 4 повороти: \n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 45 градусів\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 90 градусів\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 270 градусів\n- Праворуч (за годинниковою) до 180 градусів\n\nЗа замовчуванням, інші блоки **чекатимуть**, поки трансмісія не поверне.\n\nВи можете натиснути на стрілку, щоб активувати **і не чекати** - це змусить наступні блоки продовжувати роботу, поки трансмісія повертає.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Повернути на кут\n\nПовертає трансмісію на визначений кут, якщо налаштовано гіроскопічний датчик VEX IQ.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **повернути на кут** використовують, щоб повернути трансмісію на введене позитивне (проти годинникової стрілки) або негативне (за годинниковою стрілкою) значення.\n\nЗважаючи на поточний **кут повороту** гіродатчика, **повернути на кут** сам обере напрямок обертання.\n\nБлок **повернути на кут** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змусить трансмісію здійснити 4 повороти:\n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 90 градусів\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 180 градусів\n- Праворуч (за годинниковою) до -45 градусів\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 0 градусів\n\nЗа замовчуванням, інші блоки **чекатимуть**, поки трансмісія не поверне.\n\nВи можете натиснути на стрілку, щоб активувати **і не чекати** - це змусить наступні блоки продовжувати роботу, поки трансмісія повертає.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Змінна\n\nПовертає значення, записане у змінну.\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **змінна** використовують для отримання значень, збережених у змінній. Використайте блок **надати значення змінній**, щоб записати або оновити значення змінної.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nБлок **змінна** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nЗмінну можна створити після натискання на кнопку **Створити змінну**.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/variable/make_variable.png)"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Швидкість мотора\n\nПовертає поточну швидкість мотора VEX IQ.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Швидкість мотора** передає значення в діапазоні **від -100% до 100%** або **від -127rpm до 127rpm**.\n\nВиберіть, який мотор використати.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nВиберіть, в яких одиницях повідомляти швидкість: у % або в обертах за хвилину (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nБлок **швидкість мотора** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Об'єкт датчика зору\n\nПовертає інформацію про знайдений датчиком зору об'єкт.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЩоб використати блок **об'єкт датчика зору**, виконайте наступні кроки:\n1. Налаштуйте ваш датчик зору у вікні пристроїв.\n2. Використайте блок **зробити знімок**, щоб захопити зображення з датчика зору і пошукати на ньому сигнатури або коди кольору.\n3. Використайте блок **об'єкт існує**, щоб перевірити, чи датчик зору знайшов потрібну сигнатуру / коди кольору.\n\nЩойно датчик зору побачить об'єкт, використайте інші блоки датчика зору, щоб дізнатися більше про об'єкт.\n\n* Використайте блок **встановити для об'єкта з датчика зору індекс**, щоб вибрати об'єкт з усіх знайдених, про який ви хочете дізнатися більше. За замовчуванням, вибирається найбільший знайдений об'єкт.\n* Використайте блок **кількість об'єктів**, щоб визначити, скільки сигнатур / кодів кольору було знайдено.\n* Використайте блок **об'єкт датчика зору**, щоб отримати інформацію про знайдений об'єкт.\n\nВиберіть, який датчик зору використати.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nВиберіть, яке значення з датчика зору отримувати:\n\n* Ширина - наскільки широкий об'єкт у пікселях. Повертає значення у межах **2 - 316 px**.\n* Висота - наскільки високий об'єкт у пікселях. Повертає значення у межах **2 - 212 px**. \n* ЦентрX - повідомляє координату X центра знайденого об'єкта. Повертає значення у межах **0 - 315 px**.\n* ЦентрY - повідомляє координату Y центра знайденого об'єкта. Повертає значення у межах **0 - 211 px**.\n* Кут - повідомляє кут знайденого об'єкта. Повертає значення у межах **0 - 180 градусів**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nБлок **об'єкт датчика зору** підходить до блоків із круглим проміжком.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Чекати\n\nСтворює часову затримку певної тривалості перед наступним блоком.\n\n![wait](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВстановіть, скільки часу **чекати**.\n\nБлок **чекати** працює з десятковими, цілими числами або числовими блоками.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змінює колір LED датчика дотику VEX IQ з червоного на зелений із **затримкою** 3,25 секунд.\n\n![wait_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/wait/wait_example.png)"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Чекати поки не\n\nЧекає, поки логічний блок не поверне **істина**, і потім працюють наступні блоки.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Чекати поки не** постійно перевіряє результат логічного блока і не запустить наступні блоки, поки логічний блок не передасть **істина**.\n\nЛогічний блок **чекати поки не** приймає блоки шестикутної форми.\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад вмикає жовту підсвітку LED датчика дотику VEX IQ і чекає поки не натиснути LED датчик дотику. Щойно його натиснуть, Brain надрукує \"Done!\" на екрані.\n\n![wait_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/wait_until/wait_until_example.png)"},"when_brain_button":{"name":"when_brain_button","markdown":"# Коли кнопку на Brain\n\nЗапускає приєднаний стек блоків, коли вибрану кнопку на VEX IQ Brain  натиснуто або відтиснуто.\n\n![when_brain_button](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_brain_button/when_brain_button.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, яку кнопку Brain використати.\n\n![when_brain_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select.png)\n\nВиберіть, яка дія активує подію - **натиснуто** або **відтиснуто**.\n\n![when_brain_button_select_2](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select_2.png)  \n"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Коли отримано\n\nЗапускає приєднаний стек блоків, коли вибране повідомлення отримано від блока **надіслати**.\n![when_broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, на яке повідомлення чекати. Можна створити нове повідомлення.\n\nБлок **коли отримано** спрацює лише на повідомлення від блоків **надіслати** або **надіслати і чекати** з інших стеків.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад активує червону підсвітку LED датчика дотику VEX IQ і чекає 2 секунди, після чого передає \"message1\". \n\nЩойно повідомлення отримано, стек **коли отримано** запускає трансмісію на рух вперед, водночас із мотором ClawMotor з першого стека.\n\nДва стека продовжують працювати водночас, як показано червоними стрілками на зображенні.\n\n![when_broadcast_example](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_example.png)\n\n"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Коли бампер\n\nЗапускає приєднаний стек блоків, коли вибраний бампер VEX IQ натиснуто або відтиснуто.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, який бамперний перемикач використати.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nВиберіть, яка дія активує подію - **натиснуто** або **відтиснуто**.\n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Коли вісь контролера\n\nЗапускає приєднаний стек блоків, коли вибрана вісь джойстика контролера VEX IQ рухається.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, яку вісь джойстика контролера використати.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Коли кнопку контролера\n\nЗапускає приєднаний стек блоків, коли вибрану кнопку контролера VEX IQ натиснуто або відтиснуто.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, яку кнопку контролера використати.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_controller_button/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_controller_button/controller_button_back.png)\n\nВиберіть, яка дія активує подію - **натиснуто** або **відтиснуто**.\n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Коли почнемо\n\nЗапускає приєднаний стек блоків, коли запускається проєкт.\n\n![when_started](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПодія **коли почнемо** спрацює, коли програму запустити з меню VEX IQ Brain або кнопкою **Запуск** із VEXcode IQ.\n\nКожен новий проєкт автоматично додає блок **коли почнемо**. Проєкти підтримують до 3 блоків **коли почнемо** водночас."},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Коли таймер\n\nЗапускає приєднаний стек блоків, коли час таймера VEX IQ Brain більший за введене значення.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nТаймер Brain починає відлік після старту кожного проєкта.\n\nВиберіть бажаний час. Подія **коли таймер** спрацює, коли таймер Brain матиме час, **більший за** введене значення.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nБлок **коли таймер** працює з десятковими та цілими числами.\n\nБлок **коли таймер** не може приймати інші блоки."},"when_touchled":{"name":"when_touchled","markdown":"# Коли LED датчик дотику\n\nЗапускає приєднаний стек блоків, коли вибраний LED датчик дотику натиснуто або відтиснуто.\n\n![when_touchLED](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_touchled/when_touchled.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, який LED датчик дотику використати.\n\n![when_touchLED_select](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_touchled/when_touchled_select.png)\n\nВиберіть, яка дія активує подію - **натиснуто** або **відтиснуто**. \n\n![when_touchLED_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/when_touchled/when_touchled_condition.png)"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Поки\n\n'C'-подібний блок, який повторює блоки всередині, поки логічна умова має результат **істина**. \n\n![while](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/while/while.png)\n\n## Як це працює\n\nБлок **поки** перевіряє логічну умову лише на початку кожного циклу.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова матиме значення **істина**, блоки всередині **поки** працюватимуть.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова матиме значення **хиба**, блоки всередині **поки** пропускаються.\n\n'C'-подібний блок **поки** приймає блоки шестикутної форми.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/uk/while/while_inserted.png)"}},"cpp":{"control_break":{"name":"control_break","markdown":"# Break\n\nНегайно виходить із повторюваного циклу.\n\n```cpp\nbreak;\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЯкщо її додати в цикл, команда `break` вийде з циклу в момент виконання.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад запускає трансмісію вперед і перевіряє, чи натиснута кнопка Вгору на VEX IQ Brain.\n\nЯкщо кнопку Вгору натиснути, команда `break` вийде з циклу `while` і зупинить трансмісію.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n  if (Brain.buttonUp.pressing()) {\n    break;\n  }\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"control_break"},"control_for":{"name":"control_for","markdown":"# For\n\nПовторює код всередині фігурних дужок встановлену кількість разів.\n\n```cpp\nfor (initialization; condition; increment/decrement) {\n  // якийсь код для повторювання\n}\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВведіть значення, щоб визначити, скільки разів **повториться** код, використовуючи 3 параметри:\n\n* оголошення\n* умова\n* інкремент/декремент\n\n**Оголошення** задає початкове значення ітеративної змінної.\n\n**Умова** визначає, як довго працюватиме цикл for. Цикл припинить повторюватися, коли значення умови стане **false**.\n\n**Інкремент/декремент** змінює значення ітеративної змінної наприкінці кожного виконаного циклу.\n\n## Приклад 1\n\nЦей приклад надрукує числа від 0 до 9 на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nfor (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"%d\", i);\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```\n## Приклад 2\n\nЦей приклад запустить робота VEX IQ вперед на 250 мм, а потім поверне його праворуч на 60 градусів тричі.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 250, mm);\n\nfor (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n  Drivetrain.turnFor(right, 60, degrees);\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"control_for"},"control_if":{"name":"control_if","markdown":"# If\n\nВиконує код всередині фігурних дужок оператора if, якщо умова повертає true. \n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n  // код, який виконається, якщо умова true\n}\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Оператор if** перевіряє свою умову в круглих дужках лише один раз.\n\nЯкщо умова повертає **true**, код всередині фігурних дужок виконається.\n\nЯкщо умова повертає **false**, код всередині фігурних дужок буде пропущено.\n\n```cpp\n// Зупинити Motor1, якщо  BumperA натиснуто\nif (BumperA.pressing()) {\n  Motor1.stop();\n}\n```","signature":"control_if"},"control_if_else":{"name":"control_if_else","markdown":"# If/else\n\nОператор керування, який виконає код всередині першої або другої пари фігурних дужок залежно від того, яке логічне значення умови.\n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n  // Цей код виконається, якщо умова поверне true\n} else {\n  // Цей код виконається, якщо умова поверне false\n}\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nОператор if/else перевіряє значення логічної умови лише один раз.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова `(condition)` повертає **true**, код всередині фігурних дужок `if` виконається.\n\nЯкщо логічна умова `(condition)` повертає **false**, код всередині фігурних дужок `else` виконається.\n\n## Приклад\n\nУ цьому прикладі LED датчик дотику VEX IQ засвітиться зеленим, якщо на нього натиснути, і засвітиться червоним, якщо ні.\n\nУмову if/else можна “вкласти” або розмістити всередині циклу while, щоб LED датчик дотику перемикав колір більше, ніж один раз.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  if (TouchLED.pressing()) {\n    TouchLED.setColor(green);\n  } else {\n    TouchLED.setColor(red);\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"control_if_else"},"control_repeat":{"name":"control_repeat","markdown":"# Repeat\n\nПовторює команди всередині фігурних дужок задану в круглих дужках кількість разів.\n`repeat (number of times to repeat){code to repeat}`\n\n```\nrepeat (10) {\n\n}\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Оператор repeat** циклічно виконуватиме код всередині фігурних дужок, поки не досягне встановленої в умові кількості виконань.\n\nСпершу, задайте кількість разів, яку код повторюватиметься, вписавши в умову додатне ціле число. Умова може бути змінною або даними з датчиків.\n\nФрагмент нижче надрукує \"iteration\" на екрані Brain чотири рази. Щоразу він створюватиме новий рядок перед друкуванням наступної ітерації.\n\n```\nrepeat (4) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"iteration\");\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  wait(5, msec);\n}\n```\n\nЗверніть увагу, що **оператор repeat** не можна розміщувати в іншому операторі repeat.","signature":"repeat(10) { }"},"control_wait":{"name":"control_wait","markdown":"# Wait\n\nОчікує визначену кількість часу перед виконанням наступної команди.\n\n```cpp\nwait(time, units);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВстановіть кількість часу в **seconds** (секундах) або **msec** (мілісекундах), щоб програма почекала - `wait` - перед виконанням наступних команд.\n\n```cpp\nwait(10, seconds);\nwait(100, msec);\n```","signature":"wait(time, units);"},"control_waitUntil":{"name":"control_waitUntil","markdown":"# Wait Until\n\nПовторює частину коду, поки задана **умова** не поверне **true**.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (!condition) { \n  // Код повторюватиметься, поки умова не поверне true\n}\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЦей оператор керування постійно перевірятиме свою умову і **не** виконуватиме свій код, поки умова повертає **true**. Він може повторити весь код у фігурних дужках.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (!TouchLED.pressing()) {\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```\n\n## Приклад \n\nЦей приклад вмикає жовтий колір LED датчика дотику і чекає, поки на нього не натиснуть. Щойно натиснуть, LED датчик дотику змінить колір на зелений.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(yellow);\n\nwhile (!TouchLED.pressing()) {\n  wait(1, seconds);\n}\n\nTouchLED.setColor(green);\n```","signature":"control_waitUntil"},"control_while":{"name":"control_while","markdown":"# While\n\nЦикл, який повторює код всередині, поки **умова** має результат **true**.   \n\n```cpp\nwhile (condition) {\n  // Код повторюватиметься, поки умова повертає true\n}\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЦикл `while` перевіряє значення умови в круглих дужках на початку кожного циклу.\n\nЯкщо умова повертає значення **true**, код всередині `while` виконається.\n\nЯкщо умова повертає значення **false**, код всередині `while` буде пропущено.\n\nЦикл `while` приймає у свою умову все, що може мати значення **true** або **false**. Умови можуть бути булевими (логічними) або результатом порівнянь чи логічних операторів.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад запустить робота VEX IQ вперед, поки значення таймера менше 60 секунд.\n\nЧерез 60 секунд робот зупиниться.\n\n```cpp\nwhile(Brain.Timer.value() < 60) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"control_while"},"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain":{"name":"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain","markdown":"# Calibrate Drivetrain\n\nКалібрує трансмісію, якщо налаштовано гіроскопічний датчик VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\ncalibrateDrivetrain();\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиклик команди `calibrateDrivetrain` на початку програми для калібрування трансмісії.\n\n```cpp\nint main() {\n  // Калібрування трансмісії на початку головної функції\n  calibrateDrivetrain();\n\n  // Сюди додавати інший код\n  Drivetrain.driveFor(forward, 500, mm);\n  Drivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n}\n```\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад калібрує трансмісію VEX IQ перед рухом вперед на 200 мм і поворотом на курс 45 градусів.\n\n```cpp\ncalibrateDrivetrain();\n\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45, degrees);\n```","signature":"calibrateDrivetrain();"},"drivetrain_drive":{"name":"drivetrain_drive","markdown":"# Drive\n\nРухає трансмісію вперед.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(direction);\n```\n\nВсі мотори трансмісії запускаються вперед або назад зі швидкістю, встановленою командою `Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity`. Швидкість за замовчуванням 50 rpm (об/хв).\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Drivetrain.drive` постійно рухатиме трансмісію, поки не запрацює нова команда трансмісії або програма не зупиниться.\n\nВикористайте параметр **forward**, щоб запустити трансмісію на рух уперед.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n```\n\nВикористайте параметр **reverse**, щоб запустити трансмісію у зворотному напрямку.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(reverse);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.drive(forward);"},"drivetrain_drive_for":{"name":"drivetrain_drive_for","markdown":"# Drive For\n\nРухає трансмісію на задану відстань\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(direction, distance, units);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть напрямок - `direction` - руху трансмісії: **forward** або **reverse**. \n\nВстановіть відстань, яку проїде трансмісія, ввівши числове значення `distance`. \n\nПотім, визначте одиниці вимірювання `units`: **inches** або **mm**.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(reverse, 5, inches);\n```\n\nКоманда `Drivetrain.driveFor` за замовчуванням блокує інші команди, поки трансмісія рухається.\n\n## Необов'язкові параметри\n\nВи можете встановити значення останнього параметра `false`, щоб команда `Drivetrain.driveFor` не блокувала програму під час виконання руху.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.driveFor(forward, 1, inches);"},"drivetrain_set_drive_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Set Rotation\n\nВстановлює значення кута повороту трансмісії, якщо  налаштовано гіроскопічний датчик VEX IQ.\n\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setRotation(value, rotationUnits);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманду `Drivetrain.setRotation()` використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію кута повороту трансмісії на введене позитивне або негативне значення.\n\nКоманда `Drivetrain.setRotation()` приймає цілі, числові значення.\n\nКоманда `Drivetrain.setRoation()` **не** має обмежень у 0-359 градусів.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад поверне робота на загальний кут 210 градусів:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(120, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n```\n\n- Поворот ліворуч (проти годинникової стрілки) на 120 градусів.\n- Встановлення поточної позиції кута повороту -45 градусів.\n- Поворот ліворуч (проти годинникової стрілки) на додаткові 90 градусів (від -45 градусів до +45 градусів) через перевизначення кута в попередній команді.","signature":"Drivetrain.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Set Drive Velocity\n\nВстановлює швидкість руху трансмісії для команд `Drivetrain.drive` і `Drivetrain.driveFor`. \n\nЯкщо ця команда спрацьовує, коли трансмісія рухається, то трансмісія змінить свою швидкість на нову.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity` задає швидкість трансмісії, але не запускає її рух.\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity` приймає значення в діапазоні **від -100 до 100**, коли використано одиниці **percent** - відсотки.\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity` приймає значення в діапазоні **від -127 до 127**, коли використано одиниці **rpm** - оберти за хвилину.\n\nВстановлення швидкості трансмісії у від'ємне значення змусить її працювати у зворотному напрямку.\n\nВстановлення швидкості трансмісії в 0 спричинить зупинку трансмісії.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змусить трансмісію проїхати 300 міліметрів зі швидкістю 50%.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(50, percent);\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 30, mm);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity(50, percent);"},"drivetrain_set_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_set_heading","markdown":"# Set Heading\n\nВстановлює значення курсу гіроскопа трансмісії.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setHeading(heading, degrees);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманду `Drivetrain.setHeading` використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію курсу трансмісії. \n\n`Drivetrain.setHeading` приймає позицію в діапазоні **від 0 до 359.99** для параметра `heading`.\n\n## Приклад \n\nЦей приклад поверне робота на загальний кут 135 градусів.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setHeading(0.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees);\n```\n- Поворот ліворуч на курс 45 градусів.\n- Встановлення поточної позиції курсу робота 0 градусів.\n- Поворот ліворуч на додаткові 90 градусів, оскільки позиція курсу в попередній команді була перевизначена.","signature":"Drivetrain.setHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_rotation","markdown":"# Set Drive Rotation\n\nВстановлює значення кута повороту трансмісії, якщо налаштовано гіроскопічний датчик VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманду `Drivetrain.setRotation` використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію кута повороту трансмісії на введене позитивне або негативне значення.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад поверне робота на загальний кут 210 градусів:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(120, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n```\n\n- Поворот ліворуч (проти годинникової стрілки) на 120 градусів.\n- Встановлення поточної позиції кута повороту -45 градусів.\n- Поворот ліворуч (проти годинникової стрілки) на додаткові 90 градусів (від -45 градусів до +45 градусів) через перевизначення кута в попередній команді.","signature":"Drivetrain.setHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_stopping":{"name":"drivetrain_set_stopping","markdown":"# Set Stopping\n\nВстановлює режим гальмування трансмісії\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setStopping(brakeType);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nОсь можливі вхідні значення для параметра `brakeType`, які ви можете задати: \n\n* **brake** змушує трансмісію миттєво зупинитися і не реагувати на зовнішні сили.\n* **coast** дає змогу трансмісії поступово зменшити оберти до зупинки.\n* **hold** змушує трансмісію миттєво зупинитися і повертатиме її до позиції зупинки, якщо діють зовнішні сили.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змушує трансмісію їхати вперед 3 секунди, а потім утримувати позицію після зупинки.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setStopping(hold);\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setStopping(brake);"},"drivetrain_set_timeout":{"name":"drivetrain_set_timeout","markdown":"# Set Timeout\n\nЧасові обмеження руху трансмісії потрібні, щоб команди руху, які не змогли досягти своєї позиції, не заважали працювати наступним командам.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Drivetrain.setTimeout` використовується, щоб команди руху, які не виконалися, не блокували роботу інших команд.\n\nПриклад трансмісії, яка не досягла своєї позиції - коли під час руху робот зіткнувся зі стіною і не може закінчити свій рух.\n\nВстановіть часові обмеження тривалості руху, вказавши кількість часу в секундах - `seconds`.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(2.0, seconds);\n```\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад зупинить команду `Drivetrain.driveFor` через дві секунди, якщо трансмісія не встигне проїхати 600 міліметрів.\n\nЩойно часові обмеження або відстань будуть подолані (залежить від того, що раніше), трансмісія поверне праворуч на 90 градусів.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(2.0, seconds);\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 600, mm);\nDrivetrain.turnFor(right, 90.0, degrees);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setTimeout(1, seconds);"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Set Turn Velocity\n\nВстановлює швидкість поворотів трансмісії.\n\nЯкщо ця команда спрацьовує, коли трансмісія повертає, то трансмісія змінить свою швидкість на нову.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTurnVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity` задає швидкість повороту трансмісії, але не запускає її рух.\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity` приймає значення в діапазоні **від -100 до 100**, коли використано одиниці **percent** - відсотки.\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity` иймає значення в діапазоні **від -127 до 127**, коли використано одиниці **rpm** - оберти за хвилину.\n\nВстановлення швидкості повороту трансмісії у від'ємне значення змусить її повертати у зворотному напрямку.\n\nВстановлення швидкості повороту трансмісії в 0 спричинить зупинку трансмісії.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змусить трансмісію повертати ліворуч зі швидкістю 25%.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTurnVelocity(25, percent);\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity(50, percent);"},"drivetrain_stop":{"name":"drivetrain_stop","markdown":"# Stop\n\nЗупиняє трансмісію.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Drivetrain.stop` змушує трансмісію зупинитися.\n\nРежим гальмування можна встановити командою `Drivetrain.setStopping`.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад запустить робота VEX IQ на рух вперед на 3 секунди, а потім зупинить його.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.stop();"},"drivetrain_turn":{"name":"drivetrain_turn","markdown":"# Turn\n\nПовертає трансмісію.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(direction);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Drivetrain.turn` постійно повертатиме трансмісію, поки не запрацює нова команда трансмісії або програма не зупиниться.\n\nВикористовуйте аргумент **left**, щоб повертати трансмісію ліворуч.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n```\n\nВикористовуйте аргумент **right**, щоб повертати трансмісію праворуч.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(right);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turn(right);"},"drivetrain_turn_for":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_for","markdown":"# Turn For\n\nПовертає трансмісію на певний кут та напрямок\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(direction, angle, degrees);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЗадайте напрямок - `direction` - і кут повороту, ввівши напрямок - **left** або **right**, і кількість градусів.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(right, 270, degrees);\n```\n\nКоманда `Drivetrain.turnFor` за замовчуванням блокує інші команди, поки трансмісія повертає.\n\n## Необов'язкові параметри\n\nВи можете встановити значення останнього параметра `false`, щоб команда `Drivetrain.turnFor` не блокувала програму під час виконання руху.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(left, 90, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnFor(right, 90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_turn_to_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Turn To Heading\n\nПовертає трансмісію на визначений курс, якщо налаштовано гіроскопічний датчик VEX IQ.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading(heading, degrees);`\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманду `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` використовують, щоб повернути трансмісію на введене значення курсу, яке рахується в напрямку проти годинникової стрілки, як показано на зображенні.\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/drivetrain_turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nЗважаючи на поточну позицію гіродатчика, `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` самостійно обере напрямок обертання.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading` приймає значення в діапазоні **від 0.00 до 359.99** для параметра `heading`.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змусить трансмісію здійснити чотири повороти: \n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(270.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(180.0, degrees);\n```\n\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 45 градусів\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 90 градусів\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 270 градусів\n- Праворуч (за годинниковою) до 180 градусів\n\nКоманда `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` за замовчуванням блокує інші команди, поки трансмісія повертає.\n\n## Необов'язкові параметри\n\nВи можете встановити значення останнього параметра `false`, щоб команда `Drivetrain.turnToHeading` не блокувала програму під час виконання руху.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnToHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Turn To Rotation\n\nПовертає трансмісію на визначений кут, якщо налаштовано гіроскопічний датчик VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманду `Drivetrain.turnToRotation` використовують, щоб повернути трансмісію на введене позитивне (проти годинникової стрілки) або негативне (за годинниковою стрілкою) значення.\n\nЗважаючи на поточний кут повороту трансмісії, `Drivetrain.turnToRotation` самостійно обере напрямок обертання.\n\nПараметр `rotation` **не** обмежується діапазоном **від 0 до 359.99 градусів**. Повороти будуть повними і можуть повернути робота більш ніж на один оберт, якщо потрібно.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змусить трансмісію здійснити чотири повороти:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(90.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(180, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(0, degrees);\n```\n\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 90 градусів\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 180 градусів\n- Праворуч (за годинниковою) до -45 градусів\n- Ліворуч (проти годинникової) до 0 градусів\n\nКоманда `Drivetrain.turnToRotation` за замовчуванням блокує інші команди, поки трансмісія повертає.\n\n## Необов'язкові параметри\n\nВи можете встановити значення останнього параметра `false`, щоб команда `Drivetrain.turnToRotation` не блокувала програму під час виконання руху.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(180.0, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnToRotation(90, degrees);"},"events_brain_button_pressed":{"name":"events_brain_button_pressed","markdown":"#  Brain Button Pressed\n\nЗапускає функцію зворотного виклику, коли натиснуто кнопку VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Button.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВи маєте створити функцію, яка буде викликатися, коли натиснути кнопку на  Brain.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button pressed.\");\n}\n```\n\nФункцію `Brain.Button.pressed` можна використовувати з різними кнопками на VEX IQ Brain.\n\n- `Brain.buttonUp.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Brain.buttonDown.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Brain.buttonCheck.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Brain.Button.pressed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.buttonUp.pressed(callback);"},"events_brain_button_released":{"name":"events_brain_button_released","markdown":"# Brain Button Released\n\nЗапускає функцію зворотного виклику, коли відпущено кнопку VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Button.released(callback);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВи маєте створити функцію, яка буде викликатися, коли відпущено кнопку на  Brain.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button released.\");\n}\n```\n\nФункцію `Brain.Button.released` можна використовувати з різними кнопками на VEX IQ Brain.\n\n- `Brain.buttonUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Brain.buttonDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Brain.buttonCheck.released(buttonReleased);`\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Brain.Button.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.button.released();"},"events_brain_timer":{"name":"events_brain_timer","markdown":"# Timer Event\n\nЗапускає функцію зворотного виклику через певний проміжок часу.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.event(callback, time);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nТаймер IQ Brain починає відлік після запуску кожної програми.\n\nФункція `Brain.Timer.event` приймає 2 параметра.\n\nПерший параметр - функція зворотного виклику (**callback function**). Цю функцію спочатку потрібно створити, щоб передати її у функцію `Brain.Timer.event`.\n\nДругий параметр - час, через який запуститься функція зворотного виклику. Ця функція (**callback function**) запуститься, щойно час **Brain Timer** стане більшим за введене значення. Введений параметр `time` має бути в **мілісекундах**.\n\n```cpp\n// Функція зворотного виклику callback спрацює через 1000 мілісекунд\nBrain.Timer.event(callback, 1000);\n```\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**. \n\nУ прикладі нижче надпис \"Callback Function Called\" буде надруковано на екрані VEX IQ Brain через 10 секунд.\n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Brain.Timer.event(callbackFunction, 10000);\n}\n```","signature":"events_brain_timer"},"events_bumper_pressed":{"name":"events_bumper_pressed","markdown":"# Bumper Pressed\n\nЗапускає визначену функцію зворотного виклику **callback function**, коли натиснуто бампер.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВи маєте створити функцію, яка буде викликатися, коли натиснуто бамперний перемикач. Назвіть цю функцію, яка має спрацювати в параметрі `callback` після виконання події.\n\n```cpp\nvoid bumperPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Bumper pressed.\");\n}\n```\nПотім, передайте цю функцію як параметр функції `Bumper.pressed`.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressed(bumperPressed);\n```\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**.\n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Bumper.pressed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"BUMPER.pressed(callback);"},"events_bumper_released":{"name":"events_bumper_released","markdown":"# Bumper Released\n\nЗапускає визначену функцію, коли бампер відпущено.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.released(callback);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВи маєте створити функцію, яка буде викликатися, коли бамперний перемикач відпущено. Назвіть цю функцію, яка має спрацювати в параметрі `callback` після виконання події.\n\n```cpp\nvoid bumperReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Bumper released.\");\n}\n```\nПотім, передайте цю функцію як параметр функції `Bumper.released`.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.released(bumperReleased);\n```\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Bumper.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Bumper.released(callback);"},"events_controller_axis":{"name":"events_controller_axis","markdown":"# Controller Axis Changed\n\nЗапускає функцію зворотного виклику, коли вибрана вісь джойстиків контролера VEX IQ рухається.\n\n```cpp\nController.Axis.changed(callback);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВи маєте створити функцію зворотного виклику, яка буде викликатися, коли вісь на контролері рухається.\n\n```cpp\nvoid axisMoved() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Axis moved.\");\n}\n```\n\nВиберіть, яку вісь джойстиків контролера використати і передайте функцію зворотного виклику\n\n- `Controller.AxisA.changed(axisMoved);`\n- `Controller.AxisB.changed(axisMoved);`\n- `Controller.AxisC.changed(axisMoved);`\n- `Controller.AxisD.changed(axisMoved);`\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/events_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Controller.AxisA.changed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"`Controller.AxisA.changed(callback)`"},"events_controller_button_pressed":{"name":"events_controller_button_pressed","markdown":"# Controller Button Pressed\n\nЗапускає функцію зворотного виклику **callback function**, коли натиснуто кнопку на контролері VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВи маєте створити функцію зворотного виклику (**callback function**), яка буде викликатися, коли кнопка на контролері натиснута.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button pressed.\");\n}\n```\n\nВиберіть, яка кнопка контролера викличе функцію `pressed()` .\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/events_controller_button_pressed/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonEUp.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonEDown.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonFUp.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonFDown.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/events_controller_button_pressed/controller_button_back.png)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonLUp.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonLDown.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonRUp.pressed(buttonPressed);`\n- `Controller.ButtonRDown.pressed(buttonPressed);`","signature":"Controller.Button.pressed();"},"events_controller_button_released":{"name":"events_controller_button_released","markdown":"# Controller Button Released\n\nЗапускає функцію зворотного виклику **callback function**, коли відпущено кнопку на контролері VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.released(callback);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВи маєте створити функцію зворотного виклику (**callback function**), яка буде викликатися, коли кнопка на контролері відпущена.\n\n```cpp\nvoid buttonReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Button released.\");\n}\n```\n\nВиберіть, яка кнопка контролера викличе функцію `released()`.\n\n- `Controller.ButtonEUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonEDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonFUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonFDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonLUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonLDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonRUp.released(buttonReleased);`\n- `Controller.ButtonRDown.released(buttonReleased);`\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/events_controller_button_released/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/events_controller_button_released/controller_button_back.png)\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  Controller.ButtonRDown.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"Controller.Button.released();"},"events_event":{"name":"events_event","markdown":"# Event\n\nСтворює нову подію, щоб активувати визначену функцію користувача.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\nОб'єкт **event** можна використати, щоб активувати функцію, визначену користувачем.Для роботи необхідно створити об'єкт **event**. Це можна зробити двома способами.\n\nФункцію зворотного виклику (**callback function**) можна використати як аргумент для створеної функції.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n```\nФункцію **callback function** не обов'язково передавати у новостворену функцію.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event();\n```\nУ подію можна додати декілька функцій **callback functions**. Всі вони спрацюють одночасно, коли виконається подія.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event();\nmyEvent(callbackFunction1);\nmyEvent(callbackFunction1);\n```\nЛише **2 події функцій зворотного виклику** мають працювати водночас. Додаткові **події функцій зворотного виклику** можуть знизити продуктивність робота VEX IQ.\n\nФункція зворотного виклику виконається, коли викликати або функцію `myEvent.broadcast`, або `myEvent.broadcastAndWait`.\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**.\n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Створення нової події з назвою myEvent у головній функції main і передавання callbackFunction\n  event myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n\n  // Надсилання myEvent, активуючи виведення напису \"Function Called.\" на екрані Brain\n  myEvent.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"event myEvent = event(myEventCallback);"},"events_event_broadcast":{"name":"events_event_broadcast","markdown":"# Broadcast\n\nНадсилає повідомлення для активації будь-яких функцій, які викликані подією **Event**.\n\n```cpp\nmyEvent.broadcast();\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКод програми продовжить виконуватися після команди `myEvent.broadcast`, тому вона працюватиме водначас із функціями прослуховувачами подій event listener.\n\nПеред використанням цієї команди визначена подія має бути створена і прописана хоча б в одному зворотному виклику callback.\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast1() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\");\n}\n\nvoid runOnBroadcast2() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Створіть подію в головній функції main\n  event myEvent = event();\n\n  // Пропишіть функцію зворотного виклику в подію\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast1);\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast2);\n\n  // Активуйте подію\n  myEvent.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"EVENT.broadcast();"},"events_event_broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Broadcast and Wait\n\nНадсилає повідомлення для активації будь-яких функцій, які викликані подією **Event**, а продовження програми зупиняється.\n\n```cpp\nmyEvent.broadcastAndWait();\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `myEvent.broadcastAndWait` чекає, поки всі прослуховувачі не виконаються, а потім продовжує роботу програми. Це зупиняє виконання коду поточної функції, поки всі надіслані прослуховувачі повністю не виконаються.\n\nПеред використанням цієї команди визначена подія має бути створена і прописана хоча б в одному зворотному виклику callback.\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**.\n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Function Called.\");\n\n  wait(5, seconds);\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Пропишіть нову подію в головній функції main і передайте їй функцію callbackFunction\n  event myEvent = event(callbackFunction);\n\n  // Активуйте подію, програма чекає, поки подія не виконається\n  myEvent.broadcastAndWait();\n\n  // Ця частина не почнеться, поки callbackFunction не виконається\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Done!\");\n}\n```","signature":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait"},"events_touch_led_pressed":{"name":"events_touch_led_pressed","markdown":"# TouchLED Pressed\n\nЗапускає функцію зворотного виклику **callback function**, коли датчик дотику TouchLED натиснуто.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВи маєте створити функцію, яка буде викликатися, коли датчик дотику натиснуто. Назвіть цю функцію, яка має спрацювати в параметрі `callback` після виконання події.\n\n```cpp\nvoid touchLEDPressed() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Touch LED pressed.\");\n}\n```\nПотім, передайте цю функцію як параметр функції `TouchLED.pressed`.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.pressed(touchLEDPressed);\n```\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**. \n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  TouchLED.pressed(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"TouchLED.pressed(callback);"},"events_touch_led_released":{"name":"events_touch_led_released","markdown":"# TouchLED Released\n\nЗапускає функцію зворотного виклику **callback function**, коли датчик дотику TouchLED відпущено.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.released(callback);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВи маєте створити функцію, яка буде викликатися, коли датчик дотику відпущено. Назвіть цю функцію, яка має спрацювати в параметрі `callback` після виконання події.\n\n```cpp\nvoid touchLEDReleased() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Touch LED released.\");\n}\n```\nПотім, передайте цю функцію як параметр функції `TouchLED.released`.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.released(touchLEDReleased);\n```\n\n## Функція зворотного виклику\n\nФункція зворотного виклику - це функція, яка передається в іншу функцію як аргумент. Код всередині функції зворотного виклику (**callback function**) запрацює, коли виконається подія **event**.\n\n```cpp\nvoid callbackFunction() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Callback Function Called.\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  TouchLED.released(callbackFunction);\n}\n```","signature":"TouchLED.released(callback);"},"function_name":{"name":"function_name","markdown":"# Functions\n\nФункції - це частини коду, які використовують для виконання набору дій. \n\n```cpp\nvoid myFunction() {\n  // код функції\n}\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЩоб визначити функцію, оголосіть тип даних, які функція повертатиме.\n\n- `int`, `float`, `double`, і `string` - типи даних, які повертають найчастіше. Якщо функція не має повертати значення, оголосіть тип даних `void`.\n\nПотім, назвіть функцію зрозумілим ім'ям, яке описує те, що функція робить.\n\n```cpp\nint returnZero() {\n  return 0;\n}\n```\n\nДодайте дужки `()` з необов'язковими *параметрами* після імені функції. Декілька параметрів треба розділяти комами (параметр1, параметр2).\n\nТіло функції треба помістити у фігурні дужки `{ }`.\n    \n## Приклад\n\nЦя функція не має параметрів і не повертає значень, тому її тип (або тип даних, які вона повертає) оголошено `void`. Ця функція друкує \"The battery is low!\" на екрані VEX IQ Brain, якщо заряд батареї нижче 25%.\n\n```cpp\nvoid lowOnBattery() {\n  if (Brain.Battery.capacity(percent) < 25.0) {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"The battery is low!\");\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"function_name"},"function_thread":{"name":"function_thread","markdown":"# Thread\n\nДає змогу виконувати кілька потоків (threads) одночасно.\n\n```cpp\nthread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nТреба визначити функцію, яку буде передано зворотнім викликом в потік.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myThreadCallback() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"In a different thread!\");\n}\n```\nЩойно ви напишете функцію, можете використати її, щоб створити новий потік. Ця функія передається як функція зворотного виклику **callback function**.\n\n```cpp\nthread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n```\nПотік **thread** почне виконуватись одразу після створення. Він працює паралельно з головним потоком.\n\nЛише два потоки (**2 threads**) мають працювати водночас. Додаткові потоки можуть зменшити продуктивність робота VEX IQ.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує одночасно два лічильника на екрані VEX IQ Brain. Один буде друкуватися потоком `myThread`. Інший тоді ж друкуватиметься основним потоком.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myThreadCallback() {\n  int count = 0;\n  while(true) {\n    Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"thread1: %d\", count);\n    count++;\n    // Очікування для виконання основного потоку\n    wait(25, msec);\n  }\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Створений потік одразу почне виконання\n  thread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n  \n  int count = 0;\n  while(true) {\n    Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"main: %d\", count);\n    count++;\n    // Очікування для виконання myThread\n    wait(25, msec);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"function_thread"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Clear Line\n\nОчищує поточний рядок на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine();\n```\n\nОчищує обраний рядок на екрані Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine(1);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Brain.Screen.clearLine` приймає цілі значення **від 1 до 5** щоб очистити відповідний рядок.\n\nВи можете викликати команду без аргумента, щоб очистити поточний рядок.\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Приклад \nЦей приклад надрукує \"Hello\" у рядку 2, стовпчика 1, почекає 3 секунди, а потім очистить рядок 2.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");\nwait(3.0, seconds);\nBrain.Screen.clearLine(2);\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.clearLine();"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Clear Screen\n\nОчищує весь екран VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearScreen();\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Brain.Screen.clearScreen` не скидає позицію курсора на екрані Brain \n\nВикористовуйте команду `Brain.Screen.setCursor`, щоб встановити бажану позицію курсора на Brain.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує \"Hello\", почекає одну секунду, а потім очистить весь екран перед друком \"Goodbye\".\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");\nwait(1.0, seconds);\nBrain.Screen.clearScreen();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Goodbye\");\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.clearScreen();"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line","markdown":"# New Line\n\nВстановлює курсор для друку на екрані Brain в наступний доступний рядок.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЗа замовчуванням, усі проєкти починають із курсором в рядку 1 стовпці 1. Команда `Brain.Screen.newLine` переміщує курсор на рядок нижче на екрані Brain.\n\n---\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/looks_brain_screen_new_line/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує \"First Message\" і встановить курсор у наступний доступний рядок перед друком \"Second Message\".\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"First Message\");\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Second Message\");\n```\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/looks_brain_screen_new_line/set_cursor_welcome.png)","signature":"Brain.Screen.newLine();"},"looks_brain_screen_print":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print","markdown":"# Print\n\nДрукує значення або текст на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print();\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Brain.Screen.print` надрукує дані з позиції курсора на екрані Brain.\n\nВсі нові проєкти починають із курсором в рядку 1 стовпці 1.\n\nДрукує слова або числа.:\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"String: 123 + Words\");\n```\n\nДрукує цілі або десяткові значення:\n```cpp\n// Коли друкується ціле число, потрібен специфікатор формата\n// \"%d\" у першому параметрі\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Integer: %d\", 5 + 10);\n\n// Коли друкується десяткове число, потрібен специфікатор формата\n// \"%f\" у першому параметрі\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Decimal: %f\", 5.0 + 10.0);\n```\n\nДрукує значення команд показників датчиків:\n```cpp\n// Якщо вихідне значення ціле або десяткове число, використайте\n// \"%f\" або \"%d\" відповідно як специфікатор формата\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%d\", Brain.Timer.time());\n\n// Якщо вихідне значення булеве (логічне),\n// використайте \"%s\" як специфікатор формата\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%s\", Motor.isDone() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");"},"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Set Cursor\n\nВстановлює позицію курсора для команди `Brain.Screen.print`.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(row, col);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Brain.Screen.setCursor` потребує 2 параметра:\n\n* Параметр 1: Позиція рядка на екрані \n* Параметр 2: Позиція стовпчика на екрані\n\nВстановіть позицію курсора в рядку і стовпчику, щоб команда `Brain.Screen.print` друкувала в потрібній позиції на екрані.\n\nДопустимий діапазон для рядка `row` **від 1 до 5**.\n\nДопустимий діапазон для стовпчика `col` **від 1 до 21**.\n\n## Приклад \n\nЦей приклад встановлює позицію курсора в рядок 3, стовпчик 8, а потім друкує текст \"Hello!\" на екрані Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(3, 8);\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hello!\");\n```\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/set_cursor_hello.png)","signature":"Brain.screen.setCursor(1, 1);"},"looks_color_set_light":{"name":"looks_color_set_light","markdown":"# Set Color Sensor Light\n\nВстановлює яскравість випромінюваного світла датчика кольору VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nColor.setLight(brightness, percent);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nДатчик кольору має джерело світла, яке можна відрегулювати, щоб покращити розпізнавання кольору об'єкта або яскравості поверхні.\n\n`Color.setLight` приймає значення в діапазоні **від 0 до 100** для параметра яскравості `brightness`.\n\nЧим більший % яскравості встановлено, тим яскравіше світитиме джерело світла датчика кольору.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче встановлює яскравість світла для датчика кольору 75%.\n\n```cpp\nColor.setLight(75, percent);\n```","signature":"Color.setLight(50, percent);"},"looks_touch_led_set_brightness":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_brightness","markdown":"# Set TouchLED Brightness\n\nВстановлює рівень яскравості LED датчика дотику VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setBrightness(brightness);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`TouchLED.setBrightness` приймає значення в діапазоні **від 0 до 100** для параметра яскравості `brightness`.\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED1.setBrightness(100);\nTouchLED2.setBrightness(50);\n```\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змушує LED датчик дотику випромінювати зелене світло з яскравістю 25%.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setBrightness(25);\nTouchLED.setColor(green);\n```","signature":"TouchLED.brightness();"},"looks_touch_led_set_color":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_color","markdown":"# Set TouchLED Color\n\nВстановлює колір для LED датчика дотику VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(color);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED1.setColor(red);\nTouchLED2.setColor(green);\n```\nВиберіть колір світіння.\n\nВаріанти кольору:\n\n- `red`\n- `green`\n- `blue`\n- `white`\n- `yellow`\n- `orange`\n- `purple`\n- `red_violet`\n- `violet`\n- `blue_violet`\n- `blue_green`\n- `yellow_green`\n- `yellow_orange`\n- `red_orange`\n\nЩоб вимкнути колір LED датчика дотику, встановіть колір **colorType::none**.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(colorType::none);\n```","signature":"touchLED.color();"},"looks_touch_led_set_fade":{"name":"looks_touch_led_set_fade","markdown":"# Set TouchLED Fade\n\nВизначає, як швидко відбудеться перехід між кольорами LED датчика дотику VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setFade(fade);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED1.setFade(fast);\nTouchLED2.setFade(slow);\n```\nВиберіть, як швидко відбудеться перехід LED датчика дотику.Замініть `fade` на одну з таких опцій:\n\n* **slow** - LED датчик дотику повільно змінюватиме колір.\n* **fast** - LED датчик дотику швидко змінюватиме колір.\n* **off** - LED датчик дотику миттєво змінюватиме колір.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад повільно змінить колір LED датчика дотику з червоного на синій.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(red);\nTouchLED.setFade(slow);\nTouchLED.setColor(blue);\n```","signature":"TouchLED.setFade(fade);"},"motion_motor_set_max_torque":{"name":"motion_motor_set_max_torque","markdown":"# Motor Set Max Torque\n\nВстановлює максимальну силу обертання мотора.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setMaxTorque(value, percent);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Motor.setMaxTorque` приймає значення в діапазоні **від 0% до 100%**.\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setMaxTorque(25, percent);\nArmMotor.setMaxTorque(75, percent);\n```\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад обертатиме ClawMotor в позицію 40 градусів із крутним моментом 20%. Це дасть змогу клешні схопити об'єкт без пошкоджень від надмірного стиснення.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setMaxTorque(20, percent);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(40, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setMaxTorque(50, percent);"},"motion_motor_set_position":{"name":"motion_motor_set_position","markdown":"# Motor Set Position\n\nВстановлює значення позиції енкодера мотора VEX IQ на введену величину.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setPosition(position, units);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманду `Motor.setPosition` використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію мотора на задане значення.\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setPosition(0, degrees);\nArmMotor.setPosition(90, degrees);\n```\n\nЗазвичай, команду `Motor.setPosition` використовують, щоб скинути позицію енкодера мотора в 0.\n\nВстановіть одиниці вимірювання `units` **degrees** або **turns**.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад встановить позицію мотора ClawMotor в 50 градусів.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setPosition(50, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setPosition(0, degrees);"},"motion_motor_set_stopping":{"name":"motion_motor_set_stopping","markdown":"# Motor Set Stopping\n\nВстановлює поведінку мотора VEX IQ під час зупинки.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setStopping(brakeType);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setStopping(brake);\nArmMotor.setStopping(hold);\n```\n\nВстановіть поведінку зупинки мотора:\n- **brake** змушує мотор миттєво зупинитися.\n- **coast** дає змогу мотору поступово зменшити оберти до зупинки.\n- **hold** змушує мотор миттєво зупинитися і повертатиме його до позиції зупинки, якщо він зміститься.\n\nКоманда `Motor.setStopping` впливатиме на роботу всіх команд для мотора `Motor.stop` у цьому проєкті.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змусить мотор руки рухатися вгору 90 градусів, а потім миттєво зупинитися і компенсувати зовнішні сили (як-от гравітація), щоб утримувати позицію.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.setStopping(hold);\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 90, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setStopping(brake);"},"motion_motor_set_timeout":{"name":"motion_motor_set_timeout","markdown":"# Motor Set Timeout\n\nВстановлює часові обмеження на всі команди руху мотора, щоб зупинити його, якщо команда мотора блокує роботу і не може досягти своєї цілі.  \n\n```cpp\nMotor.setTimeout(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Motor.setTimeout` потрібна, щоб команди руху, які не змогли досягти своєї позиції, не заважали працювати наступним командам.\n\nПриклад мотору, який не досягнув своєї позиції - клешня або рука, яка зіштовхнулась із механічними обмеженнями і не може закінчити свій рух.\n\nВстановіть часові обмеження, задавши кількість часу в секундах **seconds**.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад зупинить команду `Motor.spinToPosition` через 2 секунди, якщо ClawMotor не встигне досягти позиції 270 градусів. \n\nЩойно часові обмеження або обертання будуть подолані, ClawMotor обертатиметься до позиції 90 градусів.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setTimeout(2, seconds);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(270, degrees);\nArmMotor.spinToPosition(90, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setTimeout(1, seconds);"},"motion_motor_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity","markdown":"# Set Motor Velocity\n\nВстановлює швидкість для мотора VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Motor.setVelocity` приймає значення в діапазоні **від -100% до 100%** або **від -127rpm до 127rpm**.\n\nВстановлення швидкості мотора у від'ємне значення змусить його обертатися у зворотному напрямку.\n\nВстановлення швидкості мотора в 0 спричинить його зупинку.\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setVelocity(25, percent);\nArmMotor.setVelocity(75, percent);\n```\n\nВстановіть одиниці вимірювання `units` **percent** або **rpm**(revolutions per minute - обертів за хвилину).\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад встановлює повільне обертання мотора руки зі швидкістю 25% на 90 градусів.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setVelocity(25, percent);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(90, degrees);\n```","signature":"Motor.setVelocity(50, percent);"},"motion_motor_spin":{"name":"motion_motor_spin","markdown":"# Spin Motor\n\nОбертає мотор VEX IQ в певному напрямку.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(direction);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Motor.spin` постійно крутитиме мотор, поки не запрацює інший блок мотору або програма не зупиниться.\n\n- **forward** обертає мотор вперед.\n- **reverse** обертає мотор зворотно.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(forward);\nMotor.spin(reverse);\n```","signature":"Motor.spin(forward);"},"motion_motor_spin_for":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_for","markdown":"# Spin Motor For\n\nПовертає мотор VEX IQ на певну величину.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinFor(direction, rotation, units);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Motor.spinFor` обертає мотор у заданий бік і на задану відстань.\n\nМожливі параметри:\n\n- `direction` приймає значення напрямку **forward** або **reverse**\n- `rotation` приймає числові значення величини повороту\n- `units` приймає значення одиниць **degrees** або **turns**\n\nКоманда `Motor.spinFor` блокує інші команди, поки мотор не прокрутиться на задану величину.\n\n## Необов'язкові параметри\n\nВи можете встановити значення останнього параметра `false`, щоб команда `Motor.spinFor` не блокувала програму під час виконання руху.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinFor(reverse, 360, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Motor.spinFor(forward, 90, degrees);"},"motion_motor_spin_to_position":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_to_position","markdown":"# Spin Motor To Position\n\nПовертає мотор VEX IQ у певну позицію.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinToPosition(rotation, units);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Motor.spinToPosition` повідомляє мотору, в яку позицію прокрутитися. Зважаючи на поточну позицію мотора, `Motor.spinToPosition` сама обере напрямок обертання.\n\nКоманда `Motor.spinToPosition` приймає числові значення для параметра `rotation`.\n\nВстановіть одиниці вимірювання `units` для обертання в  **degrees** або **turns**. \n\nКоманда `Motor.spinToPosition` блокує інші команди, поки мотор не прокрутиться на задану величину.\n\n## Необов'язкові параметри\n\nВи можете встановити значення останнього параметра `false`, щоб команда `Motor.spinToPosition` не блокувала програму під час виконання руху.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinToPosition(360, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Motor.spinToPosition(90, degrees);"},"motion_motor_stop":{"name":"motion_motor_stop","markdown":"# Stop Motor\n\nЗупиняє мотор.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.stop();\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n```cpp\nClawMotor.stop();\nArmMotor.stop();\n``` \n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад обертатиме мотор 3 секунди до зупинки.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.spin(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nClawMotor.stop();\n```","signature":"Motor.stop();"},"sensing_brain_battery_capacity":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_capacity","markdown":"# Battery Capacity\n\nПередає значення заряду акумулятора VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Battery.capacity(percent)\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Brain.Battery.capacity` передає числове значення **integer**, яке показує значення заряду батареї VEX IQ Brain у відсотках `percent` і повертає значення в діапазоні **від 0 до 100**.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад грає звук тривоги, якщо рівень ємності акумулятора VEX IQ нижче 25%.\n\n```cpp\nif (Brain.Battery.capacity(percent) < 25){\n  Brain.playSound(alarm);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Battery.capacity(percent)"},"sensing_brain_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_column","markdown":"# Screen Cursor Column\n\nПередає номер стовпця з екрану VEX IQ Brain, де розміщений курсор.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.column()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Brain.Screen.column` передає числове значення в діапазоні **від 1 до 21**.\n\nЗначення `Brain.Screen.column` збільшується з лівого до правого боку екрана Brain VEX IQ.","signature":"Brain.Screen.column()"},"sensing_brain_screen_pressing":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_pressing","markdown":"# Brain Button Pressing\n\nПередає значення, якщо обрана кнопка на VEX IQ Brain натиснута.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Button.pressing()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПередає **true**, якщо обрана кнопка на Brain натиснута. Передає **false**, якщо обрана кнопка на Brain не натиснута.\n\nПісля частини команди `Brain.` введіть назву кнопки на Brain, яка буде реагувати на натискання.\n\nМожливі варіанти кнопок на Brain:\n- `buttonUp`\n- `buttonDown`\n- `buttonCheck`\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад змушує робота їхати вперед.\n\nПотім, він перевіряє, чи натиснута кнопка **buttonUp**, і тоді повертає робота праворуч.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  if (Brain.buttonUp.pressing()) {\n    Drivetrain.turn(right);\n    break;\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Button.pressing()"},"sensing_brain_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_row","markdown":"# Screen Cursor Row\n\nПередає номер рядка з екрану Brain VEX IQ, де розміщений курсор.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.row()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Brain.Screen.row` передає числове значення в діапазоні  **від 1 до 5**.\n\nЗначення `Brain.Screen.row` збільшується з верхнього до нижнього боку екрана Brain VEX IQ.","signature":"sensing_brain_screen_row"},"sensing_brain_timer_reset":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_reset","markdown":"# Reset Timer\n\nСкидає таймер VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.reset();\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nТаймер Brain починає відлік після старту кожного проєкта.  Команда `Brain.Timer.reset` скидає таймер до 0 секунд.\n\n## Приклад\n\nУ цьому прикладі таймер буде скинуто, коли трансмісія проїде вперед упродовж 3 секунд. Коли мине 3 секунди, трансмісія зупиниться.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.reset();\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  if (Brain.Timer.value() > 3) {\n    break;\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"sensing_brain_timer_reset"},"sensing_brain_timer_value":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_value","markdown":"# Timer Value\n\nПовертає значення таймера з VEX IQ Brain у секундах.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.value()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nТаймер починає відлік з 0 секунд, коли програма запускається, і передає десяткові значення (*double*).\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує значення таймера Brain.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Timer: %.2f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n  \n  // Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"sensing_brain_timer_value"},"sensing_bumper_pressing":{"name":"sensing_bumper_pressing","markdown":"# Bumper Pressing\n\nПовідомляє, чи бамперний перемикач VEX IQ натиснуто.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressing()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Bumper.pressing` передає значення **true**, якщо бамперний перемикач натиснуто.\n\n\n`Bumper.pressing` передає значення **false**, якщо бамперний перемикач не натиснуто.\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nBumper2.pressing()\nBumper4.pressing()\n```\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує на екрані Brain те, чи натиснуто бамперний перемикач.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Bumper Pressed: %s\", Bumper2.pressing() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Bumper.pressing()"},"sensing_color_brightness":{"name":"sensing_color_brightness","markdown":"# Color Brightness\n\nПередає кількість світла, виміряну датчиком кольору VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nColor.brightness()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Color.brightness` передає значення в діапазоні **від 0% до 100%**.\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nColor2.brightness()\nColor4.brightness()\n```\n\nБільша кількість світла повертає більше числове значення, менша кількість - менше.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує кількість світла, зафіксованого датчиком кольору.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Brightness: %d\", Color.brightness());\n```","signature":"Color.brightness()"},"sensing_color_colorname":{"name":"sensing_color_colorname","markdown":"# Color Of\n\nПередає назву кольору, знайденого датчиком кольору VEX IQ. \n\n```cpp\nColor.colorname()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Color.colorname` може передати один із таких кольорів: \n- `red`\n- `red_violet`\n- `violet`\n- `blue_violet`\n- `blue`\n- `blue_green`\n- `green`\n- `yellow_green`\n- `yellow`\n- `yellow_orange`\n- `orange`\n- `red_orange`\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nColor4.colorname()\nColor5.colorname()\n```","signature":"Color9.colorname()"},"sensing_color_detect":{"name":"sensing_color_detect","markdown":"# Color Detects\n\nПовідомляє, якщо датчик кольору VEX IQ побачив певний колір.\n\n```cpp\nColor.detects(color)\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПередає значення  **true**, якщо датчик кольору побачив обраний колір. Передає значення **false** якщо датчик кольору побачив колір, не схожий на обраний.\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nColor1.detects(red)\nColor2.detects(blue)\n```\n\nВиберіть, який колір шукати:\n\n- `red`\n- `orange`\n- `yellow`\n- `green`\n- `blue`\n- `purple`\n- `violet`\n- `red_violet`\n- `blue_violet`\n- `blue_green`\n- `yellow_green`\n- `yellow_orange`\n- `red_orange`\n- `white`\n\nВи також можете передати **colorType::none** у параметр `color`, щоб дізнатись, що датчик кольору **не** знайшов об'єкт.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад надрукує \"Color Red\" або \"Other Color\" залежно від того, побачив датчик кольору червоний, чи ні.\n\n```cpp\nif (Color.detects(red)) { \n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Color Red\");\n} else {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Other Color\");\n}\n```","signature":"Color.detects(color)"},"sensing_color_hue":{"name":"sensing_color_hue","markdown":"# Color Hue\n\nПередає відтінок кольору, який побачив датчик кольору VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nColor.hue()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Color.hue` передає значення в діапазоні **від 0 до 360** градусів, що представляє позицію кольору на колі кольорів.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад друкує відтінок кольору, який побачив датчик кольору.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hue: %.0f\", Color.hue());\n```","signature":"Color.hue()"},"sensing_color_isNearObject":{"name":"sensing_color_isNearObject","markdown":"# Color Is Near Object\n\nПовідомляє, якщо датчик кольору VEX IQ знайшов об'єкт або поверхню.\n\n```cpp\nColor.isNearObject()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nColor5.isNearObject()\nColor7.isNearObject()\n```\n\nПередає значення **true** , коли датчик кольору бачить перешкоду або поверхню попереду датчика.\n\nПередає значення **false**, коли датчик кольору бачить пустий простір попереду датчика.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує, чи побачив датчик кольору об'єкт або поверхню.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Is Near Object: %s\", Color.isNearObject() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"Color.isNearObject()"},"sensing_controller_axis_position":{"name":"sensing_controller_axis_position","markdown":"# Controller Axis Position\n\nПередає позицію джойстика на контролері VEX IQ уздовж заданої вісі.\n\n```cpp\nController.Axis.position()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Controller.Axis.position` передає значення в діапазоні **від -100 до 100**.\n\n`Controller.Axis.position` передасть **0**, коли вісь джойстика посередині.\n\nВиберіть, яку вісь контролера передавати:\n\n* `AxisA` - лівий джойстик (вгору і вниз)\n* `AxisB` - лівий джойстик (вліво і вправо)\n* `AxisC` - правий джойстик (вліво і вправо)\n* `AxisD` - правий джойстик (вгору і вниз)\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче надрукує позицію вісі А контролера на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"AxisA Position: %.0f\", Controller.AxisA.position());\n\n  // Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\n```","signature":"Controller.Axis.position()"},"sensing_controller_button_pressing":{"name":"sensing_controller_button_pressing","markdown":"# Controller Button Pressing\n\nПовідомляє, якщо обрана кнопка на контролері VEX IQ натиснута.\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.pressing()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть, яка кнопка на контролері реагуватиме на натискання.\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/sensing_controller_button_pressing/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonEUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonEDown.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonFUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonFDown.pressing()`\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/sensing_controller_button_pressing/controller_button_back.png)\n\n- `Controller.ButtonLUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonLDown.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonRUp.pressing()`\n- `Controller.ButtonRDown.pressing()`\n\n`Controller.Button.pressing()` передає значення **true**, якщо вибрана кнопка контролера натиснута.\n\n`Controller.Button.pressing()` передає значення **false**, якщо вибрана кнопка контролера не натиснута.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад нижче запускає робота VEX IQ вперед. Якщо натиснути кнопку ButtonEUp, робот зупиниться.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  if (Controller.ButtonEUp.pressing()) {\n    Drivetrain.stop();\n    break;\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\n```","signature":"Controller.Button.pressing()"},"sensing_distance_distance":{"name":"sensing_distance_distance","markdown":"# Distance From\n\nПередає відстань до найближчого об'єкта від датчика відстані VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.distance(units)\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Distance.distance` передає значення в діапазоні **від 24 до 1000 мм** або **від 1 до 40 дюймів**.\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nDistance6.distance(mm)\nDistance8.distance(inches)\n```\n\nВстановіть, у яких одиницях повертатиме значення команда `Distance.distance`: **inches** або **mm** (міліметри). \n\n```cpp\nDistance6.distance(mm)\nDistance8.distance(inches)\n```","signature":"Distance.distance(units)"},"sensing_distance_found_object":{"name":"sensing_distance_found_object","markdown":"# Distance Found Object\n\nПовідомляє, якщо датчик відстані VEX IQ бачить об'єкт у полі зору.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.foundObject()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПередає значення **true**, коли датчик відстані бачить об'єкт або перешкоду в полі зору. Передає значення **false**, коли датчик відстані не бачить об'єктів або перешкод.\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nDistance3.foundObject()\nDistance4.foundObject()\n```\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує, чи бачить датчик відстані об'єкт або поверхню в полі зору.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Found Object: %s\", Distance.foundObject() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"Distance.foundObject()"},"sensing_drivetrain_current":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_current","markdown":"# Drivetrain Current\n\nПередає кількість струму, яку зараз використовує трансмісія.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.current(units)\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n`Drivetrain.current` передає десяткове значення (*double*) кількості струму, яку зараз використовує трансмісія.\n\n`Drivetrain.current` повертає значення відповідно до встановлених одиниць вимірювання `units`.\n\nМожливі варіанти одиниць вимірювання `units` - **amp** (ампери) або **percent**.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче надрукує значення струму (в амперах) трансмісії робота VEX IQ на екрані Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.current(amp));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.current(units)"},"sensing_drivetrain_heading":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_heading","markdown":"# Drive Heading\n\nПередає напрямок у який спрямована трансмісія.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.heading(degrees)\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Drivetrain.heading` передає значення в діапазоні **від 0.00 до 359.99 градусів**.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує курс трансмісії на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain Heading: %.2f\", Drivetrain.heading(degrees));\n\n    // Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.heading(degrees)"},"sensing_drivetrain_isDone":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_isDone","markdown":"# Drive Is Done\n\nПовідомляє, коли трансмісія закінчила рух.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.isDone()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Drivetrain.isDone` передає значення **true**, коли мотори трансмісії закінчили свою роботу.\n\n`Drivetrain.isDone` передає значення **false**, коли мотори трансмісії досі працюють.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує на екрані VEX IQ Brain те, чи трансмісія закінчила свій рух.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 1000, mm, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain is Done: %s\", Drivetrain.isDone() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.isDone()"},"sensing_drivetrain_isMoving":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_isMoving","markdown":"# Drive Is Moving\n\nПовідомляє, якщо трансмісія рухається.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.isMoving()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЦя команда передає значення **true**, якщо трансмісія рухається внаслідок роботи команди `Drivetrain.driveFor` або `Drivetrain.turnFor`, які мають встановлену відстань руху.\n\nЦя команда передає значення **false**, якщо трансмісія закінчила рух.\n\n**Зауваження:** Ця команда завжди повертає **false**, якщо виконуються команди `Drivetrain.drive` або `Drivetrain.turn` (вони *не* мають встановленої відстані руху).\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує на екрані VEX IQ Brain те, чи трансмісія ще рухається.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 1000, mm, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain is Moving: %s\", Drivetrain.isMoving() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.isMoving()"},"sensing_drivetrain_rotation":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_rotation","markdown":"# Drive Rotation\n\nПередає кут повороту трансмісії у градусах.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.rotation(degrees)\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Drivetrain.rotation` збільшує і передає значення, коли трансмісія повертає у напрямку **проти годинникової стрілки**.\n\n`Drivetrain.rotation` зменшує і передає значення, коли трансмісія повертає у напрямку **за годинниковою стрілкою**.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує кут повороту трансмісії на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Drivetrain Rotation: %.2f\", Drivetrain.rotation(degrees));\n\n  // Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.rotation(degrees)"},"sensing_drivetrain_velocity":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_velocity","markdown":"# Drivetrain Velocity\n\nПередає поточну швидкість трансмісії.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n`Drivetrain.velocity` передає десяткове значення (*double*), яке показує поточну швидкість трансмісії.\n\n`Drivetrain.velocity` передає значення в діапазоні **від -100% до 100%**, якщо одиниці вимірювання `units` - **percent**.\n\n`Drivetrain.velocity` також передає значення в **rpm** (revolutions per minute - обертів за хвилину) якщо ввести ці одиниці в параметр `units`.\n\nЯкщо отримано негативне значення, це значить, що трансмісія рухається у зворотному напрямку.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує швидкість трансмісії (у відсотках) на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.velocity(percent));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.velocity(units)"},"sensing_gyro_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_calibrate","markdown":"# Gyro Calibrate\n\nКалібрування гіроскопічного датчика потрібне для зменшення загального зміщення, спричиненого гіроскопом.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.calibrate(calibrationType);\n```\n\nВ гіроскопі виникає зміщення, і гіродатчик неправильно розпізнає рухи, навіть якщо датчик не рухається.\n\n## Як це працює\n\nГіроскоп повинен бути нерухомим, поки триває калібрування.\n\nПараметр `calibrationType` можна замінити одним із наступних варіантів, щоб встановити тривалість калібрування гіродатчика:\n- **calNormal** калібрує гіродатчик 2 секунди\n- **calSlow** калібрує гіродатчик 4 секунди\n- **calExtended** калібрує гіродатчик 8 секунди","signature":"Gyro.calibrate(calibrationType);"},"sensing_gyro_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Gyro Heading\n\nПередає поточний курс гіродатчика у градусах.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.heading()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманда `Gyro.heading` збільшує курс у напрямку **проти годинникової стрілки**.\n\n`Gyro.heading` передає значення в діапазоні **від 0.00 до 359.99**.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує курс гіродатчика на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Gyro Heading: %.2f\", Gyro.heading());\n\n  // Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Gyro.heading()"},"sensing_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Gyro Rate\n\nПередає кутову швидкість гіроскопічного датчика VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.rate()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Gyro.rate` передає значення в діапазоні **від 0 до 249.99** градусів за секунду (DPS).","signature":"Gyro.rate()"},"sensing_gyro_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Gyro Rotation\n\nПередає поточний кут повороту гіродатчика VEX IQ у градусах.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.rotation()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Gyro.rotation` збільшує значення, коли гіродатчик обертається у напрямку **проти годинникової стрілки**.\n\n`Gyro.rotation` зменшує значення, коли гіродатчик обертається у напрямку **за годинниковою стрілкою**.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує кут повороту гіродатчика на екрані VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Gyro Rotation: %.2f\", Gyro.rotation());\n\n  // Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Gyro.rotation()"},"sensing_gyro_setHeading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_setHeading","markdown":"# Gyro Set Heading\n\nВстановлює поточну позицію курсу гіроскопічного датчика у задане значення.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setHeading(heading, degrees);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Gyro.setHeading` використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію курсу гіродатчика на значення в діапазоні від **0** до **359.99**. \n\nЦю команду зазвичай використовують, щоб скинути значення курсу гіродатчика в 0.\n\n`Gyro.setHeading` може приймати десяткові або цілі значення.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЧастина коду нижче встановлює значення курсу гіродатчика в 0 градусів.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"Gyro.setHeading(heading, degrees);"},"sensing_gyro_setRotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_setRotation","markdown":"# Gyro Set Rotation\n\nВстановлює кут повороту гіродатчика VEX IQ в задане значення.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nКоманду `Gyro.setRotation` використовують, щоб перезаписати поточну позицію кута повороту гіродатчика на введене позитивне (проти годинникової стрілки) або негативне (за годинниковою стрілкою) значення.\n\n`Gyro.setRotation` приймає позицію в межах будь-якого негативного або позитивного десяткового чи цілого числа в параметр `rotation`.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче встановлює кут повороту гіродатчика в -45 градусів.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setRotation(-45, degrees);\n```","signature":"Gyro.setRotation(rotation, degrees);"},"sensing_motor_current":{"name":"sensing_motor_current","markdown":"# Motor Current\n\nПередає кількість струму, яку мотор VEX IQ зараз використовує.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.current(units)\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Motor.current` передає десяткове значення (*double*) кількості струму, яку зараз використовує мотор.\n\nКоманда `Motor.current` приймає параметр одиниць вимірювання `units` **amp** (ампери) або **percent**.\n\nДрукування струму мотору у відсотках:\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\" , Motor.current(percent));\n```\n\nДрукування струму мотору в амперах:\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.current(amp));\n```","signature":"Motor.current(units)"},"sensing_motor_isDone":{"name":"sensing_motor_isDone","markdown":"# Motor Is Done\n\nПовідомляє, якщо вибраний мотор зупинився.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.isDone()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Motor.isDone` передає значення  **true**, коли вибраний мотор закінчив свою роботу.\n\n`Motor.isDone` передає значення  **false**, коли вибраний мотор досі працює.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує на екрані VEX IQ Brain те, чи мотор ArmMotor закінчив свій рух.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 270, degrees, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"ArmMotor is Done: %s\", ArmMotor.isDone() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  // Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Motor.isDone()"},"sensing_motor_isSpinning":{"name":"sensing_motor_isSpinning","markdown":"# Motor Is Spinning\n\nПовідомляє, якщо вибраний мотор зараз обертається.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.isSpinning()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЦя команда передає значення **true**, коли вибраний мотор обертається.\n\nЦя команда передає значення **false**, коли вибраний мотор зупинено.\n\n**Зауваження:** Ця команда завжди повертає **false**, якщо мотор обертається внаслідок виконання команди `Motor.spin` (вона *не* має встановленого кута повороту).\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче надрукує на екрані VEX IQ Brain, чи обертається мотор ArmMotor.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 270, degrees, false);\n\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"ArmMotor is Spinning: %s\", ArmMotor.isSpinning() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n\n  //Коротка затримка запобігає ривкам або перериванням\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Motor.isSpinning()"},"sensing_motor_position":{"name":"sensing_motor_position","markdown":"# Motor Position\n\nПередає поточну позицію енкодера обраного мотора VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.position(units)\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Motor.position` передає десяткове значення (*double*), яке показує позицію енкодера мотора.\n\nВведіть параметр одиниць вимірювання `units` - **degrees** або **turns**.\n\nОтримання значення у відсотках (**degrees**).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Motor Position (Degrees): %.2f\", Motor.position(degrees));\n```\n\nОтримання значення в обертах (**turns**).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Motor Position (Turns): %.2f\", Motor.position(turns));\n```","signature":"Motor.position(units)"},"sensing_motor_velocity":{"name":"sensing_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Motor Velocity\n\nПовертає поточну швидкість обраного мотора VEX IQ.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Motor.velocity` передає десяткове значення (*double*), яке показує поточну швидкість мотора. \n\nЗадайте одиниці вимірювання `units`, коли використовуєте цю команду.\n\n**percent** - повертає значення в діапазоні **від -100% до 100%**.\n \n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.velocity(percent));\n```\n  \n`Motor.velocity` також повертає значення в діапазоні **від -127 до 127**, коли використано одиниці **rpm** (оберти за хвилину).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.velocity(rpm));\n```","signature":"Motor.velocity(units)"},"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled":{"name":"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled","markdown":"# Controller Enable/Disable\n\n```cpp\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = false;\n```\n\nУвімкнення або вимкнення налаштованих дій контролера з меню пристроїв. \n\n## Як це працює\n\nВстановіть увімкнення або вимкнення налаштованих дій контролера, надавши команді RemoteControlCodeEnabled значення `true` або `false`. За замовчуванням, контролер увімкнено в кожному проєкті.\n\n## Приклад\n\nНалаштовані дії у цьому прикладі використовуються для керуванням трансмісією і встановлюються у налаштуваннях контролера в меню пристроїв.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/cpp/uk/sensing_remote_control_code_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nУ цьому прикладі налаштовані дії контролера вимкнені на початку роботи програми.\n\nПотім, робот проїде вперед 150 мм.\n\nЗрештою, команда **RemoteControlCodeEnabled** вмикає контролер для відновлення керування роботом із контролера.\n\n```cpp\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = false;\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 150, mm);\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = true;\n```","signature":"RemoteControlCodeEnabled = true;"},"sensing_touchled_pressing":{"name":"sensing_touchled_pressing","markdown":"# TouchLED Pressing\n\nПовідомляє, якщо LED датчик дотику натиснуто.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.pressing()\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПередає значення **true**, якщо обраний LED датчик дотику натиснуто. Передає значення **false**, якщо обраний LED датчик дотику не натиснуто.\n\nПерша частина команди - назва пристрою.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED2.pressing()\nTouchLED4.pressing()\n```\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче надає LED датчику дотику червоний колір **red**. Коли LED датчику дотику натиснути, його колір зміниться на зелений **green**.\n\n```cpp\nTouchLED.setColor(red);\n\nwhile (!TouchLED.pressing()) {\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n\nTouchLED.setColor(green);\n```","signature":"TouchLED.pressing()"},"sensing_vision_largestObject":{"name":"sensing_vision_largestObject","markdown":"# Vision Largest Object\n\nПовертає інформацію про найбільший знайдений датчиком зору об'єкт.\n\n```cpp\nVision.largestObject\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nНеобхідно викликати команду `Vision.takeSnapshot` перед використанням команди `Vision.largestObject`.\n\nКоманда `Vision.largestObject` повертає об'єкт типу `vision::object`.\n\n```cpp\n// Зробити фото сигнатури кольору COLOR_SIG\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"X: %d\", Vision.largestObject.centerX);\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Y: %d\", Vision.largestObject.centerY);\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\n`Vision.largestObject` має тип `vision::object`, тому доступні такі властивості.\n\n- `id` - Унікальний ID, присвоєний кожному об'єкту датчиком зору, тип `int`\n- `originX` - Позиція верхньої лівої частини об'єкта по вісі X, тип `int`\n- `originY` - Позиція верхньої лівої частини об'єкта по вісі Y, тип `int`\n- `centerX` - Позиція центра об'єкта по вісі X, тип `int`\n- `centerY` - Позиція центра об'єкта по вісі Y, тип `int`\n- `width` - Ширина об'єкта, тип `int`\n- `height` - Висота об'єкта, тип `int`\n- `angle` - Кут об'єкта, тип `double`\n- `exists` - Датчик зору бачить об'єкт або ні, тип `bool`","signature":"Vision.largestObject"},"sensing_vision_objectCount":{"name":"sensing_vision_objectCount","markdown":"# Vision Object Count\n\nПовідомляє, скільки об'єктів бачить датчик зору. \n\n```cpp\nVision.objectCount\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПереконайтеся, що ви вказали назву датчика зору в першій частині команди. \n\nЩоб команда `Vision.objectCount` могла знайти об'єкти, спочатку потрібно налаштувати сигнатуру кольору.\n\nСпочатку треба викликати `Vision.takeSnapshot` для фотографування потрібної сигнатури, а потім `Vision.objectCount` зможе повідомити про кількість знайдених об'єктів.\n\n`Vision.objectCount` повертає кількість об'єктів, знайдених на останній фотографії.\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче друкує на екрані VEX IQ Brain кількість об'єктів обраної сигнатури, знайдених датчиком зору.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n\n  // Зробити фотографію обраної сигнатури\n  Vision.takeSnapshot(SIGNATURE);\n\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Number of Objects Detected: %d\", Vision.objectCount);\n\n  // Робити нову фотографію кожні 20 мілісекунд\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"Vision.objectCount"},"sensing_vision_objects":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects","markdown":"# Vision Objects\n\nПовертає масив з усіх об'єктів, які побачив датчик зору.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nНеобхідно викликати команду `Vision.takeSnapshot` перед використанням масиву `Vision.objects`.\n\n`Vision.objects` - це масив, який містить усі об'єкти, які знайшов датчик зору на останній фотографії.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\nvision::object firstObject = Vision.objects[0];\n```\nЙого можна використовувати як будь-який інший масив. Ви можете отримати доступ до об'єктів у ньому за індексом кожного елемента.\n\n```cpp\nvision::object visionObject = Vision.objects[0];\n```\n\nВи також можете використати структури керування, наприклад **цикл for**. Команду `Vision.objectCount` можна використати як умову циклу.\n\nЧастина нижче друкує на VEX IQ Brain значення центрів `centerX` і `centerY` кожного знайденого об'єкта.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\n\nfor(int i = 0; i < Vision.objectCount; i++) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"X: %d\", Vision.objects[i].centerX);\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Y: %d\", Vision.objects[i].centerY);\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n}\n```\n\n`Vision.objects` має тип `vision::object`, тому доступні такі властивості.\n\n- `id` - Унікальний ID, присвоєний кожному об'єкту датчиком зору, тип `int`\n- `originX` - Позиція верхньої лівої частини об'єкта по вісі X, тип `int`\n- `originY` - Позиція верхньої лівої частини об'єкта по вісі Y, тип `int`\n- `centerX` - Позиція центра об'єкта по вісі X, тип `int`\n- `centerY` - Позиція центра об'єкта по вісі Y, тип `int`\n- `width` - Ширина об'єкта, тип `int`\n- `height` - Висота об'єкта, тип `int`\n- `angle` - Кут об'єкта, тип `double`\n- `exists` - Датчик зору бачить об'єкт або ні, тип `bool`","signature":"Vision.objects"},"sensing_vision_objects_angle":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_angle","markdown":"# Objects angle\n\nПовертає кут об'єкта, знайденого датчиком зору.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].angle\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЩоб використати `Vision.objects[index]`, виконайте наступні кроки:\n\n1. Налаштуйте ваш датчик зору у вікні пристроїв.\n2. Використайте `Vision.takeSnapshot()`, щоб захопити зображення з датчика зору і пошукати на ньому сигнатури або коди кольору.\n3. Використайте `Vision.objects[index].exists`, щоб перевірити, чи датчик зору знайшов потрібну сигнатуру / коди кольору.\n\nЩойно датчик зору побачить об'єкт, використайте інші блоки датчика зору, щоб дізнатися більше про об'єкт.\n\n* Використайте **index** щоб вибрати об'єкт з усіх знайдених, про який ви хочете дізнатися більше. Більший об'єкт буде вище у списку,наприклад, `Vision.objects[0]` повертає найбільший об'єкт.\n* Використайте `Vision.objectCount`, щоб визначити, скільки сигнатур / кодів кольору було знайдено.\n* Додатково можна отримати таку інформацію про об'єкти: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` і `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].angle` повідомляє кут знайденого об'єкта. Повертає значення в діапазоні **0 - 180 градусів**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.screen.print(MyVision.objects[0].angle);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].angle"},"sensing_vision_objects_centerx":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_centerx","markdown":"# Objects center X\n\nПовертає координату Х центру об'єкта, знайденого датчиком зору.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].centerX\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЩоб використати `Vision.objects[index]`, виконайте наступні кроки:\n\n1. Налаштуйте ваш датчик зору у вікні пристроїв.\n2. Використайте `Vision.takeSnapshot()`, щоб захопити зображення з датчика зору і пошукати на ньому сигнатури або коди кольору.\n3. Використайте `Vision.objects[index].exists`, щоб перевірити, чи датчик зору знайшов потрібну сигнатуру / коди кольору.\n\nЩойно датчик зору побачить об'єкт, використайте інші блоки датчика зору, щоб дізнатися більше про об'єкт.\n\n* Використайте **index** щоб вибрати об'єкт з усіх знайдених, про який ви хочете дізнатися більше. Більший об'єкт буде вище у списку,наприклад, `Vision.objects[0]` повертає найбільший об'єкт.\n* Використайте `Vision.objectCount`, щоб визначити, скільки сигнатур / кодів кольору було знайдено.\n* Додатково можна отримати таку інформацію про об'єкти: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` і `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].centerX` повідомляє координату Х центру знайденого об'єкта. Повертає значення в діапазоні **0 - 315 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[1].centerX);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].centerX"},"sensing_vision_objects_centery":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_centery","markdown":"# Objects center Y\n\nПовертає координату Y центру об'єкта, знайденого датчиком зору.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].centerY\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЩоб використати `Vision.objects[index]`, виконайте наступні кроки:\n\n1. Налаштуйте ваш датчик зору у вікні пристроїв.\n2. Використайте `Vision.takeSnapshot()`, щоб захопити зображення з датчика зору і пошукати на ньому сигнатури або коди кольору.\n3. Використайте `Vision.objects[index].exists`, щоб перевірити, чи датчик зору знайшов потрібну сигнатуру / коди кольору.\n\nЩойно датчик зору побачить об'єкт, використайте інші блоки датчика зору, щоб дізнатися більше про об'єкт.\n\n* Використайте **index** щоб вибрати об'єкт з усіх знайдених, про який ви хочете дізнатися більше. Більший об'єкт буде вище у списку,наприклад, `Vision.objects[0]` повертає найбільший об'єкт.\n* Використайте `Vision.objectCount`, щоб визначити, скільки сигнатур / кодів кольору було знайдено.\n* Додатково можна отримати таку інформацію про об'єкти: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` і `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].centerY` повідомляє координату Y центру знайденого об'єкта. Повертає значення в діапазоні **0 - 211 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[2].centerY);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].centerY"},"sensing_vision_objects_exists":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_exists","markdown":"# Objects exists\n\nПовідомляє, якщо датчик зору знайшов заданий об'єкт. \n\nОб'єкт потрібно налаштувати, перш ніж команда `Vision.objects[index].exists` зможе його знайти.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].exists\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nПереконайтеся, що ви вказали назву датчика зору в першій частині команди. \n\n`Vision.objects[index].exists` повертає значення **true**, коли датчик зору знайшов заданий об'єкт.\n\n`Vision.objects[index].exists` повертає значення **false**, коли датчик зору не знайшов заданий об'єкт.\n\nПеред тим, як команда `Vision.objects[index].exists` зможе повернути значення **true** або **false**, необхідно використати `Vision.takeSnapshot()`.\n\n\n```cpp\nif(Vision.objects[0].exists){\n\n}\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].exists;"},"sensing_vision_objects_height":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_height","markdown":"# Objects height\n\nПовертає висоту об'єкта, знайденого датчиком зору.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].height\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЩоб використати `Vision.objects[index]`, виконайте наступні кроки:\n\n1. Налаштуйте ваш датчик зору у вікні пристроїв.\n2. Використайте `Vision.takeSnapshot()`, щоб захопити зображення з датчика зору і пошукати на ньому сигнатури або коди кольору.\n3. Використайте `Vision.objects[index].exists`, щоб перевірити, чи датчик зору знайшов потрібну сигнатуру / коди кольору.\n\nЩойно датчик зору побачить об'єкт, використайте інші блоки датчика зору, щоб дізнатися більше про об'єкт.\n\n* Використайте **index** щоб вибрати об'єкт з усіх знайдених, про який ви хочете дізнатися більше. Більший об'єкт буде вище у списку,наприклад, `Vision.objects[0]` повертає найбільший об'єкт.\n* Використайте `Vision.objectCount`, щоб визначити, скільки сигнатур / кодів кольору було знайдено.\n* Додатково можна отримати таку інформацію про об'єкти: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` і `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].height` повідомляє, наскільки високий об'єкт у пікселях. Повертає значення в діапазоні **2 - 212 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[3].height);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].height;"},"sensing_vision_objects_width":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_width","markdown":"# Objects width\n\nПовертає ширину об'єкта, знайденого датчиком зору.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].width\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЩоб використати `Vision.objects[index]`, виконайте наступні кроки:\n\n1. Налаштуйте ваш датчик зору у вікні пристроїв.\n2. Використайте `Vision.takeSnapshot()`, щоб захопити зображення з датчика зору і пошукати на ньому сигнатури або коди кольору.\n3. Використайте `Vision.objects[index].exists`, щоб перевірити, чи датчик зору знайшов потрібну сигнатуру / коди кольору.\n\nЩойно датчик зору побачить об'єкт, використайте інші блоки датчика зору, щоб дізнатися більше про об'єкт.\n\n* Використайте **index** щоб вибрати об'єкт з усіх знайдених, про який ви хочете дізнатися більше. Більший об'єкт буде вище у списку,наприклад, `Vision.objects[0]` повертає найбільший об'єкт.\n* Використайте `Vision.objectCount`, щоб визначити, скільки сигнатур / кодів кольору було знайдено.\n* Додатково можна отримати таку інформацію про об'єкти: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` і `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].width` повідомляє, наскільки широкий об'єкт у пікселях. Повертає значення в діапазоні **2 - 316 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[1].width);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].width;"},"sensing_vision_takeSnapshot":{"name":"sensing_vision_takeSnapshot","markdown":"# Vision Take Snapshot\n\nРобить знімок датчиком зору.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(signature);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\n`Vision.takeSnapshot` фіксує поточне зображення з датчика зору, щоб обробити і проаналізувати його на сигнатури кольору та коди.\n\nПеред використанням команди `Vision.takeSnapshot` треба налаштувати датчик зору хоча б на одну сигнатуру. Ім'я сигнатури буде згенеровано автоматично.\n\nНаприклад, якщо назва датчика `Vision1`, а сигнатура налаштована з ім'ям `REDBOX`, ім'я сигнатури буде `Vision1__REDBOX`, і для створення знімка треба викликати:\n\n```cpp\nVision1.takeSnapshot(Vision1__REDBOX);\n```\n\nЗазвичай, `Vision.takeSnapshot` треба викликати перед використанням інших команд датчика зору.\n\nПереконайтеся, що правильно назвали датчик зору і сигнатуру, коли використовуватимете цю команду. Сигнатуру датчика зору можна налаштувати з вікна налаштувань робота.","signature":"Vision.takeSnapshot(signature);"},"sound_play_note":{"name":"sound_play_note","markdown":"# Play Note\n\nГрає вибрану музичну ноту.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playNote(octave, note, duration);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nВиберіть октаву. Найнижча 1, а найвища 7. \n\nВиберіть ноту, яку грати на цій октаві:\n- `C = 0`\n- `D = 1`\n- `E = 2`\n- `F = 3`\n- `G = 4`\n- `A = 5`\n- `B = 6`\n\nВиберіть, як довго гратиме нота в **мілісекундах**:\n\n- Повна нота грає 1 секунду (1000 мілісекунд)\n- Половина ноти грає 0.5 секунд (500 мілісекунд)\n- Чверть ноти грає 0.25 секунд (250 мілісекунд)\n\nЩойно музична нота розпочне грати, наступні команди миттєво почнуть виконуватись.\n\n## Приклад\n\nЦей приклад гратиме ноту До на першій октаві (Middle C) 1 секунду.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playNote(4, 0, 1000);\n```","signature":"Brain.playNote(octave, note, duration);"},"sound_play_sound":{"name":"sound_play_sound","markdown":"# Play Sound\n\nГрає вибраний звуковий ефект із динаміків VEX IQ Brain.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playSound(sound);\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЗамініть `sound` одним із наступних звуків.\n\n- `siren`\n- `wrongWay`\n- `wrongWaySlow`\n- `fillup`\n- `headlightsOn`\n- `headlightsOff`\n- `tollBooth`\n- `alarm`\n- `tada`\n- `doorClose`\n- `ratchet`\n- `wrench`\n- `siren2`\n- `ratchet2`\n- `alarm2`\n- `powerDown`\n\n## Приклад\n\nПриклад нижче грає звук **siren**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.playSound(siren);   \n```\n\nЩойно звуковий ефект розпочне грати, наступні команди миттєво почнуть виконуватись.","signature":"Brain.playSound(sound);"},"variables_2d_arrays":{"name":"variables_2d_arrays","markdown":"# 2D Array Variables\n\nОголошує тип, ім'я, довжину 2D масиву. \n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 },\n};\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nОголосіть, який тип даних зберігатиметься у вашому 2D масиві. \n\n- `int`\n- `double`\n- `bool`\n\nНазвіть масив характерним та унікальним ім'ям. Встановіть розміри масиву всередині 2 пар квадратних дужок `[]` після імені масиву. \n\n```cpp\n// Оголошення нового 2D масиву з 3 рядками і 3 стовпцями.\n\nint my2DArray[3][3];\n```\n\nМожна ініціалізувати значення елементів масиву під час створення масиву, використовуючи фігурні дужки.\n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 }\n};\n```\n\nЗначення можна присвоїти індивідуально за індексами. Індекс завжди починається з нуля.\n\n```cpp\n// Оголошення нового масиву turnAngles із 3 рядками і 3 стовпцями\nint turnAngles[3][3];\n\n// Присвоєння значень за індексом\nint turnAngles[0][0] = 45;\nint turnAngles[0][1] = 90;\nint turnAngles[0][2] = 180;\nint turnAngles[1][0] = 270;\n```\n\nЩоб зчитати значення з масиву, введіть індекс потрібного елемента у квадратних дужках.\n\n```cpp\n// Змінній angle буде присвоєно значення 270\n\nint angle = turnAngles[1][0];\n```\n\n## Приклад\n\nУ цьому прикладі показано 2D масив типу **double**, з ім'ям `myAngles`, який зберігатиме значення кутів.\n\n```cpp\ndouble myAngles[2][3] = {\n  {45.5, 90.0, 88.2},\n  {25.0, 75.5, 45.0}\n};\n```","signature":"variables_2d_array"},"variables_arrays":{"name":"variables_arrays","markdown":"# Array Variables\n\nОголошує тип, ім'я, довжину масиву.\n\n```cpp\nint myArray[3] = { 1, 2, 3 };\n```\n\n## Як це працює\n\nОголосіть, який тип даних зберігатиметься у вашому масиві. \n\n- `int`\n- `double`\n- `bool`\n\nНазвіть масив характерним та унікальним ім'ям. Встановіть розміри масиву всередині пари квадратних дужок `[]` після імені масиву. \n\n```cpp\nint turnAngles[3];\n```\n\nМожна ініціалізувати значення елементів масиву під час створення масиву, використовуючи фігурні дужки.\n\n```cpp\nbool boolArray[2] = { false, true };\n```\n\nЗначення можна присвоїти індивідуально за індексами. Індекс завжди починається з нуля.\n\n```cpp\n// Оголошення нового масиву завдовжки 3\ndouble doubleArray[3];\n\n// Присвоєння значень за індексом\ndouble doubleArray[0] = 1.5;\ndouble doubleArray[1] = 3.14;\ndouble doubleArray[2] = 2.18;\n```\n\nЩоб зчитати значення з масиву, введіть індекс потрібного елемента у квадратних дужках.\n\n```cpp\n// Зчитує значення за індексом 2 в масиві integerArray\n\nint value = integerArray[2];\n```\n\n## Приклад\n\nУ цьому прикладі ініціалізуються значення масиву, потім дістається елемент №3 (з індексом 2) зі списку, щоб обертати мотор.\n\n```cpp\nint degreesArray[3] = { 30, 60, 90 };\nMotor.spinFor(forward, degreesArray[2], degrees);\n```","signature":"variables_arrays"},"variables_boolean":{"name":"variables_boolean","markdown":"# Boolean Variable\n\nЗберігає значення **true** або **false**.\n\n`bool myBoolean = true;`\n\n## Як це працює\n\n**Логічні змінні** зберігають значення **true** або **false**. Оголошується ключовим словом `bool` перед унікальною і характерною назвою змінної, присвоюється значення `true` або `false`. \n\n`bool goFast = true;`\n\nЛогічні змінні можна використати всередині умовних виразів керування. \n\n```cpp\nif (goFast) {\n  Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity(100, percent);\n}\n```","signature":"variables_boolean"},"variables_double":{"name":"variables_double","markdown":"# Double Variable\n\nВстановлює змінну типу `double`.\n\n`double myDouble = 1.5;`\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЗмінна типу `double` - це число з плаваючою комою (десяткове).\n\n`double pi = 3.14;`\n\nСтворіть унікальне і характерне ім'я. Потім, присвойте значення змінній.\n\n`double turnAngle = 40.5;`","signature":"variables_double"},"variables_intergers":{"name":"variables_intergers","markdown":"# Integer Variable\n\nВстановлює числову змінну з оголошенням ім'ям і значення.\n\n`int myNumber = 10;`\n\n## Як це працює\n\nСтворіть унікальне і характерне ім'я.\n\n`int driveTime = 60;`\n\nПрисвойте значення змінній. Змінна може зберігати значення датчиків або результати обчислень, якщо вони мають відповідний **тип**.\n\n```cpp\nint lowBatteryLifeWarning = Brain.Battery.capacity(percent);\n```\n\n\n## Приклад\n\nУ цьому прикладі змінній \"myVariable\" присвоюється відстань (у міліметрах), отримана датчиком відстані VEX IQ, ця змінна \"myVariable\" використовується для встановлення швидкості трансмісії.\n\n```cpp\nint myVariable = Distance7.distance(mm);\n\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(myVariable, percent);\n```","signature":"variables_intergers"},"variables_my_string":{"name":"variables_my_string","markdown":"# String Variable\n\nВстановлює змінну типу **string**.\n\n`char myString[] = \"my string\";`\n\n## Як це працює\n\nЗмінна типу **string** може зберігати комбінацію різних цифр і букв, які їй присвоюють у лапках `\" \"`.\n\nСтворіть унікальне і характерне ім'я. Потім, присвойте значення змінній **string**. В IQ змінній **string** можна присвоїти значення так.\n\n`char driveMessage[] = \"Time to Drive!\";`","signature":"variables_my_string"}}},"zh-CN":{"blocks":{"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# 加法\n\n把任意两个值加起来，并报告总和。\n\n![add](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/add/add.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**加法**可接受小数、整数或数字指令块。\n\n**加法**指令块可被用在接受圆形空白的指令块中。\n\n两个数字相加。\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/add/add_numbers.png)\n\n加法中的加数可以为变量。\n\n![add_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/add/add_variables.png)  \n\n加法中的加数可以为传感器或设备值。\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# 与\n\n报告是否两个布尔条件均为真值。\n\n![and](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/and/and.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**与**指令块在两个条件均为**真**时，报告**真**值。\n\n**与**指令块在一个（或两个）条件为**假**时，报告**假**值。\n\n**与**指令块报告**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白的指令块中。\n\n![and_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将检验VEX IQ遥控器的两个按键是否同时被按下。\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/and/and_sensors.png)\n\n 当**遥控器E上按键**和**遥控器L下按键**同时被按下时，**与**指令块将返回**真**值。\n\n 当遥控器上的一个（或两个）按键没有被按下时，**与**指令块将返回**假**值。\n\n![and_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/and/and_truth.png)"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# 电量水平\n\n报告VEX IQ主控器电池的电量水平。\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电量水平** 报告范围为 **0% 到 100%**.\n\n**电量水平** 指令块可用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示如果VEX IQ主控器**电量水平**低于50%时，播放一次警报音效。\n\n![battery_capacity_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/battery_level/battery_capacity_example_revised.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# 布尔变量\n\n报告一个布尔变量的值。\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**布尔变量**指令块用于报告存储在该变量内的一个**真**或**假**值。使用**设定布尔变量**指令块来设定或更新一个布尔变量的值。\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\n**布尔变量**指令块报告一个**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白的指令块中。\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\n布尔变量通过**定义一个布尔变量**按钮生成。\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"brain_button_pressed":{"name":"brain_button_pressed","markdown":"# 主控器按键按下\n\n报告VEX IQ主控器的一个按键是否被按下。\n\n![button_pressed_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n如果被选择的主控器按键被按下则**主控器按键按下**报告**真**值。\n\n如果被选择的主控器按键未按下则**主控器按键按下**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用主控器的哪一个按键。\n\n![button_pressed_options](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/brain_button_pressed/button_pressed_options.png)\n\n**主控器按键按下**指令块报告一个**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白的指令块中。\n\n![brainButtonPressed_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_inserted.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示直到主控器**上**按键被按下，机器人正向驱动然后右转。\n\n![brainButtonPressed_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/brain_button_pressed/brainButtonPressed_example_revised.png)\n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# 退出循环\n\n直接退出一个正在重复的循环。\n\n![break](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/break/break.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当添加到C型控制指令块时，**退出循环**指令块将退出它当前所在的循环。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示底盘正向驱动并检验VEX IQ主控器**上**按键是否被按下。 \n\n如果**上**按键被按下，**退出循环**指令块将退出永续循环并且底盘停止。\n\n![break_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Brightness of亮度百分比\n\n报告辨色仪检测到的光线亮度。\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**亮度百分比**报告范围为**0% 到 100%**。\n\n选择使用哪一个辨色仪。\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\n**亮度百分比**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# 广播\n\n广播一个消息来激活任何以**当我收到**指令块开始且正在监听广播消息的指令段。\n\n![broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n发送**广播**的指令段和收到广播消息的指令段同步运行。\n\n选择**广播**哪一条消息，也可以生成一条新消息。\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示VEX IQ触碰LED亮红灯，等待2秒后广播**消息1**。\n\n一旦消息被接收，**当我收到**指令段将正向驱动底盘同时钳爪将张开。 \n\n如同红色箭头所示两个指令段将继续同时运行。\n\n![broadcast_example_arrows](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/broadcast/broadcast_example_arrows.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# 广播并等待\n\n广播一个消息来激活任何以**当我收到**指令块开始且正在监听广播消息的指令段，同时暂停后续的指令段。\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n发送**广播**的指令段将暂停直到收到广播消息的指令段运行完成。\n\n选择**广播**哪一条消息，也可以生成一条新消息。\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示VEX IQ触碰LED亮红灯，等待2秒后广播**消息1**。\n\n一旦消息被接收，**当我收到**指令段将正向驱动底盘并且播放一个音效。\n\n如同红色箭头所示，在继续运行后续指令块之前，正在广播消息的指令段将等待，直到收到消息的指令段运行完成。\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows_3](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_example_arrows3.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# 校准陀螺仪\n\n校准VEX IQ陀螺仪用于减小由陀螺仪产生的漂移值。\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\n即使传感器没有移动，陀螺仪错误检测运动时会产生漂移。\n\n## 如何应用\n\n在校准过程中陀螺仪必须保持静止。\n\n选择使用哪一个陀螺仪。\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)\n\n选择校准时长，校准时间越长，漂移越小。\n\n![calibrate_gyro_seconds](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_seconds.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# 修改变量\n\n根据指定的值修改变量。\n\n![change_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个变量 - 被选择的变量也可以重命名或者删除。\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\n**修改变量**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n本例将演示每**重复循环**循环一次，设定底盘速度的变量值将增加10.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# 清空所有行\n\n清空整个VEX IQ主控器屏幕。\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**清空所有行**不会重置主控器的屏幕光标。使用**设定光标**指令块重置主控器的屏幕光标到期望的位置。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示打印“Hello”1秒钟，然后清空整个屏幕，打印“Goodbye”。\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# 清空行\n\n清空VEX IQ主控器屏幕其中一行。\n\n![clear_row](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**清空行**指令块可接受**1 到 5**之间的整数或数字指令块，来设定清空哪一行。\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/clear_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示在第2行第1列打印“Hello”3秒钟，然后清空第2行。\n\n![clear_row_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/clear_row/clear_row_example.png)"},"color_detects_color":{"name":"color_detects_color","markdown":"# 颜色检测\n\n报告VEX IQ辨色仪是否检测到指定颜色。\n\n![color_detects](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/color_detects_color/color_detects.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当辨色仪检测到指定颜色时，**颜色检测**报告**真**值。\n\n当辨色仪检测到不同于指定颜色时，**颜色检测**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个辨色仪。\n\n![color_detects_chosen](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/color_detects_color/color_detects_chosen.png)\n\n选择检测哪一种颜色。\n\n![color_detects_selected](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/color_detects_color/color_detects_selected.png)\n\n**颜色检测**指令块报告一个**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![color_detects_shape](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/color_detects_color/color_detects_shape.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示打印“红色”或“其他颜色”取决于辨色仪是否检测到“红色”。\n\n![color_detects_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/color_detects_color/color_detects_example.png)\n\n"},"color_of":{"name":"color_of","markdown":"# 颜色\n\n报告辨色仪检测到的颜色名称。\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/color_of/color_of_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**颜色**报告以下颜色中的一种：**红色，紫红色，紫罗兰色，蓝紫色，蓝色，蓝绿色，绿色，黄绿色，黄色，橙黄色，橙色，橙红色。**\n\n选择使用哪一个辨色仪。\n\n![color_of](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/color_of/color_of_color.png)\n\n**颜色**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![color_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/color_of/color_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# 备注\n\n允许程序员编写信息来帮助描述他们的程序。\n\n![comment_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n专业的程序员全程使用备注来帮助其他人理解他们的代码。备注同样有助于故障定位和合作。 \n\n首先，通过选择透明方块删除现有文本，然后，输入新文本，从而实现添加文本到**备注**指令块。\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n备注不改变程序或它周围的指令块。\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# 遥控器 启用/停用\n\n启用或停用设备菜单进行的遥控器配置。\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n通过下拉菜单来选择启用或停用遥控器已配置的动作。默认情况下，在每个程序中遥控器均为启用状态。\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n该示例中，配置的动作是通过在设备窗口下，遥控器配置窗口来设置的机器人底盘动作。\n\n![configured_action](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\n该示例中，当程序开始时已配置的遥控器将被停用。\n\n然后，机器人将向前运动6英寸。\n\n最后，**遥控器启用**指令块将启用遥控器从而恢复遥控器已配置动作。\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# 电机电流\n\n报告VEX IQ电机当前使用的功率值百分比（%）或 安培（amps）.\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机电流**报告范围为**0% 到 100%**或**0.0  到 1.2 amps**。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\n选择电机电流的报告单位为%或amps。\n\n![current_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\n**电机电流**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# 光标列数\n\n报告VEX IQ主控器屏幕光标位置的列数。\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**光标列数**报告范围为**1 到 21**。\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_column/row_column_index.png)  \n\n**光标列数**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示检验**光标列数**位置是否大于15，如果位置大于15，程序将设置光标至第1行，第1列，然后打印“Hello”。\n\n![cursor_column_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_column/cursor_column_example_simple.png)\n\n"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# 光标行数\n\n报告VEX IQ主控器屏幕光标位置的行数。\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**光标行数**报告范围为**1 到 5**。\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_row/row_column_index.png)\n\n**光标行数**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示检验**光标行数**位置是否大于4，如果位置大于4，程序将设置光标至第1行，第1列，然后打印“Hello”。\n\n![cursor_row_example_simple](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_row/cursor_row_example_simple.png)"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# 距离\n\n报告VEX IQ测距仪最近物体的距离值。\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**距离**报告范围为**24毫米 到 1000毫米** 或 **1英寸 到 40英寸**.\n\n选择使用哪一个测距仪。\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\n选择**距离**报告单位为英寸或毫米。\n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\n**距离**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# 除法\n\n第一个值除以第二个值并报告除法运算值。\n\n![divide](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/divide/divide.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**除法**可以接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n**除法**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。 \n\n输入数字来做除法。\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\n除法中可以用变量值。\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\n除法中可以用传感器或设备值。\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# 驱动\n\n永远驱动底盘。\n\n![drive_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动**指令块将永远运行底盘直到使用一个新的底盘指令块或程序停止。\n\n选择底盘将要驱动的方向。\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# 驱动电流\n\n报告底盘当前电流值。\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动电流**报告范围为**0% 到 100%** 或 **0.0 到 1.2 amps**.\n\n选择**驱动电流**的单位为%或安培（amps）。\n\n![drive_current_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_current/drive_current_unit.png)\n\n**驱动电流**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# 驱动至\n\n底盘驱动至一个指定的距离。\n\n![drive_for](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择底盘将要驱动的方向。\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\n**驱动至**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n通过输入一个数值并选择测量单位（英寸或毫米）来设定底盘将要驱动多远。\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到底盘驱动结束。\n\n你可以选择箭头展开**并且不等待** - 这一指令将导致其他指令块在底盘驱动的同时继续运行。\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# 驱动归位\n\n报告底盘当前归位角度值。\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动归位**报告范围为**0.00 到 359.99度**。\n\n**驱动归位**报告一个逆时针朝向，如下图。\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_heading/TopDownBot01.png)\n\n**驱动归位**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# 驱动已结束\n\n报告底盘驱动是否完成。\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当底盘电机完成驱动时，**驱动已结束**报告**真**值。\n\n当底盘电机仍在驱动，**驱动已结束**报告**假**值。\n\n**驱动已结束**指令块报告一个**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# 驱动在继续\n\n报告底盘是否正在驱动。\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当底盘电机正在驱动，**驱动在继续**报告**真**值。\n\n当底盘电机已停止，**驱动在继续**报告**假**值。\n\n**驱动在继续**指令块报告一个**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# 驱动转向\n\n当底盘配置VEX IQ陀螺仪时，报告底盘转向角度值。\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n当底盘**逆时针**方向转动时，**驱动转向**报告一个**正**值。\n\n当底盘**顺时针**方向转动时，**驱动转向**报告一个**负**值。\n\n**驱动转向**指令块被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_rotation/iq_drive_rotation_reporter_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# 驱动速度\n\n报告底盘当前速度。\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动速度**报告范围为 **-100% 到 100%** 或 **-127rpm 到 127rpm**。\n\n选择驱动速度单位为百分比（%）或转每分钟（rpm）。\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\n**驱动速度**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# 等于\n\n报告第一个值和第二个值是否相同（相等）。\n\n![equal_to](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当两个值完全相同，**等于**报告**真**值。\n\n当两个值不相同，**等于**报告**假**值。\n\n**等于**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n**等于**指令块报告一个 **真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)\n\n本例将演示如果底盘电流等于100%，在VEX IQ主控器打印“Drivetrain Stalled”。\n\n![equal_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/equal_to/equal_to_example.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# 永续\n\n永续指令块是一个C型控制指令块，它会永久重复执行所包含的任何指令块。\n\n![forever](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/forever/forever.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n将指令块放入**永续**C型控制指令块从而永远重复这些动作。\n\n你可以通过放入一个**退出循环**指令块退出一个**永续**循环。\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nC型控制指令块也可以互相被放入，这个概念叫做嵌套，在编程不同行为时可以帮助节省时间。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示每5秒播放相同音效并永远循环。\n\n![forever_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/forever/forever_example.png)"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# 函数\n\n执行一个选定的函数。\n\n![function](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/function/function.png)\n\n* **绝对值** - 绝对值\n* **下取整** - 向下取最近的整数值\n* **上取整** - 向上取最近的整数值\n* **平方根** - 平方根\n* **sin** - 正弦函数\n* **cos** - 余弦函数\n* **tan** - 正切函数\n* **asin** - 反正弦函数\n* **acos** - 反余弦函数\n* **atan** - 反正切函数\n* **ln** - 以自然数e为底的对数\n* **log** - 以10为底的对数\n* **e ^** - 自然数e的幂次方\n* **10 ^** - 10的幂次方\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**函数**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n从下拉列表中选择数学**函数**。\n\n![function_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/function/function_select.png)\n\n**函数**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。 \n\n![function_fit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# 大于\n\n报告第一个值是否大于第二个值。\n\n![greater_than](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当第一个值比第二个值大，**大于**报告**真**值。\n\n当第一个值小于或等于第二个值，**大于**报告**假**值。\n\n**大于**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n**大于**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n\n本例将演示如果电量水平大于75%，在VEX IQ主控器屏幕打印“Battery Charged!”。\n\n![greater_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/greater_than/greater_than_example.png)\n\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# 陀螺仪归位\n\n报告陀螺仪当前归位角度值。\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**陀螺仪归位**报告范围为**0.00 到 359.99**之间。\n\n**陀螺仪归位**报告一个逆时针朝向,如下图所示。\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/heading_of_gyro/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\n选择检验哪一个陀螺仪。\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\n**陀螺仪归位**指令块可被用在圆形指令块中。\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"hue_of":{"name":"hue_of","markdown":"# 色调\n\n报告VEX IQ辨色仪检测的颜色色调值。\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/hue_of/hue_of_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**色调**报告范围为**0 到 360**。\n\n选择检验哪一个辨色仪。\n\n![hue_of](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/hue_of/hue_of_color.png)\n\n**色调**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![hue_of_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/hue_of/hue_of_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# 如果 那么\n\n**如果 那么**是一个C型控制指令块，如果布尔条件报告为**真**值，则执行所包含的任何指令块。\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**如果 那么**控制指令块只会检测一次布尔条件值。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**真**值，**如果 那么**中的指令块将运行。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**假**值，**如果 那么**中的指令块将被跳过。\n\n**如果 那么**指令块可接受六角形指令块作为它的条件。\n\n![if_then](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示在每次VEX IQ碰撞开关被按下时，播放一次音效。\n\n**如果 那么**C型控制指令块可以被“嵌套”或置于永续指令块内以保证每次都会播放音效而不是只播放一次。\n\n![if_then_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/if_then/if_then_example.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# 如果 那么 否则\n\n**如果 那么 否则**是一个C型控制指令块，它根据报告的布尔值来运行**如果 那么 否则**中的第一部分或第二部分。\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**如果 那么 否则**C型控制指令块只会检验一次布尔条件。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**真**值，则**如果**部分的指令块将被运行。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**假**值，则**否则**部分的指令块将被运行。\n\n**如果 那么 否则**C型控制指令块可接受六角形指令块作为它的条件。\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例演示VEX IQ触碰LED如果被触碰，亮绿灯，当它未被触碰，则亮红灯。\n\n**如果 那么 否则**C型控制指令块可以被“嵌套”或置于永续指令块内以保证触碰LED不止一次亮红灯和绿灯。 \n\n![if_then_else_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/if_then_else/if_then_else_example.png)"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 二维数组元素\n\n报告一个二维数组中某个元素的值。\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个二维数组。该二维数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\n输入数组内被报告的元素的行（第一个数字）和列（第二个数字）位置。\n\n此处，被报告的元素位置为二维数组中第2行，第3列。\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\n**二维数组元素**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# 元素\n\n报告一个数组中某个元素的值。 \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个数组。该数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\n输入数组内元素的位置序号。此处，报告数组中第2个元素。\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\n**元素**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n本例将演示底盘速度设定为数组中第3个元素存储的值，底盘将以90%的速度正向驱动。\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 二维数组长度\n\n报告一个二维数组的行数和列数。 \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个二维数组。该二维数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\n选择报告哪个值，二维数组可以报告**行数** 或 **列数**。\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\n**二维数组长度**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# 小于\n\n报告第一个值是否比第二个值小。 \n\n![less_than](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当第一个值比第二个值小，**小于**报告**真**值。\n\n当第一个值大于或等于第二个值，**小于**报告**假**值。\n\n**小于**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n**小于**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n本例将演示如果电量水平小于25%，在VEX IQ主控器屏幕上打印“Low Battery!”。\n\n![less_than_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/less_than/less_than_example.png)\n\n"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# 电机已结束\n\n报告指定的电机转动是否已完成。\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当指定的电机转动已完成，**电机已结束**报告**真**值。\n\n当指定的电机仍在转动，**电机已结束**报告**真**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\n**电机已结束**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n报告电机是否已结束的指令块可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# 电机在转动\n\n报告指定的电机当前是否在转动。\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当指定的电机转动正在转动，**电机在转动**报告**真**值。\n\n当指定的电机转动已停止，**电机在转动**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\n**电机在转动**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# 乘法\n\n乘以两个值并报告乘积。\n\n![multiply](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**乘法**可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n**乘法**可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n乘以两个数字。\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\n乘以变量值。\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\n乘以传感器或设备值。\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# 下一行\n\n设定打印结果至主控器屏幕的下一可用行。\n\n![next_row](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n所有程序默认光标从屏幕第1行第1列开始。**下一行**指令块将在主控器屏幕上移动光标至下一行。\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/next_row/row_column_index.png)  \n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示打印“First Message”，然后设定光标至下一行，打印“Second Message”。\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/next_row/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_welcome](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/next_row/set_cursor_welcome.png)\n"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# 非\n\n报告布尔结果的相反值。\n\n![not](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/not/not.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当布尔指令块中报告**假**值，**非**指令块报告**真**值。\n\n当布尔指令块中报告**真**值，**非**指令块报告**假**值。\n\n**非**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n本例将演示当VEX IQ主控器“确认”键未被按下时，报告**真**值。 \n\n![not_sensors](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# 对象数目\n\n报告视觉传感器检测到的对象数量。\n\n一个对象需要被配置，在此之后，**对象数目**指令块才能够检测到它。\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器。\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\n在**对象数目**指令块报告对象数目之前需要使用**拍照**指令块。\n\n**对象数目**指令块只会检测来自最后拍照标记的对象的数目。\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# 对象存在\n\n报告视觉传感器是否检测到一个已配置对象。\n\n一个对象需要被配置，在此之后，**对象存在**指令块才能够检测到它。\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器。\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n当视觉传感器检测到一个已配置对象，**对象存在**报告**真**值。\n\n当视觉传感器未检测到一个已配置对象，**对象存在**报告**假**值。\n\n**对象存在**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\n在**对象存在**布尔指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值之前需要使用**拍照**指令块。"},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# 发现对象\n\n报告VEX IQ测距仪是否在它测距范围内检测到一个对象。\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当测距仪在测距范围内检测到一个对象或平面，**发现对象**报告**真**值。\n\n当测距仪在测距范围内未检测到一个对象或平面，**发现对象**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个测距仪。\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\n**发现对象**布尔指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"object_is_near":{"name":"object_is_near","markdown":"# 靠近对象\n\n报告VEX IQ辨色仪是否检测到一个对象靠近。\n\n![object_is_near](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_is_near/object_is_near_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当辨色仪检测到一个对象或表面靠近传感器前方，**靠近对象**报告**真**值。\n\n当辨色仪检测到传感器前方空白，**靠近对象**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个辨色仪。\n\n![object_is_near_color](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_is_near/object_is_near_color.png)\n\n**靠近对象**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![object_is_near_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/object_is_near/object_is_near_inserted.png)\n\n\n "},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# 或\n\n报告两个布尔条件中的一个是否为真。\n\n![or](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/or/or.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当一个（或两个）条件为**真**值，**或**指令块报告**真**值。 \n\n当两个条件均为**假**值，**或**指令块报告**假**值。\n\n**或**布尔指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\n当VEX IQ碰撞开关和VEX IQ触碰LED其中一个（或两个）被按下，**或**指令块报告**真**值，只有碰撞开关和触碰LED都未被按下时报告**假**值。\n\n![or_truth](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/or/or_truth.png)"},"play_note":{"name":"play_note","markdown":"# 播放音符\n\n播放选定的音符。\n\n![play_note](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/play_note/play_note.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择一个音符。\n\n![play_note_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/play_note/play_note_select.png)\n\n选择音符将要播放的时长。\n\n![play_note_duration](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/play_note/play_note_duration.png)\n\n* 一个**全音符**播放1秒钟（1000毫秒）\n* 一个**二分音符**播放0.5秒钟（500毫秒）\n* 一个**四分音符**播放0.25秒（250毫秒）\n\n当一个音符开始播放时，下一个指令块将立即开始。"},"play_sound":{"name":"play_sound","markdown":"# 播放音效\n\n播放选定的音效。\n\n![play_sound](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/play_sound/play_sound.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n从下拉列表中选择音效。\n\n![play_sound_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/play_sound/play_sound_select.png)\n\n当一个音效开始播放时，下一个指令块将立即开始。"},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# 遥控器位标\n\n报告遥控器一个操纵杆沿一个轴向的位标。\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用 \n\n**遥控器位标**报告范围为 **-100 到 100**之间。\n\n当一个操纵杆轴向在中心，**遥控器位标**将报告零（0）。\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\n选择操纵杆轴向来检验它的位标。\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\n**遥控器位标**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n本例将演示重复性检验遥控器操纵杆D轴，从而控制机械臂电机的转速。\n\n![position_of_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# 电机转位\n\n报告电机已转动的距离。\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机转位**以整数数值角度和小数数值转数报告电机转位。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\n选择电机转位的单位为角度或转数。\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\n**电机转位**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。 \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# 碰撞开关按下\n\n报告VEX IQ碰撞是否被按下。\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n如果碰撞开关被按下，**碰撞开关按下**报告**真**值。\n\n如果碰撞开关未被按下，**碰撞开关按下**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个碰撞开关。\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\n**碰撞开关按下**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# 遥控器按下\n\n报告遥控上某个按键是否被按下。\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n如果指定的遥控器按键被按下，**遥控器按下**报告**真**值。\n\n如果指定的遥控器按键未被按下，**遥控器按下**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用遥控器哪一个按键。\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\n**遥控器按下**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且在被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)\n\n\n本例将检验如果E上按键被按下则钳爪电机正转。\n\n![pressing_controller_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_example_revised.png)"},"pressing_touchled":{"name":"pressing_touchled","markdown":"# 触碰LED按下\n\n报告VEX IQ触碰LED是否被按下。\n\n![pressing_touch_led](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n如果选择的触碰LED被按下，**触碰LED按下**报告**真**值。\n\n如果选择的触碰LED未被按下，**触碰LED按下**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个触碰LED。\n\n![pressing_touch_led_led](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_led.png)\n\n**触碰LED按下**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![pressing_touch_led_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_touchled/pressing_touch_led_inserted.png)\n\n"},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# 打印\n\n在VEX IQ主控器屏幕打印文本或值。\n\n![look_print](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/print/look_print.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**打印**指令块将在主控器屏幕光标位置打印数据。\n\n所有新建程序都是从屏幕第1行第1列光标开始。\n\n所有指令块默认将以整数数字打印。使用**设定打印精度**指令块来调节打印的小数位数。\n\n打印字母和数字。\n\n![print_words](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/print/print_words.png)\n\n打印变量值。\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\n打印运算符计算值。\n\n![print_addition](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/print/print_addition.png)  \n\n打印传感器或设备值。\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# 我的指令块\n\n我的指令块用于生成自定义指令块。\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**我的指令块**用于生成一系列可以在一个程序中被多次使用的指令块。\n\n**我的指令块**使用**创建一个指令块**按钮来创建。\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**我的指令块**可以包含多个参数 - 文本标签，数字变量和布尔变量 - 来添加更多的功能到你的自定义指令块中。\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\n要使用一个**我的指令块**，附着调用**我的指令块**到一个帽状指令块。当**我的指令块**出现在你的程序中，包含在**我的指令块**中的程序段将使用指定的参数值运行。\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\n附着一个程序段到**我的指令块**“定义”帽状指令块，来设定当一个**我的指令块**使用时发生的动作。\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***注意：生成多个带有相同标签和变量的 我的指令块 可能导致下载你的程序时报错。***\n\n## 示例1\n\n该示例中，机器人将使用**我的指令块**来：\n\n* 播放警笛声3次。\n* 向前运动12英寸。\n* 播放警笛声3次。\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/sound_example.png)\n\n## 示例2\n\n该示例中，机器人将使用**我的指令块**来：\n\n* 向前运动15英寸\n* 在主控器屏幕打印电池电量同时移动光标至下一行\n* 机器人右转180度\n* 在主控器屏幕打印电池电量同时移动光标至下一行\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# 我的指令块\n\n我的指令块用于生成自定义指令块。\n\n![my_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**我的指令块**用于生成一系列可以在一个程序中被多次使用的指令块。\n\n**我的指令块**使用**创建一个指令块**按钮来创建。\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**我的指令块**可以包含多个参数 - 文本标签，数字变量和布尔变量 - 来添加更多的功能到你的自定义指令块中。\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\n要使用一个**我的指令块**，附着调用**我的指令块**到一个帽状指令块。当**我的指令块**出现在你的程序中，包含在**我的指令块**中的程序段将使用指定的参数值运行。\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\n附着一个程序段到**我的指令块**“定义”帽状指令块，来设定当一个**我的指令块**使用时发生的动作。\n\n![attach_function](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***注意：生成多个带有相同标签和变量的 我的指令块 可能导致下载你的程序时报错。***\n\n## 示例1\n\n该示例中，机器人将使用**我的指令块**来：\n\n* 播放警笛声3次。\n* 向前运动12英寸。\n* 播放警笛声3次。\n\n![sound_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/sound_example.png)\n\n## 示例2\n\n该示例中，机器人将使用**我的指令块**来：\n\n* 向前运动15英寸\n* 在主控器屏幕打印电池电量同时移动光标至下一行\n* 机器人右转180度\n* 在主控器屏幕打印电池电量同时移动光标至下一行\n\n![print_number](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# 随机数\n\n![random](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/random/random.png)\n\n报告指令块中从最小到最大的一个随机值。\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**随机数**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n**随机数**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n## 示例\n\n本例使用一个**随机数**指令块来随机化底盘速度。\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\n本例使用一个**随机数**指令块来随机化一个等待指令块的时间长度。\n\n![random_control](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"rate_of_gyro":{"name":"rate_of_gyro","markdown":"# 陀螺仪角速度\n\n报告VEX IQ陀螺仪传感器的角速度。\n\n![rate_of_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**陀螺仪角速度**报告范围为**0 到 249.99dps**。\n\n**陀螺仪角速度**的单位为度每秒（dps）。\n\n选择使用哪一个陀螺仪。\n\n![rate_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\n**陀螺仪角速度**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![rate_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/rate_of_gyro/rate_of_gyro_inserted.png)"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# 取余\n\n用第二个值除第一个值并报告余数。\n\n![remainder](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**取余**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n可整除的数字将报告取余为零。\n\n**取余**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示7除以2并在VEX IQ主控器屏幕打印余数“1”。\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# 重复\n\n重复指令块是一个C型控制指令块，它会以设定的次数重复执行所包含的任何指令块。\n\n![repeat](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n首先，输入一个值来指示指令块所含指令段将要**重复**多少次。\n \n**重复**C型控制指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\nC型控制指令块也可以互相被放入，这个概念叫做嵌套，在编程不同行为时可以帮助节省时间。\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/repeat/repeat_select.png)\n\n本例将演示重复播放一个音效3秒钟5次。\n\n![repeat_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/repeat/repeat_example.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# 重复直到\n\n重复直到指令块是一个C型控制指令块，它会重复执行所包含的任何指令块直到布尔条件报告为**真**值。\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## 如何应用 \n\n**重复直到**指令块只在每次循环开始时检验布尔条件。 \n\n如果布尔条件报告为**假**值，在**重复直到**指令块中的指令块将运行。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**真**值，在**重复直到**指令块中的指令块将被跳过。\n\n**重复直到**C型控制指令块可接受六角形指令块作为它的条件。 \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示，VEX IQ主控器屏幕打印计时器值，同时底盘正向驱动直到VEX IQ主控器“确认”键被按下。当“确认”键被按下时，底盘将停止。\n\n![repeat_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/repeat_until/repeat_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# 重置计时器\n\n重置VEX IQ主控器的计时器。\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## 如何应用 \n\n主控器计时器在每个程序开始时计时。**重置计时器**指令块用于重置计时器返回0秒。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例中，计时器被重置，底盘正向驱动3秒，3秒钟过后，底盘将停止。\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# 转向角度\n\n报告VEX IQ陀螺仪传感器当前转向的角度值。\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation.png](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n当陀螺仪**逆时针**方向转动时，**陀螺仪转向**报告一个**正**值。\n\n当陀螺仪**顺时针**方向转动时，**陀螺仪转向**报告一个**负**值。\n\n选择检验哪一个陀螺仪传感器。\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_devices.png)\n\n**陀螺仪转向**指令块被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_of_gyro/iq_gyro_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# 取整\n\n将输入的值取整至最近的整数。\n\n![round](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/round/round.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n小数位等于或大于0.5向上**取整**，小数位小于0.5向下**取整**.\n\n**取整**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。 \n\n**取整**指令块接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示取整2.7并将打印“3”。\n\n![round_variables](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# 设定二维数组\n\n通过输入数值来设定二维数组每个元素值。\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## 如何应用 \n\n当生成一个二维数组时，你可以设定数组的**列数**数值在1到10之间，设定数组**行数**数值在1到10之间。\n\n选择使用哪一个二维数组，该二维数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\n**设定二维数组**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# 设定数组\n\n通过输入数值来设定数组每个元素值。\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n数组的长度（1到10）在数组生成时已设定。\n\n选择使用哪一个数组，该数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\n**设定数组**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示设定数组初始值，然后报告数组第3个元素（90）从而设定机械臂位置。\n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# 设定布尔变量\n\n设定一个布尔变量为一个指定值。\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个布尔变量，该变量也可以被重命名或删除。 \n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\n选择一个布尔值。\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\n**设定布尔变量**指令块可被用在六角形指令块中。\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_color_sensor_brightness":{"name":"set_color_sensor_brightness","markdown":"# 设定辨色仪灯亮\n\n设定VEX IQ辨色仪灯光亮度。\n\n![set_color_sensor_light](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_light.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n辨色仪有一个可调节光源来帮助检测一个对象的颜色或者表面亮度。\n\n**设定辨色仪灯亮**接受范围为**0%到100%**，亮度百分比设定越高，辨色仪光源将越亮。\n\n选择使用哪一个辨色仪。\n\n![set_color_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor.png)\n\n**设定辨色仪灯亮**指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\n![set_color_sensor_2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_color_sensor_brightness/set_color_sensor_2.png)\n\n\n"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# 设定光标\n\n设定**打印**指令块光标位置。\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n设定光标行数和列数位置，从而让所有**打印**指令在VEX IQ主控器屏幕指定位置显示。\n\n**设定光标**的**行数**接受范围为**1到5**。\n\n**设定光标**的**列数**接受范围为**1到21**。\n\n![row_column_index](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_cursor/row_column_index.png)  \n\n**设定光标**指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示设定光标至第3行第8列位置，在主控器屏幕该位置打印文本“Hello!”。\n\n![set_cursor_code_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_cursor/set_cursor_code_example.png)\n\n![set_cursor_hello](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_cursor/set_cursor_hello.png)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# 设定底盘归位\n\n设定底盘陀螺仪归位值。\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定底盘归位**指令块可用于设定底盘为任意指定的逆时针朝向，如下图所示。\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n**设定底盘归位**接受范围为**0到360**度。\n\n**设定底盘归位**指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示机器人一共转动135度：\n\n![setDriveHeading_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_example_revised.png)\n\n- 左转归位至45度。\n- 设定机器人的当前位置归位为0度。\n- 根据上一条指令块设定的归位值再次左转90度。\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# 设定底盘转向\n\n当配置有VEX IQ陀螺仪时，设定底盘转向的角度值。\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n **设定底盘转向**指令块可用于设定底盘转向角度至任意指定的正值或负值。\n\n**设定底盘转向**指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例 \n\n该示例将使机器人一共转动210度:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n-左转（逆时针）至转向120度。\n-设定机器人当前位置为转向-45度。\n-根据上一条指令块设定的转向角度值再次左转（逆时针）90度（-45度到+45度）。"},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# 设定驱动停止\n\n设定底盘停止驱动时的行为。\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n* **刹车**将导致底盘立即停止。\n* **滑行**使得底盘逐渐转动至停止。\n* **锁住**将导致底盘立即停止，同时如果有移动会转回到它停止的位置。\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示使底盘正向移动3秒钟，然后在停止的位置锁住。\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# 设定驱动超时\n\n针对底盘驱动指令设定一个时间限制。\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当驱动指令块未达到它的位置时，底盘时间限制可用来防止驱动指令块阻止指令段中其他指令块的运行。\n\n一个底盘未达到它的位置的示例是当一个机器人撞到一面墙且无法完成它的移动。\n\n**设定驱动超时**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示如果底盘没有到达目标值24英寸，在2秒后结束**驱动**指令。当时间限制或距离到达，底盘将继续执行**转**指令。\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# 设定驱动速度\n\n设定底盘的速度。\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定驱动速度**只会设定底盘的速度但是不会导致底盘移动。仍然须要一个**驱动**指令块。\n\n设定 **驱动速度**接受范围为 **-100% 到 100%** 或 **-127rpm 到 127rpm**。\n\n设定底盘速度为负值将导致底盘反向移动。\n\n设定底盘速度为0将导致底盘停止。\n\n**设定驱动速度**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示底盘以50%的速度驱动前进12英寸。\n\n![setDriveVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# 设定陀螺仪归位\n\n设定陀螺仪传感器当前归位为指令块中的值。\n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定陀螺仪归位**指令块可用于设定底盘为任意指定的逆时针朝向，如下图所示。\n\n![TopDownGyro01](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_gyro_heading/TopDownGyro01.png)\n\n**设定陀螺仪归位**接受范围为**0 到 360**度。\n\n**设定陀螺仪归位**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n选择使用哪一个陀螺仪传感器。\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# 设定陀螺仪转向\n\n设定VEX IQ陀螺仪转向角度至指令块内设定的值。\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**设定陀螺仪转向**指令块可用于设定底盘转向角度至任意指定的正值（逆时针）或负值（顺时针）。\n\n**设定陀螺仪转向**指令块可接受一定范围内任意小数或整数的正值或负值数字。\n\n**设定陀螺仪转向**指令块可接受小数，整数或数字指令块。\n\n选择使用哪一个陀螺仪。\n\n![iq_gyro_setrotation_devices](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_gyro_rotation/iq_gyro_setrotation_devices.png)\n\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 置换二维数组元素\n\n更新二维数组中某个元素为一个新的值。\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n输入数组内将要被置换元素的行（第一个数）和列（第二个数）位置。\n\n选择使用哪一个数组，该数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\n**置换元素**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# 置换元素\n\n更新数组中某个元素的值。\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个数组，该数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\n**置换元素**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n\n本例将演示更新my list数组中第2个元素的值为15，且打印my list数组中第2个元素到VEX IQ主控器屏幕。\n\n![replace_item_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_array/replace_item_example.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# 设定电机转位\n\n设定VEX IQ电机编码器转位为输入值。\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机转位**指令块可用于设定电机转位为任意指定值。\n\n通常情况下，**电机转位**指令块通过设定转位为0来重置电机编码器转位。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\n选择测量单位为度数或转数。\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# 设定电机停止\n\n设定VEX IQ智能电机停止时的行为。\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用 \n\n* **刹车**将导致电机立即停止。\n* **滑行**让电机逐渐的转到停止。\n* **锁住**将导致底盘立即停止，同时如果有移动会转回到它停止的位置。\n\n**设定电机停止**将对随后程序中所有电机指令生效。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\n选择电机停止后的设置。\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示机械臂电机正转90度，然后抵抗外部作用力（比如重力）来锁住它的位置。\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# 设定电机超时\n\n针对VEX IQ智能电机运动指令设定一个时间限制。\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当驱动指令块未达到它的转位，电机时间限制可用来防止驱动指令块阻止指令段中其他指令块的运行。\n一个电机未达到转位的示例是一个机械臂或钳爪达到它的机械限制且无法完成它的转动。\n\n**设定电机超时**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示如果钳爪电机未达到270度位置，在2秒后结束**设定电机**指令。当时间限制或目标达到，钳爪电机将转位到0度。\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# 设定电机扭矩\n\n设定VEX IQ智能电机的力量。\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定电机扭矩**接受范围为**0% 到 100%**。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\n**设定电机扭矩**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示以最大扭矩为20%来转动钳爪电机转位至40度，这将使得钳爪可以抓取一个物体，且不会因为力量过大而损坏物体。\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# 设定电机转速\n\n设定VEX IQ智能电机转速。\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定电机转速**接受范围为 **-100% 到 100%** 或 **-127rpm 到 127rpm**.\n\n设定一个电机转速为负值将导致电机反转。\n\n设定一个电机转速为0将导致电机停止。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\n选择转速单位为百分比或转每分钟（rpm）。\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示设定机械臂电机转速为25%，缓慢转至90度转位。\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# 设定打印精度\n\n设定当VEX IQ主控器屏幕打印指令块时，小数点后的数字位数。\n\n![print_precision](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择将要打印到屏幕的指令块的精度级别。\n\n* 个位（1）（默认）\n* 十分位（0.1）\n* 百分位（0.01）\n* 千分位（0.001）\n* 全数字（0.000001）\n\n打印到屏幕的指令块将会取整到最近的精度级别。如下示例，1.67将会以个位精度打印为2且十分位精度为1.7。\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_touchled_brightness":{"name":"set_touchled_brightness","markdown":"# 设定触碰LED亮度\n\n设定VEX IQ触碰LED亮度水平。\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定触碰LED亮度**接受范围为**0% 到 100%**。\n\n选择使用哪一个触碰LED。\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor3](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_sensor3.png)\n\n**设定触碰LED亮度**指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness2.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示触碰LED亮度为25%亮起绿灯。\n\n![set_touchLED_brightness_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_brightness/set_touchled_brightness_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"set_touchled_color":{"name":"set_touchled_color","markdown":"# 设定触碰LED颜色\n\n设定VEX IQ触碰LED颜色。\n\n![set_touchLED_color](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color.png)\n\n## 如何应用 \n\n选择使用哪一个**触碰LED**。\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_sensor.png)\n\n选择将要显示的颜色。  \n\n![set_touchLED_color2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_color/set_touchled_color2.png)\n\n要关闭**触碰LED**颜色，设定颜色为无色。"},"set_touchled_fade":{"name":"set_touchled_fade","markdown":"# 设定触碰LED变色速度\n\n设定VEX IQ触碰LED在不同颜色之间变换的速度快慢。\n\n![set_touchLED_fade](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个触碰LED。\n\n![set_touchLED_sensor2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_sensor2.png)\n\n选择触碰LED变色的速度快慢。\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_speed](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_speed.png)\n\n* 慢 - 触碰LED将缓慢变色为一个新的颜色。\n* 快 - 触碰LED将快速变色为一个新的颜色 。 \n* 灭 - 触碰LED将立刻改变颜色。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示触碰LED缓慢变色为蓝色。\n\n![set_touchLED_fade_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_touchled_fade/set_touchled_fade_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# 设定转向速度\n\n设定底盘转向速度。\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定转向速度**只设定底盘速度但不会使得底盘移动。仍然须要一个**转**指令块。\n\n**设定转向速度**接受范围为 **-100% 到 100%** 或 **-127rpm 到 127rpm**。\n\n设定一个底盘转向速度为负值将导致底盘反向转动。\n\n设定一个底盘转向速度为0将导致底盘停止。\n\n**设定转向速度**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n本例将演示底盘以25%速度缓慢向左转。\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# 设定变量\n\n设定变量为一个指定值。\n\n![set_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个变量，这些变量也可以被重命名或删除。 \n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\n**设定变量**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n本例将演示“my variable”变量值为VEX IQ测距仪感应值，且使用“my variable”变量来设定底盘速度。\n\n![set_variable_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_variable/set_variable_example.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# 设定视觉传感器对象标号\n\n从检测到的对象之中设定对象（你想要获取更多信息的那个对象）标号。\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**对象数目**指令块可用在**设定视觉传感器对象标号**指令块之前来决定检测到的对象数目。\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器。\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\n**设定视觉传感器对象标号**指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\n\n\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# 数组长度\n\n报告一个数组中元素的数量。  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\n选择使用哪一个数组。该数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\n**数组长度**报告指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# 拍照\n\n使用视觉传感器拍照。\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**拍照**指令块将从视觉传感器的当前画面中，捕捉将被处理和分析的颜色标记和编码。 \n\n一般在使用其他视觉传感器指令块之前，首先需要一个**拍照**。\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器。\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器标记。视觉传感器标记在设备窗口中配置。\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# 转\n\n转动一个VEX IQ智能电机直到停止。\n\n![spin_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**转**指令块将永远转动一个电机直到使用一个新的电机指令块或程序停止。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\n选择转动的方向。方向名称可以在设备窗口更改。\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# 转至\n\n转动一个电机到指定的距离。\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**转至**将告诉一个电机从它当前位置以指定方向转动到指定距离。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\n选择转动的方向。方向名称可以在设备窗口更改。\n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\n**转至**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n选择测量单位为度数或转数。\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到电机完成转动。\n\n你可以选择箭头来展开**并且不等待** - 这将导致其他指令块在电机转动时同时继续运行。\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# 转至转位\n\n转动一个VEX IQ智能电机至设定的转位。\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**转至转位**将告诉电机转动到一个设定转位。根据电机当前转位，**转至转位**将决定转动的方向。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\n**转至转位**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n选择测量单位为度数或转数。\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到电机完成转动。\n\n你可以选择箭头来展开**并且不等待** - 这将导致其他指令块在电机转动时同时继续运行。\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# 停止驱动\n\n停止底盘。\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n本例将演示底盘正向驱动3秒钟后停止。\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# 停止电机\n\n停止一个VEX IQ智能电机。\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用。\n\n选择停止哪一个电机。\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示钳爪电机打开3秒钟后停止。\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# 减法\n\n从一个值减去另一个值并报告差值。\n\n![subtract](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**减法**可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n**减法**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n两个数字相减。\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\n减法中可以用变量值。\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\n减法中可以用传感器或设备值。\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# 计时器值\n\n报告VEX IQ主控器计时器秒数值。\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n在程序开始时，计时器从0秒开始计时并报告小数值。\n\n**计时器值**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示底盘正向驱动并播放一个音效，4.5秒钟之后右转90度。\n\n![timerValue_example_revised](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/timer_value/timerValue_example_revised.png)\n\n"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# 转\n\n永远转动底盘。\n\n![turn_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**转**指令块将永远转动底盘直到使用一个新的底盘指令块或程序停止。\n\n选择底盘将要转动的方向。\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# 转动\n\n将底盘转动一定的度数。\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择底盘将要转动的方向。\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\n**转动**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n通过输入一个数字度数来设定底盘将要转动多少。\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\n默认情况下，其它指令块将**等待**直到底盘完成转动。\n\n你可以选择箭头来展开**并且不等待** - 这将导致其它指令块在底盘转动时同时继续运行。\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# 归位至\n\n当底盘配置VEX IQ陀螺仪时，转动底盘至一个特定的归位位置。\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**归位至**指令块可用于转向底盘至任意逆时针归位位置，如下图所示。\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\n根据陀螺仪当前朝向，**归位至**将决定转向的方向。\n\n**归位至**接受范围为**0.00 到 359.99**度。\n\n**归位至**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示底盘做四次转向：\n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- 左转至45度\n- 左转至90度\n- 左转至270度\n- 右转至180度\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到底盘完成转向。\n\n你可以选择箭头来展开**并且不等待** - 这将导致底盘转向的同时其他指令块继续运行。\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# 转向至\n\n当底盘配置VEX IQ陀螺仪时，转动底盘至一个特定的转向角度值。\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**转向至**指令块可用于转动底盘至一个指定的正值（逆时针）或负值（顺时针）。\n\n根据底盘当前**转向**值，**转向至**将决定转动的方向。\n\n**转向至**指令块可接受小数，整数或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n该示例将导致底盘做四次转动：\n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- 左转（逆时针）至90度\n- 左转（逆时针）至180度\n- 右转（顺时针）至-45度\n- 左转（逆时针）至0度\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到底盘转动完成。\n\n-这将导致底盘转动的同时其他指令块继续运行。\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# 变量\n\n报告赋值给变量的值。\n\n![variable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/variable/variable.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**变量**指令块用于报告存储在变量中的值。使用**设定变量**指令块来设定或更新一个变量的值。\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\n**变量**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\n变量都由**定义一个变量**按钮生成。\n\n![make_variable](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# 电机转速\n\n报告VEX IQ智能电机当前转速。\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机转速**报告范围为 **-100% 到 100%** 或 **-127rpm 到 127rpm**。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\n选择**电机转速**单位为百分比（%）或转每分钟（rpm）。\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\n**电机转速**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# 视觉传感器对象\n\n报告视觉传感器检测到的一个对象信息。\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n为了使用**视觉传感器对象**指令块，使用如下步骤：\n\n1. 使用设备窗口配置你的视觉传感器。\n2. 使用**拍照**来捕捉一个视觉传感器画面并寻找某个标记/颜色编码。\n3. 使用**对象存在**来检验视觉传感器是否检测到了需要的标记/颜色编码。\n\n当视觉传感器检测到一个对象，你可以使用其他视觉传感器指令块来获取更多检测到的对象信息。\n\n* 使用**设定视觉传感器对象标号**来设定你想获取更多信息的已检测对象。默认情况下，使用检测到的最大对象。\n* 使用**对象数目**来决定需要的标记/颜色编码的对象被检测到多少个。\n* 使用**视觉传感器对象**来决定报告检测到对象的哪些信息。\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器。\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\n选择报告视觉传感器的哪一项值：\n\n* 宽度 - 对象像素有多宽，返回值范围为**2 - 316px**.\n* 高度 - 对象像素有多高，返回值范围为**2 - 212px**.\n* 中心X轴 - 报告检测到对象的中心点X轴坐标，返回值范围为**0 - 315px**.\n* 中心Y轴 - 报告检测到对象的中心点Y轴坐标，返回值范围为**0 - 211px**.\n* 角度 - 报告检测到对象的角度。返回值范围为**0 - 180度**。\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\n**视觉传感器对象**报告指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# 等待\n\n在移动到下一条指令块之前等待特定数量的时间。\n\n![wait](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/wait/wait.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择**等待**的时间数量。\n\n**等待**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![wait_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n本例将演示在**等待**3.25秒之后，VEX IQ触碰LED从红灯变为绿灯。\n\n![wait_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/wait/wait_example.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# 等到\n\n在移动到下一条指令块前，等待布尔指令块报告**真**值。\n\n![wait_until](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**等到**将重复检验布尔指令块，且不会移动到下一条指令块，直到这个布尔指令块报告**真**值。\n\n**等到**指令块可接受六角形空白指令块。\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示触碰LED亮黄灯，直到触碰LED被按下，主控器屏幕将打印“Done!”。\n\n![wait_until_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/wait_until/wait_until_example.png)\n\n\n"},"when_brain_button":{"name":"when_brain_button","markdown":"# 当主控器按键\n\n当指定的VEX IQ主控器按键被按下或松开时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_brain_button](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_brain_button/when_brain_button.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用遥控器哪一个按键。\n\n![when_brain_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select.png)\n\n选择哪一个动作将触发事件 - **按下** 或 **松开**\n\n![when_brain_button_select_2](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_brain_button/when_brain_button_select_2.png)  \n"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# 当我收到\n\n当收到指定的**广播**消息时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择接收哪一条消息。也可以生成一条新消息。\n\n**当我收到**指令块中的消息只会来自一个不同指令段中的**广播** 或 **广播并等待**指令块。\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示VEX IQ触碰LED亮红灯并等待2秒钟后，广播**message1**。\n\n当消息被收到时，**当我收到**指令段将使得底盘正向驱动且机械臂同时向上移动。\n\n如红色箭头所示，两个指令段将同时继续运行。\n\n![when_broadcast_example](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_example.png)\n\n"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# 当碰撞开关\n\n当指定的VEX IQ碰撞开关被按下或松开时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个碰撞开关。\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\n选择哪一个动作将触发事件 - **按下** 或 **松开**\n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# 当遥控器轴\n\n当指定的VEX IQ遥控器操纵杆轴移动时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用遥控器哪一个操纵杆。\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_axis/controller_button_front.jpg)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# 当遥控器按键\n\n当指定的VEX IQ遥控器按键被按下或松开时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用遥控器哪一个按键。\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_button/controller_button_front.jpg)\n\n![controller_button_back](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_button/controller_button_back.png)\n\n选择哪一个动作将触发事件 - **按下** 或 **松开**\n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# 当开始\n\n当程序开始时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_started](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**当开始**指令块可以从VEX IQ主控器菜单开始运行，也可以从VEXcode IQ Blocks **运行**按钮开始运行。\n\n所有新建程序将会自动包含一个**当开始**指令块，程序可最多支持3个**当开始**指令块。"},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# 当计时器\n\n当VEX IQ计时器大于指定值时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_timer](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n在每个程序开始时，主控器的计时器开始计时。\n\n选择时间数量。当主控器的计时器**大于**输入时间数量时，**当计时器**事件将会运行。\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\n**当计时器**指令块可接受小数或整数值。\n\n**当计时器**指令块不能接受其他指令块。"},"when_touchled":{"name":"when_touchled","markdown":"# 当触碰LED\n\n当指定的VEX IQ触碰LED被按下或松开时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_touchLED](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_touchled/when_touchled.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个触碰LED。\n\n![when_touchLED_select](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_touchled/when_touchled_select.png)\n\n选择哪一个动作将触发事件 - **按下** 或 **松开**。\n\n![when_touchLED_condition](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/when_touchled/when_touchled_condition.png)"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# 当\n\n当布尔条件报告为**真**时，重复执行内部指令段的'C'型指令块。\n\n![while](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/while/while.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**当**指令块只会在每次循环开始时检查布尔条件。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**真**，包含在**当**指令块中的指令块将运行。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**假**，包含在**当**指令块中的指令块将被跳过。\n\n**当**'C'型指令块可接受六边形指令块作为它的条件。\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/iq/blocks/zh-CN/while/while_inserted.png)"}}}};/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (data);

