var data={"en":{"blocks":{"acceleration_of":{"name":"acceleration_of","markdown":"# Acceleration of\n\nReports the acceleration value from one axis on the Analog Accelerometer.\n\n![acceleration_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Acceleration of** reports a range from **-2.0 G to 2.0 G** or **-6.0 G to 6.0 G** depending upon the jumper setting on the Analog Accelerometer.\n\nChoose which Accelerometer to use.\n\n![acceleration_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_device.png)\n\nThe reporter block **acceleration of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![acceleration_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_inserted.png)"},"activate_emergency_stop":{"name":"activate_emergency_stop","markdown":"# Activate emergency stop\n\nActivates the emergency stop (or E-stop) button for the V5 Robotic Arm.\n\n![estop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/activate_emergency_stop/estop_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe emergency stop button in the Workcell will shut off any V5 Smart Motors and Sensors connected to the V5 Brain. \n\n![estop_robot](static/help/v5/blocks/en/activate_emergency_stop/estop_robot.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_estop_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/activate_emergency_stop/select_estop_arm.png)\n\nThe **activate emergency stop** block is often used with the When bumper block from the Events category. This ensures that all V5 Smart Motors and Sensors connected to the V5 Brain will shut off once the Bumper Switch (E-stop) is pressed.\n![estop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/activate_emergency_stop/estop_example.png)"},"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Add\n\nAdds any two values together and reports the sum.\n\n![add](static/help/v5/blocks/en/add/add.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Add** can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe **add** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces, and can accept other circular blocks in it as well. \n\n\nAdd two numbers.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/en/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nAdd with values from variables.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/en/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nAdd with values from sensors or devices.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/en/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# And\n\nReports if two Boolean conditions are both true. \n\n![and](static/help/v5/blocks/en/and/and.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **and** block reports **true** when both conditions are **true**. \n\nThe **and** block reports **false** when one, or both, of the conditions are **false**.\n\nThe **and** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![and_shape](static/help/v5/blocks/en/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will check if two V5 Controller buttons are being pressed at the same time.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/en/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nThe **and** block will return **true** when both the **controller1 X button** and the **controller1 A button** are being pressed.\n\nThe **and** block will return **false** when one (or both) of the controller buttons are not pressed.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/en/and/and_truth.png)"},"angle_of":{"name":"angle_of","markdown":"# Angle of\n\nReturns the angular position of the Potentiometer.\n\n![angle_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/angle_of/angle_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Angle of** reports a range from **0% to 100%** or **0.0 to 250.0 degrees** for a V5 Potentiometer.\n\nFor a V5 Potentiometer V2, the degree range is from **0.0 to 330.0 degrees**.\n\nChoose which Potentiometer to use.\n\n![angle_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/angle_of/angle_of_device.png)\n\nChoose to report the value in % or degrees.\n\n![angle_of_block_parameters](static/help/v5/blocks/en/angle_of/angle_of_parameters.png)\n\nThe reporter block **angle of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![angle_of_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/angle_of/angle_of_inserted.png)\n"},"arm_get_joint_value":{"name":"arm_get_joint_value","markdown":"# Joint potentiometer value\n\nReports the potentiometer value of one of the four joints on the V5 Workcell.\n\n![joint_potentiometer_value](static/help/v5/blocks/en/arm_get_joint_value/joint_potentiometer_value.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **joint potentiometer value** reporter block is used to report the potentiometer value of one of the four joints on the Workcell. This reporter block can be used when determining mastering values.\n\n**Joint potentiometer value** reports a range of **0 to 4095**.\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![joint_potentiometer_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/arm_get_joint_value/joint_potentiometer_arm.png)\n\nChoose which joint to report. \n\n![joint_option_potentiometer_value](static/help/v5/blocks/en/arm_get_joint_value/joint_option_potentiometer_value.png)\n\nThe **joint potentiometer value** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![print_potentiometer_value](static/help/v5/blocks/en/arm_get_joint_value/print_potentiometer_value.png)"},"arm_get_position":{"name":"arm_get_position","markdown":"# Arm position\n\nReports the current x, y, or z-coordinate position of the arm on the Workcell.\n\n![arm_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/arm_get_position/arm_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **arm position** reporter block is used to report the current x, y, or z-coordinate position of the arm on the Workcell.\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use. \n\n![arm_position_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/arm_get_position/arm_position_arm.png)\n\nChoose which axis to report. \n\n![arm_position_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/en/arm_get_position/arm_position_axis.png)\n\nThe **arm position** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![arm_position_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/arm_get_position/arm_position_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the arm on the Workcell will move to the coordinate (6, 0, 4). Then the **print** block will print the arm's current position on the x-axis, reported from the **arm position** block, to the Console.\n\n![arm_position_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/arm_get_position/arm_position_example.png)"},"battery_current":{"name":"battery_current","markdown":"# Battery current\n\nReports the current of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\n![battery_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/battery_current/battery_current_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Battery current** reports a range from **0.0 amps to 20.0 amps**.\n\nThe reporter block **battery current** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![battery_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/battery_current/battery_current_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Battery level\n\nReports the charge level of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Battery level** reports a range from **0% to 100%**.\n\nThe reporter block **battery level** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)"},"battery_voltage":{"name":"battery_voltage","markdown":"# Battery voltage\n\nReports the voltage of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\n![battery_voltage_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Battery voltage** reports a range from **10.0 volts to 14.4 volts**.\n\nThe reporter block **battery voltage** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![battery_voltage_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_inserted.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Boolean variable\n\nReports the value of a Boolean variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Boolean variable** blocks are used to report a **true** or **false** value stored inside of the variable. Use the **set boolean variable** block to set or update the value of a boolean variable.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/v5/blocks/en/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nThe **boolean variable** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nBoolean variables are created using the **Make a Boolean** button.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"boolean_variable_virtual":{"name":"boolean_variable_virtual","markdown":"# Boolean variable\n\nReports the value of a Boolean variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Boolean variable** blocks are used to report a **true** or **false** value stored inside of the variable. Use the **set boolean variable** block to set or update the value of a boolean variable.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/v5/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nThe **boolean variable** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nBoolean variables are created using the **Make a Boolean** button.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_button.png)  \n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of a **boolean** block, select the checkbox next to its reporter block.\n\n![boolean_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the **boolean** reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![boolean_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/boolean_variable_virtual/boolean_monitor.png)\n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Break\n\nExits a repeating loop immediately.\n\n![break](static/help/v5/blocks/en/break/break.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen added to repeating 'C' block, the **break** block will exit the loop it is currently in. \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will move the Drivetrain forward and check if the V5 Brain’s screen has been pressed. \n\nIf the screen is **pressed**, the **break** block will exit the repeat forever loop and stop the Drivetrain.\n\n![break_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Brightness of\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the Light Sensor.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/v5/blocks/en/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Brightness of** reports a range from **0% to 100%**.\n\nChoose which Light Sensor to use.\n\n![brightness_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/en/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nThe reporter block **brightness of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![brightness_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Broadcast\n\nBroadcasts a message to activate any stacks that begin with a **when I receive** block listening for the broadcasted message.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/en/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe stack that sends the **broadcast** will continue to run blocks at the same time as other stacks that receive the broadcasted message.\n\nChoose which message to **broadcast**. A new message can also be created.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Broadcast and wait\n\nBroadcasts a message to activate any stacks that begin with a **when I receive** block listening for the broadcasted message while also pausing the rest of the stack.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe stack that sends the **broadcast and wait** will pause until the other stacks that receive the broadcasted message have completed.\n\nChoose which message to **broadcast**. A new message can also be created.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/v5/blocks/en/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Calibrate\n\nCalibrating the Gyro Sensor / Inertial Sensor is used to reduce the amount of drift generated by Gyro Sensor / Inertial Sensor.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nDrifting occurs when the Gyro Sensor / Inertial Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not physically moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Gyro Sensor / Inertial Sensor must remain still during the calibration process. The calibration process will take approximately 2 seconds to complete.\n\nChoose which Gyro / Inertial Sensor to use.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/en/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Change variable\n\nChanges a variable by the given value.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which variable to use - the selected variable can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nThe **Change variable** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/v5/blocks/en/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Example\nThis example will increase the variable that sets the drive velocity by 10, each time the **repeat loop** loops.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Clear all rows\n\nClears the entire Print Console, V5 Brain or Controller screen.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/v5/blocks/en/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Clear all rows** will not change the screen's (V5 Brain or Controller) cursor. Use the **set cursor** block to reset the screen's cursor to a specific position.\n\nHowever, using the **clear all rows** block with the Console option selected will reset the cursor to the top of the Print Console window.\n\nChoose which device to use. V5 Controllers will only appear if they are added in the Devices window.\n\n![clear_all_rows_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/en/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_dropdown_with_console.png)"},"clear_all_rows_virtual":{"name":"clear_all_rows_virtual","markdown":"# Clear all rows\n\nClears all the rows in the Print Console.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/v5/blocks/en/clear_all_rows_virtual/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nUse the **clear all rows** block to remove all of the lines in the Print Console.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Hello\" for one second and then clear the entire display before printing \"Goodbye\".\n\n![clear_all_rows_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/clear_all_rows_virtual/clear_all_rows_example.png)\n\n\n\n"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Clear row\n\nClears a single row on the V5 Brain or Controller screen.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/v5/blocks/en/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Clear row** block can accept integers or numeric blocks between **1 - 20**, to set which row to clear.\n\nChoose which device to use. V5 Controllers will only appear if they are added in the Devices window.\n\n![clear_row_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/en/clear_row/clear_row_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Rows\n* Small - 16 Rows\n* Medium - 12 Rows (Default)\n* Large - 8 Rows\n* Extra Large - 6 Rows\n* Super Large - 4 Rows\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/en/clear_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/clear_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Comment\n\nAllows programmers to write information to help describe their program. \n\n![comment_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nProfessional programmers use comments throughout their programs to help others understand their code. Comments can also help with troubleshooting and collaboration. \n\nAdd text into the **Comment** block by first selecting the transparent rectangle and deleting any existing text. Then, type in the new text.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Example\n\nComments do not change the program or blocks surrounding it.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Controller enabled\n\nEnables or disables Controller configured actions from the Devices menu.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose to either enable or disable the configured Controller actions by selecting the desired state from the dropdown. By default, the Controller is Enabled in every project.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThe configured action in this example is using the robot's Drivetrain behavior set by the Controller's configuration in the Devices window.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/v5/blocks/en/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nThis example will have the configured Controller disabled when the program starts. \n\nThen, the robot will drive forward for 6 inches.\n\nFinally, the **controller enabled** block will enable the Controller to restore Controller driving behaviors.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"controller_play_rumble":{"name":"controller_play_rumble","markdown":"# Controller play rumble\n\nCreates a vibrating effect on your V5 Controller.\n\n![controller_play_rumble](static/help/v5/blocks/en/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **controller play rumble** feature uses the rumble motor in your V5 controller to provide feedback.\n\nChoose which pattern to use.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_pattern](static/help/v5/blocks/en/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_pattern.png)\n\nChoose which V5 controller to use.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_device.png)\n\n\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Current of motor\n\nReports the amount of current a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group is drawing in amperes (amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Current of motor** reports a range from **0.0 to 2.5 amps**. \n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nThe reporter block **current of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Cursor column\n\nReports the column number of the V5 Brain or Controller screen cursor location.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Cursor column** reports a range from **1 to 80**.\n\nThe reporter block **cursor column** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of columns available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* Extra Small - 80 Columns\n* Small - 68 Columns\n* Medium - 48 Columns (Default)\n* Large - 32 Columns\n* Extra Large - 24 Columns\n* Super Large - 16 Columns\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/en/cursor_column/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* Standard Font - 20 Columns (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/cursor_column/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Cursor row\n\nReports the row number of the V5 Brain or Controller screen cursor location.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Cursor row** reports a range from **1 to 20**.\n\nThe reporter block **cursor row** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Rows\n* Small - 16 Rows\n* Medium - 12 Rows (Default)\n* Large - 8 Rows\n* Extra Large - 6 Rows\n* Super Large - 4 Rows\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/en/cursor_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/cursor_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"digital_in_signal":{"name":"digital_in_signal","markdown":"# Digital in\n\nReports if the digital in signal is high.\n\n![digital_in_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/digital_in_signal/digital_in_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 3-Wire ports function at a 5V logic signal voltage level.\n\nThe **digital in** block reports **true** when the digital input signal is high.\n\nThe **digital in** block reports **false** when the digital input signal is low.\n\nChoose which digital in device to use. \n\n![digital_in_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/digital_in_signal/digital_in_select.png)\n\nThe **digital in** Boolean block reports a true or false value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![digital_in_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/en/digital_in_signal/digital_in_insert.png)\n"},"distance_found_object":{"name":"distance_found_object","markdown":"# Distance object found\n\nReports if the Distance sensor sees an object within its field of view.\n\n![distance_found_object_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block1.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Distance object found** reports true when the Distance sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n**Distance object found** reports false when the Distance sensor does not detect an object or surface.\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_found_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block2.png)\n\n\nThe **distance object found** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![distance_found_object_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block3.png)\n"},"distance_found_object_virtual":{"name":"distance_found_object_virtual","markdown":"# Distance found an object\n\nReports if the Distance sensor sees an object within its field of view.\n\n![distance_found_object_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_found_object_virtual/distance_found_object_block1.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Distance found an object** reports true when the Distance sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n**Distance found an object** reports false when the Distance sensor does not detect an object or surface.\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_found_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_found_object_virtual/distance_found_object_block2.png)\n\n\nThe **Distance found an object** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![distance_found_object_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_found_object_virtual/distance_found_object_block3.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Distance found an object** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![distance_found_object_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_found_object_virtual/distance_found_object_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![distance_found_object_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_found_object_virtual/distance_found_object_monitor.png)"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Distance from\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Distance from** reports a range from **30mm to 3000mm** or **2 inches to 115 inches**.\n\nChoose which Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor to use.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nChoose whether **distance from** is reported in inches or millimeters. \n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **distance from** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"distance_object_distance":{"name":"distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Object distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the Distance sensor.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object distance** reports a range from **20mm to 2000mm**.\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether **object distance** is reported in inches or millimeters. \n\n![distance_object_distance_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block **object distance** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block4.png)\n"},"distance_object_distance_virtual":{"name":"distance_object_distance_virtual","markdown":"# Object distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the Distance sensor.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_distance_virtual/distance_object_distance_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object distance** reports a range from **20mm to 2000mm**.\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_distance_virtual/distance_object_distance_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether **Object distance** is reported in inches or millimeters. \n\n![distance_object_distance_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_distance_virtual/distance_object_distance_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Object distance** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_distance_virtual/distance_object_distance_block4.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Object distance** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![distance_object_distance_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_distance_virtual/distance_object_distance_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![distance_object_distance_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_distance_virtual/distance_object_distance_monitor.png)"},"distance_object_size":{"name":"distance_object_size","markdown":"# Object size is\n\nReports if the Distance Sensor detects the specified object size.  \n\n![distance_object_size_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe sensor determines the size of the object detected (none, small, medium, large) based on the amount of light reflected and returned to the sensor.\n\nChoose a Distance Sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_size_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block1.png)\n\nChoose which size of the object you want the sensor to check for.\n\n![distance_object_size_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block2.png)\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **true** when the Distance Sensor detects the specified size.\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **false** if it doesn't detect the specified size.\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![distance_object_size_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block3.png)\n"},"distance_object_velocity":{"name":"distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Object velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of an object in m/s.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object velocity** reports the current velocity of an object in m/s (meters per second).\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block2.png)\n\n\nThe reporter block **object velocity** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block3.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Divide\n\nDivides the first value by the second value and reports the dividend.\n\n![divide](static/help/v5/blocks/en/divide/divide.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Divide** can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe report block **divide** fits in blocks that accept circular spaces, and can accept circular blocks in it as well. \n\nEnter numbers to be divided.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/en/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nDivide with values of variables.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/en/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nDivide with values from sensors or devices.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/en/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"draw_circle":{"name":"draw_circle","markdown":"# Draw circle\n\nDraws a circle on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n![draw_circle](static/help/v5/blocks/en/draw_circle/draw_circle.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **draw circle** block requires 3 values:\n\n* Value 1: Center Point X\n* Value 2: Center Point Y\n* Value 3: Radius of Circle (in pixels)\n\nThe outside line color of the circle is determined by the **set pen color** block. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the circle is determine by the **set fill color** block. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/en/draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"draw_line":{"name":"draw_line","markdown":"# Draw line\n\nDraws a line on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n![draw_line](static/help/v5/blocks/en/draw_line/draw_line.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **draw line** block requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Beginning X coordinate\n* Value 2: Beginning Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Ending X coordinate\n* Value 4: Ending Y coordinate\n\nThe line color is determined by the **set pen color** block. The default line color is white.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/en/draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_pixel":{"name":"draw_pixel","markdown":"# Draw pixel\n\nDraws a pixel on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n![draw_pixel](static/help/v5/blocks/en/draw_pixel/draw_pixel.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **draw pixel** block requires 2 values:\n\n* Value 1: X Coodinate\n* Value 2: Y Coodinate\n\nThe pixel color is determined by the **set pen color** block. The default pixel color is white.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/en/draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_rectangle":{"name":"draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Draw rectangle\n\nDraws a rectangle on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n![draw_rectangle](static/help/v5/blocks/en/draw_rectangle/draw_rectangle.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **draw rectangle** block requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Top Left Corner X coordinate\n* Value 2: Top Left Corner Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Width of the rectangle\n* Value 4: Height of the rectangle\n\nThe outside line color of the rectangle is determined by the **set pen color** block. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the rectangle is determine by the **set fill color** block. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/en/draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Drive\n\nMoves the Drivetrain forever.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **drive** block will run the Drivetrain forever, until a new Drivetrain block is used, or the program is stopped.\n\nChoose the direction the Drivetrain will move.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Drive current\n\nReports the amount of current (power) that the Drivetrain is currently using.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive current** reports a range from **0.0 to 2.5 amps**. \n\nThe reporter block **drive current** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_efficiency":{"name":"drive_efficiency","markdown":"# Drive efficiency\n\nReports the efficiency of the Drivetrain.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive efficiency** reports the value of the power (in watts) the motor is using (input), versus the amount of power (in watts) the motor is providing (output). \n\nA V5 Drivetrain typically reaches a maximum efficiency of 65% under normal use cases.\n\n**Drive efficiency** reports a range from **0% to 100%**. \n\nThe report block **drive efficiency** fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\n![drive_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Drive for\n\nMoves the Drivetrain for a given distance.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which direction the Drivetrain will move.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\n\nSet how far the Drivetrain will move by entering a value, and choosing the unit of measurement (inches or millimeters).\n\nThe **Drive for** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Drivetrain is done moving.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Drivetrain moves.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Drive heading\n\nReports the direction that the Drivetrain is facing by using the Gyroscopic (Gyro) sensor's current angular position.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe reporter block **drive heading** reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n**Drive heading** reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**.\n\nThe reporter block **drive heading** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_heading_virtual":{"name":"drive_heading_virtual","markdown":"# Drive heading\n\nReports the direction that the Drivetrain is facing by using the Gyroscopic (Gyro) sensor's current angular position.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_heading_virtual/drive_heading.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe reporter block **Drive heading** reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n**Drive heading** reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**.\n\nThe reporter block **Drive heading** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_heading_virtual/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Drive heading** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![drive_heading_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_heading_virtual/drive_heading_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![drive_heading_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_heading_virtual/drive_heading_monitor.png)"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Drive is done\n\nReports if the Drivetrain has completed its movement.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive is done** reports **true** when the Drivetrain's motors have completed their movement.\n\n**Drive is done** reports **false** when the Drivetrain's motors are still moving.\n\nThe **drive is done** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done_virtual":{"name":"drive_is_done_virtual","markdown":"# Drive is done\n\nReports if the Drivetrain has completed its movement.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_done_virtual/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive is done** reports **true** when the Drivetrain's motors have completed their movement.\n\n**Drive is done** reports **false** when the Drivetrain's motors are still moving.\n\nThe **Drive is done** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_done_virtual/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Drive is done** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![drive_is_done_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_done_virtual/drive_is_done_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![drive_is_done_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_done_virtual/drive_is_done_monitor.png)"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Drive is moving\n\nReports if the Drivetrain is currently moving.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive is moving** reports **true** when the Drivetrain's motors are moving.\n\n**Drive is moving** reports **false** when the Drivetrain's motors are stopped.\n\nThe **drive is moving** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving_virtual":{"name":"drive_is_moving_virtual","markdown":"# Drive is moving\n\nReports if the Drivetrain is currently moving.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_moving_virtual/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive is moving** reports **true** when the Drivetrain's motors are moving.\n\n**Drive is moving** reports **false** when the Drivetrain's motors are stopped.\n\nThe **Drive is moving** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_moving_virtual/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Drive is moving** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![drive_is_moving_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_moving_virtual/drive_is_moving_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![drive_is_moving_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_is_moving_virtual/drive_is_moving_monitor.png)"},"drive_power":{"name":"drive_power","markdown":"# Drive power\n\nReports the amount of power output the Drivetrain is currently generating.\n\n![drive_power](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_power/drive_power.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive power** reports a range from **0.0 to 22.0 watts**. \n\nThe reporter block **drive power** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_power/drive_power_inserted.png)"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Drive rotation\n\nReports the Drivetrain's angle of rotation when configured with a 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor.\n\n![drive_rotation](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_rotation/drive_rotation.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive rotation** reports a **positive** value when the Drivetrain turns in a **clockwise** direction.\n\n**Drive rotation** reports a **negative** value when the Drivetrain turns in a **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\nThe reporter block **drive rotation** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_rotation_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_rotation/drive_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_rotation_virtual":{"name":"drive_rotation_virtual","markdown":"# Drive rotation\n\nReports the Drivetrain's angle of rotation when configured with a 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor.\n\n![drive_rotation](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_rotation_virtual/drive_rotation.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive rotation** reports a **positive** value when the Drivetrain turns in a **clockwise** direction.\n\n**Drive rotation** reports a **negative** value when the Drivetrain turns in a **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\nThe reporter block **Drive rotation** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_rotation_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_rotation_virtual/drive_rotation_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Drive rotation** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![drive_rotation_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_rotation_virtual/drive_rotation_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![drive_rotation_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_rotation_virtual/drive_rotation_monitor.png)"},"drive_temperature":{"name":"drive_temperature","markdown":"# Drive temperature\n\nReports the temperature of the V5 Smart Motors powering the Drivetrain.\n\n![drive_temperature](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_temperature/drive_temperature.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive temperature** reports a range from **0% to 100%**. \n\nThe reporter block **drive temperature** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_temperature_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_temperature/drive_temperature_inserted.png)"},"drive_torque":{"name":"drive_torque","markdown":"# Drive torque\n\nReports the amount of torque (rotational force) the Drivetrain is currently using.\n\n![drive_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_torque/drive_torque.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Drive torque** reports a range from **0.0 to 18.6 inch-pounds (InLB)** or **0.0 to 2.1 Newton-meters (Nm)**. \n\nChoose whether the **drive torque** is reported in inch-pounds (InLb) or Newton-meters (Nm).\n\n![drive_torque_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_torque/drive_torque_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **drive torque** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_torque/drive_torque_inserted.png)"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Drive velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\n**Drive velocity** reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-600rpm to 600rpm**.\n\n**Drive velocity** will report a \"rotations per minute\" range based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in % or in revolutions per minute (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **drive velocity** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"drive_velocity_virtual":{"name":"drive_velocity_virtual","markdown":"# Drive velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_velocity_virtual/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\n**Drive velocity** reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-600rpm to 600rpm**.\n\n**Drive velocity** will report a \"rotations per minute\" range based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in % or in revolutions per minute (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_velocity_virtual/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Drive velocity** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_velocity_virtual/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Drive velocity** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![drive_velocity_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_velocity_virtual/drive_velocity_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![drive_velocity_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/drive_velocity_virtual/drive_velocity_monitor.png)\n"},"duration":{"name":"duration","markdown":"# Set electromagnet duration\n\nSets how long the V5 Electromagnet is turned on for.\n\n![set_duration_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/duration/set_duration_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nSelect to set how long the electromagnet is powered on for a boost:\n\n* **short** - powers the electromagnet for **250ms**\n* **medium** - powers the electromagnet for **500ms**\n* **long** - powers the electromagnet for **1000ms**\n\n![set_duration_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/en/duration/set_duration_block_setting.png)\n\nChoose which electromagnet to use.\n\n![set_duration_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/en/duration/set_duration_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will tell the robot to drive forward 200mm, use the **set electromagnet duration** block to set the duration to **long**, then the **Electromagnet** will boost to pick up an object, drive forward 200mm, then drop the object.\n\n![set_duration_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/duration/set_duration_example.png)\n"},"efficiency_of_motor":{"name":"efficiency_of_motor","markdown":"# Efficiency of motor\n\nReports the efficiency of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/en/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Efficiency of motor** reports the value of the power (in watts) the motor is using (input), versus the amount of power (in watts) the motor is providing (output). \n\nA V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group typically reaches a maximum efficiency of 65% under normal use cases.\n\n**Efficiency of motor** reports a range from **0% to 100%**. \n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![motor_efficiency_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_device.png)\n\nThe report block **Efficiency of motor** fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\n![motor_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_inserted.png)"},"enable_manual_movement":{"name":"enable_manual_movement","markdown":"# Set manual movement\n\nAllows the arm of the V5 Workcell to be manually moved by hand.\n\n![set_manual_movement](static/help/v5/blocks/en/enable_manual_movement/set_manual_movement.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, the motors on the Workcell lock in place when a project is running. To be able to manually move the arm, use the **set manual movement** block in your project.\n\n![movement](static/help/v5/blocks/en/enable_manual_movement/movement.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![set_manual_movement_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/enable_manual_movement/set_manual_movement_arm.png)"},"energize":{"name":"energize","markdown":"# Energize electromagnet\n\nSets the V5 Electromagnet to two different modes: **boost** or **drop**.\n\n![set_magnet_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/energize/set_magnet_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nSelect to set that electromagnet to boost or drop\n\n* **boost** - turns on the electromagnet for as long as the duration was set\n* **drop** - releases any object the electromagnet is holding\n\nAfter energizing the magnet, the magnet will need to cool down before it can be energized again.\n\n\n![set_magnet_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/en/energize/set_magnet_block_setting.png)\n\nChoose which electromagnet to use.\n\n![set_magnet_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/en/energize/set_magnet_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the robot to drive forward 200mm, **Electromagnet** will boost to pick up an object, drive forward 200mm, then drop the object.\n\n![set_magnet_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/energize/set_magnet_example.png)\n"},"enter_mastering_mode":{"name":"enter_mastering_mode","markdown":"# Start mastering process\n\nStarts the mastering process for the four joints of the  arm on the Workcell to allow it to be calibrated to the same known location.\n\n![start_mastering_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/enter_mastering_mode/start_mastering_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **start mastering process** block begins the mastering process for the arm on the V5 Workcell. \n\nThis block is used in the 'Arm Mastering' example project."},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Equal to\n\nReports if the first value is the same as, or equal to, the second value. \n\n![equal_to](static/help/v5/blocks/en/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Equal to** reports **true** when the two values are exactly the same.\n\n**Equal to** reports **false** when the two values are not the same.\n\nThe **equal to** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe **equal to** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Forever\n\nA 'C' block that repeats any blocks contained inside forever.\n\n![forever](static/help/v5/blocks/en/forever/forever.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nPlace blocks in a **forever** 'C' block to have those actions repeat **forever**.\n\nYou can exit a **forever** loop by placing a **break** block inside.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\n'C' blocks can also be put inside of each other. This concept is called nesting which can help save time when programming different behaviors."},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Function\n\nPerforms a selected math function.\n\n![function](static/help/v5/blocks/en/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - absolute value\n* **floor** - rounds down to the nearest integer\n* **ceiling** - rounds up to the nearest integer\n* **sqrt** - square root\n* **sin** - sine\n* **cos** - cosine\n* **tan** - tangent\n* **asin** - arcsine or the inverse of sine\n* **acos** - arccosine or the inverse of cosine\n* **atan** - arctan or the inverse of tangent\n* **ln** - the natural logarithm base e\n* **log** - logarithm base 10\n* **e ^** - powers of e\n* **10 ^** - powers of 10\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **function** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose the math **function** from a list of options.\n\n![function_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/function/function_select.png)\n\nThe **function** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\n![function_fit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"gps_acceleration":{"name":"gps_acceleration","markdown":"# GPS acceleration\n\nReports the acceleration value of the specified axis on a GPS Sensor.\n\n![gps_acceleration_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_acceleration/gps_acceleration_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**GPS acceleration** reports a range of values from **-4.0 to 4.0** Gs.\n\nSelect the axis to read values from:\n\n* The **X** axis reports acceleration of the GPS Sensor's **forward and backward** rotations\n\n* The **Y** axis reports acceleration of the GPS Sensor's **left and right** rotations\n\n* The **Z** axis reports acceleration of the GPS Sensor's **up and down** movements\n\n![gps_acceleration_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_acceleration/gps_acceleration_block2.png)\n\nThe **GPS acceleration** block can also be used inside blocks with circular inputs.\n\n![gps_acceleration_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_acceleration/gps_acceleration_block3.png)\n\n"},"gps_calibrate":{"name":"gps_calibrate","markdown":"# GPS calibrate\n\nStarts the calibration process for a GPS Sensor.\n\n![gps_calibrate_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_calibrate/gps_calibrate_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe GPS Sensor must remain still during the calibration process.\n\nChoose a GPS Sensor to calibrate.\n\n![gps_calibrate_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_calibrate/gps_calibrate_block2.png)"},"gps_gyro_rate":{"name":"gps_gyro_rate","markdown":"# GPS gyro rate\n\nReports the rate of rotation from the specified axis on a GPS Sensor.\n\n![gps_gyro_rate_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_gyro_rate/gps_gyro_rate_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nSelect the axis to get rate of rotation from:\n\n* The **X** axis reports rate of rotation when a GPS Sensor rotates in the X-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n* The **Y** axis reports rate of rotation when a GPS Sensor rotates in the Y-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n* The **Z** axis reports rate of rotation when a GPS Sensor rotates in the Z-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n![gps_gyro_rate_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_gyro_rate/gps_gyro_rate_block2.png)\n\n**GPS gyro rate** can report values in either dps (degrees per second) or rpm (revolutions per minute).\n\nThe range of values reported is **-1000** to **1000** for dps, and **-167** to **167** for rpm.\n\n![gps_gyro_rate_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_gyro_rate/gps_gyro_rate_block3.png)\n\nThe **GPS gyro rate** reporter block is used inside blocks with circular inputs.\n\n![gps_gyro_rate_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_gyro_rate/gps_gyro_rate_block4.png)\n"},"gps_heading":{"name":"gps_heading","markdown":"# GPS heading\n\nReports the heading that a robot is currently facing based on a GPS Sensor's readings from the VEX GPS Field Code.\n\n![gps_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_heading/gps_heading_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **GPS heading** reporter block reports an increase in heading when a GPS Sensor rotates clockwise.\n\n**GPS heading** reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**.\n\nUsually, a GPS Sensor should be mounted facing behind a robot. In the GPS configuration, the Angle Offset is set to **180** degrees. \n\nThen, for example, if the GPS Sensor is facing the South wall as defined by the VEX GPS Field Code, the reported heading will be **0.00** degrees, which is the heading that the front of the robot is facing.\n\nHowever, a GPS Sensor can also be mounted facing other directions (e.g. the front of a robot).\n\nIn this situation, for example, the GPS Sensor's Angle Offset configuration would then need to be set to **0** degrees, which is the angular difference between the forward heading of the robot, and the heading that the GPS is facing. This way, the reported heading value will shift correctly in line with a robot's headings as it turns.\n\nIt can be used inside blocks with circular inputs.\n\n![gps_heading_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_heading/gps_heading_block2.png)\n\n"},"gps_heading_virtual":{"name":"gps_heading_virtual","markdown":"# GPS heading\n\nReports the heading that a robot is currently facing based on a GPS Sensor's readings from the VEX GPS Field Code.\n\n![gps_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_heading_virtual/gps_heading_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **GPS heading** reporter block reports an increase in heading when a GPS Sensor rotates clockwise.\n\n**GPS heading** reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**.\n\nBy default, a GPS Sensor should be mounted facing behind a robot. Then, for example, if the GPS Sensor is facing the South wall as defined by the VEX GPS Field Code, the reported heading will be **0.00** degrees, which is the heading that the front of the robot is facing.\n\nHowever, a GPS Sensor can also be mounted facing other directions (e.g. in front of a robot).\n\nIn this situation, for example, the GPS Sensor's Angle Offset configuration would then either need to be set to **180.00** or **-180.00** degrees, which is the angular difference between the default orientation (facing behind) and the selected orientation (facing forward). This way, the reported heading value will shift correctly in line with a robot's headings as it turns.\n\nIt can be used inside blocks with circular inputs.\n\n![gps_heading_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_heading_virtual/gps_heading_block2.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **GPS heading** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![gps_heading_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_heading_virtual/gps_heading_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![gps_heading_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_heading_virtual/gps_heading_monitor.png)"},"gps_orientation":{"name":"gps_orientation","markdown":"# GPS orientation\n\nReports the angle of the specified orientation axis on a GPS Sensor.\n\n![gps_orientation_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_orientation/gps_orientation_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe orientation reported is determined by the specified orientation axis.\n\n* The **roll** axis reports a value between **-180 to +180** degrees, representing the angle of a GPS Sensor when tilted left or right\n\n* The **pitch** axis reports a value between **-90 to +90** degrees, representing the angle of a GPS Sensor when tilted forward or backwards\n\n* The **yaw** axis reports a value between **-180 to +180** degrees, representing the angle of a GPS Sensor when rotated about the vertical axis\n\n![gps_orientation_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_orientation/gps_orientation_block2.png)\n\nThe **GPS orientation** reporter block can also be used in blocks with circular inputs.\n\n![gps_orientation_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_orientation/gps_orientation_block3.png)\n"},"gps_position":{"name":"gps_position","markdown":"# GPS position\n\nReports the positional offset of a GPS Sensor or a defined reference point from the center of a field.\n\n![gps_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_position/gps_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **GPS position** reporter block reports either the X or Y axis offset of a GPS Sensor or a defined reference point from the center of a field.\n\n![gps_position_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_position/gps_position_block2.png)\n\nBy default, the **GPS position** reporter block will report the offset of a GPS Sensor, but a different reference point can be set in a GPS Sensor's configuration such that the offset reported is relative to the reference point.\n\nIf a GPS Sensor is not mounted at the turning reference point of a robot (the axis around which a robot turns), the X and Y offset settings can be adjusted in the GPS Sensor's configuration so that reported values from the **GPS position** block will not change the robot is turning in-place.\n\nTo calculate the X and Y offset settings, measure the distance from the reference point to the mounted position of a GPS Sensor, and filling in the X and Y offset settings in the GPS Sensor's configuration, respectively.\n\nThe block can report offset values in mm or inches.\n\n![gps_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_position/gps_position_block3.png)\n\nIt can also be used inside blocks with circular inputs.\n\n![gps_position_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_position/gps_position_block4.png)"},"gps_position_virtual":{"name":"gps_position_virtual","markdown":"# GPS position\n\nReports the positional offset of the robot's turning reference point from the center of a field.\n\n![gps_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_position_virtual/gps_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **GPS position** reporter block reports either the X or Y axis offset of the robot's turning reference point from the center of a field.\n\n![gps_position_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_position_virtual/gps_position_block2.png)\n\nThe block can report offset values in mm or inches.\n\n![gps_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_position_virtual/gps_position_block3.png)\n\nIt can also be used inside blocks with circular inputs.\n\n![gps_position_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_position_virtual/gps_position_block4.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **GPS position** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![gps_position_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_position_virtual/gps_position_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![gps_position_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_position_virtual/gps_position_monitor.png)"},"gps_set_location":{"name":"gps_set_location","markdown":"# GPS set location\n\nSets the location for a GPS Sensor to a defined positional value.\n\n![gps_set_location_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_set_location/gps_set_location_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen a GPS Sensor is too close to the field walls to read accurate data (for example, when a robot is in a game's starting position on a field), unexpected behaviors can often occur if the program relies on the GPS's positional and heading data to work correctly.\n\nThe **GPS set location** block can be used to set the location and heading of a GPS Sensor if this information is known before the program is ran, which may help reduce GPS data inaccuracies due a GPS Sensor's proximity to the field walls when a program is started.\n\nThe first two numerical inputs are the X and Y offsets of the GPS Sensor, or a defined origin point on a robot relative to the center of a field. The X and Y offsets can be passed as either **mm** or **inches** units.\n\nThe last numerical input is the heading of the robot in its defined position. For example, if the GPS Sensor is mounted facing behind a robot and the robot is facing the West wall (heading of 270), the heading value that should be passed is 270.\n\nChoose a GPS Sensor to set location on.\n\n![gps_set_location_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_set_location/gps_set_location_block2.png)\n\nChoose which positional unit to use.\n\n![gps_set_location_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_set_location/gps_set_location_block3.png)"},"gps_signal_quality":{"name":"gps_signal_quality","markdown":"# GPS signal quality\n\nReports a GPS Sensor's current signal quality.\n\n![gps_signal_quality_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_signal_quality/gps_signal_quality_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **GPS signal quality** reporter block reports a numerical percentage value representing the current signal quality of a GPS Sensor.\n\nWhen the reported value is 100, it means that all reported positional and heading data from a GPS Sensor is valid.\n\nHowever, a reported value of 90 signals that any positional data is no longer being calculated by capturing information from the VEX Field Code, but rather through alternative means.\n\nAt 80, only GPS Sensor heading values are valid, but as more time goes by where a GPS Sensor is not scanning enough of the VEX Field Code to accurately determine position and heading information, the reported signal quality will continue to drop until 0, where any GPS Sensor data is effectively frozen and no longer valid.\n\nIt can also be used inside blocks with circular inputs.\n\n![gps_signal_quality_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/gps_signal_quality/gps_signal_quality_block2.png)"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Greater than\n\nReports if the first value is larger (greater) than the second value.  \n\n![greater_than](static/help/v5/blocks/en/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Greater than** reports **true** when the first value is larger than the second value. \n\n**Greater than** reports **false** when the first value is smaller than or equal to the second value.\n\nThe **greater than** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe **greater than** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Angle of heading\n\nReports the 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/en/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe reporter block **heading of** reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n**Heading of** reports a range between **0.00 to 359.99**.\n\nChoose which Gyro Sensor / Inertial Sensor to check.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/en/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nThe **heading of** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"if_elseif_else":{"name":"if_elseif_else","markdown":"# If then else if then else\n\nA 'C' Block that runs the blocks inside the first set of internal blocks in the **if then else if then else** block where the condition returns true.\n\n![if_elseif_else](static/help/v5/blocks/en/if_elseif_else/if_elseif_else.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **if then else if then else** 'C' Block will only check the Boolean condition once. \n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **true** on the **if** line, the blocks inside of **if** section will be run.\n\nIf the Boolean condition is **false**, the **if then else if then else** block will check the first of the **else if** lines. For each **else if** line, the block will check if the Boolean condition is reported as **true**. If it is **true**, the internal blocks directly under that line will run before continuing on to the next block under the **if then else if then else** block.\n\nIf all the Boolean conditions for the **else if** lines are **false**, the blocks inside of **else** section will be run.\n\nThe **if then else if then else** 'C' block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks for its conditions.\n\n![if_elseif_else_2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/if_elseif_else/if_elseif_else_2.png)\n\n## How to Add and Remove Conditions\n\nThe **if then else if then else** block is unique amongst the conditional blocks in that you can add additional conditional statements. The block allows for 6 **else if** conditions.\n\n![if_elseif_else_expanded](static/help/v5/blocks/en/if_elseif_else/if_elseif_else_expanded.png)\n\nTo add another **else if** condition, click on the \"+\" on the **else** line. This will add a new **else if** condition to the bottom of the current list.\n\nTo remove an **else if** condition, click on the \"-\" on the **else** line. This will remove the last **else if** condition line, but will not delete the blocks in the condition.\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# If then\n\nA 'C' Block that runs the blocks inside, if the Boolean condition is reported to be **true**.  \n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/en/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **if then** 'C' block will only check the Boolean condition once. \n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **true**, the blocks inside of **if then** will run.\n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **false**, the blocks inside of **if then** will be skipped.\n\nThe **if then** 'C' block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks as its condition.\n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/en/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# If then else\n\nA 'C' Block that runs the blocks inside the first or second parts of the **if then else**, based on the Boolean value reported.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/en/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **if then else** 'C' Block will only check the Boolean condition once. \n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **true**, the blocks inside of **if** section will be run.\n\nIf the Boolean condition is **false**, the blocks inside of **else** section will be run.\n\nThe **if then else** 'C' block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks as its condition.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/en/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)"},"inertial_acceleration":{"name":"inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Acceleration of\n\nReports the acceleration value from one of the axes (x, y, or z) on the Intertial Sensor.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n**Acceleration of** reports a range from **-4.0 to 4.0** Gs. \n\nChoose which Inertial Sensor to use.\n\n![inertial_acceleration_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_device.png)\n\nChoose which axis to use:\n\n* The **X-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **forward to backward**\n* The **Y-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **side to side**\n* The **Z-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **up to down**\n\n![inertial_acceleration_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_axis.png)\n\nThe sensing block **acceleration of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_gyrorate":{"name":"inertial_gyrorate","markdown":"# Gyro rate\n\nGets the rate of rotation from one of the axes (x, y, or z) on the Inertial Sensor.\n\n![gyro_rate_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_gyrorate/gyro_rate_block.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\n**Gyro rate** reports a range from **-1000.0 to 1000.0** in dps (degrees per second). \n\nChoose which Inertial Sensor to use.\n\n![gyroRate_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_included_block.png)\n\nChoose which axis to use.\n\n* The **X-axis** reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the X-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* The **Y-axis** reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Y-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* The **Z-axis** reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Z-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n![gyroRate_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_axis.png)\n\nThe sensing block **gyro rate** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_orientation":{"name":"inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Orientation of\n\nGets an orientation angle of the inertial sensor. Reports the unit value specified by the parameter of the inertial sensor.\n\n![orientation_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/orientation_inertial_block.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\nThe orientation reported is determined by the selected axis (x, y, or z).\n\n* The **X-axis** represents **pitch**, which reports a value between -90 to +90 degrees.\n* The **Y-axis** represents **roll**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n* The **Z-axis** represents **yaw**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n\n---\n\n**Pitch** is the angle of the robot tilted forwards and backwards.\n\n![V5_Pitch_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/V5_Pitch_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Roll** is the angle of the robot tilted left and right.\n\n![V5_Roll_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/V5_Roll_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Yaw** is angular rotation of the robot.\n\n![V5_Yaw_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/V5_Yaw_rev2.jpg)\n\n---\n\nChoose which Inertial Sensor to use.\n\n![orientation_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/orientation_included_block.png)\n\nChoose which axis to use.\n\n![orientation_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/orientation_axis.png)\n\nThe sensing block **orientation of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![orientation_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/inertial_orientation/orientation_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n\n"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Item of 2D list\n\nReports the value of an item in a 2D list. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which 2D list to use. The 2D list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nEnter the item's row (first number) and column (second number) position within the list to be reported. Here, the item in position row 2, column 3 in the 2D list is being reported.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nThe **item of 2D list** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_2d_array_virtual":{"name":"item_of_2d_array_virtual","markdown":"# Item of 2D list\n\nReports the value of an item in a 2D list. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which 2D list to use. The 2D list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nEnter the item's row (first number) and column (second number) position within the list to be reported. Here, the item in position row 2, column 3 in the 2D list is being reported.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nThe **item of 2D list** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of a 2D list, open the Monitor Console and click the 'Add Lists' button on the bottom right corner.\n\n![array_monitor_add](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/array_monitor_add.png)\n\nThen, select the checkbox for the 2D list that should be added. Multiple checkboxes can be selected if more than one 2D list is defined. Click 'Save' to add the list(s) to the Monitor Console.\n\n![array_monitor_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/array_monitor_select.png)\n\n Return to the Monitor Console to view the 2D list(s) selected for monitoring.\n\n![array_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_2d_array_virtual/array_monitor.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Item of\n\nReports the value of an item in a list. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nEnter the number of the item's position within the list. Here, the second item in list (item 2) is being reported. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nThe **item of** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the Drivetrain velocity to the value stored in item 3 of my list. The Drivetrain will now move forward at a 90% velocity.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"item_of_array_virtual":{"name":"item_of_array_virtual","markdown":"# Item of\n\nReports the value of an item in a list. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/item_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/item_of_options.png)\n\nEnter the number of the item's position within the list. Here, the second item in list (item 2) is being reported. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nThe **item of** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the Drivetrain velocity to the value stored in item 3 of my list. The Drivetrain will now move forward at a 90% velocity.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/item_of_example2.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of a list, open the Monitor Console and click the 'Add Lists' button on the bottom right corner.\n\n![array_monitor_add](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/array_monitor_add.png)\n\nThen, select the checkbox for the list that should be added. Multiple checkboxes can be selected if more than one list is defined. Click 'Save' to add the list(s) to the Monitor Console.\n\n![array_monitor_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/array_monitor_select.png)\n\nReturn to the Monitor Console to view the list(s) selected for monitoring.\n\n![array_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/item_of_array_virtual/array_monitor.png)"},"joint_move":{"name":"joint_move","markdown":"# Joint move\n\nMoves the V5 Robotic Arm to the specified (x, y, z) coordinate using joint movement.\n\n![joint_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/joint_move/joint_move_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **joint move** block moves the V5 Robotic Arm in the x, y, and z-direction using joint movement. \n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/en/joint_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_joint_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/joint_move/select_joint_arm.png)\n\nThe **joint move** block accepts decimals, integers, and numeric blocks.\n\n![joint_input](static/help/v5/blocks/en/joint_move/joint_input.png)"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Length of 2D list\n\nReports the number of rows or columns in a 2D list.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/en/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\nChoose which 2D list to use. The 2D list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nChoose which value to report. The 2D list can report either **rows** or **columns**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nThe **length of 2D list** reporter block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Less than\n\nReports if the first value is less (smaller) than the second value. \n\n![less_than](static/help/v5/blocks/en/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Less than** reports **true** when the first value is smaller than the second value. \n\n**Less than** reports **false** when the first value is greater than or equal to the second value.\n\nThe **less than** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\nThe **less than** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n"},"linear_move":{"name":"linear_move","markdown":"# Linear move\n\nMoves the V5 Robotic Arm to the specified (x, y, z) coordinate using linear movement.\n\n![linear_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/linear_move/linear_move_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **linear move** block moves the V5 Robotic Arm in the x, y, and z-direction using linear movement. \n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/en/linear_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_linear_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/linear_move/select_linear_arm.png)\n\nThe **linear move** block accepts decimals, integers, and numeric blocks.\n\n![linear_input](static/help/v5/blocks/en/linear_move/linear_input.png)"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor is done\n\nReports if the selected V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Motor is done** reports **true** when the selected Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n**Motor is done** reports **false** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is still moving.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nThe **motor is done** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"motor_is_done_virtual":{"name":"motor_is_done_virtual","markdown":"# Motor is done\n\nReports if the selected V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_done_virtual/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Motor is done** reports **true** when the selected Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n**Motor is done** reports **false** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is still moving.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_done_virtual/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nThe **Motor is done** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_done_virtual/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Motor is done** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![motor_is_done_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_done_virtual/motor_is_done_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![motor_is_done_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_done_virtual/motor_is_done_monitor.png)"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor is spinning\n\nReports if the selected V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently spinning.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Motor is spinning** reports **true** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is spinning.\n\n**Motor is spinning** reports **false** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is stopped.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nThe **motor is spinning** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"motor_is_spinning_virtual":{"name":"motor_is_spinning_virtual","markdown":"# Motor is spinning\n\nReports if the selected V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently spinning.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning_virtual/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Motor is spinning** reports **true** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is spinning.\n\n**Motor is spinning** reports **false** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is stopped.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning_virtual/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nThe **Motor is spinning** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning_virtual/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Motor is spinning** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning_virtual/motor_is_spinning_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/motor_is_spinning_virtual/motor_is_spinning_monitor.png)"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Multiply\n\nMultiplies any two values together and reports the product.\n\n![multiply](static/help/v5/blocks/en/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Multiply** can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe  **multiply** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces, and can accept circular blocks in it as well. \n\nMultiply two numbers.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/en/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nMultiply with values of variables.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/en/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nMultiply with values from sensors or devices.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/en/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Next row\n\nSets the print output cursor on the Print Console, V5 Brain or Controller screen to the next available row.\n\n![next_row](static/help/v5/blocks/en/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1. The **next row** block will move the cursor down by a single row on the screen. **Next row** will also set the cursor's column to position 1.\n\nChoose which device to use. V5 Controllers will only appear if they are added in the Devices window.\n\n![next_row_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/en/next_row/next_row_dropdown_with_console.png)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Rows\n* Small - 16 Rows\n* Medium - 12 Rows (Default)\n* Large - 8 Rows\n* Extra Large - 6 Rows\n* Super Large - 4 Rows\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/en/next_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/next_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n\n---\n\nPrinting to the Print Console requires using a **next row** block after a **print** block to output the contents of the Print Console buffer into the Print Console window.\n\n![next_row_with_print_console](static/help/v5/blocks/en/next_row/next_row_with_print_console.png)"},"next_row_virtual":{"name":"next_row_virtual","markdown":"# Set cursor to next row\n\nSets the cursor to a new line in the Print Console when using the **print** blocks. \n\n![set_cursor_next_row](static/help/v5/blocks/en/next_row_virtual/set_cursor_next_row.png)\n\n\n## How To Use\n\nUse the **set cursor to next row** block to set the cursor to a new line in the display.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will print \"Hello\" and on the next line in the display it will print \"World!\"\n\n![set_cursor_next_row_code_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/next_row_virtual/set_cursor_next_row_code_example.png)"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# Not\n\nReports the opposite (inverse) of the reported Boolean value.\n\n![not](static/help/v5/blocks/en/not/not.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **not** block reports **true** when the Boolean block inside reports **false**.\n\nThe **not** block reports **false** when the Boolean block inside reports **true**.\n\nThe **not** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will report **true** when the V5 Brain's screen is not pressed. \n\n![not_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/en/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/en/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Object count\n\nReports how many objects the Vision Sensor detects. \n\nAn object will need to be configured before the  **object count** block can detect it.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Vision Sensor to use.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nThe **snapshot of** block will need to be used before the **object count** block reports a number of objects.\n\nThe **object count** block will only detect the number of objects from the last snapshot signature.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Object exists\n\nReports if the Vision Sensor detects a configured object. \n\nAn object will need to be configured before the **object exists** block can detect it.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Vision Sensor to use.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n\n**Object exists** reports **true** when the Vision Sensor detects a configured object.\n\n**Object exists** reports **false** when the Vision Sensor does not detect a configured object.\n\nThe **object exists** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nThe **snapshot of** block will need to be used before the **object exists** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Object found\n\nReports if the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor sees an object within its field of view. \n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/en/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object found** reports **true** when the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n**Object found** reports **false** when the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor does not detect an object or surface.\n\nChoose which Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor to use.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/en/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nThe **object found** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/en/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"optical_brightness":{"name":"optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_brightness](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_brightness/optical_brightness.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_brightness_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical brightness** block reports a number value from **0%** to **100%**.\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.\n\nThe **Optical brightness** block reports number values and is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_brightness_use](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_use.png)\n"},"optical_brightness_virtual":{"name":"optical_brightness_virtual","markdown":"# Optical brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_brightness](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_brightness_virtual/optical_brightness.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_brightness_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_brightness_virtual/optical_brightness_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical brightness** block reports a number value from **0%** to **100%**.\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.\n\nThe **Optical brightness** block reports number values and is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_brightness_use](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_brightness_virtual/optical_brightness_use.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Optical brightness** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![optical_brightness_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_brightness_virtual/optical_brightness_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![optical_brightness_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_brightness_virtual/optical_brightness_monitor.png)"},"optical_detect":{"name":"optical_detect","markdown":"# Optical detects color\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects the specified color.\n\n![optical_detect](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect/optical_detect.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_detect_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect/optical_detect_device.png)\n\nChoose which color you want the sensor to check for.\n\n![optical_detect_colors](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect/optical_detect_colors.png)\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **true** when the Optical Sensor detects the specified color.\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **false** if it doesn't detect the specified color.\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![optical_detect_use](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect/optical_detect_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect_gesture":{"name":"optical_detect_gesture","markdown":"# When Optical detects a gesture \n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the Optical sensor detects a gesture.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBefore using the **When Optical detects a gesture** event, the **Optical set mode** block must be used to set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures.\n\n![optical_set_mode_gesture_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_gesture/optical_set_mode_gesture_block.png)\n\nThe **When Optical detects a gesture** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on gestures that the Optical Sensor detects.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_detects_gesture_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detects_gesture_device.png)\n\nChoose which gesture triggers the **When Optical detects a gesture** event.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block2.png)"},"optical_detect_object":{"name":"optical_detect_object","markdown":"# When Optical detects/loses \n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the Optical sensor detects or loses an object.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **When Optical detects/loses** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on whether the Optical Sensor **detects** an object in range of the sensor or **loses** an object that was in range of the sensor.\n\nChoose an optical sensor.\n\n![optical_detect_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_device.png)\n\nChoose whether the **When Optical detects/loses** event is triggered when the sensor **detects** an object, or **loses** an object.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block2.png)"},"optical_detect_virtual":{"name":"optical_detect_virtual","markdown":"# Optical detects color\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects the specified color.\n\n![optical_detect](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_virtual/optical_detect.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_detect_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_virtual/optical_detect_device.png)\n\nChoose which color you want the sensor to check for.\n\n![optical_detect_colors](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_virtual/optical_detect_colors.png)\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **true** when the Optical Sensor detects the specified color.\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **false** if it doesn't detect the specified color.\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![optical_detect_use](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_virtual/optical_detect_use.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Optical detects color** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![optical_detect_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_virtual/optical_detect_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![optical_detect_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_detect_virtual/optical_detect_monitor.png)\n"},"optical_found_object":{"name":"optical_found_object","markdown":"# Optical found object\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\n\n![optical_found_object](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_found_object/optical_found_object.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_found_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **true** when the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **false** if an object is not within range.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block should be used to check if an object is close to the Optical Sensor so that the color readings from the **Optical detects color** block are accurate.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![optical_found_object_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_condition.png)"},"optical_found_object_virtual":{"name":"optical_found_object_virtual","markdown":"# Optical found object\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\n\n![optical_found_object](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_found_object_virtual/optical_found_object.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_found_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_found_object_virtual/optical_found_object_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **true** when the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **false** if an object is not within range.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block should be used to check if an object is close to the Optical Sensor so that the color readings from the **Optical detects color** block are accurate.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![optical_found_object_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_found_object_virtual/optical_found_object_condition.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Optical found object** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![optical_found_object_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_found_object_virtual/optical_found_object_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![optical_found_object_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_found_object_virtual/optical_found_object_monitor.png)"},"optical_gesture_detected":{"name":"optical_gesture_detected","markdown":"# Optical gesture detected\n\nReports whether an Optical Sensor has detected the specified gesture.\n\n![optical_gesture_detected_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_gesture_detected/optical_gesture_detected_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Optical gesture detected** block reports whether a gesture has been detected.\n\nBefore using the **Optical gesture detected** block, the Optical Sensor needs to be set to detect gestures with the **Optical set mode** block.\n\n![optical_set_mode_gesture_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_gesture_detected/optical_set_mode_gesture_block.png)\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_gesture_detected_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_gesture_detected/optical_gesture_detected_device.png)\n\nChoose which gesture to check for.\n\n![optical_gesture_detected_gestures](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_gesture_detected/optical_gesture_detected_gestures.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below waits until the Optical Sensor detects an **up** gesture before driving the robot forward.\n\n![optical_gesture_detected_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_gesture_detected/optical_gesture_detected_example.png)"},"optical_hue":{"name":"optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical hue\n\nReports the hue of the color of an object.\n\n![optical_hue](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_hue/optical_hue.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose an optical sensor.\n\n![optical_hue_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_hue/optical_hue_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical hue** block reports a number value that is the hue of the color of an object. It returns a number between **0** and **359**, which can be thought of as the location of the color on a color wheel.\n\nThe **Optical hue** block reports number values and is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_hue_use](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_hue/optical_hue_use.png)"},"optical_hue_virtual":{"name":"optical_hue_virtual","markdown":"# Optical hue\n\nReports the hue of the color of an object.\n\n![optical_hue](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_hue_virtual/optical_hue.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose an optical sensor.\n\n![optical_hue_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_hue_virtual/optical_hue_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical hue** block reports a number value that is the hue of the color of an object. It returns a number between **0** and **359**, which can be thought of as the location of the color on a color wheel.\n\nThe **Optical hue** block reports number values and is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_hue_use](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_hue_virtual/optical_hue_use.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Optical hue** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![optical_hue_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_hue_virtual/optical_hue_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![optical_hue_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_hue_virtual/optical_hue_monitor.png)"},"optical_set_light":{"name":"optical_set_light","markdown":"# Set Optical light\n\nSets the light on the Optical Sensor to on or off.\n\n![optical_set_light](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_light/optical_set_light.png)\n\n## How To Use\nThe **Set optical light** block allows you to turn the Optical Sensor's light **on** or **off**. The light lets the sensor see objects if it is looking at an object in a dark area.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_set_light_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_device.png)\n\nChoose whether you want to set the light on the Optical Sensor to **on** or **off**.\n\n![optical_set_light_state](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_state.png)\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, we use the **Set optical light** block to turn the light on. Then, if the Optical Sensor detects an object, we print the hue.\n\n\n![optical_set_light_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_example.png)"},"optical_set_light_power":{"name":"optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Set optical light power \n\nSet the light power of V5 Optical sensor\n\n![optical_set_light_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_light_power_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Set optical light power** block accepts a range of **0%** to **100%**. This will change the brightness of the light on the Optical Sensor. If the light is off, this block will turn the light on.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_set_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_device.png)\n\nThe set optical light power block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![optical_set_power_num](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_num.png)\n\n## Example\nIn this example we use the **Set optical light power** block to set the power of the light to **50%**, then we use the **Set optical light** block to turn the light on. Then, if the Optical Sensor detects an object, we print the hue.\n\n![optical_set_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_example.png)"},"optical_set_mode":{"name":"optical_set_mode","markdown":"# Set Optical mode\n\nSets an Optical Sensor to either detect colors or gestures.\n\n![optical_set_mode_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_mode/optical_set_mode_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Set optical mode** block allows you to set an Optical Sensor to either detect colors or gestures.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_set_mode_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_mode/optical_set_mode_device.png)\n\nChoose whether you want to set the mode of the Optical Sensor to either detect colors or gestures.\n\n![optical_set_mode_mode](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_mode/optical_set_mode_mode.png)\n\nBy default, an Optical Sensor is set to always detect colors. Before using any Optical Sensor gesture blocks, the Optical Sensor must be set to detect gestures.\n\n![optical_set_mode_gesture_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/optical_set_mode/optical_set_mode_gesture_block.png)"},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# Or\n\nReports if one of two Boolean conditions are true.\n\n![or](static/help/v5/blocks/en/or/or.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **or** block reports **true** when one (or both) of the conditions are **true**. \n\nThe **or** block reports **false** when both of the conditions are **false**.\n\nThe **or** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and fits in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThe **or** block reports **true** when either the Bumper sensor is pressed, and/or the Light sensor's brightness is greater than 50%. \n\nThe **or** block reports **false** only when both the Bumper sensor is not pressed and the Light sensor's brightness is less than or equal to 50%\n\n![or_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/en/or/or_truth.png)"},"play_sound":{"name":"play_sound","markdown":"# Play VEXcode sound\n\nPlays a custom imported sound through your devices speaker.\n\n![play_sound_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/play_sound/play_sound_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nFor the **play VEXcode sound** block to run properly, the V5 Brain **MUST** stay connected to the device via a USB cable while the project is running. \n\n* If coding in app-based VEXcode V5, no additional connection steps are needed in addition to the USB connection.\n* If coding in web-based VEXcode V5, the V5 Brain needs to stay connected while using the user/console web-serial port. For more information, [view this article >](https://kb.vex.com/hc/en-us/articles/15614471185812-Connecting-to-the-User-Console-Port-in-Web-Based-VEXcode-V5)\n\n![web_serial](static/help/v5/blocks/en/play_sound/web_serial.png)\n\nChoose which sound to use. Use the default sound **game over** or add a new sound file URL in the Manage VEXcode Sounds menu.\n\n![play_sound_block_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/play_sound/play_sound_block_options.png)\n\nUser uploaded sounds will only appear as a drop-down option if they are added in the Manage VEXcode Sounds menu. For more information about adding or editing sounds, [view this article >](https://kb.vex.com/hc/en-us/articles/15613914815508-Playing-Custom-Imported-Sounds-in-a-VEXcode-V5-Project)\n\n![manage_sounds](static/help/v5/blocks/en/play_sound/manage_sounds.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will play the arrow sound as soon as the project is started and then immediately move to the next block in the stack. \nThe **play VEXcode sound** block is non-blocking and will not wait until the sound has finished playing before moving to the next block in the stack. \n\nThe drivetrain will then drive forward for the full 200mm before playing the default **game over** sound.\n\n![example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/play_sound/example.png)"},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Position of controller\n\nReports the position of a joystick on the V5 Controller along an axis.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of controller** reports a range between **-100 to 100**.\n\n**Position of controller** will report zero (0) when a joystick axis is centered.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nChoose the V5 Controller to use.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_devices.png)\n\nChoose the joystick's axis to check its position.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nThe **position of controller** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Position of motor\n\nReports the distance a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group has traveled.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of motor** reports the position of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group in integer numbers for degrees, and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nChoose which V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nChoose whether the value is reported in degrees rotated or in turns.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **position of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"position_of_motor_virtual":{"name":"position_of_motor_virtual","markdown":"# Position of motor\n\nReports the distance a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group has traveled.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of motor** reports the position of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group in integer numbers for degrees, and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nChoose which V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nChoose whether the value is reported in degrees rotated or in turns.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Position of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Position of motor** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![position_of_motor_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![position_of_motor_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_motor_virtual/position_of_motor_monitor.png)"},"position_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"position_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Position of shaft encoder\n\nReports the distance the Shaft Encoder has rotated.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of shaft encoder** reports the distance the Shaft Encoder has rotated in integer numbers for degrees, and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nChoose which Shaft Encoder to use.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_device.png)\n\nChoose whether the value is reported in degrees rotated or in turns of the Shaft Encoder. \n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **position of shaft encoder** is used in blocks with circular spaces. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_inserted.png)"},"power":{"name":"power","markdown":"# Set electromagnet power\n\nSets the V5 Electromagnet power that will be used when picking up and object with the energize block.\n\n![set_magnet_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/power/set_magnet_power_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou may need to pick up objects with a varying weights. The **set electromagnet power** block lets you control how much power the elctromagnet will use. The **set electromagnet power** block has a range of **0% to 100%**\n\nChoose which magnet to use.\n\n![set_magnet_dropdown_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/power/set_magnet_dropdown_block.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the robot to drive forward 200mm, then it will increase the power using the **set electromagnet power** block, then the **Electromagnet** will boost to pick up an object, drive forward 200mm, then drop the object.\n\n![set_magnet_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/power/set_magnet_power_example.png)\n"},"power_of_motor":{"name":"power_of_motor","markdown":"# Power of motor\n\nReports the amount of power output a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group is currently generating.\n\n![motor_power](static/help/v5/blocks/en/power_of_motor/motor_power.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Power of motor** reports a range from **0.0 to 11.0 watts**. \n\nChoose a Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![motor_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/power_of_motor/motor_power_device.png)\n\nThe reporter block **power of motor** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![motor_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/power_of_motor/motor_power_inserted.png)\n"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Pressing bumper\n\nReports if the Bumper Switch is pressed.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Pressing bumper** reports **true** if the Bumper Switch is being pressed.\n\n**Pressing bumper** reports **false** if the Bumper Switch is not pressed.\n\nChoose which Bumper Switch to use.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nThe **pressing bumper** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_bumper_virtual":{"name":"pressing_bumper_virtual","markdown":"# Pressing bumper\n\nReports if the Bumper Switch is pressed.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_bumper_virtual/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Pressing bumper** reports **true** if the Bumper Switch is being pressed.\n\n**Pressing bumper** reports **false** if the Bumper Switch is not pressed.\n\nChoose which Bumper Switch to use.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_bumper_virtual/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nThe **Pressing bumper** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_bumper_virtual/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n \n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Pressing bumper** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![pressing_bumper_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_bumper_virtual/pressing_bumper_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![pressing_bumper_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_bumper_virtual/pressing_bumper_monitor.png)"},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Pressing controller\n\nReports if a button on the V5 Controller is pressed.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Pressing controller** reports **true** if the selected Controller button is being pressed.\n\n**Pressing controller** reports **false** if the selected Controller button is not pressed.\n\nChoose which V5 Controller to use.\n\n![pressing_controller_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_device.png)\n\nChoose which Controller button to use.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nThe **pressing controller** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)"},"pressing_limit":{"name":"pressing_limit","markdown":"# Pressing limit\n\nReports if the Limit Switch is pressed.\n\n![pressing_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_limit/pressing_limit.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Pressing limit** reports **true** if the Limit Switch is being pressed.\n\n**Pressing limit** reports **false** if the Limit Switch is not pressed.\n\nChoose which Limit Switch to use.\n\n![pressing_limit_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_bumper.png)\n\nThe **pressing limit** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![pressing_limit_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_inserted.png)\n "},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text on the Print Console, V5 Brain or Controller screen.\n\n![look_print](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print/look_print.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **print** block will print data at a cursor location on the screen or on the Print Console.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1, and at row 1 on the Print Console.\n\nAll reporter blocks will be printed as integer numbers by default. Use the **set print precision** block to adjust the number of decimal places printed.\n\nChoose which device to use. V5 Controllers will only appear if they are added in the Devices window.\n\n![look_print_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print/look_print_dropdown_with_console.png)\n\nFor adding values to the Print Console buffer, only the **print** block is needed.\n\n![look_print_dropdown_console](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print/look_print_dropdown_console.png)\n\nHowever, to output the values from the Print Console buffer onto the Print Console, a **set cursor to next row** block is needed. The blocks below will print \"VEXcode\" to the Print Console and set the cursor to the next row.\n\n![look_print_set_cursor_console](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print/look_print_set_cursor_console.png)\n\nBy default, the cursor will remain on the same row after printing for any subsequent print commands.\n\nTo set the cursor on the device to the next row after printing, you can select the arrow to expand **and set cursor to next row** - this will move the cursor to the next row after printing the statement.\n\n![print_expanded](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print/print_expanded.png)\n\n---\n\nPrint words and numbers.\n\n![print_words](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print/print_words.png)\n\nPrint the reported value from a variable.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nPrint the reported calculation of an operator.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nPrint the reported value from a sensor or device.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"print_virtual":{"name":"print_virtual","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text in the Print Console.\n\n![look_print](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print_virtual/look_print.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **print** block will print data within the Monitor Window tab\n\n![monitor_tab_icon](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print_virtual/monitor_tab_icon.png)\n\nAll reporter blocks will be printed as integer (whole) numbers by default. Use the **set print precision** block to adjust the number of decimal places printed.\n\nPrint words and numbers.\n\n![print_words](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print_virtual/print_words.png)\n\nPrint the reported value from a variable.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print_virtual/print_variable1.png)  \n\nPrint the reported calculation of an operator.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print_virtual/print_addition.png)  \n\nPrint the reported value from a sensor or device.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/print_virtual/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# My blocks\n\nMy Blocks are used to create custom blocks.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**My blocks** are used to create a sequence of blocks that can be used multiple times throughout a project. \n\n**My blocks** are made using the **Make a Block** button.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**My blocks** can have multiple parameters - text labels, numberic variables, and boolean variables - to add more functionality to your custom block.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nTo use a **my block**, attach the calling **my block** to a hat block. When the **my block** is reached in your prject, the stack inside of the **my block** will run using the parameter values specified.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nAttach a stack of blocks to the **my blocks** \"define\" hat block to set the action that occur when a **my block** is used.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Note: Creating multiple My Blocks with the same labels and variables may cause errors when downloading your project.***\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the robot will use **my blocks** to:\n\n* Drive forward for 15 inches\n* Prints the battery capacity and also move the cursor to a new line on the Brain's screen\n* Turns the robot 180 degrees to the right\n* Prints the battery capacity and also move the cursor to a new line on the Brain's screen\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# My blocks\n\nMy Blocks are used to create custom blocks.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**My blocks** are used to create a sequence of blocks that can be used multiple times throughout a project. \n\n**My blocks** are made using the **Make a Block** button.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**My blocks** can have multiple parameters - text labels, numberic variables, and boolean variables - to add more functionality to your custom block.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nTo use a **my block**, attach the calling **my block** to a hat block. When the **my block** is reached in your prject, the stack inside of the **my block** will run using the parameter values specified.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nAttach a stack of blocks to the **my blocks** \"define\" hat block to set the action that occur when a **my block** is used.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Note: Creating multiple My Blocks with the same labels and variables may cause errors when downloading your project.***\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the robot will use **my blocks** to:\n\n* Drive forward for 15 inches\n* Prints the battery capacity and also move the cursor to a new line on the Brain's screen\n* Turns the robot 180 degrees to the right\n* Prints the battery capacity and also move the cursor to a new line on the Brain's screen\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/en/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Random\nReports a random value between the lowest and highest values in the block.\n\n![random](static/help/v5/blocks/en/random/random.png)\n\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe  **random** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces. \n\nThe **random** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Examples\n\nThis example uses a **random** block to randomize the drivetrain's velocity.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/v5/blocks/en/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nThis example uses a **random** block to randomize the length of a wait block.\n\n![random_control](static/help/v5/blocks/en/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"reflectivity_of":{"name":"reflectivity_of","markdown":"# Reflectivity of\n\nReports the amount of light reflected using the Line Tracker sensor.\n\n![reflectivity_of](static/help/v5/blocks/en/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nLight colored surfaces will reflect more light and will report a high reflectivity value.\n\nDark colored surfaces will reflect less light and will report a low reflectivity value.\n\n**Reflectivity of** reports a range from **0% to 100%**.\n\nChoose which Line Tracker sensor to use.\n\n![reflectivity_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/en/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_color.png)\n\nThe reporter block **reflectivity of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![reflectivity_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n\n"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Remainder\n\nDivides the first value by the second value and reports the remainder.\n\n![remainder](static/help/v5/blocks/en/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **remainder** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nNumbers that divide evenly will report a remainder of zero.\n\nThe length of the **remainder** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will divide 7 and 2 and report the remainder to print \"1\" on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/en/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Repeat\n\nA 'C' block that repeats the blocks contained inside for a set number of times.\n\n![repeat](static/help/v5/blocks/en/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nFirst enter a value to indicate how many times the stack will **repeat** the blocks contained inside.\n \nThe **repeat** 'C' block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/repeat/repeat_select.png)\n\n'C' blocks can also be put inside of each other. This concept is called nesting which can help save time when programming different behaviors."},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Repeat until\n\nA 'C' block that repeats the blocks inside until the Boolean condition is reported to be **true**.  \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/en/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **repeat until** block will only check the Boolean condition at the beginning of each loop. \n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **false**, the blocks inside of **repeat until** will run.\n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **true**, the blocks inside of **repeat until** will be skipped.\n\nThe **repeat until** 'C' block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks as its condition.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/en/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Reset timer\n\nResets the V5 Brain's timer.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/v5/blocks/en/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Brain's timer begins at the beginning of each project. The **reset timer** block is used to reset the timer back to 0 seconds.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the timer will be reset before moving the Drivetrain forward for 3 seconds. After 3 seconds has elapsed, the Drivetrain will stop.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/v5/blocks/en/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_angle":{"name":"rotation_angle","markdown":"# Angle of rotation \n\nReports a V5 Rotation sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n![rotation_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Angle of rotation** block reports values in the range of **0.00** to **359.99**.\n\nThe **Angle of rotation** block will either report increasing or decreasing values as the Rotation sensor turns.\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to get values from.\n\n![rotation_angle_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block2.png)\n\nThe **angle of rotation** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_angle_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block3.png)\n"},"rotation_angle_virtual":{"name":"rotation_angle_virtual","markdown":"# Angle of rotation \n\nReports a V5 Rotation sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n![rotation_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_angle_virtual/rotation_angle_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Angle of rotation** block reports values in the range of **0.00** to **359.99**.\n\nThe **Angle of rotation** block will either report increasing or decreasing values as the Rotation sensor turns.\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to get values from.\n\n![rotation_angle_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_angle_virtual/rotation_angle_block2.png)\n\nThe **Angle of rotation** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_angle_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_angle_virtual/rotation_angle_block3.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Angle of rotation** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![rotation_angle_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_angle_virtual/rotation_angle_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![rotation_angle_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_angle_virtual/rotation_angle_monitor.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Angle of rotation\n\nReports the 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n![rotation_position.png](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Gyro rotation** reports a **positive** value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\n**Gyro rotation** reports a **negative** value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\nChoose which Gyro Sensor / Interial Sensor to check.\n\n![rotation_position_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_devices.png)\n\nThe **Gyro rotation** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_position_inserted.png](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_inserted.png)\n"},"rotation_position":{"name":"rotation_position","markdown":"# Position of rotation \n\nReports the current rotational position of the selected V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_position/rotation_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of rotation** reports the position of a V5 Rotation sensor in integer numbers for degrees, and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nChoose which V5 Rotation sensor to use.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_position/rotation_position_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether the value is reported in degrees rotated or in turns of the V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_position/rotation_position_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block **position of rotation** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_position_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_position/rotation_position_block4.png)\n"},"rotation_position_virtual":{"name":"rotation_position_virtual","markdown":"# Position of rotation \n\nReports the current rotational position of the selected V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_position_virtual/rotation_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of rotation** reports the position of a V5 Rotation sensor in integer numbers for degrees, and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nChoose which V5 Rotation sensor to use.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_position_virtual/rotation_position_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether the value is reported in degrees rotated or in turns of the V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_position_virtual/rotation_position_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Position of rotation** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_position_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_position_virtual/rotation_position_block4.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Position of rotation** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![rotation_position_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_position_virtual/rotation_position_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![rotation_position_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_position_virtual/rotation_position_monitor.png)\n"},"rotation_set_position":{"name":"rotation_set_position","markdown":"# Set position \n\nSets a V5 Rotation sensor's current position to a defined value.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set position** block can be used to set a Rotation sensor's position.\n\nThis block is typically used to reset the position of the Rotation sensor when the value is set to 0.\n\nThe **set position** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks as an input.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block3.png)\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to use, then enter the desired position value.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block2.png)\n"},"rotation_velocity":{"name":"rotation_velocity","markdown":"# Velocity of rotation\n\nReports the current velocity of a V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to get values from.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in percent (%), revolutions per minute (rpm) or degrees per second (dps).\n\n![rotation_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block velocity of rotation is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block4.png)\n"},"rotation_velocity_virtual":{"name":"rotation_velocity_virtual","markdown":"# Velocity of rotation\n\nReports the current velocity of a V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_velocity_virtual/rotation_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to get values from.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_velocity_virtual/rotation_velocity_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in percent (%), revolutions per minute (rpm) or degrees per second (dps).\n\n![rotation_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_velocity_virtual/rotation_velocity_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block velocity of rotation is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_velocity_virtual/rotation_velocity_block4.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Velocity of rotation** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![rotation_velocity_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_velocity_virtual/rotation_velocity_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![rotation_velocity_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/rotation_velocity_virtual/rotation_velocity_monitor.png)"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Round\n\nRounds the inputed value to the nearest integer.\n\n![round](static/help/v5/blocks/en/round/round.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nDecimals that are 0.5 or greater **round** up, and decimals less than 0.5 **round** down.\n\nThe **round** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces, and can accept circular blocks in them as well. \n\nThe **round** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/en/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will round 2.7 and will print \"3\".\n\n![round_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/en/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"screen_position":{"name":"screen_position","markdown":"# Screen position\n\nReports the location of the last detected touch on the V5 Brain's touchscreen.\n\n![screen_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/screen_position/screen_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **screen position** reporter block is used to capture the X/Y location of the last press on the V5 Brain's touchscreen. This report block can be used to create interactivity between the V5 and the end user.\n\n**Screen position** reports a range of **0 to 480 pixels** when set to report the **X** coordinate.\n\n**Screen position** reports a range of **0 to 240 pixels** when set to report the **Y** coordinate.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/en/screen_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\nChoose which axis to report. \n\n![screen_position_value](static/help/v5/blocks/en/screen_position/screen_position_value.png)\n\nThe **screen position** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![screen_position_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/screen_position/screen_position_inserted.png)"},"screen_pressed":{"name":"screen_pressed","markdown":"# Screen pressed\n\nReports if the V5 Brain's touchscreen is currently being pressed.\n\n![screen_pressed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **screen pressed** Boolean block can be used together with the **screen position** to detect when and where a touch has occured on the V5 Brain's touchscreen.\n\n**Screen pressed** reports **true** when the V5 Brain's touchscreen is being pressed.\n\n**Screen pressed** reports **false** when the V5 Brain's touchscreen is not being pressed.\n\nThe **screen pressed** Boolean block reports a **true** or **false** value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![screen_pressed_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Set 2D list to\n\nSets every item in the 2D list to the entered values.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen creating a 2D list, you can set the number of **columns** of the list between 1 to 10 items and the number of **rows** of the list between 1 to 10 items.\n\nChoose which 2D list to use. The 2D list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nThe **set 2D list to** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Set list to\n\nSets every item in the list to the entered values.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen creating a list, you can set the length of the list between 1 to 10 items.\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nThe **set list to** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the list to initial values, and then report item #3 (90) from the list, to set the position of the Arm. \n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Set boolean variable\n\nSets a boolean variable to a given value.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which boolean variable to use. Boolean variables can also be renamed or deleted. \n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nChoose a Boolean value.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nThe **set boolean variable** block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks.\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# Set cursor\n\nSets the cursor location for **print** blocks on the V5 Brain or Controller screen.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet the cursor's row and column position to have a **print** command display at a specific location on the screen.\n\n**Set cursor** accepts a range for **row** of **1 to 20**.\n\n**Set cursor** accepts a range for **column** of **1 to 80**.\n\nChoose which device to use. V5 Controllers will only appear if they are added in the Devices window.\n\n![set_cursor_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_cursor/set_cursor_dropdown.png)\n\nThe **set cursor** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of columns available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Rows\n* Small - 16 Rows\n* Medium - 12 Rows (Default)\n* Large - 8 Rows\n* Extra Large - 6 Rows\n* Super Large - 4 Rows\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* Extra Small - 80 Columns\n* Small - 68 Columns\n* Medium - 48 Columns (Default)\n* Large - 32 Columns\n* Extra Large - 24 Columns\n* Super Large - 16 Columns\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* Standard Font - 20 Columns (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"set_digital_out":{"name":"set_digital_out","markdown":"# Digital out\n\nSets the logic level of a digital out 3-Wire port.\n\n![digital_out_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_digital_out/digital_out_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 3-Wire ports function at a 5V logic signal voltage level.\n\nThe **digital out** block sets the digital signal to output a high or low logic signal.\n\nChoose which digital out port to use. \n\n![digital_out_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_digital_out/digital_out_select.png)\n\nChoose to output a high or low digital logic signal.\n\n![digital_out_choose](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_digital_out/digital_out_choose.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Set drive heading\n\nSets the Drivetrain's Gyro heading value.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set drive heading** block can be used to set the Drivetrain's position to any given heading. This block can be used to reset the orientation of the Drivetrain's gyro when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n**Set drive heading** accepts a range of **0 to 360** degrees.\n\nThe **set drive heading** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Set drive rotation\n\nSets the Drivetrain's angle of rotation when configured with a 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set drive rotation** block can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive or negative value.\n\nThe **set drive rotation** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will turn the robot a total of 210 degrees:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Turn right (clockwise) to rotation 120 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current position as rotation of -45 degrees.\n- Turn right (clockwise) an additional 90 degrees (-45 degrees to +45 degrees) based on the set rotation value from the previous block."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Set drive stopping\n\nSets the behavior of the Drivetrain once it stops moving.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n* **Brake** will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop, and will not correct for outside forces.\n* **Coast** lets the Drivetrain spin gradually to a stop.\n* **Hold** will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved by an outside force, by using the built-in encoder.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the Drivetrain move forward for 3 seconds and then hold its position once stopped.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Set drive timeout\n\nSets a time limit for Drivetrain movement commands.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Drivetrain's time limit is used to prevent drive blocks that do not reach their position from preventing other blocks in the stack from running.\n\nAn example of a Drivetrain not reaching its position is when a robot is driven against a wall and cannot completed its movement.\n\nThe **set drive timeout** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will end the **drive** command after 2 second if the Drivetrain has not reached the target of 24 inches. Once the time limit or distance is reached, the Drivetrain will move on to the **turn** command.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Set drive velocity\n\nSets the speed of the Drivetrain.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set drive velocity** will set the speed of the drivetrain, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move. A **drive** block is still required.\n\n**Set drive velocity** reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-600rpm to 600rpm**.\n\n**Set drive velocity** will accept a \"rotations per minute\" range based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to move in reverse.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's velocity to 0 will cause the Drivetrain to stop.\n\nThe **set drive velocity** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose the unit of measure.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n\n"},"set_fill_color":{"name":"set_fill_color","markdown":"# Set fill color\n\nSets the color that fills in shapes drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n![set_fill_color_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set fill color** block is used to set the color of the inside of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\nChoose a fill color. \n\n![set_fill_color_color](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_color.png)  \n\nThe fill color will be used for any future objects drawn on the V5 Brain's screen."},"set_font":{"name":"set_font","markdown":"# Set font\n\nSets the style and size of font used on the V5 Brain's screen when printing numbers or text.\n\n![set_font_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_font/set_font_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThere are two different types of fonts available on the V5 Brain's screen:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - each character takes up the same width.\n* Proportional (Prop) - each character takes up different size widths based on the character.\n\nChoose which font type and size to use.\n\n![set_font_block_font](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_font/set_font_block_font.png)  \n\nThe new font size will be used for any future text written to the V5 Brain's screen."},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Set heading\n\nSets the Gyroscopic (Gyro) / Inertial sensor's current heading position to a set value.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set gyro / inertial heading** block can be used to set the Gyro's position to any clockwise heading.\n\nThis block is typically used reset the heading orientation of the Gyro / Inertial sensor when value is set to 0.\n\n**Set gyro heading** accepts a range of **0.0 to 359.99** degrees.\n\nThe **set heading** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose which Gyro / Inertial Sensor to use, then enter the desired value.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Set rotation\n\nSets the 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor's angle of rotation to the value set within the command block.\n\n![setrotation](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set gyro rotation** block can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\n**Set gyro rotation** accepts a range of any positive or negative decimal or integer number.\n\nThe **set gyro rotation** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose which Gyro Sensor to use.\n\n![setrotation_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation_devices.png)\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Replace item of 2D list\n\nUpdates an item in the 2D list to a new value.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nEnter the item's row (first number) and column (second number) position within the list to be replaced.\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nThe **replace item** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Replace item\n\nUpdates an item in the list to a new value.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nThe **replace item** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n"},"set_joint_move_speed":{"name":"set_joint_move_speed","markdown":"# Set joint speed\n\nSets the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's joint movements.\n\n![joint_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_joint_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_joint_move_speed/select_joint_speed_arm.png)\n\nChoose the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's joint movements. The default speed is **normal**.\n\n![joint_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_select.png)"},"set_led":{"name":"set_led","markdown":"# Set LED\n\nTurns an LED on or off.\n\n![set_led_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_led/set_led_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nSelect which LED to use.\n\n![set_led_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_led/set_led_block_device.png)\n\nSelect if the LED is on or off.\n\n![set_led_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_led/set_led_block_setting.png)\n\n"},"set_linear_move_speed":{"name":"set_linear_move_speed","markdown":"# Set linear speed\n\nSets the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's linear movements.\n\n![linear_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_linear_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_linear_move_speed/select_linear_speed_arm.png)\n\nChoose the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's linear movements. The default speed is **normal**.\n\n![linear_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_select.png)"},"set_mastering":{"name":"set_mastering","markdown":"# Set mastering\n\nSets the mastering values of the four joints of the V5 Robotic Arm to allow it to be calibrated to the same known location.\n\n![set_mastering_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_mastering/set_mastering_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nInput the mastering values from the V5 Brain to the **set mastering** block. \n\nThe passable threshold values for the joints are as follows:\n\n* Joint 1: 1600 - 2000\n* Joint 2: 1900 - 2400\n* Joint 3: 1700 - 2100\n* Joint 4: 200 - 650\n\n![mastering_values](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_mastering/mastering_values.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_mastering_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_mastering/select_mastering_arm.png)\n\nThe **set mastering** block accepts integers and numeric blocks.\n\n![mastering_input](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_mastering/mastering_input.png)"},"set_motor_controller_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_controller_velocity","markdown":"# Set motor controller velocity\n\nSets the speed of a Motor 393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n![set_motor_controller_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set motor controller velocity** accepts a range of **-100% to 100%**.\n\nSetting a Motor 393's velocity to a negative value will cause the Motor 393 to spin in reverse.\n\nSetting a Motor 393's velocity to 0 will cause the Motor 393 to stop.\n\nChoose which Motor 393 to use.\n\n![set_motor_controller_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_motor.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Set motor position\n\nSets the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group's encoder(s) position to the given value.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set motor position** block can be used to set a Motor or Motor Group's position to any given value.\n\nUsually, the **set motor position** block is used to set the position to 0 to reset the Motor or Motor Group's encoder(s) position.\n\nChoose which V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nChoose the unit of measurement in degrees or turns.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Set motor stopping\n\nSets the behavior of the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group once it stops spinning.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n* **Brake** will cause the Motor or Motor Group to come to an immediate stop.\n* **Coast** lets the Motor or Motor Group spin gradually to a stop.\n* **Hold** will cause the Motor or Motor Group to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved.\n\nThe behavior set by the **set motor stopping** block will be used for the remainder of the program until otherwise changed.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nChoose the Motor or Motor Group's setting after it stops.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the ArmMotor move forward for 90 degrees and then will resist outside forces (like gravity) to hold its position.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Set motor timeout\n\nSets a time limit for the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group's movement commands.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Motor or Motor Group's time limit is used to prevent motion blocks that do not reach their position from preventing other blocks in the stack from running. An example of a Motor or Motor Group not reaching its position is an arm or claw that reaches its mechanical limit and cannot complete its movement.\n\nThe **set motor timeout** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will end the **set motor** command after 2 second if the ClawMotor has not reached the position of 270 degrees. Once the time limit or target is reached, the ClawMotor will move to position 0 degrees.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Set motor torque\n\nSets the strength of the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set motor torque** accepts a range of **0% to 100%**.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nThe **set motor torque** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the Claw Motor to the 40 degree position with only 20% maximum torque. This allows the claw to grab an object without damaging it by using too much force.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Set motor velocity\n\nSets the speed of a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set motor velocity** accepts a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-600rpm to 600rpm**.\n\n**Set motor velocity** will accept a \"rotations per minute\" value based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a V5 Smart Motor's or Motor Group's velocity to a negative value will cause the Motor/Motor Group to spin in reverse.\n\nSetting a V5 Smart Motor's or Motor Groups' velocity to 0 will cause the Motor/Motor Group to stop.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nChoose if the speed is set in % or in revolutions per minute (rpm).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the Arm Motor to slowly spin at 25% speed to the 90 degree position.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_origin":{"name":"set_origin","markdown":"# Set origin position\n\nSets the origin to the current location of the end of arm tooling.\n\n![set_origin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_origin/set_origin_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, the origin on the Workcell is located in the center of the turntable.\n![turntable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_origin/turntable.png)\n\nThe **set origin position** block sets the origin to the current location of the end of arm tooling.\n\nThe end of arm tooling can be set to:\n\n* None\n* Marker (shown in image)\n* Electromagnet \n\n![marker](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_origin/marker.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![set_origin_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_origin/set_origin_insert.png)"},"set_pen_color":{"name":"set_pen_color","markdown":"# Set pen color\n\nSets the color of lines drawn on the V5 Brain's screen or the values printed to the Print Console.\n\n![set_pen_color_block_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_block_with_console.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set pen color** block is used to set the color of lines, pixels, and text drawn on the V5 Brain's screen or the values printed to the Print Console. \n\n**Set pen color** will also be used to set the color the outline of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\nChoose a pen color. \n\n![set_pen_color_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_dropdown_with_console.png)  \n\nThe pen color will be used for any future objects drawn on the V5 Brain's screen or any values printed to the Print Console until otherwise changed.\n\nWhen a program is stopped, the text color of the Print Console is reset to black."},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Set print precision\n\nSets the number of digits that appear after the decimal point when printing reporter blocks on the Print Console, V5 Brain or Controller screen.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose the level of precision that inserted reporter blocks will be printed to the Print Console or the screen.\n\n* Ones (1) (Default)\n* Tenths (0.1)\n* Hundredths (0.01)\n* Thousandths (0.001)\n* All Digits (0.000001)\n\nReporter blocks printed to the Print Console or screen will round to the nearest level of precision. For example, 1.67 will be printed as 2 at ones precision and 1.7 at tenths precision.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)\n\nChoose which device to use. V5 Controllers will only appear if they are added in the Devices window.\n\n![print_precision_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_print_precision/print_precision_dropdown_with_console.png)"},"set_print_precision_virtual":{"name":"set_print_precision_virtual","markdown":"# Set print precision\n\nSets the number of digits that appear after the decimal point when using print blocks to print variables and values to the Print Console.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_print_precision_virtual/set_print_precision.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose the level of precision that inserted reporter blocks will be printed to the screen.\n\n* Ones (1)\n* Tenths (0.1) (Default)\n* Hundredths (0.01)\n* Thousandths (0.001)\n* All Digits (0.000001)\n\nReporter blocks printed to the display will round to the nearest level of precision. For example, 1.67 will be printed as 2 at ones precision and 1.7 at tenths precision.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_print_precision_virtual/print_precision_choice.png)"},"set_shaft_encoder_position":{"name":"set_shaft_encoder_position","markdown":"# Set shaft encoder position\n\nSets the Shaft Encoder's position to the given value.\n\n![set_encoder_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set shaft encoder position** block can be used to set the Shaft Encoder's position to any given value.\n\nUsually, the **set shaft encoder position** block is used to set the position to 0, to reset the Shaft Encoder's position.\n\nChoose which Shaft Encoder to use, then set the desired value.\n\n![set_encoder_position_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_motor.png)\n\n"},"set_tool":{"name":"set_tool","markdown":"# Set tool\n\nSets the end effector or the end-of-arm tooling (EOAT) on the V5 Robotic Arm.\n\n![set_tool_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_tool/set_tool_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe end effector on the V5 Robotic Arm can be none (no attachment), an electromagnet, or a marker. \n\n![set_marker](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_tool/set_marker.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_tool_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_tool/select_tool_arm.png)\n\nChoose the tool on your V5 Robotic Arm. The default is set to **none**.\n\n![choose_tool](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_tool/choose_tool.png)"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Set turn velocity\n\nSets the speed of Drivetrain turns.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set turn velocity** will set the speed of the drivetrain, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move. A **turn** block is still required.\n\n**Set turn velocity** accepts a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-600rpm to 600rpm**.\n\n**Set turn velocity** will accept a \"rotations per minute\" value based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to turn in the opposite direction.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to 0 will cause the Drivetrain to stop.\n\nThe **set turn velocity** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Example\nThis example will make the Drivetrain turn slowly, at 25% speed, to the left.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Set variable\n\nSets a variable to a given value.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which variable to use. Variables can also be renamed or deleted. \n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nThe **set variable** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Set vision object item\n\nSets the object item (of the object you want to learn more information about) out of the number of objects detected.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **object count** block can be used before the **set vision object item** block to determine the number of objects detected.\n\nChoose which Vision Sensor to use.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nThe **set vision object item** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n\n\n"},"set_width":{"name":"set_width","markdown":"# Set pen width\n\nSets the width of the outline for shapes drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n![set_width_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_width/set_width_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set width** block is used to set the width of the line on the outside of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\nThe **set width** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/en/set_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"setangle":{"name":"setangle","markdown":"# Set angle\n\nSets the angle of the tool plate before the next [Linear move] or [Joint move] block is executed.\n\n![set_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/setangle/set_angle_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set angle** block sets the tool plate to be tilted at an angle either **up** or **down** before the next [Linear move] or [Joint move] block in a project. \n\nNote that the **set angle** block sets the angle for all future [Linear move] and [Joint move] blocks, unless it is set otherwise.\n\n![tool_plate](static/help/v5/blocks/en/setangle/tool_plate.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_set_angle_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/en/setangle/select_set_angle_arm.png)\n\nChoose the angle of the tool plate. The default is set to **up**.\n\n* The tool plate will be **horizontal** when it is set to **down**. \n* The tool plate will be **vertical** when it is set to **up**. \n\n![select_angle](static/help/v5/blocks/en/setangle/select_angle.png)\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the tool plate will begin to tilt once the [Joint move] block is executed and complete its tilting movement before the [Linear move] block.\n\n![set_angle_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/setangle/set_angle_example.png)"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Length of list\n\nReports the number of items in a list.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/en/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\nChoose which list to use. The list can also be renamed or deleted.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nThe **length of list** reporter block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/en/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# Snapshot\n\nTakes a snapshot from the Vision Sensor.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **snapshot** block will capture the current image from the Vision Sensor to be processed and analyzed for color signatures and codes. \n\nTypically, a **snapshot** is required first before using any other Vision Sensor blocks.\n\nSelect which Vision Sensor to use.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nSelect which vision signature to use. Vision signatures are configured from the Devices window.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/v5/blocks/en/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Spin\n\nSpins a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group until stopped.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **spin** block will run a Motor or Motor Group forever, until a new motion block is used or the program is stopped.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nChoose which direction to spin. Direction names can be changed in the Devices window. \n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_at_voltage":{"name":"spin_at_voltage","markdown":"# Spin at Voltage\n\nSpins a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group at a specified voltage.\n\n![spin_at_voltage](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_at_voltage/spin_at_voltage.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Spin at voltage** accepts a range from -12V to 12V.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![spin_at_voltage_option](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_at_voltage/spin_at_voltage_option.png)\n\nChoose which direction to spin. Direction names can be changed in the Devices window.\n\n![spin_at_voltage_option2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_at_voltage/spin_at_voltage_option2.png)\n\nThe **spin at voltage** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nSpinning a Motor or Motor Group at a negative voltage will cause the Motor/Motor Group to spin in the opposite direction than the one specified.\n"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Spin for\n\nSpins a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group for a given distance.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Spin for** will tell a Motor or Motor Group to travel in a given direction, for a given distance, from where it is currently located.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nChoose which direction to spin. Direction names can be changed in the Devices window. \n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nThe **spin for** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose the unit of measurement in degrees or turns.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Motor or Motor Group is done moving.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Motor or Motor Group moves.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_motor_controller":{"name":"spin_motor_controller","markdown":"# Spin motor controller\n\nSpins a Motor 393 connected to a Motor Controller 29 until stopped.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **spin** block will run a Motor 393 forever until a new motor block is used, or the program is stopped.\n\nChoose which Motor 393 to use.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_motor.png)\n\nChoose which direction to spin. Direction names can be changed in the Devices window. \n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_direction.png)"},"spin_servo":{"name":"spin_servo","markdown":"# Spin servo\n\nSpins a Servo Motor to a set position.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_servo/servo_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Spin servo** accepts a position range from **0 to 100 degrees**.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_servo/servo_port.png)\n\n"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Spin to position\n\nSpins a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group to a set position.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Spin to position** will tell a Motor or Motor Group to travel to a specific position. Based on the current position of the Motor or Motor Group, **spin to position** will determine the direction to rotate.\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nThe **spin to position** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose the unit of measurement in degrees or turns.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Motor or Motor Group is done moving.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Motor or Motor Group moves.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/en/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Stop driving\n\nStops the Drivetrain.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **stop driving** block will cause the Drivetrain to come to a complete stop and use the **set drive stopping** setting to either coast, brake, or hold its position.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will stop the Drivetrain after 3 seconds.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Stop motor\n\nStops a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to stop.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the Claw Motor open for 3 seconds before stopping.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor_controller":{"name":"stop_motor_controller","markdown":"# Stop motor controller\n\nStops a Motor 393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n![stop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Motor 393 to stop.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_motor.png)\n\nThis example will spin a Motor 393 forward for 3 seconds before stopping.\n\n![stop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_example.png)"},"stop_project":{"name":"stop_project","markdown":"# Stop project\n\nStops a running project.\n\n![stop_project](static/help/v5/blocks/en/stop_project/stop_project.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **stop project** block will cause a running project to stop. \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will drive the V5 Robot forward 200mm and turn right for 90 degrees before stopping the project.\n\n![stop_project2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/stop_project/stop_project2.png)"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Subtract\n\nSubtracts one value from another and reports the difference.\n\n![subtract](static/help/v5/blocks/en/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Subtract** can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nThe **subtract** block fits in blocks that accept circular spaces, and will accept circular block in it as well. \n\nSubtract two numbers.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/v5/blocks/en/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nSubtract with values from variables.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nSubtract with values from sensors or devices.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/en/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"temperature_of_motor":{"name":"temperature_of_motor","markdown":"# Temperature of motor\n\nReports the temperature of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n![temp_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nUsing the **temperature of motor** reporter block can help users develop logic to keep a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group from overheating during heavy use.\n\n**Temperature of motor** reports a range from **0% to 100%**. \n\nChoose which V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![temp_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nThe reporter block **temperature of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces. \n\n![temp_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Timer value\n\nReports the value of the V5 Brain's timer in seconds.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe timer starts at 0 seconds when the program starts, and reports the timer's value as a decimal value.\n\nThe reporter block **timer value** is used inside of blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n"},"timer_value_virtual":{"name":"timer_value_virtual","markdown":"# Timer value\n\nReports the value of the V5 Brain's timer in seconds.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/timer_value_virtual/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe timer starts at 0 seconds when the program starts, and reports the timer's value as a decimal value.\n\nThe reporter block **Timer value** is used inside of blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/timer_value_virtual/timerValue_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Timer value** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![timerValue_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/timer_value_virtual/timerValue_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![timerValue_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/timer_value_virtual/timerValue_monitor.png)"},"torque_of_motor":{"name":"torque_of_motor","markdown":"# Torque of motor\n\nReports the amount of torque (rotational force) a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group is currently using.\n\n![motor_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/en/torque_of_motor/motor_torque.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Torque of motor** reports a range from **0.0 to 18.6 inch-pounds (InLB)** or **0.0 to 2.1 Newton-meters (Nm)**. \n\nChoose which V5 Smart Motor's or Motor Group's torque to report.\n\n![motor_torque_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_device.png)\n\nChoose whether the **torque of motor** is reported in inch-pounds (InLb) or Newton-meters (Nm).\n\n![motor_torque_units](static/help/v5/blocks/en/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_units.png)\n\nThe reporter block **torque of motor** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![motor_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_inserted.png)"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Turn\n\nRotates the Drivetrain forever.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **turn** block will rotate the Drivetrain forever, until a new Drivetrain block is used, or the program is stopped.\n\nChoose the direction the Drivetrain will move.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Turn for\n\nRotates the Drivetrain for a given distance.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which direction the Drivetrain will turn.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\n\nSet how far the Drivetrain will move by entering a number of degrees.\n\nThe **Drive for** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Drivetrain is done turning.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Drivetrain turns.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Turn to heading\n\nTurns a Drivetrain to a specific heading, when using the Gyro sensor.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **turn to heading** block can be used to turn the Drivetrain to any given clockwise heading.\n\nBased on the current heading of the Gyro, **turn to heading** will determine which direction to turn.\n\n**Turn to heading** accepts a range of **0.00 to 359.99** degrees.\n\nThe **turn to heading** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns: \n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Right to 45 degrees\n- Right to 90 degrees\n- Right to 270 degrees\n- Left to 180 degrees\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Drivetrain is done turning.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Drivetrain turns.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Turn to rotation\n\nTurns a Drivetrain to a specific angle of rotation when configured with a 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **turn to rotation** block can be used to turn the Drivetrain to a given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\nBased on the current **rotation** value of the Drivetrain, **turn to rotation** will determine which direction to turn.\n\nThe **turn to rotation** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns: \n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Right (clockwise) to 90 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to 180 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to -45 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to 0 degrees\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Drivetrain is done turning.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Drivetrain turns.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/en/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Variable\n\nReports the numeric value assigned to the variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/variable/variable.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Variable** blocks are used to report a numeric value stored inside of the variable. Use the **set variable** block to set or update the numeric value of a variable.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nThe **variable** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nVariables are created using the **Make a Variable** button.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"variable_virtual":{"name":"variable_virtual","markdown":"# Variable\n\nReports the numeric value assigned to the variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/variable_virtual/variable.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Variable** blocks are used to report a numeric value stored inside of the variable. Use the **set variable** block to set or update the numeric value of a variable.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/variable_virtual/variable_cursor.png)\n\nThe **variable** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/variable_virtual/variable_inserted.png)\n\nVariables are created using the **Make a Variable** button.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/en/variable_virtual/make_variable.png)  \n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of a **variable** block, select the checkbox next to its reporter block.\n\n![variable_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/variable_virtual/variable_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the **variable** reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![variable_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/variable_virtual/variable_monitor.png)"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Velocity of motor\n\nReports the current velocity of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To use\n\n**Velocity of motor** reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-600rpm to 600rpm**.\n\n**Velocity of motor** will report a \"rotations per minute\" range based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in % or in revolutions per minute (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **velocity of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"velocity_of_motor_virtual":{"name":"velocity_of_motor_virtual","markdown":"# Velocity of motor\n\nReports the current velocity of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## How To use\n\n**Velocity of motor** reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-600rpm to 600rpm**.\n\n**Velocity of motor** will report a \"rotations per minute\" range based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nChoose which Motor or Motor Group to use.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in % or in revolutions per minute (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nThe reporter block **Velocity of motor** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)\n\n## Value Monitoring\n\nTo monitor the value of the **Velocity of motor** block, select the checkbox next to the reporter block.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_checkbox](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_checkbox.png)\n\nThen, open the Monitor Console to view the reporter blocks selected for monitoring.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_monitor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_motor_virtual/velocity_of_motor_monitor.png)"},"velocity_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"velocity_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Velocity of shaft encoder\n\nReports the current velocity of a Shaft Encoder.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Velocity of shaft encoder** reports a decimal value in either degrees per second (dps) or rotations per minute (rpm).\n\nChoose which Shaft Encoder to use.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_motor.png)\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in degrees per second (dps) or rotations per minute (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_unit.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Vision object\n\nReports information about a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use the **Vision object** block, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Devices window.\n2. Use **snapshot** to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use **object exists** to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code.\n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision blocks to learn more about the object detected.\n\n* Use **set vision object item** to set which detected object you want to learn more information about. By default, the largest object detected is used.\n* Use **object count** to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use **vision object** to determine which information to report from the detected object.\n\nSelect which Vision Sensor to use.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nSelect which value to report from the Vision Sensor:\n\n* Width - How wide the object is in pixels. Returns a value of **2 - 316 px**.\n* Height - How tall the object is in pixels. Returns a value of **2 - 212 px**. \n* CenterX - Reports the X coordinate of the center of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 315 px**.\n* CenterY - Reports the Y coordinate of the center of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 211 px**.\n* Angle - Reports the angle of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 180 degrees**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/en/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nThe reporter block **vision object** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Wait\n\nWaits for a specific amount of time before moving to the next block.\n\n![wait](static/help/v5/blocks/en/wait/wait.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose an amount of time to **wait**.\n\nThe **wait** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Wait until\n\nWaits for a Boolean block to report **true** before moving to the next block.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/v5/blocks/en/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Wait until** will repeatedly check a Boolean reporter block, and will not move to the next block until the Boolean report block reports **true**.\n\nThe **wait until** Boolean block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks.\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n"},"when_autonomous":{"name":"when_autonomous","markdown":"# When autonomous\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when an \"autonomous\" mode signal is received from a competition field or competition switch.\n\n![when_autonomous](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_autonomous/when_autonomous.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nAny blocks attached to the **when autonomous** event will be run when the robot is connected to a competition field or competition switch that is set to the \"autonomous\" mode.\n\nUsers can have up to 50 **when autonomous control** blocks in a project."},"when_brain_screen":{"name":"when_brain_screen","markdown":"# When brain screen\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the V5 Brain's touchscreen is pressed or released.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **when brain screen** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on touch interaction with the V5 Brain's touchscreen. \n\nUsed together with the **screen position** reporter block, users can create custom interfaces to their V5 Brain by detecting when and where touches occur on the screen.\n\nSelect which action will trigger the event - **pressed** or **released** \n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed_condition.png)"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# When I receive\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected message is received from a **broadcasted** message.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which message to listen for. A new message can also be created.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\nThe **when I receive** block will only be triggered to run from a **broadcast** or **broadcast and wait** block in a different stack."},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# When bumper\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected Bumper Switch sensor is pressed or released.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Bumper Switch to use.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nSelect which action will trigger the event - **pressed** or **released** \n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# When controller axis\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected V5 Controller joystick axis is moved.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which V5 Controller to use.\n\n![when_controller_axis_device](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_device.png)\n\nChoose which Controller joystick axis to use.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# When controller button\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected V5 Controller button is pressed or released.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which V5 Controller to use.\n\n![when_controller_button_controller](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_controller.png)\n\nChoose which Controller button to use.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\nSelect which action will trigger the event - **pressed** or **released** \n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_driver":{"name":"when_driver","markdown":"# When driver\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when a \"driver control\" mode signal is received from a competition field or competition switch.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_driver/when_driver.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nAny blocks attached to the **when driver control** event will be run when the robot is connected to a competition field or competition switch that is set to the \"driver control\" mode.\n\nA **forever** loop is highly recommended to be used with a **when driver control** event, to allow V5 Controller based commands to be frequently updated during the driver control portion of a match.\n\nUsers can have up to 50 **when driver control** blocks in a project."},"when_gps_heading_changed":{"name":"when_gps_heading_changed","markdown":"# When GPS heading changed\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when a GPS Sensor detects a heading change.\n\n![when_gps_heading_changed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_gps_heading_changed/when_gps_heading_changed_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **When GPS heading changed** event can be use to create actions or behaviors that can be triggered when a GPS Sensor detects a change in heading.\n\nChoose a GPS Sensor to detect a heading change on.\n\n![when_gps_heading_changed_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_gps_heading_changed/when_gps_heading_changed_block2.png)"},"when_limit":{"name":"when_limit","markdown":"# When limit\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the selected Limit Switch sensor is pressed or released.\n\n![when_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_limit/when_limit.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Limit Switch to use.\n\n![when_limit_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_limit/when_limit_select.png)\n\nSelect which action will trigger the event - **pressed** or **released** \n\n![when_limit_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_limit/when_limit_condition.png)\n"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# When started\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the project is started.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nA **when started** event will be run when the project is started from the V5 Brain's menu or from the **run** button in VEXcode V5.\n\nAll new projects will automatically include a **when started** block. Projects can support up to 50 **when started** blocks.\n\n**When started** will also act as the \"pre-autonomous\" mode's stack for a VRC Competition project.\n\n"},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# When timer\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the V5 Brain's timer is greater than the given value.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Brain's timer begins at the beginning of each project.\n\nChoose an amount of time. The **when timer** event will run once the Brain's timer is **greater than** the entered amount.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/v5/blocks/en/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nThe **when timer** block can accept decimals or integer values.\n\nThe **when timer** block **cannot** accept other reporter blocks."},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# While\n\nA 'C' block that repeats the blocks inside while the Boolean condition is reported to be **true**.  \n\n![while](static/help/v5/blocks/en/while/while.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **while** block will only check the Boolean condition at the beginning of each loop. \n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **true**, the blocks inside of **while** will run.\n\nIf the Boolean condition is reported as **false**, the blocks inside of **while** will be skipped.\n\nThe **while** 'C' block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks as its condition.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/en/while/while_inserted.png)"}},"python":{"control_break":{"name":"control_break","markdown":"# Break\n\nExits a repeating loop immediately.\n\n```python\nbreak\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen added inside of a loop, the `break` command will exit the loop it is currently running inside of. \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will drive the robot and check if its `bumper` has been pressed.\n\nIf the bumper is **pressed**, the `break` command will exit the `while` loop. The robot will then stop driving forward.\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n    if bumper.pressing():\n        break\n\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"break"},"control_elseif_statement":{"name":"control_elseif_statement","markdown":"# Elif\n\nA control flow statement that executes one block of commands if a condition evaluates to true. \n\n```python\nif condition:\n    pass\nelif condition2:\n    pass\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `elif` statement is a conditional that will check if its condition evaluates to **True** or **False**. It is possible to combine many conditions with the use of logical operators such as `and`, `or`, and `not`. \n\nIf the totality of the condition is **True** and all previous `if` and `elif` conditions are **False**, then the code block indented below the `elif condition:` will run.\n\nCode blocks below the `elif` should be indented four spaces.\n\nAn `elif` statement should not contain empty blocks of code. If necessary, add `pass` statements to a previously empty `elif` statement. \n\n## Example\n\nThis code will drive the robot FORWARD if the variable equals 1. If the variable equals -1, it will drive the robot REVERSE. If the variable is anything else it will stop the robot.\n\n```python\nmy_variable = 1\n\nif my_variable == 1:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nelif my_variable == -1:\n    drivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\nelse:\n    drivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"if condition:\\n\\tpass\\nelif condition:\\n\\tpass\\nelse:\\n\\tpass"},"control_for_loop":{"name":"control_for_loop","markdown":"# For\n\nA type of loop that repeats the code contained in its body for a set number of iterations.\n\n```don\nfor repeat_count in range(10):\n    pass\n```\n\n# How To Use\n\nFirst, replace `repeat_count` with a variable that will iterate through the `range()` function.\n\nSecond, replace `10` with a value to specify the end of the iteration.\n\nAdd a four-spaced indentation using the spacebar to include statements as part of the `for` control statement.\n\nA `for` statement should not contain an empty block of code. If necessary, add a `pass` statement to a previously empty for statement.\n\nNote that for loops start at the index 0 instead of 1.\n\n`For` loops can also be nested inside each other.\n\n# Example\nThe following for loop will print numbers 0 to 2:\n\n```don\nfor i in range(3):\n   brain.screen.print(i)\n   brain.screen.new_line()\n```\n   \nThis will print:\n\n```\n0\n1\n2\n```","signature":"for value in range (10"},"control_if_else_statement":{"name":"control_if_else_statement","markdown":"# If/else\nA control flow statement that executes one block of commands if a condition evaluates to true, or another block of commands if a condition evaluates to false. \n\n```don\nif condition:\n    pass\nelse:\n    pass\n\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `if` statement is a conditional that will check if its condition evaluates to **True** or **False**. It is possible to combine many conditions with the use of logical operators such as `and`, `or`, and `not`. \n\nIf the totality of the condition is **True**, then the code block indented below the `if condition:` will run. If the totality of the condition is **False**, the code block indented below the `else:` statement will run instead.\n\nCode blocks below the `if` and `else` should be indented four spaces.\n\nAn `if/else` statement should not contain empty blocks of code. If necessary, add  `pass` statements to a previously empty `if/else` statement. \n\n## Example\n\nThis `if/else` code will drive the robot FORWARD if the variable equals 1. If it does not, it will drive the robot REVERSE. \n\n```don\nif my_variable == 1:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nelse:\n    drivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"if conditio"},"control_if_statement":{"name":"control_if_statement","markdown":"# If\n\nA control statement used to decide whether a block of code will be executed based on the provided `condition`.\n\n```don\nif condition:\n    pass\n    \n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nReplace the word `condition` with an expression that can either evaluate to `True` or `False`. An evaluation to `True` will allow the statement(s) indented below the `if` statement to execute.\n\nAdd a four-spaced indentation using the **spacebar** to include statements as part of the `if` control statement. \n\nAn `if` statement should not contain an empty block of code. If necessary, add a `pass` statement to a previously empty `if` statement. \n\n## Example\n\nThis `if` statement will run if `my_variable` equals 1, causing the robot to drive forward.\n\n```don\nif my_variable == 1:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"if condition:\\n\\tpass"},"control_wait":{"name":"control_wait","markdown":"# Wait\n\nWaits for a specific amount of time before moving to the next command.\n\n```python\nwait(TIME, SECONDS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet an amount of time in **SECONDS** to have your program **wait** before executing subsequent commands.\n\n```python\nwait(10, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"wait(TIME, SECONDS)"},"control_wait_until":{"name":"control_wait_until","markdown":"# While Not\nA control statement that continues looping until the expression turns **true**.\n\n```python\nwhile not condition:\n    pass\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `while not` statement will repeatedly check the condition, and will not move to the next command until the condition reports **true.**\n\nIf the condition evaluates to **false**, the code inside of `while not` will run.\n\nIf the condition evaluates to **true**, the code inside of `while not` will be skipped, and the next command after the `while not` statement will be executed.\n\nThe `while not` statement accepts any expression that evaluates to `True` or `False` as its condition. You can place Booleans as well as expressions using comparison and logical operators. \n\nYou can also use numerical values; **0** evaluates to `False`, and any **non-zero numbers** evaluates to `True`. \n\nAdd a four-spaced indentation using the **spacebar** to include statements as part of the `while not` control statement. \n\nA `while not` statement should not contain an empty block of code. If necessary, add a `pass` statement to a previously empty `while not` statement. \n\n## Example\n\nThis `while not` loop will print \"Hello\" on separate lines until the value of my_variable is equal to 5.\n\n```python\nmy_variable = 0\n\nwhile not my_variable == 5:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\n    brain.screen.new_line()\n    my_variable += 1\n```","signature":"while not expressio"},"control_while_loop":{"name":"control_while_loop","markdown":"# While\nA loop that repeats the code in its body as long as the condition expression evaluates to **true**.   \n\n```python\nwhile condition:\n    pass\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `while` loop will only check the condition inside the parenthesis at the beginning of each loop. \n\nIf the condition evaluates to **true**, the code inside of `while` will run.\n\nIf the condition evaluates to **false**, the code inside of `while` will be skipped.\n\nThe `while` loop accepts anything that evaluates to `True` or `False` as its condition. You can place Booleans as well as expressions using comparison and logical operators. \n\nYou can also use numerical values; **0** evaluates to `False`, and any **non-zero numbers** evaluates to `True`. \n\nAdd a four-spaced indentation using the **spacebar** to include statements as part of the `while` control statement. \n\nA `while` statement should not contain an empty block of code. If necessary, add a `pass` statement to a previously empty `while` statement. \n\n## Example\n\nThis `while` loop will continue to print the word \"Hello\" on separate lines when the timer value is less than 50 seconds.\n\n```python\nwhile brain.timer.time(SECONDS) < 50:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n```","signature":"while expressio"},"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain":{"name":"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain","markdown":"# Drivetrain Calibrate\n\nCalibrates the Drivetrain's Inertial, GPS, or 3-Wire Gyro Sensor based on which device is currently configured with the Drivetrain.\n\n```python\ncalibrate_drivetrain()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain Calibrate` command will calibrate the Drivetrain's Inertial, GPS, or 3-Wire Gyro Sensor. The Drivetrain must remain stationary during the calibration process.","signature":"calibrate_drivetrain()"},"drivetrain_drive":{"name":"drivetrain_drive","markdown":"# Drive\n\nMoves the Drivetrain forever in the direction specified inside the parentheses. \n\nAll drivetrain motors run forward or in reverse at the velocity set using the `drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` command. The default velocity is 50%. \n\nNegative values will cause the Drivetrain to drive forward with a REVERSE input and in reverse with a FORWARD input.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `drivetrain.drive` command will run the Drivetrain forever, until a new drivetrain command is used, or the program is stopped.\n\n## Examples\n\nUse the `FORWARD` argument in all-capital letters to move the Drivetrain forward.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nUse the `REVERSE` argument in all-capital letters to move the Drivetrain in reverse.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.drive(FOWARD)"},"drivetrain_drive_for":{"name":"drivetrain_drive_for","markdown":"# Drive For\n\nMoves the Drivetrain for a given distance. All drivetrain motors run forward or in reverse at the velocity set by the `drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` command. After the Drivetrain has moved the input distance the Drivetrain will stop.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(DIRECTION, DISTANCE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet how far the Drivetrain will move by entering at least three valid arguments inside of the parentheses, separated by commas. \n\nThe first argument specifies the direction. Valid inputs are either `FORWARD` or `REVERSE` in all capital letters.  \n\nThe second argument specifies the distance that the V5 Robot should drive.\n\nThe third argument specifies the unit of measurement that should be used. Valid inputs are either `INCHES` or `MM` (millimeters) in all-capital letters.\n\nThe `DISTANCE` parameter accepts numeric values. Negative values will cause the V5 Robot to drive in the opposite of the input `DIRECTION`.\n\n```\ndrivetrain.drive_for(REVERSE, 5.0, INCHES)\n```\n\nThe `drive_for` command is by default a blocking command. It will prevent subsequent commands from executing until the Drivetrain movement has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameter\n\nYou can set a fourth parameter to `wait=False` to allow proceeding commands to run even before the Drivetrain is done moving.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM, wait=False)\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows the `drivetrain.drive_for` being used with a variable as a distance.\n\nThe V5 Robot will drive 200 MM forward.\n\n```don\ndistance_variable = 200\n\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, distance_variable, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 2, MM, wait=True)"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Set Drive Velocity\n\nSets the velocity of the Drivetrain for `drive` and `drive_for` commands.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` will set the Drivetrain's velocity when used with a `drive` or `drive_for` command. It will not cause the Drivetrain to move when used by itself.\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` accepts a range of values depending on what units are passed as the second parameter.\n\nIf `PERCENT` is used as the second parameter, **VELOCITY** accepts a range from **-100 to 100**.\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` can also use `RPM` as a valid **UNITS** parameter. Based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain, the range of acceptable **VELOCITY** values can vary.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to drive opposite of the `DIRECTION` passed into a `drive` or `drive_for` command.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to 0 will prevent the Drivetrain from moving even if a `drive` or `drive_for` command is used.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows that the Drivetrain will go in reverse due to a negative value.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nThis example will prevent the Drivetrain from moving.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(0, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_drive_velocity(VELOCITY, PRECENT)"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity_virtual":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity_virtual","markdown":"# Set Drive Velocity\n\nSets the velocity of the Drivetrain for `drive` and `drive_for` commands.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` will set the Drivetrain's velocity when used with a `drive` or `drive_for` command. It will not cause the Drivetrain to move when used by itself.\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` accepts a range of values depending on what units are passed as the second parameter.\n\nIf `PERCENT` is used as the second parameter, **VELOCITY** accepts a range from **-100 to 100**.\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` can also use `RPM` as a valid **UNITS** parameter. `drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` will accept a \"rotations per minute\" (RPM) value between -200 and 200.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to drive opposite of the `DIRECTION` passed into a `drive` or `drive_for` command.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to 0 will prevent the Drivetrain from moving even if a `drive` or `drive_for` command is used.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows that the Drivetrain will go in reverse due to a negative value.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nThis example will prevent the Drivetrain from moving.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(0, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_drive_velocity(VELOCITY, PRECENT)"},"drivetrain_set_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_set_heading","markdown":"# Set Heading\n\nSets the Gyro of the Drivetrain to an exact heading.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_heading(HEADING, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `drivetrain.set_heading` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's position to any given heading. This command can be used to reset the orientation of the Drivetrain's Gyro when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`drivetrain.set_heading` accepts a number value between **0 and 360** as it's first argument, and `DEGREES` written in all-capital letters as it's second argument.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example sets the Drivetrain heading to 90 degrees. \n\nSince the heading of the V5 Robot is set to 90 degrees, the subsequent `turn_to_heading` command will not cause the robot to turn as its current heading has already been set to 90 degrees.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_heading(90, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_set_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_rotation","markdown":"# Set Rotation\n\nSets the drivetrain's angle of rotation with a Gyro Sensor.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(ROTATION, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `drivetrain.set_rotation` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive or negative value.\n\nThe `ROTATION` parameter can accept numeric values.\n\nThe `ROTATION` parameter **does not** have a limit of 0-359 degrees.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will turn the robot a total of 210 degrees:\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(120, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(45, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Turn right (clockwise) to rotation 120 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current position as rotation of -45 degrees.\n- Turn right (clockwise) an additional 90 degrees (-45 degrees to +45 degrees) based on the set rotation value from the previous command.","signature":"drivetrain.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_set_stopping":{"name":"drivetrain_set_stopping","markdown":"# Set Stopping\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_stopping(MODE)\n```\n\n## How to Use\n\nReplace the `MODE` parameter with one of the following options:\n\n* BRAKE: will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop.\n* COAST: lets the Drivetrain slow gradually to a stop.\n* HOLD: will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved. \n\nThe brake mode applied by the `drivetrain.set_stopping()` command will be used for subsequent Drivetrain commands in the program unless otherwise changed.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows the robot driving forward for 200 MM before coasting to a stop.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_stopping(COAST)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_stopping(BRAKE)"},"drivetrain_set_timeout":{"name":"drivetrain_set_timeout","markdown":"# Set Timeout\n\nSets a time limit for the Drivetrain movement commands.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)\n```\n\n## How to Use\n\nThe command is used to prevent movement commands that do not reach their position from preventing other proceeding commands from running.\n\nSpecify the amount of time in `SECONDS`.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below sets the timeout of the Drivetrain to 3 seconds.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_timeout(3, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 1000, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity_percent":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity_percent","markdown":"# Set Turn Velocity\n\nSets the Drivetrain's turn velocity.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` will set the velocity of the Drivetrain when turning, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move when used without a `turn` or `turn_for` command.\n\n`drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` accepts a range of values depending on what units are passed as the second parameter.\n\nIf `PERCENT` is used as the second parameter, **VELOCITY** accepts a range from **-100 to 100**.\n\nAlternatively, `drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` can also use `RPM` as a valid **UNITS** parameter. Based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain, the range of acceptable **VELOCITY** values can vary.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to turn in the opposite of the direction passed into any following turn commands.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to 0 will prevent the Drivetrain from turning, even when using a `turn` or `turn_for` command.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the Drivetrain will turn in the opposite direction (LEFT) due to a negative value.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_turn_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity_percent_virtual":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity_percent_virtual","markdown":"# Set Turn Velocity\n\nSets the Drivetrain's turn velocity.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` will set the velocity of the Drivetrain when turning, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move when used without a `turn` or `turn_for` command.\n\n`drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` accepts a range of values depending on what units are passed as the second parameter.\n\nIf `PERCENT` is used as the second parameter, **VELOCITY** accepts a range from **-100 to 100**.\n\nAlternatively, `drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` can also use `RPM` as a valid **UNITS** parameter. `drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` will accept a \"rotations per minute\" (RPM) value between -200 and 200.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to turn in the opposite of the direction passed into any following turn commands.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to 0 will prevent the Drivetrain from turning, even when using a `turn` or `turn_for` command.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the Drivetrain will turn in the opposite direction (LEFT) due to a negative value.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_turn_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)"},"drivetrain_stop":{"name":"drivetrain_stop","markdown":"# Stop\n\nStops the Drivetrain.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `drivetrain.stop()` command stops the Drivetrain. It does not take any arguments in its parentheses.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will stop the Drivetrain after the V5 Robot has driven forward for 3 seconds.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"drivetrain.stop()"},"drivetrain_turn":{"name":"drivetrain_turn","markdown":"# Turn\n\nTurns the Drivetrain to the right or left.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `drivetrain.turn` command will rotate the Drivetrain in the given direction forever until a new drivetrain command is used, or until the program is stopped.\n\nUse the `LEFT` argument in all-capital letters to turn the Drivetrain to the left.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(LEFT)\n```\n\nUse the `RIGHT` argument in all-capital letters to turn the Drivetrain to the right.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the robot will drive forward 200 MM before turning right indefinitely.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn(RIGHT)"},"drivetrain_turn_for":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_for","markdown":"# Turn For\n\nTurns the Drivetrain for a specified number of degrees.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(DIRECTION, ANGLE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe first argument specifies the turn direction: `LEFT` or `RIGHT`, written in all-capital letters. \n\nThe second argument specifies the turn angle as a numeric value; this can be any number between 0 and 360. \n\nThe third argument is the turn units. This should be set as `DEGREES` in all-capital letters. \n\nThe `turn_for` command is by default a blocking command. It prevents any proceeding code from executing until the Drivetrain has completed its turn.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nIf the fourth argument is set to `wait=False`, proceeding commands will be allowed to execute even before the Drivetrain has completed its turn.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(LEFT, 90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will turn the V5 Robot 270 degrees to the right.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 270, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 90, DEGREES, wait=True)"},"drivetrain_turn_to_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Turn To Heading\n\nTurns the Drivetrain to a specific heading when using the Gyro or Inertial sensors.\n\n`drivetrain.turn_to_heading(HEADING, UNITS)`\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `drivetrain.turn_to_heading` command can be used to turn the Drivetrain to any given clockwise heading.\n\nBased on the current Gyro heading, `drivetrain.turn_to_heading` will determine which direction to turn.\n\nThe `HEADING` parameter accepts numeric values in the range of **0.00 to 359.99** .\n\nThe `UNITS` parameter should be set to `DEGREES`.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns: \n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(45.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(270.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(180.0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Right to 45 degrees\n- Right to 90 degrees\n- Right to 270 degrees\n- Left to 180 degrees\n\nThe `turn_to_heading` command will by default block proceeding commands until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `wait=False` as a third parameter to prevent the `turn_to_heading` command from blocking proceeding commands from executing until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(180.0, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Turn To Rotation\n\nTurns the Drivetrain to a specific angle of rotation.\n\n`drivetrain.turn_to_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)`\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `drivetrain.turn_to_rotation` command can be used to turn the Drivetrain to a given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\nBased on the current rotation of the Drivetrain, `drivetrain.turn_to_rotation` will determine which direction to turn.\n\nThe `ROTATION` parameter can accept numeric values.\n\nNumeric values are **not** limited to the range of **0 - 359.99** degrees. Turns will be absolute and may cause the robot to rotate more than once if necessary.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns:\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(180, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Right (clockwise) to 90 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to 180 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to -45 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to 0 degrees\n\nThe `drivetrain.turn_to_rotation`command will by default block proceeding commands until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameter\n\nYou can set a third parameter to  `wait=False` to prevent the `turn_to_rotation` command from blocking proceeding commands until the Drivetrain turn is completed.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(180.0, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90, DEGREES, wait=True)"},"events_brain_screen_pressed":{"name":"events_brain_screen_pressed","markdown":"#  Brain Screen Pressed\n\nRuns the callback function when the V5 Brain’s touchscreen is pressed.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.pressed()` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors based on touch interaction with the V5 Brain's touchscreen. \n\nUsed together with the `brain.screen.x_position()` and `brain.screen.y_position()` commands, users can create custom interfaces to their V5 Brain by detecting when and where touches occur on the screen.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the screen gets pressed. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_event():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Event has occurred\")\n  \n# Register event with a callback function\nbrain.screen.pressed(run_on_event)\n\n```","signature":"brain.screen.pressed(callback)"},"events_brain_screen_released":{"name":"events_brain_screen_released","markdown":"#  Brain Screen Released\n\nRuns the callback function when the V5 Brain’s touchscreen is released.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.released(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.released()` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors based on touch interaction with the V5 Brain's touchscreen. \n\nUsed together with the `brain.screen.x_position()` and `brain.screen.y_position()` commands, users can create custom interfaces to their V5 Brain by detecting when and where touches occur on the screen.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the screen gets released. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_event():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Event has occurred\")\n  \n# Register event with a callback function\nbrain.screen.released(run_on_event)\n```","signature":"brain.screen.released(callback)"},"events_brain_timer_event":{"name":"events_brain_timer_event","markdown":"# Brain Timer Event\n\nRuns the specified callback function when the V5 Brain's timer is greater than the given value.\n\n```python\nbrain.timer.event(callback, 1000)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 Brain's timer begins at the beginning of each project.\n\nSpecify the amount of time. The `brain.timer.event()` event will run once the V5 Brain's timer is **greater than** the entered amount.\n\nThe `brain.timer.event()` command can accept integer values for the number of milliseconds.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the timer is greater than the entered amount. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_event():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Event has occurred\")\n  \n# Register event with a callback function\nbrain.timer.event(run_on_event, 2000)\n```","signature":"brain.timer.event(callback, 1000)"},"events_bumper_pressed":{"name":"events_bumper_pressed","markdown":"# Bumper Pressed\n\nRuns the specified function when the bumper is pressed.\n\n```python\nbumper.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Bumper Sensor is pressed. \n\nProvide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_bumper_pressed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Bumper pressed!\")\n \n# Register event with a callback function\nbumper_a.pressed(run_on_bumper_pressed)\n```","signature":"bumper.pressed(callback)"},"events_bumper_released":{"name":"events_bumper_released","markdown":"# Bumper Released\n\nRuns the specified function when the bumper is released.\n\n```python\nbumper.released(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Bumper Sensor is released. \n\nProvide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_bumper_released():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Bumper released!\")\n \n# Register event with a callback function\nbumper_a.released(run_on_bumper_released)\n```","signature":"bumper.released(callback)"},"events_competition_autonomous":{"name":"events_competition_autonomous","markdown":"# Competition Autonomous\n\nRuns the specified function when an \"autonomous\" mode signal is received from a competition switch.\n\n```python\ndef autonomous():\n    pass\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA new competition instance can be created by passing a **driver_control** and **autonomous** callback functions.\n\nCreate an **autonomous** function to pass to a competition instance. \n\nThe specified **autonomous** function will run when an \"autonomous\" mode signal is received from a competition switch.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the \"driver control\" signal is received\ndef driver_control():\n    brain.screen.print(\"driver control signal received\")\n\n# Function to run when the \"autonomous\" signal is received\ndef autonomous():\n    brain.screen.print(\"autonomous signal received\")\n\n# Create a new Competition instance\ncompetition = Competition(driver_control, autonomous)\n```","signature":"def autonomous():\\n\\tpass"},"events_competition_drivercontrol":{"name":"events_competition_drivercontrol","markdown":"# Competition Driver Control\n\nRuns the specified function when a \"driver control\" mode signal is received from a competition switch.\n\n```python\ndef driver_control():\n    pass\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA new competition instance can be created by passing a **driver_control** and **autonomous** callback functions.\n\nCreate a **driver_control** function to pass to a competition instance. \n\nThe specified **driver_control** function will run when a \"driver control\" mode signal is received from a competition switch.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the \"driver control\" signal is received\ndef driver_control():\n    brain.screen.print(\"driver control signal received\")\n\n# Function to run when the \"autonomous\" signal is received\ndef autonomous():\n    brain.screen.print(\"autonomous signal received\")\n\n# Create a new Competition instance\ncompetition = Competition(driver_control, autonomous)\n```","signature":"def driver_control():\\n\\tpass"},"events_competition_new_competition":{"name":"events_competition_new_competition","markdown":"# New Competition\n\nCreate a new competition instance.\n\n```python\ncompetition = Competition(driver_control, autonomous)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA new competition instance can be created by passing a **driver_control** and **autonomous** callback functions.\n\nWhen a **driver control** signal is received from a competition switch, the **driver_control** callback function will be executed.\n\nSimilarly, when an **autonomous** signal is received from a competition switch, the **autonomous** callback function will be executed.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the \"driver control\" signal is received\ndef driver_control():\n    brain.screen.print(\"driver control signal received\")\n\n# Function to run when the \"autonomous\" signal is received\ndef autonomous():\n    brain.screen.print(\"autonomous signal received\")\n\n# Create a new Competition instance\ncompetition = Competition(driver_control, autonomous)\n```","signature":"competition = Competition(driver_control, autonomous)"},"events_controller_axis_changed":{"name":"events_controller_axis_changed","markdown":"# Controller Axis Changed\n\nRuns the specified function when the controller axis position changes.\n\n```python\ncontroller.axis.changed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller axis to monitor.\n\n* `axis1`\n* `axis2`\n* `axis3`\n* `axis4`\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Controller Axis position is changed. \n\nProvide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_axis_changed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Axis changed!\")\n\n  \n# Register event with a callback function.\ncontroller_1.axis1.changed(run_on_axis_changed)\n```","signature":"controller.axis.changed(callback)"},"events_controller_button_pressed":{"name":"events_controller_button_pressed","markdown":"# Controller Button Pressed\n\nRuns the specified function when the controller button is pressed.\n\n```python\ncontroller.button.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller Button to monitor.\n\n* `buttonA`\n* `buttonB`\n* `buttonX`\n* `buttonY`\n* `buttonUp`\n* `buttonDown`\n* `buttonLeft`\n* `buttonRight`\n* `buttonL1`\n* `buttonL2`\n* `buttonR1`\n* `buttonR2`\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Controller Button is pressed. \n\nProvide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_button_pressed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Button pressed!\")\n\n# Register event with a callback function.\ncontroller_1.buttonA.pressed(run_on_button_pressed)\n```","signature":"controller.button.pressed(callback)"},"events_controller_button_released":{"name":"events_controller_button_released","markdown":"# Controller Button Released\n\nRuns the specified function when the controller button is released.\n\n```python\ncontroller.button.released(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller Button to monitor.\n\n* `buttonA`\n* `buttonB`\n* `buttonX`\n* `buttonY`\n* `buttonUp`\n* `buttonDown`\n* `buttonLeft`\n* `buttonRight`\n* `buttonL1`\n* `buttonL2`\n* `buttonR1`\n* `buttonR2`\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Controller Button is released. \n\nProvide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_button_released():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Button released!\")\n\n# Register event with a callback function.\ncontroller_1.buttonA.released(run_on_button_released)\n```","signature":"controller.button.released(callback)"},"events_event":{"name":"events_event","markdown":"# Event Register Callback\n\nRegister a callback function to run when an event is triggered.\n\n```python\nevent(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nRegister a callback to a user-defined event.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"my_event triggered run_on_broadcast callback\")\n  \n# Create a new event.\nmy_event = Event()\n\n# Register a callback function to the myEvent event.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the event.\nmy_event.broadcast()\n```","signature":"EVENT(callback);"},"events_event_broadcast":{"name":"events_event_broadcast","markdown":"# Event Broadcast\n\nBroadcast event message to run listener functions.\n\n```python\nevent.broadcast()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe code will continue to run the commands after the `event.broadcast()` command so that it will run at the same time as the event listener functions.\n\nBefore using this command, a user defined event must be created and register at least one callback.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast1():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\")\n\ndef run_on_broadcast2():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(2, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\")\n  \n# Create a new event.\nmy_event = Event()\n\n# Register callback functions to event.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast1)\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast2)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the event.\nmy_event.broadcast()\n\n```","signature":"my_event.broadcast()"},"events_event_broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Event Broadcast and Wait\n\nBroadcast event message to run listener functions and wait for all listeners to finish before continuing.\n\n```cpp\nevent.broadcast_and_wait()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `event.broadcast_and_wait()` command will wait for all listeners to complete before returning. This will pause the code execution in the current function, until all the broadcast listeners have finished.\n\nBefore using this command, a user defined event must be created and register at least one callback.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast1():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\")\n\ndef run_on_broadcast2():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(2, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\")\n\n# Create a new event.\nmy_event = Event()\n\n# Register callback functions to event.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast1)\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast2)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the event and wait for completion.\nmy_event.broadcast_and_wait()\n\nbrain.screen.set_cursor(3, 1)\nbrain.screen.print(\"Listeners finished running\")\n```","signature":"my_event.broadcast_and_wait()"},"events_event_new_event":{"name":"events_event_new_event","markdown":"# New Event\n\nCreate a new event.\n\n```python\nmy_event = Event()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nUsing the above syntax, a new user-defined event can be created before registering callback functions.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast1():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\")\n\ndef run_on_broadcast2():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(2, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\")\n\n# Create new events.\nmy_event1 = Event()\nmy_event2 = Event()\n\n# Register callback functions to the events.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event1(run_on_broadcast1)\nmy_event2(run_on_broadcast2)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the events.\nmy_event1.broadcast()\nmy_event2.broadcast()\n```","signature":"my_event = Event()"},"events_gps_heading_changed":{"name":"events_gps_heading_changed","markdown":"# GPS When Heading Changed\n\nRuns the specified callback function when a GPS Sensor detects a heading change.\n\n```python\ngps.changed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to define a function to call when the GPS Sensor detects a heading change.\n\nProvide the name of the defined function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_heading_change():\n    brain.screen.print(\"GPS Heading Change Detected\")\n\n# Register event with a callback function\ngps.changed(run_on_heading_change)\n```","signature":"gps.changed(callback)"},"events_limit_pressed":{"name":"events_limit_pressed","markdown":"# Limit Pressed\n\nRuns the specified function when the Limit Switch is pressed.\n\n```python\nlimit.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Limit Switch is pressed. \n\nProvide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_limit_pressed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Limit pressed!\")\n \n# Register event with a callback function\nlimit_a.pressed(run_on_limit_pressed)\n```","signature":"limit.pressed(callback)"},"events_limit_released":{"name":"events_limit_released","markdown":"# Limit Released\n\nRuns the specified function when the Limit Switch is released.\n\n```python\nlimit.released(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Limit Switch is released. \n\nProvide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_limit_released():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Limit released!\")\n \n# Register event with a callback function\nlimit_a.released(run_on_limit_released)\n```","signature":"limit.released(callback)"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_down":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_down","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_down(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `optical.gesture_enable()` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gesture_up`\n- `gesture_down`\n- `gesture_left`\n- `gesture_right`\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_gesture_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Gesture detected!\")\n\n# Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\noptical.gesture_enable()\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.gesture_down(run_on_gesture_detected)\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_down(callback)"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_left":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_left","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_left(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `optical.gesture_enable()` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gesture_up`\n- `gesture_down`\n- `gesture_left`\n- `gesture_right`\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_gesture_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Gesture detected!\")\n\n# Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\noptical.gesture_enable()\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.gesture_left(run_on_gesture_detected)\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_left(callback)"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_right":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_right","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_right(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `optical.gesture_enable()` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gesture_up`\n- `gesture_down`\n- `gesture_left`\n- `gesture_right`\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_gesture_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Gesture detected!\")\n\n# Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\noptical.gesture_enable()\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.gesture_right(run_on_gesture_detected)\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_right(callback)"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_up":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_up","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_up(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `optical.gesture_enable()` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gesture_up`\n- `gesture_down`\n- `gesture_left`\n- `gesture_right`\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_gesture_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Gesture detected!\")\n\n# Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\noptical.gesture_enable()\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.gesture_up(run_on_gesture_detected)\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_up(callback)"},"events_optical_object_detected":{"name":"events_optical_object_detected","markdown":"# Optical Object Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when an object is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.object_detected(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `optical.object_detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when an object is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when an object is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_object_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Object detected!\")\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.object_detected(run_on_object_detected)\n```","signature":"optical.object_detected(callback)"},"events_optical_object_lost":{"name":"events_optical_object_lost","markdown":"# Optical Object Lost\n\nRuns the callback function when an object is no longer being detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.object_lost(callback)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `optical.object_lost` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when an object is no longer being detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when an object is no longer being detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_object_lost():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Object lost!\")\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.object_lost(run_on_object_lost)\n```","signature":"optical.object_lost(callback)"},"function_name":{"name":"function_name","markdown":"# Functions\n\nFunctions are blocks of code used to perform an action.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a function, create a meaningful function name. This means that the function name should accurately describe what it does.\n\nUse the **keyword** `def` before your function name to define the function.\n\nInclude parentheses `()` enclosing optional parameters after the function name, followed by a colon`:`. Multiple parameters should be separated by commas `(parameter1, parameter2)`.\n\nThe body of the function should be indented four spaces. If there isn't any code for the function to execute, a `pass` should be included in the function definition.\n\n```don\ndef my_function():\n    pass\n```\n\n## Example 1\n\nThis function has no parameters and will print \"Hello\" to the V5 Brain Screen.\n\n```don\ndef print_hello_world():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello World\")\n```\n## Example 2\n\nThis function takes one parameter, `name` and will print the value of `name` to the V5 Brain Screen.\n\n```don\ndef print_name(name):\n    brain.screen.print(name)\n```","signature":"def function_name(parameters):\\n\\tpass"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Clear Row\n\nClears a single row on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```python \nbrain.screen.clear_row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\nClears the current row on the V5 Brain screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.clear_row()\n```\n\nClears a specified row on the V5 Brain screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.clear_row(ROW)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.clear_row()` command can accept integer values between **1 - 20**, to set which row to clear. You can also call the command without any arguments to clear the current row.\n\n---\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.clear_line()"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Clear All Rows\n \nClears the entire V5 Brain screen.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`brain.screen.clear_screen()` will not change the screen's cursor. You will need to use `brain.screen.set_cursor()` command to set the screen's cursor to a specific position.","signature":"brain.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen_virtual":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen_virtual","markdown":"# Clear All Rows\n \nClears the entire Print Console and resets the cursor to the first row.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n```python\n# Print \"VEXcode V5\" on the first line, wait 2 seconds, then clear the Print Console\nbrain.screen.print(\"VEXcode V5\")\nwait(2, SECONDS)\nbrain.screen.clear_screen()\n```","signature":"brain.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle","markdown":"# Draw Circle\n\nDraws a circle on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_circle(X, Y, RADIUS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.draw_circle()` command requires 3 values:\n\n* Value 1: Center Point X\n* Value 2: Center Point Y\n* Value 3: Radius of Circle (in pixels)\n\nThe outside line color of the circle is determined by the `brain.screen.set_pen_color()` command. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the circle is determined by the `brain.screen.set_fill_color()` command. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_circle(1, 1, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_line","markdown":"# Draw Line\n\nDraws a line on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_line(START_X, START_Y, END_X, END_Y)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.draw_line()` command requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Beginning X coordinate\n* Value 2: Beginning Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Ending X coordinate\n* Value 4: Ending Y coordinate\n\nThe line color is determined by the `brain.screen.set_pen_color()` command. The default line color is white.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_line(1, 1, 10, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel","markdown":"# Draw Pixel\n\nDraws a pixel on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_pixel(X, Y)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.draw_pixel` command requires 2 values:\n\n* Value 1: X Coodinate\n* Value 2: Y Coodinate\n\nThe pixel color is determined by the `brain.screen.set_pen_color()` command. The default pixel color is white.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_pixel(1, 1)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Draw Rectangle\n\nDraws a rectangle on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_rectangle(X, Y, WIDTH, HEIGHT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.draw_rectangle()` command requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Top Left Corner X coordinate\n* Value 2: Top Left Corner Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Width of the rectangle\n* Value 4: Height of the rectangle\n\nThe border line color of the rectangle is determined by the `brain.screen.set_pen_color()` command. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the rectangle is determine by the `brain.screen.set_fill_color()` command. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_rectangle(1, 1, 10, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Next Row\n\nSets the print output cursor on the V5 Brain's screen to the next available row.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.next_row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1. The `brain.screen.next_row()` command will move the cursor down by a single row on the screen. `brain.screen.next_row()` will also set the cursor's column to position 1.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 Rows (Default)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Rows\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_brain_screen_new_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.new_line()"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line_virtual":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line_virtual","markdown":"# Next Row\n\nSets the print output cursor of the Print Console to the next line.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.next_row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the print cursor at row 1. The `brain.screen.next_row()` command will move the cursor down by a single line on the Print Console.\n\n---\n\n```python\n# Print \"VEXcode\" on the first line, then \"V5\" on the next line\nbrain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")\nbrain.screen.next_row()\nbrain.screen.print(\"V5\")\n```","signature":"brain.screen.new_line()"},"looks_brain_screen_print":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.print()` command will print data at a cursor location on the screen.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1.\n\n* Print words and numbers: \n`brain.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n\n* Print the reported value from a variable: \n`brain.screen.print(my_variable)`\n\n* Print the reported value from a sensor or device:  \n`brain.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`","signature":"brain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")"},"looks_brain_screen_print_virtual":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print_virtual","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text to the Print Console.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.print()` command will print data to the Print Console.\n\n* Print words and numbers: \n`brain.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n\n* Print numbers with decimal points:\n```brain.screen.print(\"Timer Value:\", brain.timer.time(SECONDS), precision=2)```\n\n* Print the reported value from a variable: \n`brain.screen.print(my_variable)`\n\n* Print the reported value from a sensor or device:  \n`brain.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`","signature":"brain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")"},"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Set Cursor\n\n\nSets the cursor location on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_cursor(ROW, COLUMN)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.set_cursor()` command requires 2 values:\n\n* Value 1: Screen row position \n* Value 2: Screen column position\n\nSet the cursor's row and column position to have a `brain.screen.print()` command display at a specific location on the screen.\n\nAccepts a range for **row** of **1 to 20**.\n\nAccepts a range for **column** of **1 to 80**.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 Rows (Default)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Rows\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 80 Columns\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 68 Columns\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 48 Columns (Default)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 32 Columns\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 24 Columns\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.MONO60` - 16 Columns\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color","markdown":"# Set Fill Color\n\nSets the color that fills in shapes drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_fill_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.set_fill_color()` command is used to set the color of the inside of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\nReplace the `COLOR` parameter with one of the following actions:\n\n* `Color.BLACK`\n* `Color.WHITE`\n* `Color.RED`\n* `Color.GREEN`\n* `Color.BLUE`\n* `Color.YELLOW`\n* `Color.ORANGE`\n* `Color.PURPLE`\n* `Color.CYAN`\n* `Color.TRANSPARENT`\n\nThe fill color will be used for any subsequent objects drawn on the V5 Brain's screen until it is changed again.","signature":"brain.screen.set_fill_color(Color.RED)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_font":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_font","markdown":"# Set Font\n\nSets the style and size of font used on the V5 Brain's screen when printing values.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_font(FONT_TYPE)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThere are two different types of fonts available on the V5 Brain's screen:\n\n* Monospaced (MONO) - each character takes up the same width.\n* Proportional (PROP) - each character takes up different size widths based on the character.\n\nChoose which font type and size to use by replacing the `FONT_TYPE` parameter. You can select from the following font options.\n\n* `FontType.MONO12`\n* `FontType.MONO15`\n* `FontType.MONO20`\n* `FontType.MONO30`\n* `FontType.MONO40`\n* `FontType.MONO60`\n* `FontType.PROP20`\n* `FontType.PROP30`\n* `FontType.PROP40`\n* `FontType.PROP60`\n\nThe new font size will be used for any future text written to the V5 Brain's screen until it is changed again.","signature":"brain.screen.set_font(FontType.MONO20)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color","markdown":"# Set Pen Color\n\nSets the color of lines drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.set_pen_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.set_pen_color()` command is used to set the color of lines, pixels, and text drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\n`brain.screen.set_pen_color()` can also be used to set the outline color of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\nReplace the `COLOR` parameter with one of the following options:\n\n* `Color.BLACK`\n* `Color.WHITE`\n* `Color.RED`\n* `Color.GREEN`\n* `Color.BLUE`\n* `Color.YELLOW`\n* `Color.ORANGE`\n* `Color.PURPLE`\n* `Color.CYAN`\n* `Color.TRANSPARENT`\n\nThe pen color will be used for any subsequent objects drawn on the V5 Brain's screen until it is changed again.","signature":"brain.screen.set_pen_color(COLOR)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width","markdown":"# Set Pen Width\n\nSets the width of the outline for shapes drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_pen_width(PEN_WIDTH)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `brain.screen.set_pen_width()` command is used to set the width of the line on the outside of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\nThe `brain.screen.set_pen_width()` command can accept integer values, with a larger value equating to a larger width. Replace the `PEN_WIDTH` parameter with an integer value.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.set_pen_width(10)"},"looks_console_clear_console":{"name":"looks_console_clear_console","markdown":"# Console Clear\n\nClears the Print Console.\n\n```python\nprint(\"\\033[2J\")\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `print` command used with the `\\033[2J` command sequence will clear the Print Console.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will print \"VEXcode\" and then clear the Print Console after 3 seconds.\n\n```python\nprint(\"\\033[31mVEXcode\")\nwait(3, SECONDS)\nprint(\"\\033[2J\")\n```","signature":"print(\"\\033[2J\")"},"looks_console_print":{"name":"looks_console_print","markdown":"# Console Print\n\nPrints values or text to the Print Console.\n\n```python\nprint(\"VEXcode\")\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `print` command will print data at the cursor location on the Print Console.\n\nAll new projects begin with the cursor at row 1.\n\n## Printing Lines\n\nBy default, Python will always add a new line after each `print` command.\n\nTo print multiple values to a single line, you can utilize the `end` parameter.\n\n```python\nprint(\"This text will be \", end=\"\")\nprint(\"printed on the same line\")\n```\n\n## Printing Values\n\nYou can use the Python `format` method to format the values being printed in the print statements.\n\nTo use the `format` method, you must first provide a template string with replacement fields enclosed by a set of curly braces - `{}`.\n\nThen, call the `format` method on the template string. Any parameter(s) passed into the `format` method will be inserted into the replacement fields in sequence (if there are multiple replacement fields).\n\nYou can also provide formatting options into the template string to set the number of decimal places to be printed. Any formatting options must begin with a semicolon - `:`.\n\nIn the example below, the value of the Brain Timer will be inserted into the single replacement field in the template string and printed to two decimal places.\n\n```python\nprint(\"{:.2f}\".format(brain.timer.time(SECONDS)))\n```\n\nSimilarly, the example below will print the row/column position of the Brain Cursor. The number of replacement fields (enclosed by `{}`) must match the number of parameters passed into the `format` method.\n\n```python\n# The value of brain.screen.row() will be passed into the first replacement field\n# The value of brain.screen.column() will be passed into the second replacement field\nprint(\"Row: {:d}, Column: {:d}\".format(brain.screen.row(), brain.screen.column()))\n```\n\nHere is a list of commonly-used format specifiers. Remember that to use a format specifier inside a replacement field (enclosed by `{}`), it must follow a semicolon - `:`.\n\n* `d` - Decimal Integer\n* `f` - Floating Point Number\n* `o` - Octal Integer\n* `s` - String\n\nUsing the Floating Point Number format specifier, `f`, you can also specify how many decimal places to format a number.\n\n* `.2f` - Formats a floating point number with 2 decimal places\n* `.4f` - Formats a floating point number with 4 decimal places\n\n## Printing Colors\n\nYou can use any of the color codes below with a `print` command to set the color of the text being printed.\n\nThe example below will show two ways in which a color sequence command can be used when printing. All color codes will need to be attached to an escape sequence - `\\033`.\n\n* `[31m` - Red\n* `[32m` - Green\n* `[34m` - Blue\n* `[30m` - Black\n* `[37m` - White\n* `[33m` - Yellow\n* `[91m` - Orange\n* `[35m` - Purple\n* `[36m` - Cyan\n* `[97m` - Transparent\n\n```python\n# Using color codes in-line\n# This will print \"VEXcode\" in Red to the Print Console\nprint(\"\\033[31mVEXcode\")\n\n# Using color codes in separate commands\n# Sets the print color for any subsequent prints\nprint(\"\\033[31m\")\nprint(\"VEXcode\")\n```","signature":"print(\"VEXcode\")"},"looks_controller_rumble":{"name":"looks_controller_rumble","markdown":"# Rumble Controller\n\nTriggers a vibrating effect on your V5 Controller.\n\n```python\ncontroller.rumble(\".-.-\")\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `controller.rumble(\".-.-\")` command uses the rumble motor in your V5 controller to provide feedback.\n\nYou can create any pattern you want using a combination of \".\" and \"-\" characters in the string. The \".\" character will create a short rumble. The \"-\" character will create a long rumble.","signature":"controller.rumble(\"-.-.\")"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Clear Row\n\nClears the current row on the V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_row()\n```\n\nClears a specified row on the V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_row(ROW)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `controller.screen.clear_row()` command can accept integer values between **1 - 3**, to set which row to clear. You can also call the command without any arguments to clear the current row.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_controller_screen_clear_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.clear_line()"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Clear All Rows\n\nClears the entire V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`controller.screen.clear_screen()` will not change the screen's cursor. \n\nUse the `controller.screen.set_cursor()` command to set the screen's cursor to a specific position.","signature":"controller.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_controller_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Next Row\n\nSets the print output cursor on the V5 Controller's screen to the next available row.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.next_row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1. The `controller.screen.next_row()` command will move the cursor down by a single row on the screen. `controller.screen.next_row()` will also set the cursor's column to position 1.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* Standard Font - 20 Columns (Default)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_controller_screen_new_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.new_line()"},"looks_controller_screen_print":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_print","markdown":"# Print  \n\nPrints values on the V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.print(\"VEXcode\") \n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `controller.screen.print()` command will print data at a cursor location on the screen.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1.\n\n* Print words and numbers: \n`controller.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n\n* Print the reported value from a variable:  \n`controller.screen.print(my_variable)`\n\n* Print the reported value from a sensor or device: \n`controller.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`","signature":"controller.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")"},"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Set Cursor\n\n\nSets the cursor location for **controller.screen.print()** command on the V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.set_cursor(ROW, COLUMN)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `controller.screen.set_cursor()` command requires 2 values:\n\n* Value 1: Screen row position \n* Value 2: Screen column position\n\nSet the cursor's row and column position to have a `controller.screen.print()` command display at a specific location on the screen.\n\n`controller.screen.set_cursor()` accepts a range for **row** of **1 to 3**.\n\n`controller.screen.set_cursor()` accepts a range for **column** of **1 to 20**.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* Standard Font - 20 Columns (Default)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/en/looks_controller_screen_set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)"},"looks_led_off":{"name":"looks_led_off","markdown":"# LED Off\n\nTurns a 3-Wire LED off.\n\n```python\nled.off()\n```","signature":"led.off()"},"looks_led_on":{"name":"looks_led_on","markdown":"# LED On\n\nTurns a 3-wire LED on.\n\n```python\nled.on()\n```","signature":"led.on()"},"looks_led_set":{"name":"looks_led_set","markdown":"# LED On/Off\n\nTurns a LED on or off.\n\n```don\nled.on()\n```\n```don\nled.off()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`led.on()` turns on the LED device.\n\n`led.off()` turns off the LED device.","signature":"led.set(False)"},"looks_monitor_sensor":{"name":"looks_monitor_sensor","markdown":"# Monitor Sensor\n\nThe `monitor_sensor()` command is used to add sensors to the monitor console so that the sensor values can monitored. \n\n```don\nmonitor_sensor(\"sensor_name\", \"another_sensor_name\", ...)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo monitor sensor values in the monitor console, use the `monitor_sensor()` function by adding the identifiers of the sensors as string parameters. This function should be called at the start of the program.\n\nBelow is the list of supported sensor identifiers:\n\n- `brain.timer.time`\n- `drivetrain.is_done`\n- `drivetrain.is_moving`\n- `drivetrain.heading`\n- `drivetrain.rotation`\n- `drivetrain.velocity_rpm`\n- `drivetrain.velocity_percent`\n- `intake_motor_group.is_done`\n- `intake_motor_group.is_spinning`\n- `intake_motor_group.position_degrees`\n- `intake_motor_group.position_turns`\n- `intake_motor_group.velocity_rpm`\n- `intake_motor_group.velocity_percent`\n- `bottom_distance.is_object_detected`\n- `bottom_distance.object_distance_mm`\n- `bottom_distance.object_distance_inches`\n- `bottom_line_tracker.reflectivity`\n- `middle_line_tracker.reflectivity`\n- `top_line_tracker.reflectivity`\n- `roller_optical.is_near_object`\n- `roller_optical.color`\n- `roller_optical.brightness`\n- `roller_optical.hue`\n- `gps.position_mm`\n- `gps.position_inches`\n- `gps.heading`\n\nWhen adding sensor identifiers to the monitor_sensor() command, they have to be added as strings - therefore enclosed with quotation marks:\n\n```don\nmonitor_sensor(\"bottom_line_tracker.reflectivity\")\n```\nMultiple sensor identifiers, separated by commas, can be added to the monitor_sensor() command:\n\n```don\nmonitor_sensor(“distance.object_distance_mm”, “drivetrain.rotation”, “brain.timer.time”)\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis project uses the gps position sensor identifier to show both the X and the Y position (in mm and inches) of the robot as it drives toward the vertical center of the field. It also uses the timer sensor identifier to show the time in seconds. These sensor identifiers are passed into the motor_sensor() command.\n\n- Starting Position: A\n- Orientation: Facing Red Alliance Mobile Goal\n- Preload: Zero Rings\n\n```don\ndef main():\n    monitor_sensor(\"brain.timer.time\", \"gps.position_mm\", \"gps.position_inches\")\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n    while gps.x_position(MM) < 0:\n        wait(5, MSEC)\n    drivetrain.stop()\n    drivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 90, DEGREES)\n\nmain()\n```","signature":"monitor_sensor()"},"looks_monitor_variable":{"name":"looks_monitor_variable","markdown":"# Monitor Variable\n\nThe `monitor_variable()` command is used to add variables to the monitor console so that the value of the variables can be monitored.\n\n```don\nmonitor_variable(\"my_variable\", \"my_boolean\", ...)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo add variables to the monitor console, use the `monitor_variable()` command. Add the name of the variable(s) as strings in the command. Only global variables can be monitored with the `monitor_variable()` command.\n\n## Examples\n\nIn this project, the robot will score 20 points by picking up the Yellow Mobile Goal and dropping it off in the Alliance Home Zone.\n\n- Starting Position: A\n- Orientation: Facing Yellow Mobile Goal\n- Preload: Zero Rings\n\n```don\nspin_amount = 0\n\ndef main():\n    global spin_amount\n    monitor_variable(\"spin_amount\")\n\n    # Set the spin_amount variable to 1000\n    spin_amount = 1000\n\n    # Spin the Fork Motor Group down for 1700 degrees\n    fork_motor_group.spin_for(FORWARD, 1700, DEGREES)\n    drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 1300, MM)\n\n    # Pick up the Mobile Goal by spinning \n    # the Fork Motor Group up for spin_amount (1000)\n    fork_motor_group.spin_for(REVERSE, spin_amount, DEGREES)\n    drivetrain.drive_for(REVERSE, 900, MM)\n\n    # Drop off the Mobile Goal by spinning\n    # the Fork Motor Group up for spin_amount (1000)\n    fork_motor_group.spin_for(FORWARD, spin_amount, DEGREES)\n    drivetrain.drive_for(REVERSE, 300, MM)\n\n    # Update the spin_amount by 700 (1000 + 700 = 1700)\n    spin_amount = spin_amount + 700\n\n    # Spin the Fork Motor Group up for spin_amount (1700) \n    fork_motor_group.spin_for(REVERSE, spin_amount, DEGREES)\n\n\nmain()\n```","signature":"monitor_variable()"},"magnet_drop":{"name":"magnet_drop","markdown":"# Electromagnet drop\n\nAllows the V5 Electromagnet to drop the object it is currently holding.\n\n```python\nmagnet.drop()\n```\nAfter using the `magnet.drop()` command, the magnet will need to cool down before it can be used again.\n\n## Example\nThis example will pickup an object, drive forward, then use `magnet.drop()` to drop the object.\n\n```python\nmagnet.pickup()\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\nmagnet.drop()\n```","signature":"magnet.drop()"},"magnet_pickup":{"name":"magnet_pickup","markdown":"# Electromagnet pickup\n\nAllows the V5 Electromagnet to pick up an object.\n\n```python\nmagnet.pickup()\n```\nAfter using the `magnet.pickup()` command, the magnet will need to cool down before it can be used again.\n\n## Example\nThis example will use `magnet.pickup()` to pick up an object, drive forward, and then drop the object.\n\n```python\nmagnet.pickup()\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\nmagnet.drop()\n```","signature":"magnet.pickup()"},"magnet_set_power":{"name":"magnet_set_power","markdown":"# Electromagnet set power\n\nChanges the power used by the V5 Electromagnet when picking up an object.\n\n```python\nmagnet.set_power(50)\n```\nThe power can be set from **0% to 100%**.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will use `magnet.set_power()` to set the electromagnet to full power, pick up an object, drive forward, and then drop the object.\n\n```python\nmagnet.set_power(100)\nmagnet.pickup()\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\nmagnet.drop()\n```","signature":"magnet.set_power(50)"},"motion_motor393_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor393_set_velocity","markdown":"# Set Motor Controller Velocity\n\nSets the speed of a Motor393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n```python\nmotor393.set_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `VELOCITY` parameter accepts a range of -100% to 100%.\n\nSetting a Motor393's velocity to a negative value will cause the Motor393 to spin in reverse.\n\nThe sequence below will cause the Motor393 to spin in reverse, even though the `FORWARD` parameter is passed.\n\n```python\nmotor393.set_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\nmotor393.spin(FORWARD)\n```\n\nSetting a Motor393's velocity to 0 will prevent the Motor from spinning.","signature":"motor393.set_velocity(10, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor393_spin":{"name":"motion_motor393_spin","markdown":"# Spin Motor Controller\n\nSpins a Motor393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n```python\nmotor393.spin(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command spins a Motor393 forever, until a new motor command is used or the program is stopped.\n\nChoose which direction the motor will spin to by setting the `DIRECTION` parameter to either **FORWARD** or **REVERSE**.","signature":"motor393.spin(FORWARD)"},"motion_motor393_stop":{"name":"motion_motor393_stop","markdown":"# Stop Motor Controller\n\nStops a Motor393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n```python\nmotor393.stop()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe example below will stop a Motor393 device after spinning for 3 seconds.\n\n```python\nmotor393.spin(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\nmotor393.stop()\n```","signature":"motor393.stop()"},"motion_motor_set_max_torque":{"name":"motion_motor_set_max_torque","markdown":"# Set Motor Torque\n\nSets the torque of the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.set_max_torque(AMOUNT, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command accepts a range of 0% to 100%.\n\nThe `set_max_torque` command can accept decimals, integers, or numeric values.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the Claw Motor to the 40 degree position with only 20% maximum torque. This allows the claw to grab an object without damaging it with too much force.\n\n```python\nclaw_motor.set_max_torque(20, PERCENT)\nclaw_motor.set_position(40, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_max_torque(50, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor_set_position":{"name":"motion_motor_set_position","markdown":"# Set Motor Position\n\nSets a V5 Smart Motor's or Motor Group's encoder position(s) to the given value.\n\n```python\nmotor.set_position(VALUE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command can be used to set a Motor or Motor Group's position to a given positional value.\n\nUsually, the `motor.set_position` command is used to set the position to 0 to reset a Motor or Motor Group's encoder position(s).\n\nThe `motor.set_position` command accepts **DEGREES** or **TURNS** as valid **UNITS**.","signature":"motor.set_position(0, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_set_stopping":{"name":"motion_motor_set_stopping","markdown":"# Set Motor Stopping\n\nSets the stopping behavior of a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.set_stopping(MODE)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `MODE` parameter can be replaced with any of the following options:\n\n* BRAKE: will cause the Motor/Motor Group to come to an immediate stop.\n* COAST: lets the Motor/Motor Group spin gradually to a stop.\n* HOLD: will cause the Motor/Motor Group to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved.\n\nThe stopping behavior set by this command will apply to subsequent motion commands for the entirety of the project, unless otherwise changed.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the Arm Motor spin forward for 90 degrees (to raise the arm) and then will hold its position.\n\n```python\narm_motor.set_stopping(HOLD)\narm_motor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_stopping(BRAKE)"},"motion_motor_set_timeout":{"name":"motion_motor_set_timeout","markdown":"# Set Motor Timeout\n\nSets a time limit for the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group movement commands.\n\n```python \nmotor.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA Motor or Motor Group's is used to prevent motion commands that do not reach their position from preventing subsequent commands from running. \n\nAn example of a Motor not reaching its position is an Arm or Claw that reaches its mechanical limit and cannot complete its movement.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the timeout of the `spin_to_position` commands to 2 seconds.\n\nIf the Claw Motor has not reached the position of 270 degrees after 2 seconds, the Claw Motor will stop spinning.\n\n```python\nclaw_motor.set_timeout(2, SECONDS)\nclaw_motor.spin_to_position(270, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)"},"motion_motor_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity","markdown":"# Set Motor Velocity\n\nSets the speed of a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```python \nmotor.set_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command accepts a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-600rpm to 600rpm.**\n\nAcceptable `UNITS` parameter is either `PERCENT` or `RPM`.\n\n**Set motor velocity** will accept a \"rotations per minute\" (RPM) value based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group used.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a V5 Smart Motor's velocity to a negative value will cause the Motor/Motor Group to spin in reverse.\n\nSetting a V5 Smart Motor's velocity to 0 will prevent the Motor/Motor Group from spinning.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the Arm Motor to spin at 25% speed to the 90 degree position.\n\n```python\narm_motor.set_velocity(25, PERCENT)\narm_motor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_set_velocity_virtual":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity_virtual","markdown":"# Set Motor Velocity\n\nSets the speed of a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```python \nmotor.set_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command accepts a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-200rpm to 200rpm.**\n\nAcceptable `UNITS` parameter is either `PERCENT` or `RPM`.\n\n**Set motor velocity** will accept a \"rotations per minute\" (RPM) value between -200 and 200.\n\nSetting a V5 Smart Motor's velocity to a negative value will cause the Motor/Motor Group to spin in reverse.\n\nSetting a V5 Smart Motor's velocity to 0 will prevent the Motor/Motor Group from spinning.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the Intake Motor Group to spin at 25% speed to the 90 degree position.\n\n```python\nintake_motor_group.set_velocity(25, PERCENT)\nintake_motor_group.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_spin":{"name":"motion_motor_spin","markdown":"# Spin \n\nThis command spins a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group forever, until a new motion command is used or the program is stopped.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin(FORWARD)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which direction the Motor or Motor Group will spin to either **FORWARD** or **REVERSE**.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"motor.spin(FORWARD)"},"motion_motor_spin_at_voltage":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_at_voltage","markdown":"# Motor Spin At Voltage\nSpins a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group at a specified voltage.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin(FORWARD, 10.0, VOLT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Spin at voltage** accepts a range from -12V to 12V.\n\nUse the `FORWARD` parameter to drive the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group in the forward direction.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin(FORWARD, 10.0, VOLT)\n```\n\nUse the `REVERSE ` parameter to drive the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group in the reverse direction.\n\n```cpp\nmotor.spin(REVERSE, 10.0, VOLT)\n```\n\nSpinning a Motor or Motor Group at a negative voltage will cause the Motor/Motor Group to spin in the opposite direction than the one specified.","signature":"motor.spin(FORWARD, 10.0, VOLT)"},"motion_motor_spin_for":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_for","markdown":"# Spin For\n \nThis command spins a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group for a given amount of degrees or turns.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin_for(DIRECTION, AMOUNT, UNIT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which `DIRECTION` the Motor or Motor Group will spin to: **FORWARD** or **REVERSE**.\n\nChoose the `UNIT` of measurement to be either **DEGREES** or **TURNS**.\n\nChoose whether or not this command should be waited on by proceeding commands by setting an optional fourth parameter to either **wait=True** or **wait=False**. \n\n```python\nmotor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\nBy default, this command is a blocking command unless **wait=False** is passed as the fourth parameter.","signature":"motor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES)"},"motion_motor_spin_to_position":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_to_position","markdown":"# Spin To Position\n\nSpins a V5 Smart Motor's or Motor Group's encoder(s) to the given position.\n\n```python \nmotor.spin_to_position(POSITION, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command will tell a Motor or Motor Group to travel to a specific position. Based on the current position of the Motor or Motor Group, `spin_to_position` will determine the direction to rotate.\n\nChoose the unit of measurement to be either **DEGREES** or **TURNS**.\n\nChoose whether or not this command should be waited by other commands by changing the optional third parameter to either **wait=True** or **wait=False**.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\nSetting **wait=True** means that proceeding commands will not execute until the motor spin is completed. Conversely, **wait=False** will not wait for it to be completed.  \n\nBy default, this command will have the wait to be set to **True**.","signature":"motor.spin_to_position(POSITION, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_stop":{"name":"motion_motor_stop","markdown":"# Stop Motor\n\nStops a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.stop()\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows a motor spinning for 3 seconds before stopping.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\nmotor.stop()\n```","signature":"motor.stop()"},"motion_servo_set_position":{"name":"motion_servo_set_position","markdown":"# Spin Servo\n\nSpins a Servo Motor to a set position.\n\n```python\nservo.set_position(POSITION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `servo.set_position()` command accepts a range of values from **-50** to **50** for the **POSITION** parameter.\n\n## Example\n\nThe below example spins the servo motor to 25 degrees, waits 2 seconds, then spins the motor to -25 degrees.\n\n```python\nservo.set_position(25, DEGREES)\nwait(2, SECONDS)\nservo.set_position(-25, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"servo.set_position(50, DEGREES)"},"play_vexcode_sound":{"name":"play_vexcode_sound","markdown":"# Play VEXcode sound\n\nPlays a custom imported sound through your devices speaker.\n\n```python\nplay_vexcode_sound(\"\")\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nFor the `playVexcodeSound(\"\")` command to run properly, the V5 Brain **MUST** stay connected to the device via a USB cable while the project is running. \n\n* If coding in app-based VEXcode V5, no additional connection steps are needed in addition to the USB connection.\n* If coding in web-based VEXcode V5, the V5 Brain needs to stay connected while using the user/console web-serial port. For more information, [view this article >](https://kb.vex.com/hc/en-us/articles/15614471185812-Connecting-to-the-User-Console-Port-in-Web-Based-VEXcode-V5)\n\n![web_serial](static/help/v5/python/en/play_vexcode_sound/web_serial.png)\n\nChoose which sound to use. Use the default sound **game over** or add a new sound file URL in the Manage VEXcode Sounds menu. The sound name entered in the quotes must match the name inside the Manage VEXcode Sounds menu.\n\n```python\nplay_vexcode_sound(\"game over\")\n```\nUploaded sounds can only be used if they are added in the Manage VEXcode Sounds menu. For more information about adding or editing sounds, [view this article >](https://kb.vex.com/hc/en-us/articles/15613914815508-Playing-Custom-Imported-Sounds-in-a-VEXcode-V5-Project)\n\n![manage_sounds](static/help/v5/python/en/play_vexcode_sound/manage_sounds.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will play the arrow sound as soon as the project is started and then immediately move to the next command in the stack. \nThe `playVexcodeSound(\"\")` command is non-blocking and will not wait until the sound has finished playing before moving to the next command in the project. \n\nThe drivetrain will then drive forward for the full 200mm before playing the default **game over** sound.\n\n```python\n# Begin project code\nplay_vexcode_sound(\"arrow\")\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\nplay_vexcode_sound(\"game over\")\n```","signature":"play_vexcode_sound()"},"sensing_accel_two_g.acceleration":{"name":"sensing_accel_two_g.acceleration","markdown":"# Acceleration Of Analog Accelerometer\n\nReports the acceleration value from one axis on the Analog Accelerometer.\n\n```don\naccel_2g.acceleration()\n```\n\n## How to Use\n\nThis command reports a range from **-2.0 G to 2.0 G** or **-6.0 G to 6.0 G** depending on the jumper setting on the Analog Accelerometer.","signature":"accel_2g.acceleration()"},"sensing_brain_battery_capacity":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_capacity","markdown":"# Battery Capacity\n\n\nReports the charge level of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.capacity()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBattery capacity reports a range from **0%** to **100%.**","signature":"brain.battery.capacity()"},"sensing_brain_battery_current":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_current","markdown":"# Battery Current\n\nReports the current of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBattery current reports a range from **0.0 amps** to **20.0 amps**.","signature":"brain.battery.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_brain_battery_voltage":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_voltage","markdown":"# Battery Voltage\n\nReports the voltage of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.voltage(VOLT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\nBattery voltage reports a range from **10.0 volts** to **14.4 volts**.","signature":"brain.battery.voltage(VoltageUnits.VOLT)"},"sensing_brain_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_column","markdown":"# Cursor Column\n\nReports the column value of the V5 Brain's screen cursor location.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.column()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nScreen column reports a range from **1 to 80**.\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of columns available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 80 Columns\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 68 Columns\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 48 Columns (Default)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 32 Columns\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 24 Columns\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.MONO60` - 16 Columns","signature":"brain.screen.column()"},"sensing_brain_screen_pressing":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_pressing","markdown":"# Screen Pressed\n \nReports if the V5 Brain's touchscreen is currently being pressed.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`brain.screen.pressing` reports **True** if the V5 Brain's touchscreen is being pressed.\n\n`brain.screen.pressing` reports **False** if the V5 Brain's touchscreen is not being pressed.","signature":"brain.screen.pressing()"},"sensing_brain_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_row","markdown":"# Cursor Row\n \nReports the row value of the V5 Brain's screen cursor location.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nScreen row reports a range from **1 to 20**.\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 Rows (Default)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Rows","signature":"brain.screen.row()"},"sensing_brain_screen_x_position":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_x_position","markdown":"# Brain Screen xPosition\nReports the X coordinate of the location of the last detected touch on the V5 Brain's touchscreen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.x_position()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`brain.screen.x_position()` is used to capture the X coordinate of the last press on the V5 Brain's touchscreen. \n\nIt can be used with `brain.screen.y_position()` to get the (x,y) coordinate, and create interactivity between the V5 and the end user.\n\n`brain.screen.x_position()` return an **integer** in a range of **0 to 480 pixels**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/python/en/sensing_brain_screen_x_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n```python\nmy_x_coordinate = brain.screen.x_position()\n```","signature":"brain.screen.x_position()"},"sensing_brain_screen_y_position":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_y_position","markdown":"# Brain Screen yPosition\nReports the Y coordinate of the location of the last detected touch on the V5 Brain's touchscreen.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.y_position()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`brain.screen.y_position()` is used to capture the Y coordinate of the last press on the V5 Brain's touchscreen. \n\nIt can be used with `brain.screen.x_position()` to get the (x,y) coordinate, and create interactivity between the V5 and the end user.\n\n`brain.screen.y_position()` return an **integer** in a range of **0 to 240 pixels**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/python/en/sensing_brain_screen_y_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n```python\nmy_y_coordinate = brain.screen.y_position()\n```","signature":"brain.screen.y_position()"},"sensing_brain_timer_clear":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_clear","markdown":"# Reset Timer\nResets the V5 Brain's timer.\n\n```don \nbrain.timer.clear()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Brain's timer begins at the beginning of each project. The clear timer command is reset the timer value back to 0 seconds.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the timer will be reset before moving the Drivetrain forward for 3 seconds. After 3 seconds has elapsed, the Drivetrain will stop.\n\n```don\nbrain.timer.clear()\nwhile not brain.timer.time(SECONDS) > 3:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"brain.timer.clear()"},"sensing_brain_timer_time":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_time","markdown":"# Timer Value\n\nReports the value of the V5 Brain's timer in the provided UNITS.\n\n```python\nbrain.timer.time(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe timer starts at 0 seconds when the program starts, and reports the timer's value as a decimal value.\n\nThe `UNITS` parameter accepts either **SECONDS** or **MSEC** (milliseconds) as a valid argument.\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Timer in Seconds: \", brain.timer.time(SECONDS))\n\n    # A brief wait to print values without distortion or tearing\n    wait(20, MSEC)\n```","signature":"brain.timer.time(UNITS)"},"sensing_bumper_pressing":{"name":"sensing_bumper_pressing","markdown":"# Pressing Bumper\n \nReports if the Bumper Switch is currently being pressed.\n\n```don\nbumper.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nPressing bumper reports **True** if the Bumper Switch is being pressed.\n\nPressing bumper reports **False** if the Bumper Switch is not being pressed.","signature":"bumper.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_axis_position":{"name":"sensing_controller_axis_position","markdown":"# Position Of Controller\n \nReports the position of a joystick on the V5 Controller along an axis.\n\n```don\ncontroller.axis1.position()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`controller.axis1.position` reports a range between **-100 to 100**.\n\n`controller.axis1.position` will report zero (0) when a joystick axis is centered.\n\nChoose which Controller axis to report.\n\n* axis1 - right Joystick (left and right)\n* axis2 - right Joystick (up and down)\n* axis3 - left Joystick (up and down)\n* axis4 - left Joystick (left and right)","signature":"controller.axis1.position()"},"sensing_controller_button_up_pressing":{"name":"sensing_controller_button_up_pressing","markdown":"# Pressing Controller\n \nReports if a button on the V5 Controller is pressed.\n\n```don\ncontroller.buttonUp.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nPressing controller reports **True** if the selected Controller button is being pressed.\n\nPressing controller reports **False** if the selected Controller button is not pressed.\n\nChoose which Controller button to detect for a press:\n\n* `buttonUp`\n* `buttonDown`\n* `buttonLeft`\n* `buttonRight`\n* `buttonX`\n* `buttonY`\n* `buttonA`\n* `buttonB`\n* `buttonL1`\n* `buttonL2`\n* `buttonR1`\n* `buttonR2`","signature":"controller.buttonUp.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_column","markdown":"# Cursor Column\n \nReports the column number of the Controller's screen cursor location.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.column()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCursor row reports a range from **1 to 80**.\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* Standard Font - 20 Columns (Default)","signature":"controller.screen.column()"},"sensing_controller_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_row","markdown":"# Cursor Row\n\nReports the row number of the Controller's screen cursor location.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCursor row reports a range from **1 to 20**.\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)","signature":"controller.screen.row()"},"sensing_digital_in_signal":{"name":"sensing_digital_in_signal","markdown":"# Digital In\n\nReports value of the digital in signal.\n\n```cpp\ndigital_in.value()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 3-Wire ports function at a 5V logic signal voltage level.\n\nThe `digital_in.value()` command reports **1** when the digital input signal is high.\n\nThe `digital_in.value()` command reports **0** when the digital input signal is low.","signature":"digital_in.value()"},"sensing_digital_out_set":{"name":"sensing_digital_out_set","markdown":"# Digital out\n\nSets the logic level of a digital out 3-Wire port.\n\n```cpp\ndigital_out.set(True)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 3-Wire ports function at a 5V logic signal voltage level.\n\nThe `digital_out.set(True)` command sets the digital signal to output a high or low logic signal.\n\nChoose to output a high or low digital logic signal.\n\n* Set the output to high: `digital_out.set(True)`\n* Set the output to low: `digital_out.set(False)`","signature":"digital_out.set(True)"},"sensing_distance_is_object_detected":{"name":"sensing_distance_is_object_detected","markdown":"# Distance Object Found\n\nReports if the Distance sensor sees an object within its field of view.\n\n```don\ndistance.is_object_detected()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Distance object found** reports True when the Distance sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n**Distance object found** reports False when the Distance sensor does not detect an object or surface.","signature":"distance.is_object_detected()"},"sensing_distance_object_distance":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Object Distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the Distance sensor.\n\n```don\ndistance.object_distance(MM)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object distance** reports a range from **20mm to 2000mm**.\n\nAcceptable values for `UNIT` are: MM or INCHES.","signature":"distance.object_distance(MM)"},"sensing_distance_object_size":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_size","markdown":"# Object Size\n\nReports the size of an object the Distance Sensor detects.  \n\n```\ndistance.object_size()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDetermines the size of the object detected (none, small, medium, large) based on the amount of light reflected and returned to the sensor.\n\n\nIf an object is found, the function will return `ObjectSizeType.SMALL`, `ObjectSizeType.MEDIUM`, or `ObjectSizeType.LARGE`.\n\nIf there is no object found, the function will return `ObjectSizeType.NONE`.","signature":"distance.object_size()"},"sensing_distance_object_velocity":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Object velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of an object in m/s.\n\n```\ndistance.object_velocity()\n```\n## How To Use\n\n**Object velocity** reports the current velocity of an object in m/s (meters per second).","signature":"distance.object_velocity()"},"sensing_drivetrain_current":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_current","markdown":"# Drive Current\n\nReports the amount of current that the Drivetrain is currently using.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`drivetrain.current` reports a range from **0.0 to 2.5** amps.","signature":"drivetrain.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency","markdown":"# Drive Efficiency\n \nReports the efficiency of the Drivetrain.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.efficiency(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\nDrive efficiency reports the value of the power (in watts) the motor is using (input), versus the amount of power (in watts) the motor is providing (output).\n\nA V5 Drivetrain typically reaches a maximum efficiency of **65%** under normal use cases.\n\nDrive efficiency reports a range from **0% to 100%**.","signature":"drivetrain.efficiency(PERCENT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_heading":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_heading","markdown":"# Drive Heading\n \nReports the direction that the Drivetrain is facing by using the Gyroscopic (Gyro) sensor's current angular position.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe drive heading command reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\nDrive heading reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**.","signature":"drivetrain.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_done":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_done","markdown":"# Drive Is Done\n\nReports if the Drivetrain has completed its movement.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.is_done()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDrive is done reports **True** when the robot's Drivetrain has completed its movement.\n\nDrive is done reports **False** when the robot's Drivetrain is still moving.","signature":"drivetrain.is_done()"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving","markdown":"# Drive Is Moving\n \nReports if the Drivetrain is currently moving.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.is_moving()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDrive is moving reports **True** when the Drivetrain's motors are moving.\n\nDrive is moving reports **False** when the Drivetrain's motors are stopped.","signature":"drivetrain.is_moving()"},"sensing_drivetrain_power":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_power","markdown":"# Drive Power\n\nReports the amount of power output the Drivetrain is currently generating.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.power(PowerUnits.WATT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDrive power reports a range from **0.0 to 22.0 watts**.","signature":"drivetrain.power(PowerUnits.WATT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_rotation":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_rotation","markdown":"# Drive Rotation\n \nReports the Drivetrain's angle of rotation when configured with a 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDrive rotation reports a **positive** value when the Drivetrain turns in a clockwise direction.\n\nDrive rotation reports a **negative** value when the Drivetrain turns in a counter-clockwise direction.","signature":"drivetrain.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_drivetrain_temperature":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_temperature","markdown":"# Drive Temperature\n \nReports the temperature of the V5 Smart Motors powering the Drivetrain.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.temperature(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDrive temperature reports a range from **0% to 100%**.","signature":"drivetrain.temperature(PERCENT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_torque":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_torque","markdown":"# Drive Torque\n\nReports the amount of torque (rotational force) the Drivetrain is currently using.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.torque(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`drivetrain.torque` reports a range from **0.0 to 18.6** inch-pounds (InLB) if the provided **UNITS** parameter is `TorqueUnits.INLB`.\n\nAlternatively, a range from **0.0 to 2.1** Newton-meters (Nm) is reported if the provided **UNITS** parameter is `TorqueUnits.NM`.","signature":"drivetrain.torque(units)"},"sensing_drivetrain_velocity":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_velocity","markdown":"# Drive Velocity\n \nReports the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.velocity(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`drivetrain.velocity` returns a decimal value representing the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\nAcceptable `UNITS` are **PERCENT** and **RPM**.\n\nIf the provided `UNITS` parameter is **PERCENT**, the reported values ranges between **-100% to 100%**.\n\nAlternatively, if the provided `UNITS` is **RPM**, the range of reported values vary based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm","signature":"drivetrain.velocity(UNITS)"},"sensing_encoder_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_position","markdown":"# Shaft Encoder Position\n \nReports the rotational position of the Shaft Encoder.\n\n```don\nencoder.position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `UNITS` parameter accepts either **DEGREES** or **TURNS** as a value.\n\nPosition of shaft encoder reports the distance the Shaft Encoder has rotated in integer numbers for degrees, and decimal numbers for turns.","signature":"encoder.position(DEGREES)"},"sensing_encoder_set_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_set_position","markdown":"# Set Shaft Encoder Position\n \nSets the Shaft Encoder's position to the given positional value.\n\n```python\nencoder.set_position(POSITION, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe set shaft encoder position command can be used to set the Shaft Encoder's position to any given positional value.\n\nThe `UNITS` parameter accepts either **DEGREES** or **TURNS** as a valid argument.\n\nUsually, the set shaft encoder position command is used to set the position to 0, to reset the Shaft Encoder's position.","signature":"encoder.set_position(POSITION, UNITS)"},"sensing_encoder_velocity":{"name":"sensing_encoder_velocity","markdown":"# Shaft Encoder Velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of a Shaft Encoder.\n\n```don\nencoder.velocity(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nVelocity of shaft encoder reports a decimal value in either degrees per second (dps) or rotations per minute (rpm).\n\nThe `UNITS` parameter accepts either **VelocityUnits.DPS** or **RPM** as a value.","signature":"encoder.velocity(VelocityUnits.DPS)"},"sensing_gps_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_gps_acceleration","markdown":"# GPS Acceleration\n\nReports the acceleration value of the specified axis on a GPS Sensor.\n\n```python\ngps.acceleration(AXIS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.acceleration()` command reports a numerical value in the range of **-4.0** to **4.0** Gs.\n\nIt can report acceleration values from three different axes based on the value passed as the `AXIS` parameter.\n\n* Used with the **AxisType.XAXIS** parameter, the value reported will be the acceleration value of a GPS Sensor's forward and backward rotations\n\n* Used with the **AxisType.YAXIS** parameter, the value reported will be the acceleration value of a GPS Sensor's left and right rotations\n\n* Used with the **AxisType.ZAXIS** parameter, the value reported will be the acceleration value of a GPS Sensor's up and down movements\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Print the current acceleration on the GPS Sensor's X axis\nbrain.screen.print(\"Acceleration on X: \", gps.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS))\n```","signature":"gps.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS)"},"sensing_gps_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gps_calibrate","markdown":"# GPS Calibrate\n\nStarts the calibration process for a GPS Sensor.\n\n```python\ngps.calibrate()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA GPS Sensor must remain still during the calibration process.\n\n```python\n# Calibrate the GPS Sensor before starting any program code\ngps.calibrate()\n```","signature":"gps.calibrate()"},"sensing_gps_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_gps_gyro_rate","markdown":"# GPS Gyro Rate\n\nReports the rate of rotation from the specified axis on a GPS Sensor.\n\n```python\ngps.gyro_rate(AXIS, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.gyro_rate()` command reports the rate of rotation on an axis with the range of values reported between **-1000** to **1000** if **VelocityUnits.DPS** is used as the `UNITS` parameter, or between **-167** to **167** if **VelocityUnits.RPM** is used.\n\nThe `AXIS` parameter accepts the following values for specifying which axis to get rate of rotation from:\n\n* **AxisType.XAXIS**: reports the rate of rotation when a GPS Sensor rotates in the X-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n* **AxisType.YAXIS**: reports the rate of rotation when a GPS Sensor rotates in the Y-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n* **AxisType.ZAXIS**: reports the rate of rotation when a GPS Sensor rotates in the Z-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Print gyro rate values from all GPS Sensor axes in a loop\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"GPS Gyro Rate - X Axis: \", gps.gyro_rate(AxisType.XAXIS, VelocityUnits.DPS))\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n    brain.screen.print(\"GPS Gyro Rate - Y Axis: \", gps.gyro_rate(AxisType.YAXIS, VelocityUnits.DPS))\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n    brain.screen.print(\"GPS Gyro Rate - Z Axis: \", gps.gyro_rate(AxisType.ZAXIS, VelocityUnits.DPS))\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"gps.gyro_rate(AxisType.XAXIS, VelocityUnits.DPS)"},"sensing_gps_heading":{"name":"sensing_gps_heading","markdown":"# GPS Heading\n\nReports the heading that a robot is currently facing based on a GPS Sensor's readings from the VEX GPS Field Code.\n\n```python\ngps.heading()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.heading()` command reports a range of heading values from **0.00** to **359.99** degrees, increasing in value when a GPS Sensor is rotated clockwise.\n\nUsually, a GPS Sensor should be mounted facing behind a robot. In the GPS configuration, the Angle Offset is set to **180** degrees.\n\nThen, for example, if the GPS Sensor is facing the South wall as defined by the VEX GPS Field Code, the reported heading will be **0.00** degrees, which is the heading that the front of the robot is facing.\n\nHowever, a GPS Sensor can also be mounted facing other directions (e.g. the front of a robot).\n\nIn this situation, for example, the GPS Sensor's Angle Offset configuration would then need to be set to **0** degrees, which is the angular difference between the forward heading of the robot, and the heading that the GPS is facing. This way, the reported heading value will shift correctly in line with a robot's headings as it turns.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below uses the `gps.heading()` command to stop the Drivetrain's turn when the reported GPS Sensor heading is more than or equal to 180 degrees.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n\nwhile gps.heading() < 180:\n    wait(50, MSEC)\n\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"gps.heading()"},"sensing_gps_heading_virtual":{"name":"sensing_gps_heading_virtual","markdown":"# GPS Heading\n\nReports the heading that a robot is currently facing based on a GPS Sensor's readings from the VEX GPS Field Code.\n\n```python\ngps.heading()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.heading()` command reports a range of heading values from **0.00** to **359.99** degrees, increasing in value when a GPS Sensor is rotated clockwise.\n\nBy default, a GPS Sensor should be mounted facing behind a robot. Then, for example, if the GPS Sensor is facing the South wall as defined by the VEX GPS Field Code, the reported heading will be **0.00** degrees, which is the heading that the front of the robot is facing.\n\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below uses the `gps.heading()` command to stop the Drivetrain's turn when the reported GPS Sensor heading is more than or equal to 180 degrees.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(25, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n\nwhile gps.heading() < 180:\n    wait(5, MSEC)\n\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"gps.heading()"},"sensing_gps_orientation":{"name":"sensing_gps_orientation","markdown":"# GPS Orientation\n\nReports the angle of the specified orientation axis on a GPS Sensor.\n\n```python\ngps.orientation(AXIS, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`gps.orientation()` reports a numerical value representing the angle of rotation about the specified orientation `AXIS`:\n\n* The **OrientationType.ROLL** axis reports a value between **-180** to **180** degrees, representing the angle of a GPS Sensor when tilted left or right\n\n* The **OrientationType.PITCH** axis reports a value between **-90** to **90** degrees, representing the angle of a GPS Sensor when tilted forward or backwards\n\n* The **OrientationType.YAW** axis reports a value between **-180** to **180** degrees, representing the angle of a GPS Sensor when rotated about the vertical axis\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Print the orientation of a GPS Sensor's yaw axis in a loop\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"GPS Yaw Orientation: \", gps.orientation(OrientationType.YAW, DEGREES))\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"gps.orientation(OrientationType.ROLL, DEGREES)"},"sensing_gps_quality":{"name":"sensing_gps_quality","markdown":"# GPS Signal Quality\n\nReports a GPS Sensor's current signal quality.\n\n```python\ngps.quality()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.quality()` command reports a numerical value representing the current signal quality of a GPS Sensor.\n\nWhen the reported value is **100**, it means that all reported positional and heading data from a GPS Sensor is valid.\n\nHowever, a reported value of **90** signals that any positional data is no longer being calculated by capturing information from the VEX Field Code, but rather through alternative means.\n\nAt **80**, only GPS Sensor heading values are valid, but as more time goes by where a GPS Sensor is not scanning enough of the VEX Field Code to accurately determine positiona and heading information, the reported signal quality will continue to drop until **0**, where any GPS Sensor data is effectively frozen and no longer valid.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Print a GPS Sensor's signal quality\nbrain.screen.print(\"GPS Signal Quality: \", gps.quality())\n```","signature":"gps.quality()"},"sensing_gps_set_location":{"name":"sensing_gps_set_location","markdown":"# GPS Set Location\n\nSets the location for a GPS Sensor to a defined positional value.\n\n```python\ngps.set_location(x, y, units, heading, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen a GPS Sensor is too close to the field walls to read accurate data (for example, when a robot is in a game's starting position on a field), unexpected behaviors can often occur if the program relies on the GPS's positional and heading data to work correctly.\n\nThe `gps.set_location()` command can be used to set the location and heading of a GPS Sensor if this information is known before the program is ran, which may help reduce GPS data inaccuracies due to a GPS Sensor's proximity to the field walls when a program is started.\n\nThe **x** and **y** parameters are the X and Y offsets of the GPS Sensor, or a defined origin point on a robot relative to the center of a field. The **units** parameter can either be **MM** or **INCHES**.\n\nThe **heading** parameter is the heading of the robot in its defined position. For example, if the GPS Sensor is mounted facing behind a robot and the robot is facing the West wall (heading of 270), the **heading** value that should be passed is 270.\n\n```python\n# Setting the approximate location of a GPS Sensor\n# when a robot is facing West and\n# starting at the bottom right corner of a field\ngps.set_location(56, -45, INCHES, 270, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"gps.set_location()"},"sensing_gps_set_origin":{"name":"sensing_gps_set_origin","markdown":"# GPS Set Origin\n\nSets an origin point on a robot at which GPS Sensor positional data should be based upon.\n\n```python\ngps.set_origin(X, Y, UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `GPS.set_origin()` command can be used to allow GPS positional data to correspond to another point of a robot rather than the location of a GPS Sensor.\n\nIt is commonly used when a GPS Sensor is not located on the reference point of a robot (i.e. the point about which a robot rotates). This way, when the origin is set to the reference point, reported positional data would not change when a robot is rotating in-place.\n\nThe `X` parameter takes the X axis (i.e. the axis running through the sides of a GPS Sensor) while the `Y` parameter takes the Y axis offset distance to a reference point.\n\nEither **MM** or **INCHES** are accepted for the `UNITS` parameter, depending on whether the x and y offset values are being passed as millimeters or inches, respectively.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Assuming a GPS Sensor is mounted 25mm forward from the reference point on a robot,\n# we can set the origin on the GPS Sensor to have a Y offset of 25\n\ngps.set_origin(0, 25, MM)\n```","signature":"gps.set_origin(0, 0, MM)"},"sensing_gps_xposition":{"name":"sensing_gps_xposition","markdown":"# GPS X Position\n\nReports the X positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\n```python\ngps.x_position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.x_position()` command reports the current X positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point relative to the center of a field.\n\nIf a `gps.set_origin()` command is used to set an origin point to a different part of a robot, the reported value will be the positional offset of the defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\nAlternatively, the origin point can also be set in the GPS Sensor's configuration. This can be done by measuring the X and Y distances from the intended origin point to the GPS Sensor and filling in the X and Y offset settings, respectively.\n\nValues can be reported in mm or inches, depending on whether **MM** or **INCHES** is passed in the `UNITS` parameter.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Print the current X position of a GPS Sensor\nbrain.screen.print(\"GPS X Position (MM): \", gps.x_position(MM))\n```","signature":"gps.x_position(MM)"},"sensing_gps_xposition_virtual":{"name":"sensing_gps_xposition_virtual","markdown":"# GPS X Position\n\nReports the X positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\n```python\ngps.x_position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.x_position()` command reports the current X positional offset of the V5 robot's turning reference (midpoint between the two front wheels) relative to the center of a field.\n\nValues can be reported in mm or inches, depending on whether **MM** or **INCHES** is passed in the `UNITS` parameter.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Print the current X position\nbrain.screen.print(\"GPS X Position (MM): \", gps.x_position(MM))\n```","signature":"gps.x_position(MM)"},"sensing_gps_yposition":{"name":"sensing_gps_yposition","markdown":"# GPS Y Position\n\nReports the Y positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\n```python\ngps.y_position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.y_position()` command reports the current Y positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point relative to the center of a field.\n\nIf a `gps.set_origin()` command is used to set an origin point to a different part of a robot, the reported value will be the positional offset of the defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\nAlternatively, the origin point can also be set in the GPS Sensor's configuration. This can be done by measuring the X and Y distances from the intended origin point to the GPS Sensor and filling in the X and Y offset settings, respectively.\n\nValues can be reported in mm or inches, depending on whether **MM** or **INCHES** is passed in the `UNITS` parameter.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Print the current Y position of a GPS Sensor\nbrain.screen.print(\"GPS Y Position (MM): \", gps.y_position(MM))\n```","signature":"gps.y_position(MM)"},"sensing_gps_yposition_virtual":{"name":"sensing_gps_yposition_virtual","markdown":"# GPS Y Position\n\nReports the Y positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\n```python\ngps.y_position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `gps.y_position()` command reports the current Y positional offset of the V5 robot's turning reference (midpoint between the two front wheels) relative to the center of a field.\n\nValues can be reported in mm or inches, depending on whether **MM** or **INCHES** is passed in the `UNITS` parameter.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Print the current Y position\nbrain.screen.print(\"GPS Y Position (MM): \", gps.y_position(MM))\n```","signature":"gps.y_position(MM)"},"sensing_gyro_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_calibrate","markdown":"# Calibrate Gyro Sensor\n\nCalibrating the Gyro Sensor is used to reduce the amount of drift generated by Gyro Sensor.\n\n```don\ngyro.calibrate()\n```\n\nDrifting occurs when the Gyro Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not physically moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Gyro Sensor must remain still during the calibration process. The calibration process will take approximately 2 seconds to complete.","signature":"gyro.calibrate()"},"sensing_gyro_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Gyro Angle Of Heading\n \nReports the 3-Wire Gyro Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```don\ngyro.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe command reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n`gyro.heading` reports a range between **0.00 to 359.99**.","signature":"gyro.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Gyro Angle Of Rotation\n \nReports the 3-Wire Gyro Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n```don\ngyro.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nGyro rotation reports a **positive** value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\nGyro rotation reports a **negative** value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.","signature":"gyro.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_heading","markdown":"# Set Gyro Heading\n\nSets the Gyroscopic (Gyro) Sensor's current heading position to a set value.\n \n```don\ngyro.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe set gyro heading command can be used to set the Gyro's position to any clockwise heading.\n\nThis command is typically used reset the heading orientation of the Gyro sensor when value is set to 0.\n\nThe `HEADING` parameter accepts a range of 0.0 to 359.99 degrees.\n\nThe set heading command can accept decimals, integers, or numeric values.","signature":"gyro.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_rotation","markdown":"# Set Gyro Rotation\n\nSets a 3-Wire Gyro Sensor's angle of rotation to a given value.\n\n```python \ngyro.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Set Gyro Rotation` command can be used to set a 3-Wire Gyro Sensor's angle of rotation to any given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\nThe `Set Gyro Rotation` command can accept decimals, integers, or numeric values for its `ROTATION` parameter.","signature":"gyro.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Inertial Acceleration\n\nReports the acceleration value from one of the axes (x, y, or z) on the Intertial Sensor.\n\n```don\ninertial.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nAcceleration of reports a range from **-4.0 to 4.0 Gs**.\n\nChoose which axis to use:\n\n* The **X-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **forward to backward**\n* The **Y-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **side to side**\n* The **Z-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **up to down**","signature":"inertial.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS)"},"sensing_inertial_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_calibrate","markdown":"# Calibrate Inertial Sensor\n \nCalibrating the Inertial Sensor is used to reduce the amount of drift generated by the Inertial Sensor.\n\n```don\ninertial.calibrate()\n```\n\nDrifting occurs when the Inertial Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not physically moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Inertial Sensor must remain still during the calibration process. The calibration process will take approximately 2 seconds to complete.","signature":"inertial.calibrate()"},"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Inertial Gyro Rate\n\nGets the rate of rotation from one of the axes (x, y, or z) on the Inertial Sensor.\n\n```don\ninertial.gyro_rate(AxisType.XAXIS, VelocityUnits.DPS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nGyro rate reports a range from **-1000.0 to 1000.0** in dps (degrees per second).\n\nChoose which axis to use.\n\n* The X-axis reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the X-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* The Y-axis reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Y-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* The Z-axis reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Z-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)","signature":"inertial.gyro_rate(AxisType.XAXIS, VelocityUnits.DPS)"},"sensing_inertial_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_heading","markdown":"# Inertial Angle Of Heading \n\nReports the V5 Inertial Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```don\ninertial.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `inertial.heading` command reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n`inertial.heading` reports a range from 0.00 to 359.99 degrees.","signature":"inertial.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_orientation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Inertial Orientation\n\nGets an orientation angle of the inertial sensor. Reports the unit value specified by the parameter of the inertial sensor.\n\n```don\ninertial.orientation(OrientationType.ROLL, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\nThe orientation reported is determined by the selected axis (x, y, or z).\n\n* The X-axis represents pitch, which reports a value between -90 to +90 degrees.\n* The Y-axis represents roll, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n* The Z-axis represents yaw, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)","signature":"inertial.orientation(OrientationType.ROLL , DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_rotation","markdown":"# Inertial Angle Of Rotation\n \nReports a V5 Inertial Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n```python\ninertial.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `inertial.rotation` command reports a positive value when the Inertial Sensor turns in the clockwise direction.\n\n`inertial.rotation` reports a negative value when the Inertial Sensor turns in the counter-clockwise direction.","signature":"inertial.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_heading","markdown":"# Set Inertial Heading\n\nSets the Inertial sensor's current heading position to a set value.\n\n```don\ninertial.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`inertial.set_heading` can be used to set the Inertial Sensor's position to any clockwise heading. This command is typically used to reset the orientation of the Inertial Sensor when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` is typically used to reset the heading orientation of the Inertial sensor when a value is set to 0.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` accepts a range of 0.0 to 359.99 degrees.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` can accept decimals, integers, or numeric values.","signature":"inertial.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_rotation","markdown":"# Set Inertial Rotation\n\nSets a V5 Inertial Sensor's angle of rotation to a given value.\n\n```python\ninertial.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `inertial.set_rotation` command can be used to set the inertial sensor's angle of rotation to any given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\n`inertial.set_rotation` accepts a range of any positive or negative decimal or integer.","signature":"inertial.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_light_brightness":{"name":"sensing_light_brightness","markdown":"# Light Sensor Brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the Light Sensor.\n\n```don\nlight.brightness(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`light.brightness` reports a range from **0% to 100%**.\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.","signature":"light.brightness(PERCENT)"},"sensing_limit_switch_pressing":{"name":"sensing_limit_switch_pressing","markdown":"# Pressing Limit Switch\n\nReports if the Limit Switch is currently being pressed.\n\n```don\nlimit_switch.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nPressing limit reports **True** if the Limit Switch is being pressed.\n\nPressing limit reports **False** if the Limit Switch is not being pressed.","signature":"limit_switch.pressing()"},"sensing_line_tracker_reflectivity":{"name":"sensing_line_tracker_reflectivity","markdown":"# Line Tracker Reflectivity\n\nReports the amount of light reflected using the Line Tracker sensor.\n\n```don\nline_tracker.reflectivity(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nLight-colored surfaces will reflect more light and will report a high reflectivity value.\n\nDark-colored surfaces will reflect less light and will report a low reflectivity value.\n\nThe default unit is `PERCENT` that returns an integer value from **0% to 100%**.","signature":"line_tracker.reflectivity(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_current":{"name":"sensing_motor_current","markdown":"# Motor Current\n\nReports the amount of current a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group is using in amperes (amps).\n\n```python\nmotor.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMotor current reports a range from **0.0 to 2.5 amps**.","signature":"motor.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_motor_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_motor_efficiency","markdown":"# Motor Efficiency\n \nReports the efficiency of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.efficiency(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nEfficiency of motor reports the value of the power (in watts) the Motor or Motor Group is using (input), versus the amount of power (in watts) the Motor or Motor Group is providing (output).\n\nA V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group typically reaches a maximum efficiency of 65% under normal use cases.\n\nEfficiency of motor reports a range from **0% to 100%**.","signature":"motor.efficiency(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_is_done":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor Is Done \n\nReports if the selected V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n```python\nmotor.is_done()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMotor is done reports **True** when the selected Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\nMotor is done reports **False** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is still moving.","signature":"motor.is_done()"},"sensing_motor_is_spinning":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor Is Spinning\n\nReports if the selected V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently spinning.\n\n```python\nmotor.is_spinning()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMotor is spinning reports **True** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is still moving.\n\nMotor is spinning reports **False** when the selected Motor or Motor Group is stopped.","signature":"motor.is_spinning()"},"sensing_motor_position":{"name":"sensing_motor_position","markdown":"# Motor Position\n\nReports the current rotational position of the selected V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of the specified Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.position(UNIT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMotor position reports the position of the V5 Smart Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group in integer numbers for degrees, and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nAcceptable values for `UNIT` are: **DEGREES** or **TURNS**.","signature":"motor.position(DEGREES)"},"sensing_motor_power":{"name":"sensing_motor_power","markdown":"# Motor Power\n\nReports the amount of power output a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group is currently generating.\n\n```python\nmotor.power(PowerUnits.WATT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMotor power reports a range from **0.0 to 11.0 watts**.","signature":"motor.power(PowerUnits.WATT)"},"sensing_motor_temperature":{"name":"sensing_motor_temperature","markdown":"# Motor Temperature\n\nReports the temperature of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.temperature(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nUsing the `temperature` command can help users develop logic to keep their V5 Smart Motors or Motor Groups from overheating during heavy use.\n\nMotor temperature reports a range from **0% to 100%**.","signature":"motor.temperature(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_torque":{"name":"sensing_motor_torque","markdown":"# Motor Torque\n\nReports the amount of torque (rotational force) a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group is currently using.\n\n```python\nmotor.torque(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`motor.torque` reports a range from **0.0 to 18.6** inch-pounds (InLB) if the provided **UNITS** parameter is `TorqueUnits.INLB`.\n\nAlternatively, a range from **0.0 to 2.1** Newton-meters (Nm) is reported if the provided **UNITS** parameter is `TorqueUnits.NM`.","signature":"motor.torque(UNITS)"},"sensing_motor_velocity":{"name":"sensing_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Motor Velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n```python\nmotor.velocity(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMotor velocity reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-600rpm to 600rpm**.\n\nAcceptable values for `UNIT` parameter are: **PERCENT** or **RPM**.\n\nMotor velocity will report a \"rotations per minute\" range based on the Gear Cartridge installed in a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm","signature":"motor.velocity(UNITS)"},"sensing_optical_brightness":{"name":"sensing_optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical Brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the Optical Sensor.\n\n```don\noptical.brightness()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`optical.brightness()` reports a range from **0%** to **100%**\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.","signature":"optical.brightness()"},"sensing_optical_color_found":{"name":"sensing_optical_color_found","markdown":"# Optical Color Detection\n\nReports the color that the Optical Sensor is detecting.\n\n```python\noptical.color()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`optical.color()` will return a RGB (Red, Green, Blue) value that corresponds to a color. You can use the `Color` enums to compare to the value returned by `optical.color()`\n\nYou can compare to the following values\n\n* Color.BLACK\n* Color.WHITE\n* Color.RED\n* Color.GREEN\n* Color.BLUE\n* Color.YELLOW\n* Color.ORANGE\n* Color.PURPLE\n* Color.CYAN\n\nYou can use these in a conditional statement like this:\n\n```python\nif optical.color() == Color.RED:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Red Object\")\n```","signature":"optical.color()"},"sensing_optical_gesture_detected":{"name":"sensing_optical_gesture_detected","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nReports detected gesture data from a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```python\noptical.get_gesture()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command returns an object with gesture information. To check the type of the detected gesture, access the `type` property on the returned object.\n\n```python\noptical.get_gesture().type\n```\n\nBefore using any V5 Optical Sensor gesture commands, a V5 Optical Sensor must be correctly set to detect gestures with the `optical.gesture_enable()` command.\n\nBelow are the gestures that a V5 Optical Sensor can detect:\n\n- `GestureType.UP`\n- `GestureType.DOWN`\n- `GestureType.LEFT`\n- `GestureType.RIGHT`\n\n## Example\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set a V5 Optical Sensor to detect gestures before checking for gestures.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_enable()\nwhile optical.get_gesture().type != GestureType.UP:\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\nbrain.screen.print(\"Up!\")\n```","signature":"optical.get_gesture()"},"sensing_optical_hue":{"name":"sensing_optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical Hue\nReports the hue of the color of an object.\n\n```don\noptical.hue()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`optical.hue()` reports a number value that is the hue of the color of an object. \n\nIt returns a number between **0** and **359**, which can be thought of as the location of the color on a color wheel.","signature":"optical.hue()"},"sensing_optical_object_found":{"name":"sensing_optical_object_found","markdown":"# Optical Near Object\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\n```don\noptical.is_near_object()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`optical.is_near_object()` reports **True** if an object is close enough to the Optical Sensor to get other sensing information.\n\n`optical.is_near_object()` reports **False** if an object is not close enough to the Optical Sensor to get accurate sensor readings.","signature":"optical.is_near_object()"},"sensing_optical_set_light":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light","markdown":"# Set Optical Light\nSets the light on the Optical Sensor to **on** or **off**.\n\n```don\noptical.set_light(LedStateType.ON)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`optical.set_light(LedStateType.ON)` allows you to turn the Optical Sensor's light **on** or **off**. The light lets the sensor see objects if it is looking at an object in a dark area.\n\nTo turn the light **on** you pass `LedStateType.ON`\n\n```\noptical.set_light(LedStateType.ON)\n```\n\nTo turn the light **off** you pass `LedStateType.OFF`\n\n```\noptical.set_light(LedStateType.OFF)\n```","signature":"optical.set_light(LedStateType.ON)"},"sensing_optical_set_light_power":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Set Optical Light Power\nSets the light power of V5 Optical sensor.\n\n```don\noptical.set_light_power(50, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`optical.set_light_power(50, PERCENT)` will change the brightness of the light on the Optical Sensor. \n\nThe command accepts a range of **0%** to **100%** for the intensity, and **PERCENT** as the unit. If the light is off, this command will turn the light on.","signature":"optical.set_light_power(50, PERCENT)"},"sensing_optical_set_mode_disable":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_mode_disable","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Disable\n\nSets a V5 Optical Sensor to detect colors.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_disable()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Disable` command allows you to set a V5 Optical Sensor to detect colors.\n\nBy default, a V5 Optical Sensor will be set to detect colors.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set a V5 Optical Sensor to detect colors after checking for gestures.\n\n```python\n# Detect gestures\noptical.gesture_enable()\nwhile optical.get_gesture().type != GestureType.UP:\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\nbrain.screen.print(\"Up!\")\n\nwait(1, SECONDS)\n\n# Detect colors\noptical.gesture_disable()\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    if optical.color() == Color.RED:\n        brain.screen.print(\"Red Object!\")\n    else:\n        brain.screen.print(\"Not Red Object!\")\n    wait(0.02, SECONDS)\n\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_disable()"},"sensing_optical_set_mode_enable":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_mode_enable","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Enable\n\nSets a V5 Optical Sensor to detect gestures.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_enable()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Enable` command allows you to set a V5 Optical Sensor to detect gestures.\n \nBy default, a V5 Optical Sensor will be set to detect colors.\n\nBefore using any V5 Optical Sensor gesture commands, a V5 Optical Sensor must be correctly set to detect gestures.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set a V5 Optical Sensor to detect gestures before checking for gestures.\n\n```python\noptical.gesture_enable()\nwhile optical.get_gesture().type != GestureType.UP:\n    wait(0.1, SECONDS)\nbrain.screen.print(\"Up!\")\n```","signature":"optical.gesture_enable()"},"sensing_potentiometer_angle":{"name":"sensing_potentiometer_angle","markdown":"# Potentiometer Angle\n\nReturns the angular position of the Potentiometer.\n\n```don\npotentiometer.angle(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`potentiometer.angle` returns a decimal value to report the angular position of the Potentiometer.\n\nThe `UNITS` parameter accepts either **DEGREES** or **PERCENT** as an argument.\n\nIf the provided `UNITS` is in **DEGREES**, the range of returned values will be from **0.0 to 250.0 degrees** for a V5 Potentiometer, and from **0.0 to 330.0** degrees for a V5 Potentiometer V2.\n\nAlternatively, the returned values will range from **0 to 100%** if the provided `UNITS` is in **PERCENT**.","signature":"potentiometer.angle(UNITS)"},"sensing_range_finder_distance":{"name":"sensing_range_finder_distance","markdown":"# Distance From Range Finder\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor.\n\n```don\nrange_finder.distance(UNITS)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDistance from reports a range from 30mm to 3000mm or 2 inches to 115 inches.\n\nThe `UNITS` parameter accepts either **MM** or **INCHES** as a value.","signature":"range_finder.distance(MM)"},"sensing_range_finder_found_object":{"name":"sensing_range_finder_found_object","markdown":"# Range Finder Found Object\n\nReports if the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor detects an object within its field of view.\n\n```don\nrange_finder.found_object()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nObject found reports **True** when the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\nObject found reports **False** when the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor does not detect an object or surface.","signature":"range_finder.found_object()"},"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled":{"name":"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled","markdown":"# Controller Enabled\n\nEnables or disables Controller-configured actions from the Devices menu.\n\n```don\nremote_control_code_enabled = False\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose to either enable or disable the configured Controller actions. \n\nBy default, the Controller is Enabled in every project.","signature":"remote_control_code_enabled = False"},"sensing_rotation_angle":{"name":"sensing_rotation_angle","markdown":"# Rotation Angle\nReturns the angular position of a Rotation Sensor.\n\n```don\nrotation.angle()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`rotation.angle()` returns a decimal value with the current angular position of a Rotation Sensor in degrees.","signature":"rotation.angle()"},"sensing_rotation_position":{"name":"sensing_rotation_position","markdown":"# Rotation Position\nReports the current rotational position of a Rotation Sensor.\n\n```don\nrotation.position(UNIT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`rotation.position(UNIT)`  reports the position of a Rotation Sensor in integer numbers for degrees, and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nAcceptable values for ```UNIT``` are: ```DEGREES``` or ```TURNS```.","signature":"rotation.position(DEGREES)"},"sensing_rotation_set_position":{"name":"sensing_rotation_set_position","markdown":"# Set Rotation Position\nSets a Rotation Sensor's position to the given value.\n\n```don\nrotation.set_position(0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`rotation.set_position(0, DEGREES)` can be used to set a Rotation Sensor to a given positional value.\n\nUsually, `rotation.set_position(0, DEGREES)` will be used to reset a Rotation Sensor to 0 degrees.","signature":"rotation.set_position(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_rotation_velocity":{"name":"sensing_rotation_velocity","markdown":"# Rotation Velocity\nReports the current velocity of a Rotation Sensor.\n\n```don\nrotation.velocity(UNIT)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`rotation.velocity(UNIT)` will return the velocity of a Rotation Sensor in the ```UNIT``` that is passed.\n\nAcceptable values for the ```UNIT``` parameter are:\n\n* **VelocityUnits.RPM**\n* **VelocityUnits.DPS**","signature":"rotation.velocity(PERCENT)"},"sensing_vision_largest_object":{"name":"sensing_vision_largest_object","markdown":"# Largest Object\n\nReports information about the largest detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```python\nvision.largest_object()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nConfigure the Vision Sensor by adding signatures / codes.\n\nA call to the `vision.take_snapshot` command is then required to capture an image in the Vision Sensor prior to using the `vision.largest_object` command.\n\nThe example below will print some information about a detected object onto the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n\n    # Take a snapshot with the Vision Sensor with the specified signature and store the object data into a variable\n    vision_object = vision.take_snapshot(signature)\n\n    # Check the variable to see if a valid object was detected when the snapshot was captured\n    # If yes, print the data\n    if vision_object is not None:\n        brain.screen.print(\"Center X: \", vision.largest_object().centerX)\n        brain.screen.next_row()\n\n        brain.screen.print(\"Center Y: \", vision.largest_object().centerY)\n        brain.screen.next_row()\n\n        # Take a new snapshot every 0.2 seconds\n        wait(0.2, SECONDS)\n    else:\n        brain.screen.print(\"No Object Detected\")\n```\n\nThe following is a list of properties that can be accessed on the object returned by the `vision.largest_object` command:\n\n- `id` - A unique ID assigned to each object by the Vision Sensor\n- `originX` - The top left X position of the object\n- `originY` - The top left Y position of the object\n- `centerX` - The center X position of the object\n- `centerY` - The center Y position of the object\n- `width` - The width of the object\n- `height` - The height of the object\n- `angle` - The angle of the object\n- `exists` - If the Vision Sensor detects the object or not","signature":"vision.largest_object()"},"sensing_vision_take_snapshot":{"name":"sensing_vision_take_snapshot","markdown":"# Snapshot\n\nTakes a snapshot from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```don\nvision.take_snapshot(SIGNATURE)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe snapshot command will capture the current image from the Vision Sensor to be processed and analyzed for color signatures and codes.\n\nTypically, a snapshot is required first before using any other Vision Sensor commands.","signature":"vision.take_snapshot(SIGNATURE)"},"variables_my_2d_list":{"name":"variables_my_2d_list","markdown":"# 2D List Variable\n\n2D list variables are used to store lists with multiple rows and columns.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a 2D list variable, create a unique and meaningful variable name. This means that the variable name should accurately describe the nature of its values.\n\nFor example, a 2D list variable name `coordinates`  can be used to store multiple sets of coordinate values.\n\nDeclare this list using a single equal symbol `=` after your list name followed by square brackets `[ ]`.\n\nInside these square brackets, insert multiple sets of square brackets, separated by a comma, like so: `[[ ], [ ]]`. More than two sets of square brackets can be nested within the outer-most set of square brackets.\n\nInclude values that are separated with a comma or `,` in their respective brackets. If the variable is storing strings, place the comma outside of the enclosing `\" \"`.\n\nEach inner set of brackets represents a row of list items. The index of the item within the row represents a column of the 2D list.\n\nTo access the value of within a 2D list, use the name of the list, immediately followed by two indexes enclosed in square brackets. The first index references the row, while the second index references the column in the 2D list. Keep in mind that array indexes begin at 0, not 1.\n\nFor example, given a 2D list `coordinates = [[X1, Y1], [X2, Y2]]`, the expression `coordinates[0][0]` will return `X1`. \n\n## Example 1\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_list being assigned two separate lists of colors.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [[\"Green\", \"Red\", \"Blue\"], [\"Black\", \"Yellow\", \"Orange\"]]\n```\n\n## Example 2\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_list being assigned two separate lists of numbers.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]\n```","signature":"my_2d_list = [\\n\\t[0,0,0],\\n\\t[0,0,0],\\n\\t[0,0,0]\\n]"},"variables_my_boolean":{"name":"variables_my_boolean","markdown":"# Boolean Variable\n\nBoolean variables can hold either **True** or **False** values.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a boolean variable, create a unique and meaningful variable name. This means that the name of the variable should accurately describe the value that it is storing.\n\nFor example, a variable `pressed` should be used to store the value of whether a button is pressed.\n\nDeclare this variable with a equal symbol `=` following the Boolean name. Its value can either be `True` or `False`.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example assigns a value `True` to  `my_variable` .\n\n```don\nmy_variable = True\n```","signature":"my_boolean = True"},"variables_my_list":{"name":"variables_my_list","markdown":"# List Variable\n\nList variables are used to store multiple values.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a list variable, create a meaningful variable name. This means that the variable name should accurately describe the nature of its values.\n\nFor example, a list variable `colors` can be used to store multiple color values.\n\nTo assign a list of values to a list variable, use the `=` operator, followed by comma-separated values enclosed in a set of square brackets, `[ ]`.\n\nIf the values are numbers, the separating commas should come right after each value.\n\n`my_number_list = [1, 2, 3]`\n\nIf the values are strings, the commas should go outside of the `\" \"`.\n\n`my_string_list = [\"Hello\", \"World\"]`\n\nTo access a specific value in the list variable, enter the name of the list variable, immediately followed by an index enclosed by a set of square brackets. Keep in mind that the index of an array starts at 0, not 1.\n\nFor example, `my_string_list[0]` will return the value `\"Hello\"`.\n\n## Example 1\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_list being assigned the string values of several colors.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [\"Green\", \"Red\", \"Blue\"]\n```\n\n## Example 2\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_list being assigned several numbers.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [1, 2, 3]\n```","signature":"my_list = [0,0,0]"},"variables_my_number":{"name":"variables_my_number","markdown":"# Numeric Variable\n\nNumeric variables are used to store numerical values.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a numeric variable, create a meaningful variable name. This means that the variable name should accurately describe the value that it is storing. \n\nFor example, a variable `counter` should be used to store the value of a counter.\n\nTo assign a value to the variable, use the `=` operator. \n\n## Example 1\n\nThis example keeps the default variable name `my_number` and assigns it a value of 10.\n\n```don\nmy_number = 10\n```\n## Example 2\n\nThis example gives the variable the name `three_plus_two` and stores the result of the 3 added to 2. \n\n```don\nthree_plus_two = 3 + 2\n```","signature":"my_number = 1"},"variables_my_string":{"name":"variables_my_string","markdown":"# String Variable\n\nString variables are used to store strings.\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo create a string variable, create a meaningful variable name. This means that the variable name should accurately describe its value. \n\nFor example, a variable `name` should be used to store the value of a name.\n\nTo assign a string to a string variable, use the `=` operator. It's string value can be enclosed in either `\" \"` or `' '`.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_string being assigned the string value `\"Hello\"`.\n\n```don\nmy_string = \"Hello\"\n```","signature":"my_string = \\\"Hello World\\\""},"vr_thread":{"name":"vr_thread","markdown":"# VR Thread\n\nThe VR Thread function must be used to call functions at the global level of the program. It can be used to start threads to run simultaneously.\n\n```python\nvr_thread(function_name)\n```\nNotice that the function name is passed as a reference to the `vr_thread()` call rather than calling the function inside a VR Thread such as `vr_thread(function_name())`.\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou can take any function you have in the program and pass its reference to `vr_thread()` on the global scope. Using VR Threads are necessary in order for multiple functions to run in parallel. \n\nThe functions will, in general, execute in the order that they are passed into `vr_thread()` calls. If a function is waiting for a command to complete, it will pass program execution to another function, and resume its execution when the other function finishes running, or is also waiting for a command to complete.\n\nThe functions that causes threads to switch program execution:\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM, wait=True)\ndrivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 90, DEGREES, wait=True)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES, wait=TRUE)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90, DEGREES, wait=TRUE)\ndrivetrain.set_heading(0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)\nwait(1, SECONDS)\n\nAny user-created function\n```\n\n## Example 1\n\nWe make a single function that is executed in the global scope with `vr_thread()`. The `move_drivetrain()` function will make the robot move 200 mm and then print when it is done.\n\n```python\ndef move_drivetrain():\n    drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Done moving\")\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n\nvr_thread(move_drivetrain)\n```\n\n## Example 2\n\nNow we added the `lower_fork()` function. This will move the fork down and print a message when the fork is fully lowered.\n\nWe make the call `vr_thread(lower_fork)` **after** the `vr_thread(move_drivetrain)` call. However, because `drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 500, MM)` makes the thread wait, it will switch program execution over to the `lower_fork` function, which will start lowering the fork before the drivetrain completes its movements.\n\n```python\ndef move_drivetrain():\n    drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 500, MM)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Done moving\")\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n\ndef lower_fork():\n    fork_motor_group.spin_for(FORWARD, 1700, DEGREES)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Fork lowered\")\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n\nvr_thread(move_drivetrain)\nvr_thread(lower_fork)\n```","signature":"vr_thread(function_name)"}},"cpp":{"arm_activate_emergency_stop":{"name":"arm_activate_emergency_stop","markdown":"# Activate emergency stop\n\nActivates the emergency stop (or E-stop) button for the V5 Robotic Arm.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.emergencyStop();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe emergency stop button in the Workcell will shut off any V5 Smart Motors and Sensors connected to the V5 Brain. \n\n![estop_robot](static/help/v5/cpp/en/arm_activate_emergency_stop/estop_robot.png)\n\nThe `RoboticArm.emergencyStop();` command is often used with the `bumper.pressed()` command from the Events category. This ensures that all V5 Smart Motors and Sensors connected to the V5 Brain will shut off once the Bumper Switch (E-stop) is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nvoid onEstop() {\n  arm.emergencyStop();\n}\n\nint main() {\n  emergencyStopButton.pressed(onEstop);\n}\n```","signature":"RoboticArm.emergencyStop();"},"arm_enable_manual_movement":{"name":"arm_enable_manual_movement","markdown":"# Enable manual movement\n\nAllows the arm of the V5 Workcell to be manually moved by hand.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.enableManualMovement();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, the motors on the Workcell lock in place when a project is running. To be able to manually move the arm, use the `RoboticArm.enableManualMovement();` command in your project.\n\n![movement](static/help/v5/cpp/en/arm_enable_manual_movement/movement.png)","signature":"RoboticArm.enableManualMovement();"},"arm_enter_mastering_mode":{"name":"arm_enter_mastering_mode","markdown":"# Enter mastering mode\n\nStarts the mastering process for the four joints of the arm on the Workcell to allow it to be calibrated to the same known location.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.enterMasteringMode();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `RoboticArm.enterMasteringMode();` command begins the mastering process for the arm on the V5 Workcell. \n\nThis command is used in the 'Arm Mastering' example project.","signature":"RoboticArm.enterMasteringMode();"},"arm_joint_move":{"name":"arm_joint_move","markdown":"# Joint move\n\nMoves the V5 Robotic Arm to the specified (x, y, z) coordinate using joint movement.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.moveToPositionJoint(0, 0, 0);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `RoboticArm.moveToPositionJoint(0, 0, 0);` command moves the V5 Robotic Arm in the x, y, and z-direction using joint movement. \n\nThe default position is (0, 0, 0) in the unit of inches.\n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/cpp/en/arm_joint_move/xyz_coord.png)","signature":"RoboticArm.moveToPositionJoint(0, 0, 0);"},"arm_linear_move":{"name":"arm_linear_move","markdown":"# Linear move\n\nMoves the V5 Robotic Arm to the specified (x, y, z) coordinate using linear movement.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.moveToPositionLinear(0, 0, 0);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `RoboticArm.moveToPositionLinear(0, 0, 0);` command moves the V5 Robotic Arm in the x, y, and z-direction using linear movement. \n\nThe default position is (0, 0, 0) in the unit of inches.\n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/cpp/en/arm_linear_move/xyz_coord.png)","signature":"RoboticArm.moveToPositionLinear(0, 0, 0);"},"arm_set_angle":{"name":"arm_set_angle","markdown":"# Set angle\n\nSets the angle of the tool plate before the next linear or joint movement command is executed.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setArmAngle(0);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `RoboticArm.setArmAngle(0)` command sets the tool plate to be tilted at the specified angle in degrees, before the next linear or joint movement command in a project.\n\nNote that the `RoboticArm.setArmAngle(0)` command sets the angle for all future linear or joint movement commands, unless it is set otherwise.\n\n![tool_plate](static/help/v5/cpp/en/arm_set_angle/tool_plate.png)\n\nChoose the angle of the tool plate. The default is set to **90** degrees. The accepted range is **0** to **90** degrees.\n\n* The tool plate will be **horizontal**, or parallel to the Workcell surface when it is set to 0 degrees.\n* The tool plate will be **vertical**, or perpendicular to the Workcell surface when it is set to 90 degrees.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the tool plate will begin to tilt once the joint move command is executed and complete its tilting movement before the linear move command.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setMasteringValues(1802, 2212, 1556, 369);\nRoboticArm.setArmAngle(90);\nRoboticArm.moveToPositionJoint(10, -2.8, 3);\nRoboticArm.moveToPositionLinear(9, 4.53, 3.5);\n```","signature":"RoboticArm.setArmAngle(0);"},"arm_set_joint_move_speed":{"name":"arm_set_joint_move_speed","markdown":"# Set joint speed\n\nSets the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's joint movements.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setJointMoveSpeed(25.0);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSpecify the movement speed for joint movements in degrees per second. The default speed is 25 degrees per second. You can make the arm move faster by specifying a higher speed.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setJointMoveSpeed(50.0);\n```\n\nYou can make the arm move slower by specifiying a lower speed.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setJointMoveSpeed(10.0);\n```","signature":"RoboticArm.setJointMoveSpeed(25.0);"},"arm_set_linear_move_speed":{"name":"arm_set_linear_move_speed","markdown":"# Set linear speed\n\nSets the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's linear movements.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setLinearMoveSpeed(5.0);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSpecify the movement speed for linear movements in inches per second. The default speed is 5 inches per second. You can make the arm move faster by specifying a higher speed.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setLinearMoveSpeed(10.0);\n```\n\nYou can make the arm move slower by specifiying a lower speed.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setLinearMoveSpeed(2.0);\n```","signature":"RoboticArm.setLinearMoveSpeed(5.0);"},"arm_set_mastering":{"name":"arm_set_mastering","markdown":"# Set mastering\n\nSets the mastering values of the four joints of the V5 Robotic Arm to allow it to be calibrated to the same known location.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setMasteringValues(0, 0, 0, 0);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nInput the mastering values from the V5 Brain to the `RoboticArm.setMasteringValues(0, 0, 0, 0)` command. \n\nThe passable threshold values for the joints are as follows:\n\n* Joint 1: 1600 - 2000\n* Joint 2: 1900 - 2400\n* Joint 3: 1700 - 2100\n* Joint 4: 200 - 650\n\n![mastering_values](static/help/v5/cpp/en/arm_set_mastering/mastering_values.png)","signature":"RoboticArm.setMasteringValues(0, 0, 0, 0);"},"arm_set_tool":{"name":"arm_set_tool","markdown":"# Set tool offset\n\nSets the position offset for the end effector or the end-of-arm tooling (EOAT) on the V5 Robotic Arm.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setToolTipOffset(0.0, 0.0, 0.0);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe end effector on the V5 Robotic Arm can be at a position relative to the attachment plate on the arm. To keep the coordinate space the same, you can specify the tool offsets.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setToolTipOffset(dr, dp, dz);\n```\n\n* **dr** - the distance along the X-axis from the end of the attachment plate.\n* **dp** - the distance along the Y-axis from the center of the attachment plate.\n\n![offset_xy](static/help/v5/cpp/en/arm_set_tool/offset_xy.png)\n\n* **dz** - the distance along the Z-axis from the bottom of the attachment plate.\n\n![offset_z](static/help/v5/cpp/en/arm_set_tool/offset_z.png)\n\nThe default coordinates for none, electromagnet, and marker are the following:\n\n* **none**: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0)\n* **electromagnet**: (-0.7, 0.0, -2.0)\n* **marker**: (1.05, 0.0, -1.0)","signature":"RoboticArm.setToolTipOffset(0.0, 0.0, 0.0);"},"control_break":{"name":"control_break","markdown":"# Break\n\nExits a repeating loop immediately.\n\n```cpp\nbreak;\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen added inside of a loop, the `break;` command will exit the loop it is currently running inside of. \n\n## Example\n\nThis example will move the Drivetrain forward and check if the V5 Brain’s screen has been pressed. \n\nIf the screen is **pressed**, the `break;` command will exit the while loop and stop the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n  if(Brain.Screen.pressing()) {\n    break;\n  }\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"break;"},"control_elseif":{"name":"control_elseif","markdown":"# Else If\n\nA control statement that runs the code inside the set of curly brackets based on the Boolean value of the conditional.\n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n  // Some code to run if the condition returns true\n} else if (condition2) {\n  // Some code to run if the first condition returns false and the second condition returns true\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe else if statement will only check the Boolean condition once.\n\nIf the Boolean `(condition)` is **false** and the Boolean `(condition2)` is reported as **true**, the code inside of `else if's` curly brackets will run.\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the LeftMotor will stop if the bumper is pressed and will spin forward when released.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  if (BumperA.pressing()) {\n    LeftMotor.stop();\n  } else if (!BumperA.pressing()) {\n    LeftMotor.spin(forward);\n  }\n\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"else if (true) { }"},"control_for":{"name":"control_for","markdown":"# For\n\nA type of loop that repeats the code contained inside for a set number of iterations.\n\n```cpp\nfor (initialization; condition; increment/decrement) {\n   // code here will repeat a number of times\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nFirst enter a value to indicate how many times the stack will **repeat** the code contained inside.\n\nThe **for** loop keeps track of how many times to repeat using 3 expressions:\n\n* initialization\n* condition\n* increment/decrement expression.\n\n**Initialization** specifies the initial value of the iterating variable. You can also declare a variable in the initialization statement.\n\n**Condition** is used to set the condition to specify how long the **for** loop will continue running. The **for** loop will stop looping if the counter value will return false using this condition.\n\n**Increment/decrement** expression is used to change the iterating variable at the end of each iteration of the **for** loop.\n\nThe following for-loop will print a number 0 to 9:\n\n```cpp\nfor(int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n   Brain.Screen.print(i);\n   Brain.Screen.newLine();\n}\n```\n\n**For** loops can also be put inside of each other. This concept is called nesting which can help save time when programming different behaviors.","signature":"for(int i = 0; i < length; i++) { }"},"control_if":{"name":"control_if","markdown":"# If\n\nRuns the code inside if-statement's curly brackets, if the condition returns true. \n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **if-statement** will only check its condition inside the parenthesis once.\n\nIf the condition returns **true**, the codes inside the curly brackets will run.\n\nIf the condition returns **false**, the codes inside the curly brackets will be skipped.\n\n```cpp\nif (BumperA.pressing()) {\n    Motor1.stop();\n}\n```","signature":"if(true) { }"},"control_if_else":{"name":"control_if_else","markdown":"# If/Else\n\nRuns the code inside the else-statement's curly brackets, if the if-statement's condition is false. This command must have an if-statement preceding for it to compile.\n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n\n} else {\n\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **if-statement** will only check its condition inside the parenthesis once.\n\nIf the condition returns **true**, the code inside the if-statement's curly brackets will run.\n\nIf the condition returns **false**, the code inside the else-statement's curly brackets will be skipped\n\n```cpp\nif (BumperA.pressing()) {\n    LeftMotor.stop();\n} else {\n    LeftMotor.spin(forward);\n}\n```","signature":"else { }"},"control_repeat":{"name":"control_repeat","markdown":"# repeat\n\nRepeats the code inside curly brackets for a set number of times. \n\n```\nrepeat (10) {\n\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **repeat-statement** will loop through the code contained in the brackets until it reaches the number of iterations set in the condition.\n\nFirst, set the number of times the code will loop by changing the condition to any positive integer. The condition can also be a variable or sensor data.\n\nThe snippet below will print \"iteration\" to the Brain's Screen four times. Each time, it will create a new line before printing the next iteration.\n\n```\nrepeat (4) {\n  Brain.Screen.Print(\"iteration\");\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  wait(5, msec);\n}\n```\n\nNote that the **repeat-statement** cannot be nested inside of another repeat statement.","signature":"repeat(10) { }"},"control_stop_project":{"name":"control_stop_project","markdown":"# Stop Project\n\nStops a running project.\n\n```cpp\nvexSystemExitRequest();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Stop Project` command can be used to programmatically stop an actively running project.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will drive a V5 Robot forward 200mm and turn right for 90 degrees before stopping the project.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);\nDrivetrain.turnFor(right, 90, degrees);\nvexSystemExitRequest();\n```","signature":"vexSystemExitRequest();"},"control_wait":{"name":"control_wait","markdown":"# Wait\n\nWaits for a specific amount of time before moving to the next command.\n\n```cpp\nwait(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet an amount of time in **seconds** to have your program **wait** before executing subsequent commands.\n\n```cpp\n// Wait for 5 seconds before driving forward\nwait(5, seconds);\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n```","signature":"wait(time, seconds);"},"control_wait_until":{"name":"control_wait_until","markdown":"# Wait Until\n\nRun a set of commands until the **condition** evaluates to **true** before moving to the next command.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (!condition) {\n  // Run some commands\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `while` loop will repeatedly check its condition, and will **not** execute any subsequent lines of code until the condition returns **true**.\n\n```cpp\n// Keep driving forward until the Bumper Pressing command returns true\nwhile (!Bumper.pressing()) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n}\n\n// Stop the Drivetrain after the Bumper is pressed\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"while (!condition) {\\n\\n};"},"control_while":{"name":"control_while","markdown":"# While\nA loop that repeats the code inside the curly brackets while the condition evaluates as **true**.   \n\n```cpp\nwhile (condition) {\n\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `while` loop will only check condition inside the parenthesis at the beginning of each loop. \n\nIf the condition evaluates as **true**, the code inside of `while` will run.\n\nIf the condition evaluates as **false**, the code inside of `while` will be skipped.\n\nThe `while` loop accepts anything that evaluates to true or false as its condition. You can place Booleans, and expressions using comparison and logical operators. You can also put numbers; **0** evaluates to **false**, and any **non-zero numbers** evaluates to **true**. \n\n```cpp\n// Drive forward while the timer value is less than 10 seconds\n\nwhile(Brain.Timer.time(seconds) < 10) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"while(true) { }"},"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain":{"name":"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain","markdown":"# Drivetrain Calibrate\n\nCalibrates the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\ncalibrateDrivetrain();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `calibrateDrivetrain();` command will calibrate the Drivetrain. The Drivetrain must remain stationary during the calibration process.\n\nThe `calibrateDrivetrain();` command will cause your program to wait until the calibration process is done.\n\n```cpp\ncalibrateDrivetrain();\n```","signature":"calibrateDrivetrain();"},"drivetrain_drive":{"name":"drivetrain_drive","markdown":"# Drivetrain Drive\n\nMoves the Drivetrain forever. All drivetrain motors are run forwards or backwards at the speed that was set using `Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity`, the default speed is 50 rpm.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(directionType);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.drive();` command will run the Drivetrain forever, until a new Drivetrain command is used, or the program is stopped.\n\nUse the `forward` parameter to drive the Drivetrain in the forward direction.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n```\n\nUse the `reverse` parameter to drive the Drivetrain in the reverse direction.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(reverse);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.drive(forward);"},"drivetrain_drive_for":{"name":"drivetrain_drive_for","markdown":"# Drivetrain Drive For\n\nMoves the Drivetrain for a given distance. All drivetrain motors are run forwards or backwards at the speed that was set using `Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity`. After the drivetrain has moved the requested distance the motors are stopped.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(directionType, distance, distanceUnits);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet how far the Drivetrain will move by entering a direction (`forward` or `reverse`) with a value and specifying the unit of measurement (`inches` or `mm`).\n\nThe `Drivetrain.driveFor();` accepts numeric values for `distance`.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(reverse, 5.0, inches);\n```\n\nThe **driveFor** command will block other commands until the Drivetrain movement has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to tell the **driveFor** command to not block the program until the movement has completed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 5.0, inches, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Drivetrain Set Drive Velocity\n\nSets the velocity of the Drivetrain that will be used for drive and driveFor calls. If this is used when the drive is moving, the drivetrain will be updated with the new speed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity();` will set the speed of the Drivetrain when driving straight, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move. \n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity();` accepts a range from **-100 to 100** when using the `percent` units.\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity();` accepts a range from **-600 to 600** when using the `rpm` units.\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity();` can use a \"rotations per minute\" (rpm) value based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to drive in the opposite direction.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to 0 will cause the Drivetrain to stop.","signature":"Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity(50, percent);"},"drivetrain_set_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_set_heading","markdown":"# Drivetrain Set Heading\n\nSets the Gyro of the Drivetrain to an exact heading.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setHeading(heading, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setHeading();` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's position to any given heading. This command can be used to reset the orientation of the Drivetrain's Gyro when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`Drivetrain.setHeading();` accepts a range of **0 to 360** degrees.\n\n```cpp\n// Reset the Drivetrain heading to 0\n\nDrivetrain.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_rotation","markdown":"# Drivetrain Set Rotation\n\nSets the Drivetrain's angle of rotation when configured with a 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setRotation()` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive or negative value.\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setRotation()` command can accept integers or numeric commands\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setRotation()` command **does not** have a limit of 0-359 degrees.\n\nThis example will turn the robot a total of 210 degrees:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(120, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n```\n\n- Turn right (clockwise) to rotation 120 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current position as rotation of -45 degrees.\n- Turn right (clockwise) an additional 90 degrees (-45 degrees to +45 degrees) based on the set rotation value from the previous command.","signature":"Drivetrain.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_stopping":{"name":"drivetrain_set_stopping","markdown":"# Drivetrain Set Stopping\n\nSets the brake mode of the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setStopping(brakeType);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nHere are possible `brakeType` inputs that you can specify: \n\n* `brake` will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop, and will not correct for outside forces.\n* `coast` lets the Drivetrain spin gradually to a stop.\n* `hold` will cause the Drivetrain to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved by an outside force, by using the built-in encoder.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the Drivetrain move forward for 3 seconds and then hold its position once stopped.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setStopping(hold);\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setStopping(brake);"},"drivetrain_set_timeout":{"name":"drivetrain_set_timeout","markdown":"# Drivetrain Set Timeout\n\nSets the timeout for the Drivetrain to stop moving if a blocking command cannot reach its target.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.setTimeout();` is used to prevent drive commands that do not reach their position from preventing other commands in the program from running.\n\nAn example of a Drivetrain not reaching its position is when a robot is driven against a wall and cannot complete its movement.\n\nSet the timeout by specifying the amount of time in `seconds`.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(2.0, seconds);\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will end the `Drivetrain.driveFor();` command after 2 seconds if the Drivetrain has not reached the target of 24 inches. \n\nOnce the time limit or distance is reached, the Drivetrain will move on to the `Drivetrain.turnFor();` command.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(2.0, seconds);\nDrivetrain.driveFor(24.0, inches, true);\nDrivetrain.turnFor(90.0, degrees, true);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setTimeout(1, seconds);"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Drivetrain Set Turn Velocity\n\nSets the velocity of the Drivetrain when turning. If this is used when the drivetrain is turning, the drivetrain will be updated with the new speed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTurnVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity();` will set the speed of the Drivetrain when turning, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move. \n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity();` accepts a range from **-100 to 100** when using the `percent` units.\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity();` accepts a range from **-600 to 600** when using the `rpm` units.\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity();` can use a \"rotations per minute\" (rpm) value based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to turn in the opposite direction.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's turn velocity to 0 will cause the Drivetrain to stop.","signature":"Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity(50, percent);"},"drivetrain_stop":{"name":"drivetrain_stop","markdown":"# Drivetrain Stop\n\nStops the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.stop();` command will cause the Drivetrain to come to a complete stop and use the `Drivetrain.setStopping();` to set either `coast`, `brake`, or `hold` its position.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will stop the Drivetrain after 3 seconds.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.stop();"},"drivetrain_turn":{"name":"drivetrain_turn","markdown":"# Drivetrain Turn\n\nTurns the Drivetrain indefinitely.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(turnType);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turn();` command will rotate the Drivetrain forever, until a new Drivetrain command is used, or the program is stopped.\n\nUse the `left` parameter to turn the Drivetrain to the left.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n```\n\nUse the `right` parameter to turn the Drivetrain to the right.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(right);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turn(right);"},"drivetrain_turn_for":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_for","markdown":"# Drivetrain Turn For\n\n`Drivetrain.turnFor()` causes the Drivetrain to turn for the requested angle and direction.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(turnType, angle, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSet how far the Drivetrain will move by entering a direction (`left` or `right`) and a number of degrees.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(right, 270, degrees);\n```\n\nThe **turnFor** command will block other commands until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to tell the **turnFor** command to not block the program until the movement has completed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(left, 90, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnFor(right, 90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_turn_to_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Drivetrain Turn To Heading\n\nTurns a Drivetrain to a specific heading, when using the Gyro or Inertial sensors.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading(heading, units);`\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turnToHeading();` command can be used to turn the Drivetrain to any given clockwise heading.\n\nBased on the current heading of the Gyro, `Drivetrain.turnToHeading();` will determine which direction to turn.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading();` accepts a range of **0.00 to 359.99** when using the unit `degrees`.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns: \n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(270.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(180.0, degrees);\n```\n\n- Right to 45 degrees\n- Right to 90 degrees\n- Right to 270 degrees\n- Left to 180 degrees\n\nThe **turnToHeading** command will block other commands until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to tell the **turnToHeading** command to not block the program until the movement has completed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(180.0, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnToHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Drivetrain Turn To Rotation\n\nTurns a Drivetrain to a specific angle of rotation when configured with a 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToRotation(rotation, units);`\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turnToRotation();` command can be used to turn the Drivetrain to a given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\nBased on the current **rotation** value of the Drivetrain, `Drivetrain.turnToRotation();` will determine which direction to turn.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToRotation();` can accept decimals, integers, or numeric units.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToRotation();` is **not** limited to 0-359.99 degrees. Turns will be absolute and may cause the robot to rotate more than once if necessary.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(90.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(180, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnTorotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(0, degrees);\n```\n\n- Right (clockwise) to 90 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to 180 degrees\n- Left (counter-clockwise) to -45 degrees\n- Right (clockwise) to 0 degrees\n\nThe `Drivetrain.turnToRotation();`command will block other commands until the Drivetrain turn has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to tell the `Drivetrain.turnToRotation();` command to not block the program until the movement has completed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(180.0, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnToRotation(90, degrees);"},"events_brain_screen_pressed":{"name":"events_brain_screen_pressed","markdown":"#  Brain Screen Pressed\n\nRuns the callback function when the V5 Brain’s touchscreen is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.pressed();` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors based on touch interaction with the V5 Brain's touchscreen. \n\nUsed together with the `Brain.Screen.xPosition()` and `Brain.Screen.yPosition()` commands, users can create custom interfaces to their V5 Brain by detecting when and where touches occur on the screen.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the screen gets pressed. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Brain.Screen.pressed(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.pressed(callback);"},"events_brain_screen_released":{"name":"events_brain_screen_released","markdown":"#  Brain Screen Released\n\nRuns the callback function when the V5 Brain’s touchscreen is pressed or released.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.released(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.released();` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors based on touch interaction with the V5 Brain's touchscreen. \n\nUsed together with the `Brain.Screen.xPosition()` and `Brain.Screen.yPosition()` commands, users can create custom interfaces to their V5 Brain by detecting when and where touches occur on the screen.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the screen gets released. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Brain.Screen.released(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.released(callback);"},"events_brain_timer_event":{"name":"events_brain_timer_event","markdown":"# Brain Timer Event\n\nRuns the specified callback function when the V5 Brain's timer is greater than the given value.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.event(callback, 1000);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 Brain's timer begins at the beginning of each project.\n\nSpecify the amount of time. The `Brain.Timer.event();` event will run once the V5 Brain's timer is **greater than** the entered amount.\n\nThe `Brain.Timer.event();` command can accept integer values for the number of milliseconds.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the timer is greater than the entered amount. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Brain.Timer.event(runOnEvent, 2000);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Timer.event(callback, 1000);"},"events_bumper_pressed":{"name":"events_bumper_pressed","markdown":"# Bumper Pressed\n\nRuns the specified function when the bumper is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nBumperA.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Bumper Sensor is pressed. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  BumperA.pressed(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"BUMPER.pressed(callback);"},"events_bumper_released":{"name":"events_bumper_released","markdown":"# Bumper Released\n\nRuns the specified function when the bumper is released.\n\n```cpp\nBumperA.released(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Bumper Switch is released. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  BumperA.released(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"BUMPER.released(callback);"},"events_competition_autonomous":{"name":"events_competition_autonomous","markdown":"# Competition Autonomous\n\nRuns the specified function when an \"autonomous\" mode signal is received from a competition field or competition switch.\n\nMake sure that the competition object is defined or use a competition template from the Examples Projects.\n\n```cpp\nCompetition.autonomous(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Competition Autonomous signal is received. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Create a Competition Object\ncompetition Competition;\n\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Competition.autonomous(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"Competition.autonomous(callback);"},"events_competition_drivercontrol":{"name":"events_competition_drivercontrol","markdown":"# Competition Driver Control\n\nRuns the specified function when an \"driver control\" mode signal is received from a competition field or competition switch.\n\nMake sure that the competition object is defined or use a competition template from the Examples Projects.\n\n```cpp\nCompetition.drivercontrol(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Competition Driver Control signal is received. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Create a Competition Object\ncompetition Competition;\n\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Competition.drivercontrol(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"Competition.drivercontrol(callback);"},"events_competition_new_competition":{"name":"events_competition_new_competition","markdown":"# New Competition\n\nCreate a new competition instance.\n\n```cpp\ncompetition Competition = competition();\n\ncompetition Competition;\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nUsing either of the above syntaxes, a new competition instance can be created before registering callback functions.\n\n```cpp\n// Create a new Competition instance\ncompetition Competition;\n\n// Function to run when the \"autonomous\" signal is received\nvoid runOnAutonomous() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Running autonomous\");\n}\n\n// Function to run when the \"driver control\" signal is received\nvoid runOnDriverControl() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Running driver control\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register competition event with callback functions.\n  Competition.autonomous(runOnAutonomous);\n  Competition.drivercontrol(runOnDriverControl);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"competition Competition = competition();"},"events_controller_axis_changed":{"name":"events_controller_axis_changed","markdown":"# Controller Axis Changed\n\nRuns the specified function when the controller axis value changes.\n\n```cpp\nController1.Axis1.changed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller axis to monitor.\n\n* `Axis1`\n* `Axis2`\n* `Axis3`\n* `Axis4`\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Controller Axis position is changed. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Controller1.Axis1.changed(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.AXIS.changed(callback);"},"events_controller_button_pressed":{"name":"events_controller_button_pressed","markdown":"# Controller Button Pressed\n\nRuns the specified function when the controller button is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nController1.ButtonA.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller button to monitor.\n\n* `ButtonA`\n* `ButtonB`\n* `ButtonX`\n* `ButtonY`\n* `ButtonUp`\n* `ButtonDown`\n* `ButtonLeft`\n* `ButtonRight`\n* `ButtonL1`\n* `ButtonL2`\n* `ButtonR1`\n* `ButtonR2`\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Controller Button is pressed. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Controller1.ButtonA.pressed(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.BUTTON.pressed(callback);"},"events_controller_button_released":{"name":"events_controller_button_released","markdown":"# Controller Button Released\n\nRuns the specified function when the controller button is released.\n\n```cpp\nController1.ButtonA.released(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller button to monitor.\n\n* `ButtonA`\n* `ButtonB`\n* `ButtonX`\n* `ButtonY`\n* `ButtonUp`\n* `ButtonDown`\n* `ButtonLeft`\n* `ButtonRight`\n* `ButtonL1`\n* `ButtonL2`\n* `ButtonR1`\n* `ButtonR2`\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Controller Button is released. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Controller1.ButtonA.released(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.BUTTON.released(callback);"},"events_event":{"name":"events_event","markdown":"# Event Register Callback\n\nRegister a callback function to run when an event is triggered.\n\n```cpp\nEvent(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nRegister a callback to a user-defined event.\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"myEvent triggered runOnBroadcast callback\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create a new event.\n  event myEvent;\n\n  // Register a callback function to the myEvent event.\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast);\n  \n  // Brief wait to ensure event is registered\n  wait(15, msec);\n\n  // Broadcast the event.\n  myEvent.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"EVENT(callback);"},"events_event_broadcast":{"name":"events_event_broadcast","markdown":"# Event Broadcast\n\nBroadcast event message to run listener functions.\n\n```cpp\nEvent.broadcast();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe code will continue to run the commands after the `Event.broadcast();` command so that it will run at the same time as the event listener functions.\n\nBefore using this command, a user defined event must be created and register at least one callback.\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast1() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\");\n}\n\nvoid runOnBroadcast2() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create a new event.\n  event myEvent;\n\n  // Register callback functions to event.\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast1);\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast2);\n  \n  // Brief wait to ensure event is registered\n  wait(15, msec);\n\n  // Broadcast the event.\n  myEvent.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"EVENT.broadcast();"},"events_event_broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Event Broadcast and Wait\n\nBroadcast event message to run listener functions and wait for all listeners to finish before continuing.\n\n```cpp\nEvent.broadcastAndWait();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Event.broadcastAndWait();` command will wait for all listeners to complete before returning. This will pause the code execution in the current function, until all the broadcast listeners have finished.\n\nBefore using this command, a user defined event must be created and register at least one callback.\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast1() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\");\n}\n\nvoid runOnBroadcast2() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create a new event.\n  event myEvent;\n\n  // Register callback functions to event.\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast1);\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast2);\n  \n  // Brief wait to ensure event is registered\n  wait(15, msec);\n\n  // Broadcast the event and wait for completion.\n  myEvent.broadcastAndWait();\n\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(3, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Listeners finished running\");\n}\n```","signature":"EVENT.broadcastAndWait();"},"events_event_new_event":{"name":"events_event_new_event","markdown":"# New Event\n\nCreate a new event.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event();\n\nevent myEvent;\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nUsing either of the above syntaxes, a new user-defined event can be created before registering callback functions.\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast1() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\");\n}\n\nvoid runOnBroadcast2() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create new events.\n  event myEvent1 = event();\n  event myEvent2;\n\n\n  // Register callback functions to the events.\n  myEvent1(runOnBroadcast1);\n  myEvent2(runOnBroadcast2);\n  \n  // Brief wait to ensure events are registered\n  wait(15, msec);\n  \n  // Broadcast the events.\n  myEvent1.broadcast();\n  myEvent2.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"event Event = new event();"},"events_gps_heading_changed":{"name":"events_gps_heading_changed","markdown":"# GPS When Heading Changed\n\nRuns the specified callback function when the GPS Sensor detects a heading change.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.changed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to define a function to call when the GPS Sensor detects a heading change.\n\nProvide the name of the defined function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnHeadingChange() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"GPS Heading Change Detected\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  GPS.changed(runOnHeadingChange);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"GPS.changed(callback);"},"events_limit_pressed":{"name":"events_limit_pressed","markdown":"# LimitSwitch Pressed\n\nRuns the specified function when the limit switch is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nLimitA.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Limit Switch is pressed. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  LimitA.pressed(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"LIMIT.pressed(callback);"},"events_limit_released":{"name":"events_limit_released","markdown":"# LimitSwitch Released\n\nRuns the specified function when the Limit Switch is released.\n\n```cpp\nLimitA.released(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Limit Switch is released. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  LimitA.released(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"LIMIT.released(callback);"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_down":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_down","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when the gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureDown(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `Optical.gestureEnable();` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gestureUp`\n- `gestureDown`\n- `gestureLeft`\n- `gestureRight`\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Gesture detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\n  Optical.gestureEnable();\n\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.gestureDown(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureDown(callback);"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_left":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_left","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when the gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureLeft(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `Optical.gestureEnable();` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gestureUp`\n- `gestureDown`\n- `gestureLeft`\n- `gestureRight`\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Gesture detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\n  Optical.gestureEnable();\n\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.gestureLeft(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureLeft(callback);"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_right":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_right","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when the gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureRight(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `Optical.gestureEnable();` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gestureUp`\n- `gestureDown`\n- `gestureLeft`\n- `gestureRight`\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Gesture detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\n  Optical.gestureEnable();\n\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.gestureRight(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureRight(callback);"},"events_optical_detect_gesture_up":{"name":"events_optical_detect_gesture_up","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when the gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureUp(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a gesture is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when a gesture is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\nYou will also need to ensure that the Optical Sensor is set to detect gestures by calling `Optical.gestureEnable();` before gesture commands are used.\n\n`Optical Gesture Detected` can be used to detect four different gestures:\n\n- `gestureUp`\n- `gestureDown`\n- `gestureLeft`\n- `gestureRight`\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Gesture detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Set the Optical Sensor to detect gestures\n  Optical.gestureEnable();\n\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.gestureUp(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureUp(callback);"},"events_optical_object_detected":{"name":"events_optical_object_detected","markdown":"# Optical Object Detected\n\nRuns the callback function when an object is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.objectDetected(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical.objectDetected();` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when an object is detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when an object is detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Object detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.objectDetected(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.objectDetected(callback);"},"events_optical_object_lost":{"name":"events_optical_object_lost","markdown":"# Optical Object Lost\n\nRuns the callback function when a detected object is no longer being detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.objectLost(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical.objectLost();` command can be used to trigger actions or behaviors when a V5 Optical Sensor no longer detects a previously-detected object.\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the object is no longer being detected. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the **callback** parameter.\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Object lost!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.objectLost(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.objectLost(callback);"},"function_name":{"name":"function_name","markdown":"# Functions\n\nFunctions are segments of code used to perform a set of actions.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myFunction() {\n  // function code\n}\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nTo define a function, declare the type of data that the function will return.\n\n- `int`, `float`, `double`, and `string` are commonly returned data types. If the function will not return a value declare the return type as `void`. \n\nThen, use a meaningful function name that describes what the function does.\n\n```cpp\nint returnZero() {\n  return 0;\n}\n```\n\nInclude parentheses `()` with optional *parameters* after the function name. Multiple parameters should be separated by commas (parameter1, parameter2).\n\nThe body of the function should be enclosed in curly brackets `{ }`.\n    \n## Example\n\nThis function has no parameters and returns no value and so its return type is declared as `void`. This function prints \"The battery is low!\" to the VEX V5 Brain Screen if the battery capacity is below 25%.\n\n```cpp\nvoid lowOnBattery() {\n  if (Brain.Battery.capacity() < 25.0) {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"The battery is low!\");\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"function_name"},"function_thread":{"name":"function_thread","markdown":"# Threads\n\nAllows you to execute multiple threads at the same time.\n\n```cpp\nthread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA function needs to be defined that will be passed as a callback to the thread.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myThreadCallback() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"In a different thread!\");\n}\n```\nOnce you have the function written, you can use it to make a new thread. This function is referred to as the **callback function**.\n\n```cpp\nthread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n```\nThe **thread** will start executing once it is created. It will then run at the same time as the main thread.\n    \n## Example\n\nThis example will print two counters to the VEX V5's Brain at the same time. One will be printed by the `myThread` thread. The other will be printed by the main thread at the same time.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myThreadCallback() {\n  int count = 0;\n  while (true) {\n    Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"thread1: %d\", count);\n    count++;\n    // Wait to allow the main thread to execute\n    wait(25, msec);\n  }\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Once a thread is created it begins executing\n  thread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n  \n  int count = 0;\n  while (true) {\n    Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"main: %d\", count);\n    count++;\n    // Wait to allow myThread to execute\n    wait(25, msec);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"function_thread"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Brain Screen Clear Line\nClears the current row on the V5 Brain screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine();\n```\n\nClears a specified row on the V5 Brain screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine(1);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.clearLine();` command can accept integer values between **1 - 20**, to set which row to clear. You can also call the command without any arguments to clear the current row.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of lines available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* `mono12` - 20 Rows\n* `mono15` - 16 Rows\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 12 Rows (Default)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 8 Rows\n* `mono40` / `prop40` - 6 Rows\n* `mono60` / `prop60` - 4 Rows\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.clearLine();"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Brain Screen Clear Screen\n\nClears the entire V5 Brain screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearScreen();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Brain.Screen.clearScreen();` will not change the screen's cursor. You will need to use `Brain.Screen.setCursor();` command to set the screen's cursor to a specific position.","signature":"Brain.Screen.clearScreen();"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Circle\nDraws a circle on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawCircle(1, 1, 10);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.drawCircle();` command requires 3 values:\n\n* Value 1: Center Point X\n* Value 2: Center Point Y\n* Value 3: Radius of Circle (in pixels)\n\nThe outside line color of the circle is determined by the `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the circle is determine by the `Brain.Screen.setFillColor();` command. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawCircle(1, 1, 10);"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_line","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Line\nDraws a line on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawLine(1, 1, 10, 10);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.drawLine();` command requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Beginning X coordinate\n* Value 2: Beginning Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Ending X coordinate\n* Value 4: Ending Y coordinate\n\nThe line color is determined by the `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command. The default line color is white.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawLine(1, 1, 10, 10);"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Pixel\nDraws a pixel on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawPixel(1, 1);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.drawPixel();` command requires 2 values:\n\n* Value 1: X Coodinate\n* Value 2: Y Coodinate\n\nThe pixel color is determined by the `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command. The default pixel color is white.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawPixel(1, 1);"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Brain Screen Draw Rectangle\nDraws a rectangle on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawRectangle(1, 1, 10, 10);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.drawRectangle();` command requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Top Left Corner X coordinate\n* Value 2: Top Left Corner Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Width of the rectangle\n* Value 4: Height of the rectangle\n\nThe outside line color of the rectangle is determined by the `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the rectangle is determine by the `Brain.Screen.setFillColor();` command. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawRectangle(1, 1, 10, 10);"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Brain Screen New Line\n\nSets the print output cursor on the V5 Brain's screen to the next available row.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1. The `Brain.Screen.newLine();` command will move the cursor down by a single row on the screen. `Brain.Screen.newLine();` will also set the cursor's column to position 1.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* `mono12` - 20 Rows\n* `mono15` - 16 Rows\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 12 Rows (Default)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 8 Rows\n* `mono40` / `prop40` - 6 Rows\n* `mono60` / `prop60` - 4 Rows\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_new_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.newLine();"},"looks_brain_screen_print":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print","markdown":"# Brain Screen Print\n\nPrints values or text on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hello World\");\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.print();` command will print data at a cursor location on the screen.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1.\n\n## Printing Values\n\nYou can use format specifiers to show values inside of your print statements:\n\n* `%d` - Signed decimal integer\n* `%f` - Decimal floating point number\n* `%o` - Signed octal\n* `%s` - String of characters\n* `%x` - Unsigned hexadecimal integer\n* `%c` - Character\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Time Elapsed %f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```\n\nWhen displaying values, you can specify how many decimals places to print. For example, if your value is `3.14159265`, but you only want to display `3.14`, your format specifier would be `%.2f`.\n\nThe number before the decimal in the format specifier denotes the total number of characters to be printed. If the value being printed is shorter than the total number of characters to be printed, the printed value is padded with blank spaces.\n\nThe format specifier can also contain flags, width, precision and modifiers sub-specifiers:\n\n* `%d`\t- Prints a decimal integer\n* `%6d`\t- Prints a decimal integer, with a minimum of 6 characters wide\n* `%f`\t- Prints a floating point number\n* `%6f`\t- Prints a floating point number, with a minimum of 6 characters wide\n* `%.2f`  - Prints a floating point number, with 2 decimal characters places\n* `%6.2f` - Prints a floating point number, with a minimum of 6 characters wide and 2 decimal places\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Time Elapsed %8.2f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");"},"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Cursor\n\nSets the cursor location for `Brain.Screen.print();` command on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(1, 2);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setCursor();` command requires 2 values:\n\n* Value 1: Screen row position \n* Value 2: Screen column position\n\nSet the cursor's row and column position to have a `Brain.Screen.print();` command display at a specific location on the screen.\n\nAccepts a range for **row** of **1 to 20**.\n\nAccepts a range for **column** of **1 to 80**.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* `mono12` - 20 Rows\n* `mono15` - 16 Rows\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 12 Rows (Default)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 8 Rows\n* `mono40` / `prop40` - 6 Rows\n* `mono60` / `prop60` - 4 Rows\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* `mono12` - 80 Columns\n* `mono15` - 68 Columns\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 48 Columns (Default)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 32 Columns\n* `mono40` / `prop40` - 24 Columns\n* `mono60` / `prop60` - 16 Columns\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Fill Color\n\nSets the color that fills in shapes drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setFillColor(red);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setFillColor();` command is used to set the color of the inside of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\nYou can select from the following colors\n\n* black\n* white\n* red\n* green\n* blue\n* yellow\n* orange\n* purple\n* cyan\n* transparent\n\nThe fill color will be used for any next objects drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.","signature":"Brain.Screen.setFillColor(red);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_font":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_font","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Font\n\nSets the style and size of font used on the V5 Brain's screen when printing numbers or text.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setFont(monoM);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThere are two different types of fonts available on the V5 Brain's screen:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - each character takes up the same width.\n* Proportional (Prop) - each character takes up different size widths based on the character.\n\nChoose which font type and size to use. You can select from the following font options.\n\n* `mono12`\n* `mono15`\n* `mono20`\n* `mono30`\n* `mono40`\n* `mono60`\n* `prop20`\n* `prop30`\n* `prop40`\n* `prop60`\n\nThe new font size will be used for any future text written to the V5 Brain's screen.","signature":"Brain.Screen.setFont(monoM);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Pen Color\n\nSets the color of lines drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setPenColor(color);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command is used to set the color of lines, pixels, and text drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\n`Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` will also be used to set the color the outline of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\nYou can select from the following colors:\n\n* `black`\n* `white`\n* `red`\n* `green`\n* `blue`\n* `yellow`\n* `orange`\n* `purple`\n* `cyan`\n* `transparent`\n\nThe pen color will be used for any next objects drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.","signature":"Brain.Screen.setPenColor(color);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Pen Width\n\nSets the width of the outline for shapes drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setPenWidth(5);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setPenWidth();` command is used to set the width of the line on the outside of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setPenWidth();` command can accept integer values, with a larger value equating to a larger width.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.setPenWidth(10);"},"looks_console_clear_console":{"name":"looks_console_clear_console","markdown":"# Console Clear\n\nClears the Print Console and resets the cursor.\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"\\033[2J\\n\");\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nUsing the `printf` command with the special `\\033[2J` escape sequence and code will clear the Print Console.\n\nThe newline character, `\\n` is needed in a `printf` command to output the contents of the Print Console buffer into the Print Console. In this instance, the Print Console will be immediately updated/cleared when this command is executed.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will print `VEXcode` to the Print Console, wait 2 seconds, and then clear the Console.\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"VEXcode\\n\");\nwait(2, seconds);\nprintf(\"\\033[2J\\n\");\n```","signature":"printf(\"\\033[2J\\n\");"},"looks_console_print":{"name":"looks_console_print","markdown":"# Console Print\n\nPrints values or text to the Print Console\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"VEXcode\");\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `printf` command will print data at the cursor location on the Print Console.\n\nAll new projects begin with the cursor at row 1.\n\nThe newline character, `\\n` is needed in a `printf` command to output the contents of the Print Console buffer into the Print Console.\n\n## Printing Values\n\nYou can use format specifiers to show values inside of your print statements:\n\n* `%d` - Signed decimal integer\n* `%f` - Decimal floating point number\n* `%o` - Signed octal\n* `%s` - String of characters\n* `%x` - Unsigned hexadecimal integer\n* `%c` - Character\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"Time Elapsed %f\\n\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```\n\nWhen displaying values, you can specify how many decimals places to print. For example, if your value is `3.14159265`, but you only want to display `3.14`, your format specifier would be `%.2f`.\n\nThe number before the decimal in the format specifier denotes the total number of characters to be printed. If the value being printed is shorter than the total number of characters to be printed, the printed value is padded with blank spaces.\n\nThe format specifier can also contain flags, width, precision and modifiers sub-specifiers:\n\n* `%d`\t- Prints a decimal integer\n* `%6d`\t- Prints a decimal integer, with a minimum of 6 characters wide\n* `%f`\t- Prints a floating point number\n* `%6f`\t- Prints a floating point number, with a minimum of 6 characters wide\n* `%.2f`  - Prints a floating point number, with 2 decimal characters places\n* `%6.2f` - Prints a floating point number, with a minimum of 6 characters wide and 2 decimal places\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"Screen Pressed? %s\\n\", Brain.Screen.pressing());\n```\n\n## Printing Colors\n\nYou can use any of the color codes below with a `printf` command to set the color of the text being printed. The example below will show two ways in which a color sequence command can be used when printing. All color codes will need to be attached to an escape sequence - `\\033`.\n\n* `[31m` - Red\n* `[32m` - Green\n* `[34m` - Blue\n* `[30m` - Black\n* `[37m` - White\n* `[33m` - Yellow\n* `[91m` - Orange\n* `[35m` - Purple\n* `[36m` - Cyan\n* `[97m` - Transparent\n\n```cpp\n// Using color codes in-line\n// This will print \"VEXcode\" in Red to the Print Console\nprintf(\"\\033[31m VEXcode\\n\");\n\n// Using color codes in separate commands\nprintf(\"\\033[31m\");\nprintf(\"VEXcode\\n\");\n```","signature":"printf(\"VEXcode\");"},"looks_controller_rumble":{"name":"looks_controller_rumble","markdown":"# Controller Rumble\n\nCreates a vibrating effect on your V5 Controller.\n\n```cpp\nController.rumble(\".-.-\");\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Controller.rumble();` command uses the rumble motor in your V5 controller to provide feedback.\n\nYou can create any pattern you want using a combination of \".\" and \"-\" characters in the string. The \".\" character will create a short pulse. The \"-\" character will create a long pulse.\n\nYou can also use predefined rumble options:\n\n* `rumbleLong` is the same as `\"----\"`\n* `rumbleShort` is the same as `\"....\"` \n* `rumblePulse` is the same as `\"-.-.\"`\n\n```cpp\n// The following two lines of code will do the same thing\nController.rumble(\"....\");\nController.rumble(rumbleShort);\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.rumble(rumbleShort);"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Controller Screen Clear Line\n\nClears the current row on the V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.clearLine();\n```\n\nClears a specified row on the V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.clearLine(1);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Controller.Screen.clearLine();` command can accept integer values between **1 - 3**, to set which row to clear. You can also call the command without any arguments to clear the current row.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_controller_screen_clear_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.clearLine();"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Controller Screen Clear Screen\n\nClears the entire V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.clearScreen();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Controller.Screen.clearScreen();` will not change the screen's cursor. \n\nUse the `Controller.Screen.setCursor();` command to reset the screen's cursor to a specific position.","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.clearScreen();"},"looks_controller_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Controller Screen New Line\n\nSets the print output cursor on the V5 Controller's screen to the next available row.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1. The `Controller.Screen.newLine();` command will move the cursor down by a single row on the screen. `Controller.Screen.newLine();` will also set the cursor's column to position 1.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_controller_screen_new_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.newLine();"},"looks_controller_screen_print":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_print","markdown":"# Controller Screen Print\n\nPrints values or text on the V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.print(\"Hello World\");\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Controller.Screen.print();` command will print data at a cursor location on the screen.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1.\n\n## Printing Values\n\nYou can use format specifiers to show values inside of your print statements:\n\n* `%d` - Signed decimal integer\n* `%f` - Decimal floating point number\n* `%o` - Signed octal\n* `%s` - String of characters\n* `%x` - Unsigned hexadecimal integer\n* `%c` - Character\n\n```cpp\nController1.Screen.print(\"Timer: %f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```\n\nWhen displaying values, you can specify how many decimals places to print. For example, if your value is `3.14159265` but you only want to display `3.14`, your format specifier would be `%.2f`.\n\nThe number before the decimal is how many digits before the decimal you wish to print, while the number after the decimal is how many digits after the decimal you wish to print.\n\nThe format specifier can also contain flags, width, precision and modifiers sub-specifiers:\n\n* `%d`\t- Prints a decimal integer\n* `%6d`\t- Prints a decimal integer, with a minimum of 6 characters wide\n* `%f`\t- Prints a floating point number\n* `%6f`\t- Prints a floating point number, with a minimum of 6 characters wide\n* `%.2f`  - Prints a floating point number, with 2 decimal characters places\n* `%6.2f` - Prints a floating point number, with a minimum of 6 characters wide and 2 decimal places\n\n```cpp\nController1.Screen.print(\"Timer: %8.2f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.print(\"Hello\");"},"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Controller Screen Set Cursor\n\nSets the cursor location for **Controller.Screen.print();** command on the V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.setCursor(1, 2);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Controller.Screen.setCursor();` command requires 2 values:\n\n* Value 1: Screen row position \n* Value 2: Screen column position\n\nSet the cursor's row and column position to have a `Controller.Screen.print();` command display at a specific location on the screen.\n\n`Controller.Screen.setCursor();` accepts a range for **row** of **1 to 3**.\n\n`Controller.Screen.setCursor();` accepts a range for **column** of **1 to 20**.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* Standard Font - 20 Columns (Default)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/looks_controller_screen_set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);"},"looks_led_off":{"name":"looks_led_off","markdown":"# LED Off\n\nTurns a 3-Wire LED off.\n\n```cpp\nLedA.off();\n```","signature":"LED.off();"},"looks_led_on":{"name":"looks_led_on","markdown":"# LED On\n\nTurns a 3-wire LED on.\n\n```cpp\nLedA.on();\n```","signature":"LED.on();"},"looks_led_set":{"name":"looks_led_set","markdown":"# Set LED\n\nSets the state of an LED to either *true* (on) or *false* (off).\n\n```cpp\nLEDA.set(true);\nLEDA.set(false);\n```","signature":"LED.set();"},"magnet_drop":{"name":"magnet_drop","markdown":"# Magnet Drop\n\nEnergize a V5 Electromagnet to drop an attached magnetic object.\n\n```cpp\nMagnet.drop();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Magnet.drop()` command will release the object that the V5 Electromagnet is currently attached to.\n\n```cpp\nMagnet.pickup();\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);\nMagnet.drop();\n```","signature":"MAGNET.drop();"},"magnet_pickup":{"name":"magnet_pickup","markdown":"# Magnet Pickup\n\nEnergize a V5 Electromagnet to pick up a magnetic object.\n\n```cpp\nMagnet.pickup();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Magnet.pickup()` command will energize the V5 Electromagnet to pick up a magnetic object underneath the magnet.\n\n```cpp\nMagnet.pickup();\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);\nMagnet.drop();\n```","signature":"MAGNET.pickup();"},"magnet_set_power":{"name":"magnet_set_power","markdown":"# Magnet Set Power\n\nSets the power of a V5 Electromagnet that will be used when picking up a magnetic object.\n\n```cpp\nMagnet.setPower(power);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Magnet.setPower()` command accepts a range of values from **0 to 100**  as a parameter.\n\n```cpp\nMagnet.setPower(100);\nMagnet.pickup();\n```","signature":"MAGNET.setPower(100);"},"motion_motor393_set_reversed":{"name":"motion_motor393_set_reversed","markdown":"# Motor393.setReversed();\n\nReverses the spin direction of a Motor 393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.setReversed();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command reverses the spin direction of a Motor 393.\n\n`Motor393.setReversed();` accepts a Boolean argument of `true` or `false`.\n\nSetting the `Motor393.setReversed(true);` will set the spin directions `forward` and `reverse` to the opposing spin directions. Any following `Motor393.spin();` commands will spin in the direction set by the `Motor393.setReversed();` command.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.setReversed(true);\nMotor393.spin(forward);\n```","signature":"MOTOR393.setReversed(true);"},"motion_motor393_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor393_set_velocity","markdown":"# Motor393 Set Velocity\n\nSets the speed of a Motor393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.setVelocity(velocity, percent);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe velocity parameter accepts a range of **-100% to 100%.** \n\nSetting a Motor393's velocity to a negative value will cause the Motor393 to spin in reverse.\n\nThe sequence below will cause the Motor393 to spin in reverse, even though the `forward` parameter is passed.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.setVelocity(-100, percent);\nMotor393.spin(forward);\n```\n\nSetting a Motor393's velocity to 0 will prevent the Motor from spinning.","signature":"MOTOR393.setVelocity(50, percent);"},"motion_motor393_spin":{"name":"motion_motor393_spin","markdown":"# Motor393 Spin\n\nSpins a Motor393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.spin(forward);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command spins a Motor393 forever, until a new motor command is used or the program is stopped.\n\nChoose which direction the motor will spin to by setting the direction parameter to either `forward` or `reverse`.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.spin(forward);\n```","signature":"MOTOR393.spin(forward);"},"motion_motor393_stop":{"name":"motion_motor393_stop","markdown":"# Motor393 Stop\n\nStops a Motor393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.stop();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command stops a Motor393 from spinning.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the Motor393 for three seconds and then stop.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.spin(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nMotor393.stop();\n```","signature":"MOTOR393.stop();"},"motion_motor_set_max_torque":{"name":"motion_motor_set_max_torque","markdown":"# Motor Set Max Torque\n\nSets the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group's maximum torque output.  \n\n```cpp\nMotor.setMaxTorque(value, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.setMaxTorque();` accepts a torque range of **0 to 100** using `percent` units.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the ClawMotor to the 40 degree position with only 20% maximum torque. This allows the claw to grab an object without damaging it with too much force.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setMaxTorque(20, percent);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(40, degrees);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.setMaxTorque(50, percent);"},"motion_motor_set_position":{"name":"motion_motor_set_position","markdown":"# Motor Set Position\n\nSets the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group's encoder(s) to a specified position.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setPosition(position, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Motor.setPosition();` command can be used to set the Motor or Motor Group's position to any given value.\n\nThe `Motor.setPosition();` command is typically used to set the position to 0 to reset the Motor or Motor Group's encoder(s) position.\n\nSet the position of the Motor or Motor Group by providing the `position` to any number. \n\nYou can specify the units of the value in either `degrees` or `turns`. \n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.setPosition(50, degrees);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.setPosition(0, degrees);"},"motion_motor_set_stopping":{"name":"motion_motor_set_stopping","markdown":"# Motor Set Stopping\n\nSets the V5 Smart Motor or or Motor Group's brake mode. \n\n```cpp\nMotor.setStopping(brakeType);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nHere are possible `brakeType` inputs that you can specify: \n\n* `brake` will cause the Motor or Motor Group to come to an immediate stop, and will not correct for outside forces.\n* `coast` lets the Motor or Motor Group to spin gradually to a stop.\n* `hold` will cause the Motor or Motor Group to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved by an outside force, by using the built-in encoder.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will make the ArmMotor move forward for 90 degrees and then will resist outside forces (like gravity) to hold its position.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.setStopping(hold);\nArmMotor.spinFor(90, degrees);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.setStopping(brake);"},"motion_motor_set_timeout":{"name":"motion_motor_set_timeout","markdown":"# Motor Set Timeout\n\nSets the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group's timeout to stop if a blocking command never reaches its target.  \n\n```cpp\nMotor.setTimeout(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Motor.setTimeout();` is used to prevent movement commands that do not reach their position from preventing other commands in the stack from running. An example of a Motor not reaching its position is an arm or claw that reaches its mechanical limit and cannot complete its movement.\n\nSet the timeout by specifying the amount of time in `seconds`.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will end the `Motor.spinToPosition();` command after 2 second if the ClawMotor has not reached the position of 270 degrees. \n\nOnce the time limit or target is reached, the ClawMotor will move to position 0 degrees.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setTimeout(2, seconds);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(270, degrees);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.setTimeout(1, seconds);"},"motion_motor_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity","markdown":"# Motor Set Velocity\n\nSets the V5 Smart Motor or or Motor Group's velocity.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.setVelocity();` will set the speed of the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group but will not cause the Motor or Motor Group to move. \n\n`Motor.setVelocity();` accepts a range from **-100 to 100** when using the `percent` units.\n\n`Motor.setVelocity();` accepts a range from **-600 to 600** when using the `rpm` units.\n\n`Motor.setVelocity();` can use a \"rotations per minute\" (rpm) value based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the Motor or Motor Group.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a Motor or Motor Group's velocity to a negative value will cause the Motor/Motor Group to spin in the opposite direction.\n\nSetting a Motor or Motor Group's velocity to 0 will cause the Motor/Motor Group to stop.","signature":"MOTOR.setVelocity(50, percent);"},"motion_motor_spin":{"name":"motion_motor_spin","markdown":"# Motor Spin\nSpins a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group in a direction until stopped.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(directionType);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Motor.spin();` can run a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group forever until a new motor command is used or the program is stopped.\n\nUse the `forward` parameter to drive the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group in the forward direction.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(forward);\n```\n\nUse the `reverse` parameter to drive the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group in the reverse direction.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(reverse);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.spin(forward);"},"motion_motor_spin_at_voltage":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_at_voltage","markdown":"# Motor Spin At Voltage\nSpins a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group at a specified voltage.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(directionType, voltage, volt);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Spin at voltage** accepts a range from -12V to 12V.\n\nUse the `forward` parameter to drive the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group in the forward direction.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(forward, 10.0, volt);\n```\n\nUse the `reverse` parameter to drive the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group in the reverse direction.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(reverse, 10.0, volt);\n```\n\nSpinning a Motor or Motor Group at a negative voltage will cause the Motor/Motor Group to spin in the opposite direction than the one specified.","signature":"Motor.spin(forward, 10.0, volt);"},"motion_motor_spin_for":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_for","markdown":"# Motor Spin For\n\nSpins the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group in a given direction for a specific amount of rotation.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinFor(directionType, rotation, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.spinFor();` will tell a Motor or Motor Group to travel in a given direction (`forward` or  `reverse`), for a given distance, from where it is currently located.\n\nThe `Motor.spinFor();` accepts numeric values for `rotation`.\n\nSet the distance to travel by providing the `rotation` to any number. \n\nYou can specify the units of the rotation in either `degrees` or `turns`. \n\nThe **spinFor** command will block other commands until the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group movement has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to tell the **spinFor** command to not block the program until the movement has completed.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinFor(forward, 360, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.spinFor(forward, 90, degrees);"},"motion_motor_spin_to_position":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_to_position","markdown":"# Motor Spin To Position\n\nSpins the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group to a specific rotational position.\n\n```cpp\nMotor3.spinToPosition(rotation, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.spinToPosition();` will tell a Motor or Motor Group to travel to a specific position. Based on the current position of the Motor or Motor Group, `Motor.spinToPosition();` will determine the direction to rotate.\n\nThe `Motor.spinToPosition();` accepts numeric values for `rotation`.\n\nSet the position to travel to by providing the `rotation` to any number. \n\nYou can specify the units of the rotation in either `degrees` or `turns`. \n\nThe **spinToPosition** command will block other commands until the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group movement has completed.\n\n## Optional Parameters\n\nYou can set `false` as the last parameter to tell the **spinToPosition** command to not block the program until the movement has completed.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinToPosition(360, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.spinToPosition(90, degrees);"},"motion_motor_stop":{"name":"motion_motor_stop","markdown":"# Motor Stop\n\nStops the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.stop();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Motor.stop();` command will cause the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group to come to a complete stop and use the `Motor.setStopping();` to set either `coast`, `brake`, or `hold` its position.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will spin the ClawMotor open for 3 seconds before stopping.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.spin(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nClawMotor.stop();\n```","signature":"MOTOR.stop();"},"motion_servo_set_position":{"name":"motion_servo_set_position","markdown":"# Servo Set Position\n\nSpins a V5 Servo Motor to a set position.\n\n```cpp\nServo.setPosition(position, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nSpins a servo motor to the given positional value.\n\nThe `Servo.setPosition()` command accepts a range of values from **-50** to **50** for the **position** parameter.\n\n\n## Example\n\nThis example spins the servo motor to 25 degrees, waits 2 seconds, then spins the motor to -25 degrees.\n\n```cpp\nServo.setPosition(25, degrees);\nwait(2, seconds);\nServo.setPosition(-25, degrees);\n```","signature":"SERVO.setPosition(90, degrees);"},"playVexcodeSound":{"name":"playVexcodeSound","markdown":"# Play VEXcode sound\n\nPlays a custom imported sound through your devices speaker.\n\n```cpp\nplayVexcodeSound(\"\");\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nFor the `playVexcodeSound(\"\");` command to run properly, the V5 Brain **MUST** stay connected to the device via a USB cable while the project is running. \n\n* If coding in app-based VEXcode V5, no additional connection steps are needed in addition to the USB connection.\n* If coding in web-based VEXcode V5, the V5 Brain needs to stay connected while using the user/console web-serial port. For more information, [view this article >](https://kb.vex.com/hc/en-us/articles/15614471185812-Connecting-to-the-User-Console-Port-in-Web-Based-VEXcode-V5)\n\n![web_serial](static/help/v5/cpp/en/playVexcodeSound/web_serial.png)\n\nChoose which sound to use. Use the default sound **game over** or add a new sound file URL in the Manage VEXcode Sounds menu. The sound name entered in the quotes must match the name inside the Manage VEXcode Sounds menu.\n\n```cpp\nplayVexcodeSound(\"game over\");\n```\nUploaded sounds can only be used if they are added in the Manage VEXcode Sounds menu. For more information about adding or editing sounds, [view this article >](https://kb.vex.com/hc/en-us/articles/15613914815508-Playing-Custom-Imported-Sounds-in-a-VEXcode-V5-Project)\n\n![manage_sounds](static/help/v5/cpp/en/playVexcodeSound/manage_sounds.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will play the arrow sound as soon as the project is started and then immediately move to the next command in the stack. \nThe `playVexcodeSound(\"\");` command is non-blocking and will not wait until the sound has finished playing before moving to the next command in the project. \n\nThe drivetrain will then drive forward for the full 200mm before playing the default **game over** sound.\n\n```cpp\nint main() {\n  playVexcodeSound(\"arrow\");\n  Drivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);\n  playVexcodeSound(\"game over\");\n}\n```","signature":"playVexcodeSound()"},"sensing_accel_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_accel_acceleration","markdown":"# Accelerometer Acceleration\n\nReports the acceleration value from one axis (x, y, or z) on the Analog Accelerometer.\n\nThe X-axis reports the acceleration value from the horizontal axis and the Y-axis reports the acceleration value from the vertical axis. The Z-axis reports upward acceleration.\n\n```cpp\nAccel2G.acceleration()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Accelerometer.acceleration()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) that ranges from **-2.0 G to 2.0 G** or **-6.0 G to 6.0 G** depending upon the jumper setting on the Analog Accelerometer.\n\n1.0 G is equivalent to 9.8 meters per second squared.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Accel2GB.acceleration());\n```","signature":"ACCEL.acceleration()"},"sensing_arm_get_joint_value":{"name":"sensing_arm_get_joint_value","markdown":"# Joint potentiometer value\n\nReports the potentiometer value of one of the four joints on the V5 Workcell.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.getJointValue(1);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `RoboticArm.getJointValue(1);` command is used to report the potentiometer value of one of the four joints on the Workcell. This command can be used when determining mastering values.\n\nThe `RoboticArm.getJointValue(1);` command reports a range of **0 to 4095**.\n\nChoose which joint to report. There are four joints on the Workcell: \n\n* **Joint 1:** RoboticArm.getJointValue(1);\n* **Joint 2:** RoboticArm.getJointValue(2);\n* **Joint 3:** RoboticArm.getJointValue(3);\n* **Joint 4:** RoboticArm.getJointValue(4);","signature":"RoboticArm.getJointValue(1);"},"sensing_arm_get_position":{"name":"sensing_arm_get_position","markdown":"# Axis position\n\nReports the current x, y, or z-coordinate position of the arm on the Workcell.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.getAxisPosition(xaxis);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe`RoboticArm.getAxisPosition(xaxis);` command is used to report the current x, y, or z-coordinate position of the arm on the Workcell.\n\nChoose which axis to report. The arm of the Workcell operates in the x, y, and z-axes:\n\n* **x-axis:** RoboticArm.getAxisPosition(xaxis);\n* **y-axis:** RoboticArm.getAxisPosition(yaxis);\n* **z-axis:** RoboticArm.getAxisPosition(zaxis);","signature":"RoboticArm.getAxisPosition(xaxis);"},"sensing_arm_set_position":{"name":"sensing_arm_set_position","markdown":"# Set relative position\n\nSets the origin to the current location of the end of arm tooling.\n\n```cpp\nRoboticArm.setRelativePosition(0, 0, 0);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, the origin on the Workcell is located in the center of the turntable.\n![turntable](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_arm_set_position/turntable.png)\n\nThe `RoboticArm.setRelativePosition(0, 0, 0);` command sets the origin to the current location of the end of arm tooling.\n\nThe end of arm tooling can be set to:\n\n* None\n* Marker (shown in image)\n* Electromagnet \n\n![marker](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_arm_set_position/marker.png)","signature":"RoboticArm.setRelativePosition(0, 0, 0);"},"sensing_brain_battery_capacity":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_capacity","markdown":"# Brain Battery Capacity\n\nReports the capacity of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Battery.capacity()\n```\n\n## How To Use\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Brain.Battery.capacity()` returns an **integer** that represents the Battery's capacity in the default unit of `percent`, and will return a value in the range of **0% to 100%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%d\", Brain.Battery.capacity());\n```","signature":"Brain.Battery.capacity()"},"sensing_brain_battery_current":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_current","markdown":"# Brain Battery Current\n\nReports the current of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Battery.current()\n```\n\n## How To Use\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Brain.Battery.current()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the current of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\nThe default unit is amps (`amp`) that returns a value from **0.0 to 20.0 amps**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Brain.Battery.current());\n```","signature":"Brain.Battery.current()"},"sensing_brain_battery_voltage":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_voltage","markdown":"# Brain Battery Voltage\n\nReports the voltage of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Battery.voltage()\n```\n\n## How To Use\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Brain.Battery.voltage()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) that reports the voltage of the V5 Brain's battery. \n\nThe default unit is `volt`, and the command will return a value in the range of **10 volts to 14.4 volts**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Brain.Battery.voltage());\n```","signature":"Brain.Battery.voltage()"},"sensing_brain_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_column","markdown":"# Brain Screen Column\nReports the column number of the V5 Brain screen cursor location.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.column()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Brain.Screen.column()` reports an integer which ranges from **1 to 80**.\n\n```cpp\nif (Brain.Screen.column() > 10.0) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Cursor is past column 10\");\n}\n```\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of columns available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* `mono12` - 80 Columns\n* `mono15` - 68 Columns\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 48 Columns (Default)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 32 Columns\n* `mono40` / `prop40` - 24 Columns\n* `mono60` / `prop60` - 16 Columns\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_brain_screen_column/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.column()"},"sensing_brain_screen_pressing":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_pressing","markdown":"# Brain.Screen.pressing()\n\nReports if the V5 Brain's touchscreen is currently being pressed.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.pressing()` command can be used together with the `Brain.Screen.xPosition()` and `Brain.Screen.yPosition()` to detect when and where a touch has occured on the V5 Brain's touchscreen.\n\n`Brain.Screen.pressing()` reports **true** when the V5 Brain's touchscreen is being pressed.\n\n`Brain.Screen.pressing()` reports **false** when the V5 Brain's touchscreen is not being pressed.\n\n```cpp\nif (Brain.Screen.pressing()) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Screen is being pressed!\");\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.pressing()"},"sensing_brain_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_row","markdown":"# Brain Screen Row\nReports the row number of the V5 Brain screen cursor location.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Brain.Screen.row()` reports an integer which ranges from **1 to 20**.\n\n```cpp\nif (Brain.Screen.row() > 10.0) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Cursor position is past row 10\");\n}\n```\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* `mono12` - 20 Rows\n* `mono15` - 16 Rows\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 12 Rows (Default)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 8 Rows\n* `mono40` / `prop40` - 6 Rows\n* `mono60` / `prop60` - 4 Rows\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_brain_screen_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.row()"},"sensing_brain_screen_xPosition":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_xPosition","markdown":"# Brain Screen xPosition\nReports the X coordinate of the location of the last detected touch on the V5 Brain's touchscreen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.xPosition()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Brain.Screen.xPosition()` is used to capture the X coordinate of the last press on the V5 Brain's touchscreen. \n\nIt can be used with `Brain.Screen.yPosition()` to get the (x,y) coordinate, and create interactivity between the V5 and the end user.\n\n`Brain.Screen.xPosition()` return an **integer** in a range of **0 to 480 pixels**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_brain_screen_xPosition/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n```cpp\nint myXCoordinate = Brain.Screen.xPosition();\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.xPosition()"},"sensing_brain_screen_yPosition":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_yPosition","markdown":"# Brain Screen yPosition\nReports the Y coordinate of the location of the last detected touch on the V5 Brain's touchscreen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.yPosition()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Brain.Screen.yPosition()` is used to capture the Y coordinate of the last press on the V5 Brain's touchscreen. \n\nIt can be used with `Brain.Screen.xPosition()` to get the (x,y) coordinate, and create interactivity between the V5 and the end user.\n\n`Brain.Screen.yPosition()` return an **integer** in a range of **0 to 240 pixels**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_brain_screen_yPosition/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n```cpp\nint myYCoordinate = Brain.Screen.yPosition();\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.yPosition()"},"sensing_brain_timer_clear":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_clear","markdown":"# Brain Timer Clear\n\nResets the V5 Brain's timer.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.clear();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Brain's timer begins at the beginning of each project. `Brain.Timer.clear()` is used to reset the timer back to 0 seconds.","signature":"Brain.Timer.clear();"},"sensing_brain_timer_time":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_time","markdown":"# Brain Timer Time\n\nReports the value of the V5 Brain's timer in the provided units.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.time(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not require a semicolon.\n\nThe timer starts at 0 seconds when the program starts, and returns the timer's value as a decimal value (as a *double*).\n\nThe `units` parameter accepts either **seconds** or **msec** (milliseconds) as a valid argument.\n\n```cpp\nif(Brain.Timer.time(seconds) > 3.0){\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Timer has passed 3 seconds!\");\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Timer.time(units)"},"sensing_bumper_pressing":{"name":"sensing_bumper_pressing","markdown":"# Bumper Pressing\n\nReports if the Bumper Switch is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Bumper.pressing()` returns **true** if the Bumper Switch is being pressed.\n\n`Bumper.pressing()` returns **false** if the Bumper Switch is not pressed.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(BumperA.pressing());\nBrain.Screen.print(\"BumperA pressed!\");\n```","signature":"BUMPER.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_axis_position":{"name":"sensing_controller_axis_position","markdown":"# Controller Axis Position\n\nReports the position of a joystick on the V5 Controller along an axis.\n\n```cpp\nController.Axis.position()\n```\n\n## How To Use\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Controller.Axis.position()` reports a range between **-100 to 100**.\n\n`Controller.Axis.position()` will report zero (0) when a joystick axis is centered.\n\nChoose which Controller axis to report.\n\n* `Axis1` - right Joystick (left and right)\n* `Axis2` - right Joystick (up and down)\n* `Axis3` - left Joystick (up and down)\n* `Axis4` - left Joystick (left and right)\n\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_controller_axis_position/controller_button_front.png)\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.setVelocity(Controller1.Axis3.position(), percent);\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.AXIS.position()"},"sensing_controller_button_pressing":{"name":"sensing_controller_button_pressing","markdown":"# Controller Button Pressing\n\nReports if a button on the V5 Controller is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Controller.Button.pressing()` reports **true** if the specified Controller button is being pressed.\n\n`Controller.Button.pressing()` reports **false** if the specified Controller button is not pressed.\n\nThe following Controller buttons are valid options to check if it is being pressed:\n* ButtonUp\n* ButtonDown\n* ButtonLeft\n* ButtonRight\n* ButtonX\n* ButtonB\n* ButtonY\n* ButtonA\n* ButtonL1\n* ButtonL2\n* ButtonR1\n* ButtonR2\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Controller1.ButtonUp.pressing());\n```","signature":"Controller.buttonUp.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_column","markdown":"# Controller.Screen.column()\n\nReports the column number of the V5 Controller screen cursor location.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.column()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Controller.Screen.column()` reports an integer which ranges from **1 to 19**.\n\n```cpp\nif (Controller1.Screen.column() > 10) {\n}\n```\n\n---\n\nUnlike V5 Brain, the V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. So there will always be 19 columns of spaces to print each row.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* Standard Font - 19 Columns (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_controller_screen_column/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.column()"},"sensing_controller_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_row","markdown":"# Controller.Screen.row()\n\nReports the row number of the V5 Controller screen cursor location.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Controller.Screen.row()` reports an integer which ranges from **1 to 3**.\n\n```cpp\nif (Controller1.Screen.row() > 2) {\n}\n```\n\n---\n\nUnlike V5 Brain, the V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. So there will always be 3 rows of spaces to print each row.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_controller_screen_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n\n\n\n<advanced>\n</advanced>","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.row()"},"sensing_digital_in_signal":{"name":"sensing_digital_in_signal","markdown":"# Digital in\n\nReports value of the digital in signal.\n\n```cpp\nDigitalIn.value()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 3-Wire ports function at a 5V logic signal voltage level.\n\nThe `DigitalIn.value()` command reports **1** when the digital input signal is high.\n\nThe `DigitalIn.value()` command reports **0** when the digital input signal is low.","signature":"DigitalIn.value();"},"sensing_digital_out_set":{"name":"sensing_digital_out_set","markdown":"# Digital out\n\nSets the logic level of a digital out 3-Wire port.\n\n```cpp\nDigitalOut.set(true);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 3-Wire ports function at a 5V logic signal voltage level.\n\nThe `DigitalOut.set(true);` command sets the digital signal to output a high or low logic signal.\n\nChoose to output a high or low digital logic signal.\n\n* Set the output to high: `DigitalOut.set(true);`\n* Set the output to low: `DigitalOut.set(false);`","signature":"DigitalOut.set(true);"},"sensing_distance_is_object_detected":{"name":"sensing_distance_is_object_detected","markdown":"# Distance Object Detected\n\nReports if a V5 Distance Sensor detects an object or surface in its range.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.isObjectDetected()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance.isObjectDetected()` returns **true** if an object or surface is detected in its range, and **false** if not.\n\nThe snippet below will print **TRUE** or **FALSE** depending on whether an object or surface is detected.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%s\", Distance.isObjectDetected() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.isObjectDetected()"},"sensing_distance_object_distance":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Distance Object Distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object or surface from a V5 Distance Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.objectDistance(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance.objectDistance()` accepts **mm** or **inches** as units and reports a range from **20 mm to 2000 mm** (~0.8 inches to 79.0 inches ) as a decimal value.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Distance.objectDistance(inches));\n```\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Distance.objectDistance(mm));\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.objectDistance(inches)"},"sensing_distance_object_size":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_size","markdown":"# Distance Object Size\n\nReports an estimation of the detected object's size.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.objectSize()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance.objectSize()` can be used to determine if a detected object is of a certain size.\n\nThere are three defined sizes that can be used for comparison:\n* sizeType::large\n* sizeType::medium\n* sizeType::small\n\n```cpp\nif (Distance.objectSize() == sizeType::large) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Large object detected!\");\n}\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.objectSize()"},"sensing_distance_object_velocity":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Distance Object Velocity\n\nReports the velocity of a detected object in m/s.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.objectVelocity()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance.objectVelocity()` reports the current velocity of an object in m/s (meters per second).\n\nThe velocity of a detected object will change when the object is moving while in the range of the V5 Distance Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Distance.objectVelocity());\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.objectVelocity()"},"sensing_drivetrain_current":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_current","markdown":"# Drivetrain Current\n\nReports the amount of current that the Drivetrain is currently using.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.current(amp)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`Drivetrain.current(amp)` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the amount of current a V5 Drivetrain is currently using.\n\nThe default unit is amps (`amp`) that returns a value from **0.0 to 2.5 amps**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.current(amp));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.current()"},"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency","markdown":"# Drivetrain Efficiency\n\nReports the efficiency of the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.efficiency()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`Drivetrain.efficiency()` reports the value of the power (in watts) the motors powering the Drivetrain are using (input), versus the amount of power (in watts) the motors powering the Drivetrain are providing (output). \n\nA V5 Drivetrain typically reaches a maximum efficiency of 65% under normal use cases.\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Drivetrain.efficiency()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) in the default unit of `percent`, and it will return a value from  **0.0% to 100.0%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.efficiency());\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.efficiency(percent)"},"sensing_drivetrain_heading":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_heading","markdown":"# Drivetrain Heading\n\nReports the 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.heading()\n```\n\n## How To Use\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe `Drivetrain.heading()` command reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n`Drivetrain.heading()` reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99**.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Drivetrain.heading() > 180);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.heading()"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_done":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_done","markdown":"# Drivetrain Is Done\n\nReports if the Drivetrain has completed its movement.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.isDone()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Drivetrain.isDone()` reports **true** when the Drivetrain's motors have completed their movement.\n\n`Drivetrain.isDone()` reports **false** when the Drivetrain's motors are still moving.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Drivetrain.isDone());\n```\n\nThis command returns **true** if the drivetrain is moving because of a `drive()` or `turn()` command.","signature":"Drivetrain.isDone()"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving","markdown":"# Drivetrain Is Moving\n\nReports if the Drivetrain is currently moving.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.isMoving()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command returns **true** if the drivetrain is moving because of a `driveFor()` or `turnFor()` command that *does* specify a set distance.\n\nThis command returns **false** if the drivetrain movement has completed.\n\n**Note:** This command will always return **false** if the drivetrain is moving because of a `drive()` or `turn()` command that does *not* specify a set distance.\n\n```cpp\nif (Drivetrain.isMoving()) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Moving!\");\n} else {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Not Moving!\");\n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.isMoving()"},"sensing_drivetrain_power":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_power","markdown":"# Drivetrain Power\n\nReports the amount of power output the Drivetrain is currently generating.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.power()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`Drivetrain.power()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the amount of power output the Drivetrain is currently generating.\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe default value is `watt` that returns values ranging from **0.0 to 22.0 watts**. \n\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.power());\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.power()"},"sensing_drivetrain_rotation":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_rotation","markdown":"# Drivetrain Rotation\n\nReports the Drivetrain's angle of rotation when configured with a 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.rotation()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drivetrain.rotation()`reports a **positive** value when the Drivetrain turns in a **clockwise** direction.\n\n`Drivetrain.rotation()` reports a **negative** value when the Drivetrain turns in a **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Drivetrain.rotation() > 180);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.rotation()"},"sensing_drivetrain_temperature":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_temperature","markdown":"# Drivetrain Temperature\n\nReports the temperature of the V5 Smart Motors powering the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.temperature(percent)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drivetrain.temperature(percent)` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the temperature of the V5 Smart Motors powering the Drivetrain.  \n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nSet `percent` as the unit to get values ranging from **0.0% to 100.0%**. \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.temperature(percent));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.temperature(percent)"},"sensing_drivetrain_torque":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_torque","markdown":"# Drivetrain Torque\n\nReports the amount of torque (rotational force) the Drivetrain is currently using.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.torque(Nm)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n`Drivetrain.torque(Nm)` returns a decimal as a (*double*) to report the amount of torque (rotational force) the Drivetrain is currently using. \n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe default return value is Newton-meters(`Nm`) which ranges from **0.0 to 2.1 Newton-meters (Nm)**.\n\nAlternatively, values can only be returned in Inch-pounds(`InLb`).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.torque(Nm));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.torque(InLb));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.torque(Nm)"},"sensing_drivetrain_velocity":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_velocity","markdown":"# Drivetrain Velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## How to Use\n`Drivetrain.velocity` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the current velocity of the Drivetrain. \n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nAcceptable `units` are **percent** and **rpm**.\n\nIf the provided `units` parameter is **percent**, the reported values ranges between **-100% to 100%**.\n\nAlternatively, if the provided `units` is **rpm**, the range of reported values vary based on the Gear Catridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Catridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Catridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Catridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.velocity(percent));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.velocity(units)"},"sensing_encoder_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_position","markdown":"# Encoder Position\n\nReports the distance the Shaft Encoder has rotated.\n\n```cpp\nEncoder.position(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Encoder.position()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the distance the Shaft Encoder has rotated.\n\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n\nValues can be returned in `degrees`.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", EncoderC.position(degrees));\n```\n\nValues can be returned in `turns`.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", EncoderC.position(turns));\n```","signature":"ENCODER.position(degrees)"},"sensing_encoder_set_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_set_position","markdown":"# Encoder Set Position\n\nSets the Shaft Encoder's position to the given value.\n\n```cpp\nEncoder.setPosition(position, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Encoder.setPosition()` can be used to set the Shaft Encoder's position to any given positional value.\n\nUsually, `Encoder.setPosition()` is used to set the position 0 to reset the Shaft Encoder's position.\n\nThe **units** parameter can be set to **degrees** or **turns**.\n\n```cpp\nEncoderA.setPosition(0, degrees);\nEncoderB.setPosition(0, turns);\n```","signature":"ENCODER.setPosition(position, units);"},"sensing_encoder_velocity":{"name":"sensing_encoder_velocity","markdown":"# Encoder Velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of a Shaft Encoder.\n\n```cpp\nEncoder.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Encoder.velocity()` reports a decimal value (as a *double*) in either degrees per second (`dps`) or rotations per minute (`rpm`).\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nValues can be returned in degrees per second (`dps`).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", EncoderC.velocity(dps));\n```\n\nValues can be returned in rotations per minute (`rpm`).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", EncoderC.velocity(rpm));\n```","signature":"ENCODER.velocity(dps)"},"sensing_gps_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_gps_acceleration","markdown":"# GPS Acceleration\n\nReports the acceleration value of the specified axis on a GPS Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.acceleration(axis)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `GPS.acceleration()` command reports a decimal value (as a *double*) in the range of **-4.0** to **4.0** Gs.\n\nIt can report acceleration values from three different axes based on the value passed as the `axis` parameter:\n\n* The **xaxis** reports the acceleration value of a GPS Sensor's forward and backward rotations\n\n* The **yaxis** reports the acceleration value of a GPS Sensor's left and right rotations\n\n* The **zaxis** reports the acceleration value of a GPS Sensor's up and down movements\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Acceleration on X: %f\", GPS.acceleration(xaxis));\n```","signature":"GPS.acceleration(xaxis)"},"sensing_gps_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gps_calibrate","markdown":"# GPS Calibrate\n\nStarts the calibration process for a GPS Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.calibrate();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe GPS Sensor must remain still during the calibration process.\n\n```cpp\nint main() {\n  // Calibrate the GPS sensor before starting any program code\n  GPS.calibrate();\n}\n```","signature":"GPS.calibrate();"},"sensing_gps_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_gps_gyro_rate","markdown":"# GPS Gyro Rate\n\nReports the rate of rotation from the specified axis on a GPS Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.gyroRate(axis, units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`GPS.gyroRate()` reports the rate of rotation on an axis as a *double*, with the range of values reported between **-1000** to **1000** if **dps** is used as the `units` parameter, or between **-167** to **167** if **rpm** is used.\n\nThe `axis` parameter accepts the following values for specifying which axis to get rate of rotation from:\n\n* **xaxis**: reports the rate of rotation when a GPS Sensor rotates in the X-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n* **yaxis**: reports the rate of rotation when a GPS Sensor rotates in the Y-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n* **zaxis**: reports the rate of rotation when a GPS Sensor rotates in the Z-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\n// Print all gyro rate values in a loop\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"GPS Gyro Rate - X Axis: %f\", GPS.gyroRate(xaxis, dps));\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"GPS Gyro Rate - Y Axis: %f\", GPS.gyroRate(yaxis, dps));\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"GPS Gyro Rate - Z Axis: %f\", GPS.gyroRate(zaxis, dps));\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  wait(0.1, seconds);\n}\n```","signature":"GPS.gyroRate(xaxis, dps)"},"sensing_gps_heading":{"name":"sensing_gps_heading","markdown":"# GPS Heading\n\nReports the heading that a robot is currently facing based on a GPS Sensor's readings from the VEX GPS Field Code.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.heading()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`GPS.heading()` reports a range of heading values from **0.00 to 359.99** degrees, increasing in value when a GPS Sensor is rotated clockwise.\n\nUsually, a GPS Sensor should be mounted facing behind a robot. In the GPS configuration, the Angle Offset is set to **180** degrees.\n\nThen, for example, if the GPS Sensor is facing the South wall as defined by the VEX GPS Field Code, the reported heading will be **0.00** degrees, which is the heading that the front of the robot is facing.\n\nHowever, a GPS Sensor can also be mounted facing other directions (e.g. the front of a robot).\n\nIn this situation, for example, the GPS Sensor's Angle Offset configuration would then need to be set to **0** degrees, which is the angular difference between the forward heading of the robot, and the heading that the GPS is facing. This way, the reported heading value will shift correctly in line with a robot's headings as it turns.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below uses the `GPS.heading()` command to stop the Drivetrain's turn when the reported GPS Sensor heading is more than or equal to 180 degrees.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(right);\n\nwhile (GPS.heading() < 180) {\n  wait(50, msec);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"GPS.heading()"},"sensing_gps_orientation":{"name":"sensing_gps_orientation","markdown":"# GPS Orientation\n\nReports the angle of the specified orientation axis on a GPS Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.orientation(axis, degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`GPS.orientation()` reports a *double* representing the angle of rotation about the specified orientation `axis`:\n\n* The **roll** axis reports a value between **-180** to **+180** degrees, representing the angle of a GPS Sensor when tilted left or right\n\n* The **pitch** axis reports a value between **-90** to **+90** degrees, representing the angle of a GPS Sensor when tilted forward or backwards\n\n* The **yaw** axis reports a value between **-180** to **+180** degrees, representing the angle of a GPS Sensor when rotated about the vertical axis\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\n// Print the yaw orientation in a loop\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"GPS Yaw Orientation: %f\", GPS.orientation(yaw, degrees));\n  wait(0.1, seconds);\n}\n```","signature":"GPS.orientation(roll, degrees)"},"sensing_gps_quality":{"name":"sensing_gps_quality","markdown":"# GPS Signal Quality\n\nReports a GPS Sensor's current signal quality.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.quality()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `GPS.quality()` command reports an *integer* representing the current signal quality of a GPS Sensor.\n\nWhen the reported value is **100**, it means that all reported positional and heading data from a GPS Sensor is valid.\n\nHowever, a reported value of **90** signals that any positional data is no longer being calculated by capturing information from the VEX Field Code, but rather through alternative means.\n\nAt **80**, only GPS Sensor heading values are valid, but as more time goes by where a GPS Sensor is not scanning enough of the VEX Field Code to accurately determine positiona and heading information, the reported signal quality will continue to drop until **0**, where any GPS Sensor data is effectively frozen and no longer valid.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"GPS Signal Quality: %d\", GPS.quality());\n```","signature":"GPS.quality()"},"sensing_gps_set_location":{"name":"sensing_gps_set_location","markdown":"# GPS Set Location\n\nSets the location for a GPS Sensor to a defined positional value.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.setLocation(x, y, units, heading, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nWhen a GPS Sensor is too close to the field walls to read accurate data (for example, when a robot is in a game's starting position on a field), unexpected behaviors can often occur if the program relies on the GPS's positional and heading data to work correctly.\n\nThe `GPS.setLocation()` command can be used to set the location and heading of a GPS Sensor if this information is known before the program is ran, which may help reduce GPS data inaccuracies due to a GPS Sensor's proximity to the field walls when a program is started.\n\nThe **x** and **y** parameters are the X and Y offsets of the GPS Sensor, or a defined origin point on a robot relative to the center of a field. The **units** parameter can either be **mm** or **inches**.\n\nThe **heading** parameter is the heading of the robot in its defined position. For example, if the GPS Sensor is mounted facing behind a robot and the robot is facing the West wall (heading of 270), the **heading** value that should be passed is 270.\n\n```cpp\n// Setting the approximate location of a GPS Sensor\n// when a robot is facing West and\n// starting at the bottom right corner of a field\nGPS.setLocation(56, -45, inches, 270, degrees);\n```","signature":"GPS.setLocation();"},"sensing_gps_set_origin":{"name":"sensing_gps_set_origin","markdown":"# GPS Set Origin\n\nSets an origin point on a robot at which GPS Sensor positional data should be based upon.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.setOrigin(x, y, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `GPS.setOrigin()` command can be used to allow GPS positional data to correspond to another point of a robot rather than the location of a GPS Sensor.\n\nIt is commonly used when a GPS Sensor is not located on the reference point of a robot (i.e. the point about which a robot rotates). This way, when the origin is set to the reference point, reported positional data would not change when a robot is rotating in-place.\n\nThe `x` parameter takes the X axis (i.e. the axis running through the sides of a GPS Sensor) while the `y` parameter takes the Y axis offset distance to a reference point.\n\nEither **mm** or **inches** are accepted for the `units` parameter, depending on whether the `x` and `y` offset values are being passed as millimeters or inches, respectively.\n\n```cpp\n// Assuming a GPS Sensor is mounted 25mm forward from the reference point of a robot,\n// we can set the origin on the GPS Sensor to have a Y offset of 25\nGPS.setOrigin(0, 25, mm);\n```","signature":"GPS.setOrigin(0, 0, mm);"},"sensing_gps_xposition":{"name":"sensing_gps_xposition","markdown":"# GPS X Position\n\nReports the X positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.xPosition(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `GPS.xPosition()` command reports the current X positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point relative to the center of a field.\n\nIf a `GPS.setOrigin()` command is used to set an origin point to a different part of a robot, the reported value will be the positional offset of the defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\nAlternatively, the origin point can also be set in the GPS Sensor's configuration. This can be done by measuring the X and Y distances from the intended origin point to the GPS Sensor and filling in the X and Y offset settings, respectively.\n\nValues can be reported in mm or inches as a *double*, depending on whether **mm** or **inches** is passed in the `units` parameter.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"GPS X Position (mm): %f\", GPS.xPosition(mm));\n```","signature":"GPS.xPosition(mm)"},"sensing_gps_yposition":{"name":"sensing_gps_yposition","markdown":"# GPS Y Position\n\nReports the Y positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\n```cpp\nGPS.yPosition(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `GPS.yPosition()` command reports the current Y positional offset of a GPS Sensor or defined origin point relative to the center of a field.\n\nIf a `GPS.setOrigin()` command is used to set an origin point to a different part of a robot, the reported value will be the positional offset of the defined origin point from the center of a field.\n\nAlternatively, the origin point can also be set in the GPS Sensor's configuration. This can be done by measuring the X and Y distances from the intended origin point to the GPS Sensor and filling in the X and Y offset settings, respectively.\n\nValues can be reported in mm or inches as a *double*, depending on whether **mm** or **inches** is passed in the `units` parameter.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"GPS Y Position (mm): %f\", GPS.yPosition(mm));\n```","signature":"GPS.yPosition(mm)"},"sensing_gyro_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_calibrate","markdown":"# Gyro Calibrate\n\nCalibrating the Gyro Sensor is used to reduce the amount of drift generated by Gyro Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.calibrate();\n```\n\nDrifting occurs when the Gyro Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Gyro Sensor must remain still during the calibration process. The calibration process will take approximately 1 second to complete.","signature":"GYRO.calibrate();"},"sensing_gyro_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Gyro Heading\n\nReports the 3-Wire Gyro Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.heading(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe `Gyro.heading(degrees)` command reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n`Gyro.heading(degrees)` reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99**.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Gyro.heading(degrees) > 180);\n```","signature":"GYRO.heading(degrees)"},"sensing_gyro_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Gyro Rotation\n\nReports the 3-Wire Gyro Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.rotation(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe `Gyro.rotation(degrees)` command reports a **positive** value when the Gyro turns in a **clockwise** direction.\n\n`Gyro.rotation(degrees)` reports a **negative** value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Gyro.rotation(degrees) > 180);\n```","signature":"GYRO.rotation(degrees)"},"sensing_gyro_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_heading","markdown":"# Gyro Set Heading\n\nSets the Gyroscopic (Gyro) sensor's current position to the value provided. \n\n```cpp\nGyro.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Gyro.setHeading();` can be used to set the gyro's position to any clockwise heading. This command is typically used to reset the orientation of the gyro when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`Gyro.setHeading();` can accept decimals or integers.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"GYRO.setHeading(90, degrees);"},"sensing_gyro_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_rotation","markdown":"# Gyro Set Rotation\n\nSets the 3-Wire V5 Gyro Sensor's angle of rotation to the value provided.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setRotation(0, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Gyro.setRotation();` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\n`Gyro.setRotation();` accepts any positive or negative decimal or integer number as a parameter.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setRotation(270, degrees);\nGyro.setRotation(-270, degrees);\n```","signature":"GYRO.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"sensing_inertial_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Inertial Acceleration\n\nReports the acceleration value from one of the axes (x, y, or z) on the Inertial Sensor.  \n\n* The **X-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **forward to backward**\n* The **Y-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **side to side**\n* The **Z-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **up to down**\n\n```cpp\nInertial.acceleration(axis)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Inertial.acceleration()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) that ranges from **-4.0 to 4.0 Gs**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial1.acceleration(xaxis));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial1.acceleration(yaxis));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial1.acceleration(zaxis));\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.acceleration(xaxis);"},"sensing_inertial_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_calibrate","markdown":"# Inertial Calibrate\n\nCalibrating the Inertial Sensor is used to reduce the amount of drift generated by the Inertial Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nInertial.calibrate();\n```\n\nDrifting occurs when the Inertial Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not physically moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Inertial Sensor must remain still during the calibration process. The calibration process will take approximately 2 seconds to complete.","signature":"INERTIAL.calibrate();"},"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Inertial Gyro Rate\n\nGets the rate of rotation for the specified axis (x, y, or z) on the Inertial Sensor.\n\n* The **X-axis** reports rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the X-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* The **Y-axis** reports rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Y-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n* The **Z-axis** reports rotations when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Z-Axis (based on the orientation of the sensor)\n\n```cpp\nInertial.gyroRate(axis, dps)\n```\n\n## How To Use \n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon\n\n`Inertial.gyroRate()` is used to return a range from **-1000.0 to 1000.0** in dps (degrees per second). \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial.gyroRate(xaxis, dps));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial.gyroRate(yaxis, dps));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial.gyroRate(zaxis, dps));\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.gyroRate(xaxis, dps)"},"sensing_inertial_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_heading","markdown":"# Inertial Heading\n\nReports the V5 Inertial Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nInertial.heading(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon\n\nThe `Inertial.heading(degrees)` command reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n`Inertial.heading(degrees)` reports a range from **0.00 to 359.99 degrees**\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Inertial.heading(degrees) > 180);\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.heading(degrees)"},"sensing_inertial_orientation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Inertial Orientation\n\nGets an orientation angle of the inertial sensor. Reports the unit value specified by the parameter of the inertial sensor.\n\nThe orientation reported is determined by the selected axis (x, y, or z).\n\n* The **X-axis** represents **pitch**, which reports a value between -90 to +90 degrees.\n* The **Y-axis** represents **roll**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n* The **Z-axis** represents **yaw**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n\n--\n\nPitch is the rotation around the side to side axis.\n\n![V5_Pitch_rev2](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_inertial_orientation/V5_Pitch_rev2.jpg)\n\nRoll is the rotation around the front to back axis.\n\n![V5_Roll_rev2](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_inertial_orientation/V5_Roll_rev2.jpg)\n\nYaw is rotation around the vertical axis.\n\n![V5_Yaw_rev2](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_inertial_orientation/V5_Yaw_rev2.jpg)\n\n--\n\n```cpp\nInertial.orientation(axis, units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Inertial.orientation(pitch, degrees) > 60);\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.orientation(pitch, degrees);"},"sensing_inertial_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_rotation","markdown":"# Inertial Rotation\n\nReports the V5 Inertial Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nInertial.rotation(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe `Inertial.rotation(degrees)` reports a **positive** value when the Inertial Sensor turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\n`Inertial.rotation(degrees)` reports a **negative** value when the Inertial Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Inertial20.rotation(degrees) > 180);\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.rotation(degrees)"},"sensing_inertial_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_heading","markdown":"# Inertial Set Heading\n\nSets the Inertial sensor's current heading position to a set value.\n\n```cpp\nInertial.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Inertial.setHeading()` can be used to set the Gyro's position to any clockwise heading. This command is typically used to reset the orientation of the Inertial Sensor when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`Inertial.setHeading()` accepts a range of **0.0 to 359.99** degrees.\n\n`Inertial.setHeading()` can accept decimals, integers, or other commands that return a numeric value.\n\n\n```cpp\nmyInertial.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.setHeading(0, degrees);"},"sensing_inertial_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_rotation","markdown":"# Inertial Set Rotation\n\nSets the V5 Inertial Sensor's angle of rotation to the value provided.\n\n```cpp\nInertial.setRotation(0, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Inertial.setRotation()` command can be used to set the Inertial Sensor's angle of rotation to any given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\n`Inertial.setRotation()` accepts any positive or negative decimal or integer number.\n\n```cpp\nInertial20.setRotation(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"sensing_light_brightness":{"name":"sensing_light_brightness","markdown":"# Light Brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the Light Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nLight.brightness()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Light.brightness()` reports a range from **0% to 100%**.\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe default unit is `percent` that returns an integer value from **0% to 100%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%d\", LightC.brightness());\n```","signature":"LIGHT.brightness()"},"sensing_limit_pressing":{"name":"sensing_limit_pressing","markdown":"# LimitSwitch Pressing\n\nReports if the Limit Switch is pressed.\n\n```cpp\nLimitSwitch.pressing()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`LimitSwitch.pressing()` reports **true** if the Limit Switch is being pressed.\n\n`LimitSwitch.pressing()` reports **false** if the Limit Switch is not being pressed.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(LimitSwitchB.pressing());\n```","signature":"LimitSwitch.pressing()"},"sensing_line_reflectivity":{"name":"sensing_line_reflectivity","markdown":"# LineTracker Reflectivity\n\nReports the amount of light reflected using the Line Tracker sensor.\n\n```cpp\nLineTracker.reflectivity()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nLight colored surfaces will reflect more light and will report a high reflectivity value.\n\nDark colored surfaces will reflect less light and will report a low reflectivity value.\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe default unit is `percent` that returns an integer value from **0% to 100%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%d\", LineTrackerA.reflectivity());\n```","signature":"LINETRACKER.reflectivity()"},"sensing_motor_current":{"name":"sensing_motor_current","markdown":"# Motor Current\n\nReports the amount of current a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently using in amperes (amps).\n\n```cpp\nMotor.current(amp)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.current()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the amount of current a V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently using.\n\nThe default unit is amps (`amp`) that returns a value from **0.0 to 2.5 amps**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ClawMotor.current(amp));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.current()"},"sensing_motor_direction":{"name":"sensing_motor_direction","markdown":"# Motor.direction()\n\nReports the direction a V5 Smart Motor is currently spinning.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.direction()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Motor.current()` returns a **directionType** value, so it will return either `forward` or `reverse`.\n\n\n```cpp\nif (LeftMotor.direction() == forward) {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"Left Motor is spinning forward!\");\n}\n```\n**Note:** The semicolon in the example above is used by the `print` command.","signature":"MOTOR.direction()"},"sensing_motor_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_motor_efficiency","markdown":"# Motor Efficiency\n\nReports the efficiency of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.efficiency(percent)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.efficiency()` reports the value of the power (in watts) the motor is using (input), versus the amount of power (in watts) the motor is providing (output). \n\nA V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group typically reaches a maximum efficiency of 65% under normal use cases.\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Motor.efficiency()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) in the default unit of `percent`, and it will return a value from  **0.0% to 100.0%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.efficiency(percent));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.efficiency(percent)"},"sensing_motor_is_done":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor Is Done\n\nReports if the V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.isDone()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Motor.isDone()` reports **true** when the specified Motor or Motor Group has completed its movement.\n\n`Motor.isDone()` reports **false** when the specified Motor or Motor Group has not completed its movement.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(ClawMotor.isDone());\n```","signature":"MOTOR.isDone()"},"sensing_motor_is_spinning":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor Is Spinning\n\nReports if the selected V5 Smart Motor or Motor Group is currently spinning.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.isSpinning()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThis command returns **true** if the Motor or Motor Group is moving because of a `spinFor()` command that *does* specify a set distance.\n\nThis command returns **false** if the Motor or Motor Group movement has completed.\n\n**Note:** This command will always return **false** if the Motor or Motor Group is moving because of a `spin()` command that does *not* specify a set distance.\n\n```cpp\n// The example below flashes an LED while the V5 Arm is being raised or lowered\n\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 720, degrees, false);\n\nwhile (ArmMotor.isSpinning()) {\n    LEDA.on();\n    wait(0.5, seconds);\n    LEDA.off();\n    wait(0.5, seconds);\n}\n```","signature":"MOTOR.isSpinning()"},"sensing_motor_position":{"name":"sensing_motor_position","markdown":"# Motor Position\n\nReports the distance a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group has traveled.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.position(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.position()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the distance the Shaft Encoder in a Motor has rotated.\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nValues can be returned in `degrees`.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.position(degrees));\n```\n\nValues can be returned in `turns`.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.position(turns));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.position()"},"sensing_motor_power":{"name":"sensing_motor_power","markdown":"# Motor Power\n\nReports the amount of power output a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group is currently generating.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.power(watt)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.power()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the amount of power output being generated.\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe default unit is `watt` that returns values ranging from **0.0 to 22.0 watts**. \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ClawMotor.power(watt));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.power()"},"sensing_motor_temperature":{"name":"sensing_motor_temperature","markdown":"# Motor Temperature\n\nReports the temperature of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.temperature(percent)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.temperature()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the temperature of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor in a Motor Group.  \n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nSet `percent` as the unit to get values ranging from **0.0% to 100.0%**. \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ClawMotor.temperature(percent));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.temperature(percent)"},"sensing_motor_torque":{"name":"sensing_motor_torque","markdown":"# Motor Torque\n\nReports the amount of torque (rotational force) a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group is currently using.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.torque(Nm)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.torque()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the amount of torque (rotational force) a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group is currently using.\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nValues can be returned in Newton-meters(`Nm`) which ranges from **0.0 to 2.1 Newton-meters (Nm)**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.torque(Nm));\n```\n\nValues can be returned in inch-pounds(`InLb`) which ranges from **0.0 to 18.6 inch-pounds (InLb)**. \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.torque(InLb));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.torque()"},"sensing_motor_velocity":{"name":"sensing_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Motor Velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.velocity(percent)\n```\n\n## How to Use\n\n`Motor.velocity()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the current velocity of a Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group. \n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nSpecify the unit when using this command. The two unit options are:\n\n`percent` - will return a value from **-100% to 100%**.\n \n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.velocity(percent));\n```\n  \n`Motor.velocity()` will return a `rpm` (rotations per minute) range based on the Gear Cartridge installed in a V5 Smart Motor or the first motor of a Motor Group.\n\n**Red Cartridge:** -100rpm to 100rpm  \n**Green Cartridge:** -200rpm to 200rpm  \n**Blue Cartridge:** -600rpm to 600rpm  \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.velocity(rpm));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.velocity()"},"sensing_optical_brightness":{"name":"sensing_optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical Brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.brightness()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.brightness()` reports a range of values from **0% to 100%**.\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Optical.brightness());\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.brightness()"},"sensing_optical_color":{"name":"sensing_optical_color","markdown":"# Optical Color\n\nReturns the color detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.color()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.color()` returns the closest color match base on the hue of a detected object.\n\nThe following colors can be used as a comparison to the color detected by a V5 Optical Sensor:\n* black\n* white\n* red\n* green\n* blue\n* yellow\n* orange\n* purple\n* cyan\n\n```cpp\nif (Optical.color() == red) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Red object detected!\");\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.color()"},"sensing_optical_gesture_detected":{"name":"sensing_optical_gesture_detected","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Detected\n\nReports detected gesture data from a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.getGesture()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Detected` command returns an object with gesture information. To check the type of the detected gesture, access the `type` property on the returned object.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.getGesture().type\n```\n\nBefore using any V5 Optical Sensor gesture commands, a V5 Optical Sensor must be correctly set to detect gestures with the `Optical.gestureEnable();` command.\n\nBelow are the gestures that a V5 Optical Sensor can detect:\n\n- `gestureType::up`\n- `gestureType::down`\n- `gestureType::left`\n- `gestureType::right`\n\n## Example\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set a V5 Optical Sensor to detect gestures before checking for gestures.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureEnable();\nwhile (Optical.getGesture().type != gestureType::up) {\n  wait(0.1, seconds);\n}\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Up!\");\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.getGesture()"},"sensing_optical_hue":{"name":"sensing_optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical Hue\n\nReports the hue of the object detected by a V5 Optical Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.hue()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.hue()` reports a range of values from **0 to 359**, which represents the location of the detected color on a color wheel.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Optical.hue());\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.hue()"},"sensing_optical_is_near_object":{"name":"sensing_optical_is_near_object","markdown":"# Optical Is Near Object\n\nReports if a V5 Optical Sensor detects an object in its range.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.isNearObject()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.isNearObject()` returns **true** if an object is detected, and returns **false** otherwise.\n\nIt should be used to check if an object is close to the Optical Sensor so that the color readings from the `Optical.color()` command is accurate.\n\n```cpp\nif (Optical.isNearObject() && Optical.color() == red) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Red object detected!\");\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.isNearObject()"},"sensing_optical_set_light":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light","markdown":"# Optical Set Light\n\nSets the state of the V5 Optical Sensor's LED.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLight(ledState);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.setLight()` can be used to set the state of the LED on the V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nIt accepts either **ledState::on** or **ledState::off** as a parameter.\n\n**ledState::on** will turn the LED on.\n\n**ledState::off** will turn the LED off.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLight(ledState::on);\nwait(2, seconds);\nOptical.setLight(ledState::off);\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.setLight(ledState::on);"},"sensing_optical_set_light_power":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Optical Set Light Power\n\nSets the intensity of a V5 Optical Sensor's LED.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLightPower(power, percent);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Optical.setLightPower()` can be used to set the intensity of the LED on the V5 Optical Sensor.\n\nIt accepts a range of values from **0 to 100** as the first parameter.\n\nThe second parameter is **percent**.\n\nA higher value will increase the intensity of the LED, while a lower value will decrease the intensity.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLightPower(100, percent);\nOptical.setLight(ledState::on);\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.setLightPower(100, percent);"},"sensing_optical_set_mode_disable":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_mode_disable","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Disable\n\nSets a V5 Optical Sensor to detect colors.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureDisable();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Disable` command allows you to set a V5 Optical Sensor to detect colors.\n\nBy default, a V5 Optical Sensor will be set to detect colors.\n\n## Examples\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set a V5 Optical Sensor to detect colors after checking for gestures.\n\n```cpp\n// Detect gestures\nOptical.gestureEnable();\nwhile (Optical.getGesture().type != gestureType::up) {\n  wait(0.1, seconds);\n}\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Up!\");\n\nwait(1, seconds);\n\n// Detect colors\nOptical.gestureDisable();\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  if (Optical.color() == red) {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"Red Object!\");\n  } else {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"Not Red Object!\");\n  }\n  wait(0.02, seconds);\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureDisable();"},"sensing_optical_set_mode_enable":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_mode_enable","markdown":"# Optical Gesture Enable\n\nSets a V5 Optical Sensor to detect gestures.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureEnable();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Optical Gesture Enable` command allows you to set a V5 Optical Sensor to detect gestures.\n\nBy default, a V5 Optical Sensor will be set to detect colors.\n\nBefore using any V5 Optical Sensor gesture commands, a V5 Optical Sensor must be correctly set to detect gestures.\n\n## Examples\n\nThe example shows how to correctly set a V5 Optical Sensor to detect gestures before checking for gestures.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.gestureEnable();\nwhile (Optical.getGesture().type != gestureType::up) {\n  wait(0.1, seconds);\n}\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Up!\");\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.gestureEnable();"},"sensing_pot_angle":{"name":"sensing_pot_angle","markdown":"# Potentiometer Angle\n\nReturns the angular position of the Potentiometer.\n\n```cpp\nPotentiometer.angle(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Potentiometer.angle()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the angular position of the Potentiometer.\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nSet **degrees** as the `units` parameter to get values ranging from **0.0 to 250.0 degrees** for a V5 Potentiometer, or from **0.0 to 330.0 degrees** for a V5 Potentiometer V2.\n\nIf the provided `units` parameter is in **percent**, the return values ranges from **0 to 100%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", PotentiometerA.angle(degrees));\n```","signature":"POTENTIOMETER.angle(units)"},"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled":{"name":"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled","markdown":"# Controller Enable/Disable\n\n`RemoteControlCodeEnabled = false;`\n\nEnables or disables Controller-configured actions from the Devices menu.\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose to either enable or disable the configured Controller actions by declaring it as either `true` or `false`. By default, the Controller is Enabled in every project.\n\n## Example\n\nThe configured action in this example is using the robot's Drivetrain behavior set by the Controller's configuration in the Devices window.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/v5/cpp/en/sensing_remote_control_code_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nThis example will have the configured Controller disabled when the program starts. \n\nThen, the robot will drive forward for 6 inches.\n\nFinally, the **controller enabled** command will enable the Controller to restore Controller driving behaviors.\n\n```cpp\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = false;\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 6.0, inches);\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = true;\n```","signature":"RemoteControlCodeEnabled = true;"},"sensing_rotation_angle":{"name":"sensing_rotation_angle","markdown":"# Rotation Angle\n\nReports a V5 Rotation Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.angle()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Rotation.angle()` command reports values in the range of **0.00** to **359.99**.\n\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Rotation.angle());\n```","signature":"ROTATION.angle()"},"sensing_rotation_position":{"name":"sensing_rotation_position","markdown":"# Rotation Position\n\nReports a V5 Rotation Sensor's current position.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.position(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Rotation.position()` can accept **degrees** or **turns** as units and reports positive and negative decimal values.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Rotation.position(degrees));\n```\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Rotation.position(turns));\n```","signature":"ROTATION.position(degrees)"},"sensing_rotation_reset_position":{"name":"sensing_rotation_reset_position","markdown":"# Rotation.resetPosition();\n\nResets a V5 Rotation Sensor's position to 0.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.resetPosition();\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Rotation.resetPosition()` can be used to reset the position of the Rotation Sensor to 0.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.resetPosition();\n```","signature":"ROTATION.resetPosition();"},"sensing_rotation_set_position":{"name":"sensing_rotation_set_position","markdown":"# Rotation Set Position\n\nSets a V5 Rotation Sensor's position to a specified value.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.setPosition(position, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Rotation.setPosition()` is commonly used to reset the position of the Rotation Sensor when the specified position value is 0.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.setPosition(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"ROTATION.setPosition(0, degrees);"},"sensing_rotation_velocity":{"name":"sensing_rotation_velocity","markdown":"# Rotation Velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of a V5 Rotation Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Rotation.velocity()` accepts **rpm** or **dps** as units and reports decimal values.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Rotation.velocity(rpm));\n```\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Rotation.velocity(dps));\n```","signature":"ROTATION.velocity(rpm)"},"sensing_sonar_distance":{"name":"sensing_sonar_distance","markdown":"# RangeFinder Distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor.\n\n```cpp\nRangeFinder.distance(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`RangeFinder.distance()` reports a range from **30mm to 3000mm** if the unit specified is `mm`, or **2 inches to 115 inches** if the unit specified is `inches`.\n\n```cpp\nif (RangeFinderC.distance(mm) < 400.0){\n    Drivetrain.stop();\n}\n```","signature":"RANGEFINDER.distance(mm)"},"sensing_sonar_found_object":{"name":"sensing_sonar_found_object","markdown":"# RangeFinder Found Object\nReports if the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor sees an object within its field of view. \n\n```cpp\nRangeFinder.foundObject()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`RangeFinder.foundObject()` reports **true** when the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n`RangeFinder.foundObject()` reports **false** when the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor does not detect an object or surface.","signature":"RANGEFINDER.foundObject()"},"sensing_vision_largest_object":{"name":"sensing_vision_largest_object","markdown":"# Vision Largest Object\n\nReports the largest object that the Vision Sensor sees.\n\n```cpp\nVision.largestObject\n```\n\n## How To Use\nA call to `Vision.takeSnapshot();` will need to be made before using the `Vision.largestObject` command.\n\nThe `Vision.largestObject` command will return an object of type `vision::object`.\n\n\n```cpp\n// Take a snapshot with the COLOR_SIG signature\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"X: %d\", Vision.largestObject.centerX);\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Y: %d\", Vision.largestObject.centerY);\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\nThe `Vision.largestObject` is of the type `vision::object` which has these properties which can be accessed.\n\n- `id` - A unique ID assigned to each object by the Vision Sensor, is an `int`\n- `originX` - The top left X position of the object, is an `int`\n- `originY` - The top left Y position of the object, is an `int`\n- `centerX` - The center X position of the object, is an `int`\n- `centerY` - The center Y position of the object, is an `int`\n- `width` - The width of the object, is an `int`\n- `height` - The height of the object, is an `int`\n- `angle` - The angle of the object, is a `double`\n- `exists` - If the vision sensor detects the object or not, is a `bool`","signature":"sensing_vision_largestObject;"},"sensing_vision_object_count":{"name":"sensing_vision_object_count","markdown":"# Vision Object Count\n\nReports how many objects the Vision Sensor detects. \n\nAn object will need to be configured before the `Vision.objectCount` command can detect it.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objectCount\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMake sure you specify the Vision Sensor when using this command. \n\nBefore the `Vision.objectCount` can report a number of objects, `Vision.takeSnapshot()` will need to be used.\n\n`Vision.objectCount` will only detect the number of objects from the last snapshot signature.","signature":"VISION.objectCount"},"sensing_vision_objects":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects","markdown":"# Vision Objects\n\nReports all of the objects that the Vision Sensor sees.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nA call to `Vision.takeSnapshot()` will need to be made before accessing the `Vision.objects` array.\n\nThe `Vision.objects` is an array that contains all of the objects that the Vision Sensor detects.\n\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\nvision::object firstObject = Vision.objects[0];\n```\nThis can be used like any other array. You can access the objects in it with the index of each element.\n\n```cpp\nvision::object visionObject = Vision.objects[0];\n```\n\nYou can also use it in control structures like **for loops**. The `Vision.objectCount` can be used as a loop condition.\n\nThe snippet below prints the `centerX` and `centerY` values of each detected object to the VEX V5 Brain.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\nfor(int i = 0; i < Vision.objectCount; i++) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"X: %d\", Vision.objects[i].centerX);\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Y: %d\", Vision.objects[i].centerY);\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n}\n```\n\nThe objects in the `Vision.objects` are of the type `vision::object` which has these accessible properties.\n\n- `id` - A unique ID assigned to each object by the Vision Sensor, is an `int`\n- `originX` - The top left X position of the object, is an `int`\n- `originY` - The top left Y position of the object, is an `int`\n- `centerX` - The center X position of the object, is an `int`\n- `centerY` - The center Y position of the object, is an `int`\n- `width` - The width of the object, is an `int`\n- `height` - The height of the object, is an `int`\n- `angle` - The angle of the object, is a `double`\n- `exists` - If the vision sensor detects the object or not, is a `bool`","signature":"sensing_vision_objects"},"sensing_vision_objects_angle":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_angle","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].angle\n\nReports the angle of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].angle\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision commands to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].angle` reports the angle of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 180 degrees**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.screen.print(MyVision.objects[0].angle);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].angle"},"sensing_vision_objects_centerx":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_centerx","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].centerX\n\nReports the X coordinate of the center of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].centerX\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision commands to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].centerX` reports the X coordinate of the center of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 315 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[1].centerX);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].centerX"},"sensing_vision_objects_centery":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_centery","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].centerY\n\nReports the Y coordinate of the center of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].centerY\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision commands to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].centerY` reports the Y coordinate of the center of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 211 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[2].centerY);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].centerY"},"sensing_vision_objects_exists":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_exists","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].exists\n\nReports if the Vision Sensor detects a configured object. \n\nAn object will need to be configured before the `Vision.objects[index].exists` command can detect it.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].exists\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMake sure you specify the Vision Sensor when using this command. \n\n\n`Vision.objects[index].exists` reports **true** when the Vision Sensor detects a configured object.\n\n`Vision.objects[index].exists` reports **false** when the Vision Sensor does not detect a configured object.\n\nBefore the `Vision.objects[index].exists` can report reports a **true** or **false** value, `Vision.takeSnapshot()` will need to be used.\n\n\n```cpp\nif(Vision.objects[0].exists){\n\n}\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].exists;"},"sensing_vision_objects_height":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_height","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].height\n\nReports the height of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].height\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision commands to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].height` reports how tall the object is in pixels. It returns a value of **2 - 212 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[3].height);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].height;"},"sensing_vision_objects_width":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_width","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].width\n\nReports the width of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].width\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision blocks to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].width` reports how wide the object is in pixels. It returns a value of **2 - 316 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[1].width);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].width;"},"sensing_vision_take_snapshot":{"name":"sensing_vision_take_snapshot","markdown":"# Vision Take Snapshot\n\nTakes a snapshot from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(SIG_1);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Vision.takeSnapshot()` will capture the current image from the Vision Sensor, filter out the requested signatures, and copies the detected objects's data for further analysis.\n\nTypically, `Vision.takeSnapshot()` is required first before using any other Vision Sensor commands.\n\nMake sure you specify the Vision Sensor and the vision signature when using this command. Vision signatures are configured from the Robot Configuration window.","signature":"VISION.takeSnapshot(SIGNATURE);"},"variables_2d_arrays":{"name":"variables_2d_arrays","markdown":"# 2D Array Variables\n\nDeclares the type, name, length of a 2D array. \n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 },\n};\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDeclare what type of data will be stored in your 2D array. \n\n- `int`\n- `double`\n- `bool`\n\nName the array something descriptive and unique. Set the array dimensions inside 2 pairs of square brackets `[]` just after the array name. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new 2D array with 3 rows and 3 columns\n\nint my2DArray[3][3];\n```\n\nThe values in the array can be assigned when creating the array using curly brackets.\n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 }\n};\n```\n\nThe values can also be declared individually by index. The index always starts at zero. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new turnAngles array with 3 rows and 3 columns\nint turnAngles[3][3];\n\n// Assign values by index\nturnAngles[0][0] = 45;\nturnAngles[0][1] = 90;\nturnAngles[0][2] = 180;\nturnAngles[1][0] = 270;\n```\n\nTo read values from an array, provide the index of the specific element in the square brackets.\n\n```cpp\n// The angle variable will be assigned the value of 270\n\nint angle = turnAngles[1][0];\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example shows a **double** 2D array called `myAngles` that will be a 2D array of angles.\n\n```cpp\ndouble myAngles[2][3] = {\n  {45.5, 90.0, 88.2},\n  {25.0, 75.5, 45.0}\n};\n```","signature":"variables_2d_array"},"variables_arrays":{"name":"variables_arrays","markdown":"# Array Variables\n\nDeclares the type, name, and length of an array. \n\n```cpp\nint myArray[3] = { 1, 2, 3 };\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nDeclare what type of data will be stored in your array. \n\n- `int`\n- `double`\n- `bool`\n\nName the array something descriptive and unique. Set the length of the array inside a pair of square brackets `[]` just after the array name. \n\n```cpp\nint turnAngles[3];\n```\n\nThe values in the array can be declared when creating the array using curly brackets.\n\n```cpp\nbool boolArray[2] = { false, true };\n```\n\nThe values can also be declared individually by index. The index always starts at zero. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new array of length 3\ndouble doubleArray[3];\n\n// Assign values to the array by index\ndoubleArray[0] = 1.5;\ndoubleArray[1] = 3.14;\ndoubleArray[2] = 2.18;\n```\n\nTo read values from an array, provide the index of a specific element in the square brackets.\n\n```cpp\n// Read the value at index 2 in integerArray\n\nint value = integerArray[2];\n```\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the array to initial values and then report item #3 (index number 2) from the list to spin a Motor. \n\n```cpp\nint degreesArray[3] = { 30, 60, 90 };\nMotor.spinFor(forward, degreesArray[2], degrees);\n```","signature":"variables_arrays"},"variables_boolean":{"name":"variables_boolean","markdown":"# Boolean Variable\n\nStores a **true** or **false** value.\n\n```cpp\nbool myBoolean = true;\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Boolean variables** store a **true** or **false** value. Declare with the keyword `bool` in front of a unique and descriptive variable name and set it to equal either `true` or `false`. \n\nBooleans can be used inside of control statement conditionals. \n\n```cpp\nbool goFast = true;\n\nif (goFast) {\n  Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity(100, percent);\n}\n```","signature":"variables_boolean"},"variables_double":{"name":"variables_double","markdown":"# Double Variable\n\nSets a variable to a `double` type.\n\n`double myDouble = 1.5;`\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `double` variable type is a number that has a decimal point.\n\n`double pi = 3.14;`\n\nCreate a unique and descriptive variable name. Then, assign a value to your variable.\n\n`double turnAngle = 40.5;`","signature":"variables_double"},"variables_integer":{"name":"variables_integer","markdown":"# Integer Variable\n\nSets an integer variable with a declared name and value.\n\n`int myNumber = 10;`\n\n## How To Use\n\nCreate a unique and descriptive variable name.\n\n`int driveTime = 60;`\n\nAssign a value to your variable. A variable can equal the returned value of a sensing command or the result of an equation, as long as it is declared using the correct **type**.\n\n```cpp\nint lowBatteryLifeWarning = Brain.Battery.capacity(percent);\n```\n\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will assign the distance (in inches) detected by the VEX V5 Distance Sensor to the \"myVariable\" variable and use the value of \"myVariable\" to set the speed of the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nint myVariable = Distance7.objectDistance(inches);\n\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(myVariable, percent);\n```","signature":"variables_intergers"},"variables_strings":{"name":"variables_strings","markdown":"# String Variable\n\nSets a variable to a **string** type.\n\n`char myString[] = \"my string\";`\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **string** variable type can be assigned any combination of numbers and letters, while it is enclosed in quotation marks `\" \"`.\n\nCreate a unique and descriptive variable name. Then, assign a value to your **string** variable.\n\n`char driveMessage[] = \"Time to Drive!\";`","signature":"variables_my_string"},"vexcodeinit":{"name":"vexcodeinit","markdown":"# vexcodeInit();\n\n`vexcodeInit();` is used to setup and initialization devices configured in the Robot Configuration tool. \n\n`The vexcodeInit();` should always run at the start of your \"int main\" function to ensure that your devices are configured before running any other commands.\n\nRemoving or commenting `vexcodeInit();` out can result in devices not working properly and/or unexpected behaviors when you run your project.","signature":"vexcodeInit();"}}},"es":{"blocks":{"acceleration_of":{"name":"acceleration_of","markdown":"# Aceleración de\n\nInforma el valor de aceleración de un eje en el acelerómetro analógico.\n\n![acceleration_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Aceleración de** reporta ranfo de **-2.0 G to 2.0 G** o **-6.0 G to 6.0 G** dependiendo en el estado del clip puente en el Acelerómetro Analógico.\n\nElija qué acelerómetro usar.\n\n![acceleration_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_device.png)\n\nEl bloque de reporte **Aceleración de** es usado dentro de bloques con espacio circular.\n\n![acceleration_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_inserted.png)"},"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Sumar\n\nSumar dos valores juntos e reportar la suma.\n\n![add](static/help/v5/blocks/es/add/add.png)\n\n## Como Se Usa\n\n**Sumar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque **sumar** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares, y también pueden aceptar otros bloques circulares en él.\n\nSuma dos numeros.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/es/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nAgregar con valores de variables.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/es/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nAgregar con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/es/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# Y\n\nReporta si dos condiciones booleanas son ambas verdaderas.\n\n![and](static/help/v5/blocks/es/and/and.png)\n\n## Como Se Usa\n\nEl bloque **y** reporta **verdadero** cuando ambas condiciones son **verdaderas**. \n\nEl bloque **y** reporta **falso** cuando una, o ambas, de las condiciones son **falsas**.\n\nEl bloque booleano **and** reporta un **verdadero** o **falso** valor y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![and_shape](static/help/v5/blocks/es/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo verificará si se presionan dos botones del controlador V5 al mismo tiempo.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/es/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nEl bloque **y** regresara **verdadero** cuando ambos  **controller1 X button** y el **controller1 A button** esten presionados.\n\nEl bloque **y** regresara a **falso** cuando uno (o ambos) de los botones del controlador no estan presionados.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/es/and/and_truth.png)"},"angle_of":{"name":"angle_of","markdown":"# Angulo de\n\nDevuelve la posición angular del potenciómetro.\n\n![angle_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/angle_of/angle_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Angulo de** reportar en rango de **0% a 100%** o **0.0 a 250.0 grados**.\n\nElija qué potenciómetro usara.\n\n![angle_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/angle_of/angle_of_device.png)\n\nElija informar el valor en % o grados.\n\n![angle_of_block_parameters](static/help/v5/blocks/es/angle_of/angle_of_parameters.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **angulo de** Se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![angle_of_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/angle_of/angle_of_inserted.png)\n"},"battery_current":{"name":"battery_current","markdown":"# Corriente de Bateria\n\nReporta la corriente de la batería del cerebro V5.\n\n![battery_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/battery_current/battery_current_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**corriente de Bateria** reporta un rango de **0.0 amperios a 20.0 amperios**.\n\nThe bloque que reporta **corriente de bateria** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![battery_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/battery_current/battery_current_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Nivel de Bateria\n\nInforma el nivel de carga de la batería del cerebro V5.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**nivel de bateria** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **nivel de bateria** es usado dentro de los bloques con interiores circulares.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)"},"battery_voltage":{"name":"battery_voltage","markdown":"# Voltage de bateria\n\nReporta el voltaje de la batería del cerebro V5.\n\n![battery_voltage_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**voltage de Bateria** reporta un rango de **10.0 voltios a 14.4 voltios**.\n\nThe bloque que reporta **voltage de Bateria** Se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![battery_voltage_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_inserted.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Variable Booleano\n\nReporta el valor de un variable Booleano.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nBloques de **variable Booleano** son usados para reportar valor **cierto** o **falso** archivado dentro de el variable. Usa el bloque **establecer variable booleano** para establecer actualizar el valor de un variable booleano.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nEl bloque **variable booleano** reporta un valor **cierto** o **falso** y si es usado en bloques de espacio hexagonal (seis lados).\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nVariables Booleanos son creados usando el boton **Crear un Booleano**.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Romper\n\nSale de un ciclo repetitivo inmediatamente.\n\n![break](static/help/v5/blocks/es/break/break.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nCuando se agrega a un bloque 'C' de repetir, el bloque **romper** saldrá del ciclo repetitivo en el que se encuentra actualmente.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo moverá el tren motriz hacia adelante y verificará si se presionó la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\nSi presiono l apantalla **presionada**, el bloque **romper** saldra del ciclo repetitivo y parara el tren motriz.\n\n![break_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Brillo de\n\nReporta la cantidad de luz detectada por el Sensor de Luz.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/v5/blocks/es/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Brillo de** reporta el rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija qué sensor de luz va usar.\n\n![brightness_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/es/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Brillo de** Se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![brightness_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Transmitir\n\nTransmitir un mensage para activar cualquier cúmulo que empiecen con el bloque **cuando reciba**  escuchando un mensaje de difusión.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/es/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl cúmulo que manda el bloque **transmitir** continuará ejecutando bloques al mismo tiempo que otros cúmulos que reciben el mensaje transmitido.\n\nElija qué mensaje que quiere **transmitir**. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Transmitir y Esperar\n\nTransmitir un mensaje para activar cualquier cúmulo que empiece con el bloque **cuando reciba** escuchando para un mensaje transmitido mientras también detiene el resto del cúmulo.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar \n\nEl cumulo que envia **transmitir y esperar** se detendrá hasta que los otros cumulos que reciben el mensaje enviado se hayan completado.\n\nElija qué mensaje quiere **transmitir**. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/v5/blocks/es/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Calibrar giroscopio\n\nLa calibración del giroscopio se usa para reducir la cantidad de deriva generada por el giroscopio.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nLa deriva se produce cuando el giroscopio detecta incorrectamente el movimiento aunque el sensor no se esté moviendo.\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl giroscopio debe permanecer quieto durante el proceso de calibración. El proceso de calibración tardará aproximadamente 1 segundo en completarse.\n\nElija qué giroscópico va usar.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/es/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Cambiar variable\n\nCambia una variable por el valor dado.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué variable va usar- el variable seleccionado también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **Cambiar variable** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo aumentará el variable que establece la velocidad del variador por 10, cada vez que el **ciclo de repetición** se repita.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Borrar todas las filas\n\nBorra toda la pantalla V5 Brain o Controller.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/v5/blocks/es/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Borrar todas las filas** no cambiará el cursor de la pantalla. Use el bloque **establecer cursor** para restablecer el cursor de la pantalla a una posición específica.\n\nElija qué dispositivo va usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![clear_all_rows_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/es/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_dropdown.png)"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Borrar fila\n\nBorra una sola fila en la pantalla V5 Brain o Controller.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/v5/blocks/es/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Borrar fila**  puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos entre **1 - 20**, para establecer qué fila borrar.\n\nElija qué dispositivo va usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![clear_row_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/es/clear_row/clear_row_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Brain permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará el número de filas disponibles en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n**Tamaño de Fuente V5 Brain - Numero de Filas:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Filas\n* Small - 16 Filas\n* Medium - 12 Filas (Default)\n* Large - 8 Filas\n* Extra Large - 6 Filas\n* Super Large - 4 Filas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es/clear_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nEl controlador V5 no  permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de Fuent V5 Controller - Numero de Filas:**\n\n* Fuente Standard - 3 Filas (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/clear_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Comentario\n\nPermite a los programadores escribir información para ayudar a describir su programa.\n\n![comment_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nLos programadores profesionales usan comentarios en todos sus programas para ayudar a otros a comprender su código. Los comentarios también pueden ayudar con la resolución de problemas y la colaboración.\n\nAgregue texto en el bloque de **Comentario** seleccionando primero el rectángulo transparente y eliminando cualquier texto existente. Luego, escriba el nuevo texto.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/es/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nLos comentarios no cambian el programa o los bloques que lo rodean.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Controlador habilitado\n\nHabilita o deshabilita las acciones configuradas del controlador desde el menú Dispositivos.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija habilitar o deshabilitar las acciones configuradas del controlador seleccionando el estado deseado en el menú desplegable. Por defecto, el controlador está habilitado en cada proyecto.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nLa acción configurada en este ejemplo es utilizar el comportamiento del tren de transmisión del robot establecido por la configuración del controlador en la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/v5/blocks/es/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nEste ejemplo tendrá el controlador configurado deshabilitado cuando se inicie el programa.\n\nEl robot avanzará 6 pulgadas.\n\nFinalmente, el bloque **controlador habilitado** permitirá al Controlador restaurar los comportamientos de conducción del Controlador.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"controller_play_rumble":{"name":"controller_play_rumble","markdown":"# Controlador modo de vibracion\n\nCrea un efecto de vibracion en el Controlador V5.\n\n![controller_play_rumble](static/help/v5/blocks/es/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl **controlador modo de vibracion** usa un motor de vibracionen dentro del Controlador V5 para suministrar realimentación.\n\nElija qué patrón va usar.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_pattern](static/help/v5/blocks/es/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_pattern.png)\n\nElija qué controlador V5 va usar.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_device.png)\n\n\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Corriente del motor\n\nReporta la cantidad de poder un motor V5 esta actualmente usando en amperios (amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Corriente del motor** reporta un rango de **0.0 a 2.5 amps**. \n\nElija qué motor va usar.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **corriente del motor** es usado en los bloques con espacios circular.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Columna del cursor \n\nInforma el número de columna de la ubicación del cursor de la pantalla en el cerebro V5 o Controlador.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Columna del cursor** reporta un rango de **1 a 80**.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **columna de cursor** es usado en los bloques con espacios circulares. \n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Brain  permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará el número de columnas disponibles en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del cerebro V5 - Número de columnas:**\n\n* Extra Small - 80 Columnas\n* Small - 68 Columnas\n* Medium - 48 Columnas (Default)\n* Large - 32 Columnas\n* Extra Large - 24 Columnas\n* Super Large - 16 Columnas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es/cursor_column/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nEl controlador V5 no  permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del controlador V5 - Número de columnas:**\n\n* Fuente Standard - 20 Columnas (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/cursor_column/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Fila del cursor\n\nInforma el número de fila de la ubicación del cursor en la pantalla del cerebro V5 Brain o Controlador.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Fila de cursor** reporta un rango de **1 a 20**.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **fila de cursor** es usado en bloques con espacios circular.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nEl cerebro V5 permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará el número de filas disponibles en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del cerebro V5 - Número de filas:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Filas\n* Small - 16 Filas\n* Medium - 12 Filas (Default)\n* Large - 8 Filas\n* Extra Large - 6 Filas\n* Super Large - 4 Filas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es/cursor_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nEl controlador V5 no le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del controlador V5 - Número de filas:**\n\n* Fuente Standard - 3 Filas (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/cursor_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Distancia de\n\nReporta la distancia del objeto mas cercano de el sensor de buscador de rango ultrasónico.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Distancia de** reporta el rango desde **30mm a 3000mm** o **2 inches a 115 inches**.\n\nElija qué sensor buscador de rango ultrasónico va usar.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/v5/blocks/es/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nChoose whether **distance from** is reported in inches or millimeters. \n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nElija si **distancia de** se usa dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Divide\n\nDivide el primer valor por el segundo valor e informa el dividendo.\n\n![divide](static/help/v5/blocks/es/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Divide** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **divide** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares, y también puede aceptar bloques circulares en él. \n\nIngrese los números que se dividirán.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/es/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nDividir con valores de variables.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/es/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nDivide con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/es/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"draw_circle":{"name":"draw_circle","markdown":"# Dibujar circulo\n\nDibuja un círculo en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![draw_circle](static/help/v5/blocks/es/draw_circle/draw_circle.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Dibujar circulo** require 3 valores:\n\n* Valor 1: Punto Centro X\n* Valor 2: Punto Centro Y\n* valor 3: Radio del Circulo (en pixeles)\n\nEl color de la línea exterior del círculo está determinado por bloque **establecer color de pluma**. El color de línea predeterminado es el blanco.\n\nEl color de relleno interior del círculo está determinado por el bloque **estableser color de relleno**. El color de relleno predeterminado es el negro.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es/draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"draw_line":{"name":"draw_line","markdown":"# Dibujar linea\n\nDibuja una línea en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![draw_line](static/help/v5/blocks/es/draw_line/draw_line.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dibujar linea** requiere 4 valores:\n\n* Valor 1: Comenzando X coordenada\n* Valor 2: Comenzando Y coordenada\n* Valor 3: Finalizando X coordenada\n* Valor 4: Finalizando Y coordenada\n\nEl color de la línea está determinado por el bloque **establecer color de pluma**. El color de línea predeterminado es el blanco.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es/draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_pixel":{"name":"draw_pixel","markdown":"# Dibujar un píxel\n\nDibuja un píxel en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![draw_pixel](static/help/v5/blocks/es/draw_pixel/draw_pixel.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dibujar un pixel** require 2 valores:\n\n* Valor 1: X Coordenada\n* Valor 2: Y Coordenada\n\nEl color del píxel está determinado por el bloque **establecer color de la pluma**. El color de píxel predeterminado es el blanco.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es/draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_rectangle":{"name":"draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Dibujar un rectángulo\n\nDibuja un rectángulo en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![draw_rectangle](static/help/v5/blocks/es/draw_rectangle/draw_rectangle.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dibujar un rectangulo** require 4 valores:\n\n* Valor 1: Esquina Superior Izquierda coordenada X \n* Valor 2: Esquina Superior Izquierda coordenada Y\n* Valor 3: Ancho del rectángulo\n* Valor 4: Altura del rectángulo\n\nEl color de la línea exterior del rectángulo está determinado por bloque **establecer color de pluma**. El color de línea predeterminado es el blanco.\n\nEl color de relleno interior del rectángulo se determina por el bloque **establecer color de relleno**. El color de relleno predeterminado es el negro.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es/draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Conducir\n\nMueve el tren motriz para siempre.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **conducir** energiza el tren motriz para siempre, hasta que se use un nuevo bloque de tren motriz o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija la dirección en que se moverá el tren motriz.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Corriente del tren motriz\n\nReporta la cantidad de corriente (poder) que el tren motriz esta usando actualmente.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Corriente del tren motriz** reporta un rango de **0.0 a 2.5 amperias**. \n\nEl bloque que reporta **corriente del tren motriz** es usado dentro de bloques con espacio circular.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_efficiency":{"name":"drive_efficiency","markdown":"# Eficiencia de la unidad\n\nReporta la eficiencia del Drivetrain.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Eficiencia de la unidad** informa el valor de la potencia (en vatios) que utiliza el motor (input), frente a la cantidad de potencia (en vatios) que proporciona el motor (output).\n\nUn tren motriz V5 generalmente alcanza una eficiencia máxima del 65% en casos de uso normal.\n\n**Eficiencia de la unidad** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**. \n\nEl bloque que reporta **eficiencia de la unidad** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\n![drive_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Manejar por\n\nMueve tren motriz por una distancia dada.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija en qué dirección se moverá el tren motriz.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\n\nEstablezca qué tan lejos se moverá el tren motriz ingresando un valor y eligiendo la unidad de medida (pulgadas or milímetros).\n\nEl bloque **Maneja por** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques **esperar** hasta que el tren motriz termine de moverse.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el tren motriz se mueve.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Direccion de la unidad\n\nReporta la dirección a la que se dirige el tren motriz usando la posición angular actual de el giroscopio (Gyro).\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Direccion de la unidad** reporta un aumento en la direccion al girar en sentido del reloj.\n\n**Direccion de la unidad** reporta un rangi de **0.00 a 359.99 grados**.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Direccion de la unidad** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Unidad termino\n\nReporta si el tren motriz ha completado su movimiento.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Unidad termino** reporta **verdadero** cuando los motores del tren motriz han completado su movimiento.\n\n**Unidad termino** reporta **falso** cuando los motores del tren motriz siguen en movimiento.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **unidad termino** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y es usado en bloques de espacio hexagonal (seis lados).\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Unidad está en movimiento\n\nReporta si el tren motriz se está actualmente moviendo.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Unidad está en movimiento** reporta **verdadero** cuando tren motriz esta en movimiento.\n\n**Unidad está en movimiento** reporta **falso** cuando los motores del tren motriz paran.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Unidad está en movimiento** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y es usado en bloques con espacio hexagonal (seis-lados).\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_power":{"name":"drive_power","markdown":"# Potencia de la unidad\n\nReporta la potencia producida actualmente por el tren motriz.\n\n![drive_power](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_power/drive_power.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**potencia de la unidad** reporta un rango de **0.0 a 22.0 watts**. \n\nEl bloque que reporta **potencia de la unidad** es usado dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_power/drive_power_inserted.png)"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Rotación de la unidad\n\nInforma el ángulo de rotación del tren motriz cuando se configura con un sensor giroscópico de 3 ejes o un sensor inercial V5.\n\n![drive_rotation](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_rotation/drive_rotation.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Rotación de la unidad** informa un valor **positivo** cuando el tren motriz gira en una dirección **en el sentido de las agujas del reloj**.\n\n**Rotación de la unidad** reporta un valor **negativo**  cuando el tren motriz gira en una direccion **contra las agujas del reloj**.\n\nEl cloque que reporta **Rotación de la unidad** Se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_rotation_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_rotation/drive_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_temperature":{"name":"drive_temperature","markdown":"# Temperatura de la unidad\n\nReporta la temperatura de los motores V5 energizando el tren motriz.\n\n![drive_temperature](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_temperature/drive_temperature.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Temperatura de la unidad** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**. \n\nEl bloque que reporta **temperatura de la unidad** es usado dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.=\n\n![drive_temperature_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_temperature/drive_temperature_inserted.png)"},"drive_torque":{"name":"drive_torque","markdown":"# Torque de la unidad\n\nReporta la cantidad de torque (fuerza rotacional) que el tren motriz esta usando actualmente.\n\n![drive_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_torque/drive_torque.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Torque de la unidad** reporta rango de **0.0 a 18.6 pulgadas-lbs (InLB)** o **0.0 a 2.1 Newton-metros (Nm)**. \n\nElija si el **Torque de la unidad** se reporta en pulgadas-lbs (InLb) o Newton-metros (Nm).\n\n![drive_torque_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_torque/drive_torque_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **torque de la unidad** es usado dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_torque/drive_torque_inserted.png)"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad de la unidad\n\nReporta la velocidad actual del tren motriz\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Velocidad de la unidad** reporta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\n**Velocidad de la unidad** reporta un rango de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los motores inteligentes V5 utilizados en el tren motriz.\n\n* Cartucho Rojo : -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Cartucho Verde: -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Cartucho Azul : -600rpm a 600rpm\n\nElija si la velocidad se reporta en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Velocidad de la unidady** es usado dentro de bloque con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"efficiency_of_motor":{"name":"efficiency_of_motor","markdown":"# Eficiencia del motor.\n\nReporta la eficiencia de un motor inteligente V5.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/es/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Eficiencia del motor** reporta el poder de el motor (en watts) usando (input), contra la cantidad de poder (en watts) que el motor esta proporcionando (output). \n\nUn motor inteligente V5 generalmente alcanza una eficiencia máxima del 65% en casos de uso normal.\n\n**Eficiencia del motor** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**. \n\nElija qué motor va usar.\n\n![motor_efficiency_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_device.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Eficiencia del motor** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\n![motor_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_inserted.png)"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Igual a\n\nInforma si el primer valor es el mismo, o igual al segundo valor.\n\n![equal_to](static/help/v5/blocks/es/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Igual a** reporta **verdadero** cuando dos valores son exactamente igual.\n\n**Igual a** reporta **falso** cuando dos valores no son iguales.\n\nEl bloque **Igual a** aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Igual a** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso**  y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Por siempre\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite cualquier bloque contenido adentro, para siempre.\n\n![forever](static/help/v5/blocks/es/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nColoca bloques en un bloque 'C' **Por siempre** para que esas acciones se repitan **Por siempre**.\n\nPuede salir de una repetición **Por siempre** poniendo un bloque de **Romper** dentro.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nBloques 'C' también se pueden poner uno dentro del otro. Este concepto se llama anidamiento (nesting) y puede ayudar a ahorrar tiempo al programar diferentes comportamientos."},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Función\n\nRealiza una función matemática seleccionada.\n\n![function](static/help/v5/blocks/es/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - valor absoluto\n* **floor** - redondea hacia abajo al entero más cercano\n* **ceiling** - redondea al entero más cercano\n* **sqrt** - Raiz Cuadrada\n* **sin** - sine\n* **cos** - coseno\n* **tan** - tangente\n* **asin** - Arcoseno o la inversa de sine\n* **acos** - arcocoseno o el inverso del coseno\n* **atan** - arctan o el inverso de la tangente\n* **ln** - base de logaritmo natural e\n* **log** - base de logaritmo 10\n* **e ^** - poderes de e\n* **10 ^** - poderes de 10\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Función** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija la **Función** matemática de la lista de opciones.\n\n![function_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/function/function_select.png)\n\nEl bloque de **Función** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n![function_fit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Mas grande que\n\nReporta si el primer valor es mas grande (mayor) que el segundo valor.\n\n![greater_than](static/help/v5/blocks/es/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Mas grande que** reporta **verdadero** cuando el primer valor es mayor que el segundo valor.\n\n**Mas grande que** reporta **falso** cuando el primer valor es menor o igual que el segundo valor.\n\nEl bloque **Mas grande que** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Mas grande que** reporta un valor **verdadero** or **falso** y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Dirección del giroscopio\n\nReporta la posición angular actual del sensor giroscópico (gyro).\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/es/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Dirección del giroscopio** informa un aumento en la direccion cuando gira en sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\n**Dirección del giroscopio** reporta un rango entre **0.00 a 359.99**.\n\nElija qué sensor giroscópico a verificar.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/es/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Dirección del giroscopio** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Si entonces\n\nUn bloque 'C' que ejecurta el bloque de adentro, si la condicion Booleana que reporta es **verdadera**.  \n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/es/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque 'C' **Si entonces** solo verificará la condición booleana una vez. \n\nSi la condición booleana se informa como **verdadera**, el bloque de adentro **Si entonces** se ejecutara.\n\nSi la condición booleana se informa como **falsa**, el bloque de adentro **Si entonces** será saltado.\n\nEl 'C' block **Si entonces** puede aceptar bloques con forma hexagonal (seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/es/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Si entonces más\n\nUn bloque 'C' Block que ejecuta los bloques dentro de la primera o segunda parte de **Si entonces más**, basado en el valor booleano informado.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/es/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl 'C' bloque **Si entonces más** solo verificará la condición booleana una vez.\n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **verdadero**, el bloque dentro de la seccion **si** sera ejecutado.\n\nSi la condición booleana es **falsa**, el bloque dentro de la seccion **mas** sera ejecutado.\n\nEl 'C' bloque **Si entonces más** puede aceptar bloques con forma hexagonal (seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/es/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)"},"inertial_acceleration":{"name":"inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Aceleración de\n\nInforma el valor de aceleración de uno de los ejes (x, y, o z) en el Sensor Intertial.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n**Aceleración de** reporta un rango de **-4.0 a 4.0** Gs. \n\nElija qué sensor inercial usar.\n\n![inertial_acceleration_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_device.png)\n\nElija qué eje usar:\n\n* El **X-eje** reporta la aceleración cuando se mueve el sensor inercial **lado a lado**\n* El **Y-eje** reporta la aceleración cuando se mueve el sensor inercial **arriba a abajo**\n* El **Z-eje** reporta la aceleración cuando se mueve el sensor inercial **enfrente a atras**\n\n![inertial_acceleration_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_axis.png)\n\nEl bloque sensor ** Aceleración de ** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_gyrorate":{"name":"inertial_gyrorate","markdown":"# Frecuencia del giroscopio\n\nObtiene la velocidad de rotación de uno de los ejes (x, y, o z) en el sensor inercial.\n\n![gyro_rate_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_gyrorate/gyro_rate_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Frecuencia del giroscopio** reporta un rango de **-1000.0 a 1000.0** en dps (grados por segundo). \n\nElija qué sensor inercial usar.\n\n![gyroRate_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_included_block.png)\n\nElija qué eje usar.\n\n* El **X-axis** reporta la frecuencia de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el X-Eje (basado en la orientación del sensor)\n* El **Y-axis** reporta la frecuencia de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el Y-Eje (basado en la orientación del sensor)\n* Eli **Z-axis** reporta la frecuencia de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el Z-Eje basado en la orientación del sensor)\n\n![gyroRate_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_axis.png)\n\nEl bloque sensorial **Frecuencia del giroscopio** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_orientation":{"name":"inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Orientación de\n\nObtiene un ángulo de orientación del sensor inercial. Informa el valor unitario especificado por el parámetro del sensor inercial.\n\n![orientation_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_orientation/orientation_inertial_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nLa orientación reportada está determinada por el eje seleccionado (x, y, o z).\n\n* El **X-eje** representa **pitch**, que informa un valor entre -90 a +90 grados.\n* El **Y-eje** representa **roll**, que informa un valor entre -180 a +180 grados)\n* El **Z-eje** representa **yaw**, que informa un valor entre -180 a +180 grados)\n\n---\n\n**Pitch** es el ángulo del robot inclinado hacia adelante y hacia atrás.\n\n![V5_Pitch_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_orientation/V5_Pitch_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Roll** es el ángulo del robot inclinado hacia la izquierda y hacia la derecha.\n\n![V5_Roll_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_orientation/V5_Roll_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Yaw** Es la rotación angular del robot.\n\n![V5_Yaw_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_orientation/V5_Yaw_rev2.jpg)\n\n---\n\nElija qué sensor inercial va usar.\n\n![orientation_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_orientation/orientation_included_block.png)\n\nElija qué eje vs usar.\n\n![orientation_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_orientation/orientation_axis.png)\n\nEl bloque sensorial **Orientación de** es usado dentro de bloques con espacio circular.\n\n![orientation_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/inertial_orientation/orientation_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n\n"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Elemento de la lista 2D\n\nInforma el valor de un elemento en una lista 2D.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué lista 2D usar. La lista 2D también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nIngrese la posición de la fila del elemento (primer número) y la columna (segundo número) dentro de la lista que se reportara. Aquí, se informa el elemento en la fila de posición 2, columna 3 en la lista 2D.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nEl bloque **Elemento de la lista 2D** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Artículo de\n\nInforma el valor de un elemento en una lista.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué lista usar. La lista también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nIngrese el número de la posición del elemento dentro de la lista. Aquí, se reporta el segundo elemento de la lista (elemento 2).\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nEl bloque **Artículo de** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá la velocidad de la transmisión al valor almacenado en el elemento 3 de mi lista. El tren motriz ahora avanzará a una velocidad del 90%.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Longitud de la lista 2D\n\nInforma el número de filas o columnas en una lista 2D.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/es/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué lista 2D usar. La lista 2D también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nElija qué valor informar. La lista 2D puede reportar **filas** o **columnas**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Longitud de la lista 2D** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)\n"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Menos que\n\nReports if the first value is less (smaller) than the second value. \n\n![less_than](static/help/v5/blocks/es/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Menos que** reporta **verdadero** cuando el primer valor es menor que el segundo valor. \n\n**Menos que** reporta **falso** cuando el primer valor es mayor o igual que el segundo valor.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Menos que** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\nEl bloque **Menos que** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor a terminado\n\nInforma si el motor inteligente V5 seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Motor a terminado** reporta **verdadero** cuando el motor seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\n**Motor a terminado** reporta **verdadero** cuando el motor seleccionado todavía está en movimiento.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Motor a terminado** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor está girando\n\nInforma si el motor inteligente V5 seleccionado está girando actualmente.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/v5/blocks/es/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Motor está girando** reporta **verdadero** cuando el motor seleccionado está girando.\n\n**Motor está girando** reporta **falso** cuando el motor seleccionado se detiene.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **Motor está girando** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Multiplicar\n\nMultiplica dos valores cualquiera juntos y reporta el resultado.\n\n![multiply](static/help/v5/blocks/es/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Multiplicar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque  **Multiplicar** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares, y también pueden aceptar bloques circulares en él.\n\nMultiplica dos números.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/es/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nMultiplicar con valores de variables.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/es/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nMultiplique con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/es/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Siguiente fila \n\nEstablece el cursor de impresión en la pantalla del cerebro V5 o Controlador en la siguiente fila disponible.\n\n![next_row](static/help/v5/blocks/es/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## Como utilizar \n\nPor defecto, todos los proyectos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1 columna 1. El bloque **siguiente fila** moverá el cursor hacia abajo, una sola fila en la pantalla  **Siguiente fila** también establecerá la columna del cursor en la posición 1.\n\nElija qué dispositivo usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![next_row_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/es/next_row/next_row_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Brain le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará el número de filas disponibles en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del cerebro V5 - Numero de Filas:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Filas\n* Small - 16 Filas\n* Medium - 12 Filas (Standard)\n* Large - 8 Filas\n* Extra Large - 6 Filas\n* Super Large - 4 Filas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es/next_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nEl controlador V5 no le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del controlador V5 - Numero de Filas:**\n\n* Fuente Standard - 3 filas (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/next_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# No\n\nInforma lo contrario (inverso) del valor booleano reportado.\n\n![not](static/help/v5/blocks/es/not/not.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **no** reporta **verdadero** cuando el bloque booleano dentro reporta **falso**.\n\nEl bloque **no** reporta **falso** cuando el bloque booleano dentro reporta **verdadero**.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **no** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo reporta **verdadero** cuando no se presione la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![not_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/es/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/es/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Recuento de objetos\n\nInforma cuántos objetos detecta el sensor de visión.\n\nSerá necesario configurar un objeto antes de que el bloque **recuento de objetos** pueda detectarlo.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué sensor de visión usar.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **foto de** deberá usarse antes de que el bloque **Recuento de objetos** reporte varios objetos.\n\nEl bloque **Recuento de objetos** solo detectará el número de objetos de la última firma de la foto instantánea.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Objeto existe\n\nInforma si el sensor de visión detecta un objeto configurado.\n\nSerá necesario configurar un objeto para que el bloque **Objeto existe** pueda detectarlo.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué sensor de visión usar.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n\n**Objeto existe** reporta **verdadero** cuando el sensor de visión detecta un objeto configurado.\n\n**Objeto existe** reporta **falso** cuando el sensor de visión no detecta un objeto configurado.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Objeto existe** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nEl bloque **foto de**  deberá usarse antes de el bloque Booleano **Objeto existe** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso**."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Objeto encontrado\n\nReporta si el sensor del Buscador de rango ultrasónico ve un objeto dentro de su campo de visión.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/es/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Objeto encontrado** reporta **verdadero** cuando el sensor del Buscador de rango ultrasónico ve un objeto o superficie dentro de su campo de visión.\n\n**Objeto encontrado** reporta **falso** cuando el sensor del Buscador de rango ultrasónico no detecta un objeto o superficie.\n\nElija qué sensor del Buscador de rango ultrasónico va usar.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/es/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Objeto encontrado** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso**  y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/es/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# O\n\nInforma si una de las dos condiciones booleanas es verdadera.\n\n![or](static/help/v5/blocks/es/or/or.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **verdadero** cuando una (o ambas) condiciones son **verdadero**. \n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **falso** cuando ambas condiciones son **falso**.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **o** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **verdadero** cuando se presiona el sensor Bumper y / o el brillo del sensor de luz es superior al 50%.\n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **falso** solo cuando el sensor Bumper no está presionado y el brillo del sensor de luz es menor o igual al 50%\n\n![or_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/es/or/or_truth.png)"},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Posición del controlador\n\nInforma la posición de un joystick en el controlador V5 a lo largo de un eje.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Posición del controlador** reporta rango de **-100 a 100**.\n\n**Posición del controlador** informará cero (0) cuando el eje de un joystick esté centrado.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nElija el controlador V5 para usar.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_devices.png)\n\nElija el eje del joystick para verificar su posición.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Posición del controlador** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Posición del motor\n\nReporta la distancia que ha recorrido el motor inteligente V5.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Posición del motor** informa la posición del motor inteligente V5 en números enteros para grados y números decimales para giros.\n\nElija qué motor inteligente V5 va usar.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nElija si el valor se informa en grados rotados o en vueltas del motor inteligente V5.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Posición del motor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"position_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"position_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Posición del codificador de eje\n\nReporta la distancia que ha girado el codificador de eje.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Posición del codificador de eje** reporta la distancia que ha girado el codificador de eje en números enteros para grados y números decimales para giros.\n\nElija qué codificador de eje usar.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_device.png)\n\nElija si el valor se informa en grados rotados o en turnos del codificador de eje.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Posición del codificador de eje** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_inserted.png)"},"power_of_motor":{"name":"power_of_motor","markdown":"# Poder del motor\n\nReporta la cantidad de poder de salida que genera actualmente el motor inteligente V5.\n\n![motor_power](static/help/v5/blocks/es/power_of_motor/motor_power.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Poder del motor** reporta un rango de **0.0 a 11.0 watts**. \n\nElija un motor para usar.\n\n![motor_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/power_of_motor/motor_power_device.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Poder del motor** y se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![motor_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/power_of_motor/motor_power_inserted.png)\n"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Presionar bumper\n\nReporta si se presiona el bumper.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/es/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Como utilizar \n\n**Presionar bumper** reporta **verdadero** si se presiona el bumper.\n\n**Presionar bumper** reporta **falso** si no se presiona el bumper.\n\nElija qué bumper va usar.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/es/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Presionar bumper** reporta **verdadero** o **falso** valor y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Presionando Controlador\n\nInforma si se presiona un botón en el controlador V5.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Presionando Controlador** reporta **verdadero** si se presiona el botón Controlador que es seleccionado.\n\n**Presionando Controlador** reporta **falso** si no se presiona el botón Controlador que es seleccionado.\n\nElija qué controlador V5 va usar.\n\n![pressing_controller_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_device.png)\n\nElija qué botón del controlador va usar.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **Presionando Controlador** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)"},"pressing_limit":{"name":"pressing_limit","markdown":"# Límite de presion\n\nInforma si se presiona el interruptor de límite.\n\n![pressing_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/pressing_limit/pressing_limit.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Límite de presion** reporta **verdadero** si se presiona el interruptor de límite.\n\n**Límite de presion** reporta **falso** si no se presiona el interruptor de límite.\n\nElija qué interruptor de límite usar.\n\n![pressing_limit_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/es/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_bumper.png)\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Límite de presion** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![pressing_limit_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_inserted.png)\n "},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Impresión\n\nImprime valores o texto en la pantalla del Cerebro V5 o Controlador.\n\n![look_print](static/help/v5/blocks/es/print/look_print.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Impresión** imprimirá los datos en la ubicación del cursor en la pantalla.\n\nTodos los proyectos nuevos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1, columna 1.\n\nTodos los bloques que reportan se imprimirán como números enteros. Use el bloque **establecer precisión de impresión** para ajustar la cantidad de decimales impresos.\n\nElija qué dispositivo a usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![look_print_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/es/print/look_print_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nImprime palabras y números.\n\n![print_words](static/help/v5/blocks/es/print/print_words.png)\n\nImprima el valor informado de un variable.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/v5/blocks/es/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nImprimir el cálculo reportado de un operador.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/v5/blocks/es/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nImprima el valor informado desde un sensor o dispositivo.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Mis bloques\n\nMis bloques se usan para crear bloques personalizados.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Mis bloques** se usan para crear una secuencia de bloques que se pueden usar varias veces a lo largo de un proyecto. \n\n**Mis bloques** son creados usando el boton **Make a Block**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Mis bloques** pueden tener múltiples parámetros (etiquetas de texto, variables numéricas y variables booleanas) para agregar más funcionalidad a su bloque personalizado.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nPara usar **Mi bloque**, adjunta el llamado **Mi bloque** a un bloque de sombrero. Cuando el **Mi bloque** se alcanza en un proyecto, la acomulacion dentro de  **Mi bloque** se ejecutará utilizando los valores de los parámetros especificados.\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nAdjunte una acomulacion de bloques a la **Mis bloques* \"define\" el bloque de sombrero para establecer la acción que ocurre cuando se usa un **Mi bloque**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Nota: Crear múltiples Mis Bloques con las mismas etiquetas y variables puede causar errores al descargar su proyecto.***\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **Mis bloques** para:\n\n* Conduzca hacia adelante por 15 pulgadas\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del cerebro\n* Gira el robot 180 grados a la derecha\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del cerebro\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Mis bloques\n\nMis bloques se usan para crear bloques personalizados.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Mis bloques** se usan para crear una secuencia de bloques que se pueden usar varias veces a lo largo de un proyecto. \n\n**Mis bloques** son creados usando el boton **Make a Block**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Mis bloques** pueden tener múltiples parámetros (etiquetas de texto, variables numéricas y variables booleanas) para agregar más funcionalidad a su bloque personalizado.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nPara usar **Mi bloque**, adjunta el llamado **Mi bloque** a un bloque de sombrero. Cuando el **Mi bloque** se alcanza en un proyecto, la acomulacion dentro de  **Mi bloque** se ejecutará utilizando los valores de los parámetros especificados.\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nAdjunte una acomulacion de bloques a la **Mis bloques* \"define\" el bloque de sombrero para establecer la acción que ocurre cuando se usa un **Mi bloque**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Nota: Crear múltiples Mis Bloques con las mismas etiquetas y variables puede causar errores al descargar su proyecto.***\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **Mis bloques** para:\n\n* Conduzca hacia adelante por 15 pulgadas\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del cerebro\n* Gira el robot 180 grados a la derecha\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del cerebro\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/es/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Aleatorio\nInforma un valor aleatorio entre los valores más bajos y más altos en el bloque.\n\n![random](static/help/v5/blocks/es/random/random.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Aleatorio** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\nEl bloque **Aleatorio** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplos\n\nEste ejemplo usa un bloque **Aleatorio** para aleatorizar la velocidad de la transmisión.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/v5/blocks/es/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nEste ejemplo usa un bloque **Aleatorio** para aleatorizar la longitud de un bloque de espera.\n\n![random_control](static/help/v5/blocks/es/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"reflectivity_of":{"name":"reflectivity_of","markdown":"# Reflexividad de\n\nInforma la cantidad de luz reflejada con el sensor rastreador de línea.\n\n![reflectivity_of](static/help/v5/blocks/es/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nLas superficies de color claro reflejarán más luz e informarán un alto valor de reflectividad.\n\nLas superficies de color oscuro reflejarán menos luz e informarán un valor de reflectividad bajo.\n\n**Reflexividad de** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija qué sensor rastreador de línea va usar.\n\n![reflectivity_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/es/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_color.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Reflexividad de** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![reflectivity_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n\n"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Recordatorio\n\nDivide el primer valor por el segundo valor e informa el resto.\n\n![remainder](static/help/v5/blocks/es/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Recordatorio** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLos números que se dividen en partes iguales reportarán un resultado de cero.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **Recordatorio** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo dividirá 7 y 2 e informará el resto para imprimir \"1\" en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/es/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Repetir\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques contenidos dentro por un número determinado de veces.\n\n![repeat](static/help/v5/blocks/es/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nPrimero ingrese un valor para indicar cuántas veces la acumulación va a **Repetir** los bloques contenidos dentro. \n\nEl bloque 'C' **Repetir**  puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nBloques 'C' también se pueden poner uno dentro del otro. Este concepto se llama anidamiento (nesting) y puede ayudar a ahorrar tiempo al programar diferentes comportamientos.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/repeat/repeat_select.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Repetir hasta\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques dentro hasta que se informa que la condición booleana es **verdadera**.  \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/es/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Repetir hasta** solo verificará la condición booleana al comienzo de cada ciclo. \n\nSi la condición booleana se informa como **falso**, los bloques dentro **Repetir hasta** seran ejecutados.\n\nSi la condición booleana se informa como **verdadero**, los bloques dentro **Repetir hasta** seran ejecutados.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **Repetir hasta** puede aceptar bloques con forma hexagonal (seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/es/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Restablecer temporizador\n\nRestablece el temporizador del cerebro V5.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/v5/blocks/es/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl temporizador del cerebro comienza al iniciar cada proyecto. El bloque **Restablecer temporizador** se usa para restablecer el temporizador a 0 segundos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el temporizador se reiniciará antes de mover el tren motriz hacia adelante durante 3 segundos. Después de que hayan transcurrido 3 segundos, el tren motriz se detendrá.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/v5/blocks/es/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Ángulo de rotación\n\nInforma el ángulo de rotación actual del sensor giroscópico de 3 ejes o del sensor inercial V5 en grados.\n\n![rotation_position.png](static/help/v5/blocks/es/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Rotación giroscópica** reporta un valor **positivo**  cuando el Sensor giroscopico gira en la dirección **en sentido de las agujas del reloj**.\n\n**Rotación giroscópica** reporta **negativo** cuando el Sensor giroscopico gira en la dirección **en contra de las agujas del reloj**.\n\nElija qué sensor giroscópico / sensor de inercia para verificar.\n\n![rotation_position_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/es/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_devices.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **Rotación giroscópica** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![rotation_position_inserted.png](static/help/v5/blocks/es/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_inserted.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Redondear\n\nRedondea el valor ingresado al entero más cercano.\n\n![round](static/help/v5/blocks/es/round/round.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nDecimales que son 0.5 o más seran **redondear** de mas, y decimales menos de 0.5 **redondear** de menos.\n\nEl bloque **redondear** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares, y también pueden aceptar bloques circulares en ellos.\n\nEl bloque **redondear** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/es/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo redondeará 2.7 e imprimirá \"3\".\n\n![round_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/es/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"screen_position":{"name":"screen_position","markdown":"# Posición de la pantalla\n\nInforma la ubicación del último toque detectado en la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\n![screen_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/screen_position/screen_position_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Posición de la pantalla** se utiliza para capturar la ubicación X/Y de la última pulsación en la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5. Este bloque de informe se puede utilizar para crear interactividad entre el V5 y el usuario final.\n\n**Posición de la pantalla** reporta un rango de **0 to 480 pixels** cuando se establece para reportar la coordenada **X**.\n\n**Posición de la pantalla** reporta un rango de **0 to 240 pixels** cuando se establece para reportar la coordenada **Y**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/es/screen_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\nElija qué eje reportar.\n\n![screen_position_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es/screen_position/screen_position_value.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Posición de la pantalla** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![screen_position_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/screen_position/screen_position_inserted.png)"},"screen_pressed":{"name":"screen_pressed","markdown":"# Pantalla presionada\n\nInforma si actualmente se está presionando la pantalla táctil del V5 Brain.\n\n![screen_pressed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque booleano **pantalla presionada** puede ser utilizado junto con **posición de pantalla** para detectar cuándo y dónde se ha producido un toque en la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\n**Pantalla presionada** reporta **verdadero** cuando se presiona la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\n**Pantalla presionada** reporta **falso** cuando no se presiona la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **screen pressed** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![screen_pressed_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Establecer lista 2D\n\nEstablece cada elemento en la lista 2D a los valores ingresados.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nAl crear una lista 2D, puede establecer el número de **columnas** de la lista entre 1 a 10 elementos y el número de **filas** de la lista entre 1 a 10 artículos.\n\nElija qué lista 2D va usar. La lista 2D también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer lista 2D** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Establecer lista en\n\nEstablece cada elemento de la lista a los valores ingresados.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nAl crear una lista, puede establecer la longitud de la lista entre 1 y 10 elementos.\n\nElija qué lista usar. La lista también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer lista en**  puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá la lista en valores iniciales, y luego informará el elemento #3 (90) de la lista, para establecer la posición del Brazo.\n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Establecer variable booleano\n\nEstablece un variable booleano en un valor dado.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué variable booleano va usar. Los variables booleanos también se pueden renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nElija un valor booleano.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nEl bloque **Establecer variable booleano** puede aceptar bloques de forma hexagonal (seis lados).\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# Establecer cursor\n\nEstablece la ubicación del cursor para el bloque **impresión** en la pantalla V5 Brain o Controller.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEstablezca la posición de la fila y columna del cursor para sea mostrado un comando de **impresión** en una ubicación específica en la pantalla.\n\n**Establecer cursor** acepta un rango para **fila** de **1 a 20**.\n\n**Establecer cursor** acepta un rango para **columna** de **1 a 80**.\n\nElija qué dispositivo usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![set_cursor_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_cursor/set_cursor_dropdown.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer cursor** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n---\n\nEl cerebro V5 le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará el número de columnas disponibles en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del cerebro V5 - Numero de Filas**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Filas\n* Small - 16 Filas\n* Medium - 12 Filas (Default)\n* Large - 8 Filas\n* Extra Large - 6 Filas\n* Super Large - 4 Filas\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del cerebro V5 - Numbero de Columnas:**\n\n* Extra Small - 80 Columnas\n* Small - 68 Columnas\n* Medium - 48 Columnas (Default)\n* Large - 32 Columnas\n* Extra Large - 24 Columnas\n* Super Large - 16 Columnas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nEl controlador V5 no le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del controlador V5 - Numbero de Filas:**\n\n* Fuente Estandar - 3 Filas (Default)\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del controlador V5 - Numbero de Columnas:**\n\n* Fuente Estandar - 20 Columnas (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Establecer direccion de unidad\n\nEstablece el valor de direccion del Giroscopio en el tren motriz.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Establecer direccion de unidad** se puede usar para establecer la posición del tren motriz en cualquier direccion dada. Este bloque se puede usar para restablecer la orientación del giroscopio del tren motriz cuando la direccion se establece en un valor de 0.\n\n**Establecer direccion de unidad** acepta un rango de **0 a 360** grados.\n\nEl bloque **Establecer direccion de unidad** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer la rotación del chasis\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del chasis.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** bloque se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del chasis a cualquier valor positivo o negativo dado.\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** bloque puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el robot un total de 210 grados:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Da veulta a la derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) para girar 120 grados.\n- Establezca la posición actual del robot como rotación de -45 grados.\n- Da veulta a la derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) 90 grados adicionales (-45 grados a 45 grados) en función del valor de rotación establecido del bloque anterior.\n"},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Configurar parada de la unidad\n\nEstablece el comportamiento del tren motriz una vez que deja de moverse.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n* **Brake** El tren motriz se detiene inmediatamente y no corregirá a fuerzas externas.\n* **Coast** Deja que el tren motriz gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* **Hold** El tren motriz se detiene inmediatamente y lo devuelve a su posición donde se detuvo si lo mueve una fuerza externa, utilizando el codificador incorporado.\n* \n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el tren motriz avance durante 3 segundos y luego mantenga su posición una vez que se detenga.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer tiempo de espera\n\nEstablece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del tren motriz.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl límite de tiempo del tren motriz se usa para evitar que los bloques de unidades que no alcanzan su posición eviten que otros bloques en la acumulación se ejecuten.\n\nUn ejemplo de un tren motriz que no alcanza su posición es cuando un robot es conducido contra una pared y no puede completar su movimiento.\n\nEl bloque **Establecer tiempo de espera** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo finalizará el comando **conducir** después de 2 segundos si el tren motriz no ha alcanzado el objetivo de 24 pulgadas. Una vez que se alcanza el límite de tiempo o la distancia, el tren motriz pasará al comando **girar**.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer velocidad\n\nEstablece la velocidad del tren motriz.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Establecer velocidad** establecerá la velocidad del tren motriz, pero no hará que el tren motriz se mueva. Todavía se requiere el bloque **conducir**.\n\n**Establecer velocidad** reporta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\n**Establecer velocidad** acepta un rango de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los motores inteligentes V5, utilizados en el tren motriz.\n\n* Cartucho Rojo: -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Cartucho Verde: -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Cartucho Azul: -600rpm a 600rpm\n\nEstablecer la velocidad del tren motriz en un valor negativo hará que el tren motriz se mueva en reversa.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad del tren motriz a 0 hará que el tren motriz se detenga.\n\nEl bloque **establecer velocidad** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija la unidad de medida.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n\n"},"set_fill_color":{"name":"set_fill_color","markdown":"# Establecer color de relleno\n\nEstablece el color que llena las formas dibujadas en la pantalla V5 Brain.\n\n![set_fill_color_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Establecer color de relleno** se utiliza para establecer el color del interior de los círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del cerebro V5. \n\nElige un color de relleno.\n\n![set_fill_color_color](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_color.png)  \n\nEl color de relleno se usará para cualquier objeto futuro dibujado en la pantalla del cerebro V5."},"set_font":{"name":"set_font","markdown":"# Establecer fuente\n\nEstablece el estilo y el tamaño de la fuente utilizada en la pantalla del cerebro V5 al imprimir números o texto.\n\n![set_font_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_font/set_font_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nHay dos tipos diferentes de fuentes disponibles en la pantalla V5 Brain:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - cada letra ocupa el mismo ancho.\n* Proporcional (Prop) - cada letra ocupa diferentes anchos de tamaño según el personaje.\n\nElija qué tipo de fuente y tamaño usar.\n\n![set_font_block_font](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_font/set_font_block_font.png)  \n\nEl nuevo tamaño de fuente se utilizará para cualquier texto futuro escrito en la pantalla del cerebro V5."},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Establecer direccion del giroscópio\n\nEstablece la posición actual del sensor giroscópico (gyro) en el valor dentro del bloque de comandos.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer direccion del giroscópio** se puede usar para establecer la posición del giroscopio en cualquier direccion en el sentido de las agujas del reloj. Este bloque se usa típicamente para restablecer la orientación del giroscopio cuando el encabezado se establece en un valor de 0.\n\n**establecer direccion del giroscópio** acepta un rango de **0.0 a 359.99** grados.\n\nEl bloque **establecer direccion del giroscópio** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija qué sensor giroscópico va usar, luego ingrese el valor deseado.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer la rotación del chasis\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del chasis.\n\n![setdriverotation](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** bloque se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del chasis a cualquier valor positivo o negativo dado.\n\n![setdriverotation](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation_devices.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** bloque puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Reemplazar elemento de lista 2D\n\nActualiza un elemento en la lista 2D a un nuevo valor.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nIngrese la posición de la fila del artículo (primer número) y la columna (segundo número) dentro de la lista a ser reemplazada.\n\nElija qué lista usar. La lista también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **Reemplazar elemento** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Reemplazar artículo\n\nActualiza un elemento de la lista a un nuevo valor.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nActualiza un elemento de la lista a un nuevo valor. Elija qué lista usar. La lista también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **Reemplazar artículo** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n"},"set_led":{"name":"set_led","markdown":"# Establecer LED\n\nEnciende o apaga un LED.\n\n![set_led_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_led/set_led_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nSeleccione qué LED usar.\n\n![set_led_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_led/set_led_block_device.png)\n\nSeleccione si el LED está encendido o apagado.\n\n![set_led_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_led/set_led_block_setting.png)\n\n"},"set_motor_controller_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_controller_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer la velocidad del controlador del motor\n\nEstablece la velocidad de un Motor 393 conectado a un Controlador de Motor 29.\n\n![set_motor_controller_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Establecer la velocidad del controlador del motor** accepts a range of **-100% to 100%**.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad del Motor 393 en un valor negativo hará que el Motor 393 gire en reversa.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de un Motor 393 en 0 hará que el Motor 393 se detenga.\n\nElija qué Motor 393 usar.\n\n![set_motor_controller_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_motor.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Establecer la posición del motor\n\nEstablece la posición del codificador del motor inteligente V5 en el valor dado.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **posición del motor** se puede usar para establecer la posición del motor en cualquier valor dado.\n\nGeneralmente, el bloque **posición del motor** se utiliza para establecer la posición en 0 para restablecer la posición del codificador del motor.\n\nElija qué motor inteligente V5 usar.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nElija la unidad de medida en grados o vueltas.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Establecer parada del motor\n\nEstablece el comportamiento del motor inteligente V5 una vez que deja de moverse.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n* **Brake** hará que el motor se detenga inmediatamente.\n* **Coast** deja que el motor gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* **Hold** hará que el motor se detenga inmediatamente y lo devuelva a su posición de parada si se mueve.\n\nEl bloque **establecer parada del motor** surtirá efecto para todos los comandos de motor futuros para el resto del proyecto.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nElija la configuración del motor después de que se detenga.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el motor del brazo avance 90 grados y luego resistirá las fuerzas externas (como la gravedad) para mantener su posición.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer tiempo de espera del motor\n\nEstablece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del motor inteligente V5.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl límite de tiempo del motor se usa para evitar que los bloques de movimiento que no alcanzan su posición eviten que otros bloques en la acumulación se ejecuten. Un ejemplo de un motor que no alcanza su posición es un brazo o una garra que alcanza su límite mecánico y no puede completar su movimiento.\n\nEl bloque **establecer el tiempo de espera del motor** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo finalizará el comando **establecer motor** después de 2 segundos si el motor de garra no ha alcanzado la posición de 270 grados. Una vez que se alcanza el límite de tiempo o el objetivo, el motor de garra se moverá a la posición 0 grados.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Establecer torque del motor\n\nEstablece la fuerza del motor inteligente V5.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Establecer torque del motor** acepta un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer torque del motor** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el motor de la garra a la posición de 40 grados con solo un par máximo del 20%. Esto permite que la garra agarre un objeto sin dañarlo con demasiada fuerza.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer velocidad del motor\n\nEstablece la velocidad de un motor inteligente V5.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Establecer velocidad del motor** acepta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\n**Establecer velocidad del motor** aceptará un valor de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los motores inteligentes V5 utilizados en la transmisión.\n\n* Cartridge Rojo: -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Cartridge Verde: -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Cartridge Azul: -600rpm a 600rpm\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de un motor inteligente V5 en un valor negativo hará que el motor gire en reversa.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de un motor inteligente V5 en 0 hará que el motor se detenga.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad se establece en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo configurará el motor del brazo para girar lentamente a una velocidad del 25% a la posición de 90 grados.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_pen_color":{"name":"set_pen_color","markdown":"# Establecer color de bolígrafo\n\nEstablece el color de las líneas dibujadas en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer color de bolígrafo** se usa para establecer el color de las líneas, los píxeles y el texto dibujado en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n**establecer color de bolígrafo** también se utilizará para establecer el color del contorno de los círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\nElige un color de bolígrafo.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_dropdown.png)  \n\nEl color del lápiz se usará para cualquier objeto futuro dibujado en la pantalla del cerebro V5."},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Establecer precisión de impresión\n\nEstablece el número de dígitos que aparecen después del punto decimal al imprimir bloques que reportan en la pantalla V5 Brain o Controller.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija el nivel de precisión que los bloques que reportan que se imprimirán en la pantalla.\n\n* Enteros (1) (Default)\n* Decimas (0.1)\n* Centésimas (0.01)\n* Milésimas (0.001)\n* Todos los Digitos (0.000001)\n\nLos bloques que reportan impresos en la pantalla se redondearán al nivel de precisión más cercano. Por ejemplo, 1.67 se imprimirá como 2 con precisión y 1.7 con precisión de décimas.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)\n\nElija qué dispositivo usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![print_precision_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_print_precision/print_precision_device.png)"},"set_shaft_encoder_position":{"name":"set_shaft_encoder_position","markdown":"# Establecer la posición del codificador del eje\n\nEstablece la posición del codificador de eje en el valor dado.\n\n![set_encoder_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer la posición del codificador del eje** se puede usar para establecer la posición del codificador de eje en cualquier valor dado.\n\nGeneralmente, el bloque **establecer la posición del codificador del eje** se utiliza para establecer la posición en 0, para restablecer la posición del codificador de eje.\n\nElija qué codificador de eje utilizar, luego establezca el valor deseado.\n\n![set_encoder_position_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_motor.png)\n\n"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer velocidad de giro\n\nEstablece la velocidad de los giros de la transmisión.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Establecer velocidad de giro** establecerá la velocidad del tren motriz, pero no hará que el tren motriz se mueva. Todavía se requiere un bloque **girar**.\n\n**Establecer velocidad de giro** acepta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\n**Establecer velocidad de giro** aceptará un valor de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los motores inteligentes V5 utilizados en la transmisión.\n\n*  Cartucho Rojo: -100rpm q 100rpm\n*  Cartucho Verde: -200rpm q 200rpm\n*  Cartucho Azul: -600rpm q 600rpm\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de giro de un tren motriz en un valor negativo hará que el tren motriz gire en la dirección opuesta.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de giro del tren motriz en 0 hará que el tren motriz se detenga.\n\nEl bloque **Establecer velocidad de giro** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\nEste ejemplo hará que el tren motriz gire lentamente, a una velocidad del 25%, hacia la izquierda.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Establecer variable\n\nEstablece una variable a un valor dado.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué variable usar. Las variables también se pueden renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nEl bloque **Establecer variable** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Establecer objeto de visión\n\nEstablece el elemento del objeto (objeto sobre el que desea obtener más información) fuera del número de objetos detectados.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **recuento de objetos** se puede usar antes del bloque **establecer objeto de visión** para determinar la cantidad de objetos detectados.\n\nElija qué sensor de visión usar.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer objeto de visión** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n\n"},"set_width":{"name":"set_width","markdown":"# Establecer ancho de bolígrafo\n\nEstablece el ancho del contorno de las formas dibujadas en la pantalla V5 Brain.\n\n![set_width_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_width/set_width_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer ancho** se utiliza para establecer el ancho de la línea en el exterior de los círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\nEl bloque **establecer ancho** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/es/set_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Longitud de la lista\n\nInforma el número de elementos en una lista.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/es/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué lista usar. La lista también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **longitud de la lista** encaja en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/es/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)\n"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# Foto\n\nToma una foto instantánea del sensor de visión.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **foto** capturará la imagen actual del Sensor de visión para procesarla y analizarla en busca de firmas y códigos de color. \n\nTípicamente, una **foto** se requiere primero antes de usar cualquier otro bloque del sensor de visión.\n\nSeleccione qué sensor de visión va usar.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nSeleccione qué firma de visión va usar. Las firmas de visión se configuran desde la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/v5/blocks/es/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Girar\n\nHace girar un motor inteligente V5 hasta que se detiene.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **girar** ejecuta para siempre, hasta que se use un nuevo bloque de motor o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija qué motor va usar.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nElija en qué dirección girar. Los nombres de dirección se pueden cambiar en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Girar por\n\nHace girar un motor inteligente V5 por una distancia determinada.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Girar por** le indicará a un Motor que avanze en una dirección determinada, a una distancia determinada, desde donde se encuentra actualmente.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nElija en qué dirección girar. Los nombres de dirección se pueden cambiar en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nEl bloque **girar por**  puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija la unidad de medida en grados o vueltas.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques **esperarán** hasta que el motor termine de moverse.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el motor se mueve.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)\n"},"spin_motor_controller":{"name":"spin_motor_controller","markdown":"# Controlador de motor de giro\n\nHace girar un motor 393 conectado a un controlador de motor 29 hasta que se detiene.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **girar** ejecutará un Motor 393 para siempre hasta que se use un nuevo bloque de motor o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija qué Motor 393 va usar.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_motor.png)\n\nElige en qué dirección girar. Los nombres de dirección se pueden cambiar en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_direction.png)"},"spin_servo":{"name":"spin_servo","markdown":"# Girar servo\n\nGira un servomotor a una posición establecida.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_servo/servo_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Girar servo** acepta un rango de posición de **0 a 180 grados**.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_servo/servo_port.png)\n\n"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Girar a la posición\n\nGira un motor inteligente V5 a una posición establecida.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Girar a la posición** le dirá a el motor que viaje a una posición específica. Basado en la posición actual del motor, **girar a la posición** determinará la dirección para girar.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque **girar a la posición** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\npuede elegir la unidad de medida en grados o vueltas.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques **esperar** hasta que el motor termine de moverse.\n\nPuedes seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el motor se mueve.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/es/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Dejar de conducir\n\nDetiene la transmisión.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dejar de conducir** hará que el tren motriz se detenga por completo y use la funcion **configurar parada de la unidad** para detenerse, frenar o mantener su posición.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo detendrá el tren motriz después de 3 segundos.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Parar motor\n\nPara el motor.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué motor va detener.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el motor de la garra durante 3 segundos antes de detenerse.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Restar\n\nResta un valor de otro e informa la diferencia.\n\n![subtract](static/help/v5/blocks/es/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Restar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque **sustraer** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares, y también aceptará bloques circulares en él.\n\nResta dos números.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/v5/blocks/es/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nRestar con valores de variables.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nRestar con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/es/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"temperature_of_motor":{"name":"temperature_of_motor","markdown":"# Temperatura del motor\n\nInforma la temperatura del motor inteligente V5.\n\n![temp_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nusando el bloque que reporta **temperatura del motor** puede ayudar a los usuarios a desarrollar lógica para evitar que sus motores inteligentes V5 se sobrecalienten durante el uso intensivo.\n\n**temperatura del motor** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**. \n\nElija qué motor inteligente V5 usar.\n\n![temp_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **temperatura del motor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![temp_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Valor del temporizador\n\nInforma el valor del temporizador del cerebro V5 en segundos.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nEl temporizador comienza a los 0 segundos cuando se inicia el programa e informa el valor del temporizador como un valor decimal.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **valor del temporizador** se usa dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n"},"torque_of_motor":{"name":"torque_of_motor","markdown":"# Torque del motor\n\nInforma la cantidad de torque (fuerza de rotación) que un motor inteligente V5 está utilizando actualmente.\n\n![motor_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/es/torque_of_motor/motor_torque.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Torque del motor** reporta un rango de **0.0 a 18.6 inch-pounds (InLB)** o **0.0 a 2.1 Newton-meters (Nm)**. \n\nElija el torque de motor inteligente V5 para informar.\n\n![motor_torque_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_device.png)\n\nElija si el **torque del motor** se informa en pulgadas-libras (InLb) o Newton-metros (Nm).\n\n![motor_torque_units](static/help/v5/blocks/es/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_units.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **torque del motor** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![motor_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_inserted.png)"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Girar\n\nGira la transmisión para siempre.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **girar** rotará el tren motriz para siempre, hasta que se use un nuevo bloque de tren motriz o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija la dirección en que se moverá el motriz.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Girar por\n\nGira el tren motriz para una distancia dada.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija en qué dirección girará el tren motriz.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\n\nEstablezca qué tan lejos se moverá el tren motriz ingresando una cantidad de grados.\n\nEl bloque **Manejar por** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques **esperar** hasta que el tren motriz termine de girar.\n\nPuedes seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el tren motriz gira.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Direccion de giro\n\nCambia la direccion del tren motriz a un rumbo específico, cuando se usa el sensor giroscopico.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Direccion de giro** puede usarse para girar el tren motriz a cualquier rumbo dado en sentido de las manecillas del rejo.\n\nBasado en el rumbo actual del giroscopio, **Direccion de giro** determinará en qué dirección girar.\n\n**Direccion de giro** acepta un range de **0.00 a 359.99** grados.\n\nEl bloque **Direccion de giro** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el tren motriz haga cuatro vueltas:\n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Izquierda a 45 degrees\n- Izquierda a 90 degrees\n- Izquierda a 270 degrees\n- Derecha a 180 degrees\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques **esperarán** hasta que el tren motriz termine de girar.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen ejecutándose mientras el tren motriz gira.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Dar vuelta a rotación\n\nDa vuelta al chasis a un ángulo de rotación específico utilizando el sensor Gyro de entrada.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a rotación** se puede utilizar para girar el Chasis a un valor positivo (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) o negativo (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj).\n\nSobre la base del valor **rotación** actual del chasis, **dar vuelta a rotación** determinará en qué dirección girar.\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a rotación** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis haga cuatro vueltas: \n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) a 90 grados\n- Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) a 180 grados\n- Izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) a -45 grados\n- Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) a 0 grados\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques  **esperarán** hasta que el Chasis termine de girar.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no espera** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el Chasis da vuelta.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/es/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)\n\n"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Variable\n\nInforma el valor numérico asignado a el variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Variable** se usan para informar un valor numérico almacenado dentro de el variable. Use el bloque **establecer variable** para establecer o actualizar el valor numérico de una variable.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **variable** se usa en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nLas variables se crean usando el botón **Hacer variable**.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Velocidad del motor\n\nInforma la velocidad actual de un motor inteligente V5.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Velocidad del motor** reporta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\n**Velocidad del motor** reporta un rango de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los motores inteligentes V5.\n\n* Cartucho Rojo: -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Cartucho Verde: -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Cartucho Azul: -600rpm a 600rpm\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad se informa en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **velocidad del motor** se usa en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"velocity_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"velocity_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Velocidad del codificador de eje\n\nInforma la velocidad actual de un codificador de eje.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Velocidad del codificador de eje** reporta un valor decimal en grados por segundo (dps) o rotaciones por minuto (rpm).\n\nElija qué codificador de eje usar.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_motor.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad se informa en grados por segundo (dps) o rotaciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_unit.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Objeto de visión\n\nInforma información sobre un objeto detectado desde el sensor de visión.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nPara usar el bloque **Objeto de visión**, siga los siguientes pasos:\n\n1. Configure su sensor de visión usando la ventana de Dispositivos.\n2. Use **foto** para capturar una imagen del sensor de visión y busque un código de firma / color.\n3. Use **objeto existe** para verificar si el sensor de visión detectó la firma / código de color solicitado.\n\nUna vez que el Sensor de visión detecta un objeto, puede usar otros bloques de Visión para obtener más información sobre el objeto detectado.\n\n* Use **establecer objeto de visión** para establecer sobre qué objeto detectado desea obtener más información. Por defecto, se utiliza el objeto detectado más grande.\n* Use **recuento de objetos** para determinar cuántos objetos se detectaron de ese código de firma / color solicitado.\n* Use **objeto de visión** para determinar qué información informar del objeto detectado.\n\nSeleccione qué sensor de visión usar.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nSeleccione qué valor informar desde el sensor de visión:\n\n* Ancho: Qué tan ancho es el objeto en píxeles. Devuelve un valor de **2 - 316 px**.\n* Altura: La altura del objeto en píxeles. Devuelve un valor de **2 - 212 px**.\n* CenterX: Reporta la coordenada X del centro del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 315 px**.\n* CentroY: Reporta la coordenada Y del centro del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 211 px**.\n* Ángulo: Reporta el ángulo del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 180 grados**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/es/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **objeto de visión** se usa en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Esperar\n\nEspera una cantidad de tiempo específica antes de pasar al siguiente bloque.\n\n![wait](static/help/v5/blocks/es/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija una cantidad de tiempo para **esperar**.\n\nEl bloque **espera** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Esperar hasta\n\nEspera a que un bloque booleano informe **verdadero** antes de pasar al siguiente bloque.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/v5/blocks/es/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Esperar hasta** verificara repetidamente un bloque booleano y no se moverá al siguiente bloque hasta que el bloque booleano reporte **verdadero**.\n\nThe bloque Booleano **esperar hasta** puede aceptar bloques de forma hexagonal (seis lados).\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n"},"when_autonomous":{"name":"when_autonomous","markdown":"# Cuando autonomo\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se recibe una señal de modo \"autónomo\" de un campo de competencia o interruptor de competencia.\n\n![when_autonomous](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_autonomous/when_autonomous.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nCualquier bloque conectado al evento **cuando autónomo** se ejecutará cuando el robot esté conectado a un campo de competencia o interruptor de competencia que esté configurado en el modo \"autónomo\".\n\nLos usuarios pueden tener hasta 50 bloques **cuando control autónomo** en un proyecto."},"when_brain_screen":{"name":"when_brain_screen","markdown":"# Cuando la pantalla del cerebro\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl event **cuando la pantalla del cerebro** se puede usar para crear acciones o comportamientos basados en la interacción táctil con la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\nUtilizado junto con el bloque que reporta **posición de la pantalla** los usuarios pueden crear interfaces personalizadas para su V5 Brain detectando cuándo y dónde se producen toques en la pantalla.\n\nSeleccione qué acción activará el evento: **presionado** o **liberado**\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed_condition.png)"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Cuando recibo\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques adjunta cuando el mensaje seleccionado se recibe de un mensaje **transmitir**.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué mensaje escuchar. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\nEl bloque **Cuando recibo** solo se activará para ejecutarse desde un **transmitir** o un bloque **transmitir y esperar** en una acumulación diferente"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Cuando bumper\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta el sensor del interruptor de parachoques seleccionado.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué interruptor bumper usar.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nSeleccione qué acción activará el evento: **presionado** o **liberado**\n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Cuando el eje del controlador\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se mueve el eje del joystick del controlador V5 seleccionado.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué controlador V5 usar.\n\n![when_controller_axis_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_device.png)\n\nElija qué controlador V5 usar.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Cuando el botón del controlador\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta el botón del controlador V5 seleccionado.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué controlador V5 usar.\n\n![when_controller_button_controller](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_controller.png)\n\nElija qué botón del controlador usar.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\nSeleccione qué acción activará el evento: **presionado** o **liberado**\n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)\n"},"when_driver":{"name":"when_driver","markdown":"# Cuando conductor\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se recibe una señal de modo \"control del conductor\" desde un campo de competencia o interruptor de competencia.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_driver/when_driver.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nCualquier bloque adjunto a el evento **cuando control del conductor** se ejecutará cuando el robot esté conectado a un campo de competencia o interruptor de competencia que esté configurado en el modo \"control del conductor\".\n\nUna repetition **por siempre** es muy recomendable para ser utilizada con un evento **cuando control del conductor**, para permitir que los comandos basados en el controlador V5 se actualicen con frecuencia durante la parte de control del conductor de un partido.\n\nUsuarios pueden tener hasta 50 bloques **cuando control del conductor** en un projecto."},"when_limit":{"name":"when_limit","markdown":"# Cuando limit\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta el sensor del interruptor de límite seleccionado.\n\n![when_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_limit/when_limit.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué interruptor de límite usar.\n\n![when_limit_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_limit/when_limit_select.png)\n\nSeleccione qué acción activará el evento: **presionado** o **liberado**\n\n![when_limit_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_limit/when_limit_condition.png)\n"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Cuando comenza\n\nEjecuta la acomulacion de bloques adjunta cuando se inicia el proyecto.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nUn evento **cuando comenza** se ejecutará cuando el proyecto se inicie desde el menú del cerebro V5 o desde el boton **ejecutar** en VEXcode V5 Blocks.\n\nTodos los proyectos nuevos incluirán automáticamente un bloque **cuando comenza**. Los proyectos pueden tener hasta 50 bloques **cuando comenza**.\n\n**Cuando comenza** también actuará como la acomulacion del modo \"pre-autónomo\" para un proyecto de competencia VRC.\n"},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Cuando temporizador\n\nEjecuta la acomulacion de bloques adjunta cuando el temporizador del cerebro V5 es mayor que el valor dado.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl temporizador del cerebro empieza al comienzo de cada proyecto.\n\nElige una cantidad de tiempo. El evento **cuando temporizador** se ejecutará una vez que el temporizador del cerebro sea **mas grande que** el monto ingresado.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nEl bloque **cuando temporizador** puede aceptar decimales o valores enteros.\n\nEl bloque **cuando temporizador** **no puede** Aceptar otros bloques que reportan.\n"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Mientras\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques dentro mientras se la condición booleana es **verdadero**.  \n\n![while](static/help/v5/blocks/es/while/while.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **mientras** solo verificará la condición booleana al comienzo de cada ciclo. \n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **verdadero**, el bloque dentro de **mientras** sera ejecutado.\n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **falso**, el bloque dentro de **mientras** sera omitido.\n\nEl 'C' bloque **mientras** puede aceptar bloques con forma hexagonal (seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es/while/while_inserted.png)"}},"python":{"control_break":{"name":"control_break","markdown":"# Romper\n\nSale de un bucle de repetición inmediatamente.\n\n```don\nbreak\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nCuando se añade dentro de un bucle, la orden de 'break' saldrá del bucle del que se está ejecutando actualmente. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo accionará el robot y comprobará si se ha pulsado su 'bumper'.\n\nSi el parachoques se **presiona**, la orden de 'break' saldrá del bucle while. El robot dejará de conducir hacia adelante.\n\n```don\nwhile True:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n    if bumper.pressing():\n        break\n```","signature":"break"},"control_for_loop":{"name":"control_for_loop","markdown":"# Por\n\nUn tipo de bucle que repite el código contenido en su cuerpo para un número determinado de iteraciones.\n\n```don\nfor value in range(10):\n    pass\n```\n\n# Cómo Utilizar\n\nPrimero, reemplace 'value' por una variable que se iterará a través de la función 'range()'.\n\nEn segundo lugar, sustituya '10' por un valor para especificar el final de la iteración.\n\nAgregue una sangría de cuatro espacios usando la barra espaciadora para incluir declaraciones como parte de la instrucción de control 'for'.\n\nUna declaración 'for' no debe contener un bloque de código vacío. Si es necesario, añada una declaración 'pass' a una declaración de for previamente vacía.\n\nObserve que los bucles for comienzan en el índice 0 en lugar de 1.\n\nLos bucles 'for' también pueden anidarse entre sí.\n\n# Ejemplo\nEl siguiente bucle for imprimirá los números 0 a 2:\n\n```don\nfor i in range(3):\n   brain.screen.print(i)\n   brain.screen.new_line()\n```\n   \nEsto imprimirá:\n\n```\n0\n1\n2\n```","signature":"for value in range (10"},"control_if_else_statement":{"name":"control_if_else_statement","markdown":"# Si/Si no\nUna instrucción de flujo de control que ejecuta un bloque de comandos si una condición se evalúa como true, u otro bloque de comandos si una condición se evalúa como false. \n\n```don\nif condition:\n    pass\nelse:\n    pass\n\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa instrucción 'if' es un condicional que comprobará si su condición se evalúa como **True** o **False**. Es posible combinar muchas condiciones con el uso de operadores lógicos como 'and', 'or' y 'not`. \n\nSi la totalidad de la condición es **True**, entonces el bloque de código indentado debajo de la 'condición if': se ejecutará. Si la totalidad de la condición es **False**, el bloque de código con sangría debajo de la instrucción 'else:' se ejecutará en su lugar.\n\nLos bloques de código por debajo de 'if' y 'else' deben sangrar cuatro espacios.\n\nUna declaración `if/else` no debe contener bloques de código vacíos. Si es necesario, añada las declaraciones 'pass' a una declaración 'if/else' vacía anteriormente. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEl codigo `if/else` Accionará el robot FORWARD si la variable es igual a 1. Si no, conducirá el robot REVERSE. \n\n```don\nif (my_variable == 1):\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nelse:\n    drivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"if conditio"},"control_if_statement":{"name":"control_if_statement","markdown":"# Si\n\nUna declaración de control utilizada para decidir si un bloque de código se ejecutará en función de la 'condition' proporcionada.\n\n```don\nif condition:\n    pass\n    \n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nReemplace la palabra 'condition' por una expresión que pueda evaluarse como 'True' o 'False`. Una evaluación de 'True' permitirá que las instrucciones indentadas debajo de la instrucción 'if' se ejecuten.\n\nAgregue una sangría de cuatro espacios usando la **barra espaciadora** para incluir declaraciones como parte de la declaración de control 'if'. \n\nUna declaración 'if' no debe contener un bloque de código vacío. Si es necesario, añadir una declaración 'pass' a una declaración 'if' previamente vacía. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEsta instrucción 'if' se ejecutará si 'my_variable' es igual a 1, haciendo que el robot conduzca hacia adelante.\n\n```don\nif (my_variable == 1):\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"if condition:\\n\\tpass"},"control_wait":{"name":"control_wait","markdown":"# Espera\n\nEspera una cantidad de tiempo específica antes de pasar al siguiente comando.\n\n```\nwait(TIME, UNITS)\n```\n\n## CÃ³mo Utilizar\n\nEstablezca una cantidad de tiempo en 'seconds' para que su programa **espere** antes de ejecutar comandos adicionales.\n\n```\nwait(10, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"wait(1, SECONDS)"},"control_wait_until":{"name":"control_wait_until","markdown":"# Mientras no\nInstrucción de control que continúa realizando bucles hasta que se convierte la expresión **true**.\n\n```don\nwhile not condition:\n    pass\n```\n\n## Cómo Uilizar\n\nCómo la declaración 'while not' comprobará repetidamente la condición, y no pasará al siguiente comando hasta que la condición indique **true**.\n\nSi la condición se evalúa como **false**, el código dentro de 'while not' se ejecutará.\n\nSi la condición se evalúa como **true**, el código dentro de 'while not' se omitirá, y el siguiente comando después de la instrucción 'while not' se ejecutará.\n\nLa declaración de 'while not' acepta cualquier expresión que se evalúe como 'True' o 'False' como su condición. Puede colocar booleanos, así como expresiones, utilizando operadores de comparación y lógicos. \n\nTambién puede utilizar valores numéricos; **0** evalúa a 'False`, Y cualquier **número distinto de cero** se evalúa como 'True`. \n\nAgregue una sangría de cuatro espacios usando la **barra espaciadora** para incluir declaraciones como parte de la declaración de control 'while not'. \n\nUna declaración de 'while not' no debe contener un bloque de código vacío. Si es necesario, añadir una declaración 'pasa' a una declaración 'while not' vacía. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste bucle 'while not' imprimirá \"Hello\" en líneas separadas hasta que el valor de mi variable sea igual a 5.\n\nmyVariable = 0\n\n```\nwhile not my_variable == 5:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\n    brain.screen.new_line()\n    my_variable += 1\n```","signature":"while not expressio"},"control_while_loop":{"name":"control_while_loop","markdown":"# Mientras\nBucle que repite el código en su cuerpo siempre que la expresión de condición se evalúe como **true**.   \n\n```don\nwhile condition:\n   pass\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bucle 'while' solo comprobará la condición dentro del paréntesis al principio de cada bucle. \n\nSi la condición se evalúa como **true**, el código dentro de 'while' se ejecutará.\n\nSi la condición se evalúa como **false**, el código dentro de 'while' se omitirá.\n\nEl bucle 'while' acepta todo lo que se evalúa como 'True' o 'False' como su condición. Puede colocar booleanos, así como expresiones, utilizando operadores de comparación y lógicos. \n\nTambién puede utilizar valores numéricos; *0** se evalúa como 'False', y cualquier **número distinto de cero** se evalúa como 'True'.\n\nAgregue una sangría de cuatro espacios usando la **barra espaciadora** para incluir declaraciones como parte de la declaración de control 'while'. \n\nUna instrucción 'while' no debe contener un bloque vacío de código. Si es necesario, agregue una instrucción 'pasa' a una instrucción 'while' previamente vacía. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste bucle 'while' seguirá imprimiendo la palabra \"Hello\" en líneas separadas cuando el valor del temporizador sea inferior a 50 segundos.\n\n```don\nwhile brain.timer.time(SECONDS) < 50:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\n    brain.screen.new_line()\n```","signature":"while expressio"},"drivetrain_drive":{"name":"drivetrain_drive","markdown":"# Conducir\n\nMueve el chasis por siempre en la dirección especificada dentro de los paréntesis. \n\nTodos los motores del chasis funcionan hacia adelante o hacia atrás a la velocidad establecida mediante el comando 'drivetrain.set_drive_velocity'. La velocidad predeterminada es 50%. \n\nLos valores negativos harán que el chasis conduzca hacia atrás con una entrada REVERSE y en hacia adelante con una entrada FORWARD.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'drivetrain.drive' ejecutará el chasis para siempre, hasta que se utilice un nuevo comando drivetrain, o el programa se detenga.\n\n## Ejemplos\n\nUtilice el argumento 'FORWARD' en las letras mayúsculas para mover el chasis hacia adelante.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nUtilice el argumento 'REVERSE' en las letras mayúsculas para mover la transmisión en sentido inverso.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.drive(FOWARD)"},"drivetrain_drive_for":{"name":"drivetrain_drive_for","markdown":"# Conducir Por\n\nMueve el chasis por una distancia determinada. Todos los motores del chasis funcionan hacia adelante o hacia atrás a la velocidad establecida por el comando 'drivetrain.set_drive_velocity'. Después de que el chasis haya movido la distancia de entrada, el chasis se detendrá.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(DIRECTION, DISTANCE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEstablezca la distancia a la que se moverá el chasis introduciendo al menos tres argumentos válidos dentro de los paréntesis, separados por comas. \n\nEl primer argumento especifica la dirección. Las entradas válidas son 'FORWARD' o 'REVERSE' en todas las letras mayúsculas.  \n\nEl segundo argumento especifica la distancia que debe conducir el V5 Robot.\n\nEl tercer argumento especifica la unidad de medida que debe usarse. Las entradas válidas son 'INCHES'(pulgadas) o 'MM' (milímetros) en letras mayúsculas.\n\nEl parámetro 'DISTANCE' acepta valores numéricos. Los valores negativos harán que el robot V5 conduzca en sentido contrario a la entrada 'DIRECTION'.\n\n```\ndrivetrain.drive_for(REVERSE, 5.0, INCHES)\n```\n\nEl comando \"drive_for\" es por defecto un comando de bloqueo. Evitará que se ejecuten comandos posteriores hasta que se haya completado el movimiento de chasis.\n\n## Parámetro opcional\n\nPuede establecer un cuarto parámetro en 'wait=False' para permitir que los comandos que se siguen se ejecuten incluso antes de que el chasis haya terminado de moverse.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM, wait=False)\n```\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo muestra el 'drivetrain.drive_for' que se utiliza con una variable como distancia.\n\nEl V5 Robot se conduce 200 MM hacia adelante.\n\n```don\ndistance_variable = 200\n\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, distance_variable, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 2, MM, wait=True)"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer Velocidad de Conducción\n\nEstablece la velocidad del chasis para los comandos 'drive' y 'drive_for'. La velocidad predeterminada es 50%. \n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` establecerá la velocidad del chasis cuando se utiliza con un comando 'drive' o 'drive_for'. No hará que el chasis se mueva cuando se utiliza por sí mismo.\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` acepta dos argumentos: un valor numérico de **-100  to 100**, y el argumento de la unidad 'PERCENT' escrito en letras mayúsculas. \n\nSi se establece la velocidad del chasis en un valor negativo, el chasis se encontrará en el lado opuesto de la 'DIRECTION' pasada a un comando 'Drive' o 'Drive_for'.\n\nSi se establece la velocidad del chasis en 0, se evitará que el chasis se mueva incluso si se utiliza un comando 'Drive' o 'Drive_for'.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo muestra que el chasis irá en reversa debido a un valor negativo.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nEste ejemplo evitará que el chasis se mueva.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(0, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_drive_velocity(50, PRECENT)"},"drivetrain_set_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_set_heading","markdown":"# Establecer Dirección del Chasis\n\nEstablece el Gyro del chasis en una dirección exacto.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_heading(HEADING, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'drivetrain.set_heading' se puede utilizar para establecer la posición de la chasis en cualquier dirección dado. Este comando se puede utilizar para restablecer la orientación del giroscopio del chasis cuando le dirección se establece en un valor de 0.\n\n`drivetrain.set_heading` acepta un valor numérico entre **0 y 360** ya que es el primer argumento, y 'DEGREES' escrito en letras mayúsculas como su segundo argumento.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo se establece el rumbo de la transmisión a 90 grados. \n\nDado que la dirección del V5 Robot se establece en 90 grados, el siguiente comando 'turn_to_heading' no hará que el robot gire ya que su encabezado actual ya se ha establecido en 90 grados.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_heading(90, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_set_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer Rotación\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del chasis con un sensor Gyro.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(ROTATION, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'drivetrain.set_rotation' se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del chasis a cualquier valor positivo o negativo dado.\n\nEl parámetro 'ROTATION' puede aceptar valores numéricos.\n\nEl parámetro 'ROTATION' **no** tiene un límite de 0-359 grados.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el robot un total de 210 grados:\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(120, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(45, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Turn right (clockwise) to rotation 120 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current position as rotation of -45 degrees.\n- Turn right (clockwise) an additional 90 degrees (-45 degrees to +45 degrees) based on the set rotation value from the previous command.","signature":"drivetrain.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_set_stopping":{"name":"drivetrain_set_stopping","markdown":"# Establecer Detención\n\n`drivetrain.set_stopping(MODE)` establece el comportamiento del robot cuando deja de moverse.  \n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nSustituya el parámetro 'MODE' por una de las siguientes opciones:\n\n* BRAKE (Freno): hará que el Motor se detenga inmediatamente.\n* COAST (Costa): deja que el Motor gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* HOLD (Detener): hará que el robot se detenga inmediatamente y lo devuelve a su posición de parada si se mueve. La parada del robot establecido surtirá efecto para todos los comandos futuros del robot para el resto del proyecto.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo muestra el robot conduciendo hacia adelante durante 200 MM antes de conducir por inercia hasta detenerse.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_stopping(COAST)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_stopping(BRAKE)"},"drivetrain_set_timeout":{"name":"drivetrain_set_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer Tiempo de Espera\n\n`drivetrain.set_timeout(VALUE, SECONDS)` establece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del robot.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando se utiliza para evitar que los comandos de movimiento que no alcanzan su posición impidan que otros comandos de procedimiento se ejecuten.\n\nEl comando puede aceptar valores numéricos o decimales.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo muestra un tiempo de espera que se utiliza para establecer el límite de tiempo para los movimientos de avance del chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_timeout(1, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 100, MM)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_timeout(1, SECONDS)"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity_percent":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity_percent","markdown":"# Establecer la Velocidad de Dar Vuelta\n\nEstablece la velocidad de veuletas del chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` establecerá la velocidad del chasis al girar, pero no hará que el chasis se mueva cuando se usa sin un comando de 'turn' o 'turn_for'.\n\n`drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` acepta un rango de **-100 a 100** como primer argumento. Toma las unidades, `PERCENT`, escrito en letras mayúsculas como el segundo argumento.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de vuelta del chasis en un valor negativo hará que el chasis gire en el opuesto de la dirección pasada en los siguientes comandos de giro.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de giro del chasis en 0 evitará que el chasis gire, incluso cuando se utiliza un comando 'turn' o 'turn_for'.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el chasis girará en la dirección opuesta debido a un valor negativo.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_turn_velocity(50, PERCENT)"},"drivetrain_stop":{"name":"drivetrain_stop","markdown":"# Parar\n\nPara el chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'drivetrain.stop()' detiene el chasis. No toma ningún argumento entre paréntesis.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo detendrá el chasis después de que el V5 Robot haya conducido hacia adelante durante 3 segundos.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"drivetrain.stop()"},"drivetrain_turn":{"name":"drivetrain_turn","markdown":"# Dar Vuelta\n\nHara que el chasis de vuelta a la derecha o a la izquierda.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando \"drivetrain.turn\" girará el Drivetrain en la dirección dada por siempre hasta que se utilice un nuevo comando drivetrain, o hasta que se detenga el programa.\n\nUtilice el argumento 'LEFT' en letras mayúsculas para girar el chasis a la izquierda.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(LEFT)\n```\n\nUtilice el argumento 'RIGHT' en letras mayúsculas para girar el chasis a la derecha.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn esta ejemplo, el robot avanzará 200 MM antes de girar a la derecha indefinidamente.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn(RIGHT)"},"drivetrain_turn_for":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_for","markdown":"# Dar Vuelta Por\n\nGira el chasis durante un número especificado de grados.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(DIRECTION, ANGLE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl primer argumento especifica la dirección de giro: 'LEFT' (izquierda) o 'RIGHT' (derecha), escrita en letras mayúsculas. \n\nEl segundo argumento especifica el ángulo de giro como un valor numérico; puede ser cualquier número entre 0 y 360. \n\nEl tercer argumento son las unidades de giro. Esto debe ser establecido como \"DEGREES\" en letras mayúsculas. \n\nEl comando 'turn_for' es de forma predeterminada un comando de bloqueo. Impide que se ejecute cualquier código hasta que el chasis haya completado su turno.\n\n## Parámetros Opcionales\n\nSi el cuarto argumento se establece en 'wait=False', comandos de procedimiento se les permitirá ejecutar incluso antes de que el chasis ha completado su turno.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(LEFT, 90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo girará el V5 Robot 270 grados a la derecha.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 270, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 90, DEGREES, wait=True)"},"drivetrain_turn_to_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Dar Vuelta a la Dirección\n\nGira el chasis a una dirección específica cuando se utilizan los sensores Gyro o Inertial.\n\n`drivetrain.turn_to_heading(HEADING, UNITS)`\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `drivetrain.turn_to_heading` se puede utilizar para girar el chasis a cualquier dirección dado en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\nBasado en la dirección actual del Giroscopio, `drivetrain.turn_to_heading` determinará la dirección a girar.\n\nEl parámetro `HEADING` acepta valores numéricos en el rango de **0.00 a 359.99**.\n\nEl parámetro `UNITS` (unidades) debe establecerse en `DEGREES`(grados).\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis haga cuatro vueltas: \n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(45.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(270.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(180.0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Left to 45 degrees (Izquierda a 45 grados)\n- Left to 90 degrees (Izquierda a 90 grados)\n- Left to 270 degrees (Derecha a 270 grados)\n- Right to 180 degrees (Derecha a 180 grados)\n\nEl comando `turn_to_heading` por defecto bloqueará los comandos de procedimiento hasta que el giro del chasis se haya completado.\n\n## Parámetros Optionales\n\nPuede establecer `wait=False` como tercer parámetro para prevenir el comando `turn_to_heading` de bloquear los comandos de procedimiento de ejecución hasta que el giro del chasis se haya completado.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(180.0, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Dar vuelta a la Rotación\n\nGira el chasis a un ángulo de rotación específico.\n\n`drivetrain.turn_to_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)`\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `drivetrain.turn_to_rotation` se puede utilizar para girar el chasis a un valor positivo (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) o negativo (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj).\n\nBasado en la rotación actual del chasis, `drivetrain.turn_to_rotation` determinará la dirección a girar.\n\nEl parámetro `ROTATION` puede aceptar valores numéricos.\n\nLos valores numéricos **no** son limitados al rango de **0 - 359.99** grados. Los giros serán absolutos y pueden hacer que el robot gire más de una vez si es necesario.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis haga cuatro vueltas:\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(180, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Right (Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj)) a 90 grados\n- Right(Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj)) a 180 grados\n- Left (Izquierda (en sentido opuesto al de las agujas del reloj)) a -45 grados\n- Right (Derecha(en el sentido de las agujas del reloj)) a 0 grados\n\nEl comando `drivetrain.turn_to_rotation` por defecto bloqueará los comandos de procedimiento hasta que el giro del chasis se haya completado.\n\n## Parámetro opcional\n\nPuede establecer un tercer parámetro  `wait=False` para evitar el comando `turn_to_rotation' de bloquear los comandos de procedimiento hasta que se complete el giro del chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(180.0, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90, DEGREES, wait=True)"},"function_name":{"name":"function_name","markdown":"# Función\n\nLas funciones son bloques de código que se utilizan para realizar una acción.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una función, cree un nombre de función significativo. Esto significa que el nombre de la función debe describir con precisión lo que hace.\n\nUtilice la **palabra clave** `def` antes del nombre de la función para definir la función.\n\nIncluya paréntesis `()` y encierra parámetros opcionales después del nombre de la función, seguido por un colon`:`. Múltiples parámetros deben estar separados por comas `(parameter1, parameter2)`.\n\nEl cuerpo de la función debe sangrar cuatro espacios. Si no hay ningún código para que la función se ejecute, un `pass` debe incluirse en la definición de la función.\n\n```don\ndef my_function():\n    pass\n```\n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nEsta función no tiene parámetros e imprimirá \"Hello\" en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\ndef print_hello_world():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello World\")\n```\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEsta función toma un parámetro, `name` e imprimirá el valor de `name` en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\ndef print_name(name):\n    brain.screen.print(name)\n```","signature":"def function_name(parameters):\\n\\tpass"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Borrar Fila\n\nBorra una sola fila en la pantalla del V5 Brain o Controller.\n\n```don \nbrain.screen.clear_line()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nBorra la fila actual en la pantalla V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.clear_line()\n```\n\nBorra una fila especificada en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.clear_line(ROW)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.clear_line()` puede aceptar valores enteros entre **1 - 20**, para establecer qué fila se va a borrar. También se puede llamar al comando sin ningún argumento para borrar la fila actual.\n\n---\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.clear_line()"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Borrar Todas las Filas\n \nBorra toda la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`brain.screen.clear_screen()` no cambiará el cursor de la pantalla. Tendrá que utilizar el comando `brain.screen.set_cursor()` para ajustar el cursor de la pantalla a una posición específica.","signature":"brain.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle","markdown":"# Dibujar Círculo\n\nDibuja un círculo en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_circle(X, Y, RADIUS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.draw_circle()` requiere 3 valores:\n\n* Value 1: Center Point X\n* Value 2: Center Point Y\n* Value 3: Radius of Circle (in pixels) (Radio de círculo (en pixels))\n\nEl color de la línea exterior del círculo se determina por el comando `brain.screen.set_pen_color()`. El color de línea predeterminado es blanco.\n\nEl color color de relleno interior del círculo se determina por el comando `brain.screen.set_fill_color()`. El color de relleno predeterminado es negro.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_brain_screen_draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_circle(1, 1, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_line","markdown":"# Dibujar Línea\n\nDibuja una línea en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_line(START_X, START_Y, END_X, END_Y)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.draw_line()` requiere 4 valores:\n\n* Value 1: Beginning X coordinate\n* Value 2: Beginning Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Ending X coordinate\n* Value 4: Ending Y coordinate\n\nEl color de la línea viene determinado por el comando `brain.screen.set_pen_color()`. El color de línea predeterminado es blanco.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_brain_screen_draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_line(1, 1, 10, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel","markdown":"# Dibujar Píxel\n\nDibuja un píxel en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_pixel(X, Y)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.draw_pixel` requiere 2 valores:\n\n* Value 1: X Coodinate\n* Value 2: Y Coodinate\n\nEl color del píxel viene determinado por el comando `brain.screen.set_pen_color()`. El color de píxel predeterminado es blanco.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_pixel(1, 1)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Dibujar Rectángulo\n\nDibuja un rectángulo en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_rectangle(X, Y, WIDTH, HEIGHT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.draw_rectangle()` requiere 4 valores:\n\n* Value 1: Top Left Corner X coordinate (Coordenada X de la esquina superior izquierda)\n* Value 2: Top Left Corner Y coordinate (Coordenada Y de la esquina superior izquierda)\n* Value 3: Width of the rectangle (Ancho del rectángulo)\n* Value 4: Height of the rectangle (Altura del rectángulo)\n\nEl color de la línea de borde del rectángulo viene determinado por el comando `brain.screen.set_pen_color()`. El color de línea predeterminado es blanco.\n\nEl color de relleno interior del rectángulo se determina mediante el comando `brain.screen.set_fill_color()`. El color de relleno predeterminado es negro.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_rectangle(1, 1, 10, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Siguiente fila\n\nEstablece el cursor de salida de impresión en la pantalla del V5 Brain a la siguiente fila disponible.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.new_line()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPor defecto, todos los proyectos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1 columna 1. El comando `brain.screen.new_line()` moverá el cursor hacia abajo una sola fila en la pantalla. `brain.screen.new_line()` también establecerá la columna del cursor en la posición 1.\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Brain permita cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Brain - Número de Filas:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 Filas (Por Defecto)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Filas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_brain_screen_new_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.new_line()"},"looks_brain_screen_print":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print","markdown":"# Imprimir\n\nImprime valores o texto en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.print(\"Hello World\")\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.print()` imprimirá datos en una ubicación del cursor en la pantalla.\n\nTodos los nuevos proyectos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1 columna 1.\n\n\n* Print words and numbers: \n\t`brain.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n* Print the reported value from a variable: \n\t`brain.screen.print(my_variable)`\n* Print the reported value from a sensor or device:  \n        `brain.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`","signature":"brain.screen.print(\"Hello World\")"},"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Establecer Cursor\n\n\nEstablece la ubicación del cursor en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_cursor(ROW, COLUMN)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.set_cursor()` requiere 2 valores:\n\n* Value 1: Screen row position (Posición de la fila de la pantalla)\n* Value 2: Screen column position (Posición de la columna de la pantalla)\n\nEstablezca la posición de fila y columna del cursor para que se muestre un comando `brain.screen.print()` en una ubicación específica de la pantalla.\n\nAcepta un rango para **fila** de **1 a 20**.\n\nAcepta un rango para **columna** de **1 a 80**.\n\n---\n\nEl cerebro V5 le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará al número de filas y columnas disponibles en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n**V5 Brain Tamaño De Fuente - Número de Filas:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Rows (Filas)\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Rows (Filas)\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 Rows (Default) (Filas - Por Defecto)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Rows (Filas)\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Rows (Filas)\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Rows (Filas)\n\n**V5 Brain Tamaño De Fuente - Número de Columnas:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 80 Columns (Columnas)\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 68 Columns (Columnas)\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 48 Columns (Default) (Columnas - Por Defecto)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 32 Columns (Columnas)\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 24 Columns (Columnas)\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.MONO60` - 16 Columns (Columnas)\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color","markdown":"# Establecer Color de Relleno\n\nEstablece el color que rellena las formas dibujadas en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_fill_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.set_fill_color()` se utiliza para establecer el color del interior de círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del V5 Brain. \n\nReemplace el parámetro `COLOR` por una de las siguientes acciones:\n\n* `Color.BLACK` (Negro)\n* `Color.WHITE` (Blanco)\n* `Color.RED` (Rojo)\n* `Color.GREEN` (Verde)\n* `Color.BLUE` (Azul)\n* `Color.YELLOW` (Amarillo)\n* `Color.ORANGE` (Naranja)\n* `Color.PURPLE` (Morado)\n* `Color.CYAN` (Cian)\n* `Color.TRANSPARENT` (Transparente)\n\nEl color de relleno se utilizará para los objetos posteriores dibujados en la pantalla del V5 Brain hasta que se cambie de nuevo.","signature":"brain.screen.set_fill_color(Color.RED)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_font":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_font","markdown":"# Establecer Fuente\n\nEstablece el estilo y el tamaño de la fuente utilizada en la pantalla del V5 Brain al imprimir valores.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_font(FONT_TYPE)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nHay dos tipos de fuentes disponibles en la pantalla del V5 Brain:\n\n* Monospaced (MONO) - cada carácter ocupa el mismo ancho.\n* Proportional (PROP) - cada carácter ocupa diferentes anchos de tamaño en función del carácter.\n\nElija el tipo de fuente y el tamaño que desea utilizar reemplazando el parámetro `FONT_TYPE` . Puede seleccionar entre las siguientes opciones de fuente.\n\n* `FontType.MONO12`\n* `FontType.MONO15`\n* `FontType.MONO20`\n* `FontType.MONO30`\n* `FontType.MONO40`\n* `FontType.MONO60`\n* `FontType.PROP20`\n* `FontType.PROP30`\n* `FontType.PROP40`\n* `FontType.PROP60`\n\nEl nuevo tamaño de fuente se utilizará para cualquier texto futuro escrito en la pantalla del V5 Brain hasta que se cambie de nuevo.","signature":"brain.screen.set_font(FontType.MONO20)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color","markdown":"# Establecer el Color de la Pluma\n\nEstablece el color de las líneas dibujadas en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_pen_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.set_pen_color()` se utiliza para establecer el color de las líneas, píxeles y texto dibujado en la pantalla del V5 Brain. \n\n`brain.screen.set_pen_color()` también se puede utilizar para establecer el color del contorno de los círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\nReemplace el parámetro `COLOR` por una de las siguientes opciones:\n\n* `Color.BLACK` (Negro)\n* `Color.WHITE` (Blanco)\n* `Color.RED` (Rojo)\n* `Color.GREEN` (Verde)\n* `Color.BLUE` (Azul)\n* `Color.YELLOW` (Amarillo)\n* `Color.ORANGE` (Naranja)\n* `Color.PURPLE` (Morado)\n* `Color.CYAN` (Cian)\n\nEl color de la pluma se utilizará para cualquier objeto posterior dibujado en la pantalla del V5 Brain hasta que se cambie de nuevo.","signature":"brain.screen.set_pen_color(Color.RED)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width","markdown":"# Establecer la Anchura de la Pluma\n\nEstablece el ancho del contorno de las formas dibujadas en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_pen_width(PEN_WIDTH)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.set_pen_width()` se utiliza para establecer el ancho de la línea en el exterior de círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del V5 Brain. \n\nEl comando `brain.screen.set_pen_width()` puede aceptar valores enteros, con un valor mayor que equivale a un ancho mayor. Reemplace el parámetro `PEN_WIDTH` por un valor entero.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.set_pen_width(10)"},"looks_controller_rumble":{"name":"looks_controller_rumble","markdown":"# Vibración del Controller\n\nActiva un efecto de vibración en el V5 Controller.\n\n```python\ncontroller.rumble(\".-.-\")\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `controller.rumble(\".-.-\")` utiliza el motor de vibración en su V5 Controller para proporcionar retroalimentación.\n\nPuede crear cualquier patrón que desee utilizando una combinación de caracteres \".\" y \"-\" de la cadena. El caractere \".\" creará una vibración corto. El caractere \"-\" creará una larga vibración.","signature":"controller.rumble(\"-.-.\")"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Borrar Fila\n\nBorra la fila actual en la pantalla del V5 Controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_line()\n```\n\nBorra una fila especificada en la pantalla del V5 Contoller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_line(ROW)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `controller.screen.clear_line()` puede aceptar valores enteros entre **1 - 3**, para establecer qué fila se va a borrar. También puede llamar al comando sin argumentos para borrar la fila actual.\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Controller no permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_controller_screen_clear_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.clear_line()"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Borrar Todas las Filas\n\nBorra toda la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`controller.screen.clear_screen()` no cambiará el cursor de la pantalla. \n\nUtilice el comando `controller.screen.set_cursor()` para establecer el cursor de la pantalla en una posición específica.","signature":"controller.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_controller_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Siguiente Fila\n\nEstablece el cursor de salida de impresión en la pantalla del controlador V5 en la siguiente fila disponible.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.new_line()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nDe forma predeterminada, todos los proyectos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1, columna 1. El comando `controller.screen.new_line()` moverá el cursor hacia abajo por una sola fila en la pantalla. `controller.screen.new_line()` también establecerá la columna del cursor en la posición 1.\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Controller no permita cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Brain - Número de filas:**\n\n* Standard Font (Fuente Estándar) - 3 Filas (por defecto) \n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Controller - Número de columnas:**\n\n* Standard Font (Fuente Estándar) - 20 Columnas (por defecto)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_controller_screen_new_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.new_line()"},"looks_controller_screen_print":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_print","markdown":"# Imprimir\n\nImprime valores en la pantalla del V5 Controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.print(\"Hello World\") \n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `controller.screen.print()` imprimirá los datos en la posición del cursor en la pantalla.\n\nTodos los nuevos proyectos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1, columna 1.\n\n\n* Imprimir palabras y números: \n\t`controller.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n* Imprimir el valor informado de una variable:  \n\t`controller.screen.print(my_variable)`\n* Imprime el valor notificado desde un sensor o dispositivo: \n        `controller.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`","signature":"controller.screen.print(\"Hello World\")"},"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Establecer cursor\n\n\nEstablece la ubicación del cursor para el comando **controller.screen.print()** en la pantalla del V5 Controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.set_cursor(ROW, COLUMN)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `controller.screen.set_cursor()` requiere 2 valores:\n\n* Valor 1: Posición de la fila de la pantalla \n* Valor 2: Posición de la columna de pantalla\n\n\nEstablezca la posición de fila y columna del cursor para que se muestre un comando `controller.screen.print()` en una ubicación específica de la pantalla.\n\n`controller.screen.set_cursor()` acepta un rango para **fila** de **1 a 3**.\n\n`controller.screen.set_cursor()` acepta un rango para **columna** de **1 a 20**.\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Brain no permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de Fuente del V5 Controller - Número de Filas:**\n\n* Fuente Estándar - 3 Filas (per defecto)\n\n**Tamaño de Fuente del V5 Controller - Número de Columnas:**\n\n* Fuente Estándar - 20 Columnas (por defecto)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es/looks_controller_screen_set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)"},"looks_led_set":{"name":"looks_led_set","markdown":"# LED Encendido/apagado\n\nEnciende o apaga un LED.\n\n```don\nled.on()\n```\n```don\nled.off()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`led.on()` enciende el dispositivo LED.\n\n`led.off()` apaga el dispositivo LED.","signature":"led.set(False)"},"motion_motor393_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor393_set_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer la Velocidad del Controlador del Motor\n\nEstablece la velocidad de un Motor 393 conectado a un Controlador de Motor 29.\n\n```don \nmotor393.set_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl parámetro 'VELOCITY' (Velocidad) acepta un rango de -100% a 100%.\n\nSi se establece la velocidad de un Motor 393 en un valor negativo hará que el Motor 393 gire en reversa.\n\nLa secuencia siguiente hará que el Motor 393 gire en sentido inverso, aunque se pase el parámetro 'FORWARD' (Adelante).\n\n```don\nmotor393.set_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\nmotor393.spin(FORWARD)\n```\n\nAjustar la velocidad de un Motor 393 a 0 evitará que el Motor gire.","signature":"motor393.set_velocity(10, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor393_spin":{"name":"motion_motor393_spin","markdown":"# Girar Controlador de Motor\n\nGira un Motor 393 conectado a un controlador de motor 29.\n\n```don \nmotor393.spin(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste comando gira un Motor 393 para siempre, hasta que se utiliza un nuevo comando de motor o el programa se detiene.\n\nElija a qué dirección girará el motor estableciendo el parámetro 'DIRECTION'(Dirección) en **FORWARD** (Adelante) o **REVERSE** (Hacia Atrás).","signature":"motor393.spin(FORWARD)"},"motion_motor_set_max_torque":{"name":"motion_motor_set_max_torque","markdown":"# Ajuste de la Par del Motor\n\nEstablece el par del V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.set_max_torque(AMOUNT, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste comando acepta un rango de 0% a 100%.\n\nEl comando \"set motor torque\" puede aceptar decimales, enteros o valores numéricos\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo girará el motor de garra a la posición de 40 grados con sólo un 20% de par máximo. Esto permite que la garra agarre un objeto sin dañarlo con demasiada fuerza.\n\n```don\nclaw_motor.set_max_torque(20, PERCENT)\nclaw_motor.set_position(40, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_max_torque(50, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor_set_position":{"name":"motion_motor_set_position","markdown":"# Establecer la Posición del Motor\n\nEstablece la posición del codificador del V5 Smart Motor al valor dado.\n\n```don\nmotor.set_position(VALUE, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste comando se puede utilizar para establecer la posición del motor a cualquier valor dado.\n\nNormalmente, el comando posición del motor se utiliza para establecer la posición en 0 para restablecer la posición del codificador del motor.","signature":"motor.set_position(0, DEGREES)"},"motion_motor_set_stopping":{"name":"motion_motor_set_stopping","markdown":"# Establecer Parada del Motor\n\nEstablece el comportamiento de frenado del V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.set_stopping(MODE)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl parámetro `MODE` se puede sustituir por cualquiera de las siguientes opciones:\n\n* BRAKE (Frenar): hará que el motor se detenga inmediatamente.\n* COAST (Deslizarse): deja que el motor gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* HOLD (Detener): will cause the Motor to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved.\n\nEl comportamiento de detención establecido por este comando se aplicará a los comandos de motor subsiguientes para la totalidad del proyecto, a menos que se cambie de otra manera.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el Motor de brazo gire hacia adelante durante 90 grados (para levantar el brazo) y luego mantendrá su posición.\n\n```don\narm_motor.set_stopping(HOLD)\narm_motor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_stopping(BRAKE)"},"motion_motor_set_timeout":{"name":"motion_motor_set_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer Tiempo de Espera del Motor\n\nEstablece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don \nmotor.set_timeout(AMOUNT, SECONDS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl límite de tiempo del motor se utiliza para evitar que los comandos de movimiento que no alcanzan su posición impidan que los comandos subsiguientes se ejecuten. \n\nUn ejemplo de que un motor no alcanza su posición es un brazo o una garra que alcanza su límite mecánico y no puede completar su movimiento.\n\nEl comando `set_motor_timeout` puede aceptar decimales, enteros o valores numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo finalizará el comando SET motor después de 2 segundos si el motor de claw no ha alcanzado la posición de 270 grados. Una vez alcanzado el límite de tiempo o el objetivo, el motor de claw girará a la posición 0 grados.\n\n```don\nclaw_motor.set_timeout(2, SECONDS)\nclaw_motor.spin_to_position(270, DEGREES)\nclaw_motor.spin_to_position(0, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_timeout(1, SECONDS)"},"motion_motor_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer la Velocidad del Motor\n\nEstablece la velocidad de un V5 Smart Motor.\n\n\n```don \nmotor.set_velocity(VELOCITY, UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste comando acepta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm.**\n\nEl valor 'UNIT' (Unidad) aceptable es: `PERCENT` (Por Ciento) or `RPM` (Rotación por Minuto) .\n\n**Ajuste la velocidad del motor** aceptará un valor de \"rotaciones por minuto\" (RPM) basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los V5 Smart Motor.\n\n* Red Cartridge (Cartucho de Engranaje Rojo): -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge (Cartucho de Engranaje Verde): -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge (Cartucho de Engranaje Azul): -600rpm a 600rpm\n\nSi se establece la velocidad de un V5 Smart Motor en un valor negativo, el motor girará en sentido inverso.\n\nSi se establece la velocidad de un V5 Smart Motor en 0, se evitará que el motor gire.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá que el Motor de brazo gire a una velocidad del 25% a la posición de 90 grados.\n\n```don\narm_motor.set_velocity(25, PERCENT)\narm_motor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_velocity(50, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor_spin":{"name":"motion_motor_spin","markdown":"# Girar\n\nEste comando hace girar un V5 Smart Motor por siempre, hasta que se utilice un nuevo comando del motor o se detenga el programa.\n\n```don\nmotor.spin(FORWARD)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la dirección en la que el motor girará hacia **FORWARD** (ADELANTE) o **REVERSE** (HACIA ATRÁS).\n\n```don\nmotor.spin(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"motor.spin(FORWARD)"},"motion_motor_spin_for":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_for","markdown":"# Girar Por\n \nEste comando hace girar un V5 Smart Motor durante una cantidad determinada de grados o giros.\n\n```don\nmotor.spin_for(DIRECTION, AMOUNT, UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija a qué 'DIRECTION' (Dirección) girará el motor: **FORWARD** (Adelante) o **REVERSE** (Hacia Atras).\n\nElija la 'UNIT' (UNIDAD) de medida para que sea **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS** (Vueltas).\n\nElija si este comando debe ser esperado o no, siguiendo los comandos estableciendo un cuarto parámetro opcional en **wait=True** (espera) o **wait=False** (no espera). \n\n```don\nmotor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\nEste comando es un comando de bloqueo a menos que **wait-False** (no espera) se pase como el cuarto parámetro.","signature":"motor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES)"},"motion_motor_spin_to_position":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_to_position","markdown":"# Girar a la Posición\n\nEstablece la posición del codificador del V5 Smart Motor en la cantidad dada.\n\n```don \nmotor.spin_to_position(AMOUNT, UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste mando le indicará al motor que se desplace a una posición específica. Basado en la posición actual del Motor, `spin_to_position` determinará la dirección de rotación.\n\nElija la unidad de medida para que sea **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS** (Vueltas).\n\nElija si este comando debe ser esperado o no por otros comandos, cambiando el tercer parámetro opcional a **wait=True** (espera) o **wait=False** (no espera).\n\n```don\nmotor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\nEstablecer **wait=True** (espera) significa que los comandos de procedimiento no se ejecutarán hasta que se complete el giro del motor. En cambio, **wait=False** (no espera) no esperará a que se complete.  \n\nPor defecto, este comando tendrá la espera que se establecerá en **True**.","signature":"motor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES)"},"motion_motor_stop":{"name":"motion_motor_stop","markdown":"# Detener el motor\n\nDetiene el motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.stop()\n```\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo muestra un motor girando durante 3 segundos antes de detenerse.\n\n```don\nmotor.spin(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\nmotor.stop()\n```","signature":"motor.stop()"},"motion_servo_set_position":{"name":"motion_servo_set_position","markdown":"# Girar Servo\n\nGira un Motor Servo a una posición establecida.\n\n```don \nservo.set_position(POSITION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nGira un Motor Servo al valor 'POSITION' (Posición) dado.\n\n## Ejemplo\nEl siguiente ejemplo gira el Motor Servo a 90 grados.\n\n```don\nservo.set_position(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"servo.set_position(50, DEGREES)"},"sensing_accel_two_g.acceleration":{"name":"sensing_accel_two_g.acceleration","markdown":"# Aceleración del Acelerómetro Analógico\n\nReporta del valor de aceleración de un eje en el Acelerómetro Analógico.\n\n```don\naccel_2g.acceleration()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste comando informa de un rango de **-2.0 G a 2.0 G** o **-6.0 G a 6.0 G** dependiendo de la configuración del puente en el Acelerómetro Analógico.","signature":"accel_2g.acceleration()"},"sensing_brain_battery_capacity":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_capacity","markdown":"# Capacidad de la Batería\n\n\nReporta del nivel de carga de la batería del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.capacity()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa capacidad de la batería reporta un rango de **0%** a **100%.**","signature":"brain.battery.capacity()"},"sensing_brain_battery_current":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_current","markdown":"# Corriente de la Batería\n\nReporta de la corriente de la batería del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa corriente de la batería indica un rango de **0.0 amperios** a **20.0 amperios**.","signature":"brain.battery.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_brain_battery_voltage":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_voltage","markdown":"# Voltaje de la Batería\n\nInforma del voltaje de la batería del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.voltage(VOLT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nEl voltaje de la batería indica un rango de **10.0 voltios** a **14.4 voltios**.","signature":"brain.battery.voltage(VoltageUnits.VOLT)"},"sensing_brain_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_column","markdown":"# Columna del Cursor\n\nInforma del valor de columna de la ubicación del cursor de pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.column()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa columna de pantalla informa de un rango de **1 a 80**.\n\nEl V5 Brain permita cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará al número de columnas disponibles en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Brain- Número de columnas:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 80 Columnas\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 68 Columnas\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 48 Columnas (por defecto)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 32 Columnas\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 24 Columnas\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.MONO60` - 16 Columnas","signature":"brain.screen.column()"},"sensing_brain_screen_pressing":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_pressing","markdown":"# Pantalla Presionado\n \nReporta si la pantalla táctil del V5 Brain está siendo presionada.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.pressing()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`brain.screen.pressing` reporta **True** si la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5 está siendo presionada.\n\n`brain.screen.pressing` reporta **False** si la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5 no está siendo presionada.","signature":"brain.screen.pressing()"},"sensing_brain_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_row","markdown":"# Fila del Cursor\n \nReporta del valor de fila de la ubicación del cursor de pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.row()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa fila de pantalla informa de un rango de **1 a 20**.\n\nEl V5 Brain permita cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará al número de filas disponibles en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Brain - Número de filas:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 Filas (por defecto)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Filas","signature":"brain.screen.row()"},"sensing_brain_timer_clear":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_clear","markdown":"# Restablecer Temporizador\nRestablece el temporizador del V5 Brain.\n\n```don \nbrain.timer.clear()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl temporizador del V5 Brain comienza al principio de cada proyecto. El comando CLEAR TIMER restablece el valor del temporizador a 0 segundos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el temporizador se reiniciará antes de mover el Chasis hacia adelante durante 3 segundos. Después de 3 segundos, el Chasis se detendrá.\n\n```don\nbrain.timer.clear()\nwhile not brain.timer.time(SECONDS) > 3:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"brain.timer.clear()"},"sensing_brain_timer_time":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_time","markdown":"# Valor del Temporizador\n\nReporta del valor del temporizador del V5 Brain en segundos.\n\n```don \nbrain.timer.time(SECONDS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nEl temporizador comienza a 0 segundos cuando se inicia el programa e informa del valor del temporizador como un valor decimal.","signature":"brain.timer.time(SECONDS)"},"sensing_bumper_pressing":{"name":"sensing_bumper_pressing","markdown":"# Presionando Parachoques\n \nReporta si el interruptor de parachoques se está presionando actualmente.\n\n```don\nbumper.pressing()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPresionando Parachques resultará en un valor **True**, si se esta presionado el parachoque.\n\nPresionando Parachques resultará en un valor **False**, si no se esta presionado el parachoque.","signature":"bumper.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_axis_position":{"name":"sensing_controller_axis_position","markdown":"# Posición del Controller\n \nReporta la posición de un joystick en el V5 Controller a lo largo de un eje.\n\n```don\ncontroller.axis1.position()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`controller.axis1.position` reporta de un rango entre **-100 a 100**.\n\n`controller.axis1.position` informará cero (0) cuando un eje de joystick esté centrado.\n\nElija qué eje del controlador debe informar.\n\n* axis1 (eje 1) - Joystick derecho (izquierda y derecha)\n* axis2 (eje 2)- Joystick derecho (arriba y abajo)\n* axis3 (eje 3)- Joystick izquierdo (arriba y abajo)\n* axis4 (eje 4)- Joystick izquierdo (izquierda y derecha)","signature":"controller.axis1.position()"},"sensing_controller_button_up_pressing":{"name":"sensing_controller_button_up_pressing","markdown":"# Presionando Controller\n \nReporta si esta presionado un botón del V5 Controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.buttonUp.pressing()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPresionando Controller reporta **True** si se está presionando el botón del controlador seleccionado.\n\nPresionando Controller reporta **False** si no se está presionando el botón del controlador seleccionado.\n\nElija el botón controlador que se va a detectar para una prensa:\n\n* `buttonUp`(arriba)\n* `buttonDown` (abajo)\n* `buttonLeft` (izquierda)\n* `buttonRight` (derecho)\n* `buttonX`\n* `buttonY`\n* `buttonA`\n* `buttonB`\n* `buttonL1`\n* `buttonL2`\n* `buttonR1`\n* `buttonR2`","signature":"controller.buttonUp.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_column","markdown":"# Columna del Cursor\n \nReporta el número de columna de la ubicación del cursor de la pantalla del controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.column()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa fila del cursor reporta un rango de **1 a 80**.\n\nEl V5 Controller no permita cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Controller - Número de Columnas:**\n\n* Fuente Estándar - 20 Columnas (por defecto)","signature":"controller.screen.column()"},"sensing_controller_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_row","markdown":"# Fila del Cursor\n\nReporta del número de fila de la ubicación del cursor de la pantalla del Controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.row()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nFila del Cursor reporta un rango de **1 a 20**.\n\nEl V5 Controller no permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de Fuente del V5 Controller- Número de Filas:**\n\n* Fuente Estándar - 3 Filas (por defecto)","signature":"controller.screen.row()"},"sensing_drivetrain_current":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_current","markdown":"# Corriente del Chasis\n\nInforma de la cantidad de corriente (potencia) que la transmisión está utilizando actualmente.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa corriente de conducción indica un rango de **0.0 a 2.5 amperios**.","signature":"drivetrain.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency","markdown":"# Eficiencia de la Conducción\n \nReporta de la eficiencia del Chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.efficiency(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nRficiencia de la Unidad informa del valor de la potencia (en vatios) que utiliza el motor (entrada), frente a la cantidad de potencia (en vatios) que proporciona el motor (salida).\n\nUna V5 Chasis normalmente alcanza una eficiencia máxima de **65%** en casos de uso normales.\n\nEficiencia de conducción indica un rango de **0% a 100%**","signature":"drivetrain.efficiency(PERCENT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_heading":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_heading","markdown":"# Dirección del Chasis\n \nReporta de la dirección a la que se enfrenta el Chasis utilizando la posición angular actual del sensor giroscópico (Gyro).\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando de Dirección del Chasis reporta de un aumento en el rumbo al girar en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\nDirección del Chasis reporta de un rango de **0.00 a 359.99 grados**.","signature":"drivetrain.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_done":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_done","markdown":"# Conducir ya Termino\n\nReporta si el chasis ha completado su movimiento.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.is_done()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nConducir ya termino reporta **True** cuando el Chasis ha completado su movimiento.\n\nConducir ya termino reporta **False** cuando el Chasis sigue en movimiento.","signature":"drivetrain.is_done()"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving","markdown":"# Chasis está Moviendo\n \nReporta si el Chasis se está moviendo actualmente.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.is_moving()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nChasis está moviendo reporta **True** cuando los Motores del Chasis se están moviendo.\n\nChasis está moviendo reporta **False** cuando se detienen los motores del Chasis.","signature":"drivetrain.is_moving()"},"sensing_drivetrain_power":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_power","markdown":"# Potencia del Chasis\n\nInforma de la cantidad de potencia que el Chasis está generando actualmente.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.power(PowerUnits.WATT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPotencia del Chasis informa de un rango de **0.0 a 22.0 watts**.","signature":"drivetrain.power(PowerUnits.WATT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_rotation":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_rotation","markdown":"# Rotación del Chasis\n \nReporta del ángulo de rotación del Chasis cuando se configura con un Gyro Sensor de 3 Hilos o un V5 Inertial Sensor.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nRotación del Chasis reporta un valor **positive** cuando el Chasis gira en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\nRotación del Chasis reporta un valor **negative** cuando el Chasis gira en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj.","signature":"drivetrain.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_drivetrain_temperature":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_temperature","markdown":"# Temperatura del Chasis\n \nReporta la temperatura de los V5 Smart Motors que alimentan el Chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.temperature(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nTemperatura del Chasis indica un rango de **0% a 100%**.","signature":"drivetrain.temperature(PERCENT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_torque":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_torque","markdown":"# Par de Conducción\n\nInforma de la cantidad de torsiรณn (fuerza rotacional) que utiliza actualmente el Chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.torque(TorqueUnits.NM)\n```\n\n## Cรณmo Utilizar\n\nPar de Conducción reporta un rango de **0.0 a 18.6 libras-pulgada (InLB) o 0.0 a 2.1 Newton-metros (Nm)**.","signature":"drivetrain.torque(TorqueUnits.NM)"},"sensing_drivetrain_velocity":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad de Conducciรณn\n \nReporta la velocidad actual del Chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.velocity(UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nVelocidad de Conducciรณn reporta un rango de -100% a 100% o -600rpm a 600rpm.\n\nEl parámetro 'UNIT'(Unidad) se puede reemplazar con **PERCENT** (Por Ciento) o **RPM**.\n\nVelocidad de Conducciรณn reportará un rango de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranajes instalado en los V5 Smart Motors utilizados en el Chasis.\n\n* Red Cartridge (Cartucho Rojo): -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge (Cartucho Verde): -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge (Cartucho Azul): -600rpm to 600rpm","signature":"drivetrain.velocity(PERCENT)"},"sensing_encoder_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_position","markdown":"# Posición del Codificador de Eje\n \nReporta de la posición de rotación del Codificador de Eje.\n\n```don\nencoder.position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl parámetro 'UNITS' (Unidad) acepta **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS** (Vueltas) como valor.\n\nLa posición del codificador de eje informa de la distancia que el codificador de eje ha girado en números enteros para grados, y números decimales para giros.","signature":"encoder.position(DEGREES)"},"sensing_encoder_set_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_set_position","markdown":"# Establecer la Posición del Codificador de Eje\n \nEstablece la posición del Codificador de Eje en el valor dado.\n\n```don\nencoder.set_position(VALUE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'encoder.set_position' (Establecer la Posición del Codificador de Eje) se puede utilizar para establecer la posición del codificador de eje a cualquier valor dado.\n\nEl parámetro 'UNITS' (Unidad) acepta **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS** (Vueltas) como un valor.\n\nNormalmente, el comando set shaft encoder position (Establecer la Posición del Codificador de Eje) se utiliza para ajustar la posición a 0, para restablecer la posición del codificador de eje.","signature":"encoder.set_position(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_encoder_velocity":{"name":"sensing_encoder_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad del Codificador de Eje\n\nReporta de la velocidad actual de un codificador de eje.\n\n```don\nencoder.velocity(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nVelocidad del codificador del eje indica un valor decimal en grados por segundo (dps) o rotaciones por minuto (rpm).\n\nEl parámetro 'UNITS' (Unidades) acepta **VelocityUnits.DPS** o **RPM** como valor.","signature":"encoder.velocity(VelocityUnits.DPS)"},"sensing_gyro_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_calibrate","markdown":"# Calibrar el Sensor Giroscopio\n\nCalibrar el Sensor Gyro se utiliza para reducir la cantidad de deriva generada por Sensor Gyro.\n\n```don\ngyro.calibrate()\n```\n\nLa deriva ocurre cuando el Sensor Gyro detecta incorrectamente el movimiento aunque el sensor no se esté moviendo físicamente.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl Sensor Gyro debe permanecer inmóvil durante el proceso de calibración. El proceso de calibración tardará aproximadamente 2 segundos en completarse.","signature":"gyro.calibrate()"},"sensing_gyro_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Ángulo de Dirección del Gyro\n \nReportaa la dirección actual del Sensor de Giroscopio de 3 Hilos en Grados.\n\n```don\ngyro.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando reporta un aumento en la dirección al girar en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\n`gyro.heading` reporta de un rango entre **0.00 a 359.99**.","signature":"gyro.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Ángulo de Rotación del Giro\n \nReporta del ángulo de rotación actual del Sensor de Giroscopio de 3 Hilos en grados.\n\n```don\ngyro.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nRotación del Giro reporta un valor **positive** cuando el sensor Gyro gira en la dirección **en el sentido de las agujas del reloj**.\n\nRotación del Giro reporta un valor **negative** cuando el sensor Gyro gira en la dirección **en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj**.","signature":"gyro.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_heading","markdown":"# Establecer Dirección de Giroscopio\n\nEstablecer la dirección actual del Sensor Giroscópico (Gyro) en un valor establecido.\n \n```don\ngyro.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando establecer dirección de giroscopio se puede utilizar para establecer la posición del giroscopio en cualquier dirección en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\nEste comando se utiliza normalmente para restablecer la dirección del sensor Gyro cuando el valor se establece en 0.\n\nEl parámetro 'HEADING' (dirección) acepta un rango de **0.0 a 359.99 grados**.\n\nEl comando establecer dirección puede aceptar decimales, enteros o valores numéricos.","signature":"gyro.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer Rotación de Giroscopio\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del sensor de giroscopio de 3 hilos o del sensor inercial V5 en un valor determinado.\n\n```don \ngyro.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando de Establecer Rotación de Giroscopio se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del Chasis a cualquier valor positivo (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) o negativo (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj).\n\nEl comando de Establecer Rotación de Giroscopio puede aceptar decimales, enteros o valores numéricos.","signature":"gyro.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Aceleración Inercial\n\nReporta del valor de aceleración de uno de los ejes (x, y o z) en el Sensor Intertial.\n\n```don\ninertial.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nAceleración informa de un rango de **-4.0 a 4.0 Gs**.\n\nChoose which axis to use:\n\n* El X-axis (Eje-X) informa de la aceleración cuando el sensor interial se mueve **lado a lado**\n* El Y-axis (Eje-Y) informa de la aceleración cuando el sensor interial se mueve **de arriba a abajo**\n* El Z-axis (Eje-Z) informa de la aceleración cuando el sensor interial se mueve **hacia adelante hasta atrás**","signature":"inertial.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS)"},"sensing_inertial_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_calibrate","markdown":"# Calibrar Sensor Inercial\n \nCalibración del Sensor Inercial se utiliza para reducir la cantidad de deriva generada por el Sensor Inercial.\n\n```don\ninertial.calibrate()\n```\n\nLa deriva se produce cuando el Sensor Inercial detecta incorrectamente el movimiento aunque el sensor no se esté moviendo físicamente.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl Sensor Inercial debe permanecer inmóvil durante el proceso de calibración. El proceso de calibración tardará aproximadamente 2 segundos en completarse.","signature":"inertial.calibrate()"},"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Tasa de Giroscopio Inercial\n\nObtiene la velocidad de rotación de uno de los ejes (x, y o z) en el Sensor Inercial.\n\n```don\ninertial.gyro_rate(AxisType.XAXIS, RPM)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa velocidad de giro indica un rango de **-1000.0 a 1000.0** en dps (grados por segundo).\n\nElija qué eje utilizar.\n\n* El X-Axis (Eje X) informa de la velocidad de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el eje X (basado en la orición del sensor)\n* El X-Axis (Eje Y) informa de la velocidad de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el eje Y (basado en la orición del sensor)\n* El X-Axis (Eje Z) informa de la velocidad de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el eje Z (basado en la orición del sensor)","signature":"inertial.gyro_rate(AxisType.XAXIS, RPM)"},"sensing_inertial_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_heading","markdown":"# Ángulo de Dirección Inercial \n\nReports the V5 Inertial Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```don\ninertial.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `inertial.heading` informa de un aumento en el rumbo al girar en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\n`inertial.heading` reports un rango de 0.00 a 359.99 grados.","signature":"inertial.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_orientation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Orientación Inercial\n\nObtiene un ángulo de orientación del Sensor Inercial. Informa del valor de unidad especificado por el parámetro del Sensor Inercial.\n\n```don\ninertial.orientation(OrientationType.ROLL, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nLa orientación notificada viene determinada por el eje seleccionado (x, y, o z).\n\n* El X-axis (Eje-x) representa el cabeceo, que informa de un valor entre -90 y +90 grados).\n* El Y-axis (Eje-y) representa el rollo, que informa de un valor entre -180 y +180 grados)\n* El Z-axis (Eje-z) representa la orientación, que indica un valor entre -180 y +180 grados)","signature":"inertial.orientation(OrientationType.ROLL , DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_rotation","markdown":"# Angulo de Rotación Inercial\n \nReporta del ángulo de rotación actual del V5 Sensor Inercial de 3 hilos en grados.\n\n```don\ninertial.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'inertial.rotation' reporta de un valor positivo cuando el Sensor Inercial gira en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\n`inertial.rotation` informa de un valor negativo cuando el Sensor Inercial gira en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj.","signature":"inertial.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_heading","markdown":"# Establecer Dirección del Inercial\n\nEstablece la dirección actual del Sensor Inercial en un valor establecido.\n\n```don\ninertial.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`inertial.set_heading` se puede utilizar para establecer la posición del giroscopio en cualquier dirección en el sentido de las agujas del reloj. Este comando se utiliza normalmente para restablecer la orientación del Sensor Inercial cuando la dirección se establece en un valor de 0.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` Se utiliza normalmente para restablecer la orientación de la dirección del Sensor Inercial cuando un valor se establece en 0.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` acepta un rango de 0.0 a 359.99 grados.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` pueden aceptar decimales, enteros o valores numéricos.","signature":"inertial.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer Rotación Inercial\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del Sensor Inercial de 3-Hilos en un valor determinado.\n\n```don\ninertial.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `inertial.set_rotation` se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del Sensor Inercial a cualquier valor positivo (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) o negativo (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj).\n\n`inertial.set_rotation` acepta un rango de cualquier decimal positivo o negativo o entero.","signature":"inertial.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_light_brightness":{"name":"sensing_light_brightness","markdown":"# Brillo del Sensor de Luz\n\nReporta la cantidad de luz detectada por el sensor de luz.\n\n```don\nlight.brightness(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`light.brightnes` informa de un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nUna gran cantidad de luz detectada reportará un alto valor de brillo.\n\nUna pequeña cantidad de luz detectada reportará un valor de bajo brillo.","signature":"light.brightness(PERCENT)"},"sensing_limit_switch_pressing":{"name":"sensing_limit_switch_pressing","markdown":"# Pulsando el Interruptor de Límite\n\nInforma si el Interruptor de Límite está siendo presionado.\n\n```don\nlimit_switch.pressing()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPresionar el interruptor de límite informa **True** si se está presionando el interruptor de límite.\n\nPresionar el interruptor de límite informa **False** si no se está presionando el interruptor de límite","signature":"limit_switch.pressing()"},"sensing_line_tracker_reflectivity":{"name":"sensing_line_tracker_reflectivity","markdown":"# Reflectividad del Rastreador de Línea\n\nInforma de la cantidad de luz reflejada con el Sensor de Rastreador de Línea .\n\n```don\nline_tracker.reflectivity(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLas superficies de color claro reflejarán más luz e reportarán un alto valor de reflectividad.\n\nLas superficies de color oscuro reflejarán menos luz e reportarán  un valor de reflectividad bajo.\n\nLa unidad predeterminada es 'PERCENT' (per ceinto) que devuelve un valor entero de **0% a 100%**.","signature":"line_tracker.reflectivity(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_current":{"name":"sensing_motor_current","markdown":"# Corriente del Motor\n\nInforma de la cantidad de corriente que un V5 Smart Motor está utilizando actualmente en amperios (amperios).\n\n```don\nmotor.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nCorriente de Motor reporta de un rango de **0.0 a 2.5 amperios**.","signature":"motor.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_motor_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_motor_efficiency","markdown":"# Eficiencia del Motor\n \nReporta de la eficiencia de un V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.efficiency(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEficiencia del Motor reporta del valor de la potencia (en vatios) que está utilizando el motor (entrada), frente a la cantidad de potencia (en vatios) que proporciona el motor (salida).\n\nUn V5 Smart Motor suele alcanzar una eficiencia máxima del 65% en casos de uso normales.\n\nLa eficiencia del motor reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**.","signature":"motor.efficiency(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_is_done":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor ha Terminado\n\nReporta si el V5 Smart Motor seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\n```don\nmotor.is_done()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nMotor ha Terminado reporta **True** cuando el motor seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\nMotor ha Terminado reporta **False** cuando el motor seleccionado todavía se está moviendo.","signature":"motor.is_done()"},"sensing_motor_is_spinning":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor está Girando\n\nReporta si el V5 Smart Motor seleccionado está girando actualmente.\n\n```don\nmotor.is_spinning()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nMotor está Girando reporta **True** cuando el motor seleccionado todavía se está moviendo.\n\nMotor está Girando reporta **False** cuando se detiene el motor seleccionado.","signature":"motor.is_spinning()"},"sensing_motor_position":{"name":"sensing_motor_position","markdown":"# Posición del Motor\n\nReporta de la posición de rotación actual del V5 Smart Motor seleccionado.\n\n```don\nmotor.position(UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa posición del motor informa de la posición del V5 Smart Motor en números enteros para grados, y números decimales de giros.\n\nLos valores aceptables para 'UNIT' (Unidad) son: **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS* (Vueltas).","signature":"motor.position(DEGREES)"},"sensing_motor_power":{"name":"sensing_motor_power","markdown":"# Potencia del Motor\n\nReporta de la cantidad de potencia que el V5 Smart Motor está generando actualmente.\n\n```don\nmotor.power(PowerUnits.WATT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPotencia del Motor reporta de un rango de **0.0 a 11.0 vatios**.","signature":"motor.power(PowerUnits.WATT)"},"sensing_motor_temperature":{"name":"sensing_motor_temperature","markdown":"# Temperatura del Motor\n\nInforma de la temperatura de un V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.temperature(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl uso del comando Temperatura del Motor puede ayudar a los usuarios a desarrollar lógica para evitar que sus V5 Smart Motors se sobrecalienten durante un uso intensivo.\n\nTemperatura del Motor reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**.","signature":"motor.temperature(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_torque":{"name":"sensing_motor_torque","markdown":"# Par Motor\n\nInforma de la cantidad de par (fuerza de rotación) que un V5 Smart Motor está utilizando actualmente.\n\n```don\nmotor.torque(TorqueUnits.NM)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPar Motor reporta un rango de **0.0 a 18.6 pulgadas-libras (InLB) o 0.0 a 2.1 Newton-metros (Nm)**.","signature":"motor.torque(TorqueUnits.NM)"},"sensing_motor_velocity":{"name":"sensing_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad del Motor\n\nReporta de la velocidad actual de un V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.velocity(UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nVelocidad del Motor reporta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\nLos valores aceptables para el parámetro 'UNIT' (Unidad) son: **DEGREES** (Grados) o **RPM**.\n\nVelocidad del Motor reportará de un rango de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranajes instalado en los V5 Smart Motor.\n\n* Red Cartridge (Cartucho Rojo): -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge (Cartucho Verde): -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge (Cartucho Azul): -600rpm a 600rpm","signature":"motor.velocity(PERCENT)"},"sensing_potentiometer_angle":{"name":"sensing_potentiometer_angle","markdown":"# Angulo del Potenciómetro\n\nDevuelve la posición angular del potenciómetro.\n\n```don\npotentiometer.angle(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`potentiometer.angle` devuelve un valor decimal (como un valor doble) para informar de la posición angular del potenciómetro.\n\nEl parámetro 'UNITS' (Unidads) acepta **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS** (Vueltos) como valor.","signature":"potentiometer.angle(PERCENT)"},"sensing_range_finder_distance":{"name":"sensing_range_finder_distance","markdown":"# Distancia desde el Buscador de Rangos\n\nReporta de la distancia del objeto más cercano desde el sensor Ultrasonic Range Finder.\n\n```don\nrange_finder.distance(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nDistancia Desde reporta un rango de 30 mm a 3000 mm o 2 pulgadas a 115 pulgadas.\n\nEl parámetro 'UNITS'(Unidad) acepta **MM** o **INCHES** (Pulgadas) como valor.","signature":"range_finder.distance(MM)"},"sensing_range_finder_found_object":{"name":"sensing_range_finder_found_object","markdown":"# Buscador de Rangos Encontro Objeto\n\nReporta si el sensor Ultrasonic Range Finder detecta un objeto dentro de su campo de visión.\n\n```don\nrange_finder.found_object()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nObjeto Encontrado informa **True** cuando el sensor Ultrasonic Range Finder ve un objeto o superficie dentro de su campo de visión.\n\nObjeto Encontrado informa **False** cuando el sensor Ultrasonic Range Finder no detecta un objeto o superficie.","signature":"range_finder.found_object()"},"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled":{"name":"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled","markdown":"# Controlador Activado\n\nActiva o desactiva las acciones configuradas por el Controller desde el menú dispositivos.\n\n```don\nremote_control_code_enabled = False\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nSeleccione activar o desactivar las acciones del Contoroller configuradas. \n\nDe forma predeterminada, el Controller está activado en todos los proyectos.","signature":"remote_control_code_enabled = False"},"sensing_vision_largest_object":{"name":"sensing_vision_largest_object","markdown":"# Objeto Existe\n\nReporta sobre un objeto detectado desde el Vision Sensor.\n\n```don\nvision.largest_object()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara utilizar el bloque de objetos Visión, siga estos pasos:\n\n1. Configure su Vision Sensor mediante la ventana Dispositivos.\n2. Utilice la instantánea (snapshot) para capturar una imagen de Vision Sensor y busque una firma / código de color.\n3. Utilice Objeto Existe para comprobar si el sensor de visión ha detectado la firma o el código de color solicitados.\n4. Una vez que el Vision Sensor detecta un objeto, puede utilizar otros comandos de Visión para obtener más información sobre el objeto detectado.\n\n* Utilice Definir Elemento de Objeto de Visión para establecer el objeto detectado sobre el que desea obtener más información. De forma predeterminada, se utiliza el objeto más grande detectado.\n* Utilice Recuento de Objetos para determinar cuántos objetos se han detectado de ese código de firma/color solicitado.\n* Utilice Objeto de Visión para determinar qué información se debe informar del objeto detectado.","signature":"vision.largest_object()"},"sensing_vision_take_snapshot":{"name":"sensing_vision_take_snapshot","markdown":"# Instantánea\n\nToma una instantánea del Vision Sensor.\n\n```don\nvision.take_snapshot(SIGNATURE)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando Instantánea capturará la imagen actual del sensor de visión para procesarla y analizarla en busca de códigos y firmas de color.\n\nNormalmente, primero se requiere una instantánea antes de usar cualquier otro comando de Vision Sensor.","signature":"vision.take_snapshot(SIGNATURE)"},"variables_my_2d_list":{"name":"variables_my_2d_list","markdown":"# Variable de Lista 2D\n\nLas variables de lista 2D se utilizan para almacenar listas con varias filas y columnas.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una variable de lista 2D, cree un nombre de variable único y significativo. Esto significa que el nombre de la variable debe describir con precisión la naturaleza de sus valores.\n\nPor ejemplo, una variable de lista 2D llamada \"coordenadas\" puede usarse para almacenar múltiples conjuntos de valores de coordenadas.\n\nDeclare esta lista usando un símbolo igual único '=' después del nombre de su lista seguido de corchetes '[ ]'.\n\nDentro de estos corchetes, inserte varios conjuntos de corchetes, separados por una coma, así: '[[ ], [ ]]'. Se pueden anidar más de dos conjuntos de corchetes dentro del conjunto de corchetes más externo.\n\nIncluya valores separados por una coma o ',' en sus respectivos corchetes. Si la variable está almacenando cadenas, coloque la coma fuera del encierro '\" \"'.\n\nCada conjunto interno de corchetes representa una fila de elementos de lista. El índice del elemento dentro de la fila representa una columna de la lista 2D.\n\nPara acceder al valor de una lista 2D, utilice el nombre de la lista, seguido inmediatamente de dos índices entre corchetes. El primer índice hace referencia a la fila, mientras que el segundo índice hace referencia a la columna de la lista 2D. Tenga en cuenta que los índices de matriz comienzan en 0, no en 1.\n\nPor ejemplo, dada una lista 2D 'coordenadas = [[X1, Y1], [X2, Y2]]', la expresión 'coordenadas[0][0]' devolverá 'X1'. \n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nEste ejemplo muestra que a una variable llamada my_list se le asignan dos listas de colores separadas.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [[\"Green\", \"Red\", \"Blue\"], [\"Black\", \"Yellow\", \"Orange\"]]\n```\n\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEste ejemplo muestra que a una variable llamada my_list se le asignan dos listas de números separadas.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]\n```","signature":"my_2d_list = [\\n\\t[0,0,0],\\n\\t[0,0,0],\\n\\t[0,0,0]\\n]"},"variables_my_boolean":{"name":"variables_my_boolean","markdown":"# Variable Booleana\n\nVariables booleanas pueden contener los valores **True** o **False**.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una variable booleana, cree un nombre de variable único y significativo. Esto significa que el nombre de la variable debe describir con precisión el valor que está almacenando.\n\nPor ejemplo, una variable 'pulsado' debe usarse para almacenar el valor de si se pulsa un botón.\n\nDeclare esta variable con un símbolo igual '=' después del nombre booleano. Su valor puede ser 'True' o 'Falso'.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo se asigna un valor 'True' a 'my_variable' .\n\n```don\nmy_variable = True\n```","signature":"my_boolean = True"},"variables_my_list":{"name":"variables_my_list","markdown":"# Lista de Variables\n\nListas de Variables se utilizan para almacenar varios valores.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una variable de lista, cree un nombre de variable descriptivo. Esto significa que el nombre de la variable debe describir con precisión la naturaleza de sus valores.\n\nPor ejemplo, una lista de variables 'colores' se puede utilizar para almacenar varios valores de color.\n\nPara asignar una lista de valores a una lista de variables, utilice el operador '=', seguido de valores separados por comas encerrados entre corchetes, '[ ]'.\n\nSi los valores son números, las comas de separación deben venir justo después de cada valor.\n\n`mi_lista_numerica = [1, 2, 3]`\n\nSi los valores son cadenas, las comas deben ir fuera de la '\" \"'.\n\n`mi_lista_decadenas = [\"Hello\", \"World\"]`\n\nPara acceder a un valor específico en la lista de variables, escriba el nombre de la lista de variables, seguido inmediatamente de un índice incluido por un conjunto de corchetes. Tenga en cuenta que el índice de una matriz comienza en 0, no en 1.\n\nPor ejemplo, `mi_lista_decadenas[0]` devolverá el valor `\"Hello\"`.\n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_list being assigned the string values of several colors.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [\"Green\", \"Red\", \"Blue\"]\n```\n\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEste ejemplo muestra una variable llamada my_list que se le asignan varios números.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [1, 2, 3]\n```","signature":"my_list = [0,0,0]"},"variables_my_number":{"name":"variables_my_number","markdown":"# Variable Numérica\n\nLas variables numéricas se utilizan para almacenar valores numéricos.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una variable numérica, cree un nombre de variable significativo. This means that the variable name should accurately describe the value that it is storing. \n\nPor ejemplo, se debe utilizar una variable 'contador' para almacenar el valor de un contador.\n\nPara asignar un valor a la variable, utilice el operador '='. \n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nEste ejemplo mantiene el nombre de variable por defecto 'my_number' y le asigna un valor de 10.\n\n```don\nmy_number = 10\n```\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEste ejemplo le da a la variable el nombre 'three_plus_two' y almacena el resultado de los 3 agregados a 2. \n\n```don\nthree_plus_two = 3 + 2\n```","signature":"my_number = 1"},"variables_my_string":{"name":"variables_my_string","markdown":"# Variable de Cadena\n\nVariables de Cadena se utilizan para almacenar cadenas.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una variable de cadena, cree un nombre de variable significativo. Esto significa que el nombre de la variable debe describir con precisión su valor. \n\nPor ejemplo, se debe utilizar una variable 'nombre' para almacenar el valor de un nombre.\n\nPara asignar una cadena a una variable de cadena, utilice el operador '='. Su valor de cadena se puede incluir en '\" \"' o '' ''.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo se muestra una variable llamada my_string que se le asigna el valor de cadena '\"Hello\"'.\n\n```don\nmy_string = \"Hello\"\n```","signature":"my_string = \\\"Hello World\\\""}}},"es-419":{"blocks":{"acceleration_of":{"name":"acceleration_of","markdown":"# Aceleración de\n\nInforma el valor de aceleración de un eje en el acelerómetro analógico.\n\n![acceleration_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Aceleración de** reporta ranfo de **-2.0 G to 2.0 G** o **-6.0 G to 6.0 G** dependiendo en el estado del clip puente en el Acelerómetro Analógico.\n\nElija qué acelerómetro usar.\n\n![acceleration_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_device.png)\n\nEl bloque de reporte **Aceleración de** es usado dentro de bloques con espacio circular.\n\n![acceleration_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_inserted.png)"},"activate_emergency_stop":{"name":"activate_emergency_stop","markdown":"# Activar parada de emergencia\n\nActiva el botón de parada de emergencia (o E-stop) para el V5 Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico V5).\n\n![estop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/activate_emergency_stop/estop_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl botón de parada de emergencia en el Workcell apagará cualquier Smart Motores y Sensores V5 conectado al V5 Brain. \n\n![estop_robot](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/activate_emergency_stop/estop_robot.png)\n\nElija qué Brazo Robótico utilizar.\n\n![select_estop_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/activate_emergency_stop/select_estop_arm.png)\n\nEl bloque **Activar parada de emergencia** se utiliza a menudo con el bloque de \"Cuando parachoques\" de la categoría Eventos. Esto garantiza que todos los Motores y Sensores Inteligentes V5 conectados al V5 Brain se apagarán una vez que el interruptor de parachoques (E-Stop) está pulsado.\n![estop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/activate_emergency_stop/estop_example.png)"},"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Sumar\n\nSumar dos valores juntos e reportar la suma.\n\n![add](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/add/add.png)\n\n## Como Se Usa\n\n**Sumar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque **sumar** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares, y también pueden aceptar otros bloques circulares en él.\n\nSuma dos numeros.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nAgregar con valores de variables.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nAgregar con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# Y\n\nReporta si dos condiciones booleanas son ambas verdaderas.\n\n![and](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/and/and.png)\n\n## Como Se Usa\n\nEl bloque **y** reporta **verdadero** cuando ambas condiciones son **verdaderas**. \n\nEl bloque **y** reporta **falso** cuando una, o ambas, de las condiciones son **falsas**.\n\nEl bloque booleano **and** reporta un **verdadero** o **falso** valor y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![and_shape](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo verificará si se presionan dos botones del controlador V5 al mismo tiempo.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nEl bloque **y** regresara **verdadero** cuando ambos  **controller1 X button** y el **controller1 A button** esten presionados.\n\nEl bloque **y** regresara a **falso** cuando uno (o ambos) de los botones del controlador no estan presionados.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/and/and_truth.png)"},"angle_of":{"name":"angle_of","markdown":"# Angulo de\n\nDevuelve la posición angular del potenciómetro.\n\n![angle_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/angle_of/angle_of_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Angulo de** reportar en rango de **0% a 100%** o **0.0 a 250.0 grados**.\n\nElija qué potenciómetro usara.\n\n![angle_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/angle_of/angle_of_device.png)\n\nElija informar el valor en % o grados.\n\n![angle_of_block_parameters](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/angle_of/angle_of_parameters.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **angulo de** Se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![angle_of_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/angle_of/angle_of_inserted.png)\n"},"arm_get_joint_value":{"name":"arm_get_joint_value","markdown":"# Joint potentiometer value\n\nReports the potentiometer value of one of the four joints on the V5 Workcell.\n\n![joint_potentiometer_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/arm_get_joint_value/joint_potentiometer_value.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **joint potentiometer value** reporter block is used to report the potentiometer value of one of the four joints on the Workcell. This reporter block can be used when determining mastering values.\n\n**Joint potentiometer value** reports a range of **0 to 4095**.\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![joint_potentiometer_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/arm_get_joint_value/joint_potentiometer_arm.png)\n\nChoose which joint to report. \n\n![joint_option_potentiometer_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/arm_get_joint_value/joint_option_potentiometer_value.png)\n\nThe **joint potentiometer value** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![print_potentiometer_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/arm_get_joint_value/print_potentiometer_value.png)"},"arm_get_position":{"name":"arm_get_position","markdown":"# Arm position\n\nReports the current x, y, or z-coordinate position of the arm on the Workcell.\n\n![arm_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/arm_get_position/arm_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **arm position** reporter block is used to report the current x, y, or z-coordinate position of the arm on the Workcell.\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use. \n\n![arm_position_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/arm_get_position/arm_position_arm.png)\n\nChoose which axis to report. \n\n![arm_position_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/arm_get_position/arm_position_axis.png)\n\nThe **arm position** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![arm_position_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/arm_get_position/arm_position_inserted.png)\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the arm on the Workcell will move to the coordinate (6, 0, 4). Then the **print** block will print the arm's current position on the x-axis, reported from the **arm position** block, to the Console.\n\n![arm_position_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/arm_get_position/arm_position_example.png)"},"battery_current":{"name":"battery_current","markdown":"# Corriente de Bateria\n\nReporta la corriente de la batería del cerebro V5.\n\n![battery_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/battery_current/battery_current_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**corriente de Bateria** reporta un rango de **0.0 amperios a 20.0 amperios**.\n\nThe bloque que reporta **corriente de bateria** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![battery_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/battery_current/battery_current_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Nivel de Bateria\n\nInforma el nivel de carga de la batería del cerebro V5.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**nivel de bateria** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **nivel de bateria** es usado dentro de los bloques con interiores circulares.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)"},"battery_voltage":{"name":"battery_voltage","markdown":"# voltage de bateria\n\nReporta el voltaje de la batería del cerebro V5.\n\n![battery_voltage_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**voltage de Bateria** reporta un rango de **10.0 voltios a 14.4 voltios**.\n\nThe bloque que reporta **voltage de Bateria** Se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![battery_voltage_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_inserted.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Variable Booleano\n\nReporta el valor de un variable Booleano.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nBloques de **variable Booleano** son usados para reportar valor **cierto** o **falso** archivado dentro de el variable. Usa el bloque **establecer variable booleano** para establecer actualizar el valor de un variable booleano.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nEl bloque **variable booleano** reporta un valor **cierto** o **falso** y si es usado en bloques de espacio hexagonal (seis lados).\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nVariables Booleanos son creados usando el boton **Crear un Booleano**.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Romper\n\nSale de un ciclo repetitivo inmediatamente.\n\n![break](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/break/break.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nCuando se agrega a un bloque 'C' de repetir, el bloque **romper** saldrá del ciclo repetitivo en el que se encuentra actualmente.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo moverá el tren motriz hacia adelante y verificará si se presionó la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\nSi presiono l apantalla **presionada**, el bloque **romper** saldra del ciclo repetitivo y parara el tren motriz.\n\n![break_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Brillo de\n\nReporta la cantidad de luz detectada por el Sensor de Luz.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Brillo de** reporta el rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija qué sensor de luz va usar.\n\n![brightness_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Brillo de** Se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![brightness_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Transmitir\n\nTransmitir un mensage para activar cualquier cúmulo que empiecen con el bloque **cuando reciba**  escuchando un mensaje de difusión.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl cúmulo que manda el bloque **transmitir** continuará ejecutando bloques al mismo tiempo que otros cúmulos que reciben el mensaje transmitido.\n\nElija qué mensaje que quiere **transmitir**. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Transmitir y Esperar\n\nTransmitir un mensaje para activar cualquier cúmulo que empiece con el bloque **cuando reciba** escuchando para un mensaje transmitido mientras también detiene el resto del cúmulo.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar \n\nEl cumulo que envia **transmitir y esperar** se detendrá hasta que los otros cumulos que reciben el mensaje enviado se hayan completado.\n\nElija qué mensaje quiere **transmitir**. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Calibrar giroscopio\n\nLa calibración del giroscopio se usa para reducir la cantidad de deriva generada por el giroscopio.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nLa deriva se produce cuando el giroscopio detecta incorrectamente el movimiento aunque el sensor no se esté moviendo.\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl giroscopio debe permanecer quieto durante el proceso de calibración. El proceso de calibración tardará aproximadamente 1 segundo en completarse.\n\nElija qué giroscópico va usar.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Cambiar variable\n\nCambia una variable por el valor dado.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué variable va usar- el variable seleccionado también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **Cambiar variable** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo aumentará el variable que establece la velocidad del variador por 10, cada vez que el **ciclo de repetición** se repita.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Borrar todas las filas\n\nBorra toda la pantalla V5 Brain o Controller.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Borrar todas las filas** no cambiará el cursor de la pantalla. Use el bloque **establecer cursor** para restablecer el cursor de la pantalla a una posición específica.\n\nElija qué dispositivo va usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![clear_all_rows_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_dropdown.png)"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Borrar fila\n\nBorra una sola fila en la pantalla V5 Brain o Controller.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Borrar fila**  puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos entre **1 - 20**, para establecer qué fila borrar.\n\nElija qué dispositivo va usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![clear_row_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/clear_row/clear_row_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Brain permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará el número de filas disponibles en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n**Tamaño de Fuente V5 Brain - Numero de Filas:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Filas\n* Small - 16 Filas\n* Medium - 12 Filas (Default)\n* Large - 8 Filas\n* Extra Large - 6 Filas\n* Super Large - 4 Filas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/clear_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nEl controlador V5 no  permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de Fuent V5 Controller - Numero de Filas:**\n\n* Fuente Standard - 3 Filas (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/clear_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Comentario\n\nPermite a los programadores escribir información para ayudar a describir su programa.\n\n![comment_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nLos programadores profesionales usan comentarios en todos sus programas para ayudar a otros a comprender su código. Los comentarios también pueden ayudar con la resolución de problemas y la colaboración.\n\nAgregue texto en el bloque de **Comentario** seleccionando primero el rectángulo transparente y eliminando cualquier texto existente. Luego, escriba el nuevo texto.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nLos comentarios no cambian el programa o los bloques que lo rodean.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Controlador habilitado\n\nHabilita o deshabilita las acciones configuradas del controlador desde el menú Dispositivos.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija habilitar o deshabilitar las acciones configuradas del controlador seleccionando el estado deseado en el menú desplegable. Por defecto, el controlador está habilitado en cada proyecto.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Example\n\nLa acción configurada en este ejemplo es utilizar el comportamiento del tren de transmisión del robot establecido por la configuración del controlador en la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nEste ejemplo tendrá el controlador configurado deshabilitado cuando se inicie el programa.\n\nEl robot avanzará 6 pulgadas.\n\nFinalmente, el bloque **controlador habilitado** permitirá al Controlador restaurar los comportamientos de conducción del Controlador.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"controller_play_rumble":{"name":"controller_play_rumble","markdown":"# Controlador modo de vibracion\n\nCrea un efecto de vibracion en el Controlador V5.\n\n![controller_play_rumble](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl **controlador modo de vibracion** usa un motor de vibracionen dentro del Controlador V5 para suministrar realimentación.\n\nElija qué patrón va usar.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_pattern](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_pattern.png)\n\nElija qué controlador V5 va usar.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_device.png)\n\n\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Corriente del motor\n\nReporta la cantidad de poder un motor V5 esta actualmente usando en amperios (amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Corriente del motor** reporta un rango de **0.0 a 2.5 amps**. \n\nElija qué motor va usar.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **corriente del motor** es usado en los bloques con espacios circular.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Columna del cursor \n\nInforma el número de columna de la ubicación del cursor de la pantalla en el cerebro V5 o Controlador.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Columna del cursor** reporta un rango de **1 a 80**.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **columna de cursor** es usado en los bloques con espacios circulares. \n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Brain  permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará el número de columnas disponibles en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del cerebro V5 - Número de columnas:**\n\n* Extra Small - 80 Columnas\n* Small - 68 Columnas\n* Medium - 48 Columnas (Default)\n* Large - 32 Columnas\n* Extra Large - 24 Columnas\n* Super Large - 16 Columnas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/cursor_column/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nEl controlador V5 no  permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del controlador V5 - Número de columnas:**\n\n* Fuente Standard - 20 Columnas (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/cursor_column/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Fila del cursor\n\nInforma el número de fila de la ubicación del cursor en la pantalla del cerebro V5 Brain o Controlador.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Fila de cursor** reporta un rango de **1 a 20**.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **fila de cursor** es usado en bloques con espacios circular.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nEl cerebro V5 permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará el número de filas disponibles en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del cerebro V5 - Número de filas:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Filas\n* Small - 16 Filas\n* Medium - 12 Filas (Default)\n* Large - 8 Filas\n* Extra Large - 6 Filas\n* Super Large - 4 Filas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/cursor_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nEl controlador V5 no le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del controlador V5 - Número de filas:**\n\n* Fuente Standard - 3 Filas (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/cursor_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"digital_in_signal":{"name":"digital_in_signal","markdown":"# Digital in\n\nReports if the digital in signal is high.\n\n![digital_in_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/digital_in_signal/digital_in_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 3-Wire ports function at a 5V logic signal voltage level.\n\nThe **digital in** block reports **true** when the digital input signal is high.\n\nThe **digital in** block reports **false** when the digital input signal is low.\n\nChoose which digital in device to use. \n\n![digital_in_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/digital_in_signal/digital_in_select.png)\n\nThe **digital in** Boolean block reports a true or false value and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![digital_in_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/digital_in_signal/digital_in_insert.png)\n"},"distance_found_object":{"name":"distance_found_object","markdown":"# Distancia Encontro Objeto\n\nInforma si el Distance Sensor (Sensor de Distancia) ve un objeto dentro de su campo de visión.\n\n![distance_found_object_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block1.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Distancia Encontro Objeto** informa **true** cuando el Sensor de Distancia ve un objeto o superficie dentro de su campo de visión.\n\n**Distancia Encontro Objeto** informa **false** cuando el Sensor de Distancia no detecta un objeto o superficie.\n\nElija qué Distance Sensor (Sensor de Distancia) utilizar.\n\n![distance_found_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block2.png)\n\n\nEl bloque **distancia encontro objeto** indica  **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis caras).\n\n![distance_found_object_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block3.png)\n"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Distancia de\n\nReporta la distancia del objeto mas cercano de el sensor de buscador de rango ultrasónico.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Distancia de** reporta el rango desde **30mm a 3000mm** o **2 inches a 115 inches**.\n\nElija qué sensor buscador de rango ultrasónico va usar.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nChoose whether **distance from** is reported in inches or millimeters. \n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nElija si **distancia de** se usa dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"distance_object_distance":{"name":"distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Distancia del objeto\n\nReporta la distancia del objeto más cercano a el Distance Sensor (Sensor de Distancia).\n\n![distance_object_distance_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Distancia del objeto** informa de un rango de **20mm a 2000mm**.\n\nElija el Sensor de Distancia que desea utilizar.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block2.png)\n\nElija si **distancia del objeto** se reporta en pulgadas o milímetros. \n\n![distance_object_distance_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block3.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **distancia del objeto** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block4.png)\n"},"distance_object_size":{"name":"distance_object_size","markdown":"# El Tamaño del Objeto es\n\nInforma si el Distance Sensor (Sensor de Distancia) detecta el tamaño de objeto especificado.  \n\n![distance_object_size_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl sensor determina el tamaño del objeto detectado (ninguno, pequeño, mediano, grande) en función de la cantidad de luz reflejada y devuelta al sensor.\n\nElija un (Distance Sensor) Sensor de Distancia para usar.\n\n![distance_object_size_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block1.png)\n\nElija el tamaño del objeto que desea que compruebe el sensor.\n\n![distance_object_size_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block2.png)\n\nEl bloque **el tamaño del objeto es** reporta **true** cuando la distancia El sensor detecta el tamaño especificado.\n\nEl bloque **el tamaño del objeto es** reporta **false** si no detecta el tamaño especificado.\n\nEl bloque **el tamaño del objeto es** reporta **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis caras).\n\n![distance_object_size_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block3.png)\n"},"distance_object_velocity":{"name":"distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad del Objeto\n\nInforma de la velocidad actual de un objeto en m/s.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Velocidad del Objeto** informa de la velocidad actual de un objeto en m/s (metros por segundo).\n\nElija qué Distance Sensor (Sensor de distancia) utilizar.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block2.png)\n\n\nEl bloque reportero **velocidad del objeto** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block3.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Divide\n\nDivide el primer valor por el segundo valor e informa el dividendo.\n\n![divide](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Divide** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **divide** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares, y también puede aceptar bloques circulares en él. \n\nIngrese los números que se dividirán.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nDividir con valores de variables.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nDivide con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"draw_circle":{"name":"draw_circle","markdown":"# Dibujar circulo\n\nDibuja un círculo en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![draw_circle](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/draw_circle/draw_circle.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Dibujar circulo** require 3 valores:\n\n* Valor 1: Punto Centro X\n* Valor 2: Punto Centro Y\n* valor 3: Radio del Circulo (en pixeles)\n\nEl color de la línea exterior del círculo está determinado por bloque **establecer color de pluma**. El color de línea predeterminado es el blanco.\n\nEl color de relleno interior del círculo está determinado por el bloque **estableser color de relleno**. El color de relleno predeterminado es el negro.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"draw_line":{"name":"draw_line","markdown":"# Dibujar linea\n\nDibuja una línea en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![draw_line](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/draw_line/draw_line.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dibujar linea** requiere 4 valores:\n\n* Valor 1: Comenzando X coordenada\n* Valor 2: Comenzando Y coordenada\n* Valor 3: Finalizando X coordenada\n* Valor 4: Finalizando Y coordenada\n\nEl color de la línea está determinado por el bloque **establecer color de pluma**. El color de línea predeterminado es el blanco.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_pixel":{"name":"draw_pixel","markdown":"# Dibujar un píxel\n\nDibuja un píxel en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![draw_pixel](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/draw_pixel/draw_pixel.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dibujar un pixel** require 2 valores:\n\n* Valor 1: X Coordenada\n* Valor 2: Y Coordenada\n\nEl color del píxel está determinado por el bloque **establecer color de la pluma**. El color de píxel predeterminado es el blanco.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_rectangle":{"name":"draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Dibujar un rectángulo\n\nDibuja un rectángulo en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![draw_rectangle](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/draw_rectangle/draw_rectangle.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dibujar un rectangulo** require 4 valores:\n\n* Valor 1: Esquina Superior Izquierda coordenada X \n* Valor 2: Esquina Superior Izquierda coordenada Y\n* Valor 3: Ancho del rectángulo\n* Valor 4: Altura del rectángulo\n\nEl color de la línea exterior del rectángulo está determinado por bloque **establecer color de pluma**. El color de línea predeterminado es el blanco.\n\nEl color de relleno interior del rectángulo se determina por el bloque **establecer color de relleno**. El color de relleno predeterminado es el negro.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Conducir\n\nMueve el tren motriz para siempre.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **conducir** energiza el tren motriz para siempre, hasta que se use un nuevo bloque de tren motriz o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija la dirección en que se moverá el tren motriz.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Corriente del tren motriz\n\nReporta la cantidad de corriente (poder) que el tren motriz esta usando actualmente.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Corriente del tren motriz** reporta un rango de **0.0 a 2.5 amperias**. \n\nEl bloque que reporta **corriente del tren motriz** es usado dentro de bloques con espacio circular.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_efficiency":{"name":"drive_efficiency","markdown":"# Eficiencia de la unidad\n\nReporta la eficiencia del Drivetrain.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Eficiencia de la unidad** informa el valor de la potencia (en vatios) que utiliza el motor (input), frente a la cantidad de potencia (en vatios) que proporciona el motor (output).\n\nUn tren motriz V5 generalmente alcanza una eficiencia máxima del 65% en casos de uso normal.\n\n**Eficiencia de la unidad** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**. \n\nEl bloque que reporta **eficiencia de la unidad** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\n![drive_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Manejar por\n\nMueve tren motriz por una distancia dada.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija en qué dirección se moverá el tren motriz.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\n\nEstablezca qué tan lejos se moverá el tren motriz ingresando un valor y eligiendo la unidad de medida (pulgadas or milímetros).\n\nEl bloque **Maneja por** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques **esperar** hasta que el tren motriz termine de moverse.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el tren motriz se mueve.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Direccion de la unidad\n\nReporta la dirección a la que se dirige el tren motriz usando la posición angular actual de el giroscopio (Gyro).\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Direccion de la unidad** reporta un aumento en la direccion al girar en sentido del reloj.\n\n**Direccion de la unidad** reporta un rangi de **0.00 a 359.99 grados**.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Direccion de la unidad** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Unidad termino\n\nReporta si el tren motriz ha completado su movimiento.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Unidad termino** reporta **verdadero** cuando los motores del tren motriz han completado su movimiento.\n\n**Unidad termino** reporta **falso** cuando los motores del tren motriz siguen en movimiento.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **unidad termino** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y es usado en bloques de espacio hexagonal (seis lados).\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Unidad está en movimiento\n\nReporta si el tren motriz se está actualmente moviendo.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Unidad está en movimiento** reporta **verdadero** cuando tren motriz esta en movimiento.\n\n**Unidad está en movimiento** reporta **falso** cuando los motores del tren motriz paran.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Unidad está en movimiento** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y es usado en bloques con espacio hexagonal (seis-lados).\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_power":{"name":"drive_power","markdown":"# Potencia de la unidad\n\nReporta la potencia producida actualmente por el tren motriz.\n\n![drive_power](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_power/drive_power.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**potencia de la unidad** reporta un rango de **0.0 a 22.0 watts**. \n\nEl bloque que reporta **potencia de la unidad** es usado dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_power/drive_power_inserted.png)"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Rotación de la unidad\n\nInforma el ángulo de rotación del tren motriz cuando se configura con un sensor giroscópico de 3 ejes o un sensor inercial V5.\n\n![drive_rotation](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_rotation/drive_rotation.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Rotación de la unidad** informa un valor **positivo** cuando el tren motriz gira en una dirección **en el sentido de las agujas del reloj**.\n\n**Rotación de la unidad** reporta un valor **negativo**  cuando el tren motriz gira en una direccion **contra las agujas del reloj**.\n\nEl cloque que reporta **Rotación de la unidad** Se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_rotation_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_rotation/drive_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_temperature":{"name":"drive_temperature","markdown":"# Temperatura de la unidad\n\nReporta la temperatura de los motores V5 energizando el tren motriz.\n\n![drive_temperature](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_temperature/drive_temperature.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Temperatura de la unidad** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**. \n\nEl bloque que reporta **temperatura de la unidad** es usado dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.=\n\n![drive_temperature_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_temperature/drive_temperature_inserted.png)"},"drive_torque":{"name":"drive_torque","markdown":"# Torque de la unidad\n\nReporta la cantidad de torque (fuerza rotacional) que el tren motriz esta usando actualmente.\n\n![drive_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_torque/drive_torque.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Torque de la unidad** reporta rango de **0.0 a 18.6 pulgadas-lbs (InLB)** o **0.0 a 2.1 Newton-metros (Nm)**. \n\nElija si el **Torque de la unidad** se reporta en pulgadas-lbs (InLb) o Newton-metros (Nm).\n\n![drive_torque_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_torque/drive_torque_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **torque de la unidad** es usado dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_torque/drive_torque_inserted.png)"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad de la unidad\n\nReporta la velocidad actual del tren motriz\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Velocidad de la unidad** reporta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\n**Velocidad de la unidad** reporta un rango de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los motores inteligentes V5 utilizados en el tren motriz.\n\n* Cartucho Rojo : -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Cartucho Verde: -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Cartucho Azul : -600rpm a 600rpm\n\nElija si la velocidad se reporta en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Velocidad de la unidady** es usado dentro de bloque con espacios circulares.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"duration":{"name":"duration","markdown":"# Establecer la Duración del Electroimán\n\nEstablece cuánto tiempo se enciende el V5 Electromagnet (Electroimán)  para.\n\n![set_duration_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/duration/set_duration_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nSeleccione esta opción para establecer cuánto tiempo se enciende el electroimán para una elevación:\n\n* **corto** - potencia el electroimán por **250ms**\n* **mediano ** - potencia el electroimán por **500ms**\n* **largo** - potencia el electroimán por **1000ms**\n\n![set_duration_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/duration/set_duration_block_setting.png)\n\nElija el electroimán que desea utilizar.\n\n![set_duration_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/duration/set_duration_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo le dirá al robot que conduzca hacia adelante 200 mm, utilice el bloque **establecer la duración del electroimán** para establecer la duración en **largo**, luego el **electroimán** aumentará para recoger un objeto, conducir hacia adelante 200mm, luego soltar el objeto.\n\n![set_duration_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/duration/set_duration_example.png)\n"},"efficiency_of_motor":{"name":"efficiency_of_motor","markdown":"# Eficiencia del motor.\n\nReporta la eficiencia de un motor inteligente V5.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Eficiencia del motor** reporta el poder de el motor (en watts) usando (input), contra la cantidad de poder (en watts) que el motor esta proporcionando (output). \n\nUn motor inteligente V5 generalmente alcanza una eficiencia máxima del 65% en casos de uso normal.\n\n**Eficiencia del motor** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**. \n\nElija qué motor va usar.\n\n![motor_efficiency_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_device.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Eficiencia del motor** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares. \n\n![motor_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_inserted.png)"},"enable_manual_movement":{"name":"enable_manual_movement","markdown":"# Set manual movement\n\nAllows the arm of the V5 Workcell to be manually moved by hand.\n\n![set_manual_movement](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/enable_manual_movement/set_manual_movement.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, the motors on the Workcell lock in place when a project is running. To be able to manually move the arm, use the **set manual movement** block in your project.\n\n![movement](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/enable_manual_movement/movement.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![set_manual_movement_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/enable_manual_movement/set_manual_movement_arm.png)"},"energize":{"name":"energize","markdown":"# Electroimán Energizado\n\nEstablece el V5 Electromagnet (electroimán) en dos modos diferentes: **boost** (elevar) o **drop** (soltar).\n\n![set_magnet_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/energize/set_magnet_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nSeleccione esta opción para configurar ese electroimán para elevar o soltar.\n\n* **boost** (elevar) - turns on the electromagnet for as long as the duration was set\n* **drop** (soltar) - releases any object the electromagnet is holding\n\nDespués de energizar el imán, el imán tendrá que enfriarse antes de que pueda ser energizado de nuevo.\n\n\n![set_magnet_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/energize/set_magnet_block_setting.png)\n\nElija el electroimán que desea utilizar.\n\n![set_magnet_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/energize/set_magnet_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo configurará al robot para que avance 200 mm, **Electromagnet** will boost to pick up an object, drive forward 200mm, then drop the object.\n\n![set_magnet_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/energize/set_magnet_example.png)\n"},"enter_mastering_mode":{"name":"enter_mastering_mode","markdown":"# Start mastering process\n\nStarts the mastering process for the four joints of the  arm on the Workcell to allow it to be calibrated to the same known location.\n\n![start_mastering_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/enter_mastering_mode/start_mastering_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **start mastering process** block begins the mastering process for the arm on the V5 Workcell. \n\nThis block is used in the 'Arm Mastering' example project."},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Igual a\n\nInforma si el primer valor es el mismo, o igual al segundo valor.\n\n![equal_to](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Igual a** reporta **verdadero** cuando dos valores son exactamente igual.\n\n**Igual a** reporta **falso** cuando dos valores no son iguales.\n\nEl bloque **Igual a** aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Igual a** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso**  y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Por siempre\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite cualquier bloque contenido adentro, para siempre.\n\n![forever](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nColoca bloques en un bloque 'C' **Por siempre** para que esas acciones se repitan **Por siempre**.\n\nPuede salir de una repetición **Por siempre** poniendo un bloque de **Romper** dentro.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nBloques 'C' también se pueden poner uno dentro del otro. Este concepto se llama anidamiento (nesting) y puede ayudar a ahorrar tiempo al programar diferentes comportamientos."},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Función\n\nRealiza una función matemática seleccionada.\n\n![function](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - valor absoluto\n* **floor** - redondea hacia abajo al entero más cercano\n* **ceiling** - redondea al entero más cercano\n* **sqrt** - Raiz Cuadrada\n* **sin** - sine\n* **cos** - coseno\n* **tan** - tangente\n* **asin** - Arcoseno o la inversa de sine\n* **acos** - arcocoseno o el inverso del coseno\n* **atan** - arctan o el inverso de la tangente\n* **ln** - base de logaritmo natural e\n* **log** - base de logaritmo 10\n* **e ^** - poderes de e\n* **10 ^** - poderes de 10\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Función** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija la **Función** matemática de la lista de opciones.\n\n![function_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/function/function_select.png)\n\nEl bloque de **Función** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n![function_fit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Mas grande que\n\nReporta si el primer valor es mas grande (mayor) que el segundo valor.\n\n![greater_than](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Mas grande que** reporta **verdadero** cuando el primer valor es mayor que el segundo valor.\n\n**Mas grande que** reporta **falso** cuando el primer valor es menor o igual que el segundo valor.\n\nEl bloque **Mas grande que** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Mas grande que** reporta un valor **verdadero** or **falso** y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Dirección del giroscopio\n\nReporta la posición angular actual del sensor giroscópico (gyro).\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Dirección del giroscopio** informa un aumento en la direccion cuando gira en sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\n**Dirección del giroscopio** reporta un rango entre **0.00 a 359.99**.\n\nElija qué sensor giroscópico a verificar.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Dirección del giroscopio** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Si entonces\n\nUn bloque 'C' que ejecurta el bloque de adentro, si la condicion Booleana que reporta es **verdadera**.  \n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque 'C' **Si entonces** solo verificará la condición booleana una vez. \n\nSi la condición booleana se informa como **verdadera**, el bloque de adentro **Si entonces** se ejecutara.\n\nSi la condición booleana se informa como **falsa**, el bloque de adentro **Si entonces** será saltado.\n\nEl 'C' block **Si entonces** puede aceptar bloques con forma hexagonal (seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Si entonces más\n\nUn bloque 'C' Block que ejecuta los bloques dentro de la primera o segunda parte de **Si entonces más**, basado en el valor booleano informado.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl 'C' bloque **Si entonces más** solo verificará la condición booleana una vez.\n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **verdadero**, el bloque dentro de la seccion **si** sera ejecutado.\n\nSi la condición booleana es **falsa**, el bloque dentro de la seccion **mas** sera ejecutado.\n\nEl 'C' bloque **Si entonces más** puede aceptar bloques con forma hexagonal (seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)"},"inertial_acceleration":{"name":"inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Aceleración de\n\nInforma el valor de aceleración de uno de los ejes (x, y, o z) en el Sensor Intertial.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n**Aceleración de** reporta un rango de **-4.0 a 4.0** Gs. \n\nElija qué sensor inercial usar.\n\n![inertial_acceleration_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_device.png)\n\nElija qué eje usar:\n\n* El **X-eje** reporta la aceleración cuando se mueve el sensor inercial **lado a lado**\n* El **Y-eje** reporta la aceleración cuando se mueve el sensor inercial **arriba a abajo**\n* El **Z-eje** reporta la aceleración cuando se mueve el sensor inercial **enfrente a atras**\n\n![inertial_acceleration_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_axis.png)\n\nEl bloque sensor ** Aceleración de ** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_gyrorate":{"name":"inertial_gyrorate","markdown":"# Frecuencia del giroscopio\n\nObtiene la velocidad de rotación de uno de los ejes (x, y, o z) en el sensor inercial.\n\n![gyro_rate_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_gyrorate/gyro_rate_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Frecuencia del giroscopio** reporta un rango de **-1000.0 a 1000.0** en dps (grados por segundo). \n\nElija qué sensor inercial usar.\n\n![gyroRate_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_included_block.png)\n\nElija qué eje usar.\n\n* El **X-axis** reporta la frecuencia de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el X-Eje (basado en la orientación del sensor)\n* El **Y-axis** reporta la frecuencia de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el Y-Eje (basado en la orientación del sensor)\n* Eli **Z-axis** reporta la frecuencia de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el Z-Eje basado en la orientación del sensor)\n\n![gyroRate_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_axis.png)\n\nEl bloque sensorial **Frecuencia del giroscopio** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_orientation":{"name":"inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Orientación de\n\nObtiene un ángulo de orientación del sensor inercial. Informa el valor unitario especificado por el parámetro del sensor inercial.\n\n![orientation_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_orientation/orientation_inertial_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nLa orientación reportada está determinada por el eje seleccionado (x, y, o z).\n\n* El **X-eje** representa **pitch**, que informa un valor entre -90 a +90 grados.\n* El **Y-eje** representa **roll**, que informa un valor entre -180 a +180 grados)\n* El **Z-eje** representa **yaw**, que informa un valor entre -180 a +180 grados)\n\n---\n\n**Pitch** es el ángulo del robot inclinado hacia adelante y hacia atrás.\n\n![V5_Pitch_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_orientation/V5_Pitch_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Roll** es el ángulo del robot inclinado hacia la izquierda y hacia la derecha.\n\n![V5_Roll_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_orientation/V5_Roll_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Yaw** Es la rotación angular del robot.\n\n![V5_Yaw_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_orientation/V5_Yaw_rev2.jpg)\n\n---\n\nElija qué sensor inercial va usar.\n\n![orientation_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_orientation/orientation_included_block.png)\n\nElija qué eje vs usar.\n\n![orientation_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_orientation/orientation_axis.png)\n\nEl bloque sensorial **Orientación de** es usado dentro de bloques con espacio circular.\n\n![orientation_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/inertial_orientation/orientation_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n\n"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Elemento de la lista 2D\n\nInforma el valor de un elemento en una lista 2D.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué lista 2D usar. La lista 2D también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nIngrese la posición de la fila del elemento (primer número) y la columna (segundo número) dentro de la lista que se reportara. Aquí, se informa el elemento en la fila de posición 2, columna 3 en la lista 2D.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nEl bloque **Elemento de la lista 2D** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Artículo de\n\nInforma el valor de un elemento en una lista.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué lista usar. La lista también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nIngrese el número de la posición del elemento dentro de la lista. Aquí, se reporta el segundo elemento de la lista (elemento 2).\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nEl bloque **Artículo de** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá la velocidad de la transmisión al valor almacenado en el elemento 3 de mi lista. El tren motriz ahora avanzará a una velocidad del 90%.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"joint_move":{"name":"joint_move","markdown":"# Movimiento de Junta\n\nMueve el V5 Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico V5) a la coordenada especificada (x, y, z) mediante el movimiento de las juntas.\n\n![joint_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/joint_move/joint_move_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **movimiento de Junta** mueve el Brazo Robótico V5 en la dirección x, y, and z movimiento de la junta. \n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/joint_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nElija qué Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico) usar.\n\n![select_joint_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/joint_move/select_joint_arm.png)\n\nEl bloque **movimiento de junta** acepta decimales, enteros y bloques numéricos.\n\n![joint_input](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/joint_move/joint_input.png)"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Longitud de la lista 2D\n\nInforma el número de filas o columnas en una lista 2D.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué lista 2D usar. La lista 2D también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nElija qué valor informar. La lista 2D puede reportar **filas** o **columnas**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Longitud de la lista 2D** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)\n"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Menos que\n\nReports if the first value is less (smaller) than the second value. \n\n![less_than](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Menos que** reporta **verdadero** cuando el primer valor es menor que el segundo valor. \n\n**Menos que** reporta **falso** cuando el primer valor es mayor o igual que el segundo valor.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Menos que** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\nEl bloque **Menos que** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n"},"linear_move":{"name":"linear_move","markdown":"# Movimiento lineal\n\nMueve el V5 Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico V5) a la coordenada especificada (x, y, z) mediante el movimiento lineal.\n\n![linear_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/linear_move/linear_move_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **movimiento lineal** mueve el V5 Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico V5) en la dirección x, y, and z usando movimiento lineal. \n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/linear_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nElija qué Brazo Robótico usar.\n\n![select_linear_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/linear_move/select_linear_arm.png)\n\nEl bloque **movimiento lineal** acepta decimales, enteros, y bloques numéricos.\n\n![linear_input](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/linear_move/linear_input.png)"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor a terminado\n\nInforma si el motor inteligente V5 seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Motor a terminado** reporta **verdadero** cuando el motor seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\n**Motor a terminado** reporta **verdadero** cuando el motor seleccionado todavía está en movimiento.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Motor a terminado** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor está girando\n\nInforma si el motor inteligente V5 seleccionado está girando actualmente.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Motor está girando** reporta **verdadero** cuando el motor seleccionado está girando.\n\n**Motor está girando** reporta **falso** cuando el motor seleccionado se detiene.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **Motor está girando** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Multiplicar\n\nMultiplica dos valores cualquiera juntos y reporta el resultado.\n\n![multiply](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Multiplicar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque  **Multiplicar** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares, y también pueden aceptar bloques circulares en él.\n\nMultiplica dos números.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nMultiplicar con valores de variables.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nMultiplique con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Siguiente fila \n\nEstablece el cursor de impresión en la pantalla del cerebro V5 o Controlador en la siguiente fila disponible.\n\n![next_row](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## Como utilizar \n\nPor defecto, todos los proyectos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1 columna 1. El bloque **siguiente fila** moverá el cursor hacia abajo, una sola fila en la pantalla  **Siguiente fila** también establecerá la columna del cursor en la posición 1.\n\nElija qué dispositivo usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![next_row_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/next_row/next_row_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Brain le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará el número de filas disponibles en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del cerebro V5 - Numero de Filas:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Filas\n* Small - 16 Filas\n* Medium - 12 Filas (Standard)\n* Large - 8 Filas\n* Extra Large - 6 Filas\n* Super Large - 4 Filas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/next_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nEl controlador V5 no le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del controlador V5 - Numero de Filas:**\n\n* Fuente Standard - 3 filas (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/next_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# No\n\nInforma lo contrario (inverso) del valor booleano reportado.\n\n![not](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/not/not.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **no** reporta **verdadero** cuando el bloque booleano dentro reporta **falso**.\n\nEl bloque **no** reporta **falso** cuando el bloque booleano dentro reporta **verdadero**.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **no** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo reporta **verdadero** cuando no se presione la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![not_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Recuento de objetos\n\nInforma cuántos objetos detecta el sensor de visión.\n\nSerá necesario configurar un objeto antes de que el bloque **recuento de objetos** pueda detectarlo.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué sensor de visión usar.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **foto de** deberá usarse antes de que el bloque **Recuento de objetos** reporte varios objetos.\n\nEl bloque **Recuento de objetos** solo detectará el número de objetos de la última firma de la foto instantánea.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Objeto existe\n\nInforma si el sensor de visión detecta un objeto configurado.\n\nSerá necesario configurar un objeto para que el bloque **Objeto existe** pueda detectarlo.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué sensor de visión usar.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n\n**Objeto existe** reporta **verdadero** cuando el sensor de visión detecta un objeto configurado.\n\n**Objeto existe** reporta **falso** cuando el sensor de visión no detecta un objeto configurado.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Objeto existe** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nEl bloque **foto de**  deberá usarse antes de el bloque Booleano **Objeto existe** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso**."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Objeto encontrado\n\nReporta si el sensor del Buscador de rango ultrasónico ve un objeto dentro de su campo de visión.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Objeto encontrado** reporta **verdadero** cuando el sensor del Buscador de rango ultrasónico ve un objeto o superficie dentro de su campo de visión.\n\n**Objeto encontrado** reporta **falso** cuando el sensor del Buscador de rango ultrasónico no detecta un objeto o superficie.\n\nElija qué sensor del Buscador de rango ultrasónico va usar.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Objeto encontrado** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso**  y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"optical_brightness":{"name":"optical_brightness","markdown":"# Brillo Óptico\n\nInforma de la cantidad de luz detectada por el Optical Sensor (Sensor Óptico).\n\n![optical_brightness](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_brightness/optical_brightness.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nElija un Sensor Óptico para usar.\n\n![optical_brightness_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **brillo óptico** informa de un valor numérico de **0%** a **100%**.\n\nUna gran cantidad de luz detectada reportará un alto valor de brillo.\n\nUna pequeña cantidad de luz detectada reportará un valor bajo de brillo.\n\nEl bloque **brillo óptico** informa de valores numéricos y se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![optical_brightness_use](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect":{"name":"optical_detect","markdown":"# Óptico Detecta Color\n\nReporta si el Optical Sesor (Sensor Óptico) detecta el color especificado.\n\n![optical_detect](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_detect/optical_detect.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija un Optical Sensor (Sensor Óptico) para utilizar.\n\n![optical_detect_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_detect/optical_detect_device.png)\n\nElija el color que desea que compruebe el sensor.\n\n![optical_detect_colors](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_detect/optical_detect_colors.png)\n\nEl bloque **óptico detecta color** reporta **true** cuando el Sensor Óptico detecta el color especificado.\n\nEl bloque **óptico detecta color** reporta **false** si no detecta el color especificado.\n\nEl bloque **óptico detecta color** reporta **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis caras).\n\n![optical_detect_use](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_detect/optical_detect_use.png)\n\n"},"optical_detect_gesture":{"name":"optical_detect_gesture","markdown":"# When Optical detects a gesture \n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the Optical sensor detects a gesture.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **When Optical detects a gesture** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on gestures that the Optical Sensor detects.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor.\n\n\n![optical_detects_gesture_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detects_gesture_device.png)\n\nChoose which gesture triggers the **When Optical detects a gesture** event.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block2.png)\n\n"},"optical_detect_object":{"name":"optical_detect_object","markdown":"# Cuando Óptica detecta/pierde \n\nEjecuta la pila adjunta de bloques cuando el Sensor Óptico detecta o pierde un objeto.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl evento **Cuando Óptica detecta/pierde** se puede utilizar para crear acciones o comportamientos basados en si el Sensor Óptico **detecta** un objeto en el rango del sensor o **pierde** un objeto que estaba en el rango del sensor.\n\nElija un Sensor Óptico.\n\n![optical_detect_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_device.png)\n\nElija si el evento **Cuando Óptica detecta/pierde** se activa cuando el sensor **detecta** un objeto, o **pierde** un objeto.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block2.png)"},"optical_found_object":{"name":"optical_found_object","markdown":"# Óptico Encontro Objeto\n\nReporta si el Optical Sensor (Sensor Óptico) detecta un objeto cercano a él.\n\n\n![optical_found_object](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_found_object/optical_found_object.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija un Sensor Óptico para usar.\n\n![optical_found_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **óptico encontro objeto** reporta **true** cuando el Sensor Óptico detecta un objeto cercano a él.\n\nEl bloque **óptico encontro objeto** reporta **false** si un objeto no está dentro del rango.\n\nEl bloque **óptico encontro objeto** debe utilizarse para comprobar si un objeto está cerca del Sensor Óptico para que las lecturas de color del bloque **óptica detecta color** son precisos.\n\nEl bloque **óptico encontro objeto** reporta **true** o **false** y se utiliza en bloques con espacios hexagonales (de seis lados).\n\n![optical_found_object_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_condition.png)"},"optical_hue":{"name":"optical_hue","markdown":"# Matiz Óptico\n\nInforma del matiz del color de un objeto.\n\n![optical_hue](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_hue/optical_hue.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija un Optical Sensor (Sensor Óptico).\n\n![optical_hue_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_hue/optical_hue_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **matiz óptico** notifica un valor numérico que es el matiz del color de un objeto. Devuelve un número entre **0** y **359**, que se puede considerar como la ubicación del color en la rueda de colores.\n\nEl bloque **matiz óptico** informa valores numéricos y se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![optical_hue_use](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_hue/optical_hue_use.png)"},"optical_set_light":{"name":"optical_set_light","markdown":"# Establecer Luz Óptica\n\nEnciende o apaga la luz del Optical Sensor (Sensor Óptico).\n\n![optical_set_light](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_set_light/optical_set_light.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer luz óptica** le permite encender la luz del Sensor Óptico a **encendido** o **apagado**. The light lets the sensor see objects if it is looking at an object in a dark area.\n\nElija un Optical Sensor (Sensor Óptico) para usar.\n\n![optical_set_light_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_device.png)\n\nElija si desea establecer la luz en el sensor óptico en **encendido** o **apagado**.\n\n![optical_set_light_state](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_state.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, utilizamos el bloque **establecer luz óptica** para encender la luz. Luego, si el sensor óptico detecta un objeto, imprimimos el matiz.\n\n\n![optical_set_light_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_example.png)"},"optical_set_light_power":{"name":"optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Establecer Potencia de luz Óptica \n\nAjuste la potencia de luz del V5 Optical sensor (Sensor Óptico V5).\n\n![optical_set_light_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_light_power_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer potencia de luz óptica** acepta un rango de **0%** a **100%**. Esto cambiará el brillo de la luz en el Sensor Óptico. Si la luz está apagada, este bloque encenderá la luz.\n\nElija un Optical Sensor (Sensor Óptico) .\n\n![optical_set_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_device.png)\n\nEl bloque de **establecer potencia de luz óptica** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![optical_set_power_num](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_num.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo usamos el bloque **establecer potencia de luz óptica** para establecer la potencia de la luz en **50%**, luego usamos el bloque **establecer luz óptica** para encender la luz. A continuación, si el Sensor Óptico detecta un objeto, imprimimos el matiz.\n\n![optical_set_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_example.png)"},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# O\n\nInforma si una de las dos condiciones booleanas es verdadera.\n\n![or](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/or/or.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **verdadero** cuando una (o ambas) condiciones son **verdadero**. \n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **falso** cuando ambas condiciones son **falso**.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **o** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y encaja en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **verdadero** cuando se presiona el sensor Bumper y / o el brillo del sensor de luz es superior al 50%.\n\nEl bloque **o** reporta **falso** solo cuando el sensor Bumper no está presionado y el brillo del sensor de luz es menor o igual al 50%\n\n![or_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/or/or_truth.png)"},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Posición del controlador\n\nInforma la posición de un joystick en el controlador V5 a lo largo de un eje.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Posición del controlador** reporta rango de **-100 a 100**.\n\n**Posición del controlador** informará cero (0) cuando el eje de un joystick esté centrado.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nElija el controlador V5 para usar.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_devices.png)\n\nElija el eje del joystick para verificar su posición.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Posición del controlador** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Posición del motor\n\nReporta la distancia que ha recorrido el motor inteligente V5.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Posición del motor** informa la posición del motor inteligente V5 en números enteros para grados y números decimales para giros.\n\nElija qué motor inteligente V5 va usar.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nElija si el valor se informa en grados rotados o en vueltas del motor inteligente V5.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Posición del motor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"position_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"position_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Posición del codificador de eje\n\nReporta la distancia que ha girado el codificador de eje.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Posición del codificador de eje** reporta la distancia que ha girado el codificador de eje en números enteros para grados y números decimales para giros.\n\nElija qué codificador de eje usar.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_device.png)\n\nElija si el valor se informa en grados rotados o en turnos del codificador de eje.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Posición del codificador de eje** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_inserted.png)"},"power":{"name":"power","markdown":"# Establecer Potencia Electromagnética\n\nEstablece la potencia del V5 Electromagnet (electroimán) que se utilizará al recoger un objeto con el bloque energizado.\n\n![set_magnet_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/power/set_magnet_power_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEs posible que necesite recoger objetos con diferentes pesos. El bloque **establecer potencia electromagnética** le permite controlar cuánta energía utilizará el elctroimán. El bloque **establecer potencia electromagnética** tiene un rango de **0% to 100%**\n\nElija el imán que desea utilizar.\n\n![set_magnet_dropdown_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/power/set_magnet_dropdown_block.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá el robot para conducir hacia adelante 200 mm, luego aumentará la potencia usando el bloque **establecer potencia electromagnética**, luego el **elctroimán** elevara para recoger un objeto, conducir hacia adelante 200mm, luego soltar el objeto.\n\n![set_magnet_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/power/set_magnet_power_example.png)\n"},"power_of_motor":{"name":"power_of_motor","markdown":"# Poder del motor\n\nReporta la cantidad de poder de salida que genera actualmente el motor inteligente V5.\n\n![motor_power](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/power_of_motor/motor_power.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Poder del motor** reporta un rango de **0.0 a 11.0 watts**. \n\nElija un motor para usar.\n\n![motor_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/power_of_motor/motor_power_device.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Poder del motor** y se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![motor_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/power_of_motor/motor_power_inserted.png)\n"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Presionar bumper\n\nReporta si se presiona el bumper.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Como utilizar \n\n**Presionar bumper** reporta **verdadero** si se presiona el bumper.\n\n**Presionar bumper** reporta **falso** si no se presiona el bumper.\n\nElija qué bumper va usar.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Presionar bumper** reporta **verdadero** o **falso** valor y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Presionando Controlador\n\nInforma si se presiona un botón en el controlador V5.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Presionando Controlador** reporta **verdadero** si se presiona el botón Controlador que es seleccionado.\n\n**Presionando Controlador** reporta **falso** si no se presiona el botón Controlador que es seleccionado.\n\nElija qué controlador V5 va usar.\n\n![pressing_controller_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_device.png)\n\nElija qué botón del controlador va usar.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nEl bloque booleano **Presionando Controlador** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)"},"pressing_limit":{"name":"pressing_limit","markdown":"# Límite de presion\n\nInforma si se presiona el interruptor de límite.\n\n![pressing_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/pressing_limit/pressing_limit.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Límite de presion** reporta **verdadero** si se presiona el interruptor de límite.\n\n**Límite de presion** reporta **falso** si no se presiona el interruptor de límite.\n\nElija qué interruptor de límite usar.\n\n![pressing_limit_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_bumper.png)\n\nEl bloque Booleano **Límite de presion** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![pressing_limit_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_inserted.png)\n "},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Impresión\n\nImprime valores o texto en la pantalla del Cerebro V5 o Controlador.\n\n![look_print](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/print/look_print.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Impresión** imprimirá los datos en la ubicación del cursor en la pantalla.\n\nTodos los proyectos nuevos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1, columna 1.\n\nTodos los bloques que reportan se imprimirán como números enteros. Use el bloque **establecer precisión de impresión** para ajustar la cantidad de decimales impresos.\n\nElija qué dispositivo a usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana Dispositivos.\n\n![look_print_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/print/look_print_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nImprime palabras y números.\n\n![print_words](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/print/print_words.png)\n\nImprima el valor informado de un variable.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nImprimir el cálculo reportado de un operador.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nImprima el valor informado desde un sensor o dispositivo.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Mis bloques\n\nMis bloques se usan para crear bloques personalizados.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Mis bloques** se usan para crear una secuencia de bloques que se pueden usar varias veces a lo largo de un proyecto. \n\n**Mis bloques** son creados usando el boton **Make a Block**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Mis bloques** pueden tener múltiples parámetros (etiquetas de texto, variables numéricas y variables booleanas) para agregar más funcionalidad a su bloque personalizado.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nPara usar **Mi bloque**, adjunta el llamado **Mi bloque** a un bloque de sombrero. Cuando el **Mi bloque** se alcanza en un proyecto, la acomulacion dentro de  **Mi bloque** se ejecutará utilizando los valores de los parámetros especificados.\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nAdjunte una acomulacion de bloques a la **Mis bloques* \"define\" el bloque de sombrero para establecer la acción que ocurre cuando se usa un **Mi bloque**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Nota: Crear múltiples Mis Bloques con las mismas etiquetas y variables puede causar errores al descargar su proyecto.***\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **Mis bloques** para:\n\n* Conduzca hacia adelante por 15 pulgadas\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del cerebro\n* Gira el robot 180 grados a la derecha\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del cerebro\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Mis bloques\n\nMis bloques se usan para crear bloques personalizados.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Mis bloques** se usan para crear una secuencia de bloques que se pueden usar varias veces a lo largo de un proyecto. \n\n**Mis bloques** son creados usando el boton **Make a Block**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Mis bloques** pueden tener múltiples parámetros (etiquetas de texto, variables numéricas y variables booleanas) para agregar más funcionalidad a su bloque personalizado.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nPara usar **Mi bloque**, adjunta el llamado **Mi bloque** a un bloque de sombrero. Cuando el **Mi bloque** se alcanza en un proyecto, la acomulacion dentro de  **Mi bloque** se ejecutará utilizando los valores de los parámetros especificados.\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nAdjunte una acomulacion de bloques a la **Mis bloques* \"define\" el bloque de sombrero para establecer la acción que ocurre cuando se usa un **Mi bloque**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Nota: Crear múltiples Mis Bloques con las mismas etiquetas y variables puede causar errores al descargar su proyecto.***\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el robot usará **Mis bloques** para:\n\n* Conduzca hacia adelante por 15 pulgadas\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del cerebro\n* Gira el robot 180 grados a la derecha\n* Imprime la capacidad de la batería y también mueve el cursor a una nueva línea en la pantalla del cerebro\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Aleatorio\nInforma un valor aleatorio entre los valores más bajos y más altos en el bloque.\n\n![random](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/random/random.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Aleatorio** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\nEl bloque **Aleatorio** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplos\n\nEste ejemplo usa un bloque **Aleatorio** para aleatorizar la velocidad de la transmisión.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nEste ejemplo usa un bloque **Aleatorio** para aleatorizar la longitud de un bloque de espera.\n\n![random_control](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"reflectivity_of":{"name":"reflectivity_of","markdown":"# Reflexividad de\n\nInforma la cantidad de luz reflejada con el sensor rastreador de línea.\n\n![reflectivity_of](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nLas superficies de color claro reflejarán más luz e informarán un alto valor de reflectividad.\n\nLas superficies de color oscuro reflejarán menos luz e informarán un valor de reflectividad bajo.\n\n**Reflexividad de** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija qué sensor rastreador de línea va usar.\n\n![reflectivity_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_color.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Reflexividad de** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![reflectivity_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n\n"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Recordatorio\n\nDivide el primer valor por el segundo valor e informa el resto.\n\n![remainder](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Recordatorio** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nLos números que se dividen en partes iguales reportarán un resultado de cero.\n\nLa longitud del bloque **Recordatorio** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo dividirá 7 y 2 e informará el resto para imprimir \"1\" en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Repetir\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques contenidos dentro por un número determinado de veces.\n\n![repeat](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nPrimero ingrese un valor para indicar cuántas veces la acumulación va a **Repetir** los bloques contenidos dentro. \n\nEl bloque 'C' **Repetir**  puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nBloques 'C' también se pueden poner uno dentro del otro. Este concepto se llama anidamiento (nesting) y puede ayudar a ahorrar tiempo al programar diferentes comportamientos.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/repeat/repeat_select.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Repetir hasta\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques dentro hasta que se informa que la condición booleana es **verdadera**.  \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Repetir hasta** solo verificará la condición booleana al comienzo de cada ciclo. \n\nSi la condición booleana se informa como **falso**, los bloques dentro **Repetir hasta** seran ejecutados.\n\nSi la condición booleana se informa como **verdadero**, los bloques dentro **Repetir hasta** seran ejecutados.\n\nEl bloque 'C' **Repetir hasta** puede aceptar bloques con forma hexagonal (seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Restablecer temporizador\n\nRestablece el temporizador del cerebro V5.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl temporizador del cerebro comienza al iniciar cada proyecto. El bloque **Restablecer temporizador** se usa para restablecer el temporizador a 0 segundos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el temporizador se reiniciará antes de mover el tren motriz hacia adelante durante 3 segundos. Después de que hayan transcurrido 3 segundos, el tren motriz se detendrá.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_angle":{"name":"rotation_angle","markdown":"# Angulo de Rotación\n\nInforma el ángulo de rotación actual de un V5 Rotation Sensor (Sensor de Rotación V5) en grados.\n\n![rotation_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **angulo de rotación** notifica valores en el rango de **0.00** a **359.99**.\n\nEl bloque **angulo de rotación** informará de valores crecientes o decrecientes a medida que el Sensor de Rotación gire.\n\nElija el Sensor de Rotación del que desea obtener los valores.\n\n![rotation_angle_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block2.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **angulo de rotación** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![rotation_angle_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block3.png)\n"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Ángulo de rotación\n\nInforma el ángulo de rotación actual del sensor giroscópico de 3 ejes o del sensor inercial V5 en grados.\n\n![rotation_position.png](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Rotación giroscópica** reporta un valor **positivo**  cuando el Sensor giroscopico gira en la dirección **en sentido de las agujas del reloj**.\n\n**Rotación giroscópica** reporta **negativo** cuando el Sensor giroscopico gira en la dirección **en contra de las agujas del reloj**.\n\nElija qué sensor giroscópico / sensor de inercia para verificar.\n\n![rotation_position_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_devices.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **Rotación giroscópica** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![rotation_position_inserted.png](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_inserted.png)\n"},"rotation_position":{"name":"rotation_position","markdown":"# Posición de Rotación \n\nInforma de la posición de rotación actual del V5 Rotation Sensor (Sensor de Rotación V5) seleccionado.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_position/rotation_position_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n**Posición de Rotación** informa de la posición de un V5 Rotation Sensor (Sensor de Rotación V5) en números enteros para grados y números decimales para giros.\n\nElija qué V5 Rotation Sensor (Sensor de Rotación V5) utilizar.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_position/rotation_position_block2.png)\n\nElija si el valor se notifica en grados girados o en vueltas del Sensor de Rotación V5.\n\n![rotation_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_position/rotation_position_block3.png)\n\nEl bloque reportero **posición de rotación** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![rotation_position_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_position/rotation_position_block4.png)\n"},"rotation_set_position":{"name":"rotation_set_position","markdown":"# Establecer Posición \n\nEstablece la posición actual de un V5 Rotation Sensor (Sensor de Rotación V5) en un valor definido.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer posición** se puede utilizar para establecer la posición de un Rotation Sensor (Sensor de Rotación).\n\nEste bloque se utiliza normalmente para restablecer la posición del Rotaion Sensor (Sensor de Rotación) cuando el valor se establece en 0.\n\nEl bloque **establecer posición** puede aceptar decimales, enteros, o bloques numéricos como entrada.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block3.png)\n\nElija qué Sensor de Rotación utilizar y, a continuación, introduzca el valor de posición deseado.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block2.png)\n"},"rotation_velocity":{"name":"rotation_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad de Rotación\n\nInforma de la velocidad actual de un V5 Rotation Sensor (Sensor de Rotación V5).\n\n![rotation_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el V5 Rotation Sensor (Sensor de Rotación V5) del que desea obtener los valores.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block2.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad se notifica en porcentaje (%), revoluciones por minuto (rpm) or grados por segundo (dps).\n\n![rotation_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block3.png)\n\nLa velocidad del bloque reportero de rotación se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block4.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Redondear\n\nRedondea el valor ingresado al entero más cercano.\n\n![round](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/round/round.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nDecimales que son 0.5 o más seran **redondear** de mas, y decimales menos de 0.5 **redondear** de menos.\n\nEl bloque **redondear** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares, y también pueden aceptar bloques circulares en ellos.\n\nEl bloque **redondear** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo redondeará 2.7 e imprimirá \"3\".\n\n![round_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"screen_position":{"name":"screen_position","markdown":"# Posición de la pantalla\n\nInforma la ubicación del último toque detectado en la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\n![screen_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/screen_position/screen_position_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Posición de la pantalla** se utiliza para capturar la ubicación X/Y de la última pulsación en la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5. Este bloque de informe se puede utilizar para crear interactividad entre el V5 y el usuario final.\n\n**Posición de la pantalla** reporta un rango de **0 to 480 pixels** cuando se establece para reportar la coordenada **X**.\n\n**Posición de la pantalla** reporta un rango de **0 to 240 pixels** cuando se establece para reportar la coordenada **Y**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/screen_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\nElija qué eje reportar.\n\n![screen_position_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/screen_position/screen_position_value.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **Posición de la pantalla** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![screen_position_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/screen_position/screen_position_inserted.png)"},"screen_pressed":{"name":"screen_pressed","markdown":"# Pantalla presionada\n\nInforma si actualmente se está presionando la pantalla táctil del V5 Brain.\n\n![screen_pressed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque booleano **pantalla presionada** puede ser utilizado junto con **posición de pantalla** para detectar cuándo y dónde se ha producido un toque en la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\n**Pantalla presionada** reporta **verdadero** cuando se presiona la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\n**Pantalla presionada** reporta **falso** cuando no se presiona la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\nEl bloque Booleano **screen pressed** reporta un valor **verdadero** o **falso** y se usa en bloques con espacios hexagonales (seis lados).\n\n![screen_pressed_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Establecer lista 2D\n\nEstablece cada elemento en la lista 2D a los valores ingresados.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nAl crear una lista 2D, puede establecer el número de **columnas** de la lista entre 1 a 10 elementos y el número de **filas** de la lista entre 1 a 10 artículos.\n\nElija qué lista 2D va usar. La lista 2D también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer lista 2D** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Establecer lista en\n\nEstablece cada elemento de la lista a los valores ingresados.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nAl crear una lista, puede establecer la longitud de la lista entre 1 y 10 elementos.\n\nElija qué lista usar. La lista también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer lista en**  puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá la lista en valores iniciales, y luego informará el elemento #3 (90) de la lista, para establecer la posición del Brazo.\n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Establecer variable booleano\n\nEstablece un variable booleano en un valor dado.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué variable booleano va usar. Los variables booleanos también se pueden renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nElija un valor booleano.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nEl bloque **Establecer variable booleano** puede aceptar bloques de forma hexagonal (seis lados).\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# Establecer cursor\n\nEstablece la ubicación del cursor para el bloque **impresión** en la pantalla V5 Brain o Controller.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEstablezca la posición de la fila y columna del cursor para sea mostrado un comando de **impresión** en una ubicación específica en la pantalla.\n\n**Establecer cursor** acepta un rango para **fila** de **1 a 20**.\n\n**Establecer cursor** acepta un rango para **columna** de **1 a 80**.\n\nElija qué dispositivo usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![set_cursor_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_cursor/set_cursor_dropdown.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer cursor** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n---\n\nEl cerebro V5 le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará el número de columnas disponibles en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del cerebro V5 - Numero de Filas**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Filas\n* Small - 16 Filas\n* Medium - 12 Filas (Default)\n* Large - 8 Filas\n* Extra Large - 6 Filas\n* Super Large - 4 Filas\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del cerebro V5 - Numbero de Columnas:**\n\n* Extra Small - 80 Columnas\n* Small - 68 Columnas\n* Medium - 48 Columnas (Default)\n* Large - 32 Columnas\n* Extra Large - 24 Columnas\n* Super Large - 16 Columnas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nEl controlador V5 no le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del controlador V5 - Numbero de Filas:**\n\n* Fuente Estandar - 3 Filas (Default)\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del controlador V5 - Numbero de Columnas:**\n\n* Fuente Estandar - 20 Columnas (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"set_digital_out":{"name":"set_digital_out","markdown":"# Digital out\n\nSets the logic level of a digital out 3-Wire port.\n\n![digital_out_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_digital_out/digital_out_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 3-Wire ports function at a 5V logic signal voltage level.\n\nThe **digital out** block sets the digital signal to output a high or low logic signal.\n\nChoose which digital out port to use. \n\n![digital_out_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_digital_out/digital_out_select.png)\n\nChoose to output a high or low digital logic signal.\n\n![digital_out_choose](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_digital_out/digital_out_choose.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Establecer direccion de unidad\n\nEstablece el valor de direccion del Giroscopio en el tren motriz.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Establecer direccion de unidad** se puede usar para establecer la posición del tren motriz en cualquier direccion dada. Este bloque se puede usar para restablecer la orientación del giroscopio del tren motriz cuando la direccion se establece en un valor de 0.\n\n**Establecer direccion de unidad** acepta un rango de **0 a 360** grados.\n\nEl bloque **Establecer direccion de unidad** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer la rotación del chasis\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del chasis.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** bloque se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del chasis a cualquier valor positivo o negativo dado.\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** bloque puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el robot un total de 210 grados:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Da veulta a la derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) para girar 120 grados.\n- Establezca la posición actual del robot como rotación de -45 grados.\n- Da veulta a la derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) 90 grados adicionales (-45 grados a 45 grados) en función del valor de rotación establecido del bloque anterior.\n"},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Configurar parada de la unidad\n\nEstablece el comportamiento del tren motriz una vez que deja de moverse.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n* **Brake** El tren motriz se detiene inmediatamente y no corregirá a fuerzas externas.\n* **Coast** Deja que el tren motriz gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* **Hold** El tren motriz se detiene inmediatamente y lo devuelve a su posición donde se detuvo si lo mueve una fuerza externa, utilizando el codificador incorporado.\n* \n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el tren motriz avance durante 3 segundos y luego mantenga su posición una vez que se detenga.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer tiempo de espera\n\nEstablece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del tren motriz.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl límite de tiempo del tren motriz se usa para evitar que los bloques de unidades que no alcanzan su posición eviten que otros bloques en la acumulación se ejecuten.\n\nUn ejemplo de un tren motriz que no alcanza su posición es cuando un robot es conducido contra una pared y no puede completar su movimiento.\n\nEl bloque **Establecer tiempo de espera** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo finalizará el comando **conducir** después de 2 segundos si el tren motriz no ha alcanzado el objetivo de 24 pulgadas. Una vez que se alcanza el límite de tiempo o la distancia, el tren motriz pasará al comando **girar**.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer velocidad\n\nEstablece la velocidad del tren motriz.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Establecer velocidad** establecerá la velocidad del tren motriz, pero no hará que el tren motriz se mueva. Todavía se requiere el bloque **conducir**.\n\n**Establecer velocidad** reporta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\n**Establecer velocidad** acepta un rango de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los motores inteligentes V5, utilizados en el tren motriz.\n\n* Cartucho Rojo: -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Cartucho Verde: -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Cartucho Azul: -600rpm a 600rpm\n\nEstablecer la velocidad del tren motriz en un valor negativo hará que el tren motriz se mueva en reversa.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad del tren motriz a 0 hará que el tren motriz se detenga.\n\nEl bloque **establecer velocidad** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija la unidad de medida.\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n\n"},"set_fill_color":{"name":"set_fill_color","markdown":"# Establecer color de relleno\n\nEstablece el color que llena las formas dibujadas en la pantalla V5 Brain.\n\n![set_fill_color_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Establecer color de relleno** se utiliza para establecer el color del interior de los círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del cerebro V5. \n\nElige un color de relleno.\n\n![set_fill_color_color](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_color.png)  \n\nEl color de relleno se usará para cualquier objeto futuro dibujado en la pantalla del cerebro V5."},"set_font":{"name":"set_font","markdown":"# Establecer fuente\n\nEstablece el estilo y el tamaño de la fuente utilizada en la pantalla del cerebro V5 al imprimir números o texto.\n\n![set_font_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_font/set_font_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nHay dos tipos diferentes de fuentes disponibles en la pantalla V5 Brain:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - cada letra ocupa el mismo ancho.\n* Proporcional (Prop) - cada letra ocupa diferentes anchos de tamaño según el personaje.\n\nElija qué tipo de fuente y tamaño usar.\n\n![set_font_block_font](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_font/set_font_block_font.png)  \n\nEl nuevo tamaño de fuente se utilizará para cualquier texto futuro escrito en la pantalla del cerebro V5."},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Establecer direccion del giroscópio\n\nEstablece la posición actual del sensor giroscópico (gyro) en el valor dentro del bloque de comandos.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer direccion del giroscópio** se puede usar para establecer la posición del giroscopio en cualquier direccion en el sentido de las agujas del reloj. Este bloque se usa típicamente para restablecer la orientación del giroscopio cuando el encabezado se establece en un valor de 0.\n\n**establecer direccion del giroscópio** acepta un rango de **0.0 a 359.99** grados.\n\nEl bloque **establecer direccion del giroscópio** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija qué sensor giroscópico va usar, luego ingrese el valor deseado.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer la rotación del chasis\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del chasis.\n\n![setdriverotation](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** bloque se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del chasis a cualquier valor positivo o negativo dado.\n\n![setdriverotation](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation_devices.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer la rotación del chasis** bloque puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Reemplazar elemento de lista 2D\n\nActualiza un elemento en la lista 2D a un nuevo valor.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nIngrese la posición de la fila del artículo (primer número) y la columna (segundo número) dentro de la lista a ser reemplazada.\n\nElija qué lista usar. La lista también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **Reemplazar elemento** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Reemplazar artículo\n\nActualiza un elemento de la lista a un nuevo valor.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nActualiza un elemento de la lista a un nuevo valor. Elija qué lista usar. La lista también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nEl bloque **Reemplazar artículo** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n"},"set_joint_move_speed":{"name":"set_joint_move_speed","markdown":"# Establecer la velocidad de la junta\n\nEstablece la velocidad de los movimientos articulares del V5 Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico V5).\n\n![joint_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija qué Brazo Robótico utilizar.\n\n![select_joint_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_joint_move_speed/select_joint_speed_arm.png)\n\nElija la velocidad de los movimientos de las articulaciones del V5 Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico V5). La velocidad predeterminada es **normal**.\n\n![joint_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_select.png)"},"set_led":{"name":"set_led","markdown":"# Establecer LED\n\nEnciende o apaga un LED.\n\n![set_led_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_led/set_led_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nSeleccione qué LED usar.\n\n![set_led_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_led/set_led_block_device.png)\n\nSeleccione si el LED está encendido o apagado.\n\n![set_led_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_led/set_led_block_setting.png)\n\n"},"set_linear_move_speed":{"name":"set_linear_move_speed","markdown":"# Establecer velocidad lineal\n\nEstablece la velocidad de los movimientos lineales del V5 Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico V5).\n\n![linear_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija qué Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico) usar.\n\n![select_linear_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_linear_move_speed/select_linear_speed_arm.png)\n\nElija la velocidad de los movimientos lineales del V5 Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico V5). La velocidad predeterminada es **normal**.\n\n![linear_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_select.png)"},"set_mastering":{"name":"set_mastering","markdown":"# Establecer Calibración\n\nEstablece los valores de calibración de las cuatro juntas del V5 Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico V5) para permitir su calibración en la misma ubicación conocida.\n\n![set_mastering_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_mastering/set_mastering_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nIntroduzca los valores de calibración del cerebro V5 al bloque **establecer calibración** . \n\nLos valores de umbral pasables para las juntas son los siguientes:\n\n* Junta 1: 1600 - 2000\n* Junta 2: 1900 - 2400\n* Junta 3: 1700 - 2100\n* Junta 4: 200 - 650\n\n![mastering_values](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_mastering/mastering_values.png)\n\nElija qué Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico) usar.\n\n![select_mastering_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_mastering/select_mastering_arm.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer calibración** acepta enteros y bloques numéricos.\n\n![mastering_input](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_mastering/mastering_input.png)"},"set_motor_controller_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_controller_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer la velocidad del controlador del motor\n\nEstablece la velocidad de un Motor 393 conectado a un Controlador de Motor 29.\n\n![set_motor_controller_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Establecer la velocidad del controlador del motor** accepts a range of **-100% to 100%**.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad del Motor 393 en un valor negativo hará que el Motor 393 gire en reversa.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de un Motor 393 en 0 hará que el Motor 393 se detenga.\n\nElija qué Motor 393 usar.\n\n![set_motor_controller_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_motor.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Establecer la posición del motor\n\nEstablece la posición del codificador del motor inteligente V5 en el valor dado.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **posición del motor** se puede usar para establecer la posición del motor en cualquier valor dado.\n\nGeneralmente, el bloque **posición del motor** se utiliza para establecer la posición en 0 para restablecer la posición del codificador del motor.\n\nElija qué motor inteligente V5 usar.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nElija la unidad de medida en grados o vueltas.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Establecer parada del motor\n\nEstablece el comportamiento del motor inteligente V5 una vez que deja de moverse.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n* **Brake** hará que el motor se detenga inmediatamente.\n* **Coast** deja que el motor gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* **Hold** hará que el motor se detenga inmediatamente y lo devuelva a su posición de parada si se mueve.\n\nEl bloque **establecer parada del motor** surtirá efecto para todos los comandos de motor futuros para el resto del proyecto.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nElija la configuración del motor después de que se detenga.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el motor del brazo avance 90 grados y luego resistirá las fuerzas externas (como la gravedad) para mantener su posición.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer tiempo de espera del motor\n\nEstablece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del motor inteligente V5.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl límite de tiempo del motor se usa para evitar que los bloques de movimiento que no alcanzan su posición eviten que otros bloques en la acumulación se ejecuten. Un ejemplo de un motor que no alcanza su posición es un brazo o una garra que alcanza su límite mecánico y no puede completar su movimiento.\n\nEl bloque **establecer el tiempo de espera del motor** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo finalizará el comando **establecer motor** después de 2 segundos si el motor de garra no ha alcanzado la posición de 270 grados. Una vez que se alcanza el límite de tiempo o el objetivo, el motor de garra se moverá a la posición 0 grados.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Establecer torque del motor\n\nEstablece la fuerza del motor inteligente V5.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Establecer torque del motor** acepta un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer torque del motor** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el motor de la garra a la posición de 40 grados con solo un par máximo del 20%. Esto permite que la garra agarre un objeto sin dañarlo con demasiada fuerza.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer velocidad del motor\n\nEstablece la velocidad de un motor inteligente V5.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Establecer velocidad del motor** acepta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\n**Establecer velocidad del motor** aceptará un valor de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los motores inteligentes V5 utilizados en la transmisión.\n\n* Cartridge Rojo: -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Cartridge Verde: -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Cartridge Azul: -600rpm a 600rpm\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de un motor inteligente V5 en un valor negativo hará que el motor gire en reversa.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de un motor inteligente V5 en 0 hará que el motor se detenga.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad se establece en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo configurará el motor del brazo para girar lentamente a una velocidad del 25% a la posición de 90 grados.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_origin":{"name":"set_origin","markdown":"# Set origin position\n\nSets the origin to the current location of the end of arm tooling.\n\n![set_origin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_origin/set_origin_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, the origin on the Workcell is located in the center of the turntable.\n![turntable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_origin/turntable.png)\n\nThe **set origin position** block sets the origin to the current location of the end of arm tooling.\n\nThe end of arm tooling can be set to:\n\n* None\n* Marker (shown in image)\n* Electromagnet \n\n![marker](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_origin/marker.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![set_origin_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_origin/set_origin_insert.png)"},"set_pen_color":{"name":"set_pen_color","markdown":"# Establecer color de bolígrafo\n\nEstablece el color de las líneas dibujadas en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer color de bolígrafo** se usa para establecer el color de las líneas, los píxeles y el texto dibujado en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n**establecer color de bolígrafo** también se utilizará para establecer el color del contorno de los círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\nElige un color de bolígrafo.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_dropdown.png)  \n\nEl color del lápiz se usará para cualquier objeto futuro dibujado en la pantalla del cerebro V5."},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Establecer precisión de impresión\n\nEstablece el número de dígitos que aparecen después del punto decimal al imprimir bloques que reportan en la pantalla V5 Brain o Controller.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija el nivel de precisión que los bloques que reportan que se imprimirán en la pantalla.\n\n* Enteros (1) (Default)\n* Decimas (0.1)\n* Centésimas (0.01)\n* Milésimas (0.001)\n* Todos los Digitos (0.000001)\n\nLos bloques que reportan impresos en la pantalla se redondearán al nivel de precisión más cercano. Por ejemplo, 1.67 se imprimirá como 2 con precisión y 1.7 con precisión de décimas.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)\n\nElija qué dispositivo usar. Los controladores V5 solo aparecerán si se agregan en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![print_precision_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_print_precision/print_precision_device.png)"},"set_shaft_encoder_position":{"name":"set_shaft_encoder_position","markdown":"# Establecer la posición del codificador del eje\n\nEstablece la posición del codificador de eje en el valor dado.\n\n![set_encoder_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer la posición del codificador del eje** se puede usar para establecer la posición del codificador de eje en cualquier valor dado.\n\nGeneralmente, el bloque **establecer la posición del codificador del eje** se utiliza para establecer la posición en 0, para restablecer la posición del codificador de eje.\n\nElija qué codificador de eje utilizar, luego establezca el valor deseado.\n\n![set_encoder_position_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_motor.png)\n\n"},"set_tool":{"name":"set_tool","markdown":"# Establecer Herramienta\n\nEstablece el mecanismo externo o las herramientas de extremo del brazo (EOAT) en el brazo robótico V5.\n\n![set_tool_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_tool/set_tool_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl mecanismo externo en del V5 Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico V5) no puede ser ninguno (sin fijación), un electroimán o un marcador. \n\n![set_marker](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_tool/set_marker.png)\n\nElija qué Robotic Arm (Brazo Robótico) usar.\n\n![select_tool_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_tool/select_tool_arm.png)\n\nElige la herramienta de tu (V5 Robotic Arm) Brazo Robótico V5. El valor por defecto se establece en **ninguno**.\n\n![choose_tool](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_tool/choose_tool.png)"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer velocidad de giro\n\nEstablece la velocidad de los giros de la transmisión.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Establecer velocidad de giro** establecerá la velocidad del tren motriz, pero no hará que el tren motriz se mueva. Todavía se requiere un bloque **girar**.\n\n**Establecer velocidad de giro** acepta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\n**Establecer velocidad de giro** aceptará un valor de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los motores inteligentes V5 utilizados en la transmisión.\n\n*  Cartucho Rojo: -100rpm q 100rpm\n*  Cartucho Verde: -200rpm q 200rpm\n*  Cartucho Azul: -600rpm q 600rpm\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de giro de un tren motriz en un valor negativo hará que el tren motriz gire en la dirección opuesta.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de giro del tren motriz en 0 hará que el tren motriz se detenga.\n\nEl bloque **Establecer velocidad de giro** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\nEste ejemplo hará que el tren motriz gire lentamente, a una velocidad del 25%, hacia la izquierda.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Establecer variable\n\nEstablece una variable a un valor dado.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué variable usar. Las variables también se pueden renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nEl bloque **Establecer variable** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Establecer objeto de visión\n\nEstablece el elemento del objeto (objeto sobre el que desea obtener más información) fuera del número de objetos detectados.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **recuento de objetos** se puede usar antes del bloque **establecer objeto de visión** para determinar la cantidad de objetos detectados.\n\nElija qué sensor de visión usar.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nEl bloque **establecer objeto de visión** puede aceptar enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n\n"},"set_width":{"name":"set_width","markdown":"# Establecer ancho de bolígrafo\n\nEstablece el ancho del contorno de las formas dibujadas en la pantalla V5 Brain.\n\n![set_width_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_width/set_width_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nEl bloque **establecer ancho** se utiliza para establecer el ancho de la línea en el exterior de los círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del cerebro V5.\n\nEl bloque **establecer ancho** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/set_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"setangle":{"name":"setangle","markdown":"# Set angle\n\nSets the angle of the tool plate before the next [Linear move] or [Joint move] block is executed.\n\n![set_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/setangle/set_angle_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set angle** block sets the tool plate to be tilted at an angle either **up** or **down** before the next [Linear move] or [Joint move] block in a project. \n\nNote that the **set angle** block sets the angle for all future [Linear move] and [Joint move] blocks, unless it is set otherwise.\n\n![tool_plate](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/setangle/tool_plate.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_set_angle_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/setangle/select_set_angle_arm.png)\n\nChoose the angle of the tool plate. The default is set to **up**.\n\n* The tool plate will be **horizontal** when it is set to **down**. \n* The tool plate will be **vertical** when it is set to **up**. \n\n![select_angle](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/setangle/select_angle.png)\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the tool plate will begin to tilt once the [Joint move] block is executed and complete its tilting movement before the [Linear move] block.\n\n![set_angle_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/setangle/set_angle_example.png)"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Longitud de la lista\n\nInforma el número de elementos en una lista.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué lista usar. La lista también se puede renombrar o eliminar.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **longitud de la lista** encaja en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)\n"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# foto\n\nToma una foto instantánea del sensor de visión.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **foto** capturará la imagen actual del Sensor de visión para procesarla y analizarla en busca de firmas y códigos de color. \n\nTípicamente, una **foto** se requiere primero antes de usar cualquier otro bloque del sensor de visión.\n\nSeleccione qué sensor de visión va usar.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nSeleccione qué firma de visión va usar. Las firmas de visión se configuran desde la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Girar\n\nHace girar un motor inteligente V5 hasta que se detiene.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **girar** ejecuta para siempre, hasta que se use un nuevo bloque de motor o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija qué motor va usar.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nElija en qué dirección girar. Los nombres de dirección se pueden cambiar en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Girar por\n\nHace girar un motor inteligente V5 por una distancia determinada.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Girar por** le indicará a un Motor que avanze en una dirección determinada, a una distancia determinada, desde donde se encuentra actualmente.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nElija en qué dirección girar. Los nombres de dirección se pueden cambiar en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nEl bloque **girar por**  puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nElija la unidad de medida en grados o vueltas.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques **esperarán** hasta que el motor termine de moverse.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el motor se mueve.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)\n"},"spin_motor_controller":{"name":"spin_motor_controller","markdown":"# Controlador de motor de giro\n\nHace girar un motor 393 conectado a un controlador de motor 29 hasta que se detiene.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **girar** ejecutará un Motor 393 para siempre hasta que se use un nuevo bloque de motor o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija qué Motor 393 va usar.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_motor.png)\n\nElige en qué dirección girar. Los nombres de dirección se pueden cambiar en la ventana de Dispositivos.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_direction.png)"},"spin_servo":{"name":"spin_servo","markdown":"# Girar servo\n\nGira un servomotor a una posición establecida.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_servo/servo_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Girar servo** acepta un rango de posición de **0 a 180 grados**.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_servo/servo_port.png)\n\n"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Girar a la posición\n\nGira un motor inteligente V5 a una posición establecida.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Girar a la posición** le dirá a el motor que viaje a una posición específica. Basado en la posición actual del motor, **girar a la posición** determinará la dirección para girar.\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque **girar a la posición** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\npuede elegir la unidad de medida en grados o vueltas.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques **esperar** hasta que el motor termine de moverse.\n\nPuedes seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el motor se mueve.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Dejar de conducir\n\nDetiene la transmisión.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dejar de conducir** hará que el tren motriz se detenga por completo y use la funcion **configurar parada de la unidad** para detenerse, frenar o mantener su posición.\n\n## Example\n\nEste ejemplo detendrá el tren motriz después de 3 segundos.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Parar motor\n\nPara el motor.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué motor va detener.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el motor de la garra durante 3 segundos antes de detenerse.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor_controller":{"name":"stop_motor_controller","markdown":"# Detener el Controlador del Motor\n\nDetiene un Motor 393 conectado a un Controlador de Motor 29.\n\n![stop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_block.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija el Motor 393 que desea detener.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_motor.png)\n\nEste ejemplo girará un Motor 393 hacia adelante durante 3 segundos antes de parar.\n\n![stop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_example.png)"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Restar\n\nResta un valor de otro e informa la diferencia.\n\n![subtract](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Restar** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\nEl bloque **sustraer** cabe en bloques que aceptan espacios circulares, y también aceptará bloques circulares en él.\n\nResta dos números.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nRestar con valores de variables.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nRestar con valores de sensores o dispositivos.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"temperature_of_motor":{"name":"temperature_of_motor","markdown":"# Temperatura del motor\n\nInforma la temperatura del motor inteligente V5.\n\n![temp_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nusando el bloque que reporta **temperatura del motor** puede ayudar a los usuarios a desarrollar lógica para evitar que sus motores inteligentes V5 se sobrecalienten durante el uso intensivo.\n\n**temperatura del motor** reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**. \n\nElija qué motor inteligente V5 usar.\n\n![temp_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **temperatura del motor** se utiliza en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![temp_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Valor del temporizador\n\nInforma el valor del temporizador del cerebro V5 en segundos.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\nEl temporizador comienza a los 0 segundos cuando se inicia el programa e informa el valor del temporizador como un valor decimal.\n\nEl bloque que reporta **valor del temporizador** se usa dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n"},"torque_of_motor":{"name":"torque_of_motor","markdown":"# Torque del motor\n\nInforma la cantidad de torque (fuerza de rotación) que un motor inteligente V5 está utilizando actualmente.\n\n![motor_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/torque_of_motor/motor_torque.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Torque del motor** reporta un rango de **0.0 a 18.6 inch-pounds (InLB)** o **0.0 a 2.1 Newton-meters (Nm)**. \n\nElija el torque de motor inteligente V5 para informar.\n\n![motor_torque_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_device.png)\n\nElija si el **torque del motor** se informa en pulgadas-libras (InLb) o Newton-metros (Nm).\n\n![motor_torque_units](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_units.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **torque del motor** se utiliza dentro de bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![motor_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_inserted.png)"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Girar\n\nGira la transmisión para siempre.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **girar** rotará el tren motriz para siempre, hasta que se use un nuevo bloque de tren motriz o se detenga el programa.\n\nElija la dirección en que se moverá el motriz.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Girar por\n\nGira el tren motriz para una distancia dada.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija en qué dirección girará el tren motriz.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\n\nEstablezca qué tan lejos se moverá el tren motriz ingresando una cantidad de grados.\n\nEl bloque **Manejar por** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques **esperar** hasta que el tren motriz termine de girar.\n\nPuedes seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el tren motriz gira.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Direccion de giro\n\nCambia la direccion del tren motriz a un rumbo específico, cuando se usa el sensor giroscopico.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Direccion de giro** puede usarse para girar el tren motriz a cualquier rumbo dado en sentido de las manecillas del rejo.\n\nBasado en el rumbo actual del giroscopio, **Direccion de giro** determinará en qué dirección girar.\n\n**Direccion de giro** acepta un range de **0.00 a 359.99** grados.\n\nEl bloque **Direccion de giro** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el tren motriz haga cuatro vueltas:\n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Izquierda a 45 degrees\n- Izquierda a 90 degrees\n- Izquierda a 270 degrees\n- Derecha a 180 degrees\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques **esperarán** hasta que el tren motriz termine de girar.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no esperar** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen ejecutándose mientras el tren motriz gira.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Dar vuelta a rotación\n\nDa vuelta al chasis a un ángulo de rotación específico utilizando el sensor Gyro de entrada.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a rotación** se puede utilizar para girar el Chasis a un valor positivo (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) o negativo (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj).\n\nSobre la base del valor **rotación** actual del chasis, **dar vuelta a rotación** determinará en qué dirección girar.\n\nEl bloque **dar vuelta a rotación** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis haga cuatro vueltas: \n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) a 90 grados\n- Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) a 180 grados\n- Izquierda (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj) a -45 grados\n- Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) a 0 grados\n\nPor defecto, otros bloques  **esperarán** hasta que el Chasis termine de girar.\n\nPuede seleccionar la flecha para expandir **y no espera** - esto hará que otros bloques continúen funcionando mientras el Chasis da vuelta.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)\n\n"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Variable\n\nInforma el valor numérico asignado a el variable.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **Variable** se usan para informar un valor numérico almacenado dentro de el variable. Use el bloque **establecer variable** para establecer o actualizar el valor numérico de una variable.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **variable** se usa en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nLas variables se crean usando el botón **Hacer variable**.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Velocidad del motor\n\nInforma la velocidad actual de un motor inteligente V5.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Velocidad del motor** reporta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\n**Velocidad del motor** reporta un rango de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los motores inteligentes V5.\n\n* Cartucho Rojo: -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Cartucho Verde: -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Cartucho Azul: -600rpm a 600rpm\n\nElija qué motor usar.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad se informa en % o en revoluciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **velocidad del motor** se usa en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"velocity_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"velocity_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Velocidad del codificador de eje\n\nInforma la velocidad actual de un codificador de eje.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\n**Velocidad del codificador de eje** reporta un valor decimal en grados por segundo (dps) o rotaciones por minuto (rpm).\n\nElija qué codificador de eje usar.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_motor.png)\n\nElija si la velocidad se informa en grados por segundo (dps) o rotaciones por minuto (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_unit.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Objeto de visión\n\nInforma información sobre un objeto detectado desde el sensor de visión.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nPara usar el bloque **Objeto de visión**, siga los siguientes pasos:\n\n1. Configure su sensor de visión usando la ventana de Dispositivos.\n2. Use **foto** para capturar una imagen del sensor de visión y busque un código de firma / color.\n3. Use **objeto existe** para verificar si el sensor de visión detectó la firma / código de color solicitado.\n\nUna vez que el Sensor de visión detecta un objeto, puede usar otros bloques de Visión para obtener más información sobre el objeto detectado.\n\n* Use **establecer objeto de visión** para establecer sobre qué objeto detectado desea obtener más información. Por defecto, se utiliza el objeto detectado más grande.\n* Use **recuento de objetos** para determinar cuántos objetos se detectaron de ese código de firma / color solicitado.\n* Use **objeto de visión** para determinar qué información informar del objeto detectado.\n\nSeleccione qué sensor de visión usar.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nSeleccione qué valor informar desde el sensor de visión:\n\n* Ancho: Qué tan ancho es el objeto en píxeles. Devuelve un valor de **2 - 316 px**.\n* Altura: La altura del objeto en píxeles. Devuelve un valor de **2 - 212 px**.\n* CenterX: Reporta la coordenada X del centro del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 315 px**.\n* CentroY: Reporta la coordenada Y del centro del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 211 px**.\n* Ángulo: Reporta el ángulo del objeto detectado. Devuelve un valor de **0 - 180 grados**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nEl bloque que reporta **objeto de visión** se usa en bloques con espacios circulares.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Esperar\n\nEspera una cantidad de tiempo específica antes de pasar al siguiente bloque.\n\n![wait](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija una cantidad de tiempo para **esperar**.\n\nEl bloque **espera** puede aceptar decimales, enteros o bloques numéricos.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Esperar hasta\n\nEspera a que un bloque booleano informe **verdadero** antes de pasar al siguiente bloque.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Cómo utilizar\n\n**Esperar hasta** verificara repetidamente un bloque booleano y no se moverá al siguiente bloque hasta que el bloque booleano reporte **verdadero**.\n\nThe bloque Booleano **esperar hasta** puede aceptar bloques de forma hexagonal (seis lados).\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n"},"when_autonomous":{"name":"when_autonomous","markdown":"# Cuando autonomo\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se recibe una señal de modo \"autónomo\" de un campo de competencia o interruptor de competencia.\n\n![when_autonomous](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_autonomous/when_autonomous.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nCualquier bloque conectado al evento **cuando autónomo** se ejecutará cuando el robot esté conectado a un campo de competencia o interruptor de competencia que esté configurado en el modo \"autónomo\".\n\nLos usuarios pueden tener hasta 50 bloques **cuando control autónomo** en un proyecto."},"when_brain_screen":{"name":"when_brain_screen","markdown":"# Cuando la pantalla del cerebro\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl event **cuando la pantalla del cerebro** se puede usar para crear acciones o comportamientos basados en la interacción táctil con la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5.\n\nUtilizado junto con el bloque que reporta **posición de la pantalla** los usuarios pueden crear interfaces personalizadas para su V5 Brain detectando cuándo y dónde se producen toques en la pantalla.\n\nSeleccione qué acción activará el evento: **presionado** o **liberado**\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed_condition.png)"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Cuando recibo\n\nEjecuta la pila de bloques adjunta cuando el mensaje seleccionado se recibe de un mensaje **transmitir**.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué mensaje escuchar. También se puede crear un nuevo mensaje.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\nEl bloque **Cuando recibo** solo se activará para ejecutarse desde un **transmitir** o un bloque **transmitir y esperar** en una acumulación diferente"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Cuando bumper\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta el sensor del interruptor de parachoques seleccionado.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué interruptor bumper usar.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nSeleccione qué acción activará el evento: **presionado** o **liberado**\n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Cuando el eje del controlador\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se mueve el eje del joystick del controlador V5 seleccionado.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué controlador V5 usar.\n\n![when_controller_axis_device](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_device.png)\n\nElija qué controlador V5 usar.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Cuando el botón del controlador\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta el botón del controlador V5 seleccionado.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué controlador V5 usar.\n\n![when_controller_button_controller](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_controller.png)\n\nElija qué botón del controlador usar.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\nSeleccione qué acción activará el evento: **presionado** o **liberado**\n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)\n"},"when_driver":{"name":"when_driver","markdown":"# Cuando conductor\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se recibe una señal de modo \"control del conductor\" desde un campo de competencia o interruptor de competencia.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_driver/when_driver.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nCualquier bloque adjunto a el evento **cuando control del conductor** se ejecutará cuando el robot esté conectado a un campo de competencia o interruptor de competencia que esté configurado en el modo \"control del conductor\".\n\nUna repetition **por siempre** es muy recomendable para ser utilizada con un evento **cuando control del conductor**, para permitir que los comandos basados en el controlador V5 se actualicen con frecuencia durante la parte de control del conductor de un partido.\n\nUsuarios pueden tener hasta 50 bloques **cuando control del conductor** en un projecto."},"when_limit":{"name":"when_limit","markdown":"# When limit\n\nEjecuta la acumulación de bloques adjunta cuando se presiona o suelta el sensor del interruptor de límite seleccionado.\n\n![when_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_limit/when_limit.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nElija qué interruptor de límite usar.\n\n![when_limit_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_limit/when_limit_select.png)\n\nSeleccione qué acción activará el evento: **presionado** o **liberado**\n\n![when_limit_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_limit/when_limit_condition.png)\n"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Cuando comenza\n\nEjecuta la acomulacion de bloques adjunta cuando se inicia el proyecto.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nUn evento **cuando comenza** se ejecutará cuando el proyecto se inicie desde el menú del cerebro V5 o desde el boton **ejecutar** en VEXcode V5 Blocks.\n\nTodos los proyectos nuevos incluirán automáticamente un bloque **cuando comenza**. Los proyectos pueden tener hasta 50 bloques **cuando comenza**.\n\n**Cuando comenza** también actuará como la acomulacion del modo \"pre-autónomo\" para un proyecto de competencia VRC.\n"},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Cuando temporizador\n\nEjecuta la acomulacion de bloques adjunta cuando el temporizador del cerebro V5 es mayor que el valor dado.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl temporizador del cerebro empieza al comienzo de cada proyecto.\n\nElige una cantidad de tiempo. El evento **cuando temporizador** se ejecutará una vez que el temporizador del cerebro sea **mas grande que** el monto ingresado.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nEl bloque **cuando temporizador** puede aceptar decimales o valores enteros.\n\nEl bloque **cuando temporizador** **no puede** Aceptar otros bloques que reportan.\n"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Mientras\n\nUn bloque 'C' que repite los bloques dentro mientras se la condición booleana es **verdadero**.  \n\n![while](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/while/while.png)\n\n## Como utilizar\n\nEl bloque **mientras** solo verificará la condición booleana al comienzo de cada ciclo. \n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **verdadero**, el bloque dentro de **mientras** sera ejecutado.\n\nSi la condición booleana se reporta como **falso**, el bloque dentro de **mientras** sera omitido.\n\nEl 'C' bloque **mientras** puede aceptar bloques con forma hexagonal (seis lados) como su condición.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/es-419/while/while_inserted.png)"}},"python":{"control_break":{"name":"control_break","markdown":"# Romper\n\nSale de un bucle de repetición inmediatamente.\n\n```don\nbreak\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nCuando se añade dentro de un bucle, la orden de 'break' saldrá del bucle del que se está ejecutando actualmente. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo accionará el robot y comprobará si se ha pulsado su 'bumper'.\n\nSi el parachoques se **presiona**, la orden de 'break' saldrá del bucle while. El robot dejará de conducir hacia adelante.\n\n```don\nwhile True:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n    if bumper.pressing():\n        break\n```","signature":"break"},"control_for_loop":{"name":"control_for_loop","markdown":"# Por\n\nUn tipo de bucle que repite el código contenido en su cuerpo para un número determinado de iteraciones.\n\n```don\nfor value in range(10):\n    pass\n```\n\n# Cómo Utilizar\n\nPrimero, reemplace 'value' por una variable que se iterará a través de la función 'range()'.\n\nEn segundo lugar, sustituya '10' por un valor para especificar el final de la iteración.\n\nAgregue una sangría de cuatro espacios usando la barra espaciadora para incluir declaraciones como parte de la instrucción de control 'for'.\n\nUna declaración 'for' no debe contener un bloque de código vacío. Si es necesario, añada una declaración 'pass' a una declaración de for previamente vacía.\n\nObserve que los bucles for comienzan en el índice 0 en lugar de 1.\n\nLos bucles 'for' también pueden anidarse entre sí.\n\n# Ejemplo\nEl siguiente bucle for imprimirá los números 0 a 2:\n\n```don\nfor i in range(3):\n   brain.screen.print(i)\n   brain.screen.new_line()\n```\n   \nEsto imprimirá:\n\n```\n0\n1\n2\n```","signature":"for value in range (10"},"control_if_else_statement":{"name":"control_if_else_statement","markdown":"# Si/Si no\nUna instrucción de flujo de control que ejecuta un bloque de comandos si una condición se evalúa como true, u otro bloque de comandos si una condición se evalúa como false. \n\n```don\nif condition:\n    pass\nelse:\n    pass\n\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa instrucción 'if' es un condicional que comprobará si su condición se evalúa como **True** o **False**. Es posible combinar muchas condiciones con el uso de operadores lógicos como 'and', 'or' y 'not`. \n\nSi la totalidad de la condición es **True**, entonces el bloque de código indentado debajo de la 'condición if': se ejecutará. Si la totalidad de la condición es **False**, el bloque de código con sangría debajo de la instrucción 'else:' se ejecutará en su lugar.\n\nLos bloques de código por debajo de 'if' y 'else' deben sangrar cuatro espacios.\n\nUna declaración `if/else` no debe contener bloques de código vacíos. Si es necesario, añada las declaraciones 'pass' a una declaración 'if/else' vacía anteriormente. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEl codigo `if/else` Accionará el robot FORWARD si la variable es igual a 1. Si no, conducirá el robot REVERSE. \n\n```don\nif (my_variable == 1):\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nelse:\n    drivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"if conditio"},"control_if_statement":{"name":"control_if_statement","markdown":"# Si\n\nUna declaración de control utilizada para decidir si un bloque de código se ejecutará en función de la 'condition' proporcionada.\n\n```don\nif condition:\n    pass\n    \n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nReemplace la palabra 'condition' por una expresión que pueda evaluarse como 'True' o 'False`. Una evaluación de 'True' permitirá que las instrucciones indentadas debajo de la instrucción 'if' se ejecuten.\n\nAgregue una sangría de cuatro espacios usando la **barra espaciadora** para incluir declaraciones como parte de la declaración de control 'if'. \n\nUna declaración 'if' no debe contener un bloque de código vacío. Si es necesario, añadir una declaración 'pass' a una declaración 'if' previamente vacía. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEsta instrucción 'if' se ejecutará si 'my_variable' es igual a 1, haciendo que el robot conduzca hacia adelante.\n\n```don\nif (my_variable == 1):\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"if condition:\\n\\tpass"},"control_wait":{"name":"control_wait","markdown":"# Espera\n\nEspera una cantidad de tiempo específica antes de pasar al siguiente comando.\n\n```\nwait(TIME, UNITS)\n```\n\n## CÃ³mo Utilizar\n\nEstablezca una cantidad de tiempo en 'seconds' para que su programa **espere** antes de ejecutar comandos adicionales.\n\n```\nwait(10, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"wait(1, SECONDS)"},"control_wait_until":{"name":"control_wait_until","markdown":"# Mientras no\nInstrucción de control que continúa realizando bucles hasta que se convierte la expresión **true**.\n\n```don\nwhile not condition:\n    pass\n```\n\n## Cómo Uilizar\n\nCómo la declaración 'while not' comprobará repetidamente la condición, y no pasará al siguiente comando hasta que la condición indique **true**.\n\nSi la condición se evalúa como **false**, el código dentro de 'while not' se ejecutará.\n\nSi la condición se evalúa como **true**, el código dentro de 'while not' se omitirá, y el siguiente comando después de la instrucción 'while not' se ejecutará.\n\nLa declaración de 'while not' acepta cualquier expresión que se evalúe como 'True' o 'False' como su condición. Puede colocar booleanos, así como expresiones, utilizando operadores de comparación y lógicos. \n\nTambién puede utilizar valores numéricos; **0** evalúa a 'False`, Y cualquier **número distinto de cero** se evalúa como 'True`. \n\nAgregue una sangría de cuatro espacios usando la **barra espaciadora** para incluir declaraciones como parte de la declaración de control 'while not'. \n\nUna declaración de 'while not' no debe contener un bloque de código vacío. Si es necesario, añadir una declaración 'pasa' a una declaración 'while not' vacía. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste bucle 'while not' imprimirá \"Hello\" en líneas separadas hasta que el valor de mi variable sea igual a 5.\n\nmyVariable = 0\n\n```\nwhile not my_variable == 5:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\n    brain.screen.new_line()\n    my_variable += 1\n```","signature":"while not expressio"},"control_while_loop":{"name":"control_while_loop","markdown":"# Mientras\nBucle que repite el código en su cuerpo siempre que la expresión de condición se evalúe como **true**.   \n\n```don\nwhile condition:\n   pass\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl bucle 'while' solo comprobará la condición dentro del paréntesis al principio de cada bucle. \n\nSi la condición se evalúa como **true**, el código dentro de 'while' se ejecutará.\n\nSi la condición se evalúa como **false**, el código dentro de 'while' se omitirá.\n\nEl bucle 'while' acepta todo lo que se evalúa como 'True' o 'False' como su condición. Puede colocar booleanos, así como expresiones, utilizando operadores de comparación y lógicos. \n\nTambién puede utilizar valores numéricos; *0** se evalúa como 'False', y cualquier **número distinto de cero** se evalúa como 'True'.\n\nAgregue una sangría de cuatro espacios usando la **barra espaciadora** para incluir declaraciones como parte de la declaración de control 'while'. \n\nUna instrucción 'while' no debe contener un bloque vacío de código. Si es necesario, agregue una instrucción 'pasa' a una instrucción 'while' previamente vacía. \n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste bucle 'while' seguirá imprimiendo la palabra \"Hello\" en líneas separadas cuando el valor del temporizador sea inferior a 50 segundos.\n\n```don\nwhile brain.timer.time(SECONDS) < 50:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\n    brain.screen.new_line()\n```","signature":"while expressio"},"drivetrain_drive":{"name":"drivetrain_drive","markdown":"# Conducir\n\nMueve el chasis por siempre en la dirección especificada dentro de los paréntesis. \n\nTodos los motores del chasis funcionan hacia adelante o hacia atrás a la velocidad establecida mediante el comando 'drivetrain.set_drive_velocity'. La velocidad predeterminada es 50%. \n\nLos valores negativos harán que el chasis conduzca hacia atrás con una entrada REVERSE y en hacia adelante con una entrada FORWARD.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'drivetrain.drive' ejecutará el chasis para siempre, hasta que se utilice un nuevo comando drivetrain, o el programa se detenga.\n\n## Ejemplos\n\nUtilice el argumento 'FORWARD' en las letras mayúsculas para mover el chasis hacia adelante.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nUtilice el argumento 'REVERSE' en las letras mayúsculas para mover la transmisión en sentido inverso.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.drive(FOWARD)"},"drivetrain_drive_for":{"name":"drivetrain_drive_for","markdown":"# Conducir Por\n\nMueve el chasis por una distancia determinada. Todos los motores del chasis funcionan hacia adelante o hacia atrás a la velocidad establecida por el comando 'drivetrain.set_drive_velocity'. Después de que el chasis haya movido la distancia de entrada, el chasis se detendrá.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(DIRECTION, DISTANCE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEstablezca la distancia a la que se moverá el chasis introduciendo al menos tres argumentos válidos dentro de los paréntesis, separados por comas. \n\nEl primer argumento especifica la dirección. Las entradas válidas son 'FORWARD' o 'REVERSE' en todas las letras mayúsculas.  \n\nEl segundo argumento especifica la distancia que debe conducir el V5 Robot.\n\nEl tercer argumento especifica la unidad de medida que debe usarse. Las entradas válidas son 'INCHES'(pulgadas) o 'MM' (milímetros) en letras mayúsculas.\n\nEl parámetro 'DISTANCE' acepta valores numéricos. Los valores negativos harán que el robot V5 conduzca en sentido contrario a la entrada 'DIRECTION'.\n\n```\ndrivetrain.drive_for(REVERSE, 5.0, INCHES)\n```\n\nEl comando \"drive_for\" es por defecto un comando de bloqueo. Evitará que se ejecuten comandos posteriores hasta que se haya completado el movimiento de chasis.\n\n## Parámetro opcional\n\nPuede establecer un cuarto parámetro en 'wait=False' para permitir que los comandos que se siguen se ejecuten incluso antes de que el chasis haya terminado de moverse.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM, wait=False)\n```\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo muestra el 'drivetrain.drive_for' que se utiliza con una variable como distancia.\n\nEl V5 Robot se conduce 200 MM hacia adelante.\n\n```don\ndistance_variable = 200\n\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, distance_variable, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 2, MM, wait=True)"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer Velocidad de Conducción\n\nEstablece la velocidad del chasis para los comandos 'drive' y 'drive_for'. La velocidad predeterminada es 50%. \n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` establecerá la velocidad del chasis cuando se utiliza con un comando 'drive' o 'drive_for'. No hará que el chasis se mueva cuando se utiliza por sí mismo.\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` acepta dos argumentos: un valor numérico de **-100  to 100**, y el argumento de la unidad 'PERCENT' escrito en letras mayúsculas. \n\nSi se establece la velocidad del chasis en un valor negativo, el chasis se encontrará en el lado opuesto de la 'DIRECTION' pasada a un comando 'Drive' o 'Drive_for'.\n\nSi se establece la velocidad del chasis en 0, se evitará que el chasis se mueva incluso si se utiliza un comando 'Drive' o 'Drive_for'.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo muestra que el chasis irá en reversa debido a un valor negativo.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nEste ejemplo evitará que el chasis se mueva.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(0, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_drive_velocity(50, PRECENT)"},"drivetrain_set_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_set_heading","markdown":"# Establecer Dirección del Chasis\n\nEstablece el Gyro del chasis en una dirección exacto.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_heading(HEADING, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'drivetrain.set_heading' se puede utilizar para establecer la posición de la chasis en cualquier dirección dado. Este comando se puede utilizar para restablecer la orientación del giroscopio del chasis cuando le dirección se establece en un valor de 0.\n\n`drivetrain.set_heading` acepta un valor numérico entre **0 y 360** ya que es el primer argumento, y 'DEGREES' escrito en letras mayúsculas como su segundo argumento.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo se establece el rumbo de la transmisión a 90 grados. \n\nDado que la dirección del V5 Robot se establece en 90 grados, el siguiente comando 'turn_to_heading' no hará que el robot gire ya que su encabezado actual ya se ha establecido en 90 grados.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_heading(90, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_set_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer Rotación\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del chasis con un sensor Gyro.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(ROTATION, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'drivetrain.set_rotation' se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del chasis a cualquier valor positivo o negativo dado.\n\nEl parámetro 'ROTATION' puede aceptar valores numéricos.\n\nEl parámetro 'ROTATION' **no** tiene un límite de 0-359 grados.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará girar el robot un total de 210 grados:\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(120, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(45, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Turn right (clockwise) to rotation 120 degrees.\n- Set the robot's current position as rotation of -45 degrees.\n- Turn right (clockwise) an additional 90 degrees (-45 degrees to +45 degrees) based on the set rotation value from the previous command.","signature":"drivetrain.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_set_stopping":{"name":"drivetrain_set_stopping","markdown":"# Establecer Detención\n\n`drivetrain.set_stopping(MODE)` establece el comportamiento del robot cuando deja de moverse.  \n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nSustituya el parámetro 'MODE' por una de las siguientes opciones:\n\n* BRAKE (Freno): hará que el Motor se detenga inmediatamente.\n* COAST (Costa): deja que el Motor gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* HOLD (Detener): hará que el robot se detenga inmediatamente y lo devuelve a su posición de parada si se mueve. La parada del robot establecido surtirá efecto para todos los comandos futuros del robot para el resto del proyecto.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo muestra el robot conduciendo hacia adelante durante 200 MM antes de conducir por inercia hasta detenerse.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_stopping(COAST)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_stopping(BRAKE)"},"drivetrain_set_timeout":{"name":"drivetrain_set_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer Tiempo de Espera\n\n`drivetrain.set_timeout(VALUE, SECONDS)` establece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del robot.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando se utiliza para evitar que los comandos de movimiento que no alcanzan su posición impidan que otros comandos de procedimiento se ejecuten.\n\nEl comando puede aceptar valores numéricos o decimales.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo muestra un tiempo de espera que se utiliza para establecer el límite de tiempo para los movimientos de avance del chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_timeout(1, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 100, MM)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_timeout(1, SECONDS)"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity_percent":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity_percent","markdown":"# Establecer la Velocidad de Dar Vuelta\n\nEstablece la velocidad de veuletas del chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` establecerá la velocidad del chasis al girar, pero no hará que el chasis se mueva cuando se usa sin un comando de 'turn' o 'turn_for'.\n\n`drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` acepta un rango de **-100 a 100** como primer argumento. Toma las unidades, `PERCENT`, escrito en letras mayúsculas como el segundo argumento.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de vuelta del chasis en un valor negativo hará que el chasis gire en el opuesto de la dirección pasada en los siguientes comandos de giro.\n\nEstablecer la velocidad de giro del chasis en 0 evitará que el chasis gire, incluso cuando se utiliza un comando 'turn' o 'turn_for'.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el chasis girará en la dirección opuesta debido a un valor negativo.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_turn_velocity(50, PERCENT)"},"drivetrain_stop":{"name":"drivetrain_stop","markdown":"# Parar\n\nPara el chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'drivetrain.stop()' detiene el chasis. No toma ningún argumento entre paréntesis.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo detendrá el chasis después de que el V5 Robot haya conducido hacia adelante durante 3 segundos.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"drivetrain.stop()"},"drivetrain_turn":{"name":"drivetrain_turn","markdown":"# Dar Vuelta\n\nHara que el chasis de vuelta a la derecha o a la izquierda.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando \"drivetrain.turn\" girará el Drivetrain en la dirección dada por siempre hasta que se utilice un nuevo comando drivetrain, o hasta que se detenga el programa.\n\nUtilice el argumento 'LEFT' en letras mayúsculas para girar el chasis a la izquierda.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(LEFT)\n```\n\nUtilice el argumento 'RIGHT' en letras mayúsculas para girar el chasis a la derecha.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn esta ejemplo, el robot avanzará 200 MM antes de girar a la derecha indefinidamente.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn(RIGHT)"},"drivetrain_turn_for":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_for","markdown":"# Dar Vuelta Por\n\nGira el chasis durante un número especificado de grados.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(DIRECTION, ANGLE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl primer argumento especifica la dirección de giro: 'LEFT' (izquierda) o 'RIGHT' (derecha), escrita en letras mayúsculas. \n\nEl segundo argumento especifica el ángulo de giro como un valor numérico; puede ser cualquier número entre 0 y 360. \n\nEl tercer argumento son las unidades de giro. Esto debe ser establecido como \"DEGREES\" en letras mayúsculas. \n\nEl comando 'turn_for' es de forma predeterminada un comando de bloqueo. Impide que se ejecute cualquier código hasta que el chasis haya completado su turno.\n\n## Parámetros Opcionales\n\nSi el cuarto argumento se establece en 'wait=False', comandos de procedimiento se les permitirá ejecutar incluso antes de que el chasis ha completado su turno.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(LEFT, 90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo girará el V5 Robot 270 grados a la derecha.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 270, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 90, DEGREES, wait=True)"},"drivetrain_turn_to_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Dar Vuelta a la Dirección\n\nGira el chasis a una dirección específica cuando se utilizan los sensores Gyro o Inertial.\n\n`drivetrain.turn_to_heading(HEADING, UNITS)`\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `drivetrain.turn_to_heading` se puede utilizar para girar el chasis a cualquier dirección dado en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\nBasado en la dirección actual del Giroscopio, `drivetrain.turn_to_heading` determinará la dirección a girar.\n\nEl parámetro `HEADING` acepta valores numéricos en el rango de **0.00 a 359.99**.\n\nEl parámetro `UNITS` (unidades) debe establecerse en `DEGREES`(grados).\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis haga cuatro vueltas: \n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(45.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(270.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(180.0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Left to 45 degrees (Izquierda a 45 grados)\n- Left to 90 degrees (Izquierda a 90 grados)\n- Left to 270 degrees (Derecha a 270 grados)\n- Right to 180 degrees (Derecha a 180 grados)\n\nEl comando `turn_to_heading` por defecto bloqueará los comandos de procedimiento hasta que el giro del chasis se haya completado.\n\n## Parámetros Optionales\n\nPuede establecer `wait=False` como tercer parámetro para prevenir el comando `turn_to_heading` de bloquear los comandos de procedimiento de ejecución hasta que el giro del chasis se haya completado.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(180.0, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Dar vuelta a la Rotación\n\nGira el chasis a un ángulo de rotación específico.\n\n`drivetrain.turn_to_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)`\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `drivetrain.turn_to_rotation` se puede utilizar para girar el chasis a un valor positivo (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) o negativo (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj).\n\nBasado en la rotación actual del chasis, `drivetrain.turn_to_rotation` determinará la dirección a girar.\n\nEl parámetro `ROTATION` puede aceptar valores numéricos.\n\nLos valores numéricos **no** son limitados al rango de **0 - 359.99** grados. Los giros serán absolutos y pueden hacer que el robot gire más de una vez si es necesario.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el chasis haga cuatro vueltas:\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(180, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Right (Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj)) a 90 grados\n- Right(Derecha (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj)) a 180 grados\n- Left (Izquierda (en sentido opuesto al de las agujas del reloj)) a -45 grados\n- Right (Derecha(en el sentido de las agujas del reloj)) a 0 grados\n\nEl comando `drivetrain.turn_to_rotation` por defecto bloqueará los comandos de procedimiento hasta que el giro del chasis se haya completado.\n\n## Parámetro opcional\n\nPuede establecer un tercer parámetro  `wait=False` para evitar el comando `turn_to_rotation' de bloquear los comandos de procedimiento hasta que se complete el giro del chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(180.0, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90, DEGREES, wait=True)"},"function_name":{"name":"function_name","markdown":"# Función\n\nLas funciones son bloques de código que se utilizan para realizar una acción.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una función, cree un nombre de función significativo. Esto significa que el nombre de la función debe describir con precisión lo que hace.\n\nUtilice la **palabra clave** `def` antes del nombre de la función para definir la función.\n\nIncluya paréntesis `()` y encierra parámetros opcionales después del nombre de la función, seguido por un colon`:`. Múltiples parámetros deben estar separados por comas `(parameter1, parameter2)`.\n\nEl cuerpo de la función debe sangrar cuatro espacios. Si no hay ningún código para que la función se ejecute, un `pass` debe incluirse en la definición de la función.\n\n```don\ndef my_function():\n    pass\n```\n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nEsta función no tiene parámetros e imprimirá \"Hello\" en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\ndef print_hello_world():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello World\")\n```\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEsta función toma un parámetro, `name` e imprimirá el valor de `name` en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\ndef print_name(name):\n    brain.screen.print(name)\n```","signature":"def function_name(parameters):\\n\\tpass"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Borrar Fila\n\nBorra una sola fila en la pantalla del V5 Brain o Controller.\n\n```don \nbrain.screen.clear_line()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nBorra la fila actual en la pantalla V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.clear_line()\n```\n\nBorra una fila especificada en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.clear_line(ROW)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.clear_line()` puede aceptar valores enteros entre **1 - 20**, para establecer qué fila se va a borrar. También se puede llamar al comando sin ningún argumento para borrar la fila actual.\n\n---\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.clear_line()"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Borrar Todas las Filas\n \nBorra toda la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`brain.screen.clear_screen()` no cambiará el cursor de la pantalla. Tendrá que utilizar el comando `brain.screen.set_cursor()` para ajustar el cursor de la pantalla a una posición específica.","signature":"brain.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle","markdown":"# Dibujar Círculo\n\nDibuja un círculo en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_circle(X, Y, RADIUS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.draw_circle()` requiere 3 valores:\n\n* Value 1: Center Point X\n* Value 2: Center Point Y\n* Value 3: Radius of Circle (in pixels) (Radio de círculo (en pixels))\n\nEl color de la línea exterior del círculo se determina por el comando `brain.screen.set_pen_color()`. El color de línea predeterminado es blanco.\n\nEl color color de relleno interior del círculo se determina por el comando `brain.screen.set_fill_color()`. El color de relleno predeterminado es negro.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_brain_screen_draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_circle(1, 1, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_line","markdown":"# Dibujar Línea\n\nDibuja una línea en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_line(START_X, START_Y, END_X, END_Y)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.draw_line()` requiere 4 valores:\n\n* Value 1: Beginning X coordinate\n* Value 2: Beginning Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Ending X coordinate\n* Value 4: Ending Y coordinate\n\nEl color de la línea viene determinado por el comando `brain.screen.set_pen_color()`. El color de línea predeterminado es blanco.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_brain_screen_draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_line(1, 1, 10, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel","markdown":"# Dibujar Píxel\n\nDibuja un píxel en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_pixel(X, Y)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.draw_pixel` requiere 2 valores:\n\n* Value 1: X Coodinate\n* Value 2: Y Coodinate\n\nEl color del píxel viene determinado por el comando `brain.screen.set_pen_color()`. El color de píxel predeterminado es blanco.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_pixel(1, 1)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Dibujar Rectángulo\n\nDibuja un rectángulo en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_rectangle(X, Y, WIDTH, HEIGHT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.draw_rectangle()` requiere 4 valores:\n\n* Value 1: Top Left Corner X coordinate (Coordenada X de la esquina superior izquierda)\n* Value 2: Top Left Corner Y coordinate (Coordenada Y de la esquina superior izquierda)\n* Value 3: Width of the rectangle (Ancho del rectángulo)\n* Value 4: Height of the rectangle (Altura del rectángulo)\n\nEl color de la línea de borde del rectángulo viene determinado por el comando `brain.screen.set_pen_color()`. El color de línea predeterminado es blanco.\n\nEl color de relleno interior del rectángulo se determina mediante el comando `brain.screen.set_fill_color()`. El color de relleno predeterminado es negro.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_rectangle(1, 1, 10, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Siguiente fila\n\nEstablece el cursor de salida de impresión en la pantalla del V5 Brain a la siguiente fila disponible.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.new_line()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPor defecto, todos los proyectos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1 columna 1. El comando `brain.screen.new_line()` moverá el cursor hacia abajo una sola fila en la pantalla. `brain.screen.new_line()` también establecerá la columna del cursor en la posición 1.\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Brain permita cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Brain - Número de Filas:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 Filas (Por Defecto)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Filas\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_brain_screen_new_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.new_line()"},"looks_brain_screen_print":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print","markdown":"# Imprimir\n\nImprime valores o texto en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.print(\"Hello World\")\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.print()` imprimirá datos en una ubicación del cursor en la pantalla.\n\nTodos los nuevos proyectos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1 columna 1.\n\n\n* Print words and numbers: \n\t`brain.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n* Print the reported value from a variable: \n\t`brain.screen.print(my_variable)`\n* Print the reported value from a sensor or device:  \n        `brain.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`","signature":"brain.screen.print(\"Hello World\")"},"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Establecer Cursor\n\n\nEstablece la ubicación del cursor en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_cursor(ROW, COLUMN)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.set_cursor()` requiere 2 valores:\n\n* Value 1: Screen row position (Posición de la fila de la pantalla)\n* Value 2: Screen column position (Posición de la columna de la pantalla)\n\nEstablezca la posición de fila y columna del cursor para que se muestre un comando `brain.screen.print()` en una ubicación específica de la pantalla.\n\nAcepta un rango para **fila** de **1 a 20**.\n\nAcepta un rango para **columna** de **1 a 80**.\n\n---\n\nEl cerebro V5 le permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará al número de filas y columnas disponibles en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n**V5 Brain Tamaño De Fuente - Número de Filas:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Rows (Filas)\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Rows (Filas)\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 Rows (Default) (Filas - Por Defecto)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Rows (Filas)\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Rows (Filas)\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Rows (Filas)\n\n**V5 Brain Tamaño De Fuente - Número de Columnas:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 80 Columns (Columnas)\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 68 Columns (Columnas)\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 48 Columns (Default) (Columnas - Por Defecto)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 32 Columns (Columnas)\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 24 Columns (Columnas)\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.MONO60` - 16 Columns (Columnas)\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color","markdown":"# Establecer Color de Relleno\n\nEstablece el color que rellena las formas dibujadas en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_fill_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.set_fill_color()` se utiliza para establecer el color del interior de círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del V5 Brain. \n\nReemplace el parámetro `COLOR` por una de las siguientes acciones:\n\n* `Color.BLACK` (Negro)\n* `Color.WHITE` (Blanco)\n* `Color.RED` (Rojo)\n* `Color.GREEN` (Verde)\n* `Color.BLUE` (Azul)\n* `Color.YELLOW` (Amarillo)\n* `Color.ORANGE` (Naranja)\n* `Color.PURPLE` (Morado)\n* `Color.CYAN` (Cian)\n* `Color.TRANSPARENT` (Transparente)\n\nEl color de relleno se utilizará para los objetos posteriores dibujados en la pantalla del V5 Brain hasta que se cambie de nuevo.","signature":"brain.screen.set_fill_color(Color.RED)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_font":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_font","markdown":"# Establecer Fuente\n\nEstablece el estilo y el tamaño de la fuente utilizada en la pantalla del V5 Brain al imprimir valores.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_font(FONT_TYPE)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nHay dos tipos de fuentes disponibles en la pantalla del V5 Brain:\n\n* Monospaced (MONO) - cada carácter ocupa el mismo ancho.\n* Proportional (PROP) - cada carácter ocupa diferentes anchos de tamaño en función del carácter.\n\nElija el tipo de fuente y el tamaño que desea utilizar reemplazando el parámetro `FONT_TYPE` . Puede seleccionar entre las siguientes opciones de fuente.\n\n* `FontType.MONO12`\n* `FontType.MONO15`\n* `FontType.MONO20`\n* `FontType.MONO30`\n* `FontType.MONO40`\n* `FontType.MONO60`\n* `FontType.PROP20`\n* `FontType.PROP30`\n* `FontType.PROP40`\n* `FontType.PROP60`\n\nEl nuevo tamaño de fuente se utilizará para cualquier texto futuro escrito en la pantalla del V5 Brain hasta que se cambie de nuevo.","signature":"brain.screen.set_font(FontType.MONO20)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color","markdown":"# Establecer el Color de la Pluma\n\nEstablece el color de las líneas dibujadas en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_pen_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.set_pen_color()` se utiliza para establecer el color de las líneas, píxeles y texto dibujado en la pantalla del V5 Brain. \n\n`brain.screen.set_pen_color()` también se puede utilizar para establecer el color del contorno de los círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\nReemplace el parámetro `COLOR` por una de las siguientes opciones:\n\n* `Color.BLACK` (Negro)\n* `Color.WHITE` (Blanco)\n* `Color.RED` (Rojo)\n* `Color.GREEN` (Verde)\n* `Color.BLUE` (Azul)\n* `Color.YELLOW` (Amarillo)\n* `Color.ORANGE` (Naranja)\n* `Color.PURPLE` (Morado)\n* `Color.CYAN` (Cian)\n\nEl color de la pluma se utilizará para cualquier objeto posterior dibujado en la pantalla del V5 Brain hasta que se cambie de nuevo.","signature":"brain.screen.set_pen_color(Color.RED)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width","markdown":"# Establecer la Anchura de la Pluma\n\nEstablece el ancho del contorno de las formas dibujadas en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_pen_width(PEN_WIDTH)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `brain.screen.set_pen_width()` se utiliza para establecer el ancho de la línea en el exterior de círculos y rectángulos dibujados en la pantalla del V5 Brain. \n\nEl comando `brain.screen.set_pen_width()` puede aceptar valores enteros, con un valor mayor que equivale a un ancho mayor. Reemplace el parámetro `PEN_WIDTH` por un valor entero.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.set_pen_width(10)"},"looks_controller_rumble":{"name":"looks_controller_rumble","markdown":"# Vibración del Controller\n\nActiva un efecto de vibración en el V5 Controller.\n\n```python\ncontroller.rumble(\".-.-\")\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `controller.rumble(\".-.-\")` utiliza el motor de vibración en su V5 Controller para proporcionar retroalimentación.\n\nPuede crear cualquier patrón que desee utilizando una combinación de caracteres \".\" y \"-\" de la cadena. El caractere \".\" creará una vibración corto. El caractere \"-\" creará una larga vibración.","signature":"controller.rumble(\"-.-.\")"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Borrar Fila\n\nBorra la fila actual en la pantalla del V5 Controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_line()\n```\n\nBorra una fila especificada en la pantalla del V5 Contoller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_line(ROW)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `controller.screen.clear_line()` puede aceptar valores enteros entre **1 - 3**, para establecer qué fila se va a borrar. También puede llamar al comando sin argumentos para borrar la fila actual.\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Controller no permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_controller_screen_clear_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.clear_line()"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Borrar Todas las Filas\n\nBorra toda la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`controller.screen.clear_screen()` no cambiará el cursor de la pantalla. \n\nUtilice el comando `controller.screen.set_cursor()` para establecer el cursor de la pantalla en una posición específica.","signature":"controller.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_controller_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Siguiente Fila\n\nEstablece el cursor de salida de impresión en la pantalla del controlador V5 en la siguiente fila disponible.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.new_line()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nDe forma predeterminada, todos los proyectos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1, columna 1. El comando `controller.screen.new_line()` moverá el cursor hacia abajo por una sola fila en la pantalla. `controller.screen.new_line()` también establecerá la columna del cursor en la posición 1.\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Controller no permita cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Brain - Número de filas:**\n\n* Standard Font (Fuente Estándar) - 3 Filas (por defecto) \n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Controller - Número de columnas:**\n\n* Standard Font (Fuente Estándar) - 20 Columnas (por defecto)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_controller_screen_new_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.new_line()"},"looks_controller_screen_print":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_print","markdown":"# Imprimir\n\nImprime valores en la pantalla del V5 Controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.print(\"Hello World\") \n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `controller.screen.print()` imprimirá los datos en la posición del cursor en la pantalla.\n\nTodos los nuevos proyectos comienzan con el cursor de la pantalla en la fila 1, columna 1.\n\n\n* Imprimir palabras y números: \n\t`controller.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n* Imprimir el valor informado de una variable:  \n\t`controller.screen.print(my_variable)`\n* Imprime el valor notificado desde un sensor o dispositivo: \n        `controller.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`","signature":"controller.screen.print(\"Hello World\")"},"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Establecer cursor\n\n\nEstablece la ubicación del cursor para el comando **controller.screen.print()** en la pantalla del V5 Controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.set_cursor(ROW, COLUMN)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `controller.screen.set_cursor()` requiere 2 valores:\n\n* Valor 1: Posición de la fila de la pantalla \n* Valor 2: Posición de la columna de pantalla\n\n\nEstablezca la posición de fila y columna del cursor para que se muestre un comando `controller.screen.print()` en una ubicación específica de la pantalla.\n\n`controller.screen.set_cursor()` acepta un rango para **fila** de **1 a 3**.\n\n`controller.screen.set_cursor()` acepta un rango para **columna** de **1 a 20**.\n\n---\n\nEl V5 Brain no permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de Fuente del V5 Controller - Número de Filas:**\n\n* Fuente Estándar - 3 Filas (per defecto)\n\n**Tamaño de Fuente del V5 Controller - Número de Columnas:**\n\n* Fuente Estándar - 20 Columnas (por defecto)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/es-419/looks_controller_screen_set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)"},"looks_led_set":{"name":"looks_led_set","markdown":"# LED Encendido/apagado\n\nEnciende o apaga un LED.\n\n```don\nled.on()\n```\n```don\nled.off()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`led.on()` enciende el dispositivo LED.\n\n`led.off()` apaga el dispositivo LED.","signature":"led.set(False)"},"motion_motor393_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor393_set_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer la Velocidad del Controlador del Motor\n\nEstablece la velocidad de un Motor 393 conectado a un Controlador de Motor 29.\n\n```don \nmotor393.set_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl parámetro 'VELOCITY' (Velocidad) acepta un rango de -100% a 100%.\n\nSi se establece la velocidad de un Motor 393 en un valor negativo hará que el Motor 393 gire en reversa.\n\nLa secuencia siguiente hará que el Motor 393 gire en sentido inverso, aunque se pase el parámetro 'FORWARD' (Adelante).\n\n```don\nmotor393.set_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\nmotor393.spin(FORWARD)\n```\n\nAjustar la velocidad de un Motor 393 a 0 evitará que el Motor gire.","signature":"motor393.set_velocity(10, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor393_spin":{"name":"motion_motor393_spin","markdown":"# Girar Controlador de Motor\n\nGira un Motor 393 conectado a un controlador de motor 29.\n\n```don \nmotor393.spin(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste comando gira un Motor 393 para siempre, hasta que se utiliza un nuevo comando de motor o el programa se detiene.\n\nElija a qué dirección girará el motor estableciendo el parámetro 'DIRECTION'(Dirección) en **FORWARD** (Adelante) o **REVERSE** (Hacia Atrás).","signature":"motor393.spin(FORWARD)"},"motion_motor_set_max_torque":{"name":"motion_motor_set_max_torque","markdown":"# Ajuste de la Par del Motor\n\nEstablece el par del V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.set_max_torque(AMOUNT, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste comando acepta un rango de 0% a 100%.\n\nEl comando \"set motor torque\" puede aceptar decimales, enteros o valores numéricos\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo girará el motor de garra a la posición de 40 grados con sólo un 20% de par máximo. Esto permite que la garra agarre un objeto sin dañarlo con demasiada fuerza.\n\n```don\nclaw_motor.set_max_torque(20, PERCENT)\nclaw_motor.set_position(40, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_max_torque(50, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor_set_position":{"name":"motion_motor_set_position","markdown":"# Establecer la Posición del Motor\n\nEstablece la posición del codificador del V5 Smart Motor al valor dado.\n\n```don\nmotor.set_position(VALUE, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste comando se puede utilizar para establecer la posición del motor a cualquier valor dado.\n\nNormalmente, el comando posición del motor se utiliza para establecer la posición en 0 para restablecer la posición del codificador del motor.","signature":"motor.set_position(0, DEGREES)"},"motion_motor_set_stopping":{"name":"motion_motor_set_stopping","markdown":"# Establecer Parada del Motor\n\nEstablece el comportamiento de frenado del V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.set_stopping(MODE)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl parámetro `MODE` se puede sustituir por cualquiera de las siguientes opciones:\n\n* BRAKE (Frenar): hará que el motor se detenga inmediatamente.\n* COAST (Deslizarse): deja que el motor gire gradualmente hasta detenerse.\n* HOLD (Detener): will cause the Motor to come to an immediate stop, and returns it to its stopped position if moved.\n\nEl comportamiento de detención establecido por este comando se aplicará a los comandos de motor subsiguientes para la totalidad del proyecto, a menos que se cambie de otra manera.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo hará que el Motor de brazo gire hacia adelante durante 90 grados (para levantar el brazo) y luego mantendrá su posición.\n\n```don\narm_motor.set_stopping(HOLD)\narm_motor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_stopping(BRAKE)"},"motion_motor_set_timeout":{"name":"motion_motor_set_timeout","markdown":"# Establecer Tiempo de Espera del Motor\n\nEstablece un límite de tiempo para los comandos de movimiento del V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don \nmotor.set_timeout(AMOUNT, SECONDS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl límite de tiempo del motor se utiliza para evitar que los comandos de movimiento que no alcanzan su posición impidan que los comandos subsiguientes se ejecuten. \n\nUn ejemplo de que un motor no alcanza su posición es un brazo o una garra que alcanza su límite mecánico y no puede completar su movimiento.\n\nEl comando `set_motor_timeout` puede aceptar decimales, enteros o valores numéricos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo finalizará el comando SET motor después de 2 segundos si el motor de claw no ha alcanzado la posición de 270 grados. Una vez alcanzado el límite de tiempo o el objetivo, el motor de claw girará a la posición 0 grados.\n\n```don\nclaw_motor.set_timeout(2, SECONDS)\nclaw_motor.spin_to_position(270, DEGREES)\nclaw_motor.spin_to_position(0, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_timeout(1, SECONDS)"},"motion_motor_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity","markdown":"# Establecer la Velocidad del Motor\n\nEstablece la velocidad de un V5 Smart Motor.\n\n\n```don \nmotor.set_velocity(VELOCITY, UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste comando acepta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm.**\n\nEl valor 'UNIT' (Unidad) aceptable es: `PERCENT` (Por Ciento) or `RPM` (Rotación por Minuto) .\n\n**Ajuste la velocidad del motor** aceptará un valor de \"rotaciones por minuto\" (RPM) basado en el cartucho de engranaje instalado en los V5 Smart Motor.\n\n* Red Cartridge (Cartucho de Engranaje Rojo): -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge (Cartucho de Engranaje Verde): -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge (Cartucho de Engranaje Azul): -600rpm a 600rpm\n\nSi se establece la velocidad de un V5 Smart Motor en un valor negativo, el motor girará en sentido inverso.\n\nSi se establece la velocidad de un V5 Smart Motor en 0, se evitará que el motor gire.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo establecerá que el Motor de brazo gire a una velocidad del 25% a la posición de 90 grados.\n\n```don\narm_motor.set_velocity(25, PERCENT)\narm_motor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_velocity(50, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor_spin":{"name":"motion_motor_spin","markdown":"# Girar\n\nEste comando hace girar un V5 Smart Motor por siempre, hasta que se utilice un nuevo comando del motor o se detenga el programa.\n\n```don\nmotor.spin(FORWARD)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija la dirección en la que el motor girará hacia **FORWARD** (ADELANTE) o **REVERSE** (HACIA ATRÁS).\n\n```don\nmotor.spin(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"motor.spin(FORWARD)"},"motion_motor_spin_for":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_for","markdown":"# Girar Por\n \nEste comando hace girar un V5 Smart Motor durante una cantidad determinada de grados o giros.\n\n```don\nmotor.spin_for(DIRECTION, AMOUNT, UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nElija a qué 'DIRECTION' (Dirección) girará el motor: **FORWARD** (Adelante) o **REVERSE** (Hacia Atras).\n\nElija la 'UNIT' (UNIDAD) de medida para que sea **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS** (Vueltas).\n\nElija si este comando debe ser esperado o no, siguiendo los comandos estableciendo un cuarto parámetro opcional en **wait=True** (espera) o **wait=False** (no espera). \n\n```don\nmotor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\nEste comando es un comando de bloqueo a menos que **wait-False** (no espera) se pase como el cuarto parámetro.","signature":"motor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES)"},"motion_motor_spin_to_position":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_to_position","markdown":"# Girar a la Posición\n\nEstablece la posición del codificador del V5 Smart Motor en la cantidad dada.\n\n```don \nmotor.spin_to_position(AMOUNT, UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste mando le indicará al motor que se desplace a una posición específica. Basado en la posición actual del Motor, `spin_to_position` determinará la dirección de rotación.\n\nElija la unidad de medida para que sea **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS** (Vueltas).\n\nElija si este comando debe ser esperado o no por otros comandos, cambiando el tercer parámetro opcional a **wait=True** (espera) o **wait=False** (no espera).\n\n```don\nmotor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\nEstablecer **wait=True** (espera) significa que los comandos de procedimiento no se ejecutarán hasta que se complete el giro del motor. En cambio, **wait=False** (no espera) no esperará a que se complete.  \n\nPor defecto, este comando tendrá la espera que se establecerá en **True**.","signature":"motor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES)"},"motion_motor_stop":{"name":"motion_motor_stop","markdown":"# Detener el motor\n\nDetiene el motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.stop()\n```\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEste ejemplo muestra un motor girando durante 3 segundos antes de detenerse.\n\n```don\nmotor.spin(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\nmotor.stop()\n```","signature":"motor.stop()"},"motion_servo_set_position":{"name":"motion_servo_set_position","markdown":"# Girar Servo\n\nGira un Motor Servo a una posición establecida.\n\n```don \nservo.set_position(POSITION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nGira un Motor Servo al valor 'POSITION' (Posición) dado.\n\n## Ejemplo\nEl siguiente ejemplo gira el Motor Servo a 90 grados.\n\n```don\nservo.set_position(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"servo.set_position(50, DEGREES)"},"sensing_accel_two_g.acceleration":{"name":"sensing_accel_two_g.acceleration","markdown":"# Aceleración del Acelerómetro Analógico\n\nReporta del valor de aceleración de un eje en el Acelerómetro Analógico.\n\n```don\naccel_2g.acceleration()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEste comando informa de un rango de **-2.0 G a 2.0 G** o **-6.0 G a 6.0 G** dependiendo de la configuración del puente en el Acelerómetro Analógico.","signature":"accel_2g.acceleration()"},"sensing_brain_battery_capacity":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_capacity","markdown":"# Capacidad de la Batería\n\n\nReporta del nivel de carga de la batería del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.capacity()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa capacidad de la batería reporta un rango de **0%** a **100%.**","signature":"brain.battery.capacity()"},"sensing_brain_battery_current":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_current","markdown":"# Corriente de la Batería\n\nReporta de la corriente de la batería del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa corriente de la batería indica un rango de **0.0 amperios** a **20.0 amperios**.","signature":"brain.battery.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_brain_battery_voltage":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_voltage","markdown":"# Voltaje de la Batería\n\nInforma del voltaje de la batería del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.voltage(VOLT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nEl voltaje de la batería indica un rango de **10.0 voltios** a **14.4 voltios**.","signature":"brain.battery.voltage(VoltageUnits.VOLT)"},"sensing_brain_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_column","markdown":"# Columna del Cursor\n\nInforma del valor de columna de la ubicación del cursor de pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.column()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa columna de pantalla informa de un rango de **1 a 80**.\n\nEl V5 Brain permita cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará al número de columnas disponibles en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Brain- Número de columnas:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 80 Columnas\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 68 Columnas\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 48 Columnas (por defecto)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 32 Columnas\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 24 Columnas\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.MONO60` - 16 Columnas","signature":"brain.screen.column()"},"sensing_brain_screen_pressing":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_pressing","markdown":"# Pantalla Presionado\n \nReporta si la pantalla táctil del V5 Brain está siendo presionada.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.pressing()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`brain.screen.pressing` reporta **True** si la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5 está siendo presionada.\n\n`brain.screen.pressing` reporta **False** si la pantalla táctil del cerebro V5 no está siendo presionada.","signature":"brain.screen.pressing()"},"sensing_brain_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_row","markdown":"# Fila del Cursor\n \nReporta del valor de fila de la ubicación del cursor de pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.row()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa fila de pantalla informa de un rango de **1 a 20**.\n\nEl V5 Brain permita cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla. Cambiar la fuente afectará al número de filas disponibles en la pantalla del V5 Brain.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Brain - Número de filas:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 Filas (por defecto)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Filas\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Filas","signature":"brain.screen.row()"},"sensing_brain_timer_clear":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_clear","markdown":"# Restablecer Temporizador\nRestablece el temporizador del V5 Brain.\n\n```don \nbrain.timer.clear()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl temporizador del V5 Brain comienza al principio de cada proyecto. El comando CLEAR TIMER restablece el valor del temporizador a 0 segundos.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo, el temporizador se reiniciará antes de mover el Chasis hacia adelante durante 3 segundos. Después de 3 segundos, el Chasis se detendrá.\n\n```don\nbrain.timer.clear()\nwhile not brain.timer.time(SECONDS) > 3:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"brain.timer.clear()"},"sensing_brain_timer_time":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_time","markdown":"# Valor del Temporizador\n\nReporta del valor del temporizador del V5 Brain en segundos.\n\n```don \nbrain.timer.time(SECONDS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nEl temporizador comienza a 0 segundos cuando se inicia el programa e informa del valor del temporizador como un valor decimal.","signature":"brain.timer.time(SECONDS)"},"sensing_bumper_pressing":{"name":"sensing_bumper_pressing","markdown":"# Presionando Parachoques\n \nReporta si el interruptor de parachoques se está presionando actualmente.\n\n```don\nbumper.pressing()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPresionando Parachques resultará en un valor **True**, si se esta presionado el parachoque.\n\nPresionando Parachques resultará en un valor **False**, si no se esta presionado el parachoque.","signature":"bumper.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_axis_position":{"name":"sensing_controller_axis_position","markdown":"# Posición del Controller\n \nReporta la posición de un joystick en el V5 Controller a lo largo de un eje.\n\n```don\ncontroller.axis1.position()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`controller.axis1.position` reporta de un rango entre **-100 a 100**.\n\n`controller.axis1.position` informará cero (0) cuando un eje de joystick esté centrado.\n\nElija qué eje del controlador debe informar.\n\n* axis1 (eje 1) - Joystick derecho (izquierda y derecha)\n* axis2 (eje 2)- Joystick derecho (arriba y abajo)\n* axis3 (eje 3)- Joystick izquierdo (arriba y abajo)\n* axis4 (eje 4)- Joystick izquierdo (izquierda y derecha)","signature":"controller.axis1.position()"},"sensing_controller_button_up_pressing":{"name":"sensing_controller_button_up_pressing","markdown":"# Presionando Controller\n \nReporta si esta presionado un botón del V5 Controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.buttonUp.pressing()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPresionando Controller reporta **True** si se está presionando el botón del controlador seleccionado.\n\nPresionando Controller reporta **False** si no se está presionando el botón del controlador seleccionado.\n\nElija el botón controlador que se va a detectar para una prensa:\n\n* `buttonUp`(arriba)\n* `buttonDown` (abajo)\n* `buttonLeft` (izquierda)\n* `buttonRight` (derecho)\n* `buttonX`\n* `buttonY`\n* `buttonA`\n* `buttonB`\n* `buttonL1`\n* `buttonL2`\n* `buttonR1`\n* `buttonR2`","signature":"controller.buttonUp.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_column","markdown":"# Columna del Cursor\n \nReporta el número de columna de la ubicación del cursor de la pantalla del controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.column()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa fila del cursor reporta un rango de **1 a 80**.\n\nEl V5 Controller no permita cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de fuente del V5 Controller - Número de Columnas:**\n\n* Fuente Estándar - 20 Columnas (por defecto)","signature":"controller.screen.column()"},"sensing_controller_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_row","markdown":"# Fila del Cursor\n\nReporta del número de fila de la ubicación del cursor de la pantalla del Controller.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.row()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nFila del Cursor reporta un rango de **1 a 20**.\n\nEl V5 Controller no permite cambiar el tamaño de la fuente impresa en la pantalla.\n\n**Tamaño de Fuente del V5 Controller- Número de Filas:**\n\n* Fuente Estándar - 3 Filas (por defecto)","signature":"controller.screen.row()"},"sensing_drivetrain_current":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_current","markdown":"# Corriente del Chasis\n\nInforma de la cantidad de corriente (potencia) que la transmisión está utilizando actualmente.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa corriente de conducción indica un rango de **0.0 a 2.5 amperios**.","signature":"drivetrain.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency","markdown":"# Eficiencia de la Conducción\n \nReporta de la eficiencia del Chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.efficiency(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nRficiencia de la Unidad informa del valor de la potencia (en vatios) que utiliza el motor (entrada), frente a la cantidad de potencia (en vatios) que proporciona el motor (salida).\n\nUna V5 Chasis normalmente alcanza una eficiencia máxima de **65%** en casos de uso normales.\n\nEficiencia de conducción indica un rango de **0% a 100%**","signature":"drivetrain.efficiency(PERCENT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_heading":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_heading","markdown":"# Dirección del Chasis\n \nReporta de la dirección a la que se enfrenta el Chasis utilizando la posición angular actual del sensor giroscópico (Gyro).\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando de Dirección del Chasis reporta de un aumento en el rumbo al girar en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\nDirección del Chasis reporta de un rango de **0.00 a 359.99 grados**.","signature":"drivetrain.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_done":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_done","markdown":"# Conducir ya Termino\n\nReporta si el chasis ha completado su movimiento.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.is_done()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nConducir ya termino reporta **True** cuando el Chasis ha completado su movimiento.\n\nConducir ya termino reporta **False** cuando el Chasis sigue en movimiento.","signature":"drivetrain.is_done()"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving","markdown":"# Chasis está Moviendo\n \nReporta si el Chasis se está moviendo actualmente.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.is_moving()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nChasis está moviendo reporta **True** cuando los Motores del Chasis se están moviendo.\n\nChasis está moviendo reporta **False** cuando se detienen los motores del Chasis.","signature":"drivetrain.is_moving()"},"sensing_drivetrain_power":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_power","markdown":"# Potencia del Chasis\n\nInforma de la cantidad de potencia que el Chasis está generando actualmente.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.power(PowerUnits.WATT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPotencia del Chasis informa de un rango de **0.0 a 22.0 watts**.","signature":"drivetrain.power(PowerUnits.WATT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_rotation":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_rotation","markdown":"# Rotación del Chasis\n \nReporta del ángulo de rotación del Chasis cuando se configura con un Gyro Sensor de 3 Hilos o un V5 Inertial Sensor.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nRotación del Chasis reporta un valor **positive** cuando el Chasis gira en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\nRotación del Chasis reporta un valor **negative** cuando el Chasis gira en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj.","signature":"drivetrain.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_drivetrain_temperature":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_temperature","markdown":"# Temperatura del Chasis\n \nReporta la temperatura de los V5 Smart Motors que alimentan el Chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.temperature(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nTemperatura del Chasis indica un rango de **0% a 100%**.","signature":"drivetrain.temperature(PERCENT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_torque":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_torque","markdown":"# Par de Conducción\n\nInforma de la cantidad de torsiรณn (fuerza rotacional) que utiliza actualmente el Chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.torque(TorqueUnits.NM)\n```\n\n## Cรณmo Utilizar\n\nPar de Conducción reporta un rango de **0.0 a 18.6 libras-pulgada (InLB) o 0.0 a 2.1 Newton-metros (Nm)**.","signature":"drivetrain.torque(TorqueUnits.NM)"},"sensing_drivetrain_velocity":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad de Conducciรณn\n \nReporta la velocidad actual del Chasis.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.velocity(UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nVelocidad de Conducciรณn reporta un rango de -100% a 100% o -600rpm a 600rpm.\n\nEl parámetro 'UNIT'(Unidad) se puede reemplazar con **PERCENT** (Por Ciento) o **RPM**.\n\nVelocidad de Conducciรณn reportará un rango de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranajes instalado en los V5 Smart Motors utilizados en el Chasis.\n\n* Red Cartridge (Cartucho Rojo): -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge (Cartucho Verde): -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge (Cartucho Azul): -600rpm to 600rpm","signature":"drivetrain.velocity(PERCENT)"},"sensing_encoder_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_position","markdown":"# Posición del Codificador de Eje\n \nReporta de la posición de rotación del Codificador de Eje.\n\n```don\nencoder.position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl parámetro 'UNITS' (Unidad) acepta **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS** (Vueltas) como valor.\n\nLa posición del codificador de eje informa de la distancia que el codificador de eje ha girado en números enteros para grados, y números decimales para giros.","signature":"encoder.position(DEGREES)"},"sensing_encoder_set_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_set_position","markdown":"# Establecer la Posición del Codificador de Eje\n \nEstablece la posición del Codificador de Eje en el valor dado.\n\n```don\nencoder.set_position(VALUE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'encoder.set_position' (Establecer la Posición del Codificador de Eje) se puede utilizar para establecer la posición del codificador de eje a cualquier valor dado.\n\nEl parámetro 'UNITS' (Unidad) acepta **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS** (Vueltas) como un valor.\n\nNormalmente, el comando set shaft encoder position (Establecer la Posición del Codificador de Eje) se utiliza para ajustar la posición a 0, para restablecer la posición del codificador de eje.","signature":"encoder.set_position(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_encoder_velocity":{"name":"sensing_encoder_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad del Codificador de Eje\n\nReporta de la velocidad actual de un codificador de eje.\n\n```don\nencoder.velocity(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nVelocidad del codificador del eje indica un valor decimal en grados por segundo (dps) o rotaciones por minuto (rpm).\n\nEl parámetro 'UNITS' (Unidades) acepta **VelocityUnits.DPS** o **RPM** como valor.","signature":"encoder.velocity(VelocityUnits.DPS)"},"sensing_gyro_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_calibrate","markdown":"# Calibrar el Sensor Giroscopio\n\nCalibrar el Sensor Gyro se utiliza para reducir la cantidad de deriva generada por Sensor Gyro.\n\n```don\ngyro.calibrate()\n```\n\nLa deriva ocurre cuando el Sensor Gyro detecta incorrectamente el movimiento aunque el sensor no se esté moviendo físicamente.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl Sensor Gyro debe permanecer inmóvil durante el proceso de calibración. El proceso de calibración tardará aproximadamente 2 segundos en completarse.","signature":"gyro.calibrate()"},"sensing_gyro_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Ángulo de Dirección del Gyro\n \nReportaa la dirección actual del Sensor de Giroscopio de 3 Hilos en Grados.\n\n```don\ngyro.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando reporta un aumento en la dirección al girar en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\n`gyro.heading` reporta de un rango entre **0.00 a 359.99**.","signature":"gyro.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Ángulo de Rotación del Giro\n \nReporta del ángulo de rotación actual del Sensor de Giroscopio de 3 Hilos en grados.\n\n```don\ngyro.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nRotación del Giro reporta un valor **positive** cuando el sensor Gyro gira en la dirección **en el sentido de las agujas del reloj**.\n\nRotación del Giro reporta un valor **negative** cuando el sensor Gyro gira en la dirección **en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj**.","signature":"gyro.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_heading","markdown":"# Establecer Dirección de Giroscopio\n\nEstablecer la dirección actual del Sensor Giroscópico (Gyro) en un valor establecido.\n \n```don\ngyro.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando establecer dirección de giroscopio se puede utilizar para establecer la posición del giroscopio en cualquier dirección en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\nEste comando se utiliza normalmente para restablecer la dirección del sensor Gyro cuando el valor se establece en 0.\n\nEl parámetro 'HEADING' (dirección) acepta un rango de **0.0 a 359.99 grados**.\n\nEl comando establecer dirección puede aceptar decimales, enteros o valores numéricos.","signature":"gyro.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer Rotación de Giroscopio\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del sensor de giroscopio de 3 hilos o del sensor inercial V5 en un valor determinado.\n\n```don \ngyro.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando de Establecer Rotación de Giroscopio se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del Chasis a cualquier valor positivo (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) o negativo (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj).\n\nEl comando de Establecer Rotación de Giroscopio puede aceptar decimales, enteros o valores numéricos.","signature":"gyro.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Aceleración Inercial\n\nReporta del valor de aceleración de uno de los ejes (x, y o z) en el Sensor Intertial.\n\n```don\ninertial.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nAceleración informa de un rango de **-4.0 a 4.0 Gs**.\n\nChoose which axis to use:\n\n* El X-axis (Eje-X) informa de la aceleración cuando el sensor interial se mueve **lado a lado**\n* El Y-axis (Eje-Y) informa de la aceleración cuando el sensor interial se mueve **de arriba a abajo**\n* El Z-axis (Eje-Z) informa de la aceleración cuando el sensor interial se mueve **hacia adelante hasta atrás**","signature":"inertial.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS)"},"sensing_inertial_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_calibrate","markdown":"# Calibrar Sensor Inercial\n \nCalibración del Sensor Inercial se utiliza para reducir la cantidad de deriva generada por el Sensor Inercial.\n\n```don\ninertial.calibrate()\n```\n\nLa deriva se produce cuando el Sensor Inercial detecta incorrectamente el movimiento aunque el sensor no se esté moviendo físicamente.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl Sensor Inercial debe permanecer inmóvil durante el proceso de calibración. El proceso de calibración tardará aproximadamente 2 segundos en completarse.","signature":"inertial.calibrate()"},"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Tasa de Giroscopio Inercial\n\nObtiene la velocidad de rotación de uno de los ejes (x, y o z) en el Sensor Inercial.\n\n```don\ninertial.gyro_rate(AxisType.XAXIS, RPM)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa velocidad de giro indica un rango de **-1000.0 a 1000.0** en dps (grados por segundo).\n\nElija qué eje utilizar.\n\n* El X-Axis (Eje X) informa de la velocidad de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el eje X (basado en la orición del sensor)\n* El X-Axis (Eje Y) informa de la velocidad de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el eje Y (basado en la orición del sensor)\n* El X-Axis (Eje Z) informa de la velocidad de rotación cuando el sensor inercial gira en el eje Z (basado en la orición del sensor)","signature":"inertial.gyro_rate(AxisType.XAXIS, RPM)"},"sensing_inertial_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_heading","markdown":"# Ángulo de Dirección Inercial \n\nReports the V5 Inertial Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```don\ninertial.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `inertial.heading` informa de un aumento en el rumbo al girar en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\n`inertial.heading` reports un rango de 0.00 a 359.99 grados.","signature":"inertial.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_orientation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Orientación Inercial\n\nObtiene un ángulo de orientación del Sensor Inercial. Informa del valor de unidad especificado por el parámetro del Sensor Inercial.\n\n```don\ninertial.orientation(OrientationType.ROLL, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\nLa orientación notificada viene determinada por el eje seleccionado (x, y, o z).\n\n* El X-axis (Eje-x) representa el cabeceo, que informa de un valor entre -90 y +90 grados).\n* El Y-axis (Eje-y) representa el rollo, que informa de un valor entre -180 y +180 grados)\n* El Z-axis (Eje-z) representa la orientación, que indica un valor entre -180 y +180 grados)","signature":"inertial.orientation(OrientationType.ROLL , DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_rotation","markdown":"# Angulo de Rotación Inercial\n \nReporta del ángulo de rotación actual del V5 Sensor Inercial de 3 hilos en grados.\n\n```don\ninertial.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando 'inertial.rotation' reporta de un valor positivo cuando el Sensor Inercial gira en el sentido de las agujas del reloj.\n\n`inertial.rotation` informa de un valor negativo cuando el Sensor Inercial gira en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj.","signature":"inertial.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_heading","markdown":"# Establecer Dirección del Inercial\n\nEstablece la dirección actual del Sensor Inercial en un valor establecido.\n\n```don\ninertial.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`inertial.set_heading` se puede utilizar para establecer la posición del giroscopio en cualquier dirección en el sentido de las agujas del reloj. Este comando se utiliza normalmente para restablecer la orientación del Sensor Inercial cuando la dirección se establece en un valor de 0.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` Se utiliza normalmente para restablecer la orientación de la dirección del Sensor Inercial cuando un valor se establece en 0.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` acepta un rango de 0.0 a 359.99 grados.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` pueden aceptar decimales, enteros o valores numéricos.","signature":"inertial.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_rotation","markdown":"# Establecer Rotación Inercial\n\nEstablece el ángulo de rotación del Sensor Inercial de 3-Hilos en un valor determinado.\n\n```don\ninertial.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando `inertial.set_rotation` se puede utilizar para establecer el ángulo de rotación del Sensor Inercial a cualquier valor positivo (en el sentido de las agujas del reloj) o negativo (en sentido contrario a las agujas del reloj).\n\n`inertial.set_rotation` acepta un rango de cualquier decimal positivo o negativo o entero.","signature":"inertial.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_light_brightness":{"name":"sensing_light_brightness","markdown":"# Brillo del Sensor de Luz\n\nReporta la cantidad de luz detectada por el sensor de luz.\n\n```don\nlight.brightness(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`light.brightnes` informa de un rango de **0% a 100%**.\n\nUna gran cantidad de luz detectada reportará un alto valor de brillo.\n\nUna pequeña cantidad de luz detectada reportará un valor de bajo brillo.","signature":"light.brightness(PERCENT)"},"sensing_limit_switch_pressing":{"name":"sensing_limit_switch_pressing","markdown":"# Pulsando el Interruptor de Límite\n\nInforma si el Interruptor de Límite está siendo presionado.\n\n```don\nlimit_switch.pressing()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPresionar el interruptor de límite informa **True** si se está presionando el interruptor de límite.\n\nPresionar el interruptor de límite informa **False** si no se está presionando el interruptor de límite","signature":"limit_switch.pressing()"},"sensing_line_tracker_reflectivity":{"name":"sensing_line_tracker_reflectivity","markdown":"# Reflectividad del Rastreador de Línea\n\nInforma de la cantidad de luz reflejada con el Sensor de Rastreador de Línea .\n\n```don\nline_tracker.reflectivity(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLas superficies de color claro reflejarán más luz e reportarán un alto valor de reflectividad.\n\nLas superficies de color oscuro reflejarán menos luz e reportarán  un valor de reflectividad bajo.\n\nLa unidad predeterminada es 'PERCENT' (per ceinto) que devuelve un valor entero de **0% a 100%**.","signature":"line_tracker.reflectivity(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_current":{"name":"sensing_motor_current","markdown":"# Corriente del Motor\n\nInforma de la cantidad de corriente que un V5 Smart Motor está utilizando actualmente en amperios (amperios).\n\n```don\nmotor.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nCorriente de Motor reporta de un rango de **0.0 a 2.5 amperios**.","signature":"motor.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_motor_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_motor_efficiency","markdown":"# Eficiencia del Motor\n \nReporta de la eficiencia de un V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.efficiency(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEficiencia del Motor reporta del valor de la potencia (en vatios) que está utilizando el motor (entrada), frente a la cantidad de potencia (en vatios) que proporciona el motor (salida).\n\nUn V5 Smart Motor suele alcanzar una eficiencia máxima del 65% en casos de uso normales.\n\nLa eficiencia del motor reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**.","signature":"motor.efficiency(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_is_done":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_done","markdown":"# Motor ha Terminado\n\nReporta si el V5 Smart Motor seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\n```don\nmotor.is_done()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nMotor ha Terminado reporta **True** cuando el motor seleccionado ha completado su movimiento.\n\nMotor ha Terminado reporta **False** cuando el motor seleccionado todavía se está moviendo.","signature":"motor.is_done()"},"sensing_motor_is_spinning":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Motor está Girando\n\nReporta si el V5 Smart Motor seleccionado está girando actualmente.\n\n```don\nmotor.is_spinning()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nMotor está Girando reporta **True** cuando el motor seleccionado todavía se está moviendo.\n\nMotor está Girando reporta **False** cuando se detiene el motor seleccionado.","signature":"motor.is_spinning()"},"sensing_motor_position":{"name":"sensing_motor_position","markdown":"# Posición del Motor\n\nReporta de la posición de rotación actual del V5 Smart Motor seleccionado.\n\n```don\nmotor.position(UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nLa posición del motor informa de la posición del V5 Smart Motor en números enteros para grados, y números decimales de giros.\n\nLos valores aceptables para 'UNIT' (Unidad) son: **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS* (Vueltas).","signature":"motor.position(DEGREES)"},"sensing_motor_power":{"name":"sensing_motor_power","markdown":"# Potencia del Motor\n\nReporta de la cantidad de potencia que el V5 Smart Motor está generando actualmente.\n\n```don\nmotor.power(PowerUnits.WATT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPotencia del Motor reporta de un rango de **0.0 a 11.0 vatios**.","signature":"motor.power(PowerUnits.WATT)"},"sensing_motor_temperature":{"name":"sensing_motor_temperature","markdown":"# Temperatura del Motor\n\nInforma de la temperatura de un V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.temperature(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl uso del comando Temperatura del Motor puede ayudar a los usuarios a desarrollar lógica para evitar que sus V5 Smart Motors se sobrecalienten durante un uso intensivo.\n\nTemperatura del Motor reporta un rango de **0% a 100%**.","signature":"motor.temperature(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_torque":{"name":"sensing_motor_torque","markdown":"# Par Motor\n\nInforma de la cantidad de par (fuerza de rotación) que un V5 Smart Motor está utilizando actualmente.\n\n```don\nmotor.torque(TorqueUnits.NM)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPar Motor reporta un rango de **0.0 a 18.6 pulgadas-libras (InLB) o 0.0 a 2.1 Newton-metros (Nm)**.","signature":"motor.torque(TorqueUnits.NM)"},"sensing_motor_velocity":{"name":"sensing_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Velocidad del Motor\n\nReporta de la velocidad actual de un V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```don\nmotor.velocity(UNIT)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nVelocidad del Motor reporta un rango de **-100% a 100%** o **-600rpm a 600rpm**.\n\nLos valores aceptables para el parámetro 'UNIT' (Unidad) son: **DEGREES** (Grados) o **RPM**.\n\nVelocidad del Motor reportará de un rango de \"rotaciones por minuto\" basado en el cartucho de engranajes instalado en los V5 Smart Motor.\n\n* Red Cartridge (Cartucho Rojo): -100rpm a 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge (Cartucho Verde): -200rpm a 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge (Cartucho Azul): -600rpm a 600rpm","signature":"motor.velocity(PERCENT)"},"sensing_potentiometer_angle":{"name":"sensing_potentiometer_angle","markdown":"# Angulo del Potenciómetro\n\nDevuelve la posición angular del potenciómetro.\n\n```don\npotentiometer.angle(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\n`potentiometer.angle` devuelve un valor decimal (como un valor doble) para informar de la posición angular del potenciómetro.\n\nEl parámetro 'UNITS' (Unidads) acepta **DEGREES** (Grados) o **TURNS** (Vueltos) como valor.","signature":"potentiometer.angle(PERCENT)"},"sensing_range_finder_distance":{"name":"sensing_range_finder_distance","markdown":"# Distancia desde el Buscador de Rangos\n\nReporta de la distancia del objeto más cercano desde el sensor Ultrasonic Range Finder.\n\n```don\nrange_finder.distance(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nDistancia Desde reporta un rango de 30 mm a 3000 mm o 2 pulgadas a 115 pulgadas.\n\nEl parámetro 'UNITS'(Unidad) acepta **MM** o **INCHES** (Pulgadas) como valor.","signature":"range_finder.distance(MM)"},"sensing_range_finder_found_object":{"name":"sensing_range_finder_found_object","markdown":"# Buscador de Rangos Encontro Objeto\n\nReporta si el sensor Ultrasonic Range Finder detecta un objeto dentro de su campo de visión.\n\n```don\nrange_finder.found_object()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nObjeto Encontrado informa **True** cuando el sensor Ultrasonic Range Finder ve un objeto o superficie dentro de su campo de visión.\n\nObjeto Encontrado informa **False** cuando el sensor Ultrasonic Range Finder no detecta un objeto o superficie.","signature":"range_finder.found_object()"},"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled":{"name":"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled","markdown":"# Controlador Activado\n\nActiva o desactiva las acciones configuradas por el Controller desde el menú dispositivos.\n\n```don\nremote_control_code_enabled = False\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nSeleccione activar o desactivar las acciones del Contoroller configuradas. \n\nDe forma predeterminada, el Controller está activado en todos los proyectos.","signature":"remote_control_code_enabled = False"},"sensing_vision_largest_object":{"name":"sensing_vision_largest_object","markdown":"# Objeto Existe\n\nReporta sobre un objeto detectado desde el Vision Sensor.\n\n```don\nvision.largest_object()\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara utilizar el bloque de objetos Visión, siga estos pasos:\n\n1. Configure su Vision Sensor mediante la ventana Dispositivos.\n2. Utilice la instantánea (snapshot) para capturar una imagen de Vision Sensor y busque una firma / código de color.\n3. Utilice Objeto Existe para comprobar si el sensor de visión ha detectado la firma o el código de color solicitados.\n4. Una vez que el Vision Sensor detecta un objeto, puede utilizar otros comandos de Visión para obtener más información sobre el objeto detectado.\n\n* Utilice Definir Elemento de Objeto de Visión para establecer el objeto detectado sobre el que desea obtener más información. De forma predeterminada, se utiliza el objeto más grande detectado.\n* Utilice Recuento de Objetos para determinar cuántos objetos se han detectado de ese código de firma/color solicitado.\n* Utilice Objeto de Visión para determinar qué información se debe informar del objeto detectado.","signature":"vision.largest_object()"},"sensing_vision_take_snapshot":{"name":"sensing_vision_take_snapshot","markdown":"# Instantánea\n\nToma una instantánea del Vision Sensor.\n\n```don\nvision.take_snapshot(SIGNATURE)\n```\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nEl comando Instantánea capturará la imagen actual del sensor de visión para procesarla y analizarla en busca de códigos y firmas de color.\n\nNormalmente, primero se requiere una instantánea antes de usar cualquier otro comando de Vision Sensor.","signature":"vision.take_snapshot(SIGNATURE)"},"variables_my_2d_list":{"name":"variables_my_2d_list","markdown":"# Variable de Lista 2D\n\nLas variables de lista 2D se utilizan para almacenar listas con varias filas y columnas.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una variable de lista 2D, cree un nombre de variable único y significativo. Esto significa que el nombre de la variable debe describir con precisión la naturaleza de sus valores.\n\nPor ejemplo, una variable de lista 2D llamada \"coordenadas\" puede usarse para almacenar múltiples conjuntos de valores de coordenadas.\n\nDeclare esta lista usando un símbolo igual único '=' después del nombre de su lista seguido de corchetes '[ ]'.\n\nDentro de estos corchetes, inserte varios conjuntos de corchetes, separados por una coma, así: '[[ ], [ ]]'. Se pueden anidar más de dos conjuntos de corchetes dentro del conjunto de corchetes más externo.\n\nIncluya valores separados por una coma o ',' en sus respectivos corchetes. Si la variable está almacenando cadenas, coloque la coma fuera del encierro '\" \"'.\n\nCada conjunto interno de corchetes representa una fila de elementos de lista. El índice del elemento dentro de la fila representa una columna de la lista 2D.\n\nPara acceder al valor de una lista 2D, utilice el nombre de la lista, seguido inmediatamente de dos índices entre corchetes. El primer índice hace referencia a la fila, mientras que el segundo índice hace referencia a la columna de la lista 2D. Tenga en cuenta que los índices de matriz comienzan en 0, no en 1.\n\nPor ejemplo, dada una lista 2D 'coordenadas = [[X1, Y1], [X2, Y2]]', la expresión 'coordenadas[0][0]' devolverá 'X1'. \n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nEste ejemplo muestra que a una variable llamada my_list se le asignan dos listas de colores separadas.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [[\"Green\", \"Red\", \"Blue\"], [\"Black\", \"Yellow\", \"Orange\"]]\n```\n\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEste ejemplo muestra que a una variable llamada my_list se le asignan dos listas de números separadas.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]\n```","signature":"my_2d_list = [\\n\\t[0,0,0],\\n\\t[0,0,0],\\n\\t[0,0,0]\\n]"},"variables_my_boolean":{"name":"variables_my_boolean","markdown":"# Variable Booleana\n\nVariables booleanas pueden contener los valores **True** o **False**.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una variable booleana, cree un nombre de variable único y significativo. Esto significa que el nombre de la variable debe describir con precisión el valor que está almacenando.\n\nPor ejemplo, una variable 'pulsado' debe usarse para almacenar el valor de si se pulsa un botón.\n\nDeclare esta variable con un símbolo igual '=' después del nombre booleano. Su valor puede ser 'True' o 'Falso'.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo se asigna un valor 'True' a 'my_variable' .\n\n```don\nmy_variable = True\n```","signature":"my_boolean = True"},"variables_my_list":{"name":"variables_my_list","markdown":"# Lista de Variables\n\nListas de Variables se utilizan para almacenar varios valores.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una variable de lista, cree un nombre de variable descriptivo. Esto significa que el nombre de la variable debe describir con precisión la naturaleza de sus valores.\n\nPor ejemplo, una lista de variables 'colores' se puede utilizar para almacenar varios valores de color.\n\nPara asignar una lista de valores a una lista de variables, utilice el operador '=', seguido de valores separados por comas encerrados entre corchetes, '[ ]'.\n\nSi los valores son números, las comas de separación deben venir justo después de cada valor.\n\n`mi_lista_numerica = [1, 2, 3]`\n\nSi los valores son cadenas, las comas deben ir fuera de la '\" \"'.\n\n`mi_lista_decadenas = [\"Hello\", \"World\"]`\n\nPara acceder a un valor específico en la lista de variables, escriba el nombre de la lista de variables, seguido inmediatamente de un índice incluido por un conjunto de corchetes. Tenga en cuenta que el índice de una matriz comienza en 0, no en 1.\n\nPor ejemplo, `mi_lista_decadenas[0]` devolverá el valor `\"Hello\"`.\n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nThis example shows a variable called my_list being assigned the string values of several colors.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [\"Green\", \"Red\", \"Blue\"]\n```\n\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEste ejemplo muestra una variable llamada my_list que se le asignan varios números.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [1, 2, 3]\n```","signature":"my_list = [0,0,0]"},"variables_my_number":{"name":"variables_my_number","markdown":"# Variable Numérica\n\nLas variables numéricas se utilizan para almacenar valores numéricos.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una variable numérica, cree un nombre de variable significativo. This means that the variable name should accurately describe the value that it is storing. \n\nPor ejemplo, se debe utilizar una variable 'contador' para almacenar el valor de un contador.\n\nPara asignar un valor a la variable, utilice el operador '='. \n\n## Ejemplo 1\n\nEste ejemplo mantiene el nombre de variable por defecto 'my_number' y le asigna un valor de 10.\n\n```don\nmy_number = 10\n```\n## Ejemplo 2\n\nEste ejemplo le da a la variable el nombre 'three_plus_two' y almacena el resultado de los 3 agregados a 2. \n\n```don\nthree_plus_two = 3 + 2\n```","signature":"my_number = 1"},"variables_my_string":{"name":"variables_my_string","markdown":"# Variable de Cadena\n\nVariables de Cadena se utilizan para almacenar cadenas.\n\n## Cómo Utilizar\n\nPara crear una variable de cadena, cree un nombre de variable significativo. Esto significa que el nombre de la variable debe describir con precisión su valor. \n\nPor ejemplo, se debe utilizar una variable 'nombre' para almacenar el valor de un nombre.\n\nPara asignar una cadena a una variable de cadena, utilice el operador '='. Su valor de cadena se puede incluir en '\" \"' o '' ''.\n\n## Ejemplo\n\nEn este ejemplo se muestra una variable llamada my_string que se le asigna el valor de cadena '\"Hello\"'.\n\n```don\nmy_string = \"Hello\"\n```","signature":"my_string = \\\"Hello World\\\""}}},"fi":{"blocks":{"acceleration_of":{"name":"acceleration_of","markdown":"# Kiihtyvyys\n\nAntaa kiihtyvyysarvon yhdeltä akselilta, jota mitataan Analog Accelerometer-laitteella.\n\n![acceleration_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kiihtyvyys** antaa arvoja välillä **-2.0 G - 2.0 G** tai **-6.0 G - 6.0 G** riippuen jumpperi asetuksista Analog Accelerometer-laitteessa.\n\nValitse laite, jota käytät\n\n![acceleration_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_device.png)\n\n**Kiihtyvyys** arvoja voi laittaa ympyrämuotoisiin kenttiin blokkien arvokentissä.\n\n![acceleration_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_inserted.png)"},"activate_emergency_stop":{"name":"activate_emergency_stop","markdown":"# Aktivoi hätäpysäytys\n\nAktivoi hätäpysäytyksen (tai E-stop) painikkeen V5 robottikädelle.\n\n![estop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/activate_emergency_stop/estop_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nThätäpysäytys nappi pysäyttää jokaisen työaseman V5 Älymoottorin tai sensorin, jotka on liitetty V5 aivoihin. \n\n![estop_robot](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/activate_emergency_stop/estop_robot.png)\n\nValitse mitä robottikättä käytetään\n\n![select_estop_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/activate_emergency_stop/select_estop_arm.png)\n\n**Aktivoi hätäpysäytys** blokki on usein käytetty Kun painonappia painettu -blokin kanssa. Tällä varmistetaan että kaikki V5 moottorit ja sensorit , jotka on liitetty työpöydän aivoihin, pysähtyvät samaan aikaan, kun painonappia painettu (E-stop) painettu.\n![estop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/activate_emergency_stop/estop_example.png)"},"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Lisää\n\nLisää/laske kaksi arvoa yhteen ja antaa summan.\n\n\n![add](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/add/add.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Lisää** blokissa voi käyttää kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n**Lisää** blokin voi laittaa muiden blokkien ympyräuotoisiin arvokenttiin. \n\nLaske yhteen kaksi lukua.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nLaske yhteen kaksi muuttujaa.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nLaske yhteen kahden sensorin antamaa arvoa.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# Ja\n\nRaoportoi onko kahden Boolean muuttujan molemmat arvot tosia.  \n\n![and](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/and/and.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ja** blokki antaa arvon **tosi** kun molemmat ehdot ovat **tosia**. \n\n**Ja** blokki antaa arvon **epätosi** kun molemmat tai toinen ehdoista ovat/on **epätosia**. \n\n![and_shape](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tutkitaan, onko kahta VEX IQ -ohjaimen nappia yhtäaikaa painettu alas.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/and/and_sensors.png)\n\n**Ja** blokki antaa arvon **tosi** kun molemmat **Ohjainnappi X** ja **Ohjainnappi A** on painettu alas. \n\nMuutoin **Ja** blokki antaa arvon **epätosi**.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/and/and_truth.png)"},"angle_of":{"name":"angle_of","markdown":"# Kulma\n\nAntaa 3-lanka Potentiometrin kulman.\n\n![angle_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/angle_of/angle_of_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kulma** antaa arvot välillä **0% - 100%** tai **0.0 - 250.0 astetta**.\n\nValise laite , jota käytät.\n\n![angle_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/angle_of/angle_of_device.png)\n\nvalitse yksikkö, joko % taia astetta.\n\n![angle_of_block_parameters](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/angle_of/angle_of_parameters.png)\n\n**Kulma** arvon voi sijoittaa pyöreämuotosiin blokkien arvokenttiin.\n\n![angle_of_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/angle_of/angle_of_inserted.png)\n"},"arm_get_joint_value":{"name":"arm_get_joint_value","markdown":"# Nivelen potentiometri arvo\n\nAntaa neljän robottikäden nivelen potentiometriarvot työpisteellä.\n\n![joint_potentiometer_value](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/arm_get_joint_value/joint_potentiometer_value.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Nivelen potentiometri arvo** saadaan erikseen jokaisesta nivelestä. Blokkia voi hyödyntää kun määrittelee masterointi arvot nivelille.\n\n**Nivelen potentiometri arvo** antaa arvot välillä **0 - 4095**.\n\nValitse robottikäsi, jota käytät.\n\n![joint_potentiometer_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/arm_get_joint_value/joint_potentiometer_arm.png)\n\nValitse nivel, jota käytät. \n\n![joint_option_potentiometer_value](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/arm_get_joint_value/joint_option_potentiometer_value.png)\n\n**Nivelen potentiometri arvo** arvoja voi sijoittaa ympyrämuotoisiin blokkien arvokenttiin.\n\n![print_potentiometer_value](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/arm_get_joint_value/print_potentiometer_value.png)"},"arm_get_position":{"name":"arm_get_position","markdown":"# Käden paikka\n\nAntaa tänhetkisen robottikäden paikkakoordinaatin x, y, tai z-koordinaatistossa.\n\n![arm_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/arm_get_position/arm_position_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Käden paikka** antaa käsirobotin asennon x, y, tai z-koordinaatistossa..\n\nValitse käsirobotti, jota käytetään. \n\n![arm_position_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/arm_get_position/arm_position_arm.png)\n\nvalise akseli, jota tarkastellaan. \n\n![arm_position_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/arm_get_position/arm_position_axis.png)\n\n**Käden paikka** arvoja voi sijoitta ympyrämuotoisiin kenttiin muissa blokeissa.\n\n![arm_position_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/arm_get_position/arm_position_inserted.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä käsi liikkuu koordinaattiin (6, 0, 4). **Tulosta** blokki tulostaa käden nykyisen x-asennon **Käden paikka** blokilla konsolille.\n\n![arm_position_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/arm_get_position/arm_position_example.png)"},"battery_current":{"name":"battery_current","markdown":"# Akun virrankulutus\n\nAntaa akun virrankulutuksen.\n\n![battery_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/battery_current/battery_current_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Akun virrankulutus** antaa arvot välillä **0.0 amps - 20.0 amps**.\n\n**Akun virrankulutus** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä..\n\n![battery_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/battery_current/battery_current_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Akun varaus %\n\nKertoo lataustason VEX IQ Aivojen akussa.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Akun varaus %** antaa luvun väliltä **0% - 100%**.\n\n**Akun varaus %** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)"},"battery_voltage":{"name":"battery_voltage","markdown":"# Akun lataus voltteina\n\nAntaa V5 akun lataustason voltteina.\n\n![battery_voltage_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Akun lataus voltteina** antaa arvot välillä **10.0 volts - 14.4 volts**.\n\n**Akun lataus voltteina** voi käyttää ympyrämuotoisissa blokkien arvokentissä.\n\n![battery_voltage_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_inserted.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Boolean muuttuja\n\nAntaa Boolean muuttujan arvon.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n##Miten käytetään\n\n**Boolean muuttuja** saa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi**. Käytä *Aseta arvoon** blokkia, kun päivität muuttujan arvon.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\n**Boolean muuttuja** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa toisten blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nBoolean muuttujan saa tehtyä **Tee Boolean** painikkeella.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Keskeytä\n\nKeskeyttää heti toistorakenteen sisällä komentojen suorituksen.\n\n![break](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/break/break.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun komento **keskeytä** blokki on lisätty toistorakenteen sisälle, se aiheuttaa toiston komentojen päättymisen. \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin ja tarkistaa onko Aivojen  **ylös** nappia painettu. \n\nJos **ylös** nappia on **painettu**, **keskeytä** blokki aiheuttaa toistokomentojen suorituksen päättymisen ja ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n\n![break_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Valovoima\n\nRaportoi Valosensorin havaitseman valon valovoiman/kirkkauden prosentteina.\n\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Valovoima** antaa arvot välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\nValitse Valo sensori, jota käytetään.\n\n![brightness_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\n**Valovoima** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![brightness_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Lähetä viesti\n\nLähettää viestin käynnistämään **Kun saan viestin** -blokin alla olevat blokit halutulla viestinimellä.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nViestin lähettäjän blokkipinon suoritus jatkuu heti viestilähetyksen jälkeen samaan aikaan kuin **Kun saan viestin** blokkia suoritetaan.\n\nValitse viestille nimi, joka läheteään **Lähetä viesti** -blokilla. Voit luoda myös uuden viestin.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Lähetä viesti ja odota\n\nLähettää viestin aktivoimalla **Kun saan viestin** hattublokin ja oodotetaan kunnes hattublokki on suorittasnut kaikki siinä nipussa olevat blokit.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKutsuja jää odotaan komennolla **Lähetä viesti ja odota** kunnes kutsun saanut hattublokki on suorittanut nipun komennot loppuun.\n\nValitse viestinimi, joka läheteään. Myös uusi viesti voidaan luoda samalla.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Kalibroi gyro\n\nVEX V5 Inertial sensorin tai 3-lanka Gyro sensorin kalibroinnilla estetään Gyro Sensorin virhettä (drifting).\n\nHeiluntaa tapahtuu, kun Gyro Sensori virheellisesti huomaa liikettä vaikka sensori on paikallaan.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\n# Miten käytetään\n\nGyro sensorin pitää olla levossa kun kalibrointi suoritetaan. Kalibrointi kestää n 2 s.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Muuta arvolla\n\nMuuttaa muuttujan arvoa syötetyllä määrällä.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Kuinka käytetään\n\nValitse muuttuja, voit samalla myös uudelleennimetä muuttujan tai poistaa sen.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\n**Muuta arvolla** blokissa voi käyttää kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja sekä numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTämä esimerkissä lisätään ajonopeutta 10 -yksiköllä jokaisella kierroksella **toista** blokissa.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Tyhjää kaikki rivit\n\nTyhjää Tulostus-konsolin V5 Aivojen näytön tai Ohjaimen näytön rivit.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Tyhjää kaikki rivit** ei muuta osoittimen paikkaa näytöllä. Käytä **Aseta kursori** kunnhaluat muuttaa kursorin paikkaa näytöllä.\n\n**Tyhjää kaikki rivit** blokki siirtää Tulostus konsolilla kursorin ikkunan ylös.\n\nValitse laite, jota käytät. Ohjain pitää ensiksi lisätä Laitteet-ikkunassa.\n\n![clear_all_rows_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_dropdown_with_console.png)"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Tyhjää rivi\n\nTyhjää yksittäisen rivin VEX V5 aivojen tai Ohjaimen näytöltä.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Tyhjää rivi** hyväksyy rivinumerot väliltä **1 - 20**.\n\nValitse laite , jota käytät. ohjain pitää ensiksi lisätä Laitteet -ikkunassa.\n\n![clear_row_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/clear_row/clear_row_dropdown.png)\n\n---\nV5 Aivot sallivat eikokoisia fontteja näytöllä. Fontin koko määrää, montako riviä näytölle tvoi tulostaa.\n\n**V5 Aivot Fontin koko - Rivimäärä:**\n\n* Extra Pieni - 20 riviä\n* Pieni - 16 riviä\n* Keskikokoinen - 12 riviä (Oletus\n* Iso - 8 riviä\n* Extra Iso - 6 riviä\n* Super Iso - 4 riviä\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/clear_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nV5 Ohjain ei salli erikokoisia kirjainkokoja.\n\n**V5 Controller Fontin koko - Rivimäärä:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 riviä (Oletus)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/clear_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Kommentti\n\nOhjelmoija voi kommenteilla selittää ohjelman toimintaa. \n\n![comment_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAmmattikoodaajat kommentoivat ohjelmiaan koko läpi ohjelman. Kommentit helpottavat myös virheiden selvitystä ja muiden kanssa yhteistyötä. \n\nLisää/päivitä teksti **Kommentti** blokkiin valitsemalla ensiksi neliösyöttökenttä ja päivitä teksti sitten ko.kenttään.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nKommentit eivät vaikuta muuhun suoritettavaan ohjelmaan sen ympärillä.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Ohjain\n\nVoit ottaa ohjaimen käyttöön tai poistaa käytöstä. Ohjain pitää ensiksi litätä Laitteet -ikkunassa.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOta ohjain käyttöön tai poista käytöstä. Oletuksena ohjain on käytössä.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nKäytetään ohjaimen ajopelin määritystä Laitteet -ikkunan Ohjaimen ajovalinnassa.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nAlussa Ohjain otetaan pois käytöstä. \n\nRobotti ajaa automaattina 6 tuumaa.\n\nLopuksi ohjain  **on käytössä** ja ajoa hallitaan normaalisti ohjaimen ajopelille määrityksen mukaisesti.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"controller_play_rumble":{"name":"controller_play_rumble","markdown":"# Väristä ohjainta\n\nsaa aikaan väristysilmiön V5 ohjaimeen.\n\n![controller_play_rumble](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Väristä ohjainta** ominaisuus käyttää V5 ohjaimen väristysmoottoria hyväksi.\n\nValitse väristystyyppi jota käytät.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_pattern](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_pattern.png)\n\nValitse V5 ohjain jota käytät.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_device.png)\n\n\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Moottorin sähkövirta\n\nAntaa moottorin sähkövirran käytön joko yksikössä prosentti (%) or ampeerisekunti (amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n**Moottorin sähkövirta** antaa arvot väliltä **0% - 100%** tai **0.0 - 2.5 amps**. \n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\n**Moottorin sähkövirta** arvoa voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Osoittimen sarake\n\nRaportoi VEX V5 aivojen tai ohjaimen näytöllä näkyvän osoittimen sarakearvon.\n\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Osoittimen sarake** antaa arvot välillä **1 - 80**.\n\n**Osoittimen sarake** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nV5 Aivot sallivat erikokoisia kirjaimia. Ne vaikuttavat myös näytön sarakemäärään seuraavasti:\n\n**V5 Aivojen Kirjasinkoko - sarakemäärä:**\n\n* Extra Pieni - 80 saraketta\n* Pieni - 68 saraketta\n* keskikoko - 48 saraketta (Oletus)\n* Iso - 32 saraketta\n* Extra Iso - 24 saraketta\n* Super Iso - 16 saraketta\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/cursor_column/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nV5 Ohjaimen näytöllä:\n\n**V5 Controller Kirjasinkoko - sarakemäärä:**\n\n* Standard Font - 20 Columns (Oletus)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/cursor_column/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Osoittimen rivi\n\nantaa VEX V5 aivojen tai ohjaimen näytön rivin, jolla kursori nyt on.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Osoittimen rivi** antaa rivinumeron väliltä **1 - 20**.\n\n**Osoittimen rivi** blokkia voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nV5 Aivot sallivat eikokoisia fontteja näytöllä. Fontin koko määrää, montako riviä näytölle tvoi tulostaa.\n\n**V5 Aivot Fontin koko - Rivimäärä:**\n\n* Extra Pieni - 20 riviä\n* Pieni - 16 riviä\n* Keskikokoinen - 12 riviä (Oletus\n* Iso - 8 riviä\n* Extra Iso - 6 riviä\n* Super Iso - 4 riviä\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/cursor_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nV5 Ohjain ei salli erikokoisia kirjainkokoja.\n\n**V5 Controller Fontin koko - Rivimäärä:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 riviä (Oletus)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/cursor_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"digital_in_signal":{"name":"digital_in_signal","markdown":"# Digitaalinen in\n\nAntaa tiedon, jos Digitaalinen in -sinaali on korkea.\n\n![digital_in_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/digital_in_signal/digital_in_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nV5 3-lanka porttifunktio 5V loogisen signaalin jännitetaso.\n\n**Digitaalinen in** blokki antaa arvon **tosi**jos digitaalinen in -signaali on korkea.\n\n**Digitaalinen in** blokki antaa arvon **epätosi**jos digitaalinen in -signaali on matala.\n\nValise laite, jota käytät. \n\n![digital_in_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/digital_in_signal/digital_in_select.png)\n\n**Digitaalinen in** Boolean blokki voidaan sijoittaa kuusikulmaisiin kenttiin muissa blokeissa.\n\n![digital_in_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/digital_in_signal/digital_in_insert.png)\n"},"distance_found_object":{"name":"distance_found_object","markdown":"# Löysi esineen\n\nAntaa tiedon havaitseeko etäisyysanturi esineen näkökentässään.\n\n![distance_found_object_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block1.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Löysi esineen** antaa arvon **tosi** jos se havaitsee esineen tai sen pinnan näkökentässään.\n\n**Löysi esineen** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos se ri havaitse esinetttä tai sen pintaa näkökentässään.\n\nValise etäisyysanturi, jota käytät.\n\n![distance_found_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block2.png)\n\n\n**Löysi esineen** blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoitta kuusikulmaisiin kenttiin muissa blokeissa.\n\n![distance_found_object_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block3.png)\n"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Etäisyys\n\nAntaa lähimmän esineen etäisyyden Ultrasonic etäisyysanturista.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Distance fromEtäisyys** antaa arvot välillä **30mm - 3000mm** tai **2 tuumaa - 115 tuumaa**.\n\nValitse Ultrasonic etäisyysanturi, jota käytät.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nValitse yksikkö, jolla whether **Etäisyys** mitataan joko tuumina tai mm. \n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\n**Etäisyys** blokin arvoja voi laittaa ympyrämuotoisiin kenttiin eri blokeissa.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"distance_object_distance":{"name":"distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Kohteen etäisyys\n\nAntaa lähimmän kohteen etäisyyden etäisyysanturista.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kohteen etäisyys** antaa arvot välillä **20mm - 2000mm**.\n\nValitse etäisyysanturi, jota käytät.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block2.png)\n\nValitse yksikkö, jonka **Kohteen etäisyys** antaa joko tuumina tai mm. \n\n![distance_object_distance_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block3.png)\n\n*Kohteen etäisyys** arvon voi sijoittaa ympyrämuotoisiin kenttiin muissa blokeissa.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block4.png)\n"},"distance_object_size":{"name":"distance_object_size","markdown":"# Kohteen koko\n\nAntaa tietoa, minkäkokoisen kohteen Etäisyysanturi havaitsee.  \n\n![distance_object_size_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nSensori määrittää kohten koon (Ei, pieni, keskikokoinen, laaja) siitä heijastuvan lasersäteilyn määrän perusteella.\n\nValitse sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![distance_object_size_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block1.png)\n\nAseta koko, mitä esinekokoa sensori etsii. Seinä tms on yleensä laaja valintavaihtoehto.\n\n![distance_object_size_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block2.png)\n\n**Kohteen koko** antaa arvon **tosi** jos etäisyysmittari havaitsee halutun kokoisen esineen.\n\n**Kohteen koko** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos etäisyysmittari ei havaitse halutun kokoista esinettä.\n\n**Kohteen koko** antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa kuusikulmaisten kenttien arvoiksi eri blokeissa.\n\n![distance_object_size_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block3.png)\n"},"distance_object_velocity":{"name":"distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Kohteen nopeus\n\nAntaa kohteen nopeuden yksiköss m/s.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kohteen nopeus** antaa esineen nopeuden yksikössä m/s.\n\nValitse etäisyysmittari, jota käytät\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block2.png)\n\n**Kohteen nopeus** arvoa voi käyttää ympyrämuotoissa blokkien kentissä.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block3.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Jakolasku\n\nlaskee ensimmäisen luvun jakamisen toisella luvulla.\n\n\n![divide](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Jakolasku** hyväksyy kokonais-ja desimaalilukuja sekä numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n**Jakolasku** blokin voi sijoittaa muiden blokkien pyöreisiin arvokenttiin. \n\nAnna jakolaskun tekijänumerot.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nJakolasku muuttujilla.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nJakolasku sensoreiden arvoilla.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"draw_circle":{"name":"draw_circle","markdown":"# Piirrä ympyrä\n\nPiirtää ympyrän V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n![draw_circle](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/draw_circle/draw_circle.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nThe Piirrä ympyrä** blokki vaatii 3 arvoa:\n\n* arvo 1: keskipiste X\n* arvo 2: keskipiste Y\n* arvo 3: Säde (pikseleinä)\n\nÄäriviivan väri asetetaan komennolla **aseta kynäväri**, oletus on valkoinen ääriviiva.\n\nTäyttöväri määrätään komennolla **aseta täyttöväri**, oletus on musta täyttö.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"draw_line":{"name":"draw_line","markdown":"# Piirrä viiva\n\nPiirrtää viivan V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n![draw_line](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/draw_line/draw_line.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Piirrä viiva** blokki tarvitsee 4 arvoa:\n\n* arvo 1: Alkupiste X koordinaatti\n* arvo 2: Alkupiste Y koordinaatti\n* arvo 3: Loppupiste X koordinaatti\n* arvo 4: Loppupiste Y koordinaatti\n\nViivan väri asetetaan komennolla **aseta kynäväri**.Oletus on valkoinen viiva.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_pixel":{"name":"draw_pixel","markdown":"# Piirrä pikseli\n\nPiirrä n V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n![draw_pixel](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/draw_pixel/draw_pixel.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Piirrä pikseli** blokki vaatii 2 arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: X koodinaatti\n* Arvo 1: Y koodinaatti\n\nPikselin väri määräytyy blokilla  **Aseta kynäväri**, oletus on valkoinen.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_rectangle":{"name":"draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Piirrä nelikulmio\n\nPiirtää nelikulmio V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n![draw_rectangle](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/draw_rectangle/draw_rectangle.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Piirrä nelikulmio** blokki tarvitsee 4 arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: Ylä oikea kulman X koordinaatti\n* Arvo 2: Ylä oikea kulman Y koordinaatti\n* Arvo 3: Kulmion leveys\n* Arvo 4: Kulmion korkeus\n\nÄäriviivat määräytyy komennolla **Aseta kynäväri**. Oletus on valkoinen ääriviiva.\n\nTäyttöväri määräytyy komennolla **Aseta täyttöväri** Oletus on valkoinen täyttöväri.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Aja\n\nLiikuttaa ajopeliä ikuisesti.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aja** blokki liikuttaa ajopeliä ikuisesti kunnes uusi ajoblokki käynnistyy tai ohjelman suoritus loppuu.\n\nValitse ajosuunta **Eteenpäin** tai **Taaksepäin**.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Kulkupelin sähkövirta\n\nAntaa sähkövirran kulutuksen, jota ajo/kulkupeli tällä hetkellä kuluttaa.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kulkupelin sähkövirta** raportoi kulutusarvon välillä **0% - 100%** tai **0.0 - 2.5 amps**. \n\nValitse kumpaa yksikköä käytetään % tai ampeerisekuntia (amps).\n\n**Kulkupelin sähkövirta** voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_efficiency":{"name":"drive_efficiency","markdown":"# Ajopelin tehokkuus\n\nRaportoi ajopelin tehokkuuden\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopelin tehokkuus** antaa teholuvun suhteessa mitä moottori käyttää (watt / input) suhteessa mitä moottori tuottaa (watt / output). \n\nV5 ajopeli tyypillisesti saavuttaa maksimitehokkuuden arvolla 65% normali oloissa.\n\n**Ajopelin tehokkuus** antaa arvot välillä **0% - 100%**. \n\n**Ajopelin tehokkuus** arvon voi sijoittaa ympyrämuotoisiin kenttiin muissa blokeissa. \n\n![drive_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Aja matkan\n\nAjopeli ajaa annetun matkan.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n# Miten käytetään\n\nValitse suunta, johon ajopeli liikkuu.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\n**Aja matkan** blokissa voi käyttää kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\nAnna matkan lukuarvo sekä yksikkö (tuumia tai mm).\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nOletuksena seuraavat blokit odottavat kunnes ajopelin liike loppuu.\n\nVoit valita option **ja älä odota**, jolloin seuraavat blokit käynnistyvät jo ajon aikana.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Ajopelin kulkusuunta\n\nAntaa ajopelin nykyisen kulkusuunnan.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopelin kulkusuunta** antaa arvon välillä **0.00 - 359.99 astetta**.\n\n**Ajopelin kulkusuunta** antaa kellotaulun myötäpäivään kulkusuunnan kuvan mukaan.\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopelin kulkusuunta** antaa arvon välillä **0.00 - 359.99 astetta**.\n\n**Ajopelin kulkusuunta** antaa kellotaulun vastapäivään kulkusuunnan kuvan mukaan.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Ajo on suoritettu?\n\nRaportoi onko ajopelin liike loppunut.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajo on suoritettu?** antaa arvon **tosi** kun ajopelin moottoreiden liike on loppunut.\n\n**Ajo on suoritettu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** kun ajopelin moottoreiden liike jatkuu.\n\n**Ajo on suoritettu?** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Ajopeli liikkuu?\n\nAntaa vastauksen liikkuuko ajopeli tällä hetkellä.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopeli liikkuu?** antaa arvon **tosi** jos ajopelin ajomoottorit liikkuvat.\n\n**Ajopeli liikkuu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos ajopelin ajomoottorit eivät liikku.\n\n**Ajopeli liikkuu?** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa eri blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_power":{"name":"drive_power","markdown":"# Ajopelin teho\n\nANtaa ajopelin antaman tehon määrän.\n\n![drive_power](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_power/drive_power.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopelin teho** antaa arvot välillä **0.0 - 22.0 wattia**. \n\n**Ajopelin teho** arvon voi sijoiottaa pyöreisiin kenttiin muissa blokeissa.\n\n![drive_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_power/drive_power_inserted.png)"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Ajopelin kulma\n\nAntaa ajopelin kiertymiskulman asennetun 3-lanka Gyro Sensorin tai V5 Inertial Sensorin avulla.\n\n![drive_rotation](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_rotation/drive_rotation.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopelin kulma** antaa **positiivisen** arvon kun ajopeli ajaa **myötäpäivä** suuntaan.\n\n**Ajopelin kulma** antaa **negatiivisen** arvon kun ajopeli ajaa **vastapäivä** suuntaan.\n\n**Ajopelin kulma** arvon voi sijoittaa ympyrämuotoisiin kenttiin blokeissa.\n\n![drive_rotation_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_rotation/drive_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_temperature":{"name":"drive_temperature","markdown":"# Ajopelin lämpötila\n\nAntaa ajopelin ajomoottoreiden lämpötilan.\n\n![drive_temperature](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_temperature/drive_temperature.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopelin lämpötila** antaa arvot väliltä **0% - 100%**. \n\n**Ajopelin lämpötila** arvon voi sijoittaa ympyrämuotoisiin blokkikenttiin.\n\n![drive_temperature_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_temperature/drive_temperature_inserted.png)"},"drive_torque":{"name":"drive_torque","markdown":"# Ajopelin vääntö\n\nAntaa ajopelin vääntövoimakkuuden (pyörimisvoiman).\n\n![drive_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_torque/drive_torque.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopelin vääntö** antaa arvoja välillä **0.0 - 18.6 tuuma-paunaa (InLB)** tai **0.0 - 2.1 Newton-metriä (Nm)**. \n\nValitse yksikkö, jota käytät (InLb) tai (Nm).\n\n![drive_torque_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_torque/drive_torque_unit.png)\n\n**Ajopelin vääntö** blokin arvoa voi käyttää pyöreämuotoisissa blokkikentissä.\n\n![drive_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_torque/drive_torque_inserted.png)"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Ajopelin nopeus/teho\n\nRaportoi ajopelin nykyisen nopeuden.\n\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajopelin nopeus** antaa arvon väliltä **-100% - 100%** tai **-600pm - 600rpm**\n\n**Ajopelin nopeus** yksikössä \"kierrosta minuutissa\" arvoalue riippuu V5 moottorien vaihdepakkauksesta.\n\n* Punainen vaihdepakkaus: -100rpm - 100rpm\n* Vihreä vaihdepakkaus:: -200rpm - 200rpm\n* Sininen vaihdepakkaus: -600rpm - 600rpm\n\nValitse yksikkö, jolla nopeus raportoidaan prosentti  % tai kierrosta minuutissa (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\n**Ajopelin nopeus** blokkia käytetään eri blokkien pyöreissä arvokentissä.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"duration":{"name":"duration","markdown":"# Aseta kesto\n\nAsettaa jan, kuinka kauan V5 sähkömagneetin varaus säilyy.\n\n![set_duration_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/duration/set_duration_block.png)\n\n## Miten äytetään\n\nValise kesto, kauanko magneetti toimii:\n\n* **lyhyt** - pitää varauksen **250ms**\n* **keskiverto** - pitää varauksen **500ms**\n* **pitkä** - pitää varauksen **1000ms**\n\n![set_duration_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/duration/set_duration_block_setting.png)\n\nValitse magneetti, jota käytät.\n\n![set_duration_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/duration/set_duration_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nRobotti ajaa eteenpäin 200mm, käytä **Aseta kesto** arvona **pitkä** , jolloin **Sähkömagneetti** varautuu tarttumaan esineen, aja eteenpäin 200mm ja pudota sitten esine.\n\n![set_duration_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/duration/set_duration_example.png)\n"},"efficiency_of_motor":{"name":"efficiency_of_motor","markdown":"# Moottorin teho\n\nAntaa V5 Älymoottorin teholuvun.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottorin teho** raportoi tehoarvon (watteja) moottori käyttää (input) suhteessa tehoon (watteja) siitä saadaan ulos (output). \n\nV5 Älymoottori antaa maksimitehon yleensä arvolla 65%.\n\n**Moottorin teho** antaa arvon välillä **0% - 100%**. \n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![motor_efficiency_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_device.png)\n\n**Moottorin teho** blokin arvon voi asettaa blokkien pyöreöämuotoisiin kenttiin. \n\n![motor_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_inserted.png)"},"enable_manual_movement":{"name":"enable_manual_movement","markdown":"# Salli manuaalinen liike\n\nSallii V5 Workcell robottikäden liikeen manuaalisesti.\n\n![set_manual_movement](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/enable_manual_movement/set_manual_movement.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOletuksena robottikäsi on lukittu. Jos haluat siirtää käden asentoa aseta komento **Salli manuaalinen liike** blokki ohjelmaasi.\n\n![movement](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/enable_manual_movement/movement.png)\n\nValise käytetty robottikäsi.\n\n![set_manual_movement_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/enable_manual_movement/set_manual_movement_arm.png)"},"energize":{"name":"energize","markdown":"# Vahvista tarttuminen\n\nAsettaa V5 Sähkömagneetin kahteen eri moodiin: **vahvista** or **tiputa**.\n\n![set_magnet_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/energize/set_magnet_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValise kumpaa moodia käytetään\n\n* **vahvista** - lataa sähkömagneetin tarttumista varten\n* **tiputa** - pudottaa esineen magneetista (jos esine kiinni)\n\nKun magneetti on kerran ladattu/vahvistettu, niin sen pitää jäähtyä ennen seuraavaa lataamista.\n\n\n![set_magnet_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/energize/set_magnet_block_setting.png)\n\nValitse magneetti, jota käytät.\n\n![set_magnet_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/energize/set_magnet_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nRobotti ajaa eteenpäin 200mm, **Sähkömagneetti** ladataan/vahvistetaan keräämään esine lattialta ja ajetaann eteenpän 200mm kunnes pudotetaan esine magneetista.\n\n![set_magnet_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/energize/set_magnet_example.png)\n"},"enter_mastering_mode":{"name":"enter_mastering_mode","markdown":"# Aloita hallintaprosessi\n\nAloittaa halintaprtosessin robottikäden neljän nivelen kalibroinnin samaan tiettyyn alkuasentoon.\n\n![start_mastering_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/enter_mastering_mode/start_mastering_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aloita hallintaprosessi** blokki aloittaa V5 Workcell robottikäden hallinnan. \n\nBlokki käytetään 'Robottiäden hallinta' esimerkkiohjelmassa."},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Yhtä suuri\n\nRaportoi, onko kaksi lukua yhtäsuurta. \n\n\n![equal_to](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Yhtä suuri** antaa arvon **tosi** jos kaksi lukua on yhtäsuurta.\n\n**Yhtä suuri** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos kaksi lukua ei ole yhtäsuurta\n\n**Yhtä suuri** blokin voi laittaa kokonais- ja desimaalilukja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n**Yhtä suuri** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Toista ikuisesti\n\nToistoblokki toistaa sen sisällä olevat blokit ikuisesti.\n\n![forever](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLaita silmukan alle blokit, joiden suoritus jatkuu **Toista ikuisesti**.\n\nVoit hytätä pois **Toista ikuisesti** loopista blokilla **break** silmukan sisällä.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nSilmukoita voi laittaa toistensa sisään. Sitä kutsutaan upotukseksi ja sillä voi saada ohjelmaan erilaisia ominaisuuksia.\n"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Funktio\n\nSuorittaa valitun matemaatisen funktion.\n\n![function](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/function/function.png)\n\n** **itseisarvo** - itseisarvo\n* **pyöristys alas** - lähin kokonaisluku alas pyöristys\n* **pyöristys ylös** - lähin kokonaisluku ylös pyöristys\n* **neliöjuuri** - neliöjuuri\n* **sin** - sin (vastakkaisen kateetin suhde hyponenuusaan)\n* **cos** - cos (viereisen kateetin suhde hyponenuusaan)\n* **tan** - tangentti(vastakkaisen kateetin suhde viereiseen)\n* **asin** - arc sin (sinin vastafuntio)\n* **acos** - arc cos (cosinin vastafuntio)\n* **atan** - arc tan (tangentin vastafuntio)\n* **ln** - luonnollinen logaritmi e kantaluvulla\n* **log** - 10 logaritmi\n* **e ^** - luonnollisen luvun e potenssi\n* **10 ^** - 10 potenssi\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Funktio** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaaliluvut sekä numeeriset blokit.\n\nValitse se matemaattinen **funktio** optiolistalta, jota haluat käyttää.\n\n![function_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/function/function_select.png)\n\n**funktio** blokin voi sijoittaa blokkien pyöreämuotoisiin arvokenttiin. \n\n![function_fit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Suurempi kuin\n\nRaportoi, onko tarkastelun ensimmäinen luku suurempi kuin toinen.  \n\n![greater_than](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Suurempi kuin** antaa arvon **tosi** kun ensimmäinen luku on suurempi kuin tarkastelun toinen luku. \n\n**Suurempi kuin** antaa arvon **epätosi** kun ensimmäinen luku ei ole suurempi kuin tarkastelun toinen luku. \n\n**Suurempi kuin** blokissa voi olla kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\n**Suurempi kuin** Boolean blokin arvo on **tosi** or **epätosi** ja sen voi laittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin kenttiin.\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Ajosuunta aste\n\nAntaa VEX V5 Inertial sensorin tai 3-johto Gyro sensorin tän hetkisen ajosuunnan asteina.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ajosuunta aste** antaa arvon välillä **0.00 to 359.99**.\n\n**Ajosuunta aste** raportoi kellotaulun myötäpäivään kasvavan suuntaarvon kuten kuvassa.\n\nValitse Gyro anturi, jota käytetään.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\n**Ajosuunta aste** blokkia voi käyttää blokkien pyöreissä arvokenttissä.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Jos niin\n\nEhtoblokki suorittaa ehtohaaran komennot vain jos Boolean -ehto on **tosi**.  \n \n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n# Miten käytetään\n\n**Jos niin** -ehtoblokki tarkistaa Boolean -ehdon vain kerran. \n\nJos Boolean -ehto on **tosi**, haaran sisällä olevat blokit suoritetaan.\n\nJos Boolean -ehto on **epätosi**, hypätään haaran yli seuraavaan komentoon.\n\n**Jos niin** ehtoblokkiiin voi sijoittaa ehdoksi kuusikulmaisa blokkiarvoja.\n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Jos niin muuten\n\nOn ehtoblokki, jossa suoritaan joko jos-haaran tai muuten -haaran komennot Boolean -ehdon perusteella.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Jos niin muuten** ehtoblokki testaa siinä olevaa Boolean -ehtoa vain kerran. \n\nJos Boolean -ehto on **tosi**, niin **jos** haaran blokit suoritetaan.\n\nJos Boolean -ehto on **epätosi**, niin **muuten** haaran blokit suoritetaan.\n\n**Jos niin muuten** ehtoblokkiin voi sijoittaa vain kuusikulmaisia blokkeja ehdoksi.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)"},"inertial_acceleration":{"name":"inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Kiihtyvyys\n\nAntaa Inertial -sensorin mittaaman kiihtyvyysarvot akselistossa (x, y, tai z).\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kiihtyvyys** antaa arvot välillä **-4.0 - 4.0** Gs. \n\nValitse sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![inertial_acceleration_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_device.png)\n\nValitse akseli, jonka kiihtyvyyttä tarkastelet:\n\n* **X-akseli** kuvaa kiihtyvääliikettä , kun Inertial Sensori kallistuu **eteen-taakse**\n* **Y-akseli** kuvaa kiihtyvääliikettä , kun Inertial Sensori kallistuu **sivulta-sivulle**\n* **Z-akseli** kuvaa kiihtyvääliikettä , kun Inertial Sensori kallistuu **ylös-alas**\n\n\n![inertial_acceleration_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_axis.png)\n\n**Kiihtyvyys** blokin arvoja voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa kentissä.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_gyrorate":{"name":"inertial_gyrorate","markdown":"# Inertial gyroarvo\n\nAntaa akseleiden gyroarvot koordinaatistossaxes (x, y, or z).\n\n![gyro_rate_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_gyrorate/gyro_rate_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Gyroarvo** antaa arvot välillä **-1000.0 - 1000.0** yksikkönä dps (astetta sekunnissa). \n\nValitse Inertial -sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![gyroRate_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_included_block.png)\n\nValitse akseli, jota tarkastelet.\n\n* **X-akseli** antaa kääntymisen arvon, jonka Inertial -sensori mittaa X-Akselilla (pohjautuen sensorin orientaatioon)\n* **Y-akseli** antaa kääntymisen arvon, jonka Inertial -sensori mittaa X-Akselilla (pohjautuen sensorin orientaatioon)\n* **Z-akseli** antaa kääntymisen arvon, jonka Inertial -sensori mittaa X-Akselilla (pohjautuen sensorin orientaatioon)\n\n![gyroRate_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_axis.png)\n\n**Gyroarvo** blokin arvoja voi käyttää blokkien pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_orientation":{"name":"inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Orientaatio asento\n\nAntaa Inertial -sensorin asentoarvot (x,y,z) koordinaatistossa.\n\n![orientation_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_orientation/orientation_inertial_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nHavaintoarvot on jaettu (x, y, or z) akseleille.\n\n* **X-akseli** edustaa **kallistus** (pitch) arvovälillä -90 - +90 astetta.\n* **Y-akseli** edustaa **pituus** (roll) arvovälillä -180 - +180 astetta.\n* **Z-akseli** edustaa **suunta** (YAW) arvovälillä -90 - +90 astetta.\n\n---\n\n**Kallistus** kertoo miten robotti on kallistunut eteen- tai taaksepäin pituusakselin suhteen.\n\n![V5_Pitch_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_orientation/V5_Pitch_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Pituus** kertoo miten robotti on kallistunut vasemmalle tai oikealle sivusuunnassa.\n\n![V5_Roll_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_orientation/V5_Roll_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Suunta** kertoo mihin suuntaan robotti ajaa kentällä.\n\n![V5_Yaw_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_orientation/V5_Yaw_rev2.jpg)\n\n---\n\nValitse Inertial -sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![orientation_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_orientation/orientation_included_block.png)\n\nValitse akseli,jota tarkastelet.\n\n![orientation_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_orientation/orientation_axis.png)\n\n**Orientaatio asento** arvoa voi käyttää pyöreämuotoisissa blokkikentissä.\n\n![orientation_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/inertial_orientation/orientation_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n\n"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 2D alkio\n\nAntaa halutun taulukon alkion arvon. \n\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse 2D taulukko, jota käytätä. Voit myös uudeleennimetä tai poistaa valitun taulukon.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nAnna taulukon alkion rivi (ensimmäinen luku) ja sarake (toinen luku). Tässä esimerkissä on valittu rivi 2, sarake 3.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\n**2D alkio** taulukon valitut alkionumerot voivat olla vain kokonaislukuja tai numeerisia blokinarvoja\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Luettelon alkio\n\nAntaa luettelon valitun alkion arvon. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n# Miten käytetään\n\nvalitse luettelo, jota käytetään. Voit myös uudeleennimetä tyai poistaa valitun luettelon.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nAnna luettelon alkion järjestysnumero. Tässä näytetään luettelon toisen alkion arvo. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\n**Luettelon alkio** blokin alkiovalinnassa voi olla kokonaislukuja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä ajopelin nopeuteen laitetaan arvoksi luettelon 3. alkio. Tällöin ajopelin nopeus on 90%.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"joint_move":{"name":"joint_move","markdown":"# Yhteisliike\n\nLiikuttaa V5 Robottikättä tiettyyn (x, y, z) koordinaattiin käyttäen  yheisliikettä.\n\n![joint_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/joint_move/joint_move_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Yhteisliike** blokki liikttaa V5 Robottikättä  x, y, and z-suuntaan käyttäen yhteisliikettä. \n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/joint_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nValitse robottikäsi, jota käytät.\n\n![select_joint_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/joint_move/select_joint_arm.png)\n\n**Yhteisliike** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n![joint_input](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/joint_move/joint_input.png)"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 2D taulukon pituus\n\nkeroo montako riviä tai saraketta 2d taulukossa on.   \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse 2d taulukko, jota käytetään. Voit samlla uudelleen nimetä tai poistaa 2d taulukon.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nValitse kumpaa tekijää raportoit **rivit** tai **sarakkeet**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\n** 2D taulukon pituus** arvon voi sijoittaa blokkien pyöreisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Pienempi kuin\n\nKertoo onko kahdesta luvusta vertailun ensimmäinen pienempi kuin toinen.  \n\n![less_than](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Pienempi kuin** antaa arvon **tosi**jos vertailun ensimmäinen luku on pienenmpi kuin jälkimmäinen luku. \n\n**Pienempi kuin** antaa arvon **epätosi**jos vertailun ensimmäinen luku on ei ole pienenmpi kuin jälkimmäinen luku. \n\n**Pienempi kuin** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokin arvoja.\n\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n"},"linear_move":{"name":"linear_move","markdown":"# Vaakaliike\n\nLiikuttaa V5 Robottikättä tiettyym asentoon (x, y, z) koordinaatistossa vaakaliikkeenä.\n\n![linear_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/linear_move/linear_move_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Vaakaliike** blokki liikuttaa V5 Robottikättä x, y, ja z-suunnassa käytäen vaakaliikettä. \n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/linear_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nValitse robottikäsi, jota käytät.\n\n![select_linear_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/linear_move/select_linear_arm.png)\n\n**Vaakaliike** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ka kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokkien arvoja.\n\n![linear_input](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/linear_move/linear_input.png)"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Moottorin liike loppu?\n\nKertoo jos valitun moottorin liike on valmis/päättynyt.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottorin liike loppu?** antaa arvon **tosi** jos valitun moottorin liike on valmis/päättynyt.\n\n**Moottorin liike loppu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos valittu moottori on edelleen liikkeessä.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\n**Moottorin liike loppu?** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Moottori pyörii?\n\nKertoo jos valittu moottori vielä pyörii?\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottori pyörii?** antaa arvon **tosi** kun kohdemoottori pyörii.\n\n**Moottori pyörii?** antaa arvon **epätosi** kun kohdemoottori on pysähtynyt.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\n**Mooottori pyörii?** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa muiden blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvoalueisiin.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Kertolasku\n\nantaa kahden luvun kertolaskun tuloksen.\n\n![multiply](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kertolasku** hyväksuu kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisisten blokkien arvoja.\n\n**Kertolasku** blokin voi laittaa blokkien pyöreisiin arvokohtiin. \n\nKahden luvun kertolasku.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nKahden muuttujan kertolasku.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nKahden sensoriarvon kertolasku.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Siirrä kursori seuraavalle riville\n\nSiirtää kursorin aivojen näytöllä , ohjaimen näytöllä tai Tulostus-näytöllä seuraavalle riville.\n\n![next_row](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## Mitem käytetään\n\nOletetuksena ohjelman alussa kursori on kohdassa rivi 1 sarake 1. **seuraavalle riville** blokki pudottaa kursorin seuraavalle riville. \n\nValise laite, jota käytetään. V5 Ohjain tulee näkyviin vain jos se on lisätty laitteet-ikkunassa.\n\n![next_row_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/next_row/next_row_dropdown_with_console.png)\n\n---\n\nV5 Aivot sallii muuttaa kirjasimen kokoa ja kun muuttaa kokoa, rivien määrä näytöllä muuttuu.\n\n**V5 Aivojen kirjasinkoko - Rivien määrä:**\n\n* Extra pieni - 20 Riviä\n* Pieni - 16 Riviä\n* Medium - 12 Riviä (Oletus)\n* Iso - 8 Riviä\n* Extra Iso - 6 Riviä\n* Super Iso - 4 Riviä\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/next_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nV5 Ohjaimen näytöklle ei voi muuttaa kirjasimen kokoa.\n\n**V5 Ohjaimen kirjasinkoko - Rivien määrä:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Riviä (Oletus)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/next_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n\n---\n\nTulostuskonsolille tulostus vaatii **Siirry seuraavalle riville** blokkia jokaisen **tulosta** blokin jälkeen.\n\n![next_row_with_print_console](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/next_row/next_row_with_print_console.png)"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# Ei\n\nAntaa vastakkaisen totuusarvon Boolean muuttujalle.\n\n![not](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/not/not.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ei** blokki antaa arvon **tosi** kun Boolean blokki sen sisällä antaa arvon **epätosi**.\n\n**Ei** blokki antaa arvon **epätosi** kun Boolean blokki sen sisällä antaa arvon **tosi**.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTämä esimerkki antaa arvon **tosi** kun VEX IQ Aivojen näyttöä ei ole painettu. \n\n\n![not_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Kohteiden lukumäärä\n\nKertoo montako esinekohdetta Vision -kamera havaitsee. \n\nEsine pitää aina olla määritelty Laitteet-ikkunassa ennen kuin **Kohteiden lukumäärä** voi sen havaita kuvassa.\n\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse Vision -kamera, jota käytetään.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\n*Ota kuva** blokkia pitää käyttää ennen kuin **Kohteiden lukumäärä** blokki voi laskea kohteiden määrän.\n\n**Kohteiden lukumäärä** blokki havaitsee vain merkattujen kohteiden lukumäärän viimeisestä kuvasta.\n\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Kohde havaittu\n\nKertoo jos Vision -kamera havaitsee sille määritellyn esineen. \n\nEsine pitää olla määritelty kameralle ennen kuin **Kohde havaittu** blokki voi esineen havaita.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse kamera, jota käytetään.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n**Kohde havaittu** antaa arvon **tosi** jos Vision -kamera havaitsee sille määritellyn esineen.\n\n**Kohde havaittu**  antaa arvon **epätosi** jos Vision -kamera ei havaitse sille määriteltyä esinettä.\n\n**Kohde havaittu** Boolean blokki antaa arvon **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvoalueisiin.\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\n**Ota kuva** blokki pitää aina olla käytetty ts kuva otettu ennen kuin **Kohde havaittu** Boolean blokki voi antaa arvon **tosi** tai **epätosi**."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Löysi esineen\n\nAntaa tiedon, löysikö Ultrasonic Range Finder -sensori (ultraäänellä) esineen. \n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Löysi esineen** antaa arvon **tosi** kun Ultrasonic Range Finder -sensori löytää esineen tai havaitsee pinnan kuulokentässä.\n\n**Löysi esineen** antaa arvon **epätosi** kun Ultrasonic Range Finder -sensori ei löydä esinettä tai ei havaitse pintaa kuulokentässä.\n\nChoose which Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor to use.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\n**Löysi esineen** Boolean blokki antaa joko arvon **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)"},"optical_brightness":{"name":"optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical kirkkaus\n\nAntaa lukuarvon, kuinka kirkas esine on, jonka Optical Sensori havaitsee.\n\n![optical_brightness](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_brightness/optical_brightness.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![optical_brightness_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_device.png)\n\n**Optical kirkkaus** blokki antaa arvoja välillä **0%** - **100%**.\n\nIso arvo tarkoittaa, että valaistus on kirkas.\n\nPieni arvo tarkoittaa, että valaistus on heikko.\n\n**Optical kirkkaus** blokki antaa numeroarvoja ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien pyöreämuotoisiin kenttiin.\n\n![optical_brightness_use](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect":{"name":"optical_detect","markdown":"# Optical havaitsee värin\n\nAntaa totuusarvon, jos Optical Sensori havaitsee tietyn värin.\n\n![optical_detect](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_detect/optical_detect.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse Optical Sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![optical_detect_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_detect/optical_detect_device.png)\n\nValitse väri, jota etsit.\n\n![optical_detect_colors](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_detect/optical_detect_colors.png)\n\n**Optical havaitsee värin** blokki antaa arvon **tosi** kun Optical Sensori havaitsee tietyn värin.\n\n**Optical havaitsee värin** blokki antaa arvon **epätosi** kun Optical Sensori ei havaitse tiettyä väriä.\n\n**Optical havaitsee värin** blokki antaa joko **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvoalueisiin.\n\n![optical_detect_use](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_detect/optical_detect_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect_gesture":{"name":"optical_detect_gesture","markdown":"# When Optical detects a gesture \n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the Optical sensor detects a gesture.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **When Optical detects a gesture** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on gestures that the Optical Sensor detects.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor.\n\n\n![optical_detects_gesture_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detects_gesture_device.png)\n\nChoose which gesture triggers the **When Optical detects a gesture** event.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block2.png)"},"optical_detect_object":{"name":"optical_detect_object","markdown":"# Kun Optical havaitsee/kadottaa\n\nTapahtuma, jonka totweutumisehdon mukaan sen alla olevat komennot suoritetaan. Ehdot ovat Havaitsee tai Kadottaa esineen.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kun Optical havaitsee/kadottaa** tapahtumassa komentoja toteutetaan sen mukaan, mille ehdolle Optical Sensori asetettu ts joko **havaitsee** esineen näkökentässä tai **kadottaa** esineen näkökentästään.\n\nValitse käyttämäsi Optical Sensori.\n\n![optical_detect_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_device.png)\n\nValitse **Kun Optical havaitsee/kadottaa** tapahtuman ehto, jolla sen alla olevat komennot suoritetaan ts joko **havaitsee** esineen tai **kadottaa** esineen.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block2.png)"},"optical_found_object":{"name":"optical_found_object","markdown":"# Optical löysi esineen\n\nAntaa tiedon havaitseeko Optical Sensor lähellä olevaa esinettä.\n\n\n![optical_found_object](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_found_object/optical_found_object.png)\n\n##Miten käytetään\n\nValitse Optical Sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![optical_found_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_device.png)\n\n**Optical löysi esineen** blokki antaa arvon **tosi** kun Optical Sensori havaitsee lähellä olevan esineen.\n\n**Optical löysi esineen** blokki antaa arvon **epätosi** kun Optical Sensorin näköalueella ei ole esinettä.\n\n**Optical löysi esineen** blokkia käytetään aina ensin ennenkuin esineen värisävy luetaan komennolla **Optical havaitsee värin**.\n\n**Optical löysi esineen** blokki antaa joko arvon **tosi** tai **epätosi* ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![optical_found_object_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_condition.png)"},"optical_hue":{"name":"optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical värisävy\n\nAntaa esineen värisävyn.\n\n![optical_hue](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_hue/optical_hue.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nChoose an optical sensor.\n\n![optical_hue_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_hue/optical_hue_device.png)\n\n**Optical värisävy** blokki antaa esineen värisävyn numeroarvon väliltä **0** ja **359**, joka on Vex -värispetrin arvo havaitulle värille.\n\n**Optical värisävy** blokki antaa numeroarvoja ka sen voi sijoittaa muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisiin kenttiin.\n\n![optical_hue_use](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_hue/optical_hue_use.png)"},"optical_set_light":{"name":"optical_set_light","markdown":"# Aseta Optical valo\n\nLaittaa Optical Sensorin valon päälle tai pois päältä.\n\n![optical_set_light](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_set_light/optical_set_light.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta Optical valo** blokin avulla saat Optical Sensorin valon asetuksen  **Päällä** tai **Pois**. Valon avulla on helpompi etsiä esineitä huonosti valaistuilta alueilta.\n\nValitse käyttämäsi Optical Sensori.\n\n![optical_set_light_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_device.png)\n\nValitse haluatko valon olevan **Päällä** tai **Pois**.\n\n![optical_set_light_state](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_state.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä käytämme komentoa **Aseta Optical valo** asettamaan valon päälle. Sen jälkeen kun Optical Sensori havaitsee esineen, tulostamme sen värisävyn.\n\n\n![optical_set_light_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_example.png)"},"optical_set_light_power":{"name":"optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Aseta Optical valoteho \n\nAsettaa V5 Optical -sensorin valotehon.\n\n![optical_set_light_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_light_power_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta Optical valoteho** blokki hyväksyy arvot väliltä **0%** - **100%**. Tämä muuttaa Aseta Optical -sensorin valon voimakuuden. Jos valo on pois päältä, komento laittaa valon päälle.\n\nValise haluamasi V5 Optical -sensori.\n\n![optical_set_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_device.png)\n\nAseta Optical valoteho -blokki hyväksyy arvoiksi desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja ja numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n![optical_set_power_num](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_num.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä **Aseta Optical valoteho** blokin arvoksi asetetaan **50%**, jonka jälkeen se laitetaan päälle komennolla **Aseta optical valo** . Sen jälkeern, jos sensori havaitsee esineen, tulostetaan värin värisävy.\n\n![optical_set_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_example.png)"},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# Tai\n\nraportoi onko toinen kahdesta Boolean -ehdoista totta.\n\n![or](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/or/or.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Tai** Boolean blokki antaa arvoksi **tosi** kun yksi (tai molemmat) ehdoista on **tosi**. \n\n**Tai** Boolean blokki antaa arvoksi **epätosi** kun molemmat ehdoista ovat **epätosi**.\n\n**Tai** Boolean blokki antaa arvoksi **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa blokkien kuusikulmaiseen arvokenttään.\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\n## esimerkki\n\n**Tai** blokki antaa arvoksi **tosi** kun joko toinen (tai molemmat) VEX V5 Painokytkin ja VEX V5 Valosensorin arvo on suurempi kuin 50 €.\n\n**Tai** blokki antaa arvoksi **epätosi** kun sekä VEX V5 Painokytkintä ei ole painettu eikä VEX V5 Valosensorin arvo on pienempi yhtäsuuri kuin 50 €.\n\n\n![or_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/or/or_truth.png)"},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Ohjaintatin asento\n\nraportoi, missä asennossa ohjaintatti on akselilla.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ohjaintatin asento** antaa asennosta arvon välillä **-100 - 100**.\n\n**Ohjaintatin asento** antaa arvon 0, jos tatti on akselin keskellä levossa.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nValitse ohjain, jota käytetään.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_devices.png)\n\nValitse ohjaintatti, jota käytetään.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\n**Ohjaintatin asento** raportointiblokkia käytetään blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Moottori asento\n\nMittaa V5 moottorin pyörimismatkaa.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottori asento** raportoi moottorin pyörimisasennon joko kokonaislukuna asteina tai desimaalilukuna kierroksina.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nValitse tarkastellaanko moottorin pyörimismatkaa asteina vai kierroksina.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nMoottori asento** arvoa voidaan käyttää pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"position_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"position_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Akselikierron asento\n\nAntaa akselinkierron asennon.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Akselikierron asento** raportoi määrän, jonka Akselikierron -sensori on kääntynyt kokonaislukuina asteina tai desimaalilukuina käännöksinä.\n\nValitse,mitä sensoria käytetään.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_device.png)\n\nValitse yksikkö asteina tai kierroksina. \n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_unit.png)\n\n**Akselikierron asento** blokin arvoja voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa kentissä. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_inserted.png)"},"power":{"name":"power","markdown":"# Aseta sähkömagneetin voimakkuus\n\nAsettaa V5 Sähkömagneetin voimakkuuden esineiden keräämisessä.\n\n![set_magnet_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/power/set_magnet_power_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nHaluat varmaan poikia eri painoisia esineitä.**Aseta sähkömagneetin voimakkuus** blokilla voit säätää magneetin vetovoimaa välillä **0% - 100%**\n\nValitse magneetti, jota käytetään.\n\n![set_magnet_dropdown_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/power/set_magnet_dropdown_block.png)\n\n## Eimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä robotti ajaa eteenpäin 200mm, ja  **Aseta sähkömagneetin voimakkuus** blokilla tehoa lisää poimia esine ja ajaa sitten eteenpäin 200mm kunes tiputtaa esimneen.\n\n![set_magnet_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/power/set_magnet_power_example.png)\n"},"power_of_motor":{"name":"power_of_motor","markdown":"# Moottorin teho\n\nAntaa V5 Älymoottorin tehon.\n\n![motor_power](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/power_of_motor/motor_power.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottorin teho** antaa rvojas väliltä **0.0 - 11.0 wattia**. \n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![motor_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/power_of_motor/motor_power_device.png)\n\n**Moottorin teho** blokin arvoja voi käyttää muiden blokkien ympyränmuotoisissa kentissä.\n\n![motor_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/power_of_motor/motor_power_inserted.png)\n"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Painokytkintä painettu?\n\nRaportoi, jos VEX V5 Painokytkintä on painettu.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Painokytkintä painettu?** antaa arvon **tosi** jos Painokytkintä on painettu.\n\n**Painokytkintä painettu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos Painokytkintä ei ole painettu.\n\nValitse se Painokytkin, jota käytetään.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\n**Painokytkintä on painettu.** Boolean blokki antaa arvon **tosi** or **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa kuusikulmaisten blokkien arvoalueisiin.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Ohjainnappia painettu?\n\nRaportoi kun VEX V5 ohjainnappia on painettu.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Ohjainnappia painettu?** antaa arvon **tosi** jos painonappia on painettu.\n\n**Ohjainnappia painettu?** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos painonappia ei ole painettu.\n\nValitse ohjain, jota käytät.\n\n![pressing_controller_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_device.png)\n\nValitse nappi, jota käytetään\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\n**Ohjainnappia painettu?** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sitä voi käyttää kentissä, johon tarvitaan kuusikulmainen arvokenttä.\n\npressing_controller_inserted](pressing_controller_inserted.png)"},"pressing_limit":{"name":"pressing_limit","markdown":"# Raja -sensoria painettu\n\nAntaa tiedon, onko Raja-sensoria painettu.\n\n![pressing_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/pressing_limit/pressing_limit.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Raja -sensoria painettu** antaa arvon **tosi** jos sensoria on painettu.\n\n**Raja -sensoria painettu** antaa arvon **epätosi** jos sensoria ei ole painettu.\n\nValitse sensori, jota käytetään.\n\n![pressing_limit_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_bumper.png)\n\n**Raja -sensoria painettu** Boolean blokki antaa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi** ja sen voi sijoittaa kuusikulmaisiin arvokenttiin.\n\n![pressing_limit_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_inserted.png)\n "},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Tulosta\n\nTulostaa lukuarvoja tai tekstiä Tulostus-konsolille tai V5 Aivojen näytölle tai Ohjaimen näytölle.\n\n![look_print](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/print/look_print.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Tulosta** blokki rivitulostaa dataa nykyiselle kursoripaikalle aivojen näytöllä tai Tulostus-konsolille.\n\nUudet ohjelmat tulostaa oletuksena näytön riville 1 sarakkeeseen 1 tai Tulostus-konsolin 1.riville.\n\nKaikki raportoivat tuntoaistiblokit tulostavat oletuksena kokonaislukuina. Käytä **Aseta tulostustarkkuus** blokkia, jos haluat tulostaa desimaalimuodossa arvoja.\n\nValitse laite, jolle tulostat. V5 ohjaimet pitää määritellä Laitteet-ikkunassa ennen tulostusta.\n\n![look_print_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/print/look_print_dropdown_with_console.png)\n\nKun haluat lisätä arvoja Tulostus-konsolin bufferiin, käytä vain **Tulosta** blokkia.\n\n![look_print_dropdown_console](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/print/look_print_dropdown_console.png)\n\nKäytä **Siirrä seuraavalle riville**, kun tulostat sanan \"VEXcode\" Tulostus-konsolille.\n\n![look_print_set_cursor_console](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/print/look_print_set_cursor_console.png)\n\n---\n\nTulosta tekstiä ja numeroita.\n\n![print_words](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/print/print_words.png)\n\nTulosta muuttujien arvoja.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nTulosta laskutoimitusten tuloksia.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nTulosta jonkun sensorin antama arvo.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Minun blokki\n\nMinun blokit -toimintoa käytetään, kun tehdään omia aliohjelmia.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Miten toimii\n\n**Minun blokit** käytetään, kun tehdään kutsuttavaa blokkijonoa kertaalleen niin, että sitä voi kutsua pääohjelmasta useamman kerran (kyseessä ns aliohjelma). \n\n**Minun blokki** tehdään **Tee blokki** -painikkeella.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Minun blokki** hattublokki eli aliohjelma voi sisältää useampia kutsuparametreja ja selventäviä tekstejä, numeerisia muuttujia , boolean muuttujia, joilla saa lisää toiminnallisuutta omalle aliohjelmablokille.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nJos haluat kutsua **Minun blokki** aliohjelmaa, lisää kutsu pääohjelmaan ns trikkeriblokilla, joka kutsuu **Minun blokki** hattublokkia (aliohjelmaa). Kun **Minun blokki** hattublokkia kutsutaan pääohjelmassa, niin hattublokin alla olevat blokit suoritetaan kutsujan parametriarvoilla.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nLiitä tarvittavat aliohjelman suoritusblokit nippuun **Minun blokki** hattublokin alle määrittämään aliohjelman toiminnallisuus ja kutsuvaa triggeriblokkia **Minun blokki** käytetään pääohjelmassa.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Huom!Note: Jos teet useamman Minun blokki -aliohjelman, älä käytä samoja teksteja ja muuttujanimiä. Se aiheuttaa virheen ohjelmaa ladattessa robottiin***\n\n## Esimerkki \n\nTässä esimerkissä käytetään **Minun blokki** hattublokkia:\n\n* Aja eteenpäin 15 tuumaa.\n* Tulosta akun latausaste ja siirrä kursori seuraavalle riville aivojen näytöllä\n* Käännä robottia 180 astetta oikealle\n* Tulosta akun latausaste ja siirrä kursori seuraavalle riville aivojen näytöllä\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Minun blokki\n\nMinun blokit -toimintoa käytetään, kun tehdään omia aliohjelmaproseduureja.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Miten toimii\n\n**Minun blokit** käytetään, kun tehdään kutsuttavaa blokkijonoa kertaalleen niin, että sitä voi kutsua pääohjelmasta useamman kerran (kyseessä ns aliohjelma). \n\n**Minun blokit** tehdään **Tee blokki** -painikkeella.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Minun blokki** hattublokki eli aliohjelma voi sisältää useampia kutsuparametreja ja käytöä selventäviä tekstejä, numeerisia muuttujia , boolean muuttujia, joilla saa lisää toiminnallisuutta omalle aliohjelmablokille.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**Minun blokki** hattublokki eli aliohjelma voi sisältää useampia kutsuparametreja ja käytöä selventäviä tekstejä, numeerisia muuttujia , boolean muuttujia, joilla saa lisää toiminnallisuutta omalle aliohjelmablokille.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nJos haluat kutsua **Minun blokki** aliohjelmaa, lisää kutsu pääohjelmaan ns trikkeriblokilla, joka kutsuu **Minun blokki** hattublokkia (aliohjelmaa). Kun **Minun blokki** hattublokkia kutsutaan pääohjelmassa, niin hattublokin alla olevat blokit suoritetaan kutsujan parametriarvoilla.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nLiitä tarvittavat aliohjelman suoritusblokit nippuun **Minun blokki** hattublokin alle määrittämään aliohjelman toiminnallisuus ja kutsuvaa triggeriblokkia **Minun blokki** käytetään pääohjelmassa.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Huom!Note: Jos teet useamman Minun blokki -aliohjelman, älä käytä samoja teksteja ja muuttujanimiä. Se aiheuttaa virheen ohjelmaa ladattessa robottiin***\n\n## Esimmerkki 1\n\nTässä esimerkissä käytetään **Minun blokki** hattublokkia:\n\n* Aja eteenpäin 15 tuumaa\n* Tulosta akun varaustaso ja siirrä kursori seuraavalle riville aivojen näytöllä\n* Käännä robottia 180 astetta oikealla\n* Tulosta akun varaustaso ja siirrä kursori seuraavalle riville aivojen näytöllä\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Satunnaisluku väliltä\n\nRaportoi satunnaisluvun annetulta väliltä.\n\n![random](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/random/random.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Satunnaisluku väliltä** blokkia voi käyttää ympyrämuotoisten blokkien arvojen paikalla. \n\n**Satunnaisluku väliltä** blokissa voi käyttää kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\nEsimerkissä **Satunnaisluku väliltä** blokkia käytetään arpomaan ajopelin nopeutta.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nTässä esimerkissä **Satunnaisluku väliltä** blokkia taas käytetään arpomaan odotusaikaa.\n\n![random_control](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"reflectivity_of":{"name":"reflectivity_of","markdown":"# Heijastuvuus\n\nRaportoi valon määrän Viivanseuraaja -sensori havaitsee.\n\n![reflectivity_of](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nVaalet pinnat heijastavat enenmmän valoa ja antavat korkean valon heijastuvuus-arvon.\nTummat pinnat heijastavat vähemmän valoa ja antavat matalan valon heijastuvuus-arvon.\n\n**Heijastuvuus** antaa arvoja väliltä **0% - 100%**.\n\nValitse Viivanseuraaja -sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![reflectivity_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_color.png)\n\n**Heijastuvuus** blokin arvoja voi käyttää toisten blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa kentissä.\n\n![reflectivity_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n\n"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Jakojäännös\n\nKun jaetaan luku toisella niin jakojöönnös kertoo sen luvun, joka ei mene tasan jaossa.\n\n![remainder](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Jakojäännös** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaaliluvut sekä numeeristen blokkien arvot.\n\nJos jako menee tasan, niin jakojäännös on 0.\n\n**Jakojäännös** blokki voidaan sijoittaa ympyrämuotoisen blokin arvon paikalla.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä luku 7 jaetaan luvulla 2 ja jakojäännös tulostetaan VEX IQ Aivojen näytölle\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Toista kertaa\n\nToistoblokki joka toistaa sen sisällä olevat blokit syötetyn kertamäärän.\n\n![repeat](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAnna toistokertojen lukumäärä, montako kertaa **Toista kertaa** blokin sisällä olevat blokit toistetaan.\n \n**Toista kertaa** blokki hyväksyy kokonaisluvut ja numeerisen blokin arvot.\n\nToistoja voi laittaa toisensa sisään, jolloin niitä kutsutaan upotukseksi ja sillä voidaan saada suorituksen ajansäästöä ja erilaista ohjelman käyttäytymistä.\n\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/repeat/repeat_select.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Toista kunnes\n\nToistoblokki suoritetaan niin kauan kuin sen Boolean ehto saa arvon **tosi**.   \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Toista kunnes** blokki tutkii vain Boolean ehdon aina kierroksen alussa. \n\nJos Boolean ehto on **epätosi**, blokit kierroksen sisällä toistetaan niin monta kertaa kuin **Toista kunnes** pyörii.\n\nJos Boolean ehto on **tosi**, hypätään **Toista kunnes** blokin ohi suorittamaan seuraavaa blokkia ohjelmassa.\n\n**Toista kunnes** toistoblokin ehdoksi voi laittaa minkä tahansa kuusikulmaisen muotoon.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Nollaa kello\n\nNollaa VEX V5 aivojen kellon.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAivojen kello käynnistyy aina ohjelman suorituksen aloituksesta. **Nollaa kello** blokissa kello nollataan ohjelman suorituksen aikana.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä kello nollataan ennen kuin ajopeli ajaa 3 sekuntia. Sen jälkeen ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_angle":{"name":"rotation_angle","markdown":"# Käännös asteina\n\nRaportoi VEX V% Rotatio -sensorin nykyisen kääntymiskulman asteina.\n\n![rotation_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Käännös asteina** blokki antaa rvoja väliltä **0.00** - **359.99**.\n\n**Käännös asteina** blokin arvot joko kasvata tai pienenvät kun Rotatio -sensori kääntyy.\n\nValitse se sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![rotation_angle_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block2.png)\n\n**Käännös asteina** blokin arvon voi sijoittaa pyöreisiin blokkikenttiin.\n\n![rotation_angle_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block3.png)\n"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Gyro käännös asteina\n\nRaportoi VEX V5 Inertial sensorin tai 3 -lanka Gyron antaman nykyisen kääntymiskulman asteina.\n\n![rotation_position.png](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Gyro käännös asteina** raportoi **positiivinen** arvon kun Gyro Sensori on kääntynyt **myötäpäivään**.\n\n**Gyro käännös asteina** raportoi **negatiivinen** arvon kun Gyro Sensori on kääntynyt **vastapäivään**.\n\nValitse se gyroanturi, jota käytät\n\n![rotation_position_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_devices.png)\n\n**Gyro käännös asteina** blokin arvon voi sijoittaa pyöreisiin blokkikenttiin.\n\n![rotation_position_inserted.png](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_inserted.png)\n"},"rotation_position":{"name":"rotation_position","markdown":"# Kääntymiskulman arvo\n\nAntaa valitun V5 Kääntymissensorin mittaaman arvon.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_position/rotation_position_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kääntymiskulman arvo** antaa rvot joko kokonaislukluna asteina tai desimaalilukuna kierroksina.\n\nValitse Kääntymissensori, jota käytät.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_position/rotation_position_block2.png)\n\nValitse yksikkö joko asteina tai kierroksina.\n\n![rotation_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_position/rotation_position_block3.png)\n\n**Kääntymiskulman arvo** blokin arvoja voi käyttää muidenblokkien ympyrämuotoisissa kentissä.\n\n![rotation_position_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_position/rotation_position_block4.png)\n"},"rotation_set_position":{"name":"rotation_set_position","markdown":"# Aseta kiertokulma\n\nAsettaa VEX V5 Kääntymissensorin kääntymiskulmalle arvon. .\n\n![rotation_set_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block.png)\n\n# Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta kiertokulma** blokilla voi asettaa VEX V5 Kääntymissensorin kääntymiskulmalle haluttuun asentoon, positiivinen arvo vastapäiväarvoon tai negatiivisen kulman myötöpäiväasentoon.\n\n**Aseta kiertokulma** hyväksyy kokonaislukuja ja desimaalilukuja etumerkein.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block3.png)\n\nValitse VEX V5 Kääntymissensori , jota haluat käsitellä ja anna sille haluttu arvo.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block2.png)\n"},"rotation_velocity":{"name":"rotation_velocity","markdown":"# Kääntymisen nopeus\n\nAntaa tänhetkisen V5 Kääntymissensorin mittaaman nopeuden.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValise sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block2.png)\n\nValitse yksikkö, jolla mitataan: prosenttia (%), kierrosta minuutissa (rpm) tai astetta sekunnissa (dps).\n\n![rotation_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block3.png)\n\nKääntymisen nopeus -blokkia voi käyttää blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa kentissä.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block4.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Pyöristys\n\npyöristää syöteluvun lähimpään kokonaislukuun.\n\n![round](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/round/round.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nDesimaalit 0.5 ja suuremmat **pyöristys** blokki pyöristää ylöspäin seuraavaan kokonaislukuun ja alle 0.5 **pyöristys** taas alaspäin.\n\n**Pyöristys** blokin arvo voidan sijoittaa pyöreämuotoisten alkioiden kenttään. \n\n**Pyöristys** blokkiin voi sijoittaa kokonais- ja desdimaalilukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä pyöristetään luku 2.7 tulostusblokin arvoksi ja se tulostuu  \"3\".\n\n![round_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"screen_position":{"name":"screen_position","markdown":"# Näytön paikka\n\nAntaa V5 aijonen kohdan, johon on kosketettu.\n\n![screen_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/screen_position/screen_position_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Näytön paikka** raportoi X/Y paikan johon on viimeksi kosketusnäytöllä koskettu. Komennolla saadaa lisää vuorovaikutusta käyttäjän ja V5 robotin välille ohjelmoinnissa.\n\n**Näytön paikka** blokin  *X** -koordinaatti on arvo väliltä **0 - 480 pixeliä.\n**Näytön paikka** blokin *Y** -koordinaatti on arvo väliltä **0 - 240 pixeliä.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/screen_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\nvalise koordinaatti, jota tarkastelet. \n\n![screen_position_value](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/screen_position/screen_position_value.png)\n\n**Näytön paikka** blokin arvon voi sijoittaa muiden blokkien pyöreiden arvojen paikalle.\n\n![screen_position_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/screen_position/screen_position_inserted.png)"},"screen_pressed":{"name":"screen_pressed","markdown":"# Näyttöä kosketettu\n\nkertoo jos V5 Aivojen koksetusnäyttöä on kosketettu.\n\n![screen_pressed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Näyttöä kosketettu** Boolean blokkia voi käyttää yhdessä **Näytön paikka** blokin kanssa kun V5 Näyttöä on kosketettu.\n\n**Näyttöä kosketettu** antaa **tosi** kun näyttöä on kosketettu.\n\n**Näyttöä kosketettu** antaa **epätosi** kun näyttöä ei ole kosketettu.\n\n**Näyttöä kosketettu** Boolean blokin voi sijoittaa kuusikulmaisiin blokkien kenttiin.\n\n![screen_pressed_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Aseta taulukon arvo\n\nAseta 2d taulukon alkioille arvo.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun luodaan 2d taulukko, voit määritellä **sarakkeet** määrän väliltä 1-10 alkiota ja rivien **rivit** määrän vastavasti 1-10 alkiota.\n\nValitse se taulukko, jota käsittelet. Samalla voit uudeleen nimetä tai poistaa taulukon.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\n**Aseta taulukon arvo** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Aseta luettelon arvoksi\n\nAsettaa arvot jokaiselle luettelon alkiolle.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuettelon alkioiden lukumäärä (1 - 10) määritellään, kun luettelo luodaan.\n\nValitse luettelo, jota käytätään. Samalla voi myös uudeleennimetä tai poistaa luettelon.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\n**Aseta luettelon arvoksi**blokissa voi käyttää kokonais-ja desimaalilukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä syötetään arvot (30,60,90,120) ja käytetään luettelon alkiota #3 (90) asettamamalla se Käsimoottorin kääntymiskulmaksi.\n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"V5 Ohjain Kirjasinkoko\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse boolean muuttujalle arvo, jota käytät. Voit myös uudelleen nimetä muuttujan tai poistaa sen. \n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nValitse boolean muuttuja.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\n**Aseta boolean arvoon** blokki hyväksyy kuusikulmaisen muotoisia blokkeja.\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":" Aseta kursori\n\nasettaa kursorin paikan näytöllä **tulosta** blokkia varten.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse rivi ja sarake **tulosta** komennolle VEX V5 Aivot näytöllä.\n\n**Aseta kursori** hyväksyy **rivi** väliltä **1 - 20**.\n\n**Aseta kursori** hyväksyy **sarake** väliltä **1 - 80**.\n\nValitse laite , jota käytät. V5 Ohjain pitää määritellä Laitteet -ikkunassa.\n\n![set_cursor_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_cursor/set_cursor_dropdown.png)\n\nT**Aseta kursori** bloki hyväksyy kokonaislukaja ja numeerisia blokin arvoja.\n\n---\n\nV5 Aivot sallii muuttaa fontin kokoa. Se taas vaikuttaa sarakemääriin tulostuksessa aivojen näytölle.\n\n**V5 Aivojen Kirjasinkoko - Rivien max määrä:**\n\n* Extra Pieni - 20 riviä\n* Pieni - 16 riviä\n* Medium - 12 riviä (Oletus)\n* Iso - 8 riviä\n* Extra Isoe - 6 riviä\n* Super Iso - 4 riviä\n\n**V5 Aivojen Kirjasinkoko - Sarakkeidern määrä:**\n\n* Extra Pieni - 80 saraketta\n* Extra Pieni - 68 saraketta\n* Medium - 48 saraketta (Oletus)\n* Iso - 32 saraketta\n* Extra Iso - 24 saraketta\n* Super Iso - 16 saraketta\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nV5 Ohjaimeen tulostamisessa kirjasinta ei voi muuttaa.\n\n**V5 Ohjain Kirjasinkoko - Rivien max määrä:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 riviä (Oletus)\n\n**V5 Ohjain Kirjasinkoko - Sarakkeiden määrä:**\n\n* Standard Font - 20 saraketta (Oletus)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"set_digital_out":{"name":"set_digital_out","markdown":"# Digital out\n\nSets the logic level of a digital out 3-Wire port.\n\n![digital_out_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_digital_out/digital_out_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe V5 3-Wire ports function at a 5V logic signal voltage level.\n\nThe **digital out** block sets the digital signal to output a high or low logic signal.\n\nChoose which digital out port to use. \n\n![digital_out_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_digital_out/digital_out_select.png)\n\nChoose to output a high or low digital logic signal.\n\n![digital_out_choose](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_digital_out/digital_out_choose.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Set drive heading\n\nSets the Drivetrain's Gyro heading value.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set drive heading** block can be used to set the Drivetrain's position to any given heading. This block can be used to reset the orientation of the Drivetrain's gyro when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n**Set drive heading** accepts a range of **0 to 360** degrees.\n\nThe **set drive heading** block can accept integers or numeric blocks.\n\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":" Aseta kiertokulma arvoon\n\nAsettaa ajopelin kiertokulman, kun kiertyminen on määritelty VEX V5 Inertials sensorin tai 3-lanka Gyron avulla\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta kiertokulma arvoon** blokilla voi asettaa ajopelin kääntymiskulmalle joko positiivisen tai negatiivisen arvon.\n\n**Aseta kiertokulma arvoon** blokki hyväksyy sekä kokonais- että desimaalilukuja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä robotti kääntyy yhteensä 210 astetta:\n\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Käänny vasemmalle (vastapäivään) 120 asetta.\n- Aseta robotin kääntymiskulma arvoon -45 astetta.\n- Käänny vasemmalle (vastapäivään) 90 astetta (nykyisestä arvosta -45 astetta arvoon +45 astetta edellisen asetuksen vuoksi)."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Aseta pysähdymistapa\n\nAsettaa ajopelin pysähtymistavan.\n\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n* **Jarruta** pysäyttää ajopelin heti.\n* **Älä jarruta** pysäyttää ajopelin vaiheittain.\n* **Jarrut lukossa** lukitsee ajopelin jarrut ja pitää ajoneuvon paikallaan , kun sitä yrittää ulkoisesti liikuttaa.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin 3 sekuntia ja pysähtyy jarrrut lukossa.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Aseta ajoajan päättyminen\n\nasettaa ajopelin liikumiselle aikarajan.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAjopelin ajoajan päättyminen estää ohjelman väärän pysähtymisen tilanteissa että ajopelin ajo loppuun asti on estynyt.\n\nTällainen voi tapahtua esimerkiksi että ajopeli törmää seinään ja liikkuminen estyy.\n\n**Aseta ajoajan päättyminen** blokki voi siältää kokonais- ja desimaaliluja sekä numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä ajo keskytyy **aja** komennossa kun aikaa on kulunut 2 sekuntia ellei ajopeli ole siihen mennessä saavuttanut 24 tuuman ajomatkaa. Kummassakin tapauksessa ajopeli pääsee kääntymään seuraavalla **käänny** komennolla.\n\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta ajonopeus\n\nasettaa ajopelin ajonopeuden.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta ajonopeus** asettaa ajopelin nopeuden muttei liikuta sitä. **Aja** blokki vaaditaan liikkumiseen.\n\n**Aseta ajonopeus**hyväksyy arvovälin **-100% - 100%** tai **-600rpm - 600rpm**.\n\n**Aseta ajonopeus** hyväksyy \"kierrosta minuutissa\" arvoja käytetyn vaihdepakkauksen mukaisesti seuraavasti:\n\n* Punainen vaihdepakkaus: -100rpm - 100rpm\n* Vihreä vaihdepakkaus: -200rpm - 200rpm\n* Sininen vaihdepakkaus: -600rpm - 600rpm\n\nAsettamalla ajonopeudelle negatiivisen arvon aiheuttaa samalla ajopelin kulkusuunnan muuttumisen taaksepäin.\n\nAsettamalla ajonopeudelle arvon 0 aiheuttaa samalla ajopelin pysähtymisen.\n\n**Aseta ajonopeus** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaalilukua ja numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n\n"},"set_fill_color":{"name":"set_fill_color","markdown":"# Aseta täyttöväri\n\nAsettaa muotojen täyttövärin V5 aivojen näytöllä.\n\n![set_fill_color_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta täyttöväri** blokilla valitaa ympyröiden ja kulmioiden täyttöväri. \n\nValise täyttöväri. \n\n![set_fill_color_color](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_color.png)  \n\nTäyttöväri pysyy kunnes vaihdat sen."},"set_font":{"name":"set_font","markdown":"# Aseta kirjasinlaji\n\nAsettaa kirjasimen tyylin ja koon , kun tulostetaan V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n![set_font_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_font/set_font_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKäytösdsä on kaksi eri kirjasinlajia:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - kirjainten leveys on aina sama.\n* Proportional (Prop) - kirjainten leveys vaihtelee.\n\nValistse kirjain ja koko, jota haluat käyttää.\n\n![set_font_block_font](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_font/set_font_block_font.png)  \n\nValittu kirjasin ja koko on jatkossa kaikessa kirjoituksessa."},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Aseta ajosuunta\n\nAsettaa Gyron (3-lanka Gyro/ Inertial sensori) nykyisen ajosuunnan tilalle uuden arvon. \n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n# Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta ajosuunta** blokilla voi ajopelin ajosuunnan nykyistä arvoa muuttaa kellotaulun mukaiseen arvoon kuvan mukaan.\n\nTyyppilisesti gyro nollataan ajon aikana tarpen mukaan.\n\n**Aseta ajosuunta** hyväksyy arvot välillä **0 to 360** astetta.\n\n**Aseta ajosuunta** bblokissa voi äyttää kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja ja numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\nValitse haluttu gyro.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Aseta kiertokulma\n\nAsettaa VEX V5 Inertial sensorin tai 3 lanka Gyron kääntymiskulmalle arvon. \n\n\n![setrotation](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta kiertokulma** blokilla voi asettaa ajopelin kääntymiskulman haluttuun asentoon, positiivinen arvo vastapäiväarvoon tai negatiivisen kulman myötöpäiväasentoon.\n\n**Aseta kiertokulma** hyväksyy kokonaislukuja ja desimaalilukuja etumerkein.\n\nValitse gyro, jota haluat käsitellä.\n\n![setrotation_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation_devices.png)\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Vaihda alkio 2d taulukossa\n\nPäivittää 2d taulukossahalutun alkion.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAnna 2d taulukon rivi (1.arvo) ja sarake (2.arvo), jota haluat päiviittää\n\nValitse oikea 2d taulukko. Voit mös uudelleen nietä tai poistaa taulukon.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\n**Vaihda alkio** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja sekä numeerisia blokkiarvoja.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Vaihda luettelossa alkio\n\nKorvaa luettelon tai 2d Taulukon valitun alkion arvon uudella.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse luettelo, jota käsittelet. Voit myös uudelleen nimetä tai poistaa sen.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\n**Vaihda alkio** hyväksyy desimaali- jakokonaislukuja sekä numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n"},"set_joint_move_speed":{"name":"set_joint_move_speed","markdown":"# Aseta nivelen nopeus\n\nAsettaa V5 Robottikäden nivelen nopeuden.\n\n![joint_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_block.png)\n\n## Miten kytetään\n\nValise robottikäsi,. jota käytät.\n\n![select_joint_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_joint_move_speed/select_joint_speed_arm.png)\n\nValitse V5 Robottikäden nivelen liikkeen. Oletus on **normaali**.\n\n![joint_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_select.png)"},"set_led":{"name":"set_led","markdown":"# Aseta LED\n\nLaittaa LED in päälle tai pois päältä.\n\n![set_led_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_led/set_led_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValise LED, jota käytät.\n\n![set_led_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_led/set_led_block_device.png)\n\nLaita LED päälle tai pois päältä.\n\n![set_led_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_led/set_led_block_setting.png)\n\n"},"set_linear_move_speed":{"name":"set_linear_move_speed","markdown":"# Aseta lineaarinen nopeus\n\nAsettaa V5 Robottikäden nopeuden lineaarisissa liikeeissä.\n\n![linear_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nvalise robottikäsi, jota käytät.\n\n![select_linear_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_linear_move_speed/select_linear_speed_arm.png)\n\nvaliset nopeus V5 Robottikäden lieaarisille liikeeille. Oletus on **normaali**.\n\n![linear_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_select.png)"},"set_mastering":{"name":"set_mastering","markdown":"# Aseta master-arvot\n\nAsettaa master-arvot robottikäden neljälle nivelelle haluttuun alkuasentoon.\n\n![set_mastering_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_mastering/set_mastering_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAseta master arvot V5 Aivojen avulla **Aseta master-arvot** blokkiin. \n\nHyväksytyt arvot ovat:\n\n* Nivel 1: 1800 - 2200\n* Nivel 2: 1900 - 2400\n* Nivel 3: 1400 - 1800\n* Nivel 4: 200 - 650\n\n![mastering_values](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_mastering/mastering_values.png)\n\nValitse robottikäsi, jota käytät.\n\n![select_mastering_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_mastering/select_mastering_arm.png)\n\n**Aseta master-arvot** blokki hyväksyy konaislukuja ja numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n![mastering_input](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_mastering/mastering_input.png)"},"set_motor_controller_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_controller_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta moottorin kontrollerin nopeus\n\nAsettaa nopeuden moottorille 393 yhdistetty Moottori Controllerin 29.\n\n![set_motor_controller_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta moottorin kontrollerin nopeus** hyväksyy arvot välillä **-100% - 100%**.\n\nJos arvo asetaan negatiiviseksi, moottori pyörii vastapäivään.\n\nSJos arvo asetaan 0, moottori pysähtyy.\n\nCvalise moottori, jota käytät.\n\n![set_motor_controller_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_motor.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Aseta moottori asentoon\n\nAsettaa VEX V5 Moottorin kierroslaskurille (encoder) uuden arvon.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n# Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta moottori asentoon** blokkia voi käyttää ja asettaa mikä tahansa arvo .\n\nTyypillisesti  **aseta moottori asentoon** blokilla nollataan kierroslaskuri kesken ohjelmaa.\n\nValitse haluamasi moottori.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nalitse yksikkö laskurille, asteet tai kierrokset.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Aseta moottorin pysähtymistapa\n\nAsettaa tavan, jolla moottori pysähtyminen määritellään.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n* **Jarruta** valinta aiheittaa moottorin pysähtymisen heti.\n* **Älä jarruta** valinta pysäyttää moottorin pikkuhiljaa.\n* **Jarrut lukossa** valinta aiheittaa moottorin pysähtymisen heti ja pitää sen tiukasti pysähtyneenä samassa asennossa muita voimia vastaan.\n\n**Aseta moottorin pysähtymistapa** on voimassa myös jatkossa, jos sitä ei muuteta myöhemmin.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytät.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nAseta moottorin pysähtymistapa.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä Käsimooottori pyörii eteenpäin 90 astetta ja pitää asennon esimerkiksi maan vetovoimaa vastaan samassa asennossa.\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Aseta moottorin suoritusaika\n\nAsettaa aikarajan VEX V5 Älymoottorin liikkeelle.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMoottorin aikarajaa käytetään siihen, ettei ohjelman suoritus pääty, jos moottori ei saavuta tavoiteasentoa ja näin ollen estäisi ohjelman jatkumisen loppuun. Esimerkki, jossa moottori ei saavuta tavoiteasentoa voi olla käsi- tai kouramoottori , jotka saavuttavat mekaanisen liikerajan esteen ja astetavoite estyisi.\n\nAseta moottorin suoritusaika** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä moottorille on asetettu  **Aseta moottorin suoritusaika** komennolla 2 sekuntia saavuttaa asento 270 astetta. Joko aikaraja tai tavoite saavutetaan ja Kouramoottori liikkuu asentoon 0 astetta.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Aseta moottorin vääntövoima\n\nAsettaa VEX V5 Älymoottorin vääntökyvyn.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta moottorin vääntövoima** hyväksyy arvot välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytät.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\n**Aseta moottorin vääntövoima** blokki hyväksyy kokonais- ja desimaaliluvut ja numeeriset blokkiarvot.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä Kouramoottoria pyöritetään asentoon 40 astetta vain 20 % vääntövoimalla. Valinta suojelee esinettä rikkoutumatta liian isolla voiman käytöllä.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta moottorin nopeus\n\nAsettaa VEX V5 älymoottorin nopeuden\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta moottorin nopeus** hyväksyy arvot väliltä **-100% - 100%** tai **-600 rpm - 600rpm**.\n\n\n\n**Aseta moottorin nopeus** hyväksyy arvoja \"kierrosta minuutissa\" riippuen valitusta vaihdepakkauksesta.\n\n* Punainen vaihdepakkaus: -100rpm - 100rpm\n* Vihreä vaihdepakkaus: -200rpm - 200rpm\n* Sininenvaihdepakkaus: -600rpm- 600rpm\n\nAsettamalla nopeuden miinusmerkkiseksi aiheuttaa moottorin pyörimisen taaksepäin.\n\nAsettamalla nopeuden arvoon 0 saa moottorin pysähtymään.\n\nValitse moottori, jota haluat käyttää.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nValitse nopeuden yksiköksi joko % tai kierrosta minuutissa (rpm).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä Käsimoottori pyörii hitaasti 25% nopeudella asentoon 90 astetta.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_origin":{"name":"set_origin","markdown":"# Set origin position\n\nSets the origin to the current location of the end of arm tooling.\n\n![set_origin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_origin/set_origin_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, the origin on the Workcell is located in the center of the turntable.\n![turntable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_origin/turntable.png)\n\nThe **set origin position** block sets the origin to the current location of the end of arm tooling.\n\nThe end of arm tooling can be set to:\n\n* None\n* Marker (shown in image)\n* Electromagnet \n\n![marker](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_origin/marker.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![set_origin_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_origin/set_origin_insert.png)"},"set_pen_color":{"name":"set_pen_color","markdown":"# Aseta kynän väri\n\nAsettaa kynävärin V5 Aivojen näytöllä piirtämiseen tai Tulostuskonsolille tulostukseen.\n\n![set_pen_color_block_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_block_with_console.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta kynän väri** blokkia käytetään, kun asetetaan piirtämisen väri : viivat, pixelit, teksti, kun tulostetaan V5 aivojen näyttölle tai Tulostuskonsolin näyttölle. \n\n**Aseta kynän väri** käytetään myös ympyröiden ja kulmnioiden ääriviivoihin V5 Aivojen näytöllä.\n\nValitse kynän väri\n\n![set_pen_color_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_dropdown_with_console.png)  \n\nKynän väri jää päälle asetuksen jälkeen ohjelmassa.\n\nKun ohjelma loppuu, väri palautuu arvoon musta."},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Aseta tulostuksen tarkkuus\n\nAseta desimaalien lukumäärä tulostuksessa VEX V5 Aivojen näytöllä. \n\n![print_precision](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nChoose the level of precision that inserted reporter blocks will be printed to the screen.\n\n* Kokonainen (1) (Oletus))\n* Kymmenysosat (0.1)\n* Sadasosat (0.01)\n* Tuhannesosat (0.001)\n* Kaikki desimaalit (0.000001)\n\nTulostuksessa pyöristetään aina lähimpään arvoon. Esimerkiksi 1.67 tulostetaan kokonaisena tarkkuudella arvoon 2 ja  1.7 kymmenesosa tarkkuudella.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)\n\nValitse laite, jota käytetään. \n\n![print_precision_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_print_precision/print_precision_dropdown_with_console.png)"},"set_shaft_encoder_position":{"name":"set_shaft_encoder_position","markdown":"# Aseta encoder asentoon\n\nAsettaa encoderin arvoksi haluttu luku.\n\n![set_encoder_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta encoder asentoon** blokilla Encoder'in asennoksi laitetaan haluttu luku.\n\nTavallisesti **Aseta encoder asentoon** blokin asento asetetaan arvoon 0 ts resetoidaan laite.\n\nValitse Encoder, jota käytät ja sille arvo.\n\n![set_encoder_position_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_motor.png)\n\n"},"set_tool":{"name":"set_tool","markdown":"# Aseta työkalu\n\nAsettaa robottikäden pään työkalun tai käden pään toimijan (EOAT) V5 Robottikädessä.\n\n![set_tool_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_tool/set_tool_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nPään toimija V5 Robotikädessä voi olla joku kolmesta vaihtoehdosta: ei mitään(no attachment), sähkömagneetti tai merkkaaja. \n\n![set_marker](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_tool/set_marker.png)\n\nValitse robotiikäsi, jota käytät.\n\n![select_tool_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_tool/select_tool_arm.png)\n\nValitse työkalu V5 robottikäteen. Oletuksena on **none**.\n\n![choose_tool](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_tool/choose_tool.png)"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta kääntymisnopeus\n\nAsettaa ajopelin kääntymisnopeuden.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta kääntymisnopeus** asettaa vain nopeuden ajoneuvolle, muttei liituta sitä. **Käänny** blokki tarvitaan ajoneuvon liikkumiseen.\n\n**Aseta kääntymisnopeus** hyväksyy arvot väliltä **-100% - 100%** tai **-600rpm - 600rpm**.\n\n**Aseta kääntymisnopeus** blokin arvoina voi olla desimaali- ja kokonaisluvut sekä numeerisen blokin arvot.\n\n**Aseta kääntymisnopeus** hyväksyy riippuen asennetusta vihdepakkauksesta a´seuraavat arvot \"kierrosta minuutissa\".\n\n* Punainen vaihdepakaus: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Vihreä vaihdepakaus: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Sininen vaihdepakaus: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nAsettamalla ajopelin kääntymisnopeuden negatiiviseksi se kääntyy vastakkaiseen suuntaan.\n\nAsettamalla kääntymisnopeudena arvoon 0 pysäyttää ajopelin.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä ajopeli kääntyy hitaasi 25 % nopeudella vasemmalle.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Aseta arvoon\n\nasettaa muuttujalle tietyn arvon.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse muuttuja, jota käytetään. Muuttujan voi myös nimetä uudelleen tai poistaa käytöstä. \n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\n**Aseta arvoon** blokki hyväksyy desimali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeeristem blokkien arvoja.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Merkitse Vision kohde indeksillä\n\nMerkitse Vision kohde indeksi havaitusta joukosta kohdeindeksejä.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**kohteiden lukumäärä** blokkia voi käyttää ennen **Merkitse Vision kohde indeksillä** blokkia selvittämään, montako kohdetta kamera löytää.\n\nValitse Vision -kamera, jota käytät.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\n**Merkitse Vision kohde indeksillä** blokki hyväksyy kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n\n\n"},"set_width":{"name":"set_width","markdown":"# Aseta kynäleveys\n\nAsettaa kynän lerveyden, jolla kirjoitetaan V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n![set_width_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_width/set_width_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta kynäleveys** blokilla asetetaan kynän jäljen leveys, jolla piirretään ympyröitä ta monikulmioita V5 Aivojen näytölle. \n\n**Aseta kynäleveys** blokki hyväksyy desimaali ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/set_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"setangle":{"name":"setangle","markdown":"# Aseta kulma\n\nAsettaa työkalulautasen kulman ennen kuin seuraava [Linear move] (lineaarinen liike) tai [Joint move] (Nivelliike) blokki on suoritettu.\n\n![set_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/setangle/set_angle_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Aseta kulma** blokki asettaa työkalulautasen kulman joko **ylös** tai  **alas** ennen kuin seuraava [Linear move] tai [Joint move] blokki suoritetaan. \n\nValinta on voimassa kaikille jatkon [Linear move] ja [Joint move] blokeille.\n\n![tool_plate](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/setangle/tool_plate.png)\n\nValitse robottikäsi, jota käytät.\n\n![select_set_angle_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/setangle/select_set_angle_arm.png)\n\nValitse työkalulautasen kulma. Oletus on **ylös*.\n\n* Työkalulautasen asento  **horisontaalinen** kun sen kulma on asetettu **alas**. \n* Työkalulautasen asento  **vertikaalinen** kun sen kulma on asetettu **ylös**.  \n\n![select_angle](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/setangle/select_angle.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nLautanen alkaa kallistua, kun [Joint move] blokkia suoritetaan ja kallistuminen loppuu ennen [Linear move] blokin suoritusta.\n\n![set_angle_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/setangle/set_angle_example.png)"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Luettelon pituus\n\nkertoo luettelon alkioiden määrän.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\nValitse luettelo, jota käytät. Voit samalla uudelleennimetä tai poistaa luettelo.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\n*Luettelon pituus** raportoi alkioden lukumäärän.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# ota kuva\n\nottaa kuvan Vision -kameralla.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**ota kuva** blokki ottaa kuvan nykyhetkessä ja Vision kamera tulkitsee ja analysoi merkit/värikoodit kuvasta. \n\nAina **ota kuva** vaaditaan ensiksi ennen muiden Vision -kamera blokkien käyttöä.\n\nValitse Vision -kamera.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nValitse mitä merkkiä/värikoodia käytät. Merkit määritellään etukäteen Laite-ikkunassa.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Pyöritä\n\nVEX V5 älymoottori pyörii kunnes pyöriminen pysäytetään.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Pyöritä** blokki pyörittää moottoria ikuisesti kunnes uusi moottori blokki käynnistyy tai pysäyttää pyörimisen.\n\nValitse haluttu moottori.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nValitse pyörimissuunta. Oletussuunta määritellään Laitteet -ikkunassa. \n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Pyöritä määrän\n\npyörittää V5 moottoria tietyn määrän.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Kuinka käytetään\n\n**Pyöritä määrän** kertoo moottorille pyöriä tiettyyn suuntaan tietyn määrän alkuasennosta.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytät.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nValitse moottorin pyörimissuunta. Oletussuunnat voi määritellä Laitteet -ikkunassa. \n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\n*Pyöritä määrän** voi sallia desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeerisen blokin arvoja.\n\nValitse yksiköksi joko asteita tai kierroksia.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nOletuksen muut blokit **odota** kunnes moottori on liikkunut loppuun.\n\nVoit vaihtaa option **ja älä odota**, jolloin seuraavat blokit suoritetaan samaan aikaan kun moottori pyörii.\n\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_motor_controller":{"name":"spin_motor_controller","markdown":"# Pyöritä controller moottoria\n\nPyörittää Moottoria 393 yhdistettynä Moottoir Controlleriin 29 kunnes se pysähtyy.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Pyöritä** pyörittää Moottori 393 ikuisesti kunnes uusi moottorikomento suoreiteen tai moottori pysäytetään.\n\nValitse Moottori 393 , jota käytät.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_motor.png)\n\nValise pyörimissuunta. Suunnan voi muuttaa laite-ikkunassa. \n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_direction.png)"},"spin_servo":{"name":"spin_servo","markdown":"# Pyöritä servo\n\nPyörittää Servo Mottorin tiettyyn asentoon.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_servo/servo_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Pyöritä servo** hyväksyy arvot välillä **0 - 100 astetta**.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_servo/servo_port.png)\n\n"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Pyöritä asentoon\n\nPyörittää VEX V5 älymoottoria asentoon.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetääm\n\n**Pyöritä asentoon** määrää moottoria pyörivän tiettyyn asentoon.Asento perustuu nykyiseen moottorin pyörimisasentoon, **Pyöritä asentoon** määrää pyörimissuunnan.\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytetään.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\n**Pyöritä asentoon** blokki sallii desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeerisia blokkiarvoja.\n\nValitse pyörimisyksikkönä jokio asteet tai käännöslukumäärä.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nOletuksena seuraavat blokit odottavat **odota** kunnes moottori on pyörinyt asetetun määrän.\n\nVoit muuttaa oletuksen nuolesta **ja älä odota**, jolloin seuraavat blokit suoritetaan moottorin vielä pyöriessä.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Pysähdy\n\nPysäyttää ajopelin.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Pysähdy** blokki pysäyttää ajopelin . Voit käyttää pysähtymistapaan **Aseta pysähtymistapa** asetus joko Älä jarruta, Jarruta tai Jarrut lukossa.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli pysäytetään 3 sekunnin kuluttua.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Pysäytä moottori\n\nPysäyttää moottorin.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse moottori, jonka haluat pysäyttää.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä kouramoottoria pyöritetään 3 sekuntia ennen pysäyttämistä.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor_controller":{"name":"stop_motor_controller","markdown":"# Pysäytä moottori controller\n\nPysäyttää moottorin 393 joka on yhdistetty Controller 29.\n\n![stop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse moottori, jonka haluat pysäyttää.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_motor.png)\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä moottoria pyöritetään 3 sekuntia ennen pysäyttämistä.\n\n![stop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_example.png)"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Erotus\n\nVähennyslaskussa luku vähennetään toisesta ja lasketaan tekijöiden erotus.\n\n\n![subtract](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Erotus** hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokkeja.\n\n**erotus** blokin voi sijoittaa kaikkiin pyöreisiin arvokenttiin. \n\nKahden numeron vähennyslasku.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nKahden muuttujan vähennyslasku.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nSensoriarvojen vähennyslasku.\n\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"temperature_of_motor":{"name":"temperature_of_motor","markdown":"# Moottorin lämpötila\n\nAntaa V5 moottorin lämpötilan.\n\n![temp_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottorin lämpötila** blokin avulla ohjelmoija voi seurata , ettei V5 Älymoottori kuumene liikaa raskaassa käytössä.\n\n**Moottorin lämpötila** antaa arvot välillä **0% - 100%**. \n\nValise moottori, jota käytät.\n\n![temp_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\n**Moottorin lämpötila** blokkia voi käyttää ympyränmuotoisissa arvokentissä. \n\n![temp_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Kelloaika sekunteina\n\nRaportoi VEX V5 aivojen kellon sekunteina.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKello käynnistyy ohjelman alusta ajasta nolla sekuntia ja kulunut kellon aika raportoituu sekunteina.\n\n**Kelloaika sekunteina** arvoa käytetään eri blokkien pyöreissä arvokentissä.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n"},"torque_of_motor":{"name":"torque_of_motor","markdown":"# Moottorin vääntö\n\nAntaa V5 Älymoottorin vääntömäärän (kääntövoiman) tällä hetkellä.\n\n![motor_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/torque_of_motor/motor_torque.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottorin vääntö** antaa arvot välillä **0.0 - 18.6 tuuma-paunaa (InLB)** tai **0.0 to 2.1 Newton-metriä (Nm)**. \n\nValitse moottori, jota käytät.\n\n![motor_torque_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_device.png)\n\nValitse yksikkö, jota käytät (InLb) tai (Nm).\n\n![motor_torque_units](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_units.png)\n\n**Moottorin vääntö** arvoa voi käyttää pyöreämuotoissa arvokentissä.\n\n![motor_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_inserted.png)"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Käänny\n\nKääntää ajopeliä jatkuvasti.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Käänny** blokki kääntää ajopeliä kunnes uusi ajopeli -blokki tulee käyttöön tai ohjelman suoritus loppuu.\n\nValitse suunta, johon ajopeli kääntyy.\n\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Käänny määrän\n\nKääntää ajopeliä tietyn määrän.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse suunta mihin ajopeli kääntyy.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\n**Käänny määrän** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeerisia blokinarvoja.\n\nAnna astemäärä, jonka ajopeli kääntyy.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nOletuksena muut blokit **odottaa** kunnes ajopeli on kääntynyt.\n\nVoit myös valita **ja älä odota**, jolloin seuraavat blokit suoritetaan samalla kun ajopeli kääntyy.\n\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Käänny ajosuunnasta\n\nKääntää ajopelin tiettyyn suuntaan käyttäen Gyro-sensoria.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Käänny ajosuunnasta** blokkia voi käyttää kääntämään ajopelin kellotaulun mukaiseen asentoon (kuvassa).\n\n![TopDownBot01](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_to_heading/TopDownBot01.jpg)\n\nPerustuu nykyisen gyron antamasta suunnasta , **Käänny ajosuunasta** päättelee, mihin suuntaan käännös tehdään.\n\n**Käänny ajosuunasta** hyväksyy arvoväliltä **0.00 - 359.99** asteita.\n\n**Käänny ajosuunnasta** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeeristen blokkien arvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli tekee 4 käännöstä: \n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Vasemmalle (vastapäivään) kellotaulun kohtaan 45 astetta\n- Vasemmalle (vastapäivään) kellotaulun kohtaan 90 astetta\n- Vasemmalle (vastapäivään) kellotaulun kohtaan 270 astetta\n- Oikealle (myötäpäivään) kellotaulukohtaan 180 astetta\n\nOletuksena seuraavat blokit **odotaa** kunnes ajopeli on kääntynyt.\n\nVoit valita nuolivalinnasta **ja älä odota** , joka antaa seuraaville blokeilla ajoluvan ennen ajopelin käännöstä.\n\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Käännä kiertokulmaa\n\nKääntää ajopeliä tiettyyn kulmaan lähtöasennosta käyttäen 3-lanka Gyroa tai V% Inertial sensoria.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Käännä kiertokulmaa** blokkia käytetään, kun halutaa kääntää ajopeliä tiettyyn asentoon lähtöasennosta joko vastapäivään positiivisilla arvoilla tai myötäpäivään negatiivisilla arvoilla.\n\nPerustuu nykyiselle **Ajosuunta asteina** ajopelin nykyisenä suuntana, **Käännä kiertokulmaa** määrittää suunnan etumerkillä.\n\n**Käännä kiertokulmaa** blokki hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja ja numeerisia blokinarvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä ajopeli kääntyy 4 eri kertaa: \n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Vasemmalle(vastapäivään) kohtaan 90 astetta lähtöasennosta\n- Vasemmalle(vastapäivään) 180 astetta lähtöasennosta\n- Oikealle (myötäpäivään) -45 astetta lähtöasennosta\n- Vasemmalle (myötäpäivään) 0 asetta lähtöasennosta (alkuperäinen asento)\n\nOletuksena muut blokit noudattaa **odota** kunnes ajopeli on kääntynyt.\n\nVoit valita alasvetonuolesta **ja älä odota**, jolloin siirrytään heti seuraavaan blokkiin samaan aikaan kun ajopeli kääntyy.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Muuttuja\n\nRaportoi muuttujan arvon.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Muuttuja** blokkia käytetään tallentamaan muuttujan arvoja. Käytä **Aseta arvoon** -blokkia antamaan muuttujalle alkuarvo tai muuttamaan sen arvoa.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\n**Muuttuja** raportointiblokkia käytetään muiden blokkien pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nMuuttujat luodaan **Tee muuttuja**-painikkeella.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Moottorin nopeus\n\nAntaa VEX V5 Älymoottorin nopeuden.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Moottorin nopeus** antaa nopeuden arvoväliltä **-100% - 100%** tai **-600rpm - 600rpm**.\n\n**Moottorin nopeus** antaa nopeuden \"kierrosta minuutissa\" riippuen vaihdepakkauksesta, joka on asennettuV% moottoriin.\n\n* Punainen vaihdepakkaus: -100rpm - 100rpm\n* Vihreä vaihdepakkaus: -200rpm - 200rpm\n* Sininen vaihdepakkaus: -600rpm - 600rpm\n\nValitse moottori, jota käytät.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nValitse, millä yksiköllä nopeutta tarkastellaan nopeus % tai kierrosta minuutissa (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nRaportointiblokkia **Moottorin nopeus** käytetään eri blokkien ympyrämuotoisissa kentissä.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"velocity_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"velocity_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Encoder -sensorin antama nopeus\n\nAntaa Encoder -sensorin antaman nopeuden.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Encoder -sensorin antama nopeus** antaa nopeuden joko **asteita sekunnissa** tai **kierrosta minuutissa**.\n\nValitse Encoder-laite, jota käytät.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_motor.png)\n\nValitse kumpaaa yksikköä käytetään **asteita sekunnissa** (dps) tai **kierrosta minuutissa**(rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_unit.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Vision kohde \n\nRaportoi tiedot Vision -kameran havaitsemasta kohteesta.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Vision kohde** blokin käytössä, suorita seuraavat vaiheet:\n\n1. Lisää ja määrittele Vision -kamera Laitteet -ikkunassa.\n2. **Ota kuva** Vision -kameralla ja tarkista kuvan merkki/värikoodi.\n3. Käytä **Vision kohde havaittu?** blokkia ja tarkista onko Vision -kamera löytänyt halutun merkin/ värikoodin.\n\nKun Vision -kamera havaitsee kohteen, voit käyttää muita Vision -blokkeja kertomaan tarkemmin kohteesta tietoja.\n\n* Käytä **merkitse vision kohde indeksillä** kohteesta, josta haluta lisätietoja. Oletuksena suurin kohde valitaan.\n* Käytä **kohteiden lukumäärä** kohteesta, jolla saat tietää, kuinka monta kysytyn merkin / värikoodin esinettä löytyy.\n* Käytä **vision kohde** kohteesta, jolla saat tiedot kohteen koosta ja sijainnista.\n\nValitse Vision -kamera,jota haluat käyttää.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nValitse mitä arvoa haluat Vision -kameran raportoivan:\n\n* Leveys - Kuinka leveä kohde on pixeleinä väliltä **2 - 316 px**.\n* Korkeus - Kuinka korkea kohde on pixeleinä väliltä **2 - 212 px**. \n* KeskipisteX - Raportoi kohteen X keskipisteen koordinaatin väliltä **0 - 315 px**.\n* KeskipisteY - Raportoi kohteen Y keskipisteen koordinaatin väliltä  **0 - 211 px**.\n* Kulma - Raportoi kohteen kulman väliltä **0 - 180 astetta**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nRaportointiblokkia **vision kohde** voi käyttää eri blokkien pyöreämuotoisissa arvokentissä.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Odota\n\nOdota komennolla voit määrätä ohjelman odottavan halutun sekuntimäärän ennenkuin siirrytään seuraavaan blokkiin.\n\n![wait](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/wait/wait.png)\n\n## How To Use\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse sekuntimäärä komentoon **Odota**.\n\n**Odota** blokiin voi kirjoittaa desimaali ja kokonaislukauja.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Wait until\n\nWaits for a Boolean block to report **true** before moving to the next block.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Wait until** will repeatedly check a Boolean reporter block, and will not move to the next block until the Boolean report block reports **true**.\n\nThe **wait until** Boolean block can accept hexagonal (six-sided) shaped blocks.\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n"},"when_autonomous":{"name":"when_autonomous","markdown":"# When autonomous\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when an \"autonomous\" mode signal is received from a competition field or competition switch.\n\n![when_autonomous](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_autonomous/when_autonomous.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nAny blocks attached to the **when autonomous** event will be run when the robot is connected to a competition field or competition switch that is set to the \"autonomous\" mode.\n\nUsers can have up to 50 **when autonomous control** blocks in a project."},"when_brain_screen":{"name":"when_brain_screen","markdown":"# Kun aivojen näyttöä\n\nSuorittaa pinon komentoja, kun VEX V5 Aivojen näyttöä on painettu\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed.png)\n\n## Miten äytetään\n\n**Kun aivojen näyttöä** tapahtumaa voi käyttää kun V5 AIvojen kosketusnäyttöä painamalla haluaa eri toimintoja. \n\nKun tarkentaa yhdessä **näytön paikka** arvon kanssa voi saada eriyttää toimintoja tapauksessa, jossa Aivojen kosketusnäyttöä on painettu.\n\nValitse toiminnot, jotka suoritetaan kun ksketusnäyttöä **painettu** tai **vapautettu** \n \n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed_condition.png)"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Kun saan viestin\n\nSuorittaa ehtoblokin alla nipussa olevat blokit, kun valittu viesti on saapunut.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse, mitä viestiä käytetään. Voit luoda myös uuden viestin.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n**Kun saan viestin** reagoi vain **lähetä viesti** or **lähetä viesti ja odota** blokkeihin eri komentonipuissa."},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Kun painokytkintä painettu\n\nSuorittaa halutun nipun blokkeja ehtoblokin alta, kun VEX V5 Painokytkintä on painettu tai vapautettu.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse Painokytkin, jota käytät.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nValitse ne toiminnot, jotka suoritetaan tapahtumista - **painettu** tai **vapautettu** \n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Kun ohjaintatin\n\nSuorittaa ehtoblokin alle niputetut blokit, kun VEX V5 Ohjaimen ao tattia on liikuteltu.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse Ohjain, jota käytetään.\n\n![when_controller_axis_device](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_device.png)\n\nValitse Ohjaimen tatti, jota käytetään.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Kun ohjainnappia\n\nSuoriteen blokin alla nipussa olevat komennot kun valittua VEX V5 Ohjaimen nappia on painettu ta vapautettu\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse ohjain, jota haluat käyttää.\n\n![when_controller_button_controller](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_controller.png)\n\nValitse nappi, jota haluat käyttää.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\nValitse toiminnot, jotka napin painallus käynnistää tapahtumissa  **painettu** tai **vapautettu**  \n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_driver":{"name":"when_driver","markdown":"# Kun ajetaan ohjaimella\n\nSuorittaa komennon alla olevat komennot kun \"ajetaan ohjaimella\" signaali on saatu kilpailukentältä tai kilpailusuorituksen aloituksesta.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_driver/when_driver.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKaikki blokit **Kun ajetaan ohjaimella** tapahtuman alta suoritetaan kun robotti on liitetty kilpailukenttään tai kun kilpailukytkin on on asetettu  \"ajetaan ohjaimella\" -moodiin.\n\n**Toista ikuisesti** luupia suositellaan ** Kun ajetaan ohjaimella** tapahtuman kanssa, jotta V5 ohjain toiminnot voidaan suorittaa jatkuvasti kilpailusuorituksen tässä . \n\nOhjelmassa on sallittu 50 eri ** Kun ajetaan ohjaimella** blokkia."},"when_limit":{"name":"when_limit","markdown":"# Kun raja saavutettu\n\nSuorittaa alle olevat blokit kun Raja -sensoria on painettu tai vapautettu.\n\n![when_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_limit/when_limit.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse raja-sensori, jota käytät.\n\n![when_limit_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_limit/when_limit_select.png)\n\nValitse mitä toimintoa seurataan - **painettu** tai **vapautettu** \n\n![when_limit_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_limit/when_limit_condition.png)\n"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Kun käynnissä\n\nSuorittaa sen alla nipussa olevat blokit kun ohjelma käynnistyy.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kun käynnissä** tapahtuma käynnistyy, kun VEX V5 Aivojen valikosta ko ohjelma valittu tai  **suorita ohjelma** painiketta on painettu VEXcode V5 Blocks -ohjelmassa.\n\nKaikkien uusien ohjelmien pitää automaattisesti sisältää **Kun käynnissä** blokki. Ohjelma voi sisältää korkeintaan 50 *Kun käynnissä** blokkeja.\n\n\n\n**Kun käynnissä** a käytetään myös \"esi-automaattisessa\" -moodissa VRC kilpailuohjelmassa.\n\n"},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Kun kello\n\nSuorittaa käynnistysehdolla olevat blokit, kun VEX V% Aivojen kellonaika on suurempi kuin annettu aika sekunteina.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nAivojen kello käynnistyy joka ohjelman alussa.\n\nValitse haluttu sekuntimäärä ehdon käynnistykseen.**Kun kello >** blokin alla olevat komennot suoritetaan, kun Aivojen kellon sekuntimäärä on suurempi kuin **Kun kello>** tapahtumaan annettu sekunttimäärä.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\n**Kun kello >** ehto hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaisluvut.\n\n**Kun kello >** ei hyväksy muita ehtoja.\n\n"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# While\n\nEhtoblokki, joka toistaa sen sisällä olevat blokit, kun sen Boolean ehto on **tosi**.  \n\n![while](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/while/while.png)\n\n## How To Use\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Kun** blokki tarkistaa Boolean ehdon joka toiston alussa. \n\nJos Boolean ehto on **tosi**,niin **Kun** silmukan sisällä olevat blokit suoritetaan.\n\nJos Boolean ehto on **epätosi**,niin hypätään **Kun** silmukan ohi seuraavaan komentoon.\n\n**Kun** toistoblokki hyväksyy ehdoksi kaikki kuusikulmaisen muotoiset ehtoblokit.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/fi/while/while_inserted.png)"}},"python":{"control_break":{"name":"control_break","markdown":"# Keskeytä\n\nKomennolla hypätään pois toistorakenteesta.\n\n```don\nbreak\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun lisätään `break` kommento johonkin kohtaabn toistorakennetta, se aiheutta hypyn pois siitä toiston jälkeiseen seuraavaan komentoon. \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nesimerkissä ajataan eteenpäin ja ja tarkistetaan , onko `bumper` törmäysanturia painettu.\n\nJos törmäysanturia bumber on **pressed**, 'break` komento aiheuttaa hypyn pois silmukan suorituksesta ja ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n```don\nwhile True:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n    if bumper.pressing():\n        break\n```","signature":"break"},"control_for_loop":{"name":"control_for_loop","markdown":"# Toista\n\nSilmukkakomento, jossa koodia toistetaan annetun numeron mukainen määrä.\n\n```don\nfor value in range(10):\n    pass\n```\n\n# Miten käytetään\n\nEnsiksi korvaa `value` muuttujalla , joka iteroidaan läpi `range()` funktion arvon.\n\nSitten korvaa  `10` arvolla , joka on iteraatiin lukumäärän loppuarvo.\n\nLisää komentoriveille aina 4 tyhjää osoittamaan , että rivit kuuluvat silmukan sisälle `for` ohjausrakenteessa.\n\nfor` komennnon sisällä ei saa olla tyhjää vaan lisää `pass` komento kutenedellä määritelty.\n\nHuomaa että luuppi alkaa aina indeksillä 0.\n\n`For` luuppeja voi laittaa toistensa sisään sisäkkäin.\n\n# Esimerkki\n\nSeuraava toista silmukka tulostaa luvut 0 lukuun 2 omille riveille:\n\n```don\nfor i in range(3):\n   brain.screen.print(i)\n   brain.screen.new_line()\n```\n   \nThis will print:\n\n```\n0\n1\n2\n```","signature":"for value in range (10"},"control_if_else_statement":{"name":"control_if_else_statement","markdown":"# Jos/muuten\n\nOhjauslause, joka suorittaa If -haaran, jos ehto on 'true' (tosi) ja Else -haaran jos ehto on 'false' (epätosi). \n\n```don\nif condition:\n    pass\nelse:\n    pass\n\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n'if` komento on ehto , joka saa joko arvon **True** tai **False**. Voit yhdistää ehtoihin useamman loogisen operaattorin `and`, `or`, and `not`. \n\nJos ehto saa arvon **True**, `if ehdon:` haara suoritetaan. Jos ehto saa arvon **False**, `else:` haaran komennot suoritetaan.\n\nKomentokoodi `if` ja `else` haarassa komennot on sisennetty 4 tyhjällä merkillä.\n\nif/else` komennossa ei saa olla tyhjiä rivejä vaan tyhjä korvataan komennolla `pass`. \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTämä `if/else` koodi ajaa robottia eteenpäin, jos muuttuja my_variable saa arvon 1. Jos arvo ei ole 1, ajetaan taaksenpäin. \n\n```don\nif (my_variable == 1):\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nelse:\n    drivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"if conditio"},"control_if_statement":{"name":"control_if_statement","markdown":"# Jos\n\nOhjauslause, joka päättelee, suoritetaanko ehdon `condition` toiminnot.\n\n```don\nif condition:\n    pass\n    \n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKorvaa sana `condition` Boolean lausekkeella, joka saa jokoa rvon `True` tai `False`. Jos totuusarvo on `True`, niin `if` ehdon komennot suoritetaan.\n\nLisää aina 4 tyhjää merkki **spacebar** näppäimellä `if` haaran komentojen edelle. \n\n`if` ehto ei saa olla tyhjä vaain lisää vähintään komento `pass` haaran komennoksi. \n\n## Esimerkki\n\n`if` haaran komennot ssuoritetaan , jos `my_variable`= 1, jolloin robotti ajaa eteenpäin.\n\n```don\nif (my_variable == 1):\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"if condition:\\n\\tpass"},"control_wait":{"name":"control_wait","markdown":"# Odota\n\nOdottaa asetetun ajan ennen seuraavaa komentoa.\n\n```python\nwait(TIME, SECONDS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAseta odotusaika **SECONDS** (sekuntia) , jonka haluat komennon **wait** odottavan ennen seuraavaa komentoa.\n\n```python\nwait(10, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"wait(TIME, SECONDS)"},"control_wait_until":{"name":"control_wait_until","markdown":"# Kun ei\n\nOhjauskomento jatkaa silmukan sisällä olevien komentojen suoritusta kunnes Kun ehto toteutuu eli saa arvon **true**.\n\n```python\nwhile not condition:\n    pass\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`while not` komento tarkistaa jokaisen silmukan  kierroksen alussa ehtoa ja siirtyy seuraavaan silmukan jälkeiseen komentoon vasta kun ehto saa arvon **true.**\n\nJos ehto on **false**, silmukan sisäll' oleva koodi suoritetaan.\n\nJos ehto on **true**, silmukan yli hyvätään ja seuraava komento suoritetaan ja jatketaan siitä edelleen.\n\n`while not` komento hyväksyy Boolean -lausekkeita, jotka voivat saada arvot 'True` tai `False`. Boolean -tyyppisiä ehtoja ovat vertailuehdot ja loogiset operaatiot. \n\nNumeerisina arvoina käy **0** tarkoittaen `False`, ja mikä tahansa muu numeerinen arvo vastaa arvoa `True`. \n\nLisää rivien alkuun 4 tyhjää merkkiä tarkoittaen että ne ovat osa silmuan sisällä olevia komentoja. \n\n`while not` silmukka ei saa olla tyhjä vaan lisää komento `pass` tarkoittanmaan ettei silmukassa tehdä mitään. \n\n## Esimerkki\n\n`while not` silmukka tulostaa sanan \"Hello\" viisi kertaa kunnes muuttuja my_variable saa arvon 5.\n\n```python\nmy_variable = 0\n\nwhile not my_variable == 5:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\n    brain.screen.new_line()\n    my_variable += 1\n```","signature":"while not expressio"},"control_while_loop":{"name":"control_while_loop","markdown":"# Kun\n\nSilmukka , joka toistetaan niin kauan kuin sen ehto on voimassa ts **true**.   \n\n```python\nwhile condition:\n    pass\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`while` silmukka tarkistaa sen ehdon aina jokaisen kierroksen alussa. \n\nJos ehto on **true** (tosi), silmukan sisällä oleva koodi suoritetaan.\n\nJos ehto on **false** (epätosi), silmukan sisällä oleva koodi hypätään yli ja siirrytään seuraavaan komentoon.\n\n`while` silmukka tarkastelee vain ehdon loogista arvoa joko `True` tai `False`. Ehdoksi voi sijoittaa minkä tahansa  Booleans -ehdon ilmaisun loogisen operaation tai vertailuoperaation. \n\nVoit käyttää yös nyúmeerisia arvolausekkeita ts arvo **0** merkitsee `False` ja muut **ei 0 numerot** merkistevät arvoa `True`. \n\nLisää aina 4 tyhjää merkkiä *spacebar** rivin alkuun , jolla eroitat, mitkä komennot kuuluvat `while` silmukkaan mukaan. \n\n`while` komentoa ei saa sisältyy pelkkää tyhjää vaan silloin silmukan sisään tulee `pass` komento. \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä `while` silmukassa tulsotetaan sana \"Hello\" uusille riveille kun aivojen kelloaika on alle 50 sekuntia.\n\n```python\nwhile brain.timer.time(SECONDS) < 50:\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello\")\n    brain.screen.next_row()\n```","signature":"while expressio"},"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain":{"name":"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain","markdown":"# Ajopelin gyron kalibrointi\n\nKalibroi ajopelin gyro.\n\n```python\nturn_gyro_smart.calibrate()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`turn_gyro_smart.calibrate()` komento kalibroi ajopelin gyron. Ajopelin pitää olla paikallaan kalibroinnin ajan.\n\nKomento `wait` potää lisätä ennen komentoa `turn_gyro_smart.calibrate()`, jotta kalibrointi onnistuu.\n\n```python\nturn_gyro_smart.calibrate()\nwait(3, SECONDS)\n```","signature":"turn_gyro_smart.calibrate()"},"drivetrain_drive":{"name":"drivetrain_drive","markdown":"# Aja\n\nAjopeli liikkuu ikuisuuden suuntaan, joka määritelty suluissa. \n\nKaikki ajopelin ajomoottorit ajavat eteen tai taaksepäin nopeutta , joka on määritelty komennolla `drivetrain.set_drive_velocity`, oletus on 50%. \n\nNegatiiviset nopeusarvot aiheuttavat sen, etttä ajopeli ajaa vastakkaiseen suuntaan parametrilla  FORWARD .\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.drive` komennolla ajopeli ajaa ikuisuuden, kunnes joku uusi ajokomento on annettu tai ohjelma on lopetettu.\n\n## Esimerkit\n\nKäytä `FORWARD` argumenttia isoilla kirjaimilla, kun ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nKäytä `REVERSE` argumenttia isoilla kirjaimilla, kun ajopeli peruuttaa\n\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.drive(FOWARD)"},"drivetrain_drive_for":{"name":"drivetrain_drive_for","markdown":"# Aja matka\n\nLiikuttaa ajopeliä tietyn matkan. Kaikki ajopelin moottorit ajavat joku eteen- tai taaksepäin nopeudelle, joka on annettu komennolla `drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` . Kun matka on saavutettu, ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(DIRECTION, DISTANCE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKuinka pitkän matkan ajopeli liikkuu, määrätään suluissa kolmella parametrilla pilkulla eroteltuina \n\nEnsimmäinen argumentti on suunta 'DIRECTION' joka on joko `FORWARD` tai `REVERSE` isoilla kirjaimilla.  \n\nToinen argumentti on matka `DISTANCE`, jonka ajopeli ajaa.\n\nKolmas argumetti on 'UNITS' yksikkö , jossa matka annetaan, joko `INCHES` tai `MM` (millimetriä) isoilla kirjaimilla.\n\n`DISTANCE` parameter accepts numeric values. Negative values will cause the V5 Robot to drive in the opposite of the input `DIRECTION`.\n\n```\ndrivetrain.drive_for(REVERSE, 5.0, INCHES)\n```\n\n'drive_for` komento on ns blokkaava komento ts seuraavat komennot odottavat, että ajosuoritus on valmis.\n\n## Lisäparametri\n\nVoit käyttää 4. lisäparametyria `wait=False`, jolloin seuraavat komennot eivät odota ajon loppua.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM, wait=False)\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä komennon `drivetrain.drive_for` matka-argumenttina on käytetty muuttujaa distance_variable.\n\nV5 Robotti ajaa 200 MM eteenpäin.\n\n```don\ndistance_variable = 200\n\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, distance_variable, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 2, MM, wait=True)"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta ajopelin nopeus\n\nAsettaa ajopelin nopeuden komennoille `drive` ja `drive_for`.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` komento asettaa ajopelin nopeuden komeentojen `drive` ja `drive_for` käyttöön. Komento ei liikuta ajopeliä.\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` hyväksyy arvoja, jotka riippuvat sen toisesta parametrista.\n\nJos `PERCENT` (prosenttia) on käytössä, niin nopeus **VELOCITY** hyväksyy arvot **-100 - 100**.\n\n`drivetrain.set_drive_velocity` komennon **UNITS** parametrina voi käyttää `RPM` (kierrosta minuutissa). Riippuen vaihdepakkauksesta , jotka asennettu ajomoottoreihin, **VELOCITY** arvot vaihtelevat seuraavasti:\n\n* Red Cartridge: (punainen) -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: Ivihreä) -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: (sininen) -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nJos nopeudeksi asettaa negatiivisen arvon, ajopeli liikkuu vastakkaiseen suuntaa, mitä `DIRECTION` parametrissa on asetettu komennoissa `drive` tai `drive_for`.\n\nJos nopeus asetetaan arvoon nolla, ajopeli pysähtyy komennoilla `drive` tai `drive_for`.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä Drivetrain ajaa taaksepäin, kun nopeus määrätty negatiivisella luvulla.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```\n\nTässä ajopeli ei liiku\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_drive_velocity(0, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_drive_velocity(VELOCITY, PRECENT)"},"drivetrain_set_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_set_heading","markdown":"# Aseta ajosuunta\n\nAsettaa ajopelin Gyrolle tarkan ajosuunnan.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_heading(HEADING, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.set_heading` komennolla voi ajopelin ajosuunnan muuttaa. tyypillisesti ajosuunnan arvo nollataan jossain kohtaa ohjelman suoritusta helpottamaan uuden suuunnan ottoa.\n\n`drivetrain.set_heading` hyväksyy arvot välillä **0 - 360** ensimmäisenä argumenttina ja `DEGREES` (asteet) kirjoitettuna isoilla kirjaimilla.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajosuunta asetetaan arvoon 90 astetta. \n\nKoska ajosuunta on asetettu arvoon 90 astetta, ei seuraava komento `turn_to_heading` muuta asentoa, koska se on sama asetuksen mukainen.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_heading(90, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_set_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_rotation","markdown":"# Aseta kääntymiskulma\n\nAsettaa ajopelin Gyro -sensorin kulman.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(ROTATION, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.set_rotation` komennolla Gyro sensorin arvoksi voi asettaa minkä tahansa positiivisen tai negatiivisen arvon.\n\n`ROTATION` parametri sallii numeerisia arvoja.\n\n`ROTATION` parametri ei rajoitu **does not** arvoihin 0-359 astetta.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä robotti kääntyy yhteensä 210 astetta:\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(120, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.set_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(45, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Käänny oikealle myötäpäivään kääntymiskulmaan 120 degrees.\n- Aseta nykyinen kääntymiskulma arvoon -45 astetta.\n- Käänny oikealle myötäpäivään lisää 90 astetta (-45 astetta +45 astetta) edellisen asetuksen mukaan.","signature":"drivetrain.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_set_stopping":{"name":"drivetrain_set_stopping","markdown":"```python\ndrivetrain.set_stopping(MODE)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAseta `MODE` parametrille joku seuraavista valinta:\n\n* BRAKE: pysäytttää ajopelin heti.\n* COAST: ajopeli pysähtyy vähittellen.\n* HOLD: pysäyttää ajopelin heti ja pitää pysähdysasennon, vaikka ajopeli liikkuisi muuten esim esineen päältä liukuen alas. \n\n `drivetrain.set_stopping()` komento pysyy voimassa jatkossakin niin kauan kunnes tehdään uusi määritys pysähdystavalle.\n \n## Esimerki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli ajaa 200 mm ennenkuin se pysähtyy vähitellen -optiolla.\n\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_stopping(COAST)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_stopping(BRAKE)"},"drivetrain_set_timeout":{"name":"drivetrain_set_timeout","markdown":"# Aseta aikaraja\n\n`drivetrain.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)` asettaa aikarajan, kuinka kauan robotin liikekomento jatkuu.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomentoa käytetään estämään ohjelman keskeytys jos seuraava liikekomento ei pääse tavoiteasemaan.\n\nAseta määrä sekunteina `SECONDS`.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä on asetettu 3 sekunnin aikaraja ajo komennolle.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.set_timeout(3, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 1000, MM)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity_percent":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity_percent","markdown":"# Aseta kääntymisnopeus\n\nAsettaa ajopelin kääntymisen nopeuden.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` asettaa ajopelin kääntymisnopeuden, mutta se ei liikuta ajopeliä. Nopeus asetetaan kääntymiskomennoille `turn` tai `turn_for`.\n\n`drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` hyväksyy arvoja, jotka riippuvat yksiköstää, jota käytetään toisessa parametrissa.\n\nJos `PERCENT` (prosentti) yksikkö on käytössä toisena parametrina, arvot voivat olla välillä **-100 - 100**.\n\nvaihtoehtoisesti `drivetrain.set_turn_velocity` komennon  toinen parametri **UNITS** voi olla `RPM`. Riippuen asennetuista vaihdepakkauksista ajomoottoreihin **VELOCITY** parametrin arvot voivat olla välillä:\n\n* Red Cartridge: (punainen) -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: (vihreä) -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: (sininen) -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nJos asettaa ajopelin kääntymisnopeuden negatiiviseena rvoon, ajopeli liikkuu oletetsesta vastakkaiseen suuntaan.\n\nJos asettaa ajopelin kääntymisnopeuden arvoon nolla, niin ajopeli pysähtyy komermmoilla `turn` ja `turn_for`.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli kääntyy vastakkaiseen suuuntaan vasemmalle , kun kääntymisnopeus on asetettu negatiiviseen arvoon.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.set_turn_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.set_turn_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)"},"drivetrain_stop":{"name":"drivetrain_stop","markdown":"# Pysäytä\n\nPysäytä ajopeli.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.stop()` komento pysäyttää ajopelin. Sillä ei ole argumentteja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli pysähtyy kun se on ajanut 3 sekuntia eeenpäin.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"drivetrain.stop()"},"drivetrain_turn":{"name":"drivetrain_turn","markdown":"# Käänny\n\nAjopeli kääntyy jatkuvasti joko oikealle tai vasemmalle.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.turn` komennolla ajopeli kääntyy ikuisesti haluttuun suuntaan kunnes joku uusi komento sen kumoaa tai ohjelma loppuu.\n\nKäytä `LEFT` argumenttia isoilla kirjaimilla, kun käännät vasemmalle.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(LEFT)\n```\n\nKäytä `RIGHT` argumenttia isoilla kirjaimilla, kun käännät oikealle.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopelia ajaa eteenpäin 200 MM ennen kuin kääntyy oikealle ikuisuuden.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\n\ndrivetrain.turn(RIGHT)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn(RIGHT)"},"drivetrain_turn_for":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_for","markdown":"# Käänny määrä\n\nKääntää ajopeliä määrätyn määrän asteita.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(DIRECTION, ANGLE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nEnsimmäinen argumentti komennossa määrää suunnan: `LEFT` (vasemmalle) tai `RIGHT` (oikelle), isoilla kirjaimilla . \n\nToinen argumentti määrää kulman asteina välillä  0 - 360. \n\nKolmas argumentti on käännöksen yksikkö, Se on `DEGREES` (astetta) isoilla kirjaimilla. \n\nKomento`turn_for` on ns blokkaava komento ts se estää seuraavien komentojen suorituksen , kunnes käännös on valmis.\n\n## Lisäparametrit\n\nNeljäs argumetti on ns lisäargumentti `wait=False` , jolloin seuraava komento suoritetaankin heti käännöksen alettua.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(LEFT, 90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä V5 Robotti kääntyy 270 astetta oikealle.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 270, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_for(RIGHT, 90, DEGREES, wait=True)"},"drivetrain_turn_to_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Käänny ajosuuntaan\n\nKääntää ajopeliä tiettyyn ajosuuntaan sen Gyro tai Inertial sensorin avulla.\n\n`drivetrain.turn_to_heading(HEADING, UNITS)`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.turn_to_heading` komentoa käytetään kääntämään ajopeliä halutuun kellotaulun ajosuuntaan.\n\nKomento perustuu nykyiseen Gyron ajosuuntaan ja `drivetrain.turn_to_heading` määrittää tämän mukaan mihin suuntaan käännös tehdään.\n\n`HEADING` parametri hyväksyy arvot välillä **0.00 - 359.99** .\n\nYksikkö `UNITS` parametri on asteita `DEGREES`.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli tekee neljä käännöstä: \n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(45.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(90.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(270.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(180.0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- oikealla ajosuuntaan 45 astetta\n- oikealle ajosuuntaan 90 astetta\n- Oikealle ajosuuntaan 270 astetta\n- Vasemmalle ajosuuntaan 180 astetta\n\n`turn_to_heading` kometo estää/odottaa seuraavien kometojen suorituksen kunnes se on saanut käännöäksen valmiiksi.\n\n## Lisäparametrit\n\nVoit käyttää parametria `wait=False` kolmantena parametrina, jos haluat jatkaa suoraan `turn_to_heading` komennon jälkeiseen komentoon odottamatta ajopelin käännöstä loppuun.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_heading(180.0, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_to_heading(90, DEGREES)"},"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Käännä kiertokulmaa määrän\n\nKääntää ajopeliä kiertokulman tiettyyn astemäärään nykyisen gyron astemäärän perusteella.\n\n`drivetrain.turn_to_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation` komentoa voi käyttää kääntämään ajopeliä positiivisen arvolla myötäpäivään tai negatiivisella arvolla vastapäivään.\n\nRiippuen nykyisestä kääntymiskulman arvosta gyrosensorissa `drivetrain.turn_to_rotation` päättelee mihin suuntaan se kääntyy.\n\n`ROTATION` parametri hyväksyy numeerisia rvoja.\n\nNumeeriset arvot eivät **not** rajoita arvoja välillä **0 - 359.99** astetta. Käännökset ovat absoluuttisia ja voivat kääntää robottia enemmän kuin kerran\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli tekee 4 käännöstä:\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90.0, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(180, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(-45, DEGREES)\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n- Oikealla myötäpäivään kohtaan 90 astetta\n- Oikealla myötäpäivään kohtaan 180 astetta\n- Vasemmalle vastapäivään kohtaan -45 astetta\n- Oikealla myötäpäivään kohtaan 0 astetta\n\n'drivetrain.turn_to_rotation` komento estää muiden komentojen suorituksen , jos käännös on kesken.\n\n## Lisäparametri \n\nVoit lisätä lisäparametrin `wait=False`, jolloin `turn_to_rotation` komento ei estä seuraavien komentojen suoritusta kesken käännöstä.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.turn_to_rotation(180.0, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```","signature":"drivetrain.turn_to_rotation(90, DEGREES, wait=True)"},"events_brain_screen_pressed":{"name":"events_brain_screen_pressed","markdown":"#  Aivojen näyttöä koskettu\n\nSuorittaa ns callback funktion, kun aivojen kosketusnäyttöä on kosketettu.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n'brain.screen.pressed()` komennon avulla voi laukaista toimintoja, kun näyttöä on kosketettu. \n\nYhdessä komennon `brain.screen.x_position()` ja `brain.screen.y_position()` kanssa saadaan interaktiivisuutta robotin ja käyttäjän välille.\n\nEnsiksi pitää luoda funktio sille, kun näyttöä kosketetaan ja sille nimi , jota käytetään callback-funtiossa parametrina, kun tapahtuma aktivoituu.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_event():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Event has occurred\")\n  \n# Register event with a callback function\nbrain.screen.pressed(run_on_event)\n\n```","signature":"brain.screen.pressed(callback)"},"events_brain_screen_released":{"name":"events_brain_screen_released","markdown":"#  Aivojen näyttöä vapautettu\n\nSuorittaa ns callback funktion, kun aivojen kosketusnäyttöä on kosketus vapautetaan.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.released(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`brain.screen.released()` komennon avulla voi laukaista toimintoja näytön kosketuksen vapauttamisessa. \n\nYhdessä komennon `brain.screen.x_position()` ja `brain.screen.y_position()` kanssa saadaan interaktiivisuutta robotin ja käyttäjän välille.\nEnsiksi pitää luoda funktio sille, kun näyttöä kosketus loppuu ja nimi , jota käytetään callback-funtiossa parametrina , kun tapahtuma aktivoituu.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_event():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Event has occurred\")\n  \n# Register event with a callback function\nbrain.screen.released(run_on_event)\n```","signature":"brain.screen.released(callback)"},"events_brain_timer_event":{"name":"events_brain_timer_event","markdown":"# Aivojen kello tapahtuma\n\nSuorittaa halutun callback funktion, kun V5 Aivojen kello on suurempi kuin annettu parametriarvo.\n\n```python\nbrain.timer.event(callback, 1000)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nV5 Aivojen kello käynnistyy ohjelman alussa.\n\nMääritä aikaraja tapahtumalle. `brain.timer.event()` tapahtuma suoritetaan kerran kun kello on **suurempi kuin** annettu aikaraja.\n\n`brain.timer.event()` hyväskyy kokonaislukuja ja yksikkönä on millisekunnit.\n\nLuo funktio , jota kutsutaan, kun kello käynyt yli aikarajan. Nimeä funktio ja käytä sitä tapahtuman `callback` parametrina.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_event():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Event has occurred\")\n  \n# Register event with a callback function\nbrain.timer.event(run_on_event, 2000)\n```","signature":"brain.timer.event(callback, 1000)"},"events_bumper_pressed":{"name":"events_bumper_pressed","markdown":"# Painokytkintä painettu\n\nSuorittaa halutun funktion kun painokytkintä painettu.\n\n```python\nbumper.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuo funktio, jota kutsutaan, kun painokytkintä on painettu. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi ja toiminnot. Nimi välitetään callback - parametrina kun painokytkintä on painettu.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_bumper_pressed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Bumper pressed!\")\n \n# Register event with a callback function\nbumper_a.pressed(run_on_bumper_pressed)\n```","signature":"bumper.pressed(callback)"},"events_bumper_released":{"name":"events_bumper_released","markdown":"## Painokytkin vapautettu\n\nSuorittaa halutun funktion kun painokytkin vapautetaan\n\n```python\nbumper.released(callback)\n```\n\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuo funktio, jota kutsutaan, kun painokytkin on vapautettu. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi ja toiminnot. Nimi välitetään callback - parametrina kun painokytkin on vapautettu.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_bumper_released():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Bumper released!\")\n \n# Register event with a callback function\nbumper_a.released(run_on_bumper_released)\n```","signature":"bumper.released(callback)"},"events_competition_autonomous":{"name":"events_competition_autonomous","markdown":"# Kilpailu automaattikäynnistys\n\nSuorittaa halutun funktion kun \"automaatti\" moodi signaali on kilpailuajon alussa saatu.\n\n```python\ndef autonomous():\n    pass\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nUusi kilpailu esiintymä voidaan luoda kun  **driver_control** ja **automaatti** callback functiot on saatu.\n\nLuo **automaatti** funktio, joka toimii kilpailutilanteessa. \n\nTämä **automaatti** funktio suoritetaan kun \"automaatti\" moodi signaali on kilpailussa saatu.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the \"driver control\" signal is received\ndef driver_control():\n    brain.screen.print(\"driver control signal received\")\n\n# Function to run when the \"autonomous\" signal is received\ndef autonomous():\n    brain.screen.print(\"autonomous signal received\")\n\n# Create a new Competition instance\ncompetition = Competition(driver_control, autonomous)\n```","signature":"def autonomous():\\n\\tpass"},"events_competition_drivercontrol":{"name":"events_competition_drivercontrol","markdown":"# Kilpailu ohjainkäynnistys\n\nSuorittaa halutun funktion kun \"ohjainajo\" moodi signaali on kilpailuajon alussa saatu.\n\n```python\ndef driver_control():\n    pass\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nUusi kilpailu esiintymä voidaan luoda kun  **ohjainajo** ja **automaatti** callback funktiot on saatu.\n\nLuo **ohjainkäynnistys** funktio, joka toimii kilpailutilanteessa. \n\n```python\n# Function to run when the \"driver control\" signal is received\ndef driver_control():\n    brain.screen.print(\"driver control signal received\")\n\n# Function to run when the \"autonomous\" signal is received\ndef autonomous():\n    brain.screen.print(\"autonomous signal received\")\n\n# Create a new Competition instance\ncompetition = Competition(driver_control, autonomous)\n```","signature":"def driver_control():\\n\\tpass"},"events_competition_new_competition":{"name":"events_competition_new_competition","markdown":"# Uusi kilpailu\n\nLuo uusi kilapilu ilmentymä (ohjelma).\n\n```python\ncompetition = Competition(driver_control, autonomous)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nuusi kilpailu ilmentymä ottamalla ohjelmaan mukaan **driver_control** ja **autonomous** callback -funktiot.\n\nKun **driver control** signaali kilpailukytkimestä saadaan, niin suoritetaan **driver_control** callback funktio.\n\nVastaavasti, kun **autonomous** signaali kilpailukytkimestä saadaan, niin suoritetaan **autonomous** callback funktio.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the \"driver control\" signal is received\ndef driver_control():\n    brain.screen.print(\"driver control signal received\")\n\n# Function to run when the \"autonomous\" signal is received\ndef autonomous():\n    brain.screen.print(\"autonomous signal received\")\n\n# Create a new Competition instance\ncompetition = Competition(driver_control, autonomous)\n```","signature":"competition = Competition(driver_control, autonomous)"},"events_controller_axis_changed":{"name":"events_controller_axis_changed","markdown":"# Ohjaimen tatin asentoa muutettu\n\nSuorittaa määrätyn funktion, kun ohjaimen tatin asentoa muutettu.\n\n```python\ncontroller.axis.changed(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse ohjaimen tatti, jota käsitellään.\n\n* `axis1`\n* `axis2`\n* `axis3`\n* `axis4`\n\nLuo funktio ohjaimen tatille , joka käsittelee tatin käyttöä. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi, jota käytetään `callback` parametrissa, kun tatin asentoa on muutettu kutsuttaessa itse funktiota.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_axis_changed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Axis changed!\")\n\n  \n# Register event with a callback function.\ncontroller_1.axis1.changed(run_on_axis_changed)\n```","signature":"controller.axis.changed(callback)"},"events_controller_button_pressed":{"name":"events_controller_button_pressed","markdown":"# Ohjaimen nappia painettu\n\nSuorittaa tietyn funktion kun Ohjaimen tiettyä nappia on painettu.\n\n```python\ncontroller.button.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse ohjaimen nappi (kts ohjaimesta merkinnät napeille).\n\n* `buttonA`\n* `buttonB`\n* `buttonX`\n* `buttonY`\n* `buttonUp`\n* `buttonDown`\n* `buttonLeft`\n* `buttonRight`\n* `buttonL1`\n* `buttonL2`\n* `buttonR1`\n* `buttonR2`\n\nYLuo funktio , jota kutsutaan kun ohjaimen ko. nappia on painetttu. \n\nAnna fuktiolle nimi, joka välitetään callback` paramettrissa, kun funktion toiminta suoritetaan nappia painettaessa.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_button_pressed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Button pressed!\")\n\n# Register event with a callback function.\ncontroller_1.buttonA.pressed(run_on_button_pressed)\n```","signature":"controller.button.pressed(callback)"},"events_controller_button_released":{"name":"events_controller_button_released","markdown":"# Ohjaimen nappi vapautettu\n\nSuorittaa haluton funktion komennot kun ohjaimen nappi vapautetaan.\n\n```python\ncontroller.button.released(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse ohjaimen nappi, jota käytät.\n\n* `buttonA`\n* `buttonB`\n* `buttonX`\n* `buttonY`\n* `buttonUp`\n* `buttonDown`\n* `buttonLeft`\n* `buttonRight`\n* `buttonL1`\n* `buttonL2`\n* `buttonR1`\n* `buttonR2`\n\nLuo funktio jota kutsutaan kun Ohjaimen ko nappi vapautetaan. \n\nNimeä funktio joka suoritetaan kun nappi vapautetaan ja laita se  ns `callback` funktion parametriksi.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_button_released():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Button released!\")\n\n# Register event with a callback function.\ncontroller_1.buttonA.released(run_on_button_released)\n```","signature":"controller.button.released(callback)"},"events_event":{"name":"events_event","markdown":"# Tapahtuma rekistöröi callback funtion\n\nRekistöröi callback -function käynnistyksen kun käyttäjätapahtuma on annettu.\n\n```python\nevent(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nRekisteröi callback -funktio nimettyyn käyttäjätapahtumaan.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"my_event triggered run_on_broadcast callback\")\n  \n# Create a new event.\nmy_event = Event()\n\n# Register a callback function to the myEvent event.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the event.\nmy_event.broadcast()\n```","signature":"EVENT(callback);"},"events_event_broadcast":{"name":"events_event_broadcast","markdown":"# Tapahtuman lähetys\n\nLähettää tapahtumaviestin käynnistää vastaavan tapahtumafunktion.\n\n```python\nevent.broadcast()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOhjelma jatkaa suoritusta samaan aikaan kun `event.broadcast()` komentoa suoritetaan kutsutun callback-funtion osalta.\n\nEnnen kutsun käyttöä pitää tapahtuma olla määritelty ja rekistöröidä vastaava vähintää yksi callback-funtio.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast1():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\")\n\ndef run_on_broadcast2():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(2, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\")\n  \n# Create a new event.\nmy_event = Event()\n\n# Register callback functions to event.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast1)\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast2)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the event.\nmy_event.broadcast()\n\n```","signature":"my_event.broadcast()"},"events_event_broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Tapahtuman lähetys ja odota\n\nLähettää tapahtumaviestin käynnistää vastaavan tapahtumafunktion ja odottaa kunnes funktion toimenpiteet tehty.\n\n```cpp\nevent.broadcast_and_wait()\n```\n\nMiten käytetään\n\n`event.broadcast_and_wait()` Ohjelma odottaa kun `event.broadcast()` komentoa suoritetaan kutsutun callback-funtion osalta. \n\nEnnen kutsun käyttöä pitää tapahtuma olla määritelty ja rekistöröidä vastaava vähintää yksi callback-funtio.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast1():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\")\n\ndef run_on_broadcast2():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(2, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\")\n\n# Create a new event.\nmy_event = Event()\n\n# Register callback functions to event.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast1)\nmy_event(run_on_broadcast2)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the event and wait for completion.\nmy_event.broadcast_and_wait()\n\nbrain.screen.set_cursor(3, 1)\nbrain.screen.print(\"Listeners finished running\")\n```","signature":"my_event.broadcast_and_wait()"},"events_event_new_event":{"name":"events_event_new_event","markdown":"# Uusi tapahtuma\n\nLuo uusi tapahtuma.\n\n```python\nmy_event = Event()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKäyttämällä allaolevaa syntaksia uusi käyttäjätapahtuma luodaan ennenkuin se toteuttava callback functio luodaan.\n\n```python\ndef run_on_broadcast1():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\")\n\ndef run_on_broadcast2():\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(2, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\")\n\n# Create new events.\nmy_event1 = Event()\nmy_event2 = Event()\n\n# Register callback functions to the events.\n# Wait to allow events to register\nmy_event1(run_on_broadcast1)\nmy_event2(run_on_broadcast2)\nwait(15, MSEC)\n\n# Broadcast the events.\nmy_event1.broadcast()\nmy_event2.broadcast()\n```","signature":"my_event = Event()"},"events_limit_pressed":{"name":"events_limit_pressed","markdown":"# Limit Switch painettu\n\nSuoritetaan määritelty funktio kun Limit Switch painettu.\n\n```python\nlimit.pressed(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nSensorin painallusta varten pitää määritellä funktio , jota kutsutaan painalluksen jälkeen. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi ja määrittele sen toiminta, kun tapahtuma Limit Switch painettu . Kyseessä on ns `callback` parametri tapahtumalle.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_limit_pressed():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Limit pressed!\")\n \n# Register event with a callback function\nlimit_a.pressed(run_on_limit_pressed)\n```","signature":"limit.pressed(callback)"},"events_limit_released":{"name":"events_limit_released","markdown":"# Limit Switch vapautettu\n\nSuoritetaan määritelty funktio kun Limit Switch vapautettu.\n```python\nlimit.released(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nSensorin painallusta varten pitää määritellä funktio , jota kutsutaan vapautuksen jälkeen. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi ja määrittele sen toiminta, kun tapahtuma Limit Switch vapautettu . Kyseessä on ns `callback` parametri tapahtumalle.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_limit_released():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Limit released!\")\n \n# Register event with a callback function\nlimit_a.released(run_on_limit_released)\n`","signature":"limit.released(callback)"},"events_optical_object_detected":{"name":"events_optical_object_detected","markdown":"# Optical löytää esineen\n\nSuorittaa callback funktion kun V5 Optical Sensori havaitsee esineen/kohteen.\n\n```python\noptical.object_detected(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`optical.object_detected` komentoa voi käyttää triggeröimään haluttuja toimintoja kun V5 Optical Sensori havaitsee kohteen/esineen.\n\nSinun pitää luoda funktio, joka suoritetaan kun esine havaitaan. Anna funktiolle nimi , joka annetaan **callback** parametrissa ja suoritetaan kun esine havaitaan.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_object_detected():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Object detected!\")\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.object_detected(run_on_object_detected)\n```","signature":"optical.object_detected(callback)"},"events_optical_object_lost":{"name":"events_optical_object_lost","markdown":"# Optical kohde hävisi\n\nAjetaan callback funktio, kun V5 Optical Sensori kadottaa äskeisen esineen.\n\n```python\noptical.object_lost(callback)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`optical.object_lost` komento käynnistää halutut toimenpiteet, kun V5 Optical sensori ei enää havaitse kohdetta/esinettä.\n\nLuo funktio, jota kutsutaan kun esinettä ei enää havaita. Anna funktiolle nimi , joka kutsutaan, kun tapahtuma ilmenee **callback** parametrissa.\n\n```python\n# Function to run when the event occurs\ndef run_on_object_lost():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Object lost!\")\n\n# Register an event with a callback function\noptical.object_lost(run_on_object_lost)\n```","signature":"optical.object_lost(callback)"},"function_name":{"name":"function_name","markdown":"# Funktiot\n\nFunktiot on joukko komentoja/koodinippuja , jotka suorittavat jonkin määrätyn tehtävän.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun luot funktion, anna sille kuvaava nimi, joka kuvaa sen toimintaa.\n\nKäytä **keyword** (avainsana) `def` ennen funktion nimeä, kun määrittelet funktion.\n\nSisällytä parametrit funktion nimen jälkeen sulkuihin `()` ja loppuun kaksoispiste `:`.Jos parametreja on useampi, niin laita ne pilkulla erottaen sulkujen sisään `(parameter1, parameter2)`.\n\nFunktion runkoon komennot sisennetään 4 tyhjällä merkillä. Jos komentoja ei o0le, lisää kuitenkin sana `pass` komentoriville.\n\n```don\ndef my_function():\n    pass\n```\n\n## Esimerkki 1\n\nTällä funktiolla ei ole parametreja ja se tulostaa sanan \"Hello\" V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```don\ndef print_hello_world():\n    brain.screen.print(\"Hello World\")\n```\n## Esimerkki 2\n\nTässä funktiossa on 1 paremetri `name` se tulostaa `name` muuttujan nimen V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```don\ndef print_name(name):\n    brain.screen.print(name)\n```","signature":"def function_name(parameters):\\n\\tpass"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Tyhjää rivi\n\nTyhjää yksittäisen rivin V5 aivojen tai ohjaimen näytöllä.\n\n```don \nbrain.screen.clear_row()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTyhää nykyisen kursoririvin.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.clear_row()\n```\n\nTyhjää tietyn rivin näytöllä.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.clear_row(ROW)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`brain.screen.clear_row()` komento hyväksyy arvot välillä **1 - 20**, jonka rivin tyhjää. Ilman rivinumero komento tyhjää nykyisen rivin.\n\n---\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.clear_line()"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Tyhjää näyttö\n \nTyhjää V5 Aivojen näytön.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`brain.screen.clear_screen()` komennossa kursorin paikka ei muutu. Jos haluat muuttaa sitä, käytä `brain.screen.set_cursor()` komentoa.","signature":"brain.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle","markdown":"# Piirrä ympyrä\n\nPiirtää ympyrän V5 näytölle.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_circle(X, Y, RADIUS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `brain.screen.draw_circle()` vaatii kolme arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: Keskipiste X\n* Arvo 2: Keskipiste Y\n* Arvo 3: Ympyrän säde (pikseleinä)\n\nKomento `brain.screen.set_pen_color()` määrittää kehän värin, oletuksena on valkoinen.\n\nKomento `brain.screen.set_fill_color()` määrittää täyttövärin, oletuksena on musta.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_brain_screen_draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_circle(1, 1, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_line","markdown":"# Piirrä viiva\n\nPiirtää viivan V5 aivojen näytölle.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_line(START_X, START_Y, END_X, END_Y)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`brain.screen.draw_line()` komeNto vaatii 4 arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: Alkupiste X koordinaatti\n* Arvo 2: Alkupiste Y koordinaatti\n* Arvo 3: Loppupiste X koordinaatti\n* Arvo 4: Loppupiste Y koordinaatti\n\nViivan väri määrätään komennolla `brain.screen.set_pen_color()`. Oletuksena on valkoinen viiva.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_brain_screen_draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_line(1, 1, 10, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel","markdown":"# Piirrä Pikseli (väripiste)\n\nPiirtää pikselin V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_pixel(X, Y)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `brain.screen.draw_pixel` vaatii 2 arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: X koorditaatti\n* Arvo 2: Y koorditaatti\n\npikselin väri asetetaan komennolla `brain.screen.set_pen_color()`. Oletusväri on valkoinen.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_pixel(1, 1)"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Piirrä suorakulmio\n\nPiirtää suorakulmion V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.draw_rectangle(X, Y, WIDTH, HEIGHT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `brain.screen.draw_rectangle()` vaatii 4 arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: Ylä vasen nurkka X koordinaatti\n* Arvo 2: Ylä vasen nurkka Y koordinaatti\n* Arvo 3: Leveys kulmiolle\n* Arvoe 4: Korkaus kulmiolle\n\nKomento `brain.screen.set_pen_color()` määrää reunaviivan värin. Oletus on valkoinen.\n\nTäyttöväri saadaan komennolla `brain.screen.set_fill_color()`. Oletus on musta täyttöväri.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.draw_rectangle(1, 1, 10, 10)"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Next Row\n\nSets the print output cursor on the V5 Brain's screen to the next available row.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.next_row()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1. The `brain.screen.next_row()` command will move the cursor down by a single row on the screen. `brain.screen.next_row()` will also set the cursor's column to position 1.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 Rows (Default)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Rows\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Rows\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_brain_screen_new_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.new_line()"},"looks_brain_screen_print":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print","markdown":"# Tulosta\n\nTulostaa arvoja tai tekstiä V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `brain.screen.print()` tulostaa dataa kursorin kohdalle näyttöä.\n\nKaikkien ohjelmien alussa paikka on rivi 1 sarake 1.\n\n* Tulostaa sanoja ja numeroita:* \n`brain.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n\n* Tulostaa muuttujan arvon: \n`brain.screen.print(my_variable)`\n\n* Tulostaa sensorin tai laitteen arvon:  \n`brain.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`","signature":"brain.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")"},"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Aseta kursorin paikka\n\n\nAsettaa kursorin V5 Aivojen näytöllä.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_cursor(ROW, COLUMN)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `brain.screen.set_cursor()` vaatii kaksi arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: Näytön rivinumero \n* Arvo 2: Näytön sarakenumero \n\n`brain.screen.print()` komennolla kursori haluttuun kohtaan näyttöä.\n\nRivin  **row** voi valita väliltä **1 - 20**.\n\nSarakkeen **column** voi valita väliltä **1 - 80**.\n\n---\n\nV5 Aivoille tulstettaessa voit valita kirjaisnlajin ja koon. Valinnat vaikuttavat, kuinka monta riviä ja saraketta näytölle mahtuu seuraavasti:\n\n**V5 Aivojen fontin koko - Rivien määrä:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 riviä\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 riviä\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12 riviä (Oletus)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 riviä\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 riviä\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 riviä\n\n**V5 Aivojen fontin koko - Sarakkeiden määrä:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 80 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 68 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 48 saraketta (Oletus)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 32 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 24 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.MONO60` - 16 saraketta\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color","markdown":"# Täyttöväri\n\nAsettaa muotojen täyttövärin V5 Aivojen näytöllä.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_fill_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `brain.screen.set_fill_color()` määrittää täyttövärin näytön ympyröiden ja nelikulmaisten suljettujen esineiden siällä. \n\nLisää `COLOR` paramettri seuraavista:\n\n* `Color.BLACK`\n* `Color.WHITE`\n* `Color.RED`\n* `Color.GREEN`\n* `Color.BLUE`\n* `Color.YELLOW`\n* `Color.ORANGE`\n* `Color.PURPLE`\n* `Color.CYAN`\n* `Color.TRANSPARENT` (läpinäkyvä)\n\nVäri säilyy valintana kunnes uusi värivalinta on tehty.","signature":"brain.screen.set_fill_color(Color.RED)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_font":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_font","markdown":"# Aseta fontti/kirjasinlaji\n\nAsettaa kirjasimen koon ja tyylin V5 Aivojen näytölle tulostettaessa.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_font(FONT_TYPE)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKäytössä on kaksi eri kirjasinlajia:\n\n* Monospaced (MONO) - kirjaimet ovat saman levyisiä.\n* Proportional (PROP) - jokainen kirjaimella oma leveys.\n\nValitse kirjasinlaji ja koko , jota käytät `FONT_TYPE` parametrina:\n\n* `FontType.MONO12`\n* `FontType.MONO15`\n* `FontType.MONO20`\n* `FontType.MONO30`\n* `FontType.MONO40`\n* `FontType.MONO60`\n* `FontType.PROP20`\n* `FontType.PROP30`\n* `FontType.PROP40`\n* `FontType.PROP60`\n\nFontti säilyy käytössä kunnes vaihdat sen uuteen tulostettaessa.","signature":"brain.screen.set_font(FontType.MONO20)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color","markdown":"# Aseta kynän väri\n\nAsettaa kynän värin V5 Aivojen näytölle piirrettäessä.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_pen_color(COLOR)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomentoa `brain.screen.set_pen_color()` käytetään, kun kynän väri valitaa piirrettäessä viivoja, pixeleitä tai tekstiä V5 näytölle. \n\n`brain.screen.set_pen_color()` sopii myös neliöiden ja monikolmioiden ääriviivojen piirtoon.\n\nValise joku seuraavista väreistä:\n\n* `Color.BLACK`\n* `Color.WHITE`\n* `Color.RED`\n* `Color.GREEN`\n* `Color.BLUE`\n* `Color.YELLOW`\n* `Color.ORANGE`\n* `Color.PURPLE`\n* `Color.CYAN`\n\nKynäväri säilyy kunnes otat käyttöön uuden värin.","signature":"brain.screen.set_pen_color(Color.RED)"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width","markdown":"# Aseta viivan leveys\n\nAsettaa piirrosviivan leveyden näytöllä.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.set_pen_width(PEN_WIDTH)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `brain.screen.set_pen_width()` asettaa viivan leveyden ympyröissä ja nelikulmioissa. \n\nKomento `brain.screen.set_pen_width()` hyväksyy kokonaislukuja , isompi luku niin paksumpi viiva. Korvaa `PEN_WIDTH` parametetri kokonaisluvulla.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"brain.screen.set_pen_width(10)"},"looks_console_clear_console":{"name":"looks_console_clear_console","markdown":"# Tyhjää konsoli\n\nTyhjää Tulostus konsolin.\n\n```python\nprint(\"\\033[2J\")\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`print` komentoa käytetään `\\033[2J` komentojonolla ja se tyhjää konsolin.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkisdsä tulostetaan sana \"VEXcode\" ja konsoli tyhjätään 3 sekunnin kuluttua.\n\n```python\nprint(\"\\033[31mVEXcode\")\n\nwait(2, SECONDS)\n\nprint(\"\\033[2J\")\n```","signature":"print(\"\\033[2J\")"},"looks_console_print":{"name":"looks_console_print","markdown":"# Konsoli tulostus\n\nTulostaa arvoja tai tekstiä tulostuskonsolille.\n\n```python\nprint(\"VEXcode\")\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`print` komento tulostaa dataa kursorikohtaan tulostuskonsolia.\n\nKaikki ohjelmat aloittavat aina kursorin rivin 1 kursorikohdasta.\n\n## Rivitulostus\n\nOletuksen Python lisää aina uuden rivin `print` komennon jälkeen.\n\nJos haluat tulostaa useamman arvon riville käytä `end` parametria.\n\n```python\nprint(\"This text will be \", end=\"\")\nprint(\"printed on the same line\")\n```\n\n## Arvojen tulostus\n\nVoit käyttää Pythonissä `format` metodia muokataksesi tulostustmuotoa print komennossa.\n\nKäytäessäsi `format` metodia, sinun pitää luoda peite/template tekstijono ja yhdistää osat aaltosuluilla - `{}`.\n\nKutsu `format` metodi template/muotoilu tekstijonossa. Jokainen parametri välitetään `format` method will be inserted into the replacement fields in sequence (if there are multiple replacement fields).\n\nVoit lisätä muotoiluoptioita peite/template tekstijonoon asettamaan desimaalien lukumäärän. Jokainen formaaatttioptio alkaa aina kaksoispisteellä - `:`.\n\nEsimerkissä Aivojen kello sijoitetaan yhteen korvaavaan kenttään template tekstijonossa ja se tulostetaan kahden desimaalin tarkkuudella.\n\n```python\nprint(\"{:.2f}\".format(brain.timer.time(SECONDS)))\n```\n\nVastaavasti esimerkissä alla tulostetaan kursorin rivi/sarake arvo Aivoje näytölle. Korvauskenttien lukumäärä (suluissa `{}`) täytyy vastat parametrien määrää , jotka välitetään `format` metoodiin.\n\n```python\n# The value of brain.screen.row() will be passed into the first replacement field\n# The value of brain.screen.column() will be passed into the second replacement field\nprint(\"Row: {:d}, Column: {:d}\".format(brain.screen.row(), brain.screen.column()))\n```\n\nTässä tyypilliset formaattitarkennuksia. Muitsa käyttää format tarkennuksia korvausmerkin sisällä (aaltosulkunen sisällä `{}`), ja seuraava merkki puolipiste- `:`.\n\n* `d` - Desimaali / Kokonaisluku\n* `f` - Liukuluku\n* `o` - Oktaali kokonaisluku\n* `s` - Tekstijono\n\nKäyttämällä liukulukuformaattia `f`, voit määrittää desimaalien määrän.\n\n* `.2f` - liukuluku 2 desimaalin tarkkuudella\n* `.4f` - liukuluku 4 desimaalin tarkkuudella\n\n## Tulostusvärit\n\nVoit määrittää tulostusvärin tulostuskomennossa `print` .\n\nAlla on kaksi eri tapaa määrittää tulostusväri. Kaikki värikoodit annetaan escape jonolla - `\\033`.\n\n* `[31m` - Red (punainen)\n* `[32m` - Green (vihreä)\n* `[34m` - Blue (sininen)\n* `[30m` - Black (musta)\n* `[37m` - White (valkoinen)\n* `[33m` - Yellow (keltainen)\n* `[91m` - Orange (oranssi)\n* `[35m` - Purple (purppura)\n* `[36m` - Cyan (syaani)\n* `[97m` - Transparent (läpinäkyvä)\n\n```python\n# Using color codes in-line\n# This will print \"VEXcode\" in Red to the Print Console\nprint(\"\\033[31mVEXcode\")\n\n# Using color codes in separate commands\n# Sets the print color for any subsequent prints\nprint(\"\\033[31m\")\nprint(\"VEXcode\")\n```","signature":"print(\"VEXcode\")"},"looks_controller_rumble":{"name":"looks_controller_rumble","markdown":"# Ohjainvärinä\n\nLaittaa V5 ohjaimen värisemään.\n\n```python\ncontroller.rumble(\".-.-\")\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`controller.rumble(\".-.-\")` komento käyttää V5 ohjaimen värinämoottoria.\n\nVoit säätää värinää \".\" ja \"-\" merkeillä. Merkki \".\" luo lyhyen ja merkki \"-\" pitkän värinän.","signature":"controller.rumble(\"-.-.\")"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Tyhjää rivi\n\nTyhjää nykyisen rivin V5 ohjaimen näytöllä.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_row()\n```\n\nTyhjää tietyn rivin ohjaimella.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_row(ROW)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n'controller.screen.clear_row()` komennossa hyväksytään rivinumerot **1 - 3** rivin tyhjäyksessä. Ilman numeroa tyhjätään nykyinen rivi.\n\n---\n\nV5 Ohjaimen näytön fonttia ei voi muuttaa.\n\n**V5 Ohjaimen fonttikoko - Rivimäärä:**\n\n* Standardi Fontti - 3 riviä (oletus)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_controller_screen_clear_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.clear_line()"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Tyhjää ohjaimen näytön rivit\n\nTyhjää ohjaimen näytön.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.clear_screen()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`controller.screen.clear_screen()` ei muuta kursoripaikkaa näytöllä. \n\nHalutessai käytä `controller.screen.set_cursor()` kometoa asettamaan kursorin haluttuun paikkaan.","signature":"controller.screen.clear_screen()"},"looks_controller_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Seuraava rivi\n\nSiirtää V5 ohjaimen näytöllä kursorin seuraavalle riville.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.next_row()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOletuksena kursori on aina ohjelman alussa sivillä1 sarakkeessa 1. Komento `controller.screen.next_row()` siirtää kutsoria yhden rivi alas näytöllä sarakkeeseen 1.\n\n---\n\nV5 Ohjain ei salli muuttaa tulostuksen kirjasinta.\n\n**V5 Ohjain Fontti Koko - Rivien määrä:**\n\n* Standard Fontti - 3 riviä (Oletus)\n\n**V5 Ohjain Fontti Koko - Sarakkeiden määrä:**\n\n* Standard Fontti - 20 saraketta (Oletus)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_controller_screen_new_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.new_line()"},"looks_controller_screen_print":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_print","markdown":"# Print  \n\nPrints values on the V5 Controller's screen.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.print(\"VEXcode\") \n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `controller.screen.print()` command will print data at a cursor location on the screen.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1.\n\n* Print words and numbers: \n`controller.screen.print(\"Number:\", 10)`\n\n* Print the reported value from a variable:  \n`controller.screen.print(my_variable)`\n\n* Print the reported value from a sensor or device: \n`controller.screen.print(drivetrain.is_done())`","signature":"controller.screen.print(\"VEXcode\")"},"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Aseta kursoripaikka\n\n\nAsettaa kursorin paikan ohjaimen näytöllä.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.set_cursor(ROW, COLUMN)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `controller.screen.set_cursor()` vaatii 2 arvoa:\n\n* Value 1: Näytön rivi \n* Value 2: Näytön sarake\n\nAsettamalla kursori sopiva rivi ja sarake saat tulostettua komennolla `controller.screen.print()` haluttuun kohtaan näyttöä.\n\n`controller.screen.set_cursor()` hyväksyy rivin **row** välillä **1 - 3**.\n\n`controller.screen.set_cursor()` hyväksyy sarakkeen **column** välillä **1 - 20**.\n\n---\n\nV5 Ohjainnäytölle ei voi muuttaa fontin kokoa.\n\n**V5 Ohjain Fontin koko - Rivien määrä:**\n\n* Standard Fontti - 3 riviä (Oletus)\n\n**V5 Ohjain Fontin koko - Sarakkeiden määrä**\n\n* Standard Fontti - 20 Saraketta (Oletus)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/python/fi/looks_controller_screen_set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"controller.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)"},"looks_led_off":{"name":"looks_led_off","markdown":"# LED pois\n\nSammuttaa 3-lanka LED pois päältä.\n\n```python\nled.off()\n```","signature":"led.off()"},"looks_led_on":{"name":"looks_led_on","markdown":"# LED Päälle\n\nLaittaa 3-lanka LED päälle.\n\n```python\nled.on()\n```","signature":"led.on()"},"looks_led_set":{"name":"looks_led_set","markdown":"# LED Päällä/Pois päältä\n\nLaittaa LED päälle ja pois päältä.\n\n```don\nled.on()\n```\n```don\nled.off()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetääm\n\n`led.on()` laittaa LED lampun päälle.\n\n`led.off()` laittaa LED lampun pois päältä.","signature":"led.set(False)"},"magnet_drop":{"name":"magnet_drop","markdown":"# Sähkömagneetti pudottaa\n\nAntaa sähömagneetille käskyn pudottaa siinä oleva esine.\n\n```\nmagnet.drop()\n```\nKun komento `magnet.drop()` on suoritettu, pitää magneetin jäähtyä ennen uutta käyttöä.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nPoimitaan esine , ajetaan robottia eteenpäin ja käytetään `magnet.drop()` komentoa esineen pudotukseen.\n\n```\nmagnet.pickup()\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\nmagnet.drop()\n```","signature":"magnet.drop()"},"magnet_pickup":{"name":"magnet_pickup","markdown":"# Sähkömagneetin avulla poiminta\n\nAntaa käskyn V5 sähkömagneetille poimia esine.\n\n```\nmagnet.pickup()\n```\nKomennon `magnet.pickup()` jälkeen pitää magneetin jäähtyä ennen seuraavaa magneettikomentoa.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä `magnet.pickup()` poimii esineen , ajopeli aja eteenpäin ja pudottaa esineen.\n\n```\nmagnet.pickup()\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\nmagnet.drop()\n```","signature":"magnet.pickup()"},"magnet_set_power":{"name":"magnet_set_power","markdown":"# Aseta sähkömagneetin voima\n\nMuuttaa sähkömagneetin tarttumiskykyvoimaa\n\n```\nmagnet.set_power(50)\n```\nVoimaa voi säätää välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä `magnet.set_power()` komennolla asetetaan täsyi 100 % teho, pomitaan esine , ajetaan eteenpäin ja pudotetaan esine.\n\n```\nmagnet.set_power(100)\nmagnet.pickup()\ndrivetrain.drive_for(FORWARD, 200, MM)\nmagnet.drop()\n```","signature":"magnet.set_power(50)"},"motion_motor393_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor393_set_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta Moottori Controller Nopeus\n\nAsettaa Motor393 nopeuden yhdistettynä moottori Controller 29.\n\n```python\nmotor393.set_velocity(VELOCITY, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`VELOCITY` parametriin voi asettaa arvot välillä -100% - 100%.\n\nAsettamalla negatiivisen arvon moottori pyörii taaksepäin.\n\nAlla olevassa esimerkissä moottori pyörii taaksepäin vaikka `FORWARD` parametri on käytössä.\n\n```python\nmotor393.set_velocity(-100, PERCENT)\nmotor393.spin(FORWARD)\n```\n\nJos asettaa Motor393nopeuden arvoon 0 moottori pysähtyy.","signature":"motor393.set_velocity(10, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor393_spin":{"name":"motion_motor393_spin","markdown":"# Pyöritä moottoria Controller\n\nPyörittää Motor393 yhdistettynä Moottori Controller 29.\n\n```python\nmotor393.spin(DIRECTION)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento pyörittää Motor393 ikuisesti kunnes uusi komento annetaan tai ohjelma loppuu.\n\nValise suunta asettamalla `DIRECTION` parametrin arvoksi joko **FORWARD** (eteenpäin) tai **REVERSE**.","signature":"motor393.spin(FORWARD)"},"motion_motor393_stop":{"name":"motion_motor393_stop","markdown":"# Pysäytä Servo Ohjaus\n\nPysäyttää moottorin Motor393 , jota hallitsee Moottori Controller 29.\n\n```python\nmotor393.stop()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nEsimerkissä Motor393 pysäytetään, kun ensin pyörinyt 3 s.\n\n```python\nmotor393.spin(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\nmotor393.stop()\n```","signature":"motor393.stop()"},"motion_motor_set_max_torque":{"name":"motion_motor_set_max_torque","markdown":"# Aseta maksimi moottorin vääntö\n\nAsettaa V5 älymoottorin masimi väännön.\n\n```don\nmotor.set_max_torque(AMOUNT, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento sallii arvot välillä 0% - 100%.\n\nMaksimi moottorin vääntö -komento sallii desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeerisia arvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä kouramoottori liikkuu asentoon 40 astetta maksimi moottorin väännöllä 20 %, jolloin tarttuessa esineeseen moottori ei riko esinettä.\n\n```don\nclaw_motor.set_max_torque(20, PERCENT)\nclaw_motor.set_position(40, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_max_torque(50, PERCENT)"},"motion_motor_set_position":{"name":"motion_motor_set_position","markdown":"# Aseta moottorin asento\n\nAsettaa V5 Älymoottorin kierrosasennon (encoderin) asennon annettuun arvoon.\n\n```python\nmotor.set_position(VALUE, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento sallii positiivisia arvoja.\n\nTyypillisesti komennolla nollataan asento kesken ohjelmaa.\n\nKomento `motor.set_position` hyväksyy sekä **DEGREES** (asteita) tai **TURNS** (kierroksia) yksikköinä **UNITS**.","signature":"motor.set_position(0, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_set_stopping":{"name":"motion_motor_set_stopping","markdown":"# Moottorin pysähtymistapa\n\nAsettaa V5 moottorin pysähtymistavan.\n\n```don\nmotor.set_stopping(MODE)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`MODE` parametrissa voi asettaa jonkun seuraavista tavoista:\n\n* BRAKE: moottori pysähtyy heti.\n* COAST: moottori pysähtyy vaiheittain.\n* HOLD: moottori pysähtyy herti ja pitää paikan vaikka joku ulkoinen voima sitä yrittää siirtää esim painovoima.\n\nMoottorin pysähtymsistapa säilyy ohjelman läpi ellei uusi komento sitä muuta.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä moottori pyörii eteenpäin 90 astetta (käsi nousee) ja sen jälkeen mooorroti pysähtyy 'hold' asentoon.\n\n```don\narm_motor.set_stopping(HOLD)\narm_motor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_stopping(BRAKE)"},"motion_motor_set_timeout":{"name":"motion_motor_set_timeout","markdown":"# Aseta moottorille odotusaika\n\nAsettaa moottorille odotusajan seuraavalle liikkeelle.\n\n```don \nmotor.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAseta moottorille odotusaika antaa moottorille aika-rajan , jona aikana sen pitää suorittaa meneillään oleva komento loppuun. Tällä estetään ohjelman suorituksen loppuminen kesken, kun moottori ei saavuta tavoitetta. \n\nEsimerkinä aikarajan tarpeelle Käsi - tai Kouramoottorille on, että sen kääntymisen estää sen rakenteen mekaaniset rajat tai muu este.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä aikaraja komennolle `spin_to_position` on 2 sekuntia.\n\nJos moottori ei tavoita 270 asteen kääntymsitavoitetta 2 sekunin aikana, moottori pysäytetään.\n\n```don\nclaw_motor.set_timeout(2, SECONDS)\nclaw_motor.spin_to_position(270, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_timeout(TIME, SECONDS)"},"motion_motor_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity","markdown":"# Asettaa moottorin nopeuden\n\nAsettaa V5 Älymoottorille nopeusarvon pyörimiseen.\n\n```don \nmotor.set_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento hyväksyy arvot välillä **-100% to 100%** tai **-600rpm to 600rpm.**\n\nHyväksytyt `UNITS` parametrit ovat joko `PERCENT` (%) or `RPM`.\n\n**Set motor velocity** hyväksyy  \"rotations per minute\" (RPM) arvot riippuen käytetystä vaihdepakkauksesta V5 Älymoottorissa.\n\n* Red Cartridge: (punainen) -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: (Vihreä) -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: (Sininen) -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nJos nopeuden asettaa negatiivisen arvon, moottori pyörii taaksepäin (vastapäivään).\n\nMoottorin saa pysäyhtymään, kun asettaa sille nopeusarvon 0.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä moottorin nopeus asetaan arvoon 25% ja moottori pyörii asentoon 90 astetta.\n\n```don\narm_motor.set_velocity(25, PERCENT)\narm_motor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"motor.set_velocity(VELOCITY, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_spin":{"name":"motion_motor_spin","markdown":"# Pyörii ikuisesti \n\nKomento pyörittää V5 Älymoottoria ikuisesti kunnes uusi komento lopettaa pyörimisen.\n\n```don\nmotor.spin(FORWARD)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValise suunta, johon moottori pyörii, joko **FORWARD** (eteenpäin) tai **REVERSE** (taaksepäin).\n\n```don\nmotor.spin(REVERSE)\n```","signature":"motor.spin(FORWARD)"},"motion_motor_spin_for":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_for","markdown":"# Pyöri matka\n \nKomento pyörittää V5 älymoottoria tietyn matkan joko asteina tai kierroksina.\n\n```don\nmotor.spin_for(DIRECTION, AMOUNT, UNIT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse suunta `DIRECTION` , johon moottori pyörii: **FORWARD** (eteenpäin) tai **REVERSE** (taaksepäin).\n\nValitse mittayksikkö `UNIT` joko **DEGREES** (%) tai **TURNS** (kierroksia).\n\nValitse odottaako seurava kometo pyörimisen loppuun joko **wait=True** (odota) tai **wait=False** (jatka seuraavaan komentoon heti). \n\n```don\nmotor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\nOletuksena on aina odotus ellei parametria **wait=False** ole erikseen annettu.","signature":"motor.spin_for(FORWARD, 90, DEGREES)"},"motion_motor_spin_to_position":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_to_position","markdown":"# Pyöritä asentoon\n\nPyörittää V5 Älymoottorin kierrosmittarin tiettyyn asentoon.\n\n```python \nmotor.spin_to_position(POSITION, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento kiertää moottorin asennon haluttuun kohtaan. Perustuu nykyiseen asentoon `spin_to_position` komento kertoo mihin suuntaan pyöritään että asento saavutetaan.\n\nValitse mittayksiköksi joko **DEGREES** (astetta) tai **TURNS** (kierroksia).\n\nOptiona voit valita, odotetaanko komennon suoritus loppuun **wait=True** tai siirrytäänkö heti käännöksen aika seuraavaan komentoon  **wait=False**.\n\n```python\nmotor.spin_to_position(90, DEGREES, wait=False)\n```\n\nAsettamalla **wait=True** tarkoittaa ,että ensin odotetaan se että moottori saavuttaa asetetun kohdan. Vastaavasti **wait=False** ei odota moottoorin pyörimistä tavoitteeseen ennen seuraavaa komentoa.  \n\nOletuksena on arvo **True**.","signature":"motor.spin_to_position(POSITION, UNITS)"},"motion_motor_stop":{"name":"motion_motor_stop","markdown":"# Pysäytä moottori\n\nPysäyttää moottorin.\n\n```don\nmotor.stop()\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä moottori pyörii 3 sekuntia ennen pysähtymistä.\n\n```don\nmotor.spin(FORWARD)\nwait(3, SECONDS)\nmotor.stop()\n```","signature":"motor.stop()"},"motion_servo_set_position":{"name":"motion_servo_set_position","markdown":"# Pyöritä Servo -moottoria\n\nPyörittäa Servo -moottoria tiettyyn asentoon.\n\n```python\nservo.set_position(POSITION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`servo.set_position()` komento sallii arvot **-50** - **50** parametrin **POSITION** arvoksi.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nAlla moottori pyörii asentoon 25 astetta ja odottaa 2 s ja sitten asentoon -25 astetta.\n\n```python\nservo.set_position(25, DEGREES)\nwait(2, SECONDS)\nservo.set_position(-25, DEGREES)\n```","signature":"servo.set_position(50, DEGREES)"},"sensing_accel_two_g.acceleration":{"name":"sensing_accel_two_g.acceleration","markdown":"# Analoogisen kiihdytysmittarin kiihtyvyys\n\nAntaa kiihtyvyyden Analoogisen kiihdytysmittarilla yhdellä akselilla.\n\n```don\naccel_2g.acceleration()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento antaa arvoja välillä **-2.0 G - 2.0 G** tai **-6.0 G - 6.0 G** riippuen mittarin jumperin asennoista.","signature":"accel_2g.acceleration()"},"sensing_brain_battery_capacity":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_capacity","markdown":"# Akun lataustaso\n\n\nAntaa V5 Aivojen akun lataustason.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.capacity()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAkun lataustaso on välillä **0%** - **100%.**","signature":"brain.battery.capacity()"},"sensing_brain_battery_current":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_current","markdown":"# Akun virrankäyttö\n\nAntaa V5 akun virrankäytön.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAkun virta mitataan välillä **0.0 amps** - **20.0 amps**.","signature":"brain.battery.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_brain_battery_voltage":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_voltage","markdown":"# Akun jännite\n\nAntaa V5 Aivojen akun jännitetason.\n\n```don\nbrain.battery.voltage(VOLT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAkun jännite on välillä **10.0 voltia** - **14.4 voltia**.","signature":"brain.battery.voltage(VoltageUnits.VOLT)"},"sensing_brain_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_column","markdown":"# Näytön Kursorin sarake\n\nAntaa V5 Aivojen näytöllä kursorin paikan.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.column()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nNäytön sarake voi olla välillä **1 - 80**.\n\nV5 Aivojen näytöklle voi määritellä fontin kokoa ja samaal se vaikuttaa sarakkeiden määrään.\n\n**V5 Aivojen fonttikokoe - Sarakkeiden määrä:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 80 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 68 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 48 saraketta (Oletus)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 32 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 24 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.MONO60` - 16 saraketta","signature":"brain.screen.column()"},"sensing_brain_screen_pressing":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_pressing","markdown":"# Näyttöä koskettu\n \nAntaa tiedon jos V5 aivojen kosketusnäyttöä on koskettu.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`brain.screen.pressing` antaa arvon **True** jos V5 aivojen näyttöä on koskettu.\n\n`brain.screen.pressing` antaa arvon **false** jos V5 aivojen näyttöä ei ole koskettu.","signature":"brain.screen.pressing()"},"sensing_brain_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_row","markdown":"# Kursorin rivi aivojen näytöllä\n\nAntaa kursorin rivinumeron aivojen näytöllä.\n\n```don\nbrain.screen.row()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nNäytön rivien lukumäärä oletusfontilla on välillä **1 to 20**.\n\nVoit muuttaa fontin kokoa näytöllä ja samalla se vaikuttaa rivien määrään:\n\n**V5 Aivojen fonttikoko - Rivien määrä:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 20 Riviä\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 16 Riviä\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 12Riviä (Oletus)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 8 Riviä\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 6 Riviä\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.PROP60` - 4 Riviä","signature":"brain.screen.row()"},"sensing_brain_screen_x_position":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_x_position","markdown":"# Aivojen näytön x Arvo\n\nAntaa X-koordinaatin, johon viimeksi koskettu V5 Aivojen kosketusnäytössä.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.x_position()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`brain.screen.x_position()` kaappaa viimeisimmän näytön kosketuksen x -koordinaatin. \n\nYhdessä komennon  `brain.screen.y_position()` saa molemmat koordinaatit (x,y), jolloin interaktiivisuutta voi lisätä käyttäjän ja V5 aivojen välillä.\n\n`brain.screen.x_position()` palauttaa **integer** kokonaisluvun väliltä **0 - 480 pixeliä**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/python/fi/sensing_brain_screen_x_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n```python\nmy_x_coordinate = brain.screen.x_position()\n```","signature":"brain.screen.x_position()"},"sensing_brain_screen_y_position":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_y_position","markdown":"# # Aivojen näytön y Arvo\n\nAntaa Y-koordinaatin, johon viimeksi koskettu V5 Aivojen kosketusnäytössä.\n\n```python\nbrain.screen.y_position()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`brain.screen.y_position()` kaappaa viimeisimmän näytön kosketuksen x -koordinaatin. \n\nYhdessä komennon  `brain.screen.x_position()` saa molemmat koordinaatit (x,y), jolloin interaktiivisuutta voi lisätä käyttäjän ja V5 aivojen välillä.\n\n`brain.screen.y_position()` palauttaa **integer** kokonaisluvun väliltä **0 - 240 pixeliä**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/python/fi/sensing_brain_screen_y_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n```python\nmy_y_coordinate = brain.screen.y_position()\n```","signature":"brain.screen.y_position()"},"sensing_brain_timer_clear":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_clear","markdown":"# Nollaa kello\n\nNollaa V5 Aivojen kellon.\n\n```don \nbrain.timer.clear()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAivojen kello käynnistyy ohjelman suorituksen alussa. Nollaa kello -komentoa voi käytttää ohjelman aikana aloiottaamaan ajanlasku uudelleen arvosta 0 sekuntia.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nOhjelman alussa kello nollataan. Ajopeli liikkuu eteenpäin 3 sekunnin ajan ja pysähtyy.\n\n```don\nbrain.timer.clear()\nwhile not brain.timer.time(SECONDS) > 3:\n    drivetrain.drive(FORWARD)\ndrivetrain.stop()\n```","signature":"brain.timer.clear()"},"sensing_brain_timer_time":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_time","markdown":"# Kellon aika\n\nRaportoi V5 Aivojen kellon ajan halutussa yksikössä UNITS.\n\n```python\nbrain.timer.time(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKello käynnistyy ajasta 0 ohjelman alussa ja antaa ajan desimaalilukuna.\n\n`UNITS` parametrina voi käyttää joko **SECONDS** tai **MSEC** (millisekuntia).\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n    brain.screen.print(\"Timer in Seconds: \", brain.timer.time(SECONDS))\n\n    # A brief wait to print values without distortion or tearing\n    wait(20, MSEC)\n```","signature":"brain.timer.time(UNITS)"},"sensing_bumper_pressing":{"name":"sensing_bumper_pressing","markdown":"# Painokytkintä on painetttu\n \nAntaa tiedon, onko painokytkintä painettu.\n\n```don\nbumper.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nbumper.pressing() antaa arvon **True** (tosi), jos painokytkintä on painettu.\n\nbumper.pressing() antaa arvon **False** (epätosi), jos painokytkintä ei ole painettu.","signature":"bumper.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_axis_position":{"name":"sensing_controller_axis_position","markdown":"# Ohjaimen tatin asento\n \nAntaa V5 ohjaimen tatin asennon.\n\n```don\ncontroller.axis1.position()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`controller.axis1.position` antaa arvot välillä **-100 - 100**.\n\n`controller.axis1.position` antaa arvon nolla (0) ,kun se on keskellä.\n\nValitse tatti, jota käytät.\n\n* axis1 - oikea Joystick (vasen - oikea)\n* axis2 - oikean Joystick (ylös - alas)\n* axis3 - vasen Joystick (ylös - alas)\n* axis4 - vasen Joystick (vasen - oikea)","signature":"controller.axis1.position()"},"sensing_controller_button_up_pressing":{"name":"sensing_controller_button_up_pressing","markdown":"# Ohjaimen napin painallus\n\nAntaa tiedon jos ohjaimen tiettyä nappia on painettu.\n\n```don\ncontroller.buttonUp.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\ncontroller.buttonUp.pressing() antaa arvon **True** jos ko nappia on painettu.\n\ncontroller.buttonUp.pressing() antaa arvon **False** jos ko nappia ei ole painettu.\n\nValitse mitä nappia käsittelet:\n\n* `buttonUp`\n* `buttonDown`\n* `buttonLeft`\n* `buttonRight`\n* `buttonX`\n* `buttonY`\n* `buttonA`\n* `buttonB`\n* `buttonL1`\n* `buttonL2`\n* `buttonR1`\n* `buttonR2`","signature":"controller.buttonUp.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_column","markdown":"# Kursorin sarake\n \nAntaa ohjaimen näytöltä kursorin sarakenumeron.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.column()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKursorin sarakenumero on välillä **1 - 20**.\n\nV5 Ohjainen näytölle ei voi muuttaa fontin kokoa.\n\n**V5 Ohjain Fonttikoko - Sarakkeiden lukumäärä:**\n\n* Vakio Fontti - 20 saraketta (Oletus)","signature":"controller.screen.column()"},"sensing_controller_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_row","markdown":"# Kursorin rivi\n\nAntaa ohjaimen näytön kursorin rivin.\n\n```don\ncontroller.screen.row()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKusorin rivi voi olla välillä **1 - 3**.\n\nV5 ohjaimen näytöllä fonttia ei voi muuttaa.\n\n**V5 Ohjain Fontti Koko - Rivimäärä:**\n\n* Standardi Fontti - 3 Riviä (Oletus)","signature":"controller.screen.row()"},"sensing_distance_is_object_detected":{"name":"sensing_distance_is_object_detected","markdown":"# Distance Object Found\n\nReports if the Distance sensor sees an object within its field of view.\n\n```don\ndistance.is_object_detected()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Distance object found** reports True when the Distance sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n**Distance object found** reports False when the Distance sensor does not detect an object or surface.","signature":"distance.is_object_detected()"},"sensing_distance_object_distance":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Kohteen etäisyys\n\nRaportoi Etäisyysanturin havaitseman lähimmän kohteen etäisyyden.\n\n```don\ndistance.object_distance(MM)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Object distance** antaa rvot välillä **20mm - 2000mm**.\n\nAcceptable values for `UNIT` are: MM or INCHES.","signature":"distance.object_distance(MM)"},"sensing_distance_object_size":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_size","markdown":"# Kohteen koko\n\nANtaa kohteen koon, jonka etäisyysanturi havaitsee.  \n\n```\ndistance.object_size()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMäärittää havaitun esineen koon (ei löydy, pieni,keskivertyo,laaja) perustuen valon määrään, joka heijastuu takaisin anturiin.\n\n\nJos j´kode löytyy , kunktio palauttaa `ObjectSizeType.SMALL`, `ObjectSizeType.MEDIUM`, tai `ObjectSizeType.LARGE`.\n\nJos kohdetta ei löydy, funktio palauttaa 'ObjectSizeType.NONE`.","signature":"distance.object_size()"},"sensing_distance_object_velocity":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Kohteen nopeus\n\nAntaa kavaitun kohteen nopeuden yksikkönä m/s.\n\n```\ndistance.object_velocity()\n```\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Object velocity** raportoi kohteen nykyisen nopeuden m/s (metriä per sekunti).","signature":"distance.object_velocity()"},"sensing_drivetrain_current":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_current","markdown":"# Ajopelin sähkövirta\n\nAntaa sähkövirran määrän, jota ajopeli tällähetkellä kuluttaa.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.current` raportoi arvot välillä **0.0 to 2.5** amps.","signature":"drivetrain.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency","markdown":"# Ajopelin tehokkuus\n \nAntaa ajopelin tehokkuuden.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.efficiency(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAjopelin tehokkuuss on ajoplein moottorin (output) ulostulotehon suhde sisääntulotehoon (input).\n\nV5 Ajopeli saavuttaa tyypillisesti maksimissaan  **65%** tehokkuuden.\n\nTehokkuus mitataan välillä **0% - 100%**.","signature":"drivetrain.efficiency(PERCENT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_heading":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_heading","markdown":"# Ajopelin ajosuunta\n\nAntaa ajosuunnan jota ajopeli tällä hetkellä on suuntaa Gyroscoopin (Gyro) sensorin kulman avulla.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\ndrivetrain.heading(DEGREES) komento kasvaa , kun ajopeli kääntyy myötäpäivään.\n\nDAjopelin suunta on välillä **0.00 - 359.99 astetta**.","signature":"drivetrain.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_done":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_done","markdown":"# Ajopelin liike pysähtynyt\n\nAntaa tiedon, onko ajoplin liike pysähtynyt (liikesuoritettu loppuun).\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.is_done()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n'drivetrain.is_done()' antaa arvon **True** (tosi), kun ajopeli on suorittanut liikeen loppuun.\n\n'drivetrain.is_done()' antaa arvon **False** (epätosi), kun ajopeli vielä liikkuu.","signature":"drivetrain.is_done()"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving","markdown":"# Ajopeli liikkuu\n \nAntaa tiedon, liikkuuko ajopeli tällä hetkellä.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.is_moving()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n'drivetrain.is_moving' -komento antaa arvon **True** (tosi) kun se liikkuu.\n\n'drivetrain.is_moving' -komento antaa arvon **False** (epätosi) kun se ei liiku.","signature":"drivetrain.is_moving()"},"sensing_drivetrain_power":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_power","markdown":"# Ajopelin teho\n\nAntaa ulostulotehon, jota ajopeli käyttää tällä hetkellä.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.power(PowerUnits.WATT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAjopelin teho annetaan arvovälillä  **0.0 - 22.0 wattia**.","signature":"drivetrain.power(PowerUnits.WATT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_rotation":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_rotation","markdown":"# Ajopelin kääntymiskulma\n \nAntaa ajopelin kääntymiskulman 3-lanka Gyro Sensorilla tai V5 Inertial Sensorilla.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKääntymiskulma on **positiivinen** arvo, kun ajopeli kääntyy myötäpäivään.\n\nKääntymiskulma on **negatiivinen** arvo, kun ajopeli kääntyy vastapäivään.","signature":"drivetrain.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_drivetrain_temperature":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_temperature","markdown":"# Ajopelin vetomoottoreiden lämpötila\n \nAntaa ajopelin V5 Älymoottoreiden lämpötilan.\n\n```don\ndrivetrain.temperature(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAjoplein ajomoottoreriden lämpötila mitataan välillä **0% - 100%**.","signature":"drivetrain.temperature(PERCENT)"},"sensing_drivetrain_torque":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_torque","markdown":"# Ajopelin vääntö\n\nAntaa ajopelin väännön (kiertovoiman) arvon.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.torque(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.torque` raportoi arvot välillä **0.0 - 18.6** tuuma-paunaa(InLB) jos yksikön **UNITS** parametrina on `TorqueUnits.INLB`.\n\nVaihtoehtoisesti raportoi arvot välillä **0.0 - 2.1** Newton-metriä (Nm) jos yksikön **UNITS** parametrina on `TorqueUnits.NM`.","signature":"drivetrain.torque(units)"},"sensing_drivetrain_velocity":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_velocity","markdown":"# Ajopelin nopeus\n \nAntaa ajopelin nykyisen nopeuden.\n\n```python\ndrivetrain.velocity(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`drivetrain.velocity` palauttaa desimaalilukuna ajopelin nykyisen nopeuden.\n\nYksikkö `UNITS` voi olla joko **PERCENT** (prosenttia) tai **RPM** (kierrosta minuutissa)..\n\nJos käytetään yksikön `UNITS` parametrina **PERCENT**, arvot saadaan väliltä **-100% - 100%**.\n\nVastaavasti jos yksikön `UNITS` parametrina on **RPM**, mitatut arvot riippuvat asennetuista moottorien vaihdelaatikoiden väreistä seuraavasti.\n\n* Red Cartridge: (punainen) -100rpm - 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: (vihreä) -200rpm - 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: (sininen) -600rpm - 600rpm","signature":"drivetrain.velocity(UNITS)"},"sensing_encoder_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_position","markdown":"# Akselikierros asento\n \nAntaa akselikierron Shaft Encoder -sensorin asennon.\n\n```don\nencoder.position(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nParametri `UNITS` hyväksyy joko **DEGREES** (asteita) tai **TURNS** (kierroksia) yksiköksi.\n\nAkselin asento antaa Shaft Encoder -laitteen mittaaman matkan joko kokonaisluku asteina tai desimaaliluku kierroksina.","signature":"encoder.position(DEGREES)"},"sensing_encoder_set_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_set_position","markdown":"# Aseta akselianturin (kierrosmittarin) arvo\n \nAsettaa akselianturille (kierrosmittarille) määrätyn arvon.\n\n```python\nencoder.set_position(POSITION, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAseta encoder -anturin (kierrosmittarin) arvo sopivaan haluttuun positiiviseen lukuarvoon.\n\nYksikön 'UNITS` parametrina voi olla **DEGREES** (asteita) tai **TURNS** (kierroksia).\n\nTavallisesti encoder- kierrosmittari nollataan sopivassa kohtaan ohjelmaa.","signature":"encoder.set_position(POSITION, UNITS)"},"sensing_encoder_velocity":{"name":"sensing_encoder_velocity","markdown":"# Akselin kierrosnopeus\n\nAntaa akselin kierrosnopeuden.\n\n```don\nencoder.velocity(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAkselin kierrosnopeus anta desimaaliluvun astetta sekunnssa (dps) tai kierrosta minuutissa (rpm).\n\nParametrina `UNITS` voi käyttää joko **VelocityUnits.DPS** tai **RPM**.","signature":"encoder.velocity(VelocityUnits.DPS)"},"sensing_gyro_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_calibrate","markdown":"# Kalibroi Gyro Sensor\n\nKalibroimalla Gyro Sensor vähebbetään arvon heiluntaa mitattaessa kulmaa.\n\n```don\ngyro.calibrate()\n```\n\nHeiluntaa esiintyy kun Gyro Sensor ivirheellisesti mittaa liikettä vaikka se on paikaallaan.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nGyro Sensorin pitää olla paikallaan prosessin aikana 2 sekuntia suorittamaan sen onnistuneesti loppuun.","signature":"gyro.calibrate()"},"sensing_gyro_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Gyro ajosuunta\n \nAntaa 3-lanka Gyro Sensorin nykyisen ajosuunnan asteina.\n\n```don\ngyro.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento antaa kasvavia lukuja kun se kääntyy myötäpäivään.\n\n`gyro.heading` raportoi arvot välillä **0.00 - 359.99**.","signature":"gyro.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Gyro Angle Of Rotation\n \nReports the 3-Wire Gyro Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n```don\ngyro.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nGyro rotation reports a **positive** value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\nGyro rotation reports a **negative** value when the Gyro Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.","signature":"gyro.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_heading","markdown":"# Set Gyro Heading\n\nSets the Gyroscopic (Gyro) Sensor's current heading position to a set value.\n \n```don\ngyro.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe set gyro heading command can be used to set the Gyro's position to any clockwise heading.\n\nThis command is typically used reset the heading orientation of the Gyro sensor when value is set to 0.\n\nThe `HEADING` parameter accepts a range of 0.0 to 359.99 degrees.\n\nThe set heading command can accept decimals, integers, or numeric values.","signature":"gyro.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_gyro_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_rotation","markdown":"# Set Gyro Rotation\n\nSets the 3-Wire Gyro Sensor or V5 Inertial Sensor's angle of rotation to a given value.\n\n```don \ngyro.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe set gyro rotation command can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\nThe set gyro rotation command can accept decimals, integers, or numeric values.","signature":"gyro.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Inertia kiihtyvyys\n\nRaportoin yhden akseleista (x, y, or z) kiihtyvyys mitattuna Intertial Sensorilla.\n\n```don\ninertial.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKiihtyvyys mitataan välillä **-4.0 - 4.0 Gs**.\n\nValitse mitä akselisuuntaa tarkastellaan:\n\n* **X-akseli** suunta raportoi kiihtyvyyttä liikeessä **eteenpäin taaksepäin**\n* **Y-akseli** suunta raportoi kiihtyvyyttä liikeessä **sivulta sivulle**\n* **Z-akseli** suunta raportoi kiihtyvyyttä liikeessä  **ylös alas**","signature":"inertial.acceleration(AxisType.XAXIS)"},"sensing_inertial_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_calibrate","markdown":"# Calibrate Inertial Sensor\n \nCalibrating the Inertial Sensor is used to reduce the amount of drift generated by the Inertial Sensor.\n\n```don\ninertial.calibrate()\n```\n\nDrifting occurs when the Inertial Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not physically moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Inertial Sensor must remain still during the calibration process. The calibration process will take approximately 2 seconds to complete.","signature":"inertial.calibrate()"},"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Inertia -sensorin kääntymisnopeus\n\nAntaa kääntymisnopeuden yhdeltä akselilta (x, y, tai z).\n\n```don\ninertial.gyro_rate(AxisType.XAXIS, VelocityUnits.DPS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nInertia -sensorin kääntymisnopeus antaa arvot välillä **-1000.0 - 1000.0** yksikkönä dps (astetta sekunnissa).\n\nValise akseli, jota tarkastelet. Valinnat ovat:\n\n* X-akseli raportoi kääntymisnopeuden x-akselilla\n* Y-akseli raportoi kääntymisnopeuden y-akselilla\n* Z-akseli raportoi kääntymisnopeuden z-akselilla","signature":"inertial.gyro_rate(AxisType.XAXIS, VelocityUnits.DPS)"},"sensing_inertial_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_heading","markdown":"# Inertial Angle Of Heading \n\nReports the V5 Inertial Sensor's current heading in degrees.\n\n```don\ninertial.heading(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `inertial.heading` command reports an increase in heading when rotating clockwise.\n\n`inertial.heading` reports a range from 0.00 to 359.99 degrees.","signature":"inertial.heading(DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_orientation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Inertial suunta\n\nAntaa inertial sensorin mittaaman suuntakulman. Tulos annetaan sille suunnalle (x,y tai z) , jonka parametri käytössä.\n\n```don\ninertial.orientation(OrientationType.ROLL, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTulos annetaan sille suunnalle (x,y tai z).\n\n* X-akseli edustaa pitch (eteen-taakse) välillä -90 - +90 astetta.\n* Y-akseli edustaa roll (sivulta-sivulle) välillä -180 - +180 astetta\n* Z-aakseli edustaa yaw (ylös-alas) välillä  -180 - +180 astetta","signature":"inertial.orientation(OrientationType.ROLL , DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_rotation","markdown":"# Inertial kääntymiskulma\n \nANtaa 3-lanka V5 Inertial Sensorin kääntymiskulman.\n\n```don\ninertial.rotation(DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`inertial.rotation` komento antaa positiivisen arvon kun sensori kääntyy myötäpäivään.\n\n`inertial.rotation` komento antaa negatiivisen arvon kun sensori kääntyy myötäpäivään.","signature":"inertial.rotation(DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_heading","markdown":"# Aseta Inertial -sensorin ajosuunta\n\nAsettaa Inertial -sensorin ajosuunnalle arvon.\n\n```don\ninertial.set_heading(HEADING, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`inertial.set_heading` komennolla voi asetaa Inertial Sensorin asennon mihin tahansa kellotaulun arvoon, tyypillisesti se nollataan tarpeen mukaan kesken ajoa.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` komento sallii arvot välillä 0.0 - 359.99 astetta.\n\n`inertial.set_heading` komento sallii desimaaliarvoja, kokonaislukuja ja sensoreiden numeerisia arvoja.","signature":"inertial.set_heading(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_inertial_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_rotation","markdown":"# Aseta Inertial kääntymiskulma\n\nAsettaa 3-lanka Inertial Sensorin kulman tiettyyn arvoon.\n\n```don\ninertial.set_rotation(ROTATION, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`inertial.set_rotation` komennolla voidaan asettaa joko positiiviseen (myötäpäivä) asentoon tai negatiiviseen (vastapäivä) asentoon.\n\n`inertial.set_rotation` sallii sekä postitiivisia etttä negatiivisia desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja.","signature":"inertial.set_rotation(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_light_brightness":{"name":"sensing_light_brightness","markdown":"# Valosensorin kirkkaus/valovoima\n\nRaportoi Valosensorin mittaaman valon määrän.\n\n```don\nlight.brightness(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`light.brightness` antaa arvon väliltä **0% - 100%**.\n\nKirkas valo antaa korkean valonmäärän.\n\nHimmeä tai heikko valaistus antaa pienen valon määrän.","signature":"light.brightness(PERCENT)"},"sensing_limit_switch_pressing":{"name":"sensing_limit_switch_pressing","markdown":"# Limit Switch \n\nRaportoi jos Limit Switch -sensoria on painettu.\n\n```don\nlimit_switch.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun sensoria on painettu, komento antaa arvon **True** (tosi).\n\nKun sensoria ei ole painettu, komento antaa arvon **False** (epätosi).","signature":"limit_switch.pressing()"},"sensing_line_tracker_reflectivity":{"name":"sensing_line_tracker_reflectivity","markdown":"# Viivanseuranta heijastus\n\nAntaa valon määrän, joka heijastuu Viivanseuranta-sensoriin.\n\n```don\nline_tracker.reflectivity(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nVaaleat pinnat heijastaa paremmin valoa kuin tummat pinnat ja myös heijastusarvo vaaleilla on suurempi.\n\nTummat pinnat heijastaa valoa huonommin ja myös heijastusarvo on pieni.\n\nYksikkönä käytyetään`PERCENT`(prosenttia) ja komento palauttaa kokonaislukuarvon välillä **0% - 100%**.","signature":"line_tracker.reflectivity(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_current":{"name":"sensing_motor_current","markdown":"# Moottorin sähkövirta\n\nAntaa sähkövirran määrän , jota V5 Älymoottori tällä hetkellä käyttää yksikössä (amps).\n\n```don\nmotor.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nSähkövirran määrä mitataan välillä **0.0 - 2.5 amps**.","signature":"motor.current(CurrentUnits.AMP)"},"sensing_motor_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_motor_efficiency","markdown":"# Moottorin tehokkuus\n \nAntaa V5 Älympoottrin INPUT-tehokkuuden .\n\n```don\nmotor.efficiency(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTehokkuus antaa mitatun prosenttiarvon , jota moottori käyttää : ulostulona saatavaan teho (output Wattia) suhteessa sisääntulevaan tehoon (input Watteina) .\n\nV5 Älymoottori saavuttaa tyypillisesti korkeintaan 65% tehon.\n\nTehokkuus mitataan välillä **0% - 100%**.","signature":"motor.efficiency(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_is_done":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_done","markdown":"# Moottori on suorittanut liikkeen \n\nAntaa tiedon kun moottori on suorittanut liikkeen loppuun.\n\n```don\nmotor.is_done()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMoottori on suorittanut liikkeen -komento antaa arvon **True** (tosi) kun moottori on suorittanut liikekomennon loppuun.\n\nMoottori on suorittanut liikkeen -komento antaa arvon **False** (epätosi) kun moottorin liikekomento on vielä kesken.","signature":"motor.is_done()"},"sensing_motor_is_spinning":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Moottori pyörii\n\nRaportoi, pyöriikö V5 Älymoottori tällä hetkellä.\n\n```don\nmotor.is_spinning()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMoottori pyörii -komento antaa arvon **True** (tosi), kun valittu moottori edelleen pyörii.\n\nMoottori pyörii -komento antaa arvon **False** (epätosi), kun valittu moottori on pysähtynyt.","signature":"motor.is_spinning()"},"sensing_motor_position":{"name":"sensing_motor_position","markdown":"# Moottorin asento\n\nRaportoi V5 Älymoottorin kiertoasennon tällä hetkellä.\n\n```don\nmotor.position(UNIT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nV5 Älymoottorin kiertoasento voidaan ilmaista joko kokonaislukuna asteina tai dsimaalilukuna kierroksina.\n\nYksikkönä `UNIT` voi olla: **DEGREES** (asteet) tai **TURNS** (kierroksia).","signature":"motor.position(DEGREES)"},"sensing_motor_power":{"name":"sensing_motor_power","markdown":"# Moottorin teho\n\nAntaa V5 Äly moottorin ulostulevan tehon tällä hetkellä.\n\n```don\nmotor.power(PowerUnits.WATT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMoottorin ulostuloteho mitataan arvovälillä **0.0 - 11.0 wattia**.","signature":"motor.power(PowerUnits.WATT)"},"sensing_motor_temperature":{"name":"sensing_motor_temperature","markdown":"# Moottorin lämpötila\n\nRaportoi V5 Älymoottorin lämpötilan.\n\n```don\nmotor.temperature(PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nV5 Älymoottorin lämpötila -komennon avulla voi estää moottorin kuumenemisen raskaan ajon aikana.\n\nLämpötila raportoidaan välillä **0% - 100%**.","signature":"motor.temperature(PERCENT)"},"sensing_motor_torque":{"name":"sensing_motor_torque","markdown":"# Moottorin vääntö\n\nRaportoi väännön suuruuden (kääntymisvoiman), jota V5 Äly Moottori nyt käyttää.\n\n```python\nmotor.torque(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`motor.torque` antaa arvot välillä **0.0 to 18.6** inch-pounds (InLB) jos yksikön **UNITS** parametrina on `TorqueUnits.INLB`.\n\nVaihtiehtoisesti arvon välillä **0.0 to 2.1** Newton-metriä (Nm) jos yksikön **UNITS** parametrina on `TorqueUnits.NM`.","signature":"motor.torque(UNITS)"},"sensing_motor_velocity":{"name":"sensing_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Moottorin nopeus\n\nANtaa nykyisen V5 Älymoottorin nopeuden.\n\n```python\nmotor.velocity(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMoottorin nopesu antaa arvot väliltä **-100% - 100%** tai **-600rpm - 600rpm**.\n\nYksikön `UNIT` parametrit ovat: **PERCENT** (%) or **RPM** (kierrosta minuutissa).\n\nMoottorin nopeus yksikössä \"kierrosta minuutissa\" arvot riippuvat käytetystä moottorin vaihdepakkauksesta.\n\n* Red Cartridge: (punainen) -100rpm - 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: (vihreä) -200rpm - 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: (sininen) -600rpm - 600rpm","signature":"motor.velocity(UNITS)"},"sensing_optical_brightness":{"name":"sensing_optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical kirkkaus\n\nAntaa valonmäärän, jonka Optical sensori havaitsee.\n\n```don\noptical.brightness()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`optical.brightness()` antaa arvot välillä **0%** - **100%**\n\nPaljon valoa antaa korkean arvon.\n\nVähän valoa antaa pienen arvon.","signature":"optical.brightness()"},"sensing_optical_color_found":{"name":"sensing_optical_color_found","markdown":"# Optical havaitsee värin\n\nANtaa värin, jonka Optical Sensori havaitsee.\n\n```don\noptical.color()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`optical.color()` antaa RGB (Red, Green, Blue) -arvon, joka vastaa väriä. Voit käyttää funktiota `Color` eri arvoja ja vertailla sitä `optical.color()` sensorin antamaan arvoon\n\nVoit vertailla värien arvot seuraavasti\n\n* Color.BLACK (musta)\n* Color.WHITE (valkoinen)\n* Color.RED (punainen)\n* Color.GREEN (vihreä)\n* Color.BLUE (sininen)\n* Color.YELLOW (keltainen)\n* Color.ORANGE (oranssi)\n* Color.PURPLE (purppura)\n* Color.CYAN (syaani)\n\nVoit käyttää ehtoja seuraavasti:\n\n```don\nif optical.color() == Color.RED:\n\tbrain.screen.print(\"Red Object\")\n```","signature":"optical.color()"},"sensing_optical_hue":{"name":"sensing_optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical värisävy\n\nRaportoi esineen värisävyn.\n\n```don\noptical.hue()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`optical.hue()` antaa numeroarvon kohteen värille. \n\nArvot ovat välillä **0** -**359**, ja se on värin paikka Vex värirenkaassa (värispetrissä).","signature":"optical.hue()"},"sensing_optical_object_found":{"name":"sensing_optical_object_found","markdown":"# Optical löysi esineen\n\nAntaa tiedon havaitsiko Optical Sensor lähellä esineen.\n\n```don\noptical.is_near_object()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`optical.is_near_object()` antaa **True** (Tosi) jos kohde on tarpeeksi lähellä Optical Sensoria.\n\n`optical.is_near_object()` antaa **False** (Epätosi) jos kohdetta ei löydy tarpeeksi lähellä Optical Sensoria.","signature":"optical.is_near_object()"},"sensing_optical_set_light":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light","markdown":"# Aseta Optical Valo päälle\n\n\nAsettaa valon Optical Sensoriin , joko **on** (päälle) tai **off** (pois päältä).\n\n```don\noptical.set_light(LedStateType.ON)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`optical.set_light(LedStateType.ON)` antaa laittaa Optical Sensorin valon joko **on** (päälle) tai **off** (pois). Näin voit havaita kohteen paremmin, jos yleisvalaistus on huono sensorin edessä.\n\nParametri **on** on valinta `LedStateType.ON`\n\n```\noptical.set_light(LedStateType.ON)\n```\n\nParametri **off** on valinta `LedStateType.OFF`\n\n```\noptical.set_light(LedStateType.OFF)\n```","signature":"optical.set_light(LedStateType.ON)"},"sensing_optical_set_light_power":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Aseta Optical valoteho\n\nAsettaa V5 Optical sensorin valotehon.\n\n```don\noptical.set_light_power(50, PERCENT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`optical.set_light_power(50, PERCENT)` muuttaa valon kirkkauden Optical Sensorissa. \n\nKomento valon intensiteetti toimii välillä **0%** - **100%** ja **PERCENT** (prosentti) on yksikkönä. Jos valo on poissa, niin tällä komennolla valon saa päälle.","signature":"optical.set_light_power(50, PERCENT)"},"sensing_potentiometer_angle":{"name":"sensing_potentiometer_angle","markdown":"# Potentiometrin kulma\n\nPalauttaa Potentiometrin mittaaman kulma-asennon.\n\n```don\npotentiometer.angle(UNITS)\n```\n\n##Miten käytetään\n\n`potentiometer.angle` palauttaa Potentiometrin mittaaman kulman desimaalilukuna.\n\n`UNITS` -yksikköparametri hyväksyy argumentin joko **DEGREES** (asteina) tai **PERCENT** (prosentteina).\n\n'UNITS` yksikkönä **DEGREES** antaa arvoväliltä **0.0 - 250.0 degrees**.\n\nVastaavasti `UNITS` yksikkönä **PERCENT** palauttaa arvot väliltä **0 - 100%** .","signature":"potentiometer.angle(UNITS)"},"sensing_range_finder_distance":{"name":"sensing_range_finder_distance","markdown":"# Etäisyys Range Finder -sensori\n\nAntaa lähimmän esineen etäisyyden Ultrasonic Range Finder -sensorista.\n\n```don\nrange_finder.distance(UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nEtäisyys sensorista annetaan välillä 30mm - 3000mm tai 2 tuumaa -  115 tuumaa.\n\nYksikön `UNITS` parametrina voi olla joko **MM** (mm) tai **INCHES** (tuumaa).","signature":"range_finder.distance(MM)"},"sensing_range_finder_found_object":{"name":"sensing_range_finder_found_object","markdown":"# Range Finder -sensori havaitsi esineen\n\nANtaa tietoa, onko Ultrasonic Range Finder sensori havainnut esineen/kohteen näkökentässään.\n\n```don\nrange_finder.found_object()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nJos esine/pinta on näkökentässä, sensori antaa arvon **True** (tosi).\n\nJos esine/pinta ei ole näkökentässä, sensori antaa arvon **False** (epätosi).","signature":"range_finder.found_object()"},"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled":{"name":"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled","markdown":"# Ohjain käytössä\n\nOttaa ohjaimen käyttöön tai ottaa käytöstä ohjaimen, joka on määritelty Laitteet -ikkunassa.\n\n```don\nremote_control_code_enabled = False\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse joko käytössä tai ei käytössä valinta ohjaimelle. \n\nOletuksena ohjain on käytössä.","signature":"remote_control_code_enabled = False"},"sensing_rotation_angle":{"name":"sensing_rotation_angle","markdown":"# Kiertokulma\n\nAntaa Rotation Sensorin mittaaman kiertokulman arvon.\n\n```don\nrotation.angle()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetän\n\n`rotation.angle()` antaa decimaaliluvun, jonka Rotation Sensori on mitannut asteina.","signature":"rotation.angle()"},"sensing_rotation_position":{"name":"sensing_rotation_position","markdown":"# Kääntymis asento\n\nAntaa Rotation Sensorin kääntymisasennon.\n\n```don\nrotation.position(UNIT)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`rotation.position(UNIT)`  antaa Rotation Sensorin asennon kokonaislukuna asteina tai desimaalilukuna kierroksina.\n\nHyväksytyt ```UNIT``` parametrit ovat: ```DEGREES```(asteina) tai ```TURNS``` (kierroksina).","signature":"rotation.position(DEGREES)"},"sensing_rotation_set_position":{"name":"sensing_rotation_set_position","markdown":"# Aseta Rotation asento\n\nAntaa Rotation Sensorin asennoksi halutun arvon.\n\n```don\nrotation.set_position(0, DEGREES)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`rotation.set_position(0, DEGREES)` avulla voi asettaa Rotation Sensorille halutun positiivisen arvon.\n\nTyypillisesti `rotation.set_position(0, DEGREES)` komennon avulla resetoidaan Rotation Sensor arvoon 0 astetta.","signature":"rotation.set_position(0, DEGREES)"},"sensing_rotation_velocity":{"name":"sensing_rotation_velocity","markdown":"# Pyörimisnopeus\n\nRaportoi Rotation Sensorin mittaaman pyörimisnopeuden.\n\n```don\nrotation.velocity(UNIT)\n```\n\n##Miten käytetään\n\n`rotation.velocity(UNIT)` antaa Rotation Sensorinmittaaman pyörimisnopeuden yksikössä ```UNIT``` , jonka hyväksytyt parametriarvot määritellään:\n\n\n* **VelocityUnits.RPM** (kierrosta minuutissa)\n* **VelocityUnits.DPS**(astetta sekunnissa)","signature":"rotation.velocity(PERCENT)"},"sensing_vision_largest_object":{"name":"sensing_vision_largest_object","markdown":"# Suurin esine\n\nAntaa tiedot suurimmasta Vision kameran havaitusta esineestä.\n\n```python\nvision.largest_object()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMäärittele Vision kamera lisäämällä esineiden merkit/koodit.\n\nTee `vision.take_snapshot` komento ottamaan kuva ja käytä `vision.largest_object` komentoa.\n\nEsimerkissä tulsottetaan näytölle tietoja havaitusta esineestä.\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    brain.screen.clear_screen()\n    brain.screen.set_cursor(1, 1)\n\n    # Take a snapshot with the Vision Sensor with the specified signature and store the object data into a variable\n    vision_object = vision.take_snapshot(signature)\n\n    # Check the variable to see if a valid object was detected when the snapshot was captured\n    # If yes, print the data\n    if vision_object is not None:\n        brain.screen.print(\"Center X: \", vision.largest_object().centerX)\n        brain.screen.next_row()\n\n        brain.screen.print(\"Center Y: \", vision.largest_object().centerY)\n        brain.screen.next_row()\n\n        # Take a new snapshot every 0.2 seconds\n        wait(0.2, SECONDS)\n    else:\n        brain.screen.print(\"No Object Detected\")\n```\n\nSeuraavassa listta ominaisuuksista, joita voi käyttää `vision.largest_object` komennon jälkeen:\n\n- `id` - Yksikäsitteinen ID jokaiselle Vision kamera objektille\n- `originX` - Ylä vasen X arvo esineestä\n- `originY` - Ylä vasen Y arvo esineestä\n- `centerX` - Keskipiste X arvo esineestä\n- `centerY` - Keskipiste Y arvo esineestä\n- `width` - Esineen leveys\n- `height` - Esineen korkeus\n- `angle` - Esineen kulma kameraan\n- `exists` - Havaitseeko Vision kamera esineen","signature":"vision.largest_object()"},"sensing_vision_take_snapshot":{"name":"sensing_vision_take_snapshot","markdown":"# Ota kuva\n\nOttaa kuvan Vision Kameralla.\n\n```don\nvision.take_snapshot(SIGNATURE)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOta kuva -toiminto kaappaa nykyisen kameran näkemän kuvan ja sen avulla voi analysoida kuvassa näkyviä merkkejä ja koodeja.\n\nOta kuva on aina kameran ensimmäinen komento ennen muita Vision Kameran komentoja.","signature":"vision.take_snapshot(SIGNATURE)"},"variables_my_2d_list":{"name":"variables_my_2d_list","markdown":"# 2D Taulukko\n\n2D taulukkoon voi tallentaa useammalle riville ja sarakkeisiin arvoja.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nNimeä 2D taulukko ja anna sille käyttöä kuvaava nimi .\n\nEsimerkiksi 2d taulukkoon `coordinates` voi tallentaa useamman x,y koordinaatit.\n\nYksittäinen arvo annetaan symbolin `=` jälkeen hakasuluissa `[ ]`.\n\nHakasulkujen sisällä useammat arvot annetaan taas hakasuluissa pilkulla erotettuina: `[[ ], [ ]]`. More than two sets of square brackets can be nested within the outer-most set of square brackets.\n\nAnna arvot hakasuluissa ja eroteltuna pilkulla `,`. Jos taulukko sisältää tekstikenttiä, laita ne lainausmerkkien `\" \"` sisään .\n\nJokainen sisempi hakasulku edustaa riviä. Rivin sisällä taas hakasulut merkkaavat 2d taulukon saraketta.\n\nKun haluat viitata johonkin alkioon taulukossa, anna taulukon nimi ja heti hakasuluissa rivin ja sarakkeen arvot. Ensimmäiset alkiot on aina indeksillä 0, ei 1.\n\nEsimerkiksi 2D taulukko on määritelty coordinates = [[X1, Y1], [X2, Y2]]`, ja kun viitataan taulukon ensimmäiseen arvoon `coordinates[0][0]`, se palauttaa arvon `X1`. \n\n## Esimerkki 1\n\nEsimerkissä 2d taulukkoon my_list on tallennettu kaksi erillistä värilistaa.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [[\"Green\", \"Red\", \"Blue\"], [\"Black\", \"Yellow\", \"Orange\"]]\n```\n\n## Esimerkki 2\n\nEsimerkissä 2d taulukkoon my_list on tallennettu kaksi erillistä numerolistaa.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]\n```","signature":"my_2d_list = [\\n\\t[0,0,0],\\n\\t[0,0,0],\\n\\t[0,0,0]\\n]"},"variables_my_boolean":{"name":"variables_my_boolean","markdown":"# Boolean muuttuja\n\nBoolean muuttujan arvo on joko **True** (Tosi) tai **False** (epätosi).\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun määrittelet Boolean muuttujan, anna sille kuvaava tarkoitukseensa sopiva nimi.\n\nEsimerkiksi muuttuja `pressed` kuvaa sen käyttöä, kun painonappia on painettu.\n\nKun haluat arvoja Boolean muuttujaan, käytä symboolia `=` ja sen jälkeen arvona joko `True` tai `False`.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä laitetaan arvo `True` muuttujaan  `my_variable` .\n\n```don\nmy_variable = True\n```","signature":"my_boolean = True"},"variables_my_list":{"name":"variables_my_list","markdown":"# Luettelo muuttuja\n\nLuetteloon voi tallentaa useampia muuttuja-arvoja.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAnna luettelolle järkevä nimi . Hyvällä nimellä kuvaat luettelon käyttötarkoitusta.\n\nesimerkiksi luettelonimi `colors` kuvaa sitä, että muuttujan alkiot ovat värien nimiä.\n\nKun haluat kohdisaa luettelon alkioon, käytä `=` operaattoria ja sen jälkeen arvot hakasuluissa `[ ]`.\n\nJos arvot ovat numeroita, eroita ne toisistaan pilkulla.\n\n`my_number_list = [1, 2, 3]`\n\nJos arvot ovat tekstejä, niiden ympärillä pitää olla `\" \"` merkit ja pilkut eri alkioiden välillä.\n\n`my_string_list = [\"Hello\", \"World\"]`\n\nJos haluat käyttää tiettyä luettelon alkion arvoa, nimen jälkeen hakasulkuihin alkion järjestysnumero , ensimmäinen alkio on järjestysnumerolla 0, ei 1.\n\nEsimerkiksi `my_string_list[0]` palauttaa arvon `\"Hello\"`.\n\n## Esimerkki 1\n\nesimerkissä luetteloon my_list on tallennettu värien nimiä.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [\"Green\", \"Red\", \"Blue\"]\n```\n\n## Esimerkki 2\n\nTässä esimerkissä taas luettelon my_list alkioihin on tallennettu numeroita.\n\n```don\nmy_list = [1, 2, 3]\n```","signature":"my_list = [0,0,0]"},"variables_my_number":{"name":"variables_my_number","markdown":"# Numero muuttuja\n\nNumero muuttujissa voi tallentaa numeroita.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun luot numeromuuttujan, nimeä se kuvaamaan sen tarkoitusta. \n\nEsimerkiksi numeromuuttuja `counter` käytetään tallentamaan laskimen arvoja.\n\nKun haluat asetaa arvoja muuttujaasi, käytä `=` operaattoria. \n\n## Esimerkki 1\n\nEsimerkissä muuttuja on nimeltään `my_number` ja siihen asetaan arvo 10.\n\n```don\nmy_number = 10\n```\n## Esimerkki 2\n\nEsimerkissä on muuttuja `three_plus_two` ja siihen asetaan arvoksi laskutoimiuksen 3 lisättynä 2 tulos. \n\n```don\nthree_plus_two = 3 + 2\n```","signature":"my_number = 1"},"variables_my_string":{"name":"variables_my_string","markdown":"# Tekstimuuttuja\n\nTekstimuuttujaan tallennetaan tekstiä.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTKun määritteelet tekstimuuttujan, anna sille tarkoitusta kuvaava nimi. \n\nEsimekriksi muuttuja `name` kertoo,e ttä siihen on tallennettu nimiä.\n\nKun haluat tallentaa muuttujaan arvoa, käytä operaattoria `=` operatoria. Tekstikentän ympärillä käytä joko lainausmerkkejä `\" \"` tai heittomerkkejä `' '`.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä muuttujaan my_string on tallenettu arvo `\"Hello\"`.\n\n```don\nmy_string = \"Hello\"\n```","signature":"my_string = \\\"Hello World\\\""}},"cpp":{"control_break":{"name":"control_break","markdown":"# Keskeytä\n\nKomennolla hypätään pois toistorakenteesta.\n```cpp\nbreak;\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun lisätään `break` kommento johonkin kohtaan toistorakennetta, se aiheuttaa hypyn pois silmukasta toiston jälkeiseen seuraavaan komentoon. \n\n## Esimerkki\n\nesimerkissä ajataan eteenpäin ja ja tarkistetaan , onko `bumper` törmäysanturia painettu.\n\nJos näyttöä on painettu on kosketettu, 'break` komento aiheuttaa hypyn pois silmukan suorituksesta ja ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n  if(Brain.Screen.pressing()) {\n    break;\n  }\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"break;"},"control_for":{"name":"control_for","markdown":"# Toista\n\nSilmukkakomento, jossa koodia toistetaan annetun numeron mukainen määrä.\n\n```cpp\nfor (initialization; condition; increment/decrement) {\n   // code here will repeat a number of times\n}\n```\n\n# Miten käytetään\n\nEnsiksi anna arvo, joka kertoo montako kertaa silmukka toistetaan .\n\n**for** komento tietää suorituksen aikana, montako kierrosta on mennyt:\n\n* initialization on iterointimuuttujan alkuarvo, voit myös käyttää muuttujan arvoa \n* condition kertoo montako kertaa toisto tehdään. \n* increment/decrement expression kertoo iterointimuuttujan muuutoksen kierroksen lopussa\n* \n\nHuomaa että luuppi alkaa aina indeksillä 0.\n\n`For` luuppeja voi laittaa toistensa sisään sisäkkäin.\n\n# Esimerkki\n\nSeuraava toista silmukka tulostaa luvut 0 sta lukuun 9:\n\n```cpp\nfor(int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n   Brain.Screen.print(i);\n   Brain.Screen.newLine();\n}\n```","signature":"for(int i = 0; i < length; i++) { }"},"control_if":{"name":"control_if","markdown":"# Jos\n\nOhjauslause, joka päättelee, suoritetaanko ehdon `condition` toiminnot.\n\n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nEhto tutkitaan vain kerran. Sijoita sanan `condition` tilalle  Boolean -lauseke, joka saa joko arvon `True` tai `False`. \n\nJos totuusarvo on `True`, niin `if` ehdon komennot suoritetaan.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\n`if` haaran komennot suoritetaan , jos painokytkintä on painettu ja robotti pysähtyy.\n\n```cpp\nif (BumperA.pressing()) {\n    Motor1.stop();\n}\n```","signature":"if(true) { }"},"control_if_else":{"name":"control_if_else","markdown":"# Jos/muuten\n\nOhjauslause, joka suorittaa If -haaran, jos ehto on 'true' (tosi) ja Else -haaran jos ehto on 'false' (epätosi).\n\n```cpp\nif (condition) {\n\n} else {\n\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n'if` komento on ehto , joka saa joko arvon **True** tai **False**. Voit yhdistää ehtoihin useamman loogisen operaattorin `and`, `or`, and `not`. \n\nJos ehto saa arvon **True**, `if ehdon` haaran komennot aaltosuluissa suoritetaan. Jos ehto saa arvon **False**, `else:` haaran komennot aaltosuluissa suoritetaan.\n\n```cpp\nif (BumperA.pressing()) {\n    LeftMotor.stop();\n} else {\n    LeftMotor.spin(forward);\n}\n```","signature":"else { }"},"control_repeat":{"name":"control_repeat","markdown":"# Toista\n\nToistaa aaltosulkujen sisällä olevan koodin tietyn kertamäärän. \n\n```\nrepeat (10) {\n\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**repeat-statement** koodin sisöllä olevat koodirivit suoritetaan halutun kertamääärän ehdossa.\n\nArvo pitää olla positiivinen kokonaisluku, myös muuttujan tai sensorin arvo käy.\n\nOhessa sana \"iteration\" tulostetaan aivojen näytölle neljä kertaa. Joka kerralla tehdään myös uusi rivi.\n\n```\nrepeat (4) {\n  Brain.Screen.Print(\"iteration\");\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  wait(5, msec);\n}\n```\n\nHuomaa ettei **repeat-statement** sisällä ei voi olla toista **repeat statement**.","signature":"repeat(10) { }"},"control_wait":{"name":"control_wait","markdown":"# Odota\n\nOdota tietty sekuntimäärä ennen seuraavan komennon suoritusta.\n\n```cpp\nwait(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAseta  sekuntimäärä time , kaunanko ohjelma odottaa seuraavaa komentoa.\n\n```cpp\n// Wait for 5 seconds before driving forward\nwait(5, seconds);\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n```","signature":"wait(time, seconds);"},"control_wait_until":{"name":"control_wait_until","markdown":"# Kun ei\n\nOhjauskomento jatkaa silmukan sisällä olevien komentojen suoritusta kunnes ehto toteutuu ja saa arvon **true**.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (!condition) {\n  // Run some commands\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`while not` komento tarkistaa jokaisen silmukan  kierroksen alussa ehtoa ja siirtyy seuraavaan silmukan jälkeiseen komentoon vasta kun ehto saa arvon **true.**\n\nJos ehto on **false**, silmukan sisällä oleva koodi suoritetaan.\n\nJos ehto on **true**, silmukkan yli hypätään ja seuraava komento suoritetaan ja jatketaan siitä edelleen.\n\n`while not` komento hyväksyy Boolean -lausekkeita, jotka voivat saada arvot 'True` tai `False`. Booleans tyyppisiä ehtoja ovat vertailuehdot ja loogiset operaatiot. \n\n\n`\n```cpp\n// Keep driving forward until the Bumper Pressing command returns true\nwhile (!Bumper.pressing()) {\n  Drivetrain.drive(forward);\n}\n\n// Stop the Drivetrain after the Bumper is pressed\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"while (!condition) {\\n\\n};"},"control_while":{"name":"control_while","markdown":"# Kun\n\nKoodi aaltosulkujen sisällä suoritetaan niin kauan kuun ehto saa arvon  **true**.   \n\n```cpp\nwhile (condition) {\n\n}\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`while` luuppi tarkista ehdon vain aina kierroksen alussa ts aina koko aaltosulkujen sisällä oleva koodinpätkä suoritetaan. \n\n\nJos ehto on **false**, `while` komento ohitetaan.\n\n`while` komento hyväksyy Boolean ehtoja mm vertailuehtoja ja loogisia operaattoreita.Myös numeroarvoja ts arvo **0** vastaa **false** ja muut numerot **non-zero numbers** vastaa arvoa **true**. \n\n```cpp\n// Drive forward while the timer value is less than 10 seconds\n\nwhile(Brain.Timer.time(seconds) < 10) {\n\tDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n}\n\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"while(true) { }"},"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain":{"name":"drivetrain_calibrate_drivetrain","markdown":"# Kalibroi ajopelin gyro\n\nKalibroi ajopelin gyron.\n\n```cpp\ncalibrateDrivetrain();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`calibrateDrivetrain();` Kalibroi ajopelin gyron. Apopelin pitää olla paikoillaa kalibroinnin ajan. Tällöin myös ohjelma odottaa kalibroinnin ajan.\n\n\n```cpp\ncalibrateDrivetrain();\n```","signature":"calibrateDrivetrain();"},"drivetrain_drive":{"name":"drivetrain_drive","markdown":"# Aja\n\nAjopeli liikkuu ikuisuuden suuntaan, joka määritelty suluissa. \n\nKaikki ajopelin ajomoottorit ajavat eteen tai taaksepäin nopeutta , joka on määritelty komennolla `Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity`, oletus on 50%. \n\nNegatiiviset nopeusarvot aiheuttavat sen, etttä ajopeli ajaa vastakkaiseen suuntaan parametrilla  FORWARD .\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(directionType);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.drive();` komennolla ajopeli ajaa ikuisuuden kunnes joku uusi ajokomento on annettu tai ohjelma on lopetettu.\n\n## Esimerkit\n\nKäytä `forward` argumenttia , kun ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\n```\n\nKäytä `reverse` argumenttia , kun ajopeli peruuttaa.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(reverse);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.drive(forward);"},"drivetrain_drive_for":{"name":"drivetrain_drive_for","markdown":"# Aja matka\n\nLiikuttaa ajopeliä tietyn matkan. Kaikki ajopelin moottorit ajavat joku eteen- tai taaksepäin nopeudelle, joka on annettu komennolla `Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity` . Kun matka on saavutettu, ajopeli pysähtyy.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(directionType, distance, distanceUnits);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAnna ajosuunta (`forward` tai `reverse`) ja ajomatka yksikössä (`inches` tai `mm`).\n\n`Drivetrain.driveFor();` komento hyväksyy numeerisia arvoja matkaarvoon `distance`.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(reverse, 5.0, inches);\n```\n\n**driveFor** komento estää muiden komentojen suorituksen kunnes matka on suoritettu.\n\n## Lisäparamtri\n\nVoit asettaa arvon `false` viimeiselle parametrille, jolloin **driveFor** komento ei estä seuraavia komentoja matkan ollessa kesken.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 5.0, inches, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);"},"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Drivetrain Set Drive Velocity\n\nSets the velocity of the Drivetrain that will be used for drive and driveFor calls. If this is used when the drive is moving, the drivetrain will be updated with the new speed.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity();` will set the speed of the Drivetrain when driving straight, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move. \n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity();` accepts a range from **-100 to 100** when using the `percent` units.\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity();` accepts a range from **-600 to 600** when using the `rpm` units.\n\n`Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity();` can use a \"rotations per minute\" (rpm) value based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to drive in the opposite direction.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's drive velocity to 0 will cause the Drivetrain to stop.","signature":"Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity(50, percent);"},"drivetrain_set_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_set_heading","markdown":"# Aseta ajosuunta\n\nAsettaa ajopelin Gyrolle tarkan ajosuunnan.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setHeading(heading, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.setHeading();` komennolla voi ajopelin ajosuunnan muuttaa. tyypillisesti ajosuunnan arvo nollataan jossain kohtaa ohjelman suoritusta helpottamaan uuden suuunnan ottoa.\n\n`Drivetrain.setHeading();` hyväksyy arvot välillä **0 - 360** ensimmäisenä argumenttina ja `degrees` (asteet) yksikkönä.\n\n```cpp\n// Reset the Drivetrain heading to 0\n\nDrivetrain.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_set_rotation","markdown":"# Aseta kääntymiskulma\n\nAsettaa ajopelin Gyro -sensorin kulman.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setRotation(rotation, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.setRotation()` komennolla Gyro -sensorin arvoksi voi asettaa minkä tahansa positiivisen tai negatiivisen arvon.\n\n`Drivetrain.setRotation()` sallii numeerisia arvoja.\n\n`Drivetrain.setRotation()` ei rajoitu **does not** arvoihin 0-359 astetta.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nesimerkissä robotti kääntyy yhteensä 210 astetta:\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(120, degrees);\nDrivetrain.setRotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(45, degrees);\n```\nKäänny oikealle myötäpäivään lisää 90 astetta (-45 astetta +45 astetta) edellisen asetuksen mukaan.\n\n- Käänny oikealla myötäpäivään kääntymiskulmaan 120 degrees.\n- Aseta nykyinen kääntymiskulma arvoon -45 astetta.\n- Käänny oikealle myötäpäivään lisää 90 astetta (-45 astetta +45 astetta) edellisen asetuksen mukaan.","signature":"Drivetrain.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_set_stopping":{"name":"drivetrain_set_stopping","markdown":"# Pysäytä ajo\n\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setStopping(brakeType);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAseta `brakeType` parametrille joku seuraavista valinta:\n\n* brake: pysäytttää ajopelin heti.\n* coast: ajopeli pysähtyy vähittellen.\n* hold: pysäyttää ajopelin heti ja pitää pysähdysasennon, vaikka ajopeli liikkuisi muuten esim esineen päältä liukuen alas. \n\n `drivetrain.set_stopping()` komento pysyy voimassa jatkossakin niin kauan kunnes tehdään uusi määritys pysähdystavalle.\n \n## Esimerki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli ajaa eteenpäin 3 sekuntia ennen kuin pysähtyy paikalleen.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setStopping(hold);\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setStopping(brake);"},"drivetrain_set_timeout":{"name":"drivetrain_set_timeout","markdown":"# Aseta aikaraja\n\n`Drivetrain.setTimeout();` asettaa aikarajan, kuinka kauan robotin liikekomento jatkuu.\n\n``cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomentoa käytetään estämään ohjelman keskeytys, jos seuraava liikekomento ei pääse tavoiteasemaan esimerkiksi kun robotti törm'' laitaan tai muuhun esteeseen\n\nAseta määrä sekunteina `SECONDS`.\n\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(2.0, seconds);\n```\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä on asetettu 3 sekunnin aikaraja ajo komennolle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTimeout(2.0, seconds);\nDrivetrain.driveFor(24.0, inches, true);\nDrivetrain.turnFor(90.0, degrees, true);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.setTimeout(1, seconds);"},"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity":{"name":"drivetrain_set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Aseta ajopelin nopeus\n\nAsettaa ajopelin nopeuden komennoille `drive` ja `drive_for`.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.setTurnVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity();` komento asettaa ajopelin nopeuden komeentojen `drive` ja `drive_for` käyttöön. Komento ei liikuta ajopeliä.\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity();` hyväksyy arvoja, jotka riippuvat sen toisesta parametrista.\n\nJos `PERCENT` (prosenttia) on käytössä, niin nopeus **VELOCITY** hyväksyy arvot **-100 - 100**.\n\n`Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity();` komennon **UNITS** parametrina voi käyttää `RPM` (kierrosta minuutissa). Riippuen vaihdepakkauksesta , jotka asennettu ajomoottoreihin, **VELOCITY** arvot vaihtelevat seuraavasti:\n\n* Red Cartridge: (punainen) -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: Ivihreä) -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: (sininen) -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nJos nopeudeksi asettaa negatiivisen arvon, ajopeli liikkuu vastakkaiseen suuntaa, mitä `DIRECTION` parametrissa on asetettu komennoissa `drive` tai `drive_for`.\n\nJos nopeus asetetaan arvoon nolla, ajopeli pysähtyy komennoilla `drive` tai `drive_for`.","signature":"Drivetrain.setTurnVelocity(50, percent);"},"drivetrain_stop":{"name":"drivetrain_stop","markdown":"# Pysäytä\n\nPysäytä ajopeli.\n\n`\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.stop();` komento pysäyttää ajopelin. Sillä ei ole argumentteja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli pysähtyy kun se on ajanut 3 sekuntia eeenpäin.\n\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.drive(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nDrivetrain.stop();\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.stop();"},"drivetrain_turn":{"name":"drivetrain_turn","markdown":"# Käänny\n\nAjopeli kääntyy jatkuvasti joko oikealle tai vasemmalle.\n\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(turnType);\n```\n\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.turn();`  komennolla ajopeli kääntyy ikuisesti haluttuun suuntaan kunnes joku uusi komento sen kumoaa tai ohjelma loppuu.\n\nKäytä `LEFT` argumenttia isoilla kirjaimilla, kun käännät vasemmalle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(left);\n```\n\nKäytä `RIGHT` argumenttia isoilla kirjaimilla, kun käännät oikealle.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turn(right);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turn(right);"},"drivetrain_turn_for":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_for","markdown":"# Käänny määrä\n\nKääntää ajopeliä määrätyn määrän asteita.\n\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(turnType, angle, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nEnsimmäinen argumentti komennossa määrää suunnan: `LEFT` (vasemmalle) tai `RIGHT` (oikelle), isoilla kirjaimilla . \n\nToinen argumentti määrää kulman asteina välillä  0 - 360. \n\nKolmas argumentti on käännöksen yksikkö, Se on `DEGREES` (astetta) isoilla kirjaimilla. \n\nKomento`turn_for` on ns blokkaava komento ts se estää seuraavien komentojen suorituksen , kunnes käännös on valmis.\n\n## Lisäparametrit\n\nNeljäs argumetti on ns lisäargumentti `wait=False` , jolloin seuraava komento suoritetaankin heti käännöksen alettua.\n\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(left, 90, degrees, false);\n```\n\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä V5 Robotti kääntyy 270 astetta oikealle.\n\n````cpp\nDrivetrain.turnFor(right, 270, degrees);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnFor(right, 90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_turn_to_heading":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_heading","markdown":"# AJopelin kääntyminen ajosuuntaan\n\nKääntää ajopelin tiettyyn ajosuuntaanhen Gyro tai Inertial sensorin avulla.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading(heading, units);`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading();` komennolla saadaan ajopeli kääntymään mihin tahansa myötäpäivään ajosuuntan.\n\nPohjautuu nykyiseen Gyron ajosuuntaan, `Drivetrain.turnToHeading();` päättelee kääntymissuunnan.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToHeading();` hyväksyy arvot välillä **0.00 - 359.99**, kun yksikö on asteita `degrees`.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli tekee neljä käännöstä: \n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(45.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(90.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(270.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(180.0, degrees);\n```\n\n- Oikealle suuntaan 45 astetta\n- Oikealle suuntaan 90 astetta\n- Oikealle suuntaan 270 astetta\n- vasemmalle suuntaan 180 astetta\n\n**turnToHeading** estää seuraavien komentojen suorituksen kääntymisen ajan.\n\n## Lisäparametri\n\nKun asetat arvon `false` lisäparametrille **turnToHeading** komennolle niin kääntyminesen jälkeinen komento suoritetaan heti.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToHeading(180.0, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnToHeading(90, degrees);"},"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation":{"name":"drivetrain_turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Käännä kiertokulmaa määrän\n\nKääntää ajopeliä kiertokulman tiettyyn astemäärään nykyisen gyron astemäärän perusteella.\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToRotation(rotation, units);`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToRotation();` komentoa voi käyttää kääntämään ajopeliä positiivisen arvolla myötäpäivään tai negatiivisella arvolla vastapäivään.\n\nRiippuen nykyisestä kääntymiskulman arvosta gyrosensorissa `Drivetrain.turnToRotation();` päättelee mihin suuntaan se kääntyy.\n\n`ROTATION` parametri hyväksyy numeerisia rvoja.\n\nNumeeriset arvot eivät **not** rajoita arvoja välillä **0 - 359.99** astetta. Käännökset ovat absoluuttisia ja voivat kääntää robottia enemmän kuin kerran\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä ajopeli tekee 4 käännöstä:\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(90.0, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(180, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnTorotation(-45, degrees);\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(0, degrees);\n```\n\n\n- Oikealla myötäpäivään kohtaan 90 astetta\n- Oikealla myötäpäivään kohtaan 180 astetta\n- Vasemmalle vastapäivään kohtaan -45 astetta\n- Oikealla myötäpäivään kohtaan 0 astetta\n\n`Drivetrain.turnToRotation();` komento estää muita komentojen suorituksen , jos käännös on kesken.\n\n## Lisäparametri \n\nVoit lisä paremetrin `wait=False`, jolloin `Drivetrain.turnToRotation();` komento ei estä seuraavien komentojen suoritukset kesken käännöstä.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.turnToRotation(180.0, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.turnToRotation(90, degrees);"},"events_brain_screen_pressed":{"name":"events_brain_screen_pressed","markdown":"#  Aivojen näyttöä koskettu\n\nSuorittaa ns callback -funktion, kun aivojen kosketusnäyttöä on kosketettu.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.pressed();`  komennon avulla voi laukaista toimintoja, kun näyttöä on koskettu. \n\nYhdessä komennon `Brain.Screen.xPosition();` ja `Brain.Screen.yPosition();` kanssa saadaan interaktiivisuutta robotin ja käyttäjän välille.\n\nEnsiksi pitää luoda funktio sille, kun näyttöä kosketaan ja sen nimi , jota käytetään callback-funktiossa parametrina , kun tapahtuma aktivoituu.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Brain.Screen.pressed(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.pressed(callback);"},"events_brain_screen_released":{"name":"events_brain_screen_released","markdown":"#  Aivojen näyttöä vapautettu\n\nSuorittaa ns callback funktion, kun aivojen kosketusnäyttöä on kosketus vapautetaan.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.released(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.released();` komennon avulla voi laukaista toimintoja näytön kosketuksen vapauttamisessa. \n\nYhdessä komennon `Brain.Screen.xPosition();` ja `Brain.Screen.yPosition();` kanssa saadaan interaktiivisuutta robotin ja käyttäjän välille.\n\nEnsiksi pitää luoda funktio sille, kun näyttöä kosketus loppuu ja nimi , jota käytetään callback-funtiossa parametrina , kun tapahtuma aktivoituu.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Brain.Screen.released(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.released(callback);"},"events_brain_timer_event":{"name":"events_brain_timer_event","markdown":"# Aivojen kello tapahtuma\n\nSuorittaa halutun callback -funktion, kun V5 Aivojen kello on suurempi kuin annettu parametriarvo.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.event(callback, 1000);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nV5 Aivojen kello käynnistyy ohjelman alussa.\n\nMääritä aikaraja tapahtumalle. `Brain.Timer.event();` tapahtuma suoritetaan kerran, kun kello on **suurempi kuin** annettu aikaraja.\n\n`Brain.Timer.event();` hyväskyy kokonaislukuja ja yksikkönä on millisekunnit.\n\nLuo funktio , jota kutsutaan, kun kello on käynyt yli aikarajan. Nimeä funktio ja käytä sitä tapahtuman `callback` parametrina.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Brain.Timer.event(runOnEvent, 2000);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Timer.event(callback, 1000);"},"events_bumper_pressed":{"name":"events_bumper_pressed","markdown":"# Painokytkintä painettu\n\nSuorittaa halutun funktion kun painokytkintä painettu.\n\n```cpp\nBumperA.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuo funktio, jota kutsutaan, kun painokytkintä on painettu. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi ja toiminnot. Nimi välitetään callback - parametrina kun painokytkintä on painettu.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  BumperA.pressed(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`","signature":"BUMPER.pressed(callback);"},"events_bumper_released":{"name":"events_bumper_released","markdown":"## Painokytkin vapautettu\n\nSuorittaa halutun funktion kun painokytkin vapautetaan\n\n```cpp\nBumperA.released(callback);\n```\n\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuo funktio, jota kutsutaan, kun painokytkin on vapautettu. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi ja toiminnot. Nimi välitetään callback - parametrina kun painokytkin on vapautettu.\n\n``cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  BumperA.released(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"BUMPER.released(callback);"},"events_competition_autonomous":{"name":"events_competition_autonomous","markdown":"# Kilpailu automaattikäynnistys\n\nSuorittaa halutun funktion kun \"automaatti\" moodi signaali on kilpailuajon alussa saatu.\n\n``cpp\nCompetition.autonomous(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nUusi kilpailu esiintymä voidaan luoda. kun  **driver_control** ja **automaatti** callback functiot on saatu.\n\nLuo **automaatti** funktio, joka toimii kilpailutilanteessa. \n\nTämä **automaatti** funktio suoritetaan kun \"automaatti\" moodi signaali on kilpailussa saatu.\n\nvarmista että kilpailuohjekti on määritelty tai käytä valmista mallia esimerkit ohjelmista.\n\n``cpp\n//Create a Competition Object\ncompetition Competition;\n\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Competition.autonomous(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"Competition.autonomous(callback);"},"events_competition_drivercontrol":{"name":"events_competition_drivercontrol","markdown":"# Kilpailu ohjainkäynnistys\n\nSuorittaa halutun funktion kun \"ohjainajo\" moodi signaali on kilpailuajon alussa saatu.\n\n```cpp\nCompetition.drivercontrol(callback);\n```\n\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nUusi kilpailu esiintymä voidaan luoda kun  **ohjainajo** ja **automaatti** callback -funktiot on saatu.\n\nLuo **ohjainkäynnistys** funktio, joka toimii kilpailutilanteessa. \n\n``cpp\n//Create a Competition Object\ncompetition Competition;\n\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Competition.drivercontrol(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"Competition.drivercontrol(callback);"},"events_competition_new_competition":{"name":"events_competition_new_competition","markdown":"# Uusi kilpailu\n\nLuo uusi kilapilu ilmentymä (ohjelma).\n\n```cpp\ncompetition Competition = competition();\n\ncompetition Competition;\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nLuo uusi kilpailu ilmentymä ottamalla ohjelmaan mukaan **driver_control** ja **autonomous** callback -funktiot.\n\nKun **driver control** signaali kilpailukytkimestä saadaan, niin suoritetaan **driver_control** callback funktio.\n\nVastaavasti, kun **autonomous** signaali kilpailukytkimestä saadaan, niin suoritetaan **autonomous** callback funktio.\n\n`\n```cpp\n// Create a new Competition instance\ncompetition Competition;\n\n// Function to run when the \"autonomous\" signal is received\nvoid runOnAutonomous() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Running autonomous\");\n}\n\n// Function to run when the \"driver control\" signal is received\nvoid runOnDriverControl() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Running driver control\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register competition event with callback functions.\n  Competition.autonomous(runOnAutonomous);\n  Competition.drivercontrol(runOnDriverControl);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"competition Competition = competition();"},"events_controller_axis_changed":{"name":"events_controller_axis_changed","markdown":"# Ohjaimen tatin asentoa muutettu\n\nSuorittaa määrätyn funktion, kun ohjaimen tatin asentoa muutettu.\n\n```cpp\nController1.Axis1.changed(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse ohjaimen tatti, jota käsitellään.\n\n* `Axis1`\n* `Axis2`\n* `Axis3`\n* `Axis4`\n\nLuo funktio ohjaimen tatille , joka käsittelee tatin käyttöä. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi, jota käytetään `callback` parametrissa, kun tatin asentoa on muutettu kutsuttaessa itse funktiota.\n\n`\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Controller1.Axis1.changed(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.AXIS.changed(callback);"},"events_controller_button_pressed":{"name":"events_controller_button_pressed","markdown":"# Ohjaimen nappia painettu\n\nSuorittaa tietyn funktion kun Ohjaimen tiettyä nappia on painettu.\n\n```cpp\nController1.ButtonA.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nValitse ohjaimen nappi (kts ohjaimesta merkinnät napeille).\n\n* `ButtonA`\n* `ButtonB`\n* `ButtonX`\n* `ButtonY`\n* `ButtonUp`\n* `ButtonDown`\n* `ButtonLeft`\n* `ButtonRight`\n* `ButtonL1`\n* `ButtonL2`\n* `ButtonR1`\n* `ButtonR2`\n\nLuo funktio , jota kutsutaan kun ohjaimen ko. nappia on painetttu. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi, joka välitetään kutsuparametrissa, kun funktion toiminta suoritetaan nappia painettaessa.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Controller1.ButtonA.pressed(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.BUTTON.pressed(callback);"},"events_controller_button_released":{"name":"events_controller_button_released","markdown":"# Controller Button Released\n\nRuns the specified function when the controller button is released.\n\n```cpp\nController1.ButtonA.released(callback);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Controller button to monitor.\n\n* `ButtonA`\n* `ButtonB`\n* `ButtonX`\n* `ButtonY`\n* `ButtonUp`\n* `ButtonDown`\n* `ButtonLeft`\n* `ButtonRight`\n* `ButtonL1`\n* `ButtonL2`\n* `ButtonR1`\n* `ButtonR2`\n\nYou will need to create a function to call when the Controller Button is released. Provide the name of the function that should run when the event occurs as the `callback` parameter.\n\n```cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  Controller1.ButtonA.released(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.BUTTON.released(callback);"},"events_event":{"name":"events_event","markdown":"# Tapahtuma rekistöröi callback funtion\n\nRekistöröi callback -function käynnistyksen kun käyttäjätapahtuma on annettu.\n\n``cpp\nEvent(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nRekisteröi callback -funktio nimettyyn käyttäjätapahtumaan.\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"myEvent triggered runOnBroadcast callback\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create a new event.\n  event myEvent;\n\n  // Register a callback function to the myEvent event.\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast);\n\n  // Broadcast the event.\n  myEvent.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"EVENT(callback);"},"events_event_broadcast":{"name":"events_event_broadcast","markdown":"# Tapahtuman lähetys\n\nLähettää tapahtumaviestin käynnistää vastaavan tapahtumafunktion.\n\n\n```cpp\nEvent.broadcast();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOhjelma jatkaa suoritusta samaan aikaan kun `Event.broadcast();` komentoa suoritetaan kutsutun callback-funtion osalta.\n\nEnnen kutsun käyttöä pitää tapahtuma olla määritelty ja rekistöröidä vastaava vähintää yksi callback-funtio.\n\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast1() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\");\n}\n\nvoid runOnBroadcast2() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create a new event.\n  event myEvent;\n\n  // Register callback functions to event.\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast1);\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast2);\n\n  // Broadcast the event.\n  myEvent.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"EVENT.broadcast();"},"events_event_broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"events_event_broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"## Tapahtuman lähetys ja odota\n\nLähettää tapahtumaviestin käynnistää vastaavan tapahtumafunktion ja odottaa kunnes funktion toimenpiteet tehty.\n\n```cpp\nEvent.broadcastAndWait();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Event.broadcastAndWait();` ohjelma odottaa kun komentoa suoritetaan kutsutun callback-funtion osalta. \n\nEnnen kutsun käyttöä pitää tapahtuma olla määritelty ja rekistöröidä vastaava vähintää yksi callback-funtio.\n\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast1() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\");\n}\n\nvoid runOnBroadcast2() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create a new event.\n  event myEvent;\n\n  // Register callback functions to event.\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast1);\n  myEvent(runOnBroadcast2);\n\n  // Broadcast the event and wait for completion.\n  myEvent.broadcastAndWait();\n\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(3, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Listeners finished running\");\n}\n```","signature":"EVENT.broadcastAndWait();"},"events_event_new_event":{"name":"events_event_new_event","markdown":"# Uusi tapahtuma\n\nLuo uusi tapahtuma.\n\n```cpp\nevent myEvent = event();\n\nevent myEvent;\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKäyttämällä allaolevaa syntaksia uusi käyttäjätapahtuma luodaan ennenkuin se toteuttava callback functio luodaan.\n\n```cpp\nvoid runOnBroadcast1() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast1 Running\");\n}\n\nvoid runOnBroadcast2() {\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Broadcast2 Running\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Create new events.\n  event myEvent1 = event();\n  event myEvent2;\n\n\n  // Register callback functions to the events.\n  myEvent1(runOnBroadcast1);\n  myEvent2(runOnBroadcast2);\n\n  // Broadcast the events.\n  myEvent1.broadcast();\n  myEvent2.broadcast();\n}\n```","signature":"event Event = new event();"},"events_limit_pressed":{"name":"events_limit_pressed","markdown":"# Limit Switch painettu\n\nSuoritetaan määritelty funktio kun Limit Switch painettu.\n\n```cpp\nLimitA.pressed(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nSensorin painallusta varten pitää määritellä funktio , jota kutsutaan painalluksen jälkeen. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi ja määrittele sen toiminta, kun tapahtuma Limit Switch painettu . Kyseessä on ns `callback` parametri tapahtumalle.\n\n``cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  LimitA.pressed(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"LIMIT.pressed(callback);"},"events_limit_released":{"name":"events_limit_released","markdown":"# Limit Switch vapautettu\n\nSuoritetaan määritelty funktio kun Limit Switch vapautettu.\n\n```cpp\nLimitA.released(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nSensorin painallusta varten pitää määritellä funktio , jota kutsutaan vapautuksen jälkeen. \n\nAnna funktiolle nimi ja määrittele sen toiminta, kun tapahtuma Limit Switch vapautettu . Kyseessä on ns `callback` parametri tapahtumalle.\n\n``cpp\n//Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Event has occurred\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function.\n  LimitA.released(runOnEvent);\n\n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running.\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"LIMIT.released(callback);"},"events_optical_object_detected":{"name":"events_optical_object_detected","markdown":"# Optical löytää esineen\n\nSuorittaa callback funktion kun V5 Optical Sensori havaitsee esineen/kohteen.\n\n\n```cpp\nOptical.objectDetected(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`optical.object_detected` komentoa voi käyttää triggeröimään haluttuja toimintoja kun V5 Optical Sensori havaitsee kohteen/esineen.\n\nSinun pitää luoda funktio, joka suoritetaan kun esine havaitaan. Anna funktiolle nimi , joka annetaan **callback** parametrissa ja suoritetaan kun esine havaitaan.\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Object detected!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.objectDetected(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.objectDetected(callback);"},"events_optical_object_lost":{"name":"events_optical_object_lost","markdown":"# Optical kohde hävisi\n\nAjetaan callback funktio, kun V5 Optical Sensori kadottaa äskeisen esineen.\n```cpp\nOptical.objectLost(callback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`optical.object_lost` komento käynnistää halutut toimenpiteet, kun V5 Optical sensori ei enää havaitse kohdetta/esinettä.\n\nLuo funktio, jota kutsutaan kun esinettä ei enää havaita. Anna funktiolle nimi , joka kutsutaan, kun tapahtuma ilmenee **callback** parametrissa.\n\n\n```cpp\n// Function to run when the event occurs\nvoid runOnEvent() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Object lost!\");\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Register event with a callback function\n  Optical.objectLost(runOnEvent);\n  \n  while (true) {\n    // Keep the main program running\n    wait(0.05, seconds);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.objectLost(callback);"},"function_name":{"name":"function_name","markdown":"# Funktiot\n\nFunktiot on joukko komentoja/koodinippuja , jotka suorittavat jonkin määrätyn tehtävän.\n\n```don\ndef my_function():\n    pass\n```\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKun luot funktion anna sille kuvaava nimi, joka kuvaa sen toimintaa.\n\nMäärittele, mitä muotoa tietoa olevaa tietoa se palauttaa. Muodot - `int`, `float`, `double`, ja `string` ovat tyypillisimmät. Jos funktio ei palauta , määrittele se muotoa `void`.\n\nSisällytä sulut `()` lisä *parametreille* funtionimen jälkeen. Useampi parametri erotellaan pilkulla (parameter1, parameter2).\n\nFunktion runko kirjoitetaan aaltosulkujen `{ }` sisään.\n\n```cpp\nint returnZero() {\n  return 0;\n}\n```\n\n## Esimerkki \n\nTällä 'void' funktiolla ei ole parametreja ja se tulostaa \"The battery is low!\" V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n\n```cpp\nvoid lowOnBattery() {\n  if (Brain.Battery.capacity() < 25.0) {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"The battery is low!\");\n  }\n}\n```\n```","signature":"function_name"},"function_thread":{"name":"function_thread","markdown":"# Säikeet\n\nAntaa suorittaa useamman säikeen yhtäaikaa.\n\n```cpp\nthread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMäärittele funktio ja tee callback kutsu säikeelle.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myThreadCallback() {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"In a different thread!\");\n}\n```\nKun funktio on kirjoitettu, voi käyttää sitä uudelle säikeelle. Tätä kutsutaan  **callback funktioksi**.\n\n```cpp\nthread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n```\n**thread** alkaa toimimaan heti, kun se on kirjoitettu. Se toimii yhtäaikaa kuin pääsäie.\n    \n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan kaksi laskuriarvoa VEX V5 aivojen näytölle samaan aikaan. Toisen tulostaa thread säijeosa tekstin `myThread`. Toisen taas pääsäie samaan aikaan.\n\n```cpp\nvoid myThreadCallback() {\n  int count = 0;\n  while (true) {\n    Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"thread1: %d\", count);\n    count++;\n    // Wait to allow the main thread to execute\n    wait(25, msec);\n  }\n}\n\nint main() {\n  // Once a thread is created it begins executing\n  thread myThread = thread(myThreadCallback);\n  \n  int count = 0;\n  while (true) {\n    Brain.Screen.setCursor(2, 1);\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"main: %d\", count);\n    count++;\n    // Wait to allow myThread to execute\n    wait(25, msec);\n  }\n}\n```","signature":"function_thread"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Tyhjää rivi\n\nTyhjää yksittäisen rivin V5 aivojen tai ohjaimen näytöllä.\n\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTyhjää nykyisen kursoririvin.\n\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine();\n```\n\nTyhjää tietyn rivin 1 näytöllä.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearLine(1);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.clearLine();` komento hyväksyy arvot välillä **1 - 20**, jonka rivin tyhjää. Ilman rivinumero komento tyhjää nykyisen rivin.\n\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of lines available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Aivojen fonttikoko - rivimäärä:**\n\n* `mono12` - 20 riviä\n* `mono15` - 16 riviä\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 12 riviä (oletus)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 8 riviä\n* `mono40` / `prop40` - 6 riviä\n* `mono60` / `prop60` - 4 riviä\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_clear_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.clearLine();"},"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Tyhjää V5 aivojen näyttö\n\nTyhjää koko V5 aivojen näytön.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.clearScreen();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.clearScreen();` komento ei muuta kursorin paikkaa näytöllä. Käytä `Brain.Screen.setCursor();` komentoa, jos haluat muuttaa kursorin paikkaa.","signature":"Brain.Screen.clearScreen();"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_circle","markdown":"# Piirrä ympyrä\n\nPiirtää ympyrän V5 näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawCircle(1, 1, 10);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `brain.screen.draw_circle()` vaatii kolme arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: Keskipiste X\n* Arvo 2: Keskipiste Y\n* Arvo 3: Ympyrän säde (pikseleinä)\n\nKomento `Brain.Screen.setPenColor(); määrittää kehän värin, oletuksena on valkoinen.\n\nKomento `Brain.Screen.setFillColor(); määrittää täyttövärin, oletuksena on musta.\n\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawCircle(1, 1, 10);"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_line","markdown":"# Piirrä viiva\n\nPiirtää viivan V5 aivojen näytölle.\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawLine(1, 1, 10, 10);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.drawLine();` komeNto vaatii 4 arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: Alkupiste X koordinaatti\n* Arvo 2: Alkupiste Y koordinaatti\n* Arvo 3: Loppupiste X koordinaatti\n* Arvo 4: Loppupiste Y koordinaatti\n\nViivan väri määrätään komennolla `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();`. Oletuksena on valkoinen viiva.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawLine(1, 1, 10, 10);"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel","markdown":"# Piirrä Pikseli (väripiste)\n\nPiirtää pikselin V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawPixel(1, 1);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `Brain.Screen.drawPixel();` vaatii 2 arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: X koorditaatti\n* Arvo 2: Y koorditaatti\n\nPikselin väri asetetaan komennolla `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();`. Oletusväri on valkoinen.\n\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawPixel(1, 1);"},"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Piirrä suorakulmio\n\nPiirtää suorakulmion V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.drawRectangle(1, 1, 10, 10);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `Brain.Screen.drawRectangle();' vaatii 4 arvoa:\n\n* Arvo 1: Ylä vasen nurkka X koordinaatti\n* Arvo 2: Ylä vasen nurkka Y koordinaatti\n* Arvo 3: Leveys kulmiolle\n* Arvoe 4: Korkaus kulmiolle\n\nKomento `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` määrää reunaviivan värin. Oletus on valkoinen.\n\nTäyttöväri saadaan komennolla `Brain.Screen.setFillColor();`. Oletus on musta täyttöväri.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.drawRectangle(1, 1, 10, 10);"},"looks_brain_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Aivojen näytölle uusi rivi\n\nSiirtää näytöllä kursoria seuraavalle riville.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOletuksena aina kursori on ensimmäisen rivin ensimmäisessä sarakkeessa. Komento `Brain.Screen.newLine();` siirtää kursoria yhden rivin alemmaksi. Komento `Brain.Screen.newLine();` asetaa aina kursorin ensimmäiseen sarakkeeseen.\n\n---\n\nV5 Aivoille tulostettaessa voit valita kirjaisinlajin ja koon. Valinnat vaikuttavat, kuinka monta riviä ja saraketta näytölle mahtuu seuraavasti:\n\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* `mono12` - 20 riviä\n* `mono15` - 16 riviä\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 12 riviä (Oletus)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 8 riviä\n* `mono40` / `prop40`  - 6 riviä\n* `mono60` / `prop60`  - 6 riviä\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_new_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.newLine();"},"looks_brain_screen_print":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_print","markdown":"# Tulosta\n\nTulostaa arvoja tai tekstiä V5 Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Hello World\");\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `Brain.Screen.print();` tulostaa dataa kursorin kohdalle näyttöä.\n\nKaikkien ohjelmien alussa paikka on rivi 1 sarake 1.\n\n## Tulostus arvot\n\nVoit käyttää muotoilumerkkejä print komennossasi:\n\n* `%d` - Etumerkillinen desimaaliluku\n* `%f` - Liukuluku \n* `%o` - Etumerkillinen oktaaliluku\n* `%s` - Merkkijono\n* `%x` - Etumerkitön hexadesimaaliluku\n* `%c` - Merkki\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Time Elapsed %f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```\n\nTulostettaessa voi määritellä myös desimaalien määrän. Piin koko arvo `3.14159265` voidaan kirjoittaa muodossa`3.14` kun käytät muotoilua `%.2f`.\n\nLukumäärä ennen desimaalia muotoilussa monellako merkillä tulostetaan. Jos tulostus on lyhyempi kuin muotoilu edellyttää, niin puuttuvat merkit täytetään tyhjillä.\n\nMuotoilulauseke voi sisältää myös lippuja, leveyden , tarkkuuden ja alimuotoiluja:\n\n* `%d`\t- Tulostaa desimaaliluvun\n* `%6d`\t- Tulostaa desimaaliluvun maksimissaan 6 merkkiä leveä\n* `%f`\t- Tulostaa liukuluvun\n* `%6f`\t- Tulostaa liukuluvun maksimissaan 6 merkkiä leveä\n* `%.2f`  - Tulostaa liukuluvun 2 desimaalilla\n* `%6.2f` - Tulostaa liukuluvun vähintään 6 merkkiä leveä ja kahdella desimaalilla\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Time Elapsed %8.2f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.print(\"Hello\");"},"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Cursor\n\nSets the cursor location for `Brain.Screen.print();` command on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setCursor(1, 2);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setCursor();` command requires 2 values:\n\n* Value 1: Screen row position \n* Value 2: Screen column position\n\nSet the cursor's row and column position to have a `Brain.Screen.print();` command display at a specific location on the screen.\n\nAccepts a range for **row** of **1 to 20**.\n\nAccepts a range for **column** of **1 to 80**.\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows and columns available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* `mono12` - 20 Rows\n* `mono15` - 16 Rows\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 12 Rows (Default)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 8 Rows\n* `mono40` / `prop40` - 6 Rows\n* `mono60` / `prop60` - 4 Rows\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Columns:**\n\n* `mono12` - 80 Columns\n* `mono15` - 68 Columns\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 48 Columns (Default)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 32 Columns\n* `mono40` / `prop40` - 24 Columns\n* `mono60` / `prop60` - 16 Columns\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_fill_color","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Fill Color\n\nSets the color that fills in shapes drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setFillColor(red);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setFillColor();` command is used to set the color of the inside of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\nYou can select from the following colors\n\n* black\n* white\n* red\n* green\n* blue\n* yellow\n* orange\n* purple\n* cyan\n* transparent\n\nThe fill color will be used for any next objects drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.","signature":"Brain.Screen.setFillColor(red);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_font":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_font","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Font\n\nSets the style and size of font used on the V5 Brain's screen when printing numbers or text.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setFont(monoM);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThere are two different types of fonts available on the V5 Brain's screen:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - each character takes up the same width.\n* Proportional (Prop) - each character takes up different size widths based on the character.\n\nChoose which font type and size to use. You can select from the following font options.\n\n* `mono12`\n* `mono15`\n* `mono20`\n* `mono30`\n* `mono40`\n* `mono60`\n* `prop20`\n* `prop30`\n* `prop40`\n* `prop60`\n\nThe new font size will be used for any future text written to the V5 Brain's screen.","signature":"Brain.Screen.setFont(monoM);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_color","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Pen Color\n\nSets the color of lines drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setPenColor(black);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` command is used to set the color of lines, pixels, and text drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\n`Brain.Screen.setPenColor();` will also be used to set the color the outline of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\nYou can select from the following colors\n\n* `black`\n* `white`\n* `red`\n* `green`\n* `blue`\n* `yellow`\n* `orange`\n* `purple`\n* `cyan`\n\nThe pen color will be used for any next objects drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.","signature":"Brain.Screen.setPenColor(red);"},"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width":{"name":"looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width","markdown":"# Brain Screen Set Pen Width\n\nSets the width of the outline for shapes drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.setPenWidth(5);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setPenWidth();` command is used to set the width of the line on the outside of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen. \n\nThe `Brain.Screen.setPenWidth();` command can accept integer values, with a larger value equating to a larger width.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_brain_screen_set_pen_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.setPenWidth(10);"},"looks_console_clear_console":{"name":"looks_console_clear_console","markdown":"# Console Clear\n\nClears the Print Console and resets the cursor.\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"\\033[2J\\n\");\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nUsing the `printf` command with the special `\\033[2J` escape sequence and code will clear the Print Console.\n\nThe newline character, `\\n` is needed in a `printf` command to output the contents of the Print Console buffer into the Print Console. In this instance, the Print Console will be immediately updated/cleared when this command is executed.\n\n## Example\n\nThe example below will print `VEXcode` to the Print Console, wait 2 seconds, and then clear the Console.\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"VEXcode\\n\");\nwait(2, seconds);\nprintf(\"\\033[2J\\n\");\n```","signature":"printf(\"\\033[2J\\n\");"},"looks_console_print":{"name":"looks_console_print","markdown":"# Console Print\n\nPrints values or text to the Print Console\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"VEXcode\");\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `printf` command will print data at the cursor location on the Print Console.\n\nAll new projects begin with the cursor at row 1.\n\nThe newline character, `\\n` is needed in a `printf` command to output the contents of the Print Console buffer into the Print Console.\n\n## Printing Values\n\nYou can use format specifiers to show values inside of your print statements:\n\n* `%d` - Signed decimal integer\n* `%f` - Decimal floating point number\n* `%o` - Signed octal\n* `%s` - String of characters\n* `%x` - Unsigned hexadecimal integer\n* `%c` - Character\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"Time Elapsed %f\\n\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```\n\nWhen displaying values, you can specify how many decimals places to print. For example, if your value is `3.14159265`, but you only want to display `3.14`, your format specifier would be `%.2f`.\n\nThe number before the decimal in the format specifier denotes the total number of characters to be printed. If the value being printed is shorter than the total number of characters to be printed, the printed value is padded with blank spaces.\n\nThe format specifier can also contain flags, width, precision and modifiers sub-specifiers:\n\n* `%d`\t- Prints a decimal integer\n* `%6d`\t- Prints a decimal integer, with a minimum of 6 characters wide\n* `%f`\t- Prints a floating point number\n* `%6f`\t- Prints a floating point number, with a minimum of 6 characters wide\n* `%.2f`  - Prints a floating point number, with 2 decimal characters places\n* `%6.2f` - Prints a floating point number, with a minimum of 6 characters wide and 2 decimal places\n\n```cpp\nprintf(\"Screen Pressed? %s\\n\", Brain.Screen.pressing());\n```\n\n## Printing Colors\n\nYou can use any of the color codes below with a `printf` command to set the color of the text being printed. The example below will show two ways in which a color sequence command can be used when printing. All color codes will need to be attached to an escape sequence - `\\033`.\n\n* `[31m` - Red\n* `[32m` - Green\n* `[34m` - Blue\n* `[30m` - Black\n* `[37m` - White\n* `[33m` - Yellow\n* `[91m` - Orange\n* `[35m` - Purple\n* `[36m` - Cyan\n* `[97m` - Transparent\n\n```cpp\n// Using color codes in-line\n// This will print \"VEXcode\" in Red to the Print Console\nprintf(\"\\033[31m VEXcode\\n\");\n\n// Using color codes in separate commands\nprintf(\"\\033[31m\");\nprintf(\"VEXcode\\n\");\n```","signature":"printf(\"VEXcode\");"},"looks_controller_rumble":{"name":"looks_controller_rumble","markdown":"# Ohjainvärinä\n\nLaittaa V5 ohjaimen värisemään.\n\n```cpp\nController.rumble(\".-.-\");\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Controller.rumble();` komento käyttää V5 ohjaimen värinämoottoria.\n\nVoit säätää värinää \".\" ja \"-\" merkeillä. Merkki \".\" luo lyhyen ja merkki \"-\" pitkän värinän.\n\nVoit käyttää myös esimääriteltyjä optioita:\n\n* `rumbleLong` on sama kuin `\"----\"`\n* `rumbleShort` on sama kuin `\"....\"` \n* `rumblePulse` on sama kuin `\"-.-.\"`\n\n```cpp\n// The following two lines of code will do the same thing\nController.rumble(\"....\");\nController.rumble(rumbleShort);\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.rumble(rumbleShort);"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_line","markdown":"# Tyhjää ohjaimen näytön rivi\n\nTyhjää ohjaimen näytön.\n```cpp\nController.Screen.clearLine(1);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Controller.Screen.clearLine();` ei muuta kursoripaikkaa näytöllä. \n\nHalutessasi käytä `Controller.Screen.clearLine();` komentoa asettamaan kursorin haluttuun rivipaikkaan välillä **1 - 3**.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.clearLine();\n```\n\nTyhjää tietyn rivin .\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.clearLine(1);\n```\n\nV5 Ohjaimen näytöllä ei voi muuttaa fonttikokoa.\n\n**V5 Ohjain fonttikoko - Rivimäärä:**\n\n* Standardi Fontti - 3 riviä (Oletus)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_controller_screen_clear_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.clearLine();"},"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_clear_screen","markdown":"# Tyhjää ohjaimen näytön rivit\n\nTyhjää ohjaimen näytön.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.clearScreen();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Controller.Screen.clearScreen();` ei muuta kursoripaikkaa näytöllä. \n\nHalutessai käytä `Controller.Screen.setCursor();` kometoa asettamaan kursorin haluttuun paikkaan.\n\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.clearScreen();\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.clearScreen();"},"looks_controller_screen_new_line":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_new_line","markdown":"# Ohjaimen kursori uudelle riville\n\nAsetaa tulostusta varten kursorin uudelle riville ohjaimen näytöllä.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOletuksena ohjelman alussa kursori on rivillä 1 sarakkeessa 1. `Controller.Screen.newLine();` komennolla kursori siirtyy seuraavalle riville ohjaimen näytöllä rivin ensimmäiselle sarakkeelle.\n\n---\n\nV5 ohjainen näytön tulostusfonttia ei voi muuttaa.\n\n**V5 Ohjaimen fonttikoko - Rivien määrä:**\n\n* Standardi Fontti - 3 riviä (oletus)\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_controller_screen_new_line/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.newLine();"},"looks_controller_screen_print":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_print","markdown":"# Ohajimen näytölle tulostus\n\nTulostaa arvoja V5 ohjaimen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.print(\"Hello World\");\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Controller.Screen.print();` komento tulostaa dataa kursorin kohdalle näytöllä.\n\nAina ohjelman alussa paikka on rivi 1 sarake 1.\n\n## Printing Values\n\nVoit käyttää format tarkennuksia tulostuksessa seuraavasti:\n\n* `%d` - Etumerkillinen Desimaali / Kokonaisluku\n* `%f` - Liukuluku\n* `%o` - etumerkillinen oktaali kokonaisluku\n* `%s` - Tekstijono\n* `%x` - eutumerkitön hexadecimaaliluku\n* `%c` - Merkki\n\n```cpp\nController1.Screen.print(\"Timer: %f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```\n\nTulostettavat arvoille voit määrittää desimaalien määrän, arvolle  `3.14159265` voit halutessa tulostaa kahdella desimaalilla `3.14` antamalla formaattitarkennin `%.2f`.\n\nNumero ennen desimaalia kertoo montako merkkiä haluat tulostaa, kun taas numero desimaalimerkin jälkeen kertoo monellako desimaalilla tulostetaan.\n\nFormaattitarkennin voi sisältää myös muita tarkennuksia lippuja, leveys, tarkkuus ja alitarkentimia:\n\n* `%d`\t- Tulostaa desimaali(kokonais)luvun\n* `%6d`\t- Tulostaa desimaaliluvun vähintään 6 merkin leveydellä\n* `%f`\t- Tulostaa liukuluvun\n* `%6f`\t- Tulostaa liukuluvun vähintään 6 merkin leveydellä\n* `%.2f`  - Tulostaa liukuluvun kahdella desimaalilla\n* `%6.2f` - Tulostaa desimaaliluvun vähintään 6 merkin leveydellä kahdella desimaalilla\n\n```cpp\nController1.Screen.print(\"Timer: %8.2f\", Brain.Timer.value());\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.print(\"Hello\");"},"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor":{"name":"looks_controller_screen_set_cursor","markdown":"# Aseta kursoripaikka\n\n\nAsettaa kursorin paikan ohjaimen näytöllä komentoa **Controller.Screen.print();** varten.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.setCursor(1, 2);\n```\n\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento `controller.screen.setCursor()` vaatii 2 arvoa:\n\n* Value 1: Näytön rivi \n* Value 2: Näytön sarake\n\nAsettamalla kursoriksi sopiva rivi ja sarake saat tulostettua komennolla `controller.screen.print()` haluttuun kohtaan näyttöä.\n\n`Controller.Screen.setCursor();` hyväksyy rivin **row** välillä **1 - 3**.\n\n`Controller.Screen.setCursor();` hyväksyy sarakkeen **column** välillä **1 - 20**.\n\n---\n\nV5 Ohjainnäytölle ei voi muuttaa fontin kokoa.\n\n**V5 Ohjain Fontin koko - Rivien määrä:**\n\n* Standard Fontti - 3 riviä (Oletus)\n\n**V5 Ohjain Fontin koko - Sarakkeiden määrä**\n\n* Standard Fontti - 20 Saraketta (Oletus)\n* Value 1: Screen row position \n* Value 2: Screen column position\n\n\n![controller_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/looks_controller_screen_set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);"},"looks_led_off":{"name":"looks_led_off","markdown":"# LED pois\n\nSammuttaa 3-lanka LED pois päältä.\n\n```cpp\nLedA.off();\n```","signature":"LED.off();"},"looks_led_on":{"name":"looks_led_on","markdown":"# LED Päälle\n\nLaittaa 3-lanka LED päälle.\n\n```cpp\nLedA.on();\n```","signature":"LED.on();"},"looks_led_set":{"name":"looks_led_set","markdown":"# Set LED\n\nSets the state of an LED to either *true* (on) or *false* (off).\n\n```cpp\nLEDA.set(true);\nLEDA.set(false);\n```","signature":"LED.set();"},"magnet_drop":{"name":"magnet_drop","markdown":"# Sähkömagneetti pudottaa\n\nAntaa sähömagneetille käskyn pudottaa siinä oleva esine.\n\n```\nMagnet.drop()\n```\nKun komento `magnet.drop()` on suoritettu, pitää magneetin jäähtyä ennen uutta käyttöä.\n\n## Miten käytetään esimerkki\n\nPoimitaan esine , ajetaan robottia eteenpäin ja käytetään `magnet.drop()` komentoa esineen pudotukseen.\n\n```cpp\nMagnet.pickup();\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);\nMagnet.drop();\n```","signature":"MAGNET.drop();"},"magnet_pickup":{"name":"magnet_pickup","markdown":"# Sähkömagneetin avulla poiminta\n\nAntaa käskyn V5 sähkömagneetille poimia esine.\n\n```\nMagnet.pickup();\n```\nKomennon `magnet.pickup()` jälkeen pitää magneetin jäähtyä ennen seuraavaa magneettikomentoa.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä `magnet.pickup()` poimii esineen , ajopeli aja eteenpäin ja pudottaa esineen.\n\n```cpp\nMagnet.pickup();\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 200, mm);\nMagnet.drop();\n```","signature":"MAGNET.pickup();"},"magnet_set_power":{"name":"magnet_set_power","markdown":"# Aseta sähkömagneetin voima\n\nMuuttaa sähkömagneetin tarttumiskykyvoimaa\n\n```cpp\nMagnet.setPower(power);\n```\n\nVoimaa voi säätää välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä `magnet.set_power()` komennolla asetetaan täsyi 100 % teho, pomitaan esine , ajetaan eteenpäin ja pudotetaan esine.\n\n```cpp\nMagnet.setPower(100);\nMagnet.pickup();\n```","signature":"MAGNET.setPower(100);"},"motion_motor393_set_reversed":{"name":"motion_motor393_set_reversed","markdown":"# Motor393.setReversed();\n\nMuttaa pyörimissuunnan vastakkaiseen moottorissa Motor 393 , joka kiinnitetty Motor Controller 29 laitteeseen.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.setReversed();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomennolla moottori pyörii vastakkaiseen suuntaan.\n\n`Motor393.setReversed();` hyväksyy Boolean argumentit `true` ja `false`.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nSeuraavassa esimerkissä moottori pyörii taaksepäin `Motor393.setReversed();` komennon mukaan.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.setReversed(true);\nMotor393.spin(forward);\n```","signature":"MOTOR393.setReversed(true);"},"motion_motor393_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor393_set_velocity","markdown":"# Motor393 Aseta nopeus\n\nAsettaa Motor393 nopeuden. Laite yhdistetty laitteeseen Motor Controller 29.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.setVelocity(velocity, percent);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nNopeus paramtri hyväksyy arvot välillä **-100% - 100%.** \n\nJos asettaa Motor393 laitteeen nopeudeksi negatiivisen arvon, moottori pyörii taaksepäin.\n\nTOheisessa esimerkissä moottori pyörii taaksepäin vaikka se on asetettu parametriarvoon`forward`.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.set_velocity(-100, percent);\nMotor393.spin(forward);\n```\n\nJos asetaa nopeuden arvoksi 0, moottori pysähtyy.","signature":"MOTOR393.setVelocity(50, percent);"},"motion_motor393_spin":{"name":"motion_motor393_spin","markdown":"# Motor393 Spin\n\nSpins a Motor393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.spin(forward);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThis command spins a Motor393 forever, until a new motor command is used or the program is stopped.\n\nChoose which direction the motor will spin to by setting the direction parameter to either `forward` or `reverse`.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.spin(forward);\n```","signature":"MOTOR393.spin(forward);"},"motion_motor393_stop":{"name":"motion_motor393_stop","markdown":"# Motor393 Pysäytä\n\nPysäyttää Motor393 , joka on liitetty Motor Controller 29 laitteeseen.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.stop();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento pysäyttää Motor393 laitteen pyörimisen.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nMotor393 pyörii 3 sekuntia ennen kuin se pysähtyy.\n\n```cpp\nMotor393.spin(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nMotor393.stop();\n```","signature":"MOTOR393.stop();"},"motion_motor_set_max_torque":{"name":"motion_motor_set_max_torque","markdown":"# Aseta maksimi moottorin vääntö\n\nAsettaa V5 älymoottorin masimi väännön.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setMaxTorque(value, units);\n``\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento sallii arvot välillä 0% - 100%.\n\nMaksimi moottorin vääntö -komento sallii desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja sekä numeerisia arvoja.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä kouramoottori liikkuu asentoon 40 astetta maksimi moottorin väännöllä 20 %, jolloin tarttuessa esineeseen moottori ei riko esinettä.\n\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setMaxTorque(20, percent);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(40, degrees);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.setMaxTorque(50, percent);"},"motion_motor_set_position":{"name":"motion_motor_set_position","markdown":"# Moottorin asennon asetus\n\nAsettaa V5 Älymoottorin kierrosmittarille (encoder) arvon.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setPosition(position, units);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.setPosition();` komennolle voi asettaa V5 Älymoottorin kierrosmittarille (encoder) halutun arvon.\n\n`Motor.setPosition();` komentoa käytetään tyypillisesti, kun nollataan asento.\n\nVoit käyttää 'position` arvona mitä tahansa numeroa. \n\nYksikkönä voi käyttää joko `degrees`(astetta) tai `turns` (kierroksia). \n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.setPosition(50, degrees);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.setPosition(0, degrees);"},"motion_motor_set_stopping":{"name":"motion_motor_set_stopping","markdown":"# Moottorin pysähtymistapa\n\nAsettaa V5 moottorin pysähtymistavan. \n\n```cpp\nMotor.setStopping(brakeType);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`MODE` parametrissa voi asettaa jonkun seuraavista tavoista:\n\n* BRAKE: moottori pysähtyy heti.\n* COAST: moottori pysähtyy vaiheittain.\n* HOLD: moottori pysähtyy herti ja pitää paikan vaikka joku ulkoinen voima sitä yrittää siirtää esim painovoima.\n\nMoottorin pysähtymsistapa säilyy ohjelman läpi ellei uusi komento sitä muuta.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä moottori pyörii eteenpäin 90 astetta (käsi nousee) ja sen jälkeen mooorroti pysähtyy 'hold' asentoon.\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.setStopping(hold);\nArmMotor.spinFor(90, degrees);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.setStopping(brake);"},"motion_motor_set_timeout":{"name":"motion_motor_set_timeout","markdown":"# Aseta moottorille odotusaika\n\nAsettaa moottorille odotusajan seuraavalle liikkeelle.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setTimeout(time, seconds);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAseta moottorille odotusaika antaa moottorille aika-rajan , jona aikana sen pitää suorittaa meneillään oleva komento loppuun. Tällä estetään ohjelman suorituksen loppuminen kesken, kun moottori ei saavuta tavoitetta. \n\nEsimerkinä aikarajan tarpeelle Käsi - tai Kouramoottorille on, että sen kääntymisen estää sen rakenteen mekaaniset rajat tai muu este.\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä aikaraja komennolle `spin_to_position` on 2 sekuntia.\n\nJos moottori ei tavoita 270 asteen kääntymsitavoitetta 2 sekunin aikana, moottori pysäytetään.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.setTimeout(2, seconds);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(270, degrees);\nClawMotor.spinToPosition(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.setTimeout(1, seconds);"},"motion_motor_set_velocity":{"name":"motion_motor_set_velocity","markdown":"# Asettaa moottorin nopeuden\n\nAsettaa V5 Älymoottorille nopeusarvon pyörimiseen.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.setVelocity(velocity, units);\n```\n\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomento hyväksyy arvot välillä **-100% to 100%** tai **-600rpm to 600rpm.**\n\nHyväksytyt `UNITS` parametrit ovat joko `PERCENT` (%) or `RPM`.\n\n**Set motor velocity** hyväksyy  \"rotations per minute\" (RPM) arvot riippuen käytetystä vaihdepakkauksesta V5 Älymoottorissa.\n\n* Red Cartridge: (punainen) -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: (Vihreä) -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: (Sininen) -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nJos nopeuden asettaa negatiivisen arvon, moottori pyörii taaksepäin (vastapäivään).\n\nMoottorin saa pysäyhtymään, kun asettaa sille nopeusarvon 0.","signature":"MOTOR.setVelocity(50, percent);"},"motion_motor_spin":{"name":"motion_motor_spin","markdown":"# Moottori pyörii\n\npyörittää V5 älymoottoria kunnes se pysäytetään.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(directionType);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.spin();` pyörittää V5 älymoottoria ikuisesti kunnes uusi komento sen pysäyttää tai ohjelman suoritus keskeytetään.\n\nKäytä parametria `forward` kun haluat moottorin pyörivän eteenpäin.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(forward);\n```\nKäytä parametria `reverse` kun haluat moottorin pyörivän taaksepäin.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spin(reverse);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.spin(forward);"},"motion_motor_spin_for":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_for","markdown":"# Pyöri matka\n \nKomento pyörittää V5 älymoottoria tietyn matkan joko asteina tai kierroksina.\n\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinFor(directionType, rotation, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.spinFor();` Valitse suunta `DIRECTION` , johon moottori pyörii: **FORWARD** (eteenpäin) tai **REVERSE** (taaksepäin).\n\nThe `Motor.spinFor();` hyväksyy numeerisen arvon parametriin `rotation`.\n\nValitse mittayksikkö `UNIT` joko **DEGREES** (astetta) tai **TURNS** (kierroksia).\n\n**spinFor** komento blokkaa seuraavat komennot suorituksen ajaksia oletuksena.\n\n## Lisäparametri\n\nValitse lisäparametri `false` kun  **spinFor** jälkeen seuraava komento suoritetaan ilman odotusta.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinFor(forward, 360, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.spinFor(forward, 90, degrees);"},"motion_motor_spin_to_position":{"name":"motion_motor_spin_to_position","markdown":"# Pyöritä asentoon\n\nPyörittää V5 Älymoottorin tiettyyn asentoon.\n\n```python \nmotor.spin_to_position(POSITION, UNITS)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.spinToPosition();` komento kiertää moottorin asennon haluttuun kohtaan. Perustuu nykyiseen asentoon `spin_to_position` komento kertoo mihin suuntaan pyöritään että asento saavutetaan.\n\nValitse mittayksikkö joko  **DEGREES** (astetta) tai **TURNS** (kierroksia).\n\n\n```cpp\nMotor3.spinToPosition(rotation, units);\n```\n\n\n**spinToPosition** komento estää toisten suorituksen kunnes V5 älymoottori on saavuttanut asennon.\n\n## Lisäparametri\n\nVoit valita `false` viimeiseksim parametriksi, jolloin **spinToPosition** komento ei blokkaa seuraavien komentojen suoritusta.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.spinToPosition(360, degrees, false);\n```","signature":"MOTOR.spinToPosition(90, degrees);"},"motion_motor_stop":{"name":"motion_motor_stop","markdown":"# Pysäytä moottori\n\nPysäyttää moottorin.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.stop();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.stop();` komento pysäyttää moottorin. Komennolla `Motor.setStopping();` voit asettaa pysähtymsitavan  `coast` (pysähdy heti) , `brake` (hitaasti jarruttaen), tai `hold` (pysähdy heti ja pidä asento).\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä moottori pyörii 3 sekuntia ennen pysähtymistä.\n\n```cpp\nClawMotor.spin(forward);\nwait(3, seconds);\nClawMotor.stop();\n```","signature":"MOTOR.stop();"},"motion_servo_set_position":{"name":"motion_servo_set_position","markdown":"# Servo Set Position\n\nPyörittää V5 Servo Mooottoria tiettyyn asentoon.\n\n```cpp\nServo.setPosition(position, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nPyörittää servomoottoria tiettyyn asentooon.\n\n`Servo.setPosition()` komento hyväksyy arvot välillä **-50** - **50** parametrissa **position**.\n\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä servomoottori pyörii asentoon 25 astetta ja odottaa 2 sekuntia ja pyörii vielä asentoon -25 astetta.\n\n```cpp\nServo.setPosition(25, degrees);\nwait(2, seconds);\nServo.setPosition(-25, degrees);\n```","signature":"SERVO.setPosition(90, degrees);"},"sensing_accel_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_accel_acceleration","markdown":"# Kiihtyvyysmittarin kiihtyvyys\n\nAntaa analogisen kiihtyvyysmittarin kiihtyvyysarvon akseleilla (x, y, or z).\n\nX-akselin suuntaan saadaan horisontaalinen kiihtyvyysarvo ja Y-akselilla vertikaalinen . Z-akselilla saadaan kiihtyvyys ylöspäin.\n\n```cpp\nAccel2G.acceleration()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n\n`Accelerometer.acceleration()` antaa desimaaliluvun (muotoa *double*) välillä **-2.0 G - 2.0 G** tai **-6.0 G - 6.0 G** riipuen laitteen jumpperiasetuksista.\n\n1.0 G vastaa arvoa 9.8 metriä sekunnin toisessa potenssissa.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Accel2GB.acceleration());\n```","signature":"ACCEL.acceleration()"},"sensing_brain_battery_capacity":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_capacity","markdown":"# Akun kapasiteetti\n\nANtaa V5 akun kapasiteetin.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Battery.capacity()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n\n`Brain.Battery.capacity()` antaa kokonaisluvun muotoa **integer** ja se vastaa akun kapasiteettia yksikössä `percent` (%) välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%d\", Brain.Battery.capacity());\n```","signature":"Brain.Battery.capacity()"},"sensing_brain_battery_current":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_current","markdown":"# Akun virrankulutus\n\nANtaa V5 aivojen akun virrankulutuksen.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Battery.current()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n\n`Brain.Battery.current()` antaa desimaaliluvun (muotoa *double*) V5 aivojen akun virrankulutuksen arvona.\n\nOletusyksikkö on ampeeri (`amp`) välillä **0.0 - 20.0 amps**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Brain.Battery.current());\n```","signature":"Brain.Battery.current()"},"sensing_brain_battery_voltage":{"name":"sensing_brain_battery_voltage","markdown":"# Brain Battery Voltage\n\nReports the voltage of the V5 Brain's battery.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Battery.voltage()\n```\n\n## How To Use\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n`Brain.Battery.voltage()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) that reports the voltage of the V5 Brain's battery. \n\nThe default unit is `volt`, and the command will return a value in the range of **10 volts to 14.4 volts**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Brain.Battery.voltage());\n```","signature":"Brain.Battery.voltage()"},"sensing_brain_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_column","markdown":"# Aivojen näytön kursorin sarake\nANtaa sarakenumeron, jolla kursori tällä hetekllä aivojen näytöllä.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.column()\n```\n\n```cpp\nif (Brain.Screen.column() > 10.0) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Cursor is past column 10\");\n}\n```\n---\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nNäytön sarake voi olla välillä **1 - 80**.\n\n```cpp\nif (Brain.Screen.column() > 10.0) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Cursor is past column 10\");\n}\n```\n---\n\nV5 Aivojen näytöklle voi määritellä fontin kokoa ja samaal se vaikuttaa sarakkeiden määrään.\n\n**V5 Aivojen fonttikokoe - Sarakkeiden määrä:**\n\n* `FontType.MONO12` - 80 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO15` - 68 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO20` / `FontType.PROP20` - 48 saraketta (Oletus)\n* `FontType.MONO30` / `FontType.PROP30` - 32 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO40` / `FontType.PROP40` - 24 saraketta\n* `FontType.MONO60` / `FontType.MONO60` - 16 saraketta\n* \n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_brain_screen_column/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.column()"},"sensing_brain_screen_pressing":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_pressing","markdown":"# Näyttöä koskettu\n \nAntaa tiedon jos V5 aivojen kosketusnäyttöä on koskettu.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.pressing()` komentoa voi käyttää yhdessä komentojen `Brain.Screen.xPosition()` ja `Brain.Screen.yPosition()` , jos V5 aivojen kosketusnäyttöä on koskettu ja missä kohtaan.\n\n`Brain.screen.pressing()` antaa arvon **True** jos V5 aivojen näyttöä on koskettu.\n\n`Brain.screen.pressing()` antaa arvon **false** jos V5 aivojen näyttöä ei ole koskettu.\n\n```cpp\nif (Brain.Screen.pressing()) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Screen is being pressed!\");\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.pressing()"},"sensing_brain_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_row","markdown":"# Kursorin rivi aivojen näytöllä\n\nAntaa kursorin rivinumeron V5 aivojen näytöllä.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.row()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nNäytön rivien lukumäärä oletusfontilla on välillä **1 to 20**.\n\n\n\n```cpp\nif (Brain.Screen.row() > 10.0) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Cursor position is past row 10\");\n}\n```\n---\n\nVoit muuttaa fontin kokoa näytöllä ja samalla se vaikuttaa rivien määrään:\n\n**V5 Aivojen fonttikoko - Rivien määrä:**\n\n* `mono12` - 20 riviä\n* `mono15` - 16 riviä\n* `mono20` / `prop20` - 12 riviä (Oletus)\n* `mono30` / `prop30` - 8 riviä\n* `mono40` / `prop40` - 6 riviä\n* `mono60` / `prop60` - 4 riviä\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_brain_screen_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)","signature":"Brain.Screen.row()"},"sensing_brain_screen_xPosition":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_xPosition","markdown":"# Aivojen näytön x Arvo\n\nAntaa X-koordinaatin, johon viimeksi koskettu V5 Aivojen kosketusnäytössä.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.xPosition()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`brain.screen.x_position()` kaappaa viimeisimmän näytön kosketuksen x -koordinaatin. \n\nYhdessä komennon  `brain.screen.y_position()` saa molemmat koordinaatit (x,y), jolloin interaktiivisuutta voi lisätä käyttäjän ja V5 aivojen välillä.\n\n`brain.screen.x_position()` palauttaa **integer** kokonaisluvun väliltä **0 - 480 pixeliä**.\n\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_brain_screen_xPosition/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n```cpp\nint myXCoordinate = Brain.Screen.xPosition();\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.xPosition()"},"sensing_brain_screen_yPosition":{"name":"sensing_brain_screen_yPosition","markdown":"# # Aivojen näytön y-arvo\n\nAntaa Y-koordinaatin, johon viimeksi koskettu V5 Aivojen kosketusnäytössä.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.yPosition()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Brain.Screen.yPosition()` kaappaa viimeisimmän näytön kosketuksen x -koordinaatin. \n\nYhdessä komennon  `Brain.Screen.xPosition()`  saa molemmat koordinaatit (x,y), jolloin interaktiivisuutta voi lisätä käyttäjän ja V5 aivojen välillä.\n\n\n`Brain.Screen.yPosition()` antaa kokonaisluvun **integer** arvovälillä **0 - 240 pixeliä**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_brain_screen_yPosition/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n```cpp\nint myYCoordinate = Brain.Screen.yPosition();\n```","signature":"Brain.Screen.yPosition()"},"sensing_brain_timer_clear":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_clear","markdown":"# Nollaa kello\n\nNollaa V5 Aivojen kellon.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.clear();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAivojen kello käynnistyy ohjelman suorituksen alussa. Nollaa kello -komentoa voi käytttää ohjelman aikana aloiottaamaan ajanlasku uudelleen arvosta 0 sekuntia.","signature":"Brain.Timer.clear();"},"sensing_brain_timer_time":{"name":"sensing_brain_timer_time","markdown":"# Brain Timer Time\n\nReports the value of the V5 Brain's timer in the provided units.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Timer.time(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not require a semicolon.\n\nThe timer starts at 0 seconds when the program starts, and returns the timer's value as a decimal value (as a *double*).\n\nThe `units` parameter accepts either **seconds** or **msec** (milliseconds) as a valid argument.\n\n```cpp\nif(Brain.Timer.time(seconds) > 3.0){\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Timer has passed 3 seconds!\");\n}\n```","signature":"Brain.Timer.time(units)"},"sensing_bumper_pressing":{"name":"sensing_bumper_pressing","markdown":"# Painokytkintä on painetttu\n \nAntaa tiedon, onko painokytkintä painettu.\n\n```cpp\nBumper.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nbumper.pressing() antaa arvon **True** (tosi), jos painokytkintä on painettu.\n\nbumper.pressing() antaa arvon **False** (epätosi), jos painokytkintä ei ole painettu.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(BumperA.pressing());\nBrain.Screen.print(\"BumperA pressed!\");\n```","signature":"BUMPER.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_axis_position":{"name":"sensing_controller_axis_position","markdown":"# Ohjaimen tatin asento\n \nAntaa V5 -ohjaimen tatin asennon.\n\n```cpp\nController.Axis.position()\n```\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Controller.axis1.position` antaa arvot välillä **-100 - 100**.\n\n`Controller.axis1.position` antaa arvon nolla (0) ,kun se on keskellä.\n\nValitse tatti, jota käytät.\n\n* Axis1 - oikea Joystick (vasen - oikea)\n* Axis2 - oikean Joystick (ylös - alas)\n* Axis3 - vasen Joystick (ylös - alas)\n* Axis4 - vasen Joystick (vasen - oikea)\n* \n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_controller_axis_position/controller_button_front.png)\n\n```cpp\nArmMotor.setVelocity(Controller1.Axis3.position(), percent);\n```","signature":"CONTROLLER.AXIS.position()"},"sensing_controller_button_pressing":{"name":"sensing_controller_button_pressing","markdown":"# Ohjaimen napin painallus\n\nAntaa tiedon jos V5 ohjaimen tiettyä nappia on painettu.\n\n\n```cpp\nController.Button.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n'controller.buttonUp.pressing()' antaa arvon **True** jos ko nappia on painettu.\n\n'controller.buttonUp.pressing()' antaa arvon **False** jos ko nappia ei ole painettu.\n\nValitse mitä nappia käsittelet:\n\n* `buttonUp`\n* `buttonDown`\n* `buttonLeft`\n* `buttonRight`\n* `buttonX`\n* `buttonY`\n* `buttonA`\n* `buttonB`\n* `buttonL1`\n* `buttonL2`\n* `buttonR1`\n* `buttonR2`\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Controller1.ButtonUp.pressing());\n```","signature":"Controller.buttonUp.pressing()"},"sensing_controller_screen_column":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_column","markdown":"# Controller.Screen.column()\n# Kursorin sarake\n \nAntaa ohjaimen näytöltä kursorin sarakenumeron.\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.column()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Controller.Screen.column()` antaa kokonaisluvun välillä **1 to 19**.\n\n```cpp\nif (Controller1.Screen.column() > 10) {\n}\n```\n\n---\nV5 Ohjainen näytölle ei voi muuttaa fontin kokoa.\n\n**V5 Ohjain Fonttikoko - Sarakkeiden lukumäärä:**\n\n* Standard Font - 19 saraketta (Oletus)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_controller_screen_column/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.column()"},"sensing_controller_screen_row":{"name":"sensing_controller_screen_row","markdown":"# Kursorin rivi\n\nAntaa ohjaimen näytön kursorin rivin.\n\n\n```cpp\nController.Screen.row()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Controller.Screen.row()` antaa arvot välillä **1 - 3**.\n\n```cpp\nif (Controller1.Screen.row() > 2) {\n}\n```\n\n---\n\nV5 ohjaimen näytöllä fonttia ei voi muuttaa.\n\n**V5 Ohjain Fontti Koko - Rivimäärä:**\n\n* Standardi Fontti - 3 Riviä (Oletus)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_controller_screen_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)","signature":"CONTROLLER.Screen.row()"},"sensing_distance_is_object_detected":{"name":"sensing_distance_is_object_detected","markdown":"# Havaittu esine\n\nAntaa tiedon jos V5 Etäisyysanturi havaitsee esineen näkökentässään.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.isObjectDetected()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Distance.isObjectDetected()` antaa arvon **TRUE** jos esine tai heijastava pinta onnäkökentässä ja muuten arvon **false**.\n\nAlla tulostetaan **TRUE** or **FALSE** riippuen onko esine havaittu.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%s\", Distance.isObjectDetected() ? \"TRUE\" : \"FALSE\");\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.isObjectDetected()"},"sensing_distance_object_distance":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Distance Object Distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object or surface from a V5 Distance Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.objectDistance(units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Distance.objectDistance()` accepts **mm** or **inches** as units and reports a range from **20 mm to 2000 mm** (~0.8 inches to 79.0 inches ) as a decimal value.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Distance.objectDistance(inches));\n```\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Distance.objectDistance(mm));\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.objectDistance(inches)"},"sensing_distance_object_size":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_size","markdown":"# Havaitun esineen koko\n\nAnta arvion esineen koosta , jonka tisyysanturi havaitsee.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.objectSize()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Distance.objectSize()` avulla voidaan arvioida havaitun esineen kokoa.\n\nKokoja on kolme:\n\n* sizeType::large (iso)\n* sizeType::medium (keskikoko)\n* sizeType::small (pieni)\n\n```cpp\nif (Distance.objectSize() == sizeType::large) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Large object detected!\");\n}\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.objectSize()"},"sensing_distance_object_velocity":{"name":"sensing_distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Kohteen nopeus\n\nAntaa havaitun kohteen nopeuden yksikössä m/s.\n\n```cpp\nDistance.objectVelocity()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Distance.objectVelocity()` antaa tänhetkisen kohteen nopeuden yksikössä m/s (metriä sekunnissa).\n\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Distance.objectVelocity());\n```","signature":"DISTANCE.objectVelocity()"},"sensing_drivetrain_current":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_current","markdown":"# jopelin virrankulutus\n\nNtaa virtamäärän jota ajoplei tällä hetkellä kuluttaa.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.current(amp)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.current(amp)` antaa desimaaliluvun (muotoa *double*), kun sen virrankulutus mitataan.\n\nOletusyksikköon ampeeri (`amp`) ja arvot mitataan välillä **0.0 - 2.5 amps**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.current(amp));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.current()"},"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_efficiency","markdown":"# Ajopelin tehosuhde/hyötysuhde\n\nAntaa ajopelin tehosuhteen.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.efficiency()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.efficiency()` antaa suhteen ajopelin ajomoottoreiden ulostuhoteho (output) watteina suhteessa sisääntulo (input) tehoon watteina \n\nV5 ajopeli saavuttaa tyypillisesti 65% hyötysuhteen.\n\n\n`Drivetrain.efficiency()` antaa desimaaliluvun (muotoa *double*) yksikkönä `percent` (%) ja arvon välillä  **0.0% - 100.0%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.efficiency());\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.efficiency(percent)"},"sensing_drivetrain_heading":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_heading","markdown":"# Ajopelin ajosuunta\n\nAntaa 3-lanka Gyro Sensorilla tai V5 Inertial Sensorilla nykyisen ajosuunnan asteina.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.heading()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.heading()` antaa kasvavia arvoja ajosuunnssa kun ajopeli kääntyy myötäpäivään.\n\n`Drivetrain.heading()` antaa arvot välillä **0.00 - 359.99**.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Drivetrain.heading() > 180);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.heading()"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_done":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_done","markdown":"# Ajopeli on pysähtynyt\n\nAntaa tiedon onko ajopeli lopettanut liikkeensä.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.isDone()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomennot, jotka palauttavat arvon voidaan sijoittaa toisten komentojen sisään kuten print -komennossa tao ohjauslauseissa ehtomuuttujien osana ja ilman puolipistettä.\n\n`Drivetrain.isDone()` antaa arvon **true** jos ajopeli on pysähtynyt ts suorittanut liikeensä loppuun.\n\n`Drivetrain.isDone()` antaa arvon **false** jos ajopeli on liikeessä vielä.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Drivetrain.isDone());\n```\n\nKomento antaa arvon **true** jos kyseessä on komennojen `drive()` tai `turn()` tarkastelu.","signature":"Drivetrain.isDone()"},"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_is_moving","markdown":"# Ajopeli liikkuu\n\nAntaa tiedon jatkaako ajoplei liikettä tällä hetkellä.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.isMoving()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomennot, jotka palauttavat arvon voidaan sijoittaa toisten komentojen sisään kuten print -komennossa tao ohjauslauseissa ehtomuuttujien osana ja ilman puolipistettä.\n\nKomento antaa arvon **true** jos ajopeli edelleen suorittaa komentoa `driveFor()` tai `turnFor()` , jossa on etäisyysmääre käytössä.\n\nKomento antaa arvon **false** jos ajopeli on jo pysähtynyt .\n\n**Note:** Tämä komento antaa aina vain arvon **false** jos liikettä tehdään komennoilla `drive()` tai `turn()`, jossa ei ole annettu matkaa/astemäärää.\n\n```cpp\nif (Drivetrain.isMoving()) {\n    \n} else {\n    \n}\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.isMoving()"},"sensing_drivetrain_power":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_power","markdown":"# Ajopelin teho\n\nANtaa ajopelin moottoreiden tehomäärän.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.power()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.power()` antaa desimaaliluvun (muotoa *double*) ajopelin kehottämän tehon määrälle.\n\nKomennot, jotka palauttavat arvon voidaan sijoittaa toisten komentojen sisään kuten print -komennossa tao ohjauslauseissa ehtomuuttujien osana ja ilman puolipistettä.\n\nOletusyksikkö on `watt` ja arvot ovat välillä **0.0 - 22.0 wattia**. \n\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.power());\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.power()"},"sensing_drivetrain_rotation":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_rotation","markdown":"# Ajopelin käännöskulma\n\nAntaa ajopelin käännöskulman joko 3-lankagurolla tai V5 Inertial Sensorilla mitattuna.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.rotation()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.rotation()` antaa **positiivisen** arvon, jos ajopeli kääntyy **myötäpäivään**.\n\n`Drivetrain.rotation()` antaa **nagatiivisen** arvon, jos ajopeli kääntyy **vastapäivään**.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Drivetrain.rotation() > 180);\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.rotation()"},"sensing_drivetrain_temperature":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_temperature","markdown":"# Ajopelin moottorilämpötila\n\nAntaa ajopelin ajomoottoreiden lämpötilan.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.temperature(percent)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.temperature(percent)` antaa desimaaliarvon (muotoa *double*) , kun se raportoi ajopelin ajomoottoreiden lämpötilan.  \n\nKomennot, jotka mittaavat arvoja voi laittaa muiden komentojen sisään kuten print komentoon tai toistorakenteissa ehtolausekkeisiin ilman puolipistettä.\n\nAseta `percent` yksiköksi ja arvot mitataan välillä **0.0% - 100.0%**. \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.temperature(percent));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.temperature(percent)"},"sensing_drivetrain_torque":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_torque","markdown":"# Ajopelin ajomoottoreiden vääntövoima\n\nAntaa vääntövoiman (kiertovoiman), jota ajopelin moottorit tällä hetkellä tuottaa.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.torque(Nm)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Drivetrain.torque(Nm)` antaa arvona desimaaliluvun (muotoa *double*), kun se raportoi ajopelin ajomoottoreiden vääntövoiman. \n\nOletuksena on yksikkö Newton-meters(`Nm`), jolla mitattuna arvot vaihtelee välillä **0.0 - 2.1 Newton-metriä (Nm)**.\n\nVaihtoehtona on yksikkö Tuuma Pauna (`InLB`).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.torque(Nm));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.torque(InLb));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.torque(Nm)"},"sensing_drivetrain_velocity":{"name":"sensing_drivetrain_velocity","markdown":"# Drivetrain Velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of the Drivetrain.\n\n```cpp\nDrivetrain.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## How to Use\n`Drivetrain.velocity` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the current velocity of the Drivetrain. \n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nAcceptable `units` are **percent** and **rpm**.\n\nIf the provided `units` parameter is **percent**, the reported values ranges between **-100% to 100%**.\n\nAlternatively, if the provided `units` is **rpm**, the range of reported values vary based on the Gear Catridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Catridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Catridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Catridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Drivetrain.velocity(percent));\n```","signature":"Drivetrain.velocity(units)"},"sensing_encoder_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_position","markdown":"# Kierrosmittarin asento\n\nAntaa akselin kierrosmittarin pyörimän matkan.\n\n```cpp\nEncoder.position(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Encoder.position()` palauttaa desimaaliluvun muotoa (*double*) , kun se antaa kierrosmittarin mittaaman matkan.\n\n\nTällaisia komentioja voi käyttää arvoina muissa komennoissa mm tulostuksessa tai ohjauslausekkeissa osana ehtoja.\n\n\nYksikkönä voi olla asteita `degrees` .\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", EncoderC.position(degrees));\n```\n\nYksikkönä voi olla akselin kierroksia  `turns`.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", EncoderC.position(turns));\n```","signature":"ENCODER.position(degrees)"},"sensing_encoder_set_position":{"name":"sensing_encoder_set_position","markdown":"# Encoder Set Position\n\nSets the Shaft Encoder's position to the given value.\n\n```cpp\nEncoder.setPosition(position, units);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Encoder.setPosition()` can be used to set the Shaft Encoder's position to any given positional value.\n\nUsually, `Encoder.setPosition()` is used to set the position 0 to reset the Shaft Encoder's position.\n\nThe **units** parameter can be set to **degrees** or **turns**.\n\n```cpp\nEncoderA.setPosition(0, degrees);\nEncoderB.setPosition(0, turns);\n```","signature":"ENCODER.setPosition(position, units);"},"sensing_encoder_velocity":{"name":"sensing_encoder_velocity","markdown":"# Encoder Nopeus\n\nAntaa akseli kiertomittarin / Encoderin nopeuden.\n\n```cpp\nEncoder.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Encoder.velocity()` antaa desimaaliluvun (muotoa *double*) joku asteina per sekuntti (`dps`) tai kierroksia minuutissa (`rpm`).\n\n\nArvot yksikössä astetta minuutissa (`dps`).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", EncoderC.velocity(dps));\n```\n\nArvot yksikössä kierrosta minuutissa (`rpm`).\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", EncoderC.velocity(rpm));\n```","signature":"ENCODER.velocity(dps)"},"sensing_gyro_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_gyro_calibrate","markdown":"# Gyron Kalibronti\n\nKun kalibroit Gyro Sensorin vähennät sensorin ns huojumista/heiluntaa.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.calibrate();\n```\n\nHuojumista tapahtuu aina niin että Gyro Sensori havaitsee liikettä vaikka sensori on paikallaaa.\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nGyro Sensorin pitää olla kalibroinnin ajan levossa noin 1 sekunnin ajan .","signature":"GYRO.calibrate();"},"sensing_gyro_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Gyro Ajosuunta\n\nAntaa 3-lanka Gyro Sensorin ajosuunnan tällä hetkellä asteina.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.heading(degrees)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Gyro.heading(degrees)` komennossa arvot kasvavat myötäpäivään kääntyessä.\n\n`Gyro.heading(degrees)` anta arvot välillä **0.00 - 359.99**.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Gyro.heading(degrees) > 180);\n```","signature":"GYRO.heading(degrees)"},"sensing_gyro_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Gyro kääntymiskulma\n\nAntaa 3-lanka Gyro Sensorin antaman kääntymiskulman asteina.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.rotation(degrees)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Gyro.rotation(degrees)` antaa positiivisen **positive** arvon kun gyro kääntyy myötäpäivään.\n\n`Gyro.rotation(degrees)` antaa nagatiivisen **negative** arvon kun gyro kääntyy vastapäivään.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Gyro.rotation(degrees) > 180);\n```","signature":"GYRO.rotation(degrees)"},"sensing_gyro_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_heading","markdown":"# Gyro aseta ajosuunta\n\nAsettaa Gyroscopic (Gyro) sensorin uuden nykyisen ajosuunnan. \n\n```cpp\nGyro.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Gyro.setHeading();` komennossa voi asettaa gyrona rvoksi minkä tahansa myötäpäivvä asennon. Tyypillisesti ajosuunta nollataan kesken ajoa.\n\n`Gyro.setHeading();` hyväksyy desimaali- ja kokonaislukuja.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"GYRO.setHeading(90, degrees);"},"sensing_gyro_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_gyro_set_rotation","markdown":"# Gyro Aseta kierrosaste\n\nAsettaa 3-Lanka Gyro Sensorin kierroskulman haluttuun arvoon.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setRotation(0, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nGyro.setRotation();` komento voidaan asettaa ajopelin kulmaksi minkä tahansa positiivisen (myötäpäivään) tai negatiivisen (vastapäivään) luvun kulman arvoksi.\n\n`Gyro.setRotation();` hyväksyys ekä positiivisia että negatiivisia kokonais- ja desimaalilukuja.\n\n```cpp\nGyro.setRotation(270, degrees);\nGyro.setRotation(-270, degrees);\n```","signature":"GYRO.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"sensing_inertial_acceleration":{"name":"sensing_inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Inertial kiihtyvyys\n\nAntaa Inertial Sensorin mittaaman kiihtyvyyden yhdellä akselilla (x, y, tai z) on the Inertial Sensor.  \n\n* **X-akseli** -suuntaan Inertial Sensori mittaa kiihtyvyyttä , kun robotti liikkuu akselilla **eteen - taakse**\n* **Y-akseli** -suuntaan Inertial Sensori mittaa kiihtyvyyttä , kun robotti liikkuu akselilla **sivulta sivulle**\n* **Z-akseli** -suuntaan Inertial Sensori mittaa kiihtyvyyttä , kun robotti liikkuu akselilla **ylös-alas**\n\n```cpp\nInertial.acceleration(axis)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomentoa voidaan käyttää toisten komentojen sisällä kuten tulsota-komennossa tai ohjauslauseissa osana ehtolausetta ja älä käytä puolipistettä.\n\n`Inertial.acceleration()` antaa arvot desimaalilukuna (muotoa *double*) välillä **-4.0 - 4.0 Gs**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial1.acceleration(xaxis));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial1.acceleration(yaxis));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial1.acceleration(zaxis));\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.acceleration(xaxis);"},"sensing_inertial_calibrate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_calibrate","markdown":"# Inertial kalibrointi\n\nKalibroimalla Inertial Sensori vähennetään sen mittausarvojen huojuntaa.\n\n```cpp\nInertial.calibrate()\n```\n\nHuojuntaa esiintyy, kun Inertial Sensori virheellisesti havaitsee akselien suunnassa arvojen muuitosta vaikka se on levossa.\n\n## How To Use\n\nInertial Sensorin pitää olla levossa kalibroinnin ajan noin 2 sekuntia.","signature":"INERTIAL.calibrate();"},"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate":{"name":"sensing_inertial_gyro_rate","markdown":"# Inertial Gyro nopeusarvo\n\nAntaa Inertial Sensorin mittaaman käännöksen nopeusarvon akselilla (x, y, or z).\n\n* **X-akseli** suunnassa nopeusarvon, kun Inertial Sensori kääntyy X-Akselilla (riippuen sensorin suunnasta)\n* **Y-akseli** suunnassa nopeusarvon, kun Inertial Sensori kääntyy Y-Akselilla (riippuen sensorin suunnasta)\n* **Z-akseli** suunnassa nopeusarvon, kun Inertial Sensori kääntyy Z-Akselilla (riippuen sensorin suunnasta)\n\n```cpp\nInertial.gyroRate(axis, dps)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomentoa voi käyttää muiden komentojen sisällä mm tulosta-komennossa taitoistorakenteiden ehtolauseissa ja älä käytä puolipistettä.\n\n`Inertial.gyroRate()` antaa arvot välillä **-1000.0 - 1000.0** dps (astetta sekunnissa). \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial.gyroRate(xaxis, dps));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial.gyroRate(yaxis, dps));\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Inertial.gyroRate(zaxis, dps));\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.gyroRate(xaxis, dps)"},"sensing_inertial_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_heading","markdown":"# Inertial ajosuunta\n\nANtaa V5 Inertial Sensorin mittaaman ajosuunnan asteina.\n\n```cpp\nInertial.heading(degrees)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomentoa voi kättää muiden komentojen sisällä mm tulsota -komennossa tai toistorakenteiden ehtolauseissa ja älä käytä puolipistettä.\n\n`Inertial.heading(degrees)` komennon arvo kasvaa kun ajosuuntaa kääntyy myötäpäivään.\n\n`Inertial.heading(degrees)` antaa arvon väliltä **0.00 - 359.99 astetta**\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Inertial.heading(degrees) > 180);\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.heading(degrees)"},"sensing_inertial_orientation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Inertial Orientation\n\nGets an orientation angle of the inertial sensor. Reports the unit value specified by the parameter of the inertial sensor.\n\nThe orientation reported is determined by the selected axis (x, y, or z).\n\n* The **X-axis** represents **pitch**, which reports a value between -90 to +90 degrees.\n* The **Y-axis** represents **roll**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n* The **Z-axis** represents **yaw**, which reports a value between -180 to +180 degrees)\n\n--\n\nPitch is the rotation around the side to side axis.\n\n![V5_Pitch_rev2](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_inertial_orientation/V5_Pitch_rev2.jpg)\n\nRoll is the rotation around the front to back axis.\n\n![V5_Roll_rev2](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_inertial_orientation/V5_Roll_rev2.jpg)\n\nYaw is rotation around the vertical axis.\n\n![V5_Yaw_rev2](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_inertial_orientation/V5_Yaw_rev2.jpg)\n\n--\n\n```cpp\nInertial.orientation(axis, units)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Inertial.orientation(pitch, degrees) > 60);\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.orientation(pitch, degrees);"},"sensing_inertial_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_rotation","markdown":"# Inertial Rotation\n\nReports the 3-Wire V5 Inertial Sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n```cpp\nInertial.rotation(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe `Inertial.rotation(degrees)` reports a **positive** value when the Inertial Sensor turns in the **clockwise** direction.\n\n`Inertial.rotation(degrees)` reports a **negative** value when the Inertial Sensor turns in the **counter-clockwise** direction.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(Inertial20.rotation(degrees) > 180);\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.rotation(degrees)"},"sensing_inertial_set_heading":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_heading","markdown":"# Inertial Set Heading\n\nSets the Inertial sensor's current heading position to a set value.\n\n```cpp\nInertial.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Inertial.setHeading()` can be used to set the Gyro's position to any clockwise heading. This command is typically used to reset the orientation of the Inertial Sensor when the heading is set to a value of 0.\n\n`Inertial.setHeading()` accepts a range of **0.0 to 359.99** degrees.\n\n`Inertial.setHeading()` can accept decimals, integers, or other commands that return a numeric value.\n\n\n```cpp\nmyInertial.setHeading(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.setHeading(0, degrees);"},"sensing_inertial_set_rotation":{"name":"sensing_inertial_set_rotation","markdown":"# Inertial Set Rotation\n\nSets the V5 Inertial Sensor's angle of rotation to the value provided.\n\n```cpp\nInertial.setRotation(0, degrees);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe `Inertial.setRotation()` command can be used to set the Drivetrain's angle of rotation to any given positive (clockwise) or negative (counter-clockwise) value.\n\n`Inertial.setRotation()` accepts any positive or negative decimal or integer number.\n\n```cpp\nInertial20.setRotation(0, degrees)\n```","signature":"INERTIAL.setRotation(90, degrees);"},"sensing_light_brightness":{"name":"sensing_light_brightness","markdown":"# Valon kirkkaus\n\nAntaa Light Sensorin havaitseman valon kirkkauden.\n\n```cpp\nLight.brightness()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Light.brightness()` antaa arvot välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\nIso kirkkausarvo vastaa hyvää valaistusarvoa.\n\nPieni kirkkausarvo vastaa huonoa valaistusarvoa.\n\nOletusyksikkö on `percent` (5) ja arvot ovat välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%d\", LightC.brightness());\n```","signature":"LIGHT.brightness()"},"sensing_limit_pressing":{"name":"sensing_limit_pressing","markdown":"# LimitSwitch Painettu\n\nKertoo onko Limit Switch sensoria painettu.\n\n```cpp\nLimitSwitch.pressing()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`LimitSwitch.pressing()` antaa arvon **true** jos sitä on painettu.\n\n`LimitSwitch.pressing()` antaa arvon **false** jos sitä ei ole painettu.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(LimitSwitchB.pressing());\n```","signature":"LimitSwitch.pressing()"},"sensing_line_reflectivity":{"name":"sensing_line_reflectivity","markdown":"# Viivanseuraaja valonheijastus\n\nAntaa valon määrän jonka viivanseuraaja havaitsee.\n\n```cpp\nLineTracker.reflectivity()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetän\n\nVaaleat valopinnat heijastavat valoa enenmmän kun tummat ja antavat isompia arvoja.\n\nOletusyksikkö on `percent` ja valonheijastusarvot vaihtelevat välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%d\", LineTrackerA.reflectivity());\n```","signature":"LINETRACKER.reflectivity()"},"sensing_motor_current":{"name":"sensing_motor_current","markdown":"# Moottorin sähkövirta\n\nAntaa moottorin sähkövirran arvon , jota V5 älymoottori tällä hetkellä käyttää yksikössä ampeeri (amps).\n\n```cpp\nMotor.current(amp)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.current()` antaa desimaaliluvun (muotoa *double*), kun se raportoi V5 älymoottori virrankulutusta tällä hetkellä käyttää.\n\nOletusyksikkö on ampeeri (`amp`) ja arvot mitataan välillä **0.0 - 2.5 ampeeria**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ClawMotor.current(amp));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.current()"},"sensing_motor_direction":{"name":"sensing_motor_direction","markdown":"# Motor.direction()\n\nAntaa suunnan, johon V5 älymoottori pyörii tällä hetkellä.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.direction()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomennot jotja antavat arvon voidaan käyttää muiden komentojen sisällä mm print -komennossa tai toistorakenteiden ehtolauseissa (ilman puolipistettä rivin lopussa).\n\n`Motor.current()` palauttaa **directionType** arvon, joka voi olla joko `forward` (eteenpäin) tai `reverse` (taaksepäin).\n\n\n```cpp\nif (LeftMotor.direction() == forward) {\n    Brain.Screen.print(\"Left Motor is spinning forward!\");\n}\n```\n**Note:** Puolipistettä käyttää yllä `print` -komento.","signature":"MOTOR.direction()"},"sensing_motor_efficiency":{"name":"sensing_motor_efficiency","markdown":"# Moottorin tehokkuus\n\nAntaa V5 Älymoottorin suhteellisen tehokkuuden/hyötysuhteen.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.efficiency(percent)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.efficiency()` raportoi moottorin ulostulotehon output (W) suhteen sisääntulotehoon input (W). \n\nV5 Älymoottori tyypillisesti pääsee maksimissaan 65% hyötysuhteeseen normaaliolosuhteissa.\n\nKomentoja, jotka antavat tämäntyyppisiä arvoja, käytetään muitten kuten print komentojen parametreissa tai toistorakenteiden ehdoissa.\n\n`Motor.efficiency()` antaa desimaalilukuarvoja (kuten *double*) yksikkönä `percent` (%) arvoväliltä **0.0% - 100.0%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", Motor.efficiency(percent));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.efficiency(percent)"},"sensing_motor_is_done":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_done","markdown":"# Mooottori on pysähtynyt?\n\nraportoi onko moottori suorittanut loppuun liikkeensä.\n\n\n```cpp\nMotor.isDone()\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nKomentoa käytetään yleensä muiden komentojen sisällä mm tulosta -komennossa tai toistorakenteiden ehdoissa\n\n`Motor.isDone` antaa arvon **tosi**, kun tietty moottori on pysähtynyt.\n\n`Motor.isDone` antaa arvon **epätosi**, kun tietty moottori ei ole suorittanut liikettä loppuun.\n\n```cpp\nwaitUntil(ClawMotor.isDone());\n```","signature":"MOTOR.isDone()"},"sensing_motor_is_spinning":{"name":"sensing_motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Moottori pyörii\n\nKeroo, pyöriikö V5 Älymoottori tällä hetekllä.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.isSpinning()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nKomento antaa arvon **true** jos moottori pyörii , kun komennon `spinFor()` matka on vielä kesken.\n\nKomento antaa arvon **false** jos noottorin pyörimisliike on loppunut.\n\n**Huomio** Komento antaa aina arvon **false** jos on käytetty pelkkää `spin()` komentoa (ilman matka-arvoa).\n\n```cpp\n// esimerkissä LED valo palaa aina kun käsimoottori pyörii\n\nArmMotor.spinFor(forward, 720, degrees, false);\n\nwhile (ArmMotor.isSpinning()) {\n    LEDA.on();\n    wait(0.5, seconds);\n    LEDA.off();\n    wait(0.5, seconds);\n}\n```","signature":"MOTOR.isSpinning()"},"sensing_motor_position":{"name":"sensing_motor_position","markdown":"# Motor Position\n\nReports the distance the V5 Smart Motor has traveled.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.position(degrees)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.position()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the distance the Shaft Encoder has rotated.\n\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\n\nValues can be returned in `degrees`.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.position(degrees));\n```\n\nValues can be returned in `turns`.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.position(turns));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.position()"},"sensing_motor_power":{"name":"sensing_motor_power","markdown":"# Motor Power\n\nReports the amount of power output the V5 Smart Motor is currently generating.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.power(watt)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.power()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the amount of power output the V5 Smart Motor is currently generating.\n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nThe default unit is `watt` that returns values ranging from **0.0 to 22.0 watts**. \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ClawMotor.power(watt));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.power()"},"sensing_motor_temperature":{"name":"sensing_motor_temperature","markdown":"# Motor Temperature\n\nReports the temperature of the V5 Smart Motor.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.temperature(percent)\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Motor.temperature()` returns a decimal value (as a *double*) to report the temperature of the V5 Smart Motor.  \n\nCommands that return a value are normally used inside of other statements (such as print statements) or inside of control structures (such as while loops) and do not use a semicolon.\n\nSet `percent` as the unit to get values ranging from **0.0% to 100.0%**. \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ClawMotor.temperature(percent));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.temperature(percent)"},"sensing_motor_torque":{"name":"sensing_motor_torque","markdown":"# Moottorin vääntövoima\n\nAntaa V5 Älymoottorin vääntövoiman (kiertovoiman) tällähetkellä.\n\n```cpp\nMotor.torque(Nm)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.torque()` antaa desimaaliarvon (muotoa *double*) vääntövoimalle tällä hetkellä.\n\nKomentoa voi käyttää muiden komentojen argumenttina mm tulostuksessa tai erikseen toistorakenteiden vertailuehdoissa.\n\nKomento antaa arvot välillä **0.0 - 2.1 Newton-metriä (Nm)**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.torque(Nm));\n```\n\nVToinen yksikkö on tuuma-paunaa (`InLb`) ja sen mittaväli on **0.0 - 18.6 InLb**. \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.torque(InLb));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.torque()"},"sensing_motor_velocity":{"name":"sensing_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Moottorin Nopeus\n\nRaportoi valitun VEX V5 älymoottorin nopeuden.\n\n\n```cpp\nMotor.velocity(percent)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Motor.velocity()` palauttaa desimaalilukuna (muodossa *desimaali*) tämän hetkisen moottorin nopeuden. \n\nMäärittele `yksikkö`, jota komento käyttää.\n\n**%** - palauttaa nopeuden arvon välillä **-100% - 100%**.\n \n \n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.velocity(percent));\n```\n  \n`Motor.velocity()` `Motor.velocity` voi palauttaa myös arvon **rpm** (kierrosta minuutissa) riippuen vaihdepakkauksesta moottorissa seuraavasti:\n\n**Punainen vaihdepakkaus:** -100rpm - 100rpm  \n**Vihreä vaihdepakkaus:** -200rpm to 200rpm  \n**Sininen vaihdepakkaus:** -600rpm to 600rpm  \n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", ArmMotor.velocity(rpm));\n```","signature":"MOTOR.velocity()"},"sensing_optical_brightness":{"name":"sensing_optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical.brightness()\n\nAntaa V5 Optical Sensorin havaitseman valon määrän.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.brightness()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Optical.brightness()` anta arvot välillä **0% - 100%**.\n\nMitä enemmän valoa sensori näkee sitä korkeampi on arvo.\n\nHuono valaistus aantaa matalan arvon.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Optical.brightness());\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.brightness()"},"sensing_optical_color":{"name":"sensing_optical_color","markdown":"# Optical väri\n\nPalauttaa värin nimen, jonka V5 Optical Sensori tunnistaa.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.color()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Optical.color()` palauttaa lähimmän värin, jonka se tunnistaa esineestä.\n\nSeuraavia värejä voi käytttää vertailuun, mitä V5 Optical Sensori havaitsee:\n\n* black (musta)\n* white (valkoinen)\n* red (punainen)\n* green (vihreä)\n* blue (sininen)\n* yellow (keltainen)\n* orange (oranssi)\n* purple (purppuran punainen)\n* cyan (syaani vaalen sininen)\n\n```cpp\nif (Optical.color() == red) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Red object detected!\");\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.color()"},"sensing_optical_hue":{"name":"sensing_optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical Värisävu\n\nAntaa esineen värisävyn, jonka V5 Optical Sensori tunnistaa.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.hue()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Optical.hue()` antaa värisävyn arvon välillä **0 to 359** ja vastaavan värin voi tarksitaa Vex värispektrikuvasta.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Optical.hue());\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.hue()"},"sensing_optical_is_near_object":{"name":"sensing_optical_is_near_object","markdown":"# Optical on lähellä kohdetta/esinettä\n\nKertoo, havaitseeko V5 Optical Sensori näkökestässään kojdetta/esinettä.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.isNearObject()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Optical.isNearObject()` antaa arvon **true** jos esine on havaittu ja arvon **false** muuten.\n\nIKomentoa kannattaa käyttää ja varmistaa arvo **true** aina ennen kuin käytetään `Optical.color()` komentoa itse värin etsimiseen.\n\n```cpp\nif (Optical.isNearObject() && Optical.color() == red) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Red object detected!\");\n}\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.isNearObject()"},"sensing_optical_set_light":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light","markdown":"# Optical aseta valo päälle\n\nAsetaa V5 Optical Sensorin LED valon päälle.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLight(ledState);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Optical.setLight()`komentoa käytetään laittaan V5 Optical Sensor LED valo päälle.\n\nKomento hyväksyy vaihtoehdot **ledState::on** (päällä) tai **ledState::off** (pois päältä) parametrissa.\n\n**ledState::on** laittaa LED valon päälle.\n\n**ledState::off** ottaa  LED valon pois.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLight(ledState::on);\nwait(2, seconds);\nOptical.setLight(ledState::off);\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.setLight(ledState::on);"},"sensing_optical_set_light_power":{"name":"sensing_optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Optical aseta valon teho\n\nAsettaa V5 Optical Sensorin LED valon tehon.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLightPower(power, percent);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Optical.setLightPower()`komennon avulla voi asettaa V5 Optical Sensor Led valon tehon.\n\nKomento sallii arvot **0 - 100**  ensimmäisesä parametrissa.\n\nToinen parametri on yksikkö **percent** (%).\n\nMitä korkeampi arvo sitä kirkkaampi on LED valo ja päinvastoin himmeempi.\n\n```cpp\nOptical.setLightPower(100, percent);\nOptical.setLight(ledState::on);\n```","signature":"OPTICAL.setLightPower(100, percent);"},"sensing_pot_angle":{"name":"sensing_pot_angle","markdown":"# Potentiometrin kulma\n\nPalauttaa Potentiometertrin mittaaman kulman.\n\n```cpp\nPotentiometer.angle(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Potentiometer.angle()` antaa desimaaliarvon (muotoa *double*) Potentiometrin asentokulmalle.\n\nKomentoa voi käyttää arvona muissa komennoissa (kuten tulosta komennossa) tao ohjauslausekkeiden ehdoissa.\n\nAseta **degrees** (astetta) yksiköksi `units` parametriin ja arvot saa volla välillä **0.0 - 250.0 astetta**.\n\nJos yksikkö on **percent** (%), arvot ovat välillä **0 - 100%**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%f\", PotentiometerA.angle(degrees));\n```","signature":"POTENTIOMETER.angle(units)"},"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled":{"name":"sensing_remote_control_code_enabled","markdown":"# Controller Enable/Disable\n\n`RemoteControlCodeEnabled = false;`\n\nEnables or disables Controller-configured actions from the Devices menu.\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose to either enable or disable the configured Controller actions by declaring it as either `true` or `false`. By default, the Controller is Enabled in every project.\n\n## Example\n\nThe configured action in this example is using the robot's Drivetrain behavior set by the Controller's configuration in the Devices window.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/v5/cpp/fi/sensing_remote_control_code_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nThis example will have the configured Controller disabled when the program starts. \n\nThen, the robot will drive forward for 6 inches.\n\nFinally, the **controller enabled** command will enable the Controller to restore Controller driving behaviors.\n\n```cpp\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = false;\nDrivetrain.driveFor(forward, 6.0, inches);\nRemoteControlCodeEnabled = true;\n```","signature":"RemoteControlCodeEnabled = true;"},"sensing_rotation_angle":{"name":"sensing_rotation_angle","markdown":"# Rotation Angle\n\nAntaa V5 Rotation Sensorin mittaaman pyörimiskulman asteina.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.angle()\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Rotation.angle()` antaa arvot välillä **0.00** - **359.99**.\n\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Rotation.angle());\n```","signature":"ROTATION.angle()"},"sensing_rotation_position":{"name":"sensing_rotation_position","markdown":"# Pyörimisasento\n\nAntaa V5 Rotation Sensorin tämän hetkisen asennon.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.position(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Rotation.position()` hyväksyy sekä **degrees** (asteita) että **turns** (kierroksia) ja anta sekä negatiivisia että positiivisia desimaali arvoja.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Rotation.position(degrees));\n```\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Rotation.position(turns));\n```","signature":"ROTATION.position(degrees)"},"sensing_rotation_reset_position":{"name":"sensing_rotation_reset_position","markdown":"# Rotation.resetPosition();\n\nResetoi V5 Rotation Sensorin asentoarvon arvoon 0.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.resetPosition();\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Rotation.resetPosition()` voi resetoida Rotation Sensorin asennon arvoon 0.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.resetPosition();\n```","signature":"ROTATION.resetPosition();"},"sensing_rotation_set_position":{"name":"sensing_rotation_set_position","markdown":"# Rotation aseta asento\n\nAsettaa V5 Rotation Sensorin pyörimisasennolle tietyn arvon.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.setPosition(position, degrees);\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Rotation.setPosition()` yleisesti asetetaan astearvoon 0 kesken ohjelman suoritusta.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.setPosition(0, degrees);\n```","signature":"ROTATION.setPosition(0, degrees);"},"sensing_rotation_velocity":{"name":"sensing_rotation_velocity","markdown":"# Rotation Nopeus\n\nAntaa V5 Rotation Sensorin mittaaman nopeuden.\n\n```cpp\nRotation.velocity(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`Rotation.velocity()` hyväksyy sekä **rpm** (kierrosta minuutisa)  ja **dps** (asteita sekunnissa) ja antaa desimaaliarvona nopeuden.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Rotation.velocity(rpm));\n```\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(\"%.2f\", Rotation.velocity(dps));\n```","signature":"ROTATION.velocity(rpm)"},"sensing_sonar_distance":{"name":"sensing_sonar_distance","markdown":"# RangeFinder Etäisyys\n\nAntaa Ultrasonic Range Finder sensorin mittaaman etäisyyden lähimpään havaittuun kohteeseen.\n\n```cpp\nRangeFinder.distance(units)\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`RangeFinder.distance()` antaa arvot välillä **30mm - 3000mm**, jos yksikkönä on `mm`, tai **2 inches - 115 inches**, jos yksikkönä on tuumat `inches`.\n\n```cpp\nif (RangeFinderC.distance(mm) < 400.0){\n    Drivetrain.stop();\n}\n```","signature":"RANGEFINDER.distance(mm)"},"sensing_sonar_found_object":{"name":"sensing_sonar_found_object","markdown":"# RangeFinder Found Object\nReports if the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor sees an object within its field of view. \n\n```cpp\nRangeFinder.foundObject()\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`RangeFinder.foundObject()` reports **true** when the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n`RangeFinder.foundObject()` reports **false** when the Ultrasonic Range Finder sensor does not detect an object or surface.","signature":"RANGEFINDER.foundObject()"},"sensing_vision_largest_object":{"name":"sensing_vision_largest_object","markdown":"# Vision Suurin Kohde\n\nPalauttaa Kameran kuvasta havaituista kohteista suurimman kohteen tiedot.\n\n```cpp\nVision.largestObject\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nOta kuva `Vision.takeSnapshot` ennenkuin voit käyttää suurimman kohteen tietoja `Vision.largestObject` komennolla.\n\n`Vision.largestObject` suurimman kohteen komento on luokkatyyppiä `vision::object`. \n\n\n```cpp\n// Take a snapshot with the COLOR_SIG signature\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\n\nBrain.Screen.print(\"X: %d\", Vision.largestObject.centerX);\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\nBrain.Screen.print(\"Y: %d\", Vision.largestObject.centerY);\nBrain.Screen.newLine();\n```\n\n`Vision.largestObject` on luokkatyyppiä `vision::object` , jolla on seuraavat ominaisuudet.\n\n- `id`      - Kohteen yksikäsitteinen ID numero , on tyyppiä `int`\n- `originX` - Kohten vasen yläkulma X -akselilla, on tyyppiä `int`\n- `originY` - kohteen vasen yläkulma Y -akselilla, on tyyppiä `int`\n- `centerX` - Kohteen Keskipiste X-akselilla on tyyppiä `int`\n- `centerY` - Kohteen keskipiste Y -akselilla on tyyppiä `int`\n- `width`   - Kohteen leveys on tyyyppiä `int`\n- `height`  - Kohteen korkeus on tyyppiä `int`\n- `angle`   - Kohteen muodostama kulma kameraan on tyyppiä `double`\n- `exists`  - Jos kohde löytyy on tyyppiä `bool`","signature":"sensing_vision_largestObject;"},"sensing_vision_object_count":{"name":"sensing_vision_object_count","markdown":"# Vision Kohteiden lukumäärä\n\nRaportoi montako haettua kohdetta Vision -kamera havaitsee kuvassa. \n\n\nAn object will need to be configured before the `Vision.objectCount` command can detect it.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objectCount\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMäärittele Vision -kamera käyttöön Laitteet-ikkunassa\n\nMäärittele merkit/värikoodit Kameran määritysikkunassa. \n\nOta kuva `Vision.takeSnapshot` halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla .\n\n`Vision.objectCount` antaa viimeisimmästä kuvasta havaittujen kohteiden lukumäärän.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objectCount\n```\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä tulostetaan aivojen näytölle viimeisimmän kuvan havaittujen kohteiden lukumäärä.\n\n```cpp\nwhile (true) {\n  Brain.Screen.clearScreen();\n  Brain.Screen.setCursor(1, 1);\n\n  // Ota kuva merkillä SIGNATURE\n  Vision.takeSnapshot(SIGNATURE);\n\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Number of Objects Detected: %d\", Vision.objectCount);\n\n  // Ota kuva joka 20 millisekuntia\n  wait(20, msec);\n}\n```","signature":"VISION.objectCount"},"sensing_vision_objects":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects","markdown":"# Vision Kohteet\n\nAntaa taulukon kaikista Vision -kameran havaitsemista haetuista kohteista.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAina ensimmäisenä pitää ottaa kuva `Vision.takeSnapshot` ennen komentoa `Vision.objects` taulukkoa.\n\n`Vision.objects` on taulukko, jossa on kuvasta kaikkien havaittujen kohteiden tiedot.\n\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\nvision::object firstObject = Vision.objects[0];\n```\nKuvataulukkoa voi käyttää normaalin taulukon tavoin hyödyntämällä taulukon indeksejä.\n\n```cpp\nvision::object visionObject = Vision.objects[0];\n```\n\nVoit sijoittaa sen alkioita myös toistorakenteisiin esimerkiksi **for loops** komennossa `Vision.objectCount` arvoa voi käyttäää ehdoissa.\n\nEsimerkkiohjelmasssa alla ominaisuudet `centerX` and `centerY` arvot tulostetaan Aivojen näytölle.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(COLOR_SIG);\nfor(int i = 0; i < Vision.objectCount; i++) {\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"X: %d\", Vision.objects[i].centerX);\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n  Brain.Screen.print(\"Y: %d\", Vision.objects[i].centerY);\n  Brain.Screen.newLine();\n}\n```\n\n`Vision.objects` kohteet on luokkatyyppiä `vision::object` ja sillä on nämä ominaisuudet.\n\n- `id`      - Kohteen yksikäsitteinen ID numero , on tyyppiä `int`\n- `originX` - Kohten vasen yläkulma X -akselilla, on tyyppiä `int`\n- `originY` - kohteen vasen yläkulma Y -akselilla, on tyyppiä `int`\n- `centerX` - Kohteen Keskipiste X-akselilla on tyyppiä `int`\n- `centerY` - Kohteen keskipiste Y -akselilla on tyyppiä `int`\n- `width`   - Kohteen leveys on tyyyppiä `int`\n- `height`  - Kohteen korkeus on tyyppiä `int`\n- `angle`   - Kohteen muodostama kulma kameraan on tyyppiä `double`\n- `exists`  - Jos kohde löytyy on tyyppiä `bool`","signature":"sensing_vision_objects"},"sensing_vision_objects_angle":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_angle","markdown":"# Kohteen kulma\n\nRaportoi Vision -kameran havaitseman kohteen muodostaman kulman.\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].angle\n```\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTee järjestyksessä seuraavat toimenpideaskeleet, kun käytät `Vision.objects[index]` komentoa:\n\n1. Määrittele Vision -kamerasi Laitteet - ja Kameran määritysikkunassa.\n2. Käytä `Vision.takeSnapshot()` ottamaan kuvan ja etsimään siitä nimettyä merkkiä/värikoodia.\n3. Käytä `Vision.objects[index].exists` tarkistamaan että halutun kohteen merkki/värikoodi löytyy kuvassa. \n\nKun kohde löytyy, niin voit käyttää muita Vision -komentoja selvittämään tarkempia tietoja kohteeta. \n\n* Käytä **index** muuttujaa kiinnittämään kohde, josta haluat tarkempaa tietoa. Suurinesinekohde on aina edessä, jolloin se on  `Vision.objects[0]`.\n* Käytä `Vision.objectCount` määrittämään motako samanlaista kohdetta löytyy halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla.\n* Sitten voit käyttää muita ominaisuuksia: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` ja `exists`\n## How To Use\n\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].angle` raportoi esineen kamerakulman arvolla **0 - 180 degrees**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.screen.print(MyVision.objects[0].angle);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].angle"},"sensing_vision_objects_centerx":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_centerx","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].centerX\n\n\nAntaa Vision -kameran kuvan löytämän kohteen x -akselin keskipisteen.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].centerX\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTee järjestyksessä seuraavat toimenpideaskeleet, kun käytät `Vision.objects[index]` komentoa:\n\n1. Määrittele Vision -kamerasi Laitteet - ja Kameran määritysikkunassa.\n2. Käytä `Vision.takeSnapshot()` ottamaan kuvan ja etsimään siitä nimettyä merkkiä/värikoodia.\n3. Käytä `Vision.objects[index].exists` tarkistamaan että halutun kohteen merkki/värikoodi löytyy kuvassa. \n\nKun kohde öytyy, niin voit käyttää muita Vision -komentoja selvittämään tarkempia tietoja kohteeta. \n\n* Käytä **indeksi** muuttujaa kiinnittämään kohde, josta haluat tarkempaa tietoa. Suurinesinekohde on aina edessä, jolloin se on  `Vision.objects[0]`.\n* Käytä `Vision.objectCount` määrittämään motako samanlaista kohdetta löytyy halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla.\n* Sitten voit käyttää muita ominaisuuksia: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` ja `exists`.\n\n\n---\n`Vision.objects[index].centerX` raportoi löydetyn kohteen keskipisteen X koordinaatin arvolla **0 - 315 px**.\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[1].centerX);\n```\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].centerX` raportoi löydetyn kohteen keskipisteen X koordinaatin arvolla **0 - 315 px**.","signature":"VISION.objects[0].centerX"},"sensing_vision_objects_centery":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_centery","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].centerY\n\nReports the Y coordinate of the center of a detected object from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].centerY\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nIn order to use `Vision.objects[index]`, use the following steps:\n\n1. Configure your Vision Sensor using the Robot Configuration window.\n2. Use `Vision.takeSnapshot()` to capture a Vision Sensor image and look for a signature / color code.\n3. Use `Vision.objects[index].exists` to check if the Vision Sensor detected the requested signature / color code. \n\nOnce the Vision Sensor detects an object, you can use other Vision commands to learn more about the object detected. \n\n* Use the **index** to grab which detected object you want to learn more information about. The largest object will be in the front, such that `Vision.objects[0]` returns the largest object.\n* Use `Vision.objectCount` to determine how many objects were detected of that requested signature / color code.\n* Use can get the following information about each objects: `angle`, `centerX`, `centerY`, `height`, `width` and `exists`.\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].centerY` reports the Y coordinate of the center of the detected object. Returns a value of **0 - 211 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[2].centerY);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].centerY"},"sensing_vision_objects_exists":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_exists","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].exists\n\nReports if the Vision Sensor detects a configured object. \n\nAn object will need to be configured before the `Vision.objects[index].exists` command can detect it.\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].exists\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\nMake sure you specify the Vision Sensor when using this command. \n\n\n`Vision.objects[index].exists` reports **true** when the Vision Sensor detects a configured object.\n\n`Vision.objects[index].exists` reports **false** when the Vision Sensor does not detect a configured object.\n\nBefore the `Vision.objects[index].exists` can report reports a **true** or **false** value, `Vision.takeSnapshot()` will need to be used.\n\n\n```cpp\nif(Vision.objects[0].exists){\n\n}\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].exists;"},"sensing_vision_objects_height":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_height","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].height\n\n# Kohteen korkeus\n\nRaportoi Vision -kameran havaitseman kohteen korkeuden.\n\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].height\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTee järjestyksessä seuraavat toimenpideaskeleet, kun käytät `Vision.objects[index]` komentoa:\n\n1. Määrittele Vision -kamerasi Laitteet - ja Kameran määritysikkunassa.\n2. Käytä `Vision.takeSnapshot()` ottamaan kuvan ja etsimään siitä nimettyä merkkiä/värikoodia.\n3. Käytä `Vision.objects[index].exists` tarkistamaan että halutun kohteen merkki/värikoodi löytyy kuvassa. \n\nKun kohde löytyy, niin voit käyttää muita Vision -komentoja selvittämään tarkempia tietoja kohteeta. \n\n* Käytä **indeksi** muuttujaa kiinnittämään kohde, josta haluat tarkempaa tietoa. Suurin esinekohde on aina edessä, jolloin se on  `Vision.objects[0]`.\n* Käytä `Vision.objectCount` määrittämään motako samanlaista kohdetta löytyy halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla.\n* Sitten voit käyttää muita ominaisuuksia: `angle` (kulma), `centerX` (X keskipiste), `centerY` (Y keskipiste), `height` (korkeus), `width` (leveys) and `exists` (on olemassa)\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].height` antaa tiedon, kuinka korkea esine on pixeleinä. Arvot ovat välillä **2 - 212 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[3].height);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].height;"},"sensing_vision_objects_width":{"name":"sensing_vision_objects_width","markdown":"# Vision.objects[index].width\n\nRaportoi Vision -kameran havaitseman kohteen leveyden\n\n```cpp\nVision.objects[index].width\n```\n\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nTee järjestyksessä seuraavat toimenpideaskeleet, kun käytät `Vision.objects[index]` komentoa:\n\n1. Määrittele Vision -kamerasi Laitteet - ja Kameran määritysikkunassa.\n2. Käytä `Vision.takeSnapshot()` ottamaan kuvan ja etsimään siitä nimettyä merkkiä/värikoodia.\n3. Käytä `Vision.objects[index].exists` tarkistamaan että halutun kohteen merkki/värikoodi löytyy kuvassa. \n\nKun kohde löytyy, niin voit käyttää muita Vision -komentoja selvittämään tarkempia tietoja kohteeta. \n\n* Käytä **indeksi** muuttujaa kiinnittämään kohde, josta haluat tarkempaa tietoa. Suurin esinekohde on aina edessä, jolloin se on  `Vision.objects[0]`.\n* Käytä `Vision.objectCount` määrittämään motako samanlaista kohdetta löytyy halutulla merkillä/värikoodilla.\n* Sitten voit käyttää muita ominaisuuksia: `angle` (kulma), `centerX` (X keskipiste), `centerY` (Y keskipiste), `height` (korkeus), `width` (leveys) and `exists` (on olemassa)\n\n---\n\n`Vision.objects[index].width` antaa tiedon, kuinka leveä esine on pixeleinä. Arvot ovat välillä **2 - 316 px**.\n\n```cpp\nBrain.Screen.print(MyVision.objects[1].width);\n```","signature":"VISION.objects[0].width;"},"sensing_vision_take_snapshot":{"name":"sensing_vision_take_snapshot","markdown":"# Vision Take Snapshot\n\nTakes a snapshot from the Vision Sensor.\n\n```cpp\nVision.takeSnapshot(SIG_1);\n```\n\n## How To Use\n\n`Vision.takeSnapshot()` will capture the current image from the Vision Sensor, filter out the requested signatures, and copies the detected objects's data for further analysis.\n\nTypically, `Vision.takeSnapshot()` is required first before using any other Vision Sensor commands.\n\nMake sure you specify the Vision Sensor and the vision signature when using this command. Vision signatures are configured from the Robot Configuration window.","signature":"VISION.takeSnapshot(SIGNATURE);"},"variables_2d_arrays":{"name":"variables_2d_arrays","markdown":"# 2D Taulukko Muuttuja\n\nMäärittelee tyypin,nimen ja 2d taulukon koon ja antaa alkuarvot. \n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 },\n};\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMäärittele mitä tyyppiä 2d taulukkko on. \n\n- `int`\n- `double`\n- `bool`\n\nAnna yksikäsitteinen nimi, joka kuvaa taulukkon käyttöä ja koko 2 parilla hakasulkuja `[]` heti nimen jälkeen. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new 2D array with 3 rows and 3 columns\n\nint my2DArray[3][3];\n```\nOletusarvot taulukon alkiohin voi antaa aaltosuluissa yhtäläisyysmerkin jälkeen.\n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 }\n};\n```\n\nArvoja voi myös antaa indeksi kerrallaan, ensimmäinen indeksi on aina nolla. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new turnAngles array with 3 rows and 3 columns\nint turnAngles[3][3];\n\n// Assign values by index\nturnAngles[0][0] = 45;\nturnAngles[0][1] = 90;\nturnAngles[0][2] = 180;\nturnAngles[1][0] = 270;\n```\n\nKun arvoja käyttää, pitää haluttu alkio tarkentaa hakasuluilla.\n\n```cpp\n// The angle variable will be assigned the value of 270\n\nint angle = turnAngles[1][0];\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä **desimaali** 2d taulukko`myAngles` sisältää kulma-asteita.\n\n```cpp\ndouble myAngles[2][3] = {\n  {45.5, 90.0, 88.2},\n  {25.0, 75.5, 45.0}\n};\n```\n\n\n```cpp\nint my2DArray[3][3] = { \n  { 0, 1, 2 },\n  { 3, 4, 5 },\n  { 6, 7, 8 },\n};\n```\n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new 2D array with 3 rows and 3 columns\n\nint my2DArray[3][3];\n```\n\n\nArvoja voi myös antaa indeksi kerrallaan, ensimmäinen indeksi on aina nolla. \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new turnAngles array with 3 rows and 3 columns\nint turnAngles[3][3];\n\n// Assign values by index\nint turnAngles[0][0] = 45;\nint turnAngles[0][1] = 90;\nint turnAngles[0][2] = 180;\nint turnAngles[1][0] = 270;\n```","signature":"variables_2d_array"},"variables_arrays":{"name":"variables_arrays","markdown":"# Taulukko/Luettelo Muuttuja\n\nMäärittele tyyppi, nimi ja taulukon (luettelon) nimi. \n\n```cpp\nint myArray[3] = { 1, 2, 3 };\n```\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nMäärittele minkä tyyppistä dataa taulukko sisältää. \n\n- `int`\n- `double`\n- `bool`\n\nTaulukon nimi pitää olla yksikäsitteinen ja kuvaava. Aseta taulukkona alkioiden lukumäärä hakasuluissa `[]` heti nimen jälkeen. \n\n```cpp\nint turnAngles[3];\n```\n\nAlkuarvot voi antaa heti taulukon luonnissa aaltosuluissa.\n\n```cpp\nbool boolArray[2] = { false, true };\n```\n\nArvot voi myös antaa yksitellen indeksi kerrallaan indeksiarvosta 0 lähtien.  \n\n```cpp\n// Declare a new array of length 3\ndouble doubleArray[3];\n\n// Assign values to the array by index\ndoubleArray[0] = 1.5;\ndoubleArray[1] = 3.14;\ndoubleArray[2] = 2.18;\n```\n\n\nKun sijoitat taulukon arvoja johonkin, niin valitse indeksiarvo hakasuluissa.\n\n```cpp\n// Read the value at index 2 in integerArray\n\nint value = integerArray[2];\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nEsimerkissä numerotaulukolle annetaan alkuarvot ja alkio #3 (indeksi arvo 2) sijoitetaan Moottorin kääntymiskulmaksi asteina. \n\n```cpp\nint degreesArray[3] = { 30, 60, 90 };\nMotor.spinFor(forward, degreesArray[2], degrees);\n```","signature":"variables_arrays"},"variables_boolean":{"name":"variables_boolean","markdown":"# Boolean Muuttuja\n\nMuuttaja saa arvot **tosi** tai **epätosi**.\n\n`bool myBoolean = true;`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Boolean Muuttuja** arvo voi olla **tosi** tai **epätosi**. Määrittele muuttujanimen alkuun `bool` ja anna sille alkuarvo `tosi` tai `epätosi`.\n\nBoolean muuttujia voi käyttää ohjauslausekkeiden ehtoina. \n\n```cpp\n`bool goFast = true;`\n\nif (goFast) {\n  Drivetrain.setDriveVelocity(100, percent);\n}\n```\n\nBoolean muuttujia voi käyttää ohjauskomentojen ehdoissa.","signature":"variables_boolean"},"variables_double":{"name":"variables_double","markdown":"# Desimaali Muuttuja\n\nMäärittelee muuttujan `desimaali` tyyppiseksi.\n\n`double myDouble = 1.5;`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n`desimaali` muuttujatyypin muuttuja on luku, jossa on desimaalipiste.\n\n`double pi = 3.14;`\n\nAnna muuttujalle yksikäsitteinen ja kuvaava nimi ja anna sille alkuarvo.\n\n`double turnAngle = 40.5;`","signature":"variables_double"},"variables_integer":{"name":"variables_integer","markdown":"# Kokonaisluku muuttuja\n\nMäärittelee kokonaislukumuuttujan ja antaa sille nimen ja alkuarvon.\n\n`int myNumber = 10;`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\nAnna yksikäsitteinen ja kuvaava nimi muuttujalle.\n\n`int driveTime = 60;`\n\nAnna muuttujalle alkuarvo. Muuttujan arvo voi olla jonkun sensorin antama arvo tai laskutoimituksen tulos edellyttäen, että tulos on oikeaa **tyyppiä**.\n\n```cpp\nint lowBatteryLifeWarning = Brain.Battery.capacity(percent);\n```\n\n## Esimerkki\n\nTässä esimerkissä VEX V5 etäisyysanturin mittaama etäisyysarvo sijoitetaan \"myVariable\" muuttujaan ja sen jälkeen \"myVariable\" sijoitetaan ajopelin nopeudeksi.\n\n```cpp\nint myVariable = Distance7.objectDistance(inches);\n\nDrivetrain.setDriveVelocity(myVariable, percent);\n```","signature":"variables_intergers"},"variables_strings":{"name":"variables_strings","markdown":"# Merkkijono muuttuja\n\nMäärittele muuttujan **Merkkijono** tyyppiseksi ja antaa sille nimen ja alkusisällön.\n\n`char myString[] = \"my string\";`\n\n## Miten käytetään\n\n**Merkkijono** muuttujatyyppiseen muuttujaan voi sijoittaa sekä numeroita että kirjaimia, kun ne on heittomerkkien `\" \"`välissä.\n\nLuo yksikäsitteinen ja kuvaava nimi muuttujalle. Anna sisältö **Merkkijono** muuttujalle.  Vexcodessa  **Merkkijono** muuttujatyyppin sisältö voidaan antaa näin.\n\n`char driveMessage[] = \"Time to Drive!\";`","signature":"variables_my_string"},"vexcodeinit":{"name":"vexcodeinit","markdown":"# vexcodeInit();\n\n`vexcodeInit();` käytetään määrittämään ja alustamaan laitekonfiguraatiot Robotin konfigurointivälineellä. \n\n`The vexcodeInit();` on aina  \"int main\" funktion alussa varmistamaan, että laitteet on määritelty ennen muita komentoja.\n\nKos poistat tai laitat kommenteihin  `vexcodeInit();` kohdan aiheuttaa sen, etteivät laitteet toimi kunnolla ohjelmassasi.","signature":"vexcodeInit();"}}},"pl":{"blocks":{"acceleration_of":{"name":"acceleration_of","markdown":"# Przyspieszenie\n\nPodaje wartość przyspieszenia z jednej osi na akcelerometrze analogowym.\n\n![acceleration_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Acceleration of** podaje zakres od **-2.0 G do 2.0 G** olub **-6.0 G do 6.0 G** w zależności od ustawienia zworki na akcelerometrze analogowym.\n\nWybierz akcelerometr, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![acceleration_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_device.png)\n\nBlok **acceleration of** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![acceleration_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_inserted.png)"},"activate_emergency_stop":{"name":"activate_emergency_stop","markdown":"# Aktywuj zatrzymanie awaryjne\n\nAktywuje przycisk zatrzymania awaryjnego ramienia robota V5.\n\n![estop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/activate_emergency_stop/estop_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nPrzycisk zatrzymania awaryjnego w komórce roboczej wyłączy wszelkie inteligentne silniki i czujniki V5 podłączone do mózgu V5.\n\n![estop_robot](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/activate_emergency_stop/estop_robot.png)\n\nWybierz ramię robota, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![select_estop_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/activate_emergency_stop/select_estop_arm.png)\n\nBlok **activate emergency stop** jest często używany z blokiem \"kiedy\" z kategorii Zdarzenia. Gwarantuje to, że wszystkie inteligentne silniki i czujniki V5 podłączone do mózgu V5 wyłączy się po naciśnięciu wyłącznika zderzaka (E-stop).\n![estop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/activate_emergency_stop/estop_example.png)"},"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Dodaj\n\nDodaje do siebie dwie dowolne wartości i podaje sumę.\n\n![add](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/add/add.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Dodaj** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok **dodaj** pasuje do bloków, które posiadają okrągłe wolne miejsca i mogą zawierać inne okrągłe bloki. \n\nDodawanie dwóch liczb.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nDodaj wartości ze zmiennych.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nDodaj wartości z czujników lub urządzeń.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/add/add_sensors.png)\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# I\n\nPotwierdza czy oba warunki logiczne są prawdziwe. \n\n![and](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/and/and.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **i** raportuje **prawda** kiedy oba warunki są **prawda**. \n\nBlok **i** raportuje **fałsz** kiedy jeden lub oba warunki są **fałsz**.\n\nBlok **i** raportuje **prawda** lub **fałsz** i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami\n\n![and_shape](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład sprawdzi, czy dwa przyciski kontrolera V5 są naciskane w tym samym czasie.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nBlok **and** zwróci **true** kiedy oba **controller1 X button** i **controller1 A button** są wcieśnięte.\n\nBlok **and** zwróci **false** gdy jeden (lub oba) z przycisków sterownika nie są wciśnięte.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/and/and_truth.png)"},"angle_of":{"name":"angle_of","markdown":"# Kąt\n\nZwraca pozycję kątową potencjometru.\n\n![angle_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/angle_of/angle_of_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Angle of** zwraca zakres od **0% do 100%** lub **0.0 do 250.0 stopnii**.\n\nWybierz potencjometr, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![angle_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/angle_of/angle_of_device.png)\n\nWybierz, czy wartość ma być podawana w % czy w stopniach.\n\n![angle_of_block_parameters](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/angle_of/angle_of_parameters.png)\n\nBlok **angle of** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![angle_of_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/angle_of/angle_of_inserted.png)\n"},"battery_current":{"name":"battery_current","markdown":"# Natężenie prądu w baterii\n\nPodaje natężenie prąd w baterii Mózgu V5.\n\n![battery_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/battery_current/battery_current_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Battery current** zwraca zakres od **0.0 amps do 20.0 amps**.\n\nBlok **battery current** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![battery_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/battery_current/battery_current_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Poziom baterii\n\nPodaje poziom naładowania baterii VEX V5.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Battery level** podaje zakres od **0% do 100%**.\n\nBlok **battery level** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)"},"battery_voltage":{"name":"battery_voltage","markdown":"# Napięcie baterii\n\nPodaje napięcie baterii Mózgu V5.\n\n![battery_voltage_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Battery voltage** zwraca zakres od **10.0 volts do 14.4 volts**.\n\nBlok **battery voltage** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![battery_voltage_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_inserted.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Zmienna logiczna\n\nPodaje wartość zmiennej logicznej.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **zmienna logiczna** zwraca wartość **prawda** lub **fałsz** w zależności od przechowywanej wewnątrz zmiennej. Użyj bloku **set zmienna logiczna**, aby ustawić lub zaktualizować wartość zmiennej logicznej.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nBlok **zmienna logiczna** zmiennej logicznej zwraca **prawda** lub **fałsz** value i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nWartość logiczna jest tworzona po naciśnięciu przycisku **stwórz zmienną logiczną**.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Przerwa\n\nPrzerywa istniejącą pętlę.\n\n![break](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/break/break.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nPo dodaniu do powtarzającego się bloku „C”, blok **przerwa** zakończy pętlę, w której się aktualnie znajduje.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład przesunie napęd do przodu i sprawdzi, czy przycisk VEX IQ Brain **up** jest naciśnięty. \n\nKiedy przycisk **up** jest **pressed**, blok **break** opuści pętlę  i zatrzyma układ napędowy\n\n![break_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Jasność\n\nPodaje ilość światła wykrytą przez czujnik koloru VEX IQ.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Brightness of** podaje dane w zakresie **0% do 100%**.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika koloru chcesz użyć.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nBlok **brightness of** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![brightness_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Nadaj\n\nBlok nadaj nadaje komunikat aby odtworzyć wszystkie stosy zaczynające sie od **kiedy otrzymam**, bloki te oczekuja na nadawaną wiadomość.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nStos, który wysyła **nadaj**, będzie nadal uruchamiał bloki w tym samym czasie, co inne stosy, które odbierają wiadomość.\n\nWybierz, która wwiadomość ma być nadana **nadaj**. Można również stworzyć nową wiadomość.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Nadaj i czekaj\n\nNadaje wiadomośc, aby aktywować wszystkie stosy, które zaczynaja się od  **when I receive** blok ten czeka na otrzymanie wiadomości jednocześnie blokując resztę stosu.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nStos wysyłający zgłoszenie **broadcast and wait** zatrzyma się, aż inne stosy odbierające zgłoszoną wiadomość zostaną zakończone.\n\nWybierz wiadomość do **broadcast**. Można również utworzyć nową wiadomość.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Skalibruj żyroskop\n\nKalibracja czujnika żyroskopowego VEX IQ służy do zmniejszenia wartości odchylenia generowanej przez czujnik żyroskopowy.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nDryfowanie występuje, gdy czujnik żyroskopowy nieprawidłowo wykrywa ruch, mimo że czujnik się nie porusza.\n\n## Jak używać\n\nCzujnik żyroskopowy / czujnik inercyjny musi pozostać nieruchomy podczas procesu kalibracji. Proces kalibracji zajmie około 2 sekund.\n\nWybierz, który żyroskop / czujnik bezwładnościowy ma być używany.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Zmień zmienną\n\nZmienia zmienną o podaną wartość.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz zmienną, której chcesz użyć - wybranej zmiennej można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nBlok **zmień zmienną** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie zmieniamy zmienną, która ustawia prędkość napędu, o 10 za każdym razem gdy zotanie wykonana pętla **powtórz pętlę**\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Wyczyść wszystkie wiersze\n\nCzyści cały ekran konsoli, Mózgu lub kontrolera.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Clear all rows** nie zmieni kursora na ekranie (Mózgu lub kontolera). Użyj**set cursor**, aby zresetować kursor ekranu do określonej pozycji.\n\nJednak przy użyciu bloku **clear all rows** wybranie opcji Konsola spowoduje zresetowanie pozycji kursora do górnej części okna programu Print Console.\n\nWybierz urządzenie, którego chcesz użyć. Kontrolery V5 pojawią się tylko wtedy, gdy zostaną dodane w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![clear_all_rows_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_dropdown_with_console.png)"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Wyczyść wiersz\n\nCzyści pojedynczy wiersz na ekranie mózgu lub kontrolera V5.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **Clear row** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne z przedziału od **1 do 20**, aby ustawić wiersz do wyczyszczenia.\n\nWybierz urządzenie, którego chcesz użyć. Kontrolery V5 pojawią się tylko wtedy, gdy zostaną dodane w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![clear_row_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/clear_row/clear_row_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nV5 Brain umożliwia zmianę rozmiaru czcionki drukowanej na ekranie. Zmiana czcionki wpłynie na liczbę wierszy dostępnych na ekranie Mózgu.\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki V5 Brain - Liczba wierszy:**\n\n* Bardzo małe - 20 wierszy\n* Mały - 16 wierszy\n* Średni - 12 wierszy (domyślnie)\n* Duży - 8 wierszy\n* Bardzo duży - 6 wierszy\n* Bardzo duży - 4 wiersza\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/clear_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nKontroler V5 nie pozwala na zmianę rozmiaru czcionki drukowanej na ekranie.\n\n** Rozmiar czcionki kontrolera V5 - liczba wierszy: **\n\n* Czcionka standardowa - 3 rzędy (domyślnie)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/clear_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Komentarz\n\nUmożliwia programistom pisanie informacji pomagających opisać program.\n\n![comment_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nProfesjonalni programiści używają komentarzy w swoich programach, aby pomóc innym zrozumieć ich kod. Komentarze mogą również pomóc w rozwiązywaniu problemów i we współpracy.\n\nDodaj tekst do bloku **Comment**, najpierw wybierając przezroczysty prostokąt i usuwając istniejący tekst. Następnie wpisz nowy tekst.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nKomentarze nie zmieniają programu ani otaczających go bloków.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Kontroler jest aktywny/wyłączony\n\nWłącza lub wyłącza działania skonfigurowane przez kontroler w menu Urządzenia.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, czy chcesz włączyć, czy wyłączyć skonfigurowane akcje kontrolera, wybierając żądany stan z listy rozwijanej. Domyślnie kontroler jest włączony w każdym projekcie.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie, skonfigurowana akcja wykorzystuje zachowanie układu napędowego robota, ustawione przez konfigurację kontrolera w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nW tym przykładzie skonfigurowany kontroler będzie wyłączony podczas uruchamiania programu.\n\nNastępnie robot będzie jechał do przodu przez 6 cali.\n\nW końcu blok **controller enabled** umożliwi Kontrolerowi przywrócenie zachowania, podczas jazdy.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"controller_play_rumble":{"name":"controller_play_rumble","markdown":"# Kontroler zagra dudnienie\n\nTworzy efekt wibracji na kontrolerze V5.\n\n![controller_play_rumble](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nAkcja **controller play rumble** wykorzystuje silnik wibracyjny w kontrolerze V5, aby zapewnić informację zwrotną.\n\nWybierz wzór, którego chcesz użyć.\n![controller_play_rumble_pattern](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_pattern.png)\n\nFunkcja wykorzystuje silnik wibracyjny w kontrolerze V5, aby zapewnić bezpieczeństwo zwrotną.\n\nWybierz wzór, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_device.png)\n\n\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Natężenie prądu silnika\n\nPodaje ilość energii, jaką inteligentny silnik V5 aktualnie zużywa w amperach (amps).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Current of motor** podaje dane w zakresie **0.0 do 2.5 amps**. \n\nWybierz jaki silnik użyć.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nBlok **current of motor** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Kolumna kursora\n\nPodaje numer kolumny lokalizacji kursora na ekranie Mózgu lub kontrolera.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Cursor column** podaje zakres od **1 do 80**.\n\nBlok **cursor column** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nMózg V5 umożliwia zmianę rozmiaru czcionki drukowanej na ekranie. Zmiana czcionki wpłynie na liczbę kolumn dostępnych na ekranie V5 Brain.\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki V5 Brain - Liczba kolumn:**\n\n* Bardzo małe - 80 kolumn\n* Mały - 68 kolumn\n* Średni - 48 kolumn (domyślnie)\n* Duży - 32 kolumny\n* Bardzo duży - 24 kolumny\n* Super duży - 16 kolumn\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/cursor_column/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nKontroler V5 nie pozwala na zmianę rozmiaru czcionki drukowanej na ekranie.\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki kontrolera V5 - liczba kolumn:**\n\n* Czcionka standardowa - 20 kolumn (domyślnie)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/cursor_column/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Kursor wiersza\n\nPodaje numer wiersza lokalizacji kursora na ekranie Mózgu ;ub kontrolera.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Cursor row** podaje zakres od **1 do 20**.\n\nBlok **cursor row** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nV5 Brain umożliwia zmianę rozmiaru czcionki drukowanej na ekranie. Zmiana czcionki wpłynie na liczbę wierszy dostępnych na ekranie V5 Brain.\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki V5 Brain - Liczba wierszy:**\n\n* Bardzo małe - 20 wierszy\n* Mały - 16 wierszy\n* Średni - 12 wierszy (domyślnie)\n* Duży - 8 wierszy\n* Bardzo duży - 6 wierszy\n* Bardzo duży - 4 wiersze\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/cursor_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nKontroler V5 nie pozwala na zmianę rozmiaru czcionki drukowanej na ekranie.\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki kontrolera V5 - liczba wierszy:**\n\n* Czcionka standardowa - 3 rzędy (domyślnie)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/cursor_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"distance_found_object":{"name":"distance_found_object","markdown":"# Czujnik odległości znalazł obiekt\n\nInformuje, czy czujnik odległości widzi obiekt w swoim polu widzenia.\n\n![distance_found_object_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block1.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Distance object found** zgłasza prawdę, gdy czujnik odległości widzi obiekt lub powierzchnię w swoim polu widzenia.\n\n**Distance object found** zgłasza fałsz, gdy czujnik odległości nie wykrywa obiektu lub powierzchni.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika odległości chcesz użyć.\n\n![distance_found_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block2.png)\n\nBlok **distance object found** zwraca **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![distance_found_object_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block3.png)\n"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Odległość od\n\nPodaje odległość najbliższego obiektu od czujnika odległości VEX IQ.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Distance from** podaje dane w zakresie od **30mm do 3000mm** lib **2 cali do 115 cali**.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika odległości chcesz użyć.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nWybierz czy **distance from** ma być podawana w calach czy milimetrach\n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nBlok **distance from** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"distance_object_distance":{"name":"distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Odległość obiektu\n\nPodaje odległość najbliższego obiektu od czujnika odległości.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Object distance** zwraca zakres od **20mm do 2000mm**.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika odległości chcesz użyć.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block2.png)\n\nWybierz czy **object distance** jest podawana w calach lub milimetrach.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block3.png)\n\nBlok **object distance** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block4.png)\n"},"distance_object_size":{"name":"distance_object_size","markdown":"# Rozmiar obiektu to\n\nRaportuje, czy czujnik odległości wykryje określony rozmiar obiektu. \n\n![distance_object_size_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nCzujnik określa rozmiar wykrywanego obiektu (brak, mały, średni, duży) na podstawie ilości światła odbitego i zwróconego do czujnika.\n\nWybierz czujnik odległości, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![distance_object_size_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block1.png)\n\nWybierz rozmiar obiektu, który ma być sprawdzany przez czujnik.\n\n![distance_object_size_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block2.png)\n\nBlok **Object size is** zwraca **true** gdy czujnik odległości wykryje określony rozmiar.\n\nBlok **Object size is** zwraca **false** jeśli nie wykryje określonego rozmiaru.\n\nBlok **Object size is** zwraca **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![distance_object_size_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block3.png)\n"},"distance_object_velocity":{"name":"distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Prędkość obiektu\n\nPodaje aktualną prędkość obiektu w m / s.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Object velocity** podaje aktualną prędkość obiektu w m/s (metry na sekundę).\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika odległości chcesz użyć.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block2.png)\n\n\nBlok **object velocity** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami. \n\n![distance_object_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block3.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Podziel\n\nDzieli pierwszą wartość przez drugą wartość i podaje resztę.\n\n![divide](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Divide** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok **divide** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe wypełnienia, i mogą również zawierać okrągłe bloki.\n\nWprowadź liczby do podzielenia.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nPodziel przez wartości zmiennych.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nPodzielić przez wartość z czujników lub urządzeń.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"draw_circle":{"name":"draw_circle","markdown":"# Narysuj okrąg\n\nRysuje okrąg na ekranie Mózgu V5.\n\n![draw_circle](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/draw_circle/draw_circle.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBlok **draw circle** wymaga podania 3 wartości:\n\n* Wartość 1: Punkt środkowy X\n* Wartość 2: Punkt środkowy Y\n* Wartość 3: promień okręgu (w pikselach)\n\nKolor zewnętrznej linii koła jest określany przez blok **set pen color**. Domyślnym kolorem linii jest biały.\n\nKolor wypełnienia wewnętrznego koła jest określony przez blok **set fill color**. Domyślnym kolorem wypełnienia jest czarny.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"draw_line":{"name":"draw_line","markdown":"# Narysuj linię\n\nRysuje linię na ekranie Mózgu V5.\n\n![draw_line](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/draw_line/draw_line.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **draw line** wymaga wprowadzenia 4 wartości:\n\n* Wartość 1: Początkowa współrzędna X\n* Wartość 2: Początkowa współrzędna Y.\n* Wartość 3: Końcowa współrzędna X\n* Wartość 4: Końcowa współrzędna Y.\n\nKolor linii jest określany przez blok **set pen color**. Domyślnym kolorem linii jest biały.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_pixel":{"name":"draw_pixel","markdown":"# Narysuj pixel\n\nRysuje piksel na ekranie Mózgu V5.\n\n![draw_pixel](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/draw_pixel/draw_pixel.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **draw pixel** wymaga podania 2 wartości:\n\n* Wartość 1: współrzędna X\n* Wartość 2: współrzędna Y\n\nKolor piksela jest określany przez blok **set pen color**. Domyślnym kolorem piksela jest biały.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_rectangle":{"name":"draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Narysuj prostokąt\n\nRysuje prostokąt na ekranie Mózgu V5.\n\n![draw_rectangle](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/draw_rectangle/draw_rectangle.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **draw rectangle** wymaga podania 4 wartości:\n\n* Wartość 1: Współrzędna X górnego lewego rogu\n* Wartość 2: współrzędna Y górnego lewego narożnika\n* Wartość 3: szerokość prostokąta\n* Wartość 4: wysokość prostokąta\n\nKolor zewnętrznej linii prostokąta jest określony przez blok **set pen color**. Domyślnym kolorem linii jest biały.\n\nWewnętrzny kolor wypełnienia prostokąta jest określony przez blok **set fill color**. Domyślnym kolorem wypełnienia jest czarny.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Jedź\n\nZaczyna poruszać napędem na zawsze.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **drive** uruchomi napęd, do momentu użycia nowego bloku na zawsze lub zatrzymania programu.\n\nWybierz kierunek, w którym będzie się poruszał układ napędowy.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Natężenie prądu w napędzie\n\nPodaje ilość prądu (mocy) aktualnie używanego przez układ napędowy.\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive current** podaje dane w zakresie od **0.0 do 2.5 amps**. \n\nBlok **drive current** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_efficiency":{"name":"drive_efficiency","markdown":"# Sprawność napędu\n\nPodaje sprawność układu napędowego.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Drive efficiency** podaje wartość mocy (w watach), którą silnik wykorzystuje (wejście), w porównaniu z ilością mocy (w watach), którą silnik dostarcza (wyjście).\n\nUkład napędowy V5 zazwyczaj osiąga maksymalną wydajność 65% w normalnych przypadkach użytkowania.\n\n**Drive efficiency** podaje zakres między **0% a 100%**. \n\nBlok **drive efficiency** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki.\n\n![drive_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Jedź o\n\nPrzesuwa układ napędowy na zadaną odległość.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, w którym kierunku będzie się poruszał układ napędowy.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\nUstaw, jak daleko przesunie się układ napędowy, wprowadzając wartość i wybierając jednostkę miary (cale lub milimetry).\n\nBlok **Drive for** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nDomyślnie, inne bloki **wait** aż układ napędowy zakonczy ruch.\n\nMożna strzałka wybrać opcję **and don't wait** z listy rozwijanej - spowoduje to, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy układ napędowy będzie się poruszał.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Pozycja jazdy\n\nPodaje kierunek, w którym zwrócony jest układ napędowy, na podstawie aktualnego położenia kątowego czujnika żyroskopowego.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBlok **drive heading** porusza się w kierunku zgodnym do ruchu wskazówek zegara,\n\n**Drive heading** podaje zakres od **0.00 do 359.99 stopni**.\n\nBlok **drive heading** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Zakończona jazda\n\nZgłasza, czy układ napędowy zakończył ruch.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive is done** zwraca **true** kiedy silniki układu napędowego zakończą swój ruch.\n\n**Drive is done** zwraca **false** kiedy silniki układu napędowego dalej sie poruszają.\n\nBlok **drive is done** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami..\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Napęd się porusza\n\nInformuje czy układ napędowy jest w ruchu.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive is moving** zwraca **true** kiedy silniki  są w ruchu.\n\n**Drive is moving** zwraca **false** kiedy silniki nie ruszają się.\n\nBlok **drive is moving** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_power":{"name":"drive_power","markdown":"# Moc napędowa\n\nPodaje ilość mocy wyjściowej aktualnie generowanej przez układ napędowy.\n\n![drive_power](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_power/drive_power.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Drive power** podaje zakres od **0.0 do 22.0 watów**. \n\nBlok **drive power** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_power/drive_power_inserted.png)"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Obrót napędu\n\nPodaje kąt obrotu układu napędowego w przypadku konfiguracji z 3-przewodowym czujnikiem żyroskopowym lub czujnikiem bezwładnościowym V5.\n\n![drive_rotation](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_rotation/drive_rotation.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive rotation** zwraca **positive** kiedy napęd obraca się w **clockwise** .\n\n**Drive rotation** zwraca **negative** kiedy napęd obraca się w **counter-clockwise**.\n\nBlok **drive rotation** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_rotation_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_rotation/drive_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_temperature":{"name":"drive_temperature","markdown":"# Temperatura napędu\n\nPodaje temperaturę inteligentnych silników V5 zasilających układ napędowy.\n\n![drive_temperature](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_temperature/drive_temperature.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Drive temperature** podaje zakres od **0% do 100%**. \n\nBlok **drive temperature** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_temperature_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_temperature/drive_temperature_inserted.png)"},"drive_torque":{"name":"drive_torque","markdown":"# Moment obrotowy\n\nPodaje wartość momentu obrotowego (siły obrotowej) aktualnie używanej przez układ napędowy.\n\n![drive_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_torque/drive_torque.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Drive torque** podaje wartość z zakresu **0.0 do 18.6 inch-pounds / moment siły (InLB)** lub **0.0 do 2.1 Niutonometrów (Nm)**. \n\nWybierz czy blok **drive torque** ma podawć wartości w inch-pounds / momencie siły  (InLb) czy niutonometrach (Nm).\n\n![drive_torque_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_torque/drive_torque_unit.png)\n\nBlok **drive torque** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_torque/drive_torque_inserted.png)"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Prędkość jazdy\n\nPodaje aktualną prędkość układu napędowego.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Drive velocity** podawana jest w zakresie od  **-100% do 100%** lub **-600rpm do 600rpm**.\n\n**Drive velocity** zgłosi zakres „obrotów na minutę” na podstawie wkładu zębatego zainstalowanego w inteligentnych silnikach V5 używanych w układzie napędowym.\n\n* Czerwony wkład: od -100 obr./min do 100 obr./min\n* Wkład zielony: od -200 do 200 obr./min\n* Wkład niebieski: od -600 do 600 obr./min\n\nWybierz, czy prędkość jest podawana w %, czy w obrotach na minutę (rpm).\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nBlok **drive velocity** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"duration":{"name":"duration","markdown":"# Ustaw czas trwania magnesu\n\nUstawia, jak długo elektromagnes V5 jest włączony.\n\n![set_duration_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/duration/set_duration_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz, aby ustawić, jak długo elektromagnes jest włączony w celu przyciągania:\n\n* **krótki** - zasila elektromagnes przez **250 ms**\n* **średni** - zasila elektromagnes przez **500 ms**\n* **długi** - zasila elektromagnes przez **1000 ms**\n\n![set_duration_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/duration/set_duration_block_setting.png)\n\nWybierz, którego elektromagnesu użyć.\n\n![set_duration_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/duration/set_duration_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład mówi robotowi, aby jechał do przodu 200 mm, użył bloku **set electromagnet duration** ab ustalić długość na **long**, następnie **Electromagnet** przyciągnie obiekt, aby go podnieść, przejedzie 200 mm do przodu, a następnie upuści obiekt.\n\n![set_duration_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/duration/set_duration_example.png)\n"},"efficiency_of_motor":{"name":"efficiency_of_motor","markdown":"# Sprawność silnika\n\nPodaje wydajność inteligentnego silnika V5.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Efficiency of motor** podaje wartość mocy (w watach), którą silnik wykorzystuje (wejście), w porównaniu z ilością mocy (w watach), którą silnik dostarcza (wyjście).\n\nInteligentny silnik V5 zazwyczaj osiąga maksymalną sprawność 65% w normalnych przypadkach użytkowania.\n\n**Efficiency of motor** podaje wartość z zakresu od **0% do 100%**. \n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![motor_efficiency_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_device.png)\n\nBlok **Efficiency of motor** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki.\n\n![motor_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_inserted.png)"},"energize":{"name":"energize","markdown":"# Pobudź elektromagnes\n\nUstawia elektromagnes V5 na dwa różne tryby: **podnieś** lub **upuść**.\n\n![set_magnet_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/energize/set_magnet_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz, aby ustawić przyciąganie lub odpychanie elektromagnesu\n\n* **podnieś** - włącza elektromagnes na tak długo, jak ustawiono czas\n* **upuść** - zwalnia każdy przedmiot trzymany przez elektromagnes\n\nPo włączeniu magnesu będzie on musiał ostygnąć, zanim będzie można go ponownie użyć.\n\n![set_magnet_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/energize/set_magnet_block_setting.png)\n\nWybierz, którego elektromagnesu użyć.\n\n![set_magnet_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/energize/set_magnet_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie robot będzie jechał do przodu o 200 mm, **Electromagnet** przyciągnie obiekt aby go podnieść, przejedzie 200 mm do przodu, a następnie upuści obiekt.\n\n![set_magnet_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/energize/set_magnet_example.png)\n"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Równe z\n\nPodaje, czy pierwsza wartość jest taka sama lub równa drugiej wartości. \n\n![equal_to](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Equal to** zwraca **true** gdy te dwie wartości są dokładnie takie same\n\n**Equal to** zwraca **false** gdy te dwie wartości nie są takie same\n\nBlok **equal to** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok **equal to** zwraca zmienna logiczną **true** lub **false** i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscam.\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Bez końca\n\nBlok typu „C”, który bez końca wszystkie bloki zawarte w środku.\n\n![forever](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nUmieśc bloki w bloku **forever** aby te czynności powtarzały się **forever**.\n\nMożesz wyjść z pętli **forever**umiesszczając blok **break** wewnątrz.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nBloki typu'C' można również umieścić jeden w drugim. Pojęcie to nazywa się zagnieżdżaniem, które może pomóc zaoszczędzić czas podczas programowania różnych zachowań."},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Funkcje\n\nWykonuje wybraną funkcję matematyczną.\n\n![function](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - wartośc absolutna\n* **floor** - zaokrągla w dół do najbliższej liczby całkowitej\n* **ceiling** - zaokrągla w górę do najbliższej liczby całkowitej\n* **sqrt** - pierwiastek kwadratowy\n* **sin** - sinus\n* **cos** - cosinus\n* **tan** - tanges\n* **asin** - arcsine lub odwrotność sinusa\n* **acos** - arccosine lub odwrotność cosinusa\n* **atan** - arctan lub odwrotność tangensa\n* **ln** - podstawa logarytmu naturalnego e\n* **log** - logarytm o podstawie 10\n* **e ^** - potęga e\n* **10 ^** - potęga 10\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **function** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWyberz mateematyczną **function** z listy opcji.\n\n![function_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/function/function_select.png)\n\nBlok **function** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe miejsca.\n\n![function_fit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Wiekse niż\n\nPodaje, czy pierwsza wartość jest większa niż druga wartość.  \n\n![greater_than](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Greater than** zwraca **true** gdy pierwsza wartość jest większa niż druga wartość.\n\n**Greater than** zwraca **false** gdy pierwsza wartość jest mniejsza lub równa drugiej wartości.\n\nBlok **greater than** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok **greater than** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false** i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Kąt kursu\n\nPodaje aktualny kurs 3-przewodowego czujnika żyroskopowego lub czujnika inercyjnego V5 w stopniach.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBlok **heading of** zgłasza wzrost kursu podczas obracania w prawo.\n\n**Heading of** podaje zakres od **0.00 do 359.99**.\n\nWybierz, który czujnik żyroskopowy / czujnik bezwładności chcesz sprawdzić.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nBlok **heading of** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Jeśli to \n\nBlok typu 'C' uruchamia bloki wewnątrz, jeśli warunek logiczny ma wartość **true**.  \n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **if then** 'C' sprawdzi warunek logiczny tylko raz.\n\nJeśli wartość logiczna jest **true**, blok wewnątrz **if then** zostanie wykonany.\n\nJeśli wartość logiczna jest **false**, blok wewnątrz **if then** zostanie pominięty.\n\nBlok **if then** może przyjąć sześciokątne (sześcioboczne) bloki jako warunek.\n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Jeśli to w przeciwnym razie\n\nBlok typu 'C' Block that uruchamia bloki wewnątrz pierwszej lub drugiej części **if then else**, na podstawie zgłoszonej wartości logicznej.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **if then else** sprawdzi warunek logiczny tylko raz.\n\nJeśli wartość logiczna jest **true**, blok wewnątrz **if** zostanie wykonany.\n\nJeśli wartość logiczna jest **false**, blok wewnątrz **else** zostanie wykonany.\n\nBlok **if then else** akceptuje jako warunek sześciokątne (sześcioboczne) bloki.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)"},"inertial_acceleration":{"name":"inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Przyspieszenie\n\nPodaje wartość przyspieszenia z jednej z osi (x, y lub z) czujnika bezwładności.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n**Acceleration of** podaje zakres między **-4.0 a 4.0** Gs. \n\nWybierz, który czujnik bezwładnożci użyć.\n\n![inertial_acceleration_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_device.png)\n\nWybierz, której osi użyć:\n\n* **Oś X** informuje o przyspieszeniu, gdy czujnik bezwładnościowy porusza się **do przodu do tyłu**\n* **Oś Y** informuje o przyspieszeniu, gdy czujnik bezwładnościowy porusza się **na boki**\n* **Oś Z** informuje o przyspieszeniu, gdy czujnik bezwładnościowy porusza się **w górę lub w dół**\n\n![inertial_acceleration_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_axis.png)\n\nBlok **acceleration of** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_gyrorate":{"name":"inertial_gyrorate","markdown":"# Prędkość żyroskopu\n\nPobiera szybkość obrotu z jednej z osi (x, y lub z) czujnika bezwładnościowego.\n\n![gyro_rate_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_gyrorate/gyro_rate_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Gyro rate** podaje wartość z zakresu **-1000.0 do 1000.0** w stopniach na sekundę: dps (degrees per second). \n\nWybierz, którego czujnika bezwładnościowego użyć.\n\n![gyroRate_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_included_block.png)\n\nWybierz, której osi chcesz użyć.\n\n* **Oś X** informuje o szybkości obrotu, gdy czujnik bezwładnościowy obraca się w osi X (na podstawie orientacji czujnika)\n* **Oś Y** informuje o szybkości obrotu, gdy czujnik bezwładnościowy obraca się w osi Y (na podstawie orientacji czujnika)\n* **Oś Z** informuje o prędkości obrotu, gdy czujnik bezwładnościowy obraca się w osi Z (na podstawie orientacji czujnika)\n\n![gyroRate_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_axis.png)\n\nBlok **gyro rate** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_orientation":{"name":"inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Orientacja\n\nPobiera kąt orientacji czujnika bezwładnościowego. Podaje wartość jednostkową określoną przez parametr czujnika bezwładnościowego.\n\n![orientation_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_orientation/orientation_inertial_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nPodana orientacja jest określana przez wybraną oś (x, y lub z).\n\n* **Oś X** reprezentuje **pitch**, który podaje wartość od -90 do +90 stopni.\n* **Oś Y** reprezentuje **roll**, który zgłasza wartość od -180 do +180 stopni)\n* **Oś Z** reprezentuje **yaw**, które zgłasza wartość od -180 do +180 stopni)\n\n---\n\n**Pitch** to kąt nachylenia robota do przodu i do tyłu.\n\n![V5_Pitch_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_orientation/V5_Pitch_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Roll** to kąt nachylenia robota w lewo i w prawo.\n\n![V5_Roll_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_orientation/V5_Roll_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Yaw** to kątowy obrót robota.\n\n![V5_Yaw_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_orientation/V5_Yaw_rev2.jpg)\n\n---\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika bezwładnościowego użyć.\n\n![orientation_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_orientation/orientation_included_block.png)\n\nWybierz, której osi chcesz użyć.\n\n![orientation_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_orientation/orientation_axis.png)\n\nBlok **orientation of** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![orientation_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/inertial_orientation/orientation_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n\n"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Element z listy 2D\n\nPodaje wartość elementu na liście 2D.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, której listy 2D chcesz użyć. Liście 2D można również zmienić nazwę lub usunąć.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nWprowadź lokalizację pozycji na liście: wiersz (pierwszy numer) i kolumna (druga liczba), która ma być raportowana. Tutaj zgłaszana jest pozycja o lokalizacji wiersz 2, kolumna 3 na liście 2D.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nBlok **item of 2D list** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Element z\n\nPodaje wartość danej pozycji na liście.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz listę, której chcesz użyć. Liście można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nWprowadź numer pozycji elementu na liście. Tutaj raportowana jest druga pozycja na liście (pozycja 2).\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nBlok **item of** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie ustawimy prędkość Napędu na wartość zapisaną w pozycji 3 mojej listy. Układ napędowy będzie teraz poruszał się do przodu z prędkością 90%\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"joint_move":{"name":"joint_move","markdown":"# Ruch stawów, łaczny\n\nPrzesuwa ramię robota V5 do określonej współrzędnej (x, y, z) za pomocą ruchu stawów.\n\n![joint_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/joint_move/joint_move_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **joint move** przesuwa ramię robota V5 w kierunku x, y i z za pomocą ruchu stawów.\n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/joint_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nWybierz ramię robota, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![select_joint_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/joint_move/select_joint_arm.png)\n\nBlok **joint move** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite i bloki numeryczne.\n\n![joint_input](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/joint_move/joint_input.png)"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Długośc listy 2D\n\nPodaje liczbę wierszy lub kolumn na liście 2D.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, której listy 2D chcesz użyć. Liście 2D można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nWybierz wartość do sprawdzenia. Lista 2D może raportować **rows** lub **columns**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nBlok **length of 2D list** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Mniej niż\n\nPodaje, czy pierwsza wartość jest mniejsza niż druga wartość.\n\n![less_than](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Less than** zwraca **true** gdy pierwsza wartość jest mniejsza niż druga wartość.\n\n**Less than** zwraca **false** gdy pierwsza wartość jest większa lub równa drugiej wartości.\n\nBlok **less than** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\nBlok **less than** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n"},"linear_move":{"name":"linear_move","markdown":"# Ruch liniowy\n\nPrzesuwa ramię robota V5 do określonej współrzędnej (x, y, z) przy użyciu ruchu liniowego.\n\n![linear_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/linear_move/linear_move_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **linear move** przesuwa ramię robota V5 w kierunku x, y i z przy użyciu ruchu liniowego.\n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/linear_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nWybierz ramię robota, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![select_linear_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/linear_move/select_linear_arm.png)\n\nBlok **linear move** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite i bloki numeryczne.\n\n![linear_input](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/linear_move/linear_input.png)"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Ruch zakończony\n\nInformuje o zakończeniu ruchu wybranego silnika VR.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Jak uzywać\n\n**Motor is done** zwraca **true** kiedy wybrany silnik zakończy swój ruch.\n\n**Motor is done** zwraca **true** kiedy wybrany silnik nadal się porusza.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nBlok **motor is done** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Silnik sie obraca\n\nInformuje, czy wybrany silnik VR aktualnie się obraca.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Motor is spinning** zwraca **true** kiedy obraca się wybrany silnik.\n\n**Motor is spinning** zwraca **false** gdy wybrany silnik jest zatrzymany.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nBlok **motor is spinning** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Mnożenie\n\nMnoży dowolne dwie wartości i podaje iloczyn.\n\n![multiply](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Multiply** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok  **multiply** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki, i mogą również zawierać okrągłe bloki. \n\nPomnóż dwie liczby.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nPomnóż przez wartości zmiennych.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nPomnóż przez wartości z czujników lub urządzeń.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Ustaw kursor w następnym wierszu\n\nUstawia kursor na ekranie konsoli, Mózgu lub kontrolerze na następny dostępny wiersz.\n\n![next_row](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nDomyślnie wszystkie projekty zaczynają się od kursora ekranowego w wierszu 1, kolumnie 1. Blok **next row** przesunie kursor w dół o jeden wiersz na ekranie. **Next row** ustawi również kursor w  kolumnie na pozycję 1.\n\nWybierz urządzenie, którego chcesz użyć. Kontrolery V5 pojawią się tylko wtedy, gdy zostaną dodane w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![next_row_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/next_row/next_row_dropdown_with_console.png)\n\n---\n\nMózg V5 umożliwia zmianę rozmiaru czcionki drukowanej na ekranie. Zmiana czcionki wpłynie na liczbę wierszy dostępnych na ekranie Mózgu.\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki V5 Brain - Liczba wierszy:**\n\n* Bardzo małe - 20 wierszy\n* Mały - 16 wierszy\n* Średni - 12 wierszy (domyślnie)\n* Duży - 8 wierszy\n* Bardzo duży - 6 wierszy\n* Bardzo duży - 4 wiersze\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/next_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nKontroler V5 nie pozwala na zmianę rozmiaru czcionki drukowanej na ekranie.\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki kontrolera V5 - liczba wierszy:**\n\n* Czcionka standardowa - 3 wiersze (domyślnie)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/next_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n\n---\n\nDrukowanie do Print Console wymaga użycia bloku **next row** po **print** aby wyprowadzić zawartość bufora Konsoli do okna okna Konsoli.\n\n![next_row_with_print_console](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/next_row/next_row_with_print_console.png)"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# Nie\n\nPodaje przeciwieństwo (odwrotność) podanej wartości logicznej.\n\n![not](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/not/not.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **not** zwraca **true** kiedy wartośc logiczna wewnątrz to **false**.\n\nBlok **not** zwraca **false** kiedy wartośc logiczna wewnątrz to **true**.\n\nBlok **not** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład zgłosi ** prawda **, gdy ekran Mózgu nie jest naciśnięty.\n\n![not_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Liczba obiektów\n\nPodaje, ile obiektów wykrył czujnik wizyjny.\n\nObiekt będzie musiał zostać skonfigurowany przed użyciem bloku **object count**, by ten mógł go zydentyfikować.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika wizyjnego chcesz użyć.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nBlok **snapshot of** mosi zostać uzyty przed zastosowanieem bloku **object count**, by mógł opodać liczbę obiektów.\n\nBlok **object count** poda liczbę obiektów z ostatniego, zrobionego snapshota.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Objekt istnieje\n\nInformuje, czy czujnik wizyjny wykryje skonfigurowany obiekt.\n\nObiekt będzie musiał zostać skonfigurowany przed użyciem bloku **object exists**\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika wizyjnego chcesz użyć.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n**Object exists** zgłasza **true** kiedy czujnik wykryje skonfigurowany obiekt.\n\n**Object exists** zgłasza **false** kiedy czujnik nie wykryje skonfigurowanego obiektu.\n\nBlok **object exists** zgłasza zmienną logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nBlok **snapshot of** musi zostać użyty przed blokiem **object exists** który zgłasza wartość logiczną **true** lub **false**."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Wykryto obiekt\n\nInformuje, czy czujnik odległości widzi obiekt w swoim polu widzenia. \n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Jak używac\n\n**Object found** zwraca **true** gdy czujnik odległości wykryje obiekt lub powierzchnię w swoim polu widzenia.\n\n**Object found** zwraca **false** gdy czujnik odległości nie wykryje przedmiotu lub powierzchni.\n\nWybierz, który czujnik odległości ma być używany.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nBlok **object found** zwraca wartość logioczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"optical_brightness":{"name":"optical_brightness","markdown":"# Jasność\n\nPodaje ilość światła wykrytą przez czujnik optyczny.\n\n![optical_brightness](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_brightness/optical_brightness.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\nWybierz czujnik optyczny, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![optical_brightness_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_device.png)\n\nBlok **Optical brightness** podaje wartość z zakresu od **0%** do **100%**.\n\nWykryta duża ilość światła zgłosi wysoką wartość jasności.\n\nMała ilość wykrytego światła zgłosi niską wartość jasności.\n\nBlok **Optical brightness** podaje wartości liczbowe i jest używany w blokach ze korągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![optical_brightness_use](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect":{"name":"optical_detect","markdown":"# Czujnik optyczny wykrywa kolor\n\nInformuje, czy czujnik optyczny wykryje określony kolor.\n\n![optical_detect](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_detect/optical_detect.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz czujnik optyczny, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![optical_detect_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_detect/optical_detect_device.png)\n\nWybierz kolor, który ma sprawdzać czujnik.\n\n![optical_detect_colors](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_detect/optical_detect_colors.png)\n\nBlok **Optical detects color** zwraca **true** gdy czujnik optyczny wykryje określony kolor.\n\nBlok **Optical detects color** zwraca **false** jeśli nie wykryje określonego koloru.\n\nBlok **Optical detects color** zwraca wwartości logiczne **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![optical_detect_use](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_detect/optical_detect_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect_gesture":{"name":"optical_detect_gesture","markdown":"# Kiedy czujnik optyczny wykryje gest\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków, gdy czujnik optyczny wykryje gest.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nZdarzenie **When Optical detects a gesture** można używać do tworzenia działań lub zachowań na podstawie gestów wykrywanych przez czujnik optyczny.\n\nWybierz czujnik optyczny.\n\n\n![optical_detects_gesture_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detects_gesture_device.png)\n\nWybierz, który gest wyzwala wydrzenie **When Optical detects a gesture**.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block2.png)"},"optical_detect_object":{"name":"optical_detect_object","markdown":"# Kiedy czujnik optyczny wykryje/ zgubi obiekt\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków, gdy czujnik optyczny wykryje lub zgubi obiekt.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nZdarzenie **When Optical detects/loses** może być używany do tworzenia działań lub zachowań na podstawie tego, czy czujnik optyczny **detects** obiekt w zasięgu czujnika czy **loses** obiekt znajdujący się w zasięgu czujnika\n\nWybierz czujnik optyczny.\n\n![optical_detect_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_device.png)\n\nWybierz czy zdarzenie **When Optical detects/loses** jest wyzwalane, gdy czujnik **detects** obiekt czy gdy go **loses**.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block2.png)"},"optical_found_object":{"name":"optical_found_object","markdown":"# Czujnik optyczny znalazł obiekt\n\nRaportuje, jeśli czujnik optyczny wykryje obiekt w pobliżu.\n\n![optical_found_object](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_found_object/optical_found_object.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz czujnik optyczny, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![optical_found_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_device.png)\n\nBlok **Optical found object** zgłasza **true** gdy czujnik optyczny wykryje obiekt w pobliżu.\n\nBlok **Optical found object** zgłasza **false** jeśli obiekt nie znajduje się w zasięgu.\n\nBlok **Optical found object** powinien być używany do sprawdzenia, czy obiekt znajduje się blisko czujnika optycznego, tak aby odczyty kolorów z bloku **Optical detects color** były dokładne.\n\nBlok **Optical found object** zgłasza **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![optical_found_object_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_condition.png)"},"optical_hue":{"name":"optical_hue","markdown":"# Odcień\n\nPodaje odcień koloru obiektu.\n\n![optical_hue](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_hue/optical_hue.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz czujnik optyczny.\n\n![optical_hue_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_hue/optical_hue_device.png)\n\nBlok **Optical hue** zwraca wartość liczbową określającą odcień koloru obiektu. Zwraca liczbę pomiędzy **0** a **359**, którą można traktować jako położenie koloru na kole kolorów.\n\nBlok **Optical hue** zwraca wartości liczbowe i jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![optical_hue_use](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_hue/optical_hue_use.png)"},"optical_set_light":{"name":"optical_set_light","markdown":"# Ustaw światło czujnika optycznego\n\nWłącza lub wyłącza światło czujnika optycznego.\n\n![optical_set_light](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_set_light/optical_set_light.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **Set optical light** pozwala na **on** lub **off** światła czujnika optycznego. Światło pozwala czujnikowi widzieć obiekty, jeśli patrzy na obiekt w ciemnym obszarze.\n\nWybierz czujnik optyczny, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![optical_set_light_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_device.png)\n\nWybierz, czy chcesz ustawić światło na czujniku optycznym na **on** czy **off**.\n\n![optical_set_light_state](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_state.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie użyjemy bloku **Set optical light** aby włączyć światło. Następnie, jeśli czujnik optyczny wykryje obiekt, wyświetlamy jego odcień.\n\n\n![optical_set_light_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_example.png)"},"optical_set_light_power":{"name":"optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Ustaw moc światła czujnika optycznego\n\nUstaw moc światła czujnika optycznego V5\n\n![optical_set_light_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_light_power_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **Set optical light power** b akceptuje zakres między **0%** a **100%**. Spowoduje to zmianę jasności światła czujnika optycznego. Jeśli światło jest wyłączone, ten blok włączy światło.\n\nWybierz czujnik optyczny.\n\n![optical_set_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_device.png)\n\nBlok **Set optical light power** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![optical_set_power_num](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_num.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie używamy bloku **Set optical light power** aby ustawić moc światła na **50%**, następnie używamy bloku **Set optical light** aby włączyć światło. Następnie, jeśli czujnik optyczny wykryje obiekt, wyświetlamy odcień.\n\n![optical_set_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_example.png)"},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# Lub\n\nZwraca, jeśli spełniony jest jeden z dwóch warunków logicznych.\n\n![or](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/or/or.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **or** zwraca **true** gdy jeden (lub oba) z warunków są spełnione **true**. \n\nBlok **or** zwraca **false** gdy oba warunki są spełnione**false**.\n\nBlok **or** zwraca wartośc logiczną **true** or **false**  i pasuje do bloków z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\n## Example\n\nBlok **or** zwraca **true** po naciśnięciu czujnika zderzaka i / lub jasność czujnika światła przekracza 50%.\n\nBlok **or** zwraca **false** tylko wtedy, gdy czujnik zderzaka nie jest wciśnięty, a jasność czujnika światła jest mniejsza lub równa 50%\n\n![or_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/or/or_truth.png)"},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Pozycja kontrolera\n\nPodaje położenie joysticka na kontrolerze wzdłuż osi.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Position of controller** podajee zakres między **-100 a 100**.\n\n**Position of controller** zgłosi zero (0), gdy oś joysticka jest wycentrowana.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nWybierz kontroler V5 do użycia.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_devices.png)\n\nWybierz oś joysticka, aby sprawdzić jego położenie.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nBlok **position of controller** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Pozycja silnika\n\nPodaje odległość, jaką przebył silnik.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Position of motor** podaje położenie silnika VR w liczbach całkowitych dla stopni i liczbach dziesiętnych dla obrotów.\n\nWybierz silnik VR, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nWybierz, czy wartość jest podawana w stopniach czy ilościach obrotów.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nBlok **position of motor** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"position_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"position_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Pozycja enkodera wału\n\nPodaje odległość o którą obrócił się enkoder wału.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Position of shaft encoder** podaje odległość pokonaną przez Enkoder wału w liczbach całkowitych dla stopni i liczbach dziesiętnych dla obrotów.\n\nWybierz, którego enkodera wału użyć.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_device.png)\n\nWybierz, czy wartość jest podawana w stopniach, czy w obrotach.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_unit.png)\n\nBlok **position of shaft encoder** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_inserted.png)"},"power":{"name":"power","markdown":"# Ustaw moc magnesu\n\nUstawia moc elektromagnesu V5, która będzie używana podczas podnoszenia obiektu.\n\n![set_magnet_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/power/set_magnet_power_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nMoże być konieczne podniesienie przedmiotów o różnej wadze. Blok  **set electromagnet power** pozwala kontrolować, ile mocy zużyje elektromagnes.. Blok **set electromagnet power** posiada zakres od **0% do 100%**\n\nWybierz magnes, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![set_magnet_dropdown_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/power/set_magnet_dropdown_block.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie robot będzie jechał do przodu o 200 mm, a następnie zwiększy moc za pomocą bloku **set electromagnet power**, następnie **Electromagnet** przyciągnie obiekt aby go podnieść, przejedzie 200 mm do przodu, a następnie upuści obiekt.\n\n![set_magnet_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/power/set_magnet_power_example.png)\n"},"power_of_motor":{"name":"power_of_motor","markdown":"# Moc silnika\n\nPodaje ilość mocy wyjściowej generowanej obecnie przez inteligentny silnik V5.\n\n![motor_power](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/power_of_motor/motor_power.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Power of motor** podaje zakres od **0.0 do 11.0 watts**. \n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![motor_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/power_of_motor/motor_power_device.png)\n\nBlok **power of motor** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![motor_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/power_of_motor/motor_power_inserted.png)\n"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Naciśnięcie zderzaka\n\nInformuje o naciśnięciu włącznika zderzaka.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Pressing bumper** zwraca **true** jeśli włącznik zderzaka jest wciśnięty.\n\n**Pressing bumper** zwraca **false** jeśli włącznik zderzaka nie jest wciśnięty.\n\nWybierz, którego przełącznika zderzaka użyć.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nBlok **pressing bumper** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false**  i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Naciskanie kontrolera\n\nZgłasza naciśnięcie przycisku na kontrolerze VEX V5.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Pressing controller** zwraca**true** czy wybrany przycisk kontrolera jest wciśnięty.\n\n**Pressing controller** zwraca **false** czy wybrany przycisk kontrolera nie jest wciśnięty.\n\nWybierz, którego przycisku kontrolera chcesz użyć.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nBlok **pressing controller** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)"},"pressing_limit":{"name":"pressing_limit","markdown":"# Nacisk na wyłącznik krańcowy\n\nInformuje o naciśnięciu wyłącznika krańcowego.\n\n![pressing_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/pressing_limit/pressing_limit.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Pressing limit** zwraca **true** jeśli wyłącznik krańcowy jest wciśnięty.\n\n**Pressing limit** zwraca **false** jeśli wyłącznik krańcowy nie jest wciśnięty.\n\nWybierz, którego wyłącznika krańcowego chcesz użyć.\n\n![pressing_limit_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_bumper.png)\n\nBlok **pressing limit** zwraca wartość logiczną **true** lub **false** i jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![pressing_limit_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_inserted.png)\n "},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Wyświetl\n\nDrukuje wartości lub tekst na ekranie konsoli, Mózgu lub kontrolera.\n\n![look_print](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/print/look_print.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **print** wyświetli dane w miejscu kursora na ekranie lub w konsoli.\n\nWszystkie nowe projekty zaczynają się od kursora ekranowego w wierszu 1, kolumnie 1.\n\nWszystkie bloki reporterów będą domyślnie drukowane jako liczby całkowite (całkowite). Użyj bloku **set print precision** aby dostosować liczbę drukowanych miejsc dziesiętnych.\n\nWybierz urządzenie, którego chcesz użyć. Kontrolery V5 pojawią się tylko wtedy, gdy zostaną dodane w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![look_print_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/print/look_print_dropdown_with_console.png)\n\nAby dodać wartości do buforu konsoli, tylko blok **print** jest wymagany.\n\n![look_print_dropdown_console](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/print/look_print_dropdown_console.png)\n\nJednak aby wyprowadzić wartości z bufora Print Console do Print Console, blok **set cursor to next row** jest wymagany. Poniższe bloki wyświetlą „VEXcode” na konsolii ustawią kursor w następnym wierszu.\n![look_print_set_cursor_console](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/print/look_print_set_cursor_console.png)\n\n---\n\nDrukuj słowa i liczby.\n\n![print_words](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/print/print_words.png)\n\nWyświetl zgłoszoną wartość ze zmiennej.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nWyświetl wartość obliczeń.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nWyświetl wartość z czujnika lub urządzenia.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Moje bloki\n\nMoje bloki służą do tworzenia niestandardowych bloków.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**My blocks** służą do tworzenia sekwencji bloków, których można używać wielokrotnie w całym projekcie. \n\n**My blocks** tworzy się poprzez naciśnięcie przycisku **Make a Block**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**My blocks** mogą mieć wiele parametrów - etykiety tekstowe, zmienne numeryczne i zmienne logiczne - aby dodać więcej funkcji do niestandardowego bloku.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nAby użyć **my block**, dołącz **my block** do bloku \"kapeluszowego\". Kiedy blok **my block** zostaje zaczytany przez program, stok wewnątrz **my block** zostanie uruchomiony z określonymi wartościami parametrów.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nDołącz stos bloków do **my blocks** \"zdefiniuj\" blok \"kapeluszowy\", aby ustawić kacje, które maja być wykonane, gdy używany jest **my block**.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Uwaga: Tworzenie wielu Moich bloków z tymi samymi etykietami i zmiennymi może powodować błędy podczas uruchamiania projektu na boisku.***\n\n## Przykład 1\n\nW tym przykładzie robot użyje bloku **my blocks** do:\n\n* Jedź do przodu przez 15 cali\n* Drukuje pojemność baterii, a także przesuwa kursor do nowej linii na ekranie Mózgu\n* Obraca robota o 180 stopni w prawo\n* Drukuje pojemność baterii, a także przesuwa kursor do nowej linii na ekranie Mózgu\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Mój blok\n\nMoje bloki służą do tworzenia niestandardowych bloków.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**My blocks** służą do tworzenia sekwencji bloków, których można używać wielokrotnie w całym projekcie.\n\n**My blocks** można stworzyć przez przycisk **Make a Block**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**My blocks** może mieć wiele parametrów - etykiety tekstowe, zmienne numeryczne i zmienne logiczne - aby dodać więcej funkcji do niestandardowego bloku.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nAby użyć **my block**, dodaj **my block** do bloku \"kapeluszowego\". Kiedy **my block** zostanie osiągnięty w projekcie, stos wewnątrz **my block** będzie działać z określonymi wartościami parametrów.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nDołącz stos bloków do **my blocks** \"zdefinjuj\" blok \"kapeluszowy\", aby ustawić akcję, która ma miejsce, gdy **my block** jest używany.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Uwaga: utworzenie wielu Moich bloków z tymi samymi etykietami i zmiennymi może spowodować błędy podczas pobierania projektu.***\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie robot użyje **my blocks** do:\n\n* Jedź do przodu przez 15 cali\n* Wskazuje pojemność baterii, a także przesuwa kursor do nowej linii na ekranie Mózgu\n* Obraca robota o 180 stopni w prawo\n* Wskazuje pojemność baterii, a także przesuwa kursor do nowej linii na ekranie Mózgu\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Losowo\nPoodaje losową wartość między najwyższą a najwyższą warością w bloku.\n\n![random](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/random/random.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok  **losowo** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki.\n\nBlok **losowo** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie użyjemy bloku **losowo** aby losowo ustawić prędkość układu napędowego.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\nW tym przykładzie użyjemy bloku **losowo** aby losowo określić długość bloku oczekiwania.\n\n![random_control](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"reflectivity_of":{"name":"reflectivity_of","markdown":"# Odbicie\n\nPodaje ilość światła odbitego przez czujnik śledzenia linii.\n\n![reflectivity_of](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nJasne powierzchnie będą odbijać więcej światła i będą wykazywać wysoką wartość współczynnika odbicia.\n\nCiemne powierzchnie będą odbijać mniej światła i będą zgłaszać niską wartość współczynnika odbicia.\n\n**Reflectivity of** podaje zakres od **0% do 100%**.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnikaLine Tracker chcesz użyć.\n\n![reflectivity_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_color.png)\n\nBlok **reflectivity of** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![reflectivity_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n\n"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Reszta\n\nDzieli pierwszą wartość przez drugą wartość i podaje resztę\n\n![remainder](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **remainder** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nLiczby, które dzielą się równo, będą zgłaszać resztę zero.\n\nDługość bloku **remainder** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład podzieli 7 na 2, a resztę „1” wyświetli na ekranie Mózgu VEX V5.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Powtórz\n\nBlok typu 'C'powtarza bloki zawarte w środku przez określoną liczbę razy.\n\n![repeat](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nNajpierw wprowadź wartość, aby określić, ile razy będzie się  stos wewnątrz **repeat**.\n \nBlok typu 'C' **repeat** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBloki typu 'C' można również umieścić jeden w drugim. Pojęcie to nazywa się zagnieżdżaniem, które może pomóc zaoszczędzić czas podczas programowania różnych zachowań.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/repeat/repeat_select.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Powtarzaj do\n\nBlok typu 'C, który powtarza bloki wewnątrz, aż zostanie wykonany warunek logiczny: **prawda**.  \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **repeat until** sprawdzi warunek logiczny tylko na początku każdej pętli.\n\nKiedy warunek logiczny jest zwrócony jako **fałsz**, bloki wewnątrz **repeat until** zostaną wykonane.\n\nKiedy warunek logiczny jest zwrócony jako **prawda**, bloki wewnątrz **repeat until** zostaną pominięte.\n\nBlok typu 'C' **repeat until** może przyjąć sześciokątne (sześcioboczne) bloki jako warunek.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Resetuj licznik\n\nResetuje licznik Mózgu robota.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nLicznik rozpoczyna pracę po urochumieniu projektu. Blok **reset timer** jest używany by zresetować licznik do 0s.\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie licznik czasu zostanie zresetowany przed przesunięciem układu napędowego do przodu przez 3 sekundy. Po upływie 3 sekund układ napędowy zatrzyma się.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_angle":{"name":"rotation_angle","markdown":"# Kąt rotacji\n\nPodaje bieżący kąt obrotu czujnika obrotu V5 w stopniach.\n\n![rotation_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block.png)\n\n## Jako korzystać\n\nBlok **Angle of rotation** podaje wartość z zakresu **0.00** do **359.99**.\n\nBlok **Angle of rotation** będzie zgłaszać rosnące lub malejące wartości w miarę obracania się czujnika obrotu.\n\nWybierz czujnik obrotu, z którego mają być pobierane wartości.\n\n![rotation_angle_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block2.png)\n\nBlok **angle of rotation** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![rotation_angle_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block3.png)\n"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Kąt obrotu\n\nPodaje aktualny kąt obrotu w stopniach 3-przewodowego czujnika żyroskopowego lub czujnika inercyjnego V5.\n\n![rotation_position.png](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Gyro rotation** zwraca wartość  **positive** kiedy czujnik żyroskopowy obraca się w stronę **clockwise**.\n\n**Gyro rotation** zwraca wartość  **negative** kiedy czujnik żyroskopowy obraca się w stronę**counter-clockwise**.\n\nWybierz, który czujnik żyroskopowy / czujnik interialowy chcesz sprawdzić.\n\n![rotation_position_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_devices.png)\n\nBlok **Gyro rotation** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![rotation_position_inserted.png](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_inserted.png)\n"},"rotation_position":{"name":"rotation_position","markdown":"# Pozycja rotacji\n\nPodaje bieżącą pozycję obrotową wybranego czujnika obrotu V5.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_position/rotation_position_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Position of rotation** podaje położenie czujnika obrotu V5 w liczbach całkowitych dla stopni i liczbach dziesiętnych dla obrotów.\n\nWybierz, który czujnik obrotu V5 ma być używany.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_position/rotation_position_block2.png)\n\nWybierz, czy wartość jest podawana w stopniach, czy w ilości obrotów.\n\n![rotation_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_position/rotation_position_block3.png)\n\nBlok **position of rotation** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![rotation_position_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_position/rotation_position_block4.png)\n"},"rotation_set_position":{"name":"rotation_set_position","markdown":"# Ustaw pozycję\n\nUstawia bieżącą pozycję czujnika obrotu V5 na zdefiniowaną wartość.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **set position** może być użyty do ustawienia pozycji czujnika obrotu.\n\nTen blok jest zwykle używany do resetowania położenia czujnika obrotu, gdy wartość jest ustawiona na 0.\n\nBlok **set position** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne jako dane wejściowe.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block3.png)\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika obrotu chcesz użyć, a następnie wprowadź żądaną wartość położenia.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block2.png)\n"},"rotation_velocity":{"name":"rotation_velocity","markdown":"# Pędkość rotacji\n\nPodaje aktualną prędkość czujnika obrotu V5.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz czujnik obrotu, z którego mają być pobierane wartości.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block2.png)\n\nWybierz, czy prędkość jest podawana w procentach (%), obrotach na minutę (obr / min) czy stopniach na sekundę (dps).\n\n![rotation_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block3.png)\n\nBlok jest używana w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block4.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Zaokrąglij\n\nZaokrągla wprowadzoną wartość do najbliższej liczby całkowitej.\n\n![round](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/round/round.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nLiczby dziesiętne o wartości 0,5 lub większej **round** są w górę, a mniejsze niż 0.5 **round** w dół.\n\nBlok **round** block pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki, i może również akceptować okrągłe bloki.\n\nBlok **round** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Example\n\nTen przykład zaokrągli 2,7 i wyświetli \"3\".\n\n![round_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"screen_position":{"name":"screen_position","markdown":"# Pozycja ekranu\n\nPodaje lokalizację ostatniego wykrytego dotyku na ekranie dotykowym Mózgu V5.\n\n![screen_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/screen_position/screen_position_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **screen position** reporter block służy do przechwytywania lokalizacji X / Y ostatniego naciśnięcia na ekranie dotykowym V5. Ten blok może służyć do tworzenia interakcji między V5 a użytkownikiem.\n\n**Screen position** podaje zakres od **0 do 480 pixels** kiedy jest ustawiony na zgłoszenie koordynatu **X**.\n\n**Screen position** podaje zakres od **0 do 240 pixels** kiedy jest ustawiony na zgłoszenie koordynatu **Y**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/screen_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\nWybierz oś do sprawdzenia.\n\n![screen_position_value](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/screen_position/screen_position_value.png)\n\nBlok **screen position** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![screen_position_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/screen_position/screen_position_inserted.png)"},"screen_pressed":{"name":"screen_pressed","markdown":"# Ekran wciśnięty\n\nInformuje, czy ekran dotykowy Mózgu V5 jest aktualnie wciśnięty.\n\n![screen_pressed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **screen pressed** logiczny może być używany razem z blokiem **screen position** aby wykryć, kiedy i gdzie nastąpiło dotknięcie na ekranie dotykowym.\n\n**Screen pressed** zgłasza **true** gdy ekran dotykowy V5 jest naciskany.\n\n**Screen pressed** zgłasza **false** gdy ekran dotykowy V5 nie jest naciskany.\n\nBlok **screen pressed** zgłasza wartośc logiczną **true** lub **false** jest używany w blokach z sześciokątnymi (sześciobocznymi) pustymi miejscami.\n\n![screen_pressed_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Ustaw listę 2D na\n\nUstawia wszystkie pozycje na liście 2D na wprowadzone wartości.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nTworząc listę 2D, możesz ustawić liczbę **columns** między 1 a 10 a liczbę **rows** listy między 1 a 10.\n\nWybierz, której listy 2D chcesz użyć. Liście 2D można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nBlok **set 2D list to** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_angle":{"name":"set_angle","markdown":"# Ustaw kąt\n\nUstawia kąt przed wykonaniem następnych bloków: [Linear move] lub [Joint move].\n\n![set_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_angle/set_angle_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **set angle** ustawia rownież kąt pochylenia na **up** lub **down** zanim następne blok zostanie wykonany: [Linear move] lub [Joint move]. \n\nZwróć uwagę, że blok **set angle** wyznacza kąt dla wszystkich [Linear move] i [Joint move] chyba że ustawiono inaczej.\n\n![tool_plate](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_angle/tool_plate.png)\n\nWybierz ramię robota, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![select_set_angle_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_angle/select_set_angle_arm.png)\n\nWybierz kąt płyty narzędziowej. Wartość domyślna to **up**.\n\n* Płyta narzędziowa będzie **horizontal** kiedy jest ustawiony na **down**. \n* Płyta narzędziowa będzie **vertical** kiedy jest ustawiony na **up**. \n\n![select_angle](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_angle/select_angle.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie płyta narzędziowa zacznie się przechylać po wykonaniu bloku [Joint move] i zakończy ruch przechylania przed blokiem [Linear move].\n\n![set_angle_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_angle/set_angle_example.png)"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Ustaw listę na\n\nUstawia wszystkie pozycje na liście na wprowadzone wartości.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nPodczas tworzenia listy można ustawić długość listy od 1 do 10 elementów.\n\nWybierz listę, której chcesz użyć. Liście można również zmienić jej nazwę lub usunąć.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nBlok **set list to** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład ustawi listę na wartości początkowe, a następnie zgłosi pozycję nr 3 (90) z listy, aby ustawić pozycję Ramienia.\n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Ustaw zmienną logiczną\n\nUstawia zmienną logiczną na podaną wartość.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz zmienną logiczną, której chcesz użyć. Można również zmieniać nazwy lub usuwać zmienne logiczne.\n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nWybierz wartość logiczną.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nBlok **set boolean variable** akceptuje bloki o kształcie sześciokątnym (sześciobocznym).\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# Ustaw kursor\n\nUstawia położenie kursora dla bloku **print** na ekranie Mózgu V5 lub kontrolera.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nUstaw wiersz i pozycję kolumny kursora tak, aby miały komenda **print** wyświetlała w określonym miejscu na ekranie.\n\n**Set cursor** akceptuje zakres **row** od **1 do 20**.\n\n**Set cursor** akceptuje zakres **column** od **1 do 80**.\n\nWybierz urządzenie, którego chcesz użyć. Kontrolery V5 pojawią się tylko wtedy, gdy zostaną dodane w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![set_cursor_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_cursor/set_cursor_dropdown.png)\n\nBlok **set cursor** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n---\n\nV5 Brain umożliwia zmianę rozmiaru czcionki drukowanej na ekranie. Zmiana czcionki wpłynie na liczbę kolumn dostępnych na ekranie V5.\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki V5 Brain - Liczba wierszy:**\n\n* Bardzo małe - 20 wierszy\n* Mały - 16 wierszy\n* Średni - 12 wierszy (domyślnie)\n* Duży - 8 wierszy\n* Bardzo duży - 6 wierszy\n* Bardzo duży - 4 wiersza\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki V5 Brain - Liczba kolumn:**\n\n* Bardzo małe - 80 kolumn\n* Mały - 68 kolumn\n* Średni - 48 kolumn (domyślnie)\n* Duży - 32 kolumny\n* Bardzo duży - 24 kolumny\n* Super duży - 16 kolumn\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nKontroler V5 nie pozwala na zmianę rozmiaru czcionki drukowanej na ekranie.\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki kontrolera V5 - liczba wierszy:**\n\n* Czcionka standardowa - 3 wiersza (domyślnie)\n\n**Rozmiar czcionki kontrolera V5 - liczba kolumn:**\n\n* Czcionka standardowa - 20 kolumn (domyślnie)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Ustaw kierunek napędu\n\nUstawia wartość kursu żyroskopu układu napędowego.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **set drive heading** może być użyty do ustawienia pozycji układu napędowego do dowolnego kursu. Ten blok może być użyty do zresetowania orientacji żyroskopu układu napędowego, gdy kurs jest ustawiony na wartość 0.\n\n**Set drive heading** akceptuje zakres od **0 do 360** stopni.\n\nBlok **set drive heading** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Ustaw rotację\n\nUstawia kąt obrotu napędu w przypadku konfiguracji z 3-przewodowym czujnikiem żyroskopowym lub czujnikiem bezwładnościowym V5.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **set drive rotation** można użyć do ustawienia kąta obrotu napędu na dowolną dodatnią lub ujemną wartość.\n\nBlok **set drive rotation** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład obróci robota łącznie o 210 stopni:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Obróć w prawo (zgodnie ze wskazówkami zegara) o rotację 120 stopni.\n- Ustaw aktualną pozycję robota jako obrót -45 stopni.\n- Obróć w prawo (zgodnie ze wskazówkami zegara) na dodatkowe 90 stopni (z -45 stopni do +45 stopni) na podstawie ustawionej wartości obrotu z poprzedniego bloku."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Ustaw zatrzymanie napędu\n\nUstawia zachowanie układu napędowego po zatrzymaniu się.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n* **Brake** spowoduje natychmiastowe zatrzymanie układu napędowego.\n* **Coast** pozwala układowi napędowemu obracać się stopniowo, aż do zatrzymania.\n* **Hold** spowoduje natychmiastowe zatrzymanie układu napędowego i powrót do pozycji zatrzymania, jeśli zostanie przesunięty.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje, że układ napędowy będzie poruszał się do przodu przez 3 sekundy, a następnie utrzyma tą pozycję po zatrzymaniu.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Ustaw limit czasu jazdy\n\nUstawia limit czasu dla poleceń ruchu układu napędowego.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nUstawienie limitu czasu jazdy układu napędowego, służy do zapobiegania blokom napędu, które nie osiągają swojej pozycji, uniemożliwiając pracę innych bloków w stosie.\n\nPrzykładem układu napędowego, który nie osiąga swojej pozycji, jest napotkanie ściany przez robota i niemożność zakończenia ruchu.\n\nBlok **set drive timeout** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład zakończy komendę **drive** po 2 sekundach, jeśli układ napędowy nie osiągnął celu 24 cali. Po osiągnięciu limitu czasu lub odległości układ napędowy przejdzie do **turn**.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Ustaw prędkość napędu\n\nUstawia prędkość układu napędowego.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Set drive velocity** ustawi tylko prędkość układu napędowego, ale nie spowoduje ruchu układu napędowego. Nadal wymagany jest blok **drive**.\n\n**Set drive velocity** akceptuje zakres od **-100% do 100%** lub **-600rpm do 600rpm**.\n\n**Set drive velocity** zaakceptuje zakres „obrotów na minutę” na podstawie wkładu zębatego zainstalowanego w inteligentnych silnikach V5 używanych w układzie napędowym.\n\n* Czerwony wkład: od -100 obr./min do 100 obr./min\n* Wkład zielony: od -200 do 200 obr./min\n* Wkład niebieski: od -600 do 600 obr./min\n\nUstawienie prędkości układu napędowego na wartość ujemną spowoduje, że układ napędowy porusza się do tyłu.\n\nUstawienie prędkości na 0 spowoduje zatrzymanie układu napedowego.\n\nBlok **set drive velocity** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWybierz jednostkę miary.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n\n"},"set_fill_color":{"name":"set_fill_color","markdown":"# Ustaw kolor wypełnienia\n\nUstawia kolor wypełniający kształty narysowane na ekranie V5 Brain.\n\n![set_fill_color_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **set fill color** służy do ustawiania koloru wnętrza okręgów i prostokątów rysowanych na ekranie Mózgu V5. \n\nWybierz kolor wypełnienia.\n\n![set_fill_color_color](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_color.png)  \n\nKolor wypełnienia będzie używany dla wszystkich przyszłych obiektów rysowanych na ekranie Mózgu V5."},"set_font":{"name":"set_font","markdown":"# Ustaw czcionkę\n\nUstawia styl i rozmiar czcionki używanej na ekranie V5 podczas wyświetlania liczb lub tekstu.\n\n![set_font_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_font/set_font_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nNa ekranie V5 dostępne są dwa różne typy czcionek:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - każdy znak ma taką samą szerokość.\n* Proporcjonalne (Prop) - każdy znak ma różną szerokość w zależności od znaku.\n\nWybierz typ i rozmiar czcionki, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![set_font_block_font](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_font/set_font_block_font.png)  \n\nNowy rozmiar czcionki zostanie użyty dla każdego przyszłego tekstu wyświetlanego na ekranie Mózgu V5."},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Ustaw kurs\n\nUstawia aktualną pozycję kursu czujnika żyroskopowego (żyroskopowego) / bezwładnościowego na zadaną wartość.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **set gyro / inertial heading**  można użyć do ustawienia pozycji żyroskopu zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara.\n\nTen blok jest zwykle używany do resetowania orientacji kursu żyroskopu / czujnika bezwładnościowego, gdy wartość jest ustawiona na 0.\n\n**Set gyro heading** akceptuje zakres od **0 do 360** stopni.\n\nBlok **set gyro heading** block może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWybierz, który żyroskop / czujnik bezwładnościowy ma być używany, a następnie wprowadź żądaną wartość.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Ustaw rotację\n\nUstawia kąt obrotu 3-przewodowego czujnika żyroskopowego lub czujnika inercyjnego V5 na wartość ustawioną w bloku poleceń.\n\n![setrotation](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **set gyro rotation** może być użyty do ustawienia kąta obrotu zespołu napędowego na dowolną dodatnią (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara) lub ujemną (zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara) wartość.\n\n**Set gyro rotation** akceptuje zakres dowolnej dodatniej lub ujemnej liczby dziesiętnej lub całkowitej.\n\nBlok **set gyro rotation** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika żyroskopowego chcesz użyć.\n\n![setrotation_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation_devices.png)\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Zastąp pozycję listy 2D\n\nAktualizuje element na liście 2D do nowej wartości.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWprowadź pozycję wiersza (pierwszy numer) i kolumny (drugi numer) pozycji na liście, która ma zostać zastąpiona.\n\nWybierz listę, której chcesz użyć. Liście można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nBlok **replace item** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Zamień wartość\n\nAktualizuje pozycję na liście do nowej wartości.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nWybierz listę, której chcesz użyć. Liście można również zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nBlok **replace item** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n"},"set_joint_move_speed":{"name":"set_joint_move_speed","markdown":"# Ustaw szybkość stawów\n\nUstawia prędkość ruchów stawów ramienia robota V5.\n\n![joint_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz ramię robota, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![select_joint_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_joint_move_speed/select_joint_speed_arm.png)\n\nWybierz prędkość ruchów stawów ramienia robota V5. Domyślna prędkość to **normal**.\n\n![joint_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_select.png)"},"set_led":{"name":"set_led","markdown":"# Ustaw LED\n\nWłącza lub wyłącza diodę LED.\n\n![set_led_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_led/set_led_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz, której diody LED chcesz użyć.\n\n![set_led_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_led/set_led_block_device.png)\n\nWybierz, czy dioda LED jest włączona, czy wyłączona.\n\n![set_led_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_led/set_led_block_setting.png)\n\n"},"set_linear_move_speed":{"name":"set_linear_move_speed","markdown":"# Ustaw prędkość ruchu liniowego\n\nUstawia prędkość liniowych ruchów ramienia robota V5.\n\n![linear_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz ramię robota, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![select_linear_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_linear_move_speed/select_linear_speed_arm.png)\n\nWybierz prędkość liniowych ruchów ramienia robota V5. Domyślna prędkość to **normal**.\n\n![linear_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_select.png)"},"set_mastering":{"name":"set_mastering","markdown":"# Ustaw opanowanie\n\nUstawia wartości opanowania czterech przegubów ramienia robota V5, aby umożliwić kalibrację w tej samej znanej lokalizacji.\n\n![set_mastering_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_mastering/set_mastering_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWprowadź wartości z Mózgu V5 do bloku **set mastering**. \n\nDopuszczalne wartości progowe dla połączeń są następujące:\n\n* Złącze 1: 1800 - 2200\n* Złącze 2: 1900 - 2400\n* Złącze 3: 1400 - 1800\n* Złącze 4: 200 - 650\n\n![mastering_values](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_mastering/mastering_values.png)\n\nWybierz ramię robota, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![select_mastering_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_mastering/select_mastering_arm.png)\n\nBlok **set mastering** akceptuje liczby całkowite i bloki numeryczne.\n\n![mastering_input](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_mastering/mastering_input.png)"},"set_motor_controller_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_controller_velocity","markdown":"# Ustaw prędkość kontrolera silnika\n\nUstawia prędkość silnika 393 podłączonego do sterownika silnika 29.\n\n![set_motor_controller_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Set motor controller velocity** akceptuje zakres od **-100% do 100%**.\n\nUstawienie prędkości silnika 393 na wartość ujemną spowoduje wirowanie silnika 393 do tyłu.\n\nUstawienie prędkości silnika 393 na 0 spowoduje zatrzymanie silnika 393.\n\nWybierz silnik 393, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![set_motor_controller_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_motor.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Ustaw pozycję silnika\n\nUstawia silnik robota VEX V5 na wprowadzoną wartość.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **motor position** można użyć do ustawienia dowolnej pozycji silnika.\n\nZazwyczaj, blok **motor position** służy do ustawienia pozycji na 0, aby zresetować pozycję enkodera silnika.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nWybierz jednostkę miary w stopniach lub obrotach.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Ustaw zatrzymanie silnika\n\nUstawia zachowanie inteligentnego silnika VEX V5 po zatrzymaniu się.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n* **Hamulec** spowoduje natychmiastowe zatrzymanie silnika.\n* **Coast** pozwala silnikowi obracać się stopniowo, aż do zatrzymania.\n* **Zarzymaj** spowoduje natychmiastowe zatrzymanie silnika i powrót do pozycji zatrzymania, jeśli zostanie przesunięty.\n\nBlok **set motor stopping** będzie obowiązywać dla wszystkich przyszłych poleceń silnika w pozostałej części projektu.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nWybierz ustawienie silnika po jego zatrzymaniu.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje, że silnik ramienia poruszy się do przodu o 90 stopni, a następnie oprze się siłom zewnętrznym (takim jak grawitacja), aby utrzymać swoją pozycję..\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Ustaw limit czasu silnika\n\nUstawia limit czasu dla poleceń ruchu silnika robota VEX V5.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nLimit czasu silnika służy do zapobiegania obrotom silnika, które nie osiągają swojej pozycji po określonym czasie, od zatrzymania kolejnych bloków w programie. Przykładem silnika, który nie osiąga swojej pozycji, jest ramię lub kleszcze, które osiągają swoje mechaniczne ograniczenie (maksimum zakresu ruchów) i nie mogą zakończyć ruchu.\n\nBlok **set motor timeout** może przyjmować wartości liczbowe jako dane wejściowe.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład zakończy polecenie ustalone dla silnika po 2 sekundach, jeśli silnik podnośnika nie osiągnie pozycji 270 stopni. Po osiągnięciu limitu czasu lub celu silnik podnośnika przesunie się do pozycji 0 stopni.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Ustaw moment obrotowy silnika\n\nUstawia siłę inteligentnego silnika VEX V5.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Set motor torque** akceptuje zakres od **0% do 100%**.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nBlok **set motor torque** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nW tym przykładzie silnik kleszczy zostanie obrócony do pozycji 40 stopni z maksymalnym momentem obrotowym wynoszącym tylko 20%. Pozwala to kleszczom chwycić przedmiot bez uszkodzenia go przez użycie zbyt dużej siły.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Ustaw prędkość silnika\n\nUstawia prędkość obrotów silnika.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Set motor velocity** akceptuje zakres **-100% do 100%** lub  **-600rpm do 600rpm**.\n\n**Set motor velocity** zaakceptuje wartość „obrotów na minutę” na podstawie wkładu zębatego zainstalowanego w inteligentnych silnikach V5 używanych w układzie napędowym.\n\n* Czerwony wkład: od -100 obr./min do 100 obr./min\n* Wkład zielony: od -200 do 200 obr./min\n* Wkład niebieski: od -600 do 600 obr./min\n\nUstawienie prędkości silnika na wartość ujemną spowoduje wirowanie silnika do tyłu.\n\nUstawienie prędkości silnika na 0 spowoduje, że silnik w ogóle się nie obraca.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nWybierz, czy prędkość jest ustawiona w %, czy w obrotach na minutę (obr / min).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład ustawi silnik podnośnika tak, aby powoli obracał się z prędkością 25% do pozycji 90 stopni.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_pen_color":{"name":"set_pen_color","markdown":"# Ustaw kolor pisaka\n\nUstawia kolor linii rysowanych na ekranie Mózgu V5 lub wartości wyświetlanych na Print Console.\n\n![set_pen_color_block_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_block_with_console.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **set pen color** służy do ustawiania koloru linii, pikseli i tekstu rysowanego na ekranie V5 Brain lub wartości drukowanych do Print Console.\n\n**Set pen color** będzie również używany do ustawiania koloru konturu okręgów i prostokątów rysowanych na ekranie Mózgu V5.\n\nWybierz kolor pióra. \n\n![set_pen_color_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_dropdown_with_console.png)  \n\nKolor pióra będzie używany do wszelkich przyszłych obiektów rysowanych na ekranie V5 lub jakichkolwiek wartości drukowanych w Print Console, dopóki nie zostanie zmieniony.\n\nPo zatrzymaniu programu kolor tekstu Print Console jest resetowany do czarnego."},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Ustaw precyzję wydruku\n\nUstawia liczbę cyfr, które pojawiają się po przecinku podczas wyświetlania bloków na ekranie konsoli, Mózgu lub kontrolera.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz poziom precyzji, z jakim wstawione bloki będą drukowane na ekranie.\n\n* Całości (1) (domyślnie)\n* Dziesiętne (0,1)\n* Setne (0,01)\n* Tysięczne (0,001)\n* Wszystkie cyfry (0,000001)\n\nWartości wydrukowane na wyświetlaczu zostaną zaokrąglone do najbliższego poziomu dokładności. Na przykład 1,67 zostanie wydrukowane jako 2 z dokładnością do jedności i 1,7 z dokładnością do dziesiątych.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)\n\nWybierz urządzenie, którego chcesz użyć. Kontrolery V5 pojawią się tylko wtedy, gdy zostaną dodane w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![print_precision_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_print_precision/print_precision_dropdown_with_console.png)"},"set_shaft_encoder_position":{"name":"set_shaft_encoder_position","markdown":"# Ustaw pozycję enkodera wału\n\nUstawia pozycję Encodera na podaną wartość.\n\n![set_encoder_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **set shaft encoder position** może być użyty do ustawienia pozycji Enkodera wału na dowolną podaną wartość.\n\nZazwyczaj blok **set shaft encoder position** można ustawić na 0, aby zresetować pozycję Enkodera wału.\n\nWybierz, którego enkodera wału chcesz użyć, a następnie ustaw żądaną wartość.\n\n![set_encoder_position_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_motor.png)\n\n"},"set_tool":{"name":"set_tool","markdown":"# Ustaw narzędzie\n\nUstawia efektor końcowy lub oprzyrządowanie końca ramienia (EOAT) robota V5.\n\n![set_tool_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_tool/set_tool_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nNa konca ramienia robota V5 można umieścić: nic (brak narzędzia), elektromagnes lub znacznik.\n\n![set_marker](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_tool/set_marker.png)\n\nWybierz ramię robota, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![select_tool_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_tool/select_tool_arm.png)\n\nWybierz narzędzie na ramieniu robota V5. Domyślniezostało ustawione **none**.\n![choose_tool](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_tool/choose_tool.png)"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Ustaw prędkość skrętu\n\nUstawia prędkość skrętów układu napędowego.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Set turn velocity** ustawi prędkość układu napędowego, ale nie spowoduje ruchu układu napędowego. Blok **turn** jest nadal wymagany.\n\n**Set turn velocity** akceptuje zakres od **-100% do 100%** lub **-600rpm do 600rpm**.\n\n**Set turn velocity** zaakceptuje wartość „obrotów na minutę” na podstawie wkładu zębatego zainstalowanego w inteligentnych silnikach V5 używanych w układzie napędowym.\n\n* Czerwony wkład: od -100 obr./min do 100 obr./min\n* Wkład zielony: od -200 do 200 obr./min\n* Wkład niebieski: od -600 do 600 obr./min\n\nUstawienie prędkości skrętu napędu na wartość ujemną spowoduje, że napęd skręci w przeciwnym kierunku.\n\nUstawienie prędkości skrętu w napędzie na 0 spowoduje zatrzymanie napędu.\n\nBlok **set turn velocity** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Przykład\nTen przykład spowoduje, że układ napędowy skręci powoli, z prędkością 25%, w lewo.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Ustaw zmienną\n\nUstawia zmienną na daną wartość.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz zmienną, której chcesz użyć. Zmiennym można również zmieniać nazwy lub je usuwać.\n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nBlok **set variable** akceptuje liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Ustal pozycję obiektu\n\nUstawia pozycję obiektu (obiektu, o którym chcesz uzyskać więcej informacji) z liczby wykrytych obiektów.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **object count** może zostać użyty przed blokiem **set vision object item** do określenia liczby wykrytych obiektów.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika wizyjnego chcesz użyć.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nBlok **set vision object item** akceptuje liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n\n\n"},"set_width":{"name":"set_width","markdown":"# Ustaw szerokość pióra\n\nUstawia szerokość konturu kształtów rysowanych na ekranie V5.\n\n![set_width_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_width/set_width_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **set width** służy do ustawiania szerokości linii na zewnątrz okręgów i prostokątów rysowanych na ekranie V5.\n\nBlok **set width** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/set_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Długość listy\n\nPodaje liczbę elementów na liście.  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz listę, której chcesz użyć. Liście można zmienić nazwę lub ją usunąć.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nBlok **length of list** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# Zrzut\n\nWykonuje zdjęcie - zrzut z czujnika wizyjnego.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **snapshot** przechwyci bieżący obraz z czujnika wizyjnego do przetworzenia i analizy pod kątem sygnatur i kodów kolorów.\n\nZazwyczaj blok **snapshot** jest wymagany przed użyciem jakichkolwiek innych bloków czujnika wizyjnego.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika wizyjnego chcesz użyć.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nWybierz sygnaturę wizji, której chcesz użyć. Sygnatury konfiguruje się w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Obracaj\n\nObraca silnik robota VEX V5 Motor do zatrzymania.  \n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **spin** będzie uruchamiał silnik bez końca, dopóki nie zostanie użyty nowy blok silnika lub program nie zostanie zatrzymany.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nWybierz kierunek obrotu. Nazwy kierunków można zmienić w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Obracaj o\n\nObraca silnik robota VEX IQ o zadaną wartość.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Spin for** powie silnikowi, aby jechał w danym kierunku na określoną odległość od miejsca, w którym aktualnie się znajduje.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nChoose which direction to spin. Direction names can be changed in the Devices window. \n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nBlok **spin for** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWybierz jednostkę miary w stopniach lub obrotach.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nDomyślnie inne bloki będą **wait** do zakończenia pracy silnika.\n\nMożesz wybrać strzałkę, aby rozwinąć i uwzględnić **and don't wait** - spowoduje to, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy silnik się obraca.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_motor_controller":{"name":"spin_motor_controller","markdown":"# Obracaj kontroler silnika\n\nObraca silnik 393 podłączony do sterownika silnika 29 aż do zatrzymania.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **spin** będzie uruchamiać Silnik 393 bez końca, aż do użycia nowego bloku silnika lub zatrzymania programu.\n\nWybierz silnik 393, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_motor.png)\n\nWybierz kierunek obrotu. Nazwy kierunków można zmienić w oknie Urządzenia.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_direction.png)"},"spin_servo":{"name":"spin_servo","markdown":"# Obracaj servo\n\nObraca serwomotor do ustalonej pozycji.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_servo/servo_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Spin servo** akceptuje pozycje z zakresu **0 do 100 degrees**.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_servo/servo_port.png)\n\n"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Obróć do pozycji\n\nObraca silnik robota V5 do ustalonej pozycji.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Spin to position** powie silnikowi, aby obrócił się do określonej pozycji. Na podstawie aktualnej pozycji silnika, **spin to position** określi kierunek obrotu.\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nBlok **spin to position** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nWybierz jednostkę miary w stopniach lub obrotach.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nDomyślnie inne bloki będą **wait** do zakończenia akcji silnika.\n\nMożesz wybrać strzałkę, aby rozwinąć i uwzględnić **and don't wait** - spowoduje to, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy silnik się obraca.\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Zatrzymaj jazdę\n\nZatrzymuje napęd.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nBlok **stop driving** spowoduje całkowite zatrzymanie układu napędowego i użycie **set drive stopping** ustawienie zjazdu, zahamowania lub utrzymanie pozycji.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład zatrzyma układ napędowy po 3 sekundach.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Zatrzymaj silnik\n\nZatrzymuje silnik.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz silnik do zatrzymania.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje otwarcie kleszczy na 3 sekundy przed zatrzymaniem.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor_controller":{"name":"stop_motor_controller","markdown":"# Zatrzymaj kontroler silnika\n\nZatrzymuje silnik 393 podłączony do sterownika silnika 29.\n\n![stop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz, który silnik 393 zatrzymać.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_motor.png)\n\nW tym przykładzie silnik 393 obraca się do przodu przez 3 sekundy przed zatrzymaniem..\n\n![stop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_example.png)"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Odejmowanie\n\nOdejmuje jedna wartość od drugiej i wyświetla różnicę.\n\n![subtract](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Subtract** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\nBlok **subtract** pasuje do bloków, które akceptują okrągłe bloki, i akceptuje również okrągłe bloki.\n\nOdejmij dwie liczby.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nOdejmij wartości od zmiennych.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nOdejmij wartości z czujników lub urządzeń.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"temperature_of_motor":{"name":"temperature_of_motor","markdown":"# Temperatura silnika\n\nPodaje temperaturę inteligentnego silnika V5.\n\n![temp_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nUżycie bloku **temperature of motor** może pomóc użytkownikom w opracowaniu logiki chroniącej ich inteligentne silniki V5 przed przegrzaniem podczas intensywnego użytkowania.\n\n**Temperature of motor** podaje zakres od **0% do 100%**. \n\nWybierz, którego inteligentnego silnika V5 chcesz użyć.\n\n![temp_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nBlok **temperature of motor** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![temp_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Wartość licznika\n\nPodaje wartość licznika czasu w sekundach.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nLicznik czasu startuje od 0 sekund po uruchomieniu programu i podaje wartość licznika jako wartość dziesiętną.\n\nBlok **timer value** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n"},"torque_of_motor":{"name":"torque_of_motor","markdown":"# Moment obrotowy silnika\n\nPodaje wielkość momentu obrotowego (siłę obrotową) aktualnie używanego przez inteligentny silnik V5.\n\n![motor_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/torque_of_motor/motor_torque.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Torque of motor** podaje zakres od **0.0 do 18.6 inch-pounds (InLB)** lub **0.0 do 2.1 Niutonometrów (Nm)**. \n\nWybierz z którego silnika V5 raportować moment obrotowy.\n\n![motor_torque_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_device.png)\n\nWybierz w jakich jednostkach ma być podawany **torque of motor** czy w inch-pounds (InLb) czy Niutonometrach (Nm).\n\n![motor_torque_units](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_units.png)\n\nBlok **torque of motor** jest używany wewnątrz bloków z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![motor_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_inserted.png)"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Skręć\n\nCały czas obraca układ napędowy.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **turn** będzie cały czas obracał napęd, do momentu użycia nowego bloku napędu lub zatrzymania programu.\n\nWybierz kierunek skrętu układu napędowego.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Obróć o\n\nObraca układ napędowy na zadaną odległość.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, w którym kierunku skręci się układ napędowy.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\n\nUstaw, jak daleko przesunie się układ napędowy, wprowadzając liczbę stopni.\n\nBlok **turn for** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nDomyślnie inne bloki będą **wait** dopóki układ napędowy nie skręci.\n\nMożesz wybrać strzałkę, aby rozwinąć opcje i wybrać **and don't wait** - spowoduje to, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy układ napędowy będzie się obracał.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Zmień pozycję do\n\nUstawia układ napędowy na określony kurs podczas korzystania z czujnika żyroskopowego.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBloku **turn to heading** można użyć, aby ustawić układ napędowy w dowolnym kierunku zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara.\n\nNa podstawie aktualnego kursu żyroskopu, **turn to heading** określi kierunek skrętu.\n\n**Turn to heading**  akceptuje zakres **0.00 to 359.99** stopni.\n\nBlok **turn to heading** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje, że układ napędowy wykona cztery obroty:\n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- W prawo o 45 stopni\n- W prawo o 90 stopni\n- W prawo o 270 stopni\n- W lewo do 180 stopni\n\nDomyślnie inne bloki będą **wait** dopóki układ napędowy nie skręci.\n\nMożesz wybrać strzałkę, aby rozwinąć opcje i wybrać **and don't wait** - spowoduje to, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy układ napędowy będzie się obracał.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Skręć do obrotu\n\nUstawia układ napędowy na określony kąt obrotu w przypadku konfiguracji z 3-przewodowym czujnikiem żyroskopowym lub czujnikiem bezwładnościowym V5.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **turn to rotation** można użyć, aby ustawić układ napędowy na zadaną wartość dodatnią (zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara) lub ujemną (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara).\n\nNa podstawie obecnej wartości **rotation** napędu, **turn to rotation** określi kierunek skrętu.\n\nBlok **turn to rotation** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n## Przykład\n\nTen przykład spowoduje, że układ napędowy wykona cztery obroty\n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Prawo (zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara) do 90 stopni\n- Prawo (zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara) do 180 stopni\n- W lewo (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara) do -45 stopni\n- Prawo (zgodnie z ruchem wskazówek zegara) do 0 stopni\n\nDomyślnie inne bloki będą **wait** dopóki układ napędowy nie skręci.\n\nMożesz wybrać strzałkę, aby rozwinąć opcjie i wybrać **and don't wait** - to spowoduje, że inne bloki będą nadal działać, podczas gdy układ napędowy będzie się obracał.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Zmienna\n\nPodaje wartość liczbową przypisaną do zmiennej.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBloki **Variable** służą do zgłaszania wartości liczbowej przechowywanej wewnątrz zmiennej. Użyj bloku **set variable** aby ustawić lub zaktualizować wartość liczbową zmiennej.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nBlok **variable** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nZmienne są tworzone przy użyciu przycisku **Make a Variable**.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Prędkość silnika\n\nPodaje aktualną prędkość inteligentnego silnika VEX V5.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Velocity of motor** podaje zakres między **-100% a 100%** lub **-600rpm to 600rpm**.\n\n**Velocity of motor** zgłosi zakres „obrotów na minutę” na podstawie wkładu zębatego zainstalowanego w silnikach V5 Smart Motors.\n\n* Czerwony wkład: od -100 obr./min do 100 obr./min\n* Wkład zielony: od -200 do 200 obr./min\n* Wkład niebieski: od -600 do 600 obr./min\n\nWybierz silnik, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nWybierz, czy prędkość jest podawana w %, czy w obrotach na minutę (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nBlok **velocity of motor** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"velocity_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"velocity_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Prędkość enkodera wału\n\nPodaje aktualną prędkość enkodera wału.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\n**Velocity of shaft encoder** zgłasza wartość dziesiętną w stopniach na sekundę (dps) lub w obrotach na minutę (rpm).\n\nWybierz, którego enkodera wału użyć.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_motor.png)\n\nWybierz, czy prędkość jest podawana w stopniach na sekundę (dps) czy w obrotach na minutę (rpm).\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_unit.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Vision obiekt\n\nPodaje informacje o wykrytym obiekcie z czujnika wizyjnego.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nAby użyć bloku **Vision object**, wykonaj następujące kroki:\n\n1. Skonfiguruj czujnik wizyjny za pomocą okna Urządzenia.\n2. Użyj bloku **snapshot** aby uchwycić obraz z czujnika wizyjnego i poszukać kodu podpisu / koloru.\n3. Użyj bloku **object exists** aby sprawdzić, czy czujnik wizyjny wykrył żądany kod podpisu / koloru.\n\nGdy czujnik wizyjny wykryje obiekt, możesz użyć innych bloków wizyjnych, aby dowiedzieć się więcej o wykrytym obiekcie.\n\n* Użyj bloku **set vision object item** aby ustawić, o którym wykrytym obiekcie chcesz uzyskać więcej informacji. Domyślnie używany jest największy wykryty obiekt.\n* Użyj bloku **object count** aby określić, ile obiektów zostało wykrytych z żądanego kodu podpisu / koloru.\n* Użyj bloku **vision object** aby określić, które informacje z wykrytego obiektu zgłosić.\n\nWybierz, którego czujnika wizyjnego chcesz użyć.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nWybierz, którą wartość raportować z czujnika wizyjnego:\n\n* Szerokość - szerokość obiektu w pikselach. Zwraca wartość **2 - 316 pikseli**.\n* Wysokość - wysokość obiektu w pikselach. Zwraca wartość **2 - 212 pikseli**.\n* CenterX - zgłasza współrzędną X środka wykrytego obiektu. Zwraca wartość **0 - 315 pikseli**.\n* CenterY - podaje współrzędną Y środka wykrytego obiektu. Zwraca wartość **0 - 211 pikseli**.\n* Kąt - podaje kąt wykrytego obiektu. Zwraca wartość **0 - 180 stopni**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nBlok **vision object** jest używany w blokach z okrągłymi pustymi miejscami.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Czekaj\n\nCzeka przez określony czas, zanim przejdzie do następnego bloku.\n\n![wait](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz czas **wait**.\n\nBlok **wait** może akceptować liczby dziesiętne, liczby całkowite lub bloki numeryczne.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Czekaj do\n\nCzeka na zwrócenie od bloku logicznego **prawda** przed przejściem do następnego bloku.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\n**Wait until** będzie wielokrotnie sprawdzać blok wartości logicznej i nie przejdzie do następnego bloku, dopóki wartość logiczna nie zwróci **prawda**.\n\nBlok logiczny **wait until** akceptuje bloki o kształcie sześciokątnym (sześciobocznym).\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n"},"when_autonomous":{"name":"when_autonomous","markdown":"# Kiedy autonomiczny\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków po odebraniu sygnału trybu „autonomicznego” z pola zawodów lub przełącznika zawodów.\n\n![when_autonomous](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_autonomous/when_autonomous.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWszelkie bloki dołączone do wydarzenia **when autonomous** zostaną uruchomione, gdy robot zostanie podłączony do pola zawodów lub przełącznika zawodów, który jest ustawiony w trybie „autonomicznym”.\n\nUżytkownicy mogą mieć maksymalnie 50 bloków **when autonomous control** w projekcie."},"when_brain_screen":{"name":"when_brain_screen","markdown":"# Kiedy Ekran mózgu\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków po naciśnięciu lub zwolnieniu ekranu dotykowego Mózgu V5.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nZdarzenie **when brain screen** może być używane do tworzenia działań lub zachowań opartych na interakcji dotykowej z ekranem Mózgu V5.\n\nUżywając razem z blokiem **screen position** użytkownicy mogą tworzyć niestandardowe interfejsy do swojego Mózgu V5, wykrywając, kiedy i gdzie pojawiają się dotknięcia na ekranie.\n\nWybierz akcję, która wyzwoli zdarzenie - **pressed** czy **released** \n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed_condition.png)"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Kiedy otrzymam\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków, gdy wybrana wiadomość zostanie odebrana z bloku **broadcasted**.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz wiadomość, której chcesz słuchać. Można również utworzyć nową wiadomość.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\nBlok **when I receive** zostanie uruchomiony tylko z bloku **broadcast** lub **broadcast and wait** w innym stosie."},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Kiedy zderzak\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków po naciśnięciu lub zwolnieniu wybranego czujnika zderzaka.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz, którego przełącznika zderzaka użyć.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nWybierz, które działanie wywoła zdarzenie - **pressed** lub **released** \n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Kiedy oś kontrolera\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków, gdy wybrana oś joysticka kontrolera VEX V5 jest przesuwana.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz kontroler V5, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![when_controller_axis_device](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_device.png)\n\nWybierz, której osi joysticka kontrolera chcesz użyć.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Gdy przycisk kontrolera\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków po naciśnięciu lub zwolnieniu wybranego przycisku kontrolera V5.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nWybierz kontroler V5, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![when_controller_button_controller](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_controller.png)\n\nWybierz przycisk kontrolera, którego chcesz użyć.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\nWybierz, które działanie wywoła zdarzenie - ** wciśnięcie ** lub ** zwolnienie **\n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_driver":{"name":"when_driver","markdown":"# Kiedy kierowca\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków, gdy sygnał trybu „sterowanie przez kierowcę” jest odbierany z pola zawodów lub przełącznika zawodów.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_driver/when_driver.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nKażdy blok dołaczony do bloku **when driver control** zostanie uruchomiony, gdy robot zostanie podłączony do pola zawodów lub przełącznika zawodów, który jest ustawiony na tryb „sterowanie przez kierowcę.\n\nPętla **forever** jest wysoce zalecane do użytku z **when driver control**, aby umożliwić częste aktualizowanie poleceń opartych na kontrolerze V5 podczas części meczu kontrolowanej przez gracza.\n\nUżytkownicy mogą mieć maksymalnie 50 bloków **when driver control** w projekcie."},"when_limit":{"name":"when_limit","markdown":"# Kiedy limit\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków po naciśnięciu lub zwolnieniu wybranego czujnika wyłącznika krańcowego.\n\n![when_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_limit/when_limit.png)\n\n## Jak korzystać\n\nWybierz, którego wyłącznika krańcowego chcesz użyć.\n\n![when_limit_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_limit/when_limit_select.png)\n\nWybierz akcję, która wyzwoli zdarzenie - **pressed** lub **released** \n\n![when_limit_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_limit/when_limit_condition.png)\n"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# Po uruchomieniu\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków podczas uruchamiania projektu.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nZdarzenia **When started** zostaną uruchomione, gdy program zostanie uruchomiony z menu  Mózgu VEX V5 lub przyciskiem **run** w blokach.\n\nWszystkie nowe programy będą automatycznie zawierać blok **when started**. Projekty mogą obsługiwać do 50 bloków **when started**.\n\n**When started** będzie również działał jako stos trybu „przedautonomicznego” dla projektu VRC Competition.\n\n"},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Kiedy zegar\n\nUruchamia dołączony stos bloków, gdy licznik czasu mózgu V5 jest większy niż podana wartość.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nLicznik czasu zaczyna się na początku każdego projektu.\n\nWybierz czas. Blok wydarzenia **when timer** uruchomi się, gdy zegar Mózgu jest ustawiony **greater than** na daną wartość.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nBlok **when timer** może akceptować wartości dziesiętne lub całkowite.\n\nBlok **when timer** **cannot**  akceptować innych bloków."},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Kiedy\n\nBlok typu 'C' powtarza bloki wewnątrz, podczas gdy zwrócony jest warunek logiczny **prawda**.  \n\n![while](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/while/while.png)\n\n## Jak używać\n\nBlok **while** sprawdzi warunek logiczny tylko na początku każdej pętli.\n\nKiedy wartość logiczna jest zwrócona jako **prawda**, bloki wewnątrz **while** zostaną uruchomione.\n\nKiedy wartość logiczna jest zwrócona jako **fałsz**, bloki wewnątrz **while** zostaną pominięte.\n\nBlok typu 'C' **while** może przyjąć sześciokątne (sześcioboczne) bloki jako warunek.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/pl/while/while_inserted.png)"}}},"ru":{"blocks":{"acceleration_of":{"name":"acceleration_of","markdown":"# Ускорение по оси\n\nСообщает значение ускорения по одной из осей, полученное с аналогового акселерометра.\n\n![acceleration_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **ускорения по оси** возвращает значения в диапазоне **от -2.0 G до 2.0 G** или **от -6.0 G до 6.0 G**. Диапазон зависит от места установки джампера.\n\nВыберите акселерометр для использования.\n\n![acceleration_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_device.png)\n\nБлок **ускорения по оси** может использоваться в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![acceleration_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_inserted.png)"},"activate_emergency_stop":{"name":"activate_emergency_stop","markdown":"# Activate emergency stop\n\nActivates the emergency stop (or E-stop) button for the V5 Robotic Arm.\n\n![estop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/activate_emergency_stop/estop_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe emergency stop button in the Workcell will shut off any V5 Smart Motors and Sensors connected to the V5 Brain. \n\n![estop_robot](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/activate_emergency_stop/estop_robot.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_estop_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/activate_emergency_stop/select_estop_arm.png)\n\nThe **activate emergency stop** block is often used with the When bumper block from the Events category. This ensures that all V5 Smart Motors and Sensors connected to the V5 Brain will shut off once the Bumper Switch (E-stop) is pressed.\n![estop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/activate_emergency_stop/estop_example.png)"},"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# Сумма\n\nСумма двух объектов.\n\n![add](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/add/add.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Сумма** производится между десятичными, целыми и числовыми блоками.\n\nБлок **суммы** может быть включён в блоки с овальными рамками для аргументов и может принимать в качестве значений такие же овальные блоки.\n\nСумма двух чисел.\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/add/add_numbers.png)\n\nСумма числа и переменной.\n\n![add_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/add/add_variables.png)  \n\nСумма числа и значений, получаемых с датчиков и устройств.\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# Логическое И\n\nВыражение возвращает правду, если оба аргумента оператора И - правда.\n\n![and](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/and/and.png)\n\n## ## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **логического и** возвращает **правду** в случае, если оба значения **правда**. \n\nБлок **логического и** возвращает **ложь** в случае, если хотя бы один из блоков **ложь**.\n\nЛогический блок **логического и** возвращает **правду** или **ложь** и может быть помещён в блоки, содержащие шестиугольные рамки.\n\n![and_shape](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере рассматривается проверка одновременного нажатия двух кнопок на пульте управления.\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/and/and_sensors.png)\n\nБлок **логического И** вернёт **правду** в случае, если обе кнопки на пульте управления (**Кнопка X пульта управления** и **Кнопка A пульта управления**) будут нажаты.\n\nБлок **логического И** вернёт **правду** в случае, если хотя бы одна или обе кнопки пульта управления не будут нажаты.\n\n![and_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/and/and_truth.png)"},"angle_of":{"name":"angle_of","markdown":"# Угол поворота потенциометра\n\nВозвращает значение угла поворота потенциометра.\n\n![angle_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/angle_of/angle_of_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **угла поворота потенциометра** работает в диапазонах **от 0 до 100%** или **от 0.0 до 250.0 градусов**.\n\nВыберите потенциометр для использования.\n\n![angle_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/angle_of/angle_of_device.png)\n\nВыберите единицу измерения в % или градусах.\n\n![angle_of_block_parameters](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/angle_of/angle_of_parameters.png)\n\nБлок **угла поворота потенциометра** может быть использован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![angle_of_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/angle_of/angle_of_inserted.png)\n"},"battery_current":{"name":"battery_current","markdown":"# Ток аккумулятора\n\nСообщает о текущем состоянии аккумулятора V5.\n\n![battery_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/battery_current/battery_current_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **тока аккумулятора** работает в диапазоне **от 0.0 до 20.0 А**.\n\nБлок **тока аккумулятора** может быть использован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![battery_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/battery_current/battery_current_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# Уровень заряда аккумулятора\n\nВозвращает текущее значение заряда аккумулятора контроллера.\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Уровень заряда аккумулятора** возвращает значение **от 0% до 100%**.\n\nБлок **уровня заряда аккумулятора** может быть использован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)"},"battery_voltage":{"name":"battery_voltage","markdown":"# Напряжение аккумулятора\n\nВозвращает значение напряжения аккумулятора.\n\n![battery_voltage_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **напряжения аккумулятора** возвращает значение в диапазоне **от 10.0 до 14.4 В**.\n\nБлок **напряжения аккумулятора** может быть использован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![battery_voltage_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_inserted.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# Логическая переменная\n\nСоздаёт переменную логического типа.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **логической переменной** возвращает значение **правды** или **лжи**, хранящееся внутри переменной. Используйте блок **установки логической переменной** для обновления или изменения значения переменной.\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\nБлок **логической переменной**  - логический и возвращает **правду** или **ложь**, и может использоваться в блоках, содержащих шестиугольные вставки.\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\nЛогическая переменная создаётся с помощью кнопки **Создать логическую переменную**.\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# Прервать\n\nНезамедлительно заканчивает текущий цикл.\n\n![break](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/break/break.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПри добавлении в блок цикла (блок 'C') блок **прервать** незамедлительно заканчивает выполнение цикла.  \n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссия движется вперёд в ожидании нажатия экрана контроллера.\n\nПри нажатии на экран активируется блок **прерывания** и трансмиссия остановится.\n\n![break_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# Количество яркости\n\nСообщает о наличии света в помещении посредством датчика света.\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **количества яркости** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 100%**.\n\nВыберите датчик света для использования.\n\n![brightness_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\nБлок **количества яркости** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![brightness_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# Передача сообщения\n\nПередача сообщения для активации действий, заложенных внутри блока **когда получил**.\n\n![broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **передачи сообщения** используется для параллельного выполнения действий внутри основного блока и блока приёма сообщений.\n\nВыберите сообщение для **передачи сообщения** или создайте новое сообщение.\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# Передать сообщение и ждать\n\nБлок аналогичен блоку **передачи сообщений**, но при использовании данного блока действия внутри **когда получил** блока и основной программы будут выполняться последовательно, а не параллельно.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПри использовании блока **передать сообщение и ждать**, остальные блоки программы будут ожидать выполнения действий внутри блока **когда получил**.\n\nВыберите сообщение для **передачи сообщения** или создайте новое сообщение.\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# Calibrate\n\nCalibrating the Gyro Sensor / Inertial Sensor is used to reduce the amount of drift generated by Gyro Sensor / Inertial Sensor.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\nDrifting occurs when the Gyro Sensor / Inertial Sensor incorrectly detects movement even though the sensor is not physically moving.\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe Gyro Sensor / Inertial Sensor must remain still during the calibration process. The calibration process will take approximately 2 seconds to complete.\n\nChoose which Gyro / Inertial Sensor to use.\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# Изменить переменную\n\nИзменяет значение переменной на предложенное значение.\n\n![change_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите переменную, которую необходимо изменить. Выбранная переменная может быть переименована или удалена.\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\nБлок **изменения переменной** может содержать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере значение переменной, соответствующее скорости, изменяется на 10 каждый раз при прохождении **повторяющегося цикла**.\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# Clear all rows\n\nClears the entire Print Console, V5 Brain or Controller screen.\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Clear all rows** will not change the screen's (V5 Brain or Controller) cursor. Use the **set cursor** block to reset the screen's cursor to a specific position.\n\nHowever, using the **clear all rows** block with the Console option selected will reset the cursor to the top of the Print Console window.\n\nChoose which device to use. V5 Controllers will only appear if they are added in the Devices window.\n\n![clear_all_rows_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_dropdown_with_console.png)"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# Очистить строку\n\nОчистка одной строки на экране контроллера или пульта управления.\n\n![clear_row](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **очистки строки** работает с целыми числами **от 1 до 20**, означающими номер очищаемой строки.\n\nВыберите устройство для использования. Пульт управления появится в списке устройств в случае, если он был добавлен в окне настройки устройств.w.\n\n![clear_row_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/clear_row/clear_row_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nКонтроллер V5 позволяет работать с разными размерами шрифтов. Изменение размера шрифта влияет на количество строк.\n\n**Размер шрифта на контроллере - Число строк:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 строк\n* Small - 16 строк\n* Medium - 12 строк (по умолчанию)\n* Large - 8 строк\n* Extra Large - 6 строк\n* Super Large - 4 строк\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/clear_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nКонтроллер V5 работает только с одним размером шрифта.\n\n**Ращмер шрифта на пульте управления - Число строк:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 строки (по умолчанию)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/clear_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# Комментарий\n\nПозволяет разработчику оставлять пояснения для своей программы.\n\n![comment_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПрофессиональные разработчики используют комментарии на протяжении всей программы для облегчения понимания своего кода другими разработчиками. Комментарии также могут помочь в поиске ошибок.\n\nДля добавления текста в блок **комментария** необходимо удалить предыдущий текст.\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nКомментарии никак не влияют на выполнение программы.\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# Controller enabled\n\nEnables or disables Controller configured actions from the Devices menu.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose to either enable or disable the configured Controller actions by selecting the desired state from the dropdown. By default, the Controller is Enabled in every project.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThe configured action in this example is using the robot's Drivetrain behavior set by the Controller's configuration in the Devices window.\n\n![configured_action](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\nThis example will have the configured Controller disabled when the program starts. \n\nThen, the robot will drive forward for 6 inches.\n\nFinally, the **controller enabled** block will enable the Controller to restore Controller driving behaviors.\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"controller_play_rumble":{"name":"controller_play_rumble","markdown":"# Включение эффекта вибрации\n\nЗапускает эффект вибрации на пульте управления.\n\n![controller_play_rumble](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **включения эффекта вибрации** использует специальный вибро-моторчик, обеспечивающий обратную связь.\n\nВыберите шаблон для использования.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_pattern](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_pattern.png)\n\nВыберите пульт управления для использования.\n\n![controller_play_rumble_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_device.png)\n\n\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# Ток привода\n\nВозвращает значение тока привода для текущего момента работы в  амперах (А).\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **тока привода** возвращает значения в диапазоне **от 0.0 до 2.5 А**. \n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nБлок **тока привода** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# Столбец курсора\n\nВозвращает номер столбца на экране контроллера, в которой стоит курсор.\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **столбца курсора** возвращает значения **от 1 до 80**.\n\nБлок **столбца курсора** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nКонтроллер V5 позволяет работать с разными размерами шрифтов. Изменение размера шрифта влияет на количество столбцов.\n\n**Размер шрифта на контроллере - Число столбцов:**\n\n* Extra Small - 80 столбцов\n* Small - 68 столбцов\n* Medium - 48 столбцов (по умолчанию)\n* Large - 32 столбцов\n* Extra Large - 24 столбцов\n* Super Large - 16 столбцов\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/cursor_column/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nНа пульте управление недоступно изменение размера шрифта.\n\n**Размер шрифта на пульте управления - Число столбцов:**\n\n* Standard Font - 20 столбцов (по умолчанию)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/cursor_column/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# Строка курсора\n\nВозращает значение строки, в которой установлен курсор.\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **строки курсора** возвращает значения **от 1 до 20**.\n\nБлок **строки курсора** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nКонтроллер V5 позволяет работать с разными размерами шрифтов. Изменение размера шрифта влияет на количество столбцов.\n\n**Размер шрифта на контроллере - Число строк:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 строк\n* Small - 16 строк\n* Medium - 12 строк (по умолчанию)\n* Large - 8 строк\n* Extra Large - 6 строк\n* Super Large - 4 строки\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/cursor_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nНа пульте управление недоступно изменение размера шрифта.\n\n**Размер шрифта на пульте управления - Число строк:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 строки (по умолчанию)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/cursor_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"distance_found_object":{"name":"distance_found_object","markdown":"# Distance object found\n\nReports if the Distance sensor sees an object within its field of view.\n\n![distance_found_object_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block1.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Distance object found** reports true when the Distance sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n**Distance object found** reports false when the Distance sensor does not detect an object or surface.\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_found_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block2.png)\n\n\nThe **distance object found** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![distance_found_object_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block3.png)\n"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# Расстояние до объекта\n\nСообщает о расстоянии до ближайшего объекта от датчика расстояния.\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **расстояния до объекта** считывает показания в диапазоне **от 30 мм до 3000 мм** или **от 2 до 115 дюймов**. \n\nВыберите датчик расстояния для использования.\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\nВыберите единицу измерения расстояния: миллиметры или дюймы.\n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\nБлок **расстояния до объекта** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"distance_object_distance":{"name":"distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Object distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the Distance sensor.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object distance** reports a range from **20mm to 2000mm**.\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether **object distance** is reported in inches or millimeters. \n\n![distance_object_distance_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block **object distance** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block4.png)\n"},"distance_object_size":{"name":"distance_object_size","markdown":"# Object size is\n\nReports if the Distance Sensor detects the specified object size.  \n\n![distance_object_size_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe sensor determines the size of the object detected (none, small, medium, large) based on the amount of light reflected and returned to the sensor.\n\nChoose a Distance Sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_size_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block1.png)\n\nChoose which size of the object you want the sensor to check for.\n\n![distance_object_size_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block2.png)\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **true** when the Distance Sensor detects the specified size.\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **false** if it doesn't detect the specified size.\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![distance_object_size_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block3.png)\n"},"distance_object_velocity":{"name":"distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Object velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of an object in m/s.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object velocity** reports the current velocity of an object in m/s (meters per second).\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block2.png)\n\n\nThe reporter block **object velocity** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block3.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# Деление\n\nОперация делит первое значение на второе для получения частного.\n\n![divide](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/divide/divide.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Деление** работает с десятичными, целыми или числовыми блоками.\n\nБлок **деления** может быть включён в блоки с овальными рамками для аргументов и может принимать в качестве значений такие же овальные блоки. \n\nВведите числа, с которыми необходимо произвести операцию деления.\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\nДеление между переменными.\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\nДеление значений, получаемых с различных устройств.\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"draw_circle":{"name":"draw_circle","markdown":"# Рисование окружности\n\nРисует окружность на экране контроллера.\n\n![draw_circle](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/draw_circle/draw_circle.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **рисования окружности** принимает три значения:\n\n* Значение 1: Центр окружности по X\n* Значение 2: Центр окружности по Y\n* Значение 3: Радиус окружности в пикселях\n\nЦвет линии окружности определяется блоком **установки цвета пера**. По умолчанию цвет белый.\n\nЦвет заливки окружности определяется блоком **установки цвета заливки**. По умолчанию цвет чёрный.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"draw_line":{"name":"draw_line","markdown":"# Рисование линии\n\nРисует линию на экране контроллера.\n\n![draw_line](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/draw_line/draw_line.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **рисования линии** принимает четыре значения:\n\n* Значение 1: Координата X первой точки\n* Значение 2: Координата Y первой точки\n* Значение 3: Координата X второй точки\n* Значение 4: Координата Y второй точки\n\nЦвет линии определяется блоком **установки цвета пера**. По умолчанию цвет белый.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_pixel":{"name":"draw_pixel","markdown":"# Рисование пикселя\n\nРисует пиксель на экране контроллера.\n\n![draw_pixel](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/draw_pixel/draw_pixel.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **рисования пикселей** принимает два значения:\n\n* Значение 1: X координата\n* Значение 2: Y координата\n\nЦвет пикселя определяется блоком **установки цвета пера**. По умолчанию цвет белый.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_rectangle":{"name":"draw_rectangle","markdown":"# Draw rectangle\n\nDraws a rectangle on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n![draw_rectangle](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/draw_rectangle/draw_rectangle.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **draw rectangle** block requires 4 values:\n\n* Value 1: Top Left Corner X coordinate\n* Value 2: Top Left Corner Y coordinate\n* Value 3: Width of the rectangle\n* Value 4: Height of the rectangle\n\nThe outside line color of the rectangle is determined by the **set pen color** block. The default line color is white.\n\nThe inside fill color of the rectangle is determine by the **set fill color** block. The default fill color is black.\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# Движение\n\nЗапускает непрерывное движение трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **движения** запускает непрерывное движение трансмиссии до тех пор, пока не будет использован другой блок для трансмиссии или программа не будет остановлена.\n\nВыберите направление движения для запуска трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# Ток трансмиссии\n\nВозвращает значение тока трансмиссии для текущего момента работы в амперах (А).\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **тока трансмиссии** возвращает значения в диапазоне **от 0.0 до 2.5 А**. \n\nБлок **тока трансмиссии** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_efficiency":{"name":"drive_efficiency","markdown":"# Производительность трансмиссии\n\nВозвращает значение производительности трансмисии.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **производительности трансмиссии** возвращает отношение мощностей на входе и выходе приводов трансмиссии.\n\nТрансмиссия обычно работает примерно на 65% от общей производительности.\n\nБлок **производительности трансмиссии** возвращает значения в диапазоне **от 0 до 100%**.\n\nБлок **производительности трансмиссии** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![drive_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# Движение на расстояние\n\nРеализует проезд трансмиссии на определённое расстояние.\n\n![drive_for](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите направление движения трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\nУстановите числовое значение расстояния и выберите единицу измерения (миллиметры или дюймы).\n\nБлок **движения на расстояние** принимает десятичные, целые и числовые значения..\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\nПо умолчанию остальные блоки **ждут** остановки трансмисии.\n\nВы можете выбрать из раскрывающегося списка **и не ждать** для того, чтобы параллельно с движением выполнялись другие блоки.\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# Курс движения\n\nСообщает о текущем направлении движения трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Курс движения** возвращает значения **от 0.00 до 359.99 градусов**.\n\nБлок **курс движения** сообщает об увеличении угла при вращении против часовой стрелки как показано на рисунке ниже.\n\nБлок **курс движения** может быть использован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# Движение закончено\n\nСообщает об окончании движения трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **движение закончено** возвращает **правду**, когда приводы трансмиссии закончили свою работу.\n\nБлок **движение закончено** возвращает **ложь**, когда приводы трансмиссии всё ещё работают.\n\nБлок **движение закончено** - логический и возвращает **правду** или **ложь**, и может использоваться в блоках, содержащих шестиугольные вставки.\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# Движение продолжается\n\nСообщает о движении трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **движение продолжается** возвращает **правду**, когда приводы трансмиссии работают.\n\nБлок **движение продолжается** возвращает **ложь**, когда приводы остановились.\n\nБлок **движение продолжается** - логический и возвращает **правду** или **ложь**, и может использоваться в блоках, содержащих шестиугольные вставки.\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_power":{"name":"drive_power","markdown":"# Мощность трансмиссии\n\nСообщает о текущей мощности трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_power](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_power/drive_power.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **мощности трансмиссии** работает в диапазоне **от 0.0 до 22.0 Вт**.\n\nБлок **мощности трансмиссии** может быть использован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![drive_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_power/drive_power_inserted.png)"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# Вращение движения\n\nСообщает об угле вращения трансмисии в соответствии с настройками гироскопа или инерционного датчика.\n\n![drive_rotation](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_rotation/drive_rotation.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **вращение движения** возвращает **положительное** значение в случае поворота трансмиссии **по часовой стрелке**.\n\nБлок **вращение движения** возвращает **отрицательное** значение в случае поворота трансмиссии **против часовой стрелке**.\n\nБлок **вращение движения** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![drive_rotation_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_rotation/drive_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_temperature":{"name":"drive_temperature","markdown":"# Температура приводов трансмиссии\n\nСообщает температуру приводов трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_temperature](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_temperature/drive_temperature.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **температуры приводов трансмиссии** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 100%**.\n\nБлок **температуры приводов трансмиссии** может быть ипользован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![drive_temperature_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_temperature/drive_temperature_inserted.png)"},"drive_torque":{"name":"drive_torque","markdown":"# Момент приводов трансмиссии\n\nСообщает величину момента трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_torque/drive_torque.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **момента приводов трансмиссии** работает в диапазонах **от 0.0 до 18.6 дюйм силы (InLB)** или **от 0.0 до 2.1 Нм**.\n\nВыберите единицу измерения момента.\n\n![drive_torque_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_torque/drive_torque_unit.png)\n\nБлок **момента приводов трансмиссии** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![drive_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_torque/drive_torque_inserted.png)"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# Скорость трансмиссии\n\nВозвращает текущее значение скорости трансмиссии.\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **скорости трансмисии** возвращает значения в диапазонах **от -100 до 100 %** или **от -600 до 600 об/мин**.\n\nБлок **скорости трансмисии** возвращает значение, основанное на типе установленного картриджа приводов трансмиссии.\n\n* Красный картридж: от -100 до 100 об/мин\n* Зелёный картридж: от -200 до 200 об/мин\n* Синий картридж: от -600 до 600 об/мин\n\nВыберите единицы измерения скорости в процентах или оборотах в минуту.\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\nБлок **скорости трансмисии** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"duration":{"name":"duration","markdown":"# Время работы электромагнита\n\nУстанавливает время работы электромагнита.\n\n![set_duration_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/duration/set_duration_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите длительность работы электромагнита:\n\n* **short** - включает электромагнит на **250мс**\n* **medium** - включает электромагнит на **500mмс**\n* **large** - включает электромагнит на **1000мс**\n\n![set_duration_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/duration/set_duration_block_setting.png)\n\nВыберите электромагнит для использования.\n\n![set_duration_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/duration/set_duration_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере робот проедет вперёд 200 мм, включит магнит с длительностью **large**, захватит предмет, проедет вперёд 200 мм и деактивирует магнит.\n\n![set_duration_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/duration/set_duration_example.png)\n"},"efficiency_of_motor":{"name":"efficiency_of_motor","markdown":"# Производительность привода\n\nВозвращает значение производительности привода.\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **производительности привода** возвращает отношение мощностей на входе и выходе привода.\n\nПривод обычно работает примерно на 65% от общей производительности.\n\nБлок **производительности привода** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 100%**.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![motor_efficiency_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_device.png)\n\nБлок **производительности привода** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![motor_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_inserted.png)"},"energize":{"name":"energize","markdown":"# Активация электромагнита\n\nУстанавливает электромагнит в режимы активации/деактивации.\n\n![set_magnet_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/energize/set_magnet_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите действие:\n\n* **boost** - активирует электромагнит на установленную длительность.\n* **drop** - деактивирует магнит.\n\n![set_magnet_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/energize/set_magnet_block_setting.png)\n\nВыберите электромагнит для использования.\n\n![set_magnet_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/energize/set_magnet_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере робот захватит предмет после того, как проедет 200 мм. После очередного проезда 200 мм робот отпустит предмет.\n\n![set_magnet_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/energize/set_magnet_example.png)\n"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# Сравнение\n\nСообщает равно ли первое значение второму. \n\n![equal_to](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **сравнения** возвращает **правду**, когда значения равны.\n\nБлок **сравнения** возвращает **ложь**, когда значения не равны.\n\nБлок **сравнения** десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nБлок **сравнения** - логический, возвращает **правду** или **ложь** и используется в блоках, содержащих шестигольные рамки.\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# Бесконечный цикл\n\n'C' подобный блок цикла бесконечно запускает блоки внутри себя.\n\n![forever](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/forever/forever.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПоместите блоки в **бесконечный цикл** для повторения этих блоков **бесконечно**.\n\nДля выхода из **бесконечного цикла** вы можете использовать блок **прервать**.\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\n'C' подобные блоки могут быть помещены друг в друга. Данная концепция называется \"вложенностью\", которая обеспечивает более разнообразное поведение роботов."},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# Математические операции\n\nРаботает в соответствие с выбранной функцией.\n\n\n![function](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/function/function.png)\n\n* **abs** - модуль числа\n* **floor** - округляет в меньшую сторону до ближайшего целого числа\n* **ceiling** - округляет в большую сторону до ближайшего целого числа\n* **sqrt** - корень из числа\n* **sin** - синус\n* **cos** - косинус\n* **tan** - тангенс\n* **asin** - арксинус\n* **acos** - арккосинус\n* **atan** - арктангенс\n* **ln** - натуральный логарифм по основанию e (экспонента)\n* **log** - десятичный логарифм по основанию 10\n* **e ^** - возведение e (экспоненты) в степень\n* **10 ^** - возведение десяти (10) в степень\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **математических операций** принимает десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nВыберите нужную **математическую операцию** из списка.\n\n![function_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/function/function_select.png)\n\nБлок **математических операций** может быть использован в блоках с круглой вставкой.\n\n![function_fit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# Больше\n\nСообщает больше ли значение слева по сравнению со значением справа.  \n\n![greater_than](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **больше** возвращает **правду**, когда первое значение больше второго. \n\nБлок **больше** возвращает **ложь**, когда первое значение меньше или равно второму. \n\nБлок **больше** принимает десятичные, целый или числовые блоки.\n\nБлок **больше** - логический и возвращает **правду** или **ложь**, и может использоваться в блоках, содержащих шестиугольные вставки.\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# Угол курса\n\nВозвращает значение курса гироскопа/инерцинного датчика в градусах.\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **угла курса** сообщает об увеличении угла при движении по часовой стрелке.\n\nБлок **угла курса** возвращает значение в диапазоне **от 0.00 до 359.99 градусов**.\n\nВыберите гироскоп/инерционный датчик для использования.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\nБлок **угла курса** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# Если тогда\n\n'C' подобный блок запускает блоки внутри себя, если условие после \"если\" правдиво.\n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **если тогда** в первую очередь проверяет условие. \n\nЕсли условие **правда**, то выполняются блоки внутри **если тогда**.\n\nЕсли условие **ложь**, то блоки внутри **если тогда** пропускаются и управление передаётся дальше.\n\nБлок **если тогда** может принимать шестиугольные блоки в качестве условия.\n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# Если тогда иначе\n\n'C' подобный блок **если тогда иначе** запускает блоки в первой или второй части в зависимости от условия.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **если тогда иначе** в первую очередь проверяет условие. \n\nЕсли условие **правда**, то выполняются блоки внутри **если тогда**.\n\nЕсли условие **ложь**, то выполняются блоки внутри **иначе**.\n\nБлок **если тогда иначе** может принимать шестиугольные блоки в качестве условия.\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)"},"inertial_acceleration":{"name":"inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# Acceleration of\n\nReports the acceleration value from one of the axes (x, y, or z) on the Intertial Sensor.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n**Acceleration of** reports a range from **-4.0 to 4.0** Gs. \n\nChoose which Inertial Sensor to use.\n\n![inertial_acceleration_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_device.png)\n\nChoose which axis to use:\n\n* The **X-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **forward to backward**\n* The **Y-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **side to side**\n* The **Z-axis** reports acceleration when the Inertial Sensor moves **up to down**\n\n![inertial_acceleration_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_axis.png)\n\nThe sensing block **acceleration of** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_gyrorate":{"name":"inertial_gyrorate","markdown":"# Gyro rate\n\nGets the rate of rotation from one of the axes (x, y, or z) on the Inertial Sensor.\n\n![gyro_rate_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_gyrorate/gyro_rate_block.png)\n\n## How to Use\n\n**Gyro rate** reports a range from **-1000.0 to 1000.0** in dps (degrees per second). \n\nChoose which Inertial Sensor to use.\n\n![gyroRate_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_included_block.png)\n\nChoose which axis to use.\n\n* The **X-axis** reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the X-Axis (based on the oritentation of the sensor)\n* The **Y-axis** reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Y-Axis (based on the oritentation of the sensor)\n* The **Z-axis** reports rate of rotation when the Inertial Sensor rotates in the Z-Axis (based on the oritentation of the sensor)\n\n![gyroRate_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_axis.png)\n\nThe sensing block **gyro rate** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_orientation":{"name":"inertial_orientation","markdown":"# Угол ориентации\n\nСообщает о текущем угле поворота инерционного датчика. \n\n![orientation_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_orientation/orientation_inertial_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nОриентация датчика определяется выбранной осью.\n\n* **Ось X** характеризует **наклон** в диапазоне от -90 до +90 градусов\n* **Ось Y** характеризует **вращение** в диапазоне от -180 до +180 градусов\n* **Ось Z** характеризует **отклонение** в диапазоне от -180 до +180 градусов\n---\n\n**наклон** - это угол робота при наклоне вперёд/назад.\n\n![V5_Pitch_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_orientation/V5_Pitch_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Вращение** - это угол робота при наклонах вправо/влево.\n\n![V5_Roll_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_orientation/V5_Roll_rev2.jpg)\n\n\n**Отклонение** - это угол при вращении робота.\n\n![V5_Yaw_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_orientation/V5_Yaw_rev2.jpg)\n\n---\n\nВыберите инерционный датчик для использования.\n\n![orientation_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_orientation/orientation_included_block.png)\n\nВыберите ось для использования.\n\n![orientation_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_orientation/orientation_axis.png)\n\nБлок **угла ориентации** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![orientation_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/inertial_orientation/orientation_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n\n"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Элемент двумерного массива\n\nВозвращает значение элемента двумерного массива.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите двумерный массив, который вы бы хотели использовать. Кроме того, двумерный массив может быть удалён или переименован.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\nВведите номер строки (первое число) и номер столбца (второе число) элемента, значение которого вы бы хотели получить. В этом примере выбран элемент из второй строки и третьего столбца.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\nБлок **элемента двумерного массива** принимает значения десятичных, целых или числовых блоков.\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# Элемент списка\n\nВозвращает значение элемента выбранного списка. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите список. Список может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\nВведите номер элемента в списке. В данном примере выбран второй элемент списка. \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\nБлок **элементов списка** принимает десятичные, целый или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере скорость трансмиссии будет равна значению третьего элемента списка. Теперь трансмиссия движется вперёд со скоростью 90%.\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"joint_move":{"name":"joint_move","markdown":"# Joint move\n\nMoves the V5 Robotic Arm to the specified (x, y, z) coordinate using joint movement.\n\n![joint_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/joint_move/joint_move_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **joint move** block moves the V5 Robotic Arm in the x, y, and z-direction using joint movement. \n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/joint_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_joint_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/joint_move/select_joint_arm.png)\n\nThe **joint move** block accepts decimals, integers, and numeric blocks.\n\n![joint_input](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/joint_move/joint_input.png)"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Длина 2D списка\n\nВозвращает число строк или столбцов двумерного списка.\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите 2D список. Двумерный список может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\nВыберите значение, которое необходимо узнать. Двумерный список может сообщить число **строк** или **столбцов**.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\nБлок **длины 2D списка** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# Меньше\n\nСообщает меньше ли значение слева по сравнению со значением справа.  \n\n![less_than](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **меньше** возвращает **правду**, когда первое значение меньше второго. \n\nБлок **меньше** возвращает **ложь**, когда первое значение больше или равно второму. \n\nБлок **меньше** принимает десятичные, целый или числовые блоки.\n\nБлок **меньше** - логический и возвращает **правду** или **ложь**, и может использоваться в блоках, содержащих шестиугольные вставки.\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n"},"linear_move":{"name":"linear_move","markdown":"# Linear move\n\nMoves the V5 Robotic Arm to the specified (x, y, z) coordinate using linear movement.\n\n![linear_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/linear_move/linear_move_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **linear move** block moves the V5 Robotic Arm in the x, y, and z-direction using linear movement. \n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/linear_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_linear_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/linear_move/select_linear_arm.png)\n\nThe **linear move** block accepts decimals, integers, and numeric blocks.\n\n![linear_input](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/linear_move/linear_input.png)"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# Остановка привода\n\nСообщает о завершении движения выходного вала привода.\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **остановки привода** возвращает **правду**, если привод закончил выполнение движения.\n\nБлок **остановки привода** возвращает **ложь**, если привод продолжает выполнение движения.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\nБлок **остановки привода** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# Вращение привода\n\nСообщает о движении выходного вала привода.\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **вращения привода** возвращает **правду**, если привод продолжает выполнение движения.\n\nБлок **вращения привода** возвращает **ложь**, если привод закончил выполнение движения.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\nБлок **вращения привода** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# Умножение\n\nПроизводит умножение двух указанных значений.\n\n![multiply](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Умножение** принимает десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nБлок **умножения** может быть включён в блоки с овальными рамками для аргументов и может принимать в качестве значений такие же овальные блоки. \n\nУмножение двух чисел.\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\nУмножение переменных.\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\nУмножение показаний устройств.\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# Next row\n\nSets the print output cursor on the Print Console, V5 Brain or Controller screen to the next available row.\n\n![next_row](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nBy default, all projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1. The **next row** block will move the cursor down by a single row on the screen. **Next row** will also set the cursor's column to position 1.\n\nChoose which device to use. V5 Controllers will only appear if they are added in the Devices window.\n\n![next_row_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/next_row/next_row_dropdown_with_console.png)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Brain allows you to change the size of the font printed on the screen. Changing the font will affect the number of rows available on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\n**V5 Brain Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 Rows\n* Small - 16 Rows\n* Medium - 12 Rows (Default)\n* Large - 8 Rows\n* Extra Large - 6 Rows\n* Super Large - 4 Rows\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/next_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nThe V5 Controller does not allow you to change the size of the font printed on the screen.\n\n**V5 Controller Font Size - Number of Rows:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 Rows (Default)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/next_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n\n---\n\nPrinting to the Print Console requires using a **next row** block after a **print** block to output the contents of the Print Console buffer into the Print Console window.\n\n![next_row_with_print_console](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/next_row/next_row_with_print_console.png)"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# Отрицание\n\nВозвращает противоположное значение для указанного логического блока.\n\n![not](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/not/not.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **отрицания** возвращает **правду**, когда блок внутри содержит **ложь**.\n\nБлок **отрицания** возвращает **ложь**, когда блок внутри содержит **правду**.\n\nЛогический блок **отрицания** возвращает **правду** или **ложь** и может быть помещён в блоки, содержащие шестиугольные рамки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере будет возвращено значение **правды**, если нет нажатия на экран контроллера.\n\n![not_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# Число объектов\n\nВозвращает число объектов, обнаруженных камерой. \n\nОбъекты должны быть определены заранее для их обнаружения камерой с помощью блока **числа объектов**.\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите камеру для использования.\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\nПеред использованием блока **числа объектов** необходимо воспользоваться блоком **получения снимка**.\n\nБлок **числа объектов** определяет число объектов, полученного из последнего снимка.\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# Существование объекта\n\nСообщает о наличии объекта перед камерой.\n\nОбъекты должны быть определены заранее для их обнаружения камерой с помощью блока **существования объекта**.\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите камеру для использования.\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\nБлок **существования объекта** возвращает **правду**, если камера обнаружила объект.\n\nБлок **существования объекта** возвращает **ложь**, если камера не обнаружила объект.\n\nБлок **существования объекта** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками. \n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\nПеред использованием блока **существования объекта** необходимо воспользоваться блоком **получения снимка**."},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# Наличие объекта\n\nСообщает о наличии объекта перед датчиком расстояния.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **наличия объекта** возвращает **правду**, если в диапазоне действия датчика расстояния находится объект.\n\nБлок **наличия объекта** возвращает **ложь**, если в диапазоне действия датчика расстояния нет объекта.\n\nВыберите датчик расстояния для использования.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\nБлок **наличия объекта** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"optical_brightness":{"name":"optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_brightness](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_brightness/optical_brightness.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_brightness_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical brightness** block reports a number value from **0%** to **100%**.\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.\n\nThe **Optical brightness** block reports number values and is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_brightness_use](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect":{"name":"optical_detect","markdown":"# Optical detects color\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects the specified color.\n\n![optical_detect](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_detect/optical_detect.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_detect_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_detect/optical_detect_device.png)\n\nChoose which color you want the sensor to check for.\n\n![optical_detect_colors](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_detect/optical_detect_colors.png)\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **true** when the Optical Sensor detects the specified color.\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **false** if it doesn't detect the specified color.\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![optical_detect_use](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_detect/optical_detect_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect_gesture":{"name":"optical_detect_gesture","markdown":"# When Optical detects a gesture \n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the Optical sensor detects a gesture.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **When Optical detects a gesture** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on gestures that the Optical Sensor detects.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor.\n\n\n![optical_detects_gesture_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detects_gesture_device.png)\n\nChoose which gesture triggers the **When Optical detects a gesture** event.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block2.png)"},"optical_detect_object":{"name":"optical_detect_object","markdown":"# When Optical detects/loses \n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the Optical sensor detects or loses an object.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **When Optical detects/loses** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on whether the Optical Sensor **detects** an object in range of the sensor or **loses** an object that was in range of the sensor.\n\nChoose an optical sensor.\n\n![optical_detect_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_device.png)\n\nChoose whether the **When Optical detects/loses** event is triggered when the sensor **detects** an object, or **loses** an object.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block2.png)"},"optical_found_object":{"name":"optical_found_object","markdown":"# Optical found object\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\n\n![optical_found_object](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_found_object/optical_found_object.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_found_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **true** when the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **false** if an object is not within range.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block should be used to check if an object is close to the Optical Sensor so that the color readings from the **Optical detects color** block are accurate.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![optical_found_object_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_condition.png)"},"optical_hue":{"name":"optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical hue\n\nReports the hue of the color of an object.\n\n![optical_hue](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_hue/optical_hue.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose an optical sensor.\n\n![optical_hue_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_hue/optical_hue_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical hue** block reports a number value that is the hue of the color of an object. It returns a number between **0** and **359**, which can be thought of as the location of the color on a color wheel.\n\nThe **Optical hue** block reports number values and is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_hue_use](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_hue/optical_hue_use.png)"},"optical_set_light":{"name":"optical_set_light","markdown":"# Set Optical light\n\nSets the light on the Optical Sensor to on or off.\n\n![optical_set_light](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_set_light/optical_set_light.png)\n\n## How To Use\nThe **Set optical light** block allows you to turn the Optical Sensor's light **on** or **off**. The light lets the sensor see objects if it is looking at an object in a dark area.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_set_light_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_device.png)\n\nChoose whether you want to set the light on the Optical Sensor to **on** or **off**.\n\n![optical_set_light_state](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_state.png)\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, we use the **Set optical light** block to turn the light on. Then, if the Optical Sensor detects an object, we print the hue.\n\n\n![optical_set_light_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_example.png)"},"optical_set_light_power":{"name":"optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Set optical light power \n\nSet the light power of V5 Optical sensor\n\n![optical_set_light_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_light_power_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Set optical light power** block accepts a range of **0%** to **100%**. This will change the brightness of the light on the Optical Sensor. If the light is off, this block will turn the light on.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_set_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_device.png)\n\nThe set optical light power block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![optical_set_power_num](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_num.png)\n\n## Example\nIn this example we use the **Set optical light power** block to set the power of the light to **50%**, then we use the **Set optical light** block to turn the light on. Then, if the Optical Sensor detects an object, we print the hue.\n\n![optical_set_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_example.png)"},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# Или\n\nВыражение возвращает правду, если хотя бы один из аргументов - правда.\n\n![or](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/or/or.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **или** возвращает **правду** в случае, если хотя бы одно значение **правда**. \n\nБлок **или** возвращает **ложь** в случае, если оба значения **ложь**.\n\nЛогический блок **или** возвращает **правду** или **ложь** и может быть помещён в блоки, содержащие шестиугольные рамки.\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nБлок **или** вернёт **правду**, если датчик касания будет нажат и/или значение яркости на датчике света будет больше, чем 50%. \n\nБлок **или** вернёт **ложь**, если датчик касания не будет нажат и значение яркости на датчике света будет меньше, чем 50%. \n\n![or_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/or/or_truth.png)"},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# Положение джойстика\n\nСообщает о текущем положении джойстика вдоль осей.\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **положения джойстика** возвращает значение из диапазона **от -100 до 100**.\n\nБлок **положения джойстика** возвращает ноль в случае установки джойстика в центре осей.\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\nВыберите пульт управления для использования.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_devices.png)\n\nВыберите ось джойстика.\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\nБлок **положения джойстика** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# Положение привода\n\nВозвращает значение расстояния, пройденного приводом.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **положения привода** возвращает целое значения угла поворота и целое число оборотов привода.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\nВыберите единицу измерения: угол поворота или число оборотов.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\nБлок **положения привода** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками. \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"position_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"position_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Положение оптического энкодера\n\nСообщает значение, на которое повернуля энкодер в ходе работы.\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **положения оптического энкодера** возвращает значение расстояния, пройденного энкодером, в виде целых значений градусной меры или десятичного значения оборотов.\n\nВыберите энкодер для использования.\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_device.png)\n\nВыберите единицу измерения возвращаемого значения: градусы или обороты.\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_unit.png)\n\nБлок **положения оптического энкодера** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_inserted.png)"},"power":{"name":"power","markdown":"# Мощность магнита\n\nУстанавливает мощность электрического магнита для захвата и удержания объектов.\n\n![set_magnet_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/power/set_magnet_power_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВы можете поднимать предметы, имеющие разный вес. Блок **мощности магнита** указывает мощность, с которой будет работать электромагнит. Блок **установки мощности магнита** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 100 %**.\n\nВыберите магнит для использования.\n\n![set_magnet_dropdown_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/power/set_magnet_dropdown_block.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере робот проедет вперёд 200 мм, затем увеличит мощность электромагнита, подберёт объект, проедет 200 мм и отпустит объект. \n\n![set_magnet_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/power/set_magnet_power_example.png)\n"},"power_of_motor":{"name":"power_of_motor","markdown":"# Мощность привода\n\nСообщает о текущей мощности на выходе привода.\n\n![motor_power](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/power_of_motor/motor_power.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **мощности привода** возвращает значение в диапзоне **от 0.0 до 11.0 Вт**.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![motor_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/power_of_motor/motor_power_device.png)\n\nБлок **мощности привода** может быть использован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![motor_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/power_of_motor/motor_power_inserted.png)\n"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# Нажатие датчика касания\n\nВозвращает текущее состояние датчика касания.\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **нажатия датчика касания** возвращает **правду**, если датчик касания был нажат.\n\nБлок **нажатия датчика касания** возвращает **ложь**, если датчик касания не был нажат.\n\nВыберите датчик касания для использования.\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\nБлок **нажатия датчика касания** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# Нажатие кнопок пульта управления\n\nСообщает о состоянии кнопок на пульте управления.\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **нажатия кнопок на пульте управления** возвращает **правду**, если выбранная кнопка на пульте управления нажата.\n\nБлок **нажатия кнопок на пульте управления** возвращает **ложь**, если выбранная кнопка на пульте управления не нажата.\n\nВыберите пульт управления для использования.\n\n![pressing_controller_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_device.png)\n\nВыберите кнопку контроллера для использования.\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\nБлок **нажатия кнопок на пульте управления** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)"},"pressing_limit":{"name":"pressing_limit","markdown":"# Нажатие Limit Switch\n\nСообщает о нажатии датчика касания типа Limit Switch.\n\n![pressing_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/pressing_limit/pressing_limit.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **нажатия Limit Switch** возвращает **правду**, если датчик был нажат.\n\nБлок **нажатия Limit Switch** возвращает **ложь**, если датчик не был нажат.\n\nВыберите датчик для использования.\n\n![pressing_limit_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_bumper.png)\n\nБлок **нажатия Limit Switch** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![pressing_limit_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_inserted.png)\n "},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# Print\n\nPrints values or text on the Print Console, V5 Brain or Controller screen.\n\n![look_print](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/print/look_print.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **print** block will print data at a cursor location on the screen or on the Print Console.\n\nAll new projects begin with the screen cursor at row 1 column 1, and at row 1 on the Print Console.\n\nAll reporter blocks will be printed as integer numbers by default. Use the **set print precision** block to adjust the number of decimal places printed.\n\nChoose which device to use. V5 Controllers will only appear if they are added in the Devices window.\n\n![look_print_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/print/look_print_dropdown_with_console.png)\n\nFor adding values to the Print Console buffer, only the **print** block is needed.\n\n![look_print_dropdown_console](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/print/look_print_dropdown_console.png)\n\nHowever, to output the values from the Print Console buffer onto the Print Console, a **set cursor to next row** block is needed. The blocks below will print \"VEXcode\" to the Print Console and set the cursor to the next row.\n\n![look_print_set_cursor_console](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/print/look_print_set_cursor_console.png)\n\n---\n\nPrint words and numbers.\n\n![print_words](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/print/print_words.png)\n\nPrint the reported value from a variable.\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\nPrint the reported calculation of an operator.\n\n![print_addition](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/print/print_addition.png)  \n\nPrint the reported value from a sensor or device.\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# Мои блоки\n\nСоздаёт блок с функционалом, описываемым пользователем.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Мой блок** используется для создания нового блока и позволяет использовать его неограниченное число раз в данной программе. \n\n**Мой блок** создаётся нажатием кнопки **Создать блок**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\nБлок **Мои блоки** может принимать в себя разные параметры на вход: текст, числа или логические переменные. Это позволяет расширить функциональность блока.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\nДля использования **вашего блока** поместите **ваш блок** в основное тело программы. Когда программа достигнет **вашего блока**, то запустятся блоки внутри **вашего блока**. Значения, указанные в \"шапке\" блока, могут быть использованы только внутри этого блока.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\nПрикрепите блоки к шапке вашего блока для использования.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***Примечание: Создание блоков с одинаковыми именами может привести к ошибке в работе программы на Игровых полях.***\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере **ваши блоки** будут реализовывать следующие действия:\n\n* Проехать вперёд 15 дюймов.\n* Вывод значения текущего значения заряда аккумулятора и перенос курсора на новую строку.\n* Поворот робота на 180 градусов направо.\n* Вывод значения текущего значения заряда аккумулятора и перенос курсора на новую строку.\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# Мои блоки\n\nСоздаёт блок с функционалом, описываемым пользователем.\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n**Мой блок** используется для создания нового блока и позволяет использовать его неограниченное число раз в данной программе. \n\n**Мой блок** создаётся нажатием кнопки **Создать блок**.\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\nБлок **Мои блоки** может принимать в себя разные параметры на вход: текст, числа или логические переменные. Это позволяет расширить функциональность блока.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\nДля использования **вашего блока** поместите **ваш блок** в основное тело программы. Когда программа достигнет **вашего блока**, то запустятся блоки внутри **вашего блока**. Значения, указанные в \"шапке\" блока, могут быть использованы только внутри этого блока.\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\nПрикрепите блоки к шапке вашего блока для использования.\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***Примечание: Создание блоков с одинаковыми именами может привести к ошибке в работе программы на Игровых полях.***\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере **ваши блоки** будут реализовывать следующие действия:\n\n* Проехать вперёд 15 дюймов.\n* Вывод значения текущего значения заряда аккумулятора и перенос курсора на новую строку.\n* Поворот робота на 180 градусов направо.\n* Вывод значения текущего значения заряда аккумулятора и перенос курсора на новую строку.\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# Случайное значение\n\nВозвращает случайное значение между наименьшим и наибольшим значениями блока.\n\n![random](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/random/random.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **случайного значения** может использоваться в блоках с овальными вставками. \n\nБлок **случайного значения** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример 1\n\nВ данном примере блок **случайного значения** используется для генерации случайной скорости трансмиссии.\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\n## Пример 2\n\nВ данном примере блок **случайного значения** используется для генерации случайной длительности в блоке ожидания.\n\n![random_control](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"reflectivity_of":{"name":"reflectivity_of","markdown":"# Отраженный свет\n\nСообщает о количестве отраженного света на датчике езды по линии.\n\n![reflectivity_of](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nЯркий свет будет охарактеризован более высоким значением.\n\nТёмный свет будет охарактеризован меньшим значением.\n\nБлок **отраженного света** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 100%**.\n\nВыберите датчик для использования.\n\n![reflectivity_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_color.png)\n\nБлок **отраженного света** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![reflectivity_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n\n"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# Остаток от деления\n\nДелит первое значение на второе и возвращает остаток от деления.\n\n![remainder](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **остатка от деления** может принимать десятичные, целые и числовые блоки.\n\nБлок возвращает ноль в случае, если одно число кратно другому.\n\nБлок **остатка от деления** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере остаток деления семи на два равен \"1\", поэтому на экране будет напечатана единица.\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# Цикл повторения\n\n'C' подобный блок повторяет действия внутри себя заданное число раз.\n\n![repeat](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nЗначение перед действиями блока **повторения** определяет число повторений.\n \n 'C' подобный блок **повторения** принимает целые или числовые блоки.\n\n'C' подобные блоки могут быть использованы внутри похожих блоков. Данная концепция называется \"вложенностью\" и помогает программировать более сложные алгоритмы.\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/repeat/repeat_select.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# Цикл повторять пока\n\n'C' подобный блок цикла работает до тех пор, пока условие **ложь**.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nЦикл **повторять пока** проверяет значение условия на каждой итерации цикла.\n\nЕсли условие **ложь**, то действия внутри цикла **повторять пока** будут запущены.\n\nЕсли условие **правда**, то действия внутри цикла **повторять пока** будут пропущены.\n\n'C' подобный блок цикла **повторять пока** может принимать в качестве условия шестиугольные блоки.\n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# Сбросить таймер\n\nОбнуляет таймер контроллера.\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nТаймер начинает работу в начале программы. Используйте блок **сброса таймера** для обнуления текущего значения таймера.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере таймер будет обнулён перед движением трансмиссии вперёд три секунды. После трёх секунд трансмиссия закончит работу.\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_angle":{"name":"rotation_angle","markdown":"# Angle of rotation \n\nReports a V5 Rotation sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n![rotation_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Angle of rotation** block reports values in the range of **0.00** to **359.99**.\n\nThe **Angle of rotation** block will either report increasing or decreasing values as the Rotation sensor turns.\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to get values from.\n\n![rotation_angle_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block2.png)\n\nThe **angle of rotation** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_angle_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block3.png)\n"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# Угол вращения\n\nСообщает о текущем угле вращения гироскопа или инерционного датчика.\n\n![rotation_position.png](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **угла вращения** возвращает **отрицательное** значение в случае вращения гироскопа **против часовой стрелки**.\n\nБлок **угла вращения** возвращает **положительное** значение в случае вращения гироскопа **по часовой стрелке**.\n\nВыберите датчик для использования.\n\n![rotation_position_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_devices.png)\n\nБлок **угла вращения** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![rotation_position_inserted.png](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_inserted.png)\n"},"rotation_position":{"name":"rotation_position","markdown":"# Position of rotation \n\nReports the current rotational position of the selected V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_position/rotation_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of rotation** reports the position of a V5 Rotation sensor in integer numbers for degrees, and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nChoose which V5 Rotation sensor to use.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_position/rotation_position_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether the value is reported in degrees rotated or in turns of the V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_position/rotation_position_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block **position of rotation** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_position_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_position/rotation_position_block4.png)\n"},"rotation_set_position":{"name":"rotation_set_position","markdown":"# Set position \n\nSets a V5 Rotation sensor's current position to a defined value.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set position** block can be used to set a Rotation sensor's position.\n\nThis block is typically used to reset the position of the Rotation sensor when the value is set to 0.\n\nThe **set position** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks as an input.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block3.png)\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to use, then enter the desired position value.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block2.png)\n"},"rotation_velocity":{"name":"rotation_velocity","markdown":"# Velocity of rotation\n\nReports the current velocity of a V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to get values from.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in percent (%), revolutions per minute (rpm) or degrees per second (dps).\n\n![rotation_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block velocity of rotation is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block4.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# Окргулить\n\nОкругляет заданное число до ближайшего целого значения.\n\n![round](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/round/round.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nДесятичные числа будут **округляться** меньшую сторону, если десятичная часть меньше 0.5, и в большую сторону, если десятичная часть больше или равна 0.5.\n\nБлок **округления** может быть использован в блоках с овальными вставками и сам может принимать блоки круглой формы.\n\nБлок **округления** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки. \n\n![round_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере робот проедет три дюйма вперёд после округления 2,7.\n\n![round_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"screen_position":{"name":"screen_position","markdown":"# Положение на экране\n\nСообщает положение последнего зафиксированного касания экрана.\n\n![screen_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/screen_position/screen_position_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **положения на экране** возвращает значения по осям X/Y. Данный блок может быть использован для реализации взаимодействия между контроллером и пользователем.\n\nБлок **положения на экране** работает по оси X в диапазоне **от 0 до 480 Пикселей**.\n\nБлок **положения на экране** работает по оси Y в диапазоне **от 0 до 240 Пикселей**.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/screen_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\nВыберите ось.\n\n![screen_position_value](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/screen_position/screen_position_value.png)\n\nБлок **положения на экране** может работать в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![screen_position_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/screen_position/screen_position_inserted.png)"},"screen_pressed":{"name":"screen_pressed","markdown":"# Нажатие экрана\n\nСообщает о статусе нажатия экрана контроллера.\n\n![screen_pressed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_block.png)\n\n## Как ипользовать?\n\nБлок **нажатия экрана** является логическим и может быть использован с блоком **положение на экране** для определения положения последнего касания на экране.\n\nБлок **нажатия экрана** возвращает **правду**, если экран нажат.\n\nБлок **нажатия экрана** возвращает **ложь**, если экран не нажат.\n\nБлок **нажатия экрана** является логическим и может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![screen_pressed_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# Задать 2D массив\n\nУстанавливает значения двумерного массива.\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПри создании двумерного массива вы можете указать число **строк** и **столбцов**, варьирующиеся в пределах от 1 до 10.\n\nВыберите двумерный массив. Массив может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\nБлок **задания 2D массива** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# Установить элементы списка\n\nЗадаёт значения списка.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nПри создании списка вы можете задать длину списка в диапазоне от 1 до 10 элементов.\n\nВыберите список. Список может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\nБлок **установки элементов списка** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере инициализируются значения списка после чего происходит обращение к элементу номер 3 (90) из списка для установки руки робота нужное положение.\n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# Установить логическую переменную\n\nУстанавливает значение логической переменной.\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите логическую переменную. Логические переменные могут быть переименованы или удалены.\n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\nВыберите логическую переменную.\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\nБлок **установки логической переменной** может быть использован в блоках с шестиугольными вставками.\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# Установить курсор\n\nУстанавливает курсор для печати значений на экранах контроллера или пульта.\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nУстановите значения строки и столбца для вывода значений на экран.\n\nБлок **установки курсора** работает со строками в диапазоне **от 1 до 20**.\n\nБлок **установки курсора** работает со столбцами в диапазоне **от 1 до 80**.\n\nВыберите устройство для использования. Пульт управления должен быть установлен в окне выбора устройств.\n\n![set_cursor_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_cursor/set_cursor_dropdown.png)\n\nБлок **установки курсора** может принимать целые и числовые блоки.\n\n---\n\nКонтроллер V5 позволяет работать с разными размерами шрифтов. Изменение размера шрифта влияет на количество столбцов.\n\n**Размер шрифта на контроллере - Число строк:**\n\n* Extra Small - 20 строк\n* Small - 16 строк\n* Medium - 12 строк (по умолчанию)\n* Large - 8 строк\n* Extra Large - 6 строк\n* Super Large - 4 строки\n\nКонтроллер V5 позволяет работать с разными размерами шрифтов. Изменение размера шрифта влияет на количество столбцов.\n\n**Размер шрифта на контроллере - Число столбцов:**\n\n* Extra Small - 80 столбцов\n* Small - 68 столбцов\n* Medium - 48 столбцов (по умолчанию)\n* Large - 32 столбцов\n* Extra Large - 24 столбцов\n* Super Large - 16 столбцов\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nНа пульте управление недоступно изменение размера шрифта.\n\n**Размер шрифта на пульте управления - Число строк:**\n\n* Standard Font - 3 строки (по умолчанию)\n\n**Размер шрифта на пульте управления - Число столбцов:**\n\n* Standard Font - 20 столбцов (по умолчанию)\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# Установить курс движения\n\nУстанавливает значение курса трансмиссии.\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки курса движения** может быть использован для установки углового положения трансмисии в любой точке при вращении против часовой стрелки, кроме того он может быть использован для установки текущего положения как нулевого.\n\nБлок **установки курса движения** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 359,99 градусов**.\n\nБлок **установки курса движения** может принимать целые и числовые блоки.\n\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# Установка вращения\n\nУстановка угла вращения трансмиссии.\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки вращения** может быть использован для установки положительного или отрицательного значения угла вращения.\n\nБлок **установки вращения** может принимать целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ этом примере робот повернётся в общей сложности на 210 градусов:\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- Повернуть направо (по часовой стрелке) до 120 градусов.\n- Установите текущую позицию вращения в -45 градусов.\n- Поверните направо (по часовой стрелке) на 90 градусов (от -45 до 45 градусов), полагаясь на установленное значение вращения."},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# Установка режима торможения\n\nУстанавливает характер торможения трансмиссии.\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n* **Brake** приведёт к немедленной остановке трансмиссии.\n* **Coast** привёдет к плавному торможению.\n* **Hold** приведёт к удержанию положения приводов трансмиссии после её остановки.\n\n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссии проедет вперёд три секунды после чего остановится с удержанием положени приводов.\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# Установка времени работы\n\nУстанавливает максимальное время работы команд движения трансмисии.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nУстановка максимального времени работы приводит к ограничению выполнения любых других действий, связанных с блоками движения трансмиссии.\n\nНапример, трансмиссия не достигнет конечного положения в случае движения по направлению к стене.\n\nБлок **установки времени работы** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере робот закончит движение по истечении двух секунд, не доехав 24 дюйма. После достижения порога времени трансмиссия начнёт поворот.\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# Set drive velocity\n\nSets the speed of the Drivetrain.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Set drive velocity** will set the speed of the drivetrain, but will not cause the Drivetrain to move. A **drive** block is still required.\n\n**Set drive velocity** reports a range from **-100% to 100%** or **-600rpm to 600rpm**.\n\n**Set drive velocity** will accept a \"rotations per minute\" range based on the Gear Cartridge installed in the V5 Smart Motors used in the Drivetrain.\n\n* Red Cartridge: -100rpm to 100rpm\n* Green Cartridge: -200rpm to 200rpm\n* Blue Cartridge: -600rpm to 600rpm\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's velocity to a negative value will cause the Drivetrain to move in reverse.\n\nSetting a Drivetrain's velocity to 0 will cause the Drivetrain to stop.\n\nThe **set drive velocity** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\nChoose the unit of measure.\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n\n"},"set_fill_color":{"name":"set_fill_color","markdown":"# Установка цвета заливки\n\nЗадаёт цвет заливки форм на экране контроллера.\n\n![set_fill_color_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки цвета заливки**используется для заливки окружностей и прямоугольников на экране контроллера.\n\nВыберите цвет заливки.\n\n![set_fill_color_color](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_color.png)  \n\nЦвет заливки будет использован для всех объектов после объявления блока."},"set_font":{"name":"set_font","markdown":"# Установка шрифта\n\nУстанавливает вид и размер шрифта для печати на экране контроллера текста или чисел.\n\n![set_font_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_font/set_font_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nДоступно два вида шрифтов на контроллере:\n\n* Monospaced (Mono) - все символы одинаковой высоты.\n* Proportional (Prop) - каждый символ зависит от типа ввода.\n\nВыберите тип и размер шрифта.\n\n![set_font_block_font](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_font/set_font_block_font.png)  \n\nБлок **установки шрифта** после объявления влияет на все блоки вывода."},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# Установить курс гироскопа\n\nУстанавливает текущее положение гироскопа/инерционного датчика в качестве курса.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nКурс гироскопа может быть назначен в любом положении при движении против часовой стрелки.\n\nДанный блок обычно используется для установки текущего положения в качестве нулевого.\n\nБлок **установки курса гироскопа** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 359,99** градусов.\n\nБлок **установки курса гироскопа** может принимать положительные десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nВыберите гироскоп для использования и введите желаемое значение.\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# Установка вращения гироскопа.\n\nУстанавливает текущее положение гироскопа/инерционного датчика в качестве вращения.\n\n![setrotation](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВ качестве значения для блока **установки вращения гироскопа** может быть использовано любое положительное (вращение против часовой стрелки) или отрицательное (вращение по часовой стрелке)значение.\n\nБлок **установки вращения гироскопа** может принимать любые положительные или отрицательные десятичные или целые значения.\n\nБлок **установки вращения гироскопа** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nВыберите гироскоп для использования.\n\n![setrotation_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation_devices.png)\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# Замена элементов 2D списка\n\nУстанавливает новое значение для выбранного элемента.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВведите положение элемента (сначала номер строки, затем номер столбца) элемента, который вы бы хотели заменить.\n\nВыберите список. Список может быть удалён или переименован.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\nБлок **замены элементов 2D списка** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# Замена элемента списка\n\nУстанавливает новое значение для выбранного элемента списка.\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите список. Список может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\nБлок **замены элементов списка** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n"},"set_joint_move_speed":{"name":"set_joint_move_speed","markdown":"# Set joint speed\n\nSets the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's joint movements.\n\n![joint_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_joint_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_joint_move_speed/select_joint_speed_arm.png)\n\nChoose the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's joint movements. The default speed is **normal**.\n\n![joint_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_select.png)"},"set_led":{"name":"set_led","markdown":"# Установка LED\n\nВключает или выключает лампочку.\n\n![set_led_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_led/set_led_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите LED для использования.\n\n![set_led_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_led/set_led_block_device.png)\n\nВыберите действие: активен/неактивен.\n\n![set_led_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_led/set_led_block_setting.png)\n\n"},"set_linear_move_speed":{"name":"set_linear_move_speed","markdown":"# Set linear speed\n\nSets the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's linear movements.\n\n![linear_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_linear_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_linear_move_speed/select_linear_speed_arm.png)\n\nChoose the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's linear movements. The default speed is **normal**.\n\n![linear_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_select.png)"},"set_mastering":{"name":"set_mastering","markdown":"# Set mastering\n\nSets the mastering values of the four joints of the V5 Robotic Arm to allow it to be calibrated to the same known location.\n\n![set_mastering_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_mastering/set_mastering_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nInput the mastering values from the V5 Brain to the **set mastering** block. \n\nThe passable threshold values for the joints are as follows:\n\n* Joint 1: 1800 - 2200\n* Joint 2: 1900 - 2400\n* Joint 3: 1400 - 1800\n* Joint 4: 200 - 650\n\n![mastering_values](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_mastering/mastering_values.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_mastering_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_mastering/select_mastering_arm.png)\n\nThe **set mastering** block accepts integers and numeric blocks.\n\n![mastering_input](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_mastering/mastering_input.png)"},"set_motor_controller_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_controller_velocity","markdown":"# Установка скорости контроллера привода\n\nУстанавливает скорость привода Motor 393, подключённого к контроллеру привода.\n\n![set_motor_controller_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_velocity_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки скорости контроллера привода** работает в диапазоне **от -100 до 100%**.\n\nУстановка отрицательной скорости меняет направление движения выходного вала привода.\n\nУстановка 0 остановит выбранный привод.\n\nВыберите привод Motor 393 для использования.\n\n![set_motor_controller_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_motor.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# Установка положения привода\n\nУстанавливает энкодер привода в выбранное положение.\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки положения привода** может быть использован для установки привода в любое положение. \n\nОбычно данный блок используется для установки значения энкодера в ноль.\n\nВыберите привод энкодера.\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\nВыберите единицу измерения в градусах или оборотах.\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# Установка режима торможения\n\nУстанавливает характер торможения привода.\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\n* **Brake** приведёт к немедленной остановке привода.\n* **Coast** привёдет к плавному торможению привода.\n* **Hold** приведёт к удержанию положения привода после его остановки.\n\nБлок **установки режима торможения** повлияет на режим торможения на протяжении всей программы.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\nВыберите настройки привода после остановки.\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере привод руки изменит провернётся на 90 градусов после чего будет удерживать руку в данном положении. \n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# Установка времени работы\n\nУстанавливает максимальное время работы команд движения привода.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nУстановка максимального времени работы приводит к ограничению выполнения любых других действий, связанных с блоками движения привода.\n\nИспользование блока ограничения времени работы позволяет избежать непредвиденных ситуаций, связанных, например, с достижением максимального угла работы одной из степеней свободы робота.\n\nБлок **установки времени работы** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере блок установки положения привода будет остановлен через две секунды и не достигнет положения 270 градусов. После двух секунд привод на схвате будет установлен в положение ноль.\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# Установка момента привода\n\nУстанавливает максимальный момент привода.\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки момента привода** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 100%**.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\nБлок **установки момента привода** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере привод схвата робота повернётся на 40 градусов с двадцатипроцентным (20%) моментом. Это позволит захватить объект без нанесения ущерба из-за слишком большой силы сжатия.\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# Установка скорости привода\n\nУстанавливает скорость привода.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки скорости привода** работает в диапазонах **от -100 до 100%** или **от -600 до 600 об/мин**.\n\nДиапазон значений блока **установки скорости привода** зависит от типа картриджей, установленных в приводах трансмиссии.\n\n* Красный картридж: -100 до 100 об/мин\n* Зелёный картридж: -200 до 200 об/мин\n* Синий картридж: -600 до 600 об/мин\n\nУстановка отрицательного значения изменит направление движения на противоположное.\n\nУстановка скорости, равной 0, приведёт к остановке привода.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\nЕдиницы измерения скорости: проценты (%) или обороты в минуту (об/мин).\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере рука поднимается до 90 градусов на скорости 25%.\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_pen_color":{"name":"set_pen_color","markdown":"# Set pen color\n\nSets the color of lines drawn on the V5 Brain's screen or the values printed to the Print Console.\n\n![set_pen_color_block_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_block_with_console.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set pen color** block is used to set the color of lines, pixels, and text drawn on the V5 Brain's screen or the values printed to the Print Console. \n\n**Set pen color** will also be used to set the color the outline of circles and rectangles drawn on the V5 Brain's screen.\n\nChoose a pen color. \n\n![set_pen_color_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_dropdown_with_console.png)  \n\nThe pen color will be used for any future objects drawn on the V5 Brain's screen or any values printed to the Print Console until otherwise changed.\n\nWhen a program is stopped, the text color of the Print Console is reset to black."},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# Set print precision\n\nSets the number of digits that appear after the decimal point when printing reporter blocks on the Print Console, V5 Brain or Controller screen.\n\n![print_precision](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose the level of precision that inserted reporter blocks will be printed to the Print Console or the screen.\n\n* Ones (1) (Default)\n* Tenths (0.1)\n* Hundredths (0.01)\n* Thousandths (0.001)\n* All Digits (0.000001)\n\nReporter blocks printed to the Print Console or screen will round to the nearest level of precision. For example, 1.67 will be printed as 2 at ones precision and 1.7 at tenths precision.\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)\n\nChoose which device to use. V5 Controllers will only appear if they are added in the Devices window.\n\n![print_precision_dropdown_with_console](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_print_precision/print_precision_dropdown_with_console.png)"},"set_shaft_encoder_position":{"name":"set_shaft_encoder_position","markdown":"# Установка положения оптического энкодера\n\nУстанавливает значение оптического энкодера в указанное положение.\n\n![set_encoder_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки положения оптического энкодера** может быть использован для установки энкодера в любое положение.\n\nОбычно, блок **установки положения оптического энкодера** используется для установки текущего положения в качестве нулевого.\n\nВыберите устройство и желаемое значение.\n\n![set_encoder_position_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_motor.png)\n\n"},"set_tool":{"name":"set_tool","markdown":"# Set tool\n\nSets the end effector or the end-of-arm tooling (EOAT) on the V5 Robotic Arm.\n\n![set_tool_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_tool/set_tool_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe end effector on the V5 Robotic Arm can be none (no attachment), an electromagnet, or a marker. \n\n![set_marker](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_tool/set_marker.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_tool_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_tool/select_tool_arm.png)\n\nChoose the tool on your V5 Robotic Arm. The default is set to **none**.\n\n![choose_tool](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_tool/choose_tool.png)"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# Установить скорость поворота\n\nУстанавливает скорость поворота трансмиссии.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установки скорости поворота** задаёт скорость поворота трансмиссии, но не запускает движение трансмиссии. Для запуска движения требуется блок **поворота**.\n\n**Скорость поворота** может быть задана в диапазоне **от 0% до 100%** или **от -600 до 600 об/мин**.\n\nДиапазон значений блока **установки скорости поворота** зависит от типа картриджей, установленных в приводах трансмиссии.\n\n* Красный картридж: -100 до 100 об/мин\n* Зелёный картридж: -200 до 200 об/мин\n* Синий картридж: -600 до 600 об/мин\n\nОтрицательное значение скорости поворота меняет направление движения на противоположное.\n\nУстановка скорости поворота в ноль останавливает движение трансмиссии.\n\nБлок **установки скорости поворота** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссия будет медленно поворачивать со скоростью 25% налево.\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# Установка значения переменной\n\nЗадаёт указанное значение переменной.\n\n![set_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите переменную. Переменные могут быть переименованы или удалены.\n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\nБлок **установки переменных** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# Установить индекс объекта\n\nНазначает индекс объекту, который в дальнейшем мы бы хотели исследовать подробнее.\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **числа объектов** может быть использован перед блоком **установки индекса объекта** для определения числа объектов.\n\nВыберите камеру для использования.\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\nБлок **установки индекса объекта** может принимать целые или числовые блоки.\n\n\n\n"},"set_width":{"name":"set_width","markdown":"# Установка ширины линии\n\nУстанавливает ширину линий разных форм на экране контроллера.\n\n![set_width_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_width/set_width_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **установка ширины линии** устанавливает ширину линий для окружностей и прямоугольников.\n\nБлок **установка ширины линии** принимает целые, десятичные или числовые блоки.\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/set_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"setangle":{"name":"setangle","markdown":"# Set angle\n\nSets the angle of the tool plate before the next [Linear move] or [Joint move] block is executed.\n\n![set_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/setangle/set_angle_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set angle** block sets the tool plate to be tilted at an angle either **up** or **down** before the next [Linear move] or [Joint move] block in a project. \n\nNote that the **set angle** block sets the angle for all future [Linear move] and [Joint move] blocks, unless it is set otherwise.\n\n![tool_plate](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/setangle/tool_plate.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_set_angle_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/setangle/select_set_angle_arm.png)\n\nChoose the angle of the tool plate. The default is set to **up**.\n\n* The tool plate will be **horizontal** when it is set to **down**. \n* The tool plate will be **vertical** when it is set to **up**. \n\n![select_angle](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/setangle/select_angle.png)\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the tool plate will begin to tilt once the [Joint move] block is executed and complete its tilting movement before the [Linear move] block.\n\n![set_angle_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/setangle/set_angle_example.png)"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# Длина массива\n\nВозвращает число элементов списка. \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите список. Список может быть переименован или удалён.\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\nБлок **длины массива** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# Снимок\n\nПолучает снимок с камеры.\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **снимка** получает изображение с выбранной камеры для обработки и анализа объектов.\n\nОчевидно, что блок **снимка** необходимо использовать перед вызовом других блоков для камеры.\n\nВыберите камеру для использования.\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\nВыберите объект для анализа. Получение объекта осуществляется в меню настройки камеры.\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# Вращать\n\nЗапускает привод VEX V5.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **вращения** запускает привод до вызова блока остановки привода.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\nВыберите направление вращения. Имена направлений вращения могут быть изменены в настройках устройства.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# Повернуть на\n\nЗапускает привод для поворота на определённое расстояние.\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **поворота на** запускает привод для движения на определённое расстояние от текущего положения.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\nВыберите направление вращения. Имена направлений вращения могут быть изменены в настройках устройства.\n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\nБлок Блок **поворота на** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nВыберите единицу измерения в градусах или оборотах.\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\nПо умолчанию, другие блоки будут ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота на**.\n\nНажатием на стрелку можно вызвать **и не ждать**. Данная команда позволяет не ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота на** для выполнения следующих.\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_motor_controller":{"name":"spin_motor_controller","markdown":"# Вращение привода через контроллер привода\n\nЗапуск вращения привода посредством контроллера привода.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **вращения** привода Motor 393 запускает привод до момента вызова команды остановки.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_motor.png)\n\nВыберите направление вращения привода. Имя направления вращения может быть изменено в окне настройки устройств.\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_direction.png)"},"spin_servo":{"name":"spin_servo","markdown":"# Вращение сервопривода\n\nЗапуск вращения сервопривода до указанного положения.\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_servo/servo_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **вращения сервопривода** работает в диапазоне *от 0 до 180 градусов**.\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_servo/servo_port.png)\n\n"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# Поворот в положение\n\nПоворачивает привод в указанное положение.\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **поворота в положение** указывает приводу на поворот в необходимое положение. Основываясь на текущем положении привода, блок **поворота в положение** определит направление вращения.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\nБлок **поворота в положение** может принимать деятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nВыберите единицу измерения в градусах или оборотах.\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\nПо умолчанию, другие блоки будут ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота в положение**.\n\nНажатием на стрелку можно вызвать **и не ждать**. Данная команда позволяет не ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота в положение** для выполнения следующих.\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# Остановка движения\n\nОстанавливает трансмиссию.\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **остановки движения** останавливает движение трансмиссии при использовании блока. Дополнительно можно назначить тип торможения трансмиссии.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссия остановится черз три секунды.\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# Остановить привод\n\nОстанавливает привод.\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите привод, который необходимо остановить.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примерепривод будет работать три секунды перед остановкой.\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor_controller":{"name":"stop_motor_controller","markdown":"# Stop motor controller\n\nStops a Motor 393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n![stop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Motor 393 to stop.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_motor.png)\n\nThis example will spin a Motor 393 forward for 3 seconds before stopping.\n\n![stop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_example.png)"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# Вычитание\n\nПолучает разность между первым и вторым значениями.\n\n![subtract](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **вычитания** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\nБлок **вычитания** может быть использован в блоках с овальными вставками, и сам может использовать овальные блоки.\n\nВычитание двух чисел.\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\nВычитание из переменной числа.\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\nВычитание значений датчиков и устройств.\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"temperature_of_motor":{"name":"temperature_of_motor","markdown":"# Температура привода\n\nСообщает о текущей температуре привода.\n\n![temp_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nИспользование блока **температуры привода** позволяет предотвратить излишний перегрев привода.\n\nБлок **температуры привода** работает в диапазоне **от 0 до 100%**.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![temp_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nБлок **температуры привода** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками. \n\n![temp_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# Значение таймера\n\nВозвращает текущее значение таймера в секундах.\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nТаймер запускается в начале программы, и его значение является десятичным числом.\n\nБлок **значение таймера** используется в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n"},"torque_of_motor":{"name":"torque_of_motor","markdown":"# Момент привода\n\nСообщает о текущем значении момента привода.\n\n![motor_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/torque_of_motor/motor_torque.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **момента привода** работает в диапазонах **от 0.0 до 18.6 InLB** или **от 0.0 до 2.1 Нм**.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![motor_torque_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_device.png)\n\nВыберите единицу измерения момента в InLB или ньютонов на метр (Нм).\n\n![motor_torque_units](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_units.png)\n\nБлок **момента привода** может быть использован внутри блоков с круглыми вставками.\n\n![motor_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_inserted.png)"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# Поворот\n\nБесконечно поворачивает трансмиссию.\n\n![turn_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **поворота** будет поворачивать трансмиссию бесконечно, пока не будет использован другой блок для остановки.\n\nВыберите направление поворота трансмиссии.\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# Поворот на\n\nПоворачивает трансмиссию на определённую градусную меру.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите направление поворота трансмиссии.\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\nУстановите угол поворота трансмиссии в градусах или количество оборотов.\n\nБлок **поворот на** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\nПо умолчанию, другие блоки будут ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота на**.\n\nНажатием на стрелку можно вызвать **и не ждать**. Данная команда позволяет не ждать окончания выполнения блока **поворота на** для выполнения следующих.\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# Turn to heading\n\nTurns a Drivetrain to a specific heading, when using the Gyro sensor.\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **turn to heading** block can be used to turn the Drivetrain to any given clockwise heading.\n\nBased on the current heading of the Gyro, **turn to heading** will determine which direction to turn.\n\n**Turn to heading** accepts a range of **0.00 to 359.99** degrees.\n\nThe **turn to heading** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will cause the Drivetrain to make four turns: \n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- Right to 45 degrees\n- Right to 90 degrees\n- Right to 270 degrees\n- Left to 180 degrees\n\nBy default, other blocks will **wait** until the Drivetrain is done turning.\n\nYou can select the arrow to expand **and don't wait** - this will cause other blocks to continue running while the Drivetrain turns.\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# Повернуть к вращению\n\nПоворот трансмиссии на определённый угол, установленный с помощью гироскопа/инерционного датчика.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **поворота к вращению** может быть использован для поворота по часовой стрелке (положительного поворота) и против часовой стрелки (отрицательного поворота).\n\nНаправление поворота трансмиссии определяется текущим значением **вращения**.\n\nБлок **поворота к вращению** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n## Пример\n\nВ данном примере трансмиссия сделает четыре поворота: \n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- Направо (по часовой стрелке) до 90 градусов\n- Направо (по часовой стрелке) до 180 градусов\n- Налево (против часовой стрелке) до -45 градусов\n- Направо (по часовой стрелке) до 0 градусов\n\nПо умолчанию, другие блоки будут **ждать** окончания поворота трансмисии.\n\nВы можете установить значение **и не ждать** для выполнения других действий параллельно с поворотом.\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# Переменная\n\nЗадаёт числовое значение переменной.\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/variable/variable.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлоки **переменных** используются для присваивания числового значения переменной. Используйте блок **задания переменной** для обновления значения переменной.\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\nБлок **переменной** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\nПеременные создаются нажатием кнопки **создание переменных**.\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# Скорость привода\n\nВозвращает текущую скорость привода.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nДиапазон значений блока **установки скорости привода** зависит от типа картриджей, установленных в приводах трансмиссии.\n\n* Красный картридж: -100 до 100 об/мин\n* Зелёный картридж: -200 до 200 об/мин\n* Синий картридж: -600 до 600 об/мин\n\nУстановка отрицательного значения изменит направление движения на противоположное.\n\nУстановка скорости, равной 0, приведёт к остановке привода.\n\nВыберите привод для использования.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\nЕдиницы измерения скорости: проценты (%) или обороты в минуту (об/мин).\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\nБлок **скорости привода** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"velocity_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"velocity_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# Скорость на оптическом энкодере\n\nСообщает о текущем значении скорости на оптическом энкодере.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **скорости на оптическом энкодере** сообщает значения в единицах измерения градусов в секунду (град/сек) или оборотах в минуту (об/мин).\n\nВыберите датчик для использования.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_motor.png)\n\nВыберите единицы измерения.\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_unit.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# Информация об объекте\n\nСообщает параметры найденного объекта.\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nДля использования блока **информации об объекте** необходимо проделать следующие шаги:\n\n1. Настройте камеру в окне настройки камеры.\n2. Используйте блок **снимка** для получения изображения с камеры.\n3. Используйте  блок **существования объекта** для определения наличия объекта/цвета.\n\nПосле обнаружения объекта, вы можете использовать блок **информации об объекте** для изучения его параметров.\n\n* Используйте блок **установки индекса объекта** для получения информации о нём. По умолчанию, определяются параметры самого крупного объекта.\n* Используйте блок **количества объектов** для определения количества объектов нужных сигнатуры/цвета перед камерой.\n* Используйте блок **информации об объекте** для плучения параметров объекта.\n\nВыберите камеру для использования.\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\nВыберите параметр, который необходимо получить:\n\n* Width - ширина объекта в пикселях. Возвращает значение **от 2 до 316 пикселей**.\n* Height - высота объекта в пикселях. Возвращает значение **от 2 до 212 пикселей**.\n* CenterX - сообщает координату X центра объекта. Возвращает значение **от 0 до 315 пикселей**.\n* CenterY - сообщает координату Y центра объекта. Возвращает значение **от 0 до 211 пикселей**.\n* Angle - угол наклона объекта. Возвращает значения **от 0 до 180 градусов**.\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\nБлок **информации об объекте** может быть использован в блоках с круглыми вставками.\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# Ждать\n\nЖдёт указанное время перед переходом к следующим блокам.\n\n![wait](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/wait/wait.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите требуемое значение времени в блоке **ждать**.\n\nБлок **ждать** может принимать десятичные, целые или числовые блоки.\n\n![wait_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# Ждать пока\n\nЖдёт изменения значения логического блока внутри на **правду**.\n\n![wait_until](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлок **ждать пока** непрерывно проверяет условие внутри, пока значение внутри блока не станет **правдой**.\n\nБлок **ждать пока** может принимать шестиугольные блоки.\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n"},"when_autonomous":{"name":"when_autonomous","markdown":"# Автономный режим\n\nЗапускает автономный режим работы при получении соответствующего сигнала от электронной системы управления полем.\n\n![when_autonomous](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_autonomous/when_autonomous.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nЛюбые блоки, прикрепленные к блоку **автономного режима**, запускаются при получении сигнала от системы управления полем.\n\nПользователь может иметь до 50 блоков **автономного режима**."},"when_brain_screen":{"name":"when_brain_screen","markdown":"# Касание экрана\n\nЗапускает прикреплённые блоки при нажатии или отжатии экрана контроллера.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nДанный блок **касания экрана** позволяет отрабатывать взаимодействие между пользователем и роботом.\n\nИспользование дополнительного блока **положение на экране** позволит разнообразить взаимодействие между пользователем и роботом.\n\nВыберите вид взаимодействия - **нажать** или **отпустить**.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed_condition.png)"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# Когда получил сообщение\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков после получения нужного сообщения.\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите ожидаемое сообщение. Кроме того, вы можете создать новой сообщение.\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\nБлок **получения сообщения** получает сообщения только от блоков **передачи сообщения** или **передачи сообщения и ожидания**."},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# Когда датчик касания\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков в случае нажатия/отжатия датчика касания.\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите датчик касания для использования.\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\nВыберите действие: нажат или отжат.\n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# Когда ось пульта управления\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков в случае движения джойстика на пульте управления.\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите пульт управления.\n\n![when_controller_axis_device](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_device.png)\n\nВыберите ось джойстика на пульте управления.\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# Когда кнопка на пульте управления\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков в случае нажатия/отжатия кнопки на пульте управления.\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите пульт управления.\n\n![when_controller_button_controller](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_controller.png)\n\nВыберите пульт управления для использования.\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\nВыберите действие над кнопкой: нажата или отжата.\n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_driver":{"name":"when_driver","markdown":"# Управляемый режим\n\nЗапускает управляемый режим при получении соответствующего сигнала от системы управления полем.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_driver/when_driver.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nБлоки, прикреплённые к блоку **управляемый режим**, запускаются после подачи сигнала от системы управления полем.\n\nРекомендуется использовать блок **бесконечный цикл** для непрерывного запуска команд управления с пульта.\n\nБлок **управляемого режима** может быть использован до 50 раз в программе."},"when_limit":{"name":"when_limit","markdown":"# Датчик Limit Switch\n\nЗапускает стэк блоков при активации датчика Limit Switch.\n\n![when_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_limit/when_limit.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nВыберите датчик для использования.\n\n![when_limit_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_limit/when_limit_select.png)\n\nВыберите действие: **нажат** или **отжат**.\n\n![when_limit_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_limit/when_limit_condition.png)\n"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# When started\n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the project is started.\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nA **when started** event will be run when the project is started from the V5 Brain's menu or from the **run** button in VEXcode V5.\n\nAll new projects will automatically include a **when started** block. Projects can support up to 50 **when started** blocks.\n\n**When started** will also act as the \"pre-autonomous\" mode's stack for a VRC Competition project.\n\n"},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# Когда таймер\n\nЗапускает стэк из блоков в случае, если текущее значение таймера больше установленного.\n\n![when_timer](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nТаймер контроллера запускается автоматически в начале каждой программы.\n\nВыберите величину времени. Блок **когда таймер** начнёт работы, если текущее значение таймера больше установленного.\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\nБлок **когда таймер** может принимать десятичные и целые значения.\n\nБлок **когда таймер** не может принимать другие блоки."},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# Пока\n\n'C' подобный блок цикла работает до тех пор, пока условие **правда**.\n\n![while](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/while/while.png)\n\n## Как использовать?\n\nЦикл **пока** проверяет значение условия на каждой итерации цикла.\n\nЕсли условие **правда**, то действия внутри цикла **пока** будут запущены.\n\nЕсли условие **ложь**, то действия внутри цикла **пока** будут пропущены.\n\n'C' подобный блок цикла **пока** может принимать в качестве условия шестиугольные блоки.\n\n![while_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/ru/while/while_inserted.png)"}}},"zh-CN":{"blocks":{"acceleration_of":{"name":"acceleration_of","markdown":"# 加速度\n\n报告加速计单轴方向的加速度值。\n\n![acceleration_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n根据加速计上跳线块的设置，**加速度**报告范围为 **-2.0 G to 2.0 G** 或 **-6.0 G to 6.0 G**。\n\n选择使用哪一个加速计。\n\n![acceleration_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_device.png)\n\n**加速度**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![acceleration_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/acceleration_of/acceleration_of_inserted.png)"},"activate_emergency_stop":{"name":"activate_emergency_stop","markdown":"# Activate emergency stop\n\nActivates the emergency stop (or E-stop) button for the V5 Robotic Arm.\n\n![estop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/activate_emergency_stop/estop_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe emergency stop button in the Workcell will shut off any V5 Smart Motors and Sensors connected to the V5 Brain. \n\n![estop_robot](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/activate_emergency_stop/estop_robot.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_estop_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/activate_emergency_stop/select_estop_arm.png)\n\nThe **activate emergency stop** block is often used with the When bumper block from the Events category. This ensures that all V5 Smart Motors and Sensors connected to the V5 Brain will shut off once the Bumper Switch (E-stop) is pressed.\n![estop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/activate_emergency_stop/estop_example.png)"},"add":{"name":"add","markdown":"# 加法\n\n把任意两个值加起来，并报告总和。\n\n![add](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/add/add.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**加法**可接受小数、整数或数字指令块。\n\n**加法**指令块可被用在接受圆形空白的指令块中，也可以接受其他圆形指令块。 \n\n\n两个数字相加。\n\n![add_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/add/add_numbers.png)\n\n加法中的加数可以为变量。\n\n![add_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/add/add_variables.png)  \n\n加法中的加数可以为传感器或设备值。\n\n![add_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/add/add_sensors.png)\n\n"},"and":{"name":"and","markdown":"# 与\n\n报告是否两个布尔条件均为真值。\n\n![and](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/and/and.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**与**指令块在两个条件均为**真**时，报告**真**值。\n\n**与**指令块在一个（或两个）条件为**假**时，报告**假**值。\n\n**与**指令块报告**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白的指令块中。\n\n![and_shape](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/and/and_shape.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将检验V5遥控器的两个按键是否同时被按下。\n\n![and_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/and/and_sensors.png)\n\n当**遥控器1 X 按键**和**遥控器1 A 按键**同时被按下时，**与**指令块将返回**真**值。\n\n当遥控器上的一个（或两个）按键未被按下时，**与**指令块将返回**假**值。\n\n![and_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/and/and_truth.png)"},"angle_of":{"name":"angle_of","markdown":"# 角度\n\n返回电位计的角度值。\n\n![angle_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/angle_of/angle_of_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**角度**报告范围为**0% to 100%** 或 **0.0 to 250.0 度**。\n\n选择使用哪一个电位计。\n\n![angle_of_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/angle_of/angle_of_device.png)\n\n选择**角度**单位为百分比或度。\n\n![angle_of_block_parameters](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/angle_of/angle_of_parameters.png)\n\n**角度**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![angle_of_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/angle_of/angle_of_inserted.png)\n"},"battery_current":{"name":"battery_current","markdown":"# 电池电流\n\n报告V5主控器电池电流值。\n\n![battery_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/battery_current/battery_current_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电池电流**报告范围为**0.0 amps to 20.0 amps**。\n\n**电池电流**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![battery_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/battery_current/battery_current_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"battery_level":{"name":"battery_level","markdown":"# 电量水平\n\n报告V5主控器电池的电量水平。\n\n![battery_capacity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/battery_level/battery_capacity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电量水平** 报告范围为 **0% 到 100%**。\n\n**电量水平** 指令块可用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![battery_capacity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/battery_level/battery_capacity_inserted.png)"},"battery_voltage":{"name":"battery_voltage","markdown":"# 电池电压\n\n报告V5主控器电池电压。\n\n![battery_voltage_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电池电压**报告范围为**10.0 v to 14.4 v**。\n\n**电池电压** 指令块可用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![battery_voltage_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/battery_voltage/battery_voltage_inserted.png)\n"},"boolean_variable":{"name":"boolean_variable","markdown":"# 布尔变量\n\n报告一个布尔变量的值。\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/boolean_variable/boolean_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**布尔变量**指令块用于报告存储在该变量内的一个**真**或**假**值。使用**设定布尔变量**指令块来设定或更新一个布尔变量的值。\n\n![boolean_set_value](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/boolean_variable/boolean_set_value.png)\n\n**布尔变量**指令块报告一个**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白的指令块中。\n\n![boolean_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/boolean_variable/boolean_inserted.png)\n\n布尔变量通过**定义一个布尔变量**按钮生成。\n\n![make_boolean_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/boolean_variable/boolean_button.png)  \n"},"break":{"name":"break","markdown":"# 退出循环\n\n直接退出一个正在重复的循环。\n\n![break](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/break/break.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当添加到C型控制指令块时，**退出循环**指令块将退出它当前所在的循环。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示底盘正向驱动，并检验V5主控器屏幕是否被按下。 \n\n如果屏幕被**按下**，**退出循环**指令块将退出永续循环并且底盘停止。\n\n![break_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/break/break_example.png)"},"brightness_of":{"name":"brightness_of","markdown":"# 亮度百分比\n\n报告光感器检测到的光线亮度。\n\n![brightness_of](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/brightness_of/brightness_of_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**亮度百分比**报告范围为**0% 到 100%**。\n\n选择使用哪一个光感器。\n\n![brightness_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/brightness_of/brightness_of_color.png)\n\n**亮度百分比**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![brightness_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/brightness_of/brightness_of_inserted.png)\n\n"},"broadcast":{"name":"broadcast","markdown":"# 广播\n\n广播一个消息来激活任何以**当我收到**指令块开始且正在监听广播消息的指令段。\n\n![broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/broadcast/broadcast.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n发送**广播**的指令段和收到广播消息的指令段同步运行。\n\n选择**广播**哪一条消息，也可以生成一条新消息。\n\n![broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/broadcast/broadcast_select.png)"},"broadcast_and_wait":{"name":"broadcast_and_wait","markdown":"# 广播并等待\n\n广播一个消息来激活任何以**当我收到**指令块开始且正在监听广播消息的指令段，同时暂停后续的指令段。\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n发送**广播**的指令段将暂停直到收到广播消息的指令段运行完成。\n\n选择**广播**哪一条消息，也可以生成一条新消息。\n\n![broadcast_and_wait_event_option](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/broadcast_and_wait/broadcast_and_wait_event_option.png)"},"calibrate_gyro":{"name":"calibrate_gyro","markdown":"# 校准\n\n校准陀螺仪/惯性传感器用于减小由陀螺仪/惯性传感器产生的漂移值。\n\n![calibrate_gyro_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_block.png)\n\n即使传感器物理上没有移动，陀螺仪/惯性传感器错误检测运动时会产生漂移。\n\n## 如何应用\n\n在校准过程中陀螺仪/惯性传感器必须保持静止。校准过程大约需要2秒钟完成。\n\n选择使用哪一个陀螺仪/惯性传感器。\n\n![calibrate_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/calibrate_gyro/calibrate_gyro_gyro.png)"},"change_variable":{"name":"change_variable","markdown":"# 修改变量\n\n根据指定的值修改变量。\n\n![change_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/change_variable/change_variable.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个变量 - 被选择的变量也可以重命名或者删除。\n\n![change_variable_options](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/change_variable/change_variable_options.png)\n\n**修改变量**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![change_variable_value](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/change_variable/change_variable_value.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示每**重复循环**循环一次，设定底盘速度的变量值将增加10。\n\n![change_variable_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/change_variable/change_variable_example2.png)"},"clear_all_rows":{"name":"clear_all_rows","markdown":"# 清空所有行\n\n清空V5主控器或遥控器整个屏幕。\n\n![clear_all_rows](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**清空所有行**不会重置主控器的屏幕光标。使用**设定光标**指令块重置主控器的屏幕光标到指定的位置。\n\n选择使用哪一个设备。V5遥控器只有被添加到设备窗口以后才会显示。\n\n![clear_all_rows_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/clear_all_rows/clear_all_rows_dropdown.png)"},"clear_row":{"name":"clear_row","markdown":"# 清空行\n\n清空V5主控器或遥控器屏幕其中一行。\n\n![clear_row](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/clear_row/clear_row.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**清空行**指令块可接受**1 - 20**之间的整数或数字指令块，来设定清空哪一行。\n\n选择使用哪一个设备。V5遥控器只有被添加到设备窗口以后才会显示。\n\n![clear_row_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/clear_row/clear_row_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nV5主控器允许改变屏幕打印的字体大小，更改字体将会影响V5主控器屏幕可用的行数。\n\n**V5主控器字体大小 - 行数：**\n\n* 加小号 - 20行\n* 小号 - 16行\n* 中号 - 12 行（默认）\n* 大号 - 8 行\n* 加大号 - 6 行\n* 特大号 - 4 行\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/clear_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\nV5遥控器不允许改变屏幕打印的字体大小。\n\n**V5遥控器字体大小 - 行数：**\n\n* 标准字体 - 3 行（默认 ）\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/clear_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n"},"comment":{"name":"comment","markdown":"# 备注\n\n允许程序员编写信息来帮助描述他们的程序。\n\n![comment_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/comment/comment_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n专业的程序员全程使用备注来帮助其他人理解他们的代码。备注同样有助于故障定位和合作。 \n\n首先，通过选择透明方块删除现有文本，然后，输入新文本，从而实现添加文本到**备注**指令块。\n\n![comment_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/comment/comment_example3.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n备注不改变程序或它周围的指令块。\n\n![comment_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/comment/comment_example2.png)\n\n"},"controller_is_enabled":{"name":"controller_is_enabled","markdown":"# 遥控器启用\n\n启用或停用设备菜单进行的遥控器配置。\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/controller_is_enabled/controller_block.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n通过下拉菜单来选择启用或停用遥控器已配置的动作。默认情况下，在每个程序中遥控器均为启用状态。\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/controller_is_enabled/controller_enable_disable.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n该示例中，配置的动作是通过在设备窗口下，遥控器配置窗口来设置的机器人底盘动作。\n\n![configured_action](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/controller_is_enabled/configured_action.png)\n\n该示例中，当程序开始时已配置的遥控器将被停用。\n\n然后，机器人将向前运动6英寸。\n\n最后，**遥控器启用**指令块将启用遥控器从而恢复遥控动作。\n\n![controllerDisable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/controller_is_enabled/controller_example.png)\n"},"controller_play_rumble":{"name":"controller_play_rumble","markdown":"# 遥控器播放振动\n\n在V5遥控器上生成振动效果。\n\n![controller_play_rumble](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**遥控器播放振动**功能使用V5遥控器中的振动电机来提供反馈。\n\n选择使用哪种模式。\n\n![controller_play_rumble_pattern](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_pattern.png)\n\n选择使用哪一个V5遥控器。\n\n![controller_play_rumble_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/controller_play_rumble/controller_play_rumble_device.png)\n\n\n"},"current_of_motor":{"name":"current_of_motor","markdown":"# 电机电流\n\n报告V5智能电机当前使用的功率安培值（amps）.\n\n![current_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机电流**报告范围为**0.0  到 2.5 amps**。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![current_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\n**电机电流**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![current_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/current_of_motor/current_of_motor_inserted.png)\n"},"cursor_column":{"name":"cursor_column","markdown":"# 光标列数\n\n报告V5主控器或遥控器屏幕光标位置的列数。\n\n![cursor_column_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_column/cursor_column_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**光标列数**报告范围为**1 到 80**。\n\n**光标列数**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![cursor_column_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_column/cursor_column_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nV5主控器允许改变屏幕打印的字体大小，更改字体将会影响V5主控器屏幕可用的列数。\n\n**V5主控器字体大小 - 列数：**\n\n* 加小号 - 80 列\n* 小号 - 68 列\n* 中号 - 48 列 （默认）\n* 大号 - 32 列\n* 加大号 - 24 列\n* 特大号 - 16 列\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_column/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nV5遥控器不允许改变屏幕打印的字体大小。\n\n**V5遥控器字体大小 - 列数：**\n\n* 标准字体 - 20 列（默认）\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_column/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"cursor_row":{"name":"cursor_row","markdown":"# 光标行数 \n\n报告V5主控器或遥控器屏幕光标位置的行数。\n\n![cursor_row_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_row/cursor_row_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**光标行数**报告范围为**1 到 20**。\n\n**光标行数**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![cursor_row_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_row/cursor_row_inserted.png)\n\n---\n\nV5主控器允许改变屏幕打印的字体大小，更改字体将会影响V5主控器屏幕可用的行数。\n\n**V5主控器字体大小 - 行数：**\n\n* 加小号 - 20行\n* 小号 - 16行\n* 中号 - 12 行（默认）\n* 大号 - 8 行\n* 加大号 - 6 行\n* 特大号 - 4 行\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\nV5遥控器不允许改变屏幕打印的字体大小\n\n**V5遥控器字体大小 - 行数：**\n\n* 标准字体 - 3 行（默认 ）\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/cursor_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"distance_found_object":{"name":"distance_found_object","markdown":"# Distance object found\n\nReports if the Distance sensor sees an object within its field of view.\n\n![distance_found_object_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block1.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Distance object found** reports true when the Distance sensor sees an object or surface within its field of view.\n\n**Distance object found** reports false when the Distance sensor does not detect an object or surface.\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_found_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block2.png)\n\n\nThe **distance object found** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![distance_found_object_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_found_object/distance_found_object_block3.png)\n"},"distance_from":{"name":"distance_from","markdown":"# 距离\n\n报告超声波测距仪最近物体的距离值。\n\n![distance_from_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_from/distance_from_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**距离**报告范围为**30毫米 到 3000毫米** 或 **2英寸 到 115英寸**。\n\n选择使用哪一个超声波测距仪。\n\n![distance_from_distance](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_from/distance_from_distance.png)\n\n选择**距离**报告单位为英寸或毫米。\n\n![distance_from_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_from/distance_from_unit.png)\n\n**距离**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![distance_from_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_from/distance_from_inserted.png)\n"},"distance_object_distance":{"name":"distance_object_distance","markdown":"# Object distance\n\nReports the distance of the nearest object from the Distance sensor.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object distance** reports a range from **20mm to 2000mm**.\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether **object distance** is reported in inches or millimeters. \n\n![distance_object_distance_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block **object distance** is used inside blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_object_distance_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_distance/distance_object_distance_block4.png)\n"},"distance_object_size":{"name":"distance_object_size","markdown":"# Object size is\n\nReports if the Distance Sensor detects the specified object size.  \n\n![distance_object_size_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe sensor determines the size of the object detected (none, small, medium, large) based on the amount of light reflected and returned to the sensor.\n\nChoose a Distance Sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_size_block1](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block1.png)\n\nChoose which size of the object you want the sensor to check for.\n\n![distance_object_size_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block2.png)\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **true** when the Distance Sensor detects the specified size.\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **false** if it doesn't detect the specified size.\n\nThe **Object size is** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![distance_object_size_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_size/distance_object_size_block3.png)\n"},"distance_object_velocity":{"name":"distance_object_velocity","markdown":"# Object velocity\n\nReports the current velocity of an object in m/s.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Object velocity** reports the current velocity of an object in m/s (meters per second).\n\nChoose which Distance sensor to use.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block2.png)\n\n\nThe reporter block **object velocity** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![distance_object_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/distance_object_velocity/distance_object_velocity_block3.png)\n"},"divide":{"name":"divide","markdown":"# 除法\n\n第一个值除以第二个值并报告除法运算值。\n\n![divide](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/divide/divide.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**除法**可以接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n**除法**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。也可容纳圆形指令块。\n\n输入数字来做除法。\n\n![divide_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/divide/divide_numbers.png)\n\n除法中可以用变量值。\n\n![divide_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/divide/divide_variables.png)\n\n除法中可以用传感器或设备值。\n\n![divide_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/divide/divide_sensors.png)\n\n"},"draw_circle":{"name":"draw_circle","markdown":"# 画圆形\n\n在V5主控器屏幕上画一个圆形。\n\n![draw_circle](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/draw_circle/draw_circle.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**画圆形**指令块须要3个参数值：\n\n* 参数值1：圆心X坐标\n* 参数值2：圆心Y坐标\n* 参数值3：半径（像素）\n\n圆形弧线颜色取决于**设定笔色**指令块，默认线条颜色为白色。\n\n圆形内部填充颜色取决于**设定填充色**指令块，默认填充颜色为黑色。\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/draw_circle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"draw_line":{"name":"draw_line","markdown":"# 画线段\n\n在V5主控器屏幕上画一条线段。\n\n![draw_line](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/draw_line/draw_line.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**画线段**指令块须要4个参数值：\n\n* 参数值1：起点X坐标\n* 参数值2：起点Y坐标\n* 参数值3：终点X坐标\n* 参数值4：终点Y坐标\n\n线条颜色取决于**设定笔色**指令块，默认线条颜色为白色。\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/draw_line/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_pixel":{"name":"draw_pixel","markdown":"# 画点\n\n在V5主控器屏幕上画一个点。\n\n![draw_pixel](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/draw_pixel/draw_pixel.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**画点**指令块须要2个参数值：\n\n* 参数值1：X坐标\n* 参数值2：Y坐标\n\n点的颜色取决于**设定笔色**指令块，默认点颜色为白色。\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/draw_pixel/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"draw_rectangle":{"name":"draw_rectangle","markdown":"# 画矩形\n\n在V5主控器屏幕上画一个矩形。\n\n![draw_rectangle](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/draw_rectangle/draw_rectangle.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**画矩形**指令块须要4个参数值：\n\n* 参数值1：左上角顶点X坐标\n* 参数值2：左上角顶点Y坐标\n* 参数值3：矩形宽度值\n* 参数值3：矩形高度值\n\n矩形边框颜色取决于**设定笔色**指令块，默认线条颜色为白色。\n\n矩形内部填充颜色取决于**设定填充色**指令块，默认填充颜色为黑色。\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/draw_rectangle/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)"},"drive":{"name":"drive","markdown":"# 驱动\n\n永远驱动底盘。\n\n![drive_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive/drive_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动**指令块将永远运行底盘直到使用一个新的底盘指令块或程序停止。\n\n选择底盘将要驱动的方向。\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive/drive_direction.png)  \n"},"drive_current":{"name":"drive_current","markdown":"# 驱动电流\n\n报告底盘当前电流值。\n\n![drive_current_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_current/drive_current_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动电流**报告范围为**0.0 到 2.5 amps**。\n\n**驱动电流**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_current_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_current/drive_current_inserted.png)"},"drive_efficiency":{"name":"drive_efficiency","markdown":"# 驱动效率\n\n报告底盘的效率。\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动效率**报告电机正在使用（输入）的功率（瓦特）与电机正在提供（输出）的功率（瓦特）的比值。\n\n一般在正常使用的情况下，V5底盘可达到的最大效率为65%。\n\n**驱动效率**报告范围为**0% 到 100%**。\n\n**驱动效率**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_efficiency/drive_efficiency_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_for":{"name":"drive_for","markdown":"# 驱动至\n\n底盘驱动至一个指定的距离。\n\n![drive_for](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_for/drive_for.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择底盘将要驱动的方向。\n\n![drive_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_for/drive_for_direction.png)\n\n\n通过输入一个数值并选择测量单位（英寸或毫米）来设定底盘将要驱动多远。\n\n**驱动至**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![drive_for_units](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_for/drive_for_units.png)\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到底盘驱动结束。\n\n你可以选择箭头展开**并且不等待** - 这一指令将导致其他指令块在底盘驱动的同时继续运行。\n\n![drive_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_for/drive_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"drive_heading":{"name":"drive_heading","markdown":"# 驱动归位\n\n通过陀螺仪传感器当前角度值来报告底盘当前位置。\n\n![drive_heading](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_heading/drive_heading.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当顺时针转动时，**驱动归位**指令块报告值持续增加。\n\n**驱动归位**报告范围为**0.00 到 359.99度**。\n\n**驱动归位**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_heading_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_heading/drive_heading_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_done":{"name":"drive_is_done","markdown":"# 驱动已结束\n\n报告底盘驱动是否完成。\n\n![drive_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n底盘电机完成驱动时，**驱动已结束**报告**真**值。\n\n当底盘电机仍在驱动时，**驱动已结束**报告**假**值。\n\n**驱动已结束**指令块报告一个**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_is_done/drive_is_done_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_is_moving":{"name":"drive_is_moving","markdown":"# 驱动在继续\n\n报告底盘是否正在驱动。\n\n![drive_is_moving](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当底盘电机正在驱动，**驱动在继续**报告**真**值。\n\n当底盘电机已停止，**驱动在继续**报告**假**值。\n\n**驱动在继续**指令块报告一个**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_is_moving_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_is_moving/drive_is_moving_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_power":{"name":"drive_power","markdown":"# 驱动功率\n\n报告底盘当前输出功率。\n\n![drive_power](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_power/drive_power.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动功率**报告范围为**0.0 到 22.0 瓦特**。\n\n**驱动功率**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_power/drive_power_inserted.png)"},"drive_rotation":{"name":"drive_rotation","markdown":"# 驱动转向\n\n当底盘配置一个3线陀螺仪或V5惯性传感器时，报告底盘的转向角度值。\n\n![drive_rotation](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_rotation/drive_rotation.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n当底盘**顺时针**方向转动时，**驱动转向**报告一个正值。\n\n当底盘**逆时针**方向转动时，**驱动转向**报告一个负值。\n\n**驱动转向**指令块被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_rotation_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_rotation/drive_rotation_inserted.png)\n"},"drive_temperature":{"name":"drive_temperature","markdown":"# 驱动温度\n\n报告正在驱动底盘的V5智能电机的温度。\n\n![drive_temperature](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_temperature/drive_temperature.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动温度**报告范围为**0% 到 100%**。\n\n**驱动温度**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_temperature_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_temperature/drive_temperature_inserted.png)"},"drive_torque":{"name":"drive_torque","markdown":"# 驱动扭矩\n\n报告底盘当前扭矩（转动作用力）。\n\n![drive_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_torque/drive_torque.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动扭矩**报告范围为**0.0 到 18.6 英寸-磅（InLB）** 或 **0.0 到 2.1 牛顿-米（Nm）**。\n\n选择**驱动扭矩**报告单位为英寸磅（InLB）或 牛顿米（Nm）。\n\n![drive_torque_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_torque/drive_torque_unit.png)\n\n**驱动扭矩**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_torque/drive_torque_inserted.png)"},"drive_velocity":{"name":"drive_velocity","markdown":"# 驱动速度\n\n报告底盘当前速度。\n\n![drive_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**驱动速度**报告范围为 **-100% 到 100%** 或 **-600rpm 到 600rpm**。\n\n根据底盘使用的V5智能电机中安装的齿轮盒，**驱动速度**将报告不同的“转每分钟（rpm）”范围。\n\n* 红色齿轮盒：-100rpm 到 100rpm\n* 绿色齿轮盒：-200rpm 到 200rpm\n* 蓝色齿轮盒：-600rpm 到 600rpm\n\n选择报告速度单位为百分比（%）或转每分钟（rpm）。\n\n![drive_velocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_unit.png)\n\n**驱动速度**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![drive_velocity_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/drive_velocity/drive_velocity_inserted.png)\n\n"},"duration":{"name":"duration","markdown":"# Set electromagnet duration\n\nSets how long the V5 Electromagnet is turned on for.\n\n![set_duration_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/duration/set_duration_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nSelect to set how long the electromagnet is powered on for a boost:\n\n* **short** - powers the electromagnet for **250ms**\n* **medium** - powers the electromagnet for **500ms**\n* **long** - powers the electromagnet for **1000ms**\n\n![set_duration_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/duration/set_duration_block_setting.png)\n\nChoose which electromagnet to use.\n\n![set_duration_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/duration/set_duration_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will tell the robot to drive forward 200mm, use the **set electromagnet duration** block to set the duration to **long**, then the **Electromagnet** will boost to pick up an object, drive forward 200mm, then drop the object.\n\n![set_duration_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/duration/set_duration_example.png)\n"},"efficiency_of_motor":{"name":"efficiency_of_motor","markdown":"# 电机效率\n\n报告一个V5智能电机的效率。\n\n![drive_efficiency](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机效率**报告电机正在使用（输入）的功率（瓦特）与电机正在提供（输出）的功率（瓦特）的比值。\n\n一般在正常使用的情况下，一个V5智能电机可达到的最大效率为65%。\n\n**电机效率**报告范围为**0% 到 100%**。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![motor_efficiency_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_device.png)\n\n**电机效率**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![motor_efficiency_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/efficiency_of_motor/motor_efficiency_inserted.png)"},"energize":{"name":"energize","markdown":"# Energize electromagnet\n\nSets the V5 Electromagnet to two different modes: **boost** or **drop**.\n\n![set_magnet_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/energize/set_magnet_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nSelect to set that electromagnet to boost or drop\n\n* **boost** - turns on the electromagnet for as long as the duration was set\n* **drop** - releases any object the electromagnet is holding\n\nAfter energizing the magnet, the magnet will need to cool down before it can be energized again.\n\n\n![set_magnet_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/energize/set_magnet_block_setting.png)\n\nChoose which electromagnet to use.\n\n![set_magnet_block_magnet](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/energize/set_magnet_block_magnet.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the robot to drive forward 200mm, **Electromagnet** will boost to pick up an object, drive forward 200mm, then drop the object.\n\n![set_magnet_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/energize/set_magnet_example.png)\n"},"equal_to":{"name":"equal_to","markdown":"# 等于\n\n报告第一个值和第二个值是否相同（相等）。\n\n![equal_to](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/equal_to/equal_to.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当两个值完全相同，**等于**报告**真**值。\n\n当两个值不相同，**等于**报告**假**值。\n\n**等于**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n**等于**指令块报告一个 **真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![equal_to_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/equal_to/equal_to_inserted.png)"},"forever":{"name":"forever","markdown":"# 永续\n\n永续指令块是一个C型控制指令块，它会永久重复执行所包含的任何指令块。\n\n![forever](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/forever/forever.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n将指令块放入**永续**C型控制指令块从而永远重复这些动作。\n\n你可以通过放入一个**退出循环**指令块退出一个**永续**循环。\n\n![forever_example_2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/forever/forever_example_2.png)\n\nC型控制指令块也可以互相被放入，这个概念叫做嵌套，在编程不同行为时可以帮助节省时间。"},"function":{"name":"function","markdown":"# 函数\n\n执行一个选定的数学函数。\n\n![function](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/function/function.png)\n\n* **绝对值** - 绝对值\n* **下取整** - 向下取最近的整数值\n* **上取整** - 向上取最近的整数值\n* **平方根** - 平方根\n* **sin** - 正弦函数\n* **cos** - 余弦函数\n* **tan** - 正切函数\n* **asin** - 反正弦函数\n* **acos** - 反余弦函数\n* **atan** - 反正切函数\n* **ln** - 以自然数e为底的对数\n* **log** - 以10为底的对数\n* **e ^** - 自然数e的幂次方\n* **10 ^** - 10的幂次方\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**函数**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n从下拉列表中选择数学**函数**。\n\n![function_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/function/function_select.png)\n\n**函数**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![function_fit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/function/function_fit.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"greater_than":{"name":"greater_than","markdown":"# 大于\n\n报告第一个值是否大于第二个值。\n\n![greater_than](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/greater_than/greater_than.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当第一个值比第二个值大，**大于**报告**真**值。\n\n当第一个值小于或等于第二个值，**大于**报告**假**值。\n\n**大于**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n**大于**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![greater_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/greater_than/greater_than_inserted.png)\n"},"heading_of_gyro":{"name":"heading_of_gyro","markdown":"# 归位角度\n\n报告3线陀螺仪或V5惯性传感器当前角度位置。\n\n![heading_of_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当顺时针转动时，**归位**报告值持续增加。\n\n**归位**报告范围为**0.00 到 359.99**之间。\n\n选择检验哪一个陀螺仪/惯性传感器。\n\n![heading_of_gyro_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_gyro.png)\n\n**归位**指令块可被用在圆形指令块中。\n\n![heading_of_gyro_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/heading_of_gyro/heading_of_gyro_inserted.png)\n"},"if_then":{"name":"if_then","markdown":"# 如果 那么\n\n**如果 那么**是一个C型控制指令块，如果布尔条件报告为**真**值，则执行所包含的任何指令块。\n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/if_then/if_then.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**如果 那么**控制指令块只会检测一次布尔条件值。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**真**值，**如果 那么**中的指令块将运行。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**假**值，**如果 那么**中的指令块将被跳过。\n\n**如果 那么**指令块可接受六角形指令块作为它的条件。\n\n![if_then](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/if_then/if_then_2.png)\n\n"},"if_then_else":{"name":"if_then_else","markdown":"# 如果 那么 否则\n\n**如果 那么 否则**是一个C型控制指令块，它根据报告的布尔值来运行**如果 那么 否则**中的第一部分或第二部分。\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/if_then_else/if_then_else.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**如果 那么 否则**C型控制指令块只会检验一次布尔条件。 \n\n如果布尔条件报告为**真**值，则**如果**部分的指令块将被运行。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**假**值，则**否则**部分的指令块将被运行。\n\n**如果 那么 否则**C型控制指令块可接受六角形指令块作为它的条件。\n\n![if_then_else](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/if_then_else/if_then_else_2.png)"},"inertial_acceleration":{"name":"inertial_acceleration","markdown":"# 加速度\n\n报告惯性传感器一个轴向（x,y,z）的加速度值。\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_block.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**加速度**报告范围为 **-4.0 至 4.0**Gs.\n\n选择使用哪一个惯性传感器。\n\n![inertial_acceleration_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_device.png)\n\n选择使用哪个轴向：\n\n* 当惯性传感器**左右**移动时，报告**X轴**加速度\n* 当惯性传感器**上下**移动时，报告**Y轴**加速度\n* 当惯性传感器**前后**移动时，报告**Z轴**加速度\n\n![inertial_acceleration_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_acceleration/inertial_acceleration_axis.png)\n\n**加速度**指令块被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![acceleration_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_acceleration/acceleration_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_gyrorate":{"name":"inertial_gyrorate","markdown":"# 陀螺仪速率\n\n获取惯性传感器一个轴向（x,y,z）的角速度。\n\n![gyro_rate_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_gyrorate/gyro_rate_block.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**陀螺仪速率**报告范围为 **-1000.0 至 1000.0** dps（度每秒）。\n\n选择使用哪一个惯性传感器。\n\n![gyroRate_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_included_block.png)\n\n选择使用哪一个轴向：\n\n* 当惯性传感器沿X轴（取决于传感器朝向）转动时**X轴**报告转向\n* 当惯性传感器沿Y轴（取决于传感器朝向）转动时**Y轴**报告转向\n* 当惯性传感器沿Z轴（取决于传感器朝向）转动时**Z轴**报告转向\n\n![gyroRate_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_axis.png)\n\n**陀螺仪速率**指令块被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_gyrorate/gyroRate_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n"},"inertial_orientation":{"name":"inertial_orientation","markdown":"# 偏转角\n\n获取惯性传感器偏转角度值。报告惯性传感器特定的参数单位值。\n\n![orientation_inertial_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_orientation/orientation_inertial_block.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n偏转角取决于选择的轴向（x,y,z）。\n\n* **X轴**代表**pitch**，报告值在 -90 至 +90度之间。\n* **Y轴**代表**roll**，报告值在 -180 至 +180度之间。\n* **Z轴**代表**yaw**，报告值在 -180 至 +180度之间。\n\n---\n\n**Pitch**是机器人前后倾斜的角度。\n\n![V5_Pitch_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_orientation/V5_Pitch_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Roll**是机器人左右倾斜的角度。\n\n![V5_Roll_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_orientation/V5_Roll_rev2.jpg)\n\n**Yaw**是机器人左右转向角度。\n\n![V5_Yaw_rev2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_orientation/V5_Yaw_rev2.jpg)\n\n---\n\n选择使用哪一个惯性传感器。\n\n![orientation_included_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_orientation/orientation_included_block.png)\n\n选择使用哪一个轴向。\n\n![orientation_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_orientation/orientation_axis.png)\n\n**偏转角**感应指令块被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![orientation_of_inertial_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/inertial_orientation/orientation_of_inertial_inserted.png)\n\n"},"item_of_2d_array":{"name":"item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 二维数组元素\n\n报告一个二维数组中某个元素的值。\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个二维数组。该二维数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_options.png)\n\n输入数组内被报告的元素的行（第一个数字）和列（第二个数字）位置。此处，被报告的元素位置为二维数组中第2行，第3列。\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_2.png)\n\n**二维数组元素**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_2d_array/item_of_2d_list_inserted.png)"},"item_of_array":{"name":"item_of_array","markdown":"# 元素\n\n报告一个数组中某个元素的值。 \n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_array/item_of_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个数组。该数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![item_of_options](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_array/item_of_options.png)\n\n输入数组内元素的位置序号。此处，报告数组中第2个元素。\n\n![item_of_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_array/item_of_block_2.png)\n\n**元素**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示底盘速度设定为数组中第3个元素存储的值，底盘将以90%的速度正向驱动。\n\n![item_of_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/item_of_array/item_of_example2.png)\n\n"},"joint_move":{"name":"joint_move","markdown":"# Joint move\n\nMoves the V5 Robotic Arm to the specified (x, y, z) coordinate using joint movement.\n\n![joint_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/joint_move/joint_move_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **joint move** block moves the V5 Robotic Arm in the x, y, and z-direction using joint movement. \n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/joint_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_joint_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/joint_move/select_joint_arm.png)\n\nThe **joint move** block accepts decimals, integers, and numeric blocks.\n\n![joint_input](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/joint_move/joint_input.png)"},"length_of_2d_array":{"name":"length_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 二维数组长度\n\n报告一个二维数组的行数和列数。\n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个二维数组。该二维数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_select.png)\n\n选择报告哪个值，二维数组可以报告**行数** 或 **列数**。\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_option.png)\n\n**二维数组长度**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/length_of_2d_array/size_of_2d_list_insert.png)"},"less_than":{"name":"less_than","markdown":"# 小于\n\n报告第一个值是否比第二个值小。 \n\n![less_than](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/less_than/less_than.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当第一个值比第二个值小，**小于**报告**真**值。\n\n当第一个值大于或等于第二个值，**小于**报告**假**值。\n\n**小于**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n**小于**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![less_than_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/less_than/less_than_inserted.png)\n\n"},"linear_move":{"name":"linear_move","markdown":"# Linear move\n\nMoves the V5 Robotic Arm to the specified (x, y, z) coordinate using linear movement.\n\n![linear_move_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/linear_move/linear_move_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **linear move** block moves the V5 Robotic Arm in the x, y, and z-direction using linear movement. \n\n![xyz_coord](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/linear_move/xyz_coord.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_linear_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/linear_move/select_linear_arm.png)\n\nThe **linear move** block accepts decimals, integers, and numeric blocks.\n\n![linear_input](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/linear_move/linear_input.png)"},"motor_is_done":{"name":"motor_is_done","markdown":"# 电机已结束\n\n报告指定的V5智能电机转动是否已完成。\n\n![motor_is_done_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当选择的电机转动已完成，**电机已结束**报告**真**值。\n\n当选择的电机仍在转动，**电机已结束**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![motor_is_done_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_motor.png)\n\n**电机已结束**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![motor_is_done_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_done/motor_is_done_inserted.png)\n\n\n"},"motor_is_spinning":{"name":"motor_is_spinning","markdown":"# 电机在转动\n\n报告指定的V5智能电机当前是否在转动。\n\n![motor_is_spinning](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当选择的电机转动正在转动，**电机在转动**报告**真**值。\n\n当选择的电机转动已停止，**电机在转动**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![motor_is_spinning_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_motor.png)\n\n**电机在转动**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![motor_is_spinning_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/motor_is_spinning/motor_is_spinning_inserted.png)\n"},"multiply":{"name":"multiply","markdown":"# 乘法\n\n乘以两个值并报告乘积。\n\n![multiply](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/multiply/multiply.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**乘法**可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n**乘法**可被用在圆形空白指令块中，也可以容纳圆形空白指令块。\n\n乘以两个数字。\n\n![multiply_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/multiply/multiply_numbers.png)\n\n乘以变量值。\n\n![multiply_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/multiply/multiply_variables.png)\n\n乘以传感器或设备值。\n\n![multiply_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/multiply/multiply_sensors.png)\n"},"next_row":{"name":"next_row","markdown":"# 下一行\n\n设定打印结果至V5主控器或遥控器屏幕的下一可用行。\n\n![next_row](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/next_row/next_row.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n所有程序默认光标从屏幕第1行第1列开始。**下一行**指令块将在屏幕上移动光标至下一行，\n**下一行**指令块同样会在屏幕上设定光标至第1列。\n\n选择使用哪一个设备。V5遥控器只有被添加到设备窗口以后才会显示。\n\n![next_row_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/next_row/next_row_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\nV5主控器允许改变屏幕打印的字体大小，更改字体将会影响V5主控器屏幕可用的行数。\n\n**V5主控器字体大小 - 行数：**\n\n* 加小号 - 20行\n* 小号 - 16行\n* 中号 - 12 行（默认）\n* 大号 - 8 行\n* 加大号 - 6 行\n* 特大号 - 4 行\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/next_row/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\nV5遥控器不允许改变屏幕打印的字体大小。\n\n**V5遥控器字体大小 - 行数：**\n\n* 标准字体 - 3 行（默认 ）\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/next_row/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)\n"},"not":{"name":"not","markdown":"# 非\n\n报告布尔结果的相反值。\n\n![not](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/not/not.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当布尔指令块中报告**假**值，**非**指令块报告**真**值。\n\n当布尔指令块中报告**真**值，**非**指令块报告**假**值。\n\n**非**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示当V5主控器屏幕未被按下时，报告**真**值。 \n\n![not_sensors](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/not/not_sensors.png)\n\n![not_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/not/not_truth.png)  \n\n"},"object_count":{"name":"object_count","markdown":"# 对象数目\n\n报告视觉传感器检测到的对象数量。\n\n一个对象需要被配置，在此之后，**对象数目**指令块才能够检测到它。\n\n![object_count_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/object_count/object_count_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器。\n\n![object_count_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/object_count/object_count_device.png)\n\n在**对象数目**指令块报告对象数目之前需要使用**拍照**指令块。\n\n**对象数目**指令块只会检测来自最后拍照标记的对象的数目。\n\n\n"},"object_exists":{"name":"object_exists","markdown":"# 对象存在\n\n报告视觉传感器是否检测到一个已配置对象。\n\n一个对象需要被配置，在此之后，**对象存在**指令块才能够检测到它。\n\n![object_exists_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/object_exists/object_exists_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器。\n\n![object_exists_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/object_exists/object_exists_device.png)\n\n\n当视觉传感器检测到一个已配置对象，**对象存在**报告**真**值。\n\n当视觉传感器未检测到一个已配置对象，**对象存在**报告**假**值。\n\n**对象存在**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![object_exists_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/object_exists/object_exists_inserted.png)\n\n在**对象存在**布尔指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值之前需要使用**拍照**指令块。"},"object_in_front":{"name":"object_in_front","markdown":"# 发现对象\n\n报告超声波测距仪是否在它测距范围内检测到一个对象。\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/object_in_front/object_in_front_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当测距仪在测距范围内检测到一个对象或平面，**发现对象**报告**真**值。\n\n当测距仪在测距范围内未检测到一个对象或平面，**发现对象**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个超声波测距仪。\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/object_in_front/object_in_front_distance.png)\n\n**发现对象**布尔指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![object_in_front](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/object_in_front/object_in_front_inserted.png)\n "},"optical_brightness":{"name":"optical_brightness","markdown":"# Optical brightness\n\nReports the amount of light detected by the Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_brightness](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_brightness/optical_brightness.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_brightness_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical brightness** block reports a number value from **0%** to **100%**.\n\nA large amount of light detected will report a high brightness value.\n\nA small amount of light detected will report a low brightness value.\n\nThe **Optical brightness** block reports number values and is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_brightness_use](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_brightness/optical_brightness_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect":{"name":"optical_detect","markdown":"# Optical detects color\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects the specified color.\n\n![optical_detect](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_detect/optical_detect.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_detect_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_detect/optical_detect_device.png)\n\nChoose which color you want the sensor to check for.\n\n![optical_detect_colors](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_detect/optical_detect_colors.png)\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **true** when the Optical Sensor detects the specified color.\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **false** if it doesn't detect the specified color.\n\nThe **Optical detects color** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![optical_detect_use](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_detect/optical_detect_use.png)\n"},"optical_detect_gesture":{"name":"optical_detect_gesture","markdown":"# When Optical detects a gesture \n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the Optical sensor detects a gesture.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **When Optical detects a gesture** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on gestures that the Optical Sensor detects.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor.\n\n\n![optical_detects_gesture_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detects_gesture_device.png)\n\nChoose which gesture triggers the **When Optical detects a gesture** event.\n\n![optical_detect_gesture_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_detect_gesture/optical_detect_gesture_block2.png)"},"optical_detect_object":{"name":"optical_detect_object","markdown":"# When Optical detects/loses \n\nRuns the attached stack of blocks when the Optical sensor detects or loses an object.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **When Optical detects/loses** event can be used to create actions or behaviors based on whether the Optical Sensor **detects** an object in range of the sensor or **loses** an object that was in range of the sensor.\n\nChoose an optical sensor.\n\n![optical_detect_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_device.png)\n\nChoose whether the **When Optical detects/loses** event is triggered when the sensor **detects** an object, or **loses** an object.\n\n![optical_detect_object_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_detect_object/optical_detect_object_block2.png)"},"optical_found_object":{"name":"optical_found_object","markdown":"# Optical found object\n\nReports if the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\n\n![optical_found_object](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_found_object/optical_found_object.png)\n\n## How To Use\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_found_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **true** when the Optical Sensor detects an object close to it.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **false** if an object is not within range.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block should be used to check if an object is close to the Optical Sensor so that the color readings from the **Optical detects color** block are accurate.\n\nThe **Optical found object** block reports **true** or **false** and is used in blocks with hexagonal (six-sided) spaces.\n\n![optical_found_object_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_found_object/optical_found_object_condition.png)"},"optical_hue":{"name":"optical_hue","markdown":"# Optical hue\n\nReports the hue of the color of an object.\n\n![optical_hue](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_hue/optical_hue.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose an optical sensor.\n\n![optical_hue_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_hue/optical_hue_device.png)\n\nThe **Optical hue** block reports a number value that is the hue of the color of an object. It returns a number between **0** and **359**, which can be thought of as the location of the color on a color wheel.\n\nThe **Optical hue** block reports number values and is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![optical_hue_use](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_hue/optical_hue_use.png)"},"optical_set_light":{"name":"optical_set_light","markdown":"# Set Optical light\n\nSets the light on the Optical Sensor to on or off.\n\n![optical_set_light](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_set_light/optical_set_light.png)\n\n## How To Use\nThe **Set optical light** block allows you to turn the Optical Sensor's light **on** or **off**. The light lets the sensor see objects if it is looking at an object in a dark area.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor to use.\n\n![optical_set_light_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_device.png)\n\nChoose whether you want to set the light on the Optical Sensor to **on** or **off**.\n\n![optical_set_light_state](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_state.png)\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, we use the **Set optical light** block to turn the light on. Then, if the Optical Sensor detects an object, we print the hue.\n\n\n![optical_set_light_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_set_light/optical_set_light_example.png)"},"optical_set_light_power":{"name":"optical_set_light_power","markdown":"# Set optical light power \n\nSet the light power of V5 Optical sensor\n\n![optical_set_light_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_light_power_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Set optical light power** block accepts a range of **0%** to **100%**. This will change the brightness of the light on the Optical Sensor. If the light is off, this block will turn the light on.\n\nChoose an Optical Sensor.\n\n![optical_set_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_device.png)\n\nThe set optical light power block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks.\n\n![optical_set_power_num](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_num.png)\n\n## Example\nIn this example we use the **Set optical light power** block to set the power of the light to **50%**, then we use the **Set optical light** block to turn the light on. Then, if the Optical Sensor detects an object, we print the hue.\n\n![optical_set_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/optical_set_light_power/optical_set_power_example.png)"},"or":{"name":"or","markdown":"# 或\n\n报告两个布尔条件中的一个是否为真。\n\n![or](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/or/or.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当一个（或两个）条件为**真**值，**或**指令块报告**真**值。 \n\n当两个条件均为**假**值，**或**指令块报告**假**值。\n\n**或**布尔指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![or_sensors2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/or/or_sensors2.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n 当碰撞开关被按下，和/或光感器亮度水平大于50%时，**或**指令块报告**真**值，\n\n只有当碰撞开关未被按下同时光感器亮度水平小于等于50%时，**或**指令块报告**假**值。\n\n![or_truth](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/or/or_truth.png)"},"position_of_controller":{"name":"position_of_controller","markdown":"# 遥控器位标\n\n报告V5遥控器一个操纵杆沿一个轴向的位标。\n\n![position_of_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用 \n\n**遥控器位标**报告范围为 **-100 到 100**之间。\n\n当一个操纵杆轴向在中心，**遥控器位标**将报告零（0）。\n\n![controller_button_front](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_controller/controller_button_front.png)\n\n选择使用哪一个V5遥控器。\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_devices.png)\n\n选择操纵杆轴向来检验它的位标。\n\n![position_of_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_options.png)\n\n**遥控器位标**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![position_of_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_controller/position_of_controller_inserted.png)\n\n"},"position_of_motor":{"name":"position_of_motor","markdown":"# 电机转位\n\n报告V5智能电机已转动的距离。\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机转位**以整数数值角度和小数数值转数报告V5智能电机转位。\n\n选择使用哪一个V5智能电机。\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_motor.png)\n\n选择V5智能电机转位的单位为角度或转数。 \n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_unit.png)\n\n**电机转位**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。 \n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_motor/position_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"position_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"position_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# 光轴编码器转位\n\n报告光轴编码器转动的距离。\n\n![position_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**光轴编码器转位**以整数数值角度和小数数值转数报告光轴编码器转位。\n\n选择使用哪一个光轴编码器。\n\n![position_of_motor_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_device.png)\n\n选择报告光轴编码器转动的单位为度数或转数。\n\n![position_of_motor_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_unit.png)\n\n**光轴编码器转位**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![position_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/position_of_shaft_encoder/position_of_encoder_inserted.png)"},"power":{"name":"power","markdown":"# Set electromagnet power\n\nSets the V5 Electromagnet power that will be used when picking up and object with the energize block.\n\n![set_magnet_power_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/power/set_magnet_power_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nYou may need to pick up objects with a varying weights. The **set electromagnet power** block lets you control how much power the elctromagnet will use. The **set electromagnet power** block has a range of **0% to 100%**\n\nChoose which magnet to use.\n\n![set_magnet_dropdown_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/power/set_magnet_dropdown_block.png)\n\n## Example\n\nThis example will set the robot to drive forward 200mm, then it will increase the power using the **set electromagnet power** block, then the **Electromagnet** will boost to pick up an object, drive forward 200mm, then drop the object.\n\n![set_magnet_power_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/power/set_magnet_power_example.png)\n"},"power_of_motor":{"name":"power_of_motor","markdown":"# 电机功率\n\n报告V5智能电机当前输出的功率。\n\n![motor_power](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/power_of_motor/motor_power.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机功率**报告范围为***0.0 to 11.0 瓦特**。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![motor_power_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/power_of_motor/motor_power_device.png)\n\n**电机功率**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![motor_power_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/power_of_motor/motor_power_inserted.png)\n"},"pressing_bumper":{"name":"pressing_bumper","markdown":"# 碰撞开关按下\n\n报告碰撞开关是否被按下。\n\n![pressing_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n如果碰撞开关被按下，**碰撞开关按下**报告**真**值。\n\n如果碰撞开关未被按下，**碰撞开关按下**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个碰撞开关。\n\n![pressing_bumper_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_bumper.png)\n\n**碰撞开关按下**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![pressing_bumper_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_bumper/pressing_bumper_inserted.png)\n "},"pressing_controller":{"name":"pressing_controller","markdown":"# 遥控器按下\n\n报告V5遥控上某个按键是否被按下。\n\n![pressing_controller_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n如果选定的遥控器按键被按下，**遥控器按下**报告**真**值。\n\n如果选定的遥控器按键未被按下，**遥控器按下**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个V5遥控器。\n\n![pressing_controller_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_device.png)\n\n选择使用遥控器哪一个按键。\n\n![pressing_controller_options](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_options.png)\n\n**遥控器按下**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且在被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![pressing_controller_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_controller/pressing_controller_inserted.png)"},"pressing_limit":{"name":"pressing_limit","markdown":"# 限位开关按下\n\n报告限位开关是否被按下。\n\n![pressing_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_limit/pressing_limit.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n如果限位开关被按下，**限位开关按下**报告**真**值。\n\n如果限位开关未被按下，**限位开关按下**报告**假**值。\n\n选择使用哪一个限位开关。\n\n![pressing_limit_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_bumper.png)\n\n**限位开关按下**指令块报告一个**真** 或 **假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![pressing_limit_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/pressing_limit/pressing_limit_inserted.png)\n "},"print":{"name":"print","markdown":"# 打印\n\n在V5主控器或遥控器屏幕上打印值或文本。\n\n![look_print](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/print/look_print.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**打印**指令块将在屏幕光标位置打印数据。\n\n所有新建程序都是从屏幕第1行第1列光标开始。\n\n所有指令块默认将以整数数字打印。使用**设定打印精度**指令块来调节打印的小数位数。\n\n选择使用哪一个设备。V5遥控器只有被添加到设备窗口以后才会显示。\n\n![look_print_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/print/look_print_dropdown.png)\n\n---\n\n打印字母和数字。\n\n![print_words](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/print/print_words.png)\n\n打印变量值。\n\n![print_variable1](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/print/print_variable1.png)  \n\n打印运算符计算值。\n\n![print_addition](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/print/print_addition.png)  \n\n打印传感器或设备值。\n\n![print_sensor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/print/print_sensor.png)\n\n\n"},"procedures_call":{"name":"procedures_call","markdown":"# 我的指令块\n\n我的指令块用于生成自定义指令块。\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/my_block.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**我的指令块**用于生成一系列可以在一个程序中被多次使用的指令块。\n\n**我的指令块**使用**创建一个指令块**按钮来创建。\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/make_a_block.png)\n\n**我的指令块**可以包含多个参数 - 文本标签，数字变量和布尔变量 - 来添加更多的功能到你的自定义指令块中。\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/make_variable.png)  \n\n要使用一个**我的指令块**，附着调用**我的指令块**到一个帽状指令块。当**我的指令块**出现在你的程序中，包含在**我的指令块**中的程序段将使用指定的参数值运行。\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/trigger_function.png)\n\n附着一个程序段到**我的指令块**“定义”帽状指令块，来设定当一个**我的指令块**使用时发生的动作。\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/attach_function.png)\n\n***注意：生成多个带有相同标签和变量的 我的指令块 可能导致下载你的程序时报错。***\n\n## 示例\n\n该示例中，机器人将使用**我的指令块**来：\n\n* 向前运动15英寸\n* 在主控器屏幕打印电池电量同时移动光标至下一行\n* 机器人右转180度\n* 在主控器屏幕打印电池电量同时移动光标至下一行\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_call/print_number.png)\n\n"},"procedures_definition":{"name":"procedures_definition","markdown":"# 我的指令块\n\n我的指令块用于生成自定义指令块。\n\n![my_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/my_block.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**我的指令块**用于生成一系列可以在一个程序中被多次使用的指令块。\n\n**我的指令块**使用**创建一个指令块**按钮来创建。\n\n![make_a_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/make_a_block.png)\n\n**我的指令块**可以包含多个参数 - 文本标签，数字变量和布尔变量 - 来添加更多的功能到你的自定义指令块中。\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/make_variable.png)  \n\n要使用一个**我的指令块**，附着调用**我的指令块**到一个帽状指令块。当**我的指令块**出现在你的程序中，包含在**我的指令块**中的程序段将使用指定的参数值运行。\n\n![trigger_function](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/trigger_function.png)\n\n附着一个程序段到**我的指令块**“定义”帽状指令块，来设定当一个**我的指令块**使用时发生的动作。\n\n![attach_function](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/attach_function.png)\n\n***注意：生成多个带有相同标签和变量的 我的指令块 可能导致下载你的程序时报错。***\n\n## 示例\n\n该示例中，机器人将使用**我的指令块**来：\n\n* 向前运动15英寸\n* 在主控器屏幕打印电池电量同时移动光标至下一行 \n* 机器人右转180度\n* 在主控器屏幕打印电池电量同时移动光标至下一行\n\n![print_number](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/procedures_definition/print_number.png)\n\n"},"random":{"name":"random","markdown":"# 随机数\n\n报告指令块中从最小到最大的一个随机值。\n\n![random](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/random/random.png)\n\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**随机数**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n**随机数**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例使用一个**随机数**指令块来随机化底盘速度。\n\n![random_drivetrain](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/random/random_drivetrain.png)\n\n本例使用一个**随机数**指令块来随机化一个等待指令块的时间长度。\n\n![random_control](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/random/random_control.png)\n\n"},"reflectivity_of":{"name":"reflectivity_of","markdown":"# 反射率百分比\n\n报告巡线器反射的光线亮度。\n\n![reflectivity_of](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n浅色表面将反射更多光线并报告高反射率值。\n\n深色表面将反射较少的光线并且将报告低反射率值。\n\n**反射率百分比**范围为**0% to 100%**。\n\n选择使用哪一个巡线器。\n\n![reflectivity_of_color](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_color.png)\n\n**反射率百分比**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![reflectivity_of_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/reflectivity_of/reflectivity_of_inserted.png)\n\n\n\n"},"remainder":{"name":"remainder","markdown":"# 取余\n\n用第二个值除第一个值并报告余数。\n\n![remainder](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/remainder/remainder.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**取余**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n可整除的数字将报告取余为零。\n\n**取余**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示7除以2并在V5主控器屏幕打印余数“1”。\n\n![remainder_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/remainder/remainder_numbers.png)"},"repeat":{"name":"repeat","markdown":"# 重复\n\n重复指令块是一个C型控制指令块，它会以设定的次数重复执行所包含的任何指令块。\n\n![repeat](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/repeat/repeat.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n首先，输入一个值来指示指令块所含指令段将要**重复**多少次。\n \n**重复**C型控制指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\nC型控制指令块也可以互相被放入，这个概念叫做嵌套，在编程不同行为时可以帮助节省时间。\n\n![repeat_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/repeat/repeat_select.png)"},"repeat_until":{"name":"repeat_until","markdown":"# 重复直到\n\n重复直到指令块是一个C型控制指令块，它会重复执行所包含的任何指令块直到布尔条件报告为**真**值。 \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/repeat_until/repeat_until.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**重复直到**指令块只在每次循环开始时检验布尔条件。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**假**值，在**重复直到**指令块中的指令块将运行。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**真**值，在**重复直到**指令块中的指令块将被跳过。\n\n**重复直到**C型控制指令块可接受六角形指令块作为它的条件。 \n\n![repeat_until](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/repeat_until/repeat_until_2.png)\n\n\n"},"reset_timer":{"name":"reset_timer","markdown":"# 重置计时器\n\n重置V5主控器的计时器。\n\n![resetTimer](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/reset_timer/resetTimer.png)\n\n## 如何应用 \n\n主控器计时器在每个程序开始时计时。**重置计时器**指令块用于重置计时器返回0秒。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例中，计时器被重置，底盘正向驱动3秒，3秒钟过后，底盘将停止。\n\n![resetTimer_exampleRevised](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/reset_timer/resetTimer_exampleRevised.png)"},"rotation_angle":{"name":"rotation_angle","markdown":"# Angle of rotation \n\nReports a V5 Rotation sensor's current angle of rotation in degrees.\n\n![rotation_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **Angle of rotation** block reports values in the range of **0.00** to **359.99**.\n\nThe **Angle of rotation** block will either report increasing or decreasing values as the Rotation sensor turns.\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to get values from.\n\n![rotation_angle_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block2.png)\n\nThe **angle of rotation** reporter block is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_angle_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_angle/rotation_angle_block3.png)\n"},"rotation_of_gyro":{"name":"rotation_of_gyro","markdown":"# 转向角度\n\n报告3线陀螺仪或V5惯性传感器当前转向的角度值。\n\n![rotation_position.png](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n当陀螺仪**顺时针**方向转动时，**陀螺仪转向**报告一个**正**值。\n\n当陀螺仪**逆时针**方向转动时，**陀螺仪转向**报告一个**负**值。\n\n 选择检验哪一个陀螺仪/惯性传感器。\n\n![rotation_position_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_devices.png)\n\n**陀螺仪转向**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![rotation_position_inserted.png](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_of_gyro/rotation_position_inserted.png)\n"},"rotation_position":{"name":"rotation_position","markdown":"# Position of rotation \n\nReports the current rotational position of the selected V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_position/rotation_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\n**Position of rotation** reports the position of a V5 Rotation sensor in integer numbers for degrees, and decimal numbers for turns.\n\nChoose which V5 Rotation sensor to use.\n\n![rotation_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_position/rotation_position_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether the value is reported in degrees rotated or in turns of the V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_position/rotation_position_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block **position of rotation** is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_position_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_position/rotation_position_block4.png)\n"},"rotation_set_position":{"name":"rotation_set_position","markdown":"# Set position \n\nSets a V5 Rotation sensor's current position to a defined value.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set position** block can be used to set a Rotation sensor's position.\n\nThis block is typically used to reset the position of the Rotation sensor when the value is set to 0.\n\nThe **set position** block can accept decimals, integers, or numeric blocks as an input.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block3.png)\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to use, then enter the desired position value.\n\n![rotation_set_position_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_set_position/rotation_set_position_block2.png)\n"},"rotation_velocity":{"name":"rotation_velocity","markdown":"# Velocity of rotation\n\nReports the current velocity of a V5 Rotation sensor.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Rotation sensor to get values from.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block2.png)\n\nChoose whether the velocity is reported in percent (%), revolutions per minute (rpm) or degrees per second (dps).\n\n![rotation_velocity_block3](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block3.png)\n\nThe reporter block velocity of rotation is used in blocks with circular spaces.\n\n![rotation_velocity_block4](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/rotation_velocity/rotation_velocity_block4.png)\n"},"round":{"name":"round","markdown":"# 取整\n\n将输入的值取整至最近的整数。\n\n![round](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/round/round.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n小数位等于或大于0.5向上**取整**，小数位小于0.5向下**取整**.\n\n**取整**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。 \n\n**取整**指令块接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![round_numbers](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/round/round_numbers.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示取整2.7并将打印“3”。\n\n![round_variables](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/round/round_variables.png)\n\n\n\n"},"screen_position":{"name":"screen_position","markdown":"# 屏幕坐标\n\n报告V5主控器触摸屏上最后检测到的触摸的坐标。\n\n![screen_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/screen_position/screen_position_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**屏幕坐标**指令块用于捕获V5主控器触摸屏上最后一次按下的X/Y坐标。 此指令块可用于创建V5系统与用户之间的交互。\n\n**屏幕坐标**的X坐标范围为**0 to 480 像素**。\n\n**屏幕坐标**的Y坐标范围为**0 to 240 像素**。\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/screen_position/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n选择报告哪一个坐标轴的坐标。\n\n![screen_position_value](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/screen_position/screen_position_value.png)\n\n**屏幕坐标**指令块可被用于圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![screen_position_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/screen_position/screen_position_inserted.png)"},"screen_pressed":{"name":"screen_pressed","markdown":"# 屏幕按下\n\n报告当前V5主控器的触摸屏是否正在被按下。\n\n![screen_pressed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**屏幕按下**指令块可以与**屏幕坐标**一起使用，以检测V5主控器触摸屏上触摸发生的时间和坐标。\n\n当V5主控器触摸屏正在被按下，**屏幕按下**指令块报告为**真**值。\n\n当V5主控器触摸屏没有被按下，**屏幕按下**指令块报告为**假**值。\n\n**屏幕按下**指令块报告**真**或**假**值，且可被用在六角形空白指令块中。\n\n![screen_pressed_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/screen_pressed/screen_pressed_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_2d_array_to":{"name":"set_2d_array_to","markdown":"# 设定二维数组\n\n通过输入数值来设定二维数组每个元素值。\n\n![set_2d_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to.png)\n\n## 如何应用 \n\n当生成一个二维数组时，你可以设定数组的**列数**数值在1到10之间，设定数组**行数**数值在1到10之间。\n\n选择使用哪一个二维数组，该二维数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_options.png)\n\n**设定二维数组**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_2d_array_to/set_2d_list_to_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_array_to":{"name":"set_array_to","markdown":"# 设定数组\n\n通过输入数值来设定数组每个元素值。\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_array_to/set_list_to.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n数组的长度（1到10）在数组生成时已设定。\n\n选择使用哪一个数组，该数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![set_list_to_options](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_array_to/set_list_to_options.png)\n\n**设定数组**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![set_list_to](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_array_to/set_list_to_2.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示设定数组初始值，然后报告数组第3个元素（90）从而设定机械臂位置。\n\n![set_list_to_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_array_to/set_list_to_example.png)\n\n"},"set_boolean_variable":{"name":"set_boolean_variable","markdown":"# 设定布尔变量\n\n设定一个布尔变量为一个指定值。\n\n![set_boolean_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个布尔变量，该变量也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![set_boolean_block_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_choice.png)\n\n选择一个布尔值。\n\n![set_boolean_block_value](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_value.png)\n\n**设定布尔变量**指令块可被用在六角形指令块中。\n\n![set_boolean_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_boolean_variable/set_boolean_block_inserted.png)"},"set_cursor":{"name":"set_cursor","markdown":"# 设定光标\n\n设定**打印**指令块在V5主控器或者遥控器屏幕上的光标位置。\n\n![set_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_cursor/set_cursor.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n设定光标行数和列数位置，从而让**打印**指令在屏幕指定位置显示。\n\n**设定光标**的**行数**接受范围为**1到20**。\n\n**设定光标**的**列数**接受范围为**1到80**。\n\n选择使用哪一个设备。V5遥控器只有被添加到设备窗口以后才会显示。\n\n![set_cursor_dropdown](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_cursor/set_cursor_dropdown.png)\n\n**设定光标**指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\n---\n\nV5主控器允许改变屏幕打印的字体大小，更改字体将会影响V5主控器屏幕可用的行数和列数。\n\n**V5主控器字体大小 - 行数：**\n\n* 加小号 - 20行\n* 小号 - 16行\n* 中号 - 12 行（默认）\n* 大号 - 8 行\n* 加大号 - 6 行\n* 特大号 - 4 行\n\n**V5主控器字体大小 - 列数：**\n\n* 加小号 - 80 列\n* 小号 - 68 列\n* 中号 - 48 列 （默认）\n* 大号 - 32 列\n* 加大号 - 24 列\n* 特大号 - 16 列\n\n![brain_screen_info](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_cursor/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n\n---\n\nV5遥控器不允许改变屏幕打印的字体大小。\n\n**V5遥控器字体大小 - 行数：**\n\n* 标准字体 - 3 行（默认 ）\n\n**V5遥控器字体大小 - 列数：**\n\n* 标准字体 - 20 列（默认 ）\n\n![brain_screen_info_2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_cursor/v5_controller_rows_columns.jpg)"},"set_drive_heading":{"name":"set_drive_heading","markdown":"# 设定底盘归位\n\n设定底盘3线陀螺仪/V5惯性传感器当前归位角度值。\n\n![setDriveHeading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_heading/setDriveHeading_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定底盘归位**指令块可用于设定底盘为任意指定的位置。当归位值设为0时，改指令块可用于重置底盘陀螺仪位置。\n\n**设定底盘归位**接受范围为**0到360**度。\n\n**设定底盘归位**指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\n\n"},"set_drive_rotation":{"name":"set_drive_rotation","markdown":"# 设定底盘转向\n\n当配置3线陀螺仪或V5惯性传感器时，设定底盘转向的角度。\n\n![drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_rotation/drivetrain_setdriverotation_iq.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**设定底盘转向**指令块可用于设定底盘旋转角度至任意指定的正值或负值。\n\n**设定底盘转向**指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n该示例将使机器人一共转动210度：\n\n![turntorotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_rotation/turntorotation_example.png)\n\n- 左转（逆时针）至旋转120度。\n- 设定机器人当前位置为旋转-45度。\n- 根据上一条指令块设定的旋转值再次左转（逆时针）90度（-45度到+45度）。"},"set_drive_stopping":{"name":"set_drive_stopping","markdown":"# 设定驱动停止\n\n设定底盘停止驱动时的行为。\n\n![setDriveStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n* **刹车**将导致底盘立即停止，但受外力作用仍可转动。\n* **滑行**使得底盘逐渐转动至停止。\n* **锁住**将导致底盘立即停止，同时如果受外力作用产生移动，会通过内置编码器转回到它停止的位置。\n  \n![setDriveStopping_type](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_type.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示使底盘正向移动3秒钟，然后在停止的位置锁住。\n\n![setDriveStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_stopping/setDriveStopping_example_revised.png)"},"set_drive_timeout":{"name":"set_drive_timeout","markdown":"# 设定驱动超时\n\n针对底盘驱动指令设定一个时间限制。\n\n![setDriveTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当驱动指令块未达到它的位置时，底盘时间限制可用来防止驱动指令块阻止指令段中其他指令块的运行。\n\n一个底盘未达到它的位置的示例是当一个机器人撞到一面墙且无法完成它的移动。\n\n**设定驱动超时**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示如果底盘没有到达目标值24英寸，在2秒后结束**驱动**指令。当时间限制或距离到达，底盘将继续执行**转**指令。\n\n![setDriveTimeout_example_revised2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_timeout/setDriveTimeout_example_revised2.png)\n\n"},"set_drive_velocity":{"name":"set_drive_velocity","markdown":"# 设定驱动速度\n\n设定底盘的速度。\n\n![setDriveVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定驱动速度**只会设定底盘的速度但是不会导致底盘移动。仍然须要一个**驱动**指令块。\n\n设定 **驱动速度**接受范围为 **-100% 到 100%** 或 **-600rpm 到 600rpm**。\n\n根据底盘使用的V5智能电机中安装的齿轮盒，**设定驱动速度**将报告不同的“转每分钟（rpm）”范围。\n\n* 红色齿轮盒：-100rpm 到 100rpm\n* 绿色齿轮盒：-200rpm 到 200rpm\n* 蓝色齿轮盒：-600rpm 到 600rpm\n\n设定底盘速度为负值将导致底盘反向移动。\n\n设定底盘速度为0将导致底盘停止。\n\n**设定驱动速度**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![setDriveVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_drive_velocity/setDriveVelocity_unit.png)\n\n\n"},"set_fill_color":{"name":"set_fill_color","markdown":"# 设定填充色\n\n设定V5主控器屏幕上的填充色。\n\n![set_fill_color_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定填充色**指令块将用于设定V5主控器屏幕上所画圆形和矩形内部填充色。\n\n选择一个填充的颜色。\n\n![set_fill_color_color](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_fill_color/set_fill_color_color.png)  \n该填充色将用于任何在V5主控器屏幕上所画的图形。"},"set_font":{"name":"set_font","markdown":"# 设定字体\n\n在V5主控器屏幕上打印数字或文本时，设定字体的样式和大小。\n\n![set_font_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_font/set_font_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\nV5主控器屏幕上支持两种不同样式的字体：\n\n* 等宽字体 (Mono) - 每一个字符取相同宽度。\n* 比例字体 (Prop) - 每个字符宽度按比例自动调整。\n  \n选择使用哪一种字体样式和大小。\n\n![set_font_block_font](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_font/set_font_block_font.png)  \n\n新的字体将用于在V5主控器屏幕上打印的文本。"},"set_gyro_heading":{"name":"set_gyro_heading","markdown":"# 设定归位\n\n设定陀螺仪/惯性传感器当前归位位置为设定值。\n\n![set_gyro_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定陀螺仪/惯性传感器归位**指令块可用于设定陀螺仪为任意指定的顺时针位置。当朝向值设为0时，该指令块可用于重置陀螺仪/惯性传感器朝向。\n\n**设定陀螺仪归位**接受范围为**0 到 359.99**度。\n\n**设定归位**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n选择使用哪一个陀螺仪/惯性传感器，然后输入期望值。\n\n![set_gyro_heading_gyro](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_gyro_heading/set_gyro_heading_gyro.png)\n\n\n"},"set_gyro_rotation":{"name":"set_gyro_rotation","markdown":"# 设定陀螺仪转向\n\n设定3线陀螺仪或V5惯性传感器旋转角度至指令块内设定的值。\n\n![setrotation](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**设定陀螺仪转向**指令块可用于设定底盘转向角度至任意指定的正值（顺时针）或负值（逆时针）。\n\n**设定陀螺仪转向**指令块可接受一定范围内任意小数或整数的正值或负值数字。\n\n**设定陀螺仪转向**指令块可接受小数，整数或数字指令块。\n\n选择使用哪一个陀螺仪。\n\n![setrotation_devices](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_gyro_rotation/setrotation_devices.png)\n\n\n"},"set_item_of_2d_array":{"name":"set_item_of_2d_array","markdown":"# 置换二维数组元素\n\n更新二维数组中某个元素的值。\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n输入数组内将要被置换元素的行（第一个数）和列（第二个数）位置。\n\n选择使用哪一个数组，该数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_options.png)\n\n**置换元素**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_2d_array/replace_item_2d_block_2.png)\n"},"set_item_of_array":{"name":"set_item_of_array","markdown":"# 置换元素\n\n更新数组中某个元素的值。\n\n![replace_item_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个数组，该数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![replace_item_options](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_array/replace_item_options.png)\n\n**置换元素**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![replace_item_block_2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_item_of_array/replace_item_block_2.png)\n"},"set_joint_move_speed":{"name":"set_joint_move_speed","markdown":"# Set joint speed\n\nSets the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's joint movements.\n\n![joint_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_joint_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_joint_move_speed/select_joint_speed_arm.png)\n\nChoose the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's joint movements. The default speed is **normal**.\n\n![joint_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_joint_move_speed/joint_speed_select.png)"},"set_led":{"name":"set_led","markdown":"# 设定LED\n\n打开或关闭LED。\n\n![set_led_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_led/set_led_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个LED。\n\n![set_led_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_led/set_led_block_device.png)\n\n选择LED是否打开或关闭。\n\n![set_led_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_led/set_led_block_setting.png)\n\n"},"set_linear_move_speed":{"name":"set_linear_move_speed","markdown":"# Set linear speed\n\nSets the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's linear movements.\n\n![linear_speed_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_linear_speed_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_linear_move_speed/select_linear_speed_arm.png)\n\nChoose the speed of the V5 Robotic Arm's linear movements. The default speed is **normal**.\n\n![linear_speed_select.png](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_linear_move_speed/linear_speed_select.png)"},"set_mastering":{"name":"set_mastering","markdown":"# Set mastering\n\nSets the mastering values of the four joints of the V5 Robotic Arm to allow it to be calibrated to the same known location.\n\n![set_mastering_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_mastering/set_mastering_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nInput the mastering values from the V5 Brain to the **set mastering** block. \n\nThe passable threshold values for the joints are as follows:\n\n* Joint 1: 1800 - 2200\n* Joint 2: 1900 - 2400\n* Joint 3: 1400 - 1800\n* Joint 4: 200 - 650\n\n![mastering_values](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_mastering/mastering_values.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_mastering_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_mastering/select_mastering_arm.png)\n\nThe **set mastering** block accepts integers and numeric blocks.\n\n![mastering_input](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_mastering/mastering_input.png)"},"set_motor_controller_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_controller_velocity","markdown":"# 设定电机控制器速度\n\n设定连接到电机控制器29的393电机的速度。\n\n![set_motor_controller_velocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_velocity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定电机控制器速度**接受范围为 **-100% to 100%**。\n\n设定393电机为负值时，393电机反转。\n\n设定393电机为0时，393电机停止。\n\n选择使用哪一个393电机。\n\n![set_motor_controller_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_controller_velocity/set_motor_controller_motor.png)"},"set_motor_position":{"name":"set_motor_position","markdown":"# 设定电机转位\n\n设定V5智能电机编码器转位为指定值。\n\n![setMotorPosition_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机转位**指令块可用于设定电机转位为任意指定值。\n\n通常情况下，**电机转位**指令块通过设定转位为0来重置电机编码器转位。\n\n选择使用哪一个V5智能电机。\n\n![setMotorPosition_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_motor.png)\n\n选择测量单位为度数或转数。\n\n![setMotorPosition_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_position/setMotorPosition_unit.png)"},"set_motor_stopping":{"name":"set_motor_stopping","markdown":"# 设定电机停止\n\n设定V5智能电机停止时的行为。\n\n![setMotorStopping_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用 \n\n* **刹车**将导致电机立即停止。\n* **滑行**让电机逐渐的转到停止。\n* **锁住**将导致底盘立即停止，同时如果有移动会转回到它停止的位置。\n\n**设定电机停止**将对随后程序中所有电机指令生效。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![setMotorStopping_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_motor.png)\n\n选择电机停止后的设置。\n\n![setMotorStopping_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_setting.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示机械臂电机正转90度，然后抵抗外部作用力（比如重力）来锁住它的位置。\n\n![setMotorStopping_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_stopping/setMotorStopping_example_revised.png)\n\n\n"},"set_motor_timeout":{"name":"set_motor_timeout","markdown":"# 设定电机超时\n\n针对V5智能电机运动指令设定一个时间限制。\n\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当驱动指令块未达到它的转位，电机时间限制可用来防止驱动指令块阻止指令段中其他指令块的运行。\n一个电机未达到转位的示例是一个机械臂或钳爪达到它的机械限制且无法完成它的转动。\n\n**设定电机超时**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示如果钳爪电机未达到270度位置，在2秒后结束**设定电机**指令。当时间限制或目标达到，钳爪电机将转位到0度。\n![setMotorTimeout_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_timeout/setMotorTimeout_example.png)"},"set_motor_torque":{"name":"set_motor_torque","markdown":"# 设定电机扭矩\n\n设定V5智能电机的力量。\n\n![setMotorTorque_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定电机扭矩**接受范围为**0% 到 100%**。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![setMotorTorque_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_motor.png)\n\n**设定电机扭矩**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示以最大扭矩为20%来转动钳爪电机转位至40度，这将使得钳爪可以抓取一个物体，且不会因为力量过大而损坏物体。\n\n![setMotorTorque_example_revised](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_torque/setMotorTorque_example_revised.png)"},"set_motor_velocity":{"name":"set_motor_velocity","markdown":"# 设定电机转速\n\n设定V5智能电机转速。\n\n![setMotorVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定电机转速**接受范围为 **-100% 到 100%** 或 **-600rpm 到 600rpm**.\n\n根据使用的V5智能电机中安装的齿轮盒，**设定电机转速**将报告不同的“转每分钟（rpm）”范围。\n\n* 红色齿轮盒：-100rpm 到 100rpm\n* 绿色齿轮盒：-200rpm 到 200rpm\n* 蓝色齿轮盒：-600rpm 到 600rpm\n\n设定一个V5智能电机转速为负值将导致电机反转。\n\n设定一个V5智能电机转速为0将导致电机停止。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![setMotorVelocity_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_motor.png)\n\n选择转速单位为百分比或转每分钟（rpm）。\n\n![setMotorVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示设定机械臂电机转速为25%，缓慢转至90度转位。\n\n![setMotorVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_motor_velocity/setMotorVelocity_example.png)"},"set_pen_color":{"name":"set_pen_color","markdown":"# 设定笔色\n\n设定V5主控器屏幕上画笔的颜色。\n\n![drive_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定笔色**用于设定V5主控器屏幕上画点，线，文本的颜色。\n\n**设定笔色**也用于设定V5主控器屏幕上画圆形和矩形块边框的颜色。\n\n选择一种画笔的颜色。\n\n![drive_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_pen_color/set_pen_color_dropdown.png)  \n\n**设定笔色**将用于设定V5主控器屏幕上所画图形的边框颜色。"},"set_print_precision":{"name":"set_print_precision","markdown":"# 设定打印精度\n\n设定当V5主控器或遥控器屏幕打印指令块时，小数点后的数字位数。\n\n![print_precision](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_print_precision/print_precision.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择将要打印到屏幕的指令块的精度级别。\n\n* 个位（1）（默认）\n* 十分位（0.1）\n* 百分位（0.01）\n* 千分位（0.001）\n* 全数字（0.000001）\n\n打印到屏幕的指令块将会取整到最近的精度级别。如下示例，1.67将会以个位精度打印为2且十分位精度为1.7。\n\n![print_precision_choice](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_print_precision/print_precision_choice.png)\n\n选择使用哪个设备。只有当V5遥控器被添加到设备窗口时才会显示。\n\n![print_precision_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_print_precision/print_precision_device.png)"},"set_shaft_encoder_position":{"name":"set_shaft_encoder_position","markdown":"# 设定光轴编码器转位\n\n设定光轴编码器转位为指定值。\n\n![set_encoder_position_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定光轴编码器转位**指令块可用于设定光轴编码器转位为任意指定值。\n\n通常情况下，使用**设定光轴编码器转位**设置为0来重置光轴编码转位。\n\n选择使用哪一个光轴编码器，然后设置期望值。\n\n![set_encoder_position_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_shaft_encoder_position/set_encoder_position_motor.png)\n\n"},"set_tool":{"name":"set_tool","markdown":"# Set tool\n\nSets the end effector or the end-of-arm tooling (EOAT) on the V5 Robotic Arm.\n\n![set_tool_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_tool/set_tool_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe end effector on the V5 Robotic Arm can be none (no attachment), an electromagnet, or a marker. \n\n![set_marker](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_tool/set_marker.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_tool_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_tool/select_tool_arm.png)\n\nChoose the tool on your V5 Robotic Arm. The default is set to **none**.\n\n![choose_tool](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_tool/choose_tool.png)"},"set_turn_velocity":{"name":"set_turn_velocity","markdown":"# 设定转向速度\n\n设定底盘转向速度。\n\n![setTurnVelocity_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定转向速度**只设定底盘速度但不会使得底盘移动。仍然须要一个**转**指令块。\n\n**设定转向速度**接受范围为 **-100% 到 100%** 或 **-600rpm 到 600rpm**。\n\n根据使用的V5智能电机中安装的齿轮盒，**设定转向速度**将报告不同的“转每分钟（rpm）”范围：\n\n* 红色齿轮盒：-100rpm 到 100rpm\n* 绿色齿轮盒：-200rpm 到 200rpm\n* 蓝色齿轮盒：-600rpm 到 600rpm\n\n设定一个底盘转向速度为负值将导致底盘反转。\n\n设定一个底盘转向速度为0将导致底盘停止。\n\n**设定转向速度**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![setTurnVelocity_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_unit.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本样例将演示底盘以25%的速度向左转。\n\n![setTurnVelocity_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_turn_velocity/setTurnVelocity_example.png)\n\n\n"},"set_variable":{"name":"set_variable","markdown":"# 设定变量\n\n设定变量为一个指定值。\n\n![set_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_variable/set_variable.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个变量，这些变量也可以被重命名或删除。 \n\n![set_variable_choose](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_variable/set_variable_choose.png)\n\n**设定变量**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![set_variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_variable/set_variable_inserted.png)\n\n"},"set_vision_object_index":{"name":"set_vision_object_index","markdown":"# 设定视觉传感器对象标号\n\n从检测到的对象之中设定对象（你想要获取更多信息的那个对象）标号。\n\n![set_vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**对象数目**指令块可用在**设定视觉传感器对象标号**指令块之前来决定检测到的对象数目。\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器。\n\n![set_vision_object_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_vision_object_index/set_vision_object_device.png)\n\n**设定视觉传感器对象标号**指令块可接受整数或数字指令块。\n\n\n\n"},"set_width":{"name":"set_width","markdown":"# 设定笔宽\n\n设定V5主控器屏幕上所画形状的外边框宽度。\n\n![set_width_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_width/set_width_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**设定笔宽**用于设定V5主控器屏幕上所画圆形和矩形的外边框宽度。\n\n**设定笔宽**可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![v5_row_column_brain](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/set_width/v5_row_column_brain.jpg)\n"},"setangle":{"name":"setangle","markdown":"# Set angle\n\nSets the angle of the tool plate before the next [Linear move] or [Joint move] block is executed.\n\n![set_angle_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/setangle/set_angle_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nThe **set angle** block sets the tool plate to be tilted at an angle either **up** or **down** before the next [Linear move] or [Joint move] block in a project. \n\nNote that the **set angle** block sets the angle for all future [Linear move] and [Joint move] blocks, unless it is set otherwise.\n\n![tool_plate](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/setangle/tool_plate.png)\n\nChoose which Robotic Arm to use.\n\n![select_set_angle_arm](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/setangle/select_set_angle_arm.png)\n\nChoose the angle of the tool plate. The default is set to **up**.\n\n* The tool plate will be **horizontal** when it is set to **down**. \n* The tool plate will be **vertical** when it is set to **up**. \n\n![select_angle](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/setangle/select_angle.png)\n\n## Example\n\nIn this example, the tool plate will begin to tilt once the [Joint move] block is executed and complete its tilting movement before the [Linear move] block.\n\n![set_angle_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/setangle/set_angle_example.png)"},"size_of_array":{"name":"size_of_array","markdown":"# 数组长度\n\n报告一个数组中元素的数量。  \n\n![size_of_array](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/size_of_array/size_of_array.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个数组。该数组也可以被重命名或删除。\n\n![size_of_array_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/size_of_array/size_of_array_select.png)\n\n**数组长度**报告指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![size_of_array_insert](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/size_of_array/size_of_array_insert.png)"},"snapshot":{"name":"snapshot","markdown":"# 拍照\n\n使用视觉传感器拍照。\n\n![snapshot_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/snapshot/snapshot_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**拍照**指令块将从视觉传感器的当前画面中，捕捉将被处理和分析的颜色标记和编码。\n \n\n一般在使用其他视觉传感器指令块之前，首先需要一个**拍照**。\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器。\n\n![snapshot_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/snapshot/snapshot_device.png)\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器标记。视觉传感器标记在设备窗口中配置。\n\n![snapshot_signature](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/snapshot/snapshot_signature.png)\n"},"spin":{"name":"spin","markdown":"# 转\n\n转动一个V5智能电机直到停止。\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin/spin_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**转**指令块将永远转动一个电机直到使用一个新的电机指令块或程序停止。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin/spin_motor.png)\n\n选择转动的方向。方向名称可以在设备窗口更改。\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin/spin_direction.png)"},"spin_for":{"name":"spin_for","markdown":"# 转至\n\n转动一个V5电机到指定的距离。\n\n![spin_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_for/spin_for_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**转至**将告诉一个电机从它当前位置以指定方向转动到指定距离。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![spin_for_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_for/spin_for_motor.png)\n\n选择转动的方向。方向名称可以在设备窗口更改。\n\n![spin_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_for/spin_for_direction.png)  \n\n**转至**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n选择测量单位为度数或转数。\n\n![spin_for_value](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_for/spin_for_value.png)\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到电机完成转动。\n\n你可以选择箭头来展开**并且不等待** - 这将导致其他指令块在电机转动时同时继续运行。\n\n![spin_for_dont_wait_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_for/spin_for_dont_wait_block.png)"},"spin_motor_controller":{"name":"spin_motor_controller","markdown":"# 转电机控制器\n\n转动连接到电机控制器29的393电机直到停止。\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**转电机控制器**指令块将永远转动一个393电机直到使用一个新的393电机指令块或程序停止。\n\n选择使用哪一个393电机。\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_motor.png)\n\n选择转动的方向。方向名称可以在设备窗口更改。\n\n![spin_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_motor_controller/spin_393_direction.png)"},"spin_servo":{"name":"spin_servo","markdown":"# 转伺服器\n\n转动伺服器到指定的位置。\n\n![spin_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_servo/servo_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**转伺服器**接受范围为**0 to 100 度**。\n\n![spin_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_servo/servo_port.png)\n\n"},"spin_to_position":{"name":"spin_to_position","markdown":"# 转至转位\n\n转动一个V5智能电机至设定的转位。\n\n![spin_to_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_to_position/spin_to_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**转至转位**将告诉电机转动到一个设定转位。根据电机当前转位，**转至转位**将决定转动的方向。\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![spin_to_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_to_position/spin_to_motor.png)\n\n**转至转位**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n选择测量单位为度数或转数。\n\n![spin_to_value](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_to_position/spin_to_value.png)\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到电机完成转动。\n\n你可以选择箭头来展开**并且不等待** - 这将导致其他指令块在电机转动时同时继续运行。\n\n![spin_to_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/spin_to_position/spin_to_anddontwait.png)"},"stop_driving":{"name":"stop_driving","markdown":"# 停止驱动\n\n停止底盘。\n\n![stopDriving_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/stop_driving/stopDriving_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**停止驱动**指令块将使底盘完全停止，并使用**设定驱动停止**设置滑行，刹车或锁住方式停止在其位置。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示底盘正向驱动3秒钟后停止。\n\n![stopDriving_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/stop_driving/stopDriving_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor":{"name":"stop_motor","markdown":"# 停止电机\n\n停止一个电机。\n\n![stopMotor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/stop_motor/stopMotor_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择停止哪一个电机。\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/stop_motor/stop_motor.png)\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示钳爪电机打开3秒钟后停止。\n\n![stopMotor_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/stop_motor/stopMotor_example.png)\n\n"},"stop_motor_controller":{"name":"stop_motor_controller","markdown":"# Stop motor controller\n\nStops a Motor 393 connected to a Motor Controller 29.\n\n![stop_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_block.png)\n\n## How To Use\n\nChoose which Motor 393 to stop.\n\n![stop_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_motor.png)\n\nThis example will spin a Motor 393 forward for 3 seconds before stopping.\n\n![stop_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/stop_motor_controller/stop_393_example.png)"},"subtract":{"name":"subtract","markdown":"# 减法\n\n从一个值减去另一个值并报告差值。\n\n![subtract](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/subtract/subtract.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**减法**可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n**减法**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n两个数字相减。\n\n![subtract_example1](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/subtract/subtract_example1.png)\n\n减法中可以用变量值。\n\n![subtract_example2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/subtract/subtract_example2.png)  \n\n减法中可以用传感器或设备值。\n\n![subtract_example3](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/subtract/subtract_example3.png)"},"temperature_of_motor":{"name":"temperature_of_motor","markdown":"# 电机温度\n\n报告V5智能电机的温度。\n\n![temp_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n使用**电机温度**指令块能帮助用户防止他们的V5智能电机在大量使用过程中过热。\n\n**电机温度**范围为**0% to 100%**。\n\n选择使用哪一个V5智能电机。\n\n![temp_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\n**电机温度**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![temp_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/temperature_of_motor/temp_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"timer_value":{"name":"timer_value","markdown":"# 计时器值\n\n报告V5主控器计时器秒数值。\n\n![timerValue_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/timer_value/timerValue_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n在程序开始时，计时器从0秒开始计时并报告小数值。\n\n**计时器值**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![timerValue_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/timer_value/timerValue_inserted.png)\n"},"torque_of_motor":{"name":"torque_of_motor","markdown":"# 电机扭矩\n\n报告V5智能电机当前扭矩（转动作用力）。\n\n![motor_torque](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/torque_of_motor/motor_torque.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机扭矩**范围为**0.0 到 18.6 英寸-磅（InLB）** 或者 **0.0 到 2.1 牛顿-米（Nm）**。\n\n选择报告哪一个V5智能电机的扭矩。\n\n![motor_torque_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_device.png)\n\n选择**电机扭矩**报告单位为英寸磅（InLB）或 牛顿米（Nm）。\n\n![motor_torque_units](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_units.png)\n\n**电机扭矩**指令块可被用于圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![motor_torque_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/torque_of_motor/motor_torque_inserted.png)"},"turn":{"name":"turn","markdown":"# 转\n\n永远转动底盘。\n\n![turn_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn/turn_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**转**指令块将永远转动底盘，直到使用一个新的底盘指令块或程序停止。\n\n选择底盘将要转动的方向。\n\n![turn_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn/turn_direction.png)"},"turn_for":{"name":"turn_for","markdown":"# 转至\n\n转动底盘至一个指定距离。\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn_for/turn_for_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择底盘将要转动的方向。\n\n![turn_for_direction](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn_for/turn_for_direction.png)  \n\n通过输入一个数字度数来设定底盘将要移动多远。\n\n**驱动至**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![turn_for_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn_for/turn_for_block_2.png)\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到底盘完成转动。\n\n你可以选择箭头来展开**并且不等待** - 这将导致其他指令块在底盘转动时同时继续运行。\n\n![turn_for_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn_for/turn_for_anddontwait.png)\n"},"turn_to_heading":{"name":"turn_to_heading","markdown":"# 归位至\n\n当使用陀螺仪时，底盘转动至一个特定归位位置。\n\n![turn_to_heading_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**归位至**指令块可用于转动底盘至任意指定顺时针位置。\n\n根据陀螺仪当前朝向，**归位至**将决定转动的方向。\n\n**归位至**接受范围为**0.00 到 359.99**度。\n\n**归位至**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n本例将演示底盘做四次转动：\n\n![turn_to_heading_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_example.png)\n\n- 左转至45度\n- 左转至90度\n- 左转至270度\n- 右转至180度\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到底盘完成转向。\n\n你可以选择箭头来展开**并且不等待** - 这将导致在底盘转向的同时其他指令块继续运行。\n\n![turn_to_heading_anddontwait](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_heading/turn_to_heading_anddontwait.png)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},"turn_to_rotation":{"name":"turn_to_rotation","markdown":"# 转向至\n\n当底盘配置3线陀螺仪或V5惯性传感器时，转动底盘至一个特定的转向角度。\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_iq.png)\n\n## 如何使用\n\n**转向至**指令块可用于转动底盘至一个指定的正值（顺时针）或负值（逆时针）。\n\n根据底盘当前**转向**值，**转向至**将决定转动的方向。\n\n**转向至**指令块可接受小数，整数或数字指令块。\n\n## 示例\n\n该示例将导致底盘做四次转动：\n\n![turn_to_rotation_example](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_rotation/turn_to_rotation_example.png)\n\n- 右转（顺时针）至90度\n- 右转（顺时针）至180度\n- 左转（腻时针）至-45度\n- 右转（顺时针）至0度\n\n默认情况下，其他指令块将**等待**直到底盘转动完成。\n\n你可以选择箭头来展开**并且不等待** -这将导致底盘转动的同时其他指令块继续运行。\n\n![drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/turn_to_rotation/drivetrain_turntorotation_dontwait_iq.png)"},"variable":{"name":"variable","markdown":"# 变量\n\n报告赋值给变量的值。\n\n![variable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/variable/variable.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**变量**指令块用于报告存储在变量中的值。使用**设定变量**指令块来设定或更新一个变量的值。\n\n![variable_cursor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/variable/variable_cursor.png)\n\n**变量**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![variable_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/variable/variable_inserted.png)\n\n变量都由**定义一个变量**按钮生成。\n\n![make_variable](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/variable/make_variable.png)  \n"},"velocity_of_motor":{"name":"velocity_of_motor","markdown":"# 电机转速\n\n报告V5智能电机当前转速。\n\n![velocity_of_motor_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**电机转速**报告范围为 **-100% 到 100%** 或 **-600rpm 到 600rpm**。\n\n根据使用的V5智能电机中安装的齿轮盒，**电机转速**将报告不同的“转每分钟（rpm）”范围。\n\n* 红色齿轮盒：-100rpm 到 100rpm\n* 绿色齿轮盒：-200rpm 到 200rpm\n* 蓝色齿轮盒：-600rpm 到 600rpm\n\n选择使用哪一个电机。\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_motor.png)\n\n选择**电机转速**单位为百分比（%）或转每分钟（rpm）。\n\n![velocity_of_motor_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_options_unit.png)\n\n**电机转速**指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![velocity_of_motor_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_motor/velocity_of_motor_inserted.png)"},"velocity_of_shaft_encoder":{"name":"velocity_of_shaft_encoder","markdown":"# 光轴编码器转速\n\n报告光轴编码器当前转速。\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**光轴编码器转速**以度每秒（dps）或转每分钟（rpm）的单位报告小数值。\n\n选择使用哪一个光轴编码器。\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_motor](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_motor.png)\n\n选择光轴编码器转速的单位：度每秒(dps)或转每分钟(rpm)。\n\n![velocity_of_encoder_options_unit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/velocity_of_shaft_encoder/velocity_of_encoder_options_unit.png)"},"vision_object":{"name":"vision_object","markdown":"# 视觉传感器对象\n\n报告视觉传感器检测到的一个对象信息。\n\n![vision_object_block](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/vision_object/vision_object_block.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n为了使用**视觉传感器对象**指令块，使用如下步骤：\n\n1. 使用设备窗口配置你的视觉传感器。\n2. 使用**拍照**来捕捉一个视觉传感器画面并寻找某个标记/颜色编码。\n3. 使用**对象存在**来检验视觉传感器是否检测到了需要的标记/颜色编码。\n\n当视觉传感器检测到一个对象，你可以使用其他视觉传感器指令块来获取更多检测到的对象信息。\n\n* 使用**设定视觉传感器对象标号**来设定你想获取更多信息的已检测对象。默认情况下，使用检测到的最大对象。\n* 使用**对象数目**来决定需要的标记/颜色编码的对象被检测到多少个。\n* 使用**视觉传感器对象**来决定报告检测到对象的哪些信息。\n\n选择使用哪一个视觉传感器。\n\n![vision_object_block_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/vision_object/vision_object_block_device.png)\n\n选择报告视觉传感器的哪一项值：\n\n* 宽度 - 对象像素有多宽，返回值范围为**2 - 316px**.\n* 高度 - 对象像素有多高，返回值范围为**2 - 212px**.\n* 中心X轴 - 报告检测到对象的中心点X轴坐标，返回值范围为**0 - 315px**.\n* 中心Y轴 - 报告检测到对象的中心点Y轴坐标，返回值范围为**0 - 211px**.\n* 角度 - 报告检测到对象的角度。返回值范围为**0 - 180度**。\n\n![vision_object_block_setting](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/vision_object/vision_object_block_setting.png)\n\n**视觉传感器对象**报告指令块可被用在圆形空白指令块中。\n\n![vision_object_block_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/vision_object/vision_object_block_inserted.png)\n"},"wait":{"name":"wait","markdown":"# 等待\n\n在移动到下一条指令块之前等待特定数量的时间。\n\n![wait](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/wait/wait.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择**等待**的时间数量。\n\n**等待**指令块可接受小数，整数，或数字指令块。\n\n![wait_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/wait/wait_select.png)\n\n\n"},"wait_until":{"name":"wait_until","markdown":"# 等到\n\n在移动到下一条指令块前，等待布尔指令块报告**真**值。\n\n![wait_until](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/wait_until/wait_until.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**等到**将重复检验布尔指令块，且不会移动到下一条指令块，直到这个布尔指令块报告**真**值。\n\n**等到**指令块可接受六角形空白指令块。\n\n![wait_until_2](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/wait_until/wait_until_2.png)\n\n"},"when_autonomous":{"name":"when_autonomous","markdown":"# 当自控\n\n当从竞赛场控或竞赛开关接收到“自动”模式信号时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_autonomous](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_autonomous/when_autonomous.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当机器人连接到设置为“自动”模式的竞赛场控或竞赛开关时，将自动运行**当自控**事件随后的指令段。\n\n程序中，用户最多可以使用50个**当自控**指令块。"},"when_brain_screen":{"name":"when_brain_screen","markdown":"# 当主控屏幕\n\n当V5主控器屏幕被按下或松开时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**当主控屏幕**事件可以用于创建与V5主控器触摸屏交互的动作或行为。\n\n与**屏幕坐标**指令块一起使用，通过检测屏幕上发生触摸的时间和坐标，用户可以创建V5主控器自定义交互接口。\n\n选择哪一个动作将触发事件 - **按下** 或 **松开**\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_brain_screen/when_brain_pressed_condition.png)"},"when_broadcasted":{"name":"when_broadcasted","markdown":"# 当我收到\n\n当收到指定的**广播**消息时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_broadcast](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择接收哪一条消息。也可以生成一条新消息。\n\n![when_broadcast_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_broadcasted/when_broadcast_select.png)\n\n**当我收到**指令块中的消息只会来自一个不同指令段中的**广播** 或 **广播并等待**指令块。"},"when_bumper":{"name":"when_bumper","markdown":"# 当碰撞开关\n\n当指定的碰撞开关被按下或松开时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_bumper](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_bumper/when_bumper.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个碰撞开关。\n\n![when_bumper_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_bumper/when_bumper_select.png)\n\n选择哪一个动作将触发事件 - **按下** 或 **松开**\n\n![when_bumper_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_bumper/when_bumper_condition.png)\n"},"when_controller_axis":{"name":"when_controller_axis","markdown":"# 当遥控器轴\n\n当指定的V5遥控器操纵杆轴移动时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_controller_axis](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个V5遥控器。\n\n![when_controller_axis_device](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_device.png)\n\n选择使用遥控器哪一个操纵杆。\n\n![when_controller_axis_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_axis/when_controller_axis_select.png)\n"},"when_controller_button":{"name":"when_controller_button","markdown":"# 当遥控器按键\n\n当指定的V5遥控器按键被按下或松开时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_controller_button](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_button/when_controller_button.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个V5遥控器。\n\n![when_controller_button_controller](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_controller.png)\n\n选择使用遥控器哪一个按键。\n\n![when_controller_button_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_select.png)\n\n选择哪一个动作将触发事件 - **按下** 或 **松开**\n\n![when_controller_button_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_controller_button/when_controller_button_condition.png)"},"when_driver":{"name":"when_driver","markdown":"# 当遥控\n\n当从竞赛场控或竞赛开关接收到“遥控”模式信号时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_driver/when_driver.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n当机器人连接到设置为“遥控”模式的竞赛场控或竞赛开关时，将运行**当遥控**事件随后的任何指令块。\n\n强烈建议**永续**循环与**当遥控**事件结合使用，从而允许在遥控赛段期间，频繁更新V5遥控器的指令。\n\n程序中，用户最多可以使用50个**当遥控**指令块。"},"when_limit":{"name":"when_limit","markdown":"# 当限位开关\n\n当指定的限位开关被按下或松开时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_limit](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_limit/when_limit.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n选择使用哪一个限位开关。\n\n![when_limit_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_limit/when_limit_select.png)\n\n选择哪一个动作将触发事件 - **按下** 或 **松开**\n\n![when_limit_condition](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_limit/when_limit_condition.png)\n"},"when_started":{"name":"when_started","markdown":"# 当开始\n\n当程序开始时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_started](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_started/when_started.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**当开始**指令块可以从V5主控器菜单开始运行，也可以从VEXcode V5 Blocks**运行**按钮开始运行。\n\n所有新建程序将会自动包含一个**当开始**指令块，程序可最多支持50个**当开始**指令块。\n\n**当开始**也可以作为VRC竞赛程序的准备模式指令段。\n"},"when_timer":{"name":"when_timer","markdown":"# 当计时器\n\n当V5主控器计时器大于指定值时，运行随后的指令段。\n\n![when_timer](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_timer/when_timer.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n在每个程序开始时，主控器的计时器开始计时。\n\n选择时间数量。当主控器的计时器**大于**输入时间数量时，**当计时器**事件将会运行。\n\n![when_timer_select](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/when_timer/when_timer_select.png)\n\n**当计时器**指令块可接受小数或整数值。\n\n**当计时器**指令块不能接受其他指令块。"},"while":{"name":"while","markdown":"# 当\n\n**当**是一个C型控制指令块，当布尔条件为**真**值，将重复执行所包含的指令块。\n\n![while](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/while/while.png)\n\n## 如何应用\n\n**当**指令块只在每个循环开始时检查布尔条件。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**真**值，**当**指令块所包含的指令块将运行。\n\n如果布尔条件报告为**假**值，**当**指令块所包含的指令块将被跳过。\n\n**当**C型控制指令块可接受六角形指令块作为它的条件。 \n\n![while_inserted](static/help/v5/blocks/zh-CN/while/while_inserted.png)"}}}};/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (data);

